VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast core needle biopsy\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: SUGHRA RAZA M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Kevin B Long, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Susan Lester, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aLEFT BREAST, 11 G STEREOTACTIC CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR CALCIFICATIONS:\u000a3:00, OUTER:\u000aATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA associated with columnar cell change and\u000acalcifications (see note).\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia.\u000aNote: ADH is best evaluated with excision.\u000aUPPER INNER:\u000aATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA associated with columnar cell change and\u000acalcifications (see note).\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia.\u000aNote: ADH is best evaluated with excision.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHISTORY: 74 year old woman with two suspicious clusters of calcifications in\u000athe left breast; two stereo biopsies. #1: 3:00 cluster. Differential\u000adiagnosis: DCIS vs. benign left 3:00. #2: left upper inner\u000aBREAST IMAGING FINDING:\u000a1. Left: Nonpalpable calcifications.\u000a2. Left: Nonpalpable calcifications.\u000aLOCATION:\u000a1. Left: outer\u000a2. Left: upper inner\u000aTYPE OF CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY:\u000a1. 11 G Stereotactic\u000a2. 11 G Stereotactic\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000a1. Cassette A - calcs, cassette B - no calcs - Pink. In formalin at 9:50 am.\u000a2. Cassette A - calcs, cassette B no calcs - Green. In formalin at 10:50 am.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, in two parts, each labeled with the\u000apatient's name, unit number.\u000aPart A, labeled "left breast", consists of two pink cassettes, one labeled "A\u000aCA++" containing multiple cylindrical fibrofatty soft tissues (1.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm in aggregate). The second pink cassette is labeled "B" and contains\u000amultiple cylindrical fibrofatty soft tissues (2.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate).\u000aThe specimen is submitted in toto.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Contents of pink cassette labeled "A CA++", multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Contents of pink cassette labeled "B", multi frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, labeled "left breast site #2", consists of green cassettes, one labeled\u000a"A CA++" containing multiple cylindrical fibrofatty soft tissues (1.8 x REMOVED_DATE x\u000a0.3 cm in aggregate). The second green cassette is labeled "B" and contains\u000amultiple cylindrical fibrofatty soft tissues (2.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate).\u000aThe specimen is submitted in its entirety.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Contents of green cassette labeled "A CA++", multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Contents of green cassette labeled "B", multi frags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000ajc/ag\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000aTuesday REMOVED_MONTH 17, 2009 at 11:51:27AM\u000a[report_end]
