VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID:REMOVED_CASE_ID Report Status: Signed\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aADDENDUM REPORT\u000aAddendum #1 Entered: REMOVED_DATE -0855\u005cE\u000aE\u005c\u000a*** ADDITIONAL DIAGNOSTIC INFORMATION ***\u000aThis report contains an addendum to the original for the purpose of providing\u000aadditional diagnostic information. The original diagnosis is unchanged.\u000aAJCC pTNM Staging (7th Ed.)(based on available surgical material):\u000apREMOVED_ACCESSION_IDc pNX pMX\u000aAddeundum Signed Electronically Signed MISIALEK,MICHAEL J. M.D. REMOVED_DATE \u000aDIAGNOSIS:\u000aRight breast, lumpectomy:\u000aInvasive ductal carcinoma, grade 2, REMOVED_DATE cm. (see synoptic report).\u000aDuctal carcinoma in situ, cribriform and solid types, grade 2.\u000aSYNOPTIC REPORT - INVASIVE BREAST CANCER\u000aAJCC pTNM CLASSIFICATION (6TH Ed.)(Based on available surgical material:\u000apREMOVED_ACCESSION_IDc pNX pMX\u000aHISTOLOGIC TYPE: invasive ductal carcinoma\u000aHISTOLOGIC GRADE (Nottingham System): II\u000aTUMOR LOCATION: right upper outer quadrant\u000aTUMOR SIZE (greatest dimension): REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000aLYMPHATIC/VASCULAR INVASION: none identified\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU (DCIS): present\u000aType: cribriform and solid\u000aGrade: 2\u000aExtent: multifocal\u000aSize (greatest dimension): microscopic foci within and around the\u000ainvasive tumor and focally in random\u000asections away from tumor\u000aExtensive intraductal component: absent\u000aNecrosis: present, type: punctate, focal\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU: none identified\u000aMICROCALCIFICATIONS: present within both invasive carcinoma and\u000aDCIS\u000aRESECTION MARGINS:\u000aInvasive Carcinoma: clear (greater than or equal to REMOVED_DATE cm.)\u000aDCIS: clear (greater than or equal to REMOVED_DATE cm.)\u000aIMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING (invasive carcinoma):\u000aPrior specimen REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID at the referring institution reported as:\u000aEstrogen receptor: POSITIVE (>10% of nuclei stained)\u000aProgesterone receptor: POSITIVE (>10% of nuclei stained)\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID): NEGATIVE (0) (no membrane staining)\u000aFISH: not amplified\u000aPerformed on block 3 reveals the following results:\u000aEstrogen receptor: POSITIVE (>10% of nuclei stained)\u000aProgesterone receptor: POSITIVE (>10% of nuclei stained)\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID): NEGATIVE (1+) (faint or <10% complete membrane staining)\u000aTotal Fixation Time: 7 hours\u000aSKIN:\u000aUnremarkable.\u000aADDITIONAL PATHOLOGIC FINDINGS:\u000aNon-neoplastic breast: fibrocystic changes; small fibroadenoma.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by: Michael J. Misialek, M.D.\u000aClinical diagnosis & history:\u000aRight breast cancer\u000aTissue-Designation:\u000aBreast, excision with margins - right\u000aGross description:\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin in one container, labeled "right breast\u000atissue" and consists of a 73 gram lumpectomy measuring 8 x 7 x REMOVED_DATE cm. A\u000aradiographic needle is in place. The specimen is inked intraoperatively as\u000afollows: anterior, green; inferior, blue; lateral, orange; medial, yellow;\u000aposterior, black; superior, red. Across the anterior surface is a 3 x 1 cm.\u000aportion of wrinkled unremarkable skin. The specimen is serially sectioned to\u000areveal, approximately centrally located, REMOVED_DATE cm. from the medial margin, REMOVED_DATE \u000acm. from the superior margin, 1 cm. from the inferior margin, 3 cm. from the\u000aposterior margin and REMOVED_DATE cm. deep to the skin and anterior margin and REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000afrom the lateral margin, is a firm, solid, well circumscribed tumor measuring\u000a1.1 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The remainder of the specimen is composed of unremarkable\u000afat and thin wispy, tan-pink tissue. No other mass lesions are identified.\u000aRepresentative sections are submitted.\u000aSection code: 1 - closest skin margin\u000a2-3 - entire tumor with closest anterior margin\u000a4 - closest inferior margin\u000a5 - closest superior and posterior margins\u000a6 - closest medial and lateral margins\u000a7 - breast tissue adjacent to tumor\u000a8-10 - random sections of background breast\u000aTotal fixation time is 7 hours.\u000aDictated by: MJM____(signature on file)____ REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a____(signature on file)____ REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a[report_end]
