VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast core needle biopsy\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: CHRISTINE M DENISON M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Rachel L Rucker-Schmidt, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Susan Lester, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aLEFT BREAST, UPPER OUTER, POSTERIOR, 11 G STEREOTACTIC CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR\u000aCALCIFICATIONS:\u000aFragments of a fibroadenoma with calcifications.\u000aLEFT BREAST, UPPER OUTER, ANTERIOR, 11 G STEREOTACTIC CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR\u000aCALCIFICATIONS:\u000aINVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA, well differentiated (modified Bloom-\u000aRichardson grade I/III), measuring at least REMOVED_DATE cm in size. An\u000aimmunoperoxidase study for p63 and cytokeratin REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID confirms the absence\u000aof myoepithelial cells in the area of invasion.\u000aNo lymphovascular invasion is seen in this limited specimen.\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU is present.\u000aColumnar cell change with calcifications is present.\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies are performed with the following results for\u000ainvasive carcinoma (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu NEGATIVE (0)\u000aNote: The calcifications are not associated with the carcinoma. The\u000acarcinoma may be an incidental finding.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHISTORY: 55 year old with recent MR core biopsy of left breast yielding ADH.\u000aPatient also has two groups of coarse heterogeneous ca++ LUOQ. Site 1 is LUOQ\u000aposterior. Site 2 is LUOQ anterior. The MR core site is midway between the two\u000agroups, which are 4 cm apart.\u000aBREAST IMAGING FINDING:\u000a1. Left: 7 mm, nonpalpable calcifications.\u000a2. Left: 10 mm, nonpalpable calcifications.\u000aThe lesions are 4 cm apart.\u000aLOCATION:\u000a1. Left: upper outer Posterior\u000a2. Left: upper outer Anterior\u000aTYPE OF CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY:\u000a1. 11 G Stereotactic Vacuum-assisted\u000a2. 11 G Stereotactic\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. A tissue with ca++, B remainder of tissue - 2 brown cassettes.\u000aB/2. A tissue with calcifications, B remainder of tissue - 2 pink cassettes.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, in two parts, each labeled with the\u000apatient's name and unit number.\u000aPart A, labeled "left breast site #1 L upper outer quadrant posterior",\u000aconsists of multiple tan/yellow to tan/white lobulated fibroadipose breast\u000atissue cores (2.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate). A portion of the breast tissue\u000acores are received in a brown cassette marked "A CA+2" and remainder of the\u000abreast tissue cores are received in a brown cassette marked "B". The specimen\u000ais submitted in toto.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Cassette "A CA+2", multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Cassette "B", multi frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, labeled "left breast site #2 L upper outer quadrant anterior", consists\u000aof multiple tan/yellow lobulated fibroadipose breast tissue cores (3.2 x REMOVED_DATE x\u000a0.3 cm in aggregate). A portion of the breast tissue cores are received in a\u000apink cassette marked "A CA+2" and remainder of the breast tissue cores are in a\u000apink cassette marked "B". The specimen is submitted in toto.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Cassette "A CA+2", multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Cassette "B", multi frags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000asek/ag\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a4/17/2008\u000a[report_end]
