VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Sentinel Lymph Nodes(s)\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ROGER L CHRISTIAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Qinghong Yang, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Jonathan N Glickman, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "LEFT SENTINEL LYMPH NODES" (including FSA):\u000aOne lymph node, negative for tumor (0:1).\u000a(3 H&E levels examined.)\u000aB. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "LEFT BREAST, TISSUE":\u000aTwo (2) core biopsy cavities.\u000aNo residual invasive lobular carcinoma, including margins (entire specimen\u000asubmitted for histologic examination).\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia with pagetoid spread.\u000aFibroadenomatoid change.\u000aColumnar cell hyperplasia.\u000aCalcifications associated with benign breast tissue.\u000aC. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "INFERIOR SHAVED MARGIN":\u000aBenign breast tissue with focal adenosis.\u000aCalcifications associated with benign epithelium.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Area of ADH, lt breast; area of lobular CA, Lt breast.\u000aOperation: Wire-directed excision, SNB L.\u000aOperative Findings: See op note.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Area of ADH, lt breast; area of lobular CA, Lt breast.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) Left sentinel node (FS).\u000aB/2) Left breast tissue; short - superior, long - lateral; primary tumor site.\u000aD/3) Inferior shaved margin - suture - superior (perm).\u000aRADIOLOGY: Specimen contains 2 wires, 2 clips, and residual Ca++.\u000a(Radiologist's signature is illegible.)\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "1) LEFT SENTINEL NODE" (FSA):\u000aOne lymph node, negative for tumor.\u000aOR Consultation by: JASON L. HORNICK, M.D., PH.D.\u000aResident: JAVAD BEHESHTI, M.D.\u000aThe senior physician certifies that he/she personally conducted a gross and/or\u000amicroscopic examination of the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed\u000athe rapid diagnos(es) related thereto.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in three parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart A, "#1. Left sentinel node", consists of a tan/yellow rubbery lymph node\u000a(0.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which is bisected and submitted in its entirety for\u000afrozen section as FSA.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: FSA remnant, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, "#2. Left breast tissue, short superior, long lateral, primary tumor\u000asite", consists of an irregular portion of fibrofatty tissue (5.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm), with a long suture designating lateral, and a short suture designating\u000asuperior. There is an overlying tan wrinkled grossly unremarkable skin ellipse\u000a(3.5 x REMOVED_DATE cm), along the anterior margin. There are two inserted needle\u000alocalization wires, as displayed on the accompanying radiograph. Needle\u000alocalization wire #1 (arbitrarily designated by prosector), enters along the\u000asuperior-anterior margin, and exits at the posterior margin. Needle\u000alocalization wire #2 (arbitrarily designated by the prosector) enters through\u000athe unremarkable skin ellipse on the anterior margin, and exits at the\u000aposterior-inferior margin. The specimen is received partially previously inked\u000aper pathology protocol as anterior blue, posterior black, superior red,\u000ainferior green, and medial orange. The specimen is additionally inked yellow\u000aby the prosector, along the lateral margin. The specimen is serially\u000asectioned, to reveal a biopsy cavity (0.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), containing a\u000asurgical clip, adjacent to needle localization wire #1. The biopsy cavity is\u000anow designated as biopsy cavity #1, and is REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE \u000acm from the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000amedial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior\u000amargin. There is scant additional biopsy cavity (1.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), adjacent\u000ato needle localization wire #2, containing a surgical clip. This cavity is REMOVED_DATE \u000acm anterior to biopsy cavity #1, and is REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom the lateral margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000amedial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior\u000amargin. Both cavities are surrounded by focal areas of dense white fibrous\u000atissue, with no discrete masse or lesions identified. The remaining cut\u000asurface displays 70% yellow lobulated adipose tissue, and 30% white fibrous\u000atissue, with no discrete masses or lesions identified. The specimen is\u000asequentially submitted in its entirety.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Posterior margin, radially, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross sections, containing biopsy cavity #1, with the\u000aclip identified in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross section, bisected, containing biopsy cavity #1, 1\u000afrag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross section, bisected, containing biopsy cavity #1\u000aand #2 in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross section, bisected, containing biopsy cavity #1\u000aand #2 in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID 11: Sequential cross section, bisected, containing biopsy cavity #1\u000aand biopsy cavity #2 in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, with the surgical clip in biopsy cavity #2\u000aidentified in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross section, bisected, with biopsy cavity #2 in\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross section, bisected, with biopsy cavity #2 in\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross section, bisected, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross section, bisected, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross section, bisected, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross section, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Anterior margin, with the tan skin ellipse, 3 frags each, ESS.\u000aPart C, "#3. Inferior shaved margin, suture superior", consists of an irregular\u000aportion of fibrofatty tissue (3.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), with a suture along one\u000aaspect designating the superior margin. The opposite aspect is received\u000apreviously inked green. The aspect displaying the suture is inked black by the\u000aprosector. The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal 60% yellow lobulated\u000aadipose tissue, and 40% focally dense white fibrous tissue, with no discrete\u000amasses or lesions are identified. The specimen is sequentially submitted in\u000aits entirety.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross sections.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 2 frags each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 3 frags, ESS.\u000aCP/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jonathan N Glickman M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a5/5/2008\u000a[report_end]
