VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID LYMPH NODES REGIONAL RESECTION\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aLESTER, SUSAN, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST, RE-EXCISION:\u000aINVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA, poorly differentiated (modified\u000aBloom-Richardson grade III/III), REMOVED_DATE cm, present near the prior biopsy\u000asite (see note).\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies are performed with the following results for\u000ainvasive carcinoma:\u000aCytokeratin 7 POSITIVE\u000aCytokeratin 20 NEGATIVE\u000aEstrogen receptor NEGATIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor NEGATIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu NEGATIVE\u000aTTF-1 NEGATIVE\u000aNormal epithelial cells are appropriately immunoreactive for estrogen\u000aand progesterone receptors.\u000aNo lymphovascular invasion is seen. No dermal lymphatic invasion is seen.\u000aNo carcinoma in situ is present (EIC negative).\u000aThe invasive carcinoma is < REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin focally,\u000a0.2 cm from the posterior margin, and > REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior, lateral,\u000amedial, and anterior margins.\u000aNote: The residual carcinoma appears viable and numerous mitotic figures\u000aare present. There is no histologic evidence of treatment effect.\u000aPrior to treatment, there were infrequent tumor cells positive for\u000aprogesterone receptor. In the post-treatment carcinoma, no PR positive\u000acells are seen. This change could be due to the treatment or due to tumor\u000aheterogeneity.\u000aThe immunoperoxidase profile would be consistent with a breast primary\u000asite, but is not specific for this site.\u000aLEFT AXILLARY LYMPH NODE DISSECTION:\u000aTwelve lymph nodes with no tumor seen.\u000aNote: There is no evidence in the lymph nodes of prior metastatic\u000acarcinoma.\u000aPORTACATH:\u000aPortacath (gross examination).\u000a(Clinical history: 39 year old woman with prior excision of an (at least)\u000a3.1 cm poorly differentiated carcinoma, now s/p chemotherapy.)\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Left breast cancer, core biopsy REMOVED_DATE  completed chemotherapy:\u000aadriamyocin, cytoxan, taxol.\u000aOperation: Left axillary dissection, left breast lumpectomy, removal of\u000aPortacath.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1. Left axillary content stitch marks apex.\u000a#2. Left breast tissue, long lateral short superior.\u000a#3. Portacath (gross ID only).\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by FIRESTEIN,RON,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received in three separate containers, each labeled with the\u000apatient's name and medical record number.\u000aContainer #1 is designated "axillary contents left", and is fixed in\u000aBouin's. The specimen consists of a single portion of yellow adipose tissue\u000ameasuring 6 x 5 x 3 cm and containing a single stitch designating the apex.\u000aPotential lymph nodes are identified and are completely submitted from apex to\u000abase.\u000aMICRO #1-6: 12 potential lymph nodes, 12 frags, ESS.\u000aPart two is received designated "#2. left breast tissue". The specimen consists\u000aof a single lumpectomy measuring 6 x 6 x REMOVED_DATE cm containing two stitches, the\u000along stitch designating lateral portion of the specimen and the short stitch\u000adesignating the superior portion of the specimen. The specimen is inked per\u000apathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior\u000a= blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange.\u000aThere is also an attached skin ellipse that measures 3 cm in length x REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000aThe posterior portion of the specimen is involved by a focal fibrous rubbery\u000ato firm area measuring up to REMOVED_DATE cm. The breast tissue is otherwise composed\u000aof 90% yellow adipose tissue. There is a focal area of fibrous thickening and\u000ahemorrhage measuring 2 x 2 x REMOVED_DATE cm. Focally posterior to this area is a firm\u000awell circumscribed mass that measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. This mass abuts\u000athe posterior and inferior portion of the specimen. The mass is 8 cm away from\u000alateral margin, 3 cm away from medial margin, 5 cm away from superior margin\u000aand 5 cm away from skin. The entire mass and representative sections of\u000amargins are submitted for histological evaluation.\u000aMICRO #7-9: Mass in relation to inferior and posterior margins, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMICRO #10-12: Additional biopsy cavity site to inferior and posterior margins,\u000a3 frags, RSS.\u000aMICRO #13: Superior margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMICRO #14: Lateral margin perpendicular, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMICRO #15: Medial margin perpendicular, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMICRO #16: Skin and anterior margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aPart three is received designated "portacath". The specimen consists of a\u000asingle plastic medical device with tubing measuring 5 x 2 x REMOVED_DATE cm. This is a\u000agross exam only specimen.\u000arfi\u000aReports to: IGLEHART, JAMES, DIRK M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: LYMPH NODES REGIONAL RESECTION\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: UNLISTED SURGICAL SPECIMEN - LEVEL I (GROSS ONLY)\u000a[report_end]
