VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Amend/Addenda\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Consult slide(s)\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ANN H PARTRIDGE M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-05-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000a********** Addended Report ***********\u000aResident: Russell K Dorer, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Andrea L Richardson, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aCONSULT SLIDE FROM BERKSHIRE MEDICAL CENTER, PITTSFIELD, MA:\u000aLEFT BREAST CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY FOR A MASS (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID; REMOVED_DATE ):\u000aPOORLY DIFFERENTIATED NEOPLASM, favor poorly differentiated carcinoma (See\u000anote.) The tumor contains a prominent lymphoplasmacytic infiltrate.\u000aNo lymphovascular invasion seen in this limited specimen.\u000aNo in situ carcinoma seen in this limited specimen.\u000aSpecial studies were performed at an outside institution with the following\u000aresults (not reviewed):\u000aESTROGEN RECEPTOR Negative\u000aPROGESTERONE RECEPTOR Negative\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/NEU Negative (0)\u000aImmunohistochemistry performed at BWH demonstrates the following staining\u000aprofile in tumor cells:\u000aPositive - Keratin REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID (very weak and focal in tumor cells, positive in\u000abenign epithelium)\u000aNegative - S-100, Estrogen receptor (faintly positive in normal breast\u000aepithelium), progesterone receptor, Her-2/neu, Keratin 34REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, Keratin 14,\u000aKeratin Cam5.2, p63, LCA (also only weakly positive in small lymphocytes)\u000aThe immunohistochemistry results are somewhat aberrant as the LCA is weak\u000ain admixed small lymphocytes and the ER is very weak in normal breast tissue.\u000aThese bring into question the immunogenicity of the tumor tissue and the\u000avalidity of all of the staining results. A repeat biopsy to obtain additional\u000atissue to repeat the studies is recommended to confirm the diagnosis of\u000acarcinoma.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: None given\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Mass\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aConsult slides.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aReceived from Berkshire Medical Center, Pathology Department, 725 North Street,\u000aPittsfield, MA REMOVED_CASE_ID, are eleven (11) glass slides.\u000aThe slides are labeled "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" and one (1) slide is sublabeled "1",\u000acorresponding to a left breast core biopsy (1.2 x REMOVED_DATE cm) performed on REMOVED_DATE \u000aaccording to the accompanying pathology report bearing the patient's name.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Russell K Dorer M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aResident Review by Andrea L Richardson M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Andrea L Richardson M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a4/27/2005\u000aSurgical Addendum:\u000aSubsequently received on REMOVED_DATE  are ten (10) unstained slides, labeled\u000a"REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID", which corresponds to the above case.\u000aNo further stains are performed and the diagnosis is unchanged.\u000aAddendum by Deborah A Dillon M.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aAddendum #1 by Andrea L Richardson M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a6/28/2005\u000a[report_end]
