VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast core needle biopsy\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: DARRELL N SMITH M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-05-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Russell K Dorer, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Andrea L Richardson, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aLEFT BREAST 10G ULTRASOUND-GUIDED CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY FOR A TUMOR:\u000aINVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA, poorly differentiated (modified Bloom-Richardson\u000agrade III/III),with marked lymphocytic infiltration, measuring at least REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000aNo definite lymphovascular invasion seen in this limited specimen.\u000aNo in situ carcinoma seen in this limited specimen.\u000aSpecial studies were performed with the following profile for tumor cells:\u000aCYTOKERATIN REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Positive (variable)\u000aPANKERATIN (MNF-116): Positive (variable)\u000aLCA: Negative in tumor cells (positive in lymphocytes)\u000aS-100: Positive (focally, weakly)\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for carcinoma (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor Negative\u000aProgesterone receptor Negative\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) Negative (0)\u000aInterpretation:\u000aNormal breast epithelial cells are appropriately immunoreactive for both ER and\u000aPR (internal positive control).\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000acarcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but only\u000aa portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in >10%\u000aof tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in\u000a>10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Known (L) breast cancer.\u000aTissue needed for R-receptor studies.\u000aBreast Imaging Findings: lobulated.\u000aOperation: 10 g ultrasound.\u000aOperative Findings: Solid mass.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Cancer.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aLeft breast tissue in a pink cassette.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit\u000anumber, and "L breast", is an undesignated, pink mesh cassette which contains\u000amultiple, yellow/white fibrofatty soft tissue cores (2.5 X REMOVED_DATE X REMOVED_DATE cm in\u000aaggregate).\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Left breast cores, multi frags, ESS.\u000adb/MMM\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Andrea L Richardson M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Andrea L Richardson M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a5/3/2005\u000a[report_end]
