VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: Esther Rhei M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-05-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Justine A Barletta, M.D.; Joseph Woodward Carlson, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Deborah A Dillon, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A CLIP:\u000aResidual INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA, REMOVED_DATE cm, present adjacent to biopsy site\u000achanges.\u000aNo lymphovascular invasion is seen.\u000aNo in situ carcinoma is seen.\u000aInvasive carcinoma is present >0.3 cm from all margins.\u000aNOTE: Immunohistochemical study for keratin REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/p63 demonstrates absence of\u000amyoepithelial cells around the focus of invasive carcinoma.\u000aBy report, the patient presented with a REMOVED_DATE cm mass by MRI. Following\u000aneoadjuvant chemotherapy, the mass was no longer detected on MRI. Gross\u000aexamination of the excision specimen showed a REMOVED_DATE cm fibrous area compatible\u000awith treated tumor bed. Histologic examination demonstrated a REMOVED_DATE cm focus of\u000aresidual invasive carcinoma present adjacent to biopsy site changes and in\u000aassociation with a dense lymphocytic infiltrate. Findings are compatible with a\u000agrade 4 response in the Miller-Payne system.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 43 year old female with L breast CA s/p neoadjuvant chemotherapy with\u000aCisplatin.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1 - L breast tissue (long/lat, short/sup, whip/chest wall).\u000aRADIOGRAPHY REPORT: Clip in specimen. Green, M.D.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient?s name, unit number,\u000aand "#1 - left breast tissue", and consists of a breast excision specimen (8.5\u000acm superior to inferior x REMOVED_DATE cm medial to lateral x 2 cm anterior to\u000aposterior), with three stitches designated by the surgeon as follows: short\u000astitch=superior, long stitch=lateral, whip stitch=deep. The specimen was inked\u000aby the surgeon according to the pathology protocol for the evaluation of\u000amargins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green;\u000alateral/yellow; medial/orange. There is no accompanying radiograph. The\u000aspecimen is sectioned from superior to inferior (ten slices). A wire runs from\u000athe superior aspect to slice three where there is an area of hemorrhage (3.2 x\u000a2.0 x REMOVED_DATE cm). Slices six through eight have a poorly defined fibrous areas\u000aidentified by Dr. Dillon as possible tumor bed (3.1 x REMOVED_DATE x 1 cm) that abuts\u000athe inferior, posterior, medial, and lateral margins, and is REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000asuperior, and 1 cm from the anterior margins. A representative section of the\u000apossible tumor bed (slice 7) is submitted to Tissue Bank (a frozen section of\u000athis tissue is first performed). There are no distinct masses seen. The\u000aspecimen is radiographed, revealing a clip in slice four. The entire specimen\u000ais submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: superior margin (slice one), 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: superior, and inferior margins (slice two), 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: superior and medial margins (slice three), RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: superior and lateral margins (slice three), 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: superior and lateral margins (slice four), 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: medial, posterior, and superior margins (slice four), 2\u000afrags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: lateral and posterior margins (slice five), 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: medial and superior margins (slice five), 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: medial margin (slice five), 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: lateral margin (slice five), 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: lateral, inferior, posterior margins (slice six), 3 frags,\u000aRSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: posterior and medial margins (slice six), 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: lateral and inferior margins (slice seven), 4 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: medial and anterior margins (slice seven), 4 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: additional breast parenchyma (slice seven), 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: lateral and inferior margins (slice eight), 3 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: anterior and medial margins (slice eight), 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: slice nine, 6 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: slice ten, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aJUB/lp\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Deborah A Dillon M.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Deborah A Dillon M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
