VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Christian J. Davidson, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Jacqueline M William, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aSPECIMEN DESIGNATED: RIGHT BREAST, EXCISIONAL BIOPSY FOR CALCIFICATIONS AND A\u000aCLIP:\u000aFocal Atypical ductal hyperplasia (Block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID)\u000aColumnar cell change with atypia and microcalcifications.\u000aApocrine metaplasia.\u000aBiopsy site changes.\u000aThere is no carcinoma seen upon microscopic examination of the entire\u000aspecimen, including margins.\u000aThis case was also reviewed by Dr. D. Dillon, Breast pathology, who\u000aconcurs.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 54 year old postmenopausal woman, S/P REMOVED_DATE  R breast core bxs\u000arevealing ADH.\u000aOperation: Rt breast wire localized excisional bx.\u000aOperative Findings: Not provided.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal mammo rt breast.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) right breast tissue - long stitch/lateral, short stitch/superior, whip\u000astitch/deep margin.\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000aCalcifications, clip and wire are within the specimen. Dr. Gombos.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, medical record\u000anumber, and "#1. Right breast tissue, long stitch lateral, short stitch\u000asuperior, whipstitch deep margin", and consists of a yellow/tan fragment of\u000afibroadipose tissue, measuring REMOVED_DATE cm superior to inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm anterior to\u000aposterior, and REMOVED_DATE cm medial to lateral. The long stitch designates the\u000alateral aspect and short stitch designates the superior aspect (per the\u000asurgeon). The specimen is received pre-inked per the inks protocol for the\u000aevaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red;\u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. A localization wire enters at\u000athe junction of the superior and lateral margin, and marks off an area of\u000acalcification at the superior margin with a surgical clip. The specimen is cut\u000ainto eight slices in a medial to lateral direction. The clip is seen in slice\u000a#3. The specimen consists of approximately 95% white fibrous tissue with 5%\u000ayellow adipose tissue. No focal lesions are noted. The entire specimen is\u000asubmitted for histologic analysis.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #1 (medial aspect), 4 perpendicular frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #2, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #3 (with clip removed), 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #4, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #5, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #6, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #7, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #8 (lateral margin), 3 perpendicular frags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aCJD/lp\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jacqueline M William M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed\u000aon Sunday February 22, 2009 at 12:28:00PM\u000a[report_end]
