VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID LYMPH NODE BIOPSY\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aWELCH, WILLIAM, ROBERT, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by WELCH,WILLIAM ROBERT,M.D.\u000a#1. SPECIMEN LABELED "LEFT AXILLARY SENTINEL NODE" (INCLUDING FSA):\u000aOne lymph node with no tumor seen (three levels examined).\u000a#2. SPECIMEN LABELED "LEFT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED PARTIAL MASTECTOMY, LOWER\u000aOUTER QUADRANT":\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA (0.9 CM), poorly differentiated (grade 3), with a\u000aprominent lymphocytic infiltrate.\u000aTumor is REMOVED_DATE cm from the closest lateral resection margin and greaterthan\u000a0.5 cm from all other margins.\u000aNo lymphatic/vascular invasion identified.\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN-SITU, solid type, high grade is present in 2 of 17\u000ablocks (#8 and 14) and is in association with the invasive tumor and away\u000afrom invasive tumor in two small foci (EIC negative).\u000aIn situ carcinoma is not present at margins.\u000aBiopsy site with repair reaction.\u000aFibrocystic change with cystic and apocrine metaplasia.\u000a#3. SPECIMEN LABELED "LEFT BREAST, UPPER INNER QUADRANT, WIRE LOCALIZED\u000aEXCISIONAL BIOPSY" FOR A MASS:\u000aFibrocystic change with cysts.\u000aNOTE:\u000aThe specimen consists predominantly of adipose tissue with a focal REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aarea of fibrous stroma.\u000aNo tumor seen.\u000a#4. SPECIMEN LABELED "RADIOACTIVE SENTINEL NODE":\u000aOne lymph node with no tumor seen (three levels examined).\u000a#5. SPECIMEN LABELED "ADDITIONAL LEFT AXILLARY TISSUE":\u000aFour lymph nodes with no tumor seen.\u000a#6. SPECIMEN LABELED "LEFT LOWER OUTER QUADRANT, POSTERIOR SHAVE MARGIN, DEEP":\u000aBenign breast parenchyma and skeletal muscle with cautery artifact.\u000aOne (1) lymph node with no tumor seen.\u000a#7. SPECIMEN LABELED "LEFT LOWER OUTER QUADRANT, POSTERIOR SHAVE MARGIN,\u000aSUPERIOR":\u000aBenign breast parenchyma and skeletal muscle with cautery artifact.\u000aNo tumor seen.\u000a#8. SPECIMEN LABELED "LEFT LOWER OUTER QUADRANT, POSTERIOR SHAVE MARGIN,\u000aLATERAL":\u000aSmall duct involved by pagetoid spread of CARCINOMA, levels examined.\u000a#9. SPECIMEN LABELED "LEFT LOWER OUTER QUADRANT, POSTERIOR SHAVE MARGIN,\u000aMEDIAL":\u000aBenign breast parenchyma with cautery artiface.\u000aNo tumor seen.\u000a#10. SPECIMEN LABELED "LEFT LOWER OUTER QUADRANT, POSTERIOR SHAVE MARGIN,\u000aINFERIOR":\u000aBenign breast parenchyma with cautery artifact.\u000aNo tumor seen.\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe small duct involved by pagetoid spread in specimen #8 (posterior shave\u000amargin, lateral) measures less than REMOVED_DATE cm in size and is REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000anew margin.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 59 year old surgically postmenopausal female, not on hormones whose\u000a4/28/99 mammograms demonstated a 1 cm mass in the left lower outer\u000aquadrant and a 7 mm nodule in the left upper inner quadrant. Core biopsy of the\u000aleft lower outer quadrant 1 cm mass revealed poorly differentiated carcinoma.\u000aThe 7 mm upper inner quadrant mass not amenable to core biopsy.\u000aOperation: Left breast double wire localization, partial mastectomy x 2\u000awith sentinal node biopsy and axillary node dissection.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Pre-op, Left breast cancer.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Left axillary sentinel lymph node FS\u000a2. Left breast wire localized, partial mastectomy, lower outer\u000aquadrant, short suture superior, long superior lateral.\u000a3. Left breast wire localized excisional biopsy, upper inner\u000aquadrant, short suture superior, long suture lateral.\u000a4. Radioactive sentinel node.\u000a5. Additional axillary tissue.\u000a6. Left lower outer quadrant, posterior shave margin, whip\u000astitch on deep new margin\u000a7. Left lower outer quadrant, shave margin, whip on new margin,\u000asuperior\u000a8. Left lower outer quadrant, shave margin, whip on new margin,\u000alateral\u000a9. Left lower outer quadrant, shave margin, whip on new margin,\u000amedial\u000a10. Left lower outer quadrant, shave margin, whip on new margin,\u000ainferior\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "#1, LEFT AXILLARY SENTINEL NODE", (FSA):\u000aLymph node; no tumor present.\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "#2, LEFT BREAST WIRE LOCALIZED PARTIAL MASTECTOMY" (GROSS\u000aONLY):\u000aFirm area REMOVED_DATE cm associated with biopsy site, located REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000alateral margin and REMOVED_DATE cm from posterior margin.\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "#3, LEFT BREAST WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISIONAL BIOPSY" (GROSS\u000aONLY):\u000aNo gross evidence of invasive tumor.\u000aRadiology says #2 = clip and hookwire in specimen.\u000a#3 = nodule and hookwire in specimen.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by LIGON,KEITH LLOYD,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in 10 parts in containers labeled with the\u000apatient's name and unit number.\u000aPart one, labeled "Left axillary sentinel node" is a single fragment of\u000atan/pink soft tissue REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. Representative sections submitted\u000aas FSA and one (1) gross possible lymph node is identified. Micro 1: FSA\u000alymph node, 1 frag, ESS. Micro 2: remainder of tissue, multi frag, ESS.\u000aPart two, labeled "Left breast wire localized partial mastectomy, lower outer\u000aquandrant, short = superior, long = lateral, whipstitch is chest wall", is one\u000afragment of green/yellow fibroadipose tissue with needle localization wire in\u000aplace and a short suture superior and a long suture lateral and a whipstitch at\u000athe deep margin. The specimen is REMOVED_DATE cm superior-inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000amedial-lateral, and REMOVED_DATE cm anterior-posterior. The specimen is inked for the\u000aevaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red;\u000ainferior = green; lateral = yellow medial = orange. Representative sections\u000aof margins are submitted for microscopic examination. The specimen contains a\u000a0.9 cm firm fibrotic white area, which is consistent with prior biopsy site.\u000aThe biopsy site is REMOVED_DATE cm from lateral REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior, REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000athe medial, REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior, REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000athe inferior margins. The entire specimen is submitted. Tissue in area of\u000aclip is submitted in cassette 13.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  left breast wire localized excision, superior to inferior, 1 frag,\u000aESS.\u000aPart three, labeled "Left breast, upper-inner quadrant, wire localized\u000aexcisional biopsy, short = superior, long = lateral", is a single portion of\u000ayellow-tan fibroadipose tissue, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm with a needle localization\u000awire in place and a short suture superior and a long suture lateral. There are\u000ano areas grossly suspicious for invasive carcinoma and the entire specimen is\u000asubmitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  upper inner quadrant, breast, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aPart four, labeled "Radioactive sentinel node" is one fragment of pink/tan\u000afibroadipose tissue, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm containing a single possible lymph\u000anode, bisected and entirely submitted.\u000aMicro 28: radioactive sentinel node, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aPart five, labeled "Additional left axillary tissue" is a single\u000afragment of yellow fibroadipose tissue REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm, which contains four\u000a(4) possible lymph nodes. The lymph nodes are entirely submitted.\u000aMicro 29: two (2) possible lymph nodes, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 30: two (2) possible lymph nodes, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aPart six, labeled "Left lower outer quadrant, posterior shave margin,\u000awhipstitch on new margin, deep", is a single piece of fibroadipose tissue REMOVED_DATE x\u000a2.0 x REMOVED_DATE cm. A single whipstitch on the new margin inked black. The specimen\u000ais entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  deep shave margin, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aPart seven, "Left lower outer quadrant, posterior shave margin, whip\u000aon new margin, superior", is a single fragment of yellow fibroadipose tissue,\u000a2.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm with a whipstitch on the new margin inked black. The entire\u000aspecimen is submitted.\u000aMicro 33: superior margin, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aPart eight, labeled "Left lower outer quadrant, posterior shave margin, whip on\u000anew margin, lateral", is a single portion of yellow fibroadipose tissue, REMOVED_DATE x\u000a3.0 x REMOVED_DATE cm, which has a whipstitch on the new lateral margin inked black.\u000aThe entire specimen is submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  new lateral margin, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aPart nine, labeled "Left lower outer quadrant, posterior shave margin, whip on\u000anew margin medial", is a single portion of yellow fibroadipose tissue, REMOVED_DATE x\u000a2.0 x REMOVED_DATE cm, whip a whipstitch on the new medial margin inked black. The\u000aentire specimen is submitted.\u000aMicro 37: new medial margin, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aPart ten, labeled "Left lower outer quadrant, shave margin, whip on new\u000amargin, inferior", is a single portion of yellow fibroadipose tissue, REMOVED_DATE x\u000a3.0 x REMOVED_DATE cm, which has a whipstitch on the new inferior margin inked black.\u000aThe specimen is entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  new inferior margin, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aReports to: KHACHIGIAN, LEVON, MICHAEL\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: LYMPH NODE BIOPSY\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: LYMPH NODE BIOPSY\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: LYMPH NODE BIOPSY\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN\u0