VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aNOSE, VANIA, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by NOSE,VANIA,M.D.,PH.D.\u000a1) RIGHT BREAST, EXCISION WITH WIRE-LOCALIZATION FOR A MASS:\u000aINVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aSEE NOTE.\u000aSYNOPSIS:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA\u000aSize - REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aMultifocal - no\u000aHistologic Type - solid and papillary\u000aHistologic Grade (SBR) - II (moderate)\u000aNuclear Grade - intermediate\u000aEIC - positive\u000aLymphovascular invasion - absent\u000aDermal lymphatic invasion - N/A\u000aSkin invasion - N/A\u000aSkeletal muscle invasion - N/A\u000aFinal Margins (invasive) -\u000aNegative (>0.3 cm) - anterior, superior, interior, medial,\u000alateral\u000aClose (0.1-0.3 cm specify dist)- posterior (0.2 cm)\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU: - Present\u000a- Solid, cribiform\u000a- Low nuclear grade\u000aNOTE:\u000aIt is difficult to tell the relative portions of invasive and in-situ\u000acarcinoma; however, a majority of the tumor appears invasive. A p63\u000aimmunostain highlights rare basal cells in association iwth the tumor which is\u000adiffusely REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDpositive.\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - absent\u000aOTHER FINDINGS\u000aCore biopsy site\u000aCalcifications in benign epithelium\u000aAJCC CLASSIFICATION (6th edition) - REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDc pNx MX\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER/PR/HER-2) - pending\u000aNOTE:\u000aThis tumor has been reviewed by Dr. S. Schnitt and Dr. Susan Lester, Breast\u000aPathology Service, who agree with the above diagnosis.\u000a2) MEDIAL SHAVE MARGIN:\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, solid and cribriform, with calcifications,\u000apresent in two of two (2:2) blocks.\u000aThe ductal carcinoma in situ is present less than REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000ainked resection margin, see NOTE.\u000aNOTE:\u000aIt cannot be determined from this specimen if the inked margin represents the\u000atrue final resection margin.\u000a3) LATERAL SHAVE MARGIN:\u000aBenign breast tissue.\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy.\u000a4) INTERIOR SHAVE MARGIN:\u000aBenign breast tissue.\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy.\u000a5) POSTERIOR SHAVE MARGIN:\u000aBenign breast tissue.\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy.\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aFIRST SURGICAL ADDENDUM REMOVED_DATE  DR. SUSAN LESTER\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for invasive carcinoma (block 4):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) POSITIVE (2+)\u000aNote: FISH analysis for amplification of REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu could be helpful, if\u000aclinically warranted.\u000aSEE SECOND ADDENDUM BELOW\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000acarcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but\u000aonly a portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity\u000ain >10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aSECOND SURGICAL ADDENDUM REMOVED_DATE  DR. SUSAN LESTER\u000aFISH was performed by USLABS using the PathVysion HER-2 DNA Probe Kit with the\u000afollowing results (block 4):\u000aResult: NOT AMPLIFIED\u000aThe Her-2/cen 17 ratio = REMOVED_DATE \u000aThe average of Her-2/neu copies per cell: REMOVED_DATE \u000aThe average of cen 17 copies per cell: REMOVED_DATE \u000aThe cutoff point for assessing HER-2/neu gene amplification is a ratio of REMOVED_DATE \u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 79 yo female with right breast mammographic mass, core biopsy\u000a4/16/04 demonstrates carcinoma consistent with DCIS or invasive carcinoma.\u000aOperation: R breast wire localization lumpectomy.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: R breast cancer.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000a1. Right breast tissue with stitch marking. Short suture - superior. Long\u000asuture - lateral. Whip stitch - deep margin. Inking per pathology\u000aprotocol.\u000a2. Medial shave margin.\u000a3. Superior shave margin (whip stitch new margin).\u000a4. Lateral shave margin (whip stitch new margin).\u000a5. Inferior shave margin (whip stitch new margin).\u000a6. Posterior shave margin (whip stitch chest wall margin).\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by SCHMIDT,JASON F.,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in six parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aThe first, additionally designated "#1 right breast tissue; short stitch -\u000asuperior, long stitch - lateral, whip stitch on deep margin," consists of a\u000abreast lumpectomy specimen (9.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with an embedded localization\u000awire. Accompanying the specimen is a specimen radiograph demonstrating\u000aradiopaque lesion with focal calcifications and an adjacent localization wire.\u000aThree orienting sutures are present and designated by the surgeon as follows:\u000ashort - superior, long - lateral, whip stitch - deep. The specimen has been\u000apreviously inked by the surgeon per pathology protocol for the evaluation of\u000amargins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green;\u000alateral = yellow; medial = orange. The specimen is serially sectioned from\u000amedial to lateral to reveal a tan/white firm focally hemorrhagic nodule (1.4 x\u000a1.0 x REMOVED_DATE cm). The nodule is oriented to the margin as follows: posterior -\u000a0.3 cm, anterior - REMOVED_DATE cm, superior - REMOVED_DATE cm, medial - REMOVED_DATE cm, inferior - REMOVED_DATE \u000acm, and lateral - REMOVED_DATE cm. The remainder of the breast parenchyma is composed\u000aof yellow lobulated adipose tissue with focal areas of tan/white fibrous\u000atissue and hemorrhage. Representative sections of the nodule and normal\u000atissue are submitted to the Tumor Bank. Representative sections of the\u000aspecimen are submitted for microscopic examination.\u000aMicro 1: nodule and medial and posterior margins, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 2: nodule and superior, posterior, and anterior margins, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 3: nodule and inferior and posterior margins, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 4: nodule and medial and posterior margins, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 5: breast parenchyma and superior, inferior and anterior margins, 1\u000afrag, RSS.\u000aThe second, additionally designated "#2 medial shave margin," consists of a\u000apartially fragmented portion of breast tissue (6.4 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). No\u000aorienting suture is present. The surface of the tissue is entirely inked blue.\u000aThe tissue is composed primarily of yellow lobulated adipose tissue\u000a(approximately 95%) with focal areas of tan/white fibrous tissue (approximately\u000a5%). No discrete lesions are identified. Representative sections of the\u000aspecimen are submitted for microscopic examination.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  medial shave margin, 3 frags each, RSS.\u000aThe third, additionally designated "#3 superior shave margin; whip stitch new\u000amargin," consists of a breast shave margin specimen (6.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm).\u000aThere is a single whip stitch which is designated by the surgeon as the new\u000amargin. The old margin is inked blue. The new margin is inked black. The\u000aspecimen is composed primarily of yellow lobulated adipose tissue\u000a(approximately 90%) with focal areas of tan/white fibrous tissue (approximately\u000a10%). No discrete lesions are identified. Representative sections of the\u000aspecimen are submitted for microscopic examination.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  superior shave margin, 2 frags each, RSS.\u000aThe fourth, additionally designated "#4 lateral shave margin (whip stitch new\u000amargin," consists of three portions of breast parenchyma (2.9 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm,\u000a1.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm, and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The largest portion of tissue has\u000aa whip stitch which is designated by the surgeon as the new margin. The two\u000asmaller portions of tissue are unoriented. The oriented portion of tissue is\u000ainked as follows: old margin - blue, new margin - black. The two smaller\u000aportions of tissue are inked entirely blue. The tissue is composed almost\u000aentirely of yellow lobulated adipose tissue (approximately 95%) with focal\u000aareas of tan/white fibrous tissue (approximately 5%). No discrete lesions are\u000aidentified. Representative sections of the specimen are submitted for\u000amicroscopic examination.\u000aMicro 10: lateral shave margin, oriented portion of tissue, 3 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 11: lateral shave margin, unoriented portions of tissue, 3 frags, RSS.\u000aThe fifth, additionally designated "#5 inferior shave margin (whip stitch new\u000amargin)," consists of a single portion of breast parenchyma (7.1 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm). A whip stitch is present and designated by the surgeon as new margin.\u000aThe old margin is inked blue. The new margin is inked black. The specimen is\u000acomposed primarily of yellow lobulated adipose tissue (approximately 95%) with\u000afocal areas of tan/white fibrous tissue (approximately 5%). No discrete\u000alesions are identified. Representative sections of the specimen are submitted\u000afor microscopic examination.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  inferior shave margin, 2 frags each, RSS.\u000aThe sixth, additionally labeled "#6 posterior shave margin (whip stitch chest\u000awall margin)," consists of a single portion of breast parenchyma (7.2 x REMOVED_DATE x\u000a0.7 cm). No orienting suture is present. The absence of an orienting suture\u000ais discussed with the surgeon who agrees the specimen should be processed\u000awithout orientation. The surface of the specimen is inked entirely in blue.\u000aThe specimen is composed primarily of yellow lobulated adipose tissue\u000a(approximately 95%) with focal areas of tan/white fibrous tissue\u000a(approximately 5%). No discrete lesions are identified. Representative\u000asections of the specimen are submitted for microscopic examination.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  posterior shave margin, 2 frags each, RSS.\u000ajfs\u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN\u000a[report_end]
