VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aNOSE, VANIA, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by NOSE,VANIA,M.D.,PH.D.\u000a#1. LEFT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED BIOPSY:\u000aBenign breast tissue with epithelial atypia dense stromal fibrosis, and\u000avascular changes consistent with treatment effect.\u000aFat necrosis.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000aImmunoperoxidase stains for p63 and keratin REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID confirms two foci\u000aof benign adenosis (blocks 8 and 10).\u000a#2. LEFT BREAST, SUBAREOLAR, BIOPSY:\u000aBenign breast tissue with epithelial atypia dense stromal fibrosis, and\u000avascular changes consistent with treatment effect.\u000aFat necrosis.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000aNOTE:\u000aThe specimen is entirely examined.\u000aThis case has been reviewed by Dr. Andrea Richardson, Breast Pathology\u000aService, who concurs.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: H/o left breast DCIS, s/p lumpectomy & XRT in 1998. Now with\u000aMRI suspicious of recurrence.\u000aOperation: 1. Left breast MRI guided excision - upper outer quadrant.\u000a2. Left breast subareolar excision.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: H/o left breast DCIS.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. L breast wire localized bx (MR guided). Short =\u000asuperior, long = lateral.\u000a2. L breast bx, subareolar (short = superior, long = lateral).\u000aRADIOLOGY: #1 - Marker in specimen.\u000a#2 - Nodular density in specimen. ds\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by VANGURI,VIJAY K,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received in two parts, each labeled with the patient's name and\u000aunit number.\u000aPart one, labeled "left breast wire localized biopsy", consists of a breast\u000aexcision specimen (5.0 cm from medial to lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm from superior to\u000ainferior, and REMOVED_DATE cm from anterior to posterior) with two orienting sutures\u000a(long lateral, short superior), and an embedded localization wire. An\u000aaccompanying specimen radiograph shows the localization wire adjacent to a\u000aclip. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of\u000amargins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green;\u000alateral/yellow; medial/orange. The specimen is sectioned from lateral to\u000amedial in 10 slices to reveal a collapsed biopsy site (1.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with\u000aseveral firm exogenous yellow pellets. The localization wire is embedded in\u000aslice 7 adjacent to an irregular area of rubbery fibrous tissue (1.5 x REMOVED_DATE x\u000a0.8 cm), located adjacent to the inferior and posterior margins. The remainder\u000aof breast parenchyma consists of unremarkable yellow adipose tissue. The\u000aspecimen is entirely submitted.\u000aMicro 1: slice 1 (lateral), 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro 2: slice 3, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro 3: slice 5, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  slice 6, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  slice 7, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  slice 8, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro 10: slice 9, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  slice 2, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  slices 4 & 10, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aPart two, labeled "left subareolar breast biopsy", consists of a breast\u000aexcision specimen (4.0 cm from medial to lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm from anterior to\u000aposterior, and REMOVED_DATE cm from superior to inferior) with two orienting sutures\u000a(short superior, long lateral). An accompanying specimen radiograph shows some\u000aill-defined radiopaque density. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol\u000afor the evaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red;\u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. The specimen is sectioned from\u000alateral to medial in 10 slices to reveal rubbery fibrous tissue (90% of\u000aspecimen) and unremarkable adipose tissue (comprising 10% of the specimen).\u000aThe specimen is entirely submitted.\u000aMicro 11: slice 1, lateral, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro 12: slice 3, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  slice 5, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  slice 7, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro 17: slice 9, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  slices 2 & 4, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  slices 6, 8, & 10, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aviv\u000aReports to: GOLSHAN, MEHRA M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN\u000a[report_end]
