VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, mastectomy with regional lymph nodes\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ROGER L CHRISTIAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-05-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Marian H Harris, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Jonathan N Glickman, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA) LEFT BREAST, SIMPLE MASTECTOMY (160G):\u000aBreast tissue with dense fibrosis and epithelial hyperplasia (see NOTE).\u000aPrior biopsy site.\u000aSkin with scar.\u000aSkeletal muscle with no significant pathologic change.\u000aNOTE: The patient has a history of a REMOVED_DATE cm invasive carcinoma with\u000amicrometastatic carcinoma in one lymph node, excised REMOVED_DATE  No residual in\u000asitu or invasive carcinoma present, including deep margin.\u000aB) RIGHT BREAST, SIMPLE MASTECTOMY (144G):\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia with Pagetoid spread in lactiferous sinuses of the\u000anipple (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID). (see NOTE)\u000aBreast tissue with dense fibrosis, consistent with a prior biopsy site.\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia with focal squamous metaplasia.\u000aSkin with no significant pathologic change.\u000aNo in situ or invasive carcinoma present, including deep margin.\u000aNOTE: The patient has a history of an invasive carcinoma with negative lymph\u000anodes in 1991. Slides from both parts of this case reviewed by Dr. S. Lester,\u000aBreast pathology service, who concurs.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Bilat. Breast cancer; Rt Rx'd with Rads; has just completed chemo for\u000aLt.; REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID (+).\u000aOperation: Bilat mastectomy\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: None given.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000a(1) Left breast with short stitch superior, long stitch lateral.\u000a(2) Right breast with short stitch superior, long lateral.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two parts, each labeled with the patient?s\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart A, sub labeled "1. Left breast - short stitch = superior, long stitch =\u000alateral", a 160-gm simple mastectomy specimen (16 x 15 x REMOVED_DATE cm) with a\u000awhite/tan skin ellipse (8 x REMOVED_DATE cm). Two sutures are present and designated by\u000athe surgeon as short - superior and long - lateral. There is a REMOVED_DATE cm,\u000awell-healed surgical scar along the inferior, lateral portion of the skin\u000aellipse, REMOVED_DATE cm from the unremarkable nipple (0.9 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). Deep to the\u000ascar within the lower outer quadrant, there is an ill-defined, prior excision\u000asite (3.3 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The prior excision site comes to within REMOVED_DATE cm of\u000athe deep margin, which is composed of a smooth, fascial plane that is inked\u000ablack. No gross tumor is identified. The remaining breast parenchyma is\u000apredominantly (approximately 70%) white and firm with admixed areas of yellow,\u000alobulated, adipose tissue (approximately 30%). No lymph nodes are identified.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Prior biopsy site and deep margin, 4 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Skin with scar, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Upper outer quadrant, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Upper inner quadrant, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lower outer quadrant, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lower inner quadrant, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Nipple, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aPart B, sublabeled "2. Right breast = short stitch - superior long stitch -\u000alateral", consists of a 144-gm simple mastectomy specimen (14.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm) with a white/tan skin ellipse (5.5 x REMOVED_DATE cm). Two orienting sutures are\u000apresent, designated by the surgeon as long - lateral and short - superior. The\u000askin surface is unremarkable with a centrally located nipple (0.6 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm). The deep margin is composed of a smooth, fascial plane, which is inked\u000ablack. No definitive prior excision site is identified within the breast\u000aparenchyma. The breast parenchyma is predominantly white and firm\u000a(approximately 80%) with focal areas of lobulated, yellow, adipose tissue\u000a(approximately 20%). No lymph nodes are identified.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Upper/outer quadrant and deep margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Upper/outer quadrant, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Upper/inner quadrant and deep margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Upper/inner quadrant, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lower/outer quadrant and deep margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lower/outer quadrant, 2 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lower/inner quadrant and deep margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lower/inner quadrant, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Nipple, 1 frag, RSS.\u000ajfs/MMM\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Marian H Harris M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aResident Review by Marian H Harris M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jonathan N Glickman M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a5/3/2005\u000a[report_end]
