ken in Bouins overnight. The deep surface of the specimen was inked\u000ain black. Careful sectioning revealed a hemorrhagic and somewhat thickened\u000afibrous tissue that is retroareola. No areas suspicious for invasive tumor was\u000afound grossly. The hemorrhagic area is located 3 cm from the deep margin and\u000a3.5 cm from the skin and is approximately retroareola.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  thickened and hemorrhagic area, multiple fragments, ESS.\u000aMicro 5, deep margin perpendicular to thickened hemorrhagic area, 1 fragment,\u000aRSS.\u000aMicro 6, skin with scar and subcutaneous tissue, 2 fragments, RSS.\u000aMicro 7, tissue deep to scar, inked margin, perpendicular, 2 fragments, RSS.\u000aMicro 8, tissue deep to scar and inked margin, perpendicular, 1 fragment, RSS.\u000aMicro 9, nipple and subcutaneous tissue, 1 fragment, RSS.\u000aMicro 10, upper inner quadrant, deep margin, perpendicular, 1 fragment, RSS.\u000aMicro 11, upper outer quadrant, 1 fragment, deep margin, perpendicular, RSS.\u000aMicro 12, lower inner quadrant, 1 fragment, RSS.\u000aMicro 13, lower outer quadrant, 1 fragment, RSS.\u000aMicro 14, 3 candidate lymph nodes, 5 fragments, RSS.\u000aMicro 15, 3 candidate lymph nodes, 5 fragments, ESS.\u000aMicro 16, 2 candidate lymph nodes, 6 fragments, ESS.\u000aMicro 17, 2 candidate lymph nodes, 6 fragments, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  1 candidate lymph node, 2 fragments per cassette, ESS.\u000aMicro 20, 2 candidate lymph nodes, 4 fragments, ESS.\u000aMicro 21, 2 candidate lymph nodes, 6 fragments, ESS.\u000aMicro 22, 1 candidate lymph node, 4 fragments, ESS.\u000aMicro 23, 2 candidate lymph nodes, 4 fragments, ESS.\u000aPart two, labeled "#2. additional left axillary contents", and consists of two\u000afragments of fibrofatty tissue measuring in aggregate, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000aCareful sectioning reveals two candidate lymph nodes.\u000aMicro 24, 2 candidate lymph nodes, additional axillary contents, 5 fragments,\u0