i, M.D. Signed On: 04 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 13:58 =============================================================================== *** IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum *** RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast (Left, block J): The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein. The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein. The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER-2/c-erbB-2. See note. Note: These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital. They have not been cleared or approved by the U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA). The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary; this laboratory has established and verified the test's accuracy and precision. Added by: Atul Kumar Bhan, M.D. Signed On: 07 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 10:30 GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "left breast wide excision, short stitch superior, long stitch lateral" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm fibrofatty tissue with a short suture designating superior and a long suture designating lateral. The specimen is blue inked along the anterior, black inked along the posterior, green inked along the superior, yellow inked along the inferior aspects. Serially sectioning reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm gray-white, slightly gritty, rubbery firm mass which abuts the posterior comes to within REMOVED_DATE cm of the inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm of the lateral and anterior, REMOVED_DATE cm of the medial, REMOVED_DATE cm of the superior margins. The remaining parenchyma is yellow lobulated, fibrofatty tissue with diffuse fibrocystic-type changes coming to within REMOVED_DATE cm of the anterior margin. Representative sections are submitted sequentially from medial to lateral as follows: A-B: Fibrous tissue to superior margin. C: Fibrous tissue to anterior and posterior margins. D-F: Fibrous tissue to anterior inferior margins. G-H: Full thickness section to include nodule with the nodule to the inferior aspect in H. I-J: Full thickness section of nodule with J including the nodule to the inferior aspect (closest). Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "sentinel node hot and blue #6822 left axilla" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm tan-red rubbery fatty lymph node which is bisected to reveal a tan slightly hemorrhagic smooth surface. The specimen is entirely submitted as K-L. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "additional lateral inferior" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm aggregate of focally blue dyed fibrofatty tissue fragments which are serially sectioned and entirely submitted as M-N. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "additional superior medial tissue" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm fibrofatty tissue which is serially sectioned to reveal a focally blue dyed fibrofatty tissue surface. The specimen is entirely submitted as O. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "final shaved superior half" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm aggregate of focally blue dyed fibrous tissue which is serially sectioned and entirely submitted as P-S. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "final shaved inferior half of cavity" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm aggregate of focally blue dyed fibrofatty tissue which is serially sectioned and entirely submitted as T-W. Gross Description by: LORI MARINI Resident: RESIDENT-FREE SERVICE (SGR) =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT - REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID REPORTS TO: Barbara Lynn Smith, M.D. PART A: BREAST (LEFT), EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B: LYMPH NODE (LEFT AXILLA, SENTINEL #6822), EXCISION PART C: BR