VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast core needle biopsy\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: CHRISTINE M DENISON M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-05-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Hejin P Hahn, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Deborah A Dillon, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, UPPER OUTER QUADRANT, 11 G ULTRASOUND GUIDED CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES\u000aFOR AN IRREGULAR REMOVED_DATE CM MASS (SITE #1):\u000aSclerosing adenosis with associated microcalcifications.\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia is present focally.\u000aNOTE: Histologic features of a mass-forming lesion are not seen.\u000aRadiologic/pathologic correlation is suggested.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, ANTERIOR MID UPPER AREA, 11 G STEREOTACTIC CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES\u000aFOR CALCIFICATIONS (SITE #2):\u000aCalcifications present in association with benign epithelium.\u000aNOTE: Requisition form indicates that the targeted calcifications were not\u000aobtained in this biopsy. Clinical correlation suggested.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 70-year old with 1 cm spiculated mass adjacent to pleomorphic\u000acalcifications, right upper outer quadrant. Also heterogeneous calcifications\u000ain right upper outer quadrant. Two sites sampled: 1) spiculated mass, right\u000aupper outer quadrant; 2) calcifications - anterior mid upper breast.\u000aOperation: 1) 11 G Ultrasound; 2) 11 G Stereotactic.\u000aOperative Findings: 1) No technical problems; 2) Bleeding - probable biopsy\u000athrough small artery.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: 1) Invasive carcinoma - DCIS; 2) ? DCIS - did not get\u000atargeted calcifications.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000a1) Right breast tissue - upper outer posterior mass in orange cassette.\u000a2) Right mid upper calcifications in two yellow cassettes - A = tissue with\u000acalcifications, B = remainder of tissue.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, in two parts, each labeled with the\u000apatient?s name, unit number.\u000aPart A, "Right breast site 1", received in an orange cassette labeled "Right",\u000aand consists of multiple, soft, fragmented, yellow to white tissue cores (2.0 x\u000a1.8 x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate).\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Right breast cores site 1, multiple frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, Received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and\u000a"Right breast site 2", received in two (2) yellow cassettes. One cassette is\u000alabeled "A ca++" and contains multiple, yellow/white fibrofatty soft tissue\u000acores (1.5 X REMOVED_DATE X REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate). The other cassette is labeled "B" and\u000acontains similar tissue fragments (2.8 X REMOVED_DATE X REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate).\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: "A ca++", multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: "B", multi frags, ESS.\u000adb/elw\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Deborah A Dillon M.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Deborah A Dillon M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
