VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID SENTINEL LYMPH NODE\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aODZE, ROBERT, DANIEL, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by ODZE,ROBERT DANIEL,M.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST, EXCISION, WIRE LOCALIZATION FOR A MASS (part 3), AND SENTINEL NODE\u000aBIOPSIES (parts 1 and 2):\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aNEGATIVE LYMPH NODES\u000aSYNOPSIS:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA\u000aSize - REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aMultifocal? - no\u000aHistologic Type - ductal with focal lobular features\u000aHistologic Grade (SBR) - I (well)\u000aNuclear Grade - low\u000aEIC - negative\u000aLymphovascular invasion - absent\u000aDermal lymphatic invasion - N/A\u000aSkin invasion - N/A\u000aSkeletal muscle invasion - N/A\u000aFinal Margins (invasive) -\u000aNegative (no ink on tumor) - posterior, superior, inferior, medial,\u000alateral\u000aClose (tumor <0.1 cm from margin) anterior (block 12)\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aTypes - solid\u000aNuclear grade - low\u000aCalcifications in DCIS - absent\u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - absent\u000aMicroinvasion (<0.1cm) -\u000aExtent of DCIS\u000aNumber of blocks:total - 1:18 blocks\u000aDCIS is present as a minor component of the invasive tumor\u000aFinal Margins (DCIS)\u000aNegative (>0.3 cm) - posterior, superior, inferior, medial,\u000alateral\u000aClose (0.1-0.3 cm) - anterior (block 12)\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU -\u000aLYMPH NODES\u000aSentinel Lymph Nodes - negative (3 H&E levels examined)\u000aNumber of positive nodes - 0\u000aNumber of nodes examined - 7\u000aTOTAL POSITIVE NODES (sentinel) - 0:7\u000aOTHER FINDINGS\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia\u000aCysts\u000aBiopsy cavity\u000aAJCC CLASSIFICATION - REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDc pREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID MX\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER/PR/HER-2) - performed previously\u000aLATERAL SHAVED MARGIN (part 4):\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia; Fibrocystic change including macro- and\u000amicrocysts.\u000aSUPERIOR SHAVE MARGIN (part 5):\u000aBenign breast tissue.\u000aANTERIOR SHAVED MARGIN (part 6):\u000aBenign breast tissue.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 65 year old female with s/p 1983 right breast conserving therapy,\u000awhose REMOVED_DATE  left mammogram demonstrates a REMOVED_DATE cm spiculated mass. REMOVED_DATE \u000acore biopsy revealed invasive carcinoma with ductal and lobular features.\u000aOperation: Left wire localization partial mastectomy, sentinel node biopsy\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast cancer\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1) Sentinel node hot (FS)\u000a#2) Sentinel node warm (FS)\u000a#3) Left breast tissue (short stitch/superior; long stitch/lateral; whip\u000astitch/chest wall margin)\u000a#4) Lateral shaved margin\u000a#5) Superior shaved margin (whip stitch/new margin)\u000a#6) Anterior shaved margin (stitch/new margin)\u000aRADIOLOGY: Mass in specimen. JL\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "#1. HOT SENTINEL LYMPH NODE", (FSA):\u000aNegative for tumor.\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "#2. WARM SENTINEL LYMPH NODE", (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aNegative for tumor.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by HENDERSON,JOEL M.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in six parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart one, labeled "#1. sentinel node hot", consists of a single fragment of\u000atan/yellow soft tissue (3.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). A representative portion\u000aconsisting of possible lymph nodal tissue is evaluated intraoperatively and\u000asubmitted as FSA, and the remainder of the specimen is entirely submitted.\u000aMicro 1: FSA remnant, 1 frag, ESS\u000aMicro 2: remaining possible nodal tissue, 2 frags, ESS\u000aPart two, labeled "#2. sentinel node warm", consists of an aggregate of\u000atan/yellow soft tissue (9.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), containing five possible lymph\u000anodes (largest REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). All lymph nodes are evaluated\u000aintraoperatively as REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, with the largest two (one of them inked black) each\u000abisected and one-half of each submitted as FSB, and the smaller three lymph\u000anodes (one inked blue, and one inked black) each bisected and one-half of each\u000asubmitted as REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. Remaining nodal and fibrous tissue is also submitted for\u000ahistologic examination.\u000aMicro 3: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID remnant, 2 frags, ESS\u000aMicro 4: non frozen nodal tissue corresponding to REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 2 frags, ESS\u000aMicro 5: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID remnant, 3 frags, ESS\u000aMicro 6: non frozen nodal tissue corresponding to REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 3 frags, ESS\u000aMicro 7: remaining fibrous tissue, mult frags, ESS\u000aPart three, labeled "left breast tissue", consists of a left breast partial\u000amastectomy specimen consisting of a single fragment of yellow fibroadipose\u000atissue (9.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with no attached skin. The specimen arrives\u000aaccompanied by a whole specimen radiograph, which shows a localization wire in\u000aplace, marking a density adjacent to an excision margin. The specimen itself\u000aarrived inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior\u000a= black; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow;\u000amedial = orange, but the localization wire is not present. Sectioning reveals\u000aa hemorrhagic biopsy cavity (1.1 cm in diameter) with adjacent area of firm\u000awhite tissue suspicious for carcinoma (1.3 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), that grossly\u000aextends to the anterior margin. The remainder of the specimen consists of\u000aapproximately 90% yellow adipose tissue and 10% gray fibrous tissue with no\u000aother masses or lesions identified. The entire mass and biopsy cavity is\u000asubmitted, and additional representative sections are submitted.\u000aApproximately 25% of the specimen was submitted for histologic examination.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  lateral margin, perpendicularly sectioned, 3 frags, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  biopsy cavity and mass adjacent to anterior resection margin,\u000a7 frags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  posterior margin lateral to medial, 3 frags, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  superior margin, 3 frags, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  inferior margin, 2 frags, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  medial margin, perpendicularly sectioned, 2 frags, RSS\u000aPart four, labeled "#4. lateral shaved margin stitch = new margin", consists of\u000aa single fragment of tan/yellow fibroadipose tissue (7.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). A\u000awhip stitch is present on one flat surface, corresponding to the new lateral\u000amargin. The new margin is inked black, and the old margin is inked blue. Five\u000afoci of dense fibrous tissue are identified, all of which abut the new lateral\u000amargin (largest focus REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The remaining tissue consists\u000aalmost entirely of yellow adipose tissue. All fibrous nodules are submitted.\u000aMicro 27: nodule, 2 frags, ESS\u000aMicro 28: second nodule, 3 frags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  third nodule, 5 frags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  fourth nodule, 5 frags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  fifth nodule, 2 frags, ESS\u000aPart five, labeled "#5. superior shaved margin stitch new margin", consists of\u000aa single fragment of tan/yellow fibroadipose tissue (5.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm).\u000aThere is a whip stitch on one flat surface designating the new margin. The\u000anew margin is inked black, and the old is inked blue. No discrete masses or\u000aother lesions are identified in the specimen, which consists of 80% yellow\u000aadipose tissue and 20% gray fibrous tissue. Representative sections,\u000aincluding approximately 50% of the specimen are submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  superior shaved margin, 5 frags, RSS\u000aPart six, labeled "#6. anterior shaved margin stitch new margin", consists of a\u000asingle fragment of tan/yellow fibroadipose tissue (4.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm).\u000aThere is a whip stitch on one aspect, designating the new margin. The new\u000amargin is inked black, and the old margin is inked blue. No discrete masses or\u000alesions are identified in the specimen, which consists of approximately 75%\u000ayellow adipose tissue and 25% gray fibrous tissue. Representative sections\u000aencompassing approximately 60% of the specimen, are submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  anterior shaved margin, 5 frags, RSS\u000ajmh\u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: SENTINEL LYMPH NODE\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SENTINEL LYMPH NODE\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN\u000a[report_end]
