VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aNUCCI, MARISA, ROSE, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by NUCCI,MARISA ROSE,M.D.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A CLIP MARKING AN AREA OF PREVIOUSLY\u000aBIOPSIED CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, clinging type (intermediate to focally\u000ahigh nuclear grade) is present as small foci in 11 of 24 blocks,\u000aassociated with and away from the prior biopsy site (see note).\u000aCalcifications are present. No necrosis is seen. Multiple levels\u000aexamined.\u000aDCIS is present focally at the deep margin (block 9), REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000aanterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral and inferior margins, and is not\u000aseen close to superior and medial margins.\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia is present (block 17).\u000aNOTE: The DCIS is present predominantly as columnar cells with apocrine\u000aand secretory features lining small ducts. There is a focal area of DCIS\u000awith high grade nuclei (block 9; best seen on deeper levels).\u000aThis case was also reviewed by Dr. Susan Lester and selected slides were\u000areviewed by Dr. Stuart Schnitt, and they concur with the interpretation as\u000aDCIS.\u000aThis carcinoma would be classified as AJCC Tis NX MX.\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aAn immunoperoxidase study was performed with the following result for DCIS\u000a(block 7):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies for progesterone receptor and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu were attempted,\u000abut given the small foci of DCIS present, insufficient numbers of involved\u000aducts were available for interpretation.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: History of abnormal mammogram. S/p core biopsy at BWH of RUIQ\u000acalcifications REMOVED_DATE  showing ADH, clip left.\u000aOperation: Right mammographically directed breast biopsy\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal right mammogram\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Right breast tissue at REMOVED_DATE o'clock (short = superior;\u000along = lateral)\u000aRADIOLOGY: Clip is present within specimen.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by SANTAGATA,SANDRO,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in one part, labeled with the patient's name,\u000aunit number and "Rt breast tissue", and consists of a single breast excision\u000aspecimen measuring REMOVED_DATE cm from superior to inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm from medial to\u000alateral and REMOVED_DATE cm from anterior to posterior with a short suture placed by the\u000asuture indicating the superior margin and a long suture placed by the surgeon\u000aindicating the lateral margin. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol\u000afor the evaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior =\u000ared; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange.\u000aThe specimen radiograph reveals a clip and the localization wire.\u000aThere is a localizing wire that enters the specimen at the junction of the\u000asuperior and anterior margins. The specimen is composed predominantly of\u000aadipose tissue (90%). In the area of the tip of the localizing wire is a focus\u000aof hemorrhage (0.6 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). This area of hemorrhage comes to within\u000a0.9 cm of the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the\u000asuperior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the lateral and REMOVED_DATE \u000acm of the medial margins. REMOVED_DATE cm inferior to the area of hemorrhage is a\u000asecond area of distinct hemorrhage (1.7 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). This area of\u000ahemorrhage abuts the posterior and lateral margins. Focal areas of possible\u000acalcifications are noted along the medial margin of the specimen. The specimen\u000ais serially sectioned from medial to lateral and is entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  wire localized area, 3 frags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  remainder of path of wire, 5 frags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  tissue lateral to site of localization plus second area of\u000ahemorrhage, 2 frags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  tissue medial to localized site, 2 frags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  remainder of specimen lateral to site of localization, 8 frags,\u000aESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  specimen medial to site of localization, 8 frags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  areas of possible calcification/medial margin, 4 frags, ESS\u000assa\u000aReports to: CARTER, KATHARINE M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
