VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aGLICKMAN, JONATHAN, NEIL, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by GLICKMAN,JONATHAN NEIL,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, RE-EXCISION WITH WIRE-LOCALIZATION FOR CALCIFICATIONS AND A MASS:\u000aBenign breast tissue with calcifications associated with apocrine\u000ametaplasia, cysts, and columnar hyperplasia.\u000aPrior excision site with foreign body giant cell reaction.\u000aSkin with cicatrix.\u000aThere is no residual in situ carcinoma present, including margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: History of DCIS right breast REMOVED_DATE  at BWH (positive deep margin),\u000awire localization on additional area of calcifications medial/anterior/inferior\u000ato biopsy cavity.\u000aOperation: Right mammographically-directed breast biopsy.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: DCIS right breast.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1 - right breast tissue, short = superior, long = lateral,\u000ainked per pathology protocol.\u000aRadiograph report: Mass is in the specimen (AG), calcifications in specimen.\u000aL. Frost, M.D.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by SCHMIDT,JASON F.,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "#1 - right breast tissue", and consists of a breast excision specimen (6.7\u000ax REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with an embedded localization wire. Accompanying the specimen\u000ais a specimen radiograph demonstrating the localization wire passing adjacent\u000ato a cluster of calcifications and through a stellate opaque lesion. Two\u000aorienting sutures are present, designated by the surgeon as follows: short -\u000asuperior; and, long - lateral. Attached to the anterior surface of the\u000aspecimen is a skin ellipse (3.6 x REMOVED_DATE cm) with a linear well-healed surgical\u000ascar (3.2 cm in length). The specimen has been previously inked by the surgeon\u000aaccording to the pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior =\u000ablack; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow;\u000amedial = orange. Within the breast parenchyma there is a stellate tan/white\u000afocally cystic prior excision site (2.6 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The prior excision\u000asite extends from the skin ellipse and is focally present at the inked superior\u000aand anterior resection margins and is oriented to the remaining margins as\u000afollows: lateral - REMOVED_DATE cm; medial - REMOVED_DATE cm; posterior - REMOVED_DATE cm; and, inferior\u000a- REMOVED_DATE cm. The radiographic calcifications are not associated with a grossly\u000aidentiable lesion and are REMOVED_DATE cm from the closest resection margin (anterior).\u000aRepresentative sections of the specimen are submitted for microscopic\u000aexamination.\u000aMicro #1: Prior excision site and lateral and anterior margins, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro #2: Prior excision site and anterior, superior, and inferior margins, 2\u000afrags, RSS.\u000aMicro #3: Prior excision site and posterior margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro #4: Prior excision site and anterior and superior margins, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro #5: Prior excision site and anterior margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro #6: Prior excision site and posterior margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro #7: Prior excision site and anterior and superior margins, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro #8: Prior excision site and anterior and superior margins, 3 frags,\u000aRSS.\u000aMicro #9: Calcifications and anterior margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro #10: Medial margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000ajfs/\u000aReports to: CARTER, KATHARINE M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
