MOGRAM: Clip is seen in specimen.\u000aThe specimen, received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit\u000anumber, and "right breast tissue", consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm right\u000abreast wire localization biopsy specimen which has a needle localization wire\u000aand a short stitch denoting superior and a long stitch denoting lateral. The\u000aaccompanying radiograph shows a wire localization needle and a clip at the site\u000aof a radiopaque density. The specimen is inked in six colors: black=deep,\u000ablue=anterior, green=lateral, red=medial, orange=superior, and yellow=inferior.\u000aThe specimen is serially sectioned from anterior to posterior and then\u000aradiographed. A recent biopsy cavity is identified (1.3 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The\u000aclip is identified and removed. No nodules or masses are identified. The\u000aremaining breast parenchyma is comprised predominantly of fibroadipose tissue.\u000aThe slice containing the clip and the slice on either side of that peak is\u000aentirely submitted; representative sections of each of the margins and the\u000aremaining breast tissue are submitted for histologic analysis. Approximately\u000a70% of the specimen is submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE - anterior perpendicular margins, multiple frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE - slices of tissue containing clip, REMOVED_DATE frags each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE - breast tissue surrounding area with clip, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE - breast parenchyma, REMOVED_DATE frags each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE - posterior perpendicular margin, multiple frags, ESS.\u000aReports to: SHIRLEY, ROBERT, LAWRENCE M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
