th old blood clot (1.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm. There are no gross tumor masses identified within the specimen. The\u000aremainder of the breast parenchyma consists primarily of unremarkable fatty\u000aadipose tissue. Representative sections are submitted for analysis.\u000aMicro sections:\u000aMicro 1: biopsy cavity with relation to deep margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  sections of biopsy cavity, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 7: area of hemorrhage below the area of discoloration, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 8: section of nipple, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 9: upper outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 10: lower outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 11: upper inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 12: lower inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 13: 3 lymph nodes, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 14: 2 lymph nodes, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 15: 4 lymph nodes, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aPart two, "interpectoral tissue", consists of one fragment of white/tan fatty\u000atissue (2.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The specimen is entirely submitted for analysis.\u000aMicro 16: interpectoral tissue, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aPart three, "axillary level II", consists of multiple fragments of fatty\u000ayellow/tan adipose tissue (3.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate). There are\u000aapproximately 8 lymph nodes identified all of which are entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  largest lymph node, bisected, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro 19: 3 lymph nodes, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 20: 4 lymph nodes, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aReports to: HUGHES, SARA, ANN M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY W/REGIONAL LYMPH NODES\u000a[report_end]
