VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST BIOPSY W/O MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aFLETCHER, CHRISTOPHER, D.M., M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by FLETCHER,CHRISTOPHER D.M.,M.D.\u000a1) RIGHT BREAST, NEEDLE-DIRECTED BIOPSY:\u000aBenign breast tissue with pseudoangiomatous stromal hyperplasia,\u000afibrocystic changes, sclerosing adenosis, and apocrine metaplasia.\u000aMultifocal biopsy site changes with foreign body giant cell reaction.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Recent history of atypical cells on needle aspiration.\u000aOperation: Right needle directed breast biopsy.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast - atypical cells on aspiration.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Right needle directed breast bx, short/superior,\u000along/lateral.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by SMOUSE,JASON H.,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in one part, labeled with the patient's name,\u000aunit number, and "#1, right needle directed breast bx", consists of a single\u000afragment of breast tissue measuring 5 x 4 x 2 cm with two (2) orienting sutures\u000aplaced by the surgeon designated as long/lateral, short/superior and a\u000alocalizing wire. No radiograph was present with the specimen.\u000aThe specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation\u000aof margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior =\u000agreen; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. The entire specimen is firm with\u000amost dense portion in the medial aspect of the specimen but there are no\u000awell-circumscribeed nodules palpated. The interior of the specimen consists of\u000ahard fibrous tissue with multiple small cysts measuring from less than REMOVED_DATE cm\u000ain diameter up to REMOVED_DATE cm in diameter. The fibrous tissue has a gritty\u000aconsistency and involves the entire specimen. A radiograph taken by the\u000apathologist reveals two calcifications within the specimen, multiple small\u000acysts and a dense stroma. The entire specimen is submitted for histological\u000aevaluation.\u000aMicro 1: medial margin, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  remainder of specimen, medial to lateral, with calcifications in\u000amicro 5 and micro 8, and lateral margin present in micro's 12 -\u000a14, ESS.\u000arfi\u000aReports to: MATORY, YVEDT M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST BIOPSY W/O MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
