VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Sentinel Lymph Nodes(s)\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-06-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Qinghong Yang, M.D., Ph.D.; Peter M Sadow, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Andrea L Richardson, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aLEFT BREAST, EXCISION, RE-EXCISION, AND SENTINEL LYMPH NODE BIOPSIES (INCLUDING\u000aPARTS A-C AND REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID AND REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aADENOID CYSTIC CARCINOMA (1.7 cm).\u000aNuclei are intermediate grade.\u000aNo lymphovascular invasion is identified.\u000aNo in situ carcinoma is identified.\u000aCarcinoma comes to less than REMOVED_DATE cm of the lateral (slides REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) and superior\u000a(slides REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) margins and is REMOVED_DATE cm from the deep margin, in the initial\u000aexcision.\u000aThe remaining margins (including anterior, inferior and medial) are negative\u000a(>0.3 cm) for carcinoma.\u000aA global re-excision (specimen C) was performed that showed focal epithelial\u000ahyperplasia and no evidence of carcinoma at all margins (inferomedial,\u000aanterior, superior, posterior and lateral).\u000aCore biopsy site.\u000aSclerosing adenosis.\u000aTwo (2) sentinel lymph nodes with no carcinoma present (three H&E levels\u000areviewed).\u000aAJCC (6th edition) classification: pREMOVED_ACCESSION_IDc pREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID(sn) pMX\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 72-year-old female status post left breast core biopsy 09:30 for REMOVED_DATE \u000acm mass - adenoid cystic carcinoma with no lymphovascular invasion.\u000aOperation: L breast WL lumpectomy, SNM, SLNB and ? ALND.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: None given.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Left sentinel node x2 equals hot and blue.\u000aB/2. Left breast tissue - short suture equals superior, long suture equals\u000alateral, whipstitch at deep margin.\u000aC/3. Left reexcision, short suture equals superior, long suture equals\u000alateral.\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000aMass, clips and wire in specimen: Discussed with Dr. Rhei/Chad Houston.\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "LEFT SENTINEL NODE" (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID + REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aTwo lymph nodes negative for carcinoma.\u000aOR Consultation by: JONATHAN NEIL GLICKMAN, M.D., PH.D.\u000aThe senior physician certifies that he/she personally conducted a gross and/or\u000amicroscopic examination of the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed\u000athe rapid diagnos(es) related thereto.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in three parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname, unit number.\u000aPart A, received in the frozen section lab, "#1. Left sentinel node x2 hot and\u000ablue", and consists of a blue tinged rubbery lymph node (0.9 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm)\u000aand a tan rubbery lymph node (1.6 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm - inked black). The blue\u000atinged node is inked blue, bisected and entirely frozen as REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. The larger\u000ablack-inked lymph node is bisected and entirely frozen as REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" remnant, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" remnant, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aPart B "#2. Left breast tissue (sutured as noted)", and consists of a portion\u000aof yellow/tan fibroadipose tissue (7.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with a localization wire\u000ain placed (identified in frozen section lab and removed by breast bank), and\u000aorienting sutures ("short stitch equals superior, long stitch equals lateral,\u000aand whipstitch at deep margin"). The specimen is received previously inked by\u000athe surgeon with colors corresponding to the breast inking protocol (the\u000aspecimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins:\u000aposterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow;\u000amedial/orange). There is a firm white focally blue-dyed ill-defined mass (1.7\u000ax REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), REMOVED_DATE cm from the deep, lateral and superior margins, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom the anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to the inferior margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm to the\u000amedial margin. There are two metal clips adjacent to the mass. Placement of\u000athe wire cannot be grossly appreciated due to removal of the wire during tissue\u000abanking process. The remaining breast tissue consists of approximately 80%\u000atan/yellow lobulated adipose tissue and 20% white, dense, firm fibrous stroma.\u000aRepresentative tissue submitted to the breast bank for special studies.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Mass nearest lateral, inferior and deep margin, multi frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Mass nearest superior and deep margins, multi frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Additional anterior margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin nearest mass, 4 frags, RSS.\u000aPart C, "#3. Left reexcision (sutured as noted)", and consists of a portion of\u000abrown/yellow, annular, focally disrupted fibroadipose tissue (8.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm) with a black short suture designating "superior" and a tan Vicryl suture\u000adesignating "lateral" (Dr. Rhei personally confirmed the Vicryl suture is in\u000aplace of region in which long suture may have fallen out). The specimen is\u000ainked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black;\u000aanterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange.\u000aThere is a small amount of red/brown fibromuscular tissue (1.4 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm)\u000aalong the posteromedial aspect. The specimen is serially sectioned from medial\u000ato lateral, to exhibit focally blue-dyed dense fibrous stroma, abutting the\u000ainferomedial aspect. The remaining breast tissue consists of approximately 85%\u000ayellow lobulated adipose tissue and 15% tan fibrous stroma. No other gross\u000alesions identified.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Inferomedial margin, multi frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Anterior margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Superior margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Posterior margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aDFI/ajb\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Andrea L Richardson M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a11/17/2006\u000a[report_end]
