VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: KATHARINE CARTER M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Matthew D. Stachler, M.D., Ph.D.; George Lin, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Andrea L Richardson, M.D., Ph.D.; Vania Nose, MD, PhD\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST EXCISION TWO WIRE LOCALIZATION FOR CALCIFICATIONS WITH CLIP AT\u000a9:00 AND CALCIFICATIONS AT 10:00:\u000aFocal atypical ductal hyperplasia, without associated calcifications.\u000aFocal atypical lobular hyperplasia.\u000aSclerosing adenosis.\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia.\u000aColumnar cell change, cysts, and apocrine cysts.\u000aCalcifications associated with benign epithelium and dense stroma.\u000aPrior core biopsy site.\u000aMultiple levels examined.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: History of calcifications no amenable to core biopsy - 10 o'clock and\u000acalcifications associated with clip (ALH) - 9 o'clock.\u000aOperation: Right mammographically ductal breast biopsy.\u000aOperative Findings: Not given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal mammogram.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Right breast tissue at 9 and 10 o'clock (2 wires); short = superior, long\u000a= lateral.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen was received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "#1. Right breast tissue (two wires) at 9 and 10, short equals superior,\u000along equals lateral", consists of a REMOVED_DATE gram lumpectomy specimen with two\u000alocalization wires entering on the lateral side of the specimen. One of the\u000awires is more on the superior-lateral side, one is more on the inferior-lateral\u000aside. The specimen measures REMOVED_DATE cm medial to lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm superior to\u000ainferior, and REMOVED_DATE cm anterior to posterior. On serial sectioning of the\u000aspecimen, the internal tissue is approximately 50% fibrous and 50% adipose. No\u000adiscrete masses or lumps were identified. There was one small area of\u000ahemorrhage at the end of one of the localization wires. A prior biopsy site\u000awas near (0.3 cm) the superior margin. Approximately 80% of the specimen was\u000asubmitted for histological analysis. This included approximately 85% to 90% of\u000athe fibrous tissue and the entire area within the wires that contain the\u000acalcifications. Approximately 95% of the lateral margin and 75% of the medial\u000amargin were submitted for histologic analysis.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, perpendicular, 2 frags and 1 frag respectively,\u000aRSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Previous biopsy site, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Area between the localization wires, with REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID areas of\u000atermination of the wires, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Additional fibrous areas of breast tissue, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin, perpendicular, 2 frags each, RSS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000atac/elw\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Andrea L Richardson M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000aWednesday REMOVED_MONTH 30, 2009 at 05:13:43PM\u000a[report_end]
