VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID SENTINEL LYMPH NODE\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aWELCH, WILLIAM, ROBERT, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by WELCH,WILLIAM ROBERT,M.D.\u000aCorrected Report:\u000aRIGHT BREAST EXCISION AND SENTINEL NODES BIOPSIES (#1, #2 AND #3 SPECIMEN):\u000aINVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA WITH ONE FOCUS AND DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU.\u000aSYNOPSIS:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA\u000aSize - REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aMultifocal - No\u000aHistologic Type - Ductal\u000aHistologic Grade (SBR) - III(Poor)\u000aNuclear Grade - High\u000aEIC - Negative\u000aLymphovascular invasion - Absent\u000aDermal lymphatic invasion - N/A\u000aSkin invasion - N/A\u000aSkeletal muscle invasion - N/A\u000aFinal Margins (invasive) - Negative (>0.3 cm) superior, anterior,\u000aand medial margins\u000aVery close (<0.1 cm from margin) inferior\u000a#8, lateral (#9) and posterior (#8)\u000amargins\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU - Present\u000aTypes - Solid, cribriform\u000aNuclear grade - Intermediate\u000aCalcifications in DCIS - Absent\u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - Present\u000aMicroinvasion (<0.1cm) - Absent\u000aExtent of DCIS Number of blocks/total: REMOVED_DATE blocks\u000aFinal Margins (DCIS) Negative (>0.3 cm) lateral, superior,\u000ainferior,anterior, and posterior margins\u000aVery close (<0.1 cm) medial margin (#16)\u000aLYMPH NODES\u000aSentinel lymph nodes (3 H&E levels examined): Negative\u000aNumber of positive nodes: 0\u000aNumber of nodes examined: 2\u000aAxillary lymph nodes: Negative\u000aNumber of positive nodes: 0\u000aNumber of nodes examined: 4 (in these specimens)\u000aTOTAL POSITIVE NODES (sentinel + axillary) - REMOVED_DATE (in these specimens)\u000aOTHER FINDINGS Focal secretory change\u000aAJCC CLASSIFICATION (6th edition): REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDc pREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID MX\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER/PR/HER-2) - Performed previously\u000a#4. SPECIMEN LABELED "SUPERIOR SHAVE MARGIN":\u000aFibroadipose tissue with no tumor present.\u000aTwo (2) lymph nodes with no tumor present .\u000a#5. SPECIMEN LABELED "LATERAL SHAVE MARGIN":\u000aFibroadipose tissue with no tumor present.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 33 yo preMP female stopped bresat feeding 7 mos ago. Has mass in\u000a(R) low axilla/high axillary tail. FNA suspicious but not certain of\u000aorigin. Core bx showed invasive cancer but not certain if lymph node\u000aor breast primary. MRI breast showed another lesion in breast; u/s\u000asolid - recommend biopsy.\u000aOperation: (R) breast/axillary tail excision of mass. (R) wire localized\u000abreast biopsy of MRI lesion.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: R axilla mass.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Sentinel node, hot & blue, FS.\u000a2. Sentinel node, hot not blue, FS.\u000a3. R breast tissue - long lat, short.\u000a4. Superior shave margin - whip stitch new margin.\u000a5. Lateral shave margin - whip stitch new margin.\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "1) SENTINEL NODE, HOT AND BLUE" (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aOne lymph node negative for carcinoma.\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "2) SENTINEL NODE, HOT NOT BLUE" (FSB):\u000aOne lymph node negative for carcinoma.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by YOU,MINGJIAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in five parts, labeled with the patient's name\u000aand medical record number.\u000aPart one, labeled "#1 sentine node, hot and blue", consists of one fragment of\u000apink/tan lymph node (1.5 x 1 x 1 cm). The specimen is entirely submitted as\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aMicro 1: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID remnant, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro 2: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID remnant, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aPart two, labeled "#2 sentinel node, hot not blue", consists of one fragment\u000apink/tan lymph node (1.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The specimen is entirely submitted\u000aas FSB.\u000aMicro 3: FSB remnant, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aPart three, labeled "#3 right breast tissue", consists of a 6 x 5 x REMOVED_DATE cm soft\u000atissue which is yellow/white/tan exteriorly. The surgeon designated superior\u000amargin, lateral margin and chest wall margin with short, long and whip\u000astitches, respectively. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the\u000aevaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red;\u000ainferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. A solid, white,\u000aloculated mass (1.1 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) is identified. This mass is 1 cm from the\u000asuperior margin, 1 cm from the lateral margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior and\u000aposterior margins, 2 cm from the inferior margin and 4 cm from the medial\u000amargin. A slice (1 x 1 x REMOVED_DATE cm) was taken for tumor bank, not including\u000aadjacent normal tissue. Normal samples were taken for tumor bank from the\u000amedial margin. Small fragment from trimmed tissue is placed in a separate\u000acassette. No other solid nodules or necrotic or hemorrhagic areas are\u000aidentified in the specimen.\u000aMicro 4: trimmed tissue, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  breast tissue, 6 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 8: area with definitive tumor mass, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  remainder of breast tissue, 27 frags, ESS.\u000aPart four, labeled "#4 superior shave margin", consists of a fragment of\u000ayellow/tan fatty tissue (2.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The surgeon designated the new\u000amargin with a whip stitch. The area with the whip stitch is inked in black.\u000aThe specimen is entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  superior shave margin, 5 frags, ESS.\u000aPart five, labeled "#5 lateral shave margin", consists of a fragment of\u000ayellow/pink/tan soft tissue (3.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The surgeon designated the\u000anew margin with a whip stitch. The new margin with whip stitch is inked in\u000ablack. The specimen is entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  lateral shave margin, 9 frags, ESS.\u000amjy\u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: SENTINEL LYMPH NODE\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SENTINEL LYMPH NODE\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN\u000a[report_end]
