VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST MASTECTOMY - PARTIAL OR SIMPLE\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOGINO, SHUJI, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by OGINO,SHUJI,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, SIMPLE MASTECTOMY:\u000aINVASIVE SPINDLE CELL (METAPLASTIC) CARCINOMA, poorly differentiated\u000a(modified Bloom-Richardson grade III/III), with extensive tumor\u000anecrosis (mitotic count >1HPF), 5 cm (see NOTE).\u000aNo lymphovascular invasion is seen.\u000aNo carcinoma in situ is present.\u000aThe deep margin and skin are free of carcinoma.\u000aEight (8) lymph nodes are present with no carcinoma seen.\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies performed with the following results:\u000apositive - Pan-K (focal, strong), REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.2 (focal, strong), vimentin,\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, S-100 (focal), p63 (focal)\u000anegative - 34REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, ER, PR, HER-2/neu (0),\u000aE-cadherin\u000aNOTE:\u000aThe carcinoma has a spindle cell morphology with no areas more typical of\u000abreast adenocarcinoma present.\u000aThe immunoreactivity for keratins strongly supports a diagnosis of CARCINOMA.\u000aThe positivity for p63 and S-100 also supports this diagnosis.\u000aThis carcinoma would be classified as AJCC REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID pREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Mx.\u000aThe case has been reviewed by Dr. S. Lester, Breast Pathology Service, who\u000aconcurs.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Sarcoma right breast.\u000aOperation: Right simple mastectomy.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Sarcoma right breast.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Right breast with long/superior and short/axilla\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by SMOUSE,JASON H.,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "#1, right breast with long suture superior and short suture axilla", and\u000aconsists of a 1200 gram right simple mastectomy specimen (29 x 20 x 5 cm), with\u000askin ellipse (18 x REMOVED_DATE cm), areola (3.0 x REMOVED_DATE cm), nipple (1.0 cm), and\u000aaxillary tail (8 x 6 x REMOVED_DATE cm). The skin surface is smooth with no evidence of\u000ascarring. The deep margin is inked black, and the specimen is serially\u000asectioned revealing a single well-circumsribed yellow-tan mass (5.0 x REMOVED_DATE x\u000a4.0 cm), which is located in the middle superior aspect of the specimen and is\u000a1 cm from the deep margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the skin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior skin\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior soft tissue resection margin, and greater\u000athan 5 cm from all other soft tissue and skin margins. A representative\u000asection of the tumor is submitted for cytogenetics and electron microscopy.\u000aThe remainder of the specimen consists of 40% dense fibrous tissue and 60%\u000aadipose tissue with no discrete masses or lesions. Representative sections are\u000asubmitted for histological evaluation.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  mass, 5 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 6: deep margin overlying tumor mass, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 7: skin overlying mass, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 8: superior skin margin and superior soft tissue margin, en face,\u000a1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 9: nipple, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 10: superior outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 11: inferior outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 12: superior inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 13: superior inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 14: 4 lymph nodes, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 15: 3 lymph nodes, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 16: 1 lymph node, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aReports to: BERTAGNOLLI, MONICA, MARIE M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY - PARTIAL OR SIMPLE\u000a[report_end]
