00aNOTE:\u000aA keratin (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) immunostain is negative, supporting the diagnosis.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 56 year old female s/p REMOVED_DATE  left breast core biopsy of a REMOVED_DATE cm\u000amass revealing poorly differentiated adenocarcinoma.\u000aOperation: Left breast excision, sentinel node biopsy with possible I and II\u000adissection\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast cancer\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1) Sentinel node, blue not hot\u000a#2) Sentinel node, hot and blue\u000a#3) Left breast tissue (stitch, short/superior; long/lateral; retroareolar\u000astitch on chest wall margin)\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "#1. SENTINEL NODE BLUE NOT HOT", (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aLymph nodes; no tumor present.\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "#2. SENTINEL NODE", (FSB):\u000aLymph nodes; no tumor present.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by KWAAN,MARY R.,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in three parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart one, labeled "#1. sentinel lymph node biopsy blue not hot", consists of\u000asix fragments, three of which are blue, of fatty soft tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE to\u000a0.9 cm. The specimen is entirely submitted as REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aMicro 1: sentinel lymph nodes, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID remnant, 3 frags, ESS\u000aMicro 2: sentinel lymph nodes, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID remnant, 3 frags, ESS\u000aPart two, labeled "#2. sentinel node hot and blue", consists of two lymph\u000anodes, the largest measuring REMOVED_DATE cm and inked in blue, and the second measuring\u000a0.8 cm pink/tan, and inked in black. One lymph node is bisected. All lymph\u000anodes are submitted as FSB.\u000aMicro 3: FSB remnant, 3 frags, ESS\u000aPart three, labeled "#3. left breast tissue, stitch superior, long lateral",\u000aconsists of an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm piece of breast tissue, inked by the surgeon\u000aper pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior = black;\u000aanterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial =\u000aorange. Serial sectioning reveals a white, firm mass (3.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm)\u000awith poorly defined borders. The mass is REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom the lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm from the posteror, REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom the superior and REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin. There is a second firm\u000acystic nodule that measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm and is REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial\u000amargin and REMOVED_DATE cm from the deep margin.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  mass, 1 frag each, RSS\u000aMicro 8: cystic mass, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 9: inferior margin, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 10: superior margin, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 11: fibrous/cystic areas away from the mass, 1 frag, RSS\u000amrk\u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: SENTINEL LYMPH NODE\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SENTINEL LYMPH NODE\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
