VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aBOROWSKY, ALEXANDER, D., M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by GULIZIA,JAMES MARTIN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000a1. RIGHT BREAST BIOPSY, WIRE LOCALIZATION FOR A MASS:\u000aINVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA, REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000aThe carcinoma is well differentiated (modified Bloom Richardson Grade\u000aI/III).\u000aNo lymphatic or vascular invasion seen.\u000aInvasive carcinoma is focally present at anterior (yellow) margin\u000a(block 2), inferior (blue/yellow)margin (block 5), and appears\u000ato approach within REMOVED_DATE cm of the medial (green) margin, block 3,\u000a(See Note).\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, cribriform and solid types, intermediate\u000anuclear grade is present in three (3) of eleven (11) blocks\u000a(blocks 2,3,5).\u000aIn situ carcinoma comprises approximately 10%of the area involved\u000aby the invasive tumor and is not present outside the area involved by\u000athe invasive tumor.\u000aDCIS is not present at the margins.\u000aBiopsy site with repair reaction.\u000aFibrocystic changes are present including cysts and apocrine metaplasia.\u000aMicrocalcifications are associated with benign epithelium and found\u000awithin dense fibrous tissue.\u000a2. RIGHT BREAST, ANTERIOR SHAVE MARGIN:\u000aBenign breast tissue.\u000aMonckeberg's medial sclerosis.\u000aNo tumor seen.\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: by BOROWSKY,ALEXANDER D.,M.D.\u000aThe slides are re-evaluated for margins. Tumor is extensively present in\u000aadipose tissue at the anterior margin (block #2, yellow). However, the inferior\u000aand medial margins are free of carcinoma, although ink is artifactually present\u000aat some specimen edges.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 72 year old post-menopausal female not on hormones whose REMOVED_DATE \u000amammogram supplemented by ultrasound demonstrated a REMOVED_DATE cm spiculated\u000amass in the right breast upper outer quadrant. REMOVED_DATE  core biopsy\u000arevealed invasive ductal carcinoma.\u000aOperation: Right breast wire localization excisional biopsy\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast cancer\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1) Right breast tissue (short suture/inferior; long suture/\u000alateral; whip stitch chest wall)\u000a#2) Anterior shave margin (whip stitch margin)\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000a#1. SPECIMEN LABELED "RIGHT BREAST BIOPSY" (GROSS EXAMINATION ONLY):\u000a1.5 cm mass grossly consistent with invasive carcinoma.\u000aMass is grossly REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior and deep/inferior margins and\u000a0.8 from the medial margin (closest margins).\u000aGross examination only.\u000aCase discussed with surgeon.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by STERN,HOWARD M.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart one, labeled "right needle directed breast biopsy", consists of a single\u000afragment of tan/yellow fibroadipose tissue (7.2 x REMOVED_DATE x 3 cm) with three\u000aorienting sutures (short designated inferior, long designated lateral, whip\u000adesignated deep) and a needle localization wire, re-oriented with the surgeon\u000ain the surgical cutting room after having been inked in 6 colors. The following\u000ais the re-oriented color assigment: inferior=blue/yellow, superior=black,\u000alateral=red, medial=green/yellow, superficial=yellow and deep=blue. Upon\u000asectioning there is a REMOVED_DATE cm stellate mass with central hemorrhage (0.3 cm)\u000aconsistent with biopsy cavity. The mass is REMOVED_DATE cm from the deep/inferior\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin.\u000aThe specimen contains an unremarkablae skin ellipse (2.7 x 1 cm).\u000aApproximately 40% of the tissue was submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  tumor and anterior margin, 3 frags, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  tumor and posterior margin, 3 frags, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  inferior margin, 4 frags, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  superior margin, 2 frags, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  medial margin, 5 frags, RSS\u000aMicro 11: lateral margin, 2 frags, RSS\u000aPart two, labeled "anterior shave margin, whip stitch margin", consists of\u000aa single fragment of tan/yellow fibroadipose tissue (4 x REMOVED_DATE x 1 cm) with a\u000asingle orienting whip stitch (designated margin). The designated margin is\u000ainked blac The entire specimen is submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  anterior shvae, mult frags, ESS\u000ahs\u000aReports to: KAELIN, CAROLYN, MARY M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
