VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST MASTECTOMY W/REGIONAL LYMPH NODES\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aNOSE, VANIA, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by NOSE,VANIA,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, SIMPLE MASTECTOMY:\u000aMYXOID SPINDLE CELL SARCOMA (9.7 cm), most consistent with high grade\u000amyxofibrosarcoma.\u000aNecrosis is present focally.\u000aMitoses: 19:10 HPF.\u000aResection margins are negative for tumor.\u000aLymphovascular invasion is absent.\u000aSkin with no significant pathologic change.\u000aImmunohistochemistry performed at BWH demonstrates the following staining\u000aprofile in tumor cells:\u000aPositive - SMA (focal)\u000aNegative - REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, S-100, myoREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aThe case was reviewed by Dr. C. Fletcher who concurs.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Sarcoma, R breast.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Right breast.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by YOU,MINGJIAN JAMES,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number\u000aand "right breast". The specimen consists of a REMOVED_DATE x 25 x REMOVED_DATE cm breast\u000a(2922 grams) with a white/tan skin ellipse (33 x 24 cm). There are no attached\u000aaxillary tail and skeletal muscle. A separate small fragment of yellow/tan\u000afatty tissue (12 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with an attached white/tan skin ellipse (11.5\u000ax 3 cm). No lesions are identified in the smaller fragment and excisional\u000amargin of the smaller fragment is inked in blue. The excisional margin of the\u000alarger fragment is also inked in blue. The specimen is sectioned revealing\u000aapproximately 90% of yellow/tan adipose tissue. The lower outer quadrant of\u000athe breast has a pink/white/tan solid mass (9.7 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) that is REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom the closest posterior resection margin. The mass is well circumscribed\u000aand is lobulated. There is a cystic area (5.1 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with necrotic\u000aappearance. The remaining cut surface of the mass is white/pink/tan. No\u000aother lesions suspicious for tumor are identified in the specimen. The mass\u000ais REMOVED_DATE cm from the grossly unremarkable nipple (0.7 in diamete) and its\u000asurrounding areola (6.1 x REMOVED_DATE cm). The skin is grossly unremarkable. Biopsy\u000asite is not identified. Touch preparations are made from the tumor.\u000aPhotographs are taken at the department of pathology. Representative mass is\u000asubmitted for cytogenetics, snap frozen, quick fixation, and possible EM.\u000aMicro 1: quick fix of tumor, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 2: mass close to cystic lesion, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 3: mass and closest skin surface, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 4: mass and adjacent adipose tissue, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  additional representative sections of tumor, 4 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 7: superior aspect of skin and adipose tissue resection margin, 1\u000afrag, RSS.\u000aMicro 8: inferior skin and adipose resection margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 9: lateral skin and adipose resection margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 10: medial skin and adipose tissue resection margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 11: representative tissue from the smaller fragment, 1 frag, RSS.\u000amjy\u000aReports to: OSTEEN, ROBERT, T. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY W/REGIONAL LYMPH NODES\u000a[report_end]
