VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID:REMOVED_CASE_ID Report Status: Signed\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aDIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. Left axillary sentinel lymph node, excision:\u000aNo tumor seen (0/1), (see note).\u000aB. Left breast, excisional biopsy:\u000aInvasive poorly differentiated ductal carcinoma, size estimated at REMOVED_DATE \u000acm. (see note).\u000aVery focal high grade ductal carcinoma in situ, solid and cribriform\u000atypes admixed within and adjacent to invasive tumor (see note).\u000aHealing biopsy site changes.\u000aC. Left breast "final deep margin", excision:\u000aNo diagnostic abnormalities recognized.\u000aNo invasive or in situ carcinoma seen.\u000aD. Left breast "final lateral margin", excision:\u000aNo diagnostic abnormalities recognized.\u000aNo invasive or in situ carcinoma seen.\u000aE. Left breast "final medial margin", excision:\u000aNo diagnostic abnormalities recognized.\u000aNo invasive or in situ carcinoma seen.\u000aF. Left breast "final superior margin", excision:\u000aNo diagnostic abnormalities recognized.\u000aNo invasive or in situ carcinoma seen.\u000aG. Left breast "final inferior margin", excision:\u000aNo diagnostic abnormalities recognized.\u000aNo invasive or in situ carcinoma seen.\u000aNOTE: In specimen B, the ductal carcinoma in situ is focally less than REMOVED_DATE mm.\u000afrom the anterior margin (slide REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aThe invasive carcinoma is less than REMOVED_DATE mm. from the deep (slide REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID)\u000amargin and less than REMOVED_DATE mm. from the anterior (slide REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) margin.\u000aAll additional margins (C-G) are free of tumor.\u000aFocal lymphatic/vascular invasion is seen in specimen B (slides REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aThe prior left breast needle core biopsies (S-02-REMOVED_CASE_ID) have been\u000areviewed.\u000aImmunohistochemical studies performed on block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID reveal the following\u000aresults for the infiltrating carcinoma:\u000aEstrogen receptor: POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor: POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID): NEGATIVE for overexpression.\u000aThe sentinel lymph node (part A) was examined with level sections and\u000awith keratin immunostains and does not show metastatic carcinoma.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by: Nicole A. Mihok, M.D.\u000aClinical diagnosis & history:\u000aLeft breast carcinoma\u000aTissue-Designation:\u000aA.Sentinel lymph node - left axillary\u000aB.Breast, excision with margins - left\u000aC.Breast, excision with margins - final margin, deep\u000aD.Breast, excision with margins - final margin, lateral\u000aE.Breast, excision with margins - final margin, medial\u000aF.Breast, excision with margins - superior margin\u000aG.Breast, excision with margins - inferior margin\u000aGross description:\u000aThe specimen is received in seven containers.\u000aSpecimen A labeled "left axillary sentinel lymph node" consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000ax REMOVED_DATE cm. firm, tan portion of tissue with a small amount of adjacent yellow\u000aadipose tissue. The node is bisected and both halves of the node are submitted\u000ain one cassette. 2X all.\u000aSpecimen B labeled "left lumpectomy" is received in formalin and consists of a\u000aspherical shaped portion of breast tissue that measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000aThere is a needle localization wire protruding from the specimen. There is a\u000along suture at the lateral margin and a short suture at the superior margin.\u000aThe superior half is inked blue; the inferior half, green; the deep margin,\u000ablack. The specimen is sectioned from lateral towards medial and shows a\u000ahemorrhagic streaked central portion of the tissue with surrounding tissue.\u000aThe entire specimen is submitted in eleven cassettes REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID is most lateral;\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID is most medial). 11 agg. all.\u000aSpecimen C labeled "left breast, final deep margin" consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x\u000a0.6 cm. portion of breast tissue with a suture at one edge which is designated\u000aas the true margin. This surface is inked black. The other surface is not\u000ainked. The specimen is serially sectioned and entirely submitted in two\u000acassettes labeled REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. 5X all.\u000aSpecimen D labeled "left breast, final margin lateral" consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000ax REMOVED_DATE cm. portion of breast tissue with a suture designating the true margin.\u000aThe surface is inked blue; the other surfaces are not inked. The specimen is\u000aserially sectioned and submitted entirely in one cassette labeled D. 1 agg.\u000aall.\u000aSpecimen E labeled "left breast, final medial margin" consists of two\u000aunoriented spherical shaped portions of tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000aand REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. Both portions of tissue are entirely inked blue. They\u000aare each bisected and each submitted in one cassette, labeled REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. 2 agg.\u000aall.\u000aSpecimen F labeled "left breast, superior margin" consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm. portion of breast tissue with a suture designating the true margin. This\u000amargin is inked blue. The other surfaces are not inked. The specimen is\u000aserially sectioned and submitted entirely in one cassette, labeled F. 1 agg.\u000aall.\u000aSpecimen G labeled "left breast, inferior margin" consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm. portion of breast tissue with a stitch designating the true margin. This\u000asurface is inked blue. The other surfaces are not inked. This portion is\u000aserially sectioned and entirely submitted in one cassette labeled G. 1 agg.\u000aall.\u000aDictated by: NAM____(signature on file)____DANIEL D. KOELLIKER, M.D. REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a____(signature on file)____NICOLE MIHOK, M.D. REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a[report_end]
