VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID OUTSIDE SLIDE CONSULT - BREAST\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aLESTER, SUSAN, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aCONSULT SLIDES FROM HARVARD VANGUARD MEDICAL ASSOCIATES, BOSTON, MA:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, 10:00, ULTRASOUND GUIDED CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR A NODULE\u000a(REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID; REMOVED_DATE ):\u000aINVASIVE POORLY DIFFERENTIATED CARCINOMA, measuring at least 1 cm in size\u000a(see note).\u000aLymphovascular invasion is present.\u000aA definite in situ component is not seen.\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed by the original institution with\u000athe following results (reviewed):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu NEGATIVE (1+)\u000aCEA NEGATIVE\u000aGCDFP-15 NEGATIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID NEGATIVE\u000aCalponin NEGATIVE (for myoepithelial cells in tumor)\u000aSmooth muscle alpha actin NEGATIVE (for myoepithelial cells in tumor)\u000aNote: The carcinoma is histologically similar to the patient's poorly\u000adifferentiated papillary serous adenocarcinoma.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID has been reported to be present in the majority of ovarian serous\u000acarcinomas. In one report, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID was absent in 25 studied breast\u000acarcinomas. Therefore, this finding is more supportive of a metastatic\u000aorigin for the current carcinoma. However, this finding is not considered\u000adefinitive in the absence of additional supportive studies.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: None given.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Consult slides\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by BROWNE,TARA-JANE,MB,BCH,BAO\u000aReceived from Harvard Vanguard Medical Associates, 120 Brookline Ave, Boston,\u000aMA REMOVED_CASE_ID are ten (10) slides labeled "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" and sublabeled "A-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID",\u000a"A-ER"m, "A-PR", "A-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID", "A-CEA", "A-SMA", "A-Calponin", "A-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID monoclonal",\u000a"A-GCDFP", and "B-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID", corresponding to an ultrasound-guided core needle\u000abiopsy, 10 o'clock, right breast obtained on REMOVED_DATE  according to the\u000aaccompanying pathology report bearing the patient's name.\u000aReports to: CAMPOS, SUSANA, MARIA M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: OUTSIDE SLIDE CONSULT - BREAST\u000a[report_end]
