VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aFLETCHER, CHRISTOPHER, D.M., M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by FLETCHER,CHRISTOPHER D.M.,M.D.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, NEEDLE LOCALIZATION/EXCISION FOR A MASS\u000aPOORLY DIFFERENTIATED PAPILLARY CARCINOMA, 4cm, consistent with\u000aMETASTASIS from this patient's known ovarian papillary serous\u000aadenocarcinoma ( see REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID & REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ).\u000aMultifocal lymphovascular invasion is identified.\u000aTumor involves medial, anterior, superior and inferior margins\u000aand extends to within REMOVED_DATE cm of the lateral and posterior margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: None given.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Right breast needle-loc (short/superior; long/lateral)\u000aRADIOLOGY REPORT:\u000aMass in specimen.\u000aLF/jms\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by BAILEY,GERALD P.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name unit number,\u000aand "1) right needle-localization breast biopsy (short/superior;\u000along/lateral)", and consists of an excisional breast biopsy (5.5 x REMOVED_DATE x 2 cm)\u000awith two (2) sutures, one short (superior) and one long (lateral), and a wire\u000aoriented from lateral to medioinferior. The specimen contains a mass (4 x 2 x\u000a1.5 cm) that appears to abut the superior, anterior, and inferior margins and\u000ais located REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin, and\u000a1.5 cm from the lateral margin. A radiograph is submitted with the specimen.\u000aThe specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins:\u000aposterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral\u000a= yellow; medial = orange. The specimen is serially sectioned from medial to\u000alateral, and is entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  right needle-localized breast biopsy, REMOVED_DATE frag/cass, ESS\u000aNOTE: cassettes REMOVED_DATE contain the portion of the specimen localized by the\u000aneedle.\u000ageb\u000aReports to: MATORY, YVEDT M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
