VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Amend/Addenda\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000a********** Addended Report ***********\u000aResident: Stephanie Schulte, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Shuji Ogino, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. LEFT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR CALCIFICATIONS AND A CLIP:\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia and columnar cell changes.\u000aCalcifications associated with benign breast epithelium.\u000aBiopsy site changes.\u000aFibroadipose (0.5 cm).\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy.\u000aB. RIGHT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia.\u000aSclerosing adenosis with calcifications.\u000aCalcifications associated with benign breast epithelium.\u000aThere is no invasive carcinoma.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 42-year-old premenopausal female with a family history (grandmother,\u000aaunts) of breast cancer, and radiation exposure (Chernobyl nuclear accident).\u000aThe REMOVED_DATE mammogram demonstrate right upper outer quadrant calcification. A\u000aleft breast 1 o'clock axis 8-mm density was confirmed as a solid mass on\u000aultrasound and was noted as architectural distortion on MRI.\u000aOperation: Bilateral wire localized biopsy.\u000aOperative Findings: Not given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal right mammogram, abnormal left MRI.\u000aORGANS/TISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Left breast tissue: Short superior, long lateral, whipstitch chest wall\u000ato mammography, with wire.\u000aB/2. Right breast tissue: Short superior, long lateral, whipstitch on chest\u000awall margin, to mammography, with wire.\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000aSpecimen #1: Two wires, clip, Ca++ in specimen. OR called. SR.\u000aSpecimen #2: Wire and Ca++ in specimen. OR called. SR.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aTwo specimens were received fresh, each labeled with the patient's name and\u000aunit number.\u000aSpecimen 1, "#1. Left breast tissue, short superior, long lateral, whipstitch\u000achest wall," consists of a wire localized breast excision (5.8 cm from superior\u000ato inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm from medial to lateral and REMOVED_DATE cm from anterior to\u000aposterior). Two localization wires are in place, one entering the specimen at\u000athe anterior/inferior side, the other one entering the specimen at the lateral\u000aside. The specimen is marked by a short stitch designating superior, a long\u000astitch designating lateral, and a whipstitch designating the posterior margin.\u000aAn accompanying specimen radiograph shows two localization wires with one wire\u000apointing at a clip. The center of the radiograph demonstrates punctate\u000acalcifications next to the second localization wire. The specimen was\u000apreviously inked by the surgeon according to the pathology protocol for the\u000aevaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red;\u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/ orange. The specimen is sectioned into\u000afifteen slices from superior to inferior. Slices #4 to #15 contain ill-defined\u000awhite fibrous tissue with numerous small cysts (up to REMOVED_DATE cm). Slices #9 to\u000a#15 are almost entirely composed of white fibrous tissue with small cysts.\u000aSlices #13 and #14 contains a larger cyst (0.5 cm), filled with white soft\u000amaterial. The cyst has a smooth wall. The tip of the first localization wire\u000ais located in slice #6. Accordingly, the clip must be located in slices #6 or\u000a#7.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Superior margin, perpendicular, 4 frags each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #2, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #3, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #4, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #5, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #6, ? clip, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #7, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #8, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #9, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #11, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #12, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #13, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #14, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Inferior margin, perpendicular, 5 frags, ESS.\u000aSpecimen 2, "#2. Right breast tissue: Short stitch superior, long lateral,\u000awhipstitch on chest wall margin with wire localization," consists of a wire\u000alocalized breast excision (4.8 cm from medial to lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm from superior\u000ato inferior and REMOVED_DATE cm from anterior to posterior) with a long stitch marking\u000athe lateral margin, a short stitch marking the superior margin, and a\u000awhipstitch marking the posterior margin. There is a localization wire in\u000aplace, entering the specimen at the lateral side. An accompanying specimen\u000aradiograph demonstrates the localization wire and punctate calcifications. The\u000aspecimen was previously inked by the surgeon according to the pathology\u000aprotocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue;\u000asuperior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/ orange. The specimen is\u000asectioned into thirteen slices from lateral to medial. The specimen is\u000acomposed of yellow lobulated adipose tissue intermixed with fibrous tissue\u000acontaining small cysts. The largest cyst (0.4 cm) is located in slices #10 and\u000a#11. No discrete lesions are identified.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, perpendicular, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #2, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #3, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #4, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #5, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #6, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #7, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #8, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #9, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #10, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #11, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin, perpendicular, 7 frags, ESS.\u000aSTS/lp\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Shuji Ogino M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a1/31/2007\u000aAddendum:\u000aPart A. ?Fibroadipose (0.5 cm)? should be ?Fibroadenoma (0.5 cm)?. This is an\u000aerror in transcription.\u000aThe diagnosis remains otherwise unchanged.\u000aAddendum #1 by Shuji Ogino M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
