VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: Esther Rhei M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-05-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Samuel G Katz, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Michelle S Hirsch, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aLEFT BREAST, RE-EXCISION:\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aSYNOPSIS:\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU - Present\u000aTypes - Solid and cribriform\u000aNuclear grade - Intermediate\u000aCalcifications in DCIS - Absent\u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - Absent\u000aMicroinvasion (<0.1cm) - Absent\u000aExtent of DCIS\u000aNumber of blocks/total: - REMOVED_DATE blocks (0.2 cm focus, block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID)\u000aFinal Margins (DCIS)\u000aNegative (>0.3 cm) - anterior, posterior, superior, lateral,\u000ainferior\u000aClose (0.1-0.3 cm) - medial (0.2 cm, block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID)\u000aOTHER FINDINGS - Biopsy cavity\u000a- Skin with no tumor present.\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER/PR/HER-2) - Previously performed\u000aNOTE: This case has been reviewed by Dr. D. Dillon (Breast Pathology Service),\u000awho concurs.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 70-year old female - status post left breast core biopsy for a mass,\u000arevealing ductal hyperplasia with atypia. Status post left breast wire\u000alocalization biopsy REMOVED_DATE  for DCIS. Pathology report demonstrating close\u000amargins requiring re-excision.\u000aOperation: Left breast re-excision.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast cancer.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000a1. Left breast tissue - long - lateral, short - superior, and whipstitch on\u000achest wall margin - color markings per pathology.\u000aPlease review with Breast Service (Dr. Dillon to see).\u000aPlease see comment on BS-05-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_DATE \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient?s name, unit number,\u000aand "#1 Left breast tissue", and consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm portion of\u000afibrofatty breast tissue with three orienting sutures (long - lateral, short -\u000asuperior, whipstitch - chest wall margin). There is a small piece of\u000aunremarkable skin present. The specimen is received previously inked per\u000apathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black;\u000aanterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. The\u000aspecimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral, revealing a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x\u000a0.3 cm cavity, which comes to within REMOVED_DATE cm of the anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of\u000athe posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the inferior and superior margins, REMOVED_DATE cm of\u000athe medial margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin. The cavity is surrounded\u000aby tan/white, dense fibrous tissue and fat necrosis. A silver metal clip is\u000aidentified within the dense fibrous tissue adjacent to the cavity. Remaining\u000abreast tissue consists of equal proportions of yellow/tan, lobulated fat and\u000atan/white fibrous stroma.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Breast tissue, sequentially from medial to lateral, multiple\u000afrags, ESS.\u000aNote: Cavity in Micros REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. Skin and clip in Micro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000adfi/elw\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Michelle S Hirsch M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Michelle S Hirsch M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a4/28/2005\u000a[report_end]
