erially sectioned from lateral to medial to reveal a\u000acentral area of deep red hemorrhage, and a deep gray, fluid filled cyst (0.3 cm\u000ain diameter). The specimen is approximately 70% golden yellow fatty tissue and\u000a30% fibrous tissue. The entirely specimen is serially submitted from lateral\u000ato medial for microscopic examination.\u000aMicro 1: Lateral margin, perpendicular, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Body of specimen, including inferior, superior, anterior, and\u000aposterior margins, 5 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 7: Medial margin, perpendicular, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aPart two, labeled "Sono-Rx tissue marker", consists of a white to pink, hard\u000aconcretion (0.4 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) which contains a metal clip. The specimen is\u000asubmitted for gross identification only.\u000arlr\u000aReports to: LESNIKOSKI, BETH-ANN M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: UNLISTED SURGICAL SPECIMEN - LEVEL I (GROSS ONLY)\u000a[report_end]
