VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID:REMOVED_CASE_ID Report Status: Signed\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aDIAGNOSIS:\u000aRight breast and axillary lymph nodes, right modified radical mastectomy with\u000alymph node dissection (1253 grams):\u000aInfiltrating duct carcinoma, poorly differentiated, REMOVED_DATE cm., see note.\u000aHigh grade ductal carcinoma in situ, solid and comedo type with\u000amicrocalcifications and necrosis, see note.\u000aMetastatic carcinoma in three of eleven lymph nodes (3/11).\u000aDiffuse lactational effect/change.\u000aNipple and skin with no diagnostic abnormalities recognized.\u000aSYNOPTIC REPORT: BREAST\u000aINVASIVE TUMOR:\u000a-histologic type: ductal\u000a-histologic grade: poorly differentiated\u000a-size (greatest dimension): REMOVED_DATE cm. The tumor is located at 9:00 and is\u000avery lateral.\u000a-lymphatic/vascular invasion: present\u000a-perineural invasion: none identified\u000a-microcalcification: none identified\u000a-margins for invasive tumor: The invasive tumor is less than REMOVED_DATE cm. over a\u000abroad front from the inked margin (slide 3)\u000aat the lateral non deep end of the specimen\u000aslightly inferior to the area where the upper\u000aand lower quadrants join.\u000a-immunohistochemical staining on prior specimen (S-06-3311) was reported as:\u000aEstrogen receptor: POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor: POSITIVE\u000a-immunohistochemical staining performed on block 6 reveals the following\u000aresults for the infiltrating carcinoma:\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID): NEGATIVE for overexpression\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU (DCIS):\u000a-histologic type: solid and comedo\u000a-histologic grade: high\u000a-size (greatest dimension): Microscopic foci within and around the\u000ainvasive tumor\u000a-extent: focal\u000a-extensive intraductal component: absent\u000a-necrosis in DCIS: present\u000a-microcalcifications in DCIS: present\u000a-margins for DCIS: clear (greater than or equal to REMOVED_DATE cm.)\u000aLYMPH NODES:\u000aPositive lymph nodes out of total sampled: REMOVED_DATE \u000a(3/11 non-sentinel lymph nodes).\u000a-size of largest metastasis (greatest dimension): REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000a-extranodal extension: none identified\u000aPRIOR RELATED SPECIMENS REVIEWED:\u000asite: right breast needle core biopsy specimen #: S-06-3311 date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aAJCC pTNM Classification (6th Ed.): pREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID pREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID pMX\u000aThe pathologic TNM classification above is based only on the information\u000aavailable to the pathologist, and therefore may not be accurate.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by: Nicole A. Mihok, M.D.\u000aClinical diagnosis & history:\u000aRight breast carcinoma\u000aTissue-Designation:\u000aBreast, modified radical mastectomy - right\u000aGross description:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh from the Operating Room, labeled "right breast"\u000aand consists of a REMOVED_DATE gram breast mastectomy specimen with a large ellipse\u000aof skin and multiple axillary nodes in the axillary tail. The breast measures\u000a25.5 x REMOVED_DATE x up to REMOVED_DATE cm. The axillary tail measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000aThere is a long stitch at the lateral edge of the skin. A short stitch is at\u000athe superior edge. The ellipse of skin measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. There is a\u000anipple and areola in place. The nipple is REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. and the areola\u000ais up to REMOVED_DATE cm. in greatest dimension. There are no scars or lesions\u000aidentified on the skin. The upper inner quadrant is inked blue. The upper\u000aouter quadrant is inked green. The deep margin is black. The lower inner\u000aquadrant is inked yellow. The lower outer quadrant is inked red. The specimen\u000ais serially sectioned and in the lateral edge of the breast underneath the\u000alateral skin edge is a firm mass that measures up to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The\u000amass is close to the anterior and slightly inferior peripheral margins in the\u000a9:00 area where the upper and lower outer quadrants come together. The\u000aremaining breast shows diffuse lactational effect with multiple reddish\u000anodules. No other masses are identified. Representative sections are\u000asubmitted as follows. 30 agg.\u000aSection code: 1 - nipple and adjacent skin\u000a2-6 - sections of the tumor (2 and 3 are closest margins)\u000a7 - slightly firm white area immediately adjacent to the tumor\u000a8 - deep margin closest to the tumor\u000a9-10 - random sections from the upper inner quadrant\u000a11-12 - random sections from the lower inner quadrant\u000a13-14 - random sections from the upper outer quadrant\u000a15 - random section from the medial part of the lower inner\u000aquadrant away from the area of tumor\u000a16-30 - sections of axillary lymph nodes (16 - two possible small\u000anodes not bisected; 17 - one large node bisected; 18 -\u000aone node bisected and adjacent adipose tissue; REMOVED_DATE -\u000acontain adipose tissue with possible small lymph nodes;\u000a21-22 - one large lymph node bisected; REMOVED_DATE - portions\u000aof adipose tissue with possible nodes; 26 - one node\u000abisected; 27 - two nodes; REMOVED_DATE - one adherent portion of\u000aadipose tissue trisected - it is possibly one to two\u000anodes)\u000aDictated by: NAM____(signature on file)____MICHAEL J. ROSS, M.D. REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a____(signature on file)____NICOLE MIHOK, M.D. REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a[report_end]
