VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST MASTECTOMY - PARTIAL OR SIMPLE\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aWEINSTEIN, MICHAEL, H., M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by WEINSTEIN,MICHAEL H.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000a1) LEFT BREAST, SIMPLE MASTECTOMY:\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU (0.2 cm), cribriform type, low nuclear grade,\u000ais present in a single block in the region showing prior biopsy\u000asite changes.\u000aNo invasive carcinoma is identified.\u000aPrior biopsy site changes are present.\u000aThe deep margin of resection is negative for DCIS (>0.3 cm).\u000aMicrocalcifications are noted in association with DCIS and benign\u000aepithelium.\u000a2) RIGHT MEDIAL BREAST TISSUE, REDUCTION MAMMOPLASTY:\u000aBenign breast tissue with fibrocystic changes including apocrine\u000achange and cyst formation.\u000a3) RIGHT CENTRAL BREAST TISSUE, REDUCTION MAMMOPLASTY:\u000aBenign breast tissue.\u000a4) RIGHT LATERAL BREAST TISSUE, REDUCTION MAMMOPLASTY:\u000aBenign breast tissue.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: History of DCIS and invasive cancer left breast with + margin. See\u000aFaulkner pathology.\u000aOperation: Left simple mastectomy (completion mastectomy) and right reduction.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast cancer.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Left breast (stitch marks left upper outer quadrant).\u000a2. Right medial breast tissue.\u000a3. Right central breast tissue.\u000a4. Right lateral breast tissue.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by CHANG,BRIAN S.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in four parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart one, labeled "#1, left breast, stitch marks left upper outer quadrant",\u000aconsists of a 13 x 14 x 4 cm simple mastectomy specimen with an 8 x REMOVED_DATE cm skin\u000aellipse, a REMOVED_DATE cm in diameter areola, and a REMOVED_DATE cm in diameter nipple. An\u000aorienting suture is present and marks the left upper outer quadrant. The deep\u000amargin is smooth glistening fascia in the left lower outer quadrant, there is\u000aan area of fixture to the fascia of the underlying breast tissue. The fascial\u000amargin is inked black and the specimen is serially sectioned. In the left\u000alower outer quadrant, underlying the area of fixture, there is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x\u000a1.0 cm area of hemorrhage and fibrosis grossly consistent with previous biopsy\u000asite, which is REMOVED_DATE cm from the deep fixed margin. The remainder of the breast\u000aconsists primarily of dense white, tan breast tissue. No other focal lesions\u000aare identified.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  previous biopsy cavity, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  adjacent uninvolved breast tissue, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  upper inner quadrant, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 9: lower inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 10: upper outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 11: lower outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 12: nipple, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aPart two, labeled "#2, right medial breast tissue", consists of multiple\u000afragments of skin measuring in aggregate 7 x 4 x REMOVED_DATE cm and a fragment of\u000abreast tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm with an attached portion of skin\u000ameasuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The breast tissue is inked.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  breast tissue, 3 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 15: breast tissue with cyst, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 16: skin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aPart three, labeled "#3, Right central breast tissue", consists of two\u000aunoriented fragments of breast tissue, measuring 12 x 6 x 2,5 cm and 8 x 2 x\u000a1.5 cm. The larger breast tissue fragment has an attached portion of skin,\u000ameasuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The specimen is inked black, serially sectioned\u000arevealing dense white breast tissue without focal lesions or abnormalities.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  larger breast fragment with skin, 5 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 21: smaller breast fragment, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aPart four, labeled "#4, right lateral breast tissue", consists of three (3)\u000afragments of breast tissue, measuring 6 x 6 x 3 cm, 6 x 4 x 2 cm, and 4 x 3 x\u000a1.5 cm. The largest fragment of breast tissue has a portion of skin measuring\u000a3 x 1 cm attached. All specimens are received without orientation. The middle\u000aside fragment of breast tissue has an area of hemorrhage measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aon the exterior surface. The specimens are inked black. Serial sectioning\u000aofthe three masses reveal firm white-tan breast tissue without focal lesions or\u000aabnormalities. The middle specimen with superficial hemorrhage has no\u000ahemorrhage involving parenchyma.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  largest breast fragment, 4 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 25: middle size breast specimen, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 26: smaller fragment of breast tissue, 1 frag, RSS.\u000absc\u000aReports to: CARTER, KATHARINE M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY - PARTIAL OR SIMPLE\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST REDUCTION MAMMOPLASTY\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST REDUCTION MAMMOPLASTY\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST REDUCTION MAMMOPLASTY\u000a[report_end]
