VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aHIRSCH, MICHELLE, S., M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by HIRSCH,MICHELLE S.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, EXCISION, WIRE-LOCALIZATION FOR CALCIFICATIONS AND A CLIP:\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aSYNOPSIS:\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aTypes - solid, cribriform\u000aNuclear grade - intermediate\u000aCalcifications in DCIS - present\u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - present\u000aMicroinvasion (<0.1cm) - absent\u000aExtent of DCIS\u000aNumber of blocks:total - 4:10 blocks\u000aFinal Margins (DCIS)\u000aNegative (>0.3 cm) - anterior, lateral, superior, inferior\u000aPositive (ink on DCIS) - medial, deep\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - absent\u000aAJCC CLASSIFICATION (6th edition) - Tis pNx MX\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER/PR/HER-2) - pending\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for DCIS (block 3):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) NEGATIVE (0)\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000acarcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but\u000aonly a portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity\u000ain >10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 37 year old woman, S/P REMOVED_DATE  stereotactic core biopsy for evaluation\u000aof calcifications seen on REMOVED_DATE  right breast mammogram. The specimen\u000acontains benign tissue; however, no calcifications were in the specimen,\u000atherefore localization and surgical excision is recommended.\u000aOperation: Right breast wire localization excision.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal right mammogram.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Right breast tissue - short stitch/superior, long\u000astitch/lateral, with stitch deep margin (sent for\u000amammography).\u000aRadiology Report: Calcifications and clip in specimen. Lorans\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by FACTOR,RACHEL E.,M.D.\u000aThe specimen was received fresh, labeled with the patient's name and MR#,\u000a"right breast tissue - short stitch/superior, long stitch/lateral, with stitch\u000adeep margin", consisting of a fragment of fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x 3\u000ax 1 cm. Specimen was inked by the surgeon, such that red is superior, yellow\u000ais lateral, orange is medial, black is deep, blue is anterior, and green is\u000ainferior. There is a needle in the specimen. The mammogram shows a needle and\u000aclip in the specimen with microcalcifications, about REMOVED_DATE cm from the clip. On\u000asectioning, the specimen is primarily fibrous with no distinct lesion. The\u000aspecimen is entirely submitted.\u000aMicro #1: Breast tissue with clip, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro #2-10: Remaining breast tissue, multiple frags, ESS.\u000aref/\u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
