VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aLESTER, SUSAN, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST, EXCISIONAL BIOPSY:\u000aINVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA, poorly differentiated (modified\u000aBloom-Richardson grade III/III), is present as two separate foci\u000a(2 cm and REMOVED_DATE cm), located approximately 1 cm apart.\u000aNo definite lymphovascular invasion is seen.\u000aInvasive carcinoma is present at the lateral margin and within REMOVED_DATE cm of\u000athe inferior margin.\u000aEXTENSIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, cribriform, solid, and clinging types\u000a(high nuclear grade) is present in 9 of 11 blocks. Focal necrosis\u000ais present. Calcifications are not seen.\u000aDCIS is < REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior, lateral, medial, superior, and deep\u000amargins.\u000aThe skin is not involved.\u000aNote: This carcinoma would be classified as AJCC REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDc NX MX with multiple\u000afoci of invasion.\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies will be performed and reported in an addendum.\u000aLEFT BREAST, INFERIOR SHAVE MARGIN:\u000aINVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA, REMOVED_DATE cm, poorly differentiated, is present at\u000athe margin with cautery artifact on the invasive carcinoma (see note).\u000aEXTENSIVE DCIS is present in 4 of 4 blocks.\u000aDCIS is present at the green, yellow, and black inked margins.\u000aNote: The focus of invasive carcinoma may be a portion of the invasive\u000acarcinoma present in the first specimen.\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: by RICHARDSON,ANDREA,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for both foci of invasive carcinoma (blocks 3 and 4):\u000aEstrogen receptor - Positive\u000aProgesterone receptor - Negative\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) - Negative (1+)\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000ainvasive carcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but\u000aonly a portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity\u000ain >10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Mass left breast, FNA elsewhere showd "DCIS". Core biopsy here,\u000atissue insufficient for diagnosis.\u000aOperation: Excision of left breast mass.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Tissue, left breast, stitch - long lateral, short\u000asuperior. 2. Inferior shave margin, left breast.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by GREISMAN,HARVEY A.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aThe first part is labeled "#1, Tissue, left breast stitch, long = lateral,\u000ashort = superior", and consists of a single fragment of tan-pink fibrofatty\u000atissue (6.5 cm anterior to posterior, REMOVED_DATE cm medial to lateral, and REMOVED_DATE cm\u000ainferior to superior) and attached tan skin ellipse (3.7 x REMOVED_DATE cm), which is\u000amarked with a long suture designated as lateral and a short suture designated\u000asuperior by the surgeon. Two discrete masses are identified. The larger mass\u000a(2.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) is well-circumscribed and soft, with a tan, friable cut\u000asurface. This mass extends to the inferior margin and is REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000alateral margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior margin\u000a(skin). A representative section of this mass and unremarkable breast\u000aparenchyma are given to the tumor bank. A second, very firm, poorly\u000acircumscribed, white mass is also found and measures REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest\u000adimension. This tumor is medial and approximately 1 cm from the larger mass.\u000aThe mass is REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin,\u000a0.3 cm from the deep margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin. The specimen\u000ais inked in five colors as follows: inferior = green, lateral = yellow,\u000aposterior = black, superior = red, and medial = orange. The smaller mass is\u000asubmitted entirely and representative sections of the larger mass and\u000aadjacent breast tissue are also submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  smaller mass, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  larger mass, 3 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 7: unremarkable breast parenchyma, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 8: lateral margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 13: skin with green ink, one frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  medial and inferior margins, mult frags, RSS.\u000aPart two, labeled "#2, inferior shave margin, left breast", consists of a\u000asingle fragment of tan-pink fibrofatty tissue (4.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) marked with\u000aa short suture and a long suture (the orientation is not designated by the\u000asurgeon). The tissue is inked in three colors (yellow, green, and black). No\u000alesions are identified. Approximately two-thirds of the tissue is submitted\u000afor microscopic analysis.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  inferior shave margin, left breast, multi frags, RSS.\u000aReports to: CHRISTIAN, ROGER, L. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN\u000a[report_end]
