 with the\u000apatient?s name and unit number.\u000aPart A, labeled "MRI first core, white bottom, green top", consists of two\u000awhite cassettes each with a green lid and each of which contains multiple\u000acylindrical yellow/tan cores (3.7 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate).\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: White cassette/green lid contents, multi frags in each, ESS.\u000aPart B, labeled "right breast", consists of two white cassettes. The first\u000awhite cassette labeled "A Ca++" contains multiple yellow/tan soft tissues (1.3\u000ax REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate). Second white cassette labeled "B" contains\u000amultiple pink/tan soft tissues (2.4 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate).\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: White cassette A contents (Ca++), multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: White cassette B contents, multi frags, ESS.\u000alm/lp\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-08-REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a4/17/2008\u000a[report_end]
