 or approved by the\u000aU.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA). The FDA has determined that such\u000aclearance or approval is not necessary.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Left breast wire localization excisional biopsy (to mammo + FS) - short\u000asuture superior, long suture lateral.\u000aB/2. Left breast superior margin.\u000aC/3. Left breast medial margin.\u000aD/4. Left breast inferior margin.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Specimen X-ray shows clip and intact hookwire within the specimen.\u000aSpecimen ultrasound shows the mass within the specimen. - Dr. Gombos.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in four parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart A, labeled "Left breast wire localized excision biopsy short suture\u000asuperior long suture lateral", and consists of a REMOVED_DATE cm (superior to inferior)\u000ax REMOVED_DATE cm (medial to lateral) x REMOVED_DATE cm (anterior to posterior) breast biopsy\u000awith localization wire in place and a short suture marking the superior margin\u000aand long suture marking the lateral margin. An accompanying specimen\u000aradiograph demonstrates a mass in the central portion of the specimen,\u000aassociated with the localization wire. The specimen is inked per pathology\u000aprotocol (Red; anterior, black: posterior, medial: orange, lateral: yellow,\u000ainferior: green, superior: black.). The wire enters at the posterosuperior\u000aaspect of the specimen and exits inferiorly. The specimen is sectioned to\u000areveal a tan/white firm fibrous tissue area (1.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which abuts\u000athe posterior, lateral, and inferior margins and is REMOVED_DATE cm to the anterior\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm to the medial and superior margins. Within the firm fibrous\u000atissue is a tan/white firm nodule (1.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which is located REMOVED_DATE cm\u000ato inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to the lateral margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to the superior\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm to the medial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to the posterior margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm\u000ato the anterior margin. The entire specimen is submitted for histological\u000aexamination and the section with the clip is located within block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross sections of wire localized excision specimen,\u000amulti frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, labeled "Left breast superior margin", consists of a tan/white\u000aunoriented portion of fibrous tissue (1.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with approximately\u000a75% of the surface cauterized and this surface is inked blue. The opposite\u000anon-cauterized surface is inked black. The specimen is sectioned to reveal no\u000agross lesions. The specimen is entirely submitted for histological\u000aexamination.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Left breast superior margin, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aPart C, labeled "Left breast medial margin", consists of one fragment of\u000atan/white unoriented fibrous tissue (1.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with a cauterized\u000asurface that is inked blue and the opposite surface, which is non-cauterized\u000aand inked black. The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal no gross lesions\u000aand is entirely submitted for histological examination.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Left breast medial margin, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aPart D, labeled "Left breast inferior margin", consists of one fragment of\u000atan/white unoriented fibrous tissue (1.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with one cauterized\u000asurface that is inked blue and the non-cauterized surface on the opposite side\u000ainked black. The specimen is sectioned to reveal no gross lesions and is\u000aentirely submitted for histological examination.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Left breast inferior margin, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aADA/mgd/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jacqueline M William M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed\u000aon Monday REMOVED_MONTH 20, 2009 at 00:47:42AM\u000a[report_end]
