of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but\u000aonly a portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity\u000ain >10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Hx DCIS right breast - see BWH core bx (4/28/03) positive DCIS and\u000apositive LCIS.\u000aOperation: Right mastectomy with removal level I lymphndoes.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast cancer.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Right breast and level I lymph nodes, short = superior,\u000along = lateral.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by REIMANN,JULIE DYLAN REGAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "right breast, short superior, long lateral, plus level I lymph nodes",\u000aand consists of a 973-gram mastectomy specimen (25 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with\u000aattached skin ellipse (23 x REMOVED_DATE cm) with areola (5.5 x REMOVED_DATE cm) and nipple\u000a(0.9 x REMOVED_DATE cm). There is a brown, pigmented area adjacent to the nipple on\u000athe skin ellipse (0.8 x REMOVED_DATE cm) that has the gross appearance of a seborrheic\u000akeratosis; there is no scar on the skin ellipse. The breast tissue is\u000acomposed of approximately 15% fibrous tissue, the rest is adipose tissue.\u000aThere are no grossly identifiable lesions. Radiographs taken by the\u000apathologist in the grossing room indicate two clips in the mastectomy\u000aspecimen, one located in the lower inner quadrant and the other located in the\u000alower outer quadrant. Sixteen (16) candidate lymph nodes are identified in\u000athe specimen, ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest dimension.\u000aMicro 1: fibrous tissue, slice 2 (most likely to be [inaudible] located in\u000athe inner lower quadrant), 3 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 2: fibrous tissue adjacent to the area in slicd 2 contained with clip,\u000a2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 3: fibrous tissue adjacent to the clip in slice 2, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 4: fibrous tissue adjacent to area of clip in slice 2, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 5: fibrous tissue adjacent to clip area and slice 2, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 6: fibrous tissue from upper inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  fibrous tissue in outer lower quadrant (in area containing the\u000asecond clip), REMOVED_DATE frags each, RSS.\u000aMicro 16: fibrous tissue from upper outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  fibrous tissue with nipple and tissue deep to the nipple, 1 frag\u000aeach, RSS.\u000aMicro 20: 4 candidate lymph nodes, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 21: 4 candidate lymph nodes, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 22: 4 candidate lymph nodes, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 23: 4 candidate lymph nodes, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 24: skin with brown pigmented lesion, 1 frag, ESS.\u000ajdr\u000aReports to: CARTER, KATHARINE M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY W/REGIONAL LYMPH NODES\u000a[report_end]
