the specimen.\u000aThe specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins:\u000aposterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow;\u000amedial/orange. Sectioning in the area of interest demonstrates REMOVED_DATE cm core\u000abiopsy site. The surrounding tissue shows focal hemorrhage, but is otherwise\u000awithout significant gross abnormality. Specimen is comprised of 50% to 60%\u000adense tan white fibrous tissue admixed with otherwise unremarkable tan yellow\u000aadipose tissue.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Area of interest and surrounding fibrosis dense tissue,\u000asequentially from medial to lateral (tissue with clip in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Representative fibrous tissue medial to area of interest, 2 frags,\u000aRSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Representative fibrous tissue lateral to area of interest, 3\u000afrags, ESS.\u000aDb/ag\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jeffrey F Krane M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a7/7/2006\u000a[report_end]
