s & history:\u000aLeft breast carcinoma\u000aTissue-Designation:\u000aA.Breast, excision with margins - left\u000aGross description:\u000aThe specimen is received in saline in one container, labeled "left breast mass"\u000aand consists of a 69 gram, piece of breast tissue measuring 8 x 5 x 4 cm. A\u000aportion of skin with a dimpled area in the center is present. In the\u000asuperficial surface, the skin is 3 x 2 cm. Two sutures are present. A bow-tie\u000asuture is cephalad, and a long suture is lateral. The superficial cephalad\u000aarea is inked with yellow ink, and the deep portion is inked with blue ink.\u000aSections are taken lateral to medial. The sections reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm. tumor beneath the skin invading into the inverted nipple. The remaining\u000abreast tissue is soft adipose tissue and the tumor is not near any of the deep\u000amargins. The entire tumor is embedded. 9X.\u000aDictated by: RJS____(signature on file)____DANIEL D. KOELLIKER, M.D. REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a____(signature on file)____RICHARD SAMPSON, M.D. REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a[report_end]
