 of the breast tissue cores are received in an\u000aorange cassette marked "A. Ca+2", and the remainder of the breast tissue cores\u000aare received in an orange cassette marked "B". The breast tissue cores are\u000asubmitted in toto.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Cassette "A. Ca+2", 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Remainder of soft tissue cores cassette "B", multi frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, labeled "Left breast yellow A. Ca+2/B 2:30 p.m.". consists of multiple\u000atan/white to tan/yellow lobulated fibroadipose breast tissue cores (2.5 x REMOVED_DATE x\u000a0.2 cm in aggregate). A portion of the breast tissue core is received in a\u000ayellow cassette marked "A. Ca+2", and the remainder of the breast tissue cores\u000aare received in a yellow cassette marked "B". The specimen is submitted in\u000atoto.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Cassette "A. Ca+2", 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Cassette "B", multi frags, ESS.\u000aSEK/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on Friday\u000aREMOVED_MONTH 16, 2009 at 02:36:58PM\u000a[report_end]
