VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Amend/Addenda\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ROGER L CHRISTIAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000a********** Addended Report ***********\u000aResident: Tanya Rege, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Jane E. Brock, M.B., B.S., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. LEFT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A CLIP AND CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, solid, cribriform, and micropapillary types,\u000aintermediate nuclear grade, with focal necrosis, focal calcifications, and\u000afocal mucin production, see Note.\u000aDCIS is present in six of twenty blocks (6:20) - largest focus on a slide\u000ameasures REMOVED_DATE cm (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aDCIS is multifocally present REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID,\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID). Medial, anterior, posterior, superior, and inferior margins are negative\u000afor DCIS (>0.3 cm).\u000aOther findings:\u000aCore biopsy site changes.\u000aATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA\u000aNumerous calcifications associated with benign epithelium.\u000aFibroadenomatoid change.\u000aNOTE: Immunohistochemical analysis for estrogen receptor, progesterone\u000areceptor, and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu will be performed and reported in an addendum.\u000aB. RIGHT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A CLIP AND CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aCore biopsy site.\u000aCalcifications associated with normal breast epithelium, and a fibroadenoma\u000a(0.5 cm).\u000aColumnar cell change with focal flat epithelial atypia (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aIntraductal papilloma (<0.1 cm; REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aThe margins were inked and evaluated for the final diagnosis.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: ADH LT breast, flat atypia, RT breast.\u000aOperation: Loc/excis.\u000aOperative Findings: See op note.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Not provided.\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000a1. Tissue, LT breast, hookwire, clip + few faint Ca++ in specimen. Called to\u000aOR 2:20 pm.\u000a2. Tissue, RT breast, report called to OR at 3:10 pm, but patient had left the\u000aOR.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Left breast tissue, long suture lateral, short suture superior to mammo\u000aB/2. Right breast tissue, long suture lateral, short suture superior to mammo\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two parts, labeled with the patient's name\u000aand medical record number.\u000aPart A, "#1. Left breast tissue, long suture lateral, short suture superior",\u000aand consists of one REMOVED_DATE gram breast excision (6.2 cm medial to lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000asuperior to inferior, and REMOVED_DATE cm anterior to posterior), oriented with a long\u000astitch designated lateral and a short stitch designated superior per the\u000asurgeon. A localization wire is present that enters the anterior aspect of the\u000aspecimen and exits the medial aspect. The specimen is inked per pathology\u000aprotocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue;\u000asuperior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. An accompanying\u000aradiograph demonstrates a localization wire, a clip and calcifications. Prior\u000abiopsy site with a clip is present (1.3 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), present REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000athe medial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin, and\u000a1.6 cm from the inferior margin. No additional lesions are identified. The\u000aremainder of the breast parenchyma is approximately 20% white/tan fibrous\u000atissue (located mainly at the medial aspect) and 80% yellow/tan fatty tissue.\u000aThe entire specimen is submitted for histologic examination.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Breast excision, medial to lateral, REMOVED_DATE frags each, ESS. The\u000abiopsy site is present in cassettes REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and the clip was present in the\u000atissue represented in cassette REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aPart B, "#2. Right breast tissue, long suture superior, short suture lateral".\u000aPlease note that the designation of the sutures on the specimen container\u000adiffers from the designation of the sutures on the form 86. The specimen\u000aconsists of a REMOVED_DATE gram breast excision (7.0 cm medial to lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000asuperior to inferior, and REMOVED_DATE cm anterior to posterior), oriented with a short\u000astitch designated superior and a long stitch designated lateral. The specimen\u000ais received previously inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of\u000amargins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green;\u000alateral/yellow; medial/orange, per the surgeon. The inks protocol matches the\u000alabeling of the sutures on the form 86. An accompanying radiograph\u000ademonstrates a clip hookwire, and calcifications. The hookwire is received\u000aseparately from the breast excision. A biopsy site (1.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) is\u000apresent REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial aspect, REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral aspect, abutting\u000athe superior aspect, REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior aspect, REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior\u000aaspect, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior aspect. The remainder of the breast\u000aparenchyma is approximately 30% white/tan and fibrotic (located mainly at the\u000alateral aspect), and 70% yellow/tan fatty tissue. No additional lesions are\u000aidentified.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Breast excision, REMOVED_DATE frags each, medial to lateral, ESS. The\u000abiopsy site with clip is present in cassettes REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aTR/ajb\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jane E. Brock M.B., B.S., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000aMonday REMOVED_MONTH 06, 2009 at 02:57:39PM\u000aADDENDUM:\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for DCIS (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) NEGATIVE (1+)\u000aImmunohistochemical studies for estrogen receptor, progesterone\u000areceptor, and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu were evaluated by manual morphometric analysis\u000ausing the following criteria:\u000aHormone receptor analysis:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low > 0% - < 10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not\u000ayet been determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10%\u000aof tumor cells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor\u000acells but only a portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aEquivocal (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity in >30% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aExternal controls are evaluated and show appropriate Immunoreactivity.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for\u000ainvestigational use only.\u000aAddendum #1 by Jane E. Brock M.B., B.S., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000aTuesday REMOVED_MONTH 07, 2009 at 12:22:01PM\u000a[report_end]
