th only scant associated\u000afibrous tissue and no definitive palpable or visible residual mass grossly.\u000aThe majority of the specimen is comprised of soft, lobulated tan/yellow adipose\u000atissue (at least 95%). Entire specimen is sequentially submitted from anterior\u000ato posterior, with majority of cavity and surrounding tissue in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aPerpendicular anterior end of the specimen in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, perpendicular posterior end\u000aof the specimen in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Multi frags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000adb/ag\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jane E. Brock M.B., B.S., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000aThursday REMOVED_MONTH 30, 2009 at 03:26:06PM\u000a[report_end]
