VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: BRENT T SHOJI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-06-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Elizabeth A. Steensma, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Jeffrey F Krane, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISIONAL BIOPSY FOR A MASS MARKED BY A CLIP:\u000aResidual intraductal papilloma with atypia (blocks REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID; levels\u000aexamined), apocrine metaplasia and associated microcalcifications, associated\u000awith the prior biopsy site.\u000aThe entire lesion/biopsy site has been examined histologically.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000aPortions of this case have been reviewed by Dr. S. Lester (Breast Pathology),\u000awho concurs with the diagnosis.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Abnormal core BX-papilloma with atypia for excision of entire area.\u000aOperation: R middle lobe BRBX.\u000aOperative Findings: Not given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal R mammogram.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Right breast wire-localized biopsy short superior long lateral.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Mass, clip + hook-wire are in the specimen. - Dr. Durfee.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in one part, labeled with the patient's name,\u000aunit number, and "Right breast wire-localized biopsy", and consists of an\u000airregular tan lobulated portion of fibroadipose breast tissue (6.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm). The specimen radiogram shows a central mass marked by a clip and the\u000alocalization wire. There is a needle localization wire in place, which enters\u000athrough the superior-anterior aspect of the specimen. There is a short suture\u000adesignating the superior margin and a long suture designating the lateral\u000amargin. The specimen has been previously inked per pathology protocol\u000a(superior - red, inferior - green, lateral - yellow, medial - orange, anterior\u000a- blue, and posterior - black). The specimen's sections reveal a well-defined\u000afirm red/brown to tan/white nodule (1.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which is located REMOVED_DATE \u000acm from the anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000aposterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior\u000amargin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin. The remainder of the breast\u000aparenchyma is tan/yellow and homogenous with focal areas of dense white fibrous\u000atissue constituting approximately 5% of the specimen. Representative sections\u000aare submitted for histologic examination.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Superior-anterior margin, 4 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lesion blocks REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID corresponded to area to clip.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Subjacent breast parenchyma, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Additional focal areas of dense white fibrous tissue.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Inferior margin, 4 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Remaining fibrous tissue, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aSEK/mmm\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jeffrey F Krane M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a10/3/2006\u000a[report_end]
