VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: JAMES D IGLEHART M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-06-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Oname O. Burlingame, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Xiaohua Qian, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. LEFT BREAST, UPPER OUTER QUADRANT, WIRE LOCALIZATION FOR MASSES AND A CLIP:\u000aExtensive hyalinizing fibrosis (3.1 cm).\u000aFibroadenoma (0.7 cm) with associated biopsy site changes.\u000aCalcifications associated with benign epithelium.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000aB. LEFT BREAST, LOWER OUTER QUADRANT, WIRE LOCALIZATION FOR A MASS:\u000aBenign breast tissue with columnar cell hyperplasia, sclerosing adenosis,\u000ausual epithelial hyperplasia, and apocrine cysts.\u000aCalcifications associated with benign epithelium.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 2 susp abnormalities on mammogram, LOQ looks benign, probably cyst,\u000aUOQ suspicious.\u000aOperation: Not given.\u000aOperative Findings: Not given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Not given.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Upper outer quadrant L breast needle loc, long lateral, short superior to\u000amammo.\u000aB/2. Lower outer quadrant L breast needle loc, long lateral, short superior.\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000aA - OR called. Both masses and clip in specimen (clip with known\u000afibroadenoma. Hypoechoic area adjacent). - LBT.\u000aB - Lower/outer breast 8 mm (mass - ? cyst) in specimen. OR called.\u000aLBT.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart A, "#1. Upper outer quadrant L breast needle look, long lateral, short\u000asuture", consists of an irregular fragment of yellow/tan to pink/tan\u000afibroadipose tissue (6.3 M-L X REMOVED_DATE S-I X REMOVED_DATE A-P cm) which is oriented by the\u000asurgeon with two sutures as indicated. The specimen is inked per pathology\u000aprotocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue;\u000asuperior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. There is one\u000aneedle localization wire with the tip loosely embedded in the inferolateral\u000aaspect of the specimen. The specimen was previously radiographed. The mass is\u000aserially sectioned from medial to lateral into a total of eight slices (slice 1\u000aequals medial, slice 8 equals lateral). In slices 1 through 5, there is a\u000awell-circumscribed bulging homogenous white/tan solid mass (3.1 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm). The mass is less than REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin, abuts the posterior\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE \u000acm from the anterior margin and REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin.\u000a0.2 cm lateral to the mass is a small homogenous solid circumscribed white\u000anodule (0.7 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) in which is embedded a small metal clip. The\u000anodular lesion is REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE \u000acm from the medial margin and REMOVED_DATE cm from lateral margin.\u000aThe remainder of the specimen is composed of greater than 95% yellow/tan\u000alobulated adipose tissue with less than 5% delicate white/pink fibrous stroma.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 1, large mass with closest medial margin, 1 frag in\u000aeach, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 2 and 3, large mass with closest anterior, posterior\u000aand superior margins, 1 frag in each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 2 and 3, mass with closest inferior margin and\u000aadditional posterior margin, 1 frag in each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 4, large mass with additional anterior, posterior and\u000asuperior margins and intervening tissue between mass and small nodular lesion,\u000a1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 5, small nodular lesion (site of clip) with clips\u000aanterior, posterior and inferior margins, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 5, closest superior margin and additional anterior and\u000aposterior margins, 2 small nodular lesions, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slices 7 and 8, lateral margin, closest to both large mass\u000aand small nodular lesion, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aPlease note, approximately 80% of the specimen is submitted.\u000aPart B, "#2", consists of an ovoid fragment of yellow/tan to pink/tan\u000afibroadipose tissue (5.1 M-L X REMOVED_DATE S-I X REMOVED_DATE A-P cm) which is oriented per\u000asurgeon with two sutures: the short suture equals superior, the long suture\u000aequals lateral. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the\u000aevaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red;\u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. There is one needle\u000alocalization wire in place which enters and exits the inferolateral aspect of\u000athe specimen. The specimen is previously radiographed. The specimen is\u000aserially sectioned from medial to lateral into a total of eight slices (slice 1\u000aequals medial, slice 8 equals lateral. In slice 7 (corresponding to the\u000acircled area of interest on the radiograph), there is a bulging red/brown\u000acystic lesion (0.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) which is REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin,\u000a0.2 cm from the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000athe lateral margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin and REMOVED_DATE cm from the media\u000amargin.\u000aThe remainder of the specimen is composed of approximately 80% yellow/tan\u000alobulated adipose tissue and 20% focally gritty pink/tan fibrous stroma with no\u000aadditional discrete lesions identified.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 7, entire cystic mass (disrupted during sectioning,\u000awith closest superior, anterior and posterior margins), 1\u000afrag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Remainder of slice 7, closest inferior and lateral margins\u000ato cystic mass, an additional posterior margin, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 6 bisected (tissue medial to cystic mass) to include\u000aadditional superior, inferior, anterior and posterior margins, 1 frag in each,\u000aESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: lice 8 bisected (tissue lateral to cystic mass) to include\u000aadditional inferior, superior, posterior and lateral\u000amargins, 1 frag in each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slices 2 and 3, medial margin closest to cystic mass,\u000a2 frags, RSS.\u000aPlease note, approximately 80% of the specimen is submitted.\u000aLBM/mmm\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Xiaohua Qian M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a7/30/2006\u000a[report_end]
