VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Consult material\u000aProcedure Date:\u000aOrdering Provider: TAO YANG M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Mariana A. Stoleru, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Susan Lester, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aCONSULT SLIDES FROM HARVARD VANGUARD MEDICAL CENTER, BOSTON, MA:\u000aLEFT BREAST, 1:00, ULTRASOUND GUIDED CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR A 2 CM IRREGULAR\u000aMASS (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID; REMOVED_DATE );\u000aSPINDLE CELL INVASIVE CARCINOMA, moderately differentiated, at least\u000a0.8 cm in this limited specimen (see note).\u000aNo lymphovascular invasion is seen in this limited specimen.\u000aNo carcinoma in situ is seen in this limited specimen.\u000aSpecial studies were performed at an outside institution with the\u000afollowing results for invasive carcinoma (reviewed):\u000aPankeratin POSITIVE - moderate\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID NEGATIVE\u000aBeta-catenin POSITIVE - cytoplasmic\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed at BWH with the following\u000aresults for invasive carcinoma:\u000aEstrogen receptor NEGATIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor NEGATIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu NEGATIVE (0)\u000aCytokeratin 14 POSITIVE - diffuse\u000aCytokeratin REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID POSITIVE - focal\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID NEGATIVE\u000aE-cadherin NEGATIVE\u000aNormal epithelial cells are appropriately immunoreactive for estrogen\u000aand progesterone receptors.\u000aNote: The carcinoma is only mildly cellular and infiltrates around\u000anormal lobules and into fat in a densely fibrotic background. There is mild\u000acytologic atypia and no mitoses are seen.\u000aThere is no keratin formation and p63 is negative, making a squamous cell\u000acarcinoma unlikely. There are no epithelial areas in this limited biopsy.\u000aThis type of spindle cell carcinoma may be classified as a "metaplastic\u000acarcinoma".\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 2 cm irregular hypoechoic mass at 1:00 left breast - strongly\u000asuspicious for invasive carcinoma.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: ?Fat necrosis vs. metaplastic ca?\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aConsult slides.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aReceived from Harvard Vanguard Medical Center, Pathology Department, 133\u000aBrookline Avenue, Boston, MA REMOVED_CASE_ID, are eighteen (18) glass slides (10 slides\u000aare unstained).\u000aThe slides are labeled "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" and sublabeled "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID", "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID', "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID",\u000a"REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID unstained"(REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID PANKERTIN", "PANKERATIN CONTROL", "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BETA-CATEN",\u000a"BETA-CATEN CONTROL", "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" and "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID PANKERATIN", corresponding to a left\u000abreast 1 o'clock ultrasound guided core needle biopsy (0.7 x REMOVED_DATE cm) performed\u000aon REMOVED_DATE  according to the accompanying pathology report bearing the\u000apatient's name.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000aTuesday REMOVED_MONTH 23, 2009 at 11:45:17AM\u000a[report_end]
