VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, mastectomy with regional lymph nodes\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: BRENT T SHOJI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Elgida Radoncipi, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Alessandra F Nascimento, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. LEFT BREAST AND AXILLARY TISSUE, MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY:\u000aSPINDLE CELL CARCINOMA (2.5 cm in greatest dimension).\u000aNo lymphovascular invasion identified.\u000aDeep margin negative for tumor.\u000aNo in situ component identified.\u000aTen (10) lymph nodes, negative for tumor.\u000aImmunohistochemistry performed at BWH demonstrates the following\u000astaining profile in lesional cells:\u000aPositive - pan-keratin, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.2\u000aThe immunohistochemical profile supports the above diagnosis.\u000aB. RIGHT BREAST TISSUE, EXCISION:\u000aBenign breast tissue with sclerosing adenosis, calcifications in benign\u000aepithelium, and columnar cell change.\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy.\u000aImmunostains (E-cadherin, double stain REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/3/REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) were examined for\u000afinal diagnosis.\u000aC. RIGHT BREAST TISSUE, EXCISION:\u000aSkin and fibroadipose tissue with no significant pathologic change.\u000aThe immunoperoxidase, immunofluorescence and in-situ hybridization tests\u000aperformed at Brigham and Women's Hospital were developed and their performance\u000acharacteristics determined by the Immunohistochemistry Laboratories in the\u000aDepartment of Pathology at BWH. They have not been cleared or approved by the\u000aU.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA). The FDA has determined that such\u000aclearance or approval is not necessary.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: L breast 10 o'clock spindle cell invasive carcinoma, at least REMOVED_DATE cm,\u000aalready [illegible], ER-negative, PR-negative, HER/2-negative\u000aOperation: L MRM and R [illegible] mammo\u000aClinical Diagnosis: L breast ca\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Left breast and axilla contents (stitch/axilla)\u000aB/2. Right breast tissue\u000aC/3. Rt breast tissue\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in three parts, labeled with the patient's name,\u000aMR number, and case number.\u000aPart A, "left breast plus axillary contents with stitch in the axilla",\u000aconsists of a REMOVED_DATE kilogram left modified radical mastectomy specimen (32.5 x\u000a32.0 x REMOVED_DATE cm) with a white/tan skin ellipse (22.5 x REMOVED_DATE cm) and an attached\u000aaxillary tail (11.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The nipple is inverted and measures REMOVED_DATE x\u000a1.0 cm. On cross sectioning of the specimen from medial to lateral, there is a\u000awhite/tan indurated/firm nodular area (2.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which is located in\u000athe upper outer quadrant of the left breast (corresponding to approximately 1\u000ao'clock). The remainder of the breast parenchyma consists mostly of\u000afibroadipose tissue, 85% fibroadipose tissue and 15% breast tissue. The upper\u000aouter quadrant mass is entirely submitted for microscopic examination. The\u000amass is grossly REMOVED_DATE cm from the deep margin, which is inked black. There are\u000aeight-ten lymph nodes in the axillary tail, the largest measuring REMOVED_DATE cm in\u000agreatest dimension. Lymph nodes submitted in the same cassette are\u000adifferentially inked.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Mass, 1 frag in each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Posterior margin (deep margin/inked black), 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lower inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Upper inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lower outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Upper outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Nipple, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 candidate lymph node, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 candidate lymph node bisected, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 5 candidate lymph nodes, 5 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 candidate lymph node (located in the deep margin), 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 2 candidate lymph nodes, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, labeled "#2. Right breast tissue", consists of a 775 gram right breast\u000areduction specimen, which consists of white/tan skin with underlying\u000afibroadipose tissue/breast tissue (44.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in depth). In the same\u000acontainer as the main specimen, there is a detached disrupted fragment of skin\u000ameasuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The right breast reduction specimen is unoriented and\u000aconsists of 85% fat and 15% breast tissue. Representative sections of dense\u000afibrous tissue from the specimen are submitted for microscopic examination and\u000aa fragment of the detached skin is also submitted for microscopic examination.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Representative sections of dense fibrous tissue, serially\u000asubmitted from one end to the other end, 1 frag in each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Representative sections of attached skin, 3 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Skin from detached fragment, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Representative section of dense fibrous tissue, serially\u000asubmitted from one end to the other, REMOVED_DATE frag in each, RSS.\u000aPart C is labeled "#3. Right breast tissue (continued)", and consists of one\u000afragment of skin (3.0 x REMOVED_DATE cm) with underlying yellow/tan fibroadipose tissue\u000aexcised to a thickness of REMOVED_DATE cm. There is a central linear defect on the skin\u000ameasuring REMOVED_DATE cm, no masses are grossly identified. Representative sections of\u000athe skin with underlying fibroadipose tissue are submitted for microscopic\u000aexamination.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Skin with underlying fibroadipose tissue, on edge, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Representative sections of skin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aerv\u005cpab\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Alessandra F Nascimento M.D., Electronically signed on\u000aTuesday REMOVED_MONTH 15, 2009 at 02:43:33PM\u000a[report_end]
