VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aGLICKMAN, JONATHAN, NEIL, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by GLICKMAN,JONATHAN NEIL,M.D.,PH.D.\u000a1. SPECIMEN LABELED "LEFT BREAST TISSUE", WIRE LOCALIZATION, EXCISION FOR A\u000aMASS:\u000aBenign breast tissue with epithelial hyperplasia, apocrine metaplasia,\u000aand cysts (see NOTE).\u000aBiopsy site changes.\u000aCalcifications in benign epithelium.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000a2. SPECIMEN LABELED "SUPERIOR LATERAL CORNER", WIRE LOCALIZATION, EXCSION FOR A\u000aMASS AND A CLIP:\u000aBreast tissue with extensive adenosis, cystic space (at site of clip)\u000asurrounded by chronic inflammation and numerous macrophages, consistent\u000awith prior rupture or effects of prior biopsy.\u000aCalcifications in benign epithelium.\u000aFragments of fibroadenoma.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000aNOTE: Diagnostic features of atypical ductal hyperplasia are not present.\u000aSlides reviewed by Drs. D. Dillon and S. Lester, breast pathology service, who\u000aconcur.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 54 year old female, S/P REMOVED_DATE  left breast ultrasound core biopsy of\u000athe mass demonstrating epithelial hyperplasia with atypia, in addition to a\u000afibroadenoma -- excision is recommended. Additional complex cyst unable to be\u000aaspirated, to be excised.\u000aOperation: Double wire localization, excision left breast.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Two (2) L breast masses.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000a#1 - L breast tissue, short/superior, long/lateral, whip stitch on deep margin\u000a-- mammo.\u000a#2 - L superior lateral corner with stitch new corner -- mammo.\u000a(site of previous core biopsy)\u000aRadiograph report: Specimen #1 - mass in specimen.\u000a[Dr. EP Frost] Specimen #2 - mass and clip in specimen.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by SHOLL,LYNETTE MARIE,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart one, labeled "#1 - left breast tissue, short/superior, long/lateral, with\u000awhip stitch on deep margin", consists of one fragment of fibrofatty tissue (5.2\u000ax REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with localizing wire in place. The specimen is received\u000aoriented and inked by the surgeon according to the pathology pathology protocol\u000afor the evaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red;\u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. Also received is a specimen\u000aradiograph showing a mass and wire within the specimen. The specimen is\u000aserially sectioned to reveal a dense fibrous nodule (2.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm)\u000acontaining a 1 cm long core biopsy tract that is located at the superior, deep,\u000amedial margins, REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior\u000amargin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin. The remainder of the specimen at\u000athe inferior and lateral margins consist of unremarkable adipose tissue. The\u000aentire specimen is submitted.\u000aMicro #1+2: fibrous nodule to medial and inferior margins, 2 frags in\u000acassette #1 and 1 frag in cassette #2, ESS.\u000aMicro #3+4: fibrous tissue and biopsy site to medial, superior, and inferior\u000amargins, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro #5+6: fibrous tissue and core biopsy site to posterior, superior, and\u000ainferior margins, bisected, 1 frag each cassette, ESS.\u000aMicro #7-10: fibrous tissue to superior, posterior, anterior, and inferior\u000amargins, 2 sections bisected, 1 frag each in cassettes #7+8, and\u000acassettes #9+10, ESS.\u000aMicro #11-14: breast tissue with superior, posterior, lateral and inferior\u000amargins, 2 sections bisected, 1 frag each cassette, ESS.\u000aMicro #15+16: breast tissue with inferior, superior, lateral and posterior\u000amargins, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro #17+18: breast tissue with lateral and superior margins, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro #19: breast tissue at lateral margin, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aPart two, labeled "#2 - superior lateral corner with stitch new corner",\u000aconsists of a fragment of fibroadipose tissue (3.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with wire\u000alocalizing needle in place. There is a stitch present at one aspect of the\u000aspecimen which is designated the new corner. This area is inked in black. The\u000aremainder of the specimen is inked in blue. There is an accompanying\u000aradiograph which displays the localizing wire and a clip in the specimen. The\u000aspecimen is serially sectioned to reveal a cavity filled with white granular\u000amaterial (0.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) at the site of the clip. This lesion is located\u000aapproximately REMOVED_DATE cm from the new corner. The remainder of the breast tissue\u000ais grossly unremarkable. The entire specimen is submitted.\u000aMicro #20+21: superior, lateral aspects of the specimen at the new corner, 2\u000afrags each cassette, ESS.\u000aMicro #22-24: cystic lesion at site of clip, 1 frag in cassette #22, 2 frags\u000aeach in cassette, #23+24, ESS.\u000aMicro #25+26: breast tissue, 3 frags, ESS.\u000alys/\u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN\u000a[report_end]
