VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST MASTECTOMY - PARTIAL OR SIMPLE\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aBRODSKY, GILBERT, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by BRODSKY,GILBERT,M.D.\u000a1) SPECIMEN LABELED "RIGHT BREAST, TISSUE":\u000aBenign breast tissue with complex sclerosing lesion, ductal hyperplasia,\u000aapocrine metaplasia, columnar change, fibroadenoma (0.4 cm), and\u000aintraductal papillomas.\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy or atypia.\u000a2) SPECIMEN LABELED "LEFT BREAST, TISSUE":\u000aBenign breast tissue with complex sclerosing lesion, ductal hyperplasia,\u000acalcification, intraductal papillomas, and cysts with apocrine\u000ametaplasia.\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy or atypia.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 37-yer-old female with strong family history of breast and ovarian\u000acancer. Status post core bx, LUIQ calcifications REMOVED_DATE  benign.\u000aOperation: Bilateral simple skin sparing, prophylactic mastectomies and\u000ainsertion tissue expander.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Right breast tissue, short/superior, long/lateral.\u000a2. Left breast, short/superior, long/lateral.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by YOU,MINGJIAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart one, labeled "#1, right breast tissue", consists of a 250 gram simple\u000amastectomy specimen (16.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with a white-tan skin ellipse (3.7 x\u000a3.5 cm). The nipple (1.0 cm in diameter), areola (0.1 x REMOVED_DATE cm), and the\u000aremaining skin ellipse are grossly unremarkable. The surgeon placed short and\u000along sutures to indicate the superior and lateral aspects of the specimen,\u000arespectively. There is red-tan skeletal muscle (3.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) that is\u000aattached to the upper outer quadrant of breast tissue and is inked in blue\u000aexteriorly. The deep margin is a smooth fascial plane and is inked in blue.\u000aThe specimen is sectioned, revealing approximately 60% of yellow-tan adipose\u000atissue and approximately 40% of white-tan fibrous tissue. No lesions\u000asuspicious for tumor are grossly identified. Representative breast tissue was\u000asubmitted to a tumor bank (Dr. A. Richardson's lab). The patient consented, and\u000athe tumor bank will hold onto the tissue until the case is signed out. The\u000askeletal muscle surface is also inked in black.\u000aMicro 1: Upper outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 2: Upper inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 3: Lower outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 4: Lower inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 5: nipple and adjacent skin, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 6: skeletal muscle, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  fibrous tissue, 6 frags, RSS\u000aPart two, labeled "#2, left breast", consists of a 230 gram simple mastectomy\u000aspecimen (13 x 12 x REMOVED_DATE cm) with a white-tan skin ellipse (3.5 x REMOVED_DATE cm). The\u000askin ellipse and nipple, including areola (1.5 cm in\u000adiameter), are grossly unremarkable. The surgeon placed a short sutures to\u000aindicate the superior and lateral margins, respectively. The deep margin is a\u000asmooth fascial plane without skeletal muscle present. The deep margin is inked\u000ain blue. The specimen is sectioned, revealing approximately 60% of white-tan\u000afibrous tissue and approximately 40% of yellow-tan adipose tissue. No biopsy\u000asite is identified in the specimen. No lesions suspicious for tumor are\u000aidentified. The specimen is thinly sliced and radiogaphed in the department\u000aof pathology. The radiograph demonstrated a clip, which was likely the one\u000aplaced by the radiology department for the patient's prior needle core biopsy.\u000aThe clip is REMOVED_DATE cm from the deep margin and is located in the upper inner\u000aquadrant.\u000aMicro 11: clipped breast tissue, 1 frag, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  breast tissue surrounding the clip area, 4 frags, ESS\u000aMicro 15: upper outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 16: upper inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 17: lower outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 18: lower inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 19: nipple, 1 frag, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  fibrous tissue, 4 frags, RSS\u000amjy\u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY - PARTIAL OR SIMPLE\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY - PARTIAL OR SIMPLE\u000a[report_end]
