VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: Esther Rhei M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-05-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Jacqueline M William, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: William R Welch, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZATION BIOPSY:\u000aFibroadipose tissue and scant breast parenchyma with chronic\u000ainflammation, fibrosis, foreign body giant cell reaction, and\u000ahemosiderin-laden macrophages(status post core biopsy).\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 50 y/o female S/P REMOVED_DATE  right breast ultrasound-guided core biopsy\u000aof an asymmetric mammographic density with a 9-mm, solid mass on U/S.\u000aPathology revealed fibroadipose tissue, excision recommended.\u000aOperation: Right breast wire-localization biopsy.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal Right mammogram.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/(1) Right breast tissue short suture superior, long suture lateral, whip\u000astitch deep margin --> to mammo.\u000aRADIOLOGY REPORT: Mass + clip in specimen DM (R.B.)\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient?s name, unit number,\u000aand "1. Right breast tissue, short suture - superior, long suture - lateral,\u000awhip stitch - deep margin", and consists of an excision of fibroadipose tissue,\u000ameasuring REMOVED_DATE cm from anterior to posterior, REMOVED_DATE cm from superior to inferior,\u000a1.8 cm from medial to lateral. The specimen was previously oriented and inked\u000aby the surgeon per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins:\u000aposterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow;\u000amedial/orange. There is a short suture designating superior, a long suture\u000adesignating lateral and a whip stitch designating deep. The specimen arrived\u000awith a lodged wire and an accompanying radiograph demonstrating an area of\u000aincreased density and the wire lodged within the specimen. The wire enters on\u000athe superior/anterior aspect and exits on the superior medial aspect. The\u000aspecimen was sectioned from anterior to posterior and is composed of\u000aapproximately 80% adipose tissue, 20% fibrous tissue. There is a tan/grey,\u000aslightly cystic region measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The lesion abuts the\u000asuperior and medial margins and is located REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin, REMOVED_DATE \u000acm from the anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin and approximately\u000a1.2 cm from the posterior margin. The entire specimen was submitted\u000asequentially from anterior to posterior.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Breast with main lesion in cassettes REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 9 frags, ESS.\u000ajaw/MMM\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Jacqueline M William M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by William R Welch M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
