VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aWEINSTEIN, MICHAEL, H., M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by WEINSTEIN,MICHAEL H.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISIONAL BIOPSY FOR A MAMMOGRAPHIC\u000aABNORMALITY AND A CLIP:\u000aFocally cellular fibrous stroma consistent with a fibroadenoma\u000a(0.6 cm measured from slide) in a region showing prior biopsy\u000asite changes.\u000aColumnar alteration of lobules with prominent snouts and secretions.\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the\u000aspecimen, including margins.\u000aNOTE: Dr. Andrea Richardson of the Breast Pathology Service has reviewed\u000athis case and concurs with the diagnosis.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: None given.\u000aOperation: Right needle directed breast biopsy.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal mammogram.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Right breast tissue, to mammo.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Mass in specimen. OR called @ 1:30 p.m. [illegible signature)\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by OH,KIRSTINE YUNG-TING,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in one part, labeled with the patient's name,\u000aunit number and "#1 right breast tissue", and consists of a single fragment of\u000afirm, tan/pink and yellow fibroadipose tissue (4 x 4 x REMOVED_DATE cm). The included\u000amammogram notes dense firm fibrous breast tissue with no localizing\u000acalcifications and a single clip. No localizing sutures are found on the\u000aspecimen. The entire specimen is inked black and serially sectioned. The\u000aspecimen is sectioned serially at REMOVED_DATE cm intervals and no clip is found. The\u000abreast parenchyma consists of a dense, variegated, tan/red-colored parenchyma\u000awith a single area of right yellow focal necrosis (0.3 x REMOVED_DATE cm). This entire\u000aarea is submitted. The remainder of the section is submitted in alternating\u000asections.\u000aMicro 1&2: bright yellow necrotic area, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  representative sections of remaining breast tissue, 1 frag each,\u000aRSS.\u000ako\u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
