m medial to lateral. The cut surface is tan/yellow and homogenous with\u000afocal area of dense white fibrous tissue constituting approximately 90% of the\u000abreast parenchyma. There is an irregular tan/brown to red/brown area within\u000athe fibrous tissue (0.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). There is a silver metallic clip\u000aconsistent with previous biopsy cavity. The previous biopsy cavity comes\u000awithin REMOVED_DATE cm of the inferior margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm of the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE \u000acm from the anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000alateral margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin. No discrete lesions or\u000aareas of disruption are grossly identified. The specimen is submitted in its\u000aentirety.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross sections, medial to lateral, block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID to\u000ainclude metallic clip, previous biopsy cavity, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, 3 frags, ESS.\u000asek/ag\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Alessandra F Nascimento M.D., Electronically signed on\u000a5/10/2008\u000a[report_end]
