s.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity\u000ain >10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 40 year old female with history of left breast cancer - invasive\u000atubulobular and DCIS.\u000aPalpable abnormality - ill-defined 20 mm hypoechoic area 10:00 right\u000abreast.\u000aBreast Imaging Findings: Ill-defined.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: ? malignancy vs fibrocystic parenchyma\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Core biopsy specimens (1 orange cassette)\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by RICHARDSON,ANDREA,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit\u000anumber, and "right breast core bx", in an orange cassette, and consists of\u000amultiple, soft, fragmented, yellow to white tissue cores (1.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in\u000aaggregate).\u000aMicro 1: Multi frags, ESS.\u000akks\u000aReports to: MORRIS, JUSTINE, E. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY(IES)\u000a[report_end]
