VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST MASTECTOMY W/REGIONAL LYMPH NODES\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aGLICKMAN, JONATHAN, NEIL, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by GLICKMAN,JONATHAN NEIL,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, MODIFED RADICAL MASTECTOMY (#1/3 SPECIMENS) AND\u000aADDITIONAL RIGHT AXILLARY CONTENTS (#2/3 SPECIMENS):\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA (MULTIPLE FOCI).\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU.\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU.\u000aMETASTATIC CARCINOMA TO LYMPH NODES.\u000aSYNOPSIS:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA\u000aSize - REMOVED_DATE cm (largest focus)\u000aMultifocal? - Yes\u000aHistologic Type - Mixed Ductal and Lobular\u000aHistologic Grade (SBR) - II(Moderate)\u000aNuclear Grade - Intermediate\u000aEIC - Negative\u000aLymphovascular invasion - Present\u000aDermal lymphatic invasion - Absent\u000aSkin invasion - Absent\u000aSkeletal muscle invasion - N/A\u000aFinal Margins (invasive) -\u000aNegative (no ink on tumor) - deep\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aTypes - Cribriform\u000aNuclear grade - Intermediate\u000aCalcifications in DCIS - Absent\u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - Absent\u000aExtent of DCIS\u000aNumber of blocks/total: REMOVED_DATE blocks\u000aFinal Margins (DCIS)\u000aNegative (>0.3 cm) - deep\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - Present\u000aLYMPH NODES\u000aAxillary lymph nodes Positive\u000aNumber of positive nodes: 4\u000aNumber of nodes examined: 10\u000aTOTAL POSITIVE NODES (sentinel + axillary) - REMOVED_DATE \u000aSize of largest metastatic focus REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aExtranodal extension Present\u000aOTHER FINDINGS Sclerosing adenosis\u000aCore biopsy site\u000aAJCC CLASSIFICATION - REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID pREMOVED_ACCESSION_IDbiii MX (see note)\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER/PR/HER-2) - Performed previously\u000aNOTE: Similar to the previous biopsy (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), scattered single tumor cells\u000ashow vacuolated cytoplasm and pleomorphic nuclei, possibly consistent with\u000atreatment effect. Although some degree of tumor regression within areas of\u000adense fibrosis cannot be excluded, the carcinoma appears viable with no areas\u000aof recent tumor necrosis.\u000aAlthough the original tumor size may have been larger than that observed\u000ain this post-treatment specimen, the tumor classification here is based upon\u000athe size of the largest identifiable nodule of invasive carcinoma in the\u000aresection (3.0 cm).\u000a#3. SPECIMEN LABELED "PORTACATH":\u000aPortacath (gross examination).\u000aSkin and subcutaneous tissue with focal foreign body giant cell\u000areaction.\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 40-year-old female, s/p left BCT (10/97) for Stage I REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDb REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID,\u000agrade I invasive tubular/lobular carcinoma (0.8 cm) - treated with breast\u000aradiation. In REMOVED_MONTH of 2001 she noted changes in the breast and a MRI\u000ademonstrated a right brest mass (8 cm) - a core biopsy (4/16/01) revealed\u000ainvasive carcinoma with ductal and lobular features. FNA of right axillary\u000alymph node was positive for malignant cells. S/P neo-adjuvant CEF chemotherapy\u000aOperation: Right MRM, removal of port-a-cath\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast cancer\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000a1) Right modified radical mastectomy specimen (long/axillary contents;\u000ashort/superior)\u000a2) Additional right axillary contents\u000a3) Port-a-cath\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by BARRY,MARC,M.B.,B.CH.,B.A.O.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in three parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart one, "right modified radical mastectomy specimen", consists of a\u000amastectomy specimen (22 x 19 x 3 cm) with an axillary tail (11 x 4 x 1 cm) and\u000aa skin ellipse (21 x 8 cm) containing a nipple (2 cm diameter). There is\u000aextensive fibrosis of the breast parenchyma (approximately REMOVED_DATE % of volume)\u000awith several firmer nodular areas contiguous with fibrosis. There is a nodule\u000alaterally (3 x REMOVED_DATE x 2 cm) in the upper outer quadrant lying REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000adeep edge of the specimen. There is a second irregular area of fibrosis (1.5 x\u000a1 x 1 cm) lying in the upper outer quadrant, and multiple areas of firmness\u000awithin the centrally-placed fibrosis. Fibrosis extends to within REMOVED_DATE cm of\u000adeep margin in multiple areas. In one area, centrally within the fibrosis, is\u000aa small cavity (0.5 cm in diameter). The axillary tail contains multiple\u000atan, rubbery to firm lymph node candidates which are entirely submitted. The\u000askin ellipse and nipple appear grossly unremarkable.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  lateral-most nodule, 3 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 4: second fibrotic nodule, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  fibrous tissue contiguous with first nodule, 2 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 7: fibrous tissue contiguous with second nodule, 2 frag, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  sampling from central fibrous area (approximately 11 cm in greatest\u000adimension), (cavity in cassette 11), 4 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 12: segment from upper outer quadrant,\u000aMicro 13: segment from lower outer quadrant,\u000aMicro 14: segment from upper inner quadrant,\u000aMicro 15: segment from lower inner quadrant,\u000aMicro 16: nipple, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 17: 1 lymph node, 3 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 18: 1 lymph node, 2 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 19: 1 lymph node, 2 frag, ESS\u000aMicro 20: 1 lymph node, 2 frag, ESS\u000aMicro 21: 1 lymph node, 3 frag, ESS\u000aMicro 22: 1 lymph node, 2 frag, ESS\u000aPart two, "additional right axillary contents", consists of multiple fragments\u000aof axillary fat (5 x 5 x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate) containing mutiple tan, rubbery\u000ato firm lymph node candidates which are entirely submitted.\u000aMicro 23: 1 lymph node, 2 frag, ESS\u000aMicro 24: 1 lymph node, 4 frag, ESS\u000aMicro 25: 1 lymph node, 3 frag, ESS\u000aMicro 26: 2 lymph nodes, 4 frag, ESS\u000aPart three, "port-a-cath", consists of a port-a-cath device with a length of\u000atubing (27 cm length, REMOVED_DATE cm diameter) and a disc-shaped device (3 x 3 x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm). There is a fragment of pigmented skin and dermis on subcutaneous fat\u000apresent with the port-a-cath device, which is entirely submitted for\u000amicroscopic examination.\u000aMicro 27: skin with soft tissue, 1 frag, ESS\u000amab\u000aReports to: KAELIN, CAROLYN, MARY M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY W/REGIONAL LYMPH NODES\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SKIN- OTHER THAN CYST, TAG OR DEBRIDEMENT\u000a[report_end]
