VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: BETH ANN LESNIKOSKI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Elizabeth Amy Morgan, M.D.; Ann K Folkins, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Deborah A Dillon, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A CLIP:\u000aComplex sclerosing lesion (1.0 cm) with associated florid epithelial\u000ahyperplasia, see note.\u000aBiopsy site changes are present.\u000aColumnar cell change, epithelial hyperplasia, apocrine cysts, fibroadenomatoid\u000achange and calcifications associated with benign epithelium.\u000aNote: Immunohistochemistry for p63/REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID confirms the presence of\u000amyoepithelial cells around distorted ducts.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Hx of radial scar diagnosed at South Shore Hospital, abnormal\u000amammogram with spiculated density seen best on ML view.\u000aOperation: Left breast wire-localized wide local excision.\u000aOperative Findings: Normal-appearing breast tissue.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left abnormal mammo and ultrasound and radial scar.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) Left breast tissue with wire.\u000aRADIOLOGY: clip + distortion in specimen. - Maso\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "Left breast tissue with wire", and consists of an irregular tan/yellow\u000alobulated portion of fibroadipose breast tissue (5.2 cm medial to lateral, REMOVED_DATE \u000asuperior to inferior, and REMOVED_DATE cm anterior to posterior) with a\u000aneedle-localization wire in place entering through the lateral aspect of the\u000aspecimen. There are no identifying suture designations, however, the specimen\u000ahas been previously inked per pathology protocol per the surgeon (superior red,\u000ainferior green, medial orange, lateral yellow, anterior blue, and posterior\u000ablack). The specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral. The cut\u000asurface is tan/yellow and homogeneous with predominantly admixed tan/white\u000adense fibrous tissue constituting approximately 90% of the breast parenchyma.\u000aThere is an irregular red/brown to tan/yellow granular ragged area consistent\u000awith previous biopsy cavity (1.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) which comes within REMOVED_DATE cm of\u000athe lateral margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior margin, and\u000a3.5 cm from the medial margin. Adjacent to the area is a silver-metallic clip.\u000aNo discrete lesions or areas of disruption are grossly identified. The\u000aspecimen is submitted in its entirety.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross sections, medial and lateral block, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID to\u000ainclude biopsy cavity block, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID to include slice with metallic clip, 1\u000afrag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aSEK/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Deborah A Dillon M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
