VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY(IES)\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aLESTER, SUSAN, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000a*******************************************************************************\u000aTHIS REPORT HAS BEEN AMENDED - SEE SURGICAL ADDENDUM BELOW REMOVED_DATE \u000a*******************************************************************************\u000aLEFT BREAST, LOWER INNER, 11 G STEREOTACTIC CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR A SMALL\u000aIRREGULAR DENSITY AND CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, cribriform and papillary types (intermediate\u000anuclear grade) is present, with apocrine features.\u000aMicrocalcifications are focally associated with DCIS.\u000aSingle cell necrosis is associated with DCIS.\u000aNOTE: DCIS involves a sclerosing papilloma.\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aAdditional levels were examined and the case was reviewed by Dr. Stuart Schnitt\u000aand Dr. Andrea Richardson.\u000aA subsequent excision (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) was free of malignancy. This case is also\u000areviewed.\u000aGiven the small size of the lesion in the needle biopsy which focally involves\u000aa sclerosing papilloma, the classification is changed to\u000aSEVERELY ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA, bordering on DCIS, involving a\u000asclerosing papilloma.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 55 year old with focal calcifications & small irreg density, LLIQ.\u000aOperation: 11G stereotactic.\u000aOperative findings: Ca++ in specimens.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Probable DCIS/invasive CA.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Left breast tissue in two pink casettes. A - tissue with\u000aca++. B - remainder of tissue.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by CARTER,MARK RYAN,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit\u000anumber, and "left breast", and consists of two (2) pink cassettes. One\u000acassette is labeled "A ca++" and contains multiple, soft, fragmented, yellow\u000ato white tissue cores (1.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate). The other cassette\u000ais labeled "B" and contains similar tissue fragments (1.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in\u000aaggregate).\u000aMicro 1: pink cassette labeled "A ca++", multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 2: pink cassette labeled "B", multi frags, ESS.\u000akks\u000aReports to: SEDGWICK, EMILY M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY(IES)\u000a[report_end]
