VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: BETH ANN LESNIKOSKI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Derek K Marsee, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Jonathan N Glickman, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aSPECIMEN DESIGNATED "LEFT BREAST, MASS":\u000aSpindle cell neoplasm, most consistent with atypical perineuroma,\u000asee NOTE.\u000aNo mitoses or necrosis.\u000aThe tumor is present at the anterior inked margin.\u000aThe posterior, superior, inferior, medial, and lateral margins\u000aare negative for tumor.\u000aImmunohistochemistry performed at BWH demonstrates the following staining\u000aprofile in tumor cells:\u000aPositive - REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, SMA (rare), EMA (focal)\u000aNegative - REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, Pan-K, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.2, S-100\u000aNOTE:\u000aThis lesion is considered atypical due to its infiltrative quality, which is\u000aunusual and may indicate an increased likelihood of recurrence. No overt\u000afeatures of malignancy are present. The case was reviewed by Dr. Christopher\u000aFletcher, Soft Tissue Pathology Service, who concurs.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Spindle cell neoplasm seen on core.\u000aOperation: Wide excision of left breast mass.\u000aOperative Findings: Not given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast mass.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Left breast mass.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "left breast mass", and consists of an irregular tan/yellow lobulated\u000aportion of fibroadipose breast tissue (5.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with a small portion\u000aof overlying tan/white wrinkled skin (1.4 x REMOVED_DATE cm). The specimen has been\u000apreviously inked per pathology protocol (superior/red, inferior/green,\u000alateral/yellow, medial/orange, anterior/blue, and posterior/black) and serially\u000asectioned from medial to lateral. The cut surface is tan/yellow and homogenous\u000awith a focal dense white solid hemorrhagic firm area (0.6 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm)\u000aunderlying the portion of the skin, and located REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE from the medial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom the lateral margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin. The specimen is\u000asubmitted in its entirety.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross sections (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID to include dense firm area), 1\u000afrag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, 2 frags, ESS.\u000asek/lp\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jonathan N Glickman M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a1/19/2007\u000a[report_end]
