VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: BETH ANN LESNIKOSKI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Leona A. Doyle, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Jane E. Brock, M.B., B.S., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aLEFT BREAST WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A CLIP, CALCIFICATIONS AND AN AREA OF\u000aARCHITECTURAL DISTORTION:\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, cribriform and papillary types with focal mucin\u000aproduction (intermediate nuclear grade) with focal calcifications and single\u000acell necrosis is present in 10 of 17 blocks, covering an estimated area of REMOVED_DATE \u000acm.\u000aDCIS is focally REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID). The superior, medial,\u000alateral, anterior and posterior margins are negative for DCIS (> REMOVED_DATE cm).\u000aOther findings:\u000aColumnar cell change with calcifications, cysts and flat epithelial atypia\u000aApocrine cysts\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for carcinoma (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) NEGATIVE (1+)\u000aNOTE: Dr. Susan Lester also reviewed key slides from this case and agrees with\u000athe diagnosis.\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000acarcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but only\u000aa portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in >10%\u000aof tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in\u000a>10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Abnormal mammo --> core bx for architectural distortion primary\u000alesion, with florid ductal hyperplasia.\u000aOperation: L breast wide local excision with wire localization.\u000aOperative Findings: Not provided.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: L papillary lesion/ductal hyperplasia.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) L breast tissue with wire and clip -- mammo.\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000aCalled to Dr. Lesnikoski @ 6 pm. Clip and Ca++ in specimen. SR REMOVED_DATE \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "left breast tissue and wire with clip", and consists of an irregular\u000atan/yellow lobulated portion of fibroadipose breast tissue (5.5 cm medial to\u000alateral, REMOVED_DATE cm superior to inferior, and REMOVED_DATE cm anterior to posterior) with a\u000aneedle localization wire in place entering through the medial aspect of the\u000aspecimen. The breast has been previously inked per the surgeon and is\u000aconsistent with the pathology breast inking protocol (superior/red,\u000ainferior/green, medial/orange, lateral/yellow, anterior/blue, and\u000aposterior/black); however, no definitive designating markers or stitches are\u000agrossly present. The specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral and\u000athere is an ill-defined dense white fibrous area (2.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), within\u000awhich there is a silver metallic surgical clip, consistent with the previous\u000abiopsy site. The site is located REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000athe anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin.\u000aRemainder of the breast parenchyma is tan/yellow and homogeneous with no\u000adiscrete lesions grossly identified. The specimen is submitted in its\u000aentirety.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross sections, blocks REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID to include possible\u000aprevious biopsy cavity, blocks REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID to include silver surgical metallic\u000aclip, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000asek/lp\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jane E. Brock M.B., B.S., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a10/20/2008\u000a[report_end]
