eristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital. They have not been cleared or approved by the U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA). The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary; this laboratory has established and verified the test's accuracy and precision. Added by: Atul Kumar Bhan, M.D. Signed On: 24 REMOVED_MONTH 02 at 16:00 GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name and unit number, and "sentinel node", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm piece of firm tan tissue, bivalved and submitted entirely in cassette A. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name and unit number, and "additional deep tissue", is a piece of fibrofatty tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The specimen is submitted entirely in cassette B-C. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name and unit number, and "final shaved margin medial half of cavity", are multiple fibrofatty tissues measuring in aggregate REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The specimen is serially sectioned and submitted entirely in cassettes D. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name and unit number, and "final shaved margin lateral half of cavity", is a piece of fibrofatty tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. There is a blue inked area measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The specimen is serially sectioned and submitted entirely in cassettes H-L. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name and unit number only, is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm lobular piece of fibro-fatty tissue. There is a long stitch designated by the surgeon to be lateral, and a short stitch designated by the surgeon to be superior. Anterior surface is inked blue, posterior surface - inked black. Sectioning reveals a firm, gritty, irregularly demarcated area measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The area is REMOVED_DATE cm from the mid-lateral margin. Representative sections of this firm area and the lateral specimen are submitted in cassettes M - N, from inferior to superior. Representative sections of the area in the medial half of the specimen are submitted in cassettes O - P, from inferior to superior. The inferior medial margin are submitted in radial sections in cassette Q. Fibro-fatty breast tissue is submitted in cassette R. Resident: NICOLE ANN BELSLEY, MD =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT - REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID REPORTS TO: Barbara Lynn Smith, M.D. PART A: LYMPH NODE ("SENTINEL" RIGHT AXILLA LEVEL I), EXCI PART B: BREAST (RIGHT), ADDITIONAL DEEP MARGIN PART C: BREAST (RIGHT/ MEDIAL CAVITY), FINAL SHAVED MARGIN PART D: BREAST (RIGHT/ LATERAL CAVITY), FINAL SHAVED MARGI PART E: BREAST (RIGHT), LUMPECTOMY
