VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Amend/Addenda\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000a********** Addended Report ***********\u000aResident: Dominique P. Coco, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Susan Lester, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR ARCHITECTURAL DISTORTION:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA with ductal and lobular features, moderately differentiated\u000a(modified Bloom-Richardson grade II/III), at least 3 cm in size (see note).\u000aLymphovascular invasion is present.\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, solid type (low nuclear grade), is present in two (2)\u000aof twenty-four (24) blocks (EIC negative). No necrosis or associated\u000amicrocalcifications are identified.\u000aPrior biopsy site changes are present away from the carcinoma.\u000aInvasive carcinoma is present at the medial margin (inked orange, cauterized;\u000amultifocal; blocks REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), posterior margin (inked black, cauterized;\u000amultifocal; blocks REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), and inferior margin (inked green, cauterized;\u000ablock REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID). The anterior, superior, and lateral margins are negative for\u000ainvasive carcinoma and DCIS (> REMOVED_DATE cm).\u000aCalcifications are associated with benign epithelium.\u000aNOTE: The carcinoma has a diffusely invasive pattern in dense stroma and was\u000anot identified grossly. Invasive carcinoma is present in fourteen (14) of the\u000atwenty-four (24) blocks. The carcinoma measures at least REMOVED_DATE cm on the slides.\u000aHowever, given the number of blocks involved, the size is more likely to be 3\u000ato 4 cm. Additionally, the carcinoma is present at three cauterized margins.\u000aA prior right breast core needle biopsy of an adjacent (but different) mass\u000arevealed only fibrous breast tissue (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID). Portions of the biopsy site\u000aare present in this specimen.\u000aImmunohistochemical analysis for estrogen receptor, progesterone receptor, and\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu will be performed and reported in an addendum.\u000aThis carcinoma would be classified as AJCC (6th edition) REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID NX.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 76 year old woman s/p R breast mass, biopsied by core needle on\u000a11/14/07 with benign pathology - excision needed to evaluate right breast\u000aarchitectural distortion in subareolar region seen on R breast US REMOVED_DATE \u000aHistory of Hodgkin's disease.\u000aOperation: R breast WL bx.\u000aOperative Findings: None specified.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: None specified.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) Right breast tissue; short st - superior; long st - lateral; whip st - on\u000adeep margin.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Architectural distortion in specimen. Wire intact.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "#1. Right breast tissue with stitch equals deep margin, short equals\u000asuperior, long equals lateral", and consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm excision\u000aof fibroadipose tissue, oriented with sutures by the surgeon, designating\u000asuperior (short suture), lateral (long suture), and deep margin (whipstitch).\u000aThe specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins:\u000aposterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow;\u000amedial/orange (inked by surgeon). A localizing wire enters the superior aspect\u000aof the specimen and exits at the inferior aspect. The specimen is received\u000awith a radiograph demonstrating the localizing wire in place within an area of\u000aarchitectural distortion centrally. There is a possible metallic surgical\u000aclip, remote from this area. The specimen is sectioned (thirteen total slices)\u000afrom superior to inferior, demonstrating at least 85% to 90% dense tan/white\u000alobulated fibrous tissue. The area marked by the localizing wire (centrally\u000awithin the tissue) exhibits an ill-defined possible fibrous lesion (at least\u000ainvolving slices #7, #8, and #9), that appears to be REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest\u000adimension. The lesion is surrounded by firm bright tan/yellow adipose tissue\u000aand additional fibrous tissue, radiating to the medial, anterior and posterior\u000amargins. Closest lateral margin is within REMOVED_DATE cm, closest superior margin is\u000awithin REMOVED_DATE cm, closest inferior margin is within REMOVED_DATE cm. Additionally, there\u000ais REMOVED_DATE cm prior biopsy cavity site, at least REMOVED_DATE cm superior to the area of\u000ainterest (slices #2, #3). There are no residual masses or other abnormalities\u000anoted grossly in this area. Representative tissue is submitted, to include all\u000aareas of interest.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Perpendicular superior margin (slice #1), multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slices #2, #3 (area of prior biopsy cavity), multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #5 (intervening tissue between biopsy cavity and area of\u000ainterest), 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #7, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #8, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #9, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #10, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #13 (perpendicular inferior margin), multi frags, ESS.\u000aApproximately 60% of tissue has been submitted, to include areas of interest\u000aand intervening tissue, all closest margins.\u000aDB/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a12/17/2007\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM:\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for invasive carcinoma (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) NEGATIVE (0)\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000ainvasive carcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low > 0% - < 10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor cells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but only a\u000aportion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+):Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in >10% of\u000atumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+):Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in >30% of\u000atumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aExternal controls are evaluated and show appropriate Immunoreactivity.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aAddendum #1 by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
