u000aThis is inked black. The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a large\u000aseroma cavity at the 12 o'clock position (superior to the nipple) which\u000ameasures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm and has a firm, fibrous capsule. This is filled\u000awith tan/brown serous fluid. There are multiple tan/white nodules on the\u000ainterior surface of the seroma cavity, the largest measuring REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest\u000adimension. The cavity extends to within REMOVED_DATE cm to the deep margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of\u000athe skin surface, and REMOVED_DATE cm of the nipple. No other masses or lesions are\u000anoted. The fibrous tissue surrounding the seroma cavity extends to within REMOVED_DATE \u000acm of the skin surface. Representative sections are submitted for microscopic\u000aexamination. Please note that no blue ink was used in processing of the\u000aspecimen; any blue discoloration present on histologic sections represents\u000amethylene blue dye.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Seroma cavity and surrounding firm tissue, REMOVED_DATE frags per\u000acassette, RSS (approximately 50% of cavity submitted including all nodular\u000aareas).\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Deep margin closest to seroma cavity, 2 frags per cassette, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Nipple, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Skin ellipse at closest approach to seroma cavity, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Upper outer quadrant, representative section, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lower outer quadrant, representative section, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Upper outer quadrant, representative section, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lower inner quadrant, representative section, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID through REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Random axillary fibroadipose tissue, multi frags, RSS\u000a(approximately 50% of axillary adipose tissue is submitted).\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Remainder of seroma cavity and surrounding firm tissue,\u000a1-3 frags per cassette, ESS\u000aSBL/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-08-5448\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Lucian R Chirieac M.D., Electronically signed on\u000a2/14/2008\u000a[report_end]
