VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Amend/Addenda\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ROGER L CHRISTIAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000a********** Addended Report ***********\u000aResident: David C. Park, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Jonathan N Glickman, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "LEFT BREAST, EXCISION":\u000aINVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA\u000aSize - REMOVED_DATE cm (measured off glass slide)\u000aMultifocal - No\u000aHistologic type - Ductal\u000aHistologic grade (SBR) - I (Well) (3 to 5 points)\u000aTubules - 10 to 75% (2 points)\u000aNuclear grade - Intermediate (2 points)\u000aMitotic counts - 1 point\u000aEIC - Negative\u000aLVI - Absent\u000aDermal LVI - Not applicable\u000aSkeletal muscle invasion - Not applicable\u000aFinal Margins (invasive)\u000aNegative (> REMOVED_DATE cm) - Medial, lateral, inferior\u000aClose (0.1 to REMOVED_DATE cm) - Superior (0.2 cm, block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID)\u000aAnterior (0.2 cm, block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID)\u000aVery close(<0.1 cm from margin)- Posterior (blocks REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID)\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aTypes - Cribriform\u000aNuclear grade - Intermediate\u000aCalcifications in DCIS - Present\u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - Present\u000aExtent of DCIS\u000aNumber of blocks/total - 1:9 blocks\u000aDCIS is present as a minor component of the invasive carcinoma\u000aMargins (DCIS)\u000aNegative (> REMOVED_DATE cm) - All resection margins\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - Present\u000aOTHER FINDINGS\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia with pagetoid spread\u000aCore biopsy site\u000aCalcifications in benign epithelium\u000aAJCC Classification (6th edition) - pREMOVED_ACCESSION_IDc Nx MX\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER, PR, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) - Pending\u000aB. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "SUPERIOR SHAVE MARGIN":\u000aBenign breast tissue.\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy.\u000aC. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "LATERAL SHAVE MARGIN":\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia with pagetoid spread.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Architectural distortion, lt breast, new area of core bx done wire\u000adirected excision REMOVED_DATE  @n Berkshire Med Center.\u000aOperation: Wire directed excision.\u000aOperative Findings: See op note. At area of distortion, I think we uncovered\u000aedge of CA, Inking was confusing. Red correct I then took an opposing shave\u000a(superior margin).\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Not provided.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Tissue, lt breast, short suture superior, long lateral * wire fell out of\u000aspecimen.\u000aB/2. Superior shave margin - suture: superior.\u000aC/3. Lateral shave margin - suture: lateral.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in three parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart A, "tissue, left breast", and consists of an irregular tan/yellow\u000alobulated portion of fibroadipose tissue (4.5 cm medial to lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000asuperior to inferior, and REMOVED_DATE cm anterior to posterior) with a short suture\u000adesignating the superior margin, and a long suture designating the lateral\u000amargin. Please note that per the surgeon, the specimen is not received with a\u000aneedle-localization wire. The specimen has been previously inked per the\u000asurgeon per pathology protocol (superior red, inferior green, medial orange,\u000alateral yellow, anterior blue, posterior black). The specimen is serially\u000asectioned from medial to lateral. The cut surface is tan/yellow and\u000ahomogeneous with focal areas of dense white fibrous tissue constituting\u000aapproximately 80% of the breast parenchyma. No discrete lesions are grossly\u000aidentified. The specimen is submitted in its entirety.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross sections medial to lateral, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, "superior shave margin", and consists of an irregular tan/yellow\u000alobulated portion of fibroadipose breast tissue (2.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). There is\u000aa suture designating the superior margin, which displays a convex surface which\u000ahas been previously inked red. The opposite margin is concave and ragged\u000aconsistent with old margin and is inked black. The cut surface primarily\u000aconsists of dense white fibrous tissue with a scant amount of tan/yellow\u000afibroadipose tissue present. The specimen is serially sectioned and submitted\u000ain its entirety.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross sections, 3 frags each, ESS.\u000aPart C, "lateral shave margin", and consists of an irregular tan/yellow\u000alobulated portion of fibroadipose tissue (1.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). There is a\u000asuture designating the lateral margin which marks convex surface which has been\u000apreviously inked yellow. The opposite surface is tan/yellow and focally ragged\u000aconsistent with old margin and is inked black. The cut surface primarily\u000aconsists of dense white fibrous tissue constituting approximately greater than\u000a95% of the specimen. The specimen is trisected and submitted in its entirety.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 3 frags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aSEK/ajb\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jonathan N Glickman M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a1/22/2008\u000aADDENDUM (01/28/08):\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for invasive carcinoma (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) NEGATIVE (1+) (see NOTE)\u000aNOTE: The invasive carcinoma is negative for REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/NEU, however the associated\u000aDCIS shows stronger staining for REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/NEU (weakly positive 2+).\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000acarcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but only\u000aa portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in >10%\u000aof tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in\u000a>10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aAddendum #1 by Jane E. Brock M.B., B.S., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a1/28/2008\u000a[report_end]
