here is a firm well-defined gray/white mass measuring REMOVED_DATE x\u000a1.0 x REMOVED_DATE cm. The edges of the lesion are ill-defined with a slight scalloped\u000aappearance. The closet superior margin is grossly within 1 mm. The remaining\u000amargins distances are as follows: inferior margin 1 cm, lateral margin REMOVED_DATE cm,\u000amedial margin 4 cm, posterior margin REMOVED_DATE cm, and anterior margin REMOVED_DATE cm. The\u000aremaining breast tissue is soft red/yellow fibroadipose tissue. The specimen\u000ais entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: The entire tumor and closest superior and inferior margin,\u000a3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Remaining superior margin, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Anterior margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Posterior margin, 3 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Remainder of breast excision specimen, REMOVED_DATE frags each, ESS.\u000aSF/mmm/PES\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a10/5/2006\u000a[report_end]
