tallic surgical clip. The\u000aspecimen is serially sectioned and the cut surfaces demonstrate at least 90%\u000atan/white fibrinous tissue with focal hemorrhage along the localizing wire\u000atract, but no obvious masses, lesions, or other abnormalities. The metallic\u000aclip is identified in the anterior portion of the specimen, abutting the\u000aspecimen's lateral margin. The specimen is entirely submitted sequentially\u000afrom anterior to posterior.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Entire specimen, sequentially from anterior to posterior (tissue\u000asurrounding clip in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), multi frags, ESS.\u000aDB/ajb\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Michelle S Hirsch M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a7/11/2006\u000a[report_end]
