ior/red;\u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. The localization wire enters\u000athe posterolateral aspect of the specimen and does not exit the specimen. The\u000aspecimen is received with only one suture, which is located at the superior\u000aaspect of the specimen. The specimen is sectioned from superior to inferior in\u000a11 sections. A single tan/white well-circumscribed mass is identified and\u000ameasures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The mass comes to within: Superior margin REMOVED_DATE \u000acm, inferior margin REMOVED_DATE cm, medial margin REMOVED_DATE cm and lateral margin REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000aSpecimen is accompanied by radiograph that shows a clip, a wire and the\u000aspecimen. The remainder of the specimen consists of approximately 80% fibrous\u000aand 20% adipose tissue with no other masses identifiable. The specimen is\u000aentirely submitted sequentially from superior to inferior.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 1, superior margin, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 2, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 3, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 4, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 5, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 6, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 7, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 8, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 9, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 10, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 11, 1 disrupted frag, inferior margin, ESS.\u000aNOTE: The clip was identified in slice 5, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aMDH/ajb\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Christopher D. M. Fletcher M.D. FRCPath, Electronically\u000asigned on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
