VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: JULIE L JONES M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-05-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Marianna B Ruzinova, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Xiaohua Qian, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA/1. RIGHT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR MAMMOGRAPHIC ABNORMALITY:\u000aBenign breast tissue with lobular expansion and focal lactational/secretory\u000achanges with associated calcifications.\u000aBiopsy site changes.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the\u000aspecimen, including margins.\u000aB/2. SPECIMEN LABELED "ADDITIONAL ANTERIOR TISSUE TO MAMMO":\u000aBenign breast tissue with sclerosing adenosis and columnar cell changes.\u000aCalcifications associated with benign epithelium.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the\u000aspecimen, including margins.\u000aC/3. SPECIMEN LABELED "ADDITIONAL SUPERIOR TISSUE TO MAMMO":\u000aBenign breast tissue with focal columnar cell changes.\u000aCalcifications associated with benign epithelium.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the\u000aspecimen, including margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Right breast upper/outer quadrant calcifications and mass, S/P\u000aultrasound-guided core biopsy with benign findings considered discordant.\u000aOperation: Right wire-localized excisional biopsy.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast mass and calcifications.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1 - right wire-localized excision to mammo, long stitch/lateral, short\u000astitch/superior.\u000aB/2 - additional anterior tissue to mammo, short stitch/superior, long\u000astitch/lateral.\u000aC/3 - additional superior tissue to mammo.\u000aRADIOGRAPHY REPORTS:\u000a#1 - Clip not present, wire and Ca++ in specimen, OR called. /SR\u000a#2 - Calcifications are within the specimen. No clip. Dr. Gombos\u000a#3 - Calcifications and a clip within the specimen. Dr. Gombos.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in three parts, each labeled with the patient?s\u000aname and unit number, and accompanied by three radiographs, one for each\u000aspecimen.\u000aPart A, labeled "#1 - right breast localized excision, long/lateral,\u000ashort/superior", and consists of one fragment of fibroadipose tissue, measuring\u000a3.6 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm with orienting sutures placed by the surgeon\u000a(short/superior, long/lateral), and localizing wire entering from\u000aposterior/medial to anterior/medial aspect of the specimen. The specimen is\u000ainked according to the pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins:\u000aposterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow;\u000amedial/orange. The specimen is sectioned from the lateral to medial aspect to\u000areveal a hemorrhagic area in slices two through six, measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm, which abuts the anterior and superior margins. Slices five and six also\u000ahave a necrotic cavity measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm, which is located REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom the inferior aspect, REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior aspect, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000asuperior aspect. The entire specimen is submitted for histologic evaluation.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: slices one through six (slices one and two containing the\u000acalcifications seen on the radiograph), 6 frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, labeled "#2 - additional anterior tissue, short/superior,\u000along/lateral", and consists of one fragment of fibroadipose tissue measuring\u000a2.6 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm, with a short suture placed by the surgeon to indicate the\u000asuperior aspect, and a long suture placed by the surgeon to indicate the\u000alateral aspect. The specimen is inked according to the pathology protocol for\u000athe evaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red;\u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. The specimen is sectioned from\u000alateral to medial aspect to reveal breast tissue with punctate hemorrhages,\u000awhich is entirely submitted for histologic evaluation.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: additional right breast tissue, 6 frags, ESS.\u000aPart C, labeled "#3 - additional superior tissue, mammo", and consists of two\u000aunoriented fragments of fibroadipose tissue, measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm and\u000a0.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The specimen fragments are inked black, with the larger\u000afragment sectioned to reveal a hemorrhage measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The\u000aentire specimen is submitted for histologic evaluation.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: larger fragment of breast tissue, with clip in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 5 frags,\u000aESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: smaller fragment of breast tissue, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMRU/lp\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Marianna B Ruzinova M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Xiaohua Qian M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a11/22/2005\u000a[report_end]
