VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aWELCH, WILLIAM, ROBERT, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by WELCH,WILLIAM ROBERT,M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN DESIGNATED "RIGHT BREAST MASS":\u000aFibroadenoma.\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy, including examination of margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 26 year old female with rt breast mass.\u000a*Please see core biopsy report from REMOVED_DATE \u000aClinical Diagnosis: Rt breast mass.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Rt breast mass. Short stitch superior, long stitch\u000alateral.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by BUNDOCK,ELIZABETH A.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen received fresh in one part, labeled with the patient's name, unit\u000anumber and "#1", and consists of a portion of firm, fibroadipose tissue (4 x\u000a3.2 x 3 cm) with one short suture to designate superior and one long suture to\u000adesignate lateral. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the\u000aevaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red;\u000ainferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. The surface of the\u000aspecimen is smooth, nodular and appears shelled out in numerous areas. Other\u000aareas consist of ragged fibroadipose tissue. The specimen is serially\u000asectioned at 3 mm intervals from superior to inferior, to reveal a well\u000acircumscribed, encapsulated, tan/white, firm mass which appears grossly to be\u000afully excised. A thin rim of fibrous soft tissue with focal hemorrhage rims\u000athe mass along the lateral, anterior and inferior margins. Representative\u000asections of the mass and adjacent tissue are submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  breast mass, 5 frags, RSS.\u000aeab\u000aReports to: CARTER, KATHARINE M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
