VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ROGER L CHRISTIAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Shakti Ramkissoon, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Kirstine Yung-Ting Oh, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA/2). LEFT BREAST, WIRE-DIRECTED EXCISION FOR A CLIP AND MRI ABNORMALITY:\u000aBreast parenchyma with complex sclerosing lesion, columnar cell change,\u000ausual ductal hyperplasia, intraductal papilloma, calcifications in\u000abenign epithelium, and biopsy site changes.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the\u000aspecimen, including margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Abnormal MRI, lt breast.\u000aOperation: Wire directed excision of MRI abnormal.\u000aOperative Findings: See op note.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal MRI, lt breast.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Excision L breast, long stitch lateral, short superior (mammo).\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000aClip + tissue in specimen - called to Dr. Escareno (resident) in OR by Dr. Yeh\u000a2/19/08 12:00 noon.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "excision L breast, long stitch lateral, short superior", consists of an\u000airregular tan/yellow lobulated portion of fibroadipose breast tissue (3.4 cm\u000amedial to lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm anterior to posterior, and REMOVED_DATE cm superior to\u000ainferior). There is a long suture designating the lateral margin, and a short\u000asuture designating the superior margins. The specimen has been previously\u000ainked per the surgeon per pathology protocol (superior red, inferior green,\u000amedial orange, lateral yellow, anterior blue, and posterior black). There is a\u000aneedle localization wire in placed, which enters through the lateral aspect of\u000athe specimen, exits through the superior posterior aspect of the specimen. The\u000aspecimen is serially sectioned. The cut surface is tan/yellow and homogenous\u000awith focal areas of dense white fibrous tissue constituting approximately 80%\u000aof the breast parenchyma. Within the fibrous tissue is a silver metallic clip.\u000aNo discrete lesions or previously biopsy sites are grossly identified. The\u000aspecimen is submitted in its entirety.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross sections, block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID to include metallic clip, 1\u000afrag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aPlease note that the metallic clip corresponds to the specimen received\u000aradiograph.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aSEK/ajb\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Kirstine Yung-Ting Oh M.D., Electronically signed on\u000a2/21/2008\u000a[report_end]
