VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aKRANE, JEFFREY, FRED, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by KRANE,JEFFREY FRED,M.D.,PH.D.\u000a1) RIGHT BREAST, NEEDLE DIRECTED WIRE LOCALIZATION BIOPSY:\u000aPHYLLODES TUMOR (2.5 cm).\u000aStroma is mildly hypercellular with no significant cytologic atypia.\u000aNo stromal overgrowth.\u000aMitoses number up to 12 per 10 HPF.\u000aTumor is well circumscribed.\u000aTumor extends to the lateral edge of this specimen (but see specimen 2\u000abelow).\u000aAnterior, deep, superior, inferior, and medial margins are free of tumor.\u000aResidual breast shows epithelial hyperplasia and calcification.\u000aNOTE:\u000aPhyllodes tumors with this constellation of features are unlikely to\u000ametastasize, but the possibility of local recurrence should be considered. The\u000acase was reviewed by Dr. S. Schnitt of Breast Pathology.\u000a2) SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "RIGHT BREAST, TISSUE, NEW LATERAL MARGIN":\u000aBenign breast tissue negative for tumor.\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia.\u000aPrior biopsy site.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 72 year old female with abnormal mammo - right breast.\u000aOperation: Right needle directed breast biopsy.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Right needle directed breast tissue, stitch marking short\u000asuperior, long lateral, to mammo @10:46.\u000a2. Right breast tissue, new lateral margin, suture on new margin.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Mass in specimen. JL\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by BARRY,MARC,M.B.,B.CH.,B.A.O.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number. The specimen is received with specimen mammogram of\u000aspecimen #1 showing mass in specimen.\u000aSpecimen #1, labeled "right needle directed breast tissue", consists of a\u000afragment of fibrofatty tissue (5 x 5 x 2 cm) with one localization needle and a\u000ashort and long suture. The specimen is inked by the surgeon per pathology\u000aprotocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue;\u000asuperior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange.\u000aSectioning shows a cavity (2.5 x REMOVED_DATE x 1 cm) filled with a white/tan, papillary\u000aproliferation. This lies within REMOVED_DATE cm of posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of superior\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm of inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of anterior margin, 1 cm from medial\u000amargin, and focally extending to lateral edge of specimen. The specimen is\u000asampled to include majority of mass and all margins.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  right breast tissue, 12 frags, RSS.\u000aSpecimen #2, labeled "right breast new lateral margin, stitch on new margin",\u000aconsists of a fragment of fibrofatty tissue (3.5 x 3 x 2 cm) with a stitch on\u000aone aspect. This aspect is inked yellow and the opposite aspect is inked\u000ablack. Sectioning through this fragment of tissue shows fibrosis and focal\u000ahemorrhage. Five representative sections taken for microscopic examination.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  right lateral margin, 5 frags, RSS.\u000amab\u000aReports to: IGLEHART, JAMES, DIRK M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN\u000a[report_end]
