VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, mastectomy with regional lymph nodes\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: MEHRA GOLSHAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Shakti Ramkissoon, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Jane E. Brock, M.B., B.S., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aLEFT BREAST, SKIN-SPARING SIMPLE MASTECTOMY (PART A):\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia with Pagetoid spread, involving nipple,\u000alactiferous sinuses, and central upper breast.\u000aSclerosing papilloma.\u000aCalcification in association with benign epithelium.\u000aSkin with no significant pathologic change.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, SKIN-SPARING SIMPLE MASTECTOMY, & RIGHT SENTINEL LYMPH NODES\u000a(INCLUDING PARTS B, C, and D, AND FSA AND FSB):\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA, TWO FOCI\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aMETASTATIC CARCINOMA TO LYMPH NODES\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA\u000aMultifocal - Yes (see NOTE)\u000aLesion #1 in upper central breast:\u000aSize - REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aHistologic type - Mixed ductal and lobular\u000aHistologic grade (SBR) - II (Moderate) (6 to 7 points)\u000aTubules - < 10% (3 points)\u000aNuclear grade - High (3 points)\u000aMitotic counts - 1 point\u000aLesion #2 in lower inner quadrant:\u000aSize - REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aHistologic type - Mixed ductal and lobular\u000aHistologic grade (SBR) - II (Moderate) (6 to 7 points)\u000aTubules - < 10% (3 points)\u000aNuclear grade - Intermediate (2 points)\u000aMitotic counts - 1 point\u000aEIC - Negative\u000aLVI - Absent\u000aDermal LVI - Absent\u000aDermal LVI - Absent\u000aSkeletal muscle invasion - Absent\u000aFinal Margins (invasive and in situ)\u000aNegative (> REMOVED_DATE cm) - Deep\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU - Absent\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - Absent\u000aLYMPH NODES\u000aSentinel lymph nodes - Positive (3 H&E levels examined)\u000aNumber of positive nodes - 1\u000aNumber of nodes examined - 2\u000aTOTAL POSITIVE NODES (all specimens)- 1:2\u000aSize of largest metastatic focus - REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aNumber of nodes w/micrometastases- 1 (see NOTE)\u000aNumber of nodes w/isolated tumor cells- 1 (see NOTE)\u000aOTHER FINDINGS\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia associated with lesion #2\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia\u000aCore biopsy site (x2)\u000aCalcifications in normal epithelium and columnar cell change.\u000aAJCC Classification (6th edition) - REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDb REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDmi two foci\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER, PR, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for carcinoma.\u000aLESION #1 IN UPPER CENTRAL BREAST (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE-LOW (1%-2%)\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) NEGATIVE (1+)\u000aLESION #2 IN LOWER INNER QUADRANT (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE (100%)\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) NEGATIVE (0)\u000aNOTE: The two tumors are morphologically and immunophenotypically distinct.\u000aTumor #1 has a higher nuclear grade than Tumor #2. Both tumors have mixed\u000aductal and lobular features and both show membranous staining for E-cadherin.\u000aThe morphology of the tumor in lymph nodes is clearly glandular/ductal.\u000aSentinel lymph node #1 shows tumor cells present on 1 of 3 permanent H&E levels\u000a(<0.015 cm, approximately 150 cells), best classified as isolated tumor cells.\u000aSentinel lymph node #2 contains two clusters of tumor cells (up to REMOVED_DATE cm and\u000a0.03 cm each) present on 3 of 3 permanent H&E levels, best classified as a\u000amicrometastasis. On review of the frozen slides of both lymph nodes, in\u000aretrospect, isolated tumor cells are seen in lymph node #1 and tumor cells are\u000anot seen on the slide of lymph node #2.\u000aImmunohistochemical studies for estrogen receptor, progesterone receptor, and\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu were evaluated by manual morphometric analysis using the following\u000acriteria:\u000aHormone receptor analysis:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low > 0% - < 10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10%\u000aof tumor cells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor\u000acells but only a portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aEquivocal (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity in >30% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aExternal controls are evaluated and show appropriate Immunoreactivity.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 66 year old female with right breast multicentric breast cancer - two\u000adifferent tumors.\u000aOperation: Left breast simple mastectomy, right axilla sentinel node biopsy,\u000aright breast.\u000aOperative Findings: Not provided.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast high risk of cancer and right breast\u000amulticentric cancer.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) L breast simple mastectomy (skin sparing) - short/superior, long/lateral.\u000aB/2) R axilla lymph node #1 (fs @ 11:20).\u000aC/3) right axillary sentinel lymph node #2 (fs @11:58).\u000aD/4) right breast simple mastectomy (skin sparing) - short/superior,\u000along/lateral.\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "#2 - R AXILLA LYMPH NODE #1" (FSA):\u000aOne lymph node - negative for tumor.\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "#3 - RIGHT AXILLA SENTINEL LYMPH NODE #2" (FSB):\u000aOne lymph node - negative for tumor.\u000aOR Consultation by: Lucian Chirieac, M.D.\u000aResident: Samuel P. Wyche, M.D.\u000aThe senior physician certifies that he/she personally conducted a gross and/or\u000amicroscopic examination of the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed\u000athe rapid diagnos(es) related thereto.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in four parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart A, labeled "#1. Left breast simple mastectomy (skin sparing)", which\u000aconsists of a simple mastectomy specimen (1005 grams, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm)\u000awith a short suture designating superior surface and a long suture designating\u000athe lateral surface. The specimen includes a tan/white skin ellipse (14.5 x\u000a4.0 cm), which includes an unremarkable flattened nipple (1.5 cm in greatest\u000adimension). The deep aspect of the specimen is inked black and it is serially\u000asectioned to reveal predominantly yellow lobulated fibroadipose tissue (65%)\u000aand intervening areas of white fibrous tissue (35%). No gross lesions are\u000aidentified. The specimen is radiographed to reveal no mammographic lesions,\u000acalcifications or clips within the specimen. No lymph nodes are identified in\u000athe upper outer quadrant. Representative sections are submitted for analysis.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Upper outer quadrant, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Central upper region, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Upper outer quadrant, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lower inner quadrant, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Central lower region, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lower outer quadrant, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Central aspect, to include deep margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCES