VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Amend/Addenda\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: Esther Rhei M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-05-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000a********** Addended Report ***********\u000aResident: Paula C Abreu-e-Lima, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Susan Lester, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aLEFT BREAST EXCISION WIRE LOCALIZATION FOR A MASS AND AXILLARY NODE DISSECTION\u000a(TWO SPECIMENS):\u000aINVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA, DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, AND METASTATIC CARCINOMA\u000aTO A LYMPH NODE.\u000aSYNOPSIS:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA\u000aSize - REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aMultifocal - No\u000aHistologic Type - Ductal\u000aHistologic Grade (SBR) - II (Moderate)\u000aNuclear Grade - Intermediate\u000aEIC - Negative\u000aLymphovascular invasion - Absent\u000aDermal lymphatic invasion - N/A\u000aSkin invasion - N/A\u000aSkeletal muscle invasion - N/A\u000aFinal Margins (invasive)\u000aNegative (>0.3 cm) - Anterior, lateral, superior, inferior\u000aClose - Posterior (chest wall, REMOVED_DATE cm, focal\u000a(block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID)\u000aPositive (ink on carcinoma) - Medial (multifocal, blocks REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID)\u000a(see specimen #3, for new margin)\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU - Present\u000aTypes - Cribriform, micropapillary\u000aNuclear grade - Intermediate\u000aCalcifications in DCIS - Absent\u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - Present\u000aExtent of DCIS - DCIS is a minor component of the\u000ainvasive carcinoma.\u000aFinal Margins (DCIS)\u000aNegative (>0.3 cm) - All margins\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - Absent\u000aLYMPH NODES\u000aAxillary lymph nodes: - Positive\u000aNumber of positive nodes - 1\u000aNumber of nodes examined - 17\u000aTOTAL POSITIVE NODES (all specimens) - REMOVED_DATE \u000aSize of largest metastatic focus - REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aExtranodal extension - Absent\u000aOTHER FINDINGS\u000aCore biopsy site\u000aAJCC CLASSIFICATION (6th edition) - REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID pREMOVED_ACCESSION_IDa MX\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER/PR/HER-2) - Performed previously\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "MEDIAL SHAVE MARGIN":\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia.\u000aApocrine cysts.\u000aNOTE: No residual carcinoma identified.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 80-yr-old female with left breast mass, S/P core REMOVED_DATE \u000aOperation: (L) breast wire-localized lumpectomy + Level I + II ALND.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: (L) breast cancer.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000a#1 Left axillary lymph nodes\u000a#2 Left breast tissue; short stitch - superior, long stitch - lateral, whip\u000astitch on chest wall margin, to mammo @ 13:05\u000a#3 Medial shave margin, whip stitch on new margin\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in three parts, each labeled with the patient?s\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart A, labeled "Left axillary lymph nodes", consists of an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aportion of fibroadipose tissue, containing 17 lymph nodes, ranging from REMOVED_DATE to\u000a1.9 cm in greatest dimension. The largest lymph node is firm and grossly\u000apositive.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: A single, positive, lymph node, 2 bisected, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 2 lymph nodes, bisected, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Multiple lymph nodes, differently inked, multi frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, labeled "2. Left breast tissue, short suture - superior, long -\u000alateral with stitch on chest wall margin", consists of a breast excision\u000aspecimen (5.1 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), containing three sutures (long designated\u000alateral, short designated superior, whip stitch designated chest wall margin).\u000aThe specimen is inked per surgeon according to the pathology protocol for the\u000aevaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red;\u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. The accompanying specimen\u000aradiograph shows an ill-defined, dense mass, penetrated by a single,\u000alocalization wire. The localization wire is received separate from the\u000aspecimen. The specimen was serially sectioned from superior to inferior to\u000areveal a grey/white, lobulated mass (2.1 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which grossly abuts\u000athe medial margin and extends to within REMOVED_DATE cm of the posterior and inferior,\u000a0.5 cm of the superior, REMOVED_DATE cm of the anterior and REMOVED_DATE cm of the lateral\u000amargin. The specimen is entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Mass to closest medial and posterior margins, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Mass to medial, posterior and inferior margins, 1 frag,\u000aESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Mass to closest inferior margin, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Additional inferior and lateral margins, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Superior, medial and inferior margins, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Posterior, lateral and anterior margins, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Superior margin, multi frags, ESS.\u000aPart C, labeled "3. Left breast medial shave margin, whip stitch on new\u000amargin", consists of two fragments of yellow/tan, fibroadipose tissue (4.0 x\u000a1.6 x REMOVED_DATE and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), both containing two whip stitches, one of\u000athem loosely attached. Per surgeon, by phone, two fragments of tissue were\u000asent. Within the larger fragment is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm fibrous area, which\u000agrossly abuts the new margin (inked black). However, no obvious masses are\u000agrossly identified.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Smaller fragment, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Larger fragment, fibrous area in cassette 8, multi frags,\u000aESS.\u000apal/MMM\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Paula C Abreu-e-Lima M.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a5/6/2005\u000aSurgical Addendum: (5/11/05)\u000aFISH was performed by USLABS using the PathVysion HER-2 DNA Probe Kit with the\u000afollowing results (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aResult: NOT AMPLFIEID\u000aThe Her-2/cen 17 ratio = REMOVED_DATE \u000aThe average of Her-2/neu copies per cell: REMOVED_DATE \u000aThe average of cen 17 copies per cell: REMOVED_DATE \u000aThe cutoff point for assessing HER-2/neu gene amplification is a ratio of REMOVED_DATE \u000aAddendum by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aAddendum #1 by Deborah A Dillon M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
