VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aODZE, ROBERT, DANIEL, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by ODZE,ROBERT DANIEL,M.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST, RE-EXCISION OF POSTERIOR, INFERIOR, AND MEDIAL MARGINS:\u000aBenign breast tissue with fibrosis, fat necrosis, foreign body giant cell\u000areaction to polarizable foreign material, and granulation tissue\u000aconsistent with healing prior biopsy cavity.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: None given.\u000aOperation: L breast wide local excision.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: L breast phyllodes tumor.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Re-excision of posterior, inferior & medial margins,\u000aL breast, sutures: short superior, long lateral.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by WU,DAVID,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number\u000aand "re-excision posterior, inferior and medial margins, short superior, long\u000alateral", and consists of a breast re-excision specimen (3.9 cm anterior to\u000aposterior x REMOVED_DATE cm medial-lateral x REMOVED_DATE cm superior-inferior). The specimen on\u000aits anterior portion is surfaced by a roughened fibrotic cavity consistent with\u000aprior excisional biopsy cavity site (4.0 cm medial-lateral x REMOVED_DATE cm\u000asuperior-inferior x REMOVED_DATE cm anterior-posterior). The lining of the cavity is\u000aroughened with focal areas of dense fibrous tissue with focal hemorrhage. No\u000adefinitive tumor is grossly identified. The remaining aspects of this specimen\u000aare composed of yellow fibroadipose tissue present at all margins. The\u000aspecimen comes oriented by the surgeon with a short stitch designating\u000asuperior, long lateral. The specimen is inked by the pathologist per pathology\u000aprotocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue;\u000asuperior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. Serial\u000asectioning of the specimen from medial to lateral reveals dense fibrous tissue\u000awith focal hemorrhage extending from the biopsy cavity to within REMOVED_DATE cm of the\u000amedial, REMOVED_DATE cm of the inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm of the posterior, REMOVED_DATE cm of the\u000asuperior, REMOVED_DATE cm of the lateral, and less than REMOVED_DATE cm of the anterior inked\u000amargin. It is not definitive that the fibrotic areas are residual gross tumor,\u000aas these areas may be biopsy site changes. The specimen is composed of\u000apossibly\u000a80% adipose tissue, the remainder fibrous tissue. The specimen is serially\u000asubmitted entirely from medial to lateral.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  medial perpendicular margin, 9 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  medial to lateral sequentially, entirely, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  lateral perpendicular margin, 4 frags, ESS.\u000adwu\u000aReports to: MATORY, YVEDT, L. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
