VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY(IES)\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aCONNOLLY, JAMES, L., M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by CONNOLLY,JAMES L.,M.D.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, 5:00, 14 G ULTRASOUND GUIDED CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY FOR A PALPABLE\u000aMASS:\u000aINVASIVE PLEOMORPHIC LOBULAR CARCINOMA, measuring at least REMOVED_DATE cm. in size.\u000aThe carcinoma is poorly differentiated (modified Bloom Richardson\u000aGrade III/III).\u000aNo lymphatic or vascular invasion is seen in this specimen\u000aNo in situ carcinoma is present in this limited specimen.\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for invasive carcinoma (block 1):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) POSITIVE (3+)\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000ainvasive carcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but\u000aonly a portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity\u000ain >10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 70 year old female with new right nipple inversion and palpable\u000aperiareolar mass at 5:00.\u000aOperation: 14g U/S breast core biopsy\u000aOperative findings: Cores obtained\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Suspected carcinoma\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Cores (1 blue cassette)\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by SAPP,HEIDI L.,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit\u000anumber, and "right breast", in a blue cassette, and consists of multiple, soft,\u000afragmented, yellow to white tissue cores (1.7 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate).\u000aMicro 1: Multi frags, ESS.\u000adfi\u000aReports to: FROST, ELISABETH, PEPPERELL M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY(IES)\u000a[report_end]
