VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID SENTINEL LYMPH NODE\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aGLICKMAN, JONATHAN, NEIL, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by GLICKMAN,JONATHAN NEIL,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aRIGHT BREAST SIMPLE MASTECTOMY AND SENTINEL NODE BIOPSY:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA.\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU.\u000aMETASTATIC CARCINOMA TO LYMPH NODES.\u000aSYNOPSIS:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA\u000aSize - REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aMultifocal? - No\u000aHistologic Type - Lobular\u000aHistologic Grade (SBR) - III (poor)\u000aNuclear Grade - High\u000aEIC - Negative\u000aLymphovascular invasion - Absent\u000aDermal lymphatic invasion - Absent\u000aSkin invasion - Absent\u000aSkeletal muscle invasion - N/A\u000aFinal Margins (invasive) -\u000aNegative (no ink on tumor) - Deep\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aTypes - Solid\u000aNuclear grade - Intermediate\u000aCalcifications in DCIS - Present\u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - Absent\u000aMicroinvasion (<0.1cm) - Absent\u000aExtent of DCIS - DCIS is present as a minor component of\u000athe invasive carcinoma\u000aFinal Margins (DCIS) -\u000aNegative (>0.3 cm) - Deep.\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - Absent\u000aLYMPH NODES - Positive.\u000aSentinel lymph nodes (3 H&E levels examined) - Positive (see NOTE)\u000aNumber of positive nodes - 3\u000aNumber of nodes examined - 4\u000aTOTAL POSITIVE NODES (sentinel + axillary) - REMOVED_DATE \u000aOTHER FINDINGS\u000aCysts\u000aApocrine metaplasia\u000aAJCC CLASSIFICATION - REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID pREMOVED_ACCESSION_IDa MX\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER/PR/HER-2) - Performed previously\u000aNOTE: Immunohistochemical stains of the sentinel lymph nodes (blocks 1 & 2) for\u000acytokeratins (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.2) reveal numerous (10-50 cells per lymph node)\u000aindividual tumor cells in the subcapsular sinuses of three (3) of four (4)\u000asentinel lymph nodes.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 70 year old female with right nipple inversion. Mammogram and U/S\u000ashowed 15 mm mass, hypoechoic at lower inner subareola. Core biopsy\u000a6/21 showed inverted pleomorphic lobular carcinoma.\u000aOperation: Right simple mastectomy and sentinel lymph node mapping, ? right\u000aaxillary lymph node dissection\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast cancer\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1) Sentinel node right (hot and blue)\u000a#2) Right breast stitch marking short superior, long lateral, bow tie at\u000aaxilla.\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "#1. SENTINEL NODE RIGHT HOT AND BLUE", (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID AND REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aLymph node with no tumor seen.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by LIN,JONATHAN H.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart one, labeled "#1. sentinel node right hot and blue", consists of one\u000ayellow/pink soft tissue (5.5 x 4 x REMOVED_DATE cm). Four candidate lymph nodes are\u000aidentified, the largest measuring REMOVED_DATE cm. The entire lymph nodes are submitted\u000aas REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aMicro 1: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID remnant, 2 frags, ESS\u000aMicro 2: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID remnant, 2 frags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  remainder of specimen, 5 frags, ESS\u000aPart two, labeled "#2. right breast, stitch marking short superior, long\u000alateral, bow tie at axilla", consists of an 890g right modified radical\u000amastectomy specimen (15 x 24 x REMOVED_DATE cm) with axillary tail (10 x 8 x 3 cm).\u000aThere is an attached white/tan skin ellipse (18 x 7 cm) with a central inverted\u000anipple (1.2 x REMOVED_DATE cm). The skin in the lower inner quadrant is colored blue\u000aconsistent with the sentinel node procedure. No scars are identified. A firm\u000awhite mass is immediately deep to the nipple in the lower inner quadrant (3 x 4\u000ax 3 cm). The tumor is fixed to the dermis and 3 cm from the deep black inked\u000amargin. The remainder of the breast parenchyma consists of unremarkable yellow\u000aadipose tissue interspersed with white fibrous tissue and small cysts of\u000agreatest dimension (0.3 cm). No lymph nodes were identified in the axillary\u000atail.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  tumor with skin, 4 frags, RSS\u000aMicro 10: tumor, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 11: black inked margin tissue closest to tumor, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 12: UOQ, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 13: UIQ, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 14: LOQ, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 15: LIQ, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 16: nipple, 5 frags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  possible lymph nodes, 12 frags, ESS\u000ajhl\u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: SENTINEL LYMPH NODE\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY - PARTIAL OR SIMPLE\u000a[report_end]
