GS\u000aColumnar cell change\u000aApocrine cysts\u000aSclerosing adenosis\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia\u000aCalcifications in benign epithelium\u000aAJCC Classification (6th edition) - REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDc Nx MX.\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER, PR, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) - Pending\u000aNOTE:\u000aDr. Rhei was notified by E-mail, on REMOVED_DATE  at 12 pm, by Dr. E. Morgan.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 42 yo premenopausal female whose REMOVED_DATE mammograms demonstrate grouped\u000acalcifications RUIQ & RLIQ. RLIQ also noted for complex cystic lesion\u000acorresponding to Ca++. Core biopsy revealed ALH that was found incidentally\u000awith associated Ca++. MRI demonstrates a REMOVED_DATE cm, area of enhancement 3:00 axis\u000apossibly correlating with the UIQ Ca++. Pt not amenable to core biopsy. R Ca++\u000arec for WL + excision with question of a second WL excision for area of MRI\u000aenhancement if it does not correlate with the Ca++.\u000aOperation: R breast mammographic WL + excision possible R breast MRI WL +\u000aexcision.\u000aOperative Findings: Not provided.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal R mammogram, abnormal R MRI.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA. Right breast tissue (mammo - short = superior, long = lateral, whip = chest\u000awall resection).\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000aSpecimen with abnormal Ca++ + large MR evident mass. Called OR/DG.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh and labeled with the patient's name and unit\u000anumber, and "#1. Right breast tissue, short superior, long lateral, whipstitch\u000achest wall margin", and consists of a breast excision specimen (superior to\u000ainferior REMOVED_DATE cm, medial to lateral REMOVED_DATE cm, anterior to posterior REMOVED_DATE cm)\u000acomposed predominantly of fibrous tissue. No masses are grossly identified.\u000aThere is a circumscribed area of fibrosis (1.5 cm) with cyst (0.2 cm) abutting\u000athe inferior margin. A cluster of cysts (0.5 cm), is identified within REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom the medial margin. Adjacent to the cluster of cysts, is a complex cyst\u000a(0.4 x REMOVED_DATE cm), extending to the medial margin. A cluster of calcifications\u000a(0.3 cm in greatest dimension) is located near the superior tip. A wire is\u000apresent in specimen, but is distorted. The specimen is sectioned from inferior\u000ato superior and the entire specimen is submitted for histologic evaluation.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Inferior margin, radially sectioned, multi frags each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Circumscribed area of fibrosis with cyst, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Bisected slice, one frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Bisected slice (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID with cluster of cyst), one frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Bisected slice (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID with cluster of cyst), one frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Bisected slice (including complex cyst), two frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Next serial section, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Clustered calcifications, one frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Superior margin, radially sectioned, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aEM/ajb\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Lucian R Chirieac M.D., Electronically signed on\u000a8/25/2007\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: (8/30/07)\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for invasive carcinoma and DCIS (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE - LOW\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) NEGATIVE (0)\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000ainvasive carcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low > 0% - < 10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor cells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but only a\u000aportion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+):Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in >10% of\u000atumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+):Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in >30% of\u000atumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aExternal controls are evaluated and show appropriate Immunoreactivity.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aAddendum #1 by James L Connolly M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
