VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: JULIE L JONES M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Ann K Folkins, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Andrea L Richardson, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR CALCIFICATIONS AND A CLIP:\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia, focal.\u000aColumnar hyperplasia.\u000aBiopsy cavity with repair reaction.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: None specified.\u000aOperation: None specified.\u000aOperative Findings: None specified.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: None specified.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) Mammo --> R breast wire localized excision; short - superior; long -\u000alateral.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Core Bx tissue marker, wire and Ca++s adjacent to prior core bx\u000asite in specimen. - C. Denison, MD.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number\u000aand "#1. R breast wire localized excision, short superior, long lateral", and\u000aconsists of an irregular portion of fibrofatty tissue (4.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm),\u000awith a long suture designating lateral, and a short suture designating\u000asuperior. The specimen is received previously inked per pathology protocol as\u000aanterior blue, posterior black, superior red, inferior green, lateral yellow\u000aand medial orange. Please note that a needle-localization wire is received\u000awithin the same container, and not within the specimen, as displayed on the\u000aaccompanying radiograph. The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a\u000acavity, consistent with a biopsy cavity (1.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000aanterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin, and\u000a2.0 cm from the medial margin. The cavity contains a surgical clip, as\u000adisplayed on the accompanying radiograph. The remaining cut surface displays\u000a98% yellow lobulated adipose tissue, and 2% white fibrous tissue, with no\u000aadditional masses or lesions identified. The specimen is sequentially\u000asubmitted in its entirety.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, radially, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential bisected cross section, with the cavity, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential bisected cross sections, with the cavity containing the\u000asurgical clip, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential bisected cross sections, containing the cavity, 1 frag\u000aeach, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential bisected cross sections, containing the cavity, 1 frag\u000aeach, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross sections, containing the possible area of\u000acalcifications as displayed on the accompanying radiograph.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross sections, containing the possible area of\u000acalcifications as displayed on the accompanying radiograph.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross sections, displaying the possible area of\u000acalcifications as displayed on the accompanying radiograph.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin, radially, multi frags, ESS.\u000aCP/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Andrea L Richardson M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a11/30/2007\u000a[report_end]
