VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID SOFT TISSUE TUMOR EXTENSIVE RESECTION\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aGLICKMAN, JONATHAN, NEIL, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by GLICKMAN,JONATHAN NEIL,M.D.,PH.D.\u000a#1. LEFT BREAST AND CHEST WALL MUSCLE (2350G):\u000aEXTRASKELETAL OSTEOSARCOMA, osteoblastic type, high grade (grade 3), (6.2\u000acm), involving breast parenchyma.\u000aMitoses number up to 68 per 10 HPFs.\u000aExtensive necrosis is present (approximately 60% of tumor).\u000aA separate tumor nodule (0.9 cm) is present at the posterior margin,\u000ainvading skeletal muscle (but see below).\u000aTumor is present less than REMOVED_DATE cm from the edge designated as the sternal\u000amargin, but is surrounded by a thin fibrous capsule.\u000aAll other margins (inferior, superior, medial, lateral) are free of tumor\u000a(greater than REMOVED_DATE cm).\u000aTumor is present less than REMOVED_DATE cm from the skin surface at the previous\u000abiopsy site.\u000a#2. LEFT AXILLARY SKIN:\u000aSkin and breast tissue with no tumor present.\u000a#3. ADDITIONAL MARGIN:\u000aFragments of skeletal muscle with no tumor present.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Left breast sarcoma.\u000aOperation: Left radical mastectomy.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1 - left breast and chest wall muscle (fs).\u000a#2 - left axillary skin.\u000a#3 - additional margin surrounding abdominal wall nodule.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by CHANG,PRISCILLA S.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe first part, labeled "left breast and chest wall muscle", consists of a 2350\u000amastectomy specimen (32 cm from medial to lateral, 23 cm from superior to\u000ainferior, and REMOVED_DATE cm from anterior to posterior) with a skin ellipse (29 x 17 x\u000a5 cm) and unremarkable nipple (1.2 cm). There is a raised nodule/cyst (0.9 x\u000a0.7 cm) located REMOVED_DATE cm from the nipple in the lower/outer quadrant. Deep to\u000athe nodule is a firm white/tan/yellow mass (6.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with a central\u000aarea of cavitation with abundant necrosis and hemorrhage. The tumor grossly\u000aappears to be approximately 60% necrotic. An area of the specimen was\u000adesignated by the surgeon as the sternal margin, which is a smooth fascial\u000aplane, and inked blue. The superior portion of the specimen is inked red, the\u000ainferior portion is inked green, the medial portion is inked orange, the\u000alateral portion is inked yellow, and the posterior portion is inked black.\u000aThe tumor is less than REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin and from the area\u000adesignated as the sternal margin but does not involve the fascial surface. The\u000atumor is located REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin.\u000aA portion of skeletal muscle is present at the posterior portion of the\u000aspecimen (13.8 x REMOVED_DATE cm). There is a separate tan/white nodule (0.9 x REMOVED_DATE x\u000a0.6 cm) located at the posterior/inferior portion of the specimen, associated\u000awith the skeletal muscle. The separate nodule is located 2 cm away from the\u000aprimary tumor, and is grossly at the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the sternal\u000aarea, REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin, is at the\u000aposterior margin, and at least 10 cm away from the lateral and superior\u000amargins. The main tumor mass does not invade into the skeletal muscle.\u000aRepresentative portions of the tumor were submitted for EM, cytogenetics, and\u000asnap-freezing. Gross photographs of the specimen are taken.\u000aNo lymph nodes are identified in the lateral portion of the specimen.\u000aRepresentative sections are submitted.\u000aMicro #1+2: Representative sections of tumor, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro #3+4: Tumor and skin, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro #5+6: Tumor and closest approach to blue and black margins, 2 frags,\u000aESS.\u000aMicro #7: Additional nodule and posterior margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro #8+9: Medial margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro #10: Inferior margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro #11: Lateral margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro #12+13: Superior margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro #14: Nipple, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aThe second part, labeled "#2 - left axilla skin", consists of two skin\u000aellipses. The first fragment consists of skin ellipse (15.6 x REMOVED_DATE cm) excised\u000ato a maximal depth of REMOVED_DATE cm. The second fragment consists of a skin ellipse\u000a(12.5 x REMOVED_DATE cm) excised to a maximal depth of REMOVED_DATE cm. No lesions are grossly\u000aidentified. Representative sections are submitted.\u000aMicro #15: Representative section of first skin ellipse, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro #16: Representative section of second skin ellipse, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aThe third part, labeled "#3 - additional margin surrounding abdominal wall\u000anodule", consists of eight fragments of skeletal muscle, which appear grossly\u000aunremarkable. The specimen is entirely submitted.\u000aMicro #17-21: Additional margin, multiple frags, ESS.\u000apsc/\u000aReports to: BERTAGNOLLI, MONICA, MARIE M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: SOFT TISSUE TUMOR EXTENSIVE RESECTION\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SKIN- OTHER THAN CYST, TAG OR DEBRIDEMENT\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN\u000a[report_end]
