VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Amend/Addenda\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: DIANE C LOCKHART M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-06-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000a********** Addended Report ***********\u000aResident: Michael H Roh, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Robert D Odze, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, EXCISION WIRE-LOCALIZATION FOR CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aSYNOPSIS:\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aTypes - cribriform\u000aNuclear grade - low\u000aCalcifications in DCIS - present\u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - absent\u000aMicroinvasion (<0.1cm) - absent\u000aExtent of DCIS\u000aSize (max area in one block) - REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aNumber of blocks:total - 1:13 cm\u000aFinal Margins (DCIS)\u000aNegative (>0.3 cm) - superior, inferior, posterior,\u000alateral\u000aVery close (<0.1 cm) - anteromedial\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - absent\u000aOTHER FINDINGS\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia\u000aCore biopsy site\u000aColumnar cell changes\u000aSclerosing adenosis\u000aFibroadenomatoid changes\u000aCalcifications in benign epithelium\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER/PR/HER-2) - pending\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 42 y/o woman with microcalcifications R on screening mammo.\u000aS/P core stereotactic REMOVED_DATE  Positive ADH.\u000aOperation: R needle localization breast biopsy.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: R abnl mammo.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) R breast tissue-mammo.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Clip in specimen - Meyer.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "R breast needle localization", and consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aexcision of fibroadipose tissue. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol\u000afor the evaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red;\u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. A localizing wire enters the\u000aspecimen at the superior aspect and traverses inferiorly. The accompanying\u000aradiograph demonstrates the localizing wire in place adjacent to the surgical\u000aclip. Sectioning demonstrates a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm, cavitary lesion filled\u000awith tan/white, amorphous material, consistent with patient's prior core\u000abiopsy. The remaining specimen is comprised predominantly of tan/white,\u000airregular-appearing, focally hemorrhagic fibrous tissue extending to all\u000amargins, with diffuse, scattered, dilated ducts filled with a thick, tan/yellow\u000afluid. There are no obvious masses, lesions, or other abnormalities, grossly.\u000aThe entire specimen is submitted, sequentially from superior to inferior.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Entire specimen from superior to inferior, multi frags, ESS.\u000aDB/mmm\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Robert D Odze M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM (7/20/06):\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for DCIS (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) NEGATIVE (0)\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000acarcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but only\u000aa portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in >10%\u000aof tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in\u000a>10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aAddendum #1 by Deborah A Dillon M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
