VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: BETH ANN LESNIKOSKI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Oname O. Burlingame, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Andrea L Richardson, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA) LEFT BREAST WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION:\u000aFibroadenoma (0.6 cm) with associated core biopsy site changes (see note).\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy.\u000aB) RIGHT PERIAREOLAR SKIN:\u000aSkin with no significant pathologic change.\u000aC) LEFT BREAST, ADDITIONAL ANTERIOR-MEDIAL MARGIN FOR CLIP:\u000aBenign breast tissue\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy.\u000aD) RIGHT BREAST DOUBLE WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION:\u000aNo invasive or in situ carcinoma is present (see NOTE).\u000aNo lymphovascular invasion is seen.\u000aThe margins are negative.\u000aHistologic evidence of a treated tumor bed is not definitively seen and the\u000aS-clip was abutting the deep margin of the specimen. Clinical correlation is\u000aadvised to ensure that the tumor bed was completely excised.\u000aNote: The patient presented with a palpable 4 cm breast mass in the upper outer\u000aquadrant posteriorly (4 cm x 3 cm x REMOVED_DATE cm on imaging) which on core biopsy was\u000ashown to be a poorly differentiated ductal carcinoma (see REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID). The site\u000awas marked with an s shaped clip. A second site within the right breast\u000asuspicious on imaging was biopsied pre chemotherapy. This lesion measured REMOVED_DATE \u000acm and disappeared on biopsy (?Cyst) when a knot shaped clip was placed.\u000aPathology revealed benign fibrous tissue (see REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID). A sentinel lymph\u000anode was sampled and found to be negative for carcinoma (see REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aPost chemotherapy, an MRI scan failed to identify a residual mass lesion, but\u000afound areas of clumped enhancement (complete clinical response).\u000aOn gross examination of the specimen, dense fibrous tissue was identified\u000ameasuring REMOVED_DATE cm x REMOVED_DATE cm x REMOVED_DATE cm with the s shaped clip present at the edge\u000aof this area, abutting the posterior margin. Histologically this corresponds to\u000aan area dense normal-appearing fibrous tissue with no evidence of invasive or\u000ain situ carcinoma. The area of the knot clip site is identified and lies within\u000aan area of dense fibrous breast tissue.\u000aThis corresponds to a Miller-Payne score of 5 (complete pathological response).\u000aAn RCB score can not be assigned in the absence of a lymph node dissection.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 28 y. o. female with locally advanced R breast CA - S/P neoadjuvant\u000aRx with probably fibroadenoma in L breast.\u000aOperation: None given.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: R breast CA, L breast mass (ILLEGIBLE).\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) Left breast mass: Stitches - short --> superior; long --> lateral;\u000alateral stitch also marks fibroadenoma; to mammo.\u000aB/2) Right peri-areolar skin.\u000aC/3) Additional anterior medial margin for clip, L breast; stitch - long\u000a-->lateral; short --> superior.\u000aD/4) Right lateral quadrantectomy with 2 wires; to FS Rm for re-mammo and\u000apathology weight measurement.\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000aVague opacity in specimen; no clip (MRI lesion originally) - C. Denison, MD.\u000aSpecimen #2, left; no clip visible. - C. Denison, MD.\u000aClips and wires are visualized with specimen.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aNote: Incomplete dictation.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in four parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart A, "#1. Left breast mass", consists of one fragment of tan/yellow\u000afibroadipose tissue (2.8 cm superior - inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm anterior - posterior,\u000a1.2 cm medial - lateral) with a short stitch indicating superior, a long stitch\u000aindicating lateral and marking a fibroadenoma, and a localization wire that\u000aenters specimen at the mid anterior aspect and exits the specimen at the\u000asuperior/posterior aspect. The specimen is sectioned parallel to the wire\u000asuperior to inferior. The specimen consists of approximately 40% fibrous\u000atissue and 60% adipose tissue. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol\u000afor the evaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red;\u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. No discrete masses or lesions\u000aare identified. The specimen is received with a radiograph and radiograph\u000areport stating that there is a vague opacity but no clip in the specimen. The\u000aentire specimen is submitted for histologic examination.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Superior margin, 5 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Serial section superior to inferior, 2 frags each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Inferior margin, 7 frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, "#2. Right periareolar skin", consists of an unoriented, tan/white,\u000aunremarkable skin ellipse (8.1 x REMOVED_DATE cm, REMOVED_DATE cm deep). The deep aspect is\u000ainked blue. The entire specimen is submitted for histologic examination.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Tips, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Serial sections, REMOVED_DATE frags each, ESS.\u000aPart C, "#3. Additional anterior-medial margin for clip - L breast", consists\u000aof one fragment of tan/yellow fibroadipose tissue (3.2 cm superior-inferior,\u000a1.5 cm anterior-posterior, REMOVED_DATE cm medial-lateral) with two orienting sutures\u000a(short=superior and long=lateral). The specimen is inked per pathology\u000aprotocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue;\u000asuperior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. The specimen is\u000asectioned from superior to inferior, and consists of approximately 90% adipose\u000atissue and 10% fibrous tissue. The specimen is received with a radiograph and\u000aradiograph report stating that no clip is visible in the specimen. The entire\u000aspecimen is submitted for histologic examination.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Superior margin, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Serial sections, REMOVED_DATE frags each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Inferior margin, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aPart D, "#4. Right lateral quadrantectomy with two wires", consists of a breast\u000aexcision of specimen (219-g, REMOVED_DATE cm anterior-posterior, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000asuperior-inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm medial-lateral) with two needle localization wires.\u000aWire #1, enters at the superior region of the anterior margin and does not exit\u000athe specimen. Wire #2, enters at the inferior region of the anterior margin\u000aand exits the specimen at the mid posterior margin. Wire #2 is posterior and\u000ainferior to Wire #1. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the\u000aevaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red;\u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange.\u000aA tan/white, firm, relatively well-circumscribed likely tumor bed (4.7 cm\u000amedial-lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm anterior-posterior, REMOVED_DATE cm superior-inferior) abuts the\u000aposterior margin and is REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom the inferior , and REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margins. Abutting the tumor\u000abed medially is an area of fibrous tissue and recent hemorrhage (2.5 cm\u000amedial-lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm anterior-posterior, REMOVED_DATE cm superior-inferior) through\u000awhich localization Wire #2 passed. An S-shaped clip is located in the tumor\u000abed near the posterior margin. An area of tan/white, rubbery tissue (8.0\u000amedial-lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm anterior-posterior, 2,1 cm superior-inferior) containing\u000aa knot-shaped clip and clip site is REMOVED_DATE cm from the tumor bed, abuts the\u000aposterior, lateral, medial and superior margins, and is REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000aanterior margin. The remainder of the specimen is approximately 80% tan/yellow\u000aadipose tissue. The specimen is received with three radiographs and a\u000aradiograph report stating that there are two clips and two wires visualized in\u000athe specimen. The radiographs show a knot-shaped clip located superiorly and\u000aanteriorly near Wire #1 and an S-shaped clip that is located near Wire #2. An\u000aadditional radiograph taken of the sectioned specimen shows that the S-shaped\u000aclip abuts the posterior margin in the area of the tumor bed. The specimen was\u000areviewed with Dr. Jane Brock, Fellow, Breast Pathology.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Complete cross section of specimen medial to lateral to include\u000agreatest dimension of tumor bed, wire localization area #2, and clip site (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID),\u000a1 frag each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Closest anterior margin, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Closest inferior margin to include tumor bed, REMOVED_DATE frags each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Tissue between tumor bed and region of wire localization #1,\u000aserial sections inferior to superior, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Area of localization wire #1 to include clip site (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) and\u000aclosest superior margin to tumor bed, REMOVED_DATE frags each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Superior most aspect of tumor bed, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Additional medial margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Additional lateral margin to include tumor bed, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aOOB/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-07-REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Andrea L Richardson M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a9/28/2007\u000a[report_end]
