esh, in two parts, each labeled with the patients\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart A, "#1 Right breast tissue - short stitch superior, long stitch lateral,\u000awhip stitch deep margin", consists of a single breast excision specimen (3.2 cm\u000afrom medial to lateral x REMOVED_DATE cm from inferior to superior x REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000aanterior to posterior). There is a wire entering the superior/lateral/anterior\u000aaspect of the specimen and exiting the superior/lateral/posterior aspect of the\u000aspecimen. The specimen is serially sectioned from lateral to medial such that\u000alateral is slice 1. The specimen is received already having been inked by the\u000asurgeon per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black;\u000aanterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. The\u000awire is passing between slices 1 and 2. Serial sectioning reveals an\u000aill-defined, firm, tan/white area (2.2 cm in greatest dimension). The medial\u000aend of the specimen is slice 6. The specimen is entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, slice 1, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 2, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 3, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 4, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 5, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 6, medial margin, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, "#2 Lateral shave margin - whip stitch new margin", consists of a\u000asingle fragment of tan/pink fibroadipose tissue (5.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). There is\u000aa whip stitch on one surface denoting the new margin. This surface is inked\u000ablue. The opposite surface is inked black. The specimen is serially sectioned\u000aand entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Fibroadipose tissue, multiple frags, ESS.\u000aROH/elw\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted 