medial (block #22)\u000aThe remainder of the Surgical Pathology report is unchanged.\u000aSECOND SURGICAL ADDENDUM REMOVED_DATE  DR. SUSAN LESTER\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed with the following results for DCIS\u000a(block 6):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu POSITIVE (3+)\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 55-year-old postmenopausal female, not on hormones. Status post\u000a2/11/03 left breast core biopsy of left breast sites for evaluation\u000aof a mammographic mass with pathology demonstrating benign findings\u000awithout a mass forming lesion REMOVED_DATE  U/S demonstrates a REMOVED_DATE cm mass\u000afor which biopsy is recommended.\u000aOperation: Left breast wire localization excision x 2.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal mammogram.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Left breast mass, short/superior, long/lateral,\u000awhipstitch on deep margin.\u000aWires and mass in specimen. Dr. Smith.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by YOU,MINGJIAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "#1, left breast mass", and measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm, and has two (2)\u000alocalization wires. The surgeon placed short stitch, long stitch and whipstitch\u000ato indicate the superior, lateral, and deep margins, respectively. The\u000aspecimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins:\u000aposterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral\u000a= yellow; medial = orange. The specimen is sectioned revealing approximately\u000a10% of yellow-tan adipose tissue and approximately 20% of white-tan fibrous\u000atissue. The remainder of the tissue is a white-tan semisolid mass (4.8 x REMOVED_DATE x\u000a3.0 cm). The mass is less than REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000athe inferior margin, less than REMOVED_DATE cm from anterior margin, less than REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom the posterior margin, less than REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin and REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom the medial margin. There are focal hemorrhagic areas (0.3 cm in greatest\u000adimension) in the mass. No other nodules or lesions suspicious for tumor are\u000aidentified.\u000aMicro 1: mass, superior margin, medial marign, and posterior margin, 1 frag,\u000aRSS.\u000aMicro 2: mass, superior and medial margins, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  mass, inferior, medial and anterior margins, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 6: mass, anterior and inferior margins, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 7: mass, superior margin and lateral margins, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 8: mass and superior and lateral margins, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 9: mass, posterior margin, anterior margin and superior margins, and\u000ahemorrhagic area, 3 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 10: fibrous tissue, inferior and lateral margins, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 11: fibrous tissue, lateral margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 12: fibrous tissue, inferior, posterior, superior and anterior margins,\u000a1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 13: medial margin and inferior margin and fibrous tissue, 1 frag, RSS.\u000amjy\u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
