ion, inferior, posterior shave margin, whip stitch new\u000amargin, scar anterior.\u000a2. Anterior shave margin, whip stitch new margin.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by HASKELL,HENRY D.,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart one, labeled "#1, left breast re-excision, inferior, posterior shave\u000amargin, whip stitch new margin", is a semispherical re-excision of breast\u000a(lateral to medial, REMOVED_DATE cm, inferior to superior, REMOVED_DATE cm, anterior to\u000aposterior, REMOVED_DATE cm), which is received previously inked. The specimen is inked\u000aper pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior = black;\u000aanterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial =\u000aorange. Note that all colors of ink except for the color red are used; the\u000aprior biopsy cavity is inked red at the surgical cutting bench. The lesion\u000aappears to consist of approximately 50% fibrous breast tissue; no lesion is\u000anoted. Representative sections are submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  left breast re-excision, multi frags, RSS.\u000aPart two, labeled "#2, anterior shave margin, whipstitch new margin", are two\u000a(2) fragments of fibroadipose tissue (2.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm).\u000aThe new margin is inked black and the old margin is inked blue and the specimen\u000ais entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  5 frags, ESS.\u000ahdh\u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN\u000a[report_end]
