n one part, labeled with the patient's name,\u000aunit number and "#1. L. breast tissue; inferior stitch shave margin, whip\u000astitch new margin and scar", and consists of a re-excision specimen (8.2 x REMOVED_DATE \u000ax REMOVED_DATE cm) with a biopsy cavity (3.3 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The inferior pole of the\u000aspecimen has been marked by the surgeon with a whip stitch. The area\u000asurrounding the whip stitch is inked blue. This constitutes the lowest 50% of\u000athe specimen and is designated the inferior pole. The remainder of the\u000aspecimen is inked black and is designated the superior pole. The specimen is\u000aserially sectioned and representative sections are submitted. A separate\u000afragment was included in the container which represents the skin scar\u000ameasuring REMOVED_DATE cm in length x REMOVED_DATE cm in width, and REMOVED_DATE cm in depth. The\u000asubcutaneous region is inked blue.\u000aMicro 1: skin tips, 2 frags, ESS\u000aMicro 2: scar, 1 frag, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  representative sections of breast tissue, 20 frags, RSS\u000assa\u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY - PARTIAL OR SIMPLE\u000a[report_end]
