, and REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom the anterior margin. The remaining cut surface displays 99% yellow\u000alobulated adipose tissue, and 1% white fibrous tissue, with no additional\u000adiscrete masses or lesions identified. The specimen is sequentially submitted\u000ain its entirety.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin to include the mass, radially, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross sections from medial to lateral to include the\u000amass in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, radially, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aCP/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Michelle S Hirsch M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a10/27/2007\u000a[report_end]
