mass is less than REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000ainked margin. Within the main mass, there is a discrete white/tan lobulated\u000awell-circumscribed nodule (4.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The entire specimen is inked\u000ablack. Representative sections are submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Margin with connective tissue, perpendicular, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Nodule within mass, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Area of bulging, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Representative section of mass, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Representative section of main lesion, REMOVED_DATE frags each, RSS.\u000aPart B, additionally labeled "#2. Wire-localized right breast mass", consists\u000aof one unoriented fragment of red/tan nodular soft tissue, 3-g, (3.6 x REMOVED_DATE x\u000a1.8 cm) with a localization wire. An accompanying specimen radiograph\u000ademonstrates a localization wire entering and exiting the specimen; there is a\u000auniform circumscribed mass at one end but the area of breast parenchyma above\u000athe nodule is circled. The entire specimen is inked black. On cut surface,\u000athere is a firm white/tan well-circumscribed nodule (1.7 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). This\u000anodule is within less than REMOVED_DATE cm to the black inked surface. The remaining\u000abreast parenchyma (area circled on the specimen radiograph) is fibrofatty and\u000acontains inspissated secretions. The specimen is serially sectioned and\u000aentirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Nodule and perpendicular margins of the nodular end, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Nodule, 2 frags each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Remaining fibrofatty breast lesion (circled on radiograph), REMOVED_DATE \u000afrags each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Non-nodule end margin, perpendicular, REMOVED_DATE frags, ESS.\u000aDIL/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jacqueline M William M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed\u000aon Tuesday REMOVED_MONTH 28, 2009 at 12:49:46PM\u000a[report_end]
