VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Amend/Addenda\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000a********** Addended Report ***********\u000aResident: Christopher P. Elco, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Lynette M Sholl, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. LEFT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZATION FOR CALCIFICATIONS AND A CLIP:\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aTypes - Cribriform, micropapillary\u000aNuclear grade - Low\u000aCalcifications in DCIS - Present\u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - Absent\u000aMicroinvasion (<0.1cm) - Absent\u000aExtent of DCIS\u000aNumber of blocks/total - 3:8 blocks\u000aMargins (DCIS)\u000aNegative (> REMOVED_DATE cm) - Superior, medial, anterior\u000aClose (0.1 to REMOVED_DATE cm) - Inferior (0.1 cm, block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID)\u000aVery close(<0.1 cm from margin)- Lateral (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID)\u000aPosterior (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID)\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - Absent\u000aOTHER FINDINGS\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia\u000aCore biopsy site\u000aAJCC Classification (6th edition) - Tis Nx MX\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER, PR, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) - Pending\u000aThis case was also reviewed by Dr. Susan Lester, Breast Pathology, who concurs.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 42 year old premenopausal woman with a family history of breast cancer\u000ain her mother, whose REMOVED_DATE  HVMA mammogram revealed L calcifications. On\u000a4/2/09 stereotactic core biopsy demonstrates ADH with excision recommended.\u000aOperation: L breast wire localized biopsy.\u000aOperative Findings: Not provided.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal L mammogram.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) left breast tissue, short suture/superior, long/lateral, whip stitch/deep\u000amargin (fs - mammo).\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000aHook, wire, clip and calcs in specimen. Called Dr. Rhei - 11:43 am - Swain.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in one part, labeled with the patient's name,\u000aunit number, and "#1. Left breast tissue", and consists of a REMOVED_DATE (medial to\u000alateral) x REMOVED_DATE (inferior to superior) x REMOVED_DATE (anterior to posterior) cm breast\u000abiopsy with a localization wire in place, short suture marking superior margin\u000aand a long suture marking the lateral margin. An accompanying specimen\u000aradiograph demonstrates a clip in the central portion of the specimen adjacent\u000ato the localization wire along with scattered calcifications throughout. The\u000aspecimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins:\u000aposterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow;\u000amedial/orange. The specimen is composed of over 90% dense white fibrous tissue\u000awith remaining 10% being composed of yellow adipose tissue. No definitive\u000alesion is seen and the specimen is submitted in its entirety for histological\u000aexamination.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial perpendicular sections, REMOVED_DATE frags each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, perpendicular sections, 2 or 4 frags each,\u000aESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Cross sections from medial to lateral (clip in micro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), 1 frag\u000aeach, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aCEL/lp\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Lynette M Sholl M.D., Electronically signed on Thursday\u000aMay 28, 2009 at 04:47:27PM\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM:\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for DCIS (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) NEGATIVE (1+)\u000aImmunohistochemical studies for estrogen receptor, progesterone receptor, and\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu were evaluated by manual morphometric analysis using the following\u000acriteria:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000acarcinoma is reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low > 0% - < 10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but\u000aonly a portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aEquivocal (2+):Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in\u000a>10% of tumor cells or moderate to strong complete membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity in < 30% of tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+):Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in\u000a>30% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aExternal controls are evaluated and show appropriate Immunoreactivity.\u000aThe immunoperoxidase, immunofluorescence and in-situ hybridization tests\u000aperformed at Brigham and Women's Hospital were developed and their performance\u000acharacteristics determined by the Immunohistochemistry Laboratories in the\u000aDepartment of Pathology at BWH. They have not been cleared or approved by the\u000aU.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA). The FDA has determined that such\u000aclearance or approval is not necessary.\u000aAddendum #1 by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on Friday May\u000a29, 2009 at 01:24:34PM\u000a[report_end]
