on revealed low-grade ER/PR positive REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/Neu\u000anegative DCIS with close margins.\u000aOperation: Left simple mastectomy, sentinel lymph node mapping and biopsy with\u000apossible level I-II dissection/with reconstruction.\u000aOperative Findings: Not given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast DCIS.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Left sentinel node hot blue - to FS.\u000aB/2. Left sentinel node hot NOT blue - to FS.\u000aC/3. Left breast short superior, long lateral.\u000aD/4. Left breast skin reexcision.\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "#1 LEFT SENTINEL NODE - HOT BLUE" (FSA):\u000aThree (3) lymph nodes; negative for tumor.\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "#2 LEFT SENTINEL NODE - HOT NOT BLUE" (FSB):\u000aOne (1) lymph node; negative for tumor\u000aOR Consultation by: William Robert Welch, M.D.\u000aResident: Elizabeth Morgan, M.D.\u000aThe senior physician certifies that he/she personally conducted a gross and/or\u000amicroscopic examination of the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed\u000athe rapid diagnos(es) related thereto.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in three parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart A, received in the frozen section labeled "#1. L sentinel node hot blue",\u000aconsists of multiple fragments of yellow/tan lobulated adipose tissue (1.3 x\u000a1.9 x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate). Within the adipose tissue, three lymph node\u000acandidates are identified (0.9 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm - inked black; REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm\u000a- inked blue; and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm - bisected). All four candidate fragments\u000aare frozen as FSA.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: "FSA" remnant, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Non-frozen tissue, multi frags, ESS.\u000aPart B received in the frozen section lab labeled "#2. Sentinel node hot not\u000ablue 182", consists of fragments of adipose tissue (1.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), within\u000awhich a single lymph node candidate (0.9 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) is identified. The\u000acandidate is bisected and entirely frozen as FSB.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: "FSB" remnant, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Non-frozen tissue, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aPart C, labeled "#3. L breast short superior; long lateral", consists of a left\u000asimple mastectomy specimen (820.0 grams; REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with two\u000aorienting sutures (short superior; long lateral) and a fragment of tan\u000airregular skin (9.0 x REMOVED_DATE cm), areola (4.0 x REMOVED_DATE cm) and everted nipple (1.2 cm\u000ain diameter). There is a well-healed linear scar (2.7 cm), REMOVED_DATE cm superior to\u000anipple. The deep margin is inked black and the specimen is serially sectioned\u000afrom medial to lateral, exhibiting a nodular, peripherally necrotic cavity (5.0\u000ax REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) within the upper inner quadrant, focally extending into the\u000aupper outer quadrant and coming to within REMOVED_DATE cm of the deep margin. Extending\u000afrom the cavity superiorly and laterally, is a focally blue dyed area of dense\u000anodular, cystic fibrous tissue (11.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which focally comes to\u000awithin REMOVED_DATE cm of the deep margin. Several large gray/blue fluid-filled cysts\u000a(measuring up to REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest dimension) are present within this fibrotic\u000aarea. The remaining breast tissue is composed of approximately 60% lobulated\u000aadipose tissue and 40% fibrostroma. No other definitive lesions are identified\u000agrossly. Lateral breast tissue is carefully examined for lymph node\u000acandidates, however, no lymph nodes are identified grossly.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Nipple and skin scar, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Cavity sequentially from lateral to medial to include closest\u000aapproach to deep margin, multi frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Dense fibrous area sequentially from lateral to medial\u000a(encompassing all quadrants), multi frags, RSS.\u000aPart D, labeled "L breast skin re-excision", and consists of an irregular\u000afragment of tan-pink skin and underlying soft tissue (15.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm),\u000awhich is inked and serially sectioned to exhibit an unremarkable fibrofatty cut\u000asurface.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 2 frags, RSS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000ajc/dfi/elw\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Lucian R Chirieac M.D., Electronically signed on\u000aWednesday REMOVED_MONTH 01, 2009 at 04:32:32PM\u000a[report_end]
