VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: FinalType: Surgical Pathology Pathology Report: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID OPERATION DATE: 17 REMOVED_MONTH 02 ACCESSIONED ON: 17 REMOVED_MONTH 02 at 18:52 CLINICAL DATA: Right breast cancer on core biopsy. Prior right DCIS 1993. =============================================================================== *** FINAL DIAGNOSIS *** BREAST (RIGHT), EXCISIONAL BIOPSY: INVASIVE MAMMARY CARCINOMA. SEE TABLE #1. SEE NOTE. NOTE: Certain of the tumor cells stain for e-cadherin, suggesting that the tumor is an invasive ductal carcinoma. TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS #1 INVASIVE CARCINOMA Tumor size: REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. Grade: 2. Lymphatic vessel invasion: Not identified. Blood vessel invasion: Not identified. Margin of invasive carcinoma: Invasive carcinoma extends to less than REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior margin of the specimen. Stains for receptors: Requested. BREAST (RIGHT, "SUPERIOR CAVITY, FINAL SHAVED MARGIN"), EXCISION: THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. BREAST (RIGHT, "INFERIOR CAVITY, FINAL SHAVED MARGIN"), EXCISION: THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. LYMPH NODE (RIGHT AXILLA, "SENTINEL"), EXCISION: THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 1 OF 1 LYMPH NODE. SEE NOTE. NOTE: Because of the small size of the lymph node, the sections stained for keratin do not contain lymphoid tissue. Diagnosis by: Frederick Carl Koerner, M.D. Signed On: 30 REMOVED_MONTH 02 at 09:14 =============================================================================== *** IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum *** RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast (Right, block D): The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein. The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein. The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER-2/c-erbB-2. See note. Note: These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital. They have not been cleared or approved by the U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA). The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary; this laboratory has established and verified the test's accuracy and precision. Added by: Grace T. McKee,MD Signed On: 27 REMOVED_MONTH 02 at 13:34 GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "right breast tissue lumpectomy-short stitch superior, long stitch lateral" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm portion of tan-yellow fibroadipose tissue with 2 black stitches designating the superior and lateral margins. The superior margin is inked yellow, the inferior blue, the anterior green, and the posterior black. The specimen is serially sectioned from lateral to medial to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm indurated gray-white, well-defined lesion which comes to REMOVED_DATE cm of the anterior, REMOVED_DATE cm of the posterior, REMOVED_DATE cm of the superior, REMOVED_DATE cm of the inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm of the medial, and greater REMOVED_DATE cm of the lateral margins. The remaining cut surface consists of 95% tan-yellow adipose and 5% gray white fibrous tissue. Representative sections are submitted from lateral to medial as A-E with the entire lesion as C-E. Received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "right sentinel node hot and blue level 1 count 2781" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm tan-pink lymph node with minimal attached tan-yellow adipose tissue. The specimen is bisected and entirely submitted as F. Received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "right breast final shaved margin superior cavity" are 2 irregular portions of tan-yellow fibroadipose tissue, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. No orientation is provided, and the fragments are serially sectioned to reveal a 25% dense gray-white fibrous and 75% tan-yellow adipose cut surface with no discrete lesions. The larger fragment is entirely submitted as G-H. The smaller fragment is bisected and entirely submitted as I. Received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "final shave margin inferior cavity right breast" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm aggregate of irregular tan-yellow fibroadipose tissue fragments with no orientation. The fragments are sectioned to reveal a 5% gray-white fibrous and 95% tan-yellow adipose cut surface. The specimen is entirely submitted as J-K. Gross Description by: STEPHANIE KUEHN Resident: JOHN BISSONNETTE, MD =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT - REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID REPORTS TO: Barbara Lynn Smith, M.D. PART A: LYMPH NODE(RIGHT AXILLA SENTINEL), EXCISION PART B: BREAST(RIGHT),EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART C: BREAST(RIGHT SUPERIOR CAVITY),FINAL SHAVED MARGIN PART D: BREAST(RIGHT INFERIOR CAVITY),FINAL SHAVED MARGIN
