VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Leona A. Doyle, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Lucian R Chirieac, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aSPECIMEN DESIGNATED "RIGHT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A MASS":\u000aFibroadenoma (1 cm).\u000aColumnar cell changes.\u000aApocrine metaplasia.\u000aCalcifications in benign epithelium.\u000aCore biopsy site changes.\u000aThe margins were inked and evaluated for the final diagnosis.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 41-year-old premenopausal woman with REMOVED_DATE  U/S R breast revealing\u000alobular mass UOQ with suspicious abnormality - Bx REMOVED_DATE  revealed\u000afibroadenomatoid change with apocrine metaplasia and epithelial hyperplasia.\u000aExc. recommended.\u000aOperation: R breast wire-loc bx.\u000aOperative Findings: None specified.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal rt bst. mammogram.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) Rt bst. tissue; short - superior; long - lateral; whip stitch - deep\u000amargin; to mammo (mm).\u000aRADIOLOGY: Called to OR 10:43 AM. Hookwire/mass in specimen. H. Peters\u000a#REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, medical record\u000anumber, and "#1. Right breast tissue short superior, long lateral with stitch\u000adeep margin", and consists of a REMOVED_DATE g breast excision (3.6 cm superior to\u000ainferior, REMOVED_DATE cm medial to lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm anterior to posterior) with\u000aorienting sutures designating superior, lateral, and deep margins. Ink (by\u000asurgeon). An accompanying specimen radiograph demonstrates the excision\u000aspecimen with a wire entering the lateral aspect and extending into an\u000aill-defined area of increased density associated with metallic clip.\u000aSectioning reveals that the wire and clip are associated with a diffuse firm\u000arubbery area of fibrous breast parenchyma (1.6 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), with focal\u000ahemorrhage. This area extends to the inferior and deep margins, REMOVED_DATE cm to\u000aanterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to medial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to the lateral margin and REMOVED_DATE \u000acm to the superior margin. Remaining breast parenchyma consists of adipose\u000atissue. The entire specimen is submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Inferior, anterior and posterior margins (metallic clip in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID),\u000a1-2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Superior margin, REMOVED_DATE frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aLDO/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: 5022\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Lucian R Chirieac M.D., Electronically signed on Tuesday\u000aFebruary 10, 2009 at 10:55:42AM\u000a[report_end]
