ted adipose tissue, and 40% white fibrous\u000atissue, with no additional discrete masses or lesions identified. The specimen\u000ais sequentially submitted in its entirety.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 unoriented end, radially, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross sections, with the biopsy cavity and the clip\u000aidentified in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 2 frags each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Opposite unoriented end, radially, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aCP/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jane E. Brock M.B., B.S., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000aWednesday REMOVED_MONTH 28, 2009 at 11:11:54AM\u000a[report_end]
