VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aLODA, MASSIMO, F., M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by LODA,MASSIMO F.,M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "LEFT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISIONAL BIOPSY":\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, (at least REMOVED_DATE cm), solid and comedo types, (high\u000anuclear grade), is present in four (4) of twenty (20) blocks (blocks\u000a11,17,18,19) with lobular extension.\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN-SITU is present within REMOVED_DATE cm of inferior margin\u000a(blocks 17 and 19) and REMOVED_DATE cm from lateral margin (block 11).\u000aMicrocalcifications are associated with benign breasts tissue.\u000aFibrocystic change with apocrine metaplasia and microcysts.\u000aBiopsy site with fat necrosis and reactive changes.\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aAt the request of Dr. Leroy Parker, immunoperoxidase studies are performed.\u000aMicroinvasion is present as small tumor cell clusters in stroma adjacent to\u000aDCIS (best seen on the immunoperoxidase study for REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu, block 17; measuring\u000amuch less than REMOVED_DATE cm in size).\u000aDCIS MICROINVASION\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE NEGATIVE (but few cells present)\u000aProgesterone receptor NEGATIVE NEGATIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu POSITIVE (3+) POSITIVE (3+)\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 50 year old female with left breast microcalcifications.\u000a10/19/99 core needle showed DCIS.\u000aOperation: Left breast biopsy.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast cancer.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Left breast tissue.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by QIAN,XIAOHUA,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in one (1) part, labeled with the patient's\u000aname, unit number, and "left breast tissue, S/P needle localization," and\u000aconsists of a single fragment of yellow/tan fibroadipose tissue with two\u000aneedle localization wires. The specimen is inked for the evaluation of\u000amargins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior =\u000agreen; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. Sections of margins are submitted\u000afor microscopic examination. The specimen measures REMOVED_DATE cm from inferior to\u000asuperior, REMOVED_DATE cm from anterior to posterior, and REMOVED_DATE cm from medial to lateral.\u000aThe specimen is sliced from the inferior to superior, and radiographed, and the\u000aarea of the calcifications and the clip identified. The clip is REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000aanterior, REMOVED_DATE cm posterior, REMOVED_DATE cm medial, REMOVED_DATE cm from lateral, 3 cm from the\u000asuperior, and 3 cm from the inferior margin. There are areas of hemorrhage and\u000afat necrosis associated with the biopsy site. The specimen contains\u000aapproximately 20% of white/tan fibrous tissue, which is present superiorly and\u000aanteriorly of the biopsy site. The slice containing the biopsy site and the\u000amicrocalcifications, as well as all fibrotic tissue with respective margins\u000aare submitted. Approximately 80% of the specimen is submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  slice #1, superior margin, 3 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  slice #2, perpendicular sections, with respect to medial and\u000alateral margins, from posterior to anterior, 6 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  slice #3, biopsy site, with closest anterior margin, multiple\u000afrags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  slice #3, biopsy site, with associated fibrotic tissue and\u000aclosest medial and lateral margins, multiple frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  slice #4, biopsy site, and fibrotic tissue, with closest\u000aposterior and anterior margin, multiple frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  slice #5 and #6, fibrotic tissue with closest inferior margin,\u000amultiple frags, RSS.\u000aReports to: OSTEEN, ROBERT, T. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
