VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Scott Lovitch, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Xiaohua Qian, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A CLIP:\u000aFibroadenoma (1.5 cm).\u000aColumnar cell changes.\u000aCore biopsy site.\u000aSclerosing adenosis.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000aNOTE:\u000aThe entire specimen is submitted and the atypia seen on prior core biopsy\u000a(REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, reviewed) was not present.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 43-year-old, premenopausal woman S/O REMOVED_DATE  L breast core bx's,\u000arevealing epithelial hyperplasia in focal atypia - exc recommended.\u000aPREVIOUS SURGERY: REMOVED_DATE  BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aOperation: L breast WL bx.\u000aOperative Findings: None specified.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: None specified.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) Left breast tissue, short - superior, long - lateral, whip stitch - deep\u000amargin.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Clip and wire in specimen. Called to OR. LZM.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in a single container, labeled with the\u000apatient's name, medical record number, and "#1. Left breast tissue, short\u000asuperior, long lateral, whip stitch deep margin". It consists of a single\u000awire-localized left breast excision specimen with a short suture marking\u000asuperior aspect, a long suture marking the lateral aspect, and a whip stitch\u000amarking the deep (posterior) aspect of the specimen. The specimen measures REMOVED_DATE \u000acm from superior to inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm from medial to lateral, and REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000aanterior to posterior. The specimen is received inked by the surgeon. The\u000aspecimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins:\u000aposterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow;\u000amedial/orange. There was a single wire present in the specimen which enters\u000aanteriorly, REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin, and\u000a1.2 cm from the superior margin. The wire terminated within the specimen. The\u000aradiograph shows the wire passing through a well-circumscribed, radiolucent\u000aarea which contains a mammography clip. No definitive mass is seen. Serial\u000asectioning revealed a well-circumscribed, tan/red, friable lesion measuring REMOVED_DATE \u000ax REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm, located REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000ainferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin.\u000aThe remainder of the tissue in the specimen is densely fibrotic, consistent\u000awith scarring (approximately 80% firm white fibrous tissue and 10% yellow\u000alobulated adipose tissue). The clip is identified and removed. The entire\u000aspecimen is submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Superior margin, perpendicular sections, 11 frags total, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #2, 1 frag per cassette, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #3, 1 frag per cassette, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #4, including lesion, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Remainder of slice #4 including lateral and inferior margins, 2\u000afrags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #5, including lesion, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #5, remainder including posterior, lateral, and inferior\u000amargins, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #6, including lesion and clip site, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #6, remainder including lateral and inferior margins, 3 frags,\u000aESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Inferior margin, perpendicular sections, 9 frags total, ESS.\u000aSBL/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Xiaohua Qian M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a10/17/2008\u000a[report_end]
