VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Amend/Addenda\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ROGER L CHRISTIAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-06-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000a********** Addended Report ***********\u000aResident: Michael H Roh, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Robert D Odze, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, EXCISION WIRE-LOCALIZATION FOR CALCIFICATIONS AND A CLIP:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA WITH MIXED FEATURES.\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aSYNOPSIS:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA\u000aSize - REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aMultifocal - no\u000aHistologic Type - mixed ductal and lobular\u000aHistologic Grade (SBR) - I (well)\u000aNuclear Grade - low\u000aEIC - negative\u000aLymphovascular invasion - absent\u000aDermal lymphatic invasion - N/A\u000aSkin invasion - N/A\u000aSkeletal muscle invasion - N/A\u000aFinal Margins (invasive) -\u000aNegative (>0.3 cm) - medial, lateral, inferior, superior\u000aClose (0.1-0.3 cm) - anterior (0.2 cm)\u000aVery close (<0.1cm from margin)- posterior\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aTypes - cribriform\u000aNuclear grade - low\u000aCalcifications in DCIS - present\u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - absent\u000aExtent of DCIS\u000aFinal Margins (DCIS)\u000aNegative (>0.3 cm) - anterior, medial, lateral, superior,\u000a- inferior\u000aVery close (<0.1 cm) - posterior\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - present\u000aOTHER FINDINGS\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia\u000aCore biopsy site\u000aCalcifications in benign epithelium\u000aAJCC CLASSIFICATION (6th edition) - REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID pNx MX\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER/PR/HER-2) - pending\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aClinical History: FH atypia right BRST.\u000aOperation: Right breast wire localization excisional biopsy.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Atypia, right breast.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aTissue, right breast (orange and yellow dye).\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000aComplete wire, clip and calcifications in the radiographed specimen. Findings\u000acalled to Dr. Christian by Dr. Galbez\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "tissue, right breast", and consists of an irregular, tan/yellow portion of\u000abreast (3.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) that has been previously inked according to\u000apathology protocol by the surgeon (red equals superior, yellow equals lateral,\u000aorange equals medial, green equals inferior, blue equals anterior, black equals\u000aposterior). There is a localization wire in place that enters the specimen at\u000athe anterior lateral position. The specimen is previously radiographed. The\u000aspecimen is serially sectioned from superior to inferior to show a cut surface\u000apredominantly consisting of tan/white, rubbery fibrous tissue (70%). The\u000aremaining tissue consists of focally hemorrhagic, tan/red to tan/yellow,\u000alobulated fat. A metallic clip from the previous biopsy site is identified REMOVED_DATE \u000acm from the medial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000aanterior, REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior, and REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000athe inferior.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Specimen sequentially sectioned with the slice that contain the\u000ametallic clip in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, multi frags, ESS.\u000adrd/ag\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Robert D Odze M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000aSurgical Addendum: (7/19/06)\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for invasive carcinoma (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) NEGATIVE (0)\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000acarcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but only\u000aa portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in >10%\u000aof tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in\u000a>10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aAddendum #1 by Deborah A Dillon M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
