 "2. SENTINEL LYMPH NODE (FSB):\u000aOne lymph node negative for carcinoma.\u000aOR Consultation by: JONATHAN NEIL GLICKMAN, M.D., PH.D.\u000aResident: QINGHONG YANG, MD, PHD\u000aThe senior physician certifies that he/she personally conducted a gross and/or\u000amicroscopic examination of the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed\u000athe rapid diagnos(es) related thereto.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aFour specimens were received fresh, each labeled with the patient's name and\u000aunit number.\u000aPart A, "#1. Sentinel lymph nodes - right breast", consists of two fragments of\u000aadipose tissue/lymph nodes (1.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). Each\u000alymph node is bisected and entirely submitted as REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID remnant, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID remnant, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Fibroadipose tissue, 5 frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, "#2. Sentinel lymph node - right", consists of one fragment of\u000afibroadipose tissue (1.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which is bisected and entirely\u000asubmitted as FSB.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: FSB remnant, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aPart C, "#3. Axillary contents - right", consists of two fragments of\u000atan/yellow fibroadipose tissue (1.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate), containing a\u000alymph node (1.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm).\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lymph node, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Fibroadipose tissue, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aPart D, "#4. Right former tumor site", consists of one piece of fibroadipose\u000atissue (3.3 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). One side of the specimen is previously inked in\u000ablack by the surgeon and contains a whipstitch. The opposite side of the\u000aspecimen consists of tan, firm tissue and will be inked in blue (old margin).\u000aThe specimen shows diffuse white/firm areas on cross section with focal\u000ahemorrhage.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 2 frags each, ESS.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Lucian R Chirieac M.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aAmendment #1 by Lucian R Chirieac M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
