ral Hospital. They have not been cleared or approved by the U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA). The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary; this laboratory has established and verified the test's accuracy and precision. Added by: Grace T. McKee,MD Signed On: 14 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 14:27 *** HER-2 Addendum *** RESULTS OF FLUORESCENCE IN SITU HYBRIDIZATION (FISH) FOR HER-2/NEU GENE AMPLIFICATION Breast (Right, block A): HER-2/neu gene in tumor cells: REMOVED_DATE (Not Amplified). See note. Note: Results are expressed as the average ratio of HER-2 to chromosome 17 signals in 60 tumor cell nuclei. A ratio of greater than REMOVED_DATE or equal to REMOVED_DATE indicates REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu gene amplification adjusted for chromsome 17 polysomy using PathVysion by Vysis. Added by: Atul Kumar Bhan, M.D. Signed On: 21 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 09:45 GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "lumpectomy" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm irregular blue stained tan-yellow to pink portion of fibrofatty tissue with a short stitch designating the superior aspect and a long stitch designating the lateral aspect. The superior aspect is inked green, posterior black, inferior yellow and anterior blue. The specimen is sequentially sectioned from lateral to medial to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm irregular indurated tan-white gritty mass which comes to within REMOVED_DATE cm of from the posterior, REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior margins of the specimen and REMOVED_DATE cm, REMOVED_DATE cm, REMOVED_DATE cm, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral, medial, superior and inferior margins, respectively. The uninvolved remaining parenchyma is tan-yellow to white lobulated fibrofatty unremarkable tissue. Representative sections are submitted in cassettes A-F with the closest posterior and anterior margin in cassettes A-B. Received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "sentinel nodes hot and blue 2751, 832, 330" are two tan-pink blue stained lymph nodes measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The largest node is bisected and entirely submitted in cassette G and the smaller is submitted in toto as H. Received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "final margins, medial half of cavity" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm of irregular, unoriented tan-yellow to pink portions of fibrofatty tissue with cauterization artifact. The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a tan-pink to yellow firm unremarkable cut surface. The specimen is entirely submitted in cassettes I-L. Received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "final shaved margins lateral half of cavity" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm of irregular tan-yellow to pink blue stained unoriented portions of fibrofatty tissue which are serially sectioned to reveal a unremarkable fibrofatty. The specimen is entirely submitted in cassettes M-N. Gross Description by: JENNIFER NASH Resident: JOHN BISSONNETTE, MD =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT - REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID REPORTS TO: Barbara Lynn Smith, M.D. PART A: LYMPH NODE(SENTINEL REMOVED_DATE ),EXCISION PART B: BREAST(RIGHT),EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART C: BREAST(MEDIAL HALF OF CAVITY),FINAL SHAVED MARGIN PART D: BREAST(LATERAL HALF OF CAVITY),FINAL SHAVED MARGIN
