terior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/ orange.\u000aThe specimen is sectioned superior to inferior. No discrete mass is\u000aidentified. The tissue is composed of approximately 95% adipose tissue and 5%\u000afibrous tissue. The specimen is entirely submitted for histological\u000aexamination.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Specimen submitted inferior to superior. Area around\u000alocalization wire in cassettes REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. REMOVED_DATE frags each, ESS.\u000aBEN/lp\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jacqueline M William M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed\u000aon Wednesday August 26, 2009 at 11:47:08PM\u000a[report_end]
