VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID:REMOVED_CASE_ID Report Status: Signed\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aADDENDUM REPORT\u000aAddendum #1 Entered: REMOVED_DATE -1006\u000a*** ADDITIONAL DIAGNOSTIC INFORMATION ***\u000aThis report contains an addendum to the original for the purpose of providing\u000aadditional diagnostic information. The original diagnosis is unchanged.\u000aImmunohistochemical staining performed on formalin-fixed, paraffin embedded\u000ablock 3 reveals the following result for the ductal carcinoma in situ:\u000aEstrogen receptor: POSITIVE\u000a(Antibody: 6REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. Detection system: avidin-biotin complex)\u000aAddeundum Signed Electronically Signed MIHOK,NICOLE M.D. REMOVED_DATE \u000aDIAGNOSIS:\u000aRight breast, needle localized excision:\u000aDuctal carcinoma in situ, low and intermediate grade, cribriform and\u000amicropapillary patterns, with microcalcifications, see note.\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia, columnar cell type.\u000aIntraductal papillomas.\u000aBiopsy site changes.\u000aFibrocystic changes.\u000aSYNOPTIC REPORT: BREAST\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU (DCIS):\u000a-histologic type: cribriform and micropapillary\u000a-histologic grade: predominantly low with focal intermediate\u000agrade areas\u000a-size (greatest dimension): REMOVED_DATE cm. The ductal carcinoma in situ\u000aextends across most of the REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000aspecimen\u000a-extent: multifocal\u000a-extensive intraductal component: not applicable\u000a-necrosis in DCIS: none identified\u000a-microcalcifications in DCIS: present, focal\u000a-margins for DCIS: The ductal carcinoma in situ is less than 1\u000amm. from the deep margin over a broad\u000afront. It is less than 1 mm. from the\u000asuperior margin focally. It is less than\u000a1 mm. from the inferior margin over a\u000abroad front. It is also less than 2 mm.\u000afrom the lateral margin, towards the deep\u000aaspect, focally. The medial and anterior\u000amargins are clear.\u000a-immunohistochemical staining for estrogen receptor will be performed on\u000ablock 3 and reported in an addendum to follow.\u000aPRIOR RELATED SPECIMENS REVIEWED:\u000asite: right breast, needle core biopsy specimen #: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aAJCC pTNM Classification (6th Ed.): pTis pNX pMX\u000aThe pathologic TNM classification above is based only on the information\u000aavailable to the pathologist, and therefore may not be accurate.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by: Nicole A. Mihok, M.D.\u000aClinical diagnosis & history:\u000aRight breast atypical ductal hyperplasia\u000aTissue-Designation:\u000aBreast, excision with margins - right\u000aGross description:\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin in one container, labeled "right breast\u000amass" and consists of a needle localized excision specimen with a short stitch\u000adesignating the superior edge and a long stitch on the lateral edge. The\u000aspecimen measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The superior half is inked blue; the\u000ainferior, green; the deep margin, black. The cut section shows yellowish-white\u000abreast parenchyma with a punctate reddish area consistent with prior biopsy\u000asite. The entire specimen is submitted from lateral towards medial beginning\u000ain cassette 1 to cassette 9 (9 is the most medial end of the specimen). 13\u000aagg. all, with some having lettered subdesignations, each number corresponds to\u000aone contiguous slice of tissue.\u000aDictated by: NAM____(signature on file)____MICHAEL J. ROSS, M.D. REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a____(signature on file)____NICOLE MIHOK, M.D. REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a[report_end]
