VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: BRENT T SHOJI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-05-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Patricia A. R. Brunker, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Marisa R Nucci, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, EXCISION FOR A MASS:\u000aComplex sclerosing lesion (1.4 cm).\u000aSclerosing intraductal papilloma associated with core biopsy site.\u000aFibrocystic changes including florid epithelial hyperplasia, apocrine cysts,\u000aand an (additional) intraductal papilloma.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000aImmunohistochemistry performed at BWH demonstrates the following\u000astaining profile in the lesion in question:\u000aPositive - REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and p63 double stain.\u000aThe staining profile supports the diagnosis of a complex sclerosing\u000alesion.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Excision (R) breast mass. S/p non-diagnostic core bx.\u000aOperation: Excision (R) breast mass.\u000aOperative Findings: Not provided.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast mass.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Right breast tissue, short stitch superior, long stitch lateral for\u000apermanent.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in one part, labeled with the patient?s name,\u000aunit number, and "#1. Right breast tissue, short stitch superior, long stitch\u000alateral", and consists of one fragment of yellow/white soft tissue (3.6 x REMOVED_DATE x\u000a1.8 cm), which is oriented by two sutures placed by the surgeon designating the\u000asuperior and lateral aspects. The specimen is inked in the pathology\u000adepartment per the pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins:\u000aposterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow;\u000amedial/orange. The specimen is entirely, serially submitted from the lateral\u000ato medial aspects. There is a white/chalky, tubular area in blocks REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID (0.6\u000ax REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which grossly abuts the superior margin and is located REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom the posterior, REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior, REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom the lateral, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margins. The specimen is entirely\u000asubmitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Entire specimen, chalky areas in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 12 frags total, ESS.\u000aPab/ajb\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Patricia A. R. Brunker M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Marisa R Nucci M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
