l = yellow; medial = orange. Sectioning reveals a\u000acentral area of old hemorrhage, fibrosis and fat necrosis, grossly consistent\u000awith prior biopsy/excision site, measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The distances\u000aof this area to the nearest margins are as follows: REMOVED_DATE cm to medial, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000ato lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm to inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm to superior, less than REMOVED_DATE cm to\u000aanterior and REMOVED_DATE cm to posterior. The remainder of the breast parenchyma is\u000acomposed of almost exclusively lobulated adipose tissue without any additional\u000alesions.\u000aMicro 1&2: biopsy site and nearest medial margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 3: biopsy site and nearest lateral margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 4: biopsy site and nearest inferior margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 5: biopsy site and nearest superior margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 6&7: biopsy site and nearest anterior margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 8&9: biopsy site and nearest posterior margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 10&11: additional representative biopsy site, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 12: representative uninvolved breast, 1 frag, RSS.\u000apj\u000aReports to: CARTER, KATHARINE M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
