VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aODZE, ROBERT, DANIEL, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by ODZE,ROBERT DANIEL,M.D.\u000a#1. LEFT BREAST, EXCISION OF A MASS:\u000aATYPICAL MEDULLARY CARCINOMA (1.0 cm), invasive, poorly differentiated,\u000aarising in association with a fibroadenoma.\u000aNo lymphatic or vascular invasion seen.\u000aInvasive carcinoma is focally present at the inked, lateral and\u000ainferior margin (blocks 1, 6, 11, 15).\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, solid type (high nuclear grade) is present in\u000ablocks 1, 2, 13, 14 and 15.\u000aNo necrosis or microcalcifications are associated with DCIS.\u000aDCIS is at, or within REMOVED_DATE cm, of the inked resection margins in 1 block\u000a(posterior margin).\u000aBiopsy site with repair reaction.\u000aNOTE: ER/PR will be done and reported in an addendum.The tumor shows focal\u000aareas of infiltrative borders,which is not characteristic of a typical\u000amedullary carcinoma.However,other features of medullary carcinoma are\u000apresent,so the tumor is best classified as an atypical medullary carcinoma.\u000a#2. LEFT BREAST, RE-EXCISION OF SUPERIOR MARGIN:\u000aFibrodenomatous breast tissue with no tumor seen.\u000a#3. LEFT AXILLARY LYMPH NODE DISSECTION:\u000aNine lymph nodes with no evidence of metastasis.\u000aNOTE: Additional lymph nodes will be reported as an addendum.\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: by BOROWSKY,ALEXANDER D.,M.D.\u000aAddendum, part #3.\u000aCassette key:\u000aMicro #24: 2 lymph nodes, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro #25: Fibrous tissue, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro #26: Fibrous tissue, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro #27: 4 lymph nodes, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro #28: Fibrous tissue, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro #29: Fibrous tissue, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro #30: Fibrous tissue, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro #31: 1 lymph node, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro #32: 1 lymph node, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro #33: Fibrous tissue, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro #34: Fibrous tissue, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro #35: Fibrous tissue, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro #36: 1 lymph node, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro #37: 1 lymph node, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aDIAGNOSIS:\u000a10 additional lymph nodes with no evidence of metastasis. In total, there are\u000a19 lymph nodes with no evidence of metastasis.\u000aThe entire specimen was submitted for histologic examination.\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for invasive carcinoma:\u000aEstrogen receptor negative\u000aProgesterone receptor negative\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) negative\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000ainvasive carcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive > 10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low > 0% to < 10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis: Membrane immunoreactivity is scored as a positive result if\u000apresent in the invasive carcinoma. Positive - weak signifies that the\u000aimmunoreactivity is less than that present in typical positive carcinomas.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast mass\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1. Left breast mass\u000a#2. Re-excision of superior margin\u000a#3. Left axillary node dissection\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000a#1. LEFT BREAST MASS:\u000aFibrocystic changes including 1 cm area suggestive of fibroadenoma\u000aor proliferative changes; no areas grossly suspicious for invasive\u000acarcinoma (gross only).\u000a"#2. S/P RE-EXCISION OF SUPERIOR MARGIN:"\u000aFibrocystic changes (gross only).\u000aRadiology: Ultrasound reveals mass in specimen.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by OAKES,SCOTT A.,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart one, labeled "#1. left breast mass", consists of tan/yellow adipose tissue\u000a(5.1 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with a needle localization wire in place. The short suture\u000amarks the superior margin, long suture marks the lateral margin. Within the\u000aspecimen is a tan/gray fibrous well circumscribed area measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x\u000a0.4 cm that is REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom the superior margin and REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin. The specimen is\u000ainked as follows (blue = anterior, black = posterior, green = medial, orange =\u000asuperior, yellow = inferior, red = lateral).\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  medial margin with mass, 1 fragment each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  medial margin, multiple fragments, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  anterior margin, multiple fragments, ESS.\u000aMicro 8, superior margin, 2 fragments, ESS.\u000aMicro 9, posterior margin, multiple fragments, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  lateral margin, multiple fragments, ESS.\u000aPart two, labeled "#2. left breast mass", consists of a fragment of tan/yellow\u000aadipose tissue measuring (3.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) that is unoriented. The specimen\u000aconsists mainly of tan/gray fibrous tissue and there are no areas that are\u000agrossly suspcious for invasive carcinoma.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  re-excision of superior margin, 6 fragments, ESS.\u000aPart three, labeled "#3. left axillary node dissection", consists of one\u000afragment of tan/yellow adipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. Nine lymph\u000anodes (1 cm in greatest dimension) are identified in the tissue.\u000aMicro 19, 1 lymph node, 5 fragments, ESS.\u000aMicro 20, 1 lymph node, 2 fragments, ESS.\u000aMicro 21, 2 lymph nodes, 3 fragments, ESS.\u000aMicro 22, 3 lymph nodes, 3 fragments, ESS.\u000aMicro 23, 2 lymph nodes, 4 fragments, ESS.\u000aReports to: MATORY, YVEDT M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: LYMPH NODES REGIONAL RESECTION\u000a[report_end]
