VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID:REMOVED_CASE_ID Report Status: Signed\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aADDENDUM REPORT\u000aAddendum #1 Entered: REMOVED_DATE -1043\u000a*** ADDITIONAL DIAGNOSTIC INFORMATION ***\u000aThis report contains an addendum to the original for the purpose of providing\u000aadditional diagnostic information. The original diagnosis is unchanged.\u000aImmunohistochemical staining on the formalin-fixed, paraffin-embedded blocks REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aand REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID reveals these results for the infiltrating carcinoma:\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID (larger tumor) - REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID): POSITIVE (3+) (>30% with intense,\u000acomplete membrane staining)\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID (smaller tumor) - REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID): NEGATIVE (1+) (faint or <10% complete\u000amembrane staining)\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID (4REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, Ventana Medical Systems, FDA approved) is assessed visually by\u000aquantitation of the percent and intensity of tumor cells staining.\u000aTotal fixation time 28 hours.\u000aAddeundum Signed Electronically Signed SAMPSON,RICHARD J. M.D. REMOVED_DATE \u000aDIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. Right sentinel lymph nodes, excisions:\u000aIsolated tumor cell seen in one of the three sentinel lymph nodes (0/3).\u000aB. Right chest skin, right chest wall, excision:\u000aNo diagnostic abnormalities recognized; no tumor seen.\u000aC. Right breast, simple mastectomy (1,264 grams):\u000aTwo infiltrating ductal carcinomas, REMOVED_DATE cm. and REMOVED_DATE cm. (see note)\u000aDuctal carcinoma in situ, low and high grade, cribriform, solid and\u000acomedo patterns; see note.\u000aTwo areas of prior biopsy site change.\u000aSmall fibroadenoma, REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000aMultiple small radial scars.\u000aFocal fibrocystic change.\u000aSkin and nipple with no diagnostic abnormalities recognized.\u000aSYNOPTIC REPORT: BREAST\u000aINVASIVE TUMOR:\u000a-histologic type: ductal\u000a-histologic grade: poorly differentiated, grade 3, larger (1.4 cm.)\u000atumor\u000amoderately differentiated, grade 2, smaller\u000atumor (1.0 cm.)\u000a-size (greatest dimension): REMOVED_DATE cm. and REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000a-lymphatic/vascular invasion: present in the area adjacent to the larger\u000atumor (slide REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID)\u000a-perineural invasion: none\u000a-microcalcification: none\u000a-margins for invasive tumors: clear (greater than or equal to REMOVED_DATE cm.)\u000a-immunohistochemical staining on prior specimen (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) was reported as:\u000aEstrogen receptor: POSITIVE (>10% of nuclei stained)\u000aProgesterone receptor: POSITIVE (>10% of nuclei stained)\u000a-immunohistochemical staining on prior specimen (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) was reported as:\u000aEstrogen receptor: POSITIVE, focal (1-10% of nuclei stained)\u000aProgesterone receptor: NEGATIVE (0% of nuclei stained)\u000a-immunohistochemical staining for Her2/neu will be performed on both tumors,\u000ablocks REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, and reported in an addendum to follow.\u000aEstrogen receptor (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, Ventana Medical Systems) and/or progesterone receptor\u000a(PgR 1REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, Ventana Medical Systems) is assessed visually by quantitation of\u000athe percent of tumor cells staining.\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU (DCIS):\u000a-histologic type: solid, comedo and cribriform patterns\u000a-histologic grade: high grade, adjacent to the larger tumor\u000aand low grade, adjacent to the smaller\u000atumor\u000a-size (greatest dimension): microscopic foci within and around the\u000ainvasive tumors\u000a-extent: focal\u000a-extensive intraductal component: absent\u000a-necrosis in DCIS: present\u000a-microcalcifications in DCIS: present, focal\u000a-margins for DCIS: clear (greater than or equal to REMOVED_DATE cm.)\u000aLYMPH NODES:\u000aPositive lymph nodes out of total sampled: REMOVED_DATE \u000a(0/3 sentinel lymph nodes).\u000aLymph nodes with isolated tumor cells out of total sampled: REMOVED_DATE \u000a(1/3 sentinel lymph nodes)\u000aCOMMENT: The sentinel lymph node, specimen A, is examined at multiple\u000alevels with H&E stains and immunohistochemical stains for keratin.\u000aPRIOR RELATED SPECIMENS REVIEWED:\u000aRight breast, needle core biopsies from the designated 10 o'clock position\u000aand lower outer quadrant, specimens REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, dates REMOVED_DATE  and\u000a5/13/08, have been reviewed.\u000aCOMMENT: Multiple small nodules were identified on gross examination from the\u000aarea underneath the nipple as well as the areas of the 12 o'clock position and\u000athe 9 o'clock position. These areas correspond to a small fibroadenoma, radial\u000ascar and fibrocystic change.\u000aAJCC pTNM Classification (6th Ed.): pREMOVED_ACCESSION_IDc(m) pREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID(i+)(sn) pMX\u000aThe pathologic TNM classification above is based only on the information\u000aavailable to the pathologist, and therefore may not be accurate.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by: Nicole A. Mihok, M.D.\u000aINTRA-OPERATIVE CONSULTATION:\u000aOPERATING ROOM CONSULTATION (FROZEN SECTIONS):\u000aSentinel lymph nodes x 3:\u000aA portion of each node is frozen and no tumor seen in any of the sections.\u000aFull protocol and diagnosis pending permanent sections.\u000aNAM\u000aClinical diagnosis & history:\u000aRight breast carcinoma\u000aTissue-Designation:\u000aA.Sentinel lymph node - right\u000aB.Skin, excision - right chest wall\u000aC.Breast, simple mastectomy - right\u000aGross description:\u000aThe specimen is received in three parts.\u000aSpecimen A labeled "right sentinel lymph nodes" is received fresh from the\u000aOperating Room for frozen section and consists of three lymph nodes. The\u000asmallest node measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. and has an adjacent attached adipose\u000atissue. A portion of this lymph node is frozen, and the remnant following the\u000afrozen is entirely submitted in cassette REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. The remainder of the node that\u000ais not frozen is entirely submitted in cassette REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. The medium size lymph node\u000aconsists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. lymph node with attached adipose tissue. The\u000anode is sectioned and appears to be fatty replaced. One portion of the node is\u000asampled for frozen section. The remnant following the frozen is entirely\u000asubmitted in cassettes REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. The remainder of the node that was not frozen is\u000aentirely submitted in cassette REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. The largest node consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x\u000a0.8 cm. lymph node with a small amount of attached adipose tissue. The node is\u000aserially sectioned and one portion is frozen. The remnant of the node\u000afollowing the frozen section is entirely submitted in cassettes REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. The\u000aremainder of the node that was not frozen is serially sectioned and entirely\u000asubmitted in two cassettes, labeled REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. 7 agg. all.\u000aSpecimen B labeled "right chest wall skin" consists of a circular shaped\u000aportion of skin with a stitch at the lateral edge. There is a hole in the\u000acenter of the skin. The skin surface is unremarkable. The skin in greatest\u000adiameter is REMOVED_DATE cm. The diameter of the hole is the skin is REMOVED_DATE cm. The skin\u000ais excised to a depth of REMOVED_DATE cm. The outer margin is inked black, the inner\u000aportion of the hole is inked blue and the deep margin is inked green. Four\u000arepresentative sections are submitted in cassettes REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID contains the\u000alateral and medial edge and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID contains the superior and inferior edge). 4X\u000aSpecimen C labeled "right breast" is received fresh and consists of a 1,264\u000agram, mastectomy specimen with a stitch at the lateral end. No axillary tail\u000ais seen and no palpable lymph nodes are identified. There is a nipple and\u000aareola present. The entire breast measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x up to REMOVED_DATE cm. The\u000anipple with areola is REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm., x up to REMOVED_DATE cm. The specimen is inked as\u000afollows: The upper inner quadrant is inked blue, the lower inner quadrant is\u000ainked green, the upper outer quadrant is inked red, the lower outer quadrant is\u000ainked yellow, and the deep margin is inked black.\u000aThe specimen is serially sectioned. A firm stellate mass that measures REMOVED_DATE x\u000a1.4 x REMOVED_DATE cm. is identified at the 10 o'clock position in the upper outer\u000aquadrant, and this mass is close to the non-deep margin in this area. 3 cm.\u000afrom this mass in the 12 o'clock position is a firm, nodular area that measures\u000aup to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. This are is grossly free of the margins. In the REMOVED_DATE \u000ao'clock area, approximately 7 cm. from the nipple, is a firm, nodular, white\u000aarea that measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. This mass is near the deep margin, but\u000agrossly free of the margin. In the 9 o'clock position, 5 cm. from the nipple,\u000ais a slightly firm, nodular area that is REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. Sections of the\u000aspecimen are submitted as follows:\u000aSection code: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - nipple and areola\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - largest tumor at the 10 o'clock position\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - nodular area in the 12 o'clock position\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - nodular area at the 9 o'clock position\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - tumor at the 6 to 7 o'clock location\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - small nodular foci in the central breast underneath the\u000anipple\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - random section from the upper inner quadrant\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - random section from lower inner quadrant\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - random section from upper outer quadrant\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - random section from lower outer quadrant, 15 agg.\u000aTotal fixation time is 28 hours.\u000aDictated by: NAM____(signature on file)____MICHAEL J. ROSS, M.D. REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a____(signature on file)____NICOLE MIHOK, M.D. REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a[report_end]
