biopsy specimen (5.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm),\u000awhich has been previously inked by the surgeon. The specimen bears a short\u000astitch to denote the superior, and long stitch to denote the lateral margin,\u000aand contains a wire localization needle. An accompanying radiograph\u000ademonstrates a radiopaque mass at the site of the wire localization needle.\u000aThe specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral, revealing a white,\u000afirm, well-circumscribed nodule (1.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which appears to abut the\u000aposterior and inferior margins, and is present REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom the anterior, REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial and REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin.\u000aThe remainder of the breast parenchyma is comprised predominantly of firm,\u000awhite fibrous tissue (30%) and unremarkable yellow adipose tissue (70%). The\u000anodule is entirely submitted and representative sections of the medial,\u000alateral, superior, and anterior margins are submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  nodule from medial to lateral (including posterior and inferior\u000amargins, 2 or 3 frags, ESS\u000aMicro 4: medial perpendicular margin, 2 frags, RSS\u000aMicro 5: lateral perpendicular margin, 2 frags, RSS\u000aMicro 6: superior margin, 2 frags, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  anterior margin, 1 frag each, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  representative breast parenchyma, 1 or 2 frags, RSS\u000alcl\u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
