VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Amend/Addenda\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, partial mastectomy\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000a********** Addended Report ***********\u000aResident: David C. Park, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Alessandra F Nascimento, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. RIGHT BREAST, SIMPLE MASTECTOMY (364g):\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA WITH MIXED FEATURES\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA\u000aSize - REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aMultifocal - No\u000aHistologic type - Mixed Ductal and Lobular\u000aTubules - < 10% (3 points)\u000aNuclear grade - Intermediate (2 points)\u000aMitotic counts - 1 point\u000aEIC - Negative\u000aLVI - Absent\u000aDermal LVI - Absent\u000aSkin invasion - Absent\u000aSkeletal muscle invasion - Not applicable\u000aFinal Margins (invasive)\u000aNegative (> REMOVED_DATE cm) - Deep\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU - Absent\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - Absent\u000aOTHER FINDINGS\u000aALH, core biopsy site, calcifications in benign epithelium\u000aAJCC Classification (6th edition) - pREMOVED_ACCESSION_IDb NX MX\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER, PR, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) - Pending\u000aB. LEFT BREAST, SIMPLE MASTECTOMY (432g):\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia with pagetoid spread.\u000aBreast tissue with calcifications in benign epithelium, columnar cell\u000achanges and epithelial hyperplasia.\u000aSkin with no significant pathologic change.\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 54 year old post-menopausal woman, S/P REMOVED_DATE  R breast core bxs (from\u000a10/29/08 - outside) revealing well-differentiated grade I/III IC, no LVI, S/P R\u000alumpectomy and XRT - 2000.\u000aOperation: Bilateral skin-sparing simple mastectomy, recon (TRAM Flap).\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Recurrent rt breast cancer.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) right breast - short suture/superior, long suture/lateral near old\u000alumpectomy site.\u000aB/2) lt breast - short suture/superior, long suture/lateral.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart A, "right breast - short suture/superior, long suture/lateral near old\u000alumpectomy site", consists of a 364-gram simple mastectomy specimen (22.0 x\u000a18.0 x REMOVED_DATE cm) containing nipple-areolar complex (4.2 x REMOVED_DATE cm) with an everted\u000anipple (1.3 cm in diameter) with a short stitch designating superior, long\u000astitch designating lateral. The deep surface is covered by an intact fascial\u000aplane and is inked black. The specimen is serially sectioned from medial to\u000alateral in thirteen slices to reveal a firm ill-defined white mass (1.0 x REMOVED_DATE x\u000a0.8 cm) in slice #10 located REMOVED_DATE cm from the deep margin and at the junction of\u000athe upper inner and lower inner quadrants. The remainder of the breast\u000aparenchyma consists of approximately 40% unremarkable fibrous tissue and 60%\u000aunremarkable lobulated adipose tissue. No gross evidence of prior\u000alumpectomy/serosal cavity is identified on the lateral aspect of the specimen.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Firm white mass in slice #10, bisected, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Fibrous tissue immediately medial to mass in slice #10, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Fibrous tissue immediately lateral to mass in slice #10, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Possible serosal cavity in slice #4, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Deep margin associated with mass in slice #10, perpendicular, 1 frag,\u000aRSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Fibrous tissue in upper/outer quadrant, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Fibrous tissue in lower/outer quadrant, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Scant fibrous tissue in lower/inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Scant fibrous tissue in upper/inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Nipple, 1 frag, RSS.\u000a(Micro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID corresponds to area of metallic clip).\u000aPart B, "left breast - short suture/superior, long suture/lateral", consists of\u000aa 432-gram simple mastectomy specimen (23.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) containing a\u000anipple-areolar complex (3.6 x REMOVED_DATE cm) with an everted nipple (1.4 cm in\u000adiameter) with a short stitch designating superior and long stitch designating\u000alateral. The deep margin consists of an intact fascial plane and is inked\u000ablack. The specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral in eight\u000aslices to reveal approximately 60% unremarkable lobulated adipose tissue and\u000a40% unremarkable fibrous tissue.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Fibrous tissue in upper inner quadrant, 2 frags each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Fibrous tissue in lower inner quadrant, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Fibrous tissue in lower outer quadrant, 2 frags each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Fibrous tissue in upper outer quadrant, 2 frags each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Nipple, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aDCP/lp\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Alessandra F Nascimento M.D., Electronically signed on\u000aFriday REMOVED_MONTH 02, 2009 at 09:54:13AM\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM:\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for invasive carcinoma (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE - LOW\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) NEGATIVE (1+)\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000ainvasive carcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low > 0% - < 10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor cells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but only a\u000aportion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+):Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in >10% of\u000atumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+):Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in >30% of\u000atumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aExternal controls are evaluated and show appropriate Immunoreactivity.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aAddendum #1 by Jane E. Brock M.B., B.S., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000aTuesday REMOVED_MONTH 06, 2009 at 09:38:32AM\u000a[report_end]
