VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-05-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Eric L Snyder, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Alessandra F Nascimento, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZATION FOR A MASS:\u000aPHYLLODES TUMOR, morphologically low grade (1.6 cm).\u000aMitoses number up to 2 per 10 HPF.\u000aNo necrosis is present.\u000aTumor is present at the antero-inferior margin (broad front), REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000amedial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE from the superior margin\u000aand REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin.\u000aColumnar cell hyperplasia.\u000aThis case was reviewed by Dr. D. Dillon, Breast Pathology Service, who concurs.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: None given\u000aOperation: Left breast wire loc, excisional bx\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal left mammogram\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000a1. Wire loc excisional biopsy - left breast, stitch: short superior, long\u000alateral, whip stitch deep margin\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000aMass in specimen.\u000a---E.P. Frost\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patients name, unit number,\u000aand "#1 left breast wire localized excisional biopsy inks to mammo", and\u000aconsists of an ovoid fragment of yellow-tan to tan-pink fibroadipose tissue\u000a(5.1 (M-L) x REMOVED_DATE (S-I) x REMOVED_DATE (A-P) cm), which is oriented per surgeon with two\u000asutures (shot=superior, long=lateral). The specimen is inked per pathology\u000aprotocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue;\u000asuperior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. The specimen is\u000aaccompanied by a radiograph, which shows a mass within the specimen as well as\u000athe wire. There is a needle localization wire entering the anteromedial aspect\u000awith no clear exit site. The specimen is serially sectioned from medial to\u000alateral into 8 slices (slice 1=medial). In slices REMOVED_DATE  there is a somewhat\u000adelineated white-tan lobulated firm mass (1.6 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The wire\u000atraverses the breast tissue superior t0 the mass. The mass is REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000amedial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior margin, and\u000a1.2 cm from the lateral margin. Approximately REMOVED_DATE cm inferolateral to the mass\u000ais a separate focus of dense white-tan firm fibrous tissue (slice 6, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000ax REMOVED_DATE cm), which is REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin. The remaining specimen is\u000acomposed of approximately 85% of yellow-tan lobulated adipose tissue and\u000aapproximately 15% focally dense/lumpy fibrous stroma. A definitive core biopsy\u000atract is not grossly identified. Representative sections (including entire\u000amass) are submitted. Approximately 80% of the specimen is submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: entire mass from medial to lateral (slice REMOVED_DATE ) (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID= closest\u000asuperior margin, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID=closest medial margin, and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID=closest anterior, inferior,\u000aand posterior margins), multiple frags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: slices 6 and 7 lateral margin closest to mass (no mass grossly\u000apresent), 2 frags, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: focus of dense fibrous tissue inferolateral to mass (slice 6), to\u000ainclude intervening tissue, 1 frag, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: dense/lumpy fibrous stroma away from mass (slices 7 and 8), to\u000ainclude superior, posterior, inferior, and anterior margins, 2 frags, RSS\u000aLMB/jp\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Eric L Snyder M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Alessandra F Nascimento M.D., Electronically signed on\u000a12/27/2005\u000a[report_end]
