llipse\u000a(1.8 x REMOVED_DATE cm) designating the anterior surface with a central, well-healed\u000alinear scar (1.4 cm in length), which is less than REMOVED_DATE cm from the nearest\u000aradial margin. The specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral,\u000arevealing a focally hemorrhagic, predominantly smooth-lined biopsy cavity (3.5\u000ax REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), filled with a moderate amount of serosanguineous fluid and\u000agrossly coming to within REMOVED_DATE cm of the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the\u000adeep/chest wall margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000asuperior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial\u000amargin. There is mild fibrosis and fat necrosis surrounding the periphery of\u000athe cavity. The breast tissue medial to the cavity consists predominantly of\u000adense white, focally nodular to cystic fibrous stroma admixed with scant yellow\u000alobulated adipose tissue. The breast tissue just lateral to the cavity is\u000apredominantly yellow lobulated adipose tissue with scant fibrous stroma. No\u000aother gross lesions are identified.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID+REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: biopsy cavity nearest inferior and deep/chest wall margin, 4\u000afrags total, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID+REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: biopsy cavity nearest anterior margin, to include skin, 2\u000afrags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID+REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: biopsy cavity nearest superior margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: biopsy cavity nearest lateral margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: biopsy cavity nearest medial margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID+REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: additional dense fibrous tissue medial to biopsy cavity, 3\u000afrags total, RSS.\u000adfi/lp\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Briana Gleason M.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jeffrey F Krane M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a2/8/2006\u000a[report_end]
