VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Shakti Ramkissoon, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Lucian R Chirieac, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "RIGHT BREAST, MASS, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISIONAL BIOPSY":\u000aColumnar cell change with associated calcifications, apocrine\u000ametaplasia, epithelial hyperplasia, and papilloma.\u000aSclerosing fibrosis with entrapped normal ducts.\u000aFat necrosis, hemosiderin-laden macrophages, and scar consistent with\u000aprior biopsy site.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 34-year-old premenopausal woman S/P REMOVED_DATE  R breast UOQ core bx\u000arevealing sclerosing lesion with radiologic findings - Exc. recommended.\u000aOperation: L breast WL exc. bx.\u000aOperative Findings: None specified.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast mass/abnormal mammogram.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) Right breast mass wire localization for mammography/permanent. Short -\u000asuperior; long - lateral with stitch @ deep margin.\u000aRADIOLOGY: The mass, clip and intact wire are in the specimen. Dr Yeh spoke\u000awith Dr. Rhei in OR 10:50 AM/ ER.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "#1. Right breast mass wire localization", consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afragment of fibroadipose tissue, oriented by sutures designating superior\u000a(short suture) and lateral (long suture) margins. The specimen is inked per\u000apathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black;\u000aanterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange\u000a(inked by surgeon). A localizing wire enters the anterior/superior aspect of\u000athe specimen and traverses inferiorly. The specimen is received along with a\u000aradiograph demonstrating the localizing wire in place within an ill-defined\u000alesion marked by a metallic surgical clip (centrally within the specimen). A\u000awhip stitch marks the specimen's deep margin. Please note: There is a\u000anear-full thickness defect, loosely approximated with a white suture by the\u000asurgeon, involving the majority of the central/inferior portion of the\u000aspecimen, where the lesion is presumed to be (per radiograph). Tissue in this\u000aarea is therefore obscured by this large cauterized defect (at least REMOVED_DATE cm in\u000agreatest dimension). The remaining specimen is comprised of REMOVED_DATE % dense\u000atan/white fibrous tissue without palpable or visible masses, lesions or other\u000aabnormalities grossly. The entire specimen is submitted, sequentially from\u000asuperior to inferior, with perpendicular superior margin in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, perpendicular\u000ainferior margin in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, and area of interest (per clip, localizing\u000awire) likely in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Entire specimen, sequentially from superior to inferior, multi\u000afrags, ESS.\u000aDB/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Lucian R Chirieac M.D., Electronically signed on Monday\u000aREMOVED_MONTH 12, 2009 at 01:49:29PM\u000a[report_end]
