S DESCRIPTION: by MAGI GALLUZZI,CRISTINA,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in three parts, labeled with the patient's name\u000aand unit number.\u000aPart one, labeled "Sentinel lymph nodes, right axilla", consists of three\u000afragments of fibroadipose tissue, measuring in aggregate REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000aThree lymph nodes are identified in the specimen, the largest of which measures\u000a1.4 cm in greatest dimension. The lymph nodes are serially sectioned and\u000aentirely submitted in three cassettes.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  three (3) sentinel lymhp nodes, multi frags, ESS.\u000aPart two, labeled "Axillary node sampling, right", consists of multiple\u000afragments of fibroadipose tissue measuring in aggregate 10 x 7 x REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000aTwelve (12) possible lymph nodes are identified in the specimen. The largest\u000aof which measures REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest dimension.\u000aMicro 4: three(3) lymph nodes, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 5: two (2) lymph nodes, 5 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 6: one (1) lymph node, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 7: three (3) possible lymph nodes, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aPart three, labeled "Right breast tissue", consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm\u000asegment of fibroadipose tissue partially covered by an ellipse of yellow/gray\u000askin measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. A white/gray firm nodule measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x\u000a0.9 cm is present in the subcutaneous tissue. The nodule is REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000aposterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin, and\u000a1.5 cm from the medial margin. The specimen is inked for the evaluation of\u000amargins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior =\u000agreen; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. Sections of margins are submitted\u000afor microscopic examination.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  nodules and margins of resection, 4 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 12: lateral margin of resection, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 13: medial margin of resection, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aReports to: CHRISTIAN, ROGER, L. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: LYMPH NODE BIOPSY\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: LYMPH NODE BIOPSY\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
