VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID:REMOVED_CASE_ID Report Status: Signed\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aDIAGNOSIS:\u000aRight breast (726 grams), simple mastectomy:\u000aInvasive lobular carcinoma, poorly differentiated, residual foci (see\u000asynoptic report).\u000aSYNOPTIC REPORT\u000aINVASIVE TUMOR:\u000a-histologic type: invasive lobular carcinoma, two foci\u000a-histologic grade: poorly differentiated\u000a-size (greatest dimension): residual focus adjacent and superior\u000ato medial end of cavity is REMOVED_DATE to\u000a2.5 cm.; separate REMOVED_DATE cm. focus in\u000alower outer quadrant\u000a-lymphatic/vascular invasion: none identified\u000a-perineural invasion: none identified\u000a-microcalcification in invasive tumor: none identified\u000a-margins for invasive tumor: negative (0.5 cm. from closest\u000amargin).\u000aSKIN:\u000a-nipple: unremarkable\u000a-skin/dermis: dermal chronic inflammation and fibroplasia; small benign\u000ahemangioma.\u000aADDITIONAL PATHOLOGIC FINDINGS: fibrocystic changes with sclerosing adenosis,\u000amicrocalcifications, small fibroadenomas.\u000aPRIOR RELATED SPECIMENS REVIEWED: Right breast at REMOVED_DATE o'clock needle core\u000abiopsy, S-02-REMOVED_CASE_ID (12/26/02) and report of outside right breast excision\u000a(MGH case # REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_DATE ).\u000aFinal Diagnosis by: Daniel D. Koelliker, M.D.\u000aClinical diagnosis & history:\u000aRight breast carcinoma; S/P neoadjuvant chemotherapy; had lumpectomy and\u000aaxillary lymph node dissection with positive margins\u000aTissue-Designation:\u000aBreast, simple mastectomy - right\u000aGross description:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled "right breast tissue, suture marker at\u000a12 o'clock" and consists of a 726 gram, REMOVED_DATE x 21 x 4 cm. simple mastectomy\u000aspecimen with a REMOVED_DATE x 7 cm. skin ellipse on one surface and one point marked\u000awith a suture oriented as 12 o'clock of the right breast simple mastectomy\u000aspecimen. The skin ellipse has a 3 cm. in diameter areola with a REMOVED_DATE cm. in\u000adiameter unremarkable nipple, a REMOVED_DATE cm. in diameter round, well demarcated,\u000areddish lesion of the skin located REMOVED_DATE cm. from the nipple at 9 o'clock, and a\u000a4.8 cm. long well healed linear scar located approximately 3 cm. from the\u000anipple in the REMOVED_DATE o'clock area. Otherwise, the skin surface is unremarkable.\u000aThe surrounding adipose tissue is unremarkable. The deep surface shows a\u000asmooth surface of fibroadipose tissue with no gross evidence of tumor seen.\u000aThe margins are inked. Cross sectioning demonstrates a 9 x 5 x REMOVED_DATE cm. cavity\u000awhich involves both lower quadrants. The cavity contains a small amount of\u000ablood and blood clot and has a red, granular inner layer with no gross tumor\u000aseen. Sectioning through the wall surrounding the cavity demonstrates areas of\u000afat necrosis, firm whitish-tan areas and reddish areas and an ill-defined hard\u000aarea superior to the medial end of the cavity. The remainder of the breast\u000ashows mostly yellow lobulated adipose tissue on sectioning with thin strands of\u000awhite-tan fibrous tissue and occasional rubbery, white-tan fibrous areas. No\u000agross suspicious mass lesions are seen.\u000aSection code: 1 & 2 - representative sections from medial end and upper inner\u000aquadrant\u000a3 - medial end of cavity in lower inner quadrant\u000a4-8 - lower inner quadrant including fat necrosis superior to\u000acavity\u000a9 - nipple\u000a10 - deep margin\u000a11-13 - central portion of lower half including cavity\u000a14 - firm area superior to central portion of cavity\u000a15 - skin with scar and reddish lesion\u000a16-18 - lower outer quadrant\u000a19 - upper outer quadrant\u000a20 - lateral end\u000aDictated by: DDK____(signature on file)____NICOLE MIHOK, M.D. REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a____(signature on file)____DANIEL D. KOELLIKER, M.D. REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a[report_end]
