SA.\u000aMicro 1: FSA remnant, 1 frag, ESS\u000aPart two, labeled "#2. right breast tissue", consists of three fragments of\u000afibrous breast tissue (2.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The specimen is submitted\u000aunoriented, therefore it is inked in its entirety in black and entirely\u000asubmitted for histologic analysis.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  right breast tissue, 2 frags each, ESS\u000aPart three, labeled "#3. additional right breast tissue", consists of two\u000afragments of fibrous breast tissue (3.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The specimens are\u000aentirely submitted unoriented therefore they are entirely inked in black. The\u000aspecimens are sectioned to reveal white whorled fibrous tissue within the\u000abreast tissue. The specimen is entirely submitted for histologic analysis.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  right breast tissue, REMOVED_DATE frags each, ESS\u000adwa\u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST BIOPSY W/O MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST BIOPSY W/O MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST BIOPSY W/O MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
