VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID SKIN- OTHER THAN CYST, TAG OR DEBRIDEMENT\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aODZE, ROBERT, DANIEL, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by ODZE,ROBERT DANIEL,M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "SCAR, REVISION, LATERAL ASPECT OF RIGHT MASTECTOMY"\u000a(specimen #1 of 7 specimens):\u000aSkin with cicatrix and granuloma reaction to suture material\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy.\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "ADDITIONAL RIGHT MASTECTOMY SCAR " (specimen #2 of 7\u000aspecimens):\u000aSkin and subcutaneous tissue with no significant pathologic change.\u000aLEFT BREAST, MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY (specimen #5 of 7 specimens), SENTINEL\u000aNODE BIOPSIES (specimens #3 and #4 of 7 specimens), AND AXILLARY NODE\u000aDISSECTION (specimen #7 of 7 specimens):\u000aINVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aMETASTATIC CARCINOMA TO LYMPH NODES\u000aSYNOPSIS:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA\u000aSize - REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aMultifocal - no\u000aHistologic Type - ductal\u000aHistologic Grade (SBR) - III (poor)\u000aNuclear Grade - high\u000aEIC - negative\u000aLymphovascular invasion - extensively present\u000aDermal lymphatic invasion - absent\u000aSkin invasion - absent\u000aSkeletal muscle invasion - N/A\u000aFinal Margins (invasive) -\u000aNegative (>0.3 cm) - deep margin\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aTypes - comedo, solid, cribriform\u000aNuclear grade - high\u000aCalcifications in DCIS - present\u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - present\u000aExtent of DCIS\u000aNumber of blocks:total - 6:11 blocks\u000aFinal Margins (DCIS)\u000aNegative (>0.3 cm) - deep margin\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - absent\u000aLYMPH NODES\u000aSentinel Lymph Nodes: positive (tumor presents in FSB only)\u000a(3 H&E levels examined)\u000aNumber of positive nodes - 1\u000aNumber of nodes examined - 2\u000aAxillary Lymph Nodes: - negative\u000aNumber of positive nodes - 0\u000aNumber of nodes examined - 14\u000aTOTAL POSITIVE NODES (all specimens)- 1:16\u000aSize of largest metastatic focus - REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aExtranodal extension - absent\u000aOTHER FINDINGS\u000aComplex sclerosing lesion\u000aPapilloma\u000aSclerosing adenosis\u000aFibroadenoma\u000aCalcifications in benign epithelium\u000aAJCC CLASSIFICATION (6th edition) - REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID pN MX\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER/PR/HER-2) - performed previously\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "ADDITIONAL LEFT BREAST TISSUE, SKIN" (specimen #6 of 7\u000aspecimens):\u000aSkin and subcutaneous tissue with no tumor seen.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: L mastectomy core (+) Grade III inf ductal carcinoma.\u000aOperation: Left modified radical mastectomy with sentinel node biopsy.\u000aOperative findings: Revision of right s/p mastectomy scar.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast CA.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000a1. Scar revision (lat aspect), rt mastectomy, stitch: short = superior/long=\u000alateral.\u000a2. Additional right mastectomy scar.\u000a3. Sentinel node #1 (left).\u000a4. Sentinel node #2 (left).\u000a5. Left breast with mass, long stitch lateral, short stitch superior.\u000a6. Additional left breast tissue skin.\u000a7. Left axillary contents.\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "3) SENTINEL NODE #1" (FSA):\u000aLymph node with no tumor seen.\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "4) SENTINEL NODE #2" (FSB):\u000aMetastatic carcinoma, approximately 2 mm in diameter.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by HONG,XUEFEI,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received in seven parts, each labeled with the patient's name\u000aand unit number.\u000aPart one, "#1 scar revision lateral aspect right mastectomy", consists of a tan\u000askin ellipse (5 x 3 x REMOVED_DATE cm in depth) with long stitch denoting superior and\u000ashort stitch denoting lateral. There is a healed linear scar (6.3 cm in length\u000ax REMOVED_DATE cm) which comes to the closest radial margin (medial aspect of the\u000aspecimen). The specimen is inked as follows: superior = red, inferior =\u000agreen, medial = orange, lateral = yellow, deep = black.\u000aMicro 1: medial tip, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro 2: lateral tip, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro 3&4: scar, 3 frags, RSS.\u000aPart two, "#2 additional right mastectomy scar", consists of a skin ellipse (5\u000ax REMOVED_DATE x 1 cm in depth). The specimen is inked in black. The skin surface and\u000asubcutaneous adipose tissue are unremarkable.\u000aMicro 5: additional scar, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aPart three, "#3 sentinel node #1", consists of tan/yellow adipose tissue (2.5 x\u000a2.0 x REMOVED_DATE cm). One lymph node candidate (1.9 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) is identified.\u000aThe lymph node is trisected and entirely submitted as FSA.\u000aMicro 6: FSA remnant, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aPart four, "#4 sentinel node #2 left", consists of one fragment of tan/yellow\u000aadipose tissue (2.4 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). One lymph node candidate (2.3 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm) is identified. The specimen is entirely submitted as FSB.\u000aMicro 7: FSB remnant, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aPart five, "#5 left beast with mass", consists of modified radical mastectomy\u000aspecimen (30 x 26 x 6 cm) including skin ellipse (26.5 x REMOVED_DATE cm), areola (5.4\u000acm), inverted nipple (0.8 cm diameter). The deep margin is inked in black.\u000aSectioning reveals an ill-defined, tan/white firm mass (5.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm)\u000awhich is REMOVED_DATE cm from deep margin. The tumor is located beneath the nipple and\u000aslightly towards superior. There is a possible satellite lesion (1.2 x REMOVED_DATE x\u000a0.7 cm) which is 3 cm from the main tumor and REMOVED_DATE cm from deep margin.\u000aMicro 8&9: tumor with deep margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 10&11: tumor, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 12: possible satellite nodule, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro 13: tissue between main mass and possible satellite nodule, 1 frag,\u000aRSS.\u000aMicro 14: inner upper quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 15: inner lower quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 16: outer upper quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 17: outer lower quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 18: nipple, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aNo lymph node candidates are identified in the lateral aspect of the specimen.\u000aPart six, "#6 additional left breast tissue skin", consists of two fragments of\u000askin and adipose tissue (6 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm and 14 x 5 x REMOVED_DATE cm in depth). The\u000aspecimen is inked in black. The skin and adipose tissue are grossly\u000aunremarkable. Representative sections are submitted.\u000aMicro 19: skin and adipose tissue, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aPart seven, "#7 left axillary contents", consists of multiple fragments of\u000atan/yellow adipose tissue (7 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate). Fourteen (14) lymph\u000anode candidates (up to REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest dimension) are identified.\u000aMicro 20&21: lymph node candidates, multi frags, ESS.\u000axh\u000aReports to: LESNIKOSKI, BETH-ANN M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: SKIN- OTHER THAN CYST, TAG OR DEBRIDEMENT\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SKIN- OTHER THAN CYST, TAG OR DEBRIDEMENT\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SENTINEL LYMPH NODE\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SENTINEL LYMPH NODE\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY W/REGIONAL LYMPH NODES\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SKIN- OTHER THAN CYST, TAG OR DEBRIDEMENT\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: LYMPH NODE BIOPSY\u000a[report_end]
