VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Benjamin J-C Chen, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Jane E. Brock, M.B., B.S., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. LEFT BREAST EXCISIONAL BIOPSY WIRE LOCALIZATION FOR A CLIP:\u000aBenign breast tissue with focal nuclear atypia adjacent to a recent core biopsy\u000asite with fibrosis and stromal calcification (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, levels examined).\u000aCalcifications associated with normal epithelium and sclerosing adenosis.\u000aThe margins were inked and evaluated for the final diagnosis.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 66 y/o female S/P REMOVED_DATE R mastectomy for treatment of recurrent DCIS\u000awith microinvasion after 1992 L lumpectomy for IDC atypical nuclei and apocrine\u000achange in lobules, excision recommended.\u000aOperation: L breast wire-localized biopsy.\u000aOperative Findings: None provided.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal mammogram - core with atypia; hx L breast CA.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) Left breast tissue (short suture - superior, long - lateral, whip stitch\u000aon deep margin).\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "left breast tissue short superior, long lateral, whipstitch deep margin",\u000aconsists of an irregular tan/yellow lobulated portion of fibroadipose breast\u000atissue (4.0 cm medial to lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm superior to inferior, and REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aanterior to posterior) with a short suture designating the superior margin,\u000along suture designating the lateral margin, and a whipstitch designating the\u000aposterior margin. The specimen radiograph interpreted via centricity\u000ademonstrates a wire and clip in the specimen. There is a needle localization\u000awire in place, which enters through the anterior-inferior aspect of the\u000aspecimen. The specimen has been previously inked per the surgeon per pathology\u000aprotocol (superior red, inferior green, medial orange, lateral yellow, anterior\u000ablue, and posterior black) and serially sectioned from medial to lateral. The\u000aspecimen reveals a well-circumscribed pink/tan biopsy cavity filled with a\u000atan/white granular material (1.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which comes within less than\u000a0.1 cm from the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000athe anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial\u000amargin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin. Within the biopsy site is a silver\u000ametallic surgical biopsy clip. The remainder of the breast parenchyma is\u000atan/yellow and homogeneous with predominantly dense white fibrous tissue\u000aconstituting greater than 95% of the breast parenchyma. No additional lesions\u000aor areas of disruption are grossly identified. The specimen is submitted in\u000aits entirety.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross sections medial to lateral, blocks REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID to\u000ainclude biopsy cavity, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aSEK/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jane E. Brock M.B., B.S., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000aMonday REMOVED_MONTH 04, 2010 at 07:57:41PM\u000a[report_end]
