VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aSCHNITT, STUART, J., M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by SCHNITT,STUART J.,M.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZATION FOR A MASS:\u000aFibroepithelial tumor, (see note).\u000aNOTE: The histologic features are most consistent with fibroadenoma.\u000aHowever, in some areas the stromal component extends irregularly into the\u000asurrounding tissue and extends to within REMOVED_DATE mm of the anterior and\u000alateral margins. The significane of this finding is unclear in a lesion\u000athat otherwise has features of a fibroadenoma.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Core suggestive of phyllodes tumor\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Lt breast mass\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. left needle-directed breast biopsy -\u000aStitch: Long=lateral, short=superior\u000aRADIOLOGY REPORT: Mass in specimen.\u000aD. Smith, MD\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by CARLSON,JOSEPH WOODWARD,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "Left needle-directed breast biopsy ", and consists of a needle-localized\u000abreast excision specimen (2.8 cm superior-inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm anterior-posterior,\u000a1.6 cm medial-lateral), with two sutures placed by the surgeon. The long\u000asuture is designated as lateral, and the short suture is designated as\u000asuperior. A needle-localization wire enters at the inferolateral posterior\u000aintersection and exits the specimen at the anterior surface.\u000aA specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins:\u000aposterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow;\u000amedial/orange.\u000aThe specimen radiograph accompanies the specimen which is reviewed and which\u000ademonstrates a mass in the specimen. The specimen is sectioned from inferior\u000ato superior in eight sections.\u000aMicro #1-8: Entire specimen from inferior to superior, 8 frags, ESS.\u000ajoc/\u000aReports to: IGLEHART, JAMES, DIRK M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
