VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Amend/Addenda\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Sentinel Lymph Nodes(s)\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000a********** Addended Report ***********\u000aResident: Elizabeth Amy Morgan, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Hejin P Hahn, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A CLIP AND SENTINEL NODE BIOPSY (Part\u000aA (including FSA) and Part B):\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA WITH MIXED FEATURES\u000aCARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aMETASTATIC CARCINOMA TO LYMPH NODES\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA\u000aSize - REMOVED_DATE cm and REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aMultifocal - Yes\u000aThe separate REMOVED_DATE cm focus of invasive carcinoma is located medial to the main\u000a3.6 cm mass and is associated with extensive carcinoma in situ.\u000aHistologic type - Mixed Ductal and Lobular\u000aHistologic grade (SBR) - II (Moderate) (6 to 7 points)\u000aTubules - < 10% (3 points)\u000aNuclear grade - Intermediate (2 points)\u000aMitotic counts - 2 points\u000aEIC - Positive\u000aLVI - Absent\u000aDermal LVI - Not applicable\u000aSkin invasion - Not applicable\u000aSkeletal muscle invasion - Not applicable\u000aFinal Margins (invasive)\u000aNegative (> REMOVED_DATE cm) - Superior, inferior, lateral, anterior,\u000aposterior\u000aClose (0.1 to REMOVED_DATE cm) - Medial (0.15 cm; block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID)\u000aCARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aTypes - Solid\u000aNuclear grade - Intermediate\u000aCalcifications in CIS - Present\u000aCentral necrosis in CIS - Present\u000aMicroinvasion (<0.1cm) - Present-single focus (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID)\u000aExtent of CIS\u000aNumber of blocks/total - 8:18 blocks (Blocks REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID)\u000aMargins (CIS)\u000aNegative (> REMOVED_DATE cm) - Superior, inferior, anterior, lateral\u000aClose (0.1 to REMOVED_DATE cm) - Medial (0.25 cm, focal, Block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID)\u000aPositive (ink on CIS) - Posterior (focal, Block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID)\u000aLYMPH NODES\u000aSentinel lymph nodes ? Positive (3 H&E levels examined; see\u000aNOTE)\u000aNumber of positive nodes - 1\u000aNumber of nodes examined - 1\u000aTOTAL POSITIVE NODES (all specimens)- REMOVED_DATE \u000aSize of largest metastatic focus - REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aNumber of nodes w/macrometastases- 1\u000aExtranodal extension - Absent\u000aOTHER FINDINGS\u000aCore biopsy site\u000aSclerosing adenosis\u000aFibroadenoma\u000aCalcifications in benign epithelium\u000aAJCC Classification (6th edition): REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDa(sn) MX with multiple foci of\u000ainvasion.\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER, PR, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) - Special studies on the main focus of\u000ainvasive carcinoma were performed previously. Special studies on the REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afocus of invasive carcinoma are pending.\u000aNOTE:\u000aThe metastatic deposit is not present on the frozen section slides. (Dr. Rhei\u000anotified by Dr. Morgan on REMOVED_DATE  by telephone).\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 60 year-old woman s/p REMOVED_DATE  R breast core bx revealing moderately\u000adifferentiated grade II/III IC with ductal + lobular features, no definite LVI,\u000aintermediate nuclear grade DCIS.\u000aOperation: R breast WL lumpectomy, SNM, SLNB, ? ALND.\u000aOperative Findings: Not provided.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: None given.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA. RT sentinel node hot + blue FS.\u000aB. RT breast tissue stitch = short superior, long lateral + whip stitch = deep\u000amargin (to mammo).\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000aHookwire and clip in surgical specimen. Results called to Dr. Rhei at 2:10 PM.\u000aIllegible signature.\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "RT SENTINEL NOT HOT & BLUE" (FSA):\u000aLymph node; negative for tumor.\u000aOR Consultation by: WILLIAM ROBERT WELCH, M.D.\u000aResident: WAI CHIN FOO, MD\u000aThe senior physician certifies that he/she personally conducted a gross and/or\u000amicroscopic examination of the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed\u000athe rapid diagnos(es) related thereto.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number. Please note: The containers for both specimens (Part A\u000aand Part B) are labeled "#1". However, the specimen for Part B is labeled #2\u000aon the requisition form.\u000aPart A, "#1. Rt sentinel node, hot and blue", consists of a single loose, fatty\u000asoft tissue fragment (2.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). Within the specimen is a possible\u000alymph node candidate, which is bisected and entirely submitted for\u000aintraoperative consultation as FSA. The remainder of the fatty tissue is not\u000afrozen.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: FSA remnant, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Remainder of fatty tissue, multi frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, "#1. Rt breast tissue, stitch equals short superior, long lateral,\u000awhipstitch deep margin", consists of a single lumpectomy specimen (medial to\u000alateral, REMOVED_DATE cm; anterior to posterior, REMOVED_DATE cm; superior to inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm).\u000aThe specimen is marked by the surgeon with sutures: Short equals superior,\u000along equals lateral, whipstitch equals deep margin. The specimen is inked by\u000athe surgeon per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins:\u000aposterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow;\u000amedial/orange. There is a hookwire, which enters at the superior margin, and\u000amarks a clip as noted by the accompanying radiograph. The specimen is serially\u000asectioned from lateral to medial to reveal an ill-defined, firm, white/pink,\u000airregular area at the site of the clip (3.6 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). This white,\u000airregular area grossly abuts the superior margin, comes to within REMOVED_DATE cm of the\u000aposterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the medial margin,\u000a2.1 cm of the inferior margin, and greater than REMOVED_DATE cm to the lateral margin.\u000aThere is an additional white, irregular, firm area with multiple (approximately\u000aten), well-delineated, white/yellow nodules (ranging from REMOVED_DATE to REMOVED_DATE cm in\u000agreatest dimension) that is REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm and approximately REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000athe other irregular, white area. This second area grossly abuts the inferior\u000amargin, is REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin,\u000a2.8 cm from the lateral margin, and greater than REMOVED_DATE cm to the anterior and\u000amedial margins. Additionally, there are multiple well-circumscribed,\u000ayellow/white nodules (measuring less than REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest dimension)\u000ascattered throughout the breast parenchyma. There is an additional firm area\u000athat is contiguous with the first clip area that may represent additional mass\u000aor fibrous tissue (1.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) that grossly abuts the medial margin and\u000acomes to within REMOVED_DATE cm of the anterior margin. The remainder of the breast\u000aparenchyma consists of adipose tissue. No other gross lesions or masses are\u000anoted. Approximately 50% of the specimen is submitted for histologic\u000aevaluation.\u000aA gross photograph is taken.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: First irregular, white area (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID in relation to both\u000aposterior and superior margins), multi frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Breast parenchyma between first and second irregular areas, 1 frag,\u000aRSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Second irregular area in relation to inferior and posterior\u000amargins, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Representative well-circumscribed white nodule, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Additional fibrous area at medial margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Additional white area contiguous with first area (mass\u000aversus fibrosis), 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, radially sectioned, 4 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin with fibrous area, radially sectioned, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Additional superior margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Additional posterior margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Additional inferior margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Additional anterior margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-08-REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aEM/ajb\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Hejin P Hahn M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a4/17/2008\u000aADDENDUM (04/23/08):\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for the REMOVED_DATE cm focus of invasive carcinoma (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) NEGATIVE (0)\u000aNOTE: This immunoprofile is similar to that of the larger REMOVED_DATE cm focus of\u000atumor.\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000acarcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but only\u000aa portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in >10%\u000aof tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in\u000a>10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aAddendum #1 by Jane E. Brock M.B., B.S., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a4/23/2008\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: (8/22/08)\u000aA paraffin block of invasive carcinoma was sent for the genomic health oncotype\u000aDX Breast Cancer Assay with the following results (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aRecurrence Score = 21\u000aPatients with a Recurrence Score of 21 in the clinical validation study had an\u000aAverage Rate of Recurrence at 10 years of 13% (95% CI: 10% - 17%).\u000aQUANTITATIVE HORMONE RECEPTOR ANALYSIS:\u000aER Score = REMOVED_DATE Positive\u000aPR Score = REMOVED_DATE Positive\u000aAddendum #2 by Andrea L Richardson M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a8/22/2008\u000a[report_end]
