VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Surgical margin\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ROGER L CHRISTIAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Eleanor Y. Chen, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Jeffrey F Krane, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aLEFT BREAST, RE-EXCISION, FINAL SUPERIOR MARGIN:\u000aRESIDUAL DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, cribriform, micropapillary and clinging\u000atypes (low nuclear grade), with associated microcalcifications, but without\u000anecrosis, involving 2 of 22 blocks, adjacent to biopsy site changes.\u000aDCIS is >0.3 cm from the new superior (inked red) margin.\u000aLEFT BREAST, RE-EXCISION, INFERIOR MARGIN:\u000aRESIDUAL DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, cribriform and micropapillary types (low\u000anuclear grade), without associated microcalcifications or necrosis, involving 2\u000aof 20 blocks, adjacent to biopsy site changes.\u000aDCIS is <0.1 cm from the new inferior (inked green) margin (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_DATE 2\u000acm in size; levels examined).\u000aNOTE: Both specimens are entirely submitted for histologic examination. The\u000acase is reviewed by Dr. S. Lester, Breast Pathology Service, who concurs.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: DCIS left breast - close margins.\u000aOperation: Re-excision --> close margins.\u000aOperative Findings: See Op Note.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: DCIS, lt brst.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) left breast tissue - final superior margin.\u000aB/2) left breast tissue - stitch on inferior margin.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart A, "#1. Left breast tissue, final superior margin", and consists of a REMOVED_DATE \u000ax REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm excision of fibroadipose tissue with a suture on one broad\u000asurface designating superior. This surface has been previously inked in red by\u000athe surgeon, the opposing surface is inked in blue by the prosector. Cut\u000asurfaces demonstrate unremarkable tan/yellow adipose tissue (at least 95%),\u000awith occasional tan/white fibrous septae. There is focal hemorrhage and fat\u000anecrosis along the blue-inked surface, compatible with biopsy cavity wall. The\u000aentire specimen is submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Representative sections, sequentially, multi frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Remainder breast tissue, multi frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, "#2. Left breast tissue stitch on inferior margin", and consists of an\u000a8.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm excision of fibroadipose tissue with a suture on one broad\u000asurface designating "inferior margin", previously inked in green by surgeon.\u000aThe opposing broad surface has been inked blue by the prosector. Sectioning\u000ademonstrates predominantly unremarkable soft, lobulated tan/yellow adipose\u000atissue (at least 95%), with occasional tan/white fibrous tissue. There is\u000afocal fibrosis, fat necrosis and hemorrhage along the blue-inked surface,\u000acompatible with biopsy cavity wall. There is no residual tumor or other\u000adiscrete abnormalities noted grossly. The entire specimen is submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Representative sequential sections, multi frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Remainder specimen, multi frags, ESS.\u000adb/lp\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jeffrey F Krane M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a11/2/2007\u000a[report_end]
