VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, partial mastectomy\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ROGER L CHRISTIAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: David C. Park, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Jonathan N Glickman, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aSPECIMEN DESIGNATED "LEFT BREAST, SIMPLE MASTECTOMY":\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aTypes - Cribriform\u000aNuclear grade - Low\u000aCalcifications in DCIS - Present\u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - Absent\u000aMicroinvasion (<0.1cm) - Absent\u000aExtent of DCIS\u000aNumber of blocks/total - REMOVED_DATE blocks\u000aMargins (DCIS)\u000aNegative (> REMOVED_DATE cm) - posterior (deep)\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - Absent\u000aOTHER FINDINGS\u000aBiopsy cavity\u000aSkin with scar\u000aAJCC Classification (6th edition) - pTis Nx MX.\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER, PR, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) - Performed previously\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: DCIS lt breast, incomplete resections.\u000aOperation: Lt mastectomy.\u000aOperative Findings: See Op Note.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: DCIS lt breast.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) left breast, suture long/lateral, short/superior.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number\u000aand "#1. Left breast", and consists of a left simple mastectomy specimen (1475\u000agrams; REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), to include two orienting sutures (long lateral;\u000ashort superior), brown/tan skin ellipse (24.0 x REMOVED_DATE cm), brown areola (8.0 cm\u000ain diameter), and an everted nipple (1.3 cm in diameter). There is a\u000awell-healed linear scar (6.5 cm in length) within the upper outer quadrant, REMOVED_DATE \u000acm from the radial skin margin. The deep margin is inked black and the\u000aspecimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral, exhibiting 