VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Lymph nodes, regional resection\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-06-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Eleanor Y. Chen, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Jason L Hornick, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aLEFT BREAST, MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY AND AXILLARY NODE DISSECTION (2\u000aSPECIMENS):\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA AND METASTATIC CARCINOMA TO LYMPH NODES.\u000aSYNOPSIS:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA\u000aSize - REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aMultifocal - No\u000aHistologic Type - Other (see NOTE).\u000aHistologic Grade (SBR) - III (Poor)\u000aNuclear Grade - High\u000aEIC - Negative\u000aLymphovascular invasion - Absent\u000aDermal lymphatic invasion - Absent\u000aSkin invasion - Absent\u000aSkeletal muscle invasion - N/A\u000aFinal Margins (invasive)\u000aNegative (> REMOVED_DATE cm) - deep\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU - Absent\u000aAXILLARY LYMPH NODES - Positive\u000aNumber of positive nodes - 6\u000aNumber of nodes examined - 13\u000aTOTAL POSITIVE NODES (all specimens)- REMOVED_DATE \u000aSize of largest metastatic focus - REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aExtranodal extension - Absent\u000aOTHER FINDINGS:\u000aCore biopsy site, skin with scar, papilloma, fibroadenoma.\u000aAJCC CLASSIFICATION (6th edition) - REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDc pREMOVED_ACCESSION_IDa MX\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER/PR/HER-2) - Performed previously\u000aNOTE: The tumor is composed of sheets of large epithelioid cells with abundant\u000aeosinophilic cytoplasm, including scattered pleomorphic forms, associated with\u000aa marked lymphocytic inflammatory infiltrate. Immunohistochemical studies\u000areveal the tumor cells are positive for PAN-K, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, and S-100 (focal). In situ\u000ahybridization for Epstein-Barr virus-encoded mRNA (EBER) is negative. These\u000afindings support the diagnosis of carcinoma.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 65-year-old postmenopausal female, not currently on HRT. History of\u000aright DCIS, status-post lumpectomy, radiation, declined TAM. Developed\u000aenlarged left axillary lymph nodes. Left mammogram shows interval breast mass.\u000aFNA of axilla shows malignant cells. Core biopsy of left mass shows invasive\u000acancer, possibly consistent with breast origin. CT of abdomen/chest negative\u000afor mets or lesions.\u000aOperation: Left modified radical mastectomy.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast cancer.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Axillary contents, left level 1 and 2.\u000aB/2. Left breast - stitch long/lateral, short/superior, bow tie on level 1 and\u000a2 lymph nodes.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two parts, each labeled with the patient?s\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart A, "left axillary contents, level 1 and 2", consists of multiple fragments\u000aof fibroadipose tissue (measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate) including a\u000alymph node candidate (the largest measuring REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest dimension).\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Three lymph nodes, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: One lymph node, sectioned into four, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: One lymph node, bisected, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: One lymph node, bisected, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Two lymph nodes, one bisected and inked black, 3 frags,\u000aESS.\u000aPart B, "left breast - stitch long/lateral, short/superior, bow tie on level 1\u000aand 2 lymph nodes", consists of a 750-gram left modified radical mastectomy\u000aspecimen (21.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with a white/tan skin ellipse (15.2 x REMOVED_DATE cm,\u000aexcised to a depth of REMOVED_DATE cm) and attached axillary tail (8.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm).\u000aThere is a bow tie designating level 1 and 2 lymph nodes, long stitch\u000adesignating lateral, short stitch designating superior. There is a well-healed\u000asurgical scar (5.0 cm in length) on the skin ellipse, inferior to the areola\u000aarea, in lower outer quadrant. There is a firm, nodular mass (1.8 cm in\u000agreatest dimension), located at the junction of lower outer and lower inner\u000aquadrant, at least REMOVED_DATE cm from the skin scar and REMOVED_DATE cm to the closest deep\u000amargin. The fascial plane is partially disrupted with scant skeletal muscle\u000apresent. The remainder of the breast parenchyma consists of approximately 30%\u000afibrous tissue. Six enlarged lymph nodes (ranging from REMOVED_DATE to REMOVED_DATE cm) are\u000aidentified in the axillary tail near the bow tie on level 1 and 2.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Firm lesion, with REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID including deep margin, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Breast parenchyma including fibrous stroma, adjacent to the\u000alesion, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Upper/outer quadrant including underlying deep margins, 2\u000afrags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Upper/inner quadrant, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lower/outer quadrant, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lower/inner quadrant with REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID including breast parenchyma\u000aadjacent to lesion, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Skin with scar, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Nipple, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: One lymph node, serially sectioned, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: One lymph node serially sectioned, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: One lymph node, serially sectioned, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: One lymph node, trisected, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: One lymph node, trisected, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: One lymph node, bisected, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aELC/lp\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jason L Hornick M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a10/16/2006\u000a[report_end]
