ous parenchyma. No gross lesions at the clip site can be\u000aidentified. The specimen is serially sectioned from superior to inferior and\u000aentirely submitted for histological examination with the clip site in cassette\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Superior margin, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Serial section from superior to inferior, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Inferior margin, multi frags, ESS.\u000aLC/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Lucian R Chirieac M.D., Electronically signed on Tuesday\u000aFebruary 10, 2009 at 11:03:22AM\u000a[report_end]
