VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID:REMOVED_CASE_ID Report Status: Signed\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aADDENDUM REPORT\u000aAddendum #1 Entered: REMOVED_DATE -1520\u000a*** ADDITIONAL DIAGNOSTIC INFORMATION ***\u000aThis report contains an addendum to the original for the purpose of providing\u000aadditional diagnostic information. The original diagnosis is unchanged.\u000aImmunohistochemical studies performed on block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID reveal the following results\u000afor the infiltrating carcinoma:\u000aEstrogen receptor: POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor: POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID): NEGATIVE for overexpression.\u000aAddeundum Signed Electronically Signed ROSS,MICHAEL J. M.D. REMOVED_DATE \u000aDIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. Sentinel lymph node (left axilla), excision:\u000aMetastatic poorly differentiated mammary duct carcinoma with extranodal\u000aextension.\u000aB. Left breast, excision:\u000aPoorly differentiated infiltrating duct carcinoma.\u000aDuctal carcinoma in situ, grade REMOVED_DATE \u000aC. Left breast (superior half, final shaved margin), excision:\u000aNo diagnostic abnormalities recognized.\u000aSYNOPTIC REPORT:\u000aINVASIVE TUMOR:\u000a-histologic type: ductal\u000a-histologic grade: poorly differentiated\u000a-size (greatest dimension): REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000a-lymphatic/vascular invasion: none identified\u000a-perineural invasion: none identified\u000a-microcalcification in invasive tumor: none identified\u000a-margins for invasive tumor: The surgical margins are free of\u000atumor.\u000a-immunohistochemical stains for estrogen/progesterone/REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu will be\u000aperformed on block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and reported in an addendum to follow.\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU (DCIS):\u000a-histologic type: solid and cribriform\u000a-histologic grade: REMOVED_DATE \u000a-size (greatest dimension): microscopic foci within and around\u000ainvasive tumor\u000a-extent: focal\u000a-extensive intraductal component: absent\u000a-necrosis in DCIS: none identified\u000a-microcalcifications in DCIS: none identified\u000a-margins for DCIS: ductal carcinoma in situ extends\u000afocally to within REMOVED_DATE cm. of the\u000adeep margin in section REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aLYMPH NODES:\u000aPositive lymph nodes out of total lymph nodes sampled: REMOVED_DATE \u000a-size of largest metastatic focus (greatest dimension): REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000a-extranodal extension: extensive\u000aADDITIONAL PATHOLOGIC FINDINGS: ductal hyperplasia; fibrocystic changes;\u000afibroadenoma (0.4cm.).\u000aPRIOR RELATED SPECIMENS REVIEWED:\u000aLeft breast (12 o'clock); specimen # S-03-3743; REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by: Michael J. Ross, M.D.\u000aClinical diagnosis & history:\u000aLeft breast cancer\u000aTissue-Designation:\u000aA.Sentinel lymph node - left axillary\u000aB.Breast, excision with margins - left\u000aC.Breast, excision (without margins) - left, superior half, final shaved margin\u000aGross description:\u000aThe specimen is received in three parts.\u000aSpecimen A labeled "left axillary sentinel node" consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm. portion of fat containing a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 cm. firm, tan, crescent shaped\u000anode at one edge. 9X all, labeled REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aSpecimen B labeled "left breast" consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. portion of\u000apartly yellow adipose, partly firm, tan-pink tissue containing a needle wire\u000aentering at the anterior superior aspect. A short suture marks the superior\u000amargin. A long suture marks the lateral margin. The anterior superior margin\u000ais painted with blue ink. The anterior inferior margin is painted with green\u000aink. The deep margin is painted with black ink. The specimen weighs 43 grams.\u000aThe specimen is serially sectioned from lateral to medial. Cut section reveals\u000aa REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. firm, white, stellate mass centrally. Cut section\u000aotherwise shows adipose tissue mixed with rubbery, tan-white tissue. 21X,\u000alabeled REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aSpecimen C labeled "left breast, superior half, final shaved margin" consists\u000aof a REMOVED_DATE x 2 x REMOVED_DATE cm. aggregate of predominantly yellow adipose, partly soft\u000apink tissue. The entire specimen is submitted in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. 3 agg. all.\u000aDictated by: MJR____(signature on file)____DANIEL D. KOELLIKER, M.D. REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a____(signature on file)____MICHAEL J. ROSS, M.D. REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a[report_end]
