VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID:REMOVED_CASE_ID Report Status: Signed\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aADDENDUM REPORT\u000aAddendum #1 Entered: REMOVED_DATE -1342\u000a*** ADDITIONAL DIAGNOSTIC INFORMATION ***\u000aThis report contains an addendum to the original for the purpose of providing\u000aadditional diagnostic information. The original diagnosis is unchanged.\u000aImmunohistochemical staining on the formalin-fixed, paraffin-embedded blocks\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID reveals these results for all three of the infiltrating\u000acarcinomas:\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID): NEGATIVE (no, faint, or <10% complete membrane staining)\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, avidin-biotin complex detection) is assessed visually by\u000aquantitation of the percent of tumor cells staining.\u000aAddeundum Signed Electronically Signed MIHOK,NICOLE M.D. REMOVED_DATE \u000aDIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. Sentinel lymph node, right axilla:\u000aNegative for tumor (0/1).\u000aB. Right breast, lateral margin, excision:\u000aFocus of infiltrating duct carcinoma, well differentiated (0.4 cm.).\u000aDuctal carcinoma in situ, intermediate grade, cribriform and\u000amicropapillary pattern.\u000aDuctal carcinoma in situ focally extends to lateral resection margin.\u000aMargin negative for infiltrating carcinoma.\u000aC. Right breast, medial margin, excision:\u000aProliferative fibrocystic changes with focal atypical ductal hyperplasia.\u000aD. Right breast, inferior margin, excision:\u000aFocus of infiltrating duct carcinoma, well differentiated (0.3 cm.).\u000aDuctal carcinoma in situ, intermediate grade, cribriform and\u000amicropapillary pattern.\u000aMargin negative; both the infiltrating carcinoma and ductal carcinoma in\u000asitu are REMOVED_DATE cm. from the margin.\u000aE. Right breast, superior margin, excision:\u000aBenign breast tissue.\u000aF. Right breast, needle localization, excision:\u000aMultifocal infiltrating duct carcinoma, well differentiated (see synoptic\u000areport).\u000aExtensive, multifocal ductal carcinoma in situ.\u000aSYNOPTIC REPORT:\u000aINVASIVE TUMORS:\u000a-histologic type: infiltrating duct carcinoma (three separate\u000afoci).\u000a-histologic grade: well differentiated\u000a-sizes (greatest dimension): REMOVED_DATE cm. (mid anterior tumor), REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000a(medial-inferior tumor), REMOVED_DATE cm. (lateral\u000atumor); a small REMOVED_DATE cm tumor nodule is located\u000aadjacent to the medial-inferior tumor, and may\u000abe a separate satellite lesion\u000a-lymphatic/vascular invasion: none identified\u000a-perineural invasion: none identified\u000a-microcalcification: present\u000a-margins for invasive tumor: tumor is focally < REMOVED_DATE cm. from lateral margin\u000a(REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID). See specimen B through E above for\u000aadditional margin tissue.\u000a-immunohistochemical staining on prior specimen (S-07-REMOVED_CASE_ID) was reported as:\u000aEstrogen receptor: POSITIVE (>10% of nuclei stained)\u000aProgesterone receptor: POSITIVE (>10% of nuclei stained)\u000a-immunohistochemical staining for REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu will be performed on blocks REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aand REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and reported in an addendum to follow.\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU (DCIS):\u000a-histologic type: cribriform, micropapillary, solid\u000a-histologic grade: intermediate\u000a-size (greatest dimension): Multifocal, spanning > 3 cm.\u000a-extent: multifocal\u000a-extensive intraductal component: present\u000a-necrosis in DCIS: present, focal\u000a-microcalcifications in DCIS: present\u000a-margins for DCIS: positive multifocally and over a broad\u000afront involving posterior,\u000aposterior-inferior, inferior-lateral\u000aand lateral margins. See specimens B\u000athrough E for additional margin tissue.\u000aLYMPH NODES:\u000aOne lymph node sampled is negative for malignancy (0/1)\u000a(0/1 sentinel lymph nodes; REMOVED_DATE non-sentinel lymph nodes).\u000aCOMMENT: The sentinel lymph node, specimen A, is examined at multiple levels\u000awith H&E stains and immunohistochemical stains for keratin.\u000aADDITIONAL PATHOLOGIC FINDINGS:\u000aChanges consistent with prior biopsies sites x 3.\u000aPRIOR RELATED SPECIMENS REVIEWED:\u000aRight breast needle biopsies; S-07-REMOVED_CASE_ID, S-07-REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aAJCC pTNM Classification (6th Ed.): pREMOVED_ACCESSION_IDc pREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID(sn) pMX\u000aThe pathologic TNM classification above is based only on the information\u000aavailable to the pathologist, and therefore may not be accurate.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by: Anthony R. Mattia, M.D.\u000aINTRA-OPERATIVE CONSULTATION:\u000aOPERATING ROOM CONSULTATION (FROZEN SECTION):\u000aSentinel lymph node: No tumor identified.\u000aARM\u000aClinical diagnosis & history:\u000aRight breast carcinoma\u000aTissue-Designation:\u000aA.Sentinel lymph node\u000aB.Breast, excision with margins - right, lateral\u000aC.Breast, excision with margins - right, medial\u000aD.Breast, excision with margins - right, inferior\u000aE.Breast, excision with margins - right, superior\u000aF.Breast, excision with margins - right\u000aGross description:\u000aThe specimen is received in six containers.\u000aSpecimen A is received fresh in the Operating Room, labeled "right sentinel\u000alymph node" and consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. fatty lymph node. The node\u000ais bisected, submitted entirely for frozen section and resubmitted in cassette\u000aAF. 2X all.\u000aSpecimen B is received in formalin, labeled "lateral right breast margin" and\u000aconsists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. fragment of fibroadipose tissue with a stitch\u000aalong one border marking the new margin. This border is inked black. On cut\u000asection, the specimen consists of adipose tissue with focal hemorrhage. 5 agg.\u000aall.\u000aSpecimen C is received in formalin, labeled "medial right breast margin" and\u000aconsists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. fragment of fibroadipose tissue with a stitch\u000amarking one border as the new margin. This surface is inked black. On cut\u000asection, the specimen consists of fibroadipose tissue that is partially blue\u000astained. 6X all, labeled REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aSpecimen D is received in formalin, labeled "inferior right breast margin" and\u000aconsists of a partially blue stained, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. fragment of\u000afibroadipose tissue with a suture marking the new margin. The surface is inked\u000ablack. The specimen is submitted entirely in five cassettes. 6X all.\u000aSpecimen E is received in formalin, labeled "superior right breast margin" and\u000aconsists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. fragment of fibroadipose tissue with a suture\u000amarking the new margin. The surface is inked black. The entire specimen is\u000asubmitted in four cassettes. 7X all.\u000aSpecimen F is received fresh, labeled "right breast mass, short suture\u000asuperior, long suture lateral". It consists of a 70 gram, REMOVED_DATE x 6 x 4 cm.\u000afragment of fibroadipose tissue. Portions of two localizing wires enter\u000aanteriorly and laterally and portions of two wires are free in the container.\u000aSutures are present as labeled. An accompanying specimen mammogram shows three\u000aseparate biopsy clips within the specimen. The specimen is inked as follws:\u000ablack-deep, blue-anterior, yellow-superior, green-inferior, orange-lateral,\u000aviolet-medial. On cut section, there are three separate foci of hemorrhage\u000awith biopsy clips, corresponding to the specimen mammogram. One focus is in\u000athe inferior-medial portion of the specimen, and is REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The\u000aclosest margin is the inferior-deep margin, REMOVED_DATE cm. The surrounding tissue is\u000afirm and fibrotic. There is also a focus of slightly firm tissue, REMOVED_DATE cm. in\u000adiameter that is located REMOVED_DATE cm. superior and medial to this hemorrhagic focus.\u000aThe second focus is in the mid anterior portion of the specimen, and is REMOVED_DATE x\u000a1.5 x REMOVED_DATE cm. This focus of hemorrhage is located REMOVED_DATE cm. from the anterior\u000amargin. In the superior-lateral portion of the specimen is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm. area of hemorrhage surrounded by dense fibrous parenchyma. This focus is\u000a0.8 cm. from the superior-lateral margin. The remaining breast parenchyma is\u000apredominantly dense and fibrous with admixed adipose tissue. Sections are\u000asubmitted as follows. 20X.\u000aSection code: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - entire first described biopsy site in inferior medial\u000aportion with adjacent lesion\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - entire second described biopsy site, mid anterior\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - entire third biopsy site, superior lateral\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - representative inferior margin\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - representative superior margin\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - representative deep margin\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - representative lateral margin\u000aDictated by: ARM____(signature on file)____NICOLE MIHOK, M.D. REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a____(signature on file)____ REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a[report_end]
