VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID:REMOVED_CASE_ID Report Status: Signed\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aDIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. Skin of right chest wall, excision:\u000aNo diagnostic abnormalities recognized.\u000aB. Right breast, simple mastectomy:\u000aAdditional focus of invasive ductal carcinoma, grade 1. (see note)\u000aMultifocal ductal carcinoma in situ, intermediate grade, cribriform and\u000amicropapillary types with associated necrosis.\u000aChanges consistent with prior excision site.\u000aNOTE: Upon histologic examination of the tissue surrounding the prior biopsy\u000acavity, an additional focus of infiltrating ductal carcinoma is\u000aidentified. This focus is medial to the prior excision and it's size is\u000a0.4 x REMOVED_DATE cm. It is not associated with microcalcifications or\u000aangiolymphatic invasion, however there is microscopic quantities of\u000aintermediate grade ductal carcinoma in situ associated with the invasive\u000atumor. The surgical resection margins are clear.\u000aResidual ductal carcinoma in situ is also identified laterally and\u000aposteriorly to the prior biopsy cavity. The final margins are clear.\u000aThe AJCC pTNM Classification (6th Ed.) is unchanged at pREMOVED_ACCESSION_IDc pREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID(sn) PMX\u000aThe pathologic TNM classification above is based only on the information\u000aavailable to the pathologist, and therefore may not be accurate.\u000aSee report on the prior specimen (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) for full synoptic reporting.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by: Todd E. Abbott, M.D.\u000aClinical diagnosis & history:\u000aRight breast carcinoma\u000aTissue-Designation:\u000aA.Skin, excision - right chest wall\u000aB.Breast, simple mastectomy - right\u000aGross description:\u000aThe specimen is received in two containers.\u000aSpecimen A is received in formalin, labeled "right chest wall skin, suture at\u000amedial" and consists of a long strip of skin and subcutaneous tissue that when\u000areapproximated creates a donut shaped fragment with an inside diameter of REMOVED_DATE \u000acm. and an outside diameter of REMOVED_DATE cm. There is a suture indicating the medial\u000aaspect. The specimen is sectioned and submitted as follows. 4 agg.\u000aSection code: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - 12 o'clock\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - 3 o'clock\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - 6 o'clock\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - 9 o'clock\u000aSpecimen B is received fresh, labeled "simple mastectomy, right breast" and\u000aconsists of a 641 gram, 17 x REMOVED_DATE x up to REMOVED_DATE cm. mastectomy with a suture\u000aindicating the axillary tail. There is an irregularly shaped ellipse of skin,\u000aincluding the nipple, measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The nipple is at one end of the\u000aellipse and measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. Overlying the upper outer quadrant there\u000aare dimples in the skin at REMOVED_DATE cm and REMOVED_DATE cm from ellipse end opposite the\u000anipple. The anterior surface is inked blue. The posterior surface is inked\u000aorange. The specimen is serially sectioned revealing a cystic prior biopsy\u000acavity measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. located directly posterior to the skin\u000adimples. At least three surgical clips are identified in this area. The\u000acavity is REMOVED_DATE cm. from the posterior resection margin and REMOVED_DATE cm. from the\u000anearest anterior superior resection margin. The remainder of the breast is\u000asectioned revealing yellow, lobular breast parenchyma with stringy white\u000afibrous tissue. 28 agg.\u000aSection code: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - biopsy cavity, lateral aspect\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - biopsy cavity in relation to posterior margin\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - biopsy cavity in relation to anterior superior margin\u000aand skin\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - biopsy cavity, medial aspect\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - lower outer quadrant\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - upper inner quadrant\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - lower inner quadrant\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - nipple section\u000aTotal fixation time is 8 hours.\u000aDictated by: TEA____(signature on file)____ REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a____(signature on file)____ REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a[report_end]
