VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Amend/Addenda\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-06-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000a********** Addended Report ***********\u000aResident: Jian Shen, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Andrea L Richardson, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR CALCIFICATIONS AND A CLIP:\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU.\u000aSYNOPSIS:\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU Present\u000aTypes Solid and cribriform\u000aNuclear grade Low\u000aCalcifications in DCIS Present\u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS Present\u000aMicroinvasion (<0.1cm) Absent\u000aExtent of DCIS\u000aMargins (DCIS)\u000aNumber of blocks/total REMOVED_DATE blocks\u000aEstimated overall size REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aMargins (DCIS):\u000aClose (0.1 - REMOVED_DATE cm) Medial\u000aVery close (<0.1cm) Superior, lateral, posterior, inferior\u000aPositive (ink on DCIS) Anterior\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU Absent\u000aOTHER FINDINGS:\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia.\u000aCore biopsy site.\u000aAJCC CLASSIFICATION (6th edition) Tis pNx MX\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER/PR/HER-2) Pending\u000aNOTE:\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 63-year-old postmenopausal female with history of five years of HRT\u000a(not currently), with right upper calcifications on mammogram. Stereo core\u000abiopsy REMOVED_DATE  - atypical ductal hyperplasia.\u000aOperation: Right breast wire-localized biopsy.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal right mammogram.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Right breast tissue - short suture = superior, long suture = lateral,\u000awhipstitch = deep margin. Mammo 12:45\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000aClip and many calcifications in specimen. Signed: C. Denison, M.D.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patients name, unit number,\u000aand "1. Right breast tissue - short superior, long lateral, whipstitch deep\u000amargin", and consists of one fragment of fibroadipose tissue (4.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm). The specimen is inked by the surgeon per pathology protocol for the\u000aevaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red;\u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. The localizing wire enters from\u000athe anterior aspect of the specimen towards the superior-posterior aspect. The\u000aspecimen is sectioned from superior to inferior aspect to reveal a biopsy\u000acavity in slices 3 and 4 measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm, located REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000amedial margin and REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin. Adjacent to the biopsy\u000acavity, there is an ill-defined area of fibrous tissue (1.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm).\u000aThe specimen is entirely submitted for histologic evaluation. The specimen is\u000areceived with a radiograph showing clip, mass, residual calcifications and\u000awire.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 1, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 2, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 3 (clip), 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 4, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 5, 2 frags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 6, 1 frag, ESS\u000aMRU/elw\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Marianna B Ruzinova M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Andrea L Richardson M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a1/19/2006\u000aSurgical Addendum: (1/24/06)\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU (block):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) POSITIVE (2+)\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000acarcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but only\u000aa portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in >10%\u000aof tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in\u000a>10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aAddendum by Andrea L Richardson M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aAddendum #1 by Andrea L Richardson M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a1/24/2006\u000a[report_end]
