VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-06-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Marianna B Ruzinova, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Shuji Ogino, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST RE-EXCISION:\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN-SITU.\u000aSYNOPSIS:\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU - Present\u000aTypes - Solid, cribriform, micropapillary\u000aNuclear grade - Low to focally intermediate (e.g., REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID)\u000aCalcifications in DCIS - Absent\u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - Present\u000aExtent of DCIS:\u000aNumber of blocks REMOVED_DATE blocks.\u000aFinal Margins (DCIS)\u000aNegative (> REMOVED_DATE cm) superior, posterior, anterior, lateral, medial.\u000aVery close (< REMOVED_DATE cm) inferior (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID; also in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, tumor is REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000ainferior margin).\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - Absent\u000aOTHER FINDINGS:\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia and biopsy cavity.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 63-year-old female with ductal carcinoma in-situ, right breast.\u000a10/27/05 - left breast core biopsy - "atypical ductal hyperplasia".\u000a1/13/06 - right breast wire localized excision - "ductal carcinoma in-situ"\u000awith close, positive margins. Medial - close. Superior /lateral/ posterior/\u000ainferior - very close. Anterior - positive. Atypical ductal hyperplasia.\u000aOperation: Right breast localized re-excision.\u000aPrevious Surgery: REMOVED_DATE  - BS-05-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID; REMOVED_DATE  - BS-06-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aOperative Findings: Excision - right breast tissue.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast carcinoma.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Right breast tissue - short = superior, long = lateral, whip stitch =\u000achest wall (posterior) margin, scar anterior.\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000aSurgical cavity and calcifications are in the center.\u000aSpecimen and two wires.\u000aSigned: Dr. Gombos.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patients name, unit number,\u000aand "#1 Right breast tissue", and consists of one fragment of fibroadipose\u000atissue (7.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which is inked by the surgeon, with orienting\u000asutures provided, per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins:\u000aposterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow;\u000amedial/orange. Accompanying the specimen is a radiograph showing the specimen\u000awith localizing wires, surgical cavity and surrounding mass. The localizing\u000awires are present in the specimen, one entering and exiting through the medial\u000aaspect of the specimen, and the other entering through the lateral aspect.\u000aSerial sectioning of the specimen from medial to lateral aspect reveals a\u000asurgical cavity (1.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which is surrounded by a ring of fibrous\u000atissue (up to REMOVED_DATE cm), abutting the anterior margin. The entire biopsy cavity\u000aand fibrous tissue are submitted for histologic evaluation. The rest of the\u000aspecimen consists of unremarkable yellow adipose tissue.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Surgical cavity with surrounding fibrous tissue, 9 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Superior margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMRU/elw\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Marianna B Ruzinova M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Shuji Ogino M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a2/22/2006\u000a[report_end]
