5:58 GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "left breast, long lateral - short superior", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm piece of fibrofatty tissue. The specimen is inked in black and the posterior (deep) margin is overinked in blue. The specimen is sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm white, gritty stellate mass, REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin and the medial aspect of the specimen, REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin. The lateral margin is marked with two pins and the superior margin is marked with one pin. A representative section of mass with closest posterior margin is frozen as REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, and an additional representative section of mass is frozen as REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. SECTION CODE: A: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. B: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. C-E: The remaining mass in its entirety. F: Representative section REMOVED_DATE cm inferior to the mass. G: Inferior margin taken en face. Received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name and unit number, and "left breast final shaved margins" are multiple pieces of tan yellow fibrous fatty tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate. The largest pieces are inked black. The specimens are entirely submitted in cassettes H-P. Received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name and unit number, and "left axillary lymph node" are multiple pieces of tan yellow soft fatty tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate. The fat is trimmed and lymph nodes are bisected, and one-half of the lymph nodes are submitted in cassettes Q-V. Resident: LAN WANG, MD *** INTRA-OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS *** GROSS DIAGNOSIS #1: (LEFT BREAST): MASS REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE POSTERIOR MARGIN AT THE MEDIAL ASPECT THE SPECIMEN. FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS #1 - #2: (LEFT BREAST): DIFFICULT TO FREEZE, FOCI OF ATYPICAL GLANDS, AWAIT PERMANENTS. O.R. Resident: JOHN BISSONNETTE, MD O.R. Diagnosis by: H. Thomas Aretz, MD =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT - REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID REPORTS TO: Michele Annette Gadd, M.D. PART A: BREAST(LEFT),EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B: BREAST (LEFT FINAL SHAVED MARGINS), EXCISION PART C: LYMPH NODES (LEFT AXILLA), EXCISION\u000a[report_end]
