VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aWELCH, WILLIAM, ROBERT, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by WELCH,WILLIAM ROBERT,M.D.\u000a1) RIGHT BREAST, TISSUE, EXCISION:\u000aINVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA (Bloom-Richardson grade III/III), REMOVED_DATE cm, with\u000afocal extension into a duct (blocks #1 and 2), and in association with\u000athe prior biopsy site.\u000aThe tumor is present within REMOVED_DATE cm of the nearest (inferior) margin.\u000aAll other margins are free of tumor.\u000aNo lymphatic/vascular invasion is identified.\u000aFibrocystic change with fibrosis and adenosis.\u000aThe AJCC classification of this tumor is REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Nx Mx.\u000aNOTE:\u000aImmunohistochemical analysis for estrogen receptors, progesterone receptors,\u000aand REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu will be performed and reported in an addendum.\u000a2) RIGHT BREAST (ADDITIONAL TISSUE AT 4:00), EXCISION:\u000aINVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA (Bloom-Richardson grade III/III), REMOVED_DATE cm\u000a(blocks #14 and 14).\u000aThe tumor is >0.4 cm from the new inked margin of resection.\u000aNo lymphatic/vascular invasion is identified.\u000aThe AJCC classification of this tumor is REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDa Nx Mx.\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for invasive carcinoma (block 2):\u000aEstrogen receptor NEGATIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor NEGATIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) NEGATIVE (1+)\u000aNote: Normal epithelial cells are appropriately immunoreactive for estrogen\u000aand progesterone receptors.\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000ainvasive carcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but\u000aonly a portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity\u000ain >10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: History of right axillary node dissection (breast cancer); please\u000asee previous BWH pathology reports (small cancer, right breast detected on\u000aMRI). Specimen in right breast biopsy for excision of cancer done on wire loc.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast cancer.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1. Right breast tissue.\u000a#2. Right additional tissue at 4 o'clock (paint on new margin).\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000a1. RIGHT BREAST BIOPSY, WIRE LOCALIZATION FOR A VAGUE MASS (GROSS EXAMINATION):\u000a0.8 cm irregular firm lesion grossly suspicious for invasive/treated\u000acarcinoma.\u000aThe lesion is close to the inferior margin.\u000a2. RIGHT ADDITIONAL TISSUE AT 4:00 (GROSS EXAMINATION):\u000a0.4 cm firm nodule, grossly suspicious for invasive carcinoma,\u000alocated at REMOVED_DATE cm from the new margin.\u000aThis speicmen encompasses the inferior margin of the first specimen.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by CORBO,JOSEPH,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two (2) parts, each labeled with the\u000apatient's name and unit number.\u000aPart #1, "#1. right breast tissue," consists of a portion of yellow/tan\u000afibrofatty tissue (8 x 6 x 3 cm) and a long and short orienting suture. Near\u000athe inferior margin of the specimen, there is a REMOVED_DATE cm irregular firm mass\u000agrossly suspicious for invasive/treated carcinoma. The lesion is close to the\u000ainferior margin. There are no other gross abnormalities detected in the\u000aspecimen. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of\u000amargins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green;\u000alateral = yellow; medial = orange. Representative sections of all margins are\u000asubmitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  suspicious mass, multi frags each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  superior/anterior/posterior margins (representative sections),\u000amultiple frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  medial margin, single frag each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  anterior margin, multiple frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  posterior margin, single frag each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  lateral margin, multiple frags, RSS.\u000aPart #2, "right additional tissue at 4 o'clock," consists of a portion of\u000ayellow/tan fibroadipose tissue (4 x 3 x REMOVED_DATE cm), with a long and short\u000aorienting suture. One side of the specimen is inked in black. There is a REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afirm white/tan nodule in the center of the specimen grossly suspicious for\u000ainvasive carcinoma. The remainder of the specimen is unremarkable.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  additional breast tissue, including nodule, single frag each,\u000aRSS.\u000aReports to: CARTER, KATHARINE M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SOFT TISSUE BIOPSY\u000a[report_end]
