VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID TISSUE FOR SPECIAL STUDIES ONLY\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aGLICKMAN, JONATHAN, NEIL, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by GLICKMAN,JONATHAN NEIL,M.D.,PH.D.\u000a1) SPECIMEN LABELED "SKIN RIGHT BREAST":\u000aTissue allocated for special studies.\u000aGross examination only.\u000a2) SPECIMEN LABELED "RIGHT BREAST TISSUE" (195 gm):\u000aBreast tissue with epithelial hyperplasia, fibroadenomatoid stromal\u000achange, and cysts.\u000aSkin and subcutaneous tissue with no significant pathologic change.\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy.\u000a3) SPECIMEN LABELED "LEFT TRAM FLAP FAT NECROSIS":\u000aFibroadipose tissue with fat necrosis, acute and chronic inflammation,\u000aand foreign body giant cell reaction.\u000aScant benign breast tissue.\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy.\u000a4) SPECIMEN LABELED "REDUNDANT TISSUE, ABDOMINAL WALL CLOSURE":\u000aSkin and subcutaneous tissue with no significant pathologic change.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 41 year-old female, left breast cancer status post\u000aleft mastectomy and TRAM\u000aOperation: Left TRAM flap reduction, right breast reduction,\u000aexcision redundant tissue abdmoninal wall closure.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Asymmetry status post left mastectomy with TRAM\u000aflap reconstruction.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1) Skin right breast\u000a2) Right breast tissue, 195 gm\u000a3) Left TRAM flap fat necrosis\u000a4) Redundant tissue abdominal wall closure.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by HAHN,HEJIN P.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in four parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart 1, "skin right breast", consists of a 5 x REMOVED_DATE x 1 cm aggregate of\u000apink/tan irregular skin fragments, which is entirely submitted to Dr.\u000aSakstein's lab for special studies. Gross examination only.\u000aPart 2, "right breast tissue", consists of a 195 gm, 14 x 9 x 4 cm tan/yellow\u000afibrofatty and unremarkable tan/white skin and tissue aggregate.\u000aCross-sectioning reveals approximately 40% tan/white, dense, focally lumpy\u000afibrous tissue containing a few small brown, clear fluid-filled cysts,\u000ameasuring up to REMOVED_DATE cm, admixed with approximately 60% tan/yellow, lobulated,\u000afocally hemorrhagic fat. No lesions grossly consistent with an invasive\u000acarcinoma are identified. Representative sections are submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Right breast tissue, 5 frags total, RSS.\u000aPart 3, "left TRAM flap fat necrosis", consists of a 142 gm, 12 x 10 x REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afocally hemorrhagic, focally dusky, brown to tan/yellow fibrofatty and\u000aunremarkable tan/white skin tissue aggregate. There are multiple areas of a\u000adusky brown, granular nature within a few pieces. These areas are [inaudible]\u000afocal areas of bright yellow possible fat necrosis. A representative section of\u000athe worst area is submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Hemorrhagic dusky area, multiple frags, RSS.\u000aPart 4, "redundant tissue abdominal wall closure", consists of two tan/white,\u000awrinkled skin ellipses, measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm, excised to a maximum depth of\u000a1.2 cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE [inaudible] REMOVED_DATE cm each containing a [inaudible] linear,\u000awell healed scar, measuring REMOVED_DATE cm and REMOVED_DATE cm, respectively. A representative\u000asection of each is submitted.\u000aMicro 5: Redundant tissue, abdominal wall closure, 2 frags, RSS.\u000akks\u000aReports to: HERGRUETER, CHARLES, A. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: TISSUE FOR SPECIAL STUDIES ONLY\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST REDUCTION MAMMOPLASTY\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST REDUCTION MAMMOPLASTY\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SKIN CYST, TAG OR DEBRIDEMENT\u000a[report_end]
