ompanying specimen radiograph\u000ademonstrates no clip in the specimen. The specimen is serially sectioned to\u000areveal unremarkable fibroadipose tissue. The specimen is entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: right breast biopsy, 9 frags, ESS\u000aPart B, "retroareolar shave margin," consists of one portion of cylindrical\u000afibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. There is one orienting whip\u000astitch designated by the surgeon to be the new margin. The new margin is inked\u000ablue and the old margin is inked black. The specimen in serially sectioned to\u000areveal unremarkable fibroadipose tissue. The specimen is entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: retroareolar shave margin, 9 frags, ESS\u000aMAH/jp\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Marian H Harris M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by William R Welch M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
