 of tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity\u000ain >10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Left breast 14 mm mass. Likely CA. Breast imaging finding:\u000aill-defined.\u000aOperation: Ultrasound, 11g.\u000aOperative findings: 8 cores.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Left breast tissue in blue cassettes.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by PREISINGER,ELIZABETH ANN,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit\u000anumber, and "left breast", in a single blue unlabeled cassette, and consists of\u000amultiple, soft, fragmented, yellow to white tissue cores (2.7 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in\u000aaggregate).\u000aMicro 1: Multi frags, ESS.\u000adfi\u000aReports to: TWOHIG, LORRAINE, BERNADETTE, MB\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY(IES)\u000a[report_end]
