sette is\u000alabeled "A Ca++", and the other cassette is labeled "B". The pink cassette\u000alabeled "A Ca++" contains multiple yellow/tan fragments that aggregate to REMOVED_DATE x\u000a1.5 x REMOVED_DATE cm. The pink cassette labeled "B" contains multiple tan/yellow\u000atissues that aggregate to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: labeled "A Ca++" contents, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: labeled "B" contents, multi frags, ESS.\u000apf/lp\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-08-REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jane E. Brock M.B., B.S., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a5/23/2008\u000a[report_end]
