VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ROGER L CHRISTIAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Astrid Weins, M.D., Ph.D.; Tanya Rege, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Jane E. Brock, M.B., B.S., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aLEFT BREAST DOUBLE WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR TWO BIOPSY SITES AND CLIPS:\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU, extensive (see NOTE)\u000aMultiple intraductal papillomas with sclerosis and associated columnar cell\u000achange with mild atypia and luminal necrosis (see NOTE)\u000aCore biopsy sites x 2\u000aThe margins were inked and evaluated for the final diagnosis.\u000aOther findings:\u000aFlorid epithelial hyperplasia.\u000aSkin with scar.\u000aSclerosing adenosis with calcifications.\u000aColumnar cell change with extensive calcifications.\u000aNOTE: The patient has had two prior core needle biopsies for areas of\u000acalcifications showing carcinoma in situ, intraductal papillomas and\u000acalcifications associated with columnar cell change. In this excision, two core\u000abiopsy sites are present (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aThere is extensive lobular neoplasia, seen in 14 of 14 slides submitted.\u000aE-cadherin stains performed on two blocks (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) highlight absent\u000amembrane staining in neoplastic cells. The LCIS shows positive staining for ER\u000aand PR and is focally associated with calcifications (likely incidental).\u000aAlthough most of the LCIS is low nuclear grade, some areas show more\u000apleomorphic nuclei. No necrosis is associated with the LCIS.\u000aMultiple intraductal papillomas with sclerosis are also present, and scattered\u000aadjacent lobules of columnar cell change show mild nuclear atypia with central\u000aluminal necrosis which is most likely secondary to ischemia. Dr. Susan Lester\u000ahas reviewed selected slides from this case and agrees with the diagnosis.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Bx-proven CIS (? DCIS) and LCIS areas, Lt brst; twisted loop LCIS;\u000aclip --> CIS.\u000aOperation: Wire-directed excision.\u000aOperative Findings: See op note.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Bx-proven CIS (? DCIS) and LCIS areas, Lt brst; twisted\u000aloop LCIS; clip --> CIS.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) Tissue, left breast; stitches - long --> lateral; short --> superior (to\u000aFS Rm for mammo PRDCAP\u000aRADIOLOGY: All Ca++, clips, ? spiculated mass. OR called. DFS\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in one part, labeled with the patient's name,\u000amedical record number, and "#1. Tissue, left breast", and consists of one\u000abreast excision specimen (20.1g, REMOVED_DATE cm anterior to posterior, REMOVED_DATE cm superior\u000ato inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm medial to lateral) with one tan/white skin ellipse (4.0 x\u000a0.4 cm), oriented with two stitches (designated short stitch superior, long\u000astitch lateral per surgeon) and two localization wires (J - lateral curly Q -\u000amedial). The specimen is inked according to the protocol (superior - red,\u000ainferior - green, medial-orange, lateral - yellow, anterior - blue, posterior -\u000ablack. An accompanying radiograph demonstrates calcification, a curly clip\u000apossible spiculated mass and straight clip and area of calcifications.\u000aSectioning reveals the first biopsy cavity (0.7 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) is present REMOVED_DATE \u000acm from the medial resection margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior resection margin,\u000a0.1 cm from the superior resection margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior resection\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior resection margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to the lateral\u000aresection margin. The second biopsy cavity (1.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) is present REMOVED_DATE \u000acm from the lateral resection margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial resection margin,\u000a1.5 cm to anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to posterior resection margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to\u000asuperior resection margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to inferior resection margin. There is an\u000aadjacent area of fibrosis (1.9 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) extending to inferior and\u000asuperior resection margins, REMOVED_DATE cm to the anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to the\u000aposterior resection margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to the lateral resection margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm\u000ato the medial resection margin. No additional lesions are identified. The\u000aspecimen is 25% fibrotic and 75% tan/yellow fibroadipose tissue.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Left breast, medial to lateral, REMOVED_DATE frags each, ESS.\u000aThe first biopsy cavity is present in cassettes REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID through REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID (medial aspect\u000awith curly clip). The second biopsy cavity is present in cassettes REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID through\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID (lateral aspect with straight clip).\u000aAWE/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jane E. Brock M.B., B.S., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a7/16/2008\u000a[report_end]
