rotocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black;\u000aanterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange.\u000aSpecimen is sectioned from superior to inferior to reveal unremarkable\u000afibroadipose tissue. An accompanying radiograph demonstrates and embedded\u000alocalization wire adjacent to an ill-defined, slightly radiodense lesion in\u000aslices REMOVED_DATE \u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 2f, ESS\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1f ea, ESS\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 2f, ESS\u000aSpecimen B, "lower left breast mass," consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm wire\u000alocalized breast excision that has been previously inked by the surgeon per\u000apathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black;\u000aanterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. An\u000aaccompanying radiograph demonstrates an embedded localization wire adjacent to\u000aan ill-defined slightly radiodense area. The specimen is sectioned from\u000asuperior to inferior to reveal a well-circumscribed firm white wire localized\u000amass (0.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) abutting the inferior and medial resection margins.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1f ea, RSS\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Vijay K Vanguri M.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Shuji Ogino M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a2/25/2005\u000a[report_end]
