 and\u000abosselated with a well-healed scar (4.0 x REMOVED_DATE cm), which is located at the 12\u000ao'clock position, REMOVED_DATE cm superior of the nipple-areolar complex, and REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom the radial margin. There is a focal area of blue dye surrounding the\u000anipple consistent with a previous sentinel lymph node biopsy procedure. The\u000amargin is inked black, the specimen is serially sectioned. There is a\u000awell-circumscribed tan-white fibrous previous biopsy cavity (1.1 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm), which is located within the upper outer quadrant, REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000aposterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm lateral from the nipple-areolar complex at the 10\u000ao'clock position. Within the previous biopsy site is a silver metallic\u000aprevious biopsy clip. The remainder of the fibroadipose tissue is tan-yellow\u000aand homogenous with focal areas of dense white fibrous tissue constituting 10%\u000aof the breast parenchyma. The lateral aspect of the specimen is serially\u000asectioned with no lymph nodes grossly identified. Representative sections are\u000asubmitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Nipple-areolar complex, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross sections lateral to medial to include biopsy\u000acavity, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Representative sections right upper outer quadrant, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Representative sections right lower outer quadrant, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Representative sections right upper inner quadrant, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Representative sections right lower inner quadrant, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aSEK/mmm\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Alessandra F Nascimento M.D., Electronically signed on\u000aWednesday February 03, 2010 at 04:11:38PM\u000a[report_end]
