rotocol\u000afor the evaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior =\u000ared; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. Sectioning reveals\u000athat the breast parenchyma is approximately 50% fibrous tissue. A large biopsy\u000acavity is noted (0.9 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) towards the medial margin. No other\u000alesions are grossly identified. The specimen is entirely submitted. A\u000aradiograph is taken and shows the clip is in micro #7.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  lateral margins, perpendicular sections, 7 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  superior, anterior, and posterior margins, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  posterior, anterior, and inferior margins, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  medial margin, perpendicular sections, 11 frags, ESS.\u000ajeb\u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
