VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: DAVID I SOYBEL M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Qinghong Yang, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Robert D Odze, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "LEFT BREAST, TISSUE, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR\u000aCALCIFICATIONS":\u000aBenign breast tissue with calcifications associated with lobules,\u000aand dense stroma and biopsy site changes.\u000aSkin with no significant pathologic change.\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy.\u000aB. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "POSTERIOR LEFT BREAST MARGIN":\u000aBenign breast tissue with biopsy site changes.\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy.\u000aC. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "SUPERIOR LEFT BREAST MARGIN":\u000aBenign breast tissue with no significant pathologic change.\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy.\u000aD. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "INFERIOR LEFT BREAST MARGIN":\u000aBenign breast tissue with no significant pathologic change.\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: None specified.\u000aOperation: Lt wire localized breast bx.\u000aOperative Findings: None specified.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Lt breast calcification.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) Lt breast needle loc. to mammo.\u000aB/2) Posterior left breast margin.\u000aC/3) Superior Lt breast margin.\u000aD/4) Inferior Lt breast margin.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Calcs with clip in specimen. OR called. - LBS\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in four parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart A, "#1. Left breast, needle loc", consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aexcision of fibroadipose tissue, oriented with inks by the surgeon as follows:\u000aSuperior - red, inferior - green, anterior - blue, posterior - black, medial -\u000ayellow, lateral - orange. Please note: Inking deviates from typical pathology\u000abreast inking protocol; surgeon was contacted and confirmed the presence of a\u000askin ellipse at the lateral (orange - inked) aspect of the specimen. A\u000alocalizing wire enters the surface of the REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm tan/brown lateral skin\u000aellipse, and traverses medially, exiting the posteromedial surface. (Note: Per\u000asurgeon, calcifications are present at the posterior/medial aspect of the\u000aspecimen). Sectioning demonstrates a band of dense white fibrous tissue\u000a(maximally REMOVED_DATE cm), occupying at least 60% of the specimen, extending from the\u000amedial margin to the embedded metallic surgical clip at the lateral edge of the\u000aspecimen. The fibrous tissue appears relatively unremarkable, and no discrete\u000amasses, lesions, or other abnormalities are identified grossly. Remaining\u000aspecimen is comprised of tan/yellow, lobulated adipose tissue, with scant\u000aintervening thin fibrous septate. All fibrous tissue is submitted,\u000asequentially from medial to lateral. Perpendicular medial margin is in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID,\u000aperpendicular lateral margin is in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, and area with calcifications per\u000aradiograph is submitted in micro cassettes REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. About REMOVED_DATE % of the entire\u000aspecimen is submitted for microscopic examination.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: All fibrous tissue from specimen, sequentially from medial to\u000alateral, multi frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, "#2. Posterior left breast margin", consists of an unoriented REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000ax REMOVED_DATE cm fragment of fibroadipose tissue without discrete masses, lesions, or\u000aother abnormalities grossly. Tissue is inked, serially sectioned and\u000asequentially entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Multi frags, ESS.\u000aPart C, "#3. Superior left breast margin", consists of an unoriented REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000ax REMOVED_DATE cm excision of fibroadipose tissue, entirely inked black by prosector.\u000aSectioning demonstrates unremarkable cut surfaces without masses, lesions, or\u000aother abnormalities grossly. Specimen is serially sectioned and entirely,\u000asequentially submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Multi frags each, ESS.\u000aPart D, "#4. Inferior left breast margin", consists of an unoriented REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000ax REMOVED_DATE cm fragment of tan/white fibrous tissue, entirely inked black by\u000aprosector. Cut surfaces demonstrate only dense tan/white fibrous tissue\u000awithout masses, lesions, or other abnormalities grossly. Specimen is serially\u000asectioned and entirely sequentially submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Multi frags, ESS.\u000aDB/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Robert D Odze M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
