VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: CAPRICE CHRISTIAN GREENBERG M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Kristin S. Ricci, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Lucian R Chirieac, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. RIGHT BREAST, DOUBLE WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR CALCIFICATIONS AND A CLIP:\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia.\u000aSclerosing adenosis.\u000aCalcifications in benign breast epithelium.\u000aPrior core biopsy site.\u000aNOTE: The entire specimen was examined microscopically, including margins.\u000aThe case was reviewed by Dr. Susan Lester, Breast Pathology Service, who\u000aconcurs.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 48 year old female, S/P prior core biopsy - UOQ = ADH. 2nd group of\u000acalcs @ 2nd wire.\u000aOperation: R needle localized breast biopsy.\u000aOperative Findings: Not provided.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: ADH R breast.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) R breast bx - short/superior, long/lateral.\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000aSpecimen contains 2 intact wires, Ca++, clip. L. Zorn.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "#1. Right breast clip short superior long lateral", consists of an\u000airregular portion of yellow lobulated fibrofatty tissue (3.7 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm),\u000awith a long suture designating lateral, and a short suture designating\u000asuperior. As displayed on the accompanying radiograph, two inserted needle\u000alocalization wires enter along the medial-posterior margin (1.5 cm apart from\u000aone another). One of the wires is received partially exiting specimen, at the\u000alateral margin (arbitrarily designated needle localization wire #1, which is\u000alonger as displayed in the accompanying radiograph). Please note: needle\u000alocalization wire #1 is located predominantly at the inferior margin, while\u000aneedle localization wire #2 is located predominantly at the superior margin.\u000aThe specimen is inked by the prosector per pathology protocol as the\u000aanterior/blue, posterior/black, superior/red, inferior/green, lateral/yellow\u000aand medial/orange. The specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral\u000ato reveal a well-healed biopsy cavity (1.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), containing a clip\u000a(as displayed on the accompanying radiograph). This cavity is located towards\u000aneedle localization wire #2, and is REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom the anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000alateral margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial\u000amargin. The remaining cut surface consists of 90% yellow lobulated adipose\u000atissue and 10% white fibrous tissue, with no discrete masses or lesions\u000aidentified. The specimen is sequentially submitted in its entirety.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin, radially, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross sections from medial to lateral, with the cavity\u000ain REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, with a clip identified in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, and the area of calcifications on the\u000aaccompanying radiograph in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, radially, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000acp/lp\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Lucian R Chirieac M.D., Electronically signed on Friday\u000aREMOVED_MONTH 12, 2009 at 05:12:05PM\u000a[report_end]
