VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aFLETCHER, CHRISTOPHER, D.M., M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by FLETCHER,CHRISTOPHER D.M.,M.D.\u000a#1. SPECIMEN LABELLED LEFT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZATION FOR CALCIFICATION AND A\u000aCLIP:\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aSYNOPSIS:\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU - present\u000aTypes - solid\u000aNuclear grade - intermediate\u000aDCIS partly involves a papilloma\u000aCalcifications in DCIS - present\u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - absent\u000aMicroinvasion (<0.1cm) - absent\u000aExtent of DCIS\u000aNumber of blocks:total - 4:17 blocks\u000aFinal Margins (DCIS)\u000aNegative (>0.3 cm) - superior, inferior, posterior, anterior,\u000alateral\u000aVery close (<0.1 cm) - medial (focal, block 7), see shave\u000aspecimen below\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - absent\u000aOTHER FINDINGS\u000aCore biopsy site\u000aAJCC CLASSIFICATION (6th edition): Tis pNx MX\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER/PR/HER-2) - pending\u000a#2. SPECIMEN LABELLED "LEFT BREAST, MEDIAL SHAVE"\u000aBenign breast tissue with a single focus of atypical ductal hyperplasia\u000aand cysts.\u000aSkeletal muscle is present.\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy ( including examination of margins).\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for DCIS (block 1):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) NEGATIVE (1+)\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000ainvasive carcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but\u000aonly a portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity\u000ain >10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 69 yo female, s/p REMOVED_DATE  L breast core biopsy for evaluation of\u000acalcifications noted on REMOVED_DATE  mammogram. Biopsy revealed ADH.\u000aOperation: L breast wire localization excision.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: L breast atypical ductal hyperplasia on core biopsy.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. L breast tissue - short superior, long lateral, whipped\u000astitch on chest wall margin.\u000a2. L breast medial shave - whipped stitch on new margin.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Ca++in specimen. Smith\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by FIRESTEIN,RON,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received in two separate containers, each labeled with the\u000apatient's name and unit number.\u000aContainer #1 is designated "left breast tissue". The specimen consists of a\u000asingle portion of breast tissue (5.5 x 4 x 2 cm) and contains a single wire\u000alocalizing area of calcification and clip. The specimen has been previously\u000ainked by the surgeon per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins:\u000aposterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral\u000a= yellow; medial = orange. The specimen is entirely submitted for histologic\u000aevaluation.\u000aMicro 1&2: area of clip, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 3&4: area of calcification, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 5&6: superior margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 7&8: medial margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 9: additional medial margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 10: additional superior margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 11: lateral margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 12&13: inferior and posterior margins, 3 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  additional adipose tissue, 7 frags, ESS.\u000aPart two is received designated "breast tissue, left, stitch on new margin".\u000aThe specimen consists of a single fragment of fibroadipose tissue (4 x 3 x 1\u000acm). There is a single stitch designating the new margin. Old margin is inked\u000ain black. New margin is inked in blue. The specimen is entirely submitted for\u000ahistologic evaluation.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  entire new margin, multi frags, ESS.\u000aPlease note there is a radiological report obtained with this case. It read\u000a"calcium in specimen", signed by Dr. Smith.\u000arfi\u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN\u000a[report_end]
