VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID:REMOVED_CASE_ID Report Status: Signed\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aDIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. Left breast, upper outer quadrant excision (210 grams):\u000aDuctal carcinoma in situ, high grade, solid, cribriform and\u000acomedocarcinoma types with necrosis and microcalcifications, focal.\u000aDuctal carcinoma in situ, intermediate grade, cribriform type with\u000amicrocalcifications, multifocal.\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia, multifocal.\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia, multifocal, with focal\u000amicrocalcifications.\u000aFibrocystic changes.\u000aChanges consistent with prior needle core biopsy site.\u000aB. Right breast, excision (47 grams):\u000aFocal ductal carcinoma in situ, intermediate grade, cribriform and\u000amicropapillary types.\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia, multifocal, with microcalcifications.\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia and lobular carcinoma in situ.\u000aFibrocystic changes and sclerosing adenosis with microcalcifications.\u000aSYNOPTIC REPORT, LEFT BREAST (A):\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU (DCIS):\u000a-histologic type: solid, cribriform and comedo types\u000a-histologic grade: high grade and intermediate grade\u000a-size (greatest dimension): multiple foci throughout specimen (present\u000ain 37 out of 47 sections)\u000a-extent: multifocal, extensive\u000a-necrosis in DCIS: present, focal\u000a-microcalcifications in DCIS: present\u000a-margins for DCIS: intermediate ductal carcinoma in situ is\u000afocally present less than REMOVED_DATE cm. from\u000athe margin in the following foci:\u000alateral (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), superior and superficial\u000a(REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), superficial (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), and\u000ainferior medial (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) of the left breast\u000a-immunohistochemical staining on prior specimen (S-06-REMOVED_CASE_ID) was reported as:\u000aEstrogen receptor: POSITIVE\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU (LCIS): present, focal\u000aADDITIONAL PATHOLOGIC FINDINGS:\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia, atypical ductal hyperplasia, fibrocystic\u000achanges, sclerosing adenosis, microcalcification and changes consistent\u000awith prior biopsy site.\u000aAJCC pTNM Classification (6th Ed.): pTis pNX pMX\u000aThe pathologic TNM classification above is based only on the information\u000aavailable to the pathologist, and therefore may not be accurate.\u000aCOMMENT: In the left breast specimen (A) around the prior needle core biopsy\u000asite, there is high grade ductal carcinoma in situ which is about REMOVED_DATE cm. in\u000asize (present in 5 out of 47 slides). In addition, there are foci of\u000aintermediate ductal carcinoma in situ present in multiple foci throughout the\u000aentire specimen (present in an additional 32 out of 47 slides).\u000aSYNOPTIC REPORT, RIGHT BREAST (B):\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU (DCIS):\u000a-histologic type: cribriform and micropapillary types\u000a-histologic grade: intermediate grade\u000a-size (greatest dimension): two foci, each REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000a-extent: focal\u000a-necrosis in DCIS: none identified\u000a-microcalcifications in DCIS: none identified\u000a-margins for DCIS: clear (greater than REMOVED_DATE cm) of right breast\u000aADDITIONAL PATHOLOGIC FINDINGS:\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia, atypical lobular hyperplasia, lobular carcinoma\u000ain situ and fibrocystic changes.\u000aAJCC pTNM Classification (6th Ed.): pTis pNX pMX\u000aThe pathologic TNM classification above is based only on the information\u000aavailable to the pathologist, and therefore may not be accurate.\u000aPRIOR RELATED SPECIMENS REVIEWED:\u000aLeft breast, upper outer quadrant, needle core biopsy, S-06-REMOVED_CASE_ID (07/05/06)\u000aRight breast, needle core biopsy, S-06-REMOVED_CASE_ID (07/12/06)\u000aFinal Diagnosis by: Daniel D. Koelliker, M.D.\u000aClinical diagnosis & history:\u000aDuctal carcinoma in situ of left breast; atypical ductal hyperplasia of right\u000abreast\u000aTissue-Designation:\u000aA.Breast, excision with margins - left\u000aB.Breast, excision with margins - right\u000aGross description:\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin in two containers.\u000aSpecimen A labeled "left breast mass" consists of a 210 gram, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm. portion of fibroadipose tissue. At one aspect there is a short suture\u000aoriented as superior, and 90 degrees from this is a long suture oriented as\u000alateral of the left breast. Based on these orientations, a wire enters the mid\u000asuperficial surface, and the tip of the wire exits the deep, mid surface. The\u000amargins throughout are grossly unremarkable and are inked black. The deep\u000asurface is double inked red. The specimen is cross sectioned from lateral\u000atowards medial revealing areas of yellow, lobulated adipose tissue and central\u000aand medial areas of rubbery, white-tan fibrous tissue within which there are\u000amultiple small cysts present. Located in the central to slightly superior\u000aaspect near the superficial surface, there is an area of linear red hemorrhage.\u000aThe tissue surrounding this is mostly rubbery, white-tan fibrous tissue. No\u000agrossly suspicious mass lesions are seen. Representative sections from\u000athroughout the specimen are submitted as follows:\u000aSECTION CODE: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - lateral margin\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - representative sections from lateral most portion of\u000aspecimen, which is predominantly yellow, lobulated\u000aadipose tissue\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - entire area of linear hemorrhage\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - superior to area of linear hemorrhage\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - area inferior to linear hemorrhage\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - superior margin of medial aspect of upper outer quadrant\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - entire nodular area of mid superior area with\u000asuperficial margin\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - representative inferior lateral\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - inferior margins\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - representative sections of superior medial area\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - representative sections of inferior medial area\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - medial margin\u000aSpecimen B labeled "right breast, short superior, long lateral" consists of a\u000a47 gram, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. portion of fibroadipose tissue. A long suture is\u000apresent at one aspect oriented as lateral, and 90 degrees from this is a short\u000asuture oriented as superior of the right breast. Based on these orientations,\u000athere is a wire which enters the superior aspect of the specimen. The deep\u000asurface is double inked red, and the superior half is double inked blue. The\u000aspecimen is cross sectioned from medial to lateral revealing mostly rubbery,\u000awhite-tan fibrous tissue with focal reddish areas and small cysts. Focally at\u000athe mid superficial aspect there is linear red hemorrhage. The entire\u000aspecimen is submitted from medial towards lateral in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. 35 agg. all.\u000aDictated by: DDK____(signature on file)____ REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a____(signature on file)____DANIEL D. KOELLIKER, M.D. REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a[report_end]
