VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID:REMOVED_CASE_ID Report Status: Signed\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aDIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. Left axillary sentinel lymph node #1, excision:\u000aOne lymph node with isolated tumor cells.\u000aSee synoptic report.\u000aB. Left axillary sentinel lymph node #2, excision:\u000aOne lymph node with isolated tumor cells.\u000aSee synoptic report.\u000aC. Left breast, re-excision:\u000aDuctal carcinoma in situ, intermediate grade, cribriform and\u000amicropapillary types, focal.\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia, multifocal.\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia and lobular carcinoma in situ.\u000aFibrocystic changes.\u000aPrior excision site reactive changes.\u000aSee synoptic report.\u000aSYNOPTIC REPORT:\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU (DCIS):\u000a-histologic type: cribriform and micropapillary types\u000a-histologic grade: intermediate grade\u000a-size (greatest dimension): few foci concentrated at superior/lateral\u000aand superior/medial portion of the\u000aspecimen\u000a-extent: focal\u000a-extensive intraductal component: not applicable\u000a-necrosis in DCIS: none identified\u000a-microcalcifications in DCIS: none identified\u000a-margins for DCIS: clear (greater than or equal to REMOVED_DATE cm.)\u000a-immunohistochemical staining on prior specimen (S-06-REMOVED_CASE_ID) was reported as:\u000aEstrogen receptor: POSITIVE\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU (LCIS):\u000aPresent, focal.\u000aLYMPH NODES:\u000aTwo lymph nodes with isolated tumor cells out of total sampled: REMOVED_DATE \u000a(2/2 sentinel lymph nodes).\u000aCOMMENT: The sentinel lymph nodes, specimens A and B, are examined at multiple\u000alevels with H&E stains and immunohistochemical stains for keratin.\u000aSKIN:\u000a-skin/dermis: unremarkable; focal scar\u000aADDITIONAL PATHOLOGIC FINDINGS:\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia, atypical lobular hyperplasia and lobular\u000acarcinoma in situ, fibrocystic changes, prior excision site reactive\u000achanges.\u000aPRIOR RELATED SPECIMENS REVIEWED:\u000asite: left breast, upper outer quadrant specimen #: S-06-REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000adate: REMOVED_DATE \u000aCOMMENT: The isolated tumor cells are seen with both H & E and pankeratin\u000aimmunohistochemical stains and appear less than REMOVED_DATE mm. in size.\u000aAJCC pTNM Classification (6th Ed.): pTis pREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID(i+) pMX\u000aThe pathologic TNM classification above is based only on the information\u000aavailable to the pathologist, and therefore may not be accurate.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by: Dennis J. Feen, M.D.\u000aINTRA-OPERATIVE CONSULTATION:\u000aOPERATING ROOM CONSULTATION (TISSUE EXAMINATION):\u000a#1. Sentinel lymph node #1, left axilla, biopsy: No gross tumor seen.\u000a#2. Sentinel lymph node #2, left axilla, biopsy: No gross tumor seen.\u000aMJR\u000aClinical diagnosis & history:\u000aLeft breast carcinoma\u000aTissue-Designation:\u000aA.Sentinel lymph node - #1\u000aB.Sentinel lymph node - #2\u000aC.Breast, excision with margins - left\u000aGross description:\u000aThe specimen is received in three containers.\u000aSpecimen A labeled "sentinel lymph node" consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 cm.\u000alymph node. The cut surface consists of brownish-tan lymphoid tissue with no\u000agross evidence of metastatic tumor. 3X all.\u000aSpecimen B labeled "sentinel lymph node #2" is received in formalin and\u000aconsists of a lymph node which has been previously bisected. It is 1 x REMOVED_DATE x\u000a0.5 cm. The cut surface shows a brownish-tan cortex. 3X all.\u000aSpecimen C labeled "left breast, re-excision" consists of a 182 gram, oval mass\u000aof yellowish breast tissue, REMOVED_DATE x 10 x 3 cm. On the anterior surface is an\u000aS-shaped segment of skin, 6 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. A healed linear scar runs through\u000ait. A short suture designates the superior margin and a long suture, the\u000alateral margin. The anterior superior half of the specimen is inked with blue\u000aink. The anterior inferior half of the specimen is inked with green ink. The\u000aposterior portion of the specimen is inked with black ink. The cut surface\u000ademonstrates a large cavity lined by brown granulation tissue, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm. A rim of more normal appearing breast tissue surrounds this cavity. The\u000amajority of the specimen, but not all has been submitted for microscopic\u000aexamination. 66X\u000aSection code: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - superior/lateral, sectioned lateral to medial\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - superior/medial, sectioned lateral to medial\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - medial, sectioned superior to inferior\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - inferior, sectioned lateral to medial\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - lateral, sectioned superior to inferior\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - anterior, sectioned lateral to medial\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - deep, sectioned lateral to medial\u000aDictated by: DJF____(signature on file)____DANIEL D. KOELLIKER, M.D. REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a____(signature on file)____DENNIS J. FEEN, M.D. REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a[report_end]
