xiting\u000aat the other. The specimen is inked orange at the half where the wire exits\u000aand green at the proximal half where the wire enters. The specimen is serially\u000asectioned from the distal to the proximal ends along the axis of the wire of\u000athe spcimen revealing a breast tissue that is diffusely involved with white/tan\u000afibrous tissue admixed with adipose tissue. The entire specimen is submitted.\u000aMicro 1: distal margin, perpendicular, 5 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  serial sections from distal to proximal, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 6: proximal margin, perpendicular, 8 frags, ESS.\u000aPart two, "tissue from right breast specimen B with clip", consists of a REMOVED_DATE x\u000a2.8 x REMOVED_DATE cm breast tissue, received inked per pathology protocol for the\u000aevaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red;\u000ainferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. The specimen is received\u000awith a wire inserted at the superior red inked surface and exiting from the\u000ablack (posterior) surface of the specimen. The specimen is serially sectioned\u000afrom the inferior to the superior surface along the access of the wire\u000arevealing a focally involved dense fibrous tissue at the inferior portion of\u000athe specimen with the rest of the breast tissue, yellow and fatty and\u000aunremarkable. The entire specimen is submitted.\u000aMicro 7: inferior margin, perpendicular, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  serial sections, inferior to superior, 6 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 14: superior margin, perpendicular, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aPart three, "right breast tissue additional tissue from specimen B", consists\u000aof a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm, yellow/tan, unoriented fibroadipose tissue. The\u000aspecimen is inked black for the evaluation of margins and serially sectioned.\u000aPart 1 section was found to contain the clip. This section was bisected for\u000athe removal of the clip. The entire specimen is submitted.\u000aMicro 15: section containing the clip, bisected, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 16: remainder of specimen, 5 frags, ESS.\u000ajhc\u000aReports to: CHRISTIAN, ROGER, L. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN\u000a[report_end]
