VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aNOSE, VANIA, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by NOSE,VANIA,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A CLIP AND CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia.\u000aCysts and apocrine metaplasia.\u000aBiopsy site changes.\u000aNOTE:\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins. Dr. Susan Lester concurs.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 51-year-old female, mammo REMOVED_DATE  showed upper outer lower quadrant\u000acalcifications, core biopsy REMOVED_DATE  showed ADH closely approaching DCIS.\u000aOperation: Left breast wire localization excision.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Left breast tissue - short stitch superior, long lateral,\u000awhipstitch deep margin.\u000aRADIOLOGY REPORT:\u000aWire and clip in specimen radiograph - call to Jocelyn in OR.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by FIRESTEIN,RON,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "Left wire localization breast biopsy - short superior, long lateral,\u000awhipstitch deep margin", and consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm fibrofatty breast\u000atissue with a short suture designating superior and long suture designating\u000alateral, and a whipstitch designating deep margin. The specimen radiograph\u000areveals a clip and a wire. There is a localizing wire in place. The specimen\u000ahas been previously inked by the surgeon as per pathology protocol for the\u000aevaluation of margins as follows: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior\u000a= red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. The specimen is\u000aserially sectioned from superior to inferior to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm\u000ahemorrhagic cavity with adjacent fat necrosis, designated by a metal clip,\u000acoming to within REMOVED_DATE cm of the anterior, REMOVED_DATE cm of medial, REMOVED_DATE cm of superior,\u000a1.0 cm of lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm of posterior and inferior margins. The remaining\u000aparenchyma is 60% yellow, lobulated fatty to 40% dense, white fibrous tissue\u000awith diffuse fibrocystic disease. Representative sections are submitted\u000asequentially from superior to inferior as follows. The remaining parenchyma is\u000a70% fatty to 40% fibrous tissue with diffuse fibrocystic disease.\u000aThe fibrous tissue extends to the inferior/anterior/posterior/lateral/medial\u000amargins.\u000aMicro 1: Superior margin, radial sections, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 2: Fat necrosis to posterior medial margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Designated area to posterior medial margiin, 1 frag in each, RSS.\u000aMicro 5: Remainder of hemorrhagic cavity, bisected section, with the superior\u000aposterior medial aspect in Micro 5, 1 frag in each, RSS.\u000aMicro 7: Fibrous tissue to posterior lateral medial margins, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 8: Fibrous tissue to anterior medial lateral margins.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Fibrous tissue with fibrocystic disease, bisected, 1 frag in\u000aeach, RSS.\u000aMicro 11: Fibrous tissue to posterior medial margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 12: Fibrous tissue to inferior margin, radial sections, 2 frags, ESS.\u000alm\u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
