VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY(IES)\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aLESTER, SUSAN, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST, LOWER INNER, 8 G ULTRASOUND GUIDED CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES OF A\u000aCIRCUMSCRIBED MASS:\u000aFragments of a fibroepithelial lesion with mild stromal cellularity and no\u000astromal overgrowth. The stroma of the lesion appears to focally\u000ainfiltrate into the adjacent adipose tissue. No mitotic figures are seen.\u000aNote: The presence of an irregular margin with the surrounding adipose\u000atissue is suggestive of a low grade phyllodes tumor. Excision is\u000arecommended for final classification.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 57 year old female with outside core biopsy (14g) of LLIQ nodule\u000athat showed fibroadenoma, excisional biopsy was recommended, patient\u000arequested re-biopsy by U/S core.\u000aBreast Imaging Findings: Circumscribed.\u000aOperation: 8g U/S guided\u000aOperative findings: Solid mass\u000aClinical Diagnosis: FA\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Left breast tissue (1 blue cassette)\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by BAI,HONGWEI,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit\u000anumber, and "left breast", in a light blue cassette, and consists of multiple,\u000asoft, fragmented, yellow to white tissue cores (1.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in\u000aaggregate).\u000aMicro 1: Multi frags, ESS.\u000akks\u000aReports to: SMITH, DARRELL, NOLAN M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY(IES)\u000a[report_end]
