VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aWEINSTEIN, MICHAEL, H., M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by WEINSTEIN,MICHAEL H.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED BIOPSY FOR A MASS:\u000aBenign breast tissue with cysts and microcalcifications associated with\u000abenign epithelium.\u000aSmall amount of residual fibroepithelial lesion similar to prior core\u000abiopsy (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) with adjacent prior core biopsy site changes.\u000aSee NOTE.\u000aNOTE: Although this lesion is not quite as well-circumscribed as the typical\u000afibroadenoma, there is little to suggest that it is likely to behave in\u000aan aggressive fashion. Specifically, it is fairly well-circumscribed,\u000ais not very cellular or mitotically active, and does not show significant\u000acytologic atypia or stromal overgrowth. However, it does extend to the\u000ainked inferior and medial margins of resection.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: None given.\u000aOperation: Left needle directed breast biopsy\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal mammogram - left breast\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1. Left breast tissue to mammo\u000aRADIOLOGY: Mass in specimen. E.P. Frost.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by LOMO,LESLEY C.,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in one part, labeled with the patient's name,\u000aunit number and "#1. left breast tissue", and consists of a fragmented,\u000ayellow/tan fragment of fibrofatty soft tissue (5.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which\u000acontains a short suture to designate superior, long suture to designate lateral\u000amargin, and a needle localization wire. An accompanying radiograph shows the\u000aspecimen with the needle localization wire at the site of the radiopaque\u000adensity. Due to fragmentation of the specimen it is not possible to ascertain\u000awhich portion of the specimen contains the lesion with respect to the wire.\u000aThe specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins:\u000aposterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral\u000a= yellow; medial = orange. The specimen is serially sectioned from medial to\u000alateral, revealing a small, white, rubbery nodule (0.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which\u000aabuts the medial and inferior margins; it is present REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior\u000amargin. Due to the fragmentation of the specimen it is not possible to grossly\u000aassess distance to the anterior, superior, and lateral margins. The\u000aremainder of the parenchyma is comprised predominantly of unremarkable yellow\u000aadipose tissue (80%), and white fibrous tissue (20%). The specimen is entirely\u000asubmitted.\u000aMicro 1: nodule, 1 frag, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  lateral perpendicular margins, 3 frags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  left breast wire localized biopsy, 1 or 2 frags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  medial perpendicular margins, 1 or 3 frags, ESS\u000alcl\u000aReports to: LOCKHART, DIANE, CATHERINE M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
