VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Michael A. Seidman, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Christopher D. M. Fletcher, M.D. FRCPath\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. LEFT BREAST EXCISION FOR A MASS:\u000aFIBROADENOMA (1.8 cm).\u000aAlso noted are columnar cell change, calcifications associated with benign\u000aepithelium and pseudoangiomatous stromal hyperplasia.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the\u000aspecimen, including margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 28 y/o female S/P REMOVED_DATE  OSH ultrasound-guided core biopsy, L\u000abreast, revealing fragments of a fibroadenoma. REMOVED_DATE  ultrasound demonstrates\u000aa slight increase in size of the mass, and the patient prefers excision.\u000aOperation: Excision of L breast mass.\u000aOperative Findings: None provided.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: L breast mass.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) L breast mass; short --> superior; long --> lateral; whip --> deep\u000amargin.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in one part, labeled with the patient's name,\u000aunit number, and "L breast mass", and consists of an irregular fragment of\u000afibroadipose tissue (3.5 cm M-L x REMOVED_DATE cm S-I x REMOVED_DATE cm A-P) with a short suture\u000adesignating superior, a long suture designating lateral, and a whip-stitch\u000adesignating the deep margin. The specimen is inked by the surgeon per\u000apathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black;\u000aanterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange.\u000aThe specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral to exhibit a\u000awell-circumscribed, firm, fibrous nodule (1.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), abutting the\u000aanterior margin, and located less than REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000amedial margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin. The remaining cut surface\u000aconsists of 100% fibrous tissue. An area consistent with a previous biopsy\u000asite cannot be grossly appreciated. The specimen is submitted in its entirety.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Perpendicular medial margin, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Body, sequentially submitted from medial to lateral to include\u000anodule (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), 1 frag in each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Perpendicular lateral margin, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aJC/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Christopher D. M. Fletcher M.D. FRCPath, Electronically\u000asigned on Thursday REMOVED_MONTH 03, 2009 at 01:09:38PM\u000a[report_end]
