ue fragment with a wire localizing needle and a clip. The\u000aspecimen also contains minute microcalcification. Serial sectioning of the\u000aspecimen reveals predominantly fatty yellow/tan and hemorrhagic tissue with a\u000acentral hemorrhagic area in the lateral aspect of the specimen (0.8 cm in\u000adiameter). The specimen is entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  breast tissue, 2 frags each, ESS\u000aPart two, labeled "#2. shave margin medial", consists of a single fragment of\u000ayellow/tan and red (at least REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). A whip stitch is located on\u000athe surface, which is inked blue. The opposite surface is inked black. Serial\u000asectioning reveals red/yellow hemorrhagic soft tissue with no focal mass. The\u000aspecimen is entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  breast tissue, 2 frags each, ESS\u000ako\u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN\u000a[report_end]
