aDr. S. Lester, Breast Pathology Service, has reviewed this case and concurs.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: None given.\u000aOperation: Left needle localized breast biopsy.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast mass.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Left needle localized breast biopsy -> To mammo\u000aRADIOLOGY REPORT:\u000aClip, wire, Ca+ in specimen OR called/SR\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient?s name, unit number,\u000aand "#1. Left needle localized breast biopsy", and consists of an unoriented\u000abreast excision specimen (6.7 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), containing a single localization\u000awire. The accompanying specimen radiograph shows microcalcifications, a single\u000aclip and wire. The outer surface of the specimen is inked black. Within the\u000aspecimen is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm firm gray/white area, which contains the\u000alocalization wire, a single clip and foci of hemorrhage (0.4 cm in diameter),\u000aconsistent with prior biopsy site. It is REMOVED_DATE cm from the closest resection\u000amargin. No discrete masses are grossly identified. The remaining parenchyma it\u000ais mostly composed of unremarkable adipose tissue. The specimen is entirely\u000asubmitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Breast, multi frag, ESS\u000aNOTE: Previous core biopsy site is placed in cassettes REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. Clip was\u000apresent in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aPAL/cdm\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Paula C Abreu-e-Lima M.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Lucian R Chirieac M.D., Electronically signed on\u000a9/29/2005\u000a[report_end]
