VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST MASTECTOMY W/REGIONAL LYMPH NODES\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aBRODSKY, GILBERT, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by BRODSKY,GILBERT,M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED RIGHT BREAST AND AXILLARY NODES:\u000aINVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA (5.0 cm), moderately differentiated\u000a(modified Bloom-Richardson grade 2 of 3).\u000aTumor extends to REMOVED_DATE cm from the deep resection margin,\u000aand REMOVED_DATE cm from the skin of the nipple.\u000aLymphovascular invasion is identified.\u000aMETASTATIC CARCINOMA in one of four (4) lymph nodes. The deposit measures\u000a0.3 cm, without extranodal extension.\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED AXILLARY CONTENTS ON RIGHT:\u000aEight (8) lymph nodes with no tumor seen.\u000aNote: Total of 1 of 12 nodes positive for metastatic carcinoma.\u000aAJCC stage REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDa MX.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 41 year old premenopausal female with a mammogram on REMOVED_DATE  showing\u000aa central breast mass, right skin thickening with puckering\u000asuperior to nipple (change from 1995). REMOVED_DATE  right core biopsy\u000ashowed infiltrating carcinoma with ductal and lobular features with\u000aassociated calcification. MRI demonstrates greater than 4 cm tumor,\u000awith 3 lesions, each in a different quadrant.\u000aOperation: Modified radical mastectomy.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Preop: Right breast cancer.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1. Right breast and level I and II nodes.\u000a#2. Axillary contents on right.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by FERGUSON,DAVID OWEN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two (2) parts, each labeled with the\u000apatient's name and unit number.\u000aThe first part, labeled "right breast," consists of one mastectomy specimen\u000a(16.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), with one (1) centrally located nipple and areola (3.4 x\u000a2.5 x REMOVED_DATE cm). Emanating from the upper outer quadrant is an attached fragment\u000aof tissue (13.0 cm long x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), denoted as axillary nodes on form #86.\u000aWithin the breast parenchyma, there is one (1) firm tan stellate suspicious\u000alesion (5.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), located REMOVED_DATE cm from the deep resection margin and\u000a0.5 cm from the skin and nipple, and greater than 3 cm from all other margins.\u000aThe remainder of the breast parenchyma is unusually firm, but contains no\u000adiscrete lesions.\u000aMicro #1-3 : mass in relation to deep resection margin, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000aMicro #4 : additional section of mass, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro #5 : nipple and areola, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro #6 : deep margin from upper outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro #7 : deep margin from upper inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro #8 : lower inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro #9 : upper inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro #10-13: tissue submitted entirely from axillary tail, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000aMicro #14 : breast tissue from upper outer quadrant, adjacent to axillary\u000atail, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  lymph nodes, multiple frags, RSS.\u000aThe second part, "right axillary contents," consists of one (1) fragment of\u000ayellow/tan fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The specimen was\u000astained in Bouin's and lymph nodes were isolated.\u000aReports to: KAELIN, CAROLYN, MARY M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY W/REGIONAL LYMPH NODES\u000a[report_end]
