VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID LUMPECTOMY\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aKILO, MARY, NATHANSON, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by KILO,MARY NATHANSON,M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "RIGHT BREAST TUMOR, RE-EXCISION":\u000aResidual DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU (blocks # 10, 11, 12, 13) (see note).\u000aDensely hyalinized breast stroma with sclerosing adenosis and numerous\u000amicrocalcifications in benign ducts.\u000aForeign body giant cell reaction to suture material, consistent with\u000aprevious surgery.\u000aNo invasive carcinoma present.\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia.\u000aThe margins of resection are uninvolved by tumor.\u000aNote: The in situ carcinoma is seen within single foci within each of the\u000asections and comprises a very small component of the tissue present.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: DCIS by prior excisional biopsy.\u000aOperation: Re-excision right breast tumor site\u000aClinical Diagnosis: DCIS\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Right breast tissue, light stitch toward lateral area\u000a- black stitch toward nipple\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by KUTOK,JEFFREY LORNE,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen, received fixed, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and\u000a"right breast tissue", consists of a white/yellow, irregular fragment of\u000afibrofatty tissue, measuring 5 x 3 x REMOVED_DATE cm in overall dimension. The specimen\u000acontains a white/tan, unremarkable skin ellipse, measuring 3 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm\u000awith a white stitch present at the corner designated by the surgeon to be the\u000alateral margin. A black stitch on the opposite surface is designated by the\u000asurgeon to be toward the nipple and will be taken to be the medial surface of\u000athe specimen. The specimen is inked in black and serial en face margins are\u000ataken. The remainder of the specimen is transversally sectioned from superior\u000ato inferior. The breast parenchyma is primarily dense white, fibrous tissue\u000abut is extremely firm but homogeneous without areas of necrosis or hemorrhage.\u000aNo biopsy cavity is present and the white fibrous breast tissue is not grossly\u000asuspicious for invasive carcinoma. The entire specimen is submitted for\u000ahistologic examination.\u000aMicro 1 - superior margins, taking en face, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro 2 - inferior margins, taking en face, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro 3 - anterior margins, taking en face, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE - posterior margins, taking en face, 6 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE - medial margins, taking en face, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 8 - lateral margins, taking en face, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE - transverse sections from superior to inferior, 10 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE - sections through skin, including breast tissue, 5 frags, ESS.\u000aReports to: CHRISTIAN, ROGER, L. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: LUMPECTOMY\u000a[report_end]
