activity\u000ain >10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: History of DCIS (in 1999, and ALH in 2000 - per Pathology resident)\u000anow with new calcifications, right (missed on core biopsy on REMOVED_DATE ).\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1) Tissue from right breast - 2 specimens.\u000aRADIOLOGY REPORT:\u000aCalcifications in specimen.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by OH,KIRSTINE YUNG-TING,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "Right breast tissue", and consists of two fragments of tan/white breast\u000atissue (3.6 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm, and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). Also received with the\u000aspecimen is a radiograph showing a single tissue density with three or four\u000alocalized calcifications, with a wire localization in place. The unoriented\u000aspecimen is inked blue, and the specimen is serially sectioned to reveal firm,\u000awhite breast tissue, without focal lesions. The specimen is entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Breast tissue, 1 frag each, ESS (micro REMOVED_DATE is the larger specimen;\u000amicro REMOVED_DATE is the smaller specimen)\u000ako\u000aReports to: CHRISTIAN, ROGER, L. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
