cimen has been\u000ainked by the surgeon per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins:\u000aposterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral\u000a= yellow; medial = orange. The breast tissue is uniformly and densely fibrous.\u000aThere is single cystic/hemorrhagic area measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm that\u000aapproaches to within REMOVED_DATE cm of the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the inferior\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the anterior skin surface and\u000agreater than REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral and medial margins. Representative\u000asections are submitted for histologic analysis.\u000aMicro 1: superior margin, 2 frags, RSS\u000aMicro 2: inferior margin, 2 frags, RSS\u000aMicro 3: posterior margin, 2 frags, RSS\u000aMicro 4: anterior margin, 2 frags, RSS\u000aMicro 5: lateral margin, 2 frags, RSS\u000aMicro 6: medial margin, 2 frags, RSS\u000aPart two, labeled "#2. shave margin superior right breast", consists of a\u000asingle fragment of brown/tan fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE cm from lateral\u000ato medial x REMOVED_DATE cm from anterior to posterior x REMOVED_DATE cm from superior to\u000ainferior. A short suture is placed by the surgeon to indicate the superior\u000amargin of the specimen and a long suture is placed by the surgeon to indicate\u000athe lateral margin of specimen. The superior margin has been inked red by the\u000asurgeon. The inferior is inked green. The nodule is uniformly white and\u000adensely fibrous. No areas of hemorrhage or other lesions are grossly\u000aidentified. Representative sections are submitted for histologic analysis.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  right breast tissue superior shave margin, mult frags, RSS\u000adk\u000aReports to: CHRISTIAN, ROGER, L. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN\u000a[report_end]
