VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Amend/Addenda\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-10-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000a********** Addended Report ***********\u000aResident: Kyle L. Viani, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Jacqueline M William, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. RIGHT BREAST TISSUE, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia involving sclerosing adenosis (best\u000aseen in blocks REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aPapilloma (0.2 cm).\u000aCalcifications associated with sclerosing adenosis.\u000aFibroadenomatoid changes.\u000aUsual ductal hyperplasia (E-Cadherin stains evaluated are positive\u000ain areas of ductal hyperplasia).\u000aColumnar cell change.\u000aCore biopsy site changes.\u000aDouble stains (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) reveal intact myoepithelial cells in\u000aareas of sclerosing adenosis.\u000a(Select slides were also reviewed by Dr. J. Brock, Breast Pathologist,\u000awho concurs).\u000aThe immunoperoxidase, immunofluorescence and in-situ hybridization tests\u000aperformed at Brigham and Women's Hospital were developed and their performance\u000acharacteristics determined by the Immunohistochemistry Laboratories in the\u000aDepartment of Pathology at BWH. They have not been cleared or approved by the\u000aU.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA). The FDA has determined that such\u000aclearance or approval is not necessary.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 45 y/o female S/P 2008 L BCT S/P REMOVED_DATE  R stereotactic core bx for\u000acalcifications, revealing columnar cell change with atypia, ALH with\u000acalcifications and fragments of papilloma. Excision recommended.\u000aOperation: R breast wire-localized biopsy.\u000aOperative Findings: None provided.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal R MMg; hx L breast CA.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) Right breast tissue; short suture - superior, long suture - lateral; whip\u000astitch on chest wall margin (Bioptics)\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in one part, labeled with the patient's name\u000aand medical record number.\u000aPart A, labeled "right breast tissue short suture superior, long suture\u000alateral, whip stitch on chest wall margin", contains one lumpectomy specimen\u000amarked with a short stitch (superior per surgeon) and a long stitch (lateral\u000aper surgeon). The specimen is received already inked by the surgeon. The\u000aspecimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins:\u000aposterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow;\u000amedial/orange. The localization wire is received separately and is not in the\u000aspecimen when delivered to pathology. The lumpectomy specimen (8.2 grams)\u000ameasures REMOVED_DATE cm (superior to inferior), REMOVED_DATE cm (medial to lateral), REMOVED_DATE cm\u000a(anterior to posterior). The specimen is serially sectioned from medial to\u000alateral and entirely submitted for histologic evaluation. No discrete masses\u000aor lesions are identified. The clip is identified. The breast tissue is\u000aapproximately 60% fibrous and 40% fatty. A specimen radiograph reviewed in\u000aCentricity reveals a clip and calcifications.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial tips, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Breast tissue medial to lateral (clip in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Breast tissue, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Breast tissue, sections to lateral edge, 2 frags each, ESS.\u000aKLV/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jacqueline M William M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed\u000aon Friday February 12, 2010 at 03:19:17PM\u000aADDENDUM\u000aThe entire specimen was submitted for microscopic evaluation, including inked\u000amargins.\u000aAddendum #1 by Jacqueline M William M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000aFriday February 12, 2010 at 06:25:48PM\u000a[report_end]
