nd long\u000astitch designating lateral. A localization wire enters the lateral aspect of\u000athe specimen. A biopsy clip is identified and removed.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Area surrounding biopsy clip, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Remainder of mass, REMOVED_DATE frags each, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000asei/ag\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Vania Nose MD, PhD, Electronically signed on Thursday\u000aAugust 06, 2009 at 10:14:47AM\u000a[report_end]
