VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Consult material\u000aProcedure Date:\u000aOrdering Provider: JOSEPH H ANTIN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Olga Pozdnyakova, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Jason L Hornick, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aCONSULT SLIDES FROM NORTHWEST MEDICAL CENTER, TUCSON, AZ\u000aLEFT AXILLARY LYMPH NODE, DESIGNATED 9:30, CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY (NS-2436-07-A;\u000a3/20/07):\u000aLymph node with no significant pathologic change.\u000aLEFT AXILLARY LYMPH NODE, 9 CM FROM NIPPLE, CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY (NS-2436-07-B;\u000a3/20/07):\u000aLymph node with no significant pathologic change.\u000aLEFT AXILLARY LYMP NODE, 10 CM FROM NIPPLE, CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY (NS-2436-07-C;\u000a3/20/07):\u000aLymph node with no significant pathologic change.\u000aTISSUE AROUND IMPLANT, LEFT BREAST, DEBRIDEMENT (NS-4966-07; REMOVED_DATE ):\u000aANAPLASTIC LARGE CELL LYMPHOMA, ALK-NEGATIVE.\u000aSections show fibrous stroma infiltrated by sheets of pleomorphic large cells\u000awith irregular nuclei, vesicular chromatin, prominent nucleoli and moderate to\u000aabundant eosinophilic cytoplasm. The cell exhibit high mitotic activity.\u000aNumerous neutrophils are noted.\u000aImmunohistochemical stains performed at the referring institution and review at\u000aBrigham and Women's Hospital reveal the large cells are positive for REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID,\u000avimentin, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID (subset), and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID (subset), and negative for REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, and\u000aALK-1. High proliferation rate (90%) is detected by Ki-67 stain.\u000aScattered B cells are positive for REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. Numerous neutrophils are\u000apositive for REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. Scattered plasma cells are positive for REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. Melan-A and\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID are negative.\u000aLEFT BREAST MASS, BIOPSY (NS-5186-07-A; REMOVED_DATE ):\u000aANAPLASTIC LARGE CELL LYMPHOMA.\u000aSections show fibrous tissue infiltrated by the sheets of pleomorphic large\u000acells with irregular nuclei, dispersed chromatin, prominent nucleoli and\u000amoderate to abundant eosinophilic cytoplasm. The cell exhibit high mitotic\u000aactivity. Necrosis is present.\u000aSKIN AND BREAST PARENCHYMA, DESIGNATED LATERAL BREAST WOUND, BIOPSY\u000a(NS-5186-07-B; REMOVED_DATE ):\u000aSkin, subcutaneous tissue, and breast tissue with granulation tissue and\u000aforeign body giant cell reaction, consistent with surgical site; negative for\u000atumor.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Malignant lymphoma.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aConsult slides.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aReceived from Northwest Medical Center, 6200 North LA Cholla Blvd., Tucson, AZ\u000aREMOVED_CASE_ID, are thirty-eight glass slides.\u000aNine H&E stained slides are labeled "NS-2436-07" and sublabeled "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" to "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID",\u000a"REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" to "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" and "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" to "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID", corresponding to left axillary lymph nodes,\u000adesignated 9:30 (A), 9 cm from nipple (B) and 10 cm from nipple (C), core\u000aneedle biopsies, from a procedure performed on REMOVED_DATE  according to the\u000aaccompanying surgical pathology report bearing the patient's name.\u000aTwenty slides are labeled "NS-4966-07" and sublabeled "A" (H&E, kappa, lambda,\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, ALK-1, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, Ki-67, Melan\u000aA, PAX-5, vimentin, Neg x2), corresponding to tissue around implant, left\u000abreast, debridement, from a procedure performed on REMOVED_DATE  according to the\u000aaccompanying surgical pathology report bearing the patient's name.\u000aSix H&E stained slides are labeled "NS-5186-07" and sublabeled "FSA",\u000a"REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID", "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID", "A", "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" and "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID", corresponding to left breast mass\u000abiopsy (A), and skin and breast parenchyma, designated lateral breast wound,\u000abiopsy (B), from a procedure performed on REMOVED_DATE  according to the\u000aaccompanying surgical pathology report bearing the patient's name.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jason L Hornick M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a7/11/2008\u000a[report_end]
