D_DATE cm in aggregate). The specimen is triaged\u000afor touch preps, flow cytometry, cytogenetics and frozen tissue for possible\u000amicro studies.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Formalin-fixed tissue, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: B+ fixed tissue, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, "left breast tissue", consists of a skin ellipse (1.5 x REMOVED_DATE cm) excised\u000ato a depth of REMOVED_DATE cm. The specimen is unoriented. Tissue is allocated for\u000atouch preps, flow cytometry, cytogenetics, and frozen tissue for possible micro\u000astudies.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Formalin-fixed tissue, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: B+ fixed tissue, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-08-REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aDM/lp\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Ruben D Carrasco M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a9/17/2008\u000a[report_end]
