VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Amend/Addenda\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000a********** Addended Report ***********\u000aResident: David C. Park, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Jonathan N Glickman, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aSPECIMEN DESIGNATED "LEFT BREAST, EXCISION":\u000aBenign breast tissue with abundant acute and chronic and granulomatous\u000ainflammation, with abscess cavity formation, granulation tissue, and fat\u000anecrosis.\u000aInflammation extends to resection margins.\u000aGram, fungal (MSS), and acid-fast stains are negative for organisms.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 41 yo female with large breast mass. Non-diagnostic mammogram.\u000aU/S = tubular hypoechoic area suggestive of dilated ducts and (illegible)\u000aMRI = dramatic enhancement. Core bx = inflammation. Pt. prefers excision.\u000aOperation: Left breast excision mass.\u000aOperative Findings: Not provided.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast mass.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA. Left breast mass, short suture superior, long lateral, whip stitch on chest\u000awall margin.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number\u000aand "#1. Left breast mass, SSS, LSL, whipstitch on chest wall margin", and\u000aconsists of an irregular portion of fibrofatty tissue (9.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm),\u000awith a long suture designating lateral, and a short suture designating superior\u000aand a whipstitch designating chest wall margin (posterior). The specimen is\u000ainked anterior blue, posterior black, superior red, inferior green, medial\u000ayellow and lateral orange (please note that the medial margin is inked yellow\u000aand the lateral margin is inked orange). The specimen is serially sectioned to\u000areveal 80% dense white nodular fibrous tissue, and 20% yellow lobulated adipose\u000atissue. The nodular fibrous tissue, displays nodules ranging from REMOVED_DATE 0 cm\u000ain greatest dimension. A discrete mass is not identified. Representative\u000asections, to include the nodular areas, are sequentially submitted from\u000asuperior to inferior.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Superior margin, radially, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross sections of the nodular areas, from superior to\u000ainferior, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Inferior margin, radially, 3 frags each, ESS.\u000aPlease note that the lateral margin is inked orange and the medial margin is\u000ainked yellow.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aCP/ajb\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jonathan N Glickman M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a11/14/2007\u000aADDENDUM:\u000a16s rDNA PCR was performed on tissue blocks sent to the Centers for Disease\u000aControl, Division of Infectious Disease Pathology and are reported as NEGATIVE.\u000aThe diagnosis is unchanged.\u000aAddendum #1 by Danny A. Jr. Milner M.D., Electronically signed on Wednesday\u000aAugust 12, 2009 at 04:03:32PM\u000a[report_end]
