 a whipstitch ("new margin and scar"), which is inked blue and\u000aopposing focally ragged surface which is inked black. The tissue is serially\u000asectioned, exhibiting a small amount of dense fibrosis adjacent to the probable\u000aprevious resection margin (non-true margin - black ink). The remaining tissue\u000ais predominantly yellow lobulated adipose tissue and scant fibrous stroma.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Smaller fragment of fibroadipose tissue, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Larger fragment of fibroadipose tissue, multi frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, labeled "#2. Right breast medial shaved margin whipstitch at new\u000amargin", consists of a portion of yellow/tan lobulated fibroadipose tissue (4.8\u000ax REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with a whipstitch designating "new margin" per the surgeon.\u000aThe new margin is inked blue and the opposing concave, fibrotic, focally\u000anecrotic surface (old margin) is inked black. The specimen is serially\u000asectioned, exhibiting abundant fibrosis and necrosis adjacent to the previous\u000aresection margin (non-true margin - black ink). A focus of dense white tissue\u000a(0.7 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) is present within the fibroadipose tissue, REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000ablue inked new margin. The remaining breast tissue is composed of\u000apredominantly yellow lobulated adipose with scant fibrous stroma.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Breast tissue, sequentially submitted, multi frags, ESS. Note:\u000aDense fibrous area in micro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000adfi/lp\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Gilbert Brodsky M.D., Electronically signed on Wednesday\u000aREMOVED_MONTH 16, 2009 at 10:11:34AM\u000a[report_end]
