ibrous tissue distributed\u000airregularly throughout the specimen. Site of prior biopsy, corresponding to\u000alocation of biopsy clips, is identified and consists of several firm, cystic,\u000acalcified lesions (0.2-0.4 cm in diameter). Biopsy site and irregular tissue\u000ais submitted in cassettes REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID through REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. Remaining tissue is also submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Biopsy site, REMOVED_DATE frags each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Remaining tissue, REMOVED_DATE frags each, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aSEI/ajb\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jason L Hornick M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000aFriday REMOVED_MONTH 16, 2009 at 07:14:21AM\u000a[report_end]
