VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aBROWN, FELIX, MARCEL, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by BROWN,FELIX MARCEL,M.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST EXCISION, WIRE LOCALIZATION FOR A CLIP:\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU.\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aTypes - Solid\u000aNuclear grade - Low\u000aCalcifications in DCIS - Absent\u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - Present\u000aMicroinvasion (<0.1cm) - Absent\u000aExtent of DCIS\u000aNumber of blocks/total: - REMOVED_DATE blocks\u000aFinal Margins (DCIS)\u000aNegative (>0.3 cm) - Anterior, inferior, superior, medial,\u000alateral\u000aClose (<0.1 cm) - Posterior\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - Absent\u000aOTHER FINDINGS\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia (see NOTE)\u000aSclerosing adenosis\u000aCysts\u000aApocrine metaplasia\u000aCalcifications in benign epithelium\u000aNOTE: The atypical ductal hyperplasia is often severe and bordering on DUCTAL\u000aCARCINOMA IN SITU. It blends imperceptibly with the DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aand extends as a broad front along the posterior margin, focally present at\u000aink. Further of excision along this margin is recommended.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 42-year-old female status post core biopsy left breast for an area\u000aof nodular asymmetry 6:00 axis, with pathology demonstrating\u000aatypical ductal hyperplasia, surgical excision is recommended.\u000aOperation: Left breast wire localization biopsy.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast atypical ductal hyperplasia.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Left breast tissue, long stitch - lateral,\u000ashort-superior, whipstitch, deep.\u000aClip in specimen. JL.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by HONG,XUEFEI,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin in one part, labeled with the patient's\u000aname, unit number, and "left breast tissue, short/superior, long/lateral,\u000awhipstitch/deep", consists of a wire localized breast tissue (6.6 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm) with a long stitch denoting lateral, short stitch denoting superior,\u000awhipstitch denoting deep. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the\u000aevaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red;\u000ainferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. Sectioning reveals the\u000abiopsy site (2.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which is REMOVED_DATE cm from anterior, REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000aposterior, REMOVED_DATE cm from inferior, and REMOVED_DATE cm from superior, REMOVED_DATE cm from lateral\u000aand REMOVED_DATE cm from medial. The clip is identified in the biospy site.\u000aForty-percent (40%) of the tissue is fibrotic. The biopsy site and fibrotic\u000atissue are entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  clip site, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  biospy site, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 8: medial margin, 3 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 9: lateral margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000axh\u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
