VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST MASTECTOMY - PARTIAL OR SIMPLE\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aODZE, ROBERT, DANIEL, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by ODZE,ROBERT DANIEL,M.D.\u000a#1. RIGHT BREAST, SIMPLE MASTECTOMY:\u000aFibrocystic change, non-proliferative.\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy.\u000a#2. LEFT BREAST MASTECTOMY:\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU.\u000aSYNOPSIS:\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU - Present\u000aTypes - Cribriform\u000aNuclear grade - Intermediate\u000aCalcifications in DCIS - Absent\u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - Absent\u000aMicroinvasion (<0.1cm) - Absent\u000aExtent of DCIS\u000aNumber of blocks/total: REMOVED_DATE blocks (10, 11, 12)\u000aFinal Margins (DCIS)\u000aNegative (>0.3 cm) Deep\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - Absent\u000aLYMPH NODES\u000aAxillary lymph nodes: Negative\u000aNumber of positive nodes: 0\u000aNumber of nodes examined: 5\u000aTOTAL POSITIVE NODES (sentinel + axillary) - REMOVED_DATE \u000aOTHER FINDINGS\u000aCore biopsy site\u000aCalcifications in benign epithelium\u000a#3. SPECIMEN LABELED "CORE BIOPSY SITE":\u000aSkin with cicatrix.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 74 year old female not on HRT s/p REMOVED_DATE  left core biopsy for\u000aevaluation of an area of architectural distortion with solid mass on imaging.\u000aPathology revealed DCIS.\u000aOperation: Bilateral simple mastectomy\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast cancer\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1) Right breast - stitch marking short suture superior;\u000along suture lateral\u000a#2) Left breast tissue - short superior, bow tie on palpable lymph nodes, long\u000alateral, blue suture on medial core biopsy area\u000a#3) Core biopsy site\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by SHEN,JIAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart one, labeled "#1. right breast, stitch marking short superior, long\u000alateral", consists of a siimple mastectomy specimen (25 x 24 x 3 cm) with a\u000askin ellipse (23 x 11 cm) which contains areola (5 x 3 cm). The specimen\u000acontains 90% adipose tissue with a scattered area of fibrosis. No gross tumor\u000alesion is identified. Representative sections are submitted.\u000aMicro 1: area of fibrosis located REMOVED_DATE cm to the deep incision margin, 1\u000afrag, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  area of fibrosis, 1 frag each, RSS\u000aMicro 5: UOQ, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 6: LOQ, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 7: UIQ, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 8: LIQ, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 9: nipple, 1 frag, RSS\u000aPart two, labeled "#2. left breast, short superior, bow tie on palpable lymph\u000anodes, long lateral, blue stitch medial, core biopsy area", consists of a\u000asimple mastectomy specimen (25 x 25 x 3 cm) with a skin ellipse (23 x 10 cm)\u000awhich contains areola (4.5 x REMOVED_DATE cm). The nipple measures 1 cm in diameter.\u000aNo scar is identified on the skin surface. The specimen contains axillary tail\u000a(9 x 5 x 2 cm). The sutures are identified for indication of superior and\u000alateral aspects. A blue suture is also identified to indicate the previous\u000acore biopsy area. Identified near the blue suture there is an area which is\u000agrossly consistent with core biopsy site (0.5 cm in diameter) which is located\u000a4.5 cm to the closest deep excision margin. The remainder of the specimen\u000acontains multiple areas of fibrosis, however, no gross lesion or area of\u000acalcification is identified. A black bow tie suture is identified to indicate\u000athe palpable lymph nodes. Five potential lymph nodes are identified in the\u000aarea of axillary tail which is indicated by the surgeon with black bow tie\u000asutures. The lymph nodes range in size from REMOVED_DATE to 2 cm in diameter.\u000aRepresentative sections are submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  core biopsy site, 3 frags, ESS\u000aMicro 13: closest deep excision margin to core biopsy site, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  area of fibrosis located greater than 2 cm from the deep\u000aexcision margin, 1 frag each, RSS\u000aMicro 17: UIQ, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 18: LIQ, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 19: UOQ, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 20: LOQ, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 21: nipple, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  3 potential lymph nodes, 1 frag each, ESS\u000aMicro 25: 2 potential lymph nodes, 2 frags, ESS\u000aPart three, labeled "core biopsy site", consists of a segment of tan/white skin\u000aellipse (3 x REMOVED_DATE cm, excised to a depth of REMOVED_DATE cm). On the surface of the skin\u000athere is an area of scarring (0.2 cm) identified. The specimen is entirely\u000asubmitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  core biopsy site, 3 frags, ESS\u000ajis\u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY - PARTIAL OR SIMPLE\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY W/REGIONAL LYMPH NODES\u000a[report_end]
