ntinel\u000anode biopsy\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1) R. breast, sentinel node (FS)\u000a2) R. breast lump to mammo (and permanent)\u000aRADIOLOGY REPORT:\u000aMass in specimen.\u000aD. Smith\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "1) R. BREAST, SENTINEL NODE" (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aLymph node with no tumor seen.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by KINDELBERGER,DAVID W.,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart one, "right breast, sentinel node", consists of a single fragment of\u000afibroadipose tissue with one soft, tan/red lymph node (1.7 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm).\u000aThe lymph node is entirely submitted as REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aMicro 1: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 1 frag, ESS\u000aMicro 2: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 1 frag, ESS\u000aPart two, designated "right breast, lump", consists of a fragment of\u000afibroadipose tissue (3.2 cm superior to inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm medial to lateral,\u000a1.6 cm anterior to posterior). A metal wire is embedded in the specimen. The\u000aspecimen has been previously inked by the surgeon per pathology protocol for\u000athe evaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red;\u000ainferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. No lesions are grossly\u000aidentified. The specimen is entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  right breast mass, multi frag, ESS\u000aReports to: LESNIKOSKI, BETH-ANN M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: SENTINEL LYMPH NODE\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST BIOPSY W/O MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
