VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID SURGICAL MARGIN\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOGINO, SHUJI, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by OGINO,SHUJI,M.D.,PH.D.\u000a1) RIGHT BREAST, RE-EXCISION OF SUPERIOR MARGIN:\u000aBreast tissue with atypical ductal hyperplasia (see NOTE), intraductal\u000apapilloma (0.1 cm), ductal epithelial hyperplasia, sclerosing adenosis,\u000aapocrine metaplasia, cysts, and biopsy cavity wall.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000a2) RIGHT BREAST, RE-EXCISION OF LATERAL MARGIN:\u000aBreast tissue with apocrine metaplasia, florid ductal epithelial\u000ahyperplasia, cysts, calcifications associated with benign epithelium,\u000aand biopsy cavity wall (see NOTE).\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000aNOTE:\u000aLevels were examined on block #6, 10. Selected slides (#6, 10) have been\u000areviewed by Dr. J. Connolly.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: None given.\u000aOperation: Right partial mastectomy.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast cancer.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Superior.\u000a2. Lateral.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by BUNDOCK,ELIZABETH A.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart one, labeled "#1, re-excision of right breast tissue, superior", consists\u000aof a fragment of fibrofatty tissue (3.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which is received in\u000apathology inked by the surgeon. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol\u000afor the evaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior =\u000ared; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. The inferior\u000aportion of the specimen consists of a focally ragged surface with granulation\u000atissue and fat necrosis consistent with a prior biopsy cavity. The specimen\u000ais serially sectioned from anterior to posterior, perpendicular to the new\u000asuperior margin. No masses are identified. The specimen is entirely\u000asubmitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  breast tissue, 8 frags, ESS.\u000aPart two, labeled "#2, re-excision of right breast tissue, lateral", consists\u000aof a fragment of fibrofatty tissue (4.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which is received in\u000apathology inked by the surgeon. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol\u000afor the evaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior =\u000ared; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. The medial surface\u000aof the specimen consists of rubbery white fibrous tissue and granulation\u000atissue. The lateral aspect of the specimen consists of freshly excised adipose\u000atissue. The specimen is serially sectioned from anterior to posterior,\u000aperpendicular to the lateral margin revealing 50% fibrous tissue present as\u000asmall nodules scattered throughout the specimen. There are no hard foci\u000asuggestive of invasive carcinoma. The specimen is entirely submitted in\u000aseries from anterior to posterior.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  breast tissue, 10 frags, ESS.\u000aeab\u000aReports to: LESNIKOSKI, BETH-ANN M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN\u000a[report_end]
