sts of dense fibrous parenchyma with no gross lesion can be identified\u000aat the clip site. The specimen is entirely submitted for histologic\u000aexamination with clip site and surrounding dense fibrous tissue in cassette\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Posterior margin, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Serial sections from posterior to anterior, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Anterior margin, multi frags, ESS.\u000aLC/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Robert D Odze M.D., Electronically signed on Tuesday\u000aFebruary 10, 2009 at 01:18:38PM\u000a[report_end]
