ED_DATE \u000a-size (greatest dimension): Microscopic foci in the area of\u000athe invasive tumor in specimen A\u000aand in the separate final deep\u000amargin (specimen B)\u000a-extent: Focal\u000a-extensive intraductal component: Absent\u000a-necrosis in DCIS: None identified\u000a-microcalcifications in DCIS: Present, focal\u000a-margins for DCIS:\u000aIn the partial mastectomy specimen (A), the margins are widely clear\u000a(greater than 1 cm.) of ductal carcinoma in situ. The separate final deep\u000amargin specimen (B) contains ductal carcinoma in situ.\u000aLYMPH NODES:\u000aPositive lymph nodes out of total lymph nodes sampled: REMOVED_DATE \u000a-size of largest metastatic focus (greatest dimension): REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000a-extranodal extension: present, focal.\u000aCOMMENT: There is one lymph node present adjacent to the prior sentinel\u000alymph node excision site which is completely replaced by metastatic\u000acarcinoma and which has extranodal extension. One other lymph node is\u000apresent which has a single microscopic focus in the subcapsular sinus (less\u000athan REMOVED_DATE mm.).\u000aSKIN:\u000a-nipple: Involved by invasive carcinoma\u000a-skin/dermis: Carcinoma in dermal lymphatics\u000aADDITIONAL PATHOLOGIC FINDINGS:\u000aFibrocystic changes with focal sclerosing adenosis and microcalcifications.\u000aChanges consistent with prior excision site.\u000aPRIOR RELATED SPECIMENS REVIEWED:\u000aRight breast and sentinel lymph node excisions, S-03-REMOVED_CASE_ID (10/27/03).\u000aFinal Diagnosis by: Daniel D. Koelliker, M.D.\u000aClinical diagnosis & history:\u000aRight breast carcinoma; S/P lumpectomy and sentinel node biopsy; positive\u000amargins and positive node previously\u000aTissue-Designation:\u000aA.Breast, partial mastectomy - right\u000aB.Breast, excision (without margins) - right\u000aC.Lymph nodes, dissection - right axillary\u000aGross description:\u000aThe specimen is received in three containers.\u000aSpecimen A labeled "right breast tissue" is received fresh and consists of a 43\u000agram, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. portion of fibroadipose tissue with a 7 x REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000askin ellipse on one surface and which is marked with two sutures. The skin has\u000aa central REMOVED_DATE cm. areola with an unremarkable REMOVED_DATE cm. in diameter central\u000anipple. A long suture is present at one end of the skin ellipse oriented as\u000amedial and 90 degrees to this, in the mid portion of the skin ellipse, on one\u000aedge is a short suture oriented as superior of the right breast. An apparent\u000ascar is present at the lateral end of the skin ellipse. The margins throughout\u000aare grossly free of tumor and are inked black. The deep surface is double\u000ainked red. Cross sectioning through the specimen demonstrates a 2 x REMOVED_DATE x 1\u000acm. cavity located deep and lateral to the nipple. No gross evidence of tumor\u000ais seen surrounding the cavity. The surrounding tissue is yellow lobulated\u000aadipose tissue with thin strands of white-tan fibrous tissue and focal rubbery,\u000awhite-tan fibrous areas. No suspicious areas are seen.\u000aSection code: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - lateral margin\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - lateral end of biopsy cavity\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - deep aspect of cavity\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - superior side of medial end of cavity\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - inferior side of medial aspect of cavity\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - nipple with superior margin\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - nipple with inferior margin\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - immediately medial to nipple\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - medial to nipple with superior and deep margins\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - representative sections of medial end\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - medial margin\u000aSpecimen B labeled "right breast final deep margin" is received in formalin and\u000aconsists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. portion of fibroadipose tissue with areas of\u000acautery artifact. The specimen is sectioned and entirely submitted in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000a3 agg. all.\u000aSpecimen C labeled "right axillary lymph nodes" is received in formalin and\u000aconsists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. portion of fibroadipose tissue containing\u000amultiple lymph nodes ranging from REMOVED_DATE to REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000aSection code: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - lymph nodes\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - lymph nodes and adjacent changes consistent with prior\u000aexcision site\u000aDictated by: DDK____(signature on file)____NICOLE MIHOK, M.D. REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a____(signature on file)____DANIEL D. KOELLIKER, M.D. REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a[report_end]
