nt's name\u000aand MR number.\u000aPart A, "#1. Tissue from left breast tissue mammo", consists of 51 g of\u000adisrupted lumpectomy with a whip stitch designated posterior, long stitch\u000adesignated lateral, and short stitch designated superior (medial to lateral REMOVED_DATE \u000acm, superior density of REMOVED_DATE cm, anterior to posterior REMOVED_DATE cm). A wire enters\u000athe specimen from the anterior aspect. The specimen is inked per pathology\u000aprotocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue;\u000asuperior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange.\u000aThe specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a biopsy cavity (0.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm). The cavity is marked with a clip and is located REMOVED_DATE cm to the lateral and\u000aposterior margins, REMOVED_DATE cm to the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior and\u000aanterior margins, and REMOVED_DATE cm to the medial margin. The entire specimen is\u000asubmitted for histology.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Left breast tissue, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID contains the area marked with the clip.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID contains 2 frags in each.\u000aPart B, "#2. Tissue from right breast-mammo", consists of a 31 g lumpectomy\u000a(medial to lateral REMOVED_DATE cm, superior to inferior REMOVED_DATE cm, anterior to posterior\u000a1.8 cm). The wire enters the specimen from the lateral and exits at the\u000aanterior aspect. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the\u000aevaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red;\u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. The specimen is serially\u000asectioned anterior to posterior to reveal a clip located in the area of\u000afibrosis (0.9 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The clip is located REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000ain the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000aanterior margin. The entire specimen is submitted for histology.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Right breast tissue, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID contain the area marked with a clip.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000akst/ag\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Lynette M Sholl M.D., Electronically signed on Tuesday\u000aREMOVED_MONTH 02, 2009 at 02:57:01PM\u000a[report_end]
