appears viable with mitoses present.\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: by RICHARDSON,ANDREA L.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for invasive carcinoma (block 2):\u000aEstrogen receptor - NEGATIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor - NEGATIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) - POSITIVE (3+)\u000aNOTE: Normal epithelial cells are appropriately and strongly positive for\u000aestrogen and progesterone receptors.\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000ainvasive carcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but\u000aonly a portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity\u000ain >10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 54 year old female with high-grade infiltrating ductal carcinoma of\u000athe left breast.\u000aOperation: Left modified radical mastectomy\u000aClinical Diagnosis: High-grade infiltrating ductal carcinoma left breast\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1) Left breast and axillary contents (stitch marks -\u000along/lateral, short/superior on skin, bow tie/axillary tail)\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by BAILEY,GERALD P.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number\u000aand "#1. left breast with axillary contents and marking stitches", and consists\u000aof a left modified radical mastectomy with a skin ellipse (21 x 9 cm), areola\u000a(38 x 3 cm), nipple (1.4 x REMOVED_DATE cm) and breast (27 x 23 x REMOVED_DATE cm), and axillary\u000atail (10 x 4 x REMOVED_DATE cm). The posterior surface of the specimen is inked in\u000ablack. The specimen is serially sectioned and radiographed. An 8 cm area\u000acontaining microcalcifications is identified medial to the nipple. A prior\u000aneedle core biopsy site is identified 3 cm deep and inferior to the nipple.\u000aThe biopsy site is adjacent to a REMOVED_DATE cm central hematoma and is surrounded by a\u000arubbery white tissue with no definite residual invasive carcinoma. The\u000aaxillary tail contains a lymph node (2.3 cm) with a REMOVED_DATE cm area suspicious for\u000ametastatic carcinoma. One-half of the biopsy site and a portion of the lymph\u000anode are submitted to tumor bank. The entire remaining biopsy site and\u000arepresentative sections of the area containing microcalcification, skin, and\u000afour quadrants are submitted for histologic evaluation.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  biopsy cavity, 1 frag/cass, ESS\u000aMicro 4: skin above biopsy cavity and posterior margin below biopsy\u000acavity, 1 frag/cass, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  area of microcalcifications, REMOVED_DATE frags/cass, RSS\u000aMicro 7: UIQ, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 8: UOQ, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 9: LIQ, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 10: LOQ, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 11: nipple, 2 frags, ESS\u000aMicro 12: residual lymph node with possible metastatic carcinoma, 2 frags,\u000aESS\u000aMicro 13: 4 axillary lymph nodes, 4 frags, RSS\u000aMicro 14: 7 axillary lymph nodes, 4 frags, RSS\u000aMicro 15: 2 axillary lymph nodes, 4 frags, RSS\u000aMicro 16: remainder of lymph node retrieved from tumor bank (same node as\u000amicro #12), 2 frag, ESS\u000ageb\u000aReports to: LESNIKOSKI, BETH-ANN M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY W/REGIONAL LYMPH NODES\u000a[report_end]
