en. The specimen is\u000ainked per pathology protocol as anterior blue, posterior black, superior red,\u000ainferior green, medial orange and lateral yellow, and is serially sectioned to\u000areveal a white well-delineated irregular lobulated nodule (1.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm),\u000awhich comes to REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE \u000acm from the lateral margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin. The remaining\u000acut surface displays 50% yellow lobulated adipose tissue, and 50% white fibrous\u000atissue, with no additional masses or lesions identified. The specimen is\u000asequentially submitted in its entirety.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, radially, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross sections from lateral to medial, with the nodule\u000ain REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin, radially, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000acp\u005cpab\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Hejin P Hahn M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a8/20/2007\u000a[report_end]
