VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ROBERT T OSTEEN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-06-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Kevin B Long, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Susan Lester, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. LEFT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED BREAST BIOPSY FOR A MASS:\u000aComplex sclerosing lesion with intraductal papillomas, associated with biopsy\u000asite changes.\u000aApocrine cysts.\u000aNote: There is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the entire\u000aspecimen, including margins.\u000aB. LEFT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED BREAST BIOPSY FOR A SUBAREOLAR MASS:\u000aIntraductal papillomas (largest, REMOVED_DATE cm), correlating with the\u000aRadiologic lesion.\u000aApocrine cysts.\u000aNote: There is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the entire\u000aspecimen, including margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: None given.\u000aOperation: Left needle localized breast biopsy.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal left mammogram.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Left needle localized breast biopsy - FS at 11:25.\u000aB/2. Left subareolar mass - FS at 11:30 - for mammo.\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000aA/1. Target mass, clip and intact wire contained in specimen.\u000aSigned: S. Nielsen, REMOVED_DATE  12:00 p.m.\u000aB/2. Ultrasound of specimen and radiographs show lesion and\u000aintact wire. Signed: S. Nielsen, REMOVED_DATE  12:00 p.m.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two parts, each labeled with the patients\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart A, "#1 L needle localized breast bx", consists of an unoriented REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000ax REMOVED_DATE cm fragment of fibroadipose tissue, received with a radiograph\u000ademonstrating localizing wire in place within the specimen with a density and a\u000aclip. The wire enters one pole of the specimen and exits at the mid portion of\u000athe specimen. Sectioning reveals fibrosis, fat necrosis and hemorrhage along\u000athe localizing wire tract, particularly in the area of the wire tip at the site\u000aof the density. There are no discrete lesions, with the exception of a REMOVED_DATE cm\u000anodular fat necrosis at the wire tip. The specimen is entirely submitted,\u000asequentially from pole of entry of localizing wire (wire in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Multiple frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, "#2 L subareolar mass - mammo", is received with a radiograph\u000ademonstrating localizing wire in place within the specimen, and consists of an\u000aunoriented REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm fragment of fibroadipose tissue with a\u000asuperficially embedded localizing wire at one edge. The specimen radiograph\u000areveals only a vague area of density. Sectioning demonstrates a REMOVED_DATE cm in\u000adiameter cyst, filled with a tan/white, granular, amorphous material at the\u000alocalizing wire tip, REMOVED_DATE cm from the closest blue-inked margin. Otherwise,\u000athere is a fibrodense band occupying approximately 60 to 70% of the remaining\u000aparenchyma, which is without gross abnormality.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Entire specimen, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID is lesion at wire tip, 5 frags total, ESS.\u000aWP/elw\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Kevin B Long M.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a3/1/2006\u000a[report_end]
