VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST MASTECTOMY - PARTIAL OR SIMPLE\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aKRANE, JEFFREY, FRED, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by KRANE,JEFFREY FRED,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST, TOTAL MASTECTOMY:\u000aBreast tisue with fibrosis, cysts, apocrine metaplasia, and sclerosing\u000aadenosis.\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia (block 1).\u000aColumnar alteration of lobules with prominent snouts and secretions.\u000aSkin within normal limits.\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY:\u000aBreast tissue with fibrosis and cysts.\u000aPrevious biopsy site with no tumor present.\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia.\u000aMETASTATIC CARCINOMA, in five of eleven (5:11) lymph nodes with focal\u000aextranodal extension (block 24).\u000aLargest metastatic deposit is REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000aAxillary biopsy site with foreign body giant cell reaction.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 56 year old female with right breast cancer.\u000aOperation: Left total mastectomy (prophylactic), right modified radical\u000amastectomy\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast cancer\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1) Left breast (short stitch/superior; long stitch/lateral)\u000a#2) Right breast (short stitch/superior; long stitch/lateral)\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by BENNETT,MICHAEL W.,M.B.,B.C.H\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart one, labeled "#1. left breast", consists of a left simple mastectomy\u000aspecimen which weighs 526 grams and measures REMOVED_DATE cm from inferior to superior,\u000a15.4 cm from medial to lateral, and REMOVED_DATE cm from anterior to posterior. Included\u000ais an ellipse of skin (12.1 cm medial to lateral x REMOVED_DATE cm inferior to superior)\u000awith nipple (1.2 cm in diameter x REMOVED_DATE cm). Extending throughout 80% of the\u000aspecimen is white fibrous tissue. Posterior to the skin ellipse and at a\u000adistance of REMOVED_DATE cm from the deep margin is a small cystic lesion which measures\u000a0.3 cm in maximum dimension. No other focal lesions are identified. Lymph\u000anodes are not identified.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  deep margin, 2 frags, RSS\u000aMicro 3: area of cyst, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 4: lower outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 5: lower inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 6: upper outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 7: upper inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 8: nipple, 2 frags, RSS\u000aPart two, labeled "#2. right breast", consists of a right modified radical\u000amastectomy specimen which weighs 449 grams and measures REMOVED_DATE cm from inferior\u000ato superior x REMOVED_DATE cm from medial to lateral x REMOVED_DATE cm from anterior to\u000aposterior. In addition, the axillary tail measures 8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000aAnteriorly there is an ellipse of skin which measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm with a\u000anipple measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. Beneath the nipple is a well-healed incision\u000ascar (4.4 cm) which extend to within REMOVED_DATE cm of the nipple and to within REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aof the inferior margin of the skin ellipse. Beneath the incision is a biopsy\u000acavity which measures REMOVED_DATE x 3 x REMOVED_DATE cm. The cavity is open at its inferior\u000asurface and extends in this area to the inferior margin of the specimen. The\u000aopening measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. A second opening in this area and anterior to\u000athe first measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The biopsy cavity extends to within REMOVED_DATE cm of\u000athe lateral margin, 5 cm of the medial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the superior margin\u000aand REMOVED_DATE cm of the deep margin. Ten axillary lymph nodes are identified, the\u000alargest of which measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. In addition a single lymph node\u000ais identified deep to the biopsy cavity which measures REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest\u000adimension. None of the lymph nodes appear to be involve by tumor\u000amicroscopically. An area of fat necrosis is identified which measures\u000aapproximately REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000aMicro 9: inferior aspect of biopsy cavity, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 10: lateral aspect of biopsy cavity, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 11: medial aspect of biopsy cavity, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 12: superior aspect of biopsy cavity, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 13: deep aspect of biopsy cavity (including margin), 2 frags, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  deep margin in area of biopsy cavity, 2 frags, RSS\u000aMicro 16: fibrous tissue, ILQ, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 17: fibrous tissue, IOQ, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 18: fibrous tissue, UOQ, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 19: fibrous tissue, UIQ, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 20: lymph node deep to biopsy cavity, bisected, 2 frags, ESS\u000aMicro 21: 2 bisected lymph nodes, 4 frags, ESS\u000aMicro 22: 1 bisected lymph node, 2 frags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  6 lymph nodes, 6 frags, ESS\u000aMicro 25: 1 lymph node trisected, 3 frags, ESS\u000aMicro 26: area of fat necrosis, 1 frag, RSS\u000amwb\u000aReports to: ORGILL, DENNIS, PAUL M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY - PARTIAL OR SIMPLE\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY W/REGIONAL LYMPH NODES\u000a[report_end]
