VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY(IES)\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aRICHARDSON, ANDREA, L., M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by RICHARDSON,ANDREA L.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, 2:00, 14 G ULTRASOUND GUIDED CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR AN REMOVED_DATE CM\u000aMASS:\u000aFibroepithelial lesion with myxoid stroma which is regionally\u000ahypercellular. Scattered stromal mitoses are seen.\u000aNOTE: The differential diagnosis includes a low grade phyllodes tumor or\u000aa cellular fibroadenoma. Excision is suggested for definitive diagnosis.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, 12:00, 14 G ULTRASOUND GUIDED CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR AN REMOVED_DATE CM\u000aMASS:\u000aFibroepithelial lesion with myxoid stroma which is focally\u000ahypercellular.\u000aNOTE: The differential diagnosis includes a low grade phyllodes tumor or\u000aa cellular fibroadenoma. Excision is suggested for definitive diagnosis.\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: by RICHARDSON,ANDREA L.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThere is a typographical error in the specimen heading for part 1 in the\u000aoriginal report. The first core biopsy (2:00 lesion, REMOVED_DATE cm mass) is actually\u000afrom the LEFT BREAST, not the right breast.\u000aThe second biopsy (12:00 lesion, REMOVED_DATE cm mass) is from the right breast\u000aas designated in the original report.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 21 year old female with REMOVED_DATE cm hypoechoic mass left breast 2 o'clock\u000aand REMOVED_DATE cm hypoechoic mass right breast 12 o'clock. S/p ultrasound\u000aguided core biopsy. Five passes on each side.\u000aOperation: 14g ultrasound\u000aOperative findings: Bilateral breast masses\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Fibroadenoma(s)\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Left breast core samples - orange site 1\u000aRight breast core samples - yellow site 2\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by WU,HUIQING,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin in two parts, each labeled with the\u000apatient's name and unit number.\u000aPart one, labeled "left breast site 1", in an orange cassette, and consists of\u000amultiple, soft, fragmented, yellow to white tissue cores (0.6 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in\u000aaggregate).\u000aMicro 1: Multi frags, ESS.\u000aPart two, labeled "right breast", in a yellow cassette, and consists of\u000amultiple, soft, fragmented, yellow to white tissue cores (1.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm\u000ain aggregate).\u000aMicro 2: Multi frags, ESS.\u000alm\u000aReports to: GIARDINO, ANGELA, ANN M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY(IES)\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY(IES)\u000a[report_end]
