VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aNASCIMENTO, ALESSANDRA, F., M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by NASCIMENTO,ALESSANDRA F.,M.D.\u000a#1. RIGHT BREAST MASS, EXCISION:\u000aFibroadenoma, REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000aExcision is complete.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000a#2. LEFT BREAST MASS, EXCISION:\u000aLOW GRADE PHYLLODES TUMOR (see NOTE)\u000aNOTE: Even though the specimen is partially fragmented, areas with phyllodes\u000aarchitecture and stromal overgrowth can be seen. The stromal component is\u000aalso cellular, but has minimal atypia, rare mitoses (3/10 hpf) and\u000apushing marging. The tumor is best classified as a low grade phyllodes\u000atumor. Tumor is present at inked tissue edges although fragmentation of\u000athe specimen precludes evaluation of completness of resection.\u000aThis case was reviewed by Dr. A. Richardson, breast pathology service,\u000awho concurs.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 21 year old feamle with L 2 o'clock breast mass, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm\u000asolid mass on ultrasound. Also has R 12 o'clock breast mass, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm solid mass on ultrasound. U/S guided core biopsy of both masses REMOVED_DATE \u000aMixed fibroepithelial lesion. Bilateral excision recommened.\u000aOperation: Excision bilateral breast masses.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Bilateral breast masses.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1 - R breast mass, short = superior, long = lateral, whip\u000astitch @ deep margin.\u000a#2 - L breast tissue.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by WILLIAM,JACQUELINE M.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen was received in two parts, labeled with the patient's name and\u000aunit number.\u000aPart one, "right breast mass", consists of a breast biopsy specimen, meausuring\u000a1.6 cm from superior to inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm from medial to lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000aanterior to posterior. There is a long stitch designating lateral, and a short\u000astitch designating superior. The specimen has been six inked by the surgeon\u000aper the pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black;\u000aanterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange.\u000aThe inside of the specimen is composed almost entirely of firm tan/white\u000afibrous tissue, with almost no areas of adipose tissue. Within the medial\u000aaspect of the specimen there is a white nodular area that is softer than the\u000asurrounding tissue, measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm, and located REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000amedial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin,\u000a0.2 cm from the anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom the lateral margin. No hemorrhagic areas or necrotic areas or\u000acalcifications or prior cavities are identified. The entire specimen is\u000asubmitted in slices from medial to lateral, with the first cassette being the\u000amedial margin.\u000aMicro #1; Slice one, medial and superior margins, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro #2: Slice two, medical, superior and inferior margins showing nodule, 1\u000afrag, ESS.\u000aMicro #3+4: Slices three and four with superior, inferior, anterior and\u000aposterior margins showing nodular area, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro #5: Slice five, superior, inferior, anterior, and lateral margins, 1\u000afrag, ESS.\u000aMicro #6: Slices six and seven showing superior, inferior, and lateral\u000amargins, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aPart two, "left breast tissue", consists of multiple fragments of unoriented\u000apink/tan, friable soft tissue; the largest measuring 3 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm, and the\u000asmallest measuring 1 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. In aggregate, the sample measures 3 x REMOVED_DATE \u000ax REMOVED_DATE cm. The largest specimen is composed of 80% tan/white fibrous tissue and\u000athe remainder is composed primarily of adipose tissue. There is a small area\u000aof necrosis, measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 cm. Representative sections were\u000asubmitted.\u000aMicro #7: Sections from largest fragment, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro #8: Section from largest fragment showing adipose tissue and area of\u000anecrosis, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro #9: Sections from smallest fragment, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Remainder of specimen, mult frags, ESS.\u000ajaw/\u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
