VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Elizabeth Amy Morgan, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Gilbert Brodsky, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aSPECIMEN DESIGNATED "RIGHT BREAST TISSUE":\u000aBiopsy site changes.\u000aColumnar cell change with benign calcifications.\u000aFocal atypical lobular hyperplasia.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the\u000aspecimen, including margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 59-year-old female with abnormal R mammo REMOVED_DATE  (Cooley Dickenson)\u000ademonstrating 5-mm clustered microcalcifications 12 o'clock - and S/P R breast\u000acore bx REMOVED_DATE  revealing ADH - excision recommended.\u000aOperation: R breast wire localization exc bx.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal R mammo.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aa/1) Right breast tissue, short stitch - superior, long - lateral, whip stitch\u000aon chest wall margin --> mammo.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Clip with tiny assoc calcs and fatty tissue in area of prior calcs.\u000a(ILLEGIBLE signature.)\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name and unit\u000anumber, and "#1. Right breast tissue, short stitch superior, long lateral,\u000awhipstitch on chest wall margin", and consists of one breast biopsy specimen\u000awith a localizing wire in place. Per surgeon, short stitch = superior, long\u000astitch = lateral, and whipstitch = chest wall margin (located inferolaterally).\u000aThe specimen measures REMOVED_DATE cm medial to lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm superior to inferior,\u000aand REMOVED_DATE cm anterior to posterior. The accompanying radiograph shows a surgical\u000aclip with area of tiny fragmented calcification at the site of the wire as well\u000aas two tight areas of calcification away from the wire near the inferior\u000amargin. The specimen is inked by the surgeon as follows: Red equals superior,\u000aorange equals medial, yellow equals lateral, green equals inferior, blue equals\u000aanterior, black equals posterior. There is a brown, focally hemorrhagic core\u000abiopsy site (2.4 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with surgical clip that abuts the medial and\u000aanterior and lateral margins, is REMOVED_DATE cm to the inferior margin, is REMOVED_DATE cm to\u000athe posterior margin, and is REMOVED_DATE cm to the superior margin. There is also a\u000awhite, fibrotic area (2.4 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) that abuts the inferior and lateral\u000amargins. The remainder of the specimen consists of adipose tissue. The\u000aspecimen is sectioned medial to lateral and the entire specimen is sequentially\u000asubmitted for histologic evaluation.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Breast excision specimen, sequentially sectioned from medial to\u000alateral, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID = area of clip, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID = fibrotic area (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/2 frags each,\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/1 frag each), ESS.\u000aEM/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Gilbert Brodsky M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
