erior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow;\u000amedial/orange (inked by surgeon). A localizing wire enters laterally and exits\u000amedially. The specimen is received with an accompanying radiograph\u000ademonstrating the localizing wire in place within the specimen, adjacent to an\u000aill-defined lesion in the medial aspect. Sectioning in this area demonstrates\u000apalpably firm cystic fibrodense tissue without visible, masses, lesions or\u000aother definitive abnormalities grossly. There is focal hemorrhage along the\u000alocalizing wire tract. Remainder of the specimen is comprised of REMOVED_DATE %\u000atan/white fibrous tissue admixed with soft, lobulated tan/yellow adipose\u000atissue. The entire specimen is submitted, sequentially from medial to lateral,\u000awith perpendicular medial margin in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, perpendicular lateral margin in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, and\u000aarea of interest (per radiograph, wire) likely in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Multi frags, ESS.\u000aPlease note: Tissue will be held for further fixation prior to processing.\u000aPart B, "#2. Medial inferior shaved margin, right breast, long suture lateral,\u000ashort suture superior", consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm curvilinear excision\u000aof fibroadipose tissue, oriented by sutures designating superior (short suture)\u000aand lateral (long suture) edges. The true surgical margins have been inked by\u000athe surgeon as follows: Superior - red, medial - orange, inferior - green.\u000aThe remaining surfaces are inked by the prosector for purposes of orientation\u000aonly, as follows: Lateral - yellow, anterior - blue, posterior - black. The\u000alateral aspect of the specimen is comprised of a biopsy cavity wall and likely\u000adoes not represent surgical margin. The specimen is received with an\u000aaccompanying radiograph. Sectioning demonstrates at least 95% tan/white cystic\u000afibrodense tissue without obvious masses, lesions or other abnormalities\u000agrossly. The entire specimen is submitted, sequentially from superior to\u000ainferior, with superior margin in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, perpendicular inferior margin in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Multi frags, ESS.\u000aPlease note: Tissue will held for further fixation prior to processing.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000adb/ag\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Michelle S Hirsch M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a5/23/2008\u000a[report_end]
