VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Kristin S. Ricci, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Jane E. Brock, M.B., B.S., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. LEFT BREAST WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A MASS AND A CLIP:\u000aLOW GRADE PHYLLODES TUMOR, REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest dimension, see NOTE\u000aFibroadenomas x 3 (0.8 cm, REMOVED_DATE cm and REMOVED_DATE cm, see NOTE).\u000aPhyllodes tumor is located REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000amedial margin and > REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior, inferior, anterior and lateral\u000amargins.\u000aCore biopsy site present.\u000aNOTE: The Phyllodes tumor shows a nodular and pushing margin with mild stromal\u000aovergrowth with focally increased stromal cellularity. No nuclear atypia is\u000apresent and no heterologous elements are seen. Mitoses number up to REMOVED_DATE HPF.\u000aIn addition, the excision also includes three fibroadenomas without increased\u000acellularity, stromal overgrowth and with no stromal mitoses seen. Two of the\u000aadditional foci (0.5 cm and REMOVED_DATE cm) are located medially in the specimen\u000aapproximately REMOVED_DATE cm from the Phyllodes tumor (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), and the third is\u000alocated posteriorly (0.8 cm; REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID). Dr. Susan Lester has reviewed slides of the\u000aPhyllodes tumor and the fibroadenomas from all parts and concurs with the\u000adiagnoses.\u000aB. LEFT BREAST MEDIAL SHAVE MARGIN EXCISION:\u000aBenign breast tissue including fibroadenoma, (0.3 cm), see NOTE\u000aNOTE: The fibroadenoma shows no increased stromal cellularity, stromal\u000aovergrowth or mitoses present.\u000aC. LEFT BREAST SUPERIOR SHAVE MARGIN EXCISION:\u000aBenign breast tissue negative for tumor.\u000aD. LEFT BREAST INFERIOR SHAVE MARGIN EXCISION:\u000aBenign breast tissue including fibroadenoma, (0.6 cm), see NOTE\u000aNOTE: The fibroadenoma shows no increased stromal cellularity, stromal\u000aovergrowth or mitoses present.\u000aE. LEFT BREAST LATERAL SHAVE MARGIN EXCISION:\u000aBenign breast tissue including fibroadenoma, (0.3 cm), see NOTE\u000aNOTE: The fibroadenoma shows no increased stromal cellularity, stromal\u000aovergrowth or mitoses present.\u000aF. LEFT BREAST POSTERIOR SHAVE MARGIN EXCISION:\u000aFragments of skeletal muscle, fascia and adipose tissue negative for tumor.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 52 year old female whose REMOVED_DATE  mamo demonstrated complex cyst vs.\u000asolid mass at 12:30 axis. REMOVED_DATE  core biopsy showed phyllodes tumor.\u000aOperation: Excision left breast mass with wire.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast ca.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Left breast mass with wire short superior.\u000aB/2. Left breast medial shaved margin long lateral, whip - new whip - deep\u000amargin.\u000aC/3. Left breast superior shaved margin whip new margin.\u000aD/4. Left breast inferior shaved margin whip new margin.\u000aE/5. Left breast lateral shaved margin whip new margin.\u000aF/6. Left breast posterior margin whip chest wall.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Mass, clip, hook and wire in specimen. Called Dr. Rhei at 3:51 pm on\u000a4/20/09.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in six parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart A, "L breast mass with wire", consists of a wire-localized partial\u000amastectomy specimen (5.8 cm medial to lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm inferior to superior, and\u000a4.1 cm anterior to posterior). The specimen is oriented by the surgeon with a\u000ashort suture designating superior, a long suture designating lateral and a\u000awhipstitch designating deep. The specimen is received inked by the surgeon for\u000athe evaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red;\u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. An accompanying specimen\u000aradiograph demonstrates a localizing wire entering the superior aspect of the\u000aspecimen to indicate a mass and a surgical clip. The specimen is serially\u000asectioned from superior to inferior to reveal a white/pink well-circumscribed\u000anodular mass (1.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The mass is located centrally within the\u000aspecimen and is greater than REMOVED_DATE cm from the surgical resection margins. The\u000aspecimen consists of 85% adipose tissue and 15% fibrous tissue, including the\u000amass. There are multiple cysts present, up to REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest dimension.\u000aThe specimen is submitted entirely.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Superior resection margin, radially sectioned, 3 frags each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #4, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #5, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #7, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #8, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Inferior resection margin, 3 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Anterior resection margin, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial resection margin, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Inferior resection margin, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral resection margin, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Posterior resection margin, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Superior resection margin, multi frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, "#2. L breast medial shave margin", consists of one fragment of\u000ayellow/pink soft tissue with a whip-stitch designating the new margin (3.0 x\u000a2.5 x REMOVED_DATE cm). The new margin designated with a whip-stitch is inked black.\u000aThe remainder of the specimen is inked blue. The specimen is serially\u000asectioned and submitted entirely.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Entire specimen, multi frags each, ESS.\u000aPart C, "#3. L breast superior shave margin", consists of one fragment of\u000alobulated yellow/pink fibroadipose tissue (4.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). A whip-stitch\u000ais present on one aspect of the specimen designating the new surgical margin.\u000aThe whip-stitch area is inked black and the remainder of the specimen is inked\u000ablue. The specimen is serially sectioned and submitted entirely. The majority\u000aof the specimen consists of adipose tissue.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Entire specimen, multi frags each, ESS.\u000aPart D, "#4. Left breast inferior shave margin, whip = new margin", consists of\u000aone fragment of pink/tan fibroadipose tissue (3.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The\u000aspecimen consists of 80% fibrous tissue and 20% adipose tissue. A whip-stitch\u000adesignates the new surgical margin. The area designated by the whip-stitch is\u000ainked black. The remainder of the specimen is inked blue. The specimen is\u000aserially sectioned and submitted entirely.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Entire specimen, serially sectioned, 2 frags each, ESS.\u000aPart E, "#5. L breast lateral shaved margin, whip = new margin", consists of\u000aone fragment of pink/yellow soft tissue (3.7 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The specimen\u000aconsists primarily of adipose tissue. A whip stitch designates the new\u000asurgical margin. This area is inked black and the remainder of the specimen is\u000ainked blue. The specimen is serially sectioned and submitted entirely.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Entire specimen, serially sectioned, multi frags each, ESS.\u000aPart F, "#6. L posterior shaved margin, whip = chest wall", consists of one\u000afragment of yellow/pink fibroadipose tissue (3.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The specimen\u000aconsists primarily of adipose tissue. A whip stitch designates the new\u000asurgical margin. This area is inked black and the remainder of the specimen is\u000ainked blue. The specimen is serially sectioned and submitted entirely.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Entire specimen, serially sectioned, multi frags each, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aric/ag\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jane E. Brock M.B., B.S., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000aMonday REMOVED_MONTH 27, 2009 at 04:58:45PM\u000a[report_end]
