VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aODZE, ROBERT, DANIEL, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by ODZE,ROBERT DANIEL,M.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST, RE-EXCISION:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA WITH MIXED FEATURES\u000aSYNOPSIS:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA\u000aSize - at least REMOVED_DATE cm (measured off the\u000aglass slide), see NOTE\u000aMultifocal - no\u000aHistologic Type - mixed mucinous and lobular\u000aHistologic Grade (SBR) - II (moderate)\u000aNuclear Grade - intermediate\u000aEIC - negative\u000aLymphovascular invasion - absent\u000aDermal lymphatic invasion - absent\u000aSkin invasion - absent\u000aSkeletal muscle invasion - absent\u000aFinal Margins (invasive) -\u000aPositive (ink on carcinoma) - all (unoriented), see NOTE\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU - absent\u000aOTHER FINDINGS\u000aRemote scar\u000aBiopsy cavity\u000aRecent core biopsy site\u000aSkin with scar\u000aSkeletal muscle\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER/PR/HER-2) - pending\u000aNOTE:\u000aThe tumor is present in three (3) fragments of additional tissue identified in\u000athe same container as the excision. These fragments were not oriented.\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for invasive carcinoma (block 12):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) NEGATIVE (0)\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000acarcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but\u000aonly a portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity\u000ain >10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Area of new density in former ca site of left breast originally\u000atreated in 1994.\u000aOperation: Excision dense area left breast cancer site\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Density left breast former cancer site\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1. Left breast tissue (short stitch/superior; long\u000astitch/lateral)\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by HARRIS,MARIAN HESTER,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number\u000aand "#1. left breast tissue, short stitch superior, long stitch lateral", and\u000aconsists of a fibrofatty breast tissue (6.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) partially surfaced\u000aby a tan skin ellipse (7.0 x REMOVED_DATE cm) along the anterior aspect of displaying a\u000awell-healed eccentric linear scar (3.0 cm in length) coming to within REMOVED_DATE cm of\u000athe superior inferior skin margin. There is a short suture designating\u000asuperior and a long suture designating lateral. The specimen is inked per\u000apathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black;\u000aanterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange.\u000aThe specimen is serially sectioned to reveal subjacent to the scar is a REMOVED_DATE x\u000a1.8 x REMOVED_DATE cm hemorrhagic dense fibrous area with focal fat necrosis, consistent\u000awith a previous biopsy site, with radiating fibrous strands extending to the\u000asubjacent scar, and abutting the superior/posterior, coming to within REMOVED_DATE cm of\u000athe inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm of the medial, and REMOVED_DATE cm of the lateral margins. The\u000aremaining parenchyma is yellow lobulated fatty tissue. Representative sections\u000aare submitted sequentially from medial (slice one) to lateral (slice twelve).\u000aAlso received in the same container are three fibrofatty tissues (3.5 x REMOVED_DATE x\u000a1.5 cm in aggregate) which are inked black.\u000aMicro 1: medialmost margin, 3 frags, RSS\u000aMicro 2: slice 2, cavity subjacent to skin, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 3: slice 3, cavity to superior posterior margin, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  slice 4, to include cavity to superior inferior margin in 4, and\u000afibrous tissue to posterior margin in #5, 1 frag each, RSS\u000aMicro 6: slice 5, cavity to superior inferior margin, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  entire slice 6 bisected, 1 frag each, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  lateralmost margin, slice 12, 4 frags, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  additional tissue, 10 frags, ESS\u000alm\u000aReports to: CHRISTIAN, ROGER, L. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
