D_DATE  anterior biopsy cavity: 2 frags, RSS\u000aMicro 16, upper inner quadrant: 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 17, lower inner quadrant: 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 18, lower outer quadrant: 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 19, upper outer quadrant: 1 frag, RSS\u000aPart 2 is labeled "#2 left axillary lymph nodes" and consists of two fragments\u000aof fibro-adipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE cm and REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest dimension, REMOVED_DATE \u000ax REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate. Six potential lymph nodes, ranging in size from\u000a0.5 cm to REMOVED_DATE cm, are identified within the adipose tissue.\u000aMicro 20, three potential lymph nodes: 3 frags, ESS\u000aMicro 21, one potential lymph node: 2 frags, ESS\u000aMicro 22, one potential lymph node: 1 frag, ESS\u000aMicro 23, one potential lymph node: 2 frags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  remainder of adipose tissue: multi frags, ESS\u000amcc/\u000aReports to: CHRISTIAN, ROGER, L. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY W/REGIONAL LYMPH NODES\u000a[report_end]
