VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aWEINSTEIN, MICHAEL, H., M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by WEINSTEIN,MICHAEL H.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aRIGHT BREAST WIRE LOCALIZATION BIOPSY FOR CALCIFICATIONS AND A CLIP:\u000aAtypical apocrine adenosis.\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia.\u000aNo in situ or invasive carcinoma is identified.\u000aThe inked surgical margins of resection were examined microscopically.\u000aOTHER FINDINGS:\u000aCysts.\u000aApocrine metaplasia.\u000aPrior core biopsy site changes are noted in the region containing\u000aa clip.\u000aMicrocalcifications are identified in association with benign epithelium\u000aand atypical apocrine adenosis.\u000aNOTE: Dr. Susan Lester has reviewed selected slides from this case and concurs\u000awith the diagnosis.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 46-year-old premenopausal female, not on hormones, with a positive\u000afamily of breast cancer. REMOVED_DATE  mammogram demonstrates right\u000abreast calcifications. REMOVED_DATE  core biopsy revealed atypical apocrine\u000aadenosis for which excision is recommended.\u000aOperation: Right breast wire localization biopsy.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast calcifications.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Right breast biopsy .\u000aRadiology report: calcium and clip are in specimen (J.M.).\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by LOMO,LESLEY C.,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in one part, labeled with the patient's name,\u000aunit number, and "#1, right breast biopsy", consists of a single fragment of\u000afibroadipose tissue (5.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with a localization wire. The\u000aspecimen has been previously inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of\u000amargins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green;\u000alateral = yellow; medial = orange. An accompanying radiograph shows a\u000alocalization wire in place and a clip in the specimen near an area of clustered\u000amicrocalcifications. The specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral\u000arevealing white fibrous tissue with cysts up to REMOVED_DATE cm, with organizing,\u000ahemorrhagic areas; there also appears to be skeletal muscle present. No\u000adefinite mass or lesions are identified. The specimen is radiographed. The\u000asections containing the clip and the microcalcifications are submitted\u000aentirely. Representative sections of the margins are also submitted;\u000aapproximately 75% of the specimen is submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  breast tissue with microcalcifications, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  breast tissue at site of clip, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  breast tissue immediately lateral to section with clip, 1 frag,\u000aRSS.\u000aMicro 15: medial perpendicular margins, 3 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 16: lateral perpendicular margins, 3 frags, RSS.\u000alcl\u000aReports to: KAELIN, CAROLYN, MARY M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
