VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: MEHRA GOLSHAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: David C. Park, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Alessandra F Nascimento, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZATION FOR CALCIFICATIONS AND CLIP:\u000aBreast tissue with core biopsy site changes and calcifications in benign\u000abreast epithelium.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the\u000aspecimen, including margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 46 year old female with extensive family history of breast cancer.\u000aLeft breast core biopsy reveals atypical hyperplasia.\u000aOperation: Left breast wire-localized excisional biopsy.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast atypical hyperplasia.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) Left breast mass; ? short stitch - superior; long stitch - lateral.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Clip and faint calcs in specimen (ILLEGIBLE signature with Lisa\u000aFrost.)\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "#1. Left breast mass", and consists of a disrupted REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aexcision of fibroadipose tissue, oriented by sutures designating superior\u000a(short suture) and lateral (long suture) margins. A localizing wire enters\u000aanteriorly. The posterior one-third of the specimen is entirely detached from\u000athe remainder of the specimen, and is only loosely attached by the length of\u000athe localizing wire. Tissue is partially reconstructed and likely margins are\u000ainked. Please note: True surgical margins cannot be definitively determined\u000adue to the disrupted nature of the specimen. The specimen is inked per\u000apathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black;\u000aanterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange\u000a(inked by prosector). Specimen is received with a radiograph demonstrating the\u000alocalizing wire in place adjacent to an encircled area of faint calcifications\u000amarked by a metallic surgical clip in the anterolateral portion of the\u000aspecimen. Sectioning in this area demonstrates a REMOVED_DATE cm cavity filled with\u000atan/brown amorphous material, containing the surgical clip. This cavity abuts\u000athe inferior margin, and is REMOVED_DATE cm from the closest anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom the closest superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the closest lateral margin, REMOVED_DATE \u000acm from the closest medial margin, and is remote (greater than REMOVED_DATE cm) from the\u000aposterior margin. Remaining specimen is comprised of 40% tan/white\u000aunremarkable-appearing fibrous tissue, admixed with soft, lobulated tan/yellow\u000aadipose tissue. There are no additional masses, lesions or other abnormalities\u000agrossly. Entire specimen is submitted, sequentially from anterior to\u000aposterior, with perpendicular anterior margin in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, and perpendicular\u000aposterior margin in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. Area of interest in micro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: entire specimen submitted sequentially, multiple frags, ESS.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Alessandra F Nascimento M.D., Electronically signed on\u000a9/10/2007\u000a[report_end]
