sts of a golden yellow to\u000afocally brown, ovoid, breast excision specimen (3.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) which is\u000areceived unoriented. The specimen is accompanied by a radiograph which\u000ademonstrates a surgical clip present within the specimen. The specimen is\u000aentirely inked in blue and sectioned to reveal a yellow to white, heterogenous\u000acut surface with no gross masses. A surgical clip is identified. The entire\u000aspecimen is serially submitted for microscopic examination.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  left breast tissue with clip in block 6, 9 frags, ESS.\u000arlr\u000aReports to: OSTEEN, ROBERT, T. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
