ived fresh, in two parts, each labeled with the patient?s\u000aname, unit number.\u000aSpecimen A, labeled "left needle directed breast biopsy", consists of an\u000aunoriented excision of breast tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm with an\u000aembedded localization wire. An accompanying radiograph demonstrates\u000acalcifications and a wire within the specimen. The margins are inked blue and\u000athe specimen is serially sectioned to reveal an ill-defined area of fibrous\u000atissue comprising approximately 60% of the specimen and extending to the inked\u000aresection margin, to which the wire was localized.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 2 frags each, ESS\u000aSpecimen B, labeled "left breast tissue", consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aexcision of breast tissue, inked blue and serially sectioned revealing an\u000aill-defined area of gray/red fibrous tissue comprising 90% of the specimen and\u000aextending to the inked margin.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 3 frags each, ESS\u000aViv/jl\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aMicroscopic/Diagnostic Dictation by Vijay K Vanguri M.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Review by Jonathan N Glickman M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jason L Hornick M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a12/10/2004\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for DCIS (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) (see note):\u000aEstrogen receptor - NEGATIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor - NEGATIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) - NEGATIVE (1+)\u000aNOTE: Invasive focus is no longer present on levels.\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000acarcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but\u000aonly a portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity\u000ain >10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aAddendum by Andrea L Richardson M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aAddendum #1 by Andrea L Richardson M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a12/14/2004\u000a[report_end]
