VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aKRANE, JEFFREY, FRED, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by KRANE,JEFFREY FRED,M.D.,PH.D.\u000a#1. RIGHT BREAST, WIRE DIRECTED EXCISIONAL BIOPSY FOR TWO CLIPS AND AN\u000aIRREGULAR MASS:\u000aBreast tissue with extensive biopsy site changes and hyalinized scar.\u000aSkeletal muscle with adjacent fibrosis.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000a#2. SPECIMEN LABELED "KERATOSIS OF RIGHT ABDOMEN":\u000aSeborrheic keratosis.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: R breast mass.\u000aOperation: Right breast bx. Exc of abdominal skin lesion.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast mass, abdominal skin lesion.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Right breast tissue with wires (to mammo).\u000a2. Keratosis of right abdomen.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by HAHN,HEJIN P.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart one, "#1 right breast tissue with wire", consists of a piece of breast\u000atissue (6.0 cm from medial to lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm from superior to inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom anterior to posterior) with two wires. The specimen has been inked per\u000athe surgeon per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior =\u000ablack; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow;\u000amedial = orange. The specimen is accompanied by a radiograph which\u000ademonstrates two clips and two hook wires. The specimen is serially sectioned\u000aand radiographed. Only one definitive clip is identified on the radiograph. A\u000asecond area of old hemorrhage is identified lateral to this clip which may\u000arepresent the second core biopsy site. The specimen is 20% firm white fibrous\u000atissue. No lesions are grossly identified. Representative sections are\u000asubmitted. Approximately 95% of the entire specimen is submitted. All fibrous\u000atissue is submitted.\u000aMicro 1&2: medial margin, perpendicular, 6 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 3&4: breast tissue, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 5&6: section with clip, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  serial section, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 17&18: possible second core biopsy site, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 19&20: lateral margin, perpendicular, 4 frags, RSS.\u000aPart two, "#2 keratosis of right abdomen", consists of a tan/white skin ellipse\u000a(1.1 x REMOVED_DATE cm, excised to a depth of REMOVED_DATE cm). There is an exophytic,\u000airregular, papillary nodule (0.8 x REMOVED_DATE x 05 cm) that is tan/white and abutting\u000athe side margin. The deep margin is inked black and the specimen is entirely\u000asubmitted.\u000aMicro 21: ellipse tips, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 22: body, 3 frags, ESS.\u000ahph\u000aReports to: LESNIKOSKI, BETH-ANN M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SKIN- OTHER THAN CYST, TAG OR DEBRIDEMENT\u000a[report_end]
