VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID LYMPH NODE BIOPSY\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aNASCIMENTO, ALESSANDRA, F., M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by NASCIMENTO,ALESSANDRA F.,M.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST, EXCISION WIRE-LOCALIZATION FOR A MASS AND A CLIP, AND LEFT\u000aAXILLARY LYMPH NODE BIOPSY (specimens #1 and #2 of 2 specimens):\u000aINVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA\u000aMETASTATIC CARCINOMA TO LYMPH NODE\u000aSYNOPSIS:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA\u000aSize - REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aMultifocal - no\u000aHistologic Type - ductal\u000aHistologic Grade (SBR) - II (moderate)\u000aNuclear Grade - intermediate\u000aEIC - negative\u000aLymphovascular invasion - absent\u000aDermal lymphatic invasion - N/A\u000aSkin invasion - N/A\u000aSkeletal muscle invasion - N/A\u000aFinal Margins (invasive) -\u000aNegative (>0.3 cm) - posterior, lateral, medial, superior,\u000aanterior, inferior\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU - absent\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - absent\u000aLYMPH NODES\u000aAxillary Lymph Nodes - positive\u000aNumber of positive nodes - 1\u000aNumber of nodes examined - 1\u000aTOTAL POSITIVE NODES (all specimens)- 1:1\u000aSize of largest metastatic focus - REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aExtranodal extension - present (one focus - REMOVED_DATE cm)\u000aOTHER FINDINGS\u000aCore biopsy site\u000aAJCC CLASSIFICATION (6th Edition) - REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDb pREMOVED_ACCESSION_IDa MX\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER/PR/HER-2) - pending\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: by RICHARDSON,ANDREA L.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for invasive carcinoma (block 11):\u000aEstrogen receptor - POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor - POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) - NEGATIVE (0)\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000acarcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but\u000aonly a portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity\u000ain >10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 58 year old female with L upper/inner quadrant mammorgraphic mass, S/P\u000anon-diagnostic core biopsy. FNA of L axillary lymph node, suspicious for\u000aadenocarcinoma.\u000aOperation: L breast wire localization excision, axillary lymph node biopsy.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: L breast cancer.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1 - left axillary lymph node (permanent).\u000a#2 - left breast tissue, short/superior, long/lateral, whip stitch/chest wall\u000a(to mammo).\u000aRadiograph report: Clip in specimen. Kemi Babagbemi, M.D.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by GIBSON,JOANNA A,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart one, labeled "left axillary lymph node", consists of a single tan/red/pink\u000alobulated lymph node (3.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The entire specimen is submitted.\u000aMicro #1-8: Left axillary lymph node, 8 frags, ESS.\u000aPart two, labeled "left breast tissue", consists of an oriented, wire-localized\u000abreast excision specimen (7.5 cm from superior to inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm from medial\u000ato lateral, and REMOVED_DATE cm anterior to posterior). The specimen is received with\u000athree orienting sutures: short - superior, long - lateral, whip stitch - chest\u000awall. However, the long suture is in fact present on the posterior wall, and\u000athe surgeon, Dr. Esther Rhei, was notified to follow the inks rather than the\u000asutures. The specimen is inked per the pathology protocol for the evaluation\u000aof margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green;\u000alateral/yellow; medial/orange. The specimen is accompanied by a radiograph,\u000awhich shows a clip, a hookwire within the specimen and a stellate mass.\u000aSectioning reveals an ill-defined, white, firm mass (1.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm),\u000awhich is located REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE \u000acm from superior margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin. Immediately\u000aadjacent and superior to the mass is a hemorrhagic biopsy cavity (1.8 x REMOVED_DATE cx\u000a1.1 cm), which is located REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000ainferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from superior margin,\u000a2.0 cm from the posterior, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin. The entire mass\u000aand representative sections of the biopsy cavity in relation to each margin are\u000asubmitted. The remainder of the breast parenchyma is unremarkable yellow\u000alobulated adipose tissue.\u000aMicro #9+10: Mass in relation to posterior and lateral margins, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro #11+12: Mass in relation to inferior and anterior margins, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro #13: Mass in relation to biopsy cavity and anterior margin, 1 frag,\u000aESS.\u000aMicro #14+15: Closest uninvolved medial and superior margins, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro #16+17: Biopsy cavity in relation to anterior and inferior margins, 2\u000afrags, RSS.\u000aMicro #18+19: Biopsy cavity in relation to lateral margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro #20: Closest superior, medial, and posterior margins in relation to\u000abiopsy cavity, 2 frags, ESS.\u000ajgi/\u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: LYMPH NODE BIOPSY\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
