VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST BIOPSY W/O MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aKRANE, JEFFREY, FRED, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by KRANE,JEFFREY FRED,M.D.,PH.D.\u000a#1. LEFT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION OF A MASS WITH CALCIFICATION:\u000aCalcifications are identified in association with a hyalinized\u000afibroadenoma (0.25 cm; block 4) adjacent to previous biopsy site.\u000aPrevious biopsy site with repair reaction.\u000aMicrocalcifications are also present in association with benign\u000aepithelium.\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy.\u000a#2. LEFT BREAST, SUPERIOR SHAVE MARGIN:\u000aBenign breast tissue.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 73-year-old female status post REMOVED_DATE right mastectomy for treatment\u000aof recurrent breast cancer. Status post REMOVED_DATE  core biopsy for\u000acalcifications with pathology demonstrating normal breast tissue\u000awith calcifications in the specimen.\u000aOperation: Left breast wire localization biopsy.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal left breast mammogram.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Left breast tissue - stitches short/superior, long/\u000alateral, whipstitch/chest wall margin.\u000a2. Superior shave margin - whipstitch on new margin.\u000aMammogram: Mass in specimen......J. Meyer.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by HENDERSON,JOEL M.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart one, labeled "#1, left breast tissue", consists of a single fragment of\u000atan-yellow fibroadipose tissue (5.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). There is a localization\u000awire in place, and there is a long stitch placed by the surgeon to designate\u000alateral and a short stitch to designate superior. The specimen is inked per\u000apathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior\u000a= blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange.\u000aThe specimen is accompanied by a specimen radiograph, which demonstrates an\u000aarea of increased fibrosity with focal small calcifications, that is indicated\u000aby the localization wire. Separately located in the cut specimen is an area of\u000adense fibrous tissue with focal hemorrhage (1.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) that\u000acorresponds to the location marked by the localization wire. Also at the\u000aposterior and inferior aspect of the specimen is an area of dense fibrous\u000atissue (1.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) that is not marked. The remainder of the specimen\u000aconsists of 80% yellow adipose tissue and 20% tan-gray fibrous tissue. The\u000aspecimen is sectioned from approximately inferior to superior, and entirely\u000asubmitted.\u000aMicro 1: most inferior slice, sectioned perpendicularly, 6 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  slices from inferior to superior (mass marked by localization\u000awire in cassettes 4 and 5), each slice bisected, 18 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 11: most superior slice, sectioned perpendicularly, 6 frags, ESS.\u000aPart two, labeled "#2, superior shave margin, whipstitch on new margin",\u000aconsists of a single flat fragment of fibroadipose tissue (8.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm).\u000aThe whipstitch has been placed on one of the flat surfaces by the surgeon to\u000adesignate the new margin, which is inked black. The opposite side is inked\u000ablue. The specimen consists of approximately 90% yellow adipose tissue and 10%\u000agray fibrous tissue. No suspicious lesions are identified. The specimen is\u000asectioned perpendicular to the new margin and entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  superior shave margin, 17 frags, ESS.\u000ajmh\u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST BIOPSY W/O MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN\u000a[report_end]
