 breast tissue cores (2.1 x REMOVED_DATE x\u000a0.3 cm in aggregate). The specimen is received in a blue cassette and is\u000asubmitted in toto.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Multi frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, "left breast #2 1 o'clock", consists of multiple irregular tan/yellow\u000ato white lobulated portions of fibroadipose breast tissue cores (2.2 x REMOVED_DATE x\u000a0.3 cm in aggregate). The specimen is received in a white cassette and is\u000asubmitted in toto.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Multi frags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000asek/ag\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Deborah A Dillon M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
