00awith the specimen demonstrating two masses both with calcifications, and a\u000alocalization wire within the specimen.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #1, perpendicular sections, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #2, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #3, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #4 with nodule, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #5, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #6, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #7 with nodule, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #8 with radiographically evident calcifications, perpendicular\u000asections, multi frags, ESS.\u000aJUB/lp\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Michael W Bennett M.B., B.C.H., Electronically signed on\u000a1/30/2007\u000a[report_end]
