The specimen is received with a radiograph\u000ademonstrating a hook wire in place with an ill-defined mass within what appears\u000ato be the superior/central portion of the specimen. Please note: The hook\u000awire is received pathology free-floating in the specimen container. Area of\u000ainterest is approximated by the radiograph. Sectioning demonstrates relatively\u000aunremarkable-appearing cut surfaces comprised predominantly of tan/yellow\u000aadipose tissue (at least 70%), with occasional scattered unremarkable tan/white\u000afibrous tissue (approximately REMOVED_DATE %). Tissue in the area of interest is\u000alikewise unremarkable, with a superior/medial REMOVED_DATE cm area of unremarkable\u000afibrous tissue in addition to a superior/lateral cauterized REMOVED_DATE cm defect\u000a(tissue clips versus prior cavity). There are no masses grossly. The entire\u000aspecimen is submitted, sequentially from superior to inferior, with likely area\u000aof interest in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, cauterized possible cysts (versus tissue cleft) in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID,\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Entire specimen, sequentially from superior to inferior\u000a(perpendicular superior margin in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, perpendicular inferior margin in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID,\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), multi frags, ESS.\u000aPlease note: The specimen will be held for further fixation prior to\u000aprocessing.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000adb/ag\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Robert D Odze M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
