ral to thig; aspirate\u000asent to cytology).\u000aOperation: 14 U/S breast core biopsy\u000aClinical Diagnosis: R/O fibroadenoma\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Left breast core specimens (1 brown cassette)\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by O'CONNELL,JEROME T., JR., M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit\u000anumber, and "left breast", in a brown cassette, and consists of multiple, soft,\u000afragmented, yellow to white tissue cores (1.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate).\u000aMicro 1: Multi frags, ESS.\u000artv\u000aReports to: PARKER, LEROY, MONROE M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY(IES)\u000a[report_end]
