VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aFOLKERTH, REBECCA, DUNN, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by FOLKERTH,REBECCA DUNN,M.D.\u000a1) SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "LEFT BREAST, TISSUE":\u000aINVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA, REMOVED_DATE cm, poorly differentiated (modified\u000aBloom-Richardson grade III/III), REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin and\u000a>2 cm from the remaining resection margins.\u000aNo lymphatic/vascular invasion.\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN-SITU, solid type, high nuclear grade, REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000athe medial margin. DCIS is present in REMOVED_DATE blocks.\u000aAdenosis and extensive fibrosis.\u000a2) SPECIMEN LABELED "HOT, NODE":\u000aOne (1) lymph node with no tumor present (levels examined).\u000a3) SPECIMEN LABELED "AXILLARY CONTENTS":\u000aSix (6) lymph nodes with no tumor present.\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for invasive carcinoma (block 3):\u000aEstrogen receptor NEGATIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor NEGATIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) NEGATIVE (1+)\u000aNote: Normal epithelial cells are appropriately immunoreactive for hormone\u000areceptors.\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000ainvasive carcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but\u000aonly a portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity\u000ain >10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 33-year-old with history of right breast cancer in 1993. History\u000aof cervical dysplasia. History of hypoglycemia.\u000aOperation: Sentinel node biopsy.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Left breast tissue.\u000a2. Hot node.\u000a3. Axillary contents.\u000aO. R. CONSULTATION REPORT:\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "LEFT BREAST TISSUE":\u000aNodule (1.2 cm) suspicious for carcinoma, REMOVED_DATE cm from posterior\u000amargin (gross only).\u000aSpecimen reviewed with Dr. Christian.\u000aRad: masses in specimen.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by NASCIMENTO,ALESSANDRA F.,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in three parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart one, unlabeled, consists of a single fragment of yellow/tan fibroadipose\u000atissue, measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm with two orienting sutures designated\u000ashort = superior and long = lateral. The specimen is received inked.\u000aThe specimen is inked for the evaluation of margins: posterior = black;\u000aanterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial =\u000aorange. Sections of margins are submitted for microscopic examination.\u000aAttached to the specimen, there is a skin ellipse measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. On\u000aserial sectioning, there is a lobulated mass measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm and REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aaway from the posterior margin. The mass is white/tan and firm.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  medial margin, 3 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  sections of suspicious nodules with margins, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 16: lateral margin, 3 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  additional breast tissue, 3 frags, RSS.\u000aPart two, labeled "Hot node", consists of a single fragment of tan/yellow\u000afibroadipose tissue, measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000aMicro 19: hot node, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aPart three, labeled "Axillary contents", consists of a single fragment of\u000atan/yellow fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. Six lymph nodes\u000aare identified within the specimen.\u000aMicro 21: 1 lymph node, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 21: 3 lymph nodes, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 22: 1 lymph node, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMIcro 23: 1 lymph node, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  fibroadipose tissue, multi frags, RSS.\u000aReports to: CHRISTIAN, ROGER, L. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: LYMPH NODE BIOPSY\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: LYMPH NODES REGIONAL RESECTION\u000a[report_end]
