VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Leona A. Doyle, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Jane E. Brock, M.B., B.S., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aLEFT BREAST EXCISION FOR A REMOVED_DATE CM MASS:\u000aDense fibrous breast tissue with pseudoangiomatous stromal hyperplasia (see\u000aNOTE).\u000aFocal fibroadenomatoid change.\u000aFocal epithelial hyperplasia.\u000aA prior core biopsy/procedure site is present with hemosiderin deposition and\u000anodular fibrosis seen (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aThe margins were inked and evaluated for the final diagnosis.\u000aNOTE: Per clinical notes, the patient presented with a mass in 2005 which was\u000abiopsied and found to be a fibroadenoma (slides recently reviewed, see\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID). The patient then received cryoablation therapy for the\u000afibroadenoma in 2007. Subsequently a palpable mass at the same site developed\u000awhich on recent ultrasound was noted to measure REMOVED_DATE cm x REMOVED_DATE cm x REMOVED_DATE cm and\u000ahave irregular margins.\u000aThe entire specimen received has been submitted for histological evaluation.\u000aThere is a biopsy site/procedure site with nodular fibrosis present which\u000alikely represents the site of previous fibroadenoma ablation. The remaining\u000abreast tissue is dense with pseudoangiomatous stromal hyperplasia present. The\u000adense breast tissue with PASH appears to be the histological correlate of the\u000apalpable mass and ultrasound findings. Dr. D. Dillon has also reviewed selected\u000aslides from the case and agrees with the diagnosis. Clinical and radiological\u000acorrelation is recommended.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 17-year-old woman with history of fibroadenomas in L breast with U/S\u000a7/1/08 revealing 4-cm palpable, hypoechoic mass at 1:00 - Excision was\u000arecommended.\u000aOperation: Exc of l breast mass.\u000aOperative Findings: None specified.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: None specified.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) Left breast mass; short - superior, long - lateral; whip stitch on chest\u000awall margin.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "Left breast mass, short superior, long lateral, whip stitch chest wall\u000amargin", and consists of an irregular tan/yellow lobulated portion of\u000afibroadipose breast tissue (6.0 cm medial to lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm superior to\u000ainferior, and REMOVED_DATE cm anterior to posterior) with a short suture designating\u000asuperior margin, and long suture designating lateral margin, and a whip stitch\u000adesignating the posterior margin. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol\u000a(superior red, inferior green, medial orange, lateral yellow, anterior blue,\u000aand posterior black) and is serially sectioned from medial to lateral to reveal\u000auniform well circumscribed dense white firm fibrous tissue with a small amount\u000aof attached adipose tissue. No discrete lesion is identified grossly. No areas\u000aof frank necrosis or hemorrhage is grossly identified. The entire specimen is\u000asubmitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin perpendicularly sectioned, 3 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Superior margin, 2 frags each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Inferior margin, 2 frags each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Anterior margin, 2 frags each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Posterior margin, 2 frags each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin perpendicularly sectioned, 3 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Remaining breast parenchyma, multi frags, ESS\u000aSEK/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jane E. Brock M.B., B.S., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a9/7/2008\u000a[report_end]
