VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ROGER L CHRISTIAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Javad Beheshti, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Alessandra F Nascimento, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZATION FOR CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aExtensive calcifications present in association with benign epithelium\u000aand stroma.\u000aFocus of scarring consistent with prior biopsy site.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the\u000aspecimen, including margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Microcalcs, lt brst.\u000aOperation: Wire directed excision.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Microcalcs, lt brst.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Tissue left breast, long lateral, short superior.\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000aSpecimen radiograph demonstrates Ca++ intact wire. D/w Dr. Christian @ 4:10 p.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number\u000aand "tissue, left breast", consists of a REMOVED_DATE gram portion of oriented\u000afibrofatty tissue that measures REMOVED_DATE cm from superior to inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000amedial to lateral and REMOVED_DATE cm from anterior to posterior dimension. The\u000aspecimen is received with orientation as follows: Short superior, long\u000alateral. The specimen is received with a needle-localization wire and\u000aaccompanying mammogram. The needle-localization wire enters the specimen at\u000athe superior portion of the specimen and exits through the inferior portion of\u000athe specimen. The accompanying radiograph displays focal areas of white\u000apunctate dots located near where the needle enters the specimen, the superior\u000aaspect of the specimen. The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal no\u000adiscrete mass, lesion or nodule present. Approximate specimen composition is\u000a55 to 60% diffuse white fibrous tissue with remainder unremarkable yellow\u000aadipose tissue. The specimen is submitted entirely sequentially from the\u000asuperior to the inferior aspect.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: The superior margin of resection which includes the area of\u000apunctate dots, the micro calcifications with 3 frags each, perpendicular\u000asections, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: All one full-thickness\u000asectioned divided into two pieces, 1 frag per cassette each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID through REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Inferior margins, perpendicularly taken with REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 2\u000afrags, ESS, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 3 frags, ESS, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 2 frags, ESS, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aPF/ajb\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Alessandra F Nascimento M.D., Electronically signed on\u000a2/14/2008\u000a[report_end]
