VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID LYMPH NODE BIOPSY\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aNASCIMENTO, ALESSANDRA, F., M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by NASCIMENTO,ALESSANDRA F.,M.D.\u000aRIGHT BREAST EXCISION, WIRE LOCALIZATION FOR A MASS AND A CLIP (SPECIMEN #3 OF\u000a3), SENTINEL NODE BIOPSY (SPECIMEN #1 OF 3) AND AXILLARY NODE DISSECTION\u000a(SPECIMEN #2 OF 3):\u000aINVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA,\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU,\u000aAND NEGATIVE LYMPH NODES.\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA\u000aSize - REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aMultifocal - no\u000aHistologic Type - ductal\u000aHistologic Grade (SBR) - II (moderate)\u000aNuclear Grade - intermediate\u000aEIC - negative\u000aLymphovascular invasion - absent\u000aDermal lymphatic invasion - N/A\u000aSkin invasion - N/A\u000aSkeletal muscle invasion - N/A\u000aFinal Margins (invasive)\u000aNegative (>0.3 cm) - superior, anterior, posterior, medial,\u000alateral\u000aVery close (<0.1 cm from margin) - inferior (0.1 cm, block #8, focal)\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU - present\u000aTypes - solid, cribriform\u000aNuclear grade - intermediate\u000aCalcifications in DCIS - absent\u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - absent\u000aExtent of DCIS -\u000aNumber of blocks/total - REMOVED_DATE blocks\u000aFinal Margins (DCIS)\u000aNegative (>0.3 cm) - medial, anterior, poserior, superior, inferior\u000aVery close (<0.1 cm) - lateral (block #11)\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - absent\u000aLYMPH NODES\u000aSentinel lymph nodes (3 H&E levels examined) - negative\u000aNumber of positive nodes - 0\u000aNumber of nodes examined - 2\u000aAxillary lymph nodes - negative\u000aNumber of positive nodes - 0\u000aNumber of nodes examined - 2\u000aTOTAL POSITIVE NODES (all specimens) - REMOVED_DATE \u000aOTHER FINDINGS: Core biopsy site, calcifications in benign epithelium.\u000aAJCC CLASSIFICATION (6th Edition) - REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDb pNO MX\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER/PR/HER-2) - Performed previously\u000aNOTE 1: Specimen #1 includes examination of frozen section remnants (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aNOTE 2: Selected slides of this case were reviewed by Dr. A. Richardson, breast\u000apathology service, who concurs.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: R breast cancer spiculated amss on mammo.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1 - sentinel node R breast --> FS.\u000a#2 - non-sentinel node R breast.\u000a#3 - R breast tissue --> mammo.\u000aRadiology report: Mass and marker in specimen. Dr. D. Smith.\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "#1 - SENTINEL NODE R BREAST" (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aTwo (2) lymph nodes, negative for tumor.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by GIBSON,JOANNA A,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aReceived in three parts.\u000aPart one, received fresh in the frozen section lab, labeled with the patient's\u000aname, unit number, and "#1 - sentinel node R breast", consists of two fragments\u000aof fatty tissue (3.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). Located within\u000aone fragment of tissue, a single lymph node (0.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) is identified\u000aand entirely frozen as REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. An additional lymph node candidate (2.6 x REMOVED_DATE x\u000a0.8 cm) is identified, bisected and entirely submitted as REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aMicro #1: "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" residue, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro #2: "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" residue, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro #3: "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" residue, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aPart two, received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "#2\u000a- non-sentinel node R breast", consists of two fragments of yellow/tan\u000alobulated fat (2.3 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). Three tan/pink\u000arubbery lymph nodes (ranging from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm up to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm)\u000aare identified.\u000aMicro #4: Single whole lymph node, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro #5: Single bisected lymph node, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro #6: Single bisected lymph node, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aPart three, labeled "#3 - R breast tissue", consists of a portion of fibrofatty\u000abreast tissue (6.1 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with an accompanying radiograph and a needle\u000alocalization wire. The specimen is inked per the surgeon according to the\u000apathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black;\u000aanterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange.\u000aThe specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral, revealing a\u000atan/white, firm, ill-defined mass (0.9 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which grossly comes to\u000awithin less than REMOVED_DATE cm of the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the anterior margin,\u000a1.0 cm of the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the lateral margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the\u000asuperior margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm of the medial margin. The remaining breast tissue\u000aconsists predominantly of yellow/tan lobulated fat with scant tan/white fibrous\u000astroma.\u000aMicro #7-11: Mass in relationship to inferior, posterior, anterior, and\u000alateral margins, 5 frags total, ESS (include clip).\u000aMicro #12+13: Nearest superior margin, 2 frags total, RSS.\u000aMicro #14+15: Nearest medial margin, 2 frags total, RSS.\u000adfi/\u000aReports to: LESNIKOSKI, BETH-ANN M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: LYMPH NODE BIOPSY\u000a[report_end]
