imen is entirely submitted in cassettes I and J. Received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "left breast anterior additional tissue", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm portion of breast tissue, with a stitch at the deep margin, which is inked black. Revealing unremarkable breast tissue. The entire specimen is submitted in cassettes K and L. Received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "left breast medial tissue", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm portion of breast tissue, with a stitch at the deep margin which is inked black. The specimen is serially sectioned, revealing unremarkable breast tissue, and submitted entirely in cassettes M and N. Received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "left breast inferior final shave", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm portion of breast tissue, with a stitch at the deep end which is inked black. The specimen is serially sectioned, revealing unremarkable breast tissue, and submitted in cassettes O and P. Received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "final shaved left breast superior", are two yellow-tan portions of breast tissue, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. These are not oriented. The specimens are serially sectioned, and the larger is submitted in cassette Q, the smaller in cassette R. Received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "left breast final deep shave", are two, unoriented, yellow-tan portions of breast, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. Both are serially sectioned and the larger is submitted in cassette S, and the smaller in cassette T. Resident: PAUL N. STAATS, MD =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT - REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID 