VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Consult material\u000aProcedure Date:\u000aOrdering Provider: TAD J WIECZOREK M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-10-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Mamta Gupta, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Amy Ly, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aCONSULT SLIDES FROM FAULKNER HOSPITAL, BOSTON, MA:\u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION AND ANTERIOR-MEDIAL MARGIN, EXCISION\u000a(REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, PARTS A & B; REMOVED_DATE ):\u000aSeverely atypical ductal hyperplasia bordering on low grade DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN\u000aSITU, focally associated with microcalcifications (see Note #1).\u000aIn the main wire-localized excision specimen (part A), severe ADH is present\u000a<0.1 cm from the inferior margin (slide REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), and REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral\u000amargin (slide REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aIn the separately submitted anterior-medial margin, severe ADH is present REMOVED_DATE \u000acm from the black-inked margin (see Note #2).\u000aFocal ATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA is present (see Note #3).\u000aAdditional findings:\u000aIntraductal papilloma, REMOVED_DATE cm in size (slide REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aBiopsy site changes are present in the wire-localized excision specimen.\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia and columnar cell change.\u000aApocrine cysts and microcysts.\u000aBenign breast tissue with calcifications.\u000aNOTE #1: Scattered foci of severe ADH bordering on DCIS are present on multiple\u000aslides in both the main excision specimen and the anterior-medial margin\u000aexcision. These features are best seen on slide REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, where cytoarchitectural\u000afeatures of low grade DCIS are present, but the focus measures REMOVED_DATE cm and does\u000anot meet the size criterion (0.3 cm) for this diagnosis. REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID immunostains\u000aperformed at an outside institution on slides REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID (reviewed at BWH)\u000ahighlight myoepithelial cells associated with severe ADH.\u000aNOTE #2: By report, the anterior-medial margin specimen was received with one\u000asurface inked black. The specimen was not further oriented.\u000aNOTE #3: E-cadherin immunostain performed at an outside institution on slide REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000a(reviewed at BWH) showed absence of staining in lesional cells, supporting the\u000aabove diagnosis of ALH.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Left breast atypia\u000aClinical Diagnosis: ?DCIS or severe ADH\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aConsult slides.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aReceived from Faulkner Hospital, Pathology Department, 1153 Centre Street,\u000aBoston, MA REMOVED_CASE_ID, are nineteen (19) glass slides.\u000aThe slides are labeled ?REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" and sublabeled "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" through "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID", "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID",\u000a"REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" through "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID", "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" through "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID", "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID RC REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" through "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID RC REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID", "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID",\u000a"REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID E-CADHERIN" and "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" through "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID", corresponding to A) left breast wire\u000aguided excision (3.3 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) B) left breast, anterior-medial margin,\u000aexcision (4.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) performed on REMOVED_DATE  according to the\u000aaccompanying pathology report bearing the patient's name.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Amy Ly M.D., Electronically signed on Thursday February\u000a04, 2010 at 03:31:54PM\u000a[report_end]
