VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID SENTINEL LYMPH NODE\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aBRODSKY, GILBERT, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by BRODSKY,GILBERT,M.D.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, SIMPLE MASTECTOMY (specimen #3 of 6 specimens) AND SENTINEL NODE\u000aBIOPSIES (specimens #1 and #2 of 6 specimens):\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aNEGATIVE LYMPH NODE(S)\u000aSYNOPSIS:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA - none present\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aTypes - micropapillary, clinging\u000aNuclear grade - low\u000aCalcifications in DCIS - present\u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - present\u000aMicroinvasion (<0.1cm) - absent\u000aExtent of DCIS\u000aNumber of blocks:total - 7:15 blocks\u000aFinal Margins (DCIS)\u000aClose (0.1-0.3 cm) - deep (block #7)\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - present\u000aLYMPH NODES\u000aSentinel Lymph Nodes - negative (3 H&E levels examined)\u000aNumber of positive nodes - 0\u000aNumber of nodes examined - 2\u000aTOTAL POSITIVE NODES (all specimens)- 0:2\u000aOTHER FINDINGS\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia with pagetoid spread\u000aCore biopsy site\u000aFibroadenomas\u000aCalcifications in benign epithelium\u000aAJCC CLASSIFICATION (6th edition) - Tis pREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID MX\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER/PR/HER-2) - pending\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "LOWER BREAST, BIOPSY" (specimen #4 of 6 specimens):\u000aSkin with scar.\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "MIDDLE BREAST, BIOPSY" (specimen #5 of 6 specimens):\u000aSkin with scar.\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "UPPER BREAST, BIOPSY" (specimen #6 of 6 specimens):\u000aSkin with scar.\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for DCIS (block 15):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) NEGATIVE (1+)\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000acarcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but\u000aonly a portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity\u000ain >10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 48 year old female s/p core biopsy of right breast mammographic\u000acalcifications revealing DCIS at one site, LCIS at another site.\u000aOperation: Right simple mastectomy, sentinel node biopsy and lat\u000aflap/implant reconstruction\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast cancer\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1) Right axillary sentinel node - hot and blue\u000a#2) Right axillary sentinel node - hot and blue\u000a#3) Right breast - short stitch superior; long stitch lateral\u000a#4) Lower breast biopsy\u000a#5) Middle breast biopsy\u000a#6) Upper breast biopsy\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "#1. RIGHT AXILLARY SENTINEL NODE HOT AND BLUE", (FSA):\u000aOne lymph node negative for tumor.\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "#2. RIGHT AXILLARY SENTINEL NODE HOT AND BLUE", (FSB):\u000aOnly lymph node negative for tumor.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by RUCKER-SCHMIDT,RACHEL L.,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in six parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart one, labeled "#1. right axillary sentinel node, hot and blue" consists of\u000aa single piece of pink to tan soft tissue (2.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) which is\u000abisected and entirely submitted for frozen section evaluation as FSA. The\u000aspecimen is entirely submitted for histologic examination.\u000aMicro 1: FSAR, right axillary sentinel node, 2 frags, ESS\u000aPart two, labeled "#2. right axillary sentinel node, hot and blue", consists of\u000aa single piece of pink to tan soft tissue (0.7 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) which is\u000abisected and entirely submitted for frozen section evaluation as FSB. The\u000aspecimen is entirely submitted for histologic examination.\u000aMicro 2: FSBR, right axillary sentinel node, bisected, 2 frags, ESS\u000aPart three, labeled "#3. right breast, long = lateral, short = superior",\u000aconsists of a 740 gram right simple mastectomy specimen (23.4 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm)\u000awith an attached pink/tan skin ellipse (5.6 x REMOVED_DATE cm) which includes a REMOVED_DATE cm\u000anipple. No lesions or scars are present on the skin. The specimen is received\u000awith two sutures placed by the surgeon to designate the superior and lateral\u000aorientation of the specimen. The deep margin is a smooth fascial plane,\u000awithout skeletal muscle, and is inked black. The specimen is densely fibrous\u000acentrally, and the fibrous tissue has been blue-dyed. Three deep red, punctate\u000ahemorrhages are identified, possibly representing previous core biopsy sites.\u000aThey are located in the upper middle portion of the breast (0.3 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm), the lower middle portion of the breast (1.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), and in the\u000alower outer quadrant (0.4 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The lesions are located REMOVED_DATE cm, REMOVED_DATE \u000acm, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the deep margin, respectively. The fibrous tissue has\u000amultiple clear fluid-filled cysts, ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to REMOVED_DATE cm in\u000agreatest dimension. The breast specimen is approximately 45% fibrous tissue\u000aand 65% fatty tissue. Representative sections are submitted for histologic\u000aexamination.\u000aMicro 3: upper middle area of hemorrhage, 2 frags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  lower middle area of hemorrhage, 4 frags, ESS\u000aMicro 8: lower outer area of hemorrhage, 2 frags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  UOQ, 2 frags, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  UIQ, 2 frags, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  LOQ, 2 frags, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  LIQ, 2 frags, RSS\u000aMicro 17: nipple, 1 frag, RSS\u000aPart four, labeled "#4. lower breast biopsy", consists of a single piece of\u000atan/pink soft tissue (0.3 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The specimen is entirely submitted\u000afor histologic examination.\u000aMicro 18: lower breast biopsy, 1 frag, ESS\u000aPart five, labeled "#5. middle breast biopsy", consists of a single piece of\u000atan/white soft tissue (0.3 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) which is entirely submitted for\u000ahistologic examination.\u000aMicro 19: middle breast biopsy, 1 frag, ESS\u000aPart six, labeled "#6. upper breast biopsy", consists of a single piece of\u000atan/pink soft tissue (0.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) which is entirely submitted for\u000ahistologic examination.\u000aMicro 20: upper breast biopsy, 1 frag, ESS\u000arlr\u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: SENTINEL LYMPH NODE\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SENTINEL LYMPH NODE\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY - PARTIAL OR SIMPLE\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SKIN CYST, TAG OR DEBRIDEMENT\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SKIN CYST, TAG OR DEBRIDEMENT\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SKIN CYST, TAG OR DEBRIDEMENT\u000a[report_end]
