ntry of the localizing wire and remote (1.5\u000acm) from the embedded wire tip. Cut surfaces are predominately fibrous\u000a(85-90%), with occasional focal hemorrhage (< 20% of surfaces) and no discrete\u000alesions, with the exception of the previously mentioned exposed cavity (0.6 x\u000a0.6 x REMOVED_DATE cm). The specimen is entirely submitted sequentially from lateral to\u000amedial.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Entire sequential specimen from lateral to medial (localizing\u000awire tip in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID; cavity in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) multi frags, ESS.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_IDlateral, inferior; REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDanterior, posterior, superior,\u000ainferior; REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDantertior, posterior, superior; REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDanterior,\u000aposterior, inferior; REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDanterior, posterior, superior; REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aanterior, posterior, inferior; REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDanterior, posterior, superior;\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDanterior, posterior, inferior; REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDanterior,\u000aposterior, superior; REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDanterior, posterior, inferior, medial; REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDanterior,\u000aposterior, superior, medial; REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDsuperior, posterior, medial.\u000aDB/ajb\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Kevin B Long M.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Shuji Ogino M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a1/9/2006\u000a[report_end]
