VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID SENTINEL LYMPH NODE\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aKRANE, JEFFREY, FRED, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by KRANE,JEFFREY FRED,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST EXCISION WIRE LOCALIZATION FOR A MASS AND A CLIP AND SENTINEL NODE\u000aBIOPSY (INCLUDING REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aINVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA, DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, AND METASTATIC\u000aCARCINOMA TO LYMPH NODE.\u000aSYNOPSIS:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA\u000aSize - REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aMultifocal - No\u000aHistologic Type - Ductal\u000aHistologic Grade (SBR) - II(Moderate)\u000aNuclear Grade - Intermediate\u000aEIC - Negative\u000aLymphovascular invasion - Present\u000aDermal lymphatic invasion - Absent\u000aSkin invasion - Absent\u000aSkeletal muscle invasion - N/A\u000aFinal Margins (invasive) -\u000aNegative (>0.3 cm) - Inferior, anterior,\u000aposterior, medial, lateral\u000aClose (0.2 cm) - Superior (focal, block 11)\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU - Present\u000aTypes - Solid, cribriform\u000aNuclear grade - Intermediate\u000aCalcifications in DCIS - Present\u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - Present\u000aExtent of DCIS\u000aNumber of blocks/total: REMOVED_DATE blocks\u000aFinal Margins (DCIS)\u000aNegative (>0.3 cm) - Inferior, anterior,\u000aposterior, medial, lateral\u000aClose (0.3 cm) - Superior (focal, block 11)\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - Absent\u000aLYMPH NODES\u000aSentinel lymph nodes (3 H&E levels examined): Positive (see NOTE)\u000aNumber of positive nodes - 1\u000aNumber of nodes examined - 3\u000aTOTAL POSITIVE NODES (all specimens) - REMOVED_DATE \u000aSize of largest metastatic focus less than REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aExtranodal extension Absent\u000aOTHER FINDINGS Columnar alteration of lobules with\u000aprominent snouts and secretions with\u000aatypia.\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia.\u000aCore biopsy site.\u000aAJCC CLASSIFICATION (6th edition) - REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDc pREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID MX\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER/PR/HER-2) - Pending\u000aNOTE: The metastatic focus is composed at a single cluster of approximately 10\u000acells (block 1) and is not present in the original frozen section slide.\u000aLEFT BREAST, SUPERIOR SHAVE MARGIN:\u000aBenign breast tissue with columnar alteration of lobules with prominent\u000asnouts and secretions with atypia, epithelial hyperplasia,\u000afibroadenomatous changes, complex sclerosing lesion, apocrine\u000ametaplasia, and cysts.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000aLEFT BREAST, SUPERIOR SUPERIOR SHAVE MARGIN:\u000aBenign breast tissue with columnar alteration of lobules with prominent\u000asnouts and secretions, cysts and apocrine metaplasia.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000aLEFT AXILLARY CONTENTS:\u000aFibroadipose tissue with no tumor present.\u000aNo lymph node present.\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for invasive carcinoma (block 12):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) NEGATIVE (0)\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000acarcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but\u000aonly a portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity\u000ain >10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Ca of left breast.\u000aOperation: Left sentinel lymph node bx, left needle localized breast biopsy\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast cancer\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1) Left sentinel lymph node - fs\u000a#2) Left tumor site - long lateral, short superior (mammo)\u000a#3) Superior shave margin - long lateral, short superior (loop suture marks\u000anodular density)\u000a#4) Superior, superior shave margin (long lateral, short superior, taken\u000asuperior to nodular density found in superior shave margin)\u000a#5) Left axillary contents\u000aRADIOLOGY: Mass and clip are seen in specimen. S. Raza,MD\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "#1. LEFT SENTINEL LYMPH NODES", (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aThree lymph nodes negative for carcinoma.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by CHEN,JEY-HSIN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in five parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart one, labeled "#1. left sentinel lymph nodes", consists of three lymph\u000anodes. The first node (1.4 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) is entirely submitted as REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID for\u000afrozen section analysis, the second node (1.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) is entirely\u000asubmitted as REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, and the third node (2.4 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) is entirely\u000asubmitted as REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID through 6.\u000aMicro 1: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID remnant, 1 frag, ESS\u000aMicro 2: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID remnant, 1 frag, ESS\u000aMicro 3: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID remnant, 1 frag, ESS\u000aMicro 4: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID remnant, 1 frag, ESS\u000aMicro 5: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID remnant, 1 frag, ESS\u000aMicro 6: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID remnant, 1 frag, ESS\u000aPart two, labeled "#2. left tumor site, long lateral, short superior", consists\u000aof a left breast lumpectomy specimen (6.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with tan/yellow\u000afibroadipose tissue, a tan/pink skin ellipse (4.3 x REMOVED_DATE cm) oriented with a\u000ashort suture marking the superior surface and a long suture marking the lateral\u000asurface. The specimen is received inked by the surgeon per pathology protocol\u000afor the evaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior =\u000ared; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. The skin without\u000agrossly identifiable scar is located at the anterior surface. Also received\u000awithin the specimen is a needle accompanied by a radiograph demonstrating a\u000amass and clip within the specimen. The specimen is serially sectioned from\u000amedial to lateral revealing a tan/white gritty nodule (1.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm)\u000aextending to within less than REMOVED_DATE cm at the superior surface, REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000aposterior surface, REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior surface, REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior\u000asurface, REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial surface and REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral surface.\u000aThe remaining breast parenchyma is comprised of approximately 50%\u000ayellow/tan/pink lobular tissue and approximately 50% adipose tissue. No other\u000alesions are grossly identified. Representative sections of the tumor as well\u000aas uninvolved breast parenchyma are submitted to the tumor bank.\u000aRepresentative sections are submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  tumor in relation to superior and inferior margins, mult frags,\u000aRSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  tumor in relation to superior, inferior and posterior margins, 4\u000afrags, RSS\u000aMicro 15: closest skin and anterior margin, 2 frags, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  closest lateral margin, 2 frags, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  closest medial margin, 6 frags, RSS\u000aPart three, labeled "#3. superior shave margin, long lateral, short superior",\u000aconsists of an oriented lumpectomy specimen (4 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) oriented with a\u000ashort stitch marking the superior surface and a long stitch marking the lateral\u000asurface. The specimen is received inked by the surgeon: red = superior, black\u000a= posterior, and green = medial portion of the specimen. The remainder of the\u000aspecimen is inked as follows: yellow = lateral, blue = anterior, there is a\u000aloop at the superoanterior surface of the specimen. The specimen is serially\u000asectioned from medial to lateral revealing an area of blue/green dye located\u000aat the medialmost section of the specimen (1.2 cm). The remainder of the\u000aspecimen is comprised of approximately REMOVED_DATE % yellow/tan/pink lobular tissue\u000aadmixed with yellow adipose tissue. No discrete nodule is identified. The\u000aentire specimen with serial sections from medial to lateral are submitted.\u000aMicro 20: medialmost section, perpendicular, 5 frags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  serial sections from medial to lateral, 3 frags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  lateralmost sections, perpendicular, 9 frags, ESS\u000aPart four, labeled "#4. superior, superior shave margin, short superior, long\u000alateral", consists of an oriented breast lumpectomy specimen (3.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm) oriented with a short suture designating the superior surface and a long\u000asurface designating the lateral surface. The specimen is received inked red by\u000athe surgeon at the superior surface. The remainder of the specimen is inked\u000aper pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior = black;\u000aanterior = blue; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. The\u000aspecimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral revealing approximately\u000a50% pink/tan lobular tissue located in the lateral portion of the specimen. No\u000alesions are grossly identified. The specimen is entirely submitted for\u000ahistologic examination.\u000aMicro 29: medialmost section, perpendicular, 2 frags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  serial sections from medial to lateral, 5 frags, ESS\u000aMicro 32: lateralmost section, perpendicular, 3 frags, ESS\u000aPart five, labeled "#5. left axillary contents", consists of a yellow/tan\u000afibroadipse tissue (2.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). No definitive lymph node is grossly\u000aidentified. The specimen is entirely submitted.\u000aMicro 33: left axillary contents, 1 frag, ESS\u000ajhc\u000aReports to: CHRISTIAN, ROGER, L. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: SENTINEL LYMPH NODE\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: LYMPH NODE BIOPSY\u000a[report_end]
