VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Amend/Addenda\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000a********** Addended Report ***********\u000aResident: Kevin Golden, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Kirstine Yung-Ting Oh, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA/1). LEFT BREAST, EXCISION FOR A MASS AND A CLIP:\u000aINVASIVE PAPILLARY CARCINOMA (0.7 cm), well differentiated (modified\u000aBloom-Richardson grade I/III)\u000aNo lymphovascular invasion is identified.\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, micropapillary and cribriform type, intermediate\u000anuclear grade, is present in one (1) of twenty-three (23) blocks (slide REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID;\u000aEIC negative).\u000aInvasive carcinoma is present less than REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin. The\u000aanterior, posterior, lateral, superior, and inferior margins are negative for\u000ainvasive carcinoma (>0.3 cm).\u000aMargins are negative for DCIS (>0.3 cm).\u000aOther findings:\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia.\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia.\u000aColumnar cell change with flat atypia and calcifications.\u000aCore biopsy site changes.\u000aDuct ectasia with periductal inflammation and fibrosis (mastitis obliterans).\u000aNote: The carcinoma consists of a partially intracystic and partially\u000ainfiltrative invasive papillary carcinoma, best seen in slide REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. An\u000aimmunohistochemical stain for p63-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID demonstrates the lack of\u000amyoepithelial cells both in the intracystic and infiltrative areas of the\u000atumor.\u000aAJCC Classification (6th edition): REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDb Nx\u000aThis case was reviewed by Dr. Lester and Dr. Richardson of Breast Pathology,\u000awho concur.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 80-year-old female with L breast U/S REMOVED_DATE  noting heterogenous,\u000airregular mass 7 x 8 x 6 mm at 11;30 position - WL recommended; also S/P L\u000abreast core bx REMOVED_DATE  revealing fragments of papillary lesion with atypia.\u000aOperation: L breast WL bx.\u000aOperative Findings: None specified.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: L breast mass.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) L breast tissue, short stitch - superior at palpable mass; long - lateral;\u000awhip stitch at chest wall - mammo.\u000aRADIOLOGY: 2 wires, a clip and a possible round mass are seen. - Dr. Gombos.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, medical record\u000anumber only, and consists of a portion of fibroadipose tissue (5.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm) with three orienting sutures ("short stitch superior, long stitch lateral,\u000awhipstitch at chest wall") and two intact hook wires (wire #1 entering at the\u000amedial superior aspect; wire #2 entering at the medial posterior aspect). The\u000aspecimen is inked by the surgeon per pathology protocol for the evaluation of\u000amargins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green;\u000alateral/yellow; medial/ orange. The specimen is accompanied by a radiograph,\u000aexhibiting to intact hook wires, clip adjacent to wire #2, and possible density\u000aat the superior aspect. Note, surgeon designates "Palpable mass" at short\u000astitch (superior). The specimen is serially sectioned from lateral to medial,\u000aexhibiting a firm lobulated, calcified mass (0.6 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which is at\u000athe superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the medial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the deep/posterior\u000aand anterior margins, REMOVED_DATE cm of the anterior margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm of the lateral\u000amargin. The remaining breast tissue consists of approximately 80% tan/white,\u000adense, nodular to focally cystic fibrous stroma admixed with approximately 20%\u000ayellow lobulated adipose tissue. A silver metal clip is identified adjacent to\u000ahookwire #2, REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin. No other gross lesions identified.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Breast tissue sequentially from lateral to medial, multi frags,\u000aESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Mass at superior margin.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Area of clip.\u000aDFI/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Kirstine Yung-Ting Oh M.D., Electronically signed on\u000a12/2/2007\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM (12/05/07):\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for papillary carcinoma (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) NEGATIVE (0)\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000ainvasive carcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low > 0% - < 10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor cells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but only a\u000aportion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+):Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in >10% of\u000atumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+):Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in >30% of\u000atumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aExternal controls are evaluated and show appropriate Immunoreactivity.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aAddendum #1 by Deborah A Dillon M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
