VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST MASTECTOMY - PARTIAL OR SIMPLE\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aGLICKMAN, JONATHAN, NEIL, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by GLICKMAN,JONATHAN NEIL,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST, SIMPLE MASTECTOMY:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA WITH MIXED FEATURES, ONE FOCUS\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU.\u000aSYNOPSIS:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA\u000aSize - REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aMultifocal - No\u000aHistologic Type - Mixed Ductal and Lobular\u000aHistologic Grade (SBR) - II(Moderate)\u000aNuclear Grade - Intermediate\u000aEIC - Negative\u000aLymphovascular invasion - Absent\u000aDermal lymphatic invasion - Absent\u000aSkin invasion - Absent\u000aSkeletal muscle invasion - Absent\u000aFinal Margins (invasive) -\u000aNegative (>0.3 cm) deep margin\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU -\u000aTypes - Solid\u000aNuclear grade - Intermediate\u000aCalcifications in DCIS - Absent\u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - Absent\u000aMicroinvasion (<0.1cm) - Absent\u000aExtent of DCIS DCIS is present as a minor component of\u000athe invasive carcinoma.\u000aFinal Margins (DCIS)\u000aNegative (>0.3 cm) deep margin\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - Absent\u000aOTHER FINDINGS Atypical ductal hyperplasia\u000aCore biopsy site\u000aSkeletal muscle\u000aPapilloma\u000aColumnar alteration of lobules with\u000aprominent snouts and secretions.\u000aAJCC CLASSIFICATION (6th edition): REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDc pNx MX\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER/PR/HER-2) - Performed previously\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: None given.\u000aOperation: Left simple mastectomy.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast cancer.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Left breast with short stitch superior, long\u000astitch lateral.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by YOU,MINGJIAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in one part, labeled with the patient's name,\u000aunit number and "#1 left breast". The specimen is a 359-gram breast (24 x 17 x\u000a2.0 cm) with a white/tan skin ellipse (16 x 8 cm). There is no attached\u000aaxillary tail. The nipple (1.6 cm diameter), areola (4.0 cm diameter) and skin\u000aare grossly unremarkable. The surgeon placed short and long stitches to\u000aindicate the superior and lateral aspects of the specimen, respectively. The\u000adeep margin is inked in black. There are some traces of skeletal muscle fibers\u000a(0.4 cm in greatest dimension) which are attached to the deep smooth fascia.\u000aA solid pink/yellow/white/tan mass (1.9 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) is identified. There\u000ais no necrosis or hemorrhage in the mass grossly. The mass is REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000adeep margin, and is located in the upper outer quadrant and close to the\u000acentral of the specimen. One fibrous and hemorrhagic area (0.4 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE )\u000ais identified in the upper outer quadrant and REMOVED_DATE cm laterally and superiorly\u000afrom the mass. This area may represent the prior biopsy site. No other\u000anodules or areas suspicious for tumor are identified in the specimen.\u000aApproximately 90% of the specimen is composed of yellow/tan fatty tissue and\u000aapproximately 10% of the specimen is composed of white/tan fibrous tissue.\u000aNo lymph nodes are identified in the specimen. Representative tissue and tumor\u000amass are submitted for tumor bank.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  tumor and deep margin, 3 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  tumor and surrounding area, 3 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 6: possible biopsy site, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 7: upper outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 8: upper inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 9: lower outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 10: lower inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 11: nipple, 1 frag, RSS.\u000amjy\u000aReports to: CHRISTIAN, ROGER, L. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY - PARTIAL OR SIMPLE\u000a[report_end]
