VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aLESTER, SUSAN, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR CALCIFICATIONS AND A CLIP:\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU.\u000aSYNOPSIS:\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU - Present\u000aTypes - Papillary and micropapillary, clinging\u000aNuclear grade - Low\u000aCalcifications in DCIS - Present\u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - Absent\u000aMicroinvasion (<0.1cm) - Absent\u000aExtent of DCIS\u000aNumber of blocks/total: - REMOVED_DATE blocks\u000aFinal Margins (DCIS)\u000aNegative (>0.3 cm) - anterior (skin)\u000aVery close (<0.1 cm) - inferior, posterior, lateral, medial\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - Absent\u000aOTHER FINDINGS\u000aCore biopsy site\u000aAJCC CLASSIFICATION (6th edition): Tis NX MX\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER/PR/HER-2) - Pending\u000aNOTE: The DCIS is present both adjacent to, and away, from the prior biopsy\u000asite and occupies an area measuring at least 5 cm in size. DCIS is associated\u000awith mucin production.\u000aThe superior margin is not well seen and cannot be evaluated.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU.\u000aSYNOPSIS:\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU - Present\u000aTypes - Papillary and micropapillary, clinging\u000aNuclear grade - Low\u000aCalcifications in DCIS - Present\u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - Absent\u000aMicroinvasion (<0.1cm) - Absent\u000aExtent of DCIS\u000aNumber of blocks/total: - REMOVED_DATE blocks\u000aFinal Margins (DCIS)\u000aNegative (>0.3 cm) - inferior\u000aClose (0.1) - posterior, anterior\u000aVery close (<0.1 cm) - lateral, medial\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - Absent\u000aNOTE: The superior margin is not well seen and cannot be evaluated.\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for DCIS (block 5):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) NEGATIVE (0)\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000ainvasive carcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but\u000aonly a portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity\u000ain >10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Microcalcifications associated with ADH.\u000aOperation: Wire directed right breast excision x 2\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1) Tissue from right breast (short stitch superior; long\u000astitch lateral - 2 localizing wires)\u000a#2) Tissue from right breast (single wire)\u000aRADIOLOGY: Specimen #1: OR called 11:05 - both wires, both groups of\u000acalcifications and clip are in specimen. Dr. Twohig\u000aSpecimen #2: Wire and calcifications in specimen. OR called 11:25.\u000aDr. Twohig\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by KINDELBERGER,DAVID W.,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart one, consists of a single fragment of yellow/tan fibroadipose tissue\u000ameasuring REMOVED_DATE cm from medial to lateral x REMOVED_DATE cm from superior to inferior x\u000a4.2 cm from anterior to posterior. There is a skin ellipse marking the\u000aanterior border of the specimen (3.0 x REMOVED_DATE cm). The specimen is inked by the\u000asurgeon per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior =\u000ablack; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow;\u000amedial = orange. Serial sectioning reveals multiple hemorrhagic cysts (largest\u000ameasuring REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest dimension) that appear to abut the inked inferior\u000amargin. No other lesions are grossly identified. The specimen is entirely\u000asubmitted for histologic examination. An accompanying specimen radiograph\u000ademonstrates the presence of two localizing wires, a clip, and multiple foci of\u000acalcification present in the sample.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  right breast tissue, mult frags, ESS\u000aPart two, consists of a single fragment of yellow/brown/tan fibroadipose tissue\u000ameasuring REMOVED_DATE cm from superior to inferior x REMOVED_DATE cm from lateral to medial x\u000a0.9 cm from anterior to posterior. There is a single metal localizing wire\u000aembedded within the specimen. The specimen is inked by the surgeon per\u000apathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior\u000a= blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange.\u000aThe specimen is composed of approximately REMOVED_DATE % adipose tissue and REMOVED_DATE %\u000afibrous tissue. No areas of hemorrhage or other gross lesions are appreciated.\u000aThe specimen is serially sectioned and entirely submitted for histologic\u000aanalysis. An accompanying specimen radiograph demonstrates the presence of a\u000alocalizing wire and calcifications within the specimen.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  right breast tissue from inferior to superior, mult frags, ESS\u000adk\u000aReports to: CHRISTIAN, ROGER, L. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
