sures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. Deep to the skin incision in the lower outer\u000aquadrant of the breast is an area of white fibrous tissue which measures\u000aapproximately REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. This area includes a small cystic space\u000awhich measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. Adjacent to this space is a firm area of\u000avariegated white and tan soft tissue which measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 cm. This\u000aarea extends to within REMOVED_DATE cm of the deep margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior\u000amargin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin. Three to five cm superior to this\u000asite is a second fibrous area consistent with the other biopsy site. Both\u000aareas are extensively sampled. The lateral tissue is carefully examined and\u000aall lymph nodes are completely submitted.\u000aMicro 1,2: lower outer biopsy site with deep margin, 2 frag, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  additional sections from lower outer biopsy site, 3 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 6: fibrous tissue UOQ, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 7: fibrous tissue UIQ, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 8: fibrous tissue LIQ, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 9: skin with scar, 1 frag, RSs\u000aMicro 10: nipple, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 11: largest axillary lymph node (1.2 cm) bisected, 2 frags, ESS\u000aMicro 12: possible lymph node bisected, 2 frags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE possible lymph nodes, 3 frags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  4 possible lymph nodes, bisected, 8 frags, 1 per cassette, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  upper outer biopsy site, 3 to 5 cm superior to first site, mult\u000afrags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  upper outer biopsy site, 5 cm superior to first site, 3 frag, RSS\u000aPart two, labeled "#2. ? viable skin from flaps", consists of two irregular\u000aellipses of pink/white skin which measure REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm, excised to a depth of\u000a0.3 cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm, excised to a depth of REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000aMicro 18: larger piece, 3 frags, RSS\u000aMicro 19: smaller ellipse, 1 frag, RSS\u000amwb\u000aReports to: CHRISTIAN, ROGER, L. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY - PARTIAL OR SIMPLE\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SKIN- OTHER THAN CYST, TAG OR DEBRIDEMENT\u000a[report_end]
