VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ROGER L CHRISTIAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Oname O. Burlingame, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: William R Welch, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "RIGHT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A CLIP\u000aMARKING A CORE BIOPSY SITE":\u000aColumnar cell change with flat atypia, two foci (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID)\u000aadjacent to prior biopsy site.\u000aBenign epithelial hyperplasia and apocrine cysts with associated\u000amicrocalcifications.\u000aB. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "RIGHT BREAST, MEDIAL SHAVE MARGIN NEAR CLIP SITE":\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia.\u000aMicrocalcifications associated with benign epithelium.\u000aNOTE: No carcinoma is identified after complete microscopic examination of the\u000aspecimen, including margin.\u000aDr. Susan Lester, Breast Pathology Service, has reviewed the case and concurs.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: ADH, right breast.\u000aOperation: Loc/Excision; right breast, wire loc biopsy.\u000aOperative Findings: See op notes.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: ADH, right breast.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Right breast tissue - mammo.\u000aB/2. Additional right breast tissue.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Clip and wire seen; called results to ATR at, 11:30 on REMOVED_DATE \u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart A, labeled "#1. Rt breast tissue", consists of an unoriented, wire\u000alocalized breast excision specimen (3.7 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with a needle\u000alocalization wire that traverses the greatest dimension of the specimen. The\u000abreast parenchyma is approximately 15% fibrous and 85% adipose tissue. A clip\u000ais identified in the center of the specimen adjacent to the localization wire.\u000aNo definitive masses or lesions identified. The outer surface of the specimen\u000ais inked black, and the specimen is serially sectioned and sequentially\u000asubmitted in its entirety. The specimen is received with a radiograph and\u000aradiograph report stating that a clip and wire are seen within the specimen.\u000aThe radiograph shows a clip present within the specimen adjacent to the\u000alocalization wire.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Side margin (perpendicular), 5 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Serial sections sequentially submitted with clip site in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 2 complete cross sections in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and 1 complete cross section in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, incomplete cross section in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_DATE frags each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Side margin, perpendicular, 6 frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, labeled "#2. Additional Rt breast tissue", consists of an unoriented\u000afragment of fibroadipose tissue (1.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) made up of approximately\u000a95% and 5% fibrous tissue with one focus of recent hemorrhage. No definitive\u000amasses or lesions are identified. The outer surface is inked black, and the\u000aspecimen is serially sectioned and entirely submitted for histologic\u000aexamination.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Side margin (perpendicular), 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Complete cross sections, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Side margin (perpendicular), 4 frags, ESS.\u000aOOB/md/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-07-REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by William R Welch M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
