VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ROGER L CHRISTIAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-06-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Kevin B Long, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Jason L Hornick, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. LEFT BREAST, EXCISION WIRE-LOCALIZATION FOR CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aSYNOPSIS:\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aTypes - comedo, solid\u000aNuclear grade - high\u000aCalcifications in DCIS - present\u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - present\u000aMicroinvasion - absent (see NOTE)\u000aExtent of DCIS\u000aNumber of blocks:total - 12:18 blocks\u000aMargins (DCIS)\u000aNegative (>0.3 cm) - anterior, posterior, lateral, medial\u000a(see part B for final margin)\u000aVery close (<0.1 cm) - inferior (see part B for final margin),\u000asuperior\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - absent\u000aOTHER FINDINGS\u000aCore biopsy site; calcifications in benign epithelium\u000aAJCC CLASSIFICATION (6th edition) - Tis pNx MX\u000aB. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "INFERIOR SHAVE MARGIN":\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, comedo and solid type, high nuclear grade,\u000ain two of six (2:6) blocks.\u000aDCIS is present at the medial margin and is REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior\u000amargin.\u000aNOTE: No invasive carcinoma is identified (immunohistochemical stains for\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and p63 were examined). Selected slides were also reviewed by Dr.\u000aSusan Lester (Breast Pathology Service), who concurs.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: DCIS associated with one area of calcs, left breast.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast DCIS.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) left breast tissue.\u000aB/2) inferior shave margin.\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000aWire, clip + calcifications seen in specimen images S Nielsen REMOVED_DATE  11:40 am\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two parts, each labeled with the patients\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart A, labeled "#1 - left breast tissue", consists of a REMOVED_DATE (posterior to\u000aanterior) x REMOVED_DATE (medial to lateral) x REMOVED_DATE (inferior to superior) cm breast\u000abiopsy with a localization wire in place, and a short suture marking the\u000asuperior margin and a long suture marking the lateral margin. An accompanying\u000aspecimen radiograph demonstrates the wire, clip, and an area of calcifications.\u000aThe specimen is received previously inked by the surgeon according the\u000apathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black;\u000aanterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange.\u000aThe tissue consists of approximately 50% fibrous parenchyma and 50% yellow\u000aadipose tissue. The specimen is re-radiographed, and the area of\u000acalcifications is identified in an area of firm white fibrous tissue (0.8 x REMOVED_DATE \u000ax REMOVED_DATE cm) adjacent to the clip. This area is approximately REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000ainferior, REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm from the skin (anterior), REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000athe superior, REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin.\u000aSurrounding white fibrous tissue extends from this area and abuts the inferior,\u000alateral, medial and superior margins. The anterior margin is composed of a\u000awhite/tan skin ellipse measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. Approximately 50% of the\u000aspecimen is submitted, including all fibrous tissue. The location of the\u000atissue blocks is recorded on a specimen diagram.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID+REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: area with clip, calcifications to inferior margin, 2 frags,\u000aRSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID+REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: area with calcifications and fibrous tissue to the lateral\u000aand inferior margins, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: closest medial margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: closest superior margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: fibrous tissue to inferior margin, 4 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: fibrous tissue and superior margin, 5 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: closest posterior margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: skin (anterior margin), 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: additional fibrous tissue, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aPart B, labeled "#2 - inferior shave margin", consists of a fragment of\u000afibroadipose breast tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The specimen is\u000areceived previously inked by the surgeon, with green designating new inferior\u000amargin, orange=medial margin, and yellow=lateral margin. On cut surface the\u000atissue is predominantly (approximately 80%) unremarkable yellow adipose tissue,\u000awith scattered white/tan ill-defined fibrous tissue focally abutting the new\u000ainferior margin. No masses or lesions suspicious for invasive tumor are\u000aidentified.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: fibrous tissue and inferior margin, 5 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: fibrous tissue and medial margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aKEL/lp\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jason L Hornick M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a5/31/2006\u000a[report_end]
