ious excision site, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Previous excision site in relationship to deep margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Area adjacent to previous excision site, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Additional layer of previous excision site, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: First fibrous band, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Distal portion of first fibrous band, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Deep margin to first fibrous band, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Second fibrous band, 5 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Deep margin from second fibrous band, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Skin with scar representative [not dictated].\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Upper outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lower outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lower inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Upper inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lymph node candidate bisected, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lymph node candidate trisected, 3 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lymph node candidate, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lymph node candidate, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMRU/jp\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Alessandra F Nascimento M.D., Electronically signed on\u000a7/21/2006\u000a[report_end]
