y\u000atan/yellow, multilobulated with admixed dense white fibrous tissue. No\u000adiscrete lesions or areas of disruption are grossly identified. The specimen\u000ais serially sectioned from medial to lateral and representative sections are\u000asubmitted for tissue banking and special studies. Gross photographs are taken.\u000aRepresentative sections are submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Superior margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Inferior margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Anterior margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Posterior margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Adjacent tissue to tissue banking site, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 frag, RSS.\u000aPart B, "#2. Additional left breast, lateral margin, suture old margin", and\u000aconsists of an irregular tan/yellow lobulated portion of fibroadipose tissue\u000a(4.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). There is a suture on one aspect of the specimen\u000adesignating "new margin" which is inked blue and the opposite aspect "old\u000amargin" is inked green, and the specimen is serially sectioned. The cut\u000asurface is tan/yellow homogenous with no discrete lesions or areas of\u000adisruption grossly identified. The specimen is submitted in its entirety.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross sections, block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 2 frags each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 3 frags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aSEK/ajb\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Gilbert Brodsky M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
