u000aProgesterone receptor - POSITIVE - LOW\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) - NEGATIVE (1+)\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000ainvasive carcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but\u000aonly a portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity\u000ain >10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Abnormal mammogram REMOVED_DATE  core bx REMOVED_DATE invasive carcinoma, ductal\u000aand lobular features.\u000aOperation: Left needle directed breast lumpectomy, left sentinel lymph node\u000abiopsy.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast cancer.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Left sentinel lymph node.\u000a2. Left breast tissue.\u000aLeft breast, mass in specimen. JL\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by SPRINGER,KIMBERLEY M.,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart one, labeled "#1, left sentinel lymph node", consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm fragment of yellow-tan fibroadipose tissue, containing a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acandidate lymph node. The entire lymph node is submitted.\u000aMicro 1: sentinel lymph node, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aPart two, labeled "#2, left breast tissue", consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afragment of breast tissue, received with a wire and oriented by two (2)\u000asutures. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation\u000aof margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior =\u000agreen; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. Accompanying the specimen is a\u000aradiograph demonstrating the wire in proximity to a mass. A REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afirm, white, hemorrhagic, somewhat stellate mass is present less than REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom the lateral margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior and anterior margins, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom the posterior margin, greater than 2 cm from the medial and inferior\u000amargins. The remainder of the breast tissue is approximately 10% fibrous.\u000aRepresentative sections are submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  mass, including lateral margin, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000aMicro 5: breast tissue with superior margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  posterior margin, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  breast tissue with medial margin, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  breast tissue with anterior margin, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  breast tissue with inferior margin, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000akms\u000aReports to: IGLEHART, JAMES, DIRK M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: SENTINEL LYMPH NODE\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
