VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Surgical margin\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: CHANDRAJIT P. RAUT M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-06-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Wai Chin Foo, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Susan Lester, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aLEFT BREAST, EXCISION FOR A PALPABLE MASS (INCLUDING FROZEN SECTION):\u000aPHYLLODES TUMOR, high grade, REMOVED_DATE cm, with focal lipoblastic features (block\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) (see note). There is extensive stromal overgrowth with only a very focal\u000abenign epithelial component present on deeper levels of blocks REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aThe tumor is highly cellular with moderate nuclear pleomorphism.\u000aMitoses number 13 per 10 HPFs.\u000aNo necrosis is present.\u000aThe tumor extensively invades into the surrounding breast tissue.\u000aA minor component of the tumor is less cellular and has scattered lipoblasts\u000a(block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies are performed with the following results for the tumor\u000a(block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aPAN Keratin NEGATIVE\u000aCytokeratin 14 NEGATIVE\u000aKeratin REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.2 NEGATIVE\u000aKeratin REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID NEGATIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID NEGATIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID NEGATIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID NEGATIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID NEGATIVE (predominantly in stroma)\u000aDesmin NEGATIVE\u000aSmooth muscle actin FOCALLY POSITIVE\u000aThe tumor is < REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE \u000acm from the medial margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin (see additional\u000amargins below).\u000aNote: The tumor shows only very focal biphasic features consistent with origin\u000aas a phyllodes tumor. The immunoperoxidase studies exclude the possibility of\u000aa metaplastic carcinoma and are consistent with a phyllodes tumor.\u000aThis case was reviewed by Dr. Christopher Fletcher, who concurs with this\u000ainterpretation.\u000aSUPERIOR MARGIN:\u000aBreast tissue with no tumor present.\u000aINFERIOR MARGIN:\u000aBreast tissue with no tumor present.\u000aNEW MEDIAL MARGIN:\u000aBreast tissue with no tumor present.\u000aNEW LATERAL MARGIN:\u000aBreast tissue with no tumor present.\u000aNEW DEEP MARGIN:\u000aBreast tissue with no tumor present.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aClinical History: Palpable left breast mass, biopsy consistent with sarcoma.\u000aOperation: Left breast lumpectomy.\u000aOperative Findings: Palpable mass.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Preop: Left breast sarcoma.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000a1. Left breast lumpectomy specimen, stitches: short superior, long lateral,\u000aclip equals deep margin.\u000a2. Superior: clips mark true margin, stitch marks deep margin.\u000a3. Inferior: clips mark true margin, stitch marks deep margin.\u000a4. New medial: clips mark true margin, stitch deep margin.\u000a5. New lateral: clips mark true margin, stitch deep margin.\u000aNew deep margin: clips mark the true margin, no stitch.\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "LEFT BREAST, EXCISION" (GROSS EXAMINATION):\u000aFirm lobulated mass, consistent with patient's known sarcoma.\u000aThe margins are free of tumor. The closest margin is posterior\u000a(0.5 cm).\u000aTumor is taken for Cytogenetics, EM, and for tissue banking.\u000aOR Consultation by: KEVIN LONG, M.D.\u000aResident: SUSAN LESTER, M.D., PH.D.\u000aThe senior physician certifies that he/she personally conducted a gross and/or\u000amicroscopic examination of the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed\u000athe rapid diagnos(es) related thereto.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in six parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname, unit number.\u000aPart A, is labeled "Left breast lumpectomy specimen FS", and consists of one\u000abreast excision specimen (8.9 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with orienting sutures. The\u000aspecimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins:\u000aposterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow;\u000amedial/orange. The specimen contains a white/tan firm well-circumscribed mass\u000a(2.4 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which is grossly REMOVED_DATE cm to the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000ato the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to the anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to the superior\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm to the medial margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm to the lateral margin.\u000aRepresentative sections of the mass are submitted for cytogenetics and held for\u000aEM. Representative sections of the mass are submitted to tissue bank. Gross\u000aphotographs are taken. The specimen is comprised of approximately 90% adipose\u000atissue and 10% fibrous tissue. Approximately 50% of the specimen is submitted,\u000aincluding all of the mass.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Quick fix formalin, Mass, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID through REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Inferior margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID through REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Tumor and posterior margin, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Superior margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Anterior margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Tumor with posterior margin, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Tumor with posterior margin, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Anterior margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID through REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Tumor, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID through REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Superior margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Inferior margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Tumor, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Representative fibrous breast tissue, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Additional tumor, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Additional inferior margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aPart B, "#2 left breast lumpectomy margins - to superior", and consists of one\u000afragment of fibroadipose tissue (5.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with clips designating the\u000anew true margin and a stitch designating the deep margin. The area of the new\u000amargin is inked blue (clips), the area of the deep margin is inked black, and\u000athe remainder of the specimen is inked yellow. The specimen consists of mostly\u000aadipose tissue with focal hemorrhage, but no masses are identified.\u000aRepresentative sections are submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID through REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Representative sections of superior margin, 8 frags, RSS.\u000aPart C, "#3 left breast lumpectomy margins inferior", and consists of one\u000afragment of fibroadipose tissue (6.6 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with clips designating the\u000anew margin and a stitch designating the old deep margin. The new margin marked\u000aby the clips is inked blue, and the old margin is inked black. The remainder\u000aof the specimen is inked yellow. The specimen consists of grossly normal\u000aappearing adipose tissue with no focal masses or lesions. Representative\u000asections are submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID through REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: New inferior margin, 6 frags, RSS.\u000aPart D, "#4 left breast lumpectomy margin medial (new)", and consists of one\u000afragment of fibroadipose tissue (3.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with clips designating the\u000anew margin and a stitch designating the deep. There is also a detached\u000afragment of fibroadipose tissue (1.4 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which is unoriented. On\u000athe largest specimen in the area of the clips is inked blue, the area of the\u000astitch is inked black, and the remainder of the specimen is inked yellow. The\u000aentire detached unoriented fragment is inked yellow. The specimen is entirely\u000asubmitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID through REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Oriented fragment, 7 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Detached fragment, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aPart E, "#5 left breast lumpectomy margins lateral stitch deep margin clips\u000amark true margin", and consists of one fragment of fibroadipose tissue (3.4 x\u000a2.0 x REMOVED_DATE cm) with clips marking the new lateral margin and a stitch marking\u000athe deep margin. The new lateral margin is inked blue, and the deep margin is\u000ainked black. The remainder of the specimen is inked yellow. No masses are\u000aidentified within the specimen, and it is entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID through REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: New lateral margin, 9 frags, ESS.\u000aPart F, "#6 new deep margin left breast lumpectomy", and consists of one\u000afragment of fibroadipose tissue (5.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with clips marking the new\u000adeep margin. The deep margin is inked blue and the remainder of the specimen\u000ais inked yellow. The specimen contains no masses and it is entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID through REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: New deep margin, 9 frags, RSS.\u000aAF/ajb\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a7/19/2006\u000a[report_end]
