medial to lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm anterior to\u000aposterior) with ? attached skin (1.9 x REMOVED_DATE cm) with a short stitch designating\u000asuperior and a long stitch designating lateral. The specimen is inked per\u000apathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black;\u000aanterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. An\u000aaccompanying radiograph demonstrates a metallic clip and a localization wire\u000aentering the lateral aspect of the specimen without exiting. The specimen is\u000aserially sectioned from medial to lateral in ten slices to reveal a tan/brown\u000airregular area (2.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) grossly consistent with prior biopsy site\u000aand contains a metallic clip in slice #4. The prior biopsy site is located REMOVED_DATE \u000acm to the medial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to the lateral margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to the superior\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm to the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to the anterior/skin margin, and\u000agrossly abuts the posterior margin. There is a white firm area associated with\u000athe biopsy cavity in slice #6 (0.7 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) that is located REMOVED_DATE cm to\u000athe lateral margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to the medial margin, grossly abuts the posterior\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm to the anterior/skin margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to the inferior margin, and\u000a0.8 cm to the superior margin. The remainder of the specimen consists of\u000agreater than 90% unremarkable yellow lobulated adipose tissue. All fibrous\u000atissue and >95% of the specimen are submitted for histological examination.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin, perpendicular, 12 frags total, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #2, transected in half, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #3, transected in half, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #4 containing metallic clip, transected in half, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #5, transected in half, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #6, to include firm white area, transected in half, 1 frag\u000aeach, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #7, transected in half, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #8, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #9, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, perpendicular, 2 frags, RSS (no fibrous tissue\u000alocated in lateral margin).\u000aDCP/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Gilbert Brodsky M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM:\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for DCIS (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) NEGATIVE (0)\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000ainvasive carcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low > 0% - < 10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor cells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but only a\u000aportion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+):Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in >10% of\u000atumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+):Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in >30% of\u000atumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aExternal controls are evaluated and show appropriate Immunoreactivity.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aAddendum #1 by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
