or the evaluation of\u000amargins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green;\u000alateral/yellow; medial/orange.) and sectioned from medial to lateral.\u000aSectioning shows a well circumscribed tan/white, lobulated mass occupying\u000aapproximately 90% of the parenchyma (4.4 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). No areas of\u000ahemorrhage or necrosis are identified. The mass abuts the superior, posterior,\u000aanterior, medial and lateral margins and comes to within REMOVED_DATE cm of the inferior\u000amargin. The entire specimen is examined microscopically.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 2 sections of mass to medial margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Mass to superior, anterior and posterior margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Mass to inferior, anterior and posterior margins, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sections of lateral margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Remaining specimen, multi frags, ESS\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000adrd/ag\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a11/30/2006\u000a[report_end]
