VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID:REMOVED_CASE_ID Report Status: Signed\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aADDENDUM REPORT\u000aAddendum #1 Entered: REMOVED_DATE -1536\u005cE\u000aE\u005c\u000a*** ADDITIONAL DIAGNOSTIC INFORMATION ***\u000aThis report contains an addendum to the original for the purpose of providing\u000aadditional diagnostic information. The original diagnosis is unchanged.\u000aThe pT portion of the pTNM staging on this surgical pathology report is changed\u000afrom pREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID to pREMOVED_ACCESSION_IDc. The pREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and pMX remains the same. The new pTNM\u000aclassification should read:\u000aAJCC pTNM Staging (6th Ed.)(based on available surgical material):\u000apREMOVED_ACCESSION_IDc pREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID pMX\u000aAddeundum Signed Electronically Signed FEEN,DENNIS J. M.D. REMOVED_DATE \u000aDIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. Left axillary sentinel lymph node #1, excision:\u000aMetastatic well differentiated mucinous carcinoma (0.3 cm.).\u000aB. Left axillary sentinel lymph node #2, excision:\u000aNo diagnostic abnormalities recognized.\u000aNo metastatic tumor identified.\u000aC. Left axillary lymph node, dissection:\u000aTwo (2) of eighteen (18) axillary lymph nodes are positive for metastatic\u000acarcinoma.\u000aD. Left breast, excision:\u000aWell differentiated invasive mucinous carcinoma (2.0 cm.), see synoptic\u000areport.\u000aDuctal carcinoma in situ, low grade, solid.\u000aE. Left breast, posterior margin, excision:\u000aNo diagnostic abnormalities recognized.\u000aNo tumor identified.\u000aF. Left breast, medial margin, excision:\u000aNo diagnostic abnormalities recognized.\u000aNo tumor identified.\u000aG. Left breast, inferior margin, excision:\u000aNo diagnostic abnormalities recognized.\u000aNo tumor identified.\u000aH. Left breast, superior margin, excision:\u000aWell differentiated invasive mucinous carcinoma (0.2 cm.).\u000aThe new inked margin appears free of invasive carcinoma\u000aSYNOPTIC REPORT - INVASIVE BREAST CANCER\u000aAJCC pTNM CLASSIFICATION (6TH Ed.)(Based on available surgical material:\u000apREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID pREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID pMX\u000aHISTOLOGIC TYPE: invasive ductal carcinoma, mucinous type\u000aHISTOLOGIC GRADE (Nottingham System): I\u000aTUMOR LOCATION: left breast\u000aTUMOR SIZE (greatest dimension): REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000aLYMPHATIC/VASCULAR INVASION: none identified\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU (DCIS): present\u000aType: solid\u000aGrade: I\u000aExtent: focal, confined to area near invasive\u000atumor\u000aSize (greatest dimension): REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000aNecrosis: none identified\u000aRESECTION MARGINS:\u000aInvasive Carcinoma: invasive carcinoma at margin (<0.1 cm.),\u000asection REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, involving superior margin\u000aalong a broad front\u000ain the separate superior margin (specimen\u000aH) the new margin is clear of invasive\u000acarcinoma\u000aDCIS: clear (> REMOVED_DATE cm.)\u000aIMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING (invasive carcinoma):\u000aPrior specimen REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID reported as:\u000aEstrogen receptor: POSITIVE (>10% of nuclei stained)\u000aProgesterone receptor: POSITIVE (>10% of nuclei stained)\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID): NEGATIVE (1+) (faint or <10% complete membrane\u000astaining)\u000aTotal Fixation Time: REMOVED_DATE hours\u000aLYMPH NODES:\u000aPositive nodes out of total sampled: REMOVED_DATE (1/2 sentinel nodes; REMOVED_DATE \u000anon-sentinel nodes)\u000alargest metastasis (greatest dimension): REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000aextranodal extension: focal\u000aCOMMENT: The sentinel lymph nodes, specimens REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID , are examined at\u000amultiple levels with H&E stains and immunohistochemical stains for\u000acytokeratin REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/3.\u000aADDITIONAL PATHOLOGIC FINDINGS:\u000aNon-neoplastic breast: fibrocystic changes\u000aChanges consistent with prior biopsy site.\u000aPRIOR RELATED SPECIMENS REVIEWED: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aFinal Diagnosis by: Dennis J. Feen, M.D.\u000aINTRA-OPERATIVE CONSULTATION:\u000aOPERATING ROOM CONSULTATION (FROZEN SECTION):\u000a#1. Sentinel lymph node #1, left axilla, biopsy:\u000aMetastatic mucinous carcinoma.\u000a#2. Sentinel lymph node #2, left axilla, biopsy:\u000aNo tumor seen.\u000aMJR/DJF\u000aClinical diagnosis & history:\u000aLeft breast carcinoma\u000aTissue-Designation:\u000aA.Sentinel lymph node - left\u000aB.Sentinel lymph node - left #2 count 89\u000aC.Lymph nodes, dissection - left axillary\u000aD.Breast, excision with margins - left\u000aE.Breast, excision with margins - left posterior margin\u000aF.Breast, excision with margins - left medial margin\u000aG.Breast, excision with margins - left inferior margin\u000aH.Breast, excision with margins - left superior margin\u000aGross description:\u000aSpecimen A labeled "left sentinel lymph node #1" is received in formalin. A\u000aportion has been used for frozen section of the REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. lymph node\u000aand is submitted designated "AF". The remainder is submitted designated REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aSpecimen B labeled "left sentinel lymph node #2 neoprobe count 89" is received\u000ain formalin and consists of a lymph node 2 x 2 x 2 cm. It is largely fatty\u000areplaced and only a thin rim of cortex remains. A portion has been used for\u000afrozen section and is submitted designated "BF". The remainder is submitted\u000adesignated REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aSpecimen C is labeled "left axillary node dissection". There are approximately\u000a12 lymph nodes identified in the fat pad. Several large ones are fatty\u000areplaced measuring up to 3 cm. in greatest dimensions. Other range from REMOVED_DATE to\u000a1.5 cm. in greatest dimension. The cut surface of several demonstrate some\u000ainduration. REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aSpecimen D labeled "left breast lumpectomy" is received in formalin and weighs\u000a50 grams. The overall dimensions are REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 cm. A short suture\u000adesignates the superior margin, a long suture the lateral margin. The superior\u000amargin is inked with blue ink, the inferior margin with green ink, the anterior\u000amargin with orange ink and the posterior margin with black ink. The specimen\u000awill be prefixed. There is a soft mass in the upper mid portion of the\u000aspecimen approximately REMOVED_DATE 5 cm. consisting of a mucinous appearance.\u000aSection code: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - upper portion (superior)\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - lower portion (inferior)\u000aTotal fixation time is 76 hours.\u000aSpecimen E labeled "left posterior margin" consists of an oval portion of\u000ayellow adipose tissue REMOVED_DATE x 4 x 1 cm. There is a suture designating the new\u000amargin. This margin is inked with black ink. 8X all.\u000aSpecimen F labeled "left medial margin" is received in formalin and consists of\u000aa triangular fragment of yellow adipose 4 x REMOVED_DATE x 1 cm. A suture designates\u000athe new margin which is inked with black ink. 7X all.\u000aSpecimen G labeled "left inferior margin" is received in formalin and consists\u000aof an oval portion of adipose tissue 5 x REMOVED_DATE x 1 cm. A suture on one surface\u000adesignates the new margin which is inked with black ink. The entire specimen\u000ais submitted designated REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aSpecimen H designated "left superior margin" consists of a rectangular fragment\u000aof yellow adipose tissue 3 x 3 x 1 cm. A suture designates the new margin and\u000ais inked with black ink. The entire specimen is submitted designated REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aTotal fixation time for specimens E, F, G and H is 28 hours.\u000aDictated by: DJF/LV____(signature on file)____RICHARD SAMPSON, M.D. REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a____(signature on file)____DENNIS J. FEEN, M.D. REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a[report_end]
