a, which constitutes approximately 10% of the\u000abreast parenchyma, and grossly abuts the needle localization wire. The\u000aremainder of the breast parenchyma is tan/yellow and homogenous with no\u000adiscrete lesions, areas of disruption, or previous biopsy site grossly\u000aidentified. The specimen is submitted in its entirety.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross sections medial to lateral, block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID to\u000ainclude fibrous area adjacent to needle localization wire, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aSEK/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jason L Hornick M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a3/27/2008\u000a[report_end]
