 is not\u000aoriented but there is a side with apparent cautery. This side will be inked\u000ablack. The opposite side is inked blue. Representative sections are submitted\u000afor histologic analysis.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  superior shave, 6 frags, RSS\u000aPart two, labeled '#2. posterior shave margin", consists of a single piece of\u000abreast shave margin measuring 3 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. There are no apparent masses.\u000aThe specimen consists of fibroadipose tissue and is unoriented. Apparent old\u000amargin is inked black and new margin is inked blue. The specimen is entirely\u000asubmitted for histologic analysis.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE posterior shave margin, 5 frags, ESS\u000aPart three, labeled "#3. right breast", consists of a 480g right simple\u000amastectomy specimen measuring 23 x REMOVED_DATE  cm with a white/pink skin ellipse\u000ameasuring REMOVED_DATE x 4 cm and an attached lateral tissue measuring 5 x 4 x 2 cm.\u000aThere is a REMOVED_DATE cm well-healed scar on the skin ellipse approximately REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom the nipple as well as one fresh scar that measures 4 cm and is REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000athe nipple. The specimen itself contains one short suture designating the\u000asuperior margin and one long suture designating the lateral margin. The\u000aspecimen contains a mass that measures 9 x 8 x 4 cm and is firm white and\u000anodular in appearance. The mass appears to be REMOVED_DATE cm from the deep fascial\u000amargin and REMOVED_DATE cm from the skin. The tumor appears to involve approximately\u000a70% of the breast parenchyma. The remainder of the parenchyma is\u000awhite/yellowish and appears fibrous. There are no other masses present.\u000aRepresentative sections are submitted for histologic analysis.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  tumor mass including mass in relation to deep margin, 10 frags,\u000aRSS\u000aMicro 9: skin with well-healed scar, 1 frag, ESS\u000aMicro 10: skin including tumor mass, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 11: nipple, 3 frags, ESS\u000aMicro 12: additional tumor in relationship to fascial margin, 2 frags, RSS\u000aMicro 13: UOQ, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 14: UIQ, 2 frags, RSS\u000aMicro 15: LOQ, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 16: LIQ, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 17: lateral area, 1 frag, RSS\u000arfi\u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY - PARTIAL OR SIMPLE\u000a[report_end]
