VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aHIRSCH, MICHELLE, S., M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by HIRSCH,MICHELLE S.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISIONAL BIOPSY FOR A CIRCUMSCRIBED MASS:\u000aPHYLLODES TUMOR, low grade (1.8 cm).\u000aThe majority of the tumor has hyalinized stroma; however, focally the\u000astroma is mildly to moderately cellular with moderate nuclear\u000apleomorphism.\u000aMitoses average 1:10 HPF.\u000aFocal stromal overgrowth is present.\u000aThe borders are circumscribed; no stromal invasion is seen.\u000aThe tumor is not present at the resection margin, but is <0.1 cm from the\u000aanterior margin.\u000aThe core needle biopsy site is associated with the tumor.\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia is present.\u000aThis case was reviewed by Dr. Susan Lester (Breast Pathology) who concurs.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Non-palpable mass left breast.\u000aOperation: Left wire directed excisional breast biopsy.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Non-palpable mass left breast.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Tissue, left breast.\u000aRadiograph Report: Wire/mass in specimen. Kemi Babagbemi, M.D.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by RUCKER-SCHMIDT,RACHEL L.,M.D.\u000aSpecimen is received fresh in one part, labeled with the patient's name, unit\u000anumber, and "tissue left breast", and consists of a golden yellow breast\u000aexcision specimen (5.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) which contains a localization wire. The\u000aspecimen is accompanied by a radiograph which shows the localization wire\u000awithin a well defined density. The specimen is received previously inked by\u000athe surgeon as follows: anterior = blue, posterior = black, medial = orange,\u000alateral = yellow, superior = red, and inferior = green. The specimen is\u000aserially sectioned from inferior to superior to reveal a tan/white, rubbery,\u000alobulated mass (1.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) which grossly abuts the blue-inked\u000a(anterior) margin. The tissue surrounding this mass is focally hemorrhagic,\u000aconsistent with needle tract. The mass is present REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin, and is\u000agrossly far from the inferior and lateral margins. The entire mass and\u000arepresentative sections of the breast are submitted for microscopic\u000aexamination.\u000aMicro #1-4: Mass, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro #5-9: Additional sections of breast resection (approximately 95% fatty\u000atissue), multiple frags, RSS.\u000arlr/\u000aReports to: CHRISTIAN, ROGER, L. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
