rs the specimen just inferior to the skin\u000aellipse and traverses laterally. Specimen is received with a radiograph\u000ademonstrating the localizing wire in place adjacent to a clip within the\u000aspecimen. Sectioning demonstrates an ill-defined tan/white REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm\u000amass abutting the inferior margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the closest superior margin,\u000a0.3 cm from the nearest posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the nearest anterior\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the nearest lateral margin, and remote (greater than REMOVED_DATE \u000acm) from the medial margin. Entire specimen is submitted, sequentially from\u000alateral to medial. There are no additional abnormalities grossly.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Entire specimen, sequentially (perpendicular lateral margin\u000ain REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, perpendicular margin in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), multi frags each, ESS.\u000aDB/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: 4857.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jeffrey F Krane M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a2/3/2007\u000a[report_end]
