VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aODZE, ROBERT, DANIEL, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by ODZE,ROBERT DANIEL,M.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST, NEEDLE-LOCALIZED EXCISIONAL BIOPSY:\u000aFibrocystic change, proliferative.\u000aHealing biopsy cavity.\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Architectural distortion of upper inner quadrant of left breast. Core\u000abiopsy was negative.\u000aOperation: Left breast biopsy post needle loc.\u000aOperative findings: Normal tissue (clip in specimen).\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Needle loc; left breast biopsy long lateral, short superior.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Clip is in the specimen. Dr. Kongath.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by DAVID,FRANK SAMUEL,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in one part, labeled with the patient's name,\u000aunit number, and "#1. left breast biopsy", consists of a single mass of fibrous\u000atissue REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The mass has a short suture and a long suture\u000amarkign the superior lateral aspect, respectively, and there is a wire in the\u000aspecimen. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of\u000amargins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green;\u000alateral = yellow; medial = orange. Within the mass is a firm fibrous area, REMOVED_DATE \u000acm in greatest dimension, in which a surgical clip is located. In addition\u000athere are diffuse areas of hemorrhage throughout the specimen. A mammogram\u000aaccompanying the specimen demonstrates the presence of a localizing wire, a\u000asurgical clip, and an irregular fibrous area in the center of the specimen.\u000aRepresentative sections of the specimen are submitted for histologic\u000aexamination.\u000aMICRO #1 and 2: Lateral, 7 frags, ESS.\u000aMICRO #3: Medial, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMICRO #4-9: Dense area of specimen (clip in micro #4), 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMICRO #10: Hemorrhagic area, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aReports to: IGLEHART, JAMES, DIRK M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
