VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aBROWN, FELIX, MARCEL, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by BROWN,FELIX MARCEL,M.D.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, NEEDLE-DIRECTED EXCISION FOR A MASS:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA WITH PREDOMINANTLY DUCTAL AND SOME LOBULAR FEATURES\u000a(1.2 cm), well-differentiated (Bloom-Richardson grade I/II) present in\u000atwo (2) of nineteen (19) blocks (blocks 1 and 3).\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN-SITU, solid, clinging, and focally cribriform types\u000a(intermediate nuclear grade), present in and adjacent to areas involved\u000aby invasive carcinoma, (blocks 1, 3, 5, 17).\u000aPerineural invasion is present.\u000aNo lymphatic/vascular invasion present.\u000aInvasive carcinoma is present at the blue (anterior) margin and less than\u000a0.1 cm from the red (superior) margin (blocks 1 & 3).\u000aDuctal carcinoma in-situ is present at the red (superior) margin\u000a(block 1) and less than REMOVED_DATE cm from the blue (anterior, blocks 1 & 3),\u000aorange (medial, block 3), and black (posterior, block 17) margins.\u000aMicrocalcifications are associated with ductal carcinoma in-situ.\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia.\u000aFibrocystic change with microcysts and apocrine metaplasia.\u000aNOTE: Immunohistochemical analysis for estrogen receptors, progesterone\u000areceptors, and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu will be performed and reported in an addendum.\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "TRUE SUPERIOR MARGIN":\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA WITH PREDOMINANTLY DUCTAL AND SOME LOBULAR FEATURES\u000a(0.6 cm), well-differentiated (Bloom-Richardson grade I/III) present in\u000atwo (2) of four (4) blocks (blocks 21, 22).\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN-SITU, solid and clinging types (intermediate nuclear\u000agrade), present in three (3) of four (4) blocks (blocks REMOVED_DATE ), adjacent\u000ato areas involved by invasive carcinoma.\u000aNo lymphatic/vascular invasion is identified.\u000aDuctal carcinoma in-situ is present less than REMOVED_DATE cm from the true\u000asuperior (red) margin (blocks REMOVED_DATE )\u000aMargins are negative for invasive carcinoma.\u000aNOTE: This tumor is EIC-positive and would be classified as AJCC stage\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_IDc Nx Mx.\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: by CONNOLLY,JAMES L.,M.D.\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for invasive carcinoma:\u000aEstrogen receptor Positive\u000aProgesterone receptor Positive\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) Negative (1+)\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000ainvasive carcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but\u000aonly a portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity\u000ain >10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Complex sclerosing lesion of right breast by needle core biopsy.\u000aOperation: Right needle directed breast biopsy.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal right mammogram.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1. Right needle directed breast biopsy\u000a(short suture = superior, long suture =lateral).\u000a#2. True superior margin.\u000aRadiology : Mass is in specimen----Darrell Smith, M.D.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by QIAN,XIAOHUA,M.D,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two (2) parts, each labeled with the\u000apatient's name and unit number.\u000aPart #1, "right needle directed breast biopsy," consists of a single fragment\u000aof fibroadipose tissue (6.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), with a needle localization wire in\u000aplace, and two (2) sutures, (long = lateral, and short = superior).\u000aThe specimen is inked for the evaluation of margins: posterior = black;\u000aanterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial =\u000aorange. Sections of margins are submitted for microscopic examination.\u000aSectioning reveals a mass (1.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), located at the superior and\u000athe anterior margins, 3 cm from the inferior/green margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000ablack/posterior margin. The mass is at least 1 cm away from both lateral and\u000amedial margins. The rest of the specimen consists of approximately 80% of\u000aadipose tissue, and 20% of fibrous tissue. The specimen is entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  tumor with respect to anterior, superior, and inferior margins,\u000a4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  medial margin, 5 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  lateral margin, multiple frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  body of the specimen, multiple frags, ESS.\u000aPart #2, "true superior margin," consists of a single fragment of yellow/tan\u000afibroadipose tissue measuring 3 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm, with a stitch marking the new\u000atrue margin. The new superior margin is inked in red, and the other margins are\u000ainked in black. There is an area (0.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) which is grossly\u000asuspicious for tumor, and within REMOVED_DATE cm of the new superior margin. The\u000aspecimen is cut perpendicularly with respect to the new superior margin, and\u000ais entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  new superior margin, multiple frags, ESS.\u000aReports to: KASTRINAKIS, WILLIAM, VASILIOS M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN\u000a[report_end]
