ly due to extensive necrosis. [Analysis by Frederic I. Preffer, PhD] These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital. They have not been cleared or approved by the U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA). The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary; this laboratory has established and verified the test's accuracy and precision. Added by: Judith Ann Ferry, M.D. Signed On: 17 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 17:30 GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "right breast biopsy", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm irregular portion of rubbery, tan-pink fibroadipose tissue with a long stitch designating the lateral and a short stitch designating the superior aspect. The posterior surface is inked black, the anterior blue, the superior green and the inferior yellow. The specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm lobular, well circumscribed nodule. The cut surface is tan-yellow, homogenous and soft to necrotic. The mass abuts the postero-medial and postero-inferior margins and comes to REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior, REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior and REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margins. Representative section of the nodule is submitted as FX#1 and saved frozen. Separate representative sections of the nodule are submitted in B+ fixative, sent for flow cytometry and photographs are taken. The remaining uninvolved surrounding parenchyma is dense, pink to white rubbery unremarkable fibrous tissue. Representative sections are submitted as follows: A-B: radial sections of tumor to postero-medial margin. C: nodule to postero-inferior margin. D: mass to superior margin. E-F: uninvolved parenchyma with the lateral margin, radially sectioned in cassette F. G: B+ fixed section. Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "left breast", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm irregular, tan-yellow to pink rubbery portion of fibroadipose tissue with a long stitch designating lateral and a short stitch designating the superior aspect. The posterior aspect is inked black, the anterior blue, the superior green and the inferior yellow. The specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral to reveal a dense white fibrotic cut surface with no distinct masses or lesions identified. A representative section of the parenchyma is submitted for frozen as FX#2, now as H. Representative sections are submitted sequentially from lateral to medial in cassettes I-N with the lateral margin radially sectioned in cassette I and the medial margin radially sectioned in cassette N. Gross Description by: JENNIFER NASH Resident: RESIDENT-FREE SERVICE (MJF) *** INTRA-OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS *** FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS #1: BREAST (RIGHT): NECROTIC TUMOR, CONSISTENT WITH LYMPHOMA. LYMPHOMA WORK-UP DONE. FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS #2: BREAST (LEFT): BENIGN BREAST TISSUE. O.R. Resident: NICOLE ANN BELSLEY, MD O.R. Diagnosis by: Robert Henry Young, M.D. =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: MGH-INPATIENT (FLR.UNKNOWN) REPORTS TO: James C Cusack, M.D. PART A: BREAST, (RIGHT), EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B: BREAST, (LEFT), EXCISIONAL BIOPSY
