VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID SKIN- OTHER THAN CYST, TAG OR DEBRIDEMENT\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aRICHARDSON, ANDREA, L., M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by RICHARDSON,ANDREA L.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "#1. SCAR LEFT BREAST":\u000aSkin with acute and chronic inflammation and foreign body giant cell\u000areaction to polorizable material.\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "#2. LEFT BREAST BIOPSY", WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION OF A MASS:\u000aMYOFIBROBLASTOMA, epithelioid variant, REMOVED_DATE cm, with evidence of core\u000abiopsy site.\u000aThe lesion is completely excised. Closest margins are posterior, REMOVED_DATE cm,\u000aand anterior REMOVED_DATE cm. Other margins are greater than REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000aExtensive florid ductal hyperplasia, intraductal papilloma, squamous\u000ametaplasia, apocrine metaplasia and columnar alteration.\u000aBiopsy cavity.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: None given.\u000aOperation: Left breast myofibroma\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1) Scar left breast\u000a#2) Left breast biopsy (stitch long = lateral, short = superior)\u000aRADIOLOGY: Mass in specimen. E.P. Frost,MD\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by WU,DAVID,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart one, labeled "#1. scar left breast", consists of a yellow/gray/white skin\u000aellipse (2.7 x REMOVED_DATE cm, excised to a depth of REMOVED_DATE cm). On the surface of the\u000awrinkled skin no readily discernable scar is noted. In the subcutaneous tissue\u000athere are prominent areas of white firm fibrosis intermixed with some focal\u000aareas of hemorrhage, all measuring less than REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest dimension.\u000aThe specimen is inked on its deep margin and serially sectioned for\u000amicroscopic examination.\u000aMicro 1: scar left breast, mult frags, ESS\u000aPart two, labeled "#2. left breast biopsy - short stitch superior, long\u000astitch lateral", consists of an excisional breast specimen (5.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm). The specimen is oriented by the surgeon with a short surgical suture\u000adesignating superior and a long lateral surgical suture designating lateral.\u000aThere is a wire in the mass. A radiograph accompanies the specimen is labeled\u000awith the patient's name and unit number, and demonstrates an excisional\u000aspecimen with a wire localizing a mass. No biopsy clip is noted. A detached\u000aunoriented fragment of adipose tissue (1.7 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) is included in the\u000aspecimen jar. The oriented breast specimen is inked by the pathologist per\u000apathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior\u000a= blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange.\u000aThe smaller detached, unoriented adipose tissue fragment is inked by the\u000apathologist in a single color. The larger breast excision specimen is\u000aserially sectioned from medial to lateral to reveal a well-circumscribed white\u000afirm area of nodularity (1.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) that comes within grossly REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aof the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the anterior\u000amargin, greater than REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin, greater\u000athan REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin, and greater than REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000amedial margin. There is a central area of linear hemorrhage corresponding to\u000aprobable biopsy site (0.3 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). Adjacent to this\u000awell-circumscribed firm white area inferiorly is a cystic cavity (0.4 x REMOVED_DATE x\u000a0.3 cm) with closest approach to the inferior margin within REMOVED_DATE cm and is\u000agreater than REMOVED_DATE cm from all other margins. The specimen is composed of\u000aapproximately 40% fibrous tissue and the remainder 60% adipose tissue. There\u000aare some foci of well-circumscribed firm nodularity (0.2 cm) that is within\u000a0.5 cm of the medial margin and REMOVED_DATE cm of the inferior margin and REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000athe superior margin. Representative sections of the suspected tumor mass\u000aincluding all margins are submitted for histologic examination from lateral to\u000amedial. The smaller detached adipose tissue fragment is serially sectioned to\u000areveal adipose tissue and is entirely submitted for histologic examination.\u000aMicro 2: smaller detached unoriented adipose tissue, mult frags, ESS\u000aMicro 3: lateral perpendicular margin, 3 frags, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  superior portion of specimen with well-circumscribed foci\u000asuspicious for tumor and biopsy cavity, 1 frag each, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  inferior portion of specimen submitted lateral to medial, 1 frag\u000aeach, ESS\u000aMicro 20: medial perpendicular margin, mult frags, RSS\u000adwu\u000aReports to: MATORY, YVEDT, L. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: SKIN- OTHER THAN CYST, TAG OR DEBRIDEMENT\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
