VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID OUTSIDE SLIDE CONSULT - BREAST\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aLESTER, SUSAN, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aCONSULT SLIDES FROM YALE-NEW HAVEN HOSPITAL, NEW HAVEN, CT:\u000aLEFT BREAST, 6:00, CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR A MASS (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID; REMOVED_DATE ):\u000aFat necrosis with marked chronic inflammation (see note below).\u000aNo diagnostic features of a primary vasculitis are seen.\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies for cytokeratin do not reveal cytokeratin\u000apositive cells (reviewed).\u000aLEFT CHEST, SKIN AND SOFT TISSUE EXCISION (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID; REMOVED_DATE ):\u000aFat necrosis, involving subcutaneous adipose tissue.\u000aNo diagnostic features of a primary vasculitis are seen.\u000aBy report, immunoperoxidase studies for cytokeratin are negative in the\u000ainflammatory infiltrate and studies for collagen and Factor VIII related\u000aantigen show the vasculature.\u000aNote: No malignancy is seen. By report, the entire specimen was examined\u000amicroscopically. The findings could be related to trauma or treatment.\u000aClinical correlation is suggested.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: History of left breast cancer 13 years ago treated with excision and\u000aradiation therapy.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Consult slides.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by PREISINGER,ELIZABETH ANN,M.D.\u000aReceived from Yale-New Haven Hospital, Pathology Department, 20 York Street,,\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, New Haven, CT REMOVED_CASE_ID, are six (6) slides.\u000aFour (4) slides are labeled "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" and sublabeled "1 2", "1 1 REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID", "1\u000a2 REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" and "2 2", corresponding to a left breast core needle biopsy at 6\u000ao'clock (0.1 x 1 x REMOVED_DATE cm) performed on REMOVED_DATE  according to the accompanying\u000apathology report bearing the patient's name.\u000aTwo (2) slides are labeled "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" and sublabeled "1} 1 FSC" and "1} 1ST",\u000acorresponding to 1) left chest skin excision (0.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000ax REMOVED_DATE cm) 2) left chest wall biopsy for a mass (3.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) performed\u000aon REMOVED_DATE  according to the accompanying pathology report bearing the\u000apatient's name.\u000aReports to: IGLEHART, JAMES, DIRK M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: OUTSIDE SLIDE CONSULT - BREAST\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: OUTSIDE SLIDE CONSULT - BREAST\u000a[report_end]
