VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY(IES)\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aLESTER, SUSAN, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, 11 G ULTRASOUND GUIDED CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY FOR AN IRREGULAR MASS:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA WITH FEATURES OF BOTH DUCTAL AND LOBULAR\u000aDIFFERENTIATION, measuring at least REMOVED_DATE cm in size.\u000aThe carcinoma is poorly differentiated (modified Bloom Richardson\u000aGrade III/III).\u000aNo lymphovascular invasion is seen in this limited specimen.\u000aNo in situ carcinoma is present in this limited specimen.\u000aNOTE: The carcinoma focally has an unusual myxoid/chondroid like stroma.\u000aImmunohistochemical analysis for estrogen receptor, progesterone\u000areceptor, and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu will be performed and reported in an addendum.\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aFIRST SURGICAL ADDENDUM REMOVED_DATE  DR. SUSAN LESTER\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for invasive carcinoma (block 1):\u000aEstrogen receptor NEGATIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor NEGATIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) NEGATIVE (0)\u000aNote: Normal epithelial cells are appropriately immunoreactive for estrogen\u000aand progesterone receptors.\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000ainvasive carcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but\u000aonly a portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity\u000ain >10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aSECOND SURGICAL ADDENDUM REMOVED_DATE  DR. SUSAN LESTER\u000aThe immunoperoxidase study for REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu was repeated with the same result.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 62 year old female with right breast mass.\u000aBreast Imaging Findings: Irregular.\u000aOperation: 11g U/S guided\u000aOperative findings: Solid nodule\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Cancer\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Right breast tissue (1 brown cassette)\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by BROWNE,TARA-JANE,MB,BCH,BAO\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit\u000anumber, and "right breast", in a light brown cassette, and consists of\u000amultiple, soft, fragmented, yellow to white tissue cores (1.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in\u000aaggregate).\u000aMicro 1: Multi frags, ESS.\u000akks\u000aReports to: SMITH, DARRELL, NOLAN M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY(IES)\u000a[report_end]
