 the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 73 year old female with a new ill-defined area of increased density\u000aRUOQ on mammo.\u000aBreast imaging findings: ill-defined.\u000aOperation: 14 g U/S breast core biopsy\u000aOperative findings: Multiple cores obtained\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Carcinoma vs other\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Multiple cores (1 yellow cassette)\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by CAI,YUN-CAI,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name and unit\u000anumber only, in a yellow cassette, and consists of multiple, soft, fragmented,\u000ayellow to white tissue cores (1.4 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate).\u000aMicro 1: Multi frags, ESS.\u000atr\u000aReports to: FROST, ELISABETH, PEPPERELL M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY(IES)\u000a[report_end]
