VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID LYMPH NODE BIOPSY\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aKRANE, JEFFREY, FRED, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by KRANE,JEFFREY FRED,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aRIGHT AXILLARY SENTINEL NODE "BLUE AND HOT":\u000aOne lymph node with no tumor seen (three levels examined).\u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED BIOPSY FOR A MASS:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA WITH LOBULAR AND DUCTAL FEATURES, well differentiated\u000a(modified Bloom-Richardson grade I/III), present as two foci (0.6 and\u000a< REMOVED_DATE cm; blocks REMOVED_DATE  and 11).\u000aThe larger focus is associated with the prior biopsy site.\u000aNo lymphovascular invasion is seen.\u000aThe smaller tumor focus (block 11) is present <0.1 cm from the anterior\u000amargin; all other margins are free of invasive carcinoma.\u000aEXTENSIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU is present in 10 of 10 blocks.\u000aNote: This carcinoma would be classified as AJCC REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDb pREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID MX with\u000amultiple foci of invasion.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, MEDIAL-INFERIOR SHAVE MARGIN:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA is present as a < REMOVED_DATE cm focus (block 12).\u000aNo lymphovascular invasion is seen.\u000aInvasive carcinoma is not present at the margin.\u000aEXTENSIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU is present in 10 of 15 blocks.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 73 year old postmenopausal female, not on hormones, whose REMOVED_DATE \u000amammogram demonstrated a right breast asymmetric density. A core biopsy on\u000a2/3/00 demonstrated an invasive carcinoma with ductal and lobular features.\u000aOperation: Right breast wire localized excision, sentinel node mapping with\u000apossible level I and II axillary dissection\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast cancer\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1) Right axillary sentinel node; blue and hot\u000a#2) Right breast tissue (short suture/superior; long suture/lateral; whip\u000asuture/