VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Amend/Addenda\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ISHA A MUSTAFA M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-05-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000a********** Addended Report ***********\u000aResident: Derek K Marsee, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Michelle S Hirsch, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "RIGHT BREAST, EXCISION"\u000aSUMMARY DIAGNOSIS:\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, SMALL FOCUS.\u000aSYNOPSIS:\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aTypes - solid, micropapillary\u000aNuclear grade - low to intermediate\u000aCalcifications in DCIS - absent\u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - present\u000aMicroinvasion (<0.1cm) - absent\u000aExtent of DCIS - REMOVED_DATE blocks (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID)\u000aFinal Margins (DCIS) - negative (all >0.3 cm)\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - absent\u000aOTHER FINDINGS\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia.\u000aColumnar alteration of lobules with prominent snouts and secretions.\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia.\u000aCalcifications associated with benign epithelium.\u000aCore biopsy site.\u000aAJCC CLASSIFICATION (6th edition) - Tis pNX MX\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER/PR/HER-2) - pending.\u000aThis case was reviewed by Dr. T. Ince (Breast Pathology Service), who concurs.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: None given.\u000aOperation: Right needle-directed excisional breast biopsy.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal mammo.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aRight needle-directed breast biopsy (to mammo) - sutures placed to hold\u000aspecimen back together: single short stitch - anterior; double long - lateral;\u000adouble short - medial.\u000aRADIOLOGY REPORT:\u000aWire, clip, and calcifications all in specimen.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient?s name, unit number,\u000aand "Needle-directed breast biopsy", and consists of a disrupted breast\u000aexcision specimen (5.6 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with a localization wire and three\u000aorienting sutures (single short stitch = anterior, double long = lateral,\u000adouble short = medial). The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the\u000aevaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red;\u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. An accompanying specimen\u000aradiograph demonstrates a localization wire, clip and calcifications within the\u000aspecimen. Specimen radiographs performed in the Department of Pathology\u000ademonstrate the clip localized to slice 3 and the calcifications in slices 4\u000aand 5. A biopsy site is identified (1.9 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), located REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000athe medial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin, and\u000a1.6 cm from the superior margin. The biopsy site is localized to slices 2\u000athrough 5. The specimen is entirely submitted for microscopic evaluation.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Inferior margin from slice 1, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Biopsy site in slice 2, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Biopsy site in slice 3 (containing clip), 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID+REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Contiguous sections containing biopsy site in slice 4, 1 frag\u000aeach, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID+REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Biopsy site in slice 5, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Superior margin from slice 6, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Anterior margin from slice 7, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Posterior and superior margins from slice 8, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Remainder of slice 1, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Remainder of slice 2, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Remainder of slice 3, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Remainder of slice 4, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID+REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Remainder of slice 5, REMOVED_DATE frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Remainder of slice 6, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Remainder of slice 7, REMOVED_DATE -1 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Remainder of slice 8, REMOVED_DATE -1-2 frags, ESS.\u000aDM/elw\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Michelle S Hirsch M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Michelle S Hirsch M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a11/8/2005\u000aSurgical Addendum: (11/10/05)\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) NEGATIVE (1+)\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000acarcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but only\u000aa portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in >10%\u000aof tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in\u000a>10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aAddendum by Andrea L Richardson M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aAddendum #1 by Andrea L Richardson M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a11/10/2005\u000a[report_end]
