VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID:REMOVED_CASE_ID Report Status: Signed\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aADDENDUM REPORT\u000aAddendum #1 Entered: REMOVED_DATE -0930\u000a*** ADDITIONAL DIAGNOSTIC INFORMATION ***\u000aThis report contains an addendum to the original for the purpose of providing\u000aadditional diagnostic information. The original diagnosis is unchanged.\u000aImmunohistochemical studies performed on block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID reveal the following results\u000afor the infiltrating carcinoma:\u000aEstrogen receptor: NEGATIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor: NEGATIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID): NEGATIVE for overexpression\u000aAddeundum Signed Electronically Signed FRASER,JEAN L. M.D. REMOVED_DATE \u000aDIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. Left axillary sentinel lymph node:\u000aNo evidence of malignancy in one lymph node (0/1).\u000aB. Left breast mass, excision:\u000aInfiltrating ductal carcinoma, three small foci.\u000aExtensive ductal carcinoma in situ, high nuclear grade; comedo,\u000acribriform, solid and clinging patterns with comedonecrosis and\u000acalcifications.\u000aApocrine metaplasia, cysts and florid usual intraductal hyperplasia.\u000aSee synoptic report.\u000aC. Left breast, lateral margin:\u000aDuctal carcinoma in situ, high nuclear grade, clinging pattern; focus\u000a4 mm. in size; present at the new inked margin, focal, and less than 1\u000amm. from the new inked margin, multifocal.\u000aD. Left breast, anterior margin:\u000aDuctal carcinoma in situ, high nuclear grade; solid, clinging and comedo\u000apatterns with comedonecrosis and calcifications; focus REMOVED_DATE mm. in size;\u000apresent REMOVED_DATE mm. from the new inked margin, focal.\u000aE. Left breast, superior margin:\u000aInfiltrating duct carcinoma, grade 3; focus 1 mm. in size; present\u000a1-2 mm. from the new inked margin, focal; no lymphatic/vascular\u000ainvasion identified.\u000aDuctal carcinoma in situ, high nuclear grade, solid and clinging\u000apatterns; foci up to 3 mm. in size; present less than 1 mm. from the\u000anew inked margin, focal.\u000aF. Left breast, medial margin:\u000aDuctal carcinoma in situ, high nuclear grade, solid and cribriform\u000apatterns; foci up to 7 mm. in size; present at the new inked margin,\u000afocal, and less than 1 mm. from the new inked margin, multifocal.\u000aG. Left breast, inferior margin:\u000aDuctal carcinoma in situ, high nuclear grade, solid and cribriform\u000apatterns; foci up to 7 mm. in size; present less than 1 mm. from the\u000anew inked margin, multifocal.\u000aH. Left breast, superior medial margin:\u000aDuctal carcinoma in situ, high nuclear grade, solid pattern; focus less\u000athan 1 mm. in size; present at the new inked margin, focal.\u000aSYNOPTIC REPORT: BREAST\u000aINVASIVE TUMOR:\u000a-histologic type: infiltrating ductal carcinoma\u000a-histologic grade: poorly differentiated\u000a-size (greatest dimension): three small foci up to REMOVED_DATE mm. in size (slide\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, two foci; and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID)\u000a-lymphatic/vascular invasion: none identified\u000a-perineural invasion: none identified\u000a-microcalcification: none identified\u000a-margins for invasive tumor: positive. Invasive tumor is present at the\u000aanterior margin, over a broad front, near the\u000ainferior aspect of the specimen. Invasive\u000atumor is present less than 1 mm. from the\u000ainferior margin, focal, near the lateral\u000aaspect of the specimen. Invasive tumor is\u000aalso present REMOVED_DATE mm., focal, from the new\u000ainked margin in the separately submitted\u000a"superior margin" (refer to Part E above).\u000a-immunohistochemical staining for estrogen and progesterone receptors and\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu will be performed on block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and reported in an addendum to\u000afollow.\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU (DCIS):\u000a-histologic type: comedo, cribriform, solid and clinging\u000apatterns with involvement of lobules\u000a-histologic grade: high nuclear grade\u000a-size (greatest dimension): REMOVED_DATE cm.; ductal carcinoma in situ is also\u000apresent in the separately submitted\u000amargin specimens (refer to Parts C-H\u000aabove)\u000a-extent: multifocal\u000a-extensive intraductal component: present\u000a-necrosis in DCIS: present, focal\u000a-microcalcifications in DCIS: present\u000a-margins for DCIS: positive. Ductal carcinoma in situ is\u000apresent at the lateral margin\u000a(multifocal), inferior margin\u000a(multifocal) and medial margin (focal).\u000aDuctal carcinoma in situ is present less\u000athan 1 mm. from the posterior margin\u000a(multifocal), superior margin (over a\u000abroad front) and anterior margin (over a\u000abroad front). Ductal carcinoma in situ\u000ais also present in the separately\u000asubmitted "lateral margin" (refer to Part\u000aC), "anterior margin" (refer to Part D),\u000a"superior margin" (refer to Part E),\u000a"medial margin" (refer to Part F),\u000a"inferior margin" (refer to Part G) and\u000a"superior medial margin" (refer to Part\u000aH).\u000aLYMPH NODES:\u000aThe one lymph node sampled is negative for malignancy (0/1)\u000a(0/1 sentinel lymph nodes).\u000aCOMMENT: The sentinel lymph node, specimen A, is examined at multiple\u000alevels with H&E stains and immunohistochemical stains for keratin.\u000aPRIOR RELATED SPECIMENS REVIEWED:\u000asite: left breast, upper outer quadrant, needle biopsy specimen #: S-05-REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000adate: REMOVED_DATE \u000aCOMMENT: Immunohistochemical stains for actin, calponin and smooth muscle\u000amyosin were performed to assist in the evaluation of the invasive\u000afoci in slides REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aAJCC pTNM Classification (6th Ed.): pREMOVED_ACCESSION_IDa pREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID(i-) pMX\u000aThe pathologic TNM classification above is based only on the information\u000aavailable to the pathologist, and therefore may not be accurate.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by: Jean L. Fraser, M.D.\u000aClinical diagnosis & history:\u000aLeft breast ductal carcinoma in situ; ? microinvasion\u000aTissue-Designation:\u000aA.Sentinel lymph node - left axillary\u000aB.Breast, excision with margins - left\u000aC.Breast, excision with margins - left, lateral margin\u000aD.Breast, excision with margins - left, anterior margin\u000aE.Breast, excision with margins - left, superior margin\u000aF.Breast, excision with margins - left, medial margin\u000aG.Breast, excision with margins - left, inferior margin\u000aH.Breast, excision with margins - left, superior medial margin\u000aGross description:\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin in eight containers.\u000aSpecimen A labeled "left axillary sentinel node" consists of a fragment of\u000aadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. It is bisected to reveal\u000aunremarkable adipose tissue. The entire specimen is submitted in cassette A.\u000a2X all.\u000aSpecimen B labeled "left breast mass" consists of a piece of fibrofatty breast\u000atissue measuring 4 x 2 x REMOVED_DATE cm. It is oriented with a long suture indicating\u000asuperior and a short suture indicating medial. A localization wire is in situ\u000aand emerges from the antero-lateral aspect of the specimen. The specimen is\u000ainked as follows: medial, orange; lateral, yellow; superior, blue; inferior,\u000agreen; anterior, black; posterior, red. The specimen is serially sectioned to\u000areveal fibrous and fatty parenchyma throughout. The entire specimen is\u000asubmitted in eight cassettes. 8X all.\u000aSpecimen C labeled "lateral left breast" consists of a piece of fibrofatty\u000atissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. A stitch marks the new margin side. The\u000anew margin side is inked black. The specimen is serially sectioned and\u000aentirely submitted in two cassettes. 5X all.\u000aSpecimen D labeled "anterior left breast" consists of a piece of fibrofatty\u000abreast tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. A stitch marks the new margin\u000aside. The new margin side is inked blue. The specimen is serially sectioned\u000aand submitted in two cassettes. 2 agg. all.\u000aSpecimen E labeled "superior left breast" consists of a piece of adipose tissue\u000ameasuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. A stitch marks the new margin side. The new\u000amargin side is inked black. The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal\u000afibrofatty tissue. The entire specimen is submitted in two cassettes. 7X all.\u000aSpecimen F labeled "medial left breast" consists of a fragment of fibrofatty\u000atissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. A stitch marks the new margin side. The\u000anew margin side is inked blue. The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal\u000afibrofatty parenchyma. The entire specimen is submitted in two cassettes. 7X\u000aall.\u000aSpecimen G labeled "inferior left breast" consists of a piece of fibrofatty\u000atissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. A stitch marks the new margin side. The\u000anew margin side is inked black. The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal\u000afibrofatty parenchyma. The entire specimen is submitted in two cassettes. 6X\u000aall.\u000aSpecimen H labeled "superior medial left breast" consists of a piece of\u000afibrofatty tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. A stitch marks the new margin\u000aside. The new margin side is inked blue. The specimen is serially sectioned\u000ato reveal fibrofatty parenchyma. In addition, a separate fragment of adipose\u000atissue is also identified measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The entire specimen is\u000asubmitted. 5X all.\u000aSection code: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - serially sectioned fragment marked with a stitch\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - separate fragment of adipose tissue\u000aDictated by: JLF____(signature on file)____DANIEL D. KOELLIKER, M.D. REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a____(signature on file)____ REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a[report_end]
