VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID:REMOVED_CASE_ID Report Status: Signed\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aDIAGNOSIS:\u000aLeft breast (358 gm.), simple mastectomy:\u000aDuctal carcinoma in situ, high grade, micropapillary and cribriform types\u000awith focal necrosis.\u000aChanges consistent with prior excision site.\u000aSkin with scar and nipple, free of tumor.\u000aSYNOPTIC REPORT:\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU (DCIS):\u000a-histologic type: micropapillary and cribriform types\u000a-histologic grade: high grade\u000a-size (greatest dimension): REMOVED_DATE cm. immediately adjacent to and around\u000aprior excision site\u000a-extent: multifocal\u000a-necrosis in DCIS: present, focal\u000a-microcalcifications in DCIS: none identified\u000a-margins for DCIS: clear (greater than or equal to REMOVED_DATE cm.)\u000aSKIN:\u000a-nipple: unremarkable\u000a-skin/dermis: scar\u000aADDITIONAL PATHOLOGIC FINDINGS:\u000aSmall fibroadenoma.\u000aChanges consistent with prior excision site.\u000aPRIOR RELATED SPECIMENS REVIEWED:\u000aLeft breast re-excision specimens, S-06-4458, REMOVED_DATE \u000aCOMMENT: There is no evidence of residual invasive carcinoma. See prior\u000aexcision specimens for TNM classification data.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by: Daniel D. Koelliker, M.D.\u000aClinical diagnosis & history:\u000aPositive margin after re-excision; left breast carcinoma\u000aTissue-Designation:\u000aBreast, simple mastectomy - left\u000aGross description:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled "left breast, stitch at 12 o'clock" and\u000aconsists of a 358 gram, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. simple mastectomy specimen marked\u000awith a suture oriented as 12 o'clock of the left breast. On the superficial\u000asurface, there is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. skin ellipse which has a REMOVED_DATE cm. in diameter\u000aareola with a central inverted REMOVED_DATE cm. nipple. Located approximately REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000afrom the nipple towards the 3 o'clock aspect of the specimen, there is a 3 cm.\u000along, healed linear scar on the skin surface. The margins throughout are\u000agrossly unremarkable and are inked black. On cross sectioning, the cut\u000asurface is mostly yellow lobulated adipose tissue with rubbery, thin strands of\u000awhite-tan fibrous tissue and focally rubbery fibrous areas. In the lateral\u000aaspect, there is an ill defined 1 x 1 x REMOVED_DATE cm. area of fat necrosis and\u000arubbery, firm fibrous tissue deep to the skin scar. No gross evidence of\u000asuspicious nodularity or tumor is seen in this area. The area of fat necrosis\u000aand fibrous tissue extends from the skin surface to the deep aspect.\u000aSection code: REMOVED_DATE - area of fat necrosis and fibrosis with deep margin and\u000aoverlying skin\u000a10-13 - representative sections from breast tissue surrounding\u000aarea of fat necrosis\u000a14-15 - random sections of lateral breast\u000a16-18 - nipple and central breast tissue\u000a19-22 - representative sections of medial breast tissue\u000aDictated by: DDK____(signature on file)____RICHARD SAMPSON, M.D. REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a____(signature on file)____DANIEL D. KOELLIKER, M.D. REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a[report_end]
