VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aBRODSKY, GILBERT, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by BRODSKY,GILBERT,M.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST, EXCISION FOR A MASS (specimen #1 of 4 specimens):\u000aDensely fibrous benign breast tissue.\u000aCore biopsy site.\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, SIMPLE MASTECTOMY (specimen #4 of 4 specimens), AND SENTINEL NODE\u000aBIOPSIES (specimens #2 and #3 of 4 specimens):\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU AND NEGATIVE LYMPH NODES\u000aSYNOPSIS:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA - not present\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU - present\u000aTypes - solid, cribriform, micropapillary,\u000aclinging\u000aNuclear grade - low\u000aCalcifications in DCIS - present\u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - present\u000aMicroinvasion (<0.1cm) - absent\u000aExtent of DCIS\u000aDCIS is extensive, involving three of four (3:4) quadrants\u000aFinal Margins (DCIS)\u000aNegative (>0.3 cm) - deep\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - absent\u000aLYMPH NODES\u000aSentinel Lymph Nodes - negative (3 H&E levels examined)\u000aNumber of positive nodes - 0\u000aNumber of nodes examined - 6\u000aTOTAL POSITIVE NODES (all specimens)- 0:6\u000aOTHER FINDINGS\u000aCore biopsy site\u000aSkin with scar\u000aFibroadenoma\u000aColumnar alteration of lobules with prominent snouts and secretions.\u000aAJCC CLASSIFICATION (6th edition) - Tis pREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID MX\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER/PR/HER-2) - pending\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: by RICHARDSON,ANDREA L.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for DCIS (block 8):\u000aEstrogen receptor - POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor - POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) - NEGATIVE (1+)\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000ainvasive carcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but\u000aonly a portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity\u000ain >10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 39-yer-old female status post core biopsies of the right breast for\u000aevaluation of diffuse calcifications revealing DCIS. Left breast core biopsy of\u000aa subareola nodule revealed fragments of a fibroadenoma.\u000aOperation: Right simple mastectomy with tissue expander reconstruction and left\u000abreast wire localization biopsy.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast cancer.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000a1. Left breast lump, clip not in specimen, please look for core biopsy track.\u000a2. Right sentinel node mapping (hot and blue).\u000a3. Right sentinel node mapping (hot not blue).\u000a4. Right breast, short stitch/superior, long/lateral, changes on core biopsy\u000asites.\u000aRADIOLOGY REPORT:\u000aSpecimen #1, clip not in specimen, OR called. (LBT)\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by HASKELL,HENRY D.,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in four parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart one, labeled "#1, left breast mass", is an unoriented, wire-localized\u000abreast\u000abiopsy (4.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The core biopsy tract cannot be distinguised for\u000acertain; however, a REMOVED_DATE cm track of disruption is noted and this could be core\u000abiopsy tract. The specimen is overall firm and white and consistent with\u000afibroadenoma.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  left breast mass, 4 frags, RSS.\u000aPart two, labeled "#2, right sentinel node mapping, hot and blue", is a\u000afragment of tan-yellow adipose tissue (3.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which is dissected\u000ato reveal two (2) sentinel lymph nodes (1.6 and REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest dimension,\u000aeach). They are entirely submitted.\u000aMicro 3: single lymph node, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro 4: 1 lymph node bisected, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aPart three, labeled "#3, right sentinel node, hot not blue", are three (3)\u000afragments of adipose tissue (1.7 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate). It is dissected\u000ato reveal 4 lymph nodes (largest - REMOVED_DATE cm). They are entirely submitted.\u000aMicro 5: 4 nodes, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aPart four, labeled "#4, right breast, short stitch/superior, long\u000astitch/lateral", is a 515 gram simple mastectomy specimen oriented with two (2)\u000astitches by the surgeon (21.5 cm from medial to lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm from inferior\u000ato superior, and REMOVED_DATE cm from anterior to posterior). The breast parenchyma is\u000aapproximately 40% fibrous tissue and 60% fat. REMOVED_DATE cm from the nearest deep\u000amargin is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm hemorrhagic cyst consistent with prior core\u000abiopsy site. (This is within the mid inferior breast). The fibrous breast\u000atissue is diffusely involved by a fine nodular process involving all four (4)\u000aquadrants of breast (approximate area 8 x 6 x REMOVED_DATE cm). No well-defined second\u000abiopsy cavity is seen; however, an ill-defined area of hemorrhage\u000a(approximately 3 x 3 x 2 cm) is noted in the inner and outer lower quadrant.\u000aThe specimen includes an ellipse of skin (11.0 x REMOVED_DATE cm) including nipple (1.2\u000acm). The skin is tan and wrinkled with unremarkable and two (2) prior biopsy\u000asites are indicated with ink Xs.\u000aMicro 6: nipple, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 7: skin indicated by more medial, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 8: skin and soft subcutaneous indicated by superior to nipple, 1 frag,\u000aRSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  biopsy cavity, 3 frags each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  2nd ? biopsy cavity, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000aMicro 16: upper outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 17: lower outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 18: lower inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 19: upper inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000ahdh\u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SENTINEL LYMPH NODE\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SENTINEL LYMPH NODE\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY - PARTIAL OR SIMPLE\u000a[report_end]
