VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID SENTINEL LYMPH NODE\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aBROWN, FELIX, MARCEL, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by BROWN,FELIX MARCEL,M.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST WIRE LOCALIZATION FOR A MASS AND SENTINEL NODE BIOPSY (INCLUDING\u000aFSA) (2 SPECIMENS):\u000aINVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA, DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, AND NEGATIVE LYMPH\u000aNODE.\u000aSYNOPSIS:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA\u000aSize - REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aMultifocal - No\u000aHistologic Type - Ductal with focal metaplastic\u000adifferentiation\u000aHistologic Grade (SBR) - III (Poor)\u000aNuclear Grade - Intermediate\u000aEIC - Negative\u000aLymphovascular invasion - Absent\u000aDermal lymphatic invasion - N/A\u000aSkin invasion - N/A\u000aSkeletal muscle invasion - N/A\u000aFinal Margins (invasive)\u000aNegative (>0.3 cm) - All margins\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU - Present\u000aTypes - Solid, Cribriform\u000aNuclear grade - Intermediate\u000aCalcifications in DCIS - Absent\u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - Present\u000aExtent of DCIS\u000aNumber of blocks/total: - REMOVED_DATE blocks\u000aFinal Margins (DCIS)\u000aNegative (>0.3 cm) - All margins\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - Absent\u000aLYMPH NODES\u000aSentinel lymp;h nodes (3 H&E levels examinez): - Negative\u000aNumber of positive nodes: - 0\u000aNumber of nodes examined: - 1\u000aTOTAL POSITIVE NODES (sentinel + axillary) - REMOVED_DATE \u000aAJCC CLASSIFICATION (6th edition): REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDc pREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID MX\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER/PR/HER-2) - see NOTE\u000aNOTE:\u000aImmunohistochemistry performed at BWH demonstrates the following staining\u000aprofile in tumor cells:\u000aNegative - ER, PR, TTF-1, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu, Synaptophysin, Chromogranin.\u000aLCA and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID stains were used in the evaluation of the sentinel node.\u000aThis case was also reviewed by Dr. J. Connolly, who concurs.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: See review @ BWH of HVMA core bx. Core REMOVED_DATE  LUOQ mass:\u000ainvasive ductal CA. NOTE: Dr. Susan Lester says primary looks like\u000asmall cell, ER (-), PR (-), Her2neu (-).\u000aOperation: Left sentinel node mapping and left mammographically directed\u000abiopsy.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast cancer.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Sentinel node (8920) - froz. section.\u000a2. Left needle loc. breast bx - mammo. Short stitch superior, long stitch\u000alateral. Inked per path protocol.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Specimen contains mass and wire. D. Green\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "1) SENTINEL NODE #1" (FSA):\u000aNegative for metastasis.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by KINDELBERGER,DAVID W.,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in two parts, ea ch labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart one, sublabeled "#1 sentinel node #1", consists of a single fragment of\u000apink/yellow fibroadipose tissue (2.9 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with a single pink/tan\u000alymph node (2.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The lymph node was bisected and entirely\u000asubmitted for frozen section analysis as FSA.\u000aMicro 1: sentinel node #1, bisected, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aPart two, sublabeled "#2 left needle localized breast biopsy", consists of a\u000asingle fragment of yellow/brown/tan fibroadipose tissue (8.8 cm from lateral to\u000amedial x REMOVED_DATE cm from anterior to posterior x REMOVED_DATE cm from superior to inferior).\u000aThere is a metal localizing wire embedded in the specimen. The specimen has\u000abeen inked in six colors by the surge per pathology protocol for the evaluation\u000aof margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior =\u000agreen; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. There is a firm, white, poorly\u000acircumscribed lesion (1.6 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) that comes to within REMOVED_DATE cm of the\u000asuperior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the anterior margin,\u000a1.3 cm of the posterior margin, approximately 2 cm from the lateral margin and\u000agreater than 5 cm from the medial margin. In the center of the lesion is a\u000aswell of hemorrhagic focus suggestive of a previous biopsy site. No other\u000alesions are grossly identified. The breast tissue is composed of approximately\u000a80% adipose and 20% fibrous tissue. An accompanying autoradiogram demonstrates\u000athe presence of a localizing wire and a mass within the specimen.\u000aRepresentative sections are submitted for histologic evaulation.\u000aMicro 2. lesion and posterior margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 3: lesion and superior margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 4: lesion and anterior margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 5: lesion and inferior margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 6: lesion, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 7: medial margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 8: additional posterior margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 9: additional superior margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 10: additional anterior margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 11: additional inferior margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 12: lateral margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000adk\u000aReports to: CARTER, KATHARINE M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: SENTINEL LYMPH NODE\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
