VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Amend/Addenda\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: BRENT T SHOJI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000a********** Addended Report ***********\u000aResident: Matthias D. Hofer, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Jonathan N Glickman, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA) RIGHT BREAST, EXCISION:\u000aINVASIVE TUBULAR CARCINOMA, well differentiated (modified Bloom-Richardson\u000agrade I/III), measuring REMOVED_DATE cm, associated with biopsy site changes. (See\u000aNOTE).\u000aNo lymphovascular invasion is present.\u000aNo in situ carcinoma is present.\u000aMargins are negative for tumor.\u000aAJCC Classification (6th Edition): pREMOVED_ACCESSION_IDa NX Mx\u000aNOTE: Immunostain for p63/CK REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/3 was performed. It shows absence of\u000amyoepithelial cells in the neoplastic glands, supporting the above diagnosis.\u000aImmunohistochemical analysis for estrogen receptor, progesterone receptor, and\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu will be performed and reported in an addendum.\u000aThis case and the prior biopsy (BS-07-REMOVED_CASE_ID) have been reviewed by Dr. Andrea\u000aRichardson, Dr. Susan Lester, and Dr. Michael W. Bennett, of the breast\u000apathology service.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Abnormal core Bx - ? radial scar.\u000aOperation: Right needle localization biopsy short stitch superior, long stitch\u000alateral.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal R mammogram.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA. Site not specified.\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000aDensity + distortion, clip + hookwires x2 - in specimen. Called Dr. Shoji.\u000a(no Radiologist's signature)\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name and unit number\u000aonly, consists of an ovoid fragment of yellow/tan to pink/tan fibroadipose\u000atissue (6.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which is oriented per surgeon with two sutures:\u000aShort equals superior and long equals lateral. The specimen is inked per\u000apathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black;\u000aanterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange.\u000aThe anterior aspect of the specimen exhibits a tan wrinkled skin ellipse (3.3 x\u000a1.0 cm) with no discrete lesions identified. There are two needle localization\u000awires in place. The more superior wire enters the anterior soft tissue margin\u000awith no clear exit point, and the more inferior wire enters the skin with no\u000aclear exit point. The specimen was previously radiographed (per radiologist\u000a"density and distortion, clip and hook wires x2 in specimen. Called to Dr.\u000aShoji"). The specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral to exhibit\u000aa central somewhat delineated friable red/pink hemorrhagic lesion (1.4 x REMOVED_DATE x\u000a0.9 cm), traversed by both needle localization wires. The mass comes to within\u000a0.6 cm of the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the\u000aposterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the anterior/skin margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the lateral\u000amargin, and REMOVED_DATE cm of the medial margin. A small metal clip is identified\u000awithin the parenchyma adjacent to the mass as consistent with prior core biopsy\u000aprocedure. The remainder of the cut surface is composed of approximately 20%\u000adense/nodular white/tan fibrous stroma and 80% yellow/tan lobulated adipose\u000atissue with no additional discrete lesions identified.\u000aRepresentative sections to include the mass in entirety are submitted as\u000afollows:\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, perpendicularly sectioned, 3 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Mass sequentially submitted from lateral to medial with closest\u000ainferior and superior margin, 1 frag in each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Posterior margin closest to mass, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Anterior/skin margin closest to mass, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin perpendicularly sectioned, 3 frags, RSS.\u000aPlease note approximately 30% of the specimen is submitted.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aLMB/ajb\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jonathan N Glickman M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a5/18/2007\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: (5/18/07)\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for invasive carcinoma (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE - LOW\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) NEGATIVE (1+)\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000ainvasive carcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low > 0% - < 10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor cells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but only a\u000aportion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+):Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in >10% of\u000atumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+):Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in >30% of\u000atumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aExternal controls are evaluated and show appropriate Immunoreactivity.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aAddendum #1 by Andrea L Richardson M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a5/18/2007\u000a[report_end]
