VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aBRODSKY, GILBERT, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by BRODSKY,GILBERT,M.D.\u000a1) "RIGHT BREAST PARTIAL MASTECTOMY AND CHEST WALL", RESECTION:\u000aMETASTATIC EPITHELIOID NEOPLASM consistent with patient's known\u000aMESOTHELIOMA (see NOTE), predominantly in subcutis, with focal extension\u000ainto breast parenchyma.\u000aExcision margins are multifocally positive for tumor.\u000a2) "DEEP NODULE", EXCISION:\u000aBreast tissue with no significant pathologic change.\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy.\u000a3) "RIGHT AXILLARY SCAR", EXCISION:\u000aSkin with cicatrix, with fat necrosis and foreign body giant cell\u000areaction.\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy.\u000a4) "RIGHT AXILLARY LEVEL II MASS", EXCISION:\u000aMETASTATIC MESOTHELIOMA, within lymph nodes.\u000a5) "RIGHT AXILLARY LEVEL 1 NODULES", EXCISION:\u000aMETASTATIC MESOTHELIOMA, within lymph nodes (see NOTE).\u000aThere is extranodal extension into perinodal soft tissue, with matting of\u000alarge nodes, precluding a precise count.\u000a6) "RIGHT AXILLARY LATERAL MASS", EXCISION:\u000aOne (1) lymph node with no significant pathologic change.\u000aAxillary fat with hemorrhage.\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy.\u000aNOTE: Immunohistochemical studies were done previously.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: An 81 year old female s/p REMOVED_DATE right anterolateral chest wall\u000aresection and pleurectomy for treatment for mesothelioma. On REMOVED_DATE excision of\u000achest wall recurrence (4.5 cm) and axillary recurrence (7.0 cm). Right breast\u000a3:00 axis a 3 cm mass s/p a REMOVED_DATE core biopsy revealing mesothelioma and right\u000aaxillary mass with cytology demonstrating cells consistent with recurrent\u000amesothelioma.\u000aOperation: Right breast and axillary excision\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Recurrent mesothelioma\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1) Right breast partial mastectomy and chest wall resection\u000a#2) Deep nodule\u000a#3) Right axillary scar\u000a#4) Right axillary level II mass\u000a#5) Right axillary level I nodule\u000a#6) Right axillary lateral mass\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by LIN,JONATHAN H.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in six parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart one, labeled "#1. right breast partial mastectomy and chest wall\u000aresection", and consists of a single core biopsy specimen\u000athat measures 3 x 4 x REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest dimension with an associated skin\u000aellipse that measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm and is located on blue\u000ainked surface of the specimen. The specimen is inked by the surgeon per\u000apathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior\u000a= blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange.\u000aWithin this breast biopsy specimen there is a hard white nodule that measures\u000a0.9 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. This nodule appears to approach to within REMOVED_DATE cm of the\u000ablack inked deep margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the green inked margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000aoverlying skin ellipse, REMOVED_DATE cm from the blue inked margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000ared inked margin. The mass appears to be more than 1 cm from yellow and orange\u000ainked margins. Tissue closest to the mass from all six margins are submitted\u000afor analysis.\u000aMicro 1: mass nearest black inked margin, 2 frags, RSS\u000aMicro 2: mass nearest blue inked margin with skin, 2 frags, RSS\u000aMicro 3: mass nearest red inked margin, 2 frags, RSS\u000aMicro 4: mass nearest green inked margin, 3 frags, RSS\u000aMicro 5: mass nearest yellow inked margin, 2 frags, RSS\u000aMicro 6: mass nearest orange inked margin, 2 frags, RSS\u000aPart two, labeled "#2. deep nodule", consists of one fragment of white/tan soft\u000atissue that measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The specimen is entirely submitted\u000afor histologic analysis.\u000aMicro 7: deep nodule fragment, 1 frag, ESS\u000aPart three, labeled "#3. right axillary scar", consists of one fragment of\u000ayellow/tan soft tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm with an attached skin\u000aellipse that measures 3 cm in width x REMOVED_DATE cm in length. There is a scar\u000arunning along the length of the skin ellipse that measures 3 cm. The specimen\u000ais entirely submitted for histologic analysis.\u000aMicro 8: right axillary scar tissue, 1 frag, ESS\u000aPart four, labeled "#4. right axillary level II mass", consists of multiple\u000afragments of white/tan soft tissue, the largest two fragments measure REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000ax REMOVED_DATE cm; and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. Representative cross-sections of these\u000anodules and masses are submitted for analysis.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  right axillary level II mass, 4 frags, RSS\u000aPart five, labeled "#5. right axillary level I nodules", consists of multiple\u000afragments of nodular yellow/brown/red soft tissue. The largest nodule measures\u000a2.5 x 2 x REMOVED_DATE cm, the next largest nodule measures 1 x 1 x REMOVED_DATE cm. The\u000aremaining soft tissue measures 1 x 1 x REMOVED_DATE cm. Representative sections are\u000asubmitted for histologic analysis.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  right axillary level I nodules, 6 frags, ESS\u000aPart six, labeled "#6. right axillary lateral mass", consists of one fragment\u000aof yellow/tan soft tissue that measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest\u000adimension. No specific nodules are identified within the soft tissue. The\u000aspecimen is entirely submitted for histologic analysis.\u000aMicro 13: tissue from right axillary lateral mass, 1 frag, ESS\u000ajhl\u000aReports to: KAELIN, CAROLYN, MARY M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SKIN- OTHER THAN CYST, TAG OR DEBRIDEMENT\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: LYMPH NODE BIOPSY\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: LYMPH NODES REGIONAL RESECTION\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: LYMPH NODE BIOPSY\u000a[report_end]
