ed from medial to lateral.\u000aMicro 1: medial margin, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 2: whorled lesion, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  specimen submitted medial to laterally, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro 11&12: sections at the same level, superior margin in #12, 1 frag each,\u000aESS.\u000aMicro 13&14: sections through the same level, superior and lateral margin at\u000a#14, REMOVED_DATE frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 15: lateral margin, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aPart two, "left breast mass x2, short superior, long lateral", consists of a\u000aportion of breast tissue (5.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with a cleft down the middle from\u000ainferior to superior. The specimen grossly has the appearance of two masses\u000a(one mass posterior is REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm with surrounding breast tissue and\u000aanteriorly is REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The posterior mass appears to be firmer and inked\u000aper pathology protocol - posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red;\u000ainferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. The entire specimen is\u000asubmitted from anterior to superior.\u000aMicro 16: anterior margin, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  anterior mass, from anterior to posterior, medial margin is in\u000a#18-21; lateral margin in #22&23, REMOVED_DATE frags each, ESS.\u000aThe posterior mass contains REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm, tan whorled nodule consistent\u000agrossly with a fibroadenoma. It is well encapsulated and completely excised.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  posterior mass, deep margin in #27, REMOVED_DATE frags each, RSS.\u000amrk\u000aReports to: MATORY, YVEDT, L. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST BIOPSY W/O MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST BIOPSY W/O MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
