VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aWELCH, WILLIAM, ROBERT, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by WELCH,WILLIAM ROBERT,M.D.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, LOWER INNER QUADRANT, WIRE LOCALIZED BIOPSY FOR AN ILL-DEFINED\u000aMASS AND A CLIP:\u000aINVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA, moderately differentiated (modified\u000aBloom-Richardson grade II/III), adjacent to the prior biopsy site.\u000aNo lymphovascular invasion is seen.\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, cribriform type (low nuclear grade) with\u000acalcifications, is present as a minor component of the invasive carcinoma\u000a(EIC negative). No necrosis is present.\u000aThe invasive carcinoma is not present at the margin. The closest margin\u000ais inferior (0.2 cm). DCIS is not present at the margin. The closest\u000amargin is inferior (0.4 cm).\u000aSkeletal muscle is present and is not involved.\u000aNote: The carcinoma measures REMOVED_DATE cm in this specimen, but is adjacent to\u000athe biopsy site. In the prior core needle biopsy the carcinoma measured\u000a0.7 cm.\u000aRIGHT SENTINEL NODE BIOPSY:\u000aOne lymph node with no tumor seen (3 H&E levels examined).\u000aNote: The right breast carcinoma would be classified as AJCC REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDb pREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID MX.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, UPPER OUTER QUADRANT, WIRE LOCALIZED BIOPSY FOR AN IRREGULAR\u000aMASS:\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aDCIS is < REMOVED_DATE cm from the margin (unoriented).\u000aSkeletal muscle is present and is not involved.\u000a(SUBMIT ALL THE TISSUE)\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: by WELCH,WILLIAM ROBERT,M.D.\u000aPart 3 was entirely submitted for histologic examination.\u000aThe diagnosis remains unchanged.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Two mammographic lesions:\u000a1. Right lower inner REMOVED_DATE cm ill-defined mass. Prior core needle biopsy of\u000athis area revealed an invasive carcinoma.\u000a2. Right upper outer REMOVED_DATE cm irregular mass.\u000aOperation: Needle localized wide excision right breast biopsy site and sentinel\u000alymph node biopsy\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Invasive carcinoma right breast\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1) Right breast biopsy site medial\u000a#2) Sentinel node right breast\u000a#3) Right breast biopsy site lateral\u000aRADIOLOGY: #1. Density in specimen. Dr. Leung\u000a#2. Density in specimen next to wire, consistent with lesion. Dr. Frost\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by HENDERSON,JOEL M.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in three parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart one, labeled "#1. right breast biopsy site", consists of a single fragment\u000aof tan/yellow fibroadipose tissue (8.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The specimen arrives\u000aaccompanied by a whole specimen radiograph, which shows a localization wire in\u000aplace, marking a central small density, and an adjacent localization clip. The\u000aspecimen itself arrives marked with a localization wire and has been previously\u000ainked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior = black;\u000aanterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial =\u000aorange. Within the specimen is a firm, tan, spiculated tumor mass (0.6 x REMOVED_DATE x\u000a0.5 cm), that comes to within REMOVED_DATE cm of the inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm of the superior,\u000a1.5 cm of the posterior, REMOVED_DATE cm of the anterior, REMOVED_DATE cm of the medial, and\u000a4.0 cm of the lateral margin. Associated with this small mass is a track with\u000asurrounding fat necrosis, consistent with prior biopsy site. At the opposite\u000aaspect of the specimen, is an area of unremarkable tan/gray firm fibrous tissue\u000a(1.5 x REMOVED_DATE cm), approaching the lateral and superior margins. The remainder of\u000athe specimen consists of unremarkable lobulated yellow adipose tissue with\u000aintervening strands of fibrous tissue. The specimen is sectioned from medial\u000ato lateral, and representative sections are submitted.\u000aMicro 1: medial margin, 2 frags, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  slice 4, 2 frags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  slice 5, including mass and possible biopsy tract, 3 frags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  portions of slices 6 and 7 including firm fibrous area, 2 frags,\u000aRSS\u000aMicro 9: lateral margin, 2 frags, RSS\u000aPart two, labeled "#2. sentinel node right breast", consists of a single\u000afragment of tan/yellow fibroadipose tissue (1.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). Possible\u000alymphoid tissue is identified. The specimen is bisected and entirely\u000asubmitted.\u000aMicro 10; sentinel node right breast, 2 frags, ESS\u000aPart three, labeled "#3. right breast biopsy site lateral", consists of a\u000asingle fragment of tan/yellow fibroadipose tissue (6 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The\u000aspecimen is accompanied by a whole specimen radiograph, which shows a\u000alocalization wire in place with a vague density identified in association\u000awith the localization wire. There are possible cystic lesions identified\u000athat are not associated with the localization wire. The specimen itself also\u000acontains a localization wire, and is unoriented. Centrally in the specimen,\u000athere is a region of dense fibrosity (2 x 1 x REMOVED_DATE cm), but no suspicious\u000alesions are identified in the specimen that consists of yellow lobulated\u000aadipose tissue. Representative sections (approximately 75% of the specimen)\u000aare submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  right breast biopsy site lateral aspect, 2 frags each, RSS\u000ajmh\u000aReports to: OSTEEN, ROBERT, T. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SENTINEL LYMPH NODE\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN\u000a[report_end]
