ntral inner portion of the breast, REMOVED_DATE cm from the nearest deep soft\u000atissue margin (inked black). There is a biopsy cavity (3.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm)\u000alocated in the central outer quadrant, within REMOVED_DATE cm from the nearest deep soft\u000atissue margin. This cavity is greater than REMOVED_DATE cm away from the lesion of\u000afibrosis. A biopsy cavity (4 x 4 x 2 cm) is located in the lower inner\u000aquadrant (> 1 cm from the deep margin). Eight lymph nodes are identified and\u000aare completely sampled.\u000aMicro 1: nipple, areola, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 2: skin with scar, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  areas of fibrosis near the central inner quadrant, 8 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  biopsy cavity, central outer quadrant, 7 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 18: upper inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 19: lower inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 20: upper outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 21: lower outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  lower inner quadrant biopsy site, mult frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  eight lymph nodes, mult frags, ESS.\u000aqqd\u000aReports to: OSTEEN, ROBERT, T. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY W/REGIONAL LYMPH NODES\u000a[report_end]
