VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ROGER L CHRISTIAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Scott Lovitch, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Robert D Odze, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aSPECIMEN DESIGNATED "RIGHT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A MASS AND A\u000aCLIP":\u000aBenign breast tissue with healing biopsy cavity.\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia, usual type, focal.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of this\u000aspecimen, including margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Bx's elsewhere inconclusive (read here).\u000aOperation: Wire directed excision.\u000aOperative Findings: See op note: "inked per protocol" but discrepancy.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Density Rt breast.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Right breast tissue to FS for mammo\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000aCalled to Dr. Christian in OR. Density, clip and hookwire in specimen\u000aradiograph. Odulate REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "1. Right breast tissue", and consists of an ovoid fragment of yellow/tan\u000afibroadipose tissue (3.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The specimen is received fixed inked\u000aper surgeon, according to the op note "per protocol". However, a discrepancy\u000ain the standard pathology inking protocol is identified upon receipt of the\u000aspecimen in the pathology cutting room. Via phone conversation on REMOVED_DATE \u000awith Dr. Roger Christian, the red inked surface can be interpreted as the true\u000asuperior margin and the green inked surface can be interpreted as the true\u000ainferior margin based on the presence of a needle localization wire entering\u000athe red inked surface and exiting the green inked surface. Dr. Christian\u000acannot confirm the true orientation of the blue, black, orange, and yellow\u000ainked surfaces. The specimen does not exhibit any sutures or orientation.\u000aThe specimen was previously radiographed, confirming the presence of a clip and\u000aan intact needle localization wire within the specimen. The specimen is\u000aserially sectioned from the red inked superior margin to the green inked\u000ainferior margin. In the central to inferior aspect of the specimen, there is\u000aan ill-defined firm/gritty tan/pink focally hemorrhagic lesion (0.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm), REMOVED_DATE cm from the orange inked surface, REMOVED_DATE cm from the yellow inked\u000asurface, REMOVED_DATE cm from the black inked surface, REMOVED_DATE cm from the blue inked\u000asurface, REMOVED_DATE cm from the green inked/inferior margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the red\u000ainked superior margin. A small metal clip is identified adjacent to the\u000aaforementioned lesion, REMOVED_DATE cm from the orange inked surface. The needle\u000alocalization wire traverses the lesion.\u000aThe remainder of the cut surface is composed of greater than 90% yellow/tan\u000alobulated adipose tissue and less than 10% delicate white/tan fibrous tissue.\u000aNo additional lesions are identified.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Red ink/superior margin perpendicularly sectioned, multi frags\u000atotal, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Central specimen with lesion in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID (clip site in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), 1 frag in\u000aeach, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Green inked inferior margin perpendicularly sectioned, multi frags,\u000aESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-08-REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aLMB/ajb\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Robert D Odze M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
