n blocks REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aAJCC pTNM Classification (6th Ed.): pTis pNX pMX\u000aThe pathologic TNM classification above is based only on the information\u000aavailable to the pathologist, and therefore may not be accurate.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by: Todd E. Abbott, M.D.\u000aClinical diagnosis & history:\u000aLeft breast carcinoma\u000aTissue-Designation:\u000aA.Breast, excision with margins - left\u000aB.Breast, excision with margins - left, medial margin\u000aGross description:\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin in two containers.\u000aSpecimen A labeled "left breast mass" consists of a 28 gram, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm. lumpectomy specimen with the following orienting sutures: long stitch =\u000alateral, short stitch = superior. The greatest dimension of this specimen is\u000afrom medial to lateral. Received with this specimen is a radiograph\u000ademonstrating a needle localization wire entering from the lateral aspect and\u000aterminating near the mid portion. There is a single surgical clip and numerous\u000acalcifications near the needle tip. The specimen is inked in the following\u000amanner: lateral = yellow, medial = blue, superior = red, inferior = green,\u000aanterior = black, posterior = orange. The specimen is sectioned from lateral\u000ato medial revealing yellow lobular tissue. The specimen is submitted entirely\u000afrom lateral to medial in cassettes REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. 13 agg.\u000aSpecimen B labeled "left breast medial margin" consists of a 16 gram, REMOVED_DATE x 4 x\u000a2.0 cm. flat disc of yellow lobulated adipose tissue with one stitch on one\u000abroad surface indicating the new medial margin. This surface is inked blue.\u000aThe specimen is serially sectioned and submitted entirely in cassettes REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000a8 agg. all.\u000aDictated by: TEA____(signature on file)____MICHAEL J. ROSS, M.D. REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a____(signature on file)____ REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a[report_end]
