VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aLESTER, SUSAN, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZATION FOR A CLIP MARKING AN AREA OF BIOPSIED\u000aCALCIFICATIONS:\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, solid type (low nuclear grade) is present in\u000aone of 18 blocks (block 13; levels examined, best seen in deeper levels).\u000aThe DCIS occupies an area measuring REMOVED_DATE cm. No necrosis, calcifications,\u000aor crystalloids are seen.\u000aDCIS is < REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin.\u000aSeverely atypical ductal hyperplasia, associated with crystalloids, with\u000acautery artifact, is < REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin (block 19). This\u000aarea may be an another area of DCIS, but cannot be further evaluated due\u000ato the cautery artifact. This focus is adjacent to the prior biopsy site.\u000aAnother focus of atypical ductal hyperplasia is present REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000ainferior margin (block 15; levels examined).\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia is present.\u000aA biopsy site is present.\u000aNote: The DCIS in block 13 is not immediately adjacent to the biopsy\u000asite.\u000aDr. James Connolly reviewed the slides from block 13 and concurs with the\u000adiagnosis.\u000aThis carcinoma would be classified as AJCC Tis NX MX.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: None given.\u000aOperation: Right needle localized breast biopsy\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal mammogram\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1. Needle localized breast biopsy right breast\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by BAILEY,GERALD P.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number\u000aand "#1. needle localized breast biopsy right breast", and consists of a breast\u000aspecimen (11 x 6 x 5 cm) with one wire and clip.\u000aThe specimen radiograph reveals a localization wire and a clip in an area of\u000acalcifications.\u000aThe specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins:\u000aposterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral =\u000ayellow; medial = orange. The specimen is serially sectioned into five slices\u000aand radiographed. The wire and clip are localized. The prior biopsy cavity\u000a(1.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) is located near the posterior inferior margin. All of the\u000afibrous tissue is submitted for microscopic examination.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  biopsy cavity with posterior and lateral margins, 1 frag each, ESS\u000aMicro 3: closest medial margin, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 4: closest superior margin, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 5: closest inferior margin, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 6: closest anterior margin, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 7: anterior margin, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 8: biopsy cavity, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 9: medial and superior margin, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 10: lateral margin, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 11: posterior margin, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  remainder of fibrous tissue, mult frags, ESS.\u000ageb\u000aReports to: SHOJI, BRENT, T. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
