VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast core needle biopsy\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: SUGHRA RAZA M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Matthias D. Hofer, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Deborah A Dillon, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, 9:30, 14 G ULTRASOUND GUIDED CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR A REMOVED_DATE CM\u000aMASS:\u000aFIBROEPITHELIAL LESION (see note).\u000aNOTE: The biopsy shows a stromal lesion with prominent myofibroblasts and\u000apseudoangiomatous stromal hyperplasia. Although there is no definitive stromal\u000aovergrowth, there is increased cellularity particularly in the subepithelial\u000aregion and some nuclear atypia. Mitotic figures are evident. The differential\u000adiagnosis includes a cellular fibroadenoma or a low-grade phyllodes tumor. This\u000alesion would be characterized best following excision.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, 9:30, 14 G ULTRASOUND GUIDED CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR A REMOVED_DATE CM\u000aIRREGULAR MASS:\u000aBreast tissue with pseudoangiomatous stromal hyperplasia (see note).\u000aNOTE: The biopsy of the smaller mass shows pseudoangiomatous stromal\u000ahyperplasia and prominent myofibroblasts. Although nuclear atypia is minimal\u000aand no mitotic figures are seen, histologic features are otherwise similar to\u000athose seen in the biopsy of the larger mass and likely represent the same\u000aprocess. By report, the two masses are adjacent to one another. This area would\u000abe evaluated best following excision.\u000aSlides seen also by Dr. Susan Lester, who concurs.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHISTORY: 24 y/o woman with palpable right breast mass.\u000aBREAST IMAGING FINDING:\u000a1. Right: 15-mm, palpable and circumscribed/lobulated mass.\u000a2. Right: 6-mm, nonpalpable, irregular mass.\u000aLOCATION:\u000a1. Right: 9:30\u000a2. Right: 9:30\u000aTYPE OF CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY:\u000a1. 14G Ultrasound\u000a2. 14G Ultrasound\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Four (4) in formalin at 10:55 a.m. - Green cassette.\u000aB/2. Four (4) in formalin at 11:25 a.m. - Brown cassette.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, in two parts, each labeled with the\u000apatient's name and unit number.\u000aPart A, labeled "Right breast type 1", and consists of a green cassette labeled\u000a"Right", containing multiple cylindrical focally hemorrhagic fibrofatty soft\u000atissues (1.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate). The specimen is submitted in toto.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Contents of green cassette labeled "right", multi frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, labeled "Right breast type 2", and consists of a brown cassette labeled\u000a"Right", which contains multiple cylindrical focally hemorrhagic fibrofatty\u000asoft tissues (1.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate). The specimen is submitted in\u000atoto.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Contents of brown cassette labeled "Right", multi frags total, ESS.\u000aJenC/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Deborah A Dillon M.D., Electronically signed on Tuesday\u000aREMOVED_MONTH 14, 2009 at 02:31:22PM\u000a[report_end]
