VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: MEHRA GOLSHAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Elgida Radoncipi, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Alessandra F Nascimento, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. LEFT BREAST TISSUE, WIRE LOCALIZATION BIOPSY FOR A CLIP:\u000aBreast parenchyma with calcifications in association with benign\u000aepithelium.\u000aPseudoangiomatous stromal hyperplasia.\u000aColumnar cell changes.\u000aBiopsy site changes.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the\u000aspecimen, including margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 47 yo F with left breast abnormal mammogram, core biopsy with\u000adiscordant result with imaging\u000aOperation: Left breast wire-localized excisional biopsy\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast abnormal mammogram\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Left breast wire-localized biopsy (short suture/superior,\u000along suture/lateral)\u000aRADIOLOGY COMMENT:\u000aTargeted clip/?mass in specimen. Wire intact. Called to Dr. Golshan by\u000a[illegible] at 2:30 pm.\u000a[no signature]\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "left breast wire localized excisional biopsy short suture superior long\u000alateral", consists of an irregular tan/yellow lobulated portion of fibroadipose\u000abreast tissue (4.0 cm medial to lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm anterior to posterior, and REMOVED_DATE \u000acm superior to inferior) with a short suture designating the superior margin,\u000aand a long suture designating the lateral margin. The needle localization wire\u000ais received free floating and not within the specimen. The specimen is inked\u000aper pathology protocol (superior red, inferior green, medial orange, lateral\u000ayellow, anterior blue, and posterior black), and is serially sectioned from\u000amedial to lateral. The cut surface is tan/yellow and homogeneous with focal\u000aareas of dense white fibrous tissue constituting approximately 30% of the\u000abreast parenchyma. Within the fibrous tissue is an irregular red/brown\u000ahemorrhagic area consistent with previous biopsy site (0.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm),\u000awhich comes within REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE \u000acm from the lateral margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin. No discrete\u000alesions are grossly identified. The specimen is serially sectioned and\u000asubmitted in its entirety.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross sections medial to lateral, block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID to\u000ainclude biopsy cavity, block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID to include metallic biopsy clip, 1 frag each,\u000aESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, 3 frags, ESS.\u000asek\u005cpab\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Alessandra F Nascimento M.D., Electronically signed on\u000aWednesday August 26, 2009 at 11:12:55AM\u000a[report_end]
