VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Li Chen, M.D., Ph.D.; Stephanie Schulte, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Jane E. Brock, M.B., B.S., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A MASS AND CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, solid type (low nuclear grade) without necrosis or\u000acalcifications is present (1 of 7 blocks; see Note)\u000aDCIS is REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID levels REMOVED_DATE ).\u000aOther findings:\u000aColumnar cell change with cysts, calcifications and flat epithelial atypia.\u000aFibroadenomatoid change and adenosis.\u000aBiopsy site changes are present.\u000aCalcifications associated with normal breast epithelium.\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for carcinoma (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) NEGATIVE (1+)\u000aA p63/REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID double immunohistochemical stain highlights intact myoepithelial\u000acells around the neoplastic ducts.\u000aNOTE: The focus of DCIS has a predominantly solid pattern with focal\u000acribriforming present, and spans an area of REMOVED_DATE cm in total (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID levels\u000a2-11). Dr. Susan Lester has also reviewed the slides and agrees with the\u000ainterpretation as DCIS.\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000acarcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but only\u000aa portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in >10%\u000aof tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in\u000a>10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 36 year old premenopausal woman, s/p REMOVED_DATE  R breast core biopsies\u000arevealing epithelial hyperplasia with atypia features, involving fibroadenoma -\u000aexc recommended\u000aOperation: R brest WL bx\u000aOperative Findings: Not provided\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Not provided\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Rt breast tissue (short stitch/superior; long stitch/lateral;\u000awhip stitch/chest wall margin)\u000aRADIOLOGY COMMENT:\u000aMass, Ca++, intact wire in specimen. D/W Dr. Rhei by Dr. Lizer, at 10:35 am.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "right breast tissue short stitch superior, long stitch lateral, whip\u000astitch deep margin", and consists of an irregular tan/yellow lobulated portion\u000aof fibroadipose breast tissue (3.4 cm medial to lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm superior to\u000ainferior, and REMOVED_DATE cm anterior to posterior) with a short suture designating\u000asuperior margin, long suture designating lateral margin, and whipstitch\u000adesignating the posterior/chest wall margin. There is a needle localization\u000awire in place which enters through the lateral superior aspect of the specimen\u000aand exits through the inferior aspect of the specimen. The specimen has been\u000apreviously inked per the surgeon (superior red, inferior green, medial orange,\u000alateral yellow, anterior blue, and posterior black) and is serially sectioned\u000afrom medial to lateral. The cut surface is tan and homogeneous with focal\u000aareas of dense white fibrous tissue constituting approximately 70% of the\u000abreast parenchyma. No discrete lesions are grossly identified. The specimen\u000ais submitted in its entirety.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross sections medial to lateral, 1 frag each, blocks\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID to include possible area of calcification per specimen radiograph with no\u000adistinct mass grossly identified, multiple frags ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000asek\u005cpab\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jane E. Brock M.B., B.S., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000aFriday REMOVED_MONTH 16, 2009 at 10:18:40AM\u000a[report_end]
