VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Consult material\u000aProcedure Date:\u000aOrdering Provider: NANCY U LIN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Dominique P. Coco, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Deborah A Dillon, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aCONSULT SLIDES FROM FAULKNER HOSPITAL, BOSTON, MA:\u000aRIGHT AND LEFT BREASTS, MASTECTOMIES (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID; REMOVED_DATE ):\u000aLEFT BREAST, MASTECTOMY (A):\u000aBy report, excision site changes with multifocal ATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA.\u000aBy report, one lymph node with no carcinoma seen (0/1).\u000aRIGHT BREAST, MASTECTOMY S/P NEOADJUVANT CHEMOTHERAPY (B):\u000aINVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA, moderately differentiated (modified\u000aBloom-Richardson grade II/III), present in six of six slides received for\u000areview (see note).\u000aNo lymphovascular invasion is identified.\u000aExtensive CARCINOMA IN SITU with predominantly lobular features is present.\u000aInvasive carcinoma is present at the deep margin (0.3 cm front; block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aSpecial studies were performed at an outside institution with the following\u000aresults (not reviewed):\u000aESTROGEN RECEPTOR POSITIVE\u000aPROGESTERONE RECEPTOR POSITIVE - LOW\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/NEU NEGATIVE (1+)\u000aNOTE: By report, the patient presented with an enhancing mass-like lesion in\u000athe right upper outer breast on MRI measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. Following\u000aneoadjuvant chemotherapy, there was a significant decrease in the mass-like\u000aenhancement, with patchy heterogeneous non-mass-like enhancement still present\u000aon MRI, the largest area measuring REMOVED_DATE cm in the upper outer quadrant. Following\u000amastectomy, a firm area was seen grossly in the upper-outer and lower-outer\u000aquadrants spanning a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm area, by report. Microscopic examination\u000ashows invasive lobular carcinoma present in association with stromal changes\u000acompatible with treatment effect in six of six slides reviewed. By report, an\u000aestimated 80% reduction in tumor volume is present, corresponding to a\u000aMiller-Payne Grade 3 response to chemotherapy.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: S/P right sentinel node mapping and completion right axillary node\u000adissection at BWH REMOVED_DATE  +1/7 nodes, s/p TAC chemo REMOVED_DATE  - REMOVED_DATE  for\u000alocally advanced ILC. Initial estimates of tumor size were 6 cm, clip was left\u000ain breast at time of core biopsy. Pt requests right mastectomy and\u000aprophylactic left mastectomy\u000aClinical Diagnosis: ILC and LCIS\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aConsult slides.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aReceived from Faulkner Hospital, Pathology Department, 1153 Centre Street,\u000aBoston, MA REMOVED_CASE_ID, are six (6) glass slides.\u000aThe slides are labeled "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" and sublabeled "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID", "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" and "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" through\u000a"REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID", corresponding to a right breast total mastectomy (18.4 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm)\u000aperformed on REMOVED_DATE  according to the accompanying pathology report bearing\u000athe patient's name.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Deborah A Dillon M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
