VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: BRENT T SHOJI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Astrid Weins, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Christopher D. M. Fletcher, M.D. FRCPath\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. LEFT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION:\u000aBreast tissue with focal epithelial hyperplasia, calcifications\u000aassociated with benign epithelium, sclerosing adenosis, columnar cell\u000achange, and fibroadenomatous change.\u000aBiopsy site changes are present.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: History of abnl stereo core bx @ BWH.\u000aOperation: L needle loc breast bx.\u000aOperative Findings: Not provided.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Lt abnormal mammo.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) lt needle loc breast mass - short/sup, long/lat.\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000aClip in specimen - E.P. Frost spoke with Dr. Shoji 1:32 pm.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit\u000anumber, and "left needle localized BR mass, short superior, long lateral", and\u000aconsists of an irregular tan/yellow lobulated portion of fibroadipose breast\u000atissue (4.8 cm medial to lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm anterior to posterior, and REMOVED_DATE cm\u000asuperior to inferior) with a short suture designating the superior margin, and\u000aa long suture designating the lateral margin. There is a needle localization\u000awire in place, which enters through the lateral aspect of the specimen and\u000aexits through the medial aspect of the specimen. The specimen is inked per\u000apathology protocol (superior/red, inferior/green, medial/orange,\u000alateral/yellow, anterior/blue, and posterior/black) and is serially sectioned\u000afrom medial to lateral. There is an irregular hemorrhagic ill-defined previous\u000abiopsy cavity filled with a tan/brown surgical material (2.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm),\u000awhich comes within REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE \u000acm from the medial margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin. Within the\u000aprevious biopsy cavity is a silver metallic clip. Remainder of the breast\u000aparenchyma is tan/yellow and homogeneous with focal areas of dense white\u000afibrous tissue constituting approximately 20% of the breast parenchyma. The\u000aspecimen is submitted in its entirety.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross sections, medial to lateral, blocks REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID to\u000ainclude previous biopsy cavity, blocks REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID to include metallic clip, 1 frag\u000ain each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000asek/lp\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Christopher D. M. Fletcher M.D. FRCPath, Electronically\u000asigned on Thursday REMOVED_MONTH 20, 2008 at 06:46:21PM\u000a[report_end]
