VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aLESTER, SUSAN, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, RE-EXCISION:\u000aRESIDUAL DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, micropapillary and cribriform types\u000a(low nuclear grade) is present in 1 of 19 blocks (block 11) over a REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aarea, adjacent to the prior biopsy site. No calcifications or necrosis\u000aare associated with DCIS.\u000aDCIS is REMOVED_DATE cm from the closest margin (inferior).\u000aExtensive atypical ductal hyperplasia is present throughout the specimen\u000a(levels examined).\u000aSkin with cicatrix.\u000aNOTE: The area designated as a palpable nodule by a suture consists of\u000abreast tissue with dense stroma without a specific lesion identified.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 53 year old female s/p REMOVED_DATE  right breast excision of calcifications\u000arevealing DCIS with close margins.\u000aOperation: Right breast re-excision\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast cancer\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1) Right breast tissue (short stitch superior; long\u000astitch lateral at palpable nodule; whip stitch deep margin scar anterior)\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by CHANG,MARTIN C,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number\u000aand "#1. right breast tissue, short stitch superior, long lateral at palpable\u000anodule, whip stitch deep margin, scar anterior", and consists of a single\u000afragment breast tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm, oriented with a short\u000astitch at the superior, a long stitch at the lateral aspect, and a whip stitch\u000aat the deep aspect of the specimen. At the anterior aspect of the specimen is\u000aa skin ellipse measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm containing a well-healed longitudinal\u000ascar extending the entire length of the ellipse. The specimen is received\u000ainked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior = black;\u000aanterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial =\u000aorange. At the site of the long stitch marking a "palpable nodule", there is a\u000a1.3 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm tan/pink rubbery area. A biopsy cavity is identified,\u000ameasuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm, contiguous to the anterior aspect of the\u000aspecimen, superior to the skin ellipse. In addition, the biopsy cavity\u000aapproaches the margin most closely as follows: REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior and\u000alateral, REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior and medial, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior\u000amargin. The biopsy cavity is focally surrounded by white/pink/tan rubbery\u000aarea measuring approximately REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The remainder of the breast\u000aparenchyma is mostly adipose tissue. No masses are grossly identified.\u000aNinety percent of the tissue surrounding the biopsy cavity and closest to its\u000amargins are submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  firm area near lateral stitch, 2 frags each, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  biopsy cavity from lateral to medial, mult frags, RSS\u000aMicro 20: Skin with scar, 1 frag, RSS.\u000amcc\u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
