VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aKRANE, JEFFREY, FRED, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by KRANE,JEFFREY FRED,M.D.,PH.D.\u000a1. RIGHT BREAST, LATERAL TISSUE, EXCISIONAL BIOPSY FOR A MASS:\u000aFibroadenoma (0.9 cm).\u000a2. RIGHT BREAST, CAUDAL TISSUE, EXCISIONAL BIOPSY FOR A MASS:\u000aFibroadenoma (1.4 cm).\u000a3. RIGHT BREAST, MIDDLE TISSUE, EXCISIONAL BIOPSY FOR A MASS:\u000aFibroadenoma (0.9 cm).\u000a4. RIGHT BREAST, MIDDLE MEDIAL SHAVE, BIOPSY:\u000aFibroadenoma (0.9 cm).\u000a5. RIGHT BREAST, CEPHALAD TISSUE, EXCISIONAL BIOPSY FOR A MASS:\u000aBenign breast parenchyma with dense interlobular fibrosis.\u000a6. LEFT BREAST, EXCISIONAL BIOPSY FOR A MASS:\u000aTwo fibroadenomas (0.4 cm and REMOVED_DATE cm).\u000aBenign breast parenchyma with dense interlobular fibrosis.\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: by KRANE,JEFFREY FRED,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aAdditional gross description:\u000aMICRO #10-14 remainder of specimen #5, mult frags, ESS.\u000aUpon review of the remainder of specimen #5, the original diagnosis is\u000arevised as follows:\u000a5. RIGHT BREAST, CEPHALAD TISSUE, EXCISIONAL BIOPSY FOR A MASS:\u000aFibroadenoma (1.2 cm).\u000aBenign breast parenchyma with dense interlobular fibrosis.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 17-year-old Hispanic female with history of multiple fibroadenomas\u000aand question of cystosarcomaphylloides (biopsy performed in Santo Domingo -\u000aslides unavailable; now has fibroadenomas again, per core biopsy)\u000aOperation: Bilateral breast biopsies\u000aOperative findings: Radiology Notes (per C. Denison, MD):\u000aSpecimen #2) Mass in specimen, c/w 12:00 lesion\u000aSpecimen #3) A 1 cm nodule in specimen, c/w half of right breast 1:00 caudal\u000alesion\u000aSpecimen #4) A 1 cm nodule in specimen, c/w the remainder of right breast 1:00\u000acaudal lesion\u000aSpecimen #5) A 2 cm mass in specimen, c/w right breast 1:00 cranial mass\u000aSpecimen #6) Nodule in specimen\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Bilateral breast masses\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000a1) Right breast, lateral tissue (short=superior/long=lateral)\u000a2) Right breast, caudal tissue (short=superior/long=lateral)\u000a3) Right breast, middle tissue (short=superior/long=lateral)\u000a4) Right breast, middle medial shave (whipstich=new margin)\u000a5) Right breast, cephalad tissue (short=superior/long=lateral)\u000a6) Left breast tissue (short=superior/long=lateral)\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by ENGELSGJERD,MARC C.,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in six parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart one, "right breast, lateral tissue (short=superior/long=lateral)",\u000aconsists of one fragment of nodular, white/yellow soft tissue (1.5 x REMOVED_DATE x\u000a0.5 cm) oriented by superior and lateral stitches. The exterior of the\u000aspecimen is inked as follows: superior/orange, inferior/green, lateral/yellow,\u000amedial/red, superficial/black, and deep/blue. Sections show a well\u000acircumscribed nodule (0.9 cm) with a firm, whorled, white cut surface which\u000aabuts the margin of resection, multifocally.\u000aMicro 1: 2 frag, RSS\u000aPart two, "right breast, caudal tissue (short=superior/long=lateral)", consists\u000aof one fragment of lobulated, white/tan tissue (3.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) oriented by\u000asuperior and lateral stitches. The exterior of the specimen is inked as\u000afollows: superior/orange, inferior/green, lateral/yellow, medial/red,\u000asuperficial/black, and deep/blue. Sections show a well circumscribed nodule\u000a(1.4 cm) with a whorled, white cut surface. The nodule abuts the margin of\u000aresection, multifocally.\u000aMicro 2: 2 frag, RSS\u000aPart three, "right breast, middle tissue (short=superior/long=lateral)",\u000aconsists of one fragment of firm, lobulated, white/tan tissue (2.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm) oriented by superior and lateral stitches and containing one needle\u000alocalizatin wire. The exterior of the specimen is inked as follows:\u000asuperior/orange, inferior/green, lateral/yellow, medial/red,\u000asuperficial/black, and deep/blue. Sections show a well circumscribed nodule\u000a(0.9 cm) with a whorled cut surface. The nodule abuts the margin of\u000aresection, multifocally.\u000aMicro 3: 2 frag, RSS\u000aPart four, "right breast, middle medial shave (whipstitch=new margin)",\u000aconsists of one fragment of firm, nodular, white/tan soft tissue (2.5 x REMOVED_DATE x\u000a1.5 cm) with a whipstitch on one aspect. This margin is inked black, and the\u000aremainder of the specimen is inked blue. Sections show a firm, well\u000acircumscribed, white nodule (0.9 cm) which approaches to within REMOVED_DATE cm of the\u000aindicated margin.\u000aMicro 4: 2 frag, RSS\u000aPart five, "right breast, cephalad tissue (short=superior/long=lateral)"\u000aconsists of one fragment of firm, tan/yellow tissue (3.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm)\u000aoriented by superior and lateral stitches, and containing one needle\u000alocalization wire. The exterior of the specimen is inked as follows:\u000asuperior/orange, inferior/green, lateral/yellow, medial/red,\u000asuperficial/black, and deep/blue. Sections show a well circumscribed nodule\u000a(2.3 cm) which abuts the margins of resection, multifocally.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Multi frag, RSS\u000aPart six, "left breast tissue (long=latearal/short superior", consists of one\u000afragment of firm, tan/yellow tissue (3.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) oriented by superior\u000aand lateral stitches, and containing one needle localization wire. The\u000aexterior of the specimen is inked as follows: superior/orange, inferior/green,\u000alateral/yellow, medial/red, superficial/black, and deep/blue. Sections show an\u000airregular-shaped area of firm, white tissue (2.5 cm) which abuts the margins\u000aof resection, multifocally.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Multi frag, RSS\u000ame\u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
