rior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000athe medial margin and REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin. The remaining cut\u000asurface displays 98% white-pink fibrous tissue, and 2% yellow adipose tissue,\u000awith no additional discrete masses or lesions identified. The specimen is\u000asequentially submitted in its entirety.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Anterior margin, radially, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross sections from anterior to posterior, with the\u000asurgical clip identified in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Posterior margin, radially, 3 frags, ESS.\u000acp/lp\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Robert D Odze M.D., Electronically signed on Friday\u000aREMOVED_MONTH 30, 2009 at 03:12:43PM\u000a[report_end]
