/green; lateral/yellow;\u000amedial/orange. An accompanying specimen radiograph demonstrates clip and\u000acalcifications within the specimen. The specimen contains REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm\u000apalpable yellow/white nodule, which is REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000ainferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral\u000amargin. The remainder of the specimen contains unremarkable white/yellow\u000afibroadipose tissue. The entire specimen is submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: left breast tissue from medial to lateral (tip in Micro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aand nodule in Micro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), 12 frags, ESS.\u000aASO/lp\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Alison Z Young M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Shuji Ogino M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a7/21/2005\u000a[report_end]
