VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: BETH ANN LESNIKOSKI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Astrid Weins, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Christopher D. M. Fletcher, M.D. FRCPath\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. LEFT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISIONAL BIOPSY:\u000aBreast tissue with epithelial hyperplasia, calcifications associated\u000awith benign epithelium, apocrine metaplasia, apocrine cysts, columnar\u000acell change and extensive duct ectasia.\u000aBiopsy site changes are present.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the\u000aspecimen, including margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Left breast mass.\u000aOperation: Not provided.\u000aOperative Findings: Not provided.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: L breast mass, history of L breast excisional bx.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) left breast wire localized biopsy (inking per protocol) to mammo.\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000aHook wire and calcifications seen in specimen. Spoke with Dr. Emily Kenny at\u000a2:30 pm by Dr. Lesnikoski.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "left breast, wire-localized biopsy", and consists of a tan/yellow\u000alobulated portion of fibroadipose tissue (4.8 cm medial to lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aanterior to posterior, and REMOVED_DATE cm superior to inferior) with a\u000aneedle-localization wire placed which enters through the anterior medial aspect\u000aof the specimen and exits through the posterior aspect of the specimen. There\u000aare no identifying markers or sutures present; however, the specimen has been\u000apreviously inked consistent with pathology protocol (superior/red,\u000ainferior/green, medial/orange, lateral/yellow, anterior/blue, and\u000aposterior/black). The specimen is serially sectioned. There is an irregular\u000ared/brown multicystic biopsy cavity (1.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) in which there is a\u000ametallic clip found. The previous biopsy cavity comes within REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000aposterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin, and\u000a1.2 cm from the medial margin. The remainder of the breast parenchyma is\u000atan/yellow and homogenous with focal multicystic areas and dense white fibrous\u000atissue constituting approximately 40% of the breast parenchyma. No additional\u000adiscrete lesions are grossly identified. The specimen is submitted in its\u000aentirety.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross sections, medial and lateral block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID to\u000ainclude biopsy cavity, block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID to include metallic clip, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000asek/lp\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Christopher D. M. Fletcher M.D. FRCPath, Electronically\u000asigned on Thursday REMOVED_MONTH 20, 2008 at 06:57:07PM\u000a[report_end]
