VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID:REMOVED_CASE_ID Report Status: Signed\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aDIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. Sentinel lymph node, right axillary, excision:\u000aNo evidence of malignancy in one lymph node (0/1).\u000aB. Right breast, posterior margin, excision:\u000aProliferative fibrocystic changes.\u000aC. Right breast, lumpectomy:\u000aInvasive ductal carcinoma, grade 1, with mucinous features (see synoptic\u000areport).\u000aSYNOPTIC REPORT:\u000aINVASIVE TUMOR:\u000a-histologic type: infiltrating ductal carcinoma with mucinous\u000afeatures\u000a-histologic grade: grade 1\u000a-size (greatest dimension): REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000a-lymphatic/vascular invasion: none identified\u000a-perineural invasion: none identified\u000a-microcalcification: none identified\u000a-margins for invasive tumor: clear (greater than or equal to REMOVED_DATE cm.)\u000a-immunohistochemical staining on prior specimen (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) was reported as:\u000aEstrogen receptor: POSITIVE (>10% of nuclei stained)\u000aProgesterone receptor: POSITIVE (>10% of nuclei stained)\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID): NEGATIVE (0) (no membrane staining)\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU (LCIS):\u000aNone identified.\u000aLYMPH NODES:\u000aOne lymph node sampled is negative for malignancy (0/1)\u000a(0/1 sentinel lymph nodes; REMOVED_DATE non-sentinel lymph nodes).\u000aCOMMENT: The sentinel lymph node, specimen A, is examined at multiple levels\u000awith H&E stains and immunohistochemical stains for keratin.\u000aADDITIONAL PATHOLOGIC FINDINGS:\u000aChanges consistent with prior biopsy site.\u000aPRIOR RELATED SPECIMENS REVIEWED:\u000aRight breast, upper outer quadrant, 9:30 o'clock; REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID; REMOVED_DATE \u000aCOMMENT: The mucinous portion accounts for approximately 95% of the lesion.\u000aHowever, the presence of at least some traditional invasive ductal carcinoma\u000anecessitates categorizing the tumor as an invasive ductal carcinoma with\u000amucinous features.\u000aAJCC pTNM Classification (6th Ed.): pREMOVED_ACCESSION_IDb pREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID(sn)(i-) pMX\u000aThe pathologic TNM classification above is based only on the information\u000aavailable to the pathologist, and therefore may not be accurate.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by: Todd E. Abbott, M.D.\u000aINTRA-OPERATIVE CONSULTATION:\u000aOPERATING ROOM CONSULTATION (FROZEN SECTION):\u000aSentinel lymph node, right axilla, biopsy:\u000aOne lymph node with no tumor seen in section examined.\u000aMJR\u000aClinical diagnosis & history:\u000aRight breast carcinoma\u000aTissue-Designation:\u000aA.Sentinel lymph node - right axillary\u000aB.Breast, excision with margins - right\u000aC.Breast, excision with margins - right\u000aGross description:\u000aThe specimen is received in three containers.\u000aSpecimen A is received fresh from the Operating Room, labeled "right sentinel\u000anode" and consists of a single lymph node measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. It is\u000asectioned revealing no gross tumor. A representative portion is submitted for\u000afrozen section evaluation. The frozen section remnant is submitted in cassette\u000aAF. The remaining node is submitted in cassette A. 2 agg. all.\u000aSpecimen B is received in formalin, labeled "mass, right breast, posterior\u000amargin" and consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. fragment of yellow adipose tissue\u000awith stringy white fibrous tissue intermixed. One broad surface is marked by a\u000asingle suture. The suture is identified as new margin. The surface is inked\u000ablack. The specimen is serially sectioned and submitted entirely in 13\u000acassettes. 13X all.\u000aSpecimen C is received in formalin, labeled "right lumpectomy" and consists of\u000aa 48 gram, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. lumpectomy specimen with the following orienting\u000asutures: long, lateral; short, superior. There is a needle localization wire\u000aentering the specimen from the supero-lateral aspect. The specimen is inked in\u000athe following manner: superior, blue; anterior, black; inferior, green;\u000aposterior, orange. REMOVED_DATE cm. of the medial margin and REMOVED_DATE cm. of the lateral\u000amargin are removed. The remaining center portion of the lump is cut into ten\u000aequally thick slices labeled REMOVED_DATE  from medial to lateral. There is a\u000apalpable abnormality in slices REMOVED_DATE measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x up to REMOVED_DATE cm. that\u000ais nearest the postero-inferior margin. This lesion is associated with\u000ahemorrhage. The remainder of the lumpectomy is remarkable for yellow adipose\u000aand focal white stringy tissue. 25 agg.\u000aSection code: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - representative medial margin\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - representative mid slice portions from slices REMOVED_DATE \u000arespectively\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - entire slice 6\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - entire slice 7\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - entire slice 8\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - entire slice 9\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - entire slice 10\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - entire lateral margin\u000aTotal fixation time is 28 hours.\u000aDictated by: TEA____(signature on file)____ REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a____(signature on file)____ REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a[report_end]
