VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ROGER L CHRISTIAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Wai Chin Foo, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Lucian R Chirieac, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. RIGHT BREAST, EXCISION FOR CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aBreast parenchyma with fibroadenoma, calcifications in association with\u000abenign epithelium, stromal calcifications, and biopsy site changes.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the\u000aspecimen, including margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Calcs, right breast --> core --> ADH (not with calcs).\u000aOperation: Wire-directed, and wide excision.\u000aOperative Findings: See op note.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: ADH.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Tissue, right breast - short/superior, long/lateral (for mammo).\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000aCalcifications and wire are in the specimen. Dr. Gombos.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh labeled with the patient's name, medical record\u000anumber, and "#1. Tissue, right breast - short superior, long lateral", consists\u000aof a wire localized lumpectomy specimen (S-I REMOVED_DATE cm, A-P REMOVED_DATE cm, and M-L REMOVED_DATE \u000acm) with two orienting sutures (short superior and long lateral) and a\u000aguidewire entering at the superior anterior intersection. The accompanying\u000aradiograph demonstrates calcification and a wire. Specimen is sectioned into\u000a14 slices from superior to inferior. Present in the fourth slice is a\u000awhite/gray irregular fibrotic area (0.6 cm x REMOVED_DATE cm x REMOVED_DATE cm), which extends to\u000athe lateral margin and measures REMOVED_DATE cm to the medial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to the\u000aanterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to the superior margin,\u000aand REMOVED_DATE cm to the inferior margin. There is focal hemorrhage located at the\u000acenter of the area. Immediately inferior to the area is a white/pink well\u000acircumscribed nodule (0.6 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which measures REMOVED_DATE cm to the lateral\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm to the medial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to the\u000aposterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to the superior margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm to the inferior\u000amargin. Gritty calcifications are present inferior to this nodule. The\u000aremaining breast parenchyma is unremarkable.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Superior margin cut (perpendiculars), 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Inferior margin (perpendiculars), 5 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Serial sections from superior to inferior (area in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID+REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID; nodule\u000ain REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID; and calcifications in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), 1 frag per cassette, ESS.\u000aWCF/lp\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Lucian R Chirieac M.D., Electronically signed on\u000a4/19/2007\u000a[report_end]
