VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: SARA RUSSELL M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-06-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Eric L Snyder, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Shuji Ogino, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. BREAST, RIGHT, EXCISIONAL BIOPSY:\u000aBenign breast tissue with calcifications, ductal hyperplasia, apocrine\u000ametaplasia, and cysts.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000aChanges suggestive of prior biopsy (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aB. SPECIMEN LABELED PIECE OF RIGHT BREAST MELANOMA METASTATIC NODULE":\u000aBreast tissue with METASTATIC MALIGNANT MELANOMA.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Metastatic melanoma (numerous on right, perirectal) in right breast as\u000awell as 2 cystic -vs solid r breast lesions.\u000aOperation: Right wire localized excisional breast bx.\u000aOperative Findings: Not provided.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Metastatic melanoma right breast masses.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Breast masses 23 - mammo (short wire in lesion 3)\u000aB/2. Piece of right breast melanoma metastatic nodule\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two parts, each labeled with the patients\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart A, labeled "#1. Breast masses 23 to mammo short stitch superior",\u000aconsists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm tan/yellow fibrofatty tissue with a focal dark\u000abrown/black area entirely submitted to DFCI (Susan McCrae pager # REMOVED_CASE_ID) for a\u000amelanoma vaccine production. The remainder of the tissue is submitted for\u000apathology for further analysis. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol\u000afor the evaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red;\u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange with a short stitch marking\u000asuperior margin and the long stitch marking the lateral margin. On sectioning\u000athe specimen, there is a hole that has been sutured closed in the medial part\u000aof the specimen consistent with prior removal of one mass. The remainder of\u000athe specimen is approximately 70% white fibrous tissue and 30% tan/yellow\u000aadipose tissue. No discrete additional masses are identified. The specimen is\u000aentirely submitted:\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: breast masses submitted medial to lateral REMOVED_DATE frags in each,\u000aESS.\u000aPart B, labeled "#2. Piece of right breast melanoma metastatic nodule",\u000aconsists of a single fragment of brown/black tumor with associated adipose\u000atissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in total. The fragment of tumor itself\u000ameasures approximately REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The specimen is entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Piece of right breast melanoma metastatic nodule, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aESN/ajb\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Eric L Snyder M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Shuji Ogino M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a2/10/2006\u000a[report_end]
