NING (invasive carcinoma) was performed on both of the\u000aprior needle core biopsies (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) and reported as: Estrogen\u000areceptor: POSITIVE (>10% of nuclei stained)\u000aProgesterone receptor: POSITIVE, focal (1-10% of nuclei stained) in case\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aProgesterone receptor: POSITIVE, rare (<1% of nuclei stained) in case\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID): NEGATIVE (0) (no membrane staining) in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID): NEGATIVE (1+) (faint or <10% complete membrane\u000astaining) in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aLYMPH NODES:\u000aPositive lymph nodes out of total sampled: REMOVED_DATE (1/1 sentinel lymph node;\u000a1/15 non-sentinel lymph node) - largest metastasis (greatest dimension): REMOVED_DATE \u000acm.\u000a- extranodal extension: none identified\u000a- number with micrometastases (< REMOVED_DATE cm.): 0\u000a- number with isolated tumor cells: 0\u000aSKIN:\u000aUnremarkable.\u000aPRIOR RELATED SPECIMEN REPORTS REVIEWED:\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by: Nicole A. Mihok, M.D.\u000aINTRA-OPERATIVE CONSULTATION:\u000aOPERATING ROOM CONSULTATION (TOUCH PREPARATION):\u000aRight sentinel node: Metastatic carcinoma present. Grossly measures 3 mm.\u000aMJM\u000aClinical diagnosis & history:\u000aRight breast carcinoma\u000aTissue-Designation:\u000aA.Sentinel lymph node - count 2477\u000aB.Lymph nodes, dissection - right axillary\u000aC.Breast, modified radical mastectomy - right\u000aGross description:\u000aSpecimen A labeled "sentinel node" consists of a piece of adipose tissue in\u000awhich a lymph node is present. The adipose tissue measures 3 x 2 cm. and is\u000aentirely embedded. 2 agg. all.\u000aSpecimen B labeled "right axillary contents" consists of a fat pad 8 x 6 x 1\u000acm. which contains lymph nodes. Further examination and dissection of the\u000aaxillary fat reveals the presence of fourteen yellowish-pink, glistening\u000anodules ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE cm. in greatest dimension to REMOVED_DATE x 1 x 1 cm.\u000aSection code: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - smaller nodules - 13X all.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - serially sectioned single largest nodule - 3X all.\u000aSpecimen C labeled "right mastectomy" consists of a 6,875 gram breast. The\u000aellipse of skin measures 20 x 8 cm. The nipple is centrally placed and is\u000ainverted. The breast measures 20 x 21 x 3 cm. and it is inked black. There is\u000aa palpable area centrally which is quite firm over an area approximately 5 x 4\u000ax 3 cm. A suture is present designated axillary tail. Cut sections through\u000athe breast shows the area of the mass to be very firm and gritty. It appears\u000ato be fairly well-demarcated at the edge and does not extend to the deep\u000aresection margin which is the closest margin. It is at least REMOVED_DATE cm. from the\u000adeep margin. Areas of hemorrhage are present in this mass. Sections are taken\u000aas follows. 14X.\u000aSection code: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - from the nipple and skin\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - from the mass and deep resection margin\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - from the mass\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - from random areas away from the firm area\u000aTotal fixation time is 10 hours.\u000aDictated by: RJS/LV____(signature on file)____MICHAEL J. ROSS, M.D. REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a____(signature on file)____NICOLE MIHOK, M.D. REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a[report_end]
