VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOGINO, SHUJI, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by OGINO,SHUJI,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR CALCIFICATIONS AND A CLIP:\u000aBreast tissue with columnar alteration of lobules with prominent snouts\u000aand secretions, sclerosing adenosis, apocrine metaplasia, florid\u000aductal hyperplasia, cysts, microscopic intraductal papillomas, biopsy\u000asite changes, fibroadenomatoid changes, and calcifications associated\u000awith benign epithelium.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 37 year old premenopausal female whose REMOVED_DATE mammogram demonstrate a\u000a1 cm group of calcification in the left outer breast. REMOVED_DATE  core\u000abiopsy reveals a complex sclerosing lesion, CAPSS focal atypia.\u000aOperation: Left breast wire localization excision\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left abnormal mammogram, breast core biopsy with atypia\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1. Left breast tissue (stitch short/superior; long lateral\u000awith stitch on deep margin)\u000aRADIOLOGY: Clip and calcifications in specimen. S. Durfee,MD\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by DAVID,FRANK SAMUEL,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in one part, labeled with the patient's name,\u000aunit number and "#1. left breast mass", and consists of a single mass of\u000ayellow/tan fibroadipose tissue (3.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The specimen is oriented\u000awith a short suture and long suture, which are designated by the surgeon as the\u000asuperior and lateral margins, respectively. The specimen is inked by the\u000aoperating room per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior\u000a= black; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow;\u000amedial = orange. Within the specimen is a surgical clip, and calcifications\u000awere also identified. No discrete mass is grossly appreciated. Accompanying\u000athe specimen is a mammogram which displays the presence of a localizing wire\u000aand a surgical lip, as well as diffuse microcalcifications. The specimen is\u000aentirely submitted.\u000aMicro 1: medial, ESS\u000aMicro 2: lateral, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  remainder of specimen, medial to lateral (clip in #3), ESS\u000afsd\u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
