VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: FinalType: Surgical Pathology Pathology Report: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID OPERATION DATE: 03 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON: 03 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 13:47 CLINICAL DATA: {None Provided} =============================================================================== *** FINAL DIAGNOSIS *** BREAST (RIGHT), EXCISIONAL BIOPSY: INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA, GRADE 2, REMOVED_DATE CM, INVADING LYMPHATIC VESSELS AND EXTENDING TO LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN. DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN-SITU, HIGH GRADE, HARBORING CALCIFICATIONS AND EXTENDING AWAY FROM THE MASS AND TO LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN. SEE NOTE. NOTE: Blood vessel invasion is not seen. Diagnosis by: Frederick Carl Koerner, M.D. Signed On: 05 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 13:43 =============================================================================== *** RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum *** RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast (Right): The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein. The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein. See note. Note: In this laboratory, we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way (paraffin sections) and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay. 91% of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay. 96% of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay. When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections, the predictive value of a positive result was 97% and the predictive value of a negative result was 95%. In this laboratory, we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay. Sixty-five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay, and 98% of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors. Added by: Frederick Carl Koerner, M.D. Signed On: 10 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 16:28 GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "right breast", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm portion of fibroadipose tissue, inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE cm stellate hemorrhagic firm lesion with focal calcifications, and grossly REMOVED_DATE cm from the closest margin. The lesion is submitted in cassettes A-D. The remainder of the specimen is submitted entirely in cassettes E-J. No frozen section is done. Resident: DANIELLE ELLIOTT, M.D. =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT - REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID REPORTS TO: Michele Annette Gadd, M.D. PART : BREAST (RIGHT), EXCISIONAL BIOPSY
