VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: MEHRA GOLSHAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Astrid Weins, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: William R Welch, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. LEFT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A CLIP:\u000aBenign breast tissue with ductal hyperplasia, apocrine change,\u000aand biopsy site changes.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the\u000aspecimen, including margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 45 y/o female with left breast hyperplasia with atypia on core\u000abiopsy.\u000aOperation: Left breast wire-localized excisional biopsy.\u000aPREVIOUS SURGERY; yes.\u000aOperative Findings: None provided.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast abnormal mammogram.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) Left breast excisional bx; short stitch - superior, long - lateral\u000a(mammo)\u000aRADIOLOGY: Clip, residual Ca++ and intact wire in specimen phoned to O.R. by\u000aE. Lizer at 10:15 a.m.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "left breast wire localization excisional Bx short superior long lateral",\u000aand consists of an irregular tan-yellow lobulated portion of fibroadipose\u000atissue (5.2 cm medial to lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm superior to inferior, and REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aanterior to posterior) with a short suture designating the superior margin and\u000aa long suture designating the lateral margin. There is a localization wire\u000aplaced, which enters through the lateral aspect of the specimen and exits\u000athrough the medial aspect of the specimen. The specimen is inked per pathology\u000aprotocol (superior red, inferior green, medial orange, lateral yellow, anterior\u000ablue, and posterior black) and is serially sectioned from medial to lateral.\u000aThere is a well-circumscribed dense white fibrous area with a tan-white\u000aprevious biopsy cavity (0.9 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which comes to within REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000athe anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin, and\u000a2.8 cm from the medial margin. Within the cavity is a silver metallic surgical\u000abiopsy clip. The remainder of the breast parenchyma is tan-yellow and\u000ahomogenous with focal areas of dense white fibrous tissue constituting less\u000athan 10% of the breast parenchyma. No additional lesions are grossly\u000aidentified. The specimen is serially sectioned and submitted in its entirety.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross sections medial to lateral, blocks REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID to\u000ainclude area of biopsy cavity per specimen radiograph block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID to include\u000abiopsy clip, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aSEK/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by William R Welch M.D., Electronically signed on Tuesday\u000aREMOVED_MONTH 16, 2009 at 06:27:06PM\u000a[report_end]
