 Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity\u000ain >10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Right breast mass - possibly solid, possibly cyst with thick content.\u000aOperation: 14g U/S\u000aOperative findings: Did not aspirate 14g core\u000aClinical Diagnosis: ? solid or thick fluid in cyst\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Right breast tissue (1 green cassette)\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by PREISINGER,ELIZABETH ANN,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit\u000anumber, and "right breast core bx", in a light green cassette, and consists of\u000amultiple, soft, fragmented, yellow to white tissue cores (1.1 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in\u000aaggregate).\u000aMicro 1: Multi frags, ESS.\u000akks\u000aReports to: TWOHIG, LORRAINE, BERNADETTE, MB\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY(IES)\u000a[report_end]
