VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Sentinel Lymph Nodes(s)\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ROGER L CHRISTIAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Astrid Weins, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Jane E. Brock, M.B., B.S., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aLEFT BREAST EXCISION FOR A MASS AND SENTINEL NODE BIOPSIES (2 SPECIMENS, parts\u000aA & B, including REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aINVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA two foci\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aNEGATIVE LYMPH NODE\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA\u000aSize - REMOVED_DATE cm and REMOVED_DATE cm, see NOTE\u000aTumor #1 (4.2 cm)\u000aHistologic type - Papillary and cribriform ductal carcinoma\u000awith heterologous benign bone formation\u000aHistologic grade (SBR) - III (Poor) (8 or 9 points)\u000aTubules - 10 to 75% (2 points)\u000aNuclear grade - High (3 points)\u000aMitotic counts - 3 points\u000aTumor #2 (0.3 cm)\u000aHistologic type - Ductal\u000aHistologic grade (SBR) - III (Poor) (8 or 9 points)\u000aTubules - < 10% (3 points)\u000aNuclear grade - Intermediate (2 points)\u000aMitotic counts - 3 points\u000aEIC - Negative\u000aLVI - Absent\u000aDermal LVI - Absent\u000aSkin invasion - Absent\u000aFinal Margins (invasive)\u000aNegative (> REMOVED_DATE cm) - anterior, posterior, medial, lateral,\u000ainferior, superior\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU - present\u000aTypes - Solid, Cribriform, Apocrine\u000aNuclear grade - Intermediate\u000aCalcifications in DCIS - Present\u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - Present\u000aNumber of blocks/total - REMOVED_DATE blocks associated with both invasive\u000afoci. DCIS is present as a minor component of the invasive carcinoma.\u000ap63/REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID double stains performed on both foci confirm the presence of\u000ainvasive and in situ carcinoma (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aMargins (DCIS)\u000aNegative (> REMOVED_DATE cm) - anterior, posterior, medial, lateral,\u000ainferior, superior\u000aLYMPH NODES\u000aSentinel lymph nodes - NEGATIVE (9 H&E levels examined)\u000aNumber of positive nodes - 0\u000aNumber of nodes examined - 1\u000aTOTAL POSITIVE NODES (all specimens)- REMOVED_DATE \u000aOTHER FINDINGS\u000aCore biopsy site\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER, PR, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for INVASIVE CARCINOMAS (4.2cm and REMOVED_DATE cm foci; blocks REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID,\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE-LOW\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) POSITIVE (3+)\u000aOf note, the DCIS associated with the larger invasive carcinoma is ER positive,\u000aPR positive and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID positive (3+) and the DCIS associated with the smaller\u000ainvasive carcinoma is ER positive-low, PR negative and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID positive (3+).\u000aAJCC Classification (6th edition): REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID (sn) with two foci of invasion\u000aNOTE: The main tumor mass is present in a cystic hemorrhagic cavity and shows a\u000amixture of papillary and cribriform architecture with multiple small foci of\u000abenign bone formation (osseous metaplasia). The stroma associated with this\u000acarcinoma is keratin REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID negative and does not look atypical. The second\u000ainvasive focus (0.3 cm) is present as a separate nodule admixed with DCIS (1.3\u000acm) and is located in the superior/medial breast tissue REMOVED_DATE cm from the main\u000atumor mass. This focus has pure ductal morphology.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: CA, Lt breast.\u000aOperation: SNB, Lt ax; wide excis, tumor site, Rt breast.\u000aOperative Findings: See op note.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: CA, Lt breast.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) Left axillary sentinel lymph node for frozen section.\u000aB/2) Primary tumor site, left breast; long suture - lateral; short suture -\u000asuperior (to Breast Tissue).\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "1) LEFT AXILLARY SENTINEL LYMPH NODE" (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aLymph node, negative for tumor.\u000aOR Consultation by: William Robert Welch, M.D.\u000aResident: Astrid Weins, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aThe senior physician certifies that he/she personally conducted a gross and/or\u000amicroscopic examination of the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed\u000athe rapid diagnos(es) related thereto.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname, unit number.\u000aPart A is received in the frozen lab for intraoperative consultation, labeled\u000a"left axillary sentinel lymph node", consists of a fragment of fibroadipose\u000atissue (2.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) including a tan/brown lymph node (1.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm), which is serially sectioned and entirely frozen as REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. The\u000anon-frozen tissue is entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID remnant, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID remnant, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID remnant, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Non-frozen tissue, multi frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, labeled "primary tumor site left breast, long suture lateral, short\u000asuture superior", consists of a REMOVED_DATE (medial to lateral) x REMOVED_DATE (superior to\u000ainferior) x REMOVED_DATE (anterior to posterior) cm portion of fibroadipose tissue with\u000aa REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm white skin ellipse containing a REMOVED_DATE cm well-healed surgical\u000ascar and two oriented sutures designating long-lateral and short-superior. The\u000aspecimen is inked by the surgeon per pathology protocol for the evaluation of\u000amargins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green;\u000alateral/yellow; medial/orange. REMOVED_DATE cm deep to the skin is a cystic mass (5.7 x\u000a3.3 x REMOVED_DATE cm) filled with blood and blood clot. The wall of the cavity is\u000atan/white friable and partially calcified. The solid mass occupies about\u000aone-half of the cystic cavity, and measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The mass is located\u000a0.5 cm from the anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000athe posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial\u000amargin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin. An additional tan, firm nodule\u000a(1.3 cm in greatest dimension) is found REMOVED_DATE cm away from mass #1 in the\u000asuperior/medial portion of breast tissue. The remainder of the specimen\u000acontains 98% adipose tissue and 2% tan/white fibrous tissue. A representative\u000asection of the tumor and normal is allocated to the breast tissue bank per\u000aAndrea Richardson.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Solid area of mass, 1 frag in each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Cystic area of mass, 1 frag in each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Mass to anterior margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Mass to skin, 1 frag in each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Inferior margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Posterior margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Superior margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, 1 frag in each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Mass #1 to skin and to superficial margin, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Nodule #2 in UIQ, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000aImmunohistochemical studies for estrogen receptor, progesterone\u000areceptor, and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu were evaluated by manual morphometric analysis\u000ausing the following criteria:\u000aHormone receptor analysis:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low > 0% - < 10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not\u000ayet been determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10%\u000aof tumor cells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor\u000acells but only a portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aEquivocal (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity in >30% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aExternal controls are evaluated and show appropriate Immunoreactivity.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for\u000ainvestigational use only.\u000aLMC/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jane E. Brock M.B., B.S., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000aWednesday REMOVED_MONTH 30, 2009 at 04:16:20PM\u000a[report_end]
