ragments, RSS.\u000aMicro 4, lateral margin, en face, 3 fragments, RSS.\u000aMicro 5, medial margin, en face, 3 fragments, RSS.\u000aMicro 6, posterior margin, en face, 2 fragments, RSS.\u000aMicro 7, parenchyma, medial, 2 fragments, RSS.\u000aMicro 8, parenchyma, posterior, 2 fragments, RSS.\u000aMicro 9, parenchyma, superior-posterior, 2 fragments, RSS.\u000aMicro 10, parenchyma, superior, 2 fragments, RSS.\u000aMicro 11, parenchyma, inferior, 3 fragments, RSS.\u000aMicro 12, parenchyma, lateral, 3 fragments, RSS.\u000aPart two, labeled "left breast tissue, stitch anterior-medial portion", is a\u000abreast biopsy specimen consisting of one fragment of yellow/pink fibrofatty\u000atissue (2.2 x 2 x REMOVED_DATE cm) with no stitches present. The specimen is inked in\u000ablack. The specimen is entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  breast parenchyma, multiple fragments, ESS.\u000aReports to: CARTER, KATHARINE M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
