ete masses or lesions identified. Also\u000areceived in the same container is an additional unoriented white/pink soft\u000atissue (1.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The specimen is inked black and bisected to\u000areveal a white/pink cut surface. The specimens are submitted in toto.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 end of larger unoriented soft tissue, radially, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross sections, (clip identified in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), multi frags,\u000aESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Opposite unoriented end, radially, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Additionally received smaller soft tissue, bisected, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and\u000a"B. ? Intraductal papilloma R breast", consists of a pink/tan irregular soft\u000atissue (0.3 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which is inked black and submitted in toto.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 frag, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jacqueline M William M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed\u000aon Friday February 12, 2010 at 03:38:17PM\u000a[report_end]
