VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST MASTECTOMY W/REGIONAL LYMPH NODES\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aLESTER, SUSAN, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST, MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY AND AXILLARY NODES:\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, solid and cribriform, is present in\u000aone (1) of thirteen (13) blocks (#10), in the lower inner\u000aquadrant away from the prior biopsy site.\u000aDCIS is not at the deep margin.\u000aSkeletal muscle is present and is not involved.\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia is present (block #11).\u000aPrevious biopsy site with giant cell reaction (see note).\u000aEighteen (18) lymph nodes negative for tumor. Immunoperoxidase studies on\u000atwo blocks of lymph nodes (blocks 16 and 17) do not reveal diagnostic\u000aimmunoreactivity for keratin positive tumor cells (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aNOTE: Immunohistochemistry performed on formalin-fixed tissue on a\u000agroup of atypical cells in proximity to the previous biopsy cavity\u000a(block #2) shows that the cells are negative for cytokeratins (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and\u000aPan-K), and positive for REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID confirming the histiocytic nature of the\u000acells.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: None given.\u000aOperation: Left modified radical mastectomy.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast cancer.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Left breast and axillary nodes.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by MAGI GALLUZZI,CRISTINA,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in one part, labeled with the patient's name,\u000aunit number, and "Left breast and axillary nodes", and consists of a modified\u000aradical mastectomy weighing 700 grams, and measuring 25 x 16 x REMOVED_DATE cm. An\u000airregular unpigmented fragment of skin, measuring 20 x 11 cm is present in the\u000aspecimen. The skin is centered by a grossly unremarkable nipple measuring REMOVED_DATE \u000acm in diameter. A REMOVED_DATE cm oblique well-healed scar is present in the skin, in\u000athe upper outer quadrant. The axillary tail measures 11 x 6 x REMOVED_DATE cm. The\u000aspecimen is serially sectioned to show a 7 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm cavity in the upper\u000aouter quadrant, underneath the scar. The cavity is lined by a gray-tan,\u000aglistening, focally granular membrane. The cavity is REMOVED_DATE cm from the deep\u000aresection margin. The parenchyma adjacent to the cavity shows focal areas of\u000anodularity; the largest of which measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm, and is located\u000ain the lower outer quadrant. A REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm yellow-tan firm area is\u000apresent in proximity to the wall of the cavity, in the upper outer quadrant.\u000aThe rest of the breast parenchyma consists of fibrofatty tissue.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  cavity and deep resection margin, 3 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  firm area in proximity to the cavity, in the lower outer\u000aquadrant, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 6: firm area in proximity to the cavity, in the upper outer\u000aquadrant and scar, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  firmer area in the upper outer quadrant, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  lower inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 11: lower outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 12: upper outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 13: nipple.\u000aMicro 14: 4 lymph nodes, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 15: 4 lymph nodes, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 16: 4 lymph nodes, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 17: 4 lymph nodes, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 18: 1 lymph node, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aReports to: OSTEEN, ROBERT, T. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY W/REGIONAL LYMPH NODES\u000a[report_end]
