VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID OUTSIDE SLIDE CONSULT - BREAST\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aLESTER, SUSAN, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aCONSULT SLIDES FROM SAINT ANNE'S HOSPITAL, FALL RIVER, MA:\u000aLEFT BREAST EXCISION AND SENTINEL NODE BIOPSIES (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID; REMOVED_DATE ):\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA with ductal and lobular features, moderately\u000adifferentiated (modified Bloom-Richardson grade II/III) is present as\u000amultiple foci adjacent to a prior biopsy site, the largest focus measuring\u000a1.2 cm (see note).\u000aNo lymphovascular invasion is seen.\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, solid and clinging types (high nuclear grade) is\u000apresent as a minor component associated with the invasive carcinoma (EIC\u000anegative).\u000aInvasive carcinoma is not present at the margin. DCIS is < REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000athe margin designated as inferior and posterior in one slide. Carcinoma\u000ais not seen in slides designated "lat", "ant-inf", and "medial".\u000aSkin with no tumor seen.\u000aMETASTATIC CARCINOMA is present in one of three sentinel nodes. The\u000ametastatic deposit measures REMOVED_DATE cm. No extranodal invasion is seen.\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed with the following results\u000a(reviewed):\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu NEGATIVE (1+)\u000aNote: Except for the prior biopsy site, a grossly evident tumor mass was\u000anot present. Most of the invasive carcinoma in the excision is present\u000aassociated with this biopsy site. In one slide (designated "POST-SUP")\u000athere are three foci of invasion (up to REMOVED_DATE cm in size) without an evident\u000abiopsy site. These areas may be separate foci of invasion. They are not\u000aassociated with DCIS and are > REMOVED_DATE cm from the margin.\u000aAll of the foci of invasion are similar in appearance and do not appear to\u000abe of different histologic types.\u000aA prior core needle biopsy revealed a 1 cm focus of invasion. Correlation\u000awith radiologic findings may be helpful to determine the best estimate of\u000atotal tumor size.\u000aThis carcinoma would be classified as (at least) AJCC (6th edition)\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_IDc pREMOVED_ACCESSION_IDa MX with possible multiple foci of invasion.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Breast cancer.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Consult slides.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by PREISINGER,ELIZABETH ANN,M.D.\u000aReceived from Saint Anne's Hospital, Pathology Department, 795 Middle Street,\u000aFall River, MA REMOVED_CASE_ID, are 23 slides.\u000aThe slides are labeled "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" and sublabeled "A"(REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), "B", "C"(REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), "D",\u000a"E", "E REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID POS", "E REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID NEG", "E LAT"(REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), "E POST"(REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), "E POST-SUP", "E\u000aANT-INF", "E MEDIAL", "E CLIP", "E INF-POST"(REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) and "F", corresponding to A)\u000asentinel node #1 excision (1.5 cm) B) sentinel node #2 excision (0.7 cm) C)\u000asentinel node #3 excision (2.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) D) sentinel node #4 excision\u000a(3.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) E) left breast lumpectomy (12.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) F) left\u000abreast, skin, lumpectomy (4.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) performed\u000aon REMOVED_DATE  according to the accompanying pathology report bearing the\u000apatient's name.\u000aReports to: IGLEHART, JAMES, DIRK M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: OUTSIDE SLIDE CONSULT - BREAST\u000a[report_end]
