 area of fibrosis, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 7: inner upper quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 8: inner lower quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 9: outer upper quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 10: outer lower quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 11: nipple, area of dimpling, and intervening skin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 12: medially and laterally oriented scars, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 13: 3 potential single lymph nodes, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 14: 4 potential single lymph nodes, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 15: 2 potential single lymph nodes, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 16: 2 potential single lymph nodes, 2 frags, ESS.\u000ajhc\u000aReports to: CHRISTIAN, ROGER, L. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY W/REGIONAL LYMPH NODES\u000a[report_end]
