VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Amend/Addenda\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ROBERT T OSTEEN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-05-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000a********** Addended Report ***********\u000aResident: Patricia A. R. Brunker, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Deborah A Dillon, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE-DIRECTED EXCISION FOR A CLIP:\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, cribriform type, intermediate to high nuclear grade,\u000ais present in three of thirteen (3/13) blocks adjacent to previous core biopsy\u000asite (blocks REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aMicrocalcifications and necrosis are associated with DCIS.\u000aTwo REMOVED_DATE cm foci of DCIS are present <0.1 cm from the inked unoriented margin\u000a(block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID). DCIS is present focally REMOVED_DATE cm from the inked unoriented margin\u000a(blocks REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia, apocrine cysts and columnar cell hyperplasia also\u000apresent.\u000aNOTE: Hormone receptor and Her2/neu studies are in progress. Results will be\u000areported in an addendum. This carcinoma would be classified as AJCC (6th\u000aedition) Tis NX MX.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Atypical epithelium on prior core biopsy.\u000aOperation: Rt. breast needle-directed breast biopsy.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Rule out DCIS.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Rt. breast needle-directed breast biopsy (to mammo via F.S. rm).\u000aRADIOLOGY REPORT:\u000aClip and Ca++s in specimen.\u000a- C. Denison\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in one part, labeled with the patient?s name,\u000aunit number, and "1" Right breast needle-directed breast biopsy, and consists\u000aof one unoriented, yellow/white fragment of fibrofatty, soft tissue (4.0 x REMOVED_DATE \u000ax REMOVED_DATE cm), which has a needle-localization wire exiting from one side. The\u000asurgical resection margin is inked in blue, and the specimen is entirely,\u000aserially submitted, starting from the end perpendicular to the exit site of the\u000awire. Accompanying the specimen, there is a radiograph, labeled with the\u000apatient's name and unit number and demonstrating a soft tissue mass with a\u000aneedle localization wire, an S-shaped clip and microcalcifications encircled by\u000athe radiologist.\u000aMicros REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slices 1 and 2, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicros REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slices 3 through 7, each bisected, bend in needle site in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID,\u000aclip in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, odd-numbered blocks are the arbitrarily designated\u000a"front" of the specimen, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 8, 1 frag, ESS.\u000apab/MMM\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aPrelim Dx Release by Patricia A. R. Brunker M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aNo Action - Prelim Sent by Deborah A Dillon M.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Deborah A Dillon M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM:\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for DCIS (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor - POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor - POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) - POSITIVE (3+)\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000acarcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but only\u000aa portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in >10%\u000aof tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in\u000a>10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aAddendum by James L Connolly M.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aAddendum #1 by James L Connolly M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
