reactivity\u000ain >10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: REMOVED_DATE cm mass, right upper outer quadrant.\u000aOperation: 11g Ultrasound.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: PCC\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1) Right breast core samples - brow cassette.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by CHANG,BRIAN S.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name and unit\u000anumber only, and consists of a tan, unlabeled cassete containing multiple,\u000asoft, fragmented, yellow to white tissue cores (1.3 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in\u000aaggregate).\u000aMicro 1: Multi frags, ESS.\u000adfi\u000aReports to: MEYER, JACK, E. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY(IES)\u000a[report_end]
