VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: Esther Rhei M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-05-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Paula C Abreu-e-Lima, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Deborah A Dillon, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. RIGHT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZATION EXCISION FOR A MASS AND A CLIP:\u000aINVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA, moderately differentiated (modified Bloom-Richardson\u000agrade II/III), with focal mucinous differentiation, measuring REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000aNo definitive lymphovascular invasion is seen.\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, solid and cribriform types (intermediate nuclear\u000agrade), with associated calcifications, is present in REMOVED_DATE blocks as a minor\u000acomponent (EIC negative).\u000aInvasive carcinoma is present at the anterior margin as a broad front (block\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), at the inferior margin (0.2 cm; block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID; re-excised in part C)), <0.1 cm\u000afrom the lateral margin (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID; re-excised in part D), <0.1 cm from the\u000aanterior-inferior margin (0.2 cm; block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior margin\u000afocally (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID; re-excised in part\u000aB). Invasive carcinoma is >0.3 cm from posterior and superior margins.\u000aDCIS is present focally REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior margin (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID). All other\u000amargins are >0.3 cm from DCIS.\u000aSkeletal muscle is present and shows no involvement by carcinoma.\u000aPerineural invasion is present.\u000aBiopsy site changes.\u000aCalcifications present in association with benign epithelium.\u000aB. MEDIAL SHAVE MARGIN:\u000aResidual DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU is present in one of seven slides.\u000aThe surgical margin is negative (>0.3 cm) for DCIS.\u000aNo invasive carcinoma is present.\u000aCalcifications present in benign epithelium.\u000aC. SPECIMEN LABELED "INFERIOR SHAVE MARGIN":\u000aNo residual carcinoma is seen.\u000aSkeletal muscle with no tumor present.\u000aD. SPECIMEN LABELED "LATERAL SHAVE MARGIN":\u000aNo residual carcinoma is seen.\u000aNOTE: The patient presented with a REMOVED_DATE cm mass (by MRI). Following neoadjuvant\u000achemotherapy, the mass measured REMOVED_DATE cm by MRI. Invasive carcinoma in the\u000acurrent excision measures REMOVED_DATE cm, is relatively cellular and appears viable,\u000awith little evidence of treatment effect. This may represent a grade 2 response\u000ain the Miller-Payne system.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 60 y.o. female s/p neoadjuvant chemotherapy for treatment of right\u000abreast core biopsy diagnosed invasive carcinoma (2.7 cm by MRI). s/p R sentinel\u000anode biopsy with one negative sentinel node.\u000aOperation: R breast wire localized lumpectomy\u000aOperative Findings: None given\u000aClinical Diagnosis: R breast cancer\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000a1. R breast tissue (wire loc lumpectomy, short stitch superior, long lateral,\u000awhip at R chest wall margin) to mammo\u000a2. Medial shave margin - whip stitch @ new margin\u000a3. Inferior shave margin - whip stitch new margin\u000a4. Lateral shave margin\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in four parts, each labeled with the patient?s\u000aname, unit number.\u000aPart A, "#1 right wire localized breast lumpectomy," consists of a previously\u000ainked breast excision specimen, containing a single localization wire. The\u000aspecimen (6.1 cm superior to inferior x REMOVED_DATE cm medial to lateral x REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aanterior to posterior) has three orienting sutures (short=superior,\u000along=lateral, and whip stitch=right chest wall margin). The specimen is inked\u000aper pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black;\u000aanterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. The\u000aaccompanying radiograph shows a spiculated mass, the localization wire, and a\u000asingle clip. The specimen is serially sectioned revealing a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm\u000awhite-grey stellate mass, which grossly abuts the anterior and inferior margins\u000aand extends to within REMOVED_DATE cm of the superior, REMOVED_DATE cm of the posterior, REMOVED_DATE of\u000athe medial, and REMOVED_DATE cm of the lateral margins. 90% of the mass was submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: mass to anterior and posterior margins, 1 frag each, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: mass in relation to superior, posterior, and medial margins, 3\u000afrags, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: mass to inferior and posterior margins, multiple frags, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: lateral margin, 1 frag each, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: additional inferior and medial margins, 2 frags, RSS\u000aPart B, "#2 medial shaved margin, whip-stitch at new margin," consists of a\u000abreast excision specimen (4.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), oriented by a whip-stitch\u000adesignated new margin. The new margin is inked black. The specimen is entirely\u000asubmitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: new medial margin, multiple frags, ESS\u000aPart C, "#3 inferior shaved margin, whip-stitch at new margin," consists of a\u000abreast excision specimen (4.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), oriented by a whip-stitch\u000adesignated new inferior margin. The new margin is inked blue. The specimen is\u000aentirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: new inferior margin, multiple frags, ESS\u000aPart D, "#4 lateral shaved margin," consists of an unoriented breast excision\u000aspecimen (3.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). No stitch was placed to designate the new\u000amargin. The outer surface of the specimen is inked blue. The specimen is\u000aentirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: new lateral margin, multiple frags, ESS\u000aPAL/jp\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Paula C Abreu-e-Lima M.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Deborah A Dillon M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
