VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Paul A. VanderLaan, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Lucian R Chirieac, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. RIGHT BREAST MASS, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A CLIP:\u000aFibrous breast tissue with apocrine change.\u000aCore biopsy site.\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy.\u000aThe margins were inked and evaluated.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 75 year old postmenopausal female, S/P 10 years of ER(+) R breast\u000amass. REMOVED_DATE  mammogram supplemented with U/S demonstrates a 6:00 axis 7 mm\u000amass. REMOVED_DATE  core biopsy revealed fibrous breast tissue - excision is\u000arecommended.\u000aOperation: R breast wire localized biopsy.\u000aOperative Findings: Not provided.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: R breast mass.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) right breast mass - short stitch/superior, long stitch/lateral, whip\u000astitch/deep margin.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in one part, labeled with the patient's name,\u000aunit number, and "right breast mass", and consists of an irregular fragment of\u000afibroadipose tissue (4.4 cm S-I x REMOVED_DATE cm M-L x REMOVED_DATE cm A-P) with a short suture\u000adesignating superior, a long suture designating lateral, and a whipstitch\u000adesignating deep margin. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol per\u000asurgeon for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue;\u000asuperior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/ orange. There is a\u000aneedle localization wire entering the lateral aspect of the specimen and\u000aentering through the medial aspect of the specimen. The specimen is serially\u000asectioned from superior to inferior to exhibit an ill-defined tan-white firm\u000anodule (0.6 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) located REMOVED_DATE cm to the medial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to the\u000aposterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to the lateral and\u000aanterior margins, and REMOVED_DATE cm to the inferior margin. A metallic clip is\u000aidentified within the nodule. The remaining breast parenchyma consists of 70%\u000ayellow lobulated adipose tissue to 30% white fibrous tissue.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Perpendicular superior margin, 2 frags in each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Body, sequentially submitted from superior to inferior to include\u000anodule (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) and area of clip (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), 1 frag in each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Perpendicular inferior margin, 2 frags, ESS.\u000ajc/lp\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Lucian R Chirieac M.D., Electronically signed on Monday\u000aREMOVED_MONTH 05, 2009 at 05:31:48PM\u000a[report_end]
