 deep margin, consistent with prior biopsy site. No\u000aother lesions are grossly identified. The remainder of the breast parenchyma\u000ais composed of approximately 90% adipose and 10% fibrous tissue. No lymph\u000anodes are identified within the lateral portion of the specimen.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Skin and nipple, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Representative sections of biopsy cavity, from medial to\u000alateral, 11 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Upper/outer quadrant, 1 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lower/outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lower/inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Upper/inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aBGL/mmm\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Briana Gleason M.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a11/11/2005\u000a[report_end]
