VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final Type: Surgical Pathology Pathology Report: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID OPERATION DATE: 03 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON: 03 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 13:12 CLINICAL DATA: Left upper outer quadrantectomy of breast. =============================================================================== *** FINAL DIAGNOSIS *** BREAST (LEFT, UPPER-OUTER) QUADRANTECTOMY: 1. INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA, POORLY DIFFERENTIATED, (GRADE REMOVED_DATE ). (SEE NOTE). 2. THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 8 AXILLARY LYMPH NODES. 3. FIBROCYSTIC CHANGE WITH EPITHELIOSIS. 4. RADIAL SCAR. 4. FIBROADENOMA, MICROSCOPIC. NOTE: The tumor measures REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest dimension. All examined inked surgical margins are negative for carcinoma. No vascular or lymphatic invasion is identified. Estrogen and progesterone receptor studies will be reported as an addendum. Diagnosis by: Michael Pins, M.D. Signed On: 06 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 16:37 =============================================================================== *** RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum *** RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST (LEFT): THE TUMOR CELLS DO NOT STAIN FOR ESTROGEN RECEPTOR PROTEIN. THE TUMOR CELLS DO NOT STAIN FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN. Note: In this laboratory, we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way (paraffin sections) and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay. 91% of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay. 96% of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay. When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections, the predictive value of a positive result was 97% and the predictive value of a negative result was 95%. In this laboratory, we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay. Sixty-five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay, and 98% of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors. THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY. THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES. Added by: Frederick Carl Koerner, M.D. Signed On: 17 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 16:44 GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received fresh labeled with the patient's name and unit number only is a 110 gram resection specimen of breast tissue REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm with contiguous axillary tissue REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm with a long suture designating a breast mass and short suture designating the lower cephalad margin of the axillary tissue. The external surface of the breast tissue and axillary contents is lobulated unremarkable fibroadipose tissue. Within the breast tissue is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm mobile well-circumbscribed nodule REMOVED_DATE cm. from the superior aspect and within REMOVED_DATE cm. of the anterior and deep margins. The external surface is inked black with the posterior aspect inked yellow on black, and the specimen is sectioned to reveal a well-circumscribed pink-tan mass REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest dimension extending to within REMOVED_DATE cm of the anterior resection margin and to within less than REMOVED_DATE cm of the deep margin. The remaining tissue is strands of white-pink rubbery breast parenchyma within lobulated yellow adipose tissue. Within the axilla are multiple large firm lymph nodes which on cross section have a white-tan appearance; these range in size from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The largest three are bisected and submitted in cassettes A and B. Remaining lymph nodes are submitted entirely in cassette C. Section code A-C Axillary lymph nodes. D Medial en face resection margin. E-G Representative sections of the tumor with anterior and deep margins. H-K Radial sections through the inferior margin. L-N Representative radial sections through the superior margin. O Representative radial section into the axilla. Resident: Mark vanGorder, MD =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: MGH-INPATIENT (FLR.UNKNOWN) REPORTS TO: Ashby Carter Moncure, M.D. PART : BREAST (LEFT, UPPER-OUTER) QUADRANTECTOMY\u000a[report_end]
