\u000aimmunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity\u000ain >10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 66 year old female with a new irregular mass in right breast 12:00.\u000aHistory of left breast cancer 15 years ago. Also ovarian cancer.\u000aBreast Imaging Findings: Irregular/spiculated.\u000aOperation: 14g U/S\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Invasive carcinoma\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Right breast (1 greenish-gray cassette)\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by BROWNE,TARA-JANE,MB,BCH,BAO\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit\u000anumber, and "right breast", in a light green cassette, and consists of\u000amultiple, soft, fragmented, yellow to white tissue cores (1.6 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in\u000aaggregate).\u000aMicro 1: Multi frags, ESS.\u000akks\u000aReports to: DENISON, CHRISTINE M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY(IES)\u000a[report_end]
