ht breast wire localized partial mastectomy\u000aRADIOLOGY: Mass in specimen. JL\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by LOMBARD,DAVID B.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in one part, labeled with the patient's name,\u000aunit number and "#1. right breast wire localized partial mastectomy", and\u000aconsists of a mass of fibroadipose tissue (5.5 cm lateral to medial x REMOVED_DATE cm\u000asuperior to inferior x REMOVED_DATE cm superficial to deep). The specimen has been\u000apreviously inked by the surgeon per pathology protocol for the evaluation of\u000amargins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green;\u000alateral = yellow; medial = orange. Within the sectioned specimen there is a\u000afirm with spiculated lesion (1.6 x REMOVED_DATE x 1 cm) that is grossly for suspicious\u000afor malignancy. This lesion comes to within REMOVED_DATE cm of the superior margin,\u000a0.3 cm of the lateral margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin, come close to\u000athe anterior margin, and is distant from all margins. The remainder of the\u000aspecimen consists of predominantly fatty tissue. The specimen is entirely\u000asubmitted from lateral to medial for histologic analysis.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  right breast wire localized partial mastectomy, mult frags, ESS\u000a(suspicious lesion present in #4-8)\u000adl\u000aReports to: KAELIN, CAROLYN, MARY M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY - PARTIAL OR SIMPLE\u000a[report_end]
