ting\u000athe localizing wire in place within an encircled area of scattered\u000acalcifications in the superomedial aspect of the specimen. Sectioning\u000ademonstrates unremarkable-appearing soft, lobulated tan/white adipose tissue\u000a(at least 40% of the specimen). There is a large (4.0 cm) ragged defect in the\u000aanterior/inferior surface of the specimen, which has been loosely sutured by\u000athe surgeon. The surrounding margins have been previously inked by the\u000asurgeon. There are no obvious masses, lesions or other abnormalities grossly.\u000aThe entire specimen is sequentially submitted from medial to lateral.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: breast tissue, mult frags, ESS. NOTE: Area of interest per\u000aradiograph roughly in micro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000adb\u005cpab\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Alessandra F Nascimento M.D., Electronically signed on\u000a10/15/2007\u000a[report_end]
