VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID LYMPH NODE BIOPSY\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aGULIZIA, JAMES, MARTIN, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by GULIZIA,JAMES MARTIN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000a#1. SPECIMEN LABELED "LEFT AXILLARY SENTINEL NODE":\u000aOne (1) lymph node with no evidence of metastasis seen in multiple levels.\u000a#2. SPECIMEN LABELED "LEFT BREAST TISSUE"; BREAST BIOPSY, WIRE LOCALIZATION FOR\u000aA MASS:\u000aINVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA, well to moderately differentiated (modified\u000aBloom-Richardson grade I-II/III), present as several microscopic foci,\u000alargest focus, REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000aNo lymphatic/vascular invasion seen.\u000aInvasive tumor is focally present within REMOVED_DATE cm of the inferior margin\u000a(block 22) and is focally present within REMOVED_DATE cm of the anterior margin.\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN-SITU present as multiple foci, associated with and\u000aaway from areas involved by invasive tumor.\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN-SITU, solid and cribriform types, intermediate nuclear\u000agrade, present as a single microscopic focus (block 23) away from\u000ainvasive tumor and at least 3 mm from the closest (medial) margin.\u000aSkin with cicatrix and chronic inflammation.\u000aFibrocystic change with microcysts.\u000aMicrocalcifications in association with benign epithelium.\u000aBiopsy site with repair reaction.\u000aNOTE: The specimen was entirely submitted for histologic review. ER/PR\u000aand HER-2/neu studies will be performed and reported in an addendum.\u000a#3. SPECIMEN LABELED "LEFT AXILLARY LEVEL I AND II":\u000aNine (9) lymph nodes with no evidence of metastasis.\u000aThe lymph nodes exhibit mild suppurative lymphadenitis.\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: by BOROWSKY,ALEXANDER D.,M.D.\u000aREVISED ADDENDUM REMOVED_DATE \u000aThe slides are reviewed for margin evaluation. The closest approach of tumor\u000ato a true inked margin is focal extension to REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior and\u000ainferior margins.\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for invasive carcinoma:\u000aEstrogen receptor positive\u000aProgesterone receptor positive - low\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) negative (0)\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000ainvasive carcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but\u000aonly a portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity\u000ain >10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 40 year old female surgically postmenopausal female who recently\u000aD/C HRT with a left breast UOQ palpable mass REMOVED_DATE cm by ultrasound.\u000aCore biopsy REMOVED_DATE  revealed infiltrating lobular carcinoma, and\u000aLCIS.\u000aOperation: Left breast lumpectomy with sentinel node mapping and axillary\u000adissection\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast cancer\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1) Left axillary sentinel lymph node\u000a#2) Left breast tissue (short suture/superior; long suture/lateral;\u000awhip stitch chest wall)\u000a#3) Left axillary level I and II lymph node dissection\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "#2 LEFT BREAST TISSUE, SHORT SUTURE SUPERIOR, LONG SUTURE\u000aLATERAL, WHIPSTITCH CHEST WALL (GROSS EXAMINATION ONLY)":\u000aOld biopsy site identified.\u000aFirm vaguely mass-like area present (2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), close to anterior\u000amargin (blue ink).\u000aRADIOLOGY NOTE:\u000aLesion and wire in specimen\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by DORER,RUSSELL K.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in three parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart one, labeled "left axillary sentinel node", consists of one pink/yellow\u000afragment of fibroadipose tissue (1.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). One REMOVED_DATE cm in maximum\u000adimension lymph node is found within the specimen and entirely submitted at\u000a0.2 cm intervals.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  sentinel node, 4 frags, ESS\u000aPart two, labeled "left breast tissue marked short suture superior, long suture\u000alateral, whip stitch on chest wall", and consists of a single fragment of\u000ayellow/pink fibroadipose tissue (10.1 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) oriented with three\u000asutures, a short suture designated superior, long suture designated lateral\u000aand a whip stitch on the chest wall. There is needle localization wire in\u000aplace. The specimen is oriented in the frozen section room by Dr. Kaelin.\u000aThere is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm white/tan skin ellipse on the medial side of the\u000aspecimen. The specimen is inked in the following six colors: anterior=blue,\u000aposterior=black, lateral=red, medial=green, superior=yellow and\u000ainferior=orange. According to Dr. Kaelin, the posterior margin is the deep\u000afascial plane and the anterior margin was "peeled" off the skin. Centrally\u000alocated in the specimen is a REMOVED_DATE cm in diameter biopsy cavity. In addition,\u000athere is a firm white fibrous mass (2.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) located adjacent to\u000athe anterior (blue) margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the deep margin. This mass is\u000aalso REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin and REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin.\u000aThis mass is medial to the biopsy cavity and located approximately REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000athe medial margin. The entire specimen is submitted from lateral to medial\u000amargins.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  breast biopsy, mult frags, ESS\u000aPart three, labeled "left axillary level I and II", consists of one fragment\u000aof yellow/pink fibroadipose tissue (6.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). Nine (9) lymph nodes\u000aare found after careful dissection of the specimen. The largest node measures\u000a1.1 cm in maximum dimension.\u000aMicro 40: one lymph node, 4 frags, ESS\u000aMicro 41: one lymph node, 4 frags, ESS\u000aMicro 42: one lymph node, 5 frags, ESS\u000aMicro 43: two lymph nodes, 1 inked black, 5 frags, ESS\u000aMicro 44: two lymph nodes, 1 inked black, 4 frags, ESS\u000aMicro 45: 1 lymph node, mult frags, ESS\u000aMicro 46: 1 lymph node, mult frags, ESS\u000ardo\u000aReports to: KAELIN, CAROLYN, MARY M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: LYMPH NODE BIOPSY\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: LYMPH NODE BIOPSY\u000a[report_end]
