VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Amend/Addenda\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast core needle biopsy\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: LORRAINE B TWOHIG MB,BCH,BAO\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000a********** Addended Report ***********\u000aResident: Jacqueline M William, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Deborah A Dillon, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, UPPER OUTER, 14 G ULTRASOUND GUIDED CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR AN\u000aIRREGULAR LOBULATED REMOVED_DATE CM MASS:\u000aCARCINOMA IN SITU with mixed ductal and lobular features, solid type\u000a(intermediate nuclear grade), is present.\u000aNOTE: Immunohistochemistry for E-cadherin demonstrates absence of membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity. Immunohistochemistry for p63/REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID demonstrates\u000amyoepithelial cells around foci of in situ carcinoma.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHISTORY: FH breast cancer (mother age 49) and a prior biopsy showing ALH in\u000a2005 at BWH.\u000aBREAST IMAGING FINDING:\u000a1. 7 mm, Nonpalpable and circumscribed/lobulated mass, .\u000aLOCATION:\u000a1.\u000aTYPE OF CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY:\u000a1. 14G Ultrasound\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000a1. 14G Ultrasound 4 x 14G cores - Pink\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit\u000anumber, and "right breast", and consists of one pink cassette labeled "right"\u000acontaining multiple yellow/tan to white/tan soft tissues (1.1 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in\u000aaggregate).\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Pink cassette contents, multi frags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-07-REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000alm/ag\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Deborah A Dillon M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM (8/13/07):\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for carcinoma in situ with mixed features (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor NEGATIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) WEAKLY POSITIVE (2+)\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000acarcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but only\u000aa portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in >10%\u000aof tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in\u000a>10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aAddendum #1 by Deborah A Dillon M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
