art three, "lateral", consists of two fragments of yellow fibroadipose tissue\u000awhich measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate. The specimens are inked blue,\u000aserially sectioned and entirely submitted.\u000aPart four, "left breast nodule", consists of a single nodule of a fibroadipose\u000atissue with no firm REMOVED_DATE cm round nodule. The entire specimen measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000ax REMOVED_DATE cm. There is inked section and entirely submitted. Sectioning the\u000anodule reveals a cystic structure which contains a white mucoid material.\u000aMicro sections:\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  portions of left breast biopsy, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  specimen labeled medial, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  specimen labeled lateral, ESS.\u000aMicro 11: specimen labeled left breast nodule, ESS.\u000aReports to: KANE, J.GREGORY M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
