VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY(IES)\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aBOROWSKY, ALEXANDER, D., M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by BOROWSKY,ALEXANDER D.,M.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST, UPPER INNER QUADRANT, STEREOTACTIC CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY FOR A MASS:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA, measuring at least REMOVED_DATE cm in size (see NOTE).\u000aThe carcinoma is moderately differentiated (modified Bloom Richardson\u000aGrade II/III).\u000aNo lymphovascular invasion is seen in this limited specimen.\u000aNo in situ carcinoma is present in this limited specimen.\u000aNOTE:\u000aThe tumor has predominantly lobular features.\u000aImmunohistochemical analysis for estrogen receptors, progesterone receptors,\u000aand REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu will be performed and reported in an addendum.\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: by BOROWSKY,ALEXANDER D.,M.D.\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for invasive carcinoma:\u000aCytokeratin (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) Positive\u000aEstrogen receptor Positive\u000aProgesterone receptor Positive\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) Negative (0)\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000ainvasive carcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but\u000aonly a portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity\u000ain >10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 53 year old female with a spiculated mass in LUIQ - irregular\u000ahypoechoic are on U/S.\u000aBreast Imaging Findings: Irregular/spiculated.\u000aOperation: 11g stereotactic breast core biopsy\u000aOperative findings: Cores obtained\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Suspected carcinoma\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Cores (1 orange cassette)\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by MCMENAMIN,MAIRIN,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit\u000anumber, and "left breast", in an orange cassette, and consists of multiple,\u000asoft, fragmented, yellow to white tissue cores (2.7 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in\u000aaggregate).\u000aMicro 1: Multi frags, ESS.\u000akks\u000aReports to: FROST, ELISABETH, PEPPERELL M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY(IES)\u000a[report_end]
