VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aBROWN, FELIX, MARCEL, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by BROWN,FELIX MARCEL,M.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZATION FOR A MASS WITH A CLIP, AND SENTINEL NODE\u000aBIOPSY AND AXILLARY NODE DISSECTION (#3 SPECIMENS):\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA AND NEGATIVE LYMPH NODES.\u000aSYNOPSIS:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA\u000aSize - REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aMultifocal? - no\u000aHistologic Type - lobular\u000aHistologic Grade (SBR) - III (poor)\u000aNuclear Grade - high\u000aEIC - negative\u000aLymphovascular invasion - absent\u000aDermal lymphatic invasion - N/A\u000aSkin invasion - N/A\u000aSkeletal muscle invasion - N/A\u000aFinal Margins (invasive) -\u000aNegative (no ink on tumor) - all\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU - absent\u000aLYMPH NODES\u000aSentinel Lymph Nodes (3 H&E levels examined, specimen #3) - negative\u000aNumber of positive nodes - 0\u000aNumber of nodes examined - 2\u000aAxillary Lymph Nodes (specimen #2) - negative\u000aNumber of positive nodes - 0\u000aNumber of nodes examined - 3\u000aTOTAL POSITIVE NODES (sentinel + axillary) - 0:5\u000aOTHER FINDINGS\u000aCore biopsy site\u000aAJCC CLASSIFICATION - REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDc pREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID MX\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER/PR/HER-2) - performed previously\u000aRIGHT BREAST, BREAST REDUCTION (2090g):\u000aSkin with no significant pathologic change.\u000aBreast tissue with cysts.\u000aNo tumor seen.\u000aLEFT BREAST, BREAST REDUCTION (1620g):\u000aSkin with no significant pathologic change.\u000aBreast tissue with cysts and apocrine metaplasia.\u000aNo tumor seen.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 53 year old female with non-palpable cancer of left breast.\u000aOperation: Left needle directed breast biopsy, sentinel node biopsy, bilateral\u000abreast reduction\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast cancer\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1) Area of tumor (left breast)\u000a#2) Axillary node, left\u000a#3) Sentinel node, left\u000a#4) Right breast tissue\u000a#5) Left breast tissue\u000aRADIOLOGY: Mass in specimen......J. Leung, MD\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by LOMO,LESLEY C.,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in five parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart one, labeled "#1. area of tumor, left breast", consists of a left breast\u000awire localized biopsy specimen (9.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) which contains a needle\u000alocalization wire, a short stitch denoting superior margin and a long stitch\u000adenoting lateral margin. The specimen has been previously inked per pathology\u000aprotocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue;\u000asuperior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. An\u000aaccompanying radiograph shows a clip and a wire at the site of a\u000astellate-shaped, radio-opaque mass. The specimen is serially sectioned from\u000amedial to lateral, revealing a white, hard, stellate mass (1.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm)\u000aassociated with a small area of hemorrhage and what appears to be necrosis.\u000aThe mass is REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin, greater than 2 cm from the lateral\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE \u000acm from anterior margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin. The remainder\u000aof the breast parenchyma is comprised predominantly of adipose tissue with no\u000aother lesions identified. Representative sections of the mass including\u000arelationship to anterior, posterior, and superior margins (closest), as well\u000aas of the tumor and of the margins are submitted for histologic analysis.\u000aMicro 1: tumor and anterior margin, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 2: tumor and posterior margin, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 3: tumor and superior margin, 1 frag, rSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  tumor, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 8: medial perpendicular margin, 2 frags, RSS\u000aMicro 9: lateral perpendicular margin, 2 frags, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  inferior margin, 1 frag, RSS\u000aPart two, labeled "#2. axillary node", consists of multiple fragments of\u000ayellow/tan fibroadipose tissue (5.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate). One lymph is\u000aidentified (1.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm); additional soft tissue is identified with\u000amultiple small, possible lymph nodes. The lymph node and additional soft\u000atissue containing possible lymph nodes are submitted for histologic analysis.\u000aMicro 12: 1 lymph node bisected, 2 frags, ESS\u000aMicro 13: soft tissue with multiple small possible lymph nodes, 1 frag, ESS\u000aPart three, labeled "#3. sentinel node", consists of two fragments of\u000ayellow/tan fibroadipose tissue (1.4 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm, and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm).\u000aTwo lymph nodes are identified (0.6 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm)\u000awhich are each bisected and submitted entirely.\u000aMicro 14: largest lymph node bisected, 2 frags, ESS\u000aMicro 15: lymph node, bisected, 2 frags ESS\u000aPart four, labeled "#4. right breast tissue", consists of a 2090g aggregate of\u000afibroadipose tissue with attached skin measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in\u000aaggregate. There is a portion of unremarkable skin only measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000ax REMOVED_DATE cm. A nipple is not present. The fibroadipose tissue with attached skin\u000ais unremarkable; the tan skin ellipse measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm, and the breast\u000aparenchyma is comprised of approximately 30% fibrous tissue and 70% adipose\u000atissue and is without any focal lesions or masses. Representative sections of\u000abreast tissue and skin are submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  breast parenchyma and skin, 2 frags, RSS\u000aPart five, labeled "#5. left breast tissue", consists of a 1620g specimen\u000aconsisting of four fragments of breast parenchyma, two of which contain\u000awhite/tan skin (41.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate), skin measuring up to REMOVED_DATE \u000acm in size. A nipple is not present. The breast parenchyma is comprised of\u000aapproximately 35% fibrous tissue with clear fluid-filled cysts measuring up to\u000a0.9 cm in diameter, and 65% adipose tissue. No gross lesions or masses are\u000aidentified.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  breast parenchyma with skin, 1 or 2 frags, RSS\u000alcl\u000aReports to: CHRISTIAN, ROGER, L. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: LYMPH NODES REGIONAL RESECTION\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: LYMPH NODE BIOPSY\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST REDUCTION MAMMOPLASTY\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST REDUCTION MAMMOPLASTY\u000a[report_end]
