VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Sentinel Lymph Nodes(s)\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: DIANE C LOCKHART M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Andrew M. Quinn, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Gilbert Brodsky, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. LEFT SENTINEL LYMPH NODES (including FSA):\u000aPlease see Part B.\u000aB. LEFT BREAST WIRE LOCALIZATION FOR A MASS AND A CLIP\u000aAND SENTINEL LYMPH NODES BIOPSY (including Parts A and B):\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA, WITH MIXED FEATURES\u000aNEGATIVE LYMPH NODES\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA\u000aSize - REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aMultifocal - No\u000aHistologic type - Mixed Ductal and Lobular\u000aHistologic grade (SBR) - I (Well) (3 to 5 points)\u000aTubules - < 10% (3 points)\u000aNuclear grade - Low (1 point)\u000aMitotic counts - 1 point\u000aEIC - Not applicable\u000aLVI - Absent\u000aDermal LVI - Not applicable\u000aSkin invasion - Not applicable\u000aSkeletal muscle invasion - Not applicable\u000aFinal Margins (invasive)\u000aNegative (> REMOVED_DATE cm) - Posterior, superior, medial, lateral\u000aClose (0.1 to REMOVED_DATE cm) - REMOVED_DATE cm to anterior, REMOVED_DATE to inferior\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU - Absent\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - Absent\u000aLYMPH NODES\u000aSentinel lymph nodes - Negative (3 H&E levels examined)\u000aNumber of positive nodes - 0\u000aNumber of nodes examined - 1\u000aTOTAL POSITIVE NODES (all specimens)- 0:1\u000aOTHER FINDINGS\u000aCore biopsy site\u000aCalcifications in benign epithelium\u000aFibroadenoma (0.7 cm)\u000aAJCC Classification (6th edition) - REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDc Nsn0 MX\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER, PR, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) - Performed previously at an outside\u000ainstitution\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 73 y o woman with PMH lung CA S/P RLL resection and XRT found to have\u000airreg density on screening mammogram. S/P U/S core biopsy L breast 5 o'clock\u000ainvasive ductal/lobular CA.\u000aOperation: Left SLN bx; left wire-localized lumpectomy.\u000aOperative Findings: None provided.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left invasive breast CA.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) Left SLN.\u000aB/2) Left breast tissue 5 o'clock; short - superior, long - lateral.\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "LEFT SENTINEL LYMPH NODE" (FSA):\u000aSentinel lymph node, negative for tumor.\u000aOR Consultation by: William Robert Welch, M.D.\u000aThe senior physician certifies that he/she personally conducted a gross and/or\u000amicroscopic examination of the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed\u000athe rapid diagnos(es) related thereto.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart A, labeled "#1. Left sentinel lymph node", consists of a tan rubbery lymph\u000anode, with attached yellow adipose tissue (0.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The attached\u000aadipose tissue is removed, and the lymph node is bisected and submitted in its\u000aentirety for frozen section as FSA. The remaining adipose tissue is submitted\u000afor permanents.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: FSA remnant, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Remainder of adipose tissue, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aPart B, labeled "#2. Left breast tissue 5 o'clock, short superior, long\u000alateral", consists of an irregular fragment of yellow lobulated fibrofatty\u000atissue (7.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), with a long suture designating lateral, and a\u000ashort suture designating superior. The specimen is received previously inked\u000aper pathology protocol as anterior blue, posterior black, superior red,\u000ainferior green, lateral yellow and medial orange. There is an inserted needle\u000alocalization wire, which enters along the lateral margin and traverses towards,\u000abut does not exit the anterior margin.\u000aPlease note, that this is also demonstrated in the radiograph interpreted via\u000acentricity. The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a white-tan irregular\u000aill-defined firm mass (1.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The mass is REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000aanterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin and REMOVED_DATE \u000acm from the medial margin. The mass contains a surgical clip, demonstrated on\u000athe specimen radiograph via centricity. The remaining cut surface displays 95%\u000ayellow lobulated adipose tissue, and 5% white fibrous tissue, with no\u000aadditional discrete masses or lesions identified. The specimen is sequentially\u000asubmitted in its entirety.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, radially, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross sections, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross section, bisected, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross section, bisected, with the mass in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 1 frag\u000aeach, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross section, bisected, with the mass and the\u000asurgical clip identified in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross section, bisected, with the mass in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 1 frag\u000aeach, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross section, bisected, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross section, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin, radially, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aCP/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Gilbert Brodsky M.D., Electronically signed on Thursday\u000aREMOVED_MONTH 19, 2009 at 05:26:37PM\u000a[report_end]
