_DATE cm) and a cyst (0.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) that abuts the posterior margin and\u000ais REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom the medial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000aanterior margin. The breast parenchyma is 80% adipose tissue.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin, perpendicular sections, REMOVED_DATE frags per block, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, perpendicular sections, REMOVED_DATE frags per block, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Remaining specimen sections containing old biopsy site cavity, REMOVED_DATE \u000afrags per block, ESS.\u000aNote: The cyst is contained within blocks REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000ata\u005cpab\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Michelle S Hirsch M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a7/25/2007\u000a[report_end]
