 lesion corresponds to an area of fibrous tissue.\u000aThere is no discrete mass. The margins are inked black and the specimen is\u000aentirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  breast tissue, 6 frags, ESS.\u000aPart two is labeled "left breast tissue (caudal)". The specimen consists of a\u000asingle fragment of fibroadipose tissue (3 x 2 x REMOVED_DATE cm). There is a wire in\u000athe specimen and an accompanying radiograph showing mass and calcifications in\u000arelation to the wire. The specimen is not further oriented. The margins are\u000ainked black. The area corresponding to the mass is an area of fibrous tissue.\u000aIt is irregular in appearance and comes close to the margin. This measures REMOVED_DATE \u000acm in greatest dimension. The specimen is entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  breast tissue, 7 frags, ESS.\u000amir\u000aReports to: CHRISTIAN, ROGER, L. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
