VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aMUELLER, JAMES, D., M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by MUELLER,JAMES,D.,M.D.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED BIOPSY FOR CALCIFICATIONS AND A CLIP:\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia, associated with calcifications (block 2).\u000aSclerosing adenosis associated with calcifications.\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia, apocrine metaplasia, and calcifications associated\u000awith benign epithelium are also present.\u000aPrior core biopsy site is identified.\u000aThe margins of the specimen were inked, submitted and examined\u000ahistologically.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 45 year old female with history of ADH on core - see previous BWH\u000acore biopsy report.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal right mammo\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1. Right breast tissue (short stitch/superior; long\u000astitch/lateral)\u000aRADIOLOGY: Calcifications in specimen. L. Frost,MD/LP\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by LOMO,LESLEY C.,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in one part, labeled with the patient's name,\u000aunit number and "#1. right breast tissue with stitch marked at short superior,\u000along lateral", and consists of a right breast wire localized biopsy specimen\u000a(5.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) which bears a short stitch to denote superior and long\u000astitch to denote lateral margin. The specimen also contains a wire\u000alocalization needle. An accompanying radiograph shows the specimen to contain\u000aa clip and a wire localization needle; there are at least five clusters of\u000amicrocalcifications present in the specimen. The specimen is inked per\u000apathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior =\u000ablue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. The\u000aspecimen is serially sectioned from lateral to medial revealing predominantly\u000awhite, rubbery, focally gritty breast parenchyma, with no discrete lesions or\u000amasses identified. The specimen is radiographed. The slide containing the\u000aclip is identified, and is submitted in cassette #12. The specimen is entirely\u000asubmitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  lateral perpendicular margins, 3 frags each, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  right breast wire localized biopsy from lateral to medial, 1 or 2\u000afrags each, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  medial perpendicular margin, 3 or 4 frags, ESS\u000alcl\u000aReports to: CARTER, KATHARINE M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
