VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Amend/Addenda\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: MEHRA GOLSHAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-06-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000a********** Addended Report ***********\u000aResident: Eric L Snyder, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Rebecca D Folkerth, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "RIGHT BREAST, EXCISION WIRE LOCALIZATION FOR A MASS\u000aAND A CLIP":\u000aINVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aSYNOPSIS:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA\u000aSize - REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aMultifocal - no\u000aHistologic Type - ductal\u000aHistologic Grade (SBR) - II (moderate)\u000aNuclear Grade - intermediate\u000aEIC - negative\u000aLymphovascular invasion -\u000aDermal lymphatic invasion - N/A\u000aSkin invasion - N/A\u000aSkeletal muscle invasion - N/A\u000aFinal Margins (invasive) -\u000aNegative (>0.3 cm) - superior, medial, anterior\u000aPositive (ink on carcinoma) - inferior (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID)\u000aposterior (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID)\u000alateral (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID)\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aTypes - solid, cribriform\u000aNuclear grade - intermediate\u000aCalcifications in DCIS - absent\u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - absent\u000aExtent of DCIS\u000aDCIS is present as a minor component of the invasive carcinoma\u000aFinal Margins (DCIS)\u000aNegative (>0.3 cm) - superior, medial, lateral,\u000aanterior, posterior\u000aClose (0.1-0.3 cm) - inferior (0.1 cm, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID)\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - absent\u000aOTHER FINDINGS\u000aCore biopsy site\u000aAJCC CLASSIFICATION (6th edition) - REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDb pNx MX\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER/PR/HER-2) - pending\u000aNOTE:\u000aThese results were reported to Dr. Mehra Golshan, by phone, on REMOVED_DATE  at 6:10\u000apm.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Right breast abnormal mammogram and MRI ultrasound-guided core biopsy\u000awith discordant results.\u000aOperation: Right breast wire-localized excisional biopsy.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast abnormal mammogram.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Right breast wire-loc excision.\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000aSpecimen contains intact wire, clip, and lesion. Report called to Dr. Golshan\u000ain OR, by Dr. Zorn.\u000aDr. L. Zorn\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "#1. Right breast wire-loc", and consists of a REMOVED_DATE x 6 x REMOVED_DATE cm, excisional\u000afibroadipose tissue that is oriented by sutures designating the superior (short\u000asuture) and lateral (long suture) margins. The specimen is inked per pathology\u000aprotocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue;\u000asuperior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. A localizing wire\u000aenters the specimen's lateral surface and exits posteriorly. The specimen is\u000areceived with a radiograph demonstrating the localizing wire in place within an\u000aill-defined lesion containing a metallic clip (lateral/posterior aspect of the\u000aspecimen). Sectioning in this area demonstrates an ill-defined, palpably firm,\u000atan/white lesion (at least REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 cm) abutting the inferior and\u000aposterior margins and within REMOVED_DATE cm of the closest superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of\u000athe closest lateral margin, and greater than REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior and\u000amedial margins. The mass demonstrates adjacent small cavities filled with\u000ahemorrhage and amorphous material and surrounded by fibrosis and fat necrosis\u000a(compatible with prior core biopsy site). A REMOVED_DATE cm metallic clip is noted in\u000athis area. The remaining specimen is predominantly soft, lobulated, tan/yellow\u000aadipose tissue (60% to 70%) with occasional, unremarkable, tan/white,\u000afibrodense tissue. The entire biopsy site and surrounding tissue (to include\u000amass) are submitted sequentially from lateral to medial.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Biopsy site and adjacent tissue (mass in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Anterior margin, 3 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aDB/ajb\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Rebecca D Folkerth M.D., Electronically signed on\u000a8/11/2006\u000aADDENDUM:\u000aCORRECTION:\u000aThe AJCC Classification for this lesion should be:\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_IDc pNx Mx\u000aAddendum #1 by Rebecca D Folkerth M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000aSurgical Addendum: (8/16/06)\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for invasive carcinoma (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) NEGATIVE (0)\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000acarcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but only\u000aa portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in >10%\u000aof tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in\u000a>10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aAddendum #2 by Andrea L Richardson M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a8/16/2006\u000aADDENDUM (9-21-06):\u000aNOTE:\u000aLymphovascular invasion is not identified.\u000aAddendum #3 by Rebecca D Folkerth M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM:\u000aA paraffin block of invasive carcinoma was sent for the genomic health oncotype\u000aDX Breast Cancer Assay with the following results (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aRecurrence Score = 12\u000aPatients with a Recurrence Score of 12 in the clinical validation study had an\u000aAverage Rate of Recurrence at 10 years of 8% (95% CI: 5% - 10%).\u000aAddendum #4 by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
