e patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart A, "#1. Right sentinel lymph node", consists of a tan/white lymph node\u000awith attached tan/yellow lobulated fat (1.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The cut surface\u000ais tan/yellow to blue, previously stained from dye. There is no evidence of\u000atumor grossly identifiable.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 4 frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, "#2. Right breast final inferior margin", consists of irregular\u000atan/yellow to tan/pink portion of breast tissue (3.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). One\u000asurface is tan/pink, smooth, and glistening. The opposing surface consists of\u000atan/yellow lobulated, focally cauterized fat. This surface has a suture that\u000ais demarcated as the new inferior margin. The smooth surface is inked black\u000awhile the new margin is inked green. The specimen is sectioned to show\u000atan/white fibrous tissue with focal tan/yellow fat necrosis.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Specimen serially sectioned, multi frags, ESS.\u000aPart C, "#3. Right breast final posterior margin suture equals new margin",\u000aconsists of a tan/yellow, lobulated portion of fibrofatty breast tissue (2.4 x\u000a1.8 x REMOVED_DATE cm). One aspect is tan/pink, focally disrupted and smooth, while the\u000aopposing surface consists of tan/yellow lobulated fat that is focally\u000acauterized. There is a suture demarcating this surface as the new posterior\u000amargin. This margin is inked black while the smooth surface is inked blue.\u000aThe specimen is serially sectioned to show the parenchyma consisting of focal\u000atan/white fibrous tissue with focal tan/yellow fat necrosis.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Specimen serially sectioned, multi frags total, ESS.\u000aPart D, "#4. Right breast final lateral margin", consists of a tan/yellow to\u000atan/white portion of fibrofatty breast tissue (2.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). One\u000asurface is tan/pink and smooth to focally disrupted while the other aspect\u000aconsists of tan/yellow to tan/white lobulated adipose tissue, with a suture\u000ademarcating this surface as the new lateral margin. This margin inked yellow\u000awhile the opposite surface is inked black. The specimen is serially sectioned\u000ato show tan/white, focally dense fibrous tissue and tan/yellow adipose tissue.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Specimen serially sectioned, multi frags total, ESS.\u000aDRD/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a9/11/2006\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM:\u000aPart C, specimen #3 should have been labeled ?RIGHT BREAST, FINAL POSTERIOR\u000aMARGIN?.\u000aTHE FINAL DIAGNOSIS IS UNCHANGED.\u000aAddendum #1 by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
