00aname and unit number.\u000aThe first part, "#1 right breast, stitch marking short superior", consists of a\u000a1088-gram right simple mastectomy specimen (19.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), bearing a\u000ashort suture to designate superior, a brown skin ellipse (13.5 x REMOVED_DATE cm) with a\u000a4.0 x REMOVED_DATE cm areola and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm nipple. No scar is grossly identified.\u000aThe deep margin has a smooth fascial plane which is inked in black and\u000aserially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm biopsy cavity which is REMOVED_DATE \u000acm from the deep margin and REMOVED_DATE cm from the skin. The biopsy cavity is\u000aassociated with focal areas of hemorrhage and necrosis and no residual tumor\u000ais grossly identified. One (1) lymph node is identified in the mid outer\u000abreast measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm, which is entirely submitted. The\u000aremainder of the breast parenchyma is comprised of rubbery, white fibrous\u000atissue (50%) and unremarkable yellow adipose tissue (50%).\u000aMicro 1: biopsy cavity at closest approach to margin, 3 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  biopsy cavity to include deep margin and skin and scar, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 6: upper inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 7: lower inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 8: upper outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 9: lower outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 10: nipple, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 11: lymph node, bisected, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aThe second part, sublabeled "#2 tissue from left breast", consists of a\u000a420-gram aggregate of yellow/tan, fibrofatty breast tissue and brown skin (16.0\u000ax REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate). The brown skin is wrinkled and unremarkable.\u000aSerial sectioning of the breast tissue reveals approximate equivalent amount of\u000arubbery white fibrous tissue and yellow adipose tissue, without lesions or\u000amasses suspicious for malignancy. Representative sections are submitted.\u000aMicro 12: skin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  left breast tissue, 2 frags each, RSS.\u000alcl\u000aReports to: PRIBAZ, JULIAN, JOSEPH M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: LYMPH NODE BIOPSY\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST REDUCTION MAMMOPLASTY\u000a[report_end]
