r.\u000aPart A, "#1. Right breast core needle BX", and consists of cores of\u000afibroadipose tissue aggregating REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm, embedded in toto.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Multi frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, "#2. Right breast, 4-mm punch BX", and consists of REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm\u000a(depth) white/tan circular skin, inked and embedded in toto.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 frag, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000adb/ag\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM:\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for invasive carcinoma (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor NEGATIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor NEGATIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) NEGATIVE (1+)\u000aNote: Due to the very limited amount of tumor present, poor preservation of\u000athe tissue, and the lack of normal breast epithelium to act as an internal\u000acontrol, these negative results should be interpreted with caution. Repeat\u000astudies should be performed on subsequent specimens.\u000aCOMMENT: This addendum was briefly unsigned and resigned to correct\u000ainformation within the addendum. The original report is unchanged.\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000acarcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but only\u000aa portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in >10%\u000aof tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in\u000a>10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aAddendum #1 by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aAmendment #1 by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
