VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Amend/Addenda\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, mastectomy with regional lymph nodes\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: JULIE L JONES M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000a********** Addended Report ***********\u000aResident: Elizabeth Amy Morgan, M.D.; Justine A Barletta, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Michael W Bennett, M.B., B.C.H.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. RIGHT BREAST, MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY AND AXILLARY (INCLUDING FSA):\u000aRESIDUAL INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA, poorly differentiated with prominent\u000achondroid matrix production, (modified Bloom-Richardson grade III/III),\u000amultifocal, largest focus of residual tumor REMOVED_DATE cm in a REMOVED_DATE cm tumor bed (see\u000anote).\u000aDermal invasion is present.\u000aNo lymphovascular invasion identified.\u000aNo in situ component is present.\u000aThe deep resection and skin margins are negative for tumor.\u000aMETASTATIC CARCINOMA is present as a MICROMETASTASIS (0.05 cm; 50 cells) in one\u000a(1) of sixteen (16) lymph nodes. No extranodal extension identified.\u000aTwo of the lymph nodes, in addition to the lymph node with viable tumor, show\u000avariably prominent hyalinization and hemosiderin-laden macrophages, consistent\u000awith treated tumor.\u000aFibroadenomas (largest REMOVED_DATE cm)\u000aAJCC Classification (6th edition): pyREMOVED_ACCESSION_IDc (multifocal) yREMOVED_ACCESSION_IDmi.\u000aNOTE: Due to the presence of matrix production this tumor would be classified\u000aas a metaplastic carcinoma.\u000aBy report, the pre-treatment size on physical examination was REMOVED_DATE cm. On\u000apost-treatment physical examination, the mass was 6 cm. The tumor bed on gross\u000aexamination of the mastectomy specimen was REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. Histologically the\u000atumor has 10% cellularity. These findings correspond to a Miller-Payne grade 3\u000aresponse. The Residual Cancer Burden Index (RCB)= REMOVED_DATE RCB-II.\u000aB. ADDITIONAL TISSUE AXILLARY TAIL:\u000aFibroadipose tissue negative for tumor.\u000aNo lymph nodes identified (entire specimen submitted for histologic\u000aevaluation).\u000aC. ADDITIONAL INFERIOR SKIN OF RIGHT BREAST:\u000aSeborrheic keratosis.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000aD. ADDITIONAL LATERAL SKIN:\u000aSkin and subcutaneous tissue, negative for tumor.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Right breast REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID IDC, S/P neoadjuvant chemotherapy.\u000aOperation: Right modified radical mastectomy.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast cancer.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) Rt breast and axillary contents, stitch - superior skin (FS - on skin\u000amargin between sutures).\u000aB/2) Additional tissue axillary tail (perm).\u000aC/3) Additional inferior skin of right breast (perm).\u000aD/4) Additional lateral skin (perm).\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "#1. RT BREAST STITCH SUPERIOR MARGIN" (FSA):\u000aSkin and subcutaneous negative for tumor in one representative section.\u000aArrival time: 10:18 AM\u000aReport time: 10:44 AM\u000aOR Consultation by: ALESSANDRA F. NASCIMENTO, M.D.\u000aResident: DICK HWANG, M.D., PH.D.\u000aThe senior physician certifies that he/she personally conducted a gross and/or\u000amicroscopic examination of the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed\u000athe rapid diagnos(es) related thereto.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in four parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and medical record number.\u000aPart A, labeled "Right breast and axillary contents, stitch superior skin",\u000aconsists of a 1095 gram right modified radical mastectomy specimen (25.0 x REMOVED_DATE \u000ax REMOVED_DATE cm) with a white/tan skin ellipse (19.5 x REMOVED_DATE cm) and attached axillary\u000atail (10.4 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). There is an area of skin puckering (1.5 cm in\u000agreatest dimension) overlying the right superior breast tissue. Immediately\u000abelow the skin puckering, there is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm ill-defined area of fibrosis\u000aand fat necrosis, located REMOVED_DATE cm from the closest deep margin, likely\u000arepresenting a tumor bed. There are three well-circumscribed, tan, rubbery\u000anodules (0.4 to REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest dimension), likely representing\u000afibroadenomas. The remainder of breast specimen consists of predominantly\u000aadipose tissue. The axillary tail contains at least 15 lymph nodes.\u000aRepresentative sections of the area of skin puckering is submitted for frozen\u000asection analysis as FSA. The entire tumor bed is submitted for histologic\u000aevaluation.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: FSA remnant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Likely tumor bed including deep margin and overlying skin\u000apuckering, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Breast tissue, medial and lateral to the tumor bed, 2, frags,\u000aRSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lower outer quadrant, including deep margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lower inner quadrant, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Upper inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Largest rubbery nodule, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 lymph node candidate, bisected, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 lymph node candidate, bisected, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 lymph node candidate, bisected, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 3 lymph node candidates, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 lymph node, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 lymph node candidate, bisected, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 lymph node candidate, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: lymph nodes (at least one lymph node), sectioned, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 lymph node candidate, bisected, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 lymph node candidate, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 lymph node candidate, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 2 lymph node candidates, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, labeled "additional axillary tail tissue (perm)", consists of one\u000afragment of yellow/tan fibroadipose tissue (4.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). No lymph\u000anodes are identified grossly. The entire specimen is submitted for histologic\u000aevaluation.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 2 frags, ESS.\u000aPart C, labeled "Additional inferior skin of right breast (perm)", consists of\u000aa skin ellipse and attached subcutaneous adipose tissue (9.4 x REMOVED_DATE cm, excised\u000ato a depth of REMOVED_DATE cm). Three slightly raised tan/white nodules (0.1 to REMOVED_DATE cm\u000ain greatest dimension) are present. No other gross lesions are identified.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Representative sections (including the skin nodule), 2 frags, RSS.\u000aPart D, labeled "Additional lateral skin (perm)", consists of an irregular\u000afragment of skin and attached subcutaneous tissue (5.6 x REMOVED_DATE cm, excised to a\u000adepth of REMOVED_DATE cm). No gross lesions are identified.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 2 frags, RSS.\u000aEM/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-07-REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Michael W Bennett M.B., B.C.H., Electronically signed on\u000a8/27/2007\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: (8/29/07)\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for invasive carcinoma (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor NEGATIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor NEGATIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) NEGATIVE (0)\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000ainvasive carcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low > 0% - < 10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor cells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but only a\u000aportion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+):Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in >10% of\u000atumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+):Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in >30% of\u000atumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aExternal controls are evaluated and show appropriate Immunoreactivity.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aAddendum #1 by James L Connolly M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
