VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aKRANE, JEFFREY, FRED, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by KRANE,JEFFREY FRED,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A CLIP:\u000aFocal atypical lobular hyperplasia (block 1).\u000aDense interlobular fibrosis (1.5 cm) with calcifications in benign\u000aepithelium.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000aClip identified.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Per Pathology resident: History of invasive right REMOVED_DATE cm lobular\u000acarcinoma (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID; REMOVED_DATE ), s/p excision of area. Re-excisions for\u000acalcifications in left breast with ADH (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID; REMOVED_DATE )\u000aOperation: Lt needle loc breast bx.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Atypical ductal hyperplasia, lt breast.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Lt breast tissue.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Clip in specimen. JL\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by OH,KIRSTINE YUNG-TING,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in one part, labeled with the patient's name,\u000aunit number and "#1 left breast". Attached with the specimen is a mammographic\u000aimage showing a fragment of soft tissue with a wire localizing needle and a\u000aclip present in the specimen. No microcalcifications are present in the\u000aspecimen. The specimen is received inked per pathology protocol for the\u000aevaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red;\u000ainferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange and has a wire localizing\u000aneedle present in the cyst. The breast tissue measures 7 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000aSectioning of the specimen reveals the majority of the specimen comprised of\u000ayellow/tan fibroadipose tissue. However, a small firm fragment of green inked\u000atissue (1.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) containing the clip is present. The cut surface of\u000athe nodule is homogenous and well\u000acircumscribed.\u000aMicro 1: firm nodule, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 2: medial margin of the breast tissue, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro 3: bisected fragment of breast tissue, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 4&5: bisected fragment of breast tissue, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  bisected segment of breast tissue, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro 9&10: bisected fragment of breast tissue, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro 11&12: bisected fragment of breast tissue, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro 13&14: bisected fragment of breast tissue, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro 15: breast tissue, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro 16: lateral border of breast tissue, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro 17: lateral border of breast tissue, 3 frags, ESS.\u000ako\u000aReports to: OSTEEN, ROBERT, T. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
