VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: MEHRA GOLSHAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Shakti Ramkissoon, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Jeffrey F Krane, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aSPECIMEN DESIGNATED "RIGHT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISIONAL BIOPSY":\u000aBenign breast tissue with microcalcifications in association\u000awith benign epithelium, apocrine metaplasia, cysts, columnar\u000acell change, focal epithelial hyperplasia, and dense interlobular\u000afibrosis.\u000aFocal acute hemorrhage is present, however, no definitive evidence\u000aof a prior biopsy site is seen; clinical correlation is needed.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the\u000aspecimen, including margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 35-year-old female with right breast abnormal mammogram with\u000acalcification atypia seen on outside pathology from core biopsy.\u000aOperation: Right breast wire localized excisional biopsy x 2 wires.\u000aOperative Findings: Not provided.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast abnormal mammogram.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Right breast wire localized excisional biopsy x 2 wires, short suture ?\u000asuperior, long suture ? lateral. (1 x-ray).\u000aRADIOLOGY: Called OR 34 and discussed with Dr. Golshan. Calcifications seen in\u000aspecimen ??\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "#1. Right breast wire-localized excisional biopsy x2, short suture\u000asuperior, long suture lateral", and consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm excision\u000aof fibroadipose tissue, oriented by sutures designating superior (short suture)\u000aand lateral (long suture) margins. The specimen is inked per pathology\u000aprotocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue;\u000asuperior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange (inked by\u000aprosector). Two localizing wires are present; one enters the superior aspect\u000aand exits medially and the second enters laterally and exits the\u000ainferior/posterior surface. The specimen is received with a radiograph\u000ademonstrating the localizing wires in place within the specimen, marking a\u000afaint cluster of calcifications centrally. Cut surfaces demonstrate at least\u000a75% granular tan/white fibrodense tissue, with focal hemorrhage in the area of\u000ainterest, likely consistent with prior core biopsy. There are no palpable or\u000avisible masses grossly. The entire specimen is submitted, sequentially from\u000alateral to medial, with perpendicular lateral margin in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, and perpendicular\u000amedial margin in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, and the area of interest per localizing wires likely in\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: serial sections, multi frags, ESS\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000adb/ag\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jeffrey F Krane M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a5/24/2008\u000a[report_end]
