VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aODZE, ROBERT, DANIEL, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by ODZE,ROBERT DANIEL,M.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST WIRE LOCALIZATION FOR A MASS (ONE SPECIMEN):\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU.\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU - present\u000aTypes - solid, cribriform\u000aNuclear grade - low to intermediate\u000aCalcifications in DCIS - present\u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - present\u000aMicroinvasion (<0.1cm) - absent\u000aExtent of DCIS\u000aNumber of blocks/total: REMOVED_DATE blocks\u000aFinal Margins (DCIS)\u000aNegative (>0.3 cm) anterior, posterior, inferior, medial\u000aClose (0.1-0.3 cm) superior, lateral\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - absent\u000aOTHER FINDINGS\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia.\u000aCore biopsy site.\u000aCalcifications in benign epithelium.\u000aAJCC CLASSIFICATION (6th edition) - TiS pNX MX\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER/PR/HER-2) - Pending\u000aPART II: SPECIMEN LABELED "NEW SUPERIOR MEDIAL MARGIN":\u000aBenign breast tissue with cysts and calcifications.\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy.\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for DCIS (block 5):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE - LOW\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) NEGATIVE (0)\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000acarcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but\u000aonly a portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity\u000ain >10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Mammo and core suggest intra-cystic neoplasm.\u000aOperation: Wide excision of left breast cancer\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1) Left breast (long lateral; short superior)\u000a#2) New superior - medial margin - stitch on new margin\u000aRADIOLOGY: Wire and the mass are within the specimen. Sung.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by REIMANN,JULIE DYLAN REGAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart one, labeled "#1. left breast (long lateral, short superior)", consists of\u000aa yellow/tan lumpectomy specimen (3.5 cm superior to inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aanterior to poterior and REMOVED_DATE cm medial to lateral). There is a wire protruding\u000afrom the posterolateral aspect of the specimen and the specimen is accompanied\u000aby a radiograph and a pink sheet signed by the radiologist which indicates that\u000athe wire and the mass are all within the specimen. There is a white/tan firm\u000afocally hemorrhagic lesion localized by the wire (2.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) located\u000a0.5 cm from the lateral margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin, at the anterior\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin and\u000a1.2 cm from the inferior margin. The mass has cystic areas ranging in size\u000afrom REMOVED_DATE to REMOVED_DATE cm in maximum dimension, filled with hemorrhagic fluid. The\u000aremainder of the tissue is composed of approximately 95% adipose tissue and 5%\u000afibrous tissue. The entire lesion as well as all of fibrous tissue is\u000asubmitted.\u000aMicro 1: lesion with anterior margin, 2 frags, ESS\u000aMicro 2: lesion with anterior margin, 1 frag, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  lesion with superior margin, 1 frag each, ESS\u000aMicro 5: lesion with lateral margin, 2 frags, ESS\u000aMicro 6: lesion with anterior medial margin, 1 frag, ESS\u000aMicro 7: lesion with medial, inferior, anterior margins, 1 frag, ESS\u000aMicro 8: lesion with medial margin, 1 frag, ESS\u000aMicro 9: lesion with inferior margin, 2 frags, ESS\u000aMicro 10: lesion with posterior and medial and inferior margins, 1 frag, ESS\u000aMicro 11: lesion with posterior and medial margins, 2 frags, ESS\u000aMicro 12: fibrous tissue with inferior margin, 1 frag, ESS\u000aMicro 13: fibrous tissue with posterior and inferior and medial margins, 1\u000afrag, ESS\u000aPart two, labeled "#2. new superior medial margin, stitch on new margin",\u000aconsists of one fragment of yellow/tan fibroadipose tissue (5.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm). The new margin is inked black. There is a white/tan firm fibrous area\u000a(2.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) which grossly extends to the new margin. The remainder of\u000athe specimen is composed of adipose tissue. The specimen is entirely\u000asubmitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  serial sections through specimen, 2 frags each, ESS\u000ajdr\u000aReports to: IGLEHART, JAMES, DIRK M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN\u000a[report_end]
