eral", consists of an 1165-gram\u000asimple mastectomy specimen (31.5 cm superior to inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm medial to\u000alateral, REMOVED_DATE cm anterior to posterior). A short stitch designates superior and\u000aa long stitch designates lateral per the surgeon. Also present is a skin\u000aellipse (10.6 x REMOVED_DATE cm) with a nipple areolar complex (6.5 x REMOVED_DATE cm) with a\u000aflat nipple. The deep surface of the specimen is inked black.\u000aThe specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a previous biopsy cavity (5.5 x\u000a5.0 x REMOVED_DATE cm) characterized by volume loss and surrounding fibrosis. The\u000abiopsy cavity is located in the upper inner quadrant and abuts the deep margin.\u000aNo other masses or lesions are noted. The breast is approximately 95% fatty\u000atissue and 5% fibrous tissue. The lateral breast tissue is searched for lymph\u000anodes but none are found.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Area surrounding previous biopsy cavity, REMOVED_DATE frags each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Upper inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lower inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Upper outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Upper outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lower inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Nipple, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aPart B, "left breast skin", consists of a circular fragment of skin (11.0 x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm with a central punched out area of REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The skin is unremarkable.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Left breast skin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aPart C, "right breast tissue", consists of 469 grams of breast tissue and skin\u000aare represented by eight fragments (16.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate). The\u000abreast tissue and skin are unremarkable. Representative sections are taken.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Right breast and skin, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aJWH/elw\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jane E. Brock M.B., B.S., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000aThursday February 25, 2010 at 07:26:03PM\u000a[report_end]
