VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, partial mastectomy\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ROGER L CHRISTIAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Dick Guang-Iong Hwang, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: William R Welch, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "RIGHT BREAST, SIMPLE MASTECTOMY":\u000aBenign breast tissue.\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia.\u000aSkin with no significant pathologic change.\u000aOne lymph node, negative for tumor (0:1).\u000aB. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "LEFT BREAST, SIMPLE MASTECTOMY":\u000aINVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA\u000aSize - REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aMultifocal - No\u000aHistologic type - Mixed ductal and lobular (predominantly\u000aductal)\u000aHistologic grade (SBR) - II (moderate)\u000aNuclear grade - Intermediate\u000aEIC - Absent\u000aLVI - Absent\u000aDermal LVI - Absent\u000aSkin invasion - Absent\u000aFinal Margins (invasive)\u000aNegative (> REMOVED_DATE cm) - All margins\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU - Absent\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - Absent\u000aLYMPH NODES\u000aAxillary lymph nodes - Positive\u000aNumber of positive nodes - 1\u000aNumber of nodes examined - 7\u000aTOTAL POSITIVE NODES (all specimens)- REMOVED_DATE (including Part D)\u000aSize of largest metastatic focus - REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aExtranodal extension - Absent\u000aOTHER FINDINGS\u000aBiopsy cavity\u000aCore biopsy site\u000aSkin with scar\u000aCalcifications in benign epithelium\u000aLobular hyperplasia\u000aAJCC Classification (6th edition) - REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDb REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDa MX.\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER, PR, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) - Performed previously\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Not provided.\u000aOperation: Rt simple mastectomy, lt simple mastectomy.\u000aOperative Findings: Not provided.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Recurrent lt bst Ca.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. R breast, long = lateral, short = superior.\u000aB/2. Left breast tissue - stitch is axillary tail.\u000aC/3. Left extra axillary lymph nodes.\u000aD/4. Right breast skin.\u000aE/5. Left breast skin.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in five parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart A, "#1. R breast, short superior, long lateral", and consists of a 960-g\u000aright simple mastectomy specimen (20.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) which is oriented per\u000asurgeon with two sutures as indicated. There is an adherent tan skin ellipse\u000a(9.5 x REMOVED_DATE cm) with an everted pink/tan nipple (1.3 cm in diameter) surrounded\u000aby a tan wrinkled areola (4.0 x REMOVED_DATE cm). A scar is not identified on the\u000aepithelial surface. An axillary tail is not present. The deep margin exhibits\u000ascant adherent skeletal muscle and is inked black. The specimen is serially\u000asectioned from medial to lateral to exhibit approximately 30% focally\u000adense/cystic/nodular white/tan fibrous stroma and 70% yellow/tan lobulated\u000aadipose tissue. No discrete masses or lesions are grossly identified. The\u000amost lateral breast parenchyma is examined for intramammary lymph node. One\u000alymph node candidate (1.5 cm in greatest dimension) is identified.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Nipple-areola, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Upper outer quadrant, fibrous stroma, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Upper inner quadrant, fibrous stroma, 3 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lower outer quadrant, fibrous stroma, 3 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lower inner quadrant, fibrous stroma, 3 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Representative deep margin, upper breast, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Representative deep margin, lower breast, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 bisected lymph node candidate, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, "#2. L breast tissue stitch is axillary tail", and consists of a 975-g\u000aleft mastectomy specimen consisting of breast (21.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with\u000aaxillary tail (sutured per surgeon, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). There is an adherent\u000atan skin ellipse (13.5 x REMOVED_DATE cm) with an everted pink nipple (1.2 cm in\u000adiameter) surrounded by a tan wrinkled areola (4.0 x REMOVED_DATE cm). There is a\u000awell-healed faint linear scar (4.0 cm in length), REMOVED_DATE cm lateral to the nipple.\u000aThe deep margin (inked black) is a smooth fascial plane. The specimen is\u000aserially sectioned from lateral to medial. In the lateral aspect of the\u000abreast, at the junction of the upper outer and lower outer quadrants, there is\u000aa white/tan membranous fibrous area (3.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) consistent with a\u000aretracted biopsy cavity/scar. The fibrous area grossly abuts the deep margin,\u000aand is REMOVED_DATE cm subjacent to the skin ellipse in the area of the aforementioned\u000ascar.\u000aA REMOVED_DATE cm anteromedial to the fibrous area/cavity is a bulging irregular firm\u000apink/tan mass (0.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) in the mid upper breast at the junction of\u000athe upper outer and upper inner quadrants. The small mass is REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000adeep margin, and is between the probable cavity/scar and the nipple. Embedded\u000awithin the small mass is a metal clip as consistent with prior core biopsy\u000aprocedure.\u000aThe remainder of the specimen is composed of approximately REMOVED_DATE %\u000adense/nodular/cystic white/tan fibrous stroma, and approximately 70% yellow/tan\u000alobulated adipose tissue. No additional discrete masses or lesions are grossly\u000aidentified. The axillary tail is removed and dissected for lymph node\u000acandidates.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Nipple/areola and skin with scar, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID through REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Membranous _____ area (probable biopsy cavity/scar),\u000ajunction of upper outer and lower outer quadrants, with deep margin in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID,\u000amulti frags total, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Uninvolved stroma between fibrous area/cavity and small mass, 2\u000afrags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID through REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Small mass/clip site junction upper outer and upper inner\u000aquadrants, sequentially submitted from lateral to medial, 1 frag in each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Deep margin, closest to small mass, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Fibrous stroma, upper outer quadrant, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Fibrous stroma, upper inner quadrant, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Fibrous stroma, lower outer quadrant, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Fibrous stroma, lower inner quadrant, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 3 lymph node candidates, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 lymph node candidate, bisected, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 3 lymph node candidates, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 lymph node candidate, bisected, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aPart C, "#3. Left extra-axillary lymph nodes", and consists of two fragments of\u000ayellow/tan lobulated adipose tissue (4.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate)\u000acontaining two pink/tan firm lymph node candidates (1.2 and REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest\u000adimension respectively).\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 bisected lymph node candidate, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 bisected lymph node candidate, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Dissected adipose tissue, multi frags, ESS.\u000aPart D, "#4. Right breast skin", and consists of multiple irregular fragments\u000aof tan wrinkled with a small amount of attached yellow/tan subcutaneous soft\u000atissue (9.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate). No lesions are identified on the\u000aepithelial surfaces. The adherent soft tissue is grossly unremarkable.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Skin and subcutaneous soft tissue, multi frags, RSS.\u000aPart E, "#5. Left breast skin", and consists of an unoriented annular fragment\u000aof tan wrinkled skin with a small amount of attached subcutaneous soft tissue\u000a(13.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). No discrete lesions are identified on the epithelial\u000asurface. The attached subcutaneous tissue is grossly unremarkable.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Skin and soft tissue, multi frags, RSS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-07-REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aLMB/ajb\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by William R Welch M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
