ange) to exhibit a yellow-white ill-defined\u000aindurated area (1.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) located REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior margin,\u000a0.6 cm from the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000athe inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial\u000amargin. A metallic clip is identified within this area. The specimen is\u000aentirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Perpendicular lateral margin, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Body, sequentially submitted from medial to lateral to include\u000aarea designated by metallic clip (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), 1 frag in each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Perpendicular lateral margin, 2 frags in each, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aJC/ajb\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jane E. Brock M.B., B.S., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000aSunday REMOVED_MONTH 28, 2009 at 09:24:07AM\u000a[report_end]
