VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Amend/Addenda\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: LEFT SUBAREOLAR BREAST MASS WITH WIRE AND CLIP\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: JULIE L JONES M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-06-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000a********** Addended Report ***********\u000aResident: Samuel G Katz, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Gilbert Brodsky, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "LEFT SUBAREOLAR BREAST MASS WITH WIRE AND CLIP":\u000aIntraductal papilloma (1.0 cm).\u000aRecent core biopsy changes.\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy in this part.\u000aB. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "LEFT BREAST, EXCISION":\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA WITH MIXED FEATURES\u000aSYNOPSIS:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA\u000aSize - REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aMultifocal - no\u000aHistologic Type - mixed ductal and lobular\u000aHistologic Grade (SBR) - II (moderate)\u000aNuclear Grade - low\u000aEIC - absent\u000aLymphovascular invasion - absent\u000aDermal lymphatic invasion - N/A\u000aSkin invasion - N/A\u000aSkeletal muscle invasion - N/A\u000aFinal Margins (invasive)\u000aNegative (>0.3 cm) - anterior, inferior, superior, lateral, posterior\u000aClose (0.1-0.3 cm) - medial\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU - present\u000aTypes - solid\u000aNuclear grade - low\u000aCalcifications in DCIS - absent\u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - absent\u000aExtent of DCIS\u000aDCIS is present as a minor component of the invasive carcinoma\u000aFinal Margins (DCIS)\u000aNegative (>0.3 cm) - anterior, posterior, lateral, superior, inferior\u000aClose (0.1-0.3 cm) - medial\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - absent\u000aOTHER FINDINGS\u000aComplex sclerosing lesion\u000aCalcifications in benign epithelium\u000aAJCC CLASSIFICATION (6th edition) - REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDa pNx MX\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER/PR/HER-2) - pending\u000aNOTE: Immunohistochemical "double stain": for p63 and keratin demonstrates\u000aepithelial cell nests devoid of myoepithelial cells in the invasive carcinoma.\u000aThe radiologically observed distortion correlates with a large complex\u000asclerosing lesion, with the carcinoma as an adjacent "incidental" finding. Dr.\u000aS. Lester, Breast Pathology Service, has reviewed the slide with the cancer and\u000aconcurs.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Left nipple discharge with subareolar intraductal papilloma, and left\u000aupper/outer quadrant architectural distortion.\u000aOperation: Left breast wire-localized excision REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast subareolar papilloma and UOQ architectural\u000adistortion.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) left subareolar breast mass with wire and clip; short suture=superior,\u000along suture=lateral --> mammo @ 15:38.\u000aB/2) left breast wire localized excision of architectural distortion; short\u000asuture=superior, long suture=lateral --> mammo @ 15:38.\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000aSite 1: Clip + wire are in the specimen.\u000aSite 2: Wire + dense tissue possibly with same distortion.\u000aRobyn Birdwell, M.D.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two parts, each labeled with the patients\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart A, labeled "#1 - left subareolar breast mass, with wire and clip",\u000aconsists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm ovoid fragment of fibrofatty tissue with two\u000aorienting sutures: short stitch=superior, long stitch=lateral. The specimen\u000ais accompanied by an x-ray and a pink slip with the quotation "site 1: clip and\u000awire in specimen". The specimen is received with the wire separated from the\u000aspecimen, and there is also a small metal clip at the bottom of the container.\u000aThe margins are inked according to the pathology protocol for the evaluation of\u000amargins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green;\u000alateral/yellow; medial/orange. The specimen is serially sectioned from\u000aanterior to posterior, respectively, showing a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm multifocal\u000asoft gray/white lesion in the anterior half of the specimen, located REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom the lateral margin, less than REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom the medial margin. There also appears to be two small lymph nodes at the\u000aanterior aspect, REMOVED_DATE cm and REMOVED_DATE cm (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID). There is also a dilated duct, which\u000aabuts the medial margin (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID). The rest of the cut surface is predominantly\u000afatty with patchy areas of hemorrhage and a focal area of fat necrosis in the\u000aposterior half of the specimen (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID). No other lesions are identified. The\u000aspecimen is entirely submitted from anterior to posterior, respectively, in\u000acassettes REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: anterior perpendicular margin, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: possible lymph node, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: lesion, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: dilated duct adjacent to lesion, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: posterior half of specimen with REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID containing fat necrosis,\u000a1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: perpendicular posterior margin, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, labeled "#2 - left breast, wire localized excision of architectural\u000adistortion", consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm irregular fragment of fibrofatty\u000atissue, with two orienting sutures: short stitch=superior, long\u000astitch=lateral. The specimen is accompanied by a radiograph and a notation on\u000aa pink slip, labeled "site 2: wire and dense tissue possibly of same\u000adistortion". The margins are inked according to the pathology protocol for the\u000aevaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red;\u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. The specimen is serially\u000asectioned from medial to lateral, respectively, showing a dense gray/white cut\u000asurface with a moderate amount of interspersed fat. The medial half of the\u000aspecimen is remarkable for multiple cysts, which exude clear to milky-white\u000afluid. The cysts range from REMOVED_DATE 5 cm in greatest dimension. There is also a\u000a0.3 cm focus of fat necrosis in the central aspect of the specimen, located REMOVED_DATE \u000acm from the superior margin. There are also focal patchy areas of fresh\u000ahemorrhage, particularly in the medial half of the specimen. A solid mass is\u000anot identified. The specimen is entirely submitted from medial to lateral,\u000arespectively, in cassettes REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: perpendicular medial margin, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: breast tissue from medial to center, multiple frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: focus of fat necrosis, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: center to lateral breast tissue, multiple frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: perpendicular lateral margin, 3 frags, ESS.\u000awp/lp\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Gilbert Brodsky M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000aSurgical Addendum: (6/14/06)\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for invasive carcinoma (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) NEGATIVE (0)\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000acarcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but only\u000aa portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in >10%\u000aof tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in\u000a>10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aAddendum #1 by Deborah A Dillon M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
