VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID:REMOVED_CASE_ID Report Status: Signed\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aDIAGNOSIS:\u000aLeft breast, re-excision (50 grams):\u000aDuctal carcinoma in situ, intermediate and high grades, solid and cribriform\u000atypes with retrograde involvement of lobules, with focal necrosis and\u000amicrocalcifications.\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia, columnar cell type with focal\u000amicrocalcifications.\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia.\u000aFibrocystic changes with focal ductal hyperplasia and sclerosing adenosis.\u000aSkin with scar.\u000aChanges consistent with previous excision site.\u000aSYNOPTIC REPORT:\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU (DCIS):\u000a-histologic type: solid and cribriform types with retrograde\u000ainvolvement of lobules\u000a-histologic grade: intermediate and high grades\u000a-size (greatest dimension): several cm. in the mid to superficial\u000ainferior portion of the specimen (present\u000ain 7 out of 44 slides)\u000a-extent: focal\u000a-necrosis in DCIS: present, focal\u000a-microcalcifications in DCIS: present, focal\u000a-margins for DCIS: ductal carcinoma in situ is present focally\u000aat and < REMOVED_DATE cm. over a broad front from the\u000ainferior margin in mid portion of the\u000asuperficial aspect (slides 26 and 27).\u000a-immunohistochemical staining on prior specimen (S-06-REMOVED_CASE_ID) was reported as:\u000aEstrogen receptor: POSITIVE (>10% of nuclei stained)\u000aEstrogen receptor (antibody 6REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, avidin-biotin complex detection) and\u000aprogesterone receptor (antibody PgR 1REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, avidin-biotin complex detection)\u000aquantitation of the percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the tumor cells\u000ais assessed visually.\u000aSKIN:\u000a-skin/dermis: Scar with fibroplasia and chronic inflammation.\u000aADDITIONAL PATHOLOGIC FINDINGS:\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia, columnar cell type, atypical lobular\u000ahyperplasia, fibrocystic changes with ductal hyperplasia and sclerosing\u000aadenosis.\u000aChanges consistent with prior excision site.\u000aPRIOR RELATED SPECIMENS REVIEWED:\u000aLeft breast excision; S-06-REMOVED_CASE_ID; REMOVED_DATE \u000aAJCC pTNM Classification (6th Ed.): pTis pNX pMX\u000aThe pathologic TNM classification above is based only on the information\u000aavailable to the pathologist, and therefore may not be accurate.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by: Daniel D. Koelliker, M.D.\u000aClinical diagnosis & history:\u000aDuctal carcinoma in situ; left breast mass\u000aTissue-Designation:\u000aBreast, excision with margins - left\u000aGross description:\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin in one container, labeled "left breast\u000amass, short superior, long lateral" and consists of a 50 gram, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm. excision of fibroadipose tissue which has a REMOVED_DATE cm. long, REMOVED_DATE cm. wide skin\u000aellipse on one surface and which is marked with two separate sutures. There is\u000aa short suture in the mid portion of one side of the skin ellipse oriented as\u000asuperior and 90 degrees from this at one edge is a separate long suture\u000aoriented as lateral of the left breast. Based on these orientations, there is\u000aa cavity present at the superior superficial to mid aspect extending from the\u000alateral end to the medial end. The specimen therefore has mostly fibroadipose\u000atissue from the inferior aspect, partially from the medial aspect and also from\u000athe deep aspect of the cavity. The outer margins are grossly unremarkable.\u000aThe true margins are all inked black. The specimen is cross sectioned\u000arevealing yellow lobulated adipose tissue with strands of white-tan fibrous\u000atissue throughout and areas of reddish and bright yellow discoloration\u000asurrounding the cavity. No grossly suspicious areas are seen. The entire\u000aspecimen is submitted as follows. 44 agg. all.\u000aSection code: REMOVED_DATE - deep margin, lateral\u000a3-5 - deep margin, medial\u000a6-11 - deep aspect with lateral margin from superior towards\u000ainferior\u000a12-17 - deep portion with medial margin from superior towards\u000ainferior\u000a18-20 - mid portion with cavity and lateral margin\u000a21 - mid portion with cavity and superior margin\u000a22-27 - mid portion with cavity and inferior margin\u000a28-30 - mid portion with cavity and medial margin\u000a31-39 - superficial portion with cavity and inferior margin from\u000alateral to medial\u000a40-44 - superficial margin including cavity, skin and inferior\u000aportion from lateral to medial\u000aDictated by: DDK____(signature on file)____ REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a____(signature on file)____DANIEL D. KOELLIKER, M.D. REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a[report_end]
