VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: BRENT T SHOJI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Javad Beheshti, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Alessandra F Nascimento, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZATION FOR CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aCalcifications are present in association with benign epithelium and\u000astroma.\u000aBiopsy site changes.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the\u000aspecimen, including margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 38 year old with abnormal mammo, s/p core biopsy.\u000aOperation: Right needle local biopsy\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal mammo.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1.Right breast tissue (short/superior, long lateral).\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000aSpecimen showed intact hook wire, biopsy clip, calcifications. Andy Tsai.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number\u000aand "right breast tissue", is a REMOVED_DATE gram portion of oriented fibrofatty tissue\u000athat measures REMOVED_DATE cm from medial to lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm from anterior to posterior\u000aand REMOVED_DATE cm from superior to inferior dimension. The specimen is received with\u000ashort suture superior, long suture lateral. The specimen is received with a\u000aneedle-localization wire and accompanying radiograph. There is an area circled\u000aand designated multiple small white punctate dots located at the widened\u000aportion of the needle-localization wire. There is also a metal clip inserted\u000aat the inferior mid portion of the specimen. The needle-localization wire\u000aenters from the superomedial aspect. The needle-localization wire does not\u000aexit the specimen. The specimen is inked in six colors "per pathology\u000aprotocol" with superior red, inferior green, anterior blue, posterior black,\u000amedial orange and lateral yellow. The specimen is serially sectioned from\u000alateral to medial perpendicular to the long axis. Sectioning reveals focal\u000aareas of firm dense white fibrous tissue, and a possible needle tract running\u000athrough the mid portion of the specimen that measures over an area REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x\u000a0.3 cm. A discrete mass is not identified grossly. The approximate specimen\u000acomposition is 85% diffuse white fibrous tissue with 15% unremarkable yellow\u000aadipose tissue. The clip was found in a portion of fibrofatty tissue that was\u000afree-floating at the bottom of the container. This free-floating tissue\u000ameasures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. This metal clip according to radiograph was\u000asituated at the inferior aspect of the specimen. The specimen is submitted\u000aentirely sequentially from the lateral to the medial aspect.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, perpendicularly taken, 3 frags per cassette\u000aeach, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID through REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 frag, ESS to contain the area of microcalcifications, 1\u000afrag each cassettes.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID through REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 frag each all ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin perpendicularly sectioned with REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 3 frags,\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 3 frags, both ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Multi frags of the soft tan/brown tissue that contained the\u000afree-floating metal clip.\u000apf/ag\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Alessandra F Nascimento M.D., Electronically signed on\u000a2/15/2008\u000a[report_end]
