VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Amend/Addenda\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, partial mastectomy\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: DAVID I SOYBEL M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-06-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000a********** Addended Report ***********\u000aResident: Elizabeth A. Steensma, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Susan Lester, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, SIMPLE MASTECTOMY:\u000aSPINDLE CELL SARCOMA, MOST CONSISTENT WITH A PHYLLODES TUMOR, 4 cm\u000a(see note).\u000aThe tumor consists of a cellular proliferation of short spindle cells with\u000amoderate nuclear pleomorphism.\u000aMitoses number 18 per 10 HPF?s.\u000aAn epithelial component is not seen after complete microscopic examination of\u000athe tumor.\u000aThe tumor has a circumscribed border with focal invasion into the adjacent\u000abreast tissue.\u000aNo necrosis is present.\u000aNo heterologous elements are present.\u000aThe margins are free of tumor. The closest margin is deep (2 cm).\u000aNo lymphovascular invasion is present.\u000aThe skin and nipple are not involved by tumor.\u000aBreast tissue with epithelial hyperplasia and sclerosing adenosis.\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies are performed with the following results for tumor\u000acells (blocks REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aCytokeratin 14 NEGATIVE\u000aCytokeratin PANK NEGATIVE\u000aCytokeratin CAM REMOVED_DATE NEGATIVE\u000aCytokeratin REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID NEGATIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID NEGATIVE\u000aDesmin FOCALLY POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID NEGATIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID NEGATIVE\u000aNote: The histologic appearance and immunoprofile would be most consistent\u000awith a phyllodes tumor with complete overgrowth of the epithelial component.\u000aThis case was also reviewed by Dr. Christopher Fletcher, who concurs with this\u000ainterpretation.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Right breast sarcoma. Short superior long lateral stitch.\u000aOperation: Right simple mastectomy with insertion of tissue expander.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: None given.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Right breast tissue with short superior long lateral stitch.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received unfixed for tissue banking, labeled with the patient's\u000aname, medical record number and "#1. Right breast tissue with short superior\u000along lateral stitch". It consists of a 593-gram breast (15.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm)\u000awith an overlying ellipse of tan skin (15.0 x REMOVED_DATE cm). The skin has an\u000aeccentrically placed nipple with surrounding areola (1.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm and REMOVED_DATE \u000acm in diameter respectively). A well-circumscribed, fleshy soft tan\u000ahomogeneous tumor (4.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) is located within the breast tissue\u000adirectly adjacent to the superior suture. The tumor is 2 cm from the nearest\u000adeep margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superficial\u000asuperior margin (orange ink), 10 cm from the inferior margin, 4 cm from the\u000alateral margin and 4 cm from the nipple. The surrounding breast tissue is\u000acomposed of soft yellow lobulated adipose tissue admixed with white fibrous\u000atissue with scattered cysts. A representative section of tissue directly\u000asubjacent to the nipple has been taken for banking purposes. The entire tumor\u000ais submitted for histologic examination. The lateral tissue is carefully\u000aexamined, but no lymph nodes are identified.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Tumor including tumor to superficial margin (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) and tumor\u000ato adjacent fibrocystic breast tissue (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), 10 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Upper/outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lower/outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Upper/inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lower/inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Nipple, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Deep margin, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Remainder of tumor, mult frags, ESS.\u000aNote: There is no block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000adf/lp\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a9/22/2006\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM:\u000aIf this tumor is classified as a PHYLLODES tumor, it would be considered to be\u000aof moderate grade.\u000aAddendum #1 by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
