VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast core needle biopsy\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: LORRAINE B. SMITH MB,BCH,BAO\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Qinghong Yang, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Susan Lester, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, UPPER OUTER, 11 G STEREOTACTIC CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR\u000aINCREASING LINEAR CALCIFICATIONS AT A PRIOR EXCISIONAL SITE:\u000aATYPICAL CELLS are present in one duct profile (< REMOVED_DATE cm, only seen in\u000ablock REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, first level) (see note).\u000aFibrosis and acellular debris, consistent with prior excisional site.\u000aNote: The atypical cells may be atypical lobular hyperplasia. However,\u000athe cells are no longer present in the deeper levels and cannot be evaluated\u000afurther. A small focus of recurrent ductal carcinoma in situ cannot be\u000aexcluded.\u000aAlthough the mammographic calcifications may be related to the prior\u000asurgical changes, specific calcifications are not seen microscopically. This\u000alesion would be evaluated best with excision.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHISTORY: 61 year old female with history of DCIS with microinvasion in the\u000aright breast upper inner quadrant in 1988. She was treated with radiation\u000atherapy. She then developed calcifications in the upper outer quadrant and was\u000adiagnosed with DCIS, solid type with low grade nuclei, 4 cm away from the prior\u000acancer. She now has increasing linear calcifications (1 cm) at this site.\u000aBREAST IMAGING FINDING:\u000a1. Nonpalpable calcifications.\u000aLOCATION:\u000a1. Upper outer, prior excisional site\u000aTYPE OF CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY:\u000a1. 11 G Stereotactic\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000a1. 11 G Stereotactic - pink cassettes.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit\u000anumber, and "right breast", contains two pink cassettes, one labeled "A"\u000aconsisting of multiple cylindrical fibrofatty soft tissues (1.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm\u000ain aggregate). The second pink cassette is labeled "B" and contains multiple\u000acylindrical focally hemorrhagic fibrofatty soft tissues (2.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm).\u000aThe specimen is submitted in toto.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Contents of cassette labeled "A", multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Contents of cassette labeled "B", multi frags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000ajc/ag\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on Friday\u000aREMOVED_MONTH 31, 2009 at 02:01:38PM\u000a[report_end]
