VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: MEHRA GOLSHAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-10-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Vinodh Pillai, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Andrea L Richardson, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA/1. RIGHT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISIONAL BIOPSY FOR CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, solid type (low to intermediate nuclear grade), is\u000apresent.\u000aDCIS is present in three (3) of ten (10) blocks and involves an area measuring\u000a0.9 cm on a single slide.\u000aDCIS is associated with microcalcifications and focal necrosis.\u000aDCIS is present at the medial margin, is < REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior and\u000asuperior margins and REMOVED_DATE cm from posterior margin. The lateral and inferior\u000amargins are negative for DCIS.\u000aA previous remote surgical site is present.\u000aMild epithelial cytologic atypia consistent with radiation effect.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 61 y/o female with h/o right breast cancer & DCIS recurrence.\u000aPatient does not wish to have mastectomy. New right breast calcifications.\u000aOperation: Right breast wire-localized excisional biopsy.\u000aOperative Findings: None provided.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast, abnormal mammogram.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) Right breast wire-localized excisional bx; short suture - superior, long\u000asuture - lateral.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, MR number, and\u000a"#1. Right breast wire localized excision biopsy short suture superior long\u000asuture lateral", consists of a wire-localized excision specimen (medial to\u000alateral - REMOVED_DATE cm, superior to inferior - REMOVED_DATE cm and anterior to posterior - REMOVED_DATE \u000acm). There is a wire running from lateral to medial. Specimen is inked per\u000apathology protocol as anterior - blue, posterior - black, medial - orange,\u000alateral - yellow, superior - red and inferior - green. The specimen is\u000aserially sectioned from medial to lateral to reveal an area of biopsy cavity,\u000awhich is REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin and REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin, and\u000ameasures REMOVED_DATE cm x REMOVED_DATE cm x REMOVED_DATE cm. The specimen consists of greater than 70%\u000afibrous stroma. Specimen is entirely submitted for histological examination.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Area of biopsy cavity, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Remaining breast parenchyma, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aVIP/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Andrea L Richardson M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000aFriday REMOVED_MONTH 29, 2010 at 05:14:00PM\u000a[report_end]
