rts, labeled with the patient's name\u000aand medical record number.\u000aPart A, labeled "#1. Right breast, stitch equals lateral breast tissue\u000a(axilla)", consists of a right simple mastectomy specimen with breast (702\u000agrams, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with skin ellipse (10.8 x REMOVED_DATE cm). The axillary\u000atail (10.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) has a stitch designated lateral per surgeon. No\u000askeletal muscle is grossly identified. The nipple measures REMOVED_DATE cm in diameter\u000aand REMOVED_DATE cm high. Sectioning of the specimen reveals a clip located between the\u000alower outer and lower inner quadrants (about 6 o'clock). At the clip is a firm\u000aarea (0.4 cm in diameter) with focal hemorrhage. The firm area is located REMOVED_DATE \u000acm from the deep margin. A REMOVED_DATE cm superior to the clip is an area of\u000ahemorrhage (2.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). This area is located REMOVED_DATE cm from the deep\u000amargin. No other lesions were identified and no lymph nodes were grossly\u000aidentified in the axilla. The normal breast tissue was approximately 95% fat\u000aand 5% fibrous tissue.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Nipple, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Deep margin to clip area, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Area with clip, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Deep margin to hemorrhagic area, REMOVED_DATE frags each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Hemorrhagic area, REMOVED_DATE frags each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Upper outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Upper inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lower outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lower inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Hematoma in axilla bisected, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aPart B, labeled "#2. proximal right axillary node", consists of two fragments\u000aof fibroadipose 