VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOGINO, SHUJI, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by OGINO,SHUJI,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "TISSUE FROM LEFT BREAST":\u000aColumnar alteration of lobules with prominent snouts and secretions.\u000aApocrine metaplasia with cyst formation.\u000aDense fibrous stroma with pseudoangiomatous stromal hyperplasia.\u000aNo core biopsy site is identified.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen.\u000aNOTE: Dense fibrous stroma may be a cause of the mass lesion clinically.\u000aClinical correlation is recommended.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Mass left breast - core biopsy showed PASH.\u000aOperation: Tissue from left breast.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Tissue from left breast.\u000aRadiograph report: Mass is in specimen.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by RUCKER-SCHMIDT,RACHEL L.,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in one part, labeled with the patient's name,\u000aunit number, and "left breast biopsy", and consists of an unoriented breast\u000aexcision specimen (4.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) which contains a localization wire. The\u000aspecimen is accompanied by a radiograph showing the localization wire adjacent\u000ato a density within the specimen. The specimen is entirely inked in blue and\u000aserially sectioned to reveal dense, white, homogeneous cut surface with scant\u000aintermixed, golden yellow fatty tissue (approximately 95% fibrous tissue and 5%\u000afatty tissue). The fibrous tissue contains multiple clear fluid-filled cysts\u000a(0.1 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). No gross masses are identified. Approximately 95% of\u000athe specimen is submitted for microscopic examination.\u000aMicro #1-9: Left breast biopsy, multiple frags, RSS.\u000arlr/\u000aReports to: CHRISTIAN, ROGER, L. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
