VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ROGER L CHRISTIAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-06-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Joanna A Gibson, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: William R Welch, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "LATERAL MASS, LEFT BREAST":\u000aFibroadenoma (1.0 cm).\u000aFocal Atypical ductal hyperplasia associated with\u000acolumnar cell hyperplasia.\u000aCalcifications associated with benign epithelium.\u000aB. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "MEDIAL MASS, LEFT BREAST":\u000aFibroadenoma (1.2 cm).\u000aInterlobular fibrosis.\u000aNOTE:\u000aThis case was reviewed by Dr. A. Richardson of the Breast Pathology Service.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 2 masses - left breast.\u000aOperation: Wire localized biopsies left breast.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: 2 masses - left breast.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Lateral mass - left breast.\u000aB/2. Medial mass - left breast.\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000aMass and wire in specimen. EP Frost.\u000aMass and wire in specimen. EP Frost.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two parts, each labeled with the patients\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart A, labeled "Lateral mass - left breast", and consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm oval fragment of fibrofatty tissue with a needle localization wire in situ.\u000aThe specimen is accompanied by a radiograph and a notation by the clinician\u000aindicating mass and wire in specimen (Dr. E.P. Frost). The radiograph shows a\u000adensity as well as an S-shaped metal clip. The specimen is inked in black and\u000aserially sectioned showing a somewhat circumscribed REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm soft\u000alobulated white lesion adjacent to the wire, which abuts the inked margin. The\u000aremaining parenchyma is dense white fibrous with little fat and focal fresh\u000ahemorrhage. No other suspicious areas are identified.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: multi frags, RSS.\u000a(lesion entirely submitted in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aPart B, labeled "Medial mass - left breast", consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aovoid fragment of fibrofatty tissue with a needle localization wire in situ and\u000aa whip stitch along one side. The side with the stitch is inked blue and the\u000arest of the margin in black. The specimen is accompanied by a radiograph and a\u000anote indicating mass and wire in the specimen (Dr. E.P. Frost). Sectioning\u000ashows a predominately dense white cut surface with scant fat and a\u000awell-circumscribed (1.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) lobulated pink/white lesion grossly\u000aconsistent with a fibroadenoma. There is also a REMOVED_DATE cm cyst (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID). No other\u000alesions are identified.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Six frags total, with fibroadenoma in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, and cyst in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, RSS.\u000aWP/ajb\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Joanna A Gibson M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aPrelim Dx Release by Joanna A Gibson M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aNo Action - Prelim Sent by Joanna A Gibson M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by William R Welch M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
