sing\u000abetween these sections), 1 frag per cassette, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Representative sections of lateral margin (orange), 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Representative sections of skin and medial margin (yellow), 2\u000afrags total, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Representative sections of superior margin (red), 2 frags\u000atotal, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Representative sections of anterior margin (black), 2 frags\u000atotal, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Representative sections of posterior margin (blue), 2 frags\u000atotal, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Additional representative sections of mass, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aPart B, "#2. Left axillary sentinel lymph node; 3000 counts", consists of a\u000asingle fragment of tan/yellow fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000aWithin this tissue, there is a single lymph node measuring REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest\u000adimension. This node is bisected and entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Bisected sentinel lymph node, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aroh/ag\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Vania Nose MD, PhD, Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
