VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: JAMES D IGLEHART M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: John W. Hanna, M.D., Ph.D.; Astrid Weins, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Alessandra F Nascimento, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. RIGHT BREAST TISSUE, WIRE LOCALIZATION FOR A CLIP:\u000aBenign breast tissue with focus of apocrine adenosis and collagenous\u000aspherulosis.\u000aBiopsy site changes are present.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the\u000aspecimen, including margins.\u000aNOTE: Selected slides of this specimen were also reviewed by Dr. S. Lester,\u000aDirector of Breast Pathology Service, who concurs.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Microcalcifications, atypical changes right breast.\u000aOperation: Right breast after needle localization.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Clip in specimen. OR called. LB Smith.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Right breast biopsy after needle localization suture long lateral - short\u000asuperior.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name and medical\u000arecord number, and "#1. Right breast biopsy after needle localization - suture\u000along lateral - short superior", consists of one breast excision (9.8 grams, REMOVED_DATE \u000acm from superior to inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm from anterior to posterior, and REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom medial to lateral), oriented with a long stitch designated lateral, and a\u000ashort stitch designated superior per the surgeon. The accompanying specimen\u000aradiograph is reviewed and a clip is identified. No localization wire is\u000apresent. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of\u000amargins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green;\u000alateral/yellow; medial/orange. The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal\u000aapproximately 80% white/tan, firm fibrous tissue and 20% yellow lobulated\u000aadipose tissue. No clip can be identified within the specimen. Found in the\u000asame container is a detached fragment of unoriented breast tissue that contains\u000athe clip. The specimen is entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Detached fragment containing clip, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Serial sections from superior to inferior, REMOVED_DATE frags each, ESS.\u000aawe/ag\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Alessandra F Nascimento M.D., Electronically signed on\u000aWednesday August 26, 2009 at 12:15:58PM\u000a[report_end]
