VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID SURGICAL MARGIN\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aKRANE, JEFFREY, FRED, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by KRANE,JEFFREY FRED,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZATION FOR CALCIFICATIONS (specimen #1 of 5\u000aspecimens):\u000aSeverely atypical ductal hyperplasia bordering on DCIS associated with\u000acolumnar alteration of lobules with prominent snouts and secretions with\u000acalcifications, present <0.1 cm from the inked margin.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZATION FOR CALCIFICATIONS AND A CLIP (specimen #2 of 5\u000aspecimens); SENTINEL NODE, BIOPSIES (specimen #4 of 5 specimens); AND AXILLARY\u000aNODE DISSECTION (specimen #3 of 5 specimens):\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA WITH MIXED FEATURES, MULTIPLE FOCI\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aMETASTATIC CARCINOMA TO LYMPH NODES\u000aSYNOPSIS:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA\u000aSize - REMOVED_DATE cm, with smaller foci up to REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aMultifocal - yes (see NOTE)\u000aHistologic Type - mixed ductal and lobular\u000aHistologic Grade (SBR) - II (moderate)\u000aNuclear Grade - intermediate\u000aEIC - positive\u000aLymphovascular invasion - present\u000aDermal lymphatic invasion - absent\u000aSkin invasion - absent\u000aSkeletal muscle invasion - absent\u000aFinal Margins (invasive) -\u000aNegative (>0.3 cm) - lateral, superior, anterior, posterior\u000aVery close (<0.1 cm from margin) medial (focal), inferior (focal)\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU - present\u000aTypes - solid, cribriform\u000aNuclear grade - intermediate\u000aCalcifications in DCIS - present\u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - present\u000aExtent of DCIS\u000aNumber of blocks/total - REMOVED_DATE blocks\u000aFinal Margins (DCIS)\u000aNegative (>0.3 cm) - anterior, superior\u000aClose (0.3 cm) - posterior (focal)\u000aVery close (<0.1 cm) - lateral (multifocal), inferior\u000a(multifocal), medial (focal)\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - present\u000aLYMPH NODES\u000aSentinel Lymph Nodes - positive (3 H&E levels examined)\u000aNumber of positive nodes - 2\u000aNumber of nodes examined - 3\u000aAxillary Lymph Nodes - negative\u000aNumber of positive nodes - 0\u000aNumber of nodes examined - 3\u000aTOTAL POSITIVE NODES (sentinel + axillary)- 2:6\u000aSize of largest metastatic focus- REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aExtranodal extension - present\u000aOTHER FINDINGS\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia\u000aCore biopsy site\u000aSkeletal muscle\u000aPapilloma\u000aAJCC CLASSIFICATION (6th edition): REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDc pREMOVED_ACCESSION_IDa MX (with multiple foci of\u000ainvasion)\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER/PR/HER-2) - performed previously\u000aNOTE:\u000aThere are multiple foci of invasion. It is not possible to determine the exact\u000anumber as the areas of invasion were radiologically and grossly occult.\u000aThe largest area of invasion is associated with the core needle biopsy site and\u000athe clip.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, SHAVE MARGIN, SUPERIOR AND LATERAL (specimen #5 of 5 specimens):\u000aINVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA, well differentiated (modified\u000aBloom-Richardson grade I/III) (low nuclear grade), present as two (2)\u000afoci (0.3 cm and REMOVED_DATE cm) (see NOTE).\u000aLymphovascular invasion is present.\u000aInvasive carcinoma is present focally at the inferior margin.\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, cribriform type (intermediate nuclear grade),\u000ais present in five of nine (5:9) blocks and is focally <0.1 cm from the\u000ainferior margin.\u000aOther margins are distantly free of invasive carcinoma and DCIS.\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU.\u000aNOTE:\u000aThe two (2) foci of invasive carcinoma present in the shave margin specimen are\u000aapparently separate from the larger tumor mass in the main resection specimen.\u000aThe closest approach of carcinoma to the new superior and lateral margins is\u000aDCIS REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin in block 47.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Cancer right breast, left inner quadrant.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Tissue right breast\u000a2. Tumor site right breast\u000a3. Axillary contents, right\u000a4. Sentinel lymph nodes - right\u000a5. Shave margin - right (superior, lateral aspect)\u000aRADIOLOGY REPORT:\u000aSpecimen 1: Calcifications in specimen.\u000aSpecimen 2: Senory clip and calcification clusters in specimen.\u000aDr. D. Smith\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by BENNETT,MICHAEL W.,M.B.,B.C.H\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in five parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart 1, "Tissue right breast", consists of a\u000aportion of fibrofatty tissue (3.6 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). A localizing needle enters\u000athe specimen at one margin and protrudes from the opposite end. The specimen is\u000anot oriented. The half of the specimen where the needle enters is inked\u000ablack, and the opposite end where the needles protrudes is inked blue. The\u000aspecimen radiograph reveals a single localization wire with a cluster of\u000acalcifications.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Entire specimen, black to blue, 8 frags, ESS\u000aPart 2, "Tumor site, right breast", consists of an ellipse of skin (5.3 x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm) with attached fibrofatty tissue, excised to a depth of 5 cm. The ellipse of\u000askin is marked by the surgeon with two sutures. The specimen is inked per\u000apathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior\u000a= blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange.\u000aTwo wire localizing needles enter the specimen at the superior surface.\u000aThe specimen is serially sectioned from deep to anterior. Approximately 30% of\u000athe specimen consists of white fibrous tissue which extends to all margins.\u000aFollowing sectioning the specimen is x-rayed and the clip identified in\u000acassette #18. The specimen radiograph reveals two (2) wires: one marking a\u000aclip and one marking adjacent calcifications.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Entire fibrofatty tissue, posterior to anterior, 29 frags, ESS\u000aMicro 32: Skin ellipse, 3 frags, RSS\u000aMicro 33: Skin ellipse tips, 2 frags, ESS\u000aPart 3, "Axillary contents right", conssists of two fragments of fibrofatty\u000atissue (2.4 x 1 x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate). Three possible lymph nodes are\u000aidentified, the largest of which measures REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest dimension.\u000aMicro 34: Three bisected lymph nodes, 6 frags, ESS\u000aMicro 35: Remaining fibrofatty tissue, 1 frag, ESS\u000aPart 4, "Sentinel lymph nodes - right", consists of three lymph node-like\u000anodules, the largest of which measures REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest dimensions and\u000aappears macroscopically to be involved by tumor.\u000aMicro 36: Largest sentinel node bisected, 2 frags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Two sentinel nodes bisected, 4 frags, ESS\u000aPart 5, "Shave margin - right", consists of a portion of fibrofatty tissue (4.5\u000acm - medial to lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm - anterior to posterior, and REMOVED_DATE cm - superior\u000ato inferior). The specimen has been marked by the surgeon with two sutures. A\u000ashort suture has been placed on one surface and the area inked red. A long\u000asuture has been placed on another surface. A third surface has been inked\u000ablack. The specimen consists of approximately 80% white fibrous tissue which\u000aextends to all margins with the exception of the posterior. The entire specimen\u000ais serially sectioned from medial to lateral and entirely submitted for\u000ahistological examination.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Entire specimen, 14 frags, ESS\u000amwb\u000aReports to: CHRISTIAN, ROGER, L. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: LYMPH NODES REGIONAL RESECTION\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SENTINEL LYMPH NODE\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN\u000a[report_end]
