VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Amend/Addenda\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: MEHRA GOLSHAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000a********** Addended Report ***********\u000aResident: Samuel P. Wyche, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Hejin P Hahn, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZATION FOR CALCIFICATIONS AND\u000aCORE BIOPSY SITE:\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aTypes - Solid, Cribriform\u000aNuclear grade - Intermediate\u000aCalcifications in DCIS - Present\u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - Present\u000aExtent of DCIS\u000aNumber of blocks/total - REMOVED_DATE blocks\u000aMargins (DCIS)\u000aNegative (> REMOVED_DATE cm) - Superior, medial, lateral,\u000aposterior\u000aClose (0.1 to REMOVED_DATE cm) - Inferior (0.1 cm, focal, block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID)\u000aVery close(<0.1 cm from margin)- Anterior (focal, block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID)\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - Absent\u000aOTHER FINDINGS\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia\u000aCore biopsy site (see NOTE)\u000aAJCC Classification (6th edition) - Tis NX Mx\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER, PR, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) - Pending\u000aNOTE:\u000aCore biopsy site extends to anterior margin.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 46 year old female with right breast hyperplasia with atypia and LCIS\u000aon core biopsy.\u000aOperation: Right breast wire-localized excisional biopsy.\u000aOperative Findings: Not provided.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast abnormal mammogram.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) right breast wire loc excisional bx - short suture/superior 1022, long\u000asuture/lateral 1037.\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000aMicrocalcs in specimen. OR called. LBS.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number\u000aand "#1. Right breast wire loc Bx, superior - short suture, lateral - long\u000asuture", consists of an irregular portion of fibrofatty tissue (5.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm), with a long suture designating lateral, and a short suture designating\u000asuperior. There is an inserted needle-localization wire, which enters along\u000athe lateral margins, and exits along the medial margins, as displayed on the\u000aaccompanying radiograph. The specimen is inked by the prosector according to\u000athe pathology protocol as follows: anterior/blue, posterior/black,\u000asuperior/red, inferior/green, medial/yellow and lateral/orange. The specimen\u000ais serially sectioned to reveal 90% dense white fibrous tissue, and 2% yellow\u000alobulated adipose tissue, with no discrete masses or lesions identified. A\u000adefinitive core biopsy site is not grossly identified. The specimen is\u000asequentially submitted in its entirety.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, radially, 2 frags each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross sections from lateral to medial, with the\u000apossible area of concern on the accompanying radiograph in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 1 frag each,\u000aESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin, radially, which also may contain the area of concern\u000aon the accompanying radiograph, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000acp/lp\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Hejin P Hahn M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a7/22/2008\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM (7/23/08):\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for DCIS (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) NEGATIVE (0)\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000ainvasive carcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low > 0% - < 10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor cells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but only a\u000aportion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+):Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in >10% of\u000atumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+):Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in >30% of\u000atumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aExternal controls are evaluated and show appropriate Immunoreactivity.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aAddendum #1 by Deborah A Dillon M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
