VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aWELCH, WILLIAM, ROBERT, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by WELCH,WILLIAM ROBERT,M.D.\u000aRIGHT INFERIOR BREAST, EXCISION OF A MASS:\u000aLipomatous mature adipose tissue.\u000aScant benign breast ductal tissue.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000aLEFT BREAST, EXCISION WITH WIRE LOCALIZATION FOR A CLIP:\u000aBenign breast tissue with apocrine metaplasia and biopsy site changes; see\u000anote.\u000aNOTE: No residual columnar alteration with atypia (seen in prior biopsy,\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID; reviewed) is identified. The entire specimen is submitted for\u000ahistologic evaluation.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 57-year-old female status post REMOVED_DATE  core biopsy left breast UOQ\u000a3 mm cluster of calcifications revealing atypical ductal hyperplasia.\u000aRight breast palpable mass, 5 cm consistent with lipoma or hamartoma.\u000aOperation: Left breast wire localization excision, right breast excision.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left abnormal mammogram, atypical ductal hyperplasia.\u000aRight breast mass.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Right inferior breast mass (? lipoma).\u000a2. Left needle directed breast bx.\u000aSpecimen #2: Clip in specimen, OR called.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by DAVID,FRANK SAMUEL,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart one, labeled "#1, right inferior breast mass", consists of a single mass,\u000ayellow-tan fibrofatty tissue, 7 x REMOVED_DATE x 2 cm. The specimen is inked per\u000apathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior\u000a= blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange.\u000aThe interior of the specimen is uniformly yellow and fatty, with no grossly\u000adiscernible fibrous tissue. No discrete masses or suspicious lesions are\u000aidentified. Representative sections are submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  multi frags, RSS.\u000aPart two, labeled "#2, left needle localized breast bx", consists of a single\u000amass of yellow-tan fibroadipose tissue, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. There is a\u000alocalizing clip protruding from the specimen.\u000aThe specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation\u000aof margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior =\u000agreen; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. Within the specimen is a REMOVED_DATE cm in\u000adiameter hemorrhagic biopsy cavity, but no discrete masses or suspicious\u000alesions are identified. Accompanying the specimen is a mammogram, which\u000ademonstrates the presence of a localizing wire and a clip. The specimen is\u000aentirely submitted.\u000aMicro 6: lateral, ESS.\u000aMicro 7: medial, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  remainder of specimen, lateral to medial, ESS.\u000afsd\u000aReports to: KAELIN, CAROLYN, MARY, M.PH. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
