 will be reported in an addendum.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by: Richard J. Sampson, M.D.\u000aClinical diagnosis & history:\u000aHistory of benign biopsies inner left breast, now has architectural distortion\u000aof mammogram and at least three nodules, 9 and 10 'clock near areola;\u000ainfiltrating duct carcinoma\u000aTissue-Designation:\u000aA.Breast, needle biopsy - left at 9 o'clock\u000aB.Breast, needle biopsy - left at 10 o'clock\u000aGross description:\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin in two containers.\u000aSpecimen A labeled "guided breast biopsy #1", designated "9 o'clock" consists\u000aof three firm, yellowish-white needle biopsies with attached blood clot ranging\u000ain size from 1 cm. in length x REMOVED_DATE cm. in diameter to REMOVED_DATE cm. in length x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm. in diameter. 3X all.\u000aSpecimen B labeled "guided breast biopsy #2", designated "10 o'clock" consists\u000aof four firm, yellowish-tan, glistening needle biopsies with attached blood\u000aclot ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE cm. in length x REMOVED_DATE cm. in diameter to REMOVED_DATE cm. in\u000alength x REMOVED_DATE cm. in diameter. 4X all.\u000aDictated by: LV____(signature on file)____ REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a____(signature on file)____RICHARD SAMPSON, M.D. REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a[report_end]
