VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID:REMOVED_CASE_ID Report Status: Signed\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aADDENDUM REPORT\u000aAddendum #1 Entered: REMOVED_DATE -1148\u000a*** ADDITIONAL DIAGNOSTIC INFORMATION ***\u000aThis report contains an addendum to the original for the purpose of providing\u000aadditional diagnostic information. The original diagnosis is unchanged.\u000aImmunohistochemical studies performed on block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID (1 o'clock) reveal the\u000afollowing results for the infiltrating carcinoma:\u000aEstrogen receptor: POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor: POSITIVE\u000aAddeundum Signed Electronically Signed SAMPSON,RICHARD J. M.D. REMOVED_DATE \u000aDIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. Left breast, 1 o'clock, excision:\u000aModerately differentiated infiltrating duct carcinoma (1.0 cm.), (at\u000asuperior-superficial margin) with separate REMOVED_DATE cm. focus at a\u000asuperior-superficial margin.\u000aDuctal carcinoma in situ, cribriform/solid, grade REMOVED_DATE \u000aLobular carcinoma in situ, focal.\u000aB. Left breast, 10 o'clock, excision:\u000aModerately differentiated infiltrating duct carcinoma, multifocal up to\u000a1.4 cm. with tumor at deep and superficial margins.\u000aDuctal carcinoma in situ (solid and cribriform), grade REMOVED_DATE \u000aFibroadenoma with sclerosis.\u000aC. Left breast, 9 o'clock, excision:\u000aModerately differentiated infiltrating duct carcinoma (0.6 cm.) within\u000a0.1 cm. of a superficial-inferior margin.\u000aDuctal carcinoma in situ (solid and cribriform type), grade REMOVED_DATE \u000aD. Left axillary sentinel lymph nodes (2):\u000aNo tumor seen (0/2).\u000aE. Left axillary fat:\u000aAdipose tissue, no lymph nodes present.\u000aF. Left breast, anterior margin, excision:\u000aDuctal hyperplasia, focal.\u000aG. Left breast, posterior margin, excision:\u000aDuctal carcinoma in situ, solid type, grade REMOVED_DATE  focal (at margin).\u000aFocal atypical lobular hyperplasia and lobular carcinoma in situ (focally\u000aat resection margin).\u000aFibrocystic changes.\u000aH. Left breast, inferior margin, excision:\u000aFibrocystic changes.\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia, focal.\u000aI. Left breast, medial margin, excision:\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia.\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia.\u000aAdenosis.\u000aJ. Left breast, lateral margin, excision:\u000aDuct carcinoma in situ, focal, at margin.\u000aK. Left breast, superior margin, excision:\u000aFocus of infiltrating carcinoma, REMOVED_DATE cm. at definitive margin.\u000aSYNOPTIC REPORT: BREAST\u000aINVASIVE TUMOR:\u000a-histologic type: ductal\u000a-histologic grade: moderately differentiated\u000a-size (greatest dimension): REMOVED_DATE cm., also 2 other foci REMOVED_DATE and REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000a-lymphatic/vascular invasion: none identified\u000a-perineural invasion: none identified\u000a-microcalcification: present\u000a-margins for invasive tumor: positive focally in superior definitive margin.\u000aA focus of infiltrating carcinoma is present\u000aat a "definitive" superior margin (section\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID). The largest tumor is present at a\u000asuperior-superficial margin, focally\u000a(specimen A). The second tumor is present\u000aat a deep and superficial margin (specimen\u000aB). The third tumor is present REMOVED_DATE cm. from\u000aa superficial-inferior margin (specimen C).\u000aHowever, separate margin sections from\u000aanterior, posterior, inferior, medial,\u000alateral aspects of the incision are negative\u000afor tumor. It is not possible to know the\u000arelation between the three separate tumors\u000aand to the separate margin and sections.\u000a-immunohistochemical staining on prior specimen (S-05-REMOVED_CASE_ID) was reported as:\u000a9 o'clock: Estrogen positive and progesterone weakly positive\u000a10 o'clock: Estrogen positive and progesterone positive\u000a-immunohistochemical staining for REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu is performed on blocks REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and is negative in all three areas.\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU (DCIS):\u000a-histologic type: solid-cribriform\u000a-histologic grade: REMOVED_DATE \u000a-size (greatest dimension): microscopic foci within and around the\u000ainvasive tumor\u000a-extent: multifocal\u000a-extensive intraductal component: absent\u000a-necrosis in DCIS: present, focal\u000a-microcalcifications in DCIS: present\u000a-margins for DCIS: positive focally at a definitive lateral\u000amargin (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) and a definitive posterior\u000amargin (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU (LCIS):\u000aPresent, multifocal.\u000aLYMPH NODES:\u000aThe lymph node sampled is negative for malignancy (0/2)\u000a(0/2 sentinel lymph nodes).\u000aCOMMENT: The sentinel lymph node, specimen D, is examined at multiple levels\u000awith H&E stains and immunohistochemical stains for keratin.\u000aADDITIONAL PATHOLOGIC FINDINGS:\u000aBiopsy site, microcalcifications.\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia, atypical lobular hyperplasia, fibrocystic\u000achanges.\u000aE. cadherin stains confirms that the in situ carcinoma is ductal in sections\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. Calponin stain in section REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID is consistent with infiltrating\u000acarcinoma.\u000aPRIOR RELATED SPECIMENS REVIEWED:\u000asite: left breast, 9 & 10 o'clock specimen #: S-05-REMOVED_CASE_ID date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aAJCC pTNM Classification (6th Ed.): pREMOVED_ACCESSION_IDc pREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID(i-) pMX\u000aThe pathologic TNM classification above is based only on the information\u000aavailable to the pathologist, and therefore may not be accurate.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by: Richard J. Sampson, M.D.\u000aINTRA-OPERATIVE CONSULTATION:\u000aOPERATING ROOM CONSULTATION (FROZEN SECTION):\u000aSentinel lymph node: No tumor seen.\u000aJLF\u000aClinical diagnosis & history:\u000aLeft breast carcinoma\u000aTissue-Designation:\u000aA.Breast, excision with margins - 1 o'clock margin, left\u000aB.Breast, excision with margins - 10 o'clock margin, left\u000aC.Breast, excision with margins - 9 o'clock margin, left\u000aD.Lymph node, biopsy - axillary, left breast\u000aE.Specimen designated as - left axillary tissue\u000aF.Breast, excision (without margins) - anterior margin, left breast\u000aG.Breast, excision with margins - posterior margin, left breast\u000aH.Breast, excision with margins - inferior margin, left breast\u000aI.Breast, excision with margins - medial margin, left breast\u000aJ.Breast, excision with margins - lateral margin, left breast\u000aK.Breast, excision with margins - superior margin, left breast\u000aGross description:\u000aThe specimen is received in eleven containers.\u000aSpecimen A is labeled "1 o'clock" and consists of a piece of breast tissue\u000awhich measures 3 x REMOVED_DATE x 1 cm. and weighs 6 grams. A wire marker is present\u000agoing from one end of the specimen, and two orienting sutures are present, a\u000along suture is lateral and a short suture is superior. The entire specimen is\u000ainked with black ink, the deep margin is so oriented and inked with blue,\u000aand the lateral superficial margin is inked with yellow ink. Sections are\u000ataken from superior to inferior. 8X all.\u000aSpecimen B is labeled "left breast mass, 10 o'clock" and consists of a piece of\u000abreast tissue 3 x 2 x REMOVED_DATE cm. A wire marker goes through the specimen and two\u000aorienting sutures are present. A long suture designated lateral and a short\u000asuture designated superior. The specimen weighs 6 grams. The entire specimen\u000ais inked with black ink and the deep margin is inked with blue in addition to\u000athe black. The superior margin is inked yellow in addition to the black.\u000aSections are taken from lateral to medial. 8X all.\u000aSpecimen C is labeled "left breast mass, 9 o'clock" and consists of a piece of\u000abreast tissue REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The specimen weighs 3 grams. A wire marker\u000ais present and two sutures. The long suture is lateral and the short suture\u000asuperior. The entire specimen is inked with black ink. Using this\u000aorientation, the deep margin is inked also in blue ink, and the lateral\u000asuperficial margin is inked with yellow. Sections are taken from superior to\u000ainferior. 5X all.\u000aSpecimen D is labeled "left breast axillary node" and consists of a lymph node\u000aand fat pad submitted for frozen section. The left node is approximately 1 cm.\u000ain diameter. The entire specimen is 2 x 2 x 1 cm. 2 agg. all. A frozen\u000asection is labeled DF. The remaining tissue is labeled D.\u000aSpecimen E is labeled "left axillary tissue" and consists of a piece of fatty\u000atissue REMOVED_DATE x 1 x 1 cm. which does not contain definite lymph node. 2X all.\u000aSpecimen F is labeled "anterior margin of left breast" and consists of multiple\u000ashreds of tissue 2 x 2 x 1 cm. 2 agg. all.\u000aSpecimen G is labeled "posterior margin of left breast" and consists of a\u000asingle piece of fatty tissue which has a concave and convex side. The specimen\u000ameasures 5 x 3 x REMOVED_DATE cm. Sutures are present on the concave side, designating\u000athe new margin. This margin is inked with black, and the opposite side is not\u000ainked at all. 9X all.\u000aSpecimen H is labeled "inferior margin of left breast" and consists of a piece\u000aof fatty tissue 4 x 2 x REMOVED_DATE cm. with one suture on the convex side of the\u000aspecimen, designating the new margin. This margin is inked and the opposite\u000amargin is not inked. 6X all, labeled REMOVED_DATE \u000aSpecimen I is labeled "medial margin of left breast" and consists of a piece of\u000atissue REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 cm. There is a mark on the convex portion of the\u000aspecimen, designated the new margin. This is inked with black and the other\u000aside is not inked. 3X all.\u000aSpecimen J is labeled "lateral margin of left breast" and consists of a piece\u000aof breast tissue 3 x 2 cm. with a concave and convex side. A suture is present\u000aon the middle of the convex side, designated the new margin. This margin is\u000ainked with black, and the opposite margin is not inked. Sections are taken\u000afrom one end to the other and entirely embedded. 3X all.\u000aSpecimen K is labeled "superior margin of left breast" and consists of a piece\u000aof tissue with a convex side and measures REMOVED_DATE x 1 x REMOVED_DATE cm. Two sutures are\u000apresent and the convex side designated the new margin. This margin is inked\u000awith black. The opposite margin is not inked. Sections are taken from one end\u000ato the other. 9X all.\u000aDictated by: RJS____(signature on file)____ REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a____(signature on file)____RICHARD SAMPSON, M.D. REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a[report_end]
