VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID:REMOVED_CASE_ID Report Status: Signed\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aDIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. Left breast, final deep margin, re-excision:\u000aNo residual carcinoma identified.\u000aChanges consistent with prior excision site.\u000aB. Left breast, final superior margin, re-excision:\u000aFocus of residual infiltrating ductal carcinoma, less than 1 mm in size,\u000alocated greater than 2 mm. from the new inked margin.\u000aUsual intraductal hyperplasia, cysts, and fibroadenoma.\u000aChanges consistent with prior excision site.\u000aC. Left breast, final lateral margin, re-excision:\u000aResidual ductal carcinoma in situ, low to intermediate nuclear grade,\u000asolid pattern, foci up to REMOVED_DATE mm. in size, present at the new inked\u000amargin, over a broad front.\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia.\u000aCysts, usual intraductal hyperplasia, and apocrine metaplasia.\u000aChanges consistent with prior excision site.\u000aD. Left breast, deep margin, re-excision:\u000aNo residual carcinoma identified.\u000aChanges consistent with prior excision site.\u000aE. Left breast, superior margin, re-excision:\u000aNo residual carcinoma identified.\u000aChanges consistent with prior excision site.\u000aF. Left breast, lateral margin, re-excision:\u000aResidual ductal carcinoma in situ, low to intermediate nuclear grade,\u000asolid pattern, foci up to 3 mm. in size, present at the new inked\u000amargin, focally.\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia.\u000aCysts, usual intraductal hyperplasia, and small radial scar.\u000aChanges consistent with prior excision site.\u000aNOTE: Immunohistochemical stains for E-Cadherin were performed on sections\u000afrom specimens C and F. These demonstrate positive staining in ductal\u000acarcinoma in situ and negative staining in atypical lobular hyperplasia.\u000aThe patient's prior breast excision (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) has been reviewed.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by: Jean L. Fraser, M.D.\u000aClinical diagnosis & history:\u000aLeft breast carcinoma; left breast carcinoma\u000aTissue-Designation:\u000aA.Breast, excision (without margins) - left, final deep margin\u000aB.Breast, excision with margins - left, final superior margin\u000aC.Breast, excision with margins - left, final lateral margin\u000aD.Breast, excision with margins - left, deep margin\u000aE.Breast, excision with margins - left, superior margin\u000aF.Breast, excision with margins - left, lateral margin\u000aGross description:\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin in six parts.\u000aSpecimen A labeled "final deep" consists of multiple fragments of adipose\u000atissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. in aggregate. No orienting sutures are\u000aidentified. The fragments are examined and no gross abnormalities are noted.\u000aThe fragments are submitted entirely in two cassettes. 2 agg. all.\u000aSpecimen B labeled "final superior" consists of a fragment of fibrofatty tissue\u000ameasuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. A stitch marks the new margin side. The new\u000amargin side is inked blue. The specimen is serially sectioned perpendicular to\u000athe new margin side to reveal focal fat necrosis adjacent to the biopsy site.\u000aThe specimen is submitted entirely in five cassettes. 5 agg. all.\u000aSpecimen C labeled "final lateral" consists of a fragment of fibrofatty tissue\u000ameasuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. A stitch marks the new margin side. The new\u000amargin side is inked black. The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal\u000afibrofatty tissue. The specimen is submitted entirely in four cassettes. 4\u000aagg. all.\u000aSpecimen D labeled "deep" consists of a piece of fibrofatty tissue measuring\u000a3.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. A stitch marks the new margin side. The new margin side\u000ais inked in blue. The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal foci of fat\u000anecrosis. The specimen is submitted entirely in five cassettes. 5 agg. all.\u000aSpecimen E labeled "superior" consists of a fragment of fibrofatty tissue\u000ameasuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. A stitch marks the new margin side. The new\u000amargin side is inked black. The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal\u000ahemorrhage and fat necrosis. The specimen is submitted entirely in 7\u000acassettes. 7 agg. all.\u000aSpecimen F labeled "lateral" consists of a fragment of fibrofatty tissue\u000ameasuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. A stitch marks the new margin side. The new\u000amargin side is inked blue. The specimen is serially sectioned and\u000asubmitted entirely in two cassettes. 4X all.\u000aDictated by: JLF____(signature on file)____NICOLE MIHOK, M.D. REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a____(signature on file)____ REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a[report_end]
