VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID:REMOVED_CASE_ID Report Status: Signed\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aDIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. Skin of left chest wall, excision:\u000aNo diagnostic abnormalities recognized.\u000aB. Skin of left lateral chest wall, excision:\u000aNo diagnostic abnormalities recognized.\u000aC. Left breast, mastectomy:\u000aNo residual infiltrating carcinoma identified.\u000aFocus of residual ductal carcinoma in situ.\u000aChanges consistent with prior excision site with foci of dense\u000afibrosis/scarring and stromal hyalinization.\u000aSmall fibroadenomas, cysts, sclerosing adenosis, and usual intraductal\u000ahyperplasia.\u000aUnremarkable nipple and areola.\u000aSee synoptic report.\u000aSYNOPTIC REPORT: BREAST\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU (DCIS):\u000a-histologic type: solid, involving a duct and lobule adjacent\u000ato the prior excision site\u000a-histologic grade: intermediate nuclear grade\u000a-size (greatest dimension): REMOVED_DATE cm. (see slide REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID)\u000a-extent: focal\u000a-extensive intraductal component: not applicable\u000a-necrosis in DCIS: none identified\u000a-microcalcifications in DCIS: none identified\u000a-margins for DCIS: clear (greater than or equal to REMOVED_DATE cm.)\u000aSKIN:\u000a-nipple: unremarkable\u000a-skin/dermis: unremarkable\u000aADDITIONAL PATHOLOGIC FINDINGS:\u000aSmall fibroadenomas, cysts, sclerosing adenosis, usual intraductal\u000ahyperplasia and changes consistent with prior excision site.\u000aPRIOR RELATED SPECIMENS REVIEWED:\u000asite: left breast, re-excision specimen #: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by: Jean L. Fraser, M.D.\u000aClinical diagnosis & history:\u000aLeft breast carcinoma with positive margins; negative sentinel node; had AC x4\u000abetween last re-excision and now\u000aTissue-Designation:\u000aA.Skin, excision - left chest wall\u000aB.Skin, excision - left lateral chest wall\u000aC.Breast, simple mastectomy - left\u000aGross description:\u000aThe specimen is received in three containers.\u000aSpecimen A labeled "left chest wall skin" is received fresh and consists of a\u000aring shaped excision of skin measuring REMOVED_DATE cm. in greatest diameter and up to\u000a1.5 cm. in width. The skin is excised to a depth of up to REMOVED_DATE cm. The skin\u000asurfaces are grossly unremarkable. A suture marks the lateral direction. With\u000athe suture designated as 12 o'clock, the specimen is represented as follows: 4\u000aagg.\u000aSection code: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - 12 o'clock\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - 3 o'clock\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - 6 o'clock\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - 9 o'clock\u000aSpecimen B labeled "left lateral chest wall skin" is received fresh and\u000aconsists of a triangular shaped skin excision measuring REMOVED_DATE x 4 cm., excised to\u000aa depth of REMOVED_DATE cm. The skin surface is grossly unremarkable. The specimen is\u000asubmitted entirely in three cassettes. 3 agg. all.\u000aSpecimen C labeled "left breast, stitch at 12 o'clock" is received fresh and\u000aconsists of a mastectomy specimen weighing 510 grams. The specimen measures 21\u000ax 16 x 3 cm. The attached skin consists of a nipple areolar complex. The\u000aareola measures REMOVED_DATE cm. in diameter and the nipple measures REMOVED_DATE cm. in\u000adiameter. Both are grossly unremarkable. The deep surface consists of smooth\u000afascia. The deep margin is inked black. The superficial margin is inked blue.\u000aThe specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a somewhat stellate shaped area of\u000afibrotic breast parenchyma containing small, firm areas of nodularity. This\u000aregion is located centrally, just superior to the attached nipple areolar\u000acomplex. The stellate area measures approximately 5 cm. in size. The firm,\u000anodular areas measure up to REMOVED_DATE cm. in size. The firm tissue extends laterally\u000aas well. Other that this abnormality, the remaining parenchyma is largely\u000acomposed of adipose tissue with minimal strands of admixed breast parenchyma.\u000a20 agg. The specimen is represented as follows:\u000aSECTION CODE: 1 - nipple and areolar skin\u000a2-9 - stellate and nodular areas of central breast\u000a10 & 11 - upper outer quadrant\u000a12 & 13 - lower outer quadrant\u000a14 & 15 - lower central breast tissue\u000a16 & 17 - lower inner quadrant\u000a18 & 19 - upper inner quadrant\u000a20 - upper central breast tissue\u000aDictated by: JLF____(signature on file)____MICHAEL J. ROSS, M.D. REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a____(signature on file)____ REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a[report_end]
