VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID SENTINEL LYMPH NODE\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aWELCH, WILLIAM, ROBERT, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by WELCH,WILLIAM ROBERT,M.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZATION FOR A MASS (specimen #2 of 2 specimens) AND\u000aSENTINEL NODE BIOPSY (specimen #1 of 2 specimens) (including REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aINVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA, MUCINOUS (COLLOID) TYPE\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aNEGATIVE LYMPH NODE\u000aSYNOPSIS:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA\u000aSize - REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aMultifocal - no\u000aHistologic Type - mucinous\u000aHistologic Grade (SBR) - I (well)\u000aNuclear Grade - low\u000aEIC - negative\u000aLymphovascular invasion - absent\u000aDermal lymphatic invasion - N/A\u000aSkin invasion - N/A\u000aSkeletal muscle invasion - N/A\u000aFinal Margins (invasive) -\u000aNegative (>0.3 cm) - posterior, superior, medial, lateral\u000aPositive (ink on carcinoma) - anterior (focal, block #6)\u000ainferior (focal, block #20)\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aTypes - solid, mucinous with pagetoid spread\u000aand lobular involvement\u000aNuclear grade - high\u000aCalcifications in DCIS - absent\u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - absent\u000aExtent of DCIS\u000aNumber of blocks:total - 4:19 blocks\u000aFinal Margins (DCIS)\u000aNegative (>0.3 cm) - anterior, posterior, superior, inferior,\u000amedial, lateral\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - absent\u000aLYMPH NODES\u000aSentinel Lymph Nodes - negative (3 H&E levels examined)\u000aNumber of positive nodes - 0\u000aNumber of nodes examined - 1\u000aTOTAL POSITIVE NODES (all specimens)- 0:1\u000aOTHER FINDINGS\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia with pagetoid spread\u000aCore biopsy site\u000aAJCC CLASSIFICATION (6th edition) - REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDb pREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID MX\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER/PR/HER-2) - pending\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for invasive carcinoma (block 7):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) NEGATIVE (1+)\u000aNote: The same results were obtained on the prior core needle biopsy performed\u000aat HVMA.\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000acarcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but\u000aonly a portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity\u000ain >10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: History of left breast nodule, edge of areola at 6 o'clock core biopsy\u000aat HVMA on REMOVED_DATE - confirmed by BWH pathology department REMOVED_DATE  showed invasive\u000acancer. ER positive, PR positive, Her2Neu negative.\u000aOperation: Left mammographically-directed breast biopsy and sentinel node\u000amapping.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast cancer.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1 - left sentinel nodes #1 (fs).\u000a#2 - left breast tissue at 6 o'clock (short/superior, long/lateral), inked per\u000apathology protocol.\u000aRadiology report: Mass and wire in specimen. Keme Babagbemi, M.D.\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "#1 - LEFT SENTINEL NODE #1" (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aLymph node negative for metastasis.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by CHANG,MARTIN C,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart one is labeled "#1 - left sentinel node #1", and consists of a single\u000afragment of tan/yellow soft tissue, measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm, containing a\u000asingle lymph node, measuring REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest dimension. The lymph node is\u000aentirely submitted as REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aMicro #1: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID remnant, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro #2: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID remnant, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro #3: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID remnant, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aPart two is labeled "#2 - left breast tissue at 6 o'clock, short/superior,\u000along/lateral". It consists of a single fragment of fibroadipose tissue,\u000ameasuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The specimen is oriented with two surgical\u000asutures, designating superior and lateral aspects (short and long,\u000arespectively). The specimen is received inked per the pathology protocol for\u000athe evaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red;\u000ainferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. Contained within the\u000aspecimen is a single localization wire corresponding to the mass on the\u000aaccompanying specimen radiogram. The greatest dimensions of the specimen are\u000amedial to lateral, and superior to inferior, respectively. Contained within\u000athe specimen is a single continuous irregularly-shaped tan/gray gritty mass,\u000ameasuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest dimension, and extending to within REMOVED_DATE \u000acm of the anterior, REMOVED_DATE cm of the inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm of the posterior, REMOVED_DATE cm of\u000athe lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm of the medial, and REMOVED_DATE cm of the superior resection\u000amargins. The remainder of the breast parenchyma is grossly unremarkable. The\u000amass and its closest margins are submitted in their entirety.\u000aMicro #4: Medial edge, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro #5-17: Nodule in relation to closest margins, multiple frags, ESS.\u000aMicro #18: Lateral edge, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro #19-22: Additional margins, multiple frags, ESS.\u000amcc/\u000aReports to: CARTER, KATHARINE M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: SENTINEL LYMPH NODE\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
