VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST MASTECTOMY W/REGIONAL LYMPH NODES\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aODZE, ROBERT, DANIEL, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by ODZE,ROBERT DANIEL,M.D.\u000a1) RIGHT BREAST, MASTECTOMY:\u000aBenign breast tissue with fibrocystic change.\u000aSkin with no significant pathologic change.\u000a2) LEFT BREAST, SIMPLE MASTECTOMY:\u000aINVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA\u000aSYNOPSIS:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA\u000aSize - REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aMultifocal - yes (see NOTE)\u000aHistologic Type - lobular\u000aHistologic Grade (SBR) - II (moderate)\u000aNuclear Grade - intermediate\u000aEIC - negative\u000aLymphovascular invasion - absent\u000aDermal lymphatic invasion - absent\u000aSkin invasion - absent\u000aSkeletal muscle invasion - absent\u000aFinal Margins (invasive) -\u000aNegative (>0.3 cm) - deep\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU - absent\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - present\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER/PR/HER-2) - performed previously\u000aNOTE:\u000aThe invasive carcinoma was not evident on gross examination. Consecutive\u000asections through the region of the palpable mass prior to treatment (at the\u000anipple) reveals an (at least )5 cm area of invasive carcinoma. Additional\u000asections of grossly normal tissue from the upper outer and upper inner\u000aquadrants (several centimeters from the main mass) reveal additional foci of\u000ainvasive carcioma (up to REMOVED_DATE cm in size). There is no histologic evidence of\u000atreatment effect on the tumor.\u000a3) SPECIMEN LABELED "PORT-A-CATH":\u000aGross examination only.\u000a4) SPECIMEN LABELED "ADDIITONAL MEDIAL SKIN, LEFT BREAST":\u000aSkin with no significant pathologic change.\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy.\u000a5) SPECIMEN LABELED "ADDITIONAL RIGHT BREAST TISSUE":\u000aBenign breast tissue.\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 55 yo F with multifocal & invasive lobular left breast. Rx Taxol\u000a& AZ. S/p L breast lumpectomy & sentinel node bx, prophylactic\u000aright simple mastectomy.\u000aOperation: Left mastectomy, prophylactic right mastectomy, removal of\u000aportacath.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Breast cancer.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Right breast - short sup skin 12:00, long lat tail.\u000a2. Left breast - short superior skin 12:00, long lateral tail.\u000a3. Portacath - ID only.\u000a4. Additional medial skin, L breast.\u000a5. Additional left breast tissue.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by CHANG,PRISCILLA S.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in five parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aThe first part, labeled "#1 right short superior skin @ 12:00 long lateral\u000atail", is a 2149-gram right mastectomy specimen (34 x 22 x 5 cm) with a\u000awhite/tan skin ellipse (31 x REMOVED_DATE cm) with an inverted nipple (1.9 cm). The\u000aspecimen is received with two orienting sutures. No scars are identified on\u000athe skin. The deep margin is a smooth fascial plane without skeletal muscle\u000apresent, which is inked black. The breast parenchyma contains numerous\u000ablue/black cysts and is diffusely fibrous. No masses are grossly identified.\u000aThe lateral portion of the specimen is thinly sliced but no lymph nodes are\u000aidentified. Representative sections are submitted.\u000aMicro 1: upper outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 2: upper inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 3: lower inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 4: lower outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 5: nipple, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aThe second part, labeled "#2 left breast - short superior skin 12:00 long\u000alateral tail", consists of a 2277-gram left mastectomy specimen (33 x 24 x 5\u000acm) with a white/tan skin ellipse (30 x REMOVED_DATE cm) with an inverted nipple (2.0\u000acm). No scars are identified on the skin surface but mild dimpling of the skin\u000amedial and superior to the nipple is identified. No definitive masses are\u000aidentified in the specimen. The deep margin is a smooth fascial plane.\u000aSerial sectioning reveals multiple blue/black cysts but no definitive tumor.\u000aThe tissue directly under the nipple and lateral to the nipple is firm to the\u000atouch over an area of 5 cm, located 3 cm from the deep margin, which which is\u000asuspicious for residual treated tumor. No core biopsy site is grossly\u000aidentified. The gross findings were reviewed with Dr. Lester. The lateral\u000asoft tissue is thinly sectioned but no lymph nodes are identified.\u000aRepresentative sections are submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  5 cm area deep to nipple submitted from medial to lateral,\u000aincluding nipple in micro 6 and 7, 10 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 13: upper inner quadrant, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 14: upper outer quarant, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 15: lower outer quadrant, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 16: lower inner quadrant, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 17: skin with area of dimpling, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  deep margin closest to possible tumor, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aThe third part, labeled "#3 portacath ID only", consists of a portion of\u000aplastic (2.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) labeled "BARD REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" with attached tubing\u000ameasuring 21 cm long x REMOVED_DATE cm in diameter, grossly consistent with a portacath.\u000aThe fourth part, labeled "#4 additional medial skin left breast", consits\u000aof a single fragment of pink/tan skin measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm, excised to a\u000amaximal depth of REMOVED_DATE cm. The specimen is unoriented and no lesions are grossly\u000aidentified. Representative sections are submitted.\u000aMicro 18: additional medial skin, left breast, 4 frags, RSS.\u000aThe fifth part, labeled "#5 additional right breast tissue" (please NOTE: the\u000aform 86 states "left" and the container is labeled "right"), consists of two\u000afragments of fibroadipose tissue. The first part measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aand the second measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. No lesions are grossly identified.\u000aBoth specimens are less than 5% comprised of firm white fibrous tissue.\u000aRepresentative sections are submitted.\u000aMicro 19: larger fragment, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 20: smaller fragment, 3 frags, RSS.\u000apsc\u000aReports to: LESNIKOSKI, BETH-ANN M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY W/REGIONAL LYMPH NODES\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY W/REGIONAL LYMPH NODES\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: UNLISTED SURGICAL SPECIMEN - LEVEL I (GROSS ONLY)\u000a[report_end]
