VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID SKIN- OTHER THAN CYST, TAG OR DEBRIDEMENT\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aMCKEE, PHILLIP, H., M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by MCKEE,PHILLIP H.,M.D.\u000a#1. LEFT BREAST SCAR:\u000aSkin with cicatrix/repair reaction.\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy.\u000a#2. LEFT BREAST TISSUE, RE-EXCISION:\u000aThe sections show fibroadipose tissue with biopsy site, fat necrosis, fibrosis,\u000aand repair reaction.\u000aOnly a limited amount of breast parenchyma is present within the specimen.\u000aThere is no atypical ductal hyperplasia present or evidence of malignancy.\u000a#3. LEFT BREAST, DEEP NODULE:\u000aThe sections show further biopsy site inflammatory changes.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 51-year-old postmenopausal female, not on hormone replacement\u000atherapy, whose mammogram (9/1/98) demonstrated a new cluster of calcifications\u000ain the left upper outer quadrant; a core biopsy (10/13/98) revealed highly\u000aatypical ductal hyperplasia; a partial mastectomy (11/2/98) revealed severely\u000aatypical ductal hyperplasia, bordering on DCIS, present <0.1 cm from the\u000aanterior resection margin.\u000aOperation: Double wire-localization re-excision\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast ADH/DCIS\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1) Left breast scar\u000a2) Left breast tissue (whip stitch=new margin)\u000a3) Deep nodule, left breast\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by CHAN,JENNIFER A.,M.D.,C.M.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in three parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart one, "1) left breast scar", consists of a single tan/white skin ellipse\u000a(2.3 x REMOVED_DATE cm, excised to REMOVED_DATE cm depth). There is a well healed surgical scar\u000a(1.8 cm) within the skin ellipse. The remainder of the specimen is\u000aunremarkable. The entire specimen is submitted.\u000aMicro 1: Left breast scar, multi frag, ESS\u000aPart two, "2) left breast tissue (whip stitch=new margin)", consists of a\u000asingle fragment of yellow/tan fibroadipose tissue (5.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with a\u000astitch on one surface indicating the new anterior margin. The surface opposite\u000athe new margin is pink/tan and fibrotic, consistent with an old biopsy site.\u000aThere are no masses or nodules within the specimen. The new margin is inked in\u000ablue, and the entire specimen is submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Left breast tissue, including new anterior margin, 1 frag/cass,\u000aESS\u000aPart three, "3) deep nodule, left breast", consists of a single unoriented\u000afragment of yellow/tan fibroadipose tissue (2.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The entire\u000aspecimen is inked black. Within the specimen, there is a firm, white, fibrotic\u000aarea (1.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). There are no other nodules or masses. This fibrous\u000aarea is ill-defined and appproaches the inked black resection margin by REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000aThe entire specimen is submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Deep nodule, left breast, multi frag, ESS\u000ajch\u000aReports to: KAELIN, CAROLYN, MARY M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: SKIN- OTHER THAN CYST, TAG OR DEBRIDEMENT\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
