roadipose\u000atissue, oriented with three, surgical sutures: A short at the superior, a long\u000aat the lateral, and whip stitch at deep margin. It measures REMOVED_DATE (M-L) x REMOVED_DATE \u000a(S-I) x REMOVED_DATE (A-P) cm. The specimen is received inked. The specimen is inked\u000aper pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black;\u000aanterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange.\u000aThe specimen is received with the localization wire detached from tissue.\u000aCorrelation with the specimen radiogram, based on the shape, indicates that the\u000atwo mammographic masses are located at the medial and lateral poles of the\u000aspecimen. Neither mass is distinctly identifiable, grossly.\u000aThe specimen is serially sectioned into 12 slices from medial to lateral. The\u000atissue is composed of homogeneous-appearing, fibrous tissue, with no distinct\u000amass lesions identified. The medial edge is arbitrarily designated as Slice 1,\u000aand the specimen entirely submitted in serial sections.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 1 (medial edge), longitudinal sections, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 2, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 3, inferior, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 3, superior, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 4, inferior, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 4, superior, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 5, inferior, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 5, superior, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 6, inferior, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 6, superior, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 7, inferior, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 7, superior, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 8, inferior, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 8, superior, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 9, inferior, 2 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 9, superior, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 10, inferior, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 10, superior, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 11, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral edge (Slice 12), longitudinal, multiple frags, ESS.\u000amcc/MMM\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Martin C Chang M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Gilbert Brodsky M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
