VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aCORSON, JOSEPH, M., M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by CORSON,JOSEPH M.,M.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST TISSUE:\u000aINVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA, modified Bloom-Richardson grade I/III, in a\u000asingle REMOVED_DATE cm focus.\u000aThe tumor is near the juncture of the medial and anterior margins, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom the medial margin and REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior margin.\u000aLymphatic/vascular invasion is not identified.\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN-SITU is present as multiple foci.\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia.\u000aFibrocystic change with epithelial hyperplasia, ductal dilatation, dense\u000astromal fibrosis, adenosis and apocrine metaplasia.\u000aMicrocalcifications in association with atypical and benign ducts.\u000aBiopsy site identified in area of fibrocystic change.\u000aNOTE: There is a 2 cm area of fibrocystic change with dense stromal fibosis\u000acontaining the core needle tract which correlates with the palpable and\u000aultrasound detected mass. The small invasive tumor and lobular\u000acarcinoma in situ are incidental findings.\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: by BOROWSKY,ALEXANDER D.,M.D.\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for invasive carcinoma:\u000aEstrogen receptor - Positive\u000aProgesterone receptor - Positive\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) - Negative (0)\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000ainvasive carcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but\u000aonly a portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity\u000ain >10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 52 year old female with a left mass, REMOVED_DATE  mammogram was unreveal-\u000aing, U/S demonstrates a 16 mm solid mass at the 12 o'clock axis.\u000aBiopsy was recommended, core biopsy revealed dense interlobular stroma,\u000aexcision of the mass is recommended.\u000aOperation: Left breast biopsy\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast mass\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Left breast tissue (color coded only)\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by CORBO,JOSEPH,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number\u000aand "left breast tissue", and consists of a yellow/tan portion of fibroadipose\u000atissue (5 x 4 x REMOVED_DATE cm). In the center of the specimen there is an ill-defined\u000aspherical area of firmness (2 cm in diameter). There is focal hemorrhage in\u000athe center of this firm area (0.7 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The specimen is inked for\u000athe evaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior =\u000ared; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. Sections of margins\u000aare submitted for microscopic examination. but this is not explicitly stated.\u000aThe specimen is entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  breast biopsy (submitted serially from lateral to medial; area of\u000afirmness primarily in cassette REMOVED_DATE ), mult frags, ESS\u000ajc\u000aReports to: KAELIN, CAROLYN, MARY M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
