lack. The entire specimen is submitted for\u000ahistological analysis.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  larger breast fragment specimen, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 7: smaller fragment, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aPart two, sublabeled "Medial shave margin", consists of a single fragment of\u000ayellow/tan fibroadipose tissue (5.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). A single whipstitch is\u000apresent orienting the specimen on the new margin; this margin is inked green.\u000aThe remainder of the specimen is inked black. The specimen consists almost\u000aentirely of dense white fibrous tissue. The entire specimen is submitted for\u000ahistological analysis.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  cross sections of medial shave margin, multi frags, ESS.\u000aReports to: KAELIN, CAROLYN, MARY M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
