VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID:REMOVED_CASE_ID Report Status: Signed\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aDIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. Left breast, localization excision:\u000aInvasive ductal carcinoma, poorly differentiated, REMOVED_DATE cm. in size.\u000aDuctal carcinoma in situ, high grade, comedocarcinoma type with necrosis\u000aand microcalcifications.\u000aChanges consistent with prior needle core biopsy site.\u000aB. Additional tissue of left breast, excision:\u000aDuctal carcinoma in situ, high grade, comedocarcinoma type with necrosis.\u000aFibrocystic changes with ductal hyperplasia.\u000aC. Final lateral margin of left breast, excision:\u000aNo diagnostic abnormalities recognized.\u000aD. Final medial margin of left breast, excision:\u000aFibrocystic changes with focal ductal hyperplasia.\u000aE. Final deep margin, excision:\u000aNo diagnostic abnormalities recognized.\u000aF. Left axillary lymph nodes, dissection:\u000aNine lymph nodes with no evidence of malignancy (0/9).\u000aSYNOPTIC REPORT BREAST:\u000aINVASIVE TUMOR:\u000a-histologic type: Invasive ductal\u000a-histologic grade: Poorly differentiated\u000a-size (greatest dimension): REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000a-lymphatic/vascular invasion: None identified\u000a-perineural invasion: None identified\u000a-microcalcification in invasive tumor: None identified\u000a-margins for invasive tumor:\u000aInvasive carcinoma is REMOVED_DATE to REMOVED_DATE cm. from the mid superficial margin in a\u000amicroscopic focus and is REMOVED_DATE to REMOVED_DATE cm. from the mid deep margin in a\u000amicroscopic focus (both at superior end of specimen).\u000a-immunohistochemical staining performed on block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID reveal the following\u000aresults for the infiltrating carcinoma:\u000aEstrogen receptor: NEGATIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor: NEGATIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID): POSITIVE for overexpression.\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU (DCIS):\u000a-histologic type: Comedocarcinoma type\u000a-histologic grade: High grade\u000a-size (greatest dimension): Multifocal, spanning several cm.\u000a(largest focus REMOVED_DATE cm.)\u000a-extent: Multifocal\u000a-extensive intraductal component: Absent\u000a-necrosis in DCIS: Present, extensive\u000a-microcalcifications in DCIS: Present\u000a-margins for DCIS:\u000aIn the localization specimen (A), ductal carcinoma in situ is focally less\u000athan REMOVED_DATE cm. from the superior deep margin in a microscopic focus, and is\u000apresent at and less than REMOVED_DATE cm. from the lateral and anterior margins in\u000amultiple foci from mid to inferior aspects. Ductal carcinoma in situ is\u000apresent in the separate "additional tissue" specimen where it is less than\u000a0.1 cm. from the medial inferior margin in a microscopic focus.\u000aLYMPH NODES:\u000aA total of 9 lymph nodes sampled are all negative for malignancy (0/9).\u000aADDITIONAL PATHOLOGIC FINDINGS:\u000aFibrocystic changes with ductal hyperplasia.\u000aChanges consistent with prior biopsy site.\u000aPRIOR RELATED SPECIMENS REVIEWED:\u000aLeft breast at 12 o'clock, needle core biopsies; REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by: Daniel D. Koelliker, M.D.\u000aClinical diagnosis & history:\u000aLeft breast carcinoma; calcifications noted anterior to nodule\u000aTissue-Designation:\u000aA.Breast, excision with margins - left\u000aB.Breast, excision with margins - left, additional tissue\u000aC.Breast, excision with margins - left, final lateral margin\u000aD.Breast, excision with margins - left, final medial margin\u000aE.Breast, excision with margins - left, final deep margin\u000aF.Lymph nodes, dissection - left axillary\u000aGross description:\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin in six containers.\u000aSpecimen A labeled "left breast lump needle loc" consists of a 48 gram, REMOVED_DATE x\u000a5.3 x REMOVED_DATE cm. portion of fibroadipose tissue with a localizing wire\u000aand marked with two orienting sutures and accompanied by a specimen x-ray. At\u000aone end is a short suture oriented as superior and in the mid portion of one\u000aside is a long suture oriented as lateral of the left breast. Based on these\u000aorientations, there is a wire which extends out of the tissue in the mid\u000asuperficial and lateral inferior area aspects of the specimen. The margins are\u000agrossly unremarkable and are inked black throughout. The deep surface is\u000adouble inked red and the lateral half is double inked blue. Cross sectioning\u000afrom superior towards inferior demonstrates a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. hard,\u000awhite-tan nodule with focal reddish discoloration and surrounding bright yellow\u000atissue located in the superior most aspect of the specimen. Cross sectioning\u000athe remainder of the specimen demonstrates mostly yellow lobulated adipose\u000atissue with focal thin strands of white-tan fibrous tissue. In the inferior\u000aportion there is an area of linear hemorrhage. No additional suspicious areas\u000aare seen. Nearly all but trimmed edges of the specimen is embedded. 31 agg.\u000aSection code: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - superior margin\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - entire tumor from superior towards inferior\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - entire remainder of superior to mid portion\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - entire mid portion\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - inferior portion including entire area of hemorrhage\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - remainder of inferior portion\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - inferior margin\u000aSpecimen B labeled "left breast additional tissue" consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x\u000a1.0 cm. portion of fibroadipose tissue which has two orienting sutures, with a\u000ashort suture at one aspect oriented as nipple superior and 90 degrees from this\u000ais a long suture oriented as lateral. One surface appears to be a concave area\u000awith red, granular, hemorrhagic surface. The opposite surface is grossly\u000aunremarkable and is inked black. The specimen is bisected into medial and\u000alateral halves and is cross sectioned from superior towards inferior\u000ademonstrating yellow, lobulated adipose tissue with focal white-tan fibrous\u000atissue. No grossly suspicious areas are seen. The entire specimen is\u000asubmitted as follows: 8 agg. all.\u000aSection code: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - medial half from superior to inferior\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - lateral half from superior towards inferior\u000aSpecimen C labeled "final lateral margin" consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000aportion of fibroadipose tissue with an orienting suture on one surface oriented\u000aas side away from tumor. This surface, marked with the suture, is inked black.\u000aThe specimen is cross sectioned and entirely submitted sequentially in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000a5 agg. all.\u000aSpecimen D labeled "final medial margin" consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000aaggregate of two portions of fibroadipose tissue, one of which is marked with a\u000asuture oriented as side away from tumor. The surface marked with the suture is\u000ainked black. The entire specimen is submitted as follows: 8 agg. all.\u000aSection code: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - sequential sections of inked portion\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - entire separate portion\u000aSpecimen E labeled "final deep margin, stitch is new margin" consists of a REMOVED_DATE \u000ax REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. portion of fibroadipose tissue which is marked on one surface\u000awith two separate sutures, designated as new margin and inked black. The\u000aspecimen is cross sectioned and serially submitted in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. 9 agg. all.\u000aSpecimen F labeled "left axillary lymph nodes" consists of a 9 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000aaggregate of portions of adipose tissue. The tissue is dissected revealing\u000amultiple lymph nodes ranging from REMOVED_DATE to REMOVED_DATE cm. in greatest dimension. The\u000alarger nodes show fatty replacement of the lymph node hilum. All of the\u000alymph nodes are submitted, each entirely submitted as follows:\u000aSection code: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - multiple separate lymph nodes\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - one lymph node sectioned\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - multiple separate lymph nodes\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - largest lymph node entirely\u000aDictated by: DDK____(signature on file)____MICHAEL J. ROSS, M.D. REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a____(signature on file)____DANIEL D. KOELLIKER, M.D. REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a[report_end]
