VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID:REMOVED_CASE_ID Report Status: Signed\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aADDENDUM REPORT\u000aAddendum #1 Entered: REMOVED_DATE -1429\u000a*** ADDITIONAL DIAGNOSTIC INFORMATION ***\u000aThis report contains an addendum to the original for the purpose of providing\u000aadditional diagnostic information. The original diagnosis is unchanged.\u000aFluorescence in situ hybridization (FISH) with probes for REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu performed at\u000aMayo Medical Laboratories on blocks REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID reveals the following results\u000afor the infiltrating carcinoma:\u000aBoth foci in the specimen showed NO evidence of REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu gene amplification.\u000aAddeundum Signed Electronically Signed KOELLIKER,DANIEL D. M.D. REMOVED_DATE \u000aDIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. Left breast, localization excision (94 grams):\u000aInvasive ductal carcinoma, moderately differentiated, REMOVED_DATE cm. in size.\u000aInvasive ductal carcinoma, moderately differentiated, REMOVED_DATE cm. in size.\u000aDuctal carcinoma in situ, intermediate grade, cribriform type with\u000anecrosis and focal microcalcifications.\u000aFocal lobular carcinoma in situ.\u000aChanges consistent with prior needle core biopsy sites (two).\u000aB. Sentinel lymph node, left #1, excision:\u000aNo diagnostic abnormalities recognized.\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy (0/1).\u000aC. Sentinel lymph node, left #2, excision:\u000aNo diagnostic abnormalities recognized.\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy (0/1).\u000aD. Sentinel lymph node, left #3, excision:\u000aNo diagnostic abnormalities recognized.\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy (0/1).\u000aE. Sentinel lymph node, left #4, excision:\u000aNo diagnostic abnormalities recognized.\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy (0/1).\u000aF. Sentinel lymph node, left #5, excision:\u000aNo diagnostic abnormalities recognized.\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy (0/1).\u000aG. Sentinel lymph node, left #6, excision:\u000aNo diagnostic abnormalities recognized.\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy (0/1).\u000aH. Lymph nodes, left axillary, excisions:\u000aThree lymph nodes with no diagnostic abnormalities recognized.\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy (0/3).\u000aSYNOPTIC REPORT:\u000aINVASIVE TUMOR:\u000a-histologic type: invasive ductal carcinoma, two\u000aadjacent foci\u000a-histologic grade: moderately differentiated, both foci\u000a-size (greatest dimension): REMOVED_DATE cm. and REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000a-lymphatic/vascular invasion: none identified\u000a-perineural invasion: none identified\u000a-microcalcification in invasive tumor: none identified\u000a-margins for invasive tumor: The larger invasive carcinoma is focally\u000a0.2 cm. from the medial margin (slide REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID). The smaller invasive\u000acarcinoma is focally less than REMOVED_DATE cm. (slide REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) and REMOVED_DATE 2 cm. (slide\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) from the deep margin at the inferior aspect.\u000a-immunohistochemical staining for estrogen and progesterone receptors has\u000abeen performed on the prior specimen (S-05-6371) and both were positive.\u000a-immunohistochemical staining performed on blocks REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID reveal the\u000afollowing results for the infiltrating carcinoma:\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID): 2+ staining. Further evaluation by\u000afluorescence in situ hybridization (FISH)\u000amethod will be performed and results\u000areported in an addendum to follow.\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU (DCIS):\u000a-histologic type: cribriform type\u000a-histologic grade: intermediate grade\u000a-size (greatest dimension): Microscopic foci within and around\u000athe invasive tumor\u000a-extent: focal\u000a-extensive intraductal component: absent\u000a-necrosis in DCIS: present, focal\u000a-microcalcifications in DCIS: present\u000a-margins for DCIS: Ductal carcinoma in situ is present less than REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000afrom the deep margin in two microscopic foci (slides REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU (LCIS): present, focal\u000aLYMPH NODES:\u000aA total of nine lymph nodes sampled are all negative for malignancy\u000a(0/6 sentinel lymph nodes; REMOVED_DATE non-sentinel lymph nodes).\u000aCOMMENT: The sentinel lymph nodes, specimens B-G, are examined at\u000amultiple levels with H&E stains and with immunohistochemical stains for\u000akeratin.\u000aADDITIONAL PATHOLOGIC FINDINGS:\u000aChanges consistent with prior biopsy site.\u000aPRIOR RELATED SPECIMENS REVIEWED:\u000aLeft breast, needle core biopsies (two); S-05-6371 A and B; REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by: Daniel D. Koelliker, M.D.\u000aINTRA-OPERATIVE CONSULTATION:\u000aOPERATING ROOM CONSULTATION (TISSUE EXAMINATION):\u000a#1. Sentinel lymph node #1: No gross tumor seen.\u000a#2. Sentinel lymph node #2: No gross tumor seen.\u000a#3. Sentinel lymph node #3: No gross tumor seen.\u000a#4. Sentinel lymph node #4: No gross tumor seen.\u000a#5. Sentinel lymph node #5: No gross tumor seen.\u000a#6. Sentinel lymph node #6: No gross tumor seen.\u000aDDK\u000aClinical diagnosis & history:\u000aLeft breast carcinoma\u000aTissue-Designation:\u000aA.Breast, excision with margins - left\u000aB.Sentinel lymph node - #1\u000aC.Sentinel lymph node - #2\u000aD.Sentinel lymph node - #3\u000aE.Sentinel lymph node - #4\u000aF.Sentinel lymph node - #5\u000aG.Sentinel lymph node - #6\u000aH.Lymph node, biopsy - non-sentinel\u000aGross description:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in eight containers.\u000aSpecimen A labeled "left breast mass, long lateral, short superior, two knots\u000ainferior" consists of a 94 gram, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 cm. portion of fibroadipose\u000atissue containing a localizing wire and marked with three separate sutures.\u000aThe outer surfaces are focally bluish discolored and are grossly free of tumor.\u000aThe margins throughout are inked black. The deep margin is double inked red,\u000aand the lateral margin is double inked blue. The specimen has a wire entering\u000athe superior aspect of the superficial aspect of the lateral surface. A short\u000asuture is at the superior aspect. A double knotted suture is at the inferior\u000aaspect. A long suture is at the lateral aspect. The outer margins are grossly\u000afree of tumor. Located in the middle of the specimen on sectioning, slightly\u000ainferior to the midline is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. hard mass which has soft,\u000apunctate, yellowish areas within in it and focal linear hemorrhage. Located\u000a0.5 to REMOVED_DATE cm. from the inferior aspect of this larger tumor and slightly\u000alateral to it is a separate REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. hard nodule which has focal\u000alinear hemorrhage adjacent to it. Most of the remaining tissue is adipose\u000atissue with thin strands of white-tan fibrous tissue. No additional suspicious\u000alesions are seen. Representative sections are submitted from superior towards\u000ainferior as follows:\u000aSECTION CODE: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - superior margin\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - representative sections of superior portion of\u000aspecimen\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - sections from immediately superior to mass\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - sections of larger mass\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - additional representative margins\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - intervening tissue\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - separate inferior and posterior lateral nodule\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - tissue inferior to nodule\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - inferior margin\u000aSpecimen B labeled "sentinel node #1, 7778" is examined in the Operating Room\u000aand consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. lymph node which is sectioned in the\u000aOperating Room revealing no gross evidence of tumor. The entire specimen is\u000asubmitted in B. 4X all.\u000aSpecimen C labeled "sentinel node #2, 5832" consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000alymph node which is sectioned in the Operating Room and demonstrates no gross\u000aevidence of tumor. The entire specimen is submitted in C. 3X all.\u000aSpecimen D labeled "sentinel node #3" is examined in the Operating Room and on\u000asectioning there is no gross evidence of tumor. It consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x\u000a0.5 cm. lymph node. It is entirely submitted in D. 4X all.\u000aSpecimen E labeled "sentinel node #4" consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. lymph\u000anode which is sectioned and examined in the Operating Room. There is no gross\u000aevidence of tumor seen. The entire specimen is submitted in E. 2X all.\u000aSpecimen F labeled "sentinel node #5" is examined in the Operating Room and\u000aconsists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. lymph node which is sectioned revealing no\u000agross evidence of tumor. The entire specimen is submitted in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. 2 agg.\u000aall.\u000aSpecimen G labeled "sentinel node #6" is examined in the Operating Room and on\u000asectioning, there is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. lymph node with no gross evidence of\u000atumor seen. The entire specimen is submitted in G. 1 agg. all.\u000aSpecimen H labeled "non-sentinel nodes" consists of three separate lymph nodes\u000awhich are sectioned and submitted in their respective cassettes, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. 3 agg.\u000aall.\u000aDictated by: DDK____(signature on file)____DENNIS J. FEEN, M.D. REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a____(signature on file)____DANIEL D. KOELLIKER, M.D. REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a[report_end]
