VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID:REMOVED_CASE_ID Report Status: Signed\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aDIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. Skin of left breast, excision:\u000aDermal chronic inflammation and fibroplasia.\u000aChanges consistent with prior excision site.\u000aB. Left breast, inferior margin, re-excision:\u000aDuctal carcinoma in situ, intermediate grade, cribriform type, single\u000amicroscopic focus adjacent to prior excision site (see note).\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia with microcalcifications, focal.\u000aChanges consistent with prior excision site.\u000aNOTE: The entire specimen is submitted. In one section (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), there is a\u000asingle REMOVED_DATE cm. focus of ductal carcinoma in situ adjacent to the prior\u000aexcision site; the margins are free of ductal carcinoma in situ (closest\u000aextent is REMOVED_DATE 4 cm. from the inked margin).\u000aThere is no evidence of residual invasive carcinoma. The prior excision\u000a(S-05-7178) has been reviewed.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by: Daniel D. Koelliker, M.D.\u000aClinical diagnosis & history:\u000aInfiltrating ductal carcinoma in situ left breast\u000aTissue-Designation:\u000aA.Skin, excision - left breast\u000aB.Breast, excision with margins - left inferior margin\u000aGross description:\u000aThe specimen is received in two parts.\u000aSpecimen A labeled "skin" consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. ellipse of skin and\u000asubcutis to a depth of 1 cm. The skin is C-shaped and has a partly smooth,\u000apartly elevated surface. The area of elevation measures 4 x REMOVED_DATE cm. 4 agg,\u000alabeled REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aSpecimen B labeled "left breast inferior margin" consists of a REMOVED_DATE x 6 x 2 cm.\u000aportion of predominantly yellow adipose, partly soft, pink tissue with a convex\u000aand a concave surface. The convex surface is covered by fat. The concave\u000asurface is somewhat irregular and congested. The convex surface is marked with\u000aa double suture as the true inferior margin. A short suture marks the superior\u000amargin and a long suture marks the lateral margin. The superior half of the\u000aspecimen is painted with blue ink, and the inferior half of the specimen is\u000apainted with black ink. The specimen is serially sectioned from medial to\u000alateral, labeled REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. Cut section reveals predominantly yellow adipose\u000atissue with areas of firm, white tissue. 26 agg. all.\u000aDictated by: MJR____(signature on file)____DENNIS J. FEEN, M.D. REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a____(signature on file)____DANIEL D. KOELLIKER, M.D. REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a[report_end]
