aSclerosing adenosis.\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia (slide 26, 28)\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "7) LEFT BREAST, INFERIOR":\u000aSclerosing adenosis.\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia and papillomatosis.\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "8) LEFT BREAST, MEDIAL":\u000aLobular hyperplasia.\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "9) LEFT BREAST, SKIN":\u000aSkin with no significant pathologic change.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: REMOVED_DATE  (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), lt. br. core bx. revealed inv. duct. ca.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast mass\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1) Sentinel Node (FS)\u000a2) Lt breast tissue with mass\u000a3) Lt breast anterior (black/prior resection; blue/new margin)\u000a4) Lt breast lateral (black/prior resection; yellow/new margin)\u000a5) Lt breast posterior (black/prior resection; blue/new margin)\u000a6) Lt breast superior (black/prior resection; red/new margin)\u000a7) Lt breast inferior (black/prior resection; green/new margin)\u000a8) Lt breast medial (black/prior resection; orange/new margin - sub-areolar)\u000a9) Lt breast skin (double/nipple margin; short/superior; long/lateral)\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "1) SENTINEL NODE" (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aOne (1) lymph node, negative for tumor.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by SCHMIDT,JASON F.,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in 9 parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart one, "1) sentinel node", consists of a single fragment of yellow/tan,\u000afatty soft tissue (1.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), grossly consistent with a lymph node.\u000aThe specimen is bisected and entirely frozen as REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aMicro 1: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 1 frag, ESS\u000aMicro 2: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 1 frag, ESS\u000aPart two, "2) lt breast tissue with mass", consists of a portion of fibrofatty\u000abreast tissue (6.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) which has been previously inked per\u000apathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior\u000a= blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange.\u000aA white/tan, ill-defined, firm, focally stellate mass (2.4 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm)\u000awith multiple hemorrhagic foci, grossly consistent with previous breast core\u000abiopsy site, is present less than REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral and anterior margins,\u000a0.2 cm from the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000aposterior margin, and 3 cm from the inferior margin. Continguous with and\u000aanterior/inferior to the aforementioned mass, there is a firm cavity (1.3 x REMOVED_DATE \u000ax REMOVED_DATE cm) containing red/brown clotted blood and surrounding fat necrosis.\u000aThe cavity grossly comes to within REMOVED_DATE cm of the anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of\u000athe lateral margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the medial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the inferior\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the superior margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm of the posterior margin.\u000aThe remaining breast tissue consists of REMOVED_DATE % yellow, tan, lobulated fat and\u000a25-30% tan/white, fibrous stroma. No other lesions are grossly identified.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  mass in relation to lateral and anterior margins, 2 frag, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  mass in relation to medial and anterior margins, 2 frag, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  mass nearest superior margin, 3 frag, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  posterior margin nearest mass, 2 frag, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  probable contiguous biopsy cavity, adjacent to mass, to include\u000aanterior, medial, and lateral margins, 4 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 14: additional probably biopsy cavity in relation to inferior margin,\u000a1 frag, RSS\u000aPart three, "3) lt breast anterior", consists of a portion of fibrofatty tissue\u000a(6.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The tissue is received previously inked blue ("new\u000amargin") and black ("prior resection") by the surgeon. A tan/white, indurated\u000alesion (1.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) is identified which grossly appears to extend to\u000aboth black- and blue-inked margins. The remaining breast tissue consists of\u000apredominantly yellow/tan, lobulated fat and scant tan/white, fibrous stroma.\u000aNo other lesions are grossly identified.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  firm lesion, 4 frag, ESS\u000aMicro 17: adjacent breast tissue, 1 frag, RSS\u000aPart four, "4) lt breast lateral", consists of a portion of fibrofatty breast\u000atissue (5.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) which has been previously inked black ("prior\u000aresection") and yellow ("new margin") by the surgeon. A tan/white, indurated\u000afocus (0.3 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) is noted abutting the black-inked margin and coming\u000ato within REMOVED_DATE cm of the new margin. The remaining breast tissue consists of\u000apredominantly yellow/tan, lobulated fat with only scant tan/white, fibrous\u000astroma. No other lesions are identified.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  lesion and adjacent breast tissue, 4 frag, ESS\u000aPart five, "5) lt breast posterior", consists of a portion of fibrofatty breast\u000atissue (6.3 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) which has been previously inked black ("prior\u000aresection") and blue ("new margin") by the surgeon. The breast tissue\u000aconsists of 60% yellow/tan, lobulated fat and 40% tan/white, focally dense to\u000alumpy, fibrous stroma extending to both the new margin and the prior resection\u000amargin. A definitive mass is not identified.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  lumpy, dense, fibrous tissue, multi frag, ESS\u000aPart six, "6) lt breast superior", consists of a portion of fibrofatty breast\u000atissue (6.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) which has been previously inked black ("prior\u000aresection") and red ("new margin") by the surgeon. A white/tan, firm, fibrous\u000aarea (1.3 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) present at the prior resection margin comes to within\u000a0.2 cm of the new margin. The remaining breast tissue consists of\u000apredominantly yellow/tan, lobulated fat. No other lesions are identified.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  lumpy, dense, fibrous stroma in relation to new margin and prior\u000aresection margin, multi frag, ESS\u000aPart seven, "7) lt breast inferior", consists of a portion of fibrofatty breast\u000atissue (9.3 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) which has been previously inked black ("prior\u000aresection margin") and green ("new margin") by the surgeon. The breast tissue\u000aconsists of 70% yellow/tan, lobulated fat and 30% tan/white, fibrous stroma.\u000aNo definitive lesions are identified.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  breast tissue, 4 frag, RSS\u000aPart eight, "8) lt breast medial", consists of a portion of fibrofatty breast\u000atissue (7.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) which has been previously inked black ("prior\u000aresection margin") and orange ("new margin-subareolar") by the surgeon. The\u000abreast tissue consists of 80% yellow/tan, lobulated fat and 20% tan/white,\u000afibrous stroma. No lesions are grossly identified.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  breast stroma, 4 frag, RSS\u000aPart nine, "9) lt breast skin (double suture/nipple margin)", consists of a\u000atriangular portion of tan, diffusely wrinkled skin (6.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with\u000athree (3) sutures: double suture/nipple margin, short/superior, and\u000along/lateral. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation\u000aof margins: posterior = black; anterior = skin; superior = red; inferior =\u000agreen; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. No lesions are identified on the\u000aunremarkable skin. The breast tissue consists of predominantly yellow/tan,\u000alobulated fat and scant fibrous tissue; no lesions are grossly identified.\u000aMicro 34: skin and subjacent breast stroma, 2 frag, RSS\u000adfi\u000aReports to: LESNIKOSKI, BETH-ANN M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: LYMPH NODE BIOPSY\