VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final Type: Surgical Pathology Pathology Report: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID OPERATION DATE: 24 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON: 24 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 16:23 CLINICAL DATA: 62 year old woman with a breast lesion. =============================================================================== *** FINAL DIAGNOSIS *** BREAST (RIGHT), LUMPECTOMY: 1. INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA (80%), MODERATELY TO POORLY DIFFERENTIATED, GRADE REMOVED_DATE  EXTENDING TO WITHIN REMOVED_DATE CM OF THE ANTEROLATERAL RESECTION MARGIN (SLIDE A LEVELS). 2. DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU (20%), COMEDO AND SOLID TYPES, EXTENDING TO WITHING REMOVED_DATE CM OF THE CENTAL ANTERIOR RESECTION MARGIN (SLIDE D LEVELS). 2. FOCAL ATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA. NOTE: Lymphatic/vascular space invasion is identified. The tumor (invasive and in situ components) measures REMOVED_DATE cm. LYMPH NODES (RIGHT AXILLARY DISSECTION): METASTATIC DUCTAL CARCINOMA TO SEVEN OF THIRTY-FOUR AXILLARY LYMPH NODES (7/34), SEE NOTE. NOTE: In one of the positive lymph nodes tumor is present within adipose tissue which is not definitively part of the lymph node. However, the capsule of this node is not discrete. Diagnosis by: HANSEN,KATHLEEN K (RI) Signed On: 29 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 09:04 =============================================================================== *** RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum *** RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST (RIGHT): The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein. The tumor cells stains for progesterone receptor protein. See note. Note: In this laboratory, we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way (paraffin sections) and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay. 91% of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay. 96% of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay. When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections, the predictive value of a positive result was 97% and the predictive value of a negative result was 95%. In this laboratory, we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay. Sixty-five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay, and 98% of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors. THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY. THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES. Added by: Frederick Carl Koerner, M.D. Signed On: 20 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 11:09 *** HER-2 Addendum *** RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR HER-2/c-erbREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Breast (Right): The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER-2/c-erb-2. See note. Note: This test was developed and its performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital. It has not been cleared or approved by the U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA). The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary; this laboratory has established and verified the test's accuracy and precision. Added by: Frederick Carl Koerner, M.D. Signed On: 28 MAY 99 at 07:22 GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab, labeled with the patient's name and unit number, is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm piece of breast tissue with an overlying skin ellipse, measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. There is suture designating the medial margin. Sectioning through the breast parenchyma demonstrates a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm irregular stellate yellow-tan, hard mass that is grossly REMOVED_DATE cm from the closest anterolateral soft tissue margin. The tumor is at least REMOVED_DATE cm from each of the other margins. SECTION CODE: A: tumor and closest anterolateral soft tissue margin B: tumor and central soft tissue margin C: tumor and overlying skin ellipse D: tumor and central anterior soft tissue margin E: representative deep margin F: representative medial margin and breast tissue G: representative medial margin and breast tissue HandI: representative lateral breast tissue and soft tissue margin. NOTE: The margins are all taken radially. Labeled "axilla", is an aggregate of adipose tissue, measuring REMOVED_DATE 0 x REMOVED_DATE cm. Lymph nodes are dissected from this tissue and all or half of each node identified are submitted in cassettes J through T. Resident: C. Diana Jordan, MD =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: MGH-INPATIENT (FLR.UNKNOWN) REPORTS TO: Herbert Charles Hoover Jr., M.D. PART A: RIGHT AXILLA PART B: RIGHT BREAST\u000a[report_end]
