VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aCORSON, JOSEPH, M., M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by CORSON,JOSEPH M.,M.D.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A MASS:\u000aIntraductal papilloma, (0.7 cm), with intraductal hyperplasia.\u000aThere is a biopsy site with epithelial displacement associated\u000awith the papilloma.\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia.\u000aPapillary apocrine hyperplasia, focal.\u000aFibrocystic changes including apocrine metaplasia and cysts\u000aare present.\u000aFibroadenomatoid change.\u000aNOTE: The margins are inked and evaluated.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 52 year old perimenopausal female not on hormones, whose REMOVED_DATE \u000amammogram supplemented by REMOVED_DATE ultrasound demonstrates two nodular\u000adensities in the right outer breast. Cores biopsy of REMOVED_DATE  was\u000anon-diagnostic and excision is recommended.\u000aOperation: Right breast wire localization excision x 2.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast mass x 2.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Right breast tissue (short suture = superior,\u000along suture = lateral, whip stitch - chest wall margin).\u000aShort wire = superior, long wire = inferior.\u000aRadiology: The nodules are present in the specimen----D. Smith, M.D.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by DRAPKIN,RONNY I.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in one (1) part, labeled with the patient's\u000aname, unit number, and "needle localized right breast tissue," and consists of\u000aa single fragment of firm pink/yellow fibroadipose tissue (6.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm),\u000athat is oriented with a short suture designating the superior margin, a long\u000asuture designating the lateral margin, a whip stitch designating the chest wall\u000amargin, a short wire designating superior, and a long wire designating\u000ainferior. The specimen is inked by the surgeon as follows: anterior = blue,\u000aposterior = black, medial = orange, lateral = yellow, superior = red, and\u000ainferior = green. The specimen appears to be focally disrupted at various\u000amargins (possibly due to excision or mammography). The entire specimen is\u000asubmitted. There is a single nodule (0.9 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) present at the\u000aperiphery (lateral margin) of the mass that is pink/white and firm.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  right breast tissue, multiple frags each, ESS.\u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
