gative for malignancy (1/1 sentinel lymph node).\u000a-largest metastatic focus (greatest dimension): REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000a-extranodal extension: focal\u000aPRIOR RELATED SPECIMENS REVIEWED:\u000aLeft breast, needle biopsy, S-03-8006, REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by: Richard J. Sampson, M.D.\u000aClinical diagnosis & history:\u000aLeft breast carcinoma\u000aTissue-Designation:\u000aA.Sentinel lymph node - left axillary\u000aB.Breast, excision with margins - left\u000aC.Breast, excision with margins - left final shaved margin\u000aGross description:\u000aSpecimen A labeled "left axillary sentinel node" consists of a sentinel node\u000awhich is partially replaced by what appears to be a mass of tumor tissue.\u000aOverall, it measures 2 x 2 x 2 cm. 5X all.\u000aSpecimen B labeled "left breast biopsy" consists of a mass of breast tissue\u000ameasuring 5 x 4 x REMOVED_DATE cm. Two marks are present, one of which is a long suture\u000adesignated lateral and a short suture designated superior. When so oriented,\u000athe deep margin is inked with blue ink; the superior superficial margin is\u000ainked with yellow ink. Sections are taken from lateral to medial. 20X.\u000aSpecimen C labeled "final shaved margin, stitch furthest from tumor" consists\u000aof a flat piece of tissue which measures 5 x 5 x REMOVED_DATE cm. There is a stitch\u000apresent on one of the flat sides which is designated furthest from tumor. That\u000aside is inked; the opposite side is not inked. 8X all.\u000aDictated by: RJS____(signature on file)____DENNIS J. FEEN, M.D. REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a____(signature on file)____RICHARD SAMPSON, M.D. REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a[report_end]
