e other. The entire specimen is submitted in cassettes\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. 7 agg. all.\u000aSpecimen B labeled "left axillary contents" consists of a portion of axillary\u000afat with a skin ellipse on the surface and a separate smaller submitted portion\u000aof adipose tissue with a staple. The smaller portion of tissue with the staple\u000ais REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The staple is removed. This portion of tissue is\u000abisected and shows a tan, grossly unremarkable lymph node. The larger specimen\u000ais REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. and the ellipse of skin on the surface, REMOVED_DATE cm. in\u000alength and up to REMOVED_DATE cm. in diameter. It has a well healed scar running along\u000athe surface. Sections through the specimen show multiple firm, brown lymph\u000anodes. Representative sections are submitted. 7 agg.\u000aSection code: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - unattached portion of lymph node, bisected, as well as the\u000aentire skin ellipse\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - nodes, none are bisected\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - each one node, bisected\u000aDictated by: NAM____(signature on file)____RICHARD SAMPSON, M.D. REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a____(signature on file)____NICOLE MIHOK, M.D. REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a[report_end]
