VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID:REMOVED_CASE_ID Report Status: Signed\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aDIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. Right breast, excision (multiple fragments):\u000aDuctal carcinoma in situ, multifocal.\u000aSclerosing adenosis.\u000aBiopsy site.\u000aB. Left breast, excision:\u000aModerately differentiated infiltrating duct carcinoma (0.6 cm.) present\u000aover multiple inked edges of specimen.\u000aDuctal carcinoma in situ, grade REMOVED_DATE \u000aC. Left breast, final anterior margin:\u000aInfiltrating duct carcinoma, present multifocally at a definitive margin.\u000aDuctal carcinoma in situ, grade REMOVED_DATE \u000aD. Left breast, final medial margin:\u000aDuctal carcinoma in situ, involving adenosis (at definitive margin).\u000aE. Left breast, final medial margin:\u000aDuctal carcinoma in situ (at definitive margin).\u000aF. Left breast, final superior margin:\u000aDuctal carcinoma in situ in situ (at definitive margin).\u000aG. Left breast, final inferior margin:\u000aSclerosing adenosis.\u000aSYNOPTIC REPORT: LEFT BREAST, Specimen B\u000aINVASIVE TUMOR:\u000a-histologic type: ductal\u000a-histologic grade: moderately differentiated\u000a-size (greatest dimension): REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000a-lymphatic/vascular invasion: none identified\u000a-perineural invasion: none identified\u000a-microcalcification: present\u000a-margins for invasive tumor: positive at inked margin on primary excision.\u000aPositive at definitive anterior and medial\u000amargins over a broad front.\u000a-immunohistochemical staining on prior specimen (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) was reported as:\u000aEstrogen receptor: POSITIVE (>10% of nuclei stained)\u000aProgesterone receptor: POSITIVE (>10% of nuclei stained)\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID): NEGATIVE (no, faint, or <10% complete membrane\u000astaining)\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU (DCIS):\u000a-histologic type: solid/cribriform\u000a-histologic grade: REMOVED_DATE \u000a-size (greatest dimension): microscopic foci within and around the\u000ainvasive tumor\u000a-extent: focal\u000a-extensive intraductal component: present\u000a-necrosis in DCIS: none identified\u000a-microcalcifications in DCIS: present\u000a-margins for DCIS: clear (greater than or equal to REMOVED_DATE cm.)\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU (LCIS), (in right breast):\u000aPresent, focal.\u000aADDITIONAL PATHOLOGIC FINDINGS:\u000aFibrocystic changes.\u000aChanges consistent with prior biopsy site.\u000aPRIOR RELATED SPECIMENS REVIEWED:\u000asite: left breast upper outer quadrant spec#: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aCOMMENT: In the right breast biopsy, specimen "A", E-cadherin stain is\u000apositive in the in-situ tumor diagnostic of ductal phenotype. The actin stain\u000aand calponin stain confirms that the tumor is in situ. Margins of resection\u000acannot be evaluated because the specimen is in multiple pieces.\u000aIn the left breast biopsy, specimen "B", the E-cadherin stain is also positive\u000ashowing that this is also a ductal tumor. Calponin and myosin stains show the\u000atumor mostly in situ but with some areas of infiltration.\u000aAJCC pTNM Classification (6th Ed.): pREMOVED_ACCESSION_IDb pNX pMX\u000aThe pathologic TNM classification above is based only on the information\u000aavailable to the pathologist, and therefore may not be accurate.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by: Richard J. Sampson, M.D.\u000aClinical diagnosis & history:\u000aBreast carcinoma; status post radiation therapy; sentinel node, pretherapy\u000anegative; left breast cancer; right breast atypia on MRI pre chemo\u000aTissue-Designation:\u000aA.Breast, excision (without margins) - right\u000aB.Breast, excision with margins - left\u000aC.Breast, excision with margins - left final anterior margin\u000aD.Breast, excision with margins - final lateral margin\u000aE.Breast, excision with margins - left final medial margin\u000aF.Breast, excision with margins - left final superior margin\u000aG.Breast, excision with margins - left final inferior margin\u000aGross description:\u000aThe specimen is received in seven containers.\u000aSpecimen A labeled "right breast" consists of fragments of adipose tissue with\u000asome areas of hemorrhagic tissue and all aggregates 3 x 3 x 1 cm. This is\u000afragmented and not inked. Some firm areas are present in the adipose tissue\u000anext to the hemorrhagic areas. The larger pieces are bisected. 3 agg. all.\u000aSpecimen B labeled "left breast mass" consists of a 7 gram, piece of tissue and\u000aconsists of a 3 x 2 x 1 cm. A wire marker is present, but no orienting\u000asutures. The entire specimen is inked black. The specimen is rather firm, but\u000awith no definite tumors. 5X all.\u000aSpecimen C labeled "left breast" consists of fragmented pieces of tissue, two\u000aof which is sutures, designated the "true margin". These portions are inked\u000awith black ink. These and the several other small pieces are submitted\u000aentirely for permanent section. The two pieces that were marked measures REMOVED_DATE x\u000a0.8 x REMOVED_DATE cm. and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. 4 agg. all.\u000aSpecimen D labeled "final lateral margin" consists of three pieces of rather\u000aflat tissue, each of them is marked with a suture. One piece is REMOVED_DATE x 1 x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm., the second is 1 x 1 x REMOVED_DATE cm., and the third is REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. In\u000aeach one flat side marked with a suture is inked black. Each piece is\u000abisected. 6X all.\u000aSpecimen E labeled "final medial margin" consists of a single piece of breast\u000atissue 1 x 1 x REMOVED_DATE cm., and has a suture at one flat margin. The specimen is\u000ainked on that side with black ink, and entirely embedded. 3X all.\u000aSpecimen F labeled "final superior margin" consists of piece of breast tissue 2\u000ax 1 x REMOVED_DATE cm. with a suture at one flat margin, designated the true margin.\u000aThis margin is inked black. 3X all.\u000aSpecimen G labeled "final inferior margin" consists of a flat piece of breast\u000atissue REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. with suture present in the middle portion of the\u000amargin, which is designated " true margin". This side of the specimen is inked\u000ablack, and the specimen is entirely embedded.\u000aDictated by: RJS____(signature on file)____ REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a____(signature on file)____RICHARD SAMPSON, M.D. REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a[report_end]
