VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID:REMOVED_CASE_ID Report Status: Signed\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aDIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. Right breast, simple mastectomy:\u000aFocal atypical ductal hyperplasia.\u000aLobular carcinoma in situ.\u000aSclerosing adenosis; ductal hyperplasia; duct ectasia; fibrocystic\u000achanges; fibroadenomas (4); microcalcifications in benign ducts.\u000aNipple with no diagnostic abnormalities recognized.\u000aChanges consistent with prior excision site.\u000aB. Skin of right chest wall, excision:\u000aNo diagnostic abnormalities recognized.\u000aC. Left breast, simple mastectomy:\u000aResidual focus of well differentiated infiltrating duct carcinoma (0.1\u000acm.) at excision site (upper-outer quadrant).\u000aDuctal carcinoma in situ, grade REMOVED_DATE  solid type, with retrograde lobular\u000aspread at excision site (upper-outer quadrant, REMOVED_DATE cm.) and at upper\u000ainner quadrant (0.1 cm.).\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia.\u000aFocal ductal hyperplasia; sclerosis adenosis; radial scar; duct ectasia;\u000afibroadenoma; fibrocystic changes; microcalcifications in benign ducts.\u000aNipple with no diagnostic abnormalities recognized.\u000aChanges consistent with prior excision site.\u000aD. Left breast, (labeled "scar"), final margin, excision:\u000aFibroadipose tissue with fibrosis and no tumor seen.\u000aE. Left breast, (labeled "tail") final margin, excision:\u000aBreast parenchyma and fibroadipose tissue with no tumor seen.\u000aF. Skin of left chest wall, excision:\u000aNo diagnostic abnormalities recognized.\u000aNOTE: No residual ductal carcinoma in situ is seen in specimen A. E-Cadherin\u000astain is negative and 34 Beta REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID cytokeratin stain is positive in the\u000alobular carcinoma in situ in specimen A consistent with the diagnosis.\u000aMyosin stain on specimen C confirms the presence of a microscopic focus of\u000aresidual infiltrating ductal carcinoma associated with ductal carcinoma in\u000asitu at the excision site. No lymphatic/vascular invasion or\u000aperineural invasion is seen. The surgical margins are free of invasive\u000aand in situ carcinoma in specimen C (greater than REMOVED_DATE cm.). The previous\u000aright and left breast excisions (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) have been reviewed.\u000aThe pTNM classification for the right breast is pTis nNX pMX based on the\u000aprior excision. The pTNM classification for the left breast has been\u000apreviously reported (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aFinal Diagnosis by: Michael J. Ross, M.D.\u000aClinical diagnosis & history:\u000aBilateral breast carcinoma; status post chemo for left invasive, right ductal\u000acarcinoma in situ\u000aTissue-Designation:\u000aA.Breast, simple mastectomy - right\u000aB.Skin, excision - right chest wall\u000aC.Breast, simple mastectomy - left\u000aD.Breast, excision with margins - left\u000aE.Breast, excision with margins - left tail\u000aF.Skin, excision - left chest wall\u000aGross description:\u000aThe specimen is received in six parts.\u000aSpecimen A labeled "right breast" is received fresh and consists of a 174 gram,\u000a16 x REMOVED_DATE x up to 2 cm. subcutaneous mastectomy specimen, surmounted by an\u000aeccentrically placed 3 x REMOVED_DATE cm. nipple. A stitch marks the 12 o'clock\u000aposition. The posterior-lateral margin is painted with black ink, the\u000aposterior-medial margin is painted with blue ink, and the anterior margin is\u000apainted with green ink. Cut section through the breast reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x\u000a1.3 cm. area of hemorrhage and fat necrosis surrounded by firm, tan-white\u000atissue and yellow adipose tissue. This area is located at the mid lateral\u000aaspect of the specimen. The specimen consists predominantly of yellow adipose\u000atissue superiorly. The specimen is serially sectioned from superior to\u000ainferior. A few cysts measuring up to REMOVED_DATE cm. in diameter are present\u000acentrally. Sections REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID include the biopsy site.\u000aSection code: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - nipple, 4X\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - serial sections, superior to inferior, 35 agg.\u000aSpecimen B labeled "right chest wall" consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. circular\u000aportion of skin with a smooth, tan surface. The skin measures REMOVED_DATE cm. in\u000awidth. A suture marks the lateral position.\u000aSection code: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - lateral, 2X\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - superior, 2X\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - inferior, 2X\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - medial, 2X\u000aSpecimen C labeled "left breast" is received fresh and consists of a 172 gram,\u000a14.5 x 12 x REMOVED_DATE cm. subcutaneous mastectomy with eccentrically inferiorly\u000aplaced REMOVED_DATE x 3 cm. nipple with a smooth, tan surface. A suture marks the 6\u000ao'clock position according to the surgical requisition form. The container\u000astates "stitch at 12 o'clock". With the suture at the 6 o'clock position, the\u000aanterior surface is painted with green ink, the posterior-lateral margin is\u000apainted with black ink, and the posterior-medial margin is painted with blue\u000aink. There is slight puckering of the posterior margin at the mid-lateral\u000aaspect of the specimen. Cut section reveals a REMOVED_DATE x 1 x 1 cm. area of firm,\u000atan tissue at the mid-lateral aspect of the specimen near the zone of\u000apuckering. Cut section through the remainder of the breast reveals firm,\u000atan-white tissue admixed with yellow adipose tissue.\u000aSection code: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - excision site, 5X\u000aCD - deep margin, 1X\u000aNI - nipple, 2X\u000aCLI - lower inner quadrant, 1X\u000aCLO - lower outer quadrant, 1X\u000aCUI - upper inner quadrant, 1X\u000aCUO - upper outer quadrant, 1X\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - additional sections near excision site, 7 agg.\u000aSpecimen D labeled "left breast scar" consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. portion\u000aof yellow adipose tissue. A stitch marks the final margin. The side of the\u000aspecimen with the stitch is inked. The specimen is serially sectioned and\u000asubmitted in cassette D. 5X all.\u000aSpecimen E labeled "left breast tail" consists of two portions of yellow\u000aadipose tissue measuring in aggregate REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. A stitch marks the\u000afinal margin of each specimen. The specimen surface with the stitch is painted\u000awith ink. The specimens are each serially sectioned.\u000aSection code: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - one specimen, 2 agg. all.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - second specimen, 2 agg. all.\u000aSpecimen F labeled "left chest wall" consists of a 4 x 3 cm. circular portion\u000aof skin, and subcutis to a depth of REMOVED_DATE cm. The skin width is up to REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000aand has a smooth, tan surface. A stitch marks the lateral margin.\u000aSection code: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - lateral, 2X\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - inferior, 2X\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - medial, 2X\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - superior, 2X\u000aDictated by: MJR____(signature on file)____ REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a____(signature on file)____MICHAEL J. ROSS, M.D. REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a[report_end]
