agranulation tissue. Four centimeters medial to the cyst, is a small, firm\u000anodule (1.1 cm) that is REMOVED_DATE cm from the deep black-inked margin.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  upper inner quadrant cyst, 2 frag, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  upper inner quadrant nodule, 3 frag, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  upper inner quadrant, 2 frag, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  upper inner quadrant, 2 frag, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  lower outer quadrant, 2 frag, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  lower inner quadrant, 2 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 13: nipple, 4 frag, RSS\u000aPart two, "right axillary contents", consists of a single fragment of\u000apink/yellow fibroadipose tissue (7.5 x 5 x REMOVED_DATE cm). Three tan possible lymph\u000anodes are identified, the largest measuring REMOVED_DATE cm, which is grossly involved\u000aby tumor.\u000aMicro 14: largest lymph node, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 15: single lymph node, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 16: single lymph node, bisected, 2 frag, ESS\u000aMicro 17: two possible lymph nodes, 2 frag, ESS\u000aMicro 18: one lymph node, 3 frag, ESS\u000aMicro 19: four possible lymph nodes, 4 frag, ESS\u000aaji\u000aReports to: CHRISTIAN, ROGER, L. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY W/REGIONAL LYMPH NODES\u000a[report_end]
