VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aODZE, ROBERT, DANIEL, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by ODZE,ROBERT DANIEL,M.D.\u000a1) SPECIMEN LABELED "CORE BIOPSY, SCAR SITE":\u000aSkin and subcutaneous tissue with ulceration, acute inflammation, fat\u000anecrosis and granulation tissue formation, foreign body reaction, and\u000aabscess.\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy.\u000a2) SPECIMEN LABELED "RIGHT BREAST, TISSUE", WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISIONAL BIOPSY\u000aFOR CALCIFICATION:\u000aBreast tissue with calcifications in benign epithelium, sclerosing\u000aadenosis, focal epithelial hyperplasia, and healing core biopsy site.\u000aFocal abscess formation is present at core biopsy site.\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 65 year old female on ERT has 4 mm calcifications in RUOQ. Breast\u000acore biopsy attempted but calcifications not obtained. For excisional biopsy.\u000aOf note, patient developed open draining wound at core biopsy incision site.\u000aOperation: Right wire localized breast biopsy\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right abnormal mammo\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1) Core biopsy scar site\u000a#2) Right breast tissue (short stitch/superior; long stitch/lateral; whip on\u000adeep margin)\u000aRADIOLOGY: #1) Stainless steel biopsy marker ring. C. Denison, MD\u000a#2) Calcifications in specimen. C. Denison, MD\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by PADERA,ROBERT F.,JR.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart one, labeled "#1. core biopsy scar site", consists of a white/tan skin\u000aellipse measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm with underlying soft tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm, excised to a depth of REMOVED_DATE cm. On the skin surface there is an area of\u000aulceration measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm with surrounding erythema. The specimen is\u000aunoriented. The margins are inked black. The specimen is serially sectioned\u000ato reveal unremarkable adipose tissue with a ring measuring REMOVED_DATE cm in diameter\u000amade of metal present in the deep aspect of the specimen adjacent to the inked\u000aresection margin. The tissue in this area is composed of unremarkable adipose\u000atissue. Representative sections are submitted for histologic analysis.\u000aMicro 1: tissue around ring, 2 frags, ESS\u000aMicro 2: skin closest to ring, 2 frags, RSS\u000aMicro 3: additional skin and subcutaneous tissue, 2 frags, RSS\u000aPart two, labeled "#2. right breast tissue", consists of a single fragment of\u000abreast tissue that is received with two orienting sutures. A double long\u000asuture indicates lateral and a double short suture indicates superior. The\u000aspecimen is received with a wire in place. The specimen is inked by the\u000asurgeon per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior =\u000ablack; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow;\u000amedial = orange. The specimen measures REMOVED_DATE cm from medial to lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom anterior to posterior, and REMOVED_DATE cm from superior to inferior. Upon\u000asectioning the breast there is a firm area suspicious for calcifications\u000ameasuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm that is present adjacent to the inferior margin.\u000aThis correlates with the area designated on the radiograph. In addition a\u000asecond firm fibrous area suspicious for calcifications is present adjacent to\u000athe superior margin in the lateral aspect of the specimen. The first described\u000aarea is REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE \u000acm from the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000athe lateral margin. The second described area is present adjacent to the\u000asuperior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin, and\u000a2.7 cm from the medial margin. The specimen is serially sectioned and entirely\u000asubmitted for histologic analysis from medial to lateral.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  right breast tissue from medial to lateral, mult frags, ESS. The\u000afirst described lesion is primarily in cassettes REMOVED_DATE  and the\u000asecond described lesion is primarily in cassettes REMOVED_DATE \u000arp\u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
