VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID:REMOVED_CASE_ID Report Status: Signed\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aDIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. Skin of right breast, excision:\u000aDermal scar and foreign body giant cell reaction.\u000aB. Right breast, simple mastectomy:\u000aResidual ductal carcinoma in situ, intermediate grade, solid and\u000acribriform types, with associated microcalcifications, see note.\u000aNo residual invasive ductal carcinoma identified.\u000aChanges consistent with prior excisions.\u000aNOTE: No residual invasive ductal carcinoma is present. Residual solid and\u000acribriform type ductal carcinoma in situ is identified and appears as\u000amicroscopic foci within and around the prior excision site. The largest\u000aresidual focus is 1 cm. Microcalcifications are present. However, no\u000anecrosis is identified. The margins are clear of ductal carcinoma in situ\u000a(greater than or equal to REMOVED_DATE cm.).\u000aPlease refer to prior excision specimen (MS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, Massachusetts\u000aGeneral Hospital) for pathologic staging data.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by: Todd E. Abbott, M.D.\u000aClinical diagnosis & history:\u000aRight breast carcinoma\u000aTissue-Designation:\u000aA.Skin scar (NOS) - right breast\u000aB.Breast, simple mastectomy - right\u000aGross description:\u000aThe specimen is received in two containers.\u000aSpecimen A is received in formalin, labeled "right breast biopsy scar" and\u000aconsists of a single elliptical shaped fragment of skin and subcutaneous\u000atissue. The ellipse measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. and is excised to a depth of REMOVED_DATE \u000acm. The skin surface is remarkable for a centrally placed depressed, possibly\u000aulcerated lesion measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. Representative sections through the\u000amid point of the ellipse are submitted in cassettes REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. 2 agg.\u000aSpecimen B is received fresh, labeled "right breast" and consists of a 1,078\u000agram mastectomy with a stitch indicating the axillary tail. It measures 25 x\u000a20 x up to 5 cm. with a nipple and areola measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The nipple\u000ais not inverted. In the upper outer quadrant, REMOVED_DATE cm. from the nipple, there\u000ais a possible palpable abnormality measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. Sectioning\u000athrough the breast and upper outer quadrant reveals an area of parenchymal\u000afirmness and associated hemorrhagic corresponding to the palpable abnormality\u000aand measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x approximately REMOVED_DATE cm. The remainder of the breast\u000aparenchyma is remarkable for focal increased stringy fibrous tissue consistent\u000awith fibrocystic changes. 25 agg.\u000aSection code: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - nipple section\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - candidate area of fibrosis from upper outer quadrant\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - representative upper inner quadrant\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - representative lower outer quadrant\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - representative lower inner quadrant\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - prior biopsy site\u000aTotal fixation time is 12 hours.\u000aThere is a palpable abnormality in the upper outer quadrant approximately 4 to\u000a6 cm. from the nipple. Cut sections reveal an area of hemorrhage, fibrosis\u000aand fat necrosis measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. It is REMOVED_DATE cm. from the\u000aposterior margin.\u000aDictated by: TEA____(signature on file)____DENNIS J. FEEN, M.D. REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a____(signature on file)____ REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a[report_end]
