VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Li Chen, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Gilbert Brodsky, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aSPECIMEN DESIGNATED "LEFT BREAST, 12 O'CLOCK WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION\u000aFOR ARCHITECTURAL DISTORTION":\u000aFocal complex sclerosing lesion, at least 1 cm (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aAn immunoperoxidase study for cytokeratin REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and p63\u000ademonstrates the presence of myoepithelial cells in the lesion.\u000aApocrine metaplasia.\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia.\u000aNOTE: No malignancy is seen after complete microscopic examination of the\u000aspecimen, including the margins.\u000aThis case was also reviewed by Dr. Susan Lester, Breast Pathology Service, who\u000aconcurs.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 40-year-old female (premenopausal) with mammogram of L breast on\u000a6/19/07 showing architectural distortion at 12 o'clock demonstrating suspicious\u000aabnormality; not amenable to core bx.\u000aOperation: None given.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: None given.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) Left breast tissue stitch, short - superior, long - lateral, whip - deep\u000amargin.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Area in question in specimen - fibrosis, radial scar; R/O CA\u000aDG\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "#1. Left breast tissue with stitch deep margin suture, short superior,\u000along lateral", and consists of a focally disrupted irregular fragment of\u000ayellow/tan to pink/tan fibroadipose tissue (4.4 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which is\u000aoriented per surgeon as indicated. The superoposterior aspect of the specimen\u000ais focally ragged/disrupted. The specimen is inked by the surgeon per\u000apathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black;\u000aanterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/ orange.\u000aThere is one needle localization wire in placed entering the superolateral\u000aaspect of the specimen and exiting the posterior/deep aspect of the specimen.\u000aThe specimen was previously radiographed, and the radiograph shows areas of\u000adense breast tissue (without a discrete mass) and the localization wire. The\u000aspecimen is serially sectioned from anterior to posterior to exhibit\u000aapproximately 25% focally dense/vaguely nodular white/tan fibrous stroma and\u000a75% yellow/tan lobulated adipose tissue. There are focal areas of hemorrhage\u000asurrounding the needle localization wire. No discrete masses or lesions are\u000agrossly identified. The specimen is entirely sequentially submitted from\u000aanterior to posterior.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Anterior margin perpendicularly sectioned, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Central specimen, multi frags total, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Posterior/deep margin perpendicularly sectioned, multi frags in\u000aeach, ESS.\u000aLM/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-07-REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Gilbert Brodsky M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
