l aspects, and a whip\u000astitch orienting the chest wall resection margin. Accompanying the specimen is\u000aa radiograph, labeled with the patient's name and unit number, depicting a\u000afragment of soft tissue approximating the specimen with two needle localization\u000awires, a clip, and areas of multi-calcifications that are encircled by the\u000aradiologist. The specimen is serially sectioned from superior (slice 1) to\u000ainferior, there is a white, cylindrical, chalk-like lesion (0.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm), located in slice 5 from the superior margin, which is located REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000athe medial, REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior, REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000aposterior, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin. A\u000asurgical clip is identified by radiographing microcassettes and dissecting out\u000athe clip from block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID prior to processing, to allow for smooth cutting. The\u000aspecimen is entirely submitted from superior to inferior.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Superior margin, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Serial sections from superior to inferior, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Inferior aspect, 3 frags each, ESS.\u000aPab/ajb\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Alessandra F Nascimento M.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Alessandra F Nascimento M.D., Electronically signed on\u000a2/10/2005\u000a[report_end]
