d, yellow/red/tan\u000afibrofatty soft tissue cores (0.6 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate). The third\u000aorange cassette is labeled "B" and contains a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm aggregate of\u000ayellow/tan/red focally hemorrhagic fibrofatty soft tissue cores.\u000aMicro 1: white unlabeled cassette, mult frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 2: "A", multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 3: "B", multi frags, ESS.\u000aPart two, labeled "#2. right UOQ", and consists of two (2) yellow cassettes.\u000aOne cassette is labeled "A" with calcifications and contains multiple, soft,\u000afragmented, yellow to white tissue cores (2.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate).\u000aThe other cassette is labeled "B" and contains similar tissue fragments (1.7 x\u000a1.0 x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate).\u000aMicro 4: "A", multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 5: "B", multi frags, ESS.\u000adfi\u000aReports to: DENISON, CHRISTINE M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY(IES)\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY(IES)\u000a[report_end]
