DATE cm S-I x REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aA-P) with a short suture designating superior and a long suture designating\u000alateral. The needle localization wire is received in the same container as the\u000aspecimen however it is not within the specimen. The specimen is inked per\u000apathology protocol, the specimen is inked by the surgeon per pathology protocol\u000afor the evaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red;\u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. The specimen is received with a\u000aradiograph. The specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral to\u000aexhibit 90% dense white fibrous tissue to 10% yellow lobulated homogeneous\u000aunremarkable adipose tissue. There is an ill-defined hemorrhagic area (1.5 x\u000a1.0 x REMOVED_DATE cm) abutting the superior margin.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Perpendicular medial margin, multi frags in each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Body, sequentially submitted from medial to lateral to include\u000aarea of hemorrhage (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), 1 frag in each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Perpendicular lateral margin, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, labeled "posterior margin", consists of an unoriented fragment of\u000afibroadipose tissue (1.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) which is received with an accompanied\u000aradiograph. The specimen is inked and serially sectioned to exhibit 98% dense\u000awhite fibrous tissue to 2% yellow lobulated adipose tissue. No masses or\u000alesions are grossly appreciated.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Multi frags in each, ESS.\u000aJenC/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Xiaohua Qian M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on Friday\u000aREMOVED_MONTH 19, 2009 at 06:12:03PM\u000a[report_end]
