VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY(IES)\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aASTER, JON, CHRISTOPHER, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by ASTER,JON CHRISTOPHER,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST 14 G CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY:\u000aNECROTIZING LYMPHADENITIS\u000aSections show fragments of lymph node with follicular and\u000aintrafollicular hyperplasia and a single focus of acute\u000ainflammation and necrosis surrounded by histiocytes.\u000aSpecial stains for microorganisms (Gram stain, MSS,\u000aSteiner stains) are negative.\u000aNo mammary duct or lobules are identified.\u000aNOTE:\u000aThe findings are most consistent with infectious etiology.\u000aThe differential diagnosis includes Cat-Scratch disease; correlation\u000awith other clinical data is suggested.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 39 y.o. female with left breast complex mass via ultrasound.\u000aOperation: Left breast core biopsy.\u000aOperative findings: Heterogeneous solid mass.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: R/o carcinoma.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1 Left breast core biopsy specimen - u/s-guided 14g core\u000abiopsy (green cassette).\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by KUTOK,JEFFREY LORNE,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit\u000anumber, and "left breast", in a green cassette, and consists of multiple soft,\u000afragmented, yellow to white tissue cores (0.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm).\u000aMicro 1: Multi frag, ESS.\u000atr\u000aReports to: KAELIN, CAROLYN, MARY M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY(IES)\u000a[report_end]
