VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aDORFMAN, DAVID, MICHAEL, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by DORFMAN,DAVID MICHAEL,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST TISSUE, BIOPSY:\u000aSections reveal a REMOVED_DATE cm lymph node with follicular and\u000ainterfollicular hyperplasia, including a majority of small\u000around to irregular lymphocytes and scattered larger transformed\u000acells. "Monocytoid" change is also focally noted.\u000aScattered small collection of epithelioid histiocytes are noted\u000awithin germinal centers and in interfollicular areas.\u000aNo organisms are seen on Gram, silver (MSS) or on Steiner stains.\u000aImmunohistochemical study of paraffin embedded material for\u000atoxoplasma is negative.\u000aNOTE:\u000aThe findings are consistent with a benign reactive process with\u000asome features raising the possiblity of toxoplasmic lymphadenitis.\u000aClinical correlation is advised.\u000aDiagnostic features of involvement by a lymphoproliferative disorder\u000aare not seen.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 39 year old female with tender left breast upper outer quadrant mass,\u000aplus left axillary adenopathy. On REMOVED_DATE  the patient was noted to have a\u000a2.5 cm upper outer quadrant left breast density with irregular margins on\u000amammogram. Ultrasound revealed a 2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm solid irregular nodule.\u000aOn REMOVED_DATE  the patient underwent ultrasound-guided core biopsy that was\u000aconsistent with cat scratch disease. Mammogram and biopsy appeared to be\u000adiscordant, thus biopsy recommended.\u000aOperation: Left breast biopsy.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Left breast biopsy.\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "#1 LEFT BREAST TISSUE" (SMA):\u000a1.4 cm nodule - smear shows small lymphocytes.\u000aTissue taken for culture, snap freeze and B-5 fixation.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by GULIZIA,JAMES MARTIN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number\u000aand "left breast tissue", and consists of an oriented yellow/pink fibroadipose\u000asoft tissue fragment, 5 x 3 x REMOVED_DATE cm, containing a well-circumscribed REMOVED_DATE x\u000a1.2 x REMOVED_DATE cm nodule, which is soft in consistency, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior\u000amargin. Touch preps and smears are prepared. A portion is sent for\u000amicrobiologic cultures as requested by the surgeon. Representative tissue is\u000asnap frozen for potential marker studies, a portion is fixed in B-5, and a\u000aportion is fixed in formalin. The specimen is oriented with a short suture on\u000athe "superior" position and a long suture on the "lateral" position. The\u000aspecimen is inked black.\u000aMicro #1 : B-5 fixed tissue, RSS, multiple frags, 1 cassette.\u000aMicro #2 : additional representative formalin-fixed sections of nodule,\u000aRSS, 3 frags, 2 cassettes.\u000aReports to: KAELIN, CAROLYN, MARY M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
