VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Amend/Addenda\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: JULIE L JONES M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000a********** Addended Report ***********\u000aResident: Oname O. Burlingame, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Vania Nose, MD, PhD\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. RIGHT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR CALCIFICATIONS AND A CLIP:\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aSYNOPSIS:\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU Present\u000aTypes Solid, Cribriform\u000aNuclear grade Low to Intermediate\u000aCalcifications in DCIS Present\u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS Present\u000aMicroinvasion (<0.1cm) Absent\u000aExtent of DCIS Largest focus is REMOVED_DATE cm (1/15 blocks, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, best seen on\u000alevel 4)\u000aFinal Margins (DCIS)\u000aNegative (>0.3 cm) anterior, posterior, lateral, superior, inferior\u000aVery close (<0.1 cm) medial (see NOTE)\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU Absent\u000aOTHER FINDINGS: Atypical ductal hyperplasia, core biopsy site, columnar cell\u000achange with calcifications.\u000aAJCC CLASSIFICATION (6th edition): pTis pNX MX\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER/PR): Pending\u000aNOTE: The biopsy site and areas of atypical ductal hyperplasia are very close\u000a(<0.1 cm) from the anterior and posterior margins. Involvement of adjacent\u000atissue by DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU cannot be excluded.\u000aB. RIGHT BREAST, "ADDITIONAL INFERIOR" MARGIN:\u000aBreast tissue with no carcinoma seen.\u000aNOTE: The entire specimen was examined microscopically, including margins.\u000aThis case was reviewed by Dr. Susan Lester, Chief, Breast Pathology Service.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aClinical History: Right breast ADH on core needle biopsy for calcs.\u000aOperation: Right breast wire - localized excisional biopsy.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast atypical ductal hyperplasia on core biopsy.\u000aORGANS/TISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Right breast wire - localized excision - short stitch superior, long\u000astitch lateral.\u000aB/2. Right breast additional inferior tissue - short stitch anterior, long\u000astitch lateral.\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000aCalcifications, clip and wire in specimen - calcifications go near one edge of\u000aspecimen.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname, and unit number.\u000aPart A, "#1. RT breast wire localized excision short - superior, long -\u000alateral", consists of (3.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) lobulated fibroadipose tissue\u000afragments containing a short stitch denoting superior and a long stitch\u000adenoting lateral. A needle localization wire in place, and an accompanying\u000aradiograph. The needle localization wire enters the lateral aspect, extending\u000amedially with the hook exiting the middle of the medial aspect. The specimen\u000ais inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black;\u000aanterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange.\u000aThe radiograph is oriented by the ink and needle. The specimen is sectioned\u000afrom medial to lateral. There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm area of tan/red\u000ahemorrhage surrounding biopsy clip, which is REMOVED_DATE cm to the nearest deep margin,\u000a0.3 cm from the nearest anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the nearest superior\u000amargin and REMOVED_DATE cm to the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the nearest medial\u000amargin, and at least REMOVED_DATE cm from the nearest lateral margin. Approximately 60%\u000atan/white dense, focally hemorrhagic fibrous tissue admixed with approximately\u000a40% tan/yellow lobulated focally hemorrhagic fat. The entire specimen is\u000aserially sectioned and entirely sequentially submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, radial section, 5 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID through REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Specimen from lateral to medial, biopsy cavity/clip in\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 11 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin, radial sections, 5 frags total, ESS.\u000aPart B, "#2. RT breast additional inferior tissue - short anterior, long\u000alateral", consists of a (2.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) tan/yellow fibroadipose tissue\u000acontaining a short stitch denoting anterior and a long stitch denoting lateral.\u000aThe specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins:\u000aposterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow;\u000amedial/orange. The specimen is sectioned to reveal approximately 80% tan/white\u000adense fibrous tissue containing focal smooth-walled cyst averaging REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000aThis is admixed with approximately 20% tan/yellow lobulated focally hemorrhagic\u000afat. No lesions grossly consistent with invasive carcinoma are identified.\u000aSpecimen is entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Posterior margin, radial sections, 5 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Body from posterior to anterior, 6 frags total, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Anterior margin, radial sections, 5 frags total, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aoob/elw\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Vania Nose MD, PhD, Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM\u000aA. RIGHT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR CALCIFICATIONS AND A CLIP:\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for in-situ ductal carcinoma (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aESTROGEN RECEPTOR - POSITIVE\u000aPROGESTERONE RECEPTOR - POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/NEU (C-ERB-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) - POSITIVE (2+)\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000acarcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but only\u000aa portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in >10%\u000aof tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in\u000a>10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aAddendum #1 by Michael W Bennett M.B., B.C.H., Electronically signed on\u000a2/21/2007\u000a[report_end]
