s: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red;\u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange (inked by prosector). The cavity\u000ais maximally REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm, is exposed at the lateral aspect; radiating\u000afibrous tissue, extends to all additional margins, with exception of the\u000asuperior margin, which is within REMOVED_DATE cm. There are no gross abnormalities\u000anoted upon sectioning. Entire specimen is submitted, sequentially from\u000asuperior to inferior, with en face superior sections in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and perpendicular\u000ainferior aspect is REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Multi frags, ESS.\u000aDB/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Hejin P Hahn M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a3/15/2007\u000a[report_end]
