VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID:REMOVED_CASE_ID Report Status: Signed\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aDIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. Right breast, excision:\u000aRadial scar.\u000aFibrocystic changes.\u000aB. Left axillary sentinel lymph node:\u000aTwo lymph nodes, no metastatic tumor seen.\u000aC. Left breast, excision:\u000aWell differentiated infiltrating duct carcinoma (1.5 x REMOVED_DATE cm.).\u000aDuctal carcinoma in situ, cribriform type (grade REMOVED_DATE ).\u000aFibrocystic changes.\u000aD. Left breast final inferior margin, excision:\u000aFibrocystic changes (no tumor seen).\u000aE. Left breast (final shave), excision:\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia, focal (not at resection margin).\u000aRadial scar.\u000aF. Left breast (posterior margin), excision:\u000aFibroadipose tissue.\u000aNOTE: The inked resection margins are free of tumor in specimen C but the\u000aclosest margin is REMOVED_DATE cm. No vascular/lymphatic invasion is seen. The\u000aradial scar in specimen E has basal cells demonstrated on calponin\u000astain. The sentinel lymph node (B) is studied with three levels of H&E\u000aand three of pankeratin. The previous needle biopsies are reviewed\u000a(S-02-REMOVED_CASE_ID).\u000aImmunohistochemical studies performed on block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID reveal the following\u000aresults for the infiltrating carcinoma:\u000aEstrogen receptor: POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor: POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID): NEGATIVE for overexpression.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by: Richard J. Sampson, M.D.\u000aClinical diagnosis & history:\u000aLeft breast carcinoma; radial scar on right side\u000aTissue-Designation:\u000aA.Breast, excision with margins - right\u000aB.Sentinel lymph node - left axillary\u000aC.Breast, excision with margins - left\u000aD.Breast, excision with margins - left final inferior margin\u000aE.Breast, excision with margins - left final shave\u000aF.Breast, excision with margins - left posterior margin\u000aGross description:\u000aSpecimen A labeled "right breast biopsy" is received in formalin and consists\u000aof two fragments of tissue. The smaller is yellowish-grey 1 x 1 x REMOVED_DATE cm.; the\u000alarger, 2 x REMOVED_DATE x 1 cm. At the periphery, a small wire is attached. Each\u000aspecimen is inked with black ink. The small specimen is bisected and submitted\u000ain REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. The larger specimen with the wire is serially sectioned and\u000asubmitted in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. 8X.\u000aSpecimen B labeled "left axillary sentinel lymph node" is received in formalin\u000aand consists of a brownish lymph node with some surrounding yellow fat REMOVED_DATE x 1\u000ax REMOVED_DATE cm. The cut surface of the lymph node reveals a brown-tan cortex. The\u000acentral portion is yellowish-white. The specimen is serially sectioned and\u000asubmitted in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. 6X.\u000aSpecimen C labeled "left breast biopsy" is received in formalin and consists of\u000aan oval mass of yellowish-red adipose tissue 4 x 3 x REMOVED_DATE cm. There is a long\u000asuture designating the lateral margin and a short suture, the superior margin.\u000aA wire exits from the lateral edge. The margins are inked with black ink. The\u000acut surface reveals some greyish-white areas. No discrete masses are noted.\u000aThe entire specimen is embedded sectioned lateral to medial with the superior\u000aportion demonstrated by a notch. 9X all, labeled REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aSpecimen D labeled "left final inferior margin" is received in formalin and\u000aconsists of a fragment of yellow adipose tissue 3 x 1 x REMOVED_DATE cm. A suture\u000adesignates the furthest surface from the biopsy site. This is marked with\u000ablack ink. The entire specimen is submitted in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. 3X all.\u000aSpecimen E labeled "left final shave" is received in formalin and consists of\u000atwo fragments of tissue. The smaller is 1 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. and the larger, 2 x\u000a1 x REMOVED_DATE cm. Each is inked with black ink. There are no orienting suture\u000amarkings. 6X all, labeled REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aSpecimen F labeled "left posterior margin" is received in formalin and consists\u000aof a single, oval fragment of yellow adipose tissue REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The\u000amargins are inked. 3X all.\u000aDictated by: DJF____(signature on file)____DENNIS J. FEEN, M.D. REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a____(signature on file)____RICHARD SAMPSON, M.D. REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a[report_end]
