VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Amend/Addenda\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Skin biopsy (other than cyst, tag, debrid or repair\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: BETH ANN LESNIKOSKI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000a********** Addended Report ***********\u000aResident: Mariana A. Stoleru, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Susan Lester, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aLEFT BREAST SKIN, REMOVED_DATE CM PUNCH BIOPSY:\u000aINVASIVE POORLY DIFFERENTIATED CARCINOMA, is present predominantly as\u000adermal lymphvascular invasion.\u000aThe dermis is not ulcerated.\u000aNote: Immunoperoxidase studies will be performed and reported in an\u000aaddendum.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: L breast cancer, s/p lumpectomy 2005, now with recurrence diagnosed\u000aat South Shore Hospital. Now with 3 x 5 cm erythematous skin thickening.\u000aRadiation Rx: 2005\u000aChemotherapy: 2005\u000aHormonal Rx provided.\u000aOperation: L dermal punch biopsy.\u000aOperative Findings: None specified.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: L breast cancer; R/O skin involvement.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) L breast 4-mm dermal punch.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit\u000anumber, and "Breast dermal punch", and consists of a tan skin punch (0.4 cm in\u000adiameter x REMOVED_DATE cm in depth). A definitive lesion is not grossly identifiable.\u000aThe specimen is inked and bisected.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 2 frags, ESS.\u000aDFI/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000aTuesday REMOVED_MONTH 20, 2009 at 11:29:31AM\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM:\u000aSubsequently requested and received are the following pathology reports from\u000aSouth Shore Hospital:\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID; REMOVED_DATE  left breast, 4:00, ultrasound guided core needle biopsies\u000afor a REMOVED_DATE cm solid nodule - invasive ductal carcinoma, negative for ER, PR, and\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu ("FISH analysis confirms negative REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDneu stain"). The size of the\u000acarcinoma on the core is not provided.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - this report is not received. According to Dr. Lesnikoski, there\u000awas a REMOVED_DATE cm poorly differentiated invasive carcinoma, EIC positive with\u000anumerous foci of microinvasion, and isolated tumor cells in one of two sentinel\u000alymph nodes.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID; REMOVED_DATE  left breast excision and axillary node dissection - no\u000aresidual carcinoma present, possible isolated tumor cells in one of 13 lymph\u000anodes.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID; REMOVED_DATE  left breast stereotactic guided core needle biopsies for\u000acalcifications at previous excision site - invasive ductal carcinoma, DCIS, ER\u000anegative, PR 1 to 4%, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID 3+.\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for invasive carcinoma (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor NEGATIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor NEGATIVE (RARE CELLS POSITIVE (< 1%)\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) POSITIVE (3+)\u000aExternal controls are appropriately positive.\u000aNote: These results confirm the results reported by the outside hospital on the\u000amost recent left breast core needle biopsy (South Shore Hospital; REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aMethod for Hormone receptor analysis:\u000aEstrogen receptor, progesterone receptor, and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu were evaluated by manual\u000amorphometric analysis using the following criteria:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low > 0% - < 10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor cells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but only a\u000aportion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+):Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in >10% of\u000atumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+):Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in >30% of\u000atumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aExternal controls are evaluated and show appropriate Immunoreactivity.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aAddendum #1 by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on Tuesday\u000aREMOVED_MONTH 27, 2009 at 08:01:55PM\u000a[report_end]
