VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-06-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Briana Gleason, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Jeffrey F Krane, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. LEFT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A CLIP AND CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aColumnar cell change associated with calcifications.\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia.\u000aApocrine cysts associated with calcifications.\u000aFibroadenomatoid change.\u000aCalcifications in benign epithelium.\u000aCore biopsy site.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Abnormal left breast mammo, core bx: ALH and calcifications not\u000aassociated with ALH.\u000aOperation: Wire localized breast excision for a clip and calcifications.\u000aOperative Findings: Not provided.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: None given.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Left breast tissue - short stitch superior, long stitch lateral, whip\u000astitch - chest wall margin.\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000aClip and Ca++ in specimen. (C. Denison, M.D.)\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patients name, unit number,\u000aand "#1. Left breast tissue - short stitch - superior, long stitch lateral,\u000awhip chest wall margin", and consists of an ovoid fragment of yellow/tan to\u000atan/pink fibroadipose tissue (5.5 M-L x REMOVED_DATE S-I x REMOVED_DATE A-P cm), which is\u000aoriented per surgeon as indicated. The specimen was previously inked per\u000asurgeon per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black;\u000aanterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. A\u000aneedle localization wire is received separately within the specimen container.\u000aThe specimen 