VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: MEHRA GOLSHAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-06-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Michael H Roh, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Lucian R Chirieac, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "RIGHT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISIONAL BIOPSY":\u000aBenign breast tissue with sclerosing adenosis, fibroadenomatoid changes,\u000acalcifications in benign epithelium, apocrine metaplasia, columnar\u000acell changes, and duct ectasia.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000aB. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "LEFT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISIONAL BIOPSY":\u000aBenign breast tissue with sclerosing adenosis, fibroadenomatoid changes,\u000acalcifications in benign epithelium, apocrine metaplasia, columnar\u000acell changes, and duct ectasia.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000aC. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "LEFT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISIONAL BIOPSY":\u000aBenign breast tissue with sclerosing adenosis, and apocrine metaplasia.\u000aFibroadenoma.\u000aCore biopsy site.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Left breast abnormal mammogram calcifications, left breast abnormal\u000amammogram mass. Right breast abnormal mammogram calcifications. Sister with\u000apremenopausal breast cancer.\u000aOperation:\u000a1: Right breast wire localized excisional biopsy.\u000a2. Left breast wire localized excisional biopsy, calcifications.\u000a3. Left breast wire localized excisional biopsy, mass.\u000aClinical Diagnosis:\u000a1. Left breast abnormal mammogram, calcifications.\u000a2. Left breast abnormal mammogram, mass.\u000a3. Right breast abnormal mammogram, calcifications.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1: RT breast wire localized excisional biopsy, short-suture superior,\u000along-suture lateral.\u000aB/2: Left breast wire localized excisional biopsy, calcifications,\u000ashort-suture superior, long-suture lateral.\u000aC/3: Left breast wire localized excisional biopsy, mass, short-suture\u000asuperior, long-suture lateral - all to mammo.\u000aRADIOLOGY COMMENT:\u000aSpecimen "A":\u000aR calcs in specimen.\u000aDr. Babagbemi\u000aSpecimen "B":\u000aCalc in specimen.\u000aDr. Babagbemi\u000aSpecimen "C":\u000aNo clip seen. Mass seen by US.\u000aDr. Babagbemi\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in 3 parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart A, "#1 RT breast wire localized excisional biopsy, short-suture superior,\u000along-suture lateral", consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm excision of fibroadipose\u000atissue that is oriented by sutures designating the superior (short-suture) and\u000alateral (long-suture) margins. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol\u000afor the evaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red;\u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. A localizing wire enters the\u000asuperior aspect of the specimen and exits the inferior/anterior surface. The\u000aaccompanying radiograph demonstrates the localizing wire in place within the\u000aspecimen adjacent to a small focus of calcifications, toward the specimen's\u000amedial pole. Sectioning demonstrates irregular-appearing, dense, tan/white,\u000afibrous tissue with occasional dilated ducts containing a thick, yellow fluid\u000a(? DCIS). This irregular-appearing fibrous tissue comprises at least 85% of\u000athe specimen and is present at all margins. There are no obvious masses. The\u000aentire specimen is submitted, sequentially from medial to lateral (with area of\u000ainterest in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Entire specimen, sequentially from medial to lateral, multi\u000afrags, ESS.\u000aPart B, "#2 left breast wire localized excisional biopsy, short-suture\u000asuperior, long-suture lateral, calcifications", consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm excision of fibroadipose tissue that is oriented by sutures designating the\u000asuperior (short-suture) and lateral (long-suture) margins. The specimen is\u000ainked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black;\u000aanterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. A\u000alocalizing wire enters the superolateral surface of the specimen and traverses\u000amedially. The accompanying radiograph demonstrates the localizing wire in\u000aplace within the specimen adjacent to a small focus of calcifications centrally\u000awithin the specimen. Sectioning demonstrates tan/white fibrous tissue (at\u000aleast 95% of specimen) with focally dilated ducts filled with a (10% of the\u000aspecimen). Fibrous tissue abuts all margins. There are no obvious masses.\u000aThe entire specimen is submitted, sequentially from lateral to medial, with the\u000aarea of interest in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID through REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Entire specimen, sequentially from lateral to medial, multi\u000afrags, ESS.\u000aPart C, "#3 left breast wire localized excisional biopsy, mass, short-suture\u000asuperior, long-lateral", consists of a disrupted-appearing REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aexcision of fibroadipose tissue that is oriented by sutures designating the\u000asuperior (short-suture) and lateral (long-suture) margins. The specimen is\u000ainked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black;\u000aanterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. A\u000alocalizing wire enters the medial surface of the specimen and traverses\u000alaterally, and the accompanying radiograph demonstrates the localizing wire in\u000aplace within the specimen. The anterior surface of the specimen exhibits a\u000alarge, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm disruption (disrupted surfaces do not represent true\u000asurgical margin and therefore are not inked). Sectioning demonstrates\u000ahemorrhagic, dense, tan/white fibrous tissue, (at least 85% of specimen)\u000awithout definitive masses, lesions, or other abnormalities, grossly. The\u000aentire specimen is submitted, sequentially from inferior to superior.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Entire specimen, sequentially from inferior to superior, multi\u000afrags, ESS.\u000aDB/sj\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Lucian R Chirieac M.D., Electronically signed on\u000a7/17/2006\u000a[report_end]
