VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID SKIN- OTHER THAN CYST, TAG OR DEBRIDEMENT\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aODZE, ROBERT, DANIEL, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by ODZE,ROBERT DANIEL,M.D.\u000a1) RIGHT SUPERIOR BREAST, SCAR, EXCISION:\u000aSkin with scar.\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy.\u000a2) RIGHT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED BIOPSY FOR A MASS:\u000aFibrocystic change, proliferative.\u000aNo residual atypical lesion is identified.\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 43 year old female with two hypoechoic lesions right breast UIQ.\u000aS/P core biopsy revealing a papillary lesion with atypia for which excision is\u000arecommended.\u000aOperation: Right breast wl. biopsy x 2\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast mass x 2\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1) Right superior breast scar\u000a#2) Right breast wire loc x 2, partial mastectomy\u000aRADIOLOGY: 2 hypoechoic lesions in the specimen. E.P. Frost (no films)\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by LOMO,LESLEY C.,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart one, labeled "#1. right superior breast scar", consists of a white skin\u000aellipse (3.4 x REMOVED_DATE cm, excised to a depth of REMOVED_DATE cm), which contains a white,\u000alinear, well-healed scar (2.0 x REMOVED_DATE cm). The margin of the unoriented specimen\u000ais inked in black. The specimen is serially sectioned, revealing a cut\u000asubepidermal area of dense fibrosis subjacent to the scar. No lesions or\u000amasses are suggestive of malignancy. Representative sections are submitted.\u000aMicro 1: skin ellipse tips, 2 frags, ESS\u000aMicro 2: right superior breast scar, 3 frags, RSS\u000aPart two, labeled "#2. right breast wire loc x 2, partial mastectomy",\u000aconsists of a single right breast wire localized excisional biopsy specimen\u000a(5.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which contains one needle localization wire. The\u000aspecimen has been previously inked by the surgeon inked per pathology protocol\u000afor the evaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior =\u000ared; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. Also there are\u000amultiple sutures in place within the specimen. The specimen is serially\u000asectioned from lateral to medial, revealing that the sutures hold intact two\u000aseparate fragments of breast tissue, the interior of which contains what\u000aappears a biopsy cavity. The specimen is comprised predominantly of\u000aunremarkable white fibrous tissue (85%) and unremarkable yellow adipose tissue\u000a(15%). No masses of lesions suspicous for malignancy are grossly identified.\u000aNo films are received with the specimen. The specimen is entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  lateral perpendicular margin, mult frags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  right breast needle localized biopsy, 2 are full sized, ESS\u000aMicro 14: medial perpendicular margin, mult frags, ESS\u000alcl\u000aReports to: KAELIN, CAROLYN, MARY M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: SKIN- OTHER THAN CYST, TAG OR DEBRIDEMENT\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
