ositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but\u000aonly a portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity\u000ain >10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 43 year old post-menopausal female on HRT x REMOVED_DATE  years until now.\u000a#1) Positive 6:00 palpable lump REMOVED_DATE cm, left breast.\u000a#2) Second lesion 7:30-8:00, 6 mm left breast.\u000aOperation: #1) Biopsy with 11g U/S vacuum\u000a#2) Biopsy with 14g U/S\u000aClinical Diagnosis: R/O invasive carcinoma\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Left breast US core biopsy x 2\u000a#1) Yellow cassette\u000a#2) Brown cassette\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by BAI,HONGWEI,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin in two parts, each labeled with the\u000apatient's name and unit\u000anumber.\u000aPart one, labeled "left breast #1", in a yellow cassette, and consists of\u000amultiple, soft, fragmented, yellow to white tissue cores (2.3 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in\u000aaggregate).\u000aMicro 1: Multi frags, ESS.\u000aPart two, labeled "left breast #2", in a tan cassette, and consists of\u000amultiple, soft, fragmented, yellow to white tissue cores (1.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in\u000aaggregate).\u000aMicro 2: Multi frags, ESS.\u000adfi\u000aReports to: LEUNG, JESSICA, WAI M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY(IES)\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY(IES)\u000a[report_end]
