VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST MASTECTOMY W/REGIONAL LYMPH NODES\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aGLICKMAN, JONATHAN, NEIL, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by GLICKMAN,JONATHAN NEIL,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST, MASTECTOMY (specimen #1 of 4 specimens), SENTINEL NODE BIOPSY, AND\u000aAXILLARY NODE DISSECTION (specimens REMOVED_DATE of 4 specimens):\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA, MULTIPLE FOCI\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aNEGATIVE LYMPH NODES\u000aSYNOPSIS:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA - present as a main mass (2.5 cm) and\u000athree (3) satellite nodules (0.9 cm,\u000a0.8 cm, and REMOVED_DATE cm)\u000aMultifocal - yes\u000aHistologic Type - mixed ductal and lobular\u000aHistologic Grade (SBR) - II (moderate)\u000aNuclear Grade - intermediate\u000aEIC - negative\u000aLymphovascular invasion - absent\u000aDermal lymphatic invasion - absent\u000aSkin invasion - absent\u000aSkeletal muscle invasion - absent\u000aFinal Margins (invasive) -\u000aClose (tumor <0.1 cm from margin) deep (one (1) satellite nodule, focal)\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aTypes - solid, cribriform\u000aNuclear grade - intermediate\u000aCalcifications in DCIS - absent\u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - present\u000aExtent of DCIS\u000aNumber of blocks:total - 7:11 blocks\u000aFinal Margins (DCIS)\u000aClose (0.1-0.3 cm) - deep (blocks #4 & 6)\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - absent\u000aLYMPH NODES\u000aSentinel Lymph Nodes - negative (3 H&E levels examined)\u000aNumber of positive nodes - 0\u000aNumber of nodes examined - 4\u000aAxillary Lymph Nodes - negative\u000aNumber of positive nodes - 0\u000aNumber of nodes examined - 9\u000aTOTAL POSITIVE NODES (sentinel + axillary)- 0:13\u000aOTHER FINDINGS\u000aCysts\u000aApocrine metaplasia\u000aSkeletal muscle\u000aAJCC CLASSIFICATION - REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID pREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID MX\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER/PR/HER-2) - performed previously\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 43 year old female with left breast cancer.\u000aOperation: Left modified radical mastectomy, tram flap reconstruction\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast cancer\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1) Left breast (long lateral axillary tail, short superior\u000askin margin)\u000a#2) Sentinel nodes\u000a#3) Axillary contents\u000a#4) Non-sentinel node\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "#4. NON-SENTINEL NODE", (FSA):\u000aNegative for tumor.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by JEDLICKA,PAVEL J.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in four parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart one, labeled "#1. left breast", consists of a 284g simple mastectomy\u000aspecimen, composed of breast (17.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) and attached skin ellipse\u000a(3.7 x REMOVED_DATE cm) with a REMOVED_DATE cm nipple. A long suture is present in the\u000alateral-most breast tissue and a short suture in the superior aspect of the\u000askin ellipse. No scar is grossly evident. The deep surface is defined by\u000afascia and scant attached skeletal muscle, and it is inked black. Sectioning\u000areveals a centrally located hard, ovoid, tan tumor mass measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x\u000a2.1 cm and located REMOVED_DATE cm from the nearest deep margin. Three additional\u000aseparate, hard nodules are present nearby the main tumor mass. One nodule\u000ameasures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm, and is located REMOVED_DATE cm inferolateral to the main\u000atumor mass and REMOVED_DATE cm from the nearest deep margin. One nodule measures REMOVED_DATE x\u000a0.7 x REMOVED_DATE cm and is located REMOVED_DATE cm inferior to the main tumor mass and REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom the nearest deep margin. One measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm, and is located\u000a0.6 cm inferomedial to the main tumor mass and REMOVED_DATE cm from the nearest deep\u000amargin. The remaining breast parenchyma consists of appoximately 50% tan,\u000arubbery fibrous tissue and 50% yellow lobulated adipose tissue with no\u000aadditional lesions. Representative tissue from the main tumor mass is\u000asubmitted to the tumor bank for special studies.\u000aMicro 1: main tumor mass and nearest deep margin, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  additional main tumor mass, 2 frags, RSS\u000aMicro 4: inferolateral nodule and nearest deep margin, 2 frags, RSS\u000aMicro 5: inferior nodule and nearest deep margin, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 6: inferomedial nodule and nearest deep margin, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 7: UOQ, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 8: LOQ, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 9: LIQ, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 10: UIQ, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 11: skin and nipple, 1 frag, RSS\u000aPart two, labeled "#2. sentinel node #1", consists of a single fragment of\u000ayellow/pink/tan soft tissue (3.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). Four candidate lymph nodes\u000aare identified, measuring up to REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000aMicro 12: 4 candidate lymph nodes, 4 frags, ESS\u000aPart three, labeled "#3. axillary contents", consists of a single fragment of\u000ayellow/tan soft tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. Four candidate lymph\u000anodes are identified, measuring up to REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000aMicro 13: 4 candidate lymph nodes, 3 frags, ESS\u000aMicro 14: remainder of specimen, mult frags, ESS\u000aPart four, labeled "#4. non-sentinel node", consists of a single fragment of\u000ayellow/pink/tan soft tissue (4.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) containing a single candidate\u000alymph node measuring REMOVED_DATE cm. One-half of the candidate lymph node is submitted\u000aas FSA.\u000aMicro 15: FSA remnant, 1 frag, ESS\u000aMicro 16: non-frozen candidate lymph node fragment, 1 frag, ESS\u000aMicro 17: remainder of specimen, 1 frag, ESS\u000apj\u000aReports to: LESNIKOSKI, BETH-ANN M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY W/REGIONAL LYMPH NODES\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SENTINEL LYMPH NODE\u000a[report_end]
