ted. Note: The two invasive carcinomas display slightly different characteristics. Diagnosis by: Frederick Carl Koerner, M.D. Signed On: 18 MAY 03 at 07:41 =============================================================================== *** IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum *** RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast (left) blocks F and N: The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein. The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein. The tumor cells show moderate (2+) overexpression of HER-2/c-erbB-2. See note. Note: These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital. They have not been cleared or approved by the U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA). The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary; this laboratory has established and verified the test's accuracy and precision. Added by: Grace T. McKee,MD Signed On: 21 MAY 03 at 12:59 ** REVISED REMOVED_DATE  ** *** HER-2 Addendum *** RESULTS OF FLUORESCENCE IN SITU HYBRIDIZATION (FISH) FOR HER-2/NEU GENE AMPLIFICATION Breast (Left, block F): HER-2/neu gene in tumor cells: REMOVED_DATE (Amplified). See note. Note: Results are expressed as the average ratio of HER-2 to chromosome 17 signals in 60 tumor cell nuclei. A ratio of greater than REMOVED_DATE or equal to REMOVED_DATE indicates REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu gene amplification adjusted for chromosome 17 polysomy using PathVysion by Vysis. Added by: Grace T. McKee,MD Signed On: 27 MAY 03 at 08:43 GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "right breast mass" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm irregular firm to rubbery tan-yellow to pink lobulated portion of unoriented fibroadipose tissue which is inked black. The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm well-circumscribed, firm to rubbery tan-yellow to white homogeneous nodule which abuts the black inked margin. The specimen is entirely submitted in cassettes A-B, with the nodule in cassette B. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "excision left breast with 2 localization wires" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm irregular portion of tan-yellow to pink lobulated fibroadipose tissue with a short stitch designating the superior aspect and a long stitch designating the lateral. There are 2 localization wires in place. The most superior localization wire is designated wire #1 and the inferior localization wire is designated wire #2. The posterior aspect is inked black, the anterior blue, the lateral green and the medial yellow. The specimen is sequentially submitted from superior to inferior to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm well-circumscribed, firm gritty tan-white mass located at tip of localization wire #1. The mass comes to within REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior, lateral aspects, REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior, REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior and REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior aspect. The remaining uninvolved parenchyma is tan-pink to yellow, lobulated unremarkable fibroadipose tissue with no additional discrete masses or lesions identified. Representative sections are submitted in cassettes C-L with the area denoted by localization wire #1 (containing the entire mass) in cassettes C-F, the area denoted by needle localization wire #2 in cassettes G-I, and uninvolved parenchyma in cassettes J-L. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "12 o'clock nodule" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm irregular portion of unoriented tan-yellow to pink lobulated portion of fibrofatty tissue. The unoriented specimen is inked black, serially sectioned to reveal a oval, well-circumscribed firm tan-white mass measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm coming to within 