d fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "left breast" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm left modified radical mastectomy with a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm axillary tail. The anterior is inked blue, the posterior is inked black. The overlying REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm tan-pink skin has a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm unremarkable nipple-areola complex. A REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm, firm to rubbery, tan-white mass is REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin and is REMOVED_DATE cm from anterior margin. The mass is surrounded by fibrosis and yellow areas of fat necrosis. The remaining parenchyma contains ill-defined scattered areas of fibrosis with cysts. Multiple lymph nodes are identified in the axillary tissue ranging from REMOVED_DATE cm to REMOVED_DATE cm. Representative sections are submitted as follows: K-M: Entire mass. N-P: Breast parenchyma away from mass (medial to lateral). Q-S: Bisected lymph nodes, one in each cassette. T: 4 possible whole lymph nodes. U: 3 whole lymph nodes. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "additional axillary tissue" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm fragment of adipose tissue. No lymph nodes are grossly identified. The entire specimen is submitted in cassettes V-X. Resident: RANIA M. SELIEM, MD *** INTRA-OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS *** GROSS DIAGNOSIS #1: BREAST (RIGHT), SIMPLE MASTECTOMY: NO CARCINOMA GROSSLY IDENTIFIED. O.R. Diagnosis by: Andrew Eric Rosenberg, M.D. =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: MGH-INPATIENT (FLR.UNKNOWN) REPORTS TO: Barbara Lynn Smith, M.D. PART A: BREAST (RIGHT), PART B: BREAST(LEFT),MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY PART C: LYMPH NODE(LEFT AXILLA,ADDITIONAL),EXCISION
