VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-06-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Justine A Barletta, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Alessandra F Nascimento, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZATION FOR A MASS:\u000aFibroadenoma (0.8 cm).\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 29 year old woman with L breast mass. REMOVED_DATE /06 L breast core bx\u000afragments of fibroadenoma. REMOVED_DATE  L breast U/S oval REMOVED_DATE cm mass\u000apresent as ? known fibroadenoma\u000aOperation: Left breast wire directed excisional biopsy\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast mass.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Left breast tissue short suture superior, long suture lateral, whip\u000astitch on deep margin\u000aRADIOLOGY: Mass ultra-sounded and is present with hookwire in specimen.\u000aCalled to OR by HP @ 10:59 am\u000aNo radiologist's signature on form.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in one part, in a container labeled with the\u000apatients name, unit number, and left breast tissue, short suture superior\u000along suture lateral, whip stitch on deep margin for mammo, and consists of an\u000aoriented, wire-localized breast excision specimen (2.5 cm medial to lateral,\u000a2.2 cm superior to inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm anterior to posterior) with three sutures\u000adesignated by the surgeon as follows: short=superior, long=lateral, whip\u000astitch=deep margin. A localization wire runs through the whip stitch; however,\u000ait does not enter the specimen. The specimen is inked according to the\u000apathology protocol to aid in evaluation of margins: superior/red,\u000ainferior/green, anterior/blue, posterior/black, medial/orange, lateral/yellow.\u000aSectioning reveals a well-demarcated, nodular, white mass (0.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm)\u000athat extends to the medial, superior, inferior, anterior, and posterior\u000amargins, and is located REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin. The remainder of the\u000abreast parenchyma is composed of 80% fibrous tissue and 20% adipose tissue.\u000aThe entire specimen is submitted. A radiograph accompanies the specimen\u000ademonstrating a localization wire within the specimen as well as a ill defined\u000adensity.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Perpendicular sections of medial margins, 5 frags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Central portion of specimen (serially submitted from medial to\u000aLateral), 6 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Perpendicular sections of lateral margin, 6 frags, ESS.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Alessandra F Nascimento M.D., Electronically signed on\u000a3/14/2006\u000a[report_end]
