VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID SENTINEL LYMPH NODE\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aBROWN, FELIX, MARCEL, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by BROWN,FELIX MARCEL,M.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZATION FOR A MASS (#3 OF 4 SPECIMENS) AND SENTINEL NODE\u000aBIOPSIES (#1 [including FSA] AND #2 [including FSB] OF 4 SPECIMENS):\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA, DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, AND NEGATIVE LYMPH NODES.\u000aSYNOPSIS:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA\u000aSize - REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aMultifocal? - No\u000aHistologic Type - Mixed ductal and lobular\u000aHistologic Grade (SBR) - II (Moderate)\u000aNuclear Grade - Intermediate\u000aEIC - Negative\u000aLymphovascular invasion - Present\u000aDermal lymphatic invasion - N/A\u000aSkin invasion - N/A\u000aSkeletal muscle invasion - N/A\u000aFinal Margins (invasive) -\u000aNegative (no ink on tumor) - Anterior, superior, inferior, medial, and\u000alateral.\u000aClose (tumor <0.1 cm from margin) - Posterior (broad front, block 11)\u000aPositive (ink on tumor) - Posterior (focal, block 11)\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aTypes - Solid\u000aNuclear grade - Intermediate\u000aCalcifications in DCIS - Absent\u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - Absent\u000aExtent of DCIS\u000aNumber of blocks/total: - REMOVED_DATE blocks.\u000aFinal Margins (DCIS)\u000aNegative (>0.3 cm): - Anterior, superior, inferior, medial\u000aand lateral.\u000aClose (<0.1 cm): - Posterior, focal (block 11).\u000aPositive (ink on DCIS): - Posterior, focal (block 12).\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - Absent.\u000aLYMPH NODES:\u000aSentinel lymph nodes (3 H&E levels examined): Negative\u000aNumber of positive nodes: - 0\u000aNumber of nodes examined: - 3\u000aTOTAL POSITIVE NODES (sentinel + axillary) - REMOVED_DATE \u000aOTHER FINDINGS: Cysts, calcifications in benign epithelium, and core biopsy\u000asite.\u000aAJCC CLASSIFICATION - REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDc pREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID MX\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER/PR/HER-2) - Performed previously.\u000aLEFT BREAST, DEEP/INFERIOR SHAVE MARGIN (#4 OF 4 SPECIMENS):\u000aBreast tissue and skeletal muscle with no tumor seen.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Core biopsy positive for left breast UOQ cancer\u000aOperation: Left sentinel node mapping and left wire-loc. PM\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Cancer left breast\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1) Left axillary "hot" sentinel node >140\u000a2) Left axillary "hottest" sentinel node >200\u000a3) Left breast needle-localization/partial mastectomy (for mammo)\u000a4) Left breast deep/inferior shave margin (stitch on margin)\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000aMass in specimen.\u000aS.D. (full signature illegible)\u000a(NOTE: Specimen received from mammo 11:30 a.m. in frozen room (no patient\u000alabel on container) - AJI)\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "1) LEFT AXILLARY "HOT" SENTINEL NODE" (FSA):\u000aNegative for tumor.\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "2) LEFT AXILLARY "HOTTEST" NODE >200" (FSB):\u000aNegative for tumor.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by LOMO,LESLEY C.,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in four parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart one, "1) left axillary "hot" sentinel node", consists of a single fragment\u000aof yellow/tan/pink soft tissue (4.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with two (2) lymph nodes\u000a(1.4 cm and REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest dimensions). The smaller lymph node is inked in\u000ablack, and one-half of each fragment is submitted as FSA. The lymph nodes are\u000aentirely submitted.\u000aMicro 1: FSAR, 2 frag, ESS\u000aMicro 2: non-FSR, 2 frag, ESS\u000aPart two, "2) left axillary "hottest" node >200", consists of a single fragment\u000aof yellow/tan/pink soft tissue (3.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) in which one (1) lymph node\u000ais identified (1.7 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). One-half of the lymph node is submitted as\u000aFSB, and the entire lymph node is submitted.\u000aMicro 3: FSBR, 1 frag, ESS\u000aMicro 4: non-FSR, 1 frag, ESS\u000aPart three (which was received from mammography at 11:30 a.m. with no patient\u000alabel on the container but was accompanied by a pink sheet bearing the\u000apatient's name and unit number) consists of a single fragment of fibrofatty\u000abreast tissue (4.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) which bears a needle-localization wire and\u000ahas been previously inked by the surgeon per pathology protocol for the\u000aevaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red;\u000ainferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. An accompanying\u000aradiograph shows the specimen with a needle-localization wire at the site of a\u000aradiopaque irregular mass. The specimen is serially sectioned from superior\u000ato inferior revealing a white, firm, irregular mass (1.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) which\u000aabuts the lateral, anterior, and posterior margins; it is present REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000athe superior, REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margins.\u000aNo other masses or lesions suspicious for malignancy are grossly identified.\u000aThe entire specimen is submitted sequentially from superior to inferior; the\u000amass is submitted in blocks REMOVED_DATE \u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  superior perpendicular margin, multi frag, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  breast biopsy from superior to inferior, 1 frag, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  inferior perpendicular margin, 2 or 3 frag, ESS\u000aPart four, "4) left breast, deep/inferior shave margin", consists of a single\u000afragment of yellow/tan fibrofatty breast tissue (3.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) which\u000acontains a suture designating the new margin. The area designated by the\u000asuture is inked in black, and the side opposite is inked in blue. The specimen\u000ais serially sectioned to reveal a small, firm area (0.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) which\u000aabuts the edge inked in blue (old margin) and is present REMOVED_DATE cm from the new\u000amargin (inked black). The remainder of the specimen is comprised of\u000aunremarkable fibrofatty breast tissue. The specimen is entirely submitted.\u000aMicro 17: shave margin to include nodule, 2 frag, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  remainder of specimen, 3 frag, ESS\u000alcl\u000aReports to: KAELIN, CAROLYN, MARY M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: SENTINEL LYMPH NODE\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SENTINEL LYMPH NODE\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN\u000a[report_end]
