fied\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU (DCIS): present\u000aType: solid and cribriform types\u000aGrade: 2\u000aExtent: focal\u000aSize (greatest dimension): microscopic foci within and around the\u000ainvasive tumor\u000aExtensive intraductal component: absent\u000aNecrosis: none identified\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU: none identified\u000aMICROCALCIFICATIONS: present in benign tissue\u000aRESECTION MARGINS:\u000aInvasive Carcinoma: The main tumor is clear of the margins\u000a(greater than or equal to REMOVED_DATE cm.)\u000aOne of the microscopic foci of invasive\u000acarcinoma is close (less than REMOVED_DATE cm.),\u000ato the posterior margin\u000aDCIS: clear (greater than or equal to REMOVED_DATE cm.)\u000aIMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING (invasive carcinoma):\u000aPrior specimen REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID reported as:\u000aEstrogen receptor: POSITIVE (>10% of nuclei stained)\u000aProgesterone receptor: POSITIVE (>10% of nuclei stained)\u000aPerformed on block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID reveals the following results:\u000aEstrogen receptor: POSITIVE (>10% of nuclei stained)\u000aProgesterone receptor: POSITIVE (>10% of nuclei stained)\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID): NEGATIVE (0) (no membrane staining)\u000aTotal Fixation Time: 11 hours\u000aLYMPH NODES:\u000aOne node sampled is negative for tumor (0/1); (0/1 sentinel nodes)\u000aNumber of nodes with isolated tumor cells (less than or equal to REMOVED_DATE cm.): 1\u000aThe sentinel lymph node, specimen A, is examined at multiple levels with\u000aH & E stains and immunohistochemical stains for cytokeratin REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/3.\u000aADDITIONAL PATHOLOGIC FINDINGS:\u000aFibrocystic changes with associated microcalcifications.\u000aChanges consistent with prior biopsy site.\u000aPRIOR RELATED SPECIMENS REVIEWED:\u000aLeft breast; REMOVED_DATE  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aRight breast; REMOVED_DATE  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aFinal Diagnosis by: Todd E. Abbott, M.D.\u000aINTRA-OPERATIVE CONSULTATION:\u000aOPERATING ROOM CONSULTATION (TOUCH PREPARATION):\u000aLeft sentinel lymph node:\u000aNo evidence of carcinoma.\u000aTEA\u000aClinical diagnosis & history:\u000aLeft breast carcinoma\u000aTissue-Designation:\u000aA.Sentinel lymph node - left\u000aB.Breast, excision with margins - left\u000aGross description:\u000aThe specimen is received in two containers.\u000aSpecimen A is received fresh from the Operating Room, labeled "left sentinel\u000alymph node" and consists of a fragment of adipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x\u000a1.0 cm. containing a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. lymph node. A touch preparation is\u000aperformed. The lymph node tissue is submitted in cassette REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. The remaining\u000aadipose tissue is submitted in cassette REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. 2 agg. all.\u000aSpecimen B is received fresh, labeled "left breast lump" and consists of an 80\u000agram, 7 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. lumpectomy specimen with the following orienting marks;\u000ashort, superficial; long, lateral; wire exits anterior. The superior and\u000aanterior surfaces of the specimen are disrupted making inking difficult. The\u000aspecimen is inked as follows with the superficial suture assumed to be\u000asuperior: superior, blue; anterior, black; inferior, green; posterior, orange.\u000aThe specimen is sectioned revealing a palpable and visible abnormality in the\u000amiddle of the lump near the posterior margin. The palpable abnormality\u000ameasures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. and is grossly REMOVED_DATE cm. from the posterior margin\u000anear its intersection with the superior margin. Cut sections of the remaining\u000abreast parenchyma reveal no abnormality. 25 agg.\u000aSection code: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - tumor\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - lateral margin\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - middle specimen\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - medial margin\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - additional middle third\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - additional medial third\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - additional lateral third\u000aTotal fixation time for REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID is 11 hours.\u000aTotal fixation time for REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID is ________\u000aDictated by: TEA____(signature on file)____DENNIS J. FEEN, M.D. REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a____(signature on file)____ REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a[report_end]
