VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID:REMOVED_CASE_ID Report Status: Signed\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aADDENDUM REPORT\u000aAddendum #1 Entered: REMOVED_DATE -0932\u005cE\u000aE\u005c\u000a*** ADDITIONAL DIAGNOSTIC INFORMATION ***\u000aThis report contains an addendum to the original for the purpose of providing\u000aadditional diagnostic information. The original diagnosis is unchanged.\u000aSlides from both excisions in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and from the previous biopsy (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID)\u000awere reviewed by Dr. Frederick C. Koerner of the Massachusetts General Hospital\u000awho agreed with our interpretation in all areas. His full comments are as\u000afollows:\u000a"The sections of the core biopsy specimen from the right breast disclose a\u000afocus of low grade ductal carcinoma in situ harboring calcifications. The\u000aexcision specimen from the same breast contains more of the carcinoma in situ\u000ain the region of the biopsy site. The focus in question at the edge of block\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID displays a slight proliferation of ductal-type epithelial cells. Although\u000athe cells along the basement membranes of the affected acini appear larger than\u000athe usual hyperplastic ductal cells, these proliferative cells do not display\u000athe morphological characteristics of the carcinoma cells. Furthermore, the\u000acentrally situated cells in this focus appear smaller and more compact that the\u000aperipheral ones. This finding reflects the phenomenon of maturation and\u000athereby suggests a benign nature for the population. I would classify this\u000apopulation as immature ductal hyperplasia. The excision of the biopsy site in\u000athe left breast exhibits a few foci of ductal epithelial proliferation.\u000aAlthough certain of them such as those on slides REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID represent immature\u000aductal hyperplasia, I would regard a few cells near the mark on slide REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID as\u000aatypical."\u000aAddeundum Signed Electronically Signed SAMPSON,RICHARD J. M.D. REMOVED_DATE \u000aDIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. Right breast, excision:\u000aDuctal carcinoma in situ, cribriform, grade REMOVED_DATE in two foci.\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia.\u000aB. Left breast, excision:\u000aExcision site.\u000aExtensive atypical ductal hyperplasia and flat epithelial atypia.\u000aNo residual infiltrating carcinoma or ductal carcinoma in situ present.\u000aSYNOPTIC REPORT - DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU - specimen A\u000aAJCC pTNM CLASSIFICATION (6TH Ed.)(Based on available surgical material:\u000apTis pREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID pMX\u000aHISTOLOGIC TYPE: cribriform\u000aTUMOR SITE(S): right\u000aHISTOLOGIC GRADE (Nuclear): low (grade 1\u000aTUMOR SIZE (greatest dimension): multifocal, spanning 2 cm. (largest\u000afocus REMOVED_DATE cm.)\u000aNECROSIS: absent\u000aMICROCALCIFICATIONS: present within DCIS; present within DCIS\u000aand benign tissue\u000aRESECTION MARGINS: clear (> REMOVED_DATE cm.)\u000aIMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING (for the DCIS):\u000aPrior specimen REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID reported as:\u000aEstrogen receptor: POSITIVE (>10% of nuclei stained)\u000aOTHER FINDINGS:\u000aExtensive atypical ductal hyperplasia associated with ductal carcinoma in\u000asitu and close to margins.\u000aChanges consistent with prior biopsy.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by: Richard J. Sampson, M.D.\u000aClinical diagnosis & history:\u000aDuctal carcinoma in situ of right breast, infiltrating ductal carcinoma of left\u000abreast with positive margins\u000aTissue-Designation:\u000aA.Breast, excision with margins - right\u000aB.Breast, excision with margins - left\u000aGross description:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in two containers.\u000aSpecimen A labeled "right breast, long lateral, short superior" consists of a\u000apiece of breast tissue weighing 42 grams and measuring 5 x 4 x 3 cm. with a\u000awire marker coming from the lateral portion of the specimen and two orienting\u000asutures. One long suture is designated lateral and a short suture is\u000adesignated superior. Using this orientation, the deep margin is inked with\u000ablack; the superficial superior margin is inked with green; the superficial\u000ainferior margin is inked with blue. Multiple cut sections through the specimen\u000ashows a REMOVED_DATE cm. lesion present near the inferior margin. 17X all, labeled\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aSpecimen B labeled "left breast" consists of a piece of breast tissue\u000aweighing 152 grams and measuring 8 x 7 x 4 cm. There is an ellipse of skin\u000apresent, 5 x REMOVED_DATE cm. Two orienting sutures are present; a long suture\u000adesignates lateral and two short sutures designate superior. Using this\u000aorientation, the deep margin is inked with black; the superficial superior\u000amargin is inked with green; the superficial inferior margin is inked with\u000ablue. Sections are taken from lateral to medial revealing a biopsy cavity\u000aapproximately 2 x 2 x 2 cm. which is surrounded yellowish fat necrosis.\u000aMultiple sections are taken. 21X, labeled REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aTotal fixation time is greater than 48 hours.\u000aDictated by: LV/RJS____(signature on file)____ REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a____(signature on file)____RICHARD SAMPSON, M.D. REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a[report_end]
