VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Consult material\u000aProcedure Date:\u000aOrdering Provider: JAY HARRIS M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Rachel L Rucker-Schmidt, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Jane E. Brock, M.B., B.S., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aCONSULT SLIDES FROM FAULKNER HOSPITAL, BOSTON, MA:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, MASTECTOMY (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID; REMOVED_DATE ):\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, solid and cribriform types with apocrine features,\u000acalcifications and necrosis (intermediate to high nuclear grade) is present in\u000aone (1) of one (1) block, reviewed. By report DCIS is present in one (1) of\u000aseventy-two (72) blocks, and located in the upper outer quadrant (see NOTE).\u000aNo lymphovascular invasion is present.\u000aBy report, no residual invasive carcinoma is present.\u000aThe deep margin is negative for carcinoma.\u000aBy report, prior biopsy site changes are present in the upper inner quadrant\u000a(correlate of prior benign biopsy, see REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aSpecial studies were performed at an outside institution with the following\u000aresults for DCIS (reviewed):\u000aESTROGEN RECEPTOR POSITIVE\u000aPROGESTERONE RECEPTOR POSITIVE-LOW\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/NEU POSITIVE (3+)\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID POSITIVE (rare cells)\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID NEGATIVE\u000aBRST-2 NEGATIVE\u000aNOTE: The patient presented with a right axillary mass which was found to be ER\u000apositive-low, PR positive-low metastatic carcinoma involving a lymph node (6 cm\u000aby report; see REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID). An area of right breast upper inner quadrant\u000aenhancement on MRI was biopsied and reported benign (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), and a right\u000abreast primary invasive carcinoma site was not located before chemotherapy was\u000ainitiated. By report, extensive sampling of the post chemotherapy mastectomy\u000aspecimen (> 70 blocks) has not revealed either a tumor bed, or invasive\u000acarcinoma present in the specimen. A Miller-Payne Score or RCB score cannot be\u000aassigned in this case. No additional lymph nodes were identified in the\u000amastectomy specimen.\u000aThis case could be classified as: AJCC Classification (6th edition): ypTis.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Right inflammatory carcinoma right breast\u000aClinical Diagnosis: DCIS\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aConsult slides.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aReceived from Faulkner Hospital, Pathology Department, 1153 Centre Street,\u000aBoston, MA REMOVED_CASE_ID, are seven (7) glass slides.\u000aThe slides are labeled "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" and sublabeled "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID (1)", "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID ER", "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID PR",\u000a"REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/NEU", "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID", "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" and "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BRST-20", corresponding to a right\u000abreast total mastectomy (22.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) performed on REMOVED_DATE  according\u000ato the accompanying pathology report bearing the patient's name.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jane E. Brock M.B., B.S., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a4/22/2008\u000a[report_end]
