VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: JULIE L JONES M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-06-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Eleanor Y. Chen, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Alessandra F Nascimento, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "LEFT BREAST MASS":\u000aPHYLLODES TUMOR, low grade (0.7 cm in greatest dimension).\u000aMitoses number <1 per 10 HPF.\u000aNo necrosis is identified.\u000aTumor is <0.1 cm from the inked resection margin.\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "RIGHT BREAST MASS":\u000aFibroadenoma (1.2 cm).\u000aCalcifications associated with benign epithelium.\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy.\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "RIGHT BREAST CLIP":\u000aGross examination only.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Right breast mass S/P core demonstrating fibroadenoma, now enlarging,\u000aand new left breast mass S/P core showing a fibroepithelial lesion.\u000aOperation: Bilateral wire-localized excisional breast biopsy.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Bilateral breast mass.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Left breast mass (mammo).\u000aB/2. Right breast mass (mammo).\u000aC/3. Right breast clip.\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000aSpecimen #1: Mass and wire in specimen. R. Birdwell, M.D.\u000aSpecimen #2: Right, mass and wire. No clip in specimen (Phoned-->OR). R\u000aBirdwell, M.D.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in three parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart A, "#1 - left breast mass", and consists of an irregular tan to tan/yellow\u000aportion of unoriented breast tissue (3.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with a localization\u000awire entering from one aspect. The specimen is previously radiographed. The\u000aradiograph demonstrates a mass and a wire within the specimen. The specimen is\u000ainked black and serially sectioned. The cut surface shows a well-defined\u000atan/white nodule towards one end of the specimen (0.9 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). This\u000aspecimen abuts one aspect of the specimen. There is another irregular\u000aill-defined tan/white firm area towards the opposite end of the specimen (0.3 x\u000a0.2 x REMOVED_DATE cm), which is REMOVED_DATE cm from the larger lesion. The main parenchyma\u000aconsists of tan/yellow to tan/white fibroadipose tissue.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Specimen sequentially sectioned with the smaller mass in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aand the larger mass in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, multiple frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, "#2 - right breast mass", and consists of an irregular tan to\u000atan/yellow unoriented portion of breast tissue (2.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). There is\u000aa needle localization wire entering the specimen from one aspect. The specimen\u000ais previously radiographed. The radiograph shows a mass and a wire within the\u000aspecimen. The specimen is inked black and serially sectioned to show a\u000awell-defined tan/white mass, with a gritty cut surface (1.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm)\u000athat focally abuts the margin of the specimen. The main parenchyma consists\u000alargely of tan/yellow lobulated adipose tissue (70%).\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Multiple frags with the lesion in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, ESS.\u000aPart C, "#3 - right breast clip", and consists of a silver surgical clip (0.2 x\u000a0.2 x less than REMOVED_DATE cm). No sections are submitted, gross examination only.\u000adrd/lp\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Alessandra F Nascimento M.D., Electronically signed on\u000a8/3/2006\u000a[report_end]
