VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: JULIE L JONES M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-06-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Eleanor Y. Chen, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Shuji Ogino, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "LEFT BREAST, RE-EXCISION":\u000aBenign breast parenchyma with no residual phyllodes tumor.\u000aBiopsy site changes and mild epithelial hyperplasia.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000aB. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "LEFT BREAST":\u000aBenign breast parenchyma with no significant pathologic change.\u000aNo residual phyllodes tumor is present.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000a(Levels examined, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: None given.\u000aOperation: Left breast reexcision.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast mass, phyllodes tumor.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Left breast reexcision, short - superior, long - lateral.\u000aB/2. Left breast final margins, short - superior, long - lateral.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, in two parts, each labeled with the\u000apatient's name and unit number.\u000aPart A, "Left breast reexcision, short - superior, long - lateral", consists of\u000areexcision breast tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. There is a biopsy\u000acavity measuring REMOVED_DATE cm in diameter. The specimen is inked for the evaluation\u000aof margins: Posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green;\u000alateral/yellow; medial/orange. The biopsy wall is hemorrhagic, surrounded by\u000ascant fibrous tissue and scattered fat necrosis. It is REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000asuperior margin and REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin. The remaining margins\u000aare at least REMOVED_DATE cm from the cavity and are taken as perpendicular sections for\u000amicroscopic examination. The remainder of the specimen consists of yellow\u000aadipose tissue. No areas grossly suspicious for residual tumor is seen.\u000aApproximately 80% of the specimen (at least 90% of the biopsy cavity) is\u000asubmitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Biopsy cavity to superior and posterior margins, 1 frag,\u000aRSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Biopsy cavity to inferior and anterior margins, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Biopsy cavity to superior, inferior, and posterior margins,\u000a1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Biopsy cavity to inferior and anterior margins, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Biopsy cavity to lateral and superior margins, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Biopsy cavity to anterior, medial, posterior margins,\u000a2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Biopsy cavity to posterior margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Biopsy cavity to superior and posterior margins, 1 frag,\u000aRSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Biopsy cavity to posterior and superior margins, 1 frag,\u000aRSS.\u000aPart B, "Left breast - final margins, short - superior, long - lateral",\u000aconsists of breast tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE (superior to inferior) x REMOVED_DATE (medial to\u000alateral) x REMOVED_DATE (anterior to posterior) cm. The specimen is inked for the\u000aevaluation of margins: Posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red;\u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. The breast parenchyma consists\u000aof mostly yellow adipose tissue with very scant fibrous tissue. The specimen\u000ais serially sectioned from superior to inferior, and is entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: The entire specimen serially sectioned from superior to\u000ainferior margins, 6 frags, ESS.\u000aELC/mmm\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Shuji Ogino M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a8/24/2006\u000a[report_end]
