VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aBRENN, THOMAS, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by BRENN,THOMAS,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST, EXCISION WIRE-LOCALIZATION FOR A MASS:\u000aINVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA, THREE (3) FOCI\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aSYNOPSIS:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA\u000aSize - REMOVED_DATE cm, REMOVED_DATE cm, and REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aMultifocal - yes\u000aHistologic Type - ductal\u000aHistologic Grade (SBR) - I (well)\u000aNuclear Grade - intermediate\u000aEIC - positive\u000aLymphovascular invasion - not seen\u000aDermal lymphatic invasion - N/A\u000aSkin invasion - N/A\u000aSkeletal muscle invasion - absent\u000aFinal Margins (invasive) -\u000aNegative (>0.3 cm) - anterior, posterior, inferior,\u000asuperior, medial\u000aClose (0.1-0.3 cm) - lateral\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aTypes - cribriform, papillary, micropapillary\u000aNuclear grade - intermediate\u000aCalcifications in DCIS - absent\u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - absent\u000aMicroinvasion (<0.1cm) - absent\u000aExtent of DCIS\u000aNumber of blocks:total - 14:15 blocks\u000aFinal Margins (DCIS)\u000aNegative (>0.3 cm) - posterior, anterior\u000aVery close (<0.1 cm) - lateral, medial, inferior, superior\u000aPositive (ink on DCIS) - lateral, medial, inferior, superior\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - absent\u000aOTHER FINDINGS\u000aCore biopsy site\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER/PR/HER-2):\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for invasive carcinoma (block 1):\u000aEstrogen receptor - POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor - POSITIVE (low)\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) - NEGATIVE (1+)\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000acarcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but\u000aonly a portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity\u000ain >10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aNOTE: This biopsy shows extensive intraductal carcinoma with three separate\u000aareas of invasion measuring up to REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest dimension.\u000aImunohistochemistry for p63 was evaluated for the diagnosis.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Core biopsy complex cyst - ADH bordering on DCIS left breast.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1 - left breast tissue - short/superior, long/lateral,\u000awhipped stitch/posterior.\u000aRadiograph report: Mass in specimen. D. Smith, M.D.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by BROCK,JANE E.,M.B.,B.S.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in one part, labeled with the patient's name and\u000aunit number and "#1 - left breast tissue, short/superior, long/lateral,\u000awhipped/posterior", and consists of a wire localized lumpectomy specimen (6.5\u000acm from anterior to posterior, REMOVED_DATE cm medial to lateral, and REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000asuperior to inferior), with an attached skin ellipse forming the anterior\u000asurface (3.0 cm x REMOVED_DATE cm) which is pink and unremarkable. The specimen is\u000areceived inked by the surgeon. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol\u000afor the evaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior =\u000ared; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. A radiograph is\u000areceived with the specimen, which demonstrates a wire and an ill-defined mass\u000ain the specimen. Sectioning reveals an area which is firm and nodular\u000a(1.5 cm x REMOVED_DATE cm x REMOVED_DATE cm), which abuts the superior margin, is REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000alateral margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin, extends as a band of fibrous\u000atissue without nodularity to the anterior skin ellipse margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000aanterior margin, and is REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin and REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000amedial margin. The remainder of the specimen is approximately 20% firm fibrous\u000atissue with a rubbery texture. Ninety (90%) percent of the tissue is\u000asubmitted.\u000aMicro #1-7: Firm nodular fibrous tissue, 7 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro #8-14: Remainder of fibrous tissue, 7 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro #15: Medial and lateral margins, 4 frags, RSS.\u000ajeb/\u000aReports to: CHRISTIAN, ROGER, L. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
