VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID:REMOVED_CASE_ID Report Status: Signed\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aDIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. Sentinel node, #1 (one node):\u000aNo metastatic tumor seen (one node).\u000aH&E and pankeratin levels studied.\u000aB. Sentinel node, #2 (one node):\u000aMetastatic carcinoma, few foci less than REMOVED_DATE cm. (in H&E and keratin).\u000aH&E and pankeratin levels studied.\u000aC. Sentinel node, #3 (one node):\u000aFew keratin positive cells (not seen in H&E).\u000aH&E and pankeratin levels studied.\u000aD. Lymph nodes of left axilla, non-sentinel:\u000aNo metastatic tumor seen in two lymph nodes.\u000aH&E and keratin stains studied.\u000aE. Left breast, excision of cavity:\u000aDuctal carcinoma in situ, high grade (3/3), comedocarcinoma type, with\u000acalcification present REMOVED_DATE cm. from inked resection margin focally\u000a(focus about 1 x 1 cm.).\u000aF. Left breast, excision:\u000aPoorly differentiated infiltrating duct carcinoma (3 x 2 x 2 cm.).\u000aDuctal carcinoma in situ, high grade (3/3), comedocarcinoma type, with\u000acalcification associated with and remote from the infiltrating tumor\u000awith lobular extension.\u000aG. Skin of left chest, excision:\u000aModerately differentiated squamous cell carcinoma, invasive (surgically\u000acleared).\u000aNOTE: In specimen F, infiltrating carcinoma is seen at inked resection margins\u000aover a broad front. Focal lymphatic/vascular invasion is seen.\u000aImmunohistochemical studies performed on block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID reveal the following\u000aresults for the infiltrating carcinoma:\u000aEstrogen receptor: NEGATIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor: NEGATIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID): POSITIVE (3+ staining).\u000aThe relationship between specimens E and F is uncertain and the surgical\u000amargins cannot be evaluated but are probably positive for the\u000ainfiltrating tumor. The previous needle biopsies are reviewed\u000a(S-03-198).\u000aFinal Diagnosis by: Richard J. Sampson, M.D.\u000aINTRA-OPERATIVE CONSULTATION:\u000aOPERATING ROOM CONSULTATION (TISSUE EXAMINATION):\u000aThree sentinel lymph nodes examined; no gross tumor seen; will process for full\u000asentinel lymph node protocol.\u000aNAM\u000aClinical diagnosis & history:\u000aLeft breast mass; keratoacanthoma of chest\u000aTissue-Designation:\u000aA.Sentinel lymph node - #1, left breast\u000aB.Sentinel lymph node - #2, left breast\u000aC.Sentinel lymph node - #3, left breast\u000aD.Lymph node, biopsy - left breast\u000aE.Breast, excision with margins - left\u000aF.Breast, excision with margins - left\u000aG.Skin, excision - chest\u000aGross description:\u000aThe specimen is received in seven containers.\u000aSpecimen A labeled "sentinel node #1" consists of a piece of fatty tissue REMOVED_DATE x\u000a0.5 x REMOVED_DATE cm. 1X all.\u000aSpecimen B labeled "sentinel node #2" consists of a mass of fatty tissue with\u000asome lymph nodes present measuring 1 x 1 x REMOVED_DATE cm. 1X all.\u000aSpecimen C labeled "sentinel node #3" consists of two pieces of lymph node\u000abearing adipose tissue, both aggregating 2 x 1 x 3 cm. 2X all.\u000aSpecimen D labeled "lymph nodes of left breast, non-sentinel node" consists of\u000afibrofatty tissue and lymph nodes 2 x 1 x REMOVED_DATE cm. 1X all.\u000aSpecimen E labeled "excision cavity, left breast" consists of a piece of fatty\u000abreast tissue 6 x 4 x 2 cm. without orienting marks. On cut section, the\u000atissue is largely adipose tissue with some discoloration with blue dye. 12X\u000aall.\u000aSpecimen F consists of a globoid mass of breast tissue 5 x 5 x 3 cm. A wire\u000amarker is present but no orienting sutures. The entire specimen is inked with\u000ablack ink. Sections are taken from one end towards the other noting that there\u000ais an area of firmness with irregular borders measuring 3 x 2 x 2 cm. The area\u000aof irregularity seems to extend very close to the margin of the specimen in one\u000afocus. The entire specimen is submitted. 21X all.\u000aSpecimen G labeled "keratoacanthoma from chest" consists of a piece of skin REMOVED_DATE \u000ax 1 cm. resected to a depth of 1 cm. of subcutaneous tissue. The specimen is\u000ainked. The surface is somewhat shaggy. 4X all.\u000aDictated by: RJS____(signature on file)____MICHAEL J. ROSS, M.D. REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a____(signature on file)____RICHARD SAMPSON, M.D. REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a[report_end]
