ivity in >10% of tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity\u000ain >10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Non-palpable mass left breast with nipple retraction.\u000aOperation: Left breast biopsy.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Microcalcifications left breast.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Mass left breast.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by YANG,TAO,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit\u000anumber, and "#1, left breast tissue", consists of two (2) pieces of tan-pink\u000asoft tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm respectively.\u000aThe smaller piece is marked by a suture and both pieces are not oriented.\u000aMicro 1: larger piece, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 2: smaller piece, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aty\u000aReports to: CHRISTIAN, ROGER, L. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST BIOPSY W/O MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
