al Diagnosis: Left breast carcinoma.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Left breast, stitch at tail (with axillary contents)\u000aand axillary contents.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by LEE,BENJAMIN H.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in one part, labeled with the patient's name,\u000aunit number and "left breast and axillary contents (stitch on tail)", and\u000aconsists of a 1030-gram, left modified radical mastectomy specimen (20.0 x REMOVED_DATE \u000ax REMOVED_DATE cm in overall dimension) with a tan skin ellipse (22 x 10 cm). The\u000askin ellipse contains a REMOVED_DATE cm areola with an inverted nipple. An axillary\u000atail measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm and is denoted by a suture. The inferior\u000aaspect of the areola contains a REMOVED_DATE cm, curvilinear, healed scar. The deep\u000afascial plane is inked in black. On cut section, there is an ill-defined,\u000adense, tan/gray, infiltrative tumor mass (approximately REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm)\u000awhich resides directly beneath the inverted nipple and is approximately REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom the deep fascial margin. Within this dense, firm area are changes\u000aconsistent with a biopsy site. Approximately REMOVED_DATE cm medial to the large tumor\u000amass is a smaller spiculated dense area (1.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The second\u000anodule is REMOVED_DATE cm from the deep fascial plane. The remainder of the breast\u000aparenchyma is comprised primarily of fatty adipose tissue interposed with\u000afibrous strands of connective tissue. Representative sections are submitted\u000afor analysis.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  sections of large tumor mass and biopsy site, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000aMicro 5: deep margin to large mass, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 6: breast between large mass and medial tumor, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  sections of smaller medial tumor mass, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro 11: deep margin to medial tumor mass, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 12: section of nipple, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 13: upper inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 14: lower inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 15: upper outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 16: lower outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 17: 4 lymph nodes, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 18: 4 lymph nodes, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 19: 1 lymph node bisected, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 20: 1 lymph node, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro 21: 3 lymph nodes, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 22: 1 lymph nodes, 2 frags, ESS.\u000abhl\u000aReports to: LOFGREN, ROBERT, H., MD\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY W/REGIONAL LYMPH NODES\u000a[report_end]
