REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), with a long suture\u000adesignating lateral, and a short suture designating superior. There is an\u000ainserted needle localization wire, which enters along the posterior margin, and\u000aexits along the anterior margin. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol\u000aas anterior blue, posterior black, superior red, inferior green, lateral\u000ayellow, and medial orange. The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a\u000awell-healed biopsy cavity, containing a surgical clip (0.6 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm).\u000aThe cavity with the clip is REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000alateral margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin.\u000aRemaining cut surface displays 50% yellow lobulated adipose tissue, and 50%\u000awhite fibrous tissue, with no additional discrete masses or lesions identified.\u000aThe specimen is sequentially submitted in its entirety.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Anterior margin, radially, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross sections from anterior to posterior, with the\u000abiopsy cavity in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, and a surgical clip identified in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Posterior margin, radially, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aPlease note that the specimen is received with a specimen radiograph,\u000acorresponding to the gross findings.\u000aCP/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Vania Nose MD, PhD, Electronically signed on Wednesday\u000aREMOVED_MONTH 21, 2009 at 02:09:07PM\u000a[report_