VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Amend/Addenda\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Sentinel Lymph Nodes(s)\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: JULIE L JONES M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000a********** Addended Report ***********\u000aResident: Qinghong Yang, M.D., Ph.D.; Martin C Chang, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: William R Welch, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, SIMPLE MASTECTOMY, AND 2 SENTINEL NODE BIOPSIES (3 SPECIMENS):\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA with lobular and ductal features, moderately differentiated\u000a(modified Bloom-Richardson grade II/III), single focus, grossly measuring REMOVED_DATE \u000acm.\u000aLymphovascular invasion is present, in foci around the tumor.\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, solid type (high nuclear grade) is present in 5 of 9\u000ablocks. DCIS is associated with central necrosis. No calcifications are\u000aassociated with DCIS.\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU is present.\u000aInvasive carcinoma is present REMOVED_DATE cm from the deep resection margin.\u000aDCIS is present REMOVED_DATE cm from the deep resection margin.\u000aSkin and nipple are free of carcinoma.\u000aSkeletal muscle is present and is free of carcinoma.\u000aMETASTATIC CARCINOMA is present in 1 of 4 sentinel lymph nodes (multiple levels\u000aexamined), see NOTE.\u000aNOTE: ISOLATED TUMOR CELLS are present as metastases in one (1) of four (4)\u000asentinel lymph nodes, in seven (7) cell clusters largest measuring <0.02 cm\u000a(multiple levels examined). Immunohistochemistry for REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/3 is positive in\u000atumor cells within the lymph node.\u000aAJCC Classification (6th edition): REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID pREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID(i+)(sn)\u000aSpecial studies (ER, PR, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID): Pending (Block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aCase reviewed by Dr. A. Richardson, Breast Pathology Service, who concurs.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Right breast IDC on core biopsy.\u000aOperation: Right skin sparing total mastectomy and SNB.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast cancer.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Right axillary sentinel node hot FS.\u000aB/2. Right axillary sentinel node cold.\u000aC/3. Right breast with stitch on superior skin.\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "RIGHT SENTINAL AXILLARY NODES HOT" (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aThree lymph nodes identified, negative for tumor.\u000aOR Consultation by: GILBERT BRODSKY, M.D.\u000aResident: VIJAY K VANGURI, M.D.; KEVIN LONG, M.D.\u000aThe senior physician certifies that he/she personally conducted a gross and/or\u000amicroscopic examination of the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed\u000athe rapid diagnos(es) related thereto.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in three parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname, unit number.\u000aPart A, "#1. Right sentinel axillary node hot", received fresh in the frozen\u000asection room, consists of three separate lymph node candidates. Lymph node\u000acandidate #1 (3.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with previously trimmed of adherent adipose\u000atissue, bisected and entirely frozen as REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. Lymph node candidate #2 (1.1 x\u000a1.0 x REMOVED_DATE cm) was previously bisected and entirely frozen as REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. Lymph node\u000acandidate #3 (0.9 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) was previously bisected and entirely frozen\u000aas REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. In addition fragments of adipose tissue (1.4 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in\u000aaggregate) were identified and not frozen.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID remnant (node #1 bisected), 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID remnant (node #2 bisected), 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID remnant (node #3 bisected), 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Non-frozen adipose tissue trimmed from node #1, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, "#2. Additional right sentinel lymph node cold", consists of one\u000apink/tan lymph node candidate (0.5 cm in greatest dimension) with a small\u000aamount of adherent adipose tissue. The specimen is submitted in toto.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 frag, ESS.\u000aPart C, "#3. Right breast with stitch superior skin", consists of a 124 g\u000asimple mastectomy specimen (14.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with an adherent tan skin\u000aellipse (7.2 x REMOVED_DATE cm). The specimen is oriented per surgeon with a stitch\u000adesignating the superior aspect of the skin. The skin exhibits a central pink\u000aareola (2.5 x REMOVED_DATE cm) and a pink/tan everted nipple (0.8 cm in diameter). No\u000ascar is identified on the skin surface. The deep margin (inked black) is a\u000asmooth fascial plane. The specimen is serially sectioned from medial to\u000alateral. In the upper outer quadrant, there is a poorly delineated indurated\u000aspeculated tan/white mass (2.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which comes to within REMOVED_DATE cm of\u000athe deep margin. The mass exhibits punctate areas of hemorrhage (up to REMOVED_DATE cm\u000ain greatest dimension), and an embedded small metal clip. The remainder of the\u000acut surface is composed of approximately 70% yellow/tan lobulated adipose\u000atissue and 30% focally dense/nodular white/tan fibrostroma. No additional\u000adiscrete masses or lesions are identified.\u000aAn axillary tail is not present. The most lateral breast parenchyma is\u000aexamined for intramammary lymph node candidates, but none are grossly\u000aidentified.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Nipple/areola, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Mass with adjacent uninvolved parenchyma (deep margin in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), 1\u000afrag in each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Fibrous stroma, upper outer quadrant away from mass, 3 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Fibrous stroma, upper inner quadrant, 3 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Fibrous stroma, lower outer quadrant, 3 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Fibrous stroma, lower inner quadrant, 3 frags, RSS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aLMB/ajb\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by William R Welch M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000aSurgical Addendum: (1/22/07)\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for invasive carcinoma (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) NEGATIVE (1+)\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000acarcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but only\u000aa portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in >10%\u000aof tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in\u000a>10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aAddendum #1 by Michael W Bennett M.B., B.C.H., Electronically signed on\u000a1/22/2007\u000aAdditional keratin immunohistochemistry was performed on remaining sentinel\u000alymph nodes, which detected isolated tumor cell clusters in one additional\u000alymph node. Therefore, isolated tumor cell clusters (largest contiguous\u000acluster measuring <0.02 cm) are present in 2 of 4 sentinel nodes. In one node\u000aseveral clusters are present close to each other over a REMOVED_DATE cm area, however,\u000athis does not change the AJCC staging of REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID(i+).\u000aAddendum #2 by Andrea L Richardson M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a1/25/2007\u000a[report_end]
