VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Amend/Addenda\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: DIANE C LOCKHART M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000a********** Addended Report ***********\u000aResident: Anna Laury, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Jane E. Brock, M.B., B.S., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A CLIP AND MASS:\u000aINVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA, moderately differentiated (modified Bloom-Richardson\u000agrade II/III), measuring REMOVED_DATE cm (see NOTE).\u000aNo lymphovascular invasion is seen.\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, papillary and cribriform types (intermediate nuclear\u000agrade) without necrosis or calcifications is associated with the invasive\u000acarcinoma and core biopsy site (4 of 12 blocks; EIC positive).\u000aInvasive carcinoma is focally < REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) and\u000afocally REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior margin (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID). Posterior, superior, medial and\u000alateral margins are negative for invasive carcinoma (> REMOVED_DATE cm).\u000aDCIS is focally REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior margin (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID; a papillary lesion\u000ainvolved by DCIS), and focally REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aPosterior, superior, inferior, medial and lateral margins are negative for DCIS\u000a(> REMOVED_DATE cm).\u000aOther findings:\u000aCalcifications in benign epithelium.\u000aColumnar cell change with cysts and atypia.\u000aApocrine cysts.\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for invasive carcinoma (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) NEGATIVE (0)\u000aNOTE: In retrospect the atypical lesion seen in the biopsy represents a small\u000aportion of invasive carcinoma, which is better seen in this excision specimen.\u000aDr. Susan Lester has reviewed key slides of invasive carcinoma and DCIS from\u000athis case and agrees with the diagnosis.\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000acarcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but only\u000aa portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in >10%\u000aof tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in\u000a>10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Abnormal mammo. Atypical sclerosing lesion.\u000aOperation: Not provided\u000aOperative Findings: Not provided\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Not provided\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) Right breast tissue - needle localized -> FS\u000aFor mammo - short stitch/superior; long stitch/lateral\u000aRADIATION; Clip, mass, and wire are in specimen.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number\u000aand "#1. Right breast tissue, needle loc, long lateral, short superior",\u000aconsists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm excision of fibroadipose tissue, oriented by\u000asutures designating superior (short suture) and lateral (long suture) margins.\u000aThe specimen has been inked by the surgeon as follows: The specimen is inked\u000aper pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black;\u000aanterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. A\u000alocalizing wire enters the lateral aspect of the specimen and traverses\u000amedially. The specimen is received with an accompanying radiograph\u000ademonstrating a localizing wire in place within the specimen adjacent to a\u000acentral ill-defined area of abnormality with an associated metallic clip.\u000aSectioning demonstrates a probably firm fibrous area (0.9 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with\u000aassociated metallic surgical clip, compatible with prior biopsy site. This\u000afirm tissue abuts the less than REMOVED_DATE cm from the closest anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000ainferior margin, and remote (greater than REMOVED_DATE cm) from the lateral medial\u000amargins. Remaining specimen is predominantly comprised of soft, lobulated\u000atan/yellow adipose tissue (greater than 95%), with occasional thin tan/white\u000afibrous septate. The specimen is entirely submitted for histological\u000aevaluation. Tissue will be held for further fixation prior to processing.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential representative sections, to include entire area of\u000ainterest (per clip, localizing wire radiograph) and closest margin, multi\u000afrags, ESS. Please note: Perpendicular medial margin in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, perpendicular\u000alateral margin in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, and area of interest predominantly in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID (tissue with\u000aclip in micro cassette REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: remainder of specimen, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aDB/mgd/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jane E. Brock M.B., B.S., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a10/15/2008\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: (4/1/09)\u000aFISH was performed by Clarient using the PathVysion HER-2 DNA Probe Kit with\u000athe following (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aResults: NOT AMPLIFIED\u000aHER-2/CEP-17 ratio = REMOVED_DATE \u000aThe average of HER-2 copies per cell: REMOVED_DATE \u000aThe average centromere 17 copies per cell: REMOVED_DATE \u000aREFERENCE RANGE:\u000aNOT AMPLIFIED HER-2/CEP-17 ratio < REMOVED_DATE \u000aEQUIVOCAL HER-2/CEP-17 ratio REMOVED_DATE to REMOVED_DATE \u000aAMPLIFIED REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/CEP-17 ratio > REMOVED_DATE \u000aAddendum #1 by Andrea L Richardson M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000aWednesday REMOVED_MONTH 01, 2009 at 05:55:50PM\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: (4/10/09)\u000aA paraffin block of invasive carcinoma was sent for the genomic health oncotype\u000aDX Breast Cancer Assay with the following results (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aRecurrence Score = 14\u000aPatients with a Recurrence Score of 14 in the clinical validation study had an\u000aAverage Rate of Recurrence at 10 years of 9% (95% CI: 6% - 11%).\u000aQUANTITATIVE SINGLE GENE REPORT:\u000aER Score = REMOVED_DATE Positive\u000aPR Score = REMOVED_DATE Positive\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Score = REMOVED_DATE Negative\u000aAddendum #2 by Andrea L Richardson M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000aFriday REMOVED_MONTH 10, 2009 at 11:15:51AM\u000a[report_end]
