tologic Type - ductal\u000aHistologic Grade (SBR) - II (moderate)\u000aNuclear Grade - intermediate\u000aEIC - positive\u000aLymphovascular invasion - absent\u000aDermal lymphatic invasion - absent\u000aSkin invasion - absent\u000aSkeletal muscle invasion - absent\u000aFinal Margins (invasive)\u000aNegative (>0.3 cm) - deep (posterior)\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU - present\u000aTypes - solid, cribriform\u000aNuclear grade - intermediate\u000aCalcifications in DCIS - present\u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - present\u000aExtent of DCIS\u000aEstimated overall size - REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aFinal Margins (DCIS)\u000aNegative (>0.3 cm) - deep (posterior)\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - absent\u000aOTHER FINDINGS\u000aScar consistent with healed old biopsy site\u000aCore biopsy site\u000aSkeletal muscle\u000aOne intraparenchymal lymph node with no tumor present (0:1)\u000aAJCC CLASSIFICATION (6th edition) - REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDa pREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID MX\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER/PR/HER-2) - performed previously\u000aNOTE: Multiple separate foci (approximately 5) of invasive carcinoma are\u000apresent within the area of DCIS, ranging from REMOVED_DATE to REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest\u000adimension.\u000aC) LEFT BREAST, SKIN:\u000aSkin and subcutis with no tumor present.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 65 year-old woman with PMH (L) invasive ductal Ca s/p (L)\u000aBCT/XRT/chemo tx with MGH; (L) ca was node neg ER/PR (+); took Tamoxifen for 5\u000ayrs presented with (L) recurrence and (R) breast new primary invasive\u000alobular/ductal mixed GR II/III (+) DCIS.\u000aOperation: (L) simple mastectomy, (R) simple mastectomy, (R) SLN bx.\u000aOperative Findings: Not provided.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: B/L invasive breast Ca.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. (R) breast and axillary contents, short stitch axilla, long stitch tail\u000awith Spence - to path.\u000aB/2. (L) breast stitch/tail of Spence.\u000aC/3. Breast skin (L).\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in three parts, each labeled with the patients\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart A, labeled "#1. (R) breast and axillary contents", consists of a 671 gm\u000a(post fixation, post breast tissue banking) is a mastectomy specimen composed\u000aof right breast (23.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with eccentric small tan/white skin\u000aellipse (3.5 x REMOVED_DATE cm) with an everted pink/tan nipple (1.2 cm in maximum\u000adimension) and tan wrinkled areola (3.0 cm in greatest dimension). A\u000adefinitive scar is not identified on the epithelial surface. The specimen is\u000aoriented per surgeon with sutures designating the axillary tail (9.0 x REMOVED_DATE x\u000a1.0 cm). The specimen was previously sectioned by the breast tumor bank\u000ainvestigator from medial to lateral. At the junction of the upper outer and\u000alower outer quadrant, there is a poorly delineated spiculated indurated\u000awhite/pink mass (1.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which is REMOVED_DATE cm from the blacked inked\u000adeep margin (which a smooth fascial plane). Adjacent to the mass are multiple\u000apunctate foci of hemorrhage (0.1 cm - REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest dimension) as\u000aconsistent with prior core biopsy. Representative of the mass was previously\u000ataken for breast tumor bank. Approximately REMOVED_DATE cm inferior to the mass is a\u000afirm tan/white cyst (0.8 cm in greatest dimension) filled with red/brown blood\u000aclot. The remainder of the specimen is composed of approximately 40% diffusely\u000adense/lumpy/cystic white/tan fibrous stroma and approximately 60% yellow/tan\u000alobulated adipose tissue. No additional discrete lesions are grossly\u000aidentified. The axillary tail is removed and dissected for lymph node\u000acandidates. Approximately thirty pink/tan rubbery lymph node candidates\u000a(ranging from REMOVED_DATE cm to REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest dimension) are identified.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Nipple/areola, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Remainder of mass with adjacent areas of hemorrhage, 1 frag each,\u000aESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Deep margin closest to mass (no mass grossly present), 2 frags,\u000aESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Large cyst filled with clot inferior to mass (lower outer\u000aquadrant), 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Dense fibrous stroma away from mass, upper outer quadrant, 3\u000afrags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Dense fibrous stroma, upper inner quadrant, 3 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Dense fibrous stroma away from mass, lower outer quadrant, 3\u000afrags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Dense fibrous stroma, lower inner quadrant, 3 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 2 bisected lymph node candidates (1 inked blue), 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 2 bisected lymph node candidates (1 inked blue), 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 6 lymph node candidates, 6 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 6 lymph node candidates, 6 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 8 small lymph node candidates, 8 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 5 small lymph node candidates, 5 frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, labeled "#2. Left breast stitch tail of Spence", consists of a 414 gm\u000amastectomy specimen (17.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with two separate eccentric skin\u000aellipses. The first skin ellipse (3.2 x REMOVED_DATE cm) is adherent to the\u000aanterior/medial aspect of the specimen and exhibits a pink/tan everted nipple\u000a(0.9 cm in maximum dimension) and a tan wrinkled areola (3.0 cm in maximum\u000adimension) with no definitive scar identified. The second skin ellipse (3.8 x\u000a1.2 cm) is adherent to the anterior/superior/lateral aspect of the specimen and\u000aexhibits a central well-healed retracted linear scar (2.3 cm in length). The\u000aspecimen is oriented per surgeon with suture designating the small axillary\u000atail (4.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The deep margin (inked black) is predominantly a\u000asmooth fascial plane with a focal area of puckering (1.5 x REMOVED_DATE cm) in the upper\u000aouter quadrant, corresponding to the superior/lateral skin ellipse with the\u000ascar. The specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral to exhibit two\u000aseparate masses. Mass "1" (2.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) is in the upper outer quadrant,\u000aabutting the deep margin and the aforementioned area of puckering, and REMOVED_DATE cm\u000adeep to the skin ellipse with the scar. Mass "1" exhibits a poorly-delineated\u000aspiculated white/tan indurated cut surface. Approximately REMOVED_DATE cm medial to and\u000aslightly inferior to mass "1" is mass "2" (2.1 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) in the central\u000abreast, at the junction of the upper inner and lower inner quadrants. Mass "2"\u000aexhibits a poorly-delineated spiculated indurated white/pink cut surface and\u000acomes to within REMOVED_DATE cm of the black inked deep margin. Adjacent to mass "2"\u000aare multiple small punctate areas of hemorrhage (0.1 cm to REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest\u000adimension) and foci of gritty yellow/tan probable fat necrosis as consistent\u000awith prior core biopsy procedure. The remainder of the specimen is composed of\u000aapproximately 40% diffusely dense/lumpy white/tan fibrous stroma and\u000aapproximately 60% yellow/tan lobulated adipose tissue with no additional\u000adiscrete lesions grossly identified. A small axillary tail is removed and\u000adissected for lymph node candidates. Two pink/tan rubbery lymph node\u000acandidates (each REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest dimension) are identified in the small\u000aaxillary tail.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Skin ellipse with nipple/areola, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Mass "1", full thickness sections to include skin ellipse with\u000ascar and puckered deep margin, sequentially entirely submitted\u000afrom lateral to medial, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Intervening tissue between mass "1" and mass "2" (no discrete\u000alesions identified), 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Deep margin, closest to mass "2" (no mass grossly present), 2\u000afrags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID:Mass "2" entirely sequentially submitted from lateral to medial\u000ato include adjacent areas of hemorrhage and fat necrosis (maximum\u000adimension best represented in blocks REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), 1 frag each,\u000aESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Dense fibrous stroma upper outer quadrant, away from mass "1", 3\u000afrags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Dense fibrous stroma upper inner quadrant, away from mass "1", 3\u000afrags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Dense fibrous stroma lower outer quadrant, 3 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Dense fibrous stroma lower inner quadrant, away from mass "1", 4\u000afrags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 2 lymph node candidates, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aPart C, labeled "#3. Breast skin (L)", consists of an aggregate of multiple\u000airregular fragments of tan/white wrinkled skin with a small amount of attached\u000ayellow/tan to tan/pink fibrofatty tissue (8.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate). No\u000adiscrete lesions are identified on the epithelial surfaces or within the\u000afibrofatty tissue.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Multi frags, RSS.\u000aLMB/ajb\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Kevin B Long M.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Review by Jason L Hornick M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jason L Hornick M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a12/20/2005\u000a[report_end]
