ear old female diagnosed with right breast cancer, right\u000aaxillary biopsy REMOVED_DATE  FNA of right axillary biopsy reveals invasive ductal\u000acarcinoma - Stein Bloom Richards grade II, ER/PR positive.\u000aOperation: Right mastectomy\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right Breast cancer\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1) Right breast cancer (short suture/superior; long\u000asuture/lateral; axillary tail with nodes)\u000a#2) Right axillary contents\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by HASKELL,HENRY D.,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart one, labeled "#1. right breast, short suture superior, long suture lateral\u000atail with nodes", consists of a right modified radical mastectomy specimen (26\u000ax 16 x REMOVED_DATE cm) with an attached axillary tail (5 x 4 x 1 cm), and a white/tan\u000askin ellipse (16 x 8 cm) including nipple (1.4 cm), and areola (2.5 cm). A\u000afirm, tan/white mass is present in the inner lower quadrant (approximately 7 x\u000a3.5 x REMOVED_DATE cm) which appears to extend to the outer lower quadrant. The entire\u000abreast is firm and distorted by the presence of approximately thirty cysts\u000afilled with brown/red fluid located throughout the breast. The mass appears to\u000aapproach to approximately REMOVED_DATE cm of the black inked deep margin.\u000aMicro 1: woody white nodule, LIQ, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 2: cyst and apparent lesion at 5 cm distance from cassette 1,1 frag,\u000aRSS\u000aMicro 3: area at 7 cm distance from section 1 including cyst showing closest\u000aapproach to margin (LOQ), 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  additional sections showing tumor with respective margins, LIQ, 1\u000afrag each, RSS\u000aMicro 7: UIQ, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 8: OUQ, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 9: nipple and areola\u000aMicro 10: attached nodes, 2 nodes, 2 frags, ESS\u000aMicro 11: attached nodes, 3 nodes, 3 frags, ESS\u000aMicro 12: attached nodes, 2 nodes, 2 frags, ESS\u000aMicro 13: attached nodes, 1 node, 2 frags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  additional sections of deep margin, 1 frag/cass, RSS\u000aPart two, labeled "#2. right axillary contents", consists of a single fragment\u000aof fibroadipose tissue (4 x 2 x REMOVED_DATE cm). Four apparent nodes are found, the\u000alargest is REMOVED_DATE cm (this is the largest node in both parts).\u000aMicro 14: 2 apparent nodes, 2 frags, ESS\u000aMicro 15: 1 node, 2 frags, ESS\u000aMicro 16: largest node, 2 frags, 1 node, ESS\u000ahdh\u000aReports to: LESNIKOSKI, BETH-ANN M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY W/REGIONAL LYMPH NODES\u000a[report_end]
