ides and four (4)\u000aunstained slides labeled "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID". The stained slides are sublabeled "A 1\u000aIP-H&E", "A 1 H&E", "A 1 NIR", "A 1 OMIS" x2, "A 1 HMWK 903", "A 1 REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID", "A\u000a1 ACT-HHF-35", "A 1 S 100", "A 1 KER COCKTAIL", "A 1 REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID(ENDO)", "A 1\u000aDesmin", "A 2 H&E", and "A 2 LEVEL". The four unstained slides are sublabeled\u000a"REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID". These all correspond to left breast, from a procedure performed on\u000a12/29/03, according to the accompanying report bearing the patient's name.\u000aThe slides are also labeled "SW-04-REMOVED_CASE_ID", corresponding to a\u000aconsultation dated REMOVED_DATE  by Emory University Hospital bearing the patient's\u000aname.\u000aAlso received is report accessioned #REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, dated REMOVED_DATE  corresponding to\u000aan FNA of the breast, that bears the patient's name.\u000aReports to: MORGAN, JEFFREY, ARNOLD M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: OUTSIDE SLIDE CONSULT - SRSS\u000a[report_end]
