VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID SOFT TISSUE BIOPSY\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aHIRSCH, MICHELLE, S., M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by HIRSCH,MICHELLE S.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "LEFT CHEST WALL MASS" (including FSA):\u000aUNCLASSIFIED SPINDLE CELL SARCOMA, present adjacent to hyalinized\u000astromal tissue (see NOTE) (see COMMENT).\u000aNOTE: The permanent section demonstrates scant pleomorphic cells\u000aconsistent with the spindle cell sarcoma. These cells were not\u000apresent in the frozen section slides.\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "LEFT BREAST" (SIMPLE MASTECTOMY, 130 grams):\u000aBreast tissue with cyts, epithelial hyperplasia, and a\u000afibroadenoma (1.2 cm).\u000aMicrocalcifications are associated with benign epithelium.\u000aSkeletal muscle with no significant pathologic change.\u000aSkin with cicatrix.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the\u000aspecimen, including margins.\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "CHEST WALL TUMOR WITH RIBS":\u000aUNCLASSIFIED SPINDLE CELL SARCOMA with myogenic differentiation,\u000amorphologically low to intermediate grade, associated with\u000ahyalinized stromal tissue.\u000aNo necrosis is identified.\u000aMitoses number < REMOVED_DATE HPFs.\u000aTumor extends to within REMOVED_DATE cm of the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the\u000ainferior margin, and is greater than REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior, lateral,\u000aand medial margins.\u000aReactive fibroblasts are present at the inked anterior portion of the\u000aspecimen (adjacent to mastectomy specimen, see part 2 above).\u000aImmunohistochemistry performed at BWH demonstrates the following\u000astaining profile in tumor cells:\u000aPositive - desmin\u000aNegative - caldesmon, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, Pan-k\u000aCOMMENT: The morphologic and immunophenotypic findings are most\u000aconsistent with an unclassified spindle cell sarcoma with myogenic\u000adifferentiation. The findings are likely radiation associated.\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: by HIRSCH,MICHELLE S.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe tumor measures REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest dimension.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: H/o breast CA now with new suspicious ca++ axillary tail and XRT -\u000aassociated sarcoma - chest wall.\u000aOperation: Resection of chest wall sarcoma and left simple mastectomy\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Radiation-assoc. sarcoma and L breast microcalcifications\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1) Left chest wall mass to confirm lesional tissue - fs\u000a#2) Left breast - long stitch axillary tail - fs\u000a#3) Chest wal tumor with ribs - fs\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "LEFT CHEST WALL MASS - TO CONFIRM LESIONAL TISSUE" (FSA):\u000aHyalinized stromal tissue.\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "#3. CHEST WALL TUMOR WITH RIBS" (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID AND REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aAtypical spindle cell neoplasm (1.4 cm).\u000aTissue sent for cytogenetics.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by BENNETT,MICHAEL W.,M.B.B.C.H.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in three parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart one, labeled "#1. Left chest wall mass to confirm lesional tissue",\u000aconsists of one fragment of white/pink soft tissue (0.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The\u000aspecimen is entirely submitted in frozen section A.\u000aMicro 1: FSA remnant, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aPart two, labeled "#2. Left breast - long stitch axillary tail", consists of a\u000aleft simple mastectomy specimen (130 g, REMOVED_DATE cm medial to lateral x REMOVED_DATE cm\u000ainferior to superior x REMOVED_DATE cm anterior to posterior). The specimen has been\u000amarked by the surgion with a suture in the axillary tail. There is an\u000aanterior skin ellipse (12.0 x REMOVED_DATE cm) which includes the areola (2.3 cm in\u000adiameter) and nipple (1.1 cm in diameter x REMOVED_DATE cm in length). Adjacent and\u000ainframedial to the larger ellipse is second skin ellipse (9.2 x REMOVED_DATE cm). The\u000askin ellipse includes a remote scar, which is inframedial to the nipple (2.5 x\u000a0.1 cm). On the posterior suface there is an area of muscle (7.5 x REMOVED_DATE cm)\u000athat the surgeon has marked with four sutures representing the deep surface\u000athat abuts the next specimen (part three) anteriorly. This area is REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom the inferior and lateral margins of the specimen, REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000aanterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial medial, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior\u000amargin. The deep surface of the specimen is inked black. No discrete or\u000afocal lesions are identified grossly in the breast. A radiograph is taken. No\u000asuspicious microcalcifications are identified in the axillary tail. No lymph\u000anodes are identified in the axillary tail. Representative sections are\u000asubmitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  axillary tail, 4 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 4: superior/lateral quadrant, fibrous tissue, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 5: superior/medial fibrous tissue, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  area abutting specimen #3. (inked blue), 4 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 8: inframedial quadrant, fibrous tissue, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 9: infralateral fibrous tissue, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 10: nipple, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 11: scar, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aPart three, labeled "#3. Chest wall tumor with ribs", consists of a portion of\u000atwo ribs with attached soft tissue (5.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). A stitch has been\u000aplaced by the surgeon to designate the superior margin. On the superficial\u000aaspect there is a portion of attached muscle (4.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The deep\u000amargin is inked black, the anterior portion of the specimen (which does not\u000arepresent true magin; see specimen #2.) is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE \u000ax REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm white/gray frim nodule which abuts the anterior surface, and is\u000a0.4 cm from posterior/deep resection margin. The resection margins are inked\u000aas follows: black = deep, blue = anterior, orange = medial, yellow = lateral,\u000ared = superior, green = inferior. The mass is REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE \u000acm from the lateral margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin. The superior\u000arib measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm and the inferior rib measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm. Representative sections of the nodule are submitted frozen section REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. A portion of the tissue is quick-fixed and an additional portion is sent\u000afor cytogenetics. Representative sections are submitted.\u000aMicro 12: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID remnant, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro 13: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID remnant, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro 14: Qiuck-fix, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro 15: remainder of nodule,\u000aMicro 16: additional anterior edge (not true margin),\u000aMicro 17: lateral margin, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro 18: medial margin, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro 19: superior rib, lateral margin, 1 frag, ESS\u000aMicro 20: superior rib, medial margin, 2 frags, ESS\u000aMicro 21: superior rib, superior margin, 1 frag, ESS\u000aMicro 22: inferior rib, lateral margin, 1 frag, ESS\u000aMicro 23: inferior rib, medial margin, 1 frag, ESS\u000aMicro 24: superior rib, superior margin, 1 frag, ESS\u000amwb\u000aReports to: BERTAGNOLLI, MONICA, MARIE M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: SOFT TISSUE BIOPSY\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY W/REGIONAL LYMPH NODES\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SOFT TISSUE MASS OR SIMPLE EXCISION\u000a[report_end]
