VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast core needle biopsy\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ELISABETH P FROST M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-06-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Rachel E Factor, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Susan Lester, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, 8:00, 11 G ULTRASOUND GUIDED CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR A PALPABLE\u000aILL-DEFINED CYSTIC AREA:\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU involving areas of sclerosing adenosis.\u000aNodular sclerosing adenosis (at least REMOVED_DATE cm).\u000aApocrine cysts.\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies are performed with the following results for LCIS\u000a(block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu NEGATIVE\u000aE-cadherin NEGATIVE\u000aAn immunoperoxidase study for p63 and cytokeratin confirms the presence of\u000amyoepithelial cells in areas of LCIS.\u000aNote: The immunoperoxidase findings are typical for LCIS. Although there is a\u000acomplex pattern of adenosis and LCIS, no invasion is seen.\u000aA specific correlate for a mass forming lesion is not seen. Radiologic\u000acorrelation is suggested to ensure the biopsy is representative of the\u000aradiologic lesion.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 41 year old female with cysts and enhancement, right beast 8\u000ao'clock.\u000aOperation: 11-G ultrasound.\u000aOperative Findings: Cores obtained - directly visualized in area.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Cyst, rule out malignancy.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Cores in brown cassette.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit\u000anumber, and "right breast", and consists of a single brown cassette. Within\u000athe brown cassette, are multiple yellow/tan fibroadipose tissue cores (2.2 x\u000a1.4 x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate).\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Multi frags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000adfi/ag\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a12/21/2006\u000a[report_end]
