VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aLESTER, SUSAN, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A MASS:\u000aFocal dense interlobular stroma, correlating with the area of the\u000amammographic density.\u000aNote: No malignancy is seen after microscopic evaluation of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, 9:00, EXCISION:\u000aPHYLLODES TUMOR, intermediate grade (4.5 cm).\u000aApproximately 10% of the tumor stroma is hypercellular with moderate\u000anuclear pleomorphism.\u000aMitoses number up to 3 per 1 HPF.\u000aThe borders are well circumscribed.\u000aMinimal stromal overgrowth is present.\u000aNo heterologous elements are present. No necrosis is present.\u000aThe closest margin is posterior (0.2 cm). The remaining margins are\u000a> REMOVED_DATE cm from the tumor. Grossly, the tumor appeared to be very close to\u000amedial and inferior margins. However, on microscopic examination, these\u000aareas consist of dense breast tissue.\u000aNote: An unusual feature of this phyllodes tumor is that 90% of the\u000astroma shows very minimal cellularity.\u000aADDITIONAL INFERIOR MARGIN:\u000aApocrine metaplasia.\u000aNote: No phyllodes tumor is seen.\u000aADDITIONAL MEDIAL MARGIN:\u000aApocrine metaplasia.\u000aNote: No phyllodes tumor is seen.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: None given.\u000aOperation: Right breast wire localization @ 12 o'clock, right partial\u000amastectomy.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Phyllodes tumor @ 9 o'clock.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Wire localization @ 12 o'clock, right breast.\u000a2. 9 o'clock palpable phyllodes tumor. * Both specimens marked per protocol.\u000a3. Additional inferior margin. Black marks prior resection margin. Green is\u000anew true inferior margin.\u000a4. Additional medial margin. Black marks prior resection margin, orange marks\u000anew true medial margin.\u000aRADIOLOGY REPORT: Mass in specimen. Dr. Denison\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "2) 9 O'CLOCK PALPABLE PHYLLODES TUMOR" (FSA):\u000aOn macroscopic exam, tumor extends to within 1 mm of medial and inferior\u000amargins.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by CHANG,MARTIN C,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in three parts, labeled with the patient's name\u000aand unit number.\u000aPart one, "wire localization 12 o'clock right breast", consists of a single\u000afragment of breast tissue (4 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). There is a wire and a radiograph\u000ashowing the wire in relation to a mass. The mass in the mammogram corresponds\u000ato a white/tan, well-delineated, firm, homogenous mass (1.3 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm).\u000aThe mass abuts the superior, medial and anterior margins and is located REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom the inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior and 1 cm from the lateral margins.\u000aThe remainder of the breast parenchyma is mostly adipose tissue with no other\u000amasses or nodules present.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  mass, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  surrounding tissue and closest margins, multi frags, RSS.\u000aPart two, labeled "9 o'clock Phyllodes palpable tumor", consists of a single\u000afragment of breast tissue (9.2 cm from superior to inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm from medial\u000ato lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm from anterior to posterior). A yellow/tan firm nodule (4.5\u000ax REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) is present and is located REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial and inferior\u000amargins, REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin,\u000a0.8 cm from the superior margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior margin. The\u000aspecimen was sent to the Frozen Section Room for evaluation of margins.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  tumor and closest margins, multi frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  tumor, mult frags, RSS.\u000aPart three, "additional inferior margin", consists of a single fragment of\u000afibroadipose tissue (5.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The new margin is inked in green and\u000athe old margin is inked in black. No nodules or masses are present. The\u000aspecimen is entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  additional inferior margin, multi frags, ESS.\u000aPart four, "additional medial margin", consists of a single fragment of\u000afibroadipose tissue (4 x 3 x 1 cm). A tumor mass measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm\u000ais present and is adjacent to the new margin focally. The new margin is\u000aentirely submitted in longitudinal sections.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  new medial margin, multi frags, ESS.\u000afm\u000aReports to: LESNIKOSKI, BETH-ANN M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN\u000a[report_end]
