VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: DIANE C LOCKHART M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Ann K Folkins, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Andrea L Richardson, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A MASS:\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU (1.4 cm), solid, clinging and cribriform types,\u000aintermediate grade with focal necrosis and no calcifications, involving\u000asclerosing adenosis.\u000aNo definite invasive carcinoma seen (p63/keratin immunohistochemical stain\u000aexamined).\u000aDCIS is less than REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000aposterior margin (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), and REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID). The superior,\u000alateral, and anterior margins are negative for in situ carcinoma (>0.3 cm).\u000aFibroadenoma (0.7 cm).\u000aBiopsy site changes.\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for in situ carcinoma (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) POSITIVE (3+)\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000acarcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but only\u000aa portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in >10%\u000aof tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in\u000a>10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 48 year old woman, S/P U/S core bx of nodule seen on mammogram,\u000ainconclusive for DCIS. Recommended for needle loc excision.\u000aOperation: R needle localization breast biopsy.\u000aOperative Findings: Not provided.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: R abnl mammogram.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) R breast tissue to mammo (via frozen section room).\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000aClip and intact wire in specimen. Dr. Baldwin.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "right breast tissue", and consists of a tan/yellow lobulated portion of\u000afibroadipose breast tissue (4.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with a needle localization wire\u000aentering through the superior lateral aspect of the specimen and exiting\u000athrough the medial aspect of the specimen. The specimen has been previously\u000ainked per the surgeon via pathology protocol (superior/red, inferior/green,\u000amedial/orange, lateral/yellow, anterior/blue, and posterior/black) and is\u000aserially sectioned from lateral to medial. The cut surface is tan/yellow and\u000alobulated with focal areas of dense white fibrous tissue constituting\u000aapproximately 80% of the breast parenchyma. The specimen is received with a\u000aradiograph taking a metallic clip. There is an irregular red/brown granular\u000aarea within the dense white fibrous tissue (0.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) within which is\u000athe metallic clip, which comes within REMOVED_DATE cm of the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of\u000athe anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the inferior\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the medial margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm of the lateral margin. No\u000adiscrete lesions are grossly identified. The specimen is submitted in its\u000aentirety.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID; Sequential cross sections lateral to medial, block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID to include\u000ametallic clip, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin, 3 frags, ESS.\u000asek/lp\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Andrea L Richardson M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a11/27/2007\u000a[report_end]
