VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: DIANE C LOCKHART M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Scott Lovitch, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Xiaohua Qian, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. RIGHT BREAST, RE-EXCISION FOR SEROMA AND POSITIVE MARGINS ON PRIOR\u000aEXCISION":\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia (single focus, block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) involving sclerosing\u000aAdenosis; see NOTE.\u000aExtensive sclerosing adenosis.\u000aCore biopsy site.\u000aCalcifications in benign epithelium.\u000aFibroadenoma (0.3cm).\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000aB. RIGHT BREAST, EXCISION AND WIRE LOCALIZATION FOR ENHANCING AREA ON MRI":\u000aSclerosing adenosis, diffuse.\u000aFibroadenoma (0.8 cm).\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000aNOTE:\u000aImmunohistochemistry performed at BWH demonstrates the following staining\u000aprofile in lesional (ADH) cells:\u000aPositive - p63, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aNegative - HER-2/neu\u000aThe immunohistochemical profile supports the above diagnosis. This case was\u000aalso reviewed by Dr. Andrea Richardson, of Breast Pathology Service, who\u000aconcurs with the above diagnosis.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Known DCIS right needs re-excision, additional lesion seen on post-op\u000aMRI which has wire in it for excision today.\u000aOperation: Right breast partial mastectomy re-excision. R MRI guided wire loc\u000abreast biopsy.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: R DCIS.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. R re-excision seroma.\u000aB/2. R needle loc breast tissue.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Mass/wire in specimen. OR Called; DGS.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart A, "#1. Right reexcision seroma", consists of a breast excision (5.0 cm\u000asuperior to inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm anterior to posterior, REMOVED_DATE cm lateral to medial)\u000awith a skin ellipse (4.1 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) that is wrinkled and tan/white. There\u000ais a well-healed linear scar (3.6 cm). A long stitch designates lateral and a\u000ashort stitch designates superior. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol\u000afor the evaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red;\u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. The specimen is serially\u000asectioned from superior to inferior to reveal a stellate scar (2.6 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm) that extends to within REMOVED_DATE cm to the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to the medial\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm to the anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000ato the skin ellipse, REMOVED_DATE cm to the medial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to the lateral margin.\u000aOn further sectioning, there is a hemorrhagic, multiloculated cystic cavity\u000a(1.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) that is located REMOVED_DATE cm to the anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to\u000athe posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to the medial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to the lateral\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm to the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to the inferior margin, and REMOVED_DATE \u000acm from the skin ellipse.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Superior margin, perpendicular, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Specimen serially sectioned from superior to inferior, 1 frag\u000aeach, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Inferior margin, perpendicular, multi frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, "#2. Right needle localized breast tissue", consists of a wire\u000alocalized breast excision (1.6 cm anterior to posterior, REMOVED_DATE cm medial to\u000alateral, REMOVED_DATE cm superior to inferior) with a short stitch designating superior\u000aand a long stitch designating lateral. An accompanying specimen radiograph\u000ashows a localization wire entering the superolateral aspect of the specimen and\u000aexiting at the anterior/inferior/medial aspect. The localization wire\u000a(according to the specimen radiograph) is adjacent to an ill-defined mass\u000alesion near the medial aspect of the specimen. The specimen is serially\u000asectioned from lateral to medial to reveal a dense white firm area (4.1 x REMOVED_DATE x\u000a0.8 cm) and is located REMOVED_DATE cm to the lateral margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to the medial\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm to the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to\u000athe anterior margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm to the posterior margin. There is a small\u000ahemorrhagic area (1.4 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) that is located REMOVED_DATE cm to the inferior\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm to the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000ato the anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to the lateral margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm to the medial\u000amargin.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, perpendicular, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Specimen serially sectioned from lateral to medial, multi frags,\u000aESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin, perpendicular, multi frags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-07-REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000adcp/ag\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Xiaohua Qian M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a1/4/2008\u000a[report_end]
