VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aKRANE, JEFFREY, FRED, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by KRANE,JEFFREY FRED,M.D.,PH.D.\u000a#1. LEFT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A MASS:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA, LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU, AND NEGATIVE LYMPH NODE.\u000aSYNOPSIS:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA\u000aSize - REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aMultifocal? - No\u000aHistologic Type - Mixed ductal and lobular, with\u000apredominantly lobular features\u000aHistologic Grade (SBR) - II (moderate)\u000aNuclear Grade - Intermediate\u000aEIC - Negative\u000aLymphovascular invasion - Absent\u000aDermal lymphatic invasion - N/A\u000aSkin invasion - N/A\u000aSkeletal muscle invasion - N/A\u000aFinal Margins (invasive) -\u000aNegative (no ink on tumor) anterior, posterior, inferior,\u000asuperior, medial, lateral\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - Present\u000aOne lymph node in lateral portion of specimen with no tumor seen.\u000aOTHER FINDINGS\u000aColumnar alteration of lobules with prominent snouts and secretions, with\u000aatypia\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia with pagetoid spread\u000aFlorid epithelial hyperplasia\u000aCysts\u000aApocrine metaplasia\u000aCalcificiations in benign epithelium\u000aArterial calcifications\u000aCore biopsy site\u000aAJCC CLASSIFICATION - REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDc pREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID MX\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER/PR/HER-2) - Performed previously\u000a#2. LEFT BREAST, SUPERIOR SHAVE MARGIN:\u000aBenign breast tissue with no tumor seen.\u000a#3. LEFT BREAST, LATERAL SHAVE MARGIN:\u000aBreast tissue with atypical lobular hyperplasia, cysts, calcifications in\u000aassociation with benign epithelium and arterial calcifications.\u000aNo residual invasive carcinoma seen.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 76 yo female s/p 1999 R BCT for DCIS. S/p L u/s guided core biopsy\u000aof an ill-defined mammographically occult mass with pathology\u000arevealing invasive carcinoma with ductal & lobular features.\u000aOperation: L breast wire localization partial mastectomy, sentinel node\u000abiopsy.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: L breast cancer.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Left breast tissue, short stitch sueprior, long stitch\u000alateral, whip new margin.\u000a2. L breast tissue, superior shave margin, whip stitch new\u000amargin.\u000a3. L breast tissue, lateral shave margin, whip stitch new\u000amargin.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Mass in specimen. D.Smith,MD\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by HAHN,HEJIN P.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in three parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart one, labeled "#1 left breast tissue, short stitch, long stitch lateral,\u000awhip stitch chest wall margin", consists of a piece of breast tissue (6.0 x REMOVED_DATE \u000ax REMOVED_DATE cm) with two orienting suture that have been inked by the surgeon per\u000apathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior\u000a= blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange.\u000aThe specimen is accompanied by a radiograph and a radiologist reading "mass in\u000aspecimen". There is a firm, white area (1.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) that is REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom the closest superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the closest lateral margin, REMOVED_DATE \u000acm from the closest anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the closest inferior margin,\u000a0.8 cm from the closest posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the closest medial\u000amargin. The tumor area contains focal hemorrhage which likely represents the\u000aprior core biopsy site. Representative sections of the tumor were sent to the\u000atumor bank. Eighty (80%) percent of the specimen is firm, white fibrous\u000atissue. The entire specimen is submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  firm area with core biopsy site, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  adjacent sections, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  lateral margin, perpendicular, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  medial margin, perpendicular, multi frags, ESS.\u000aPart two, labeled "#2 left breast tissue, superior shave margin, whip stitch\u000anew margin", consists of a fragment of breast tissue (3.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with\u000aa stitch denoting new margin, which is inked blue. The old margin is inked\u000ablack. The specimen is serially sectioned revealing that the specimen is\u000aentirely composed of yellow/tan adipose tissue. The specimen is entirely\u000asubmitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  superior shave margin, multi frags, ESS.\u000aPart three, labeled "#3 lateral shave margin, whip stitch new margin", consists\u000aof two fragments of breast tissue (3.6 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm)\u000awith stitches on each piece designating new margin which is inked blue. The\u000aspecimen is serially sectioned revealing that it is composed entirely of\u000ayellow/pink, slightly hemorrhagic adipose tissue. The specimen is entirely\u000asubmitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  lateral shave margin, multi frags, ESS.\u000ahph\u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN\u000a[report_end]
