whip stitch at the chest wall margins. The\u000aspecimen is received per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins:\u000aposterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral\u000a= yellow; medial = orange. Examination of the specimen radiogram reveals no\u000abiopsy clip or calcifications within the specimen. The specimen measures REMOVED_DATE \u000a(S-I) x REMOVED_DATE (M-L) x REMOVED_DATE cm. It is submitted in its entirety in serial sections\u000afrom medial to lateral.\u000aMicro 1: medial edge, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  specimen in serial sections from medial to lateral, 1 frag each,\u000aESS.\u000aMicro 9&10: lateral edge, multi frags, ESS.\u000amcc\u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
