olors by the pathologist such that black = deep\u000amargin, blue = superior margin, green = inferior margin, orange = medial\u000amargin, and yellow = lateral margin. The breast parenchyma is sectioned to\u000areveal a red/tan, ill-defined indurated area (4.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) that\u000aapproaches to within REMOVED_DATE cm of the deep margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the inferior margin,\u000a2.5 cm of the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the medial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the\u000alateral margin and extends to immediately beneath the skin surface.\u000aRepresentative sections are submitted for histologic examination.\u000aMicro 1: tumor mass (quick fix section), 1 frag, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  deep margin, 2 frags, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  deep margin (including skeletal muscle), 2 frags, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  medial margin, 2 frags, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  lateral margin, 2 frags, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  inferior margin, 2 frags, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  superior margin, 2 frags, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  tumor, 3 frags, RSS\u000aMicro 17: tumor deep to skin, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 18: nipple, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 19: 2 potential axillary lymph nodes, 2 frags, ESS\u000adk\u000aReports to: BERTAGNOLLI, MONICA, MARIE M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY W/REGIONAL LYMPH NODES\u000a[report_end]
