ly sectioned to\u000areveal a well-healed biopsy cavity (0.6 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), containing white\u000asemi-solid material, and a metallic surgical clip. The cavity is less than REMOVED_DATE \u000acm from the medial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000ainferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior\u000amargin and REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior margin. The remaining cut surface displays\u000a85% white fibrous tissue, and 15% yellow lobulated adipose tissue, with no\u000aadditional discrete masses or lesions identified. The specimen is sequentially\u000asubmitted in its entirety.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Anterior margin, radially, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross sections from anterior to posterior, with the\u000acavity in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, and the surgical clip in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 2 frags each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: posterior margin, radially, 3 frags, ESS.\u000acp/lp\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Deborah A Dillon M.D., Electronically signed on Saturday\u000aREMOVED_MONTH 07, 2009 at 01:56:33PM\u000a[report_end]
