ctions of margins\u000aare submitted for microscopic examination. Serial sectioning reveals a\u000apartially cystic mass (1.1 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), with tan/yellow solid areas and\u000aa single cystic cavity. The mass is REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior resection margin\u000aand REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior resection margin. This specimen is entirely\u000asequentially submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  left breast tissue, multiple frags, ESS.\u000aPart two, labeled "Left breast cyst wall", consists of one partially cauterized\u000afragment of tan soft tissue (3.4 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). One surface of the\u000aspecimenis pink and smooth consistent with cyst wall lining.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  left breast cyst wall, 10 frags, ESS.\u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
