VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Amend/Addenda\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast core needle biopsy\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: SUGHRA RAZA M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000a********** Addended Report ***********\u000aResident: Mariana A. Stoleru, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Deborah A Dillon, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, LOWER OUTER, 11 G STEREOTACTIC CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR\u000aCALCIFICATIONS:\u000aCARCINOMA IN SITU, solid type (intermediate to high nuclear grade), with focal\u000aassociated calcification, is present.\u000aATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA is present.\u000aCalcifications associated with columnar cell change and microcysts.\u000aNOTE: The majority of the calcifications are present in association with\u000acolumnar cell change and microcysts.\u000aImmunohistochemical analysis for estrogen receptor, progesterone receptor, and\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu will be performed and reported in an addendum.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHISTORY: New R breast Ca++.\u000aBREAST IMAGING FINDING:\u000a1. Right: 3 mm and calcifications.\u000aLOCATION:\u000a1. Right: lower outer\u000aTYPE OF CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY:\u000a1. 11G Stereotactic\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000a1. 11G Stereotactic; A - with Ca+; B - no Ca++ - Brown cassette.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit\u000anumber, and "Stereo Rt brown", and consists of cores of fibroadipose tissue,\u000areceived in two brown cassette, each with a brown lid, A CA++ (1.7 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm) and B (1.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm).\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Right breast brown cassette A cores, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Right breast brown cassette B cores, multi frags, ESS.\u000aDB/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Deborah A Dillon M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM (9/01/08):\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for in situ carcinoma (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor NEGATIVE (rare cells weakly positive)\u000aProgesterone receptor NEGATIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) NEGATIVE (1+)\u000aNote: Normal epithelial cells are appropriately immunoreactive for estrogen\u000aand progesterone receptors.\u000aImmunohistochemistry for E-cadherin demonstrates absence of membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity in the in situ carcinoma. Morphology and immunophenotype\u000asupport classification as CARCINOMA IN SITU with ductal and lobular features.\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000ainvasive carcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low > 0% - < 10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor cells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but only a\u000aportion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+):Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in >10% of\u000atumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+):Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in >30% of\u000atumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aExternal controls are evaluated and show appropriate Immunoreactivity.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aAddendum #1 by Deborah A Dillon M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
