cal record number.\u000aPart A, labeled "#1. Right total mastectomy - short stitch, superior and long\u000astitch, lateral", consists of a mastectomy specimen (915.0 grams, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000asuperior to inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm medial to lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm anterior to posterior)\u000awith skin ellipse (8.5 x REMOVED_DATE cm) with areola (3.0 x REMOVED_DATE cm) and with everted\u000anipple (1.0 cm in diameter x REMOVED_DATE cm in height). There are two orienting\u000asutures with short superior and long lateral per surgeon. The deep aspect of\u000athe specimen is inked black. There is a cavity, which is opened to both the\u000adeep/posterior and anterior aspect of the specimen with an opening measuring\u000a3.2 x REMOVED_DATE cm with the anterior-posterior dimension measuring REMOVED_DATE cm. The\u000acavity is located in the central outer aspect of the specimen and is lateral to\u000athe lateral aspect of the skin ellipse. Sectioning the specimen reveals no\u000aother lesions. The specimen is approximately 10% fibrous and 90% adipose\u000atissue. In addition, there are separately received attached fragments of\u000afibroadipose tissue (9.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate). No lymph nodes or\u000askeletal muscle are grossly identified. The cavity is entirely submitted for\u000ahistologic evaluation.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Nipple, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial aspect of cavity with skin in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Superior aspect of cavity, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Inferior aspect of cavity with skin in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 1 frag each,\u000aESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral aspect of cavity with skin in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Upper outer, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Upper inner, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lower outer, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lower inner, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aPart B, labeled "#2. Right breast skin", consists of an ovoid donut-shaped\u000afragment of skin (outer ovoid dimension REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE and inner ovoid dimension\u000a9.7 x REMOVED_DATE cm, with width range, REMOVED_DATE to REMOVED_DATE cm, and depth up to REMOVED_DATE cm). There\u000ais a well-healed linear scar (2.5 cm) that extends to skin edge. The deep\u000aaspect of the specimen is inked blue.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Scar, 5 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Additional representative sections of skin, 3 frag, RSS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aGL/ag\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Xiaohua Qian M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000aWednesday February 25, 2009 at 08:21:50PM\u000a[report_end]
