VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST MASTECTOMY - PARTIAL OR SIMPLE\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aLODA, MASSIMO, F., M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by LODA,MASSIMO F.,M.D.\u000a1) RIGHT BREAST, SIMPLE MASTECTOMY (727g):\u000aBreast parenchyma with fibrocystic change and cysts.\u000aSkin with cicatrix.\u000aBiopsy site with repair reaction and small fibroadenoma.\u000aMicrocalcifications (Block 5) are seen in association with benign breast\u000aparenchyma.\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy.\u000a2) RIGHT BREAST, MEDIAL FLAP:\u000aBreast parenchyma with no significant pathologic change.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 46 year old post-menopausal female, not on hormones whose REMOVED_DATE \u000amammograms and ultrasound demonstrated 2 nodule areas in the right\u000abreast. Core biopsy revealed a fibroadenoma and a fibroadenoma\u000aversus phyllodes tumor. On REMOVED_DATE  excision revealed phyllodes\u000atumor.\u000aOperation: Right simple mastectomy\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Pre-op, right phyllodes tumor.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Right breast, short suture/superior; long suture/lateral\u000a2. Right breast, medial flap\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by LIGON,KEITH LLOYD,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in two parts, labeled with the patient's name\u000aand unit number.\u000aPart one, "1, right breast", is a single 727 gram simple mastectomy specimen\u000a(22 x17 x 4 cm) with a tan skin ellipse 4 x 4 cm and nipple areolar complex REMOVED_DATE \u000acm in diameter and a nipple REMOVED_DATE cm in diameter. There is a well-healed scar at\u000athe upper-outer quadrant of the skin ellipse which is REMOVED_DATE cm in length.\u000aThere is a short suture superior and a long suture lateral. The specimen\u000acontains a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm clear fluid filled biopsy cavity in the lateral\u000athird of the breast. The biopsy cavity has areas of fibrosis around it with\u000afat necrosis. The biopsy cavity is REMOVED_DATE cm from the deep resection margin, REMOVED_DATE \u000acm from the skin surface, REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000asuperior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral and REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin.\u000aThere is a single portion of skeletal muscle REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm on the deep\u000aaspect of the specimen. The biopsy cavity is REMOVED_DATE cm from the portion of\u000askeletal muscle. No masses or suspicious lesions are noted. The breast\u000aparenchyma is mostly fatty. Note - REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior non-skin resection\u000amargin.\u000aMicro 1: nipple, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 2: scar with biopsy cavity, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 3: anterior resection margin with cavity, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 4: anterior resection margin with cavity, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  deep margin with cavity, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  superior margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  inferior margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  medial margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  lateral margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 15: deep margin with skeletal muscle, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 16: upper-inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 17: lower-inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 18: upper-outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 19: lower-outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aPart two, "2, right breast superior medial flap" are multiple fragments of\u000ayellow fibroadipose tissue (7 x 4 x 1 cm in aggregate) with no lymph nodes or\u000agross lesions identified. The entire specimen is submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  right breast, superior medial flap, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aReports to: KAELIN, CAROLYN, MARY M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY - PARTIAL OR SIMPLE\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
