VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aBRODSKY, GILBERT, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by BRODSKY,GILBERT,M.D.\u000a1) SPECIMEN LABELED "RIGHT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED PARTIAL MASTECTOMY":\u000aBenign breast tissue with epithelial hyperplasia, apocrine metaplasia,\u000acysts, stromal fibrosis, prior biopsy site, and focal intraductal\u000apolarizable crystalline material consistent with calcium oxalate.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000a2) SPECIMEN LABELED "RIGHT BREAST, DUCT, EXCISION":\u000aLactiferous duct with mild periductal chronic inflammation and mild duct\u000aectasia.\u000aApocrine metaplasia.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 42-year-old premenopausal female, not on hormone with right breast\u000abloody nipple discharge and a cluster of calcifications. REMOVED_DATE  ductogram\u000ademonstrates moderate duct dilitation and stricturing. REMOVED_DATE  core biopsy\u000afor calcifications.\u000aOperation: Right breast wire localized partial mastectomy and right breast\u000aduct excision.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal right mammogram.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Right breast wire localized partial mastectomy.\u000a2. Right breast duct excision, stitch divided duct inking per pathology\u000aprotocol.\u000aCa++ clip in specimen/JL.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by BARRY,MARC,MB,BCH,BAO\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart one, labeled "#1, right breast wire loc, partial mastectomy", is received\u000atogether with specimen mammogram showing calcifications, clip in specimen\u000alocalization needle. The specimen consists of a fragment of fibrofatty tissue,\u000a2.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. There is a wire localization needle and clip present in\u000aspecimen. Sections of the specimen show hemorrhage and fibrosis. The specimen\u000ais serially sectioned from superior to inferior and submitted in toto for\u000amicroscopic examination. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the\u000aevaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red;\u000ainferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. Specimen X-rays of blocks\u000awere taken for calcifications.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  right breast tissue with clip in block 2, 11 frags, ESS.\u000aPart two, labeled "#2, right breast duct excision, stitch on divided duct,\u000ainking per pathology protocol", consists of fragments of fibrous tissue, REMOVED_DATE x\u000a1.5 x REMOVED_DATE cm with a stitch at one aspect (inked blue). The specimen is inked\u000aper pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior = black;\u000aanterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial =\u000aorange. The specimen sectioned and submitted in toto for microscopic\u000aexamination.\u000aMicro 8: anterior portion, longitudinal sections, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  transverse sections from anterior to posterior, 12 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 14: posterior, longitudinal sections, 2 frags, ESS.\u000amab\u000aReports to: KAELIN, CAROLYN, MARY M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
