VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Sentinel Lymph Nodes(s)\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Astrid Weins, M.D., Ph.D.; Martin C Chang, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Jason L Hornick, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. LEFT SENTINEL LYMPH NODES (including REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aPlease see Part B.\u000aB. LEFT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZATION FOR A MASS AND A CLIP AND SENTINEL LYMPH NODE\u000aBIOPSY (Parts A and B):\u000aINVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aNEGATIVE LYMPH NODES\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA\u000aSize - REMOVED_DATE cm and REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aMultifocal - Yes (slides REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID; see NOTE)\u000aHistologic type - Lobular\u000aHistologic grade (SBR) - II (Moderate) (6 to 7 points)\u000aTubules - < 10% (3 points)\u000aNuclear grade - Intermediate (2 points)\u000aMitotic counts - 1 point\u000aEIC - Not applicable\u000aLVI - Absent\u000aDermal LVI - Not applicable\u000aSkin invasion - Not applicable\u000aSkeletal muscle invasion - Not applicable\u000aSpecimen margins (invasive); see separately submitted final lateral margin\u000aNegative (> REMOVED_DATE cm) - Medial, anterior, posterior, superior,\u000ainferior\u000aClose (0.1 to REMOVED_DATE cm) - Lateral (0.2 cm; focal); see below for\u000afinal margin\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU - Absent\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - Present (extensive)\u000aLYMPH NODES\u000aSentinel lymph nodes - Negative (3 H&E levels examined)\u000aNumber of positive nodes - 0\u000aNumber of nodes examined - 2\u000aTOTAL POSITIVE NODES (all specimens)- 0:2\u000aOTHER FINDINGS\u000aCore biopsy site\u000aCalcifications in benign epithelium\u000aAJCC Classification (6th edition) - REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDc REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID (sn) MX (with multiple foci of\u000ainvasion)\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER, PR, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) - Performed previously at BWH\u000aNOTE: Two (2) distinct foci of invasive lobular carcinoma are seen. The\u000asmaller focus is well-differentiated. An E-cadherin immunostain demonstrates\u000aloss of membranous staining in both invasive and in-situ lobular carcinoma. In\u000athe main excision specimen, the biopsy cavity is REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral\u000amargin. However, the separately submitted final lateral margin is evaluated in\u000aPart C.\u000aC. LEFT BREAST, LATERAL SHAVE MARGIN:\u000aBreast tissue, negative for tumor.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 70 year old female with a history of ADH, REMOVED_DATE  mammogram\u000asupplemental with L U/S demonstrates a 1 cm solid mass. REMOVED_DATE  core biopsy\u000arevealed grade II IDC ER+, PR low +, Her2/neu 2+, FISH not amplified.\u000aOperation: Left breast wire localized lumpectomy, sentinel node mapping, biopsy\u000aand possible level I and II dissection.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast cancer.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Left sentinel lymph node - hot and blue x 2.\u000aB/2. Left breast tissue - short stitch superior/long stitch lateral/whip stitch\u000ain chest wall margin to mammo/tissue bank.\u000aC/3. Left breast lateral shave margin, whip stitch new margin.\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "LEFT SENTINEL LYMPH NODES, HOT AND BLUE" (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aTwo (2) lymph nodes negative for tumor.\u000aOR Consultation by: Jeffrey Fred Krane, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aResident: Leona A. Doyle, M.D., Cheryl Adackapara, M.D.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Intact wire, with mass and clip present. J. Wang/C. Denison\u000aIntact wire with mass and clip present. J. Wang/C. Denison\u000aThe senior physician certifies that he/she personally conducted a gross and/or\u000amicroscopic examination of the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed\u000athe rapid diagnos(es) related thereto.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in three parts, each part labeled with the\u000apatient's name and medical record number.\u000aPart A, labeled "#1. Left sentinel lymph node hot and blue x2", consists of two\u000afragments of tan/red fibroadipose tissue (4.6 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x\u000a0.3 cm), each containing one firm blue lymph node, the largest measuring REMOVED_DATE x\u000a1.0 x REMOVED_DATE cm, with extensive fatty replacement. The largest lymph node is\u000abisected and entirely submitted in the frozen section room as REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000a(each containing one-half). The smaller lymph node (0.6 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) is\u000aentirely submitted in the frozen section room as REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID remnant, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID remnant, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID remnant, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Non-frozen fibroadipose tissue, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aPart B, labeled "#2. Left breast tissue, short stitch superior, long stitch\u000alateral, whip stitch chest wall margin", consists of a wire localized excision\u000a(9.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), oriented by the surgeon with a short stitch designated\u000asuperior, a long stitch designated lateral, and a whip stitch designated chest\u000awall margin. The specimen is previously inked by the surgeon and is oriented\u000ain the frozen section room. The wire is removed after reviewing the specimen\u000aradiograph. Please note: As described in the frozen section room, the whip\u000astitch is found on the blue (anterior) rather than the black (posterior) aspect\u000aof the specimen. This discordance was discussed with the surgeon in the frozen\u000asection room. The specimen is also difficult to orient as the ink has\u000aextensively run on the specimen.\u000aA solid white/tan mass (1.1 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) is identified REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000alateral, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior, REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior, REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000aanterior, REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial and REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin. A biopsy\u000acavity containing a clip is identified within the lesion. The clip is removed.\u000aA portion of the tumor was taken for protocol REMOVED_DATE in the frozen section\u000aroom. The specimen is submitted from superior to inferior with the biopsy\u000acavity in cassette REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. Approximately 60% of the specimen are submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Superior margin, 2 frags each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE frags each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Biopsy cavity to lateral margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Posterior + medial margin near biopsy cavity, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Representative sections of inferior, medial, posterior and\u000alateral margins, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Superior margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Posterior and medial margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aPart C, labeled "#3. Left breast lateral shave margin - whip stitch new\u000amargin", consists of a disrupted fragment of fibroadipose tissue (18.0 x REMOVED_DATE x\u000aup to REMOVED_DATE cm). According to the specimen label, the specimen is supposed to be\u000aoriented with a whip stitch designated as new margin. However, this stitch is\u000anot found attached to the specimen, thus orientation is not possible. The\u000aspecimen is inked black in its entirety and serially sectioned. Note: The\u000amain, more solid portion of the specimen is submitted in cassettes REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID,\u000aattached fibroadipose tissue is found in cassettes REMOVED_DATE \u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Serial sections, REMOVED_DATE frags each, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aawe/ag\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jason L Hornick M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000aFriday May 29, 2009 at 12:17:25PM\u000a[report_end]
