VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: KATHARINE CARTER M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Samuel P. Wyche, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Xiaohua Qian, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. RIGHT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZATION, EXCISIONAL BIOPSY FOR A MASS AND A CLIP:\u000aBenign breast tissue with a nodular area (1.0 cm) of adenosis adjacent\u000ato the core biopsy site.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the\u000aspecimen, including margins.\u000aA double stain for p63/REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID demonstrated positive staining for\u000amyoepithelial cells.\u000a(Levels examined.)\u000aNOTE: Selected slides (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) were also reviewed by Dr. S. Lester,\u000aBreast Pathologist, who concurs.\u000aThe immunoperoxidase, immunofluorescence and in-situ hybridization tests\u000aperformed at Brigham and Women's Hospital were developed and their performance\u000acharacteristics determined by the Immunohistochemistry Laboratories in the\u000aDepartment of Pathology at BWH. They have not been cleared or approved by the\u000aU.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA). The FDA has determined that such\u000aclearance or approval is not necessary.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: History of abnormal mammogram - 1 cm nodule right superior breast core\u000abiopsy REMOVED_DATE  - Path dense stroma felt to be discordant with imaging and\u000aexcisional bx recommended by radiologist - clip left.\u000aOperation: Right mammographically directed breast biopsy.\u000aOperative Findings: Not provided.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal mammogram right breast.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Right breast @ 12 o'clock (mammo) - short superior, long lateral.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Clip in specimen - E. P. Frost.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "right breast tissue short stitch superior long stitch lateral", consists\u000aof an irregular tan-yellow lobulated portion of fibroadipose breast tissue (5.4\u000acm medial to lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm superior to inferior, and REMOVED_DATE cm anterior to\u000aposterior) with a short suture designating superior margin, long suture\u000adesignating lateral margin. There is a new localization wire in place, which\u000aenters through the lateral anterior aspect of the specimen and exits through\u000athe posterior aspect of the specimen. The specimen is inked per pathology\u000aprotocol (superior red, inferior green, medial large, lateral yellow, anterior\u000ablue, and posterior black) and is serially sectioned from medial to lateral.\u000aThere is a well-circumscribed dense white smooth fibrous previous biopsy cavity\u000afilled with a tan-white granular surgical material. Within the previous biopsy\u000acavity is a silver metallic previous biopsy clip. The biopsy cavity (1.0 x REMOVED_DATE \u000ax REMOVED_DATE cm) comes within REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000aposterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin. The\u000aremainder of the breast parenchyma is tan-yellow homogenous with no additional\u000alesions or areas of disruption grossly identified. There are focal areas of\u000adense white fibrous tissue, which constitutes approximately less than 10% of\u000athe breast parenchyma. The specimen is serially sectioned and submitted in its\u000aentirety.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross sections medial to lateral block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID to\u000ainclude biopsy cavity, block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID to include area of metallic biopsy clip, 1\u000afrag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aSEK/mgd/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Xiaohua Qian M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000aThursday REMOVED_MONTH 16, 2009 at 03:37:49PM\u000a[report_end]
