EMOVED_DATE cm from the superior, REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior, REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000aanterior, REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial and REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000ainferior margin. REMOVED_DATE cm medial to this nodule is a second nodule white/tan,\u000awhich is also well circumscribed (0.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), and REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000aanterior REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior, REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial, REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000asuperior, REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin. The\u000anodules are grossly consistent with fibroadenomas. 70% of the specimen was\u000asubmitted for microscopic evaluation.\u000aMicro #1: Anterior margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro #2: Lateral and posterior margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro #3-6: Fragments likely containing the microcalcifications, first nodule\u000apresent in Micro #3 and 5, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000aMicro #7: Second nodule, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro #8: Medial, posterior and inferior margins, related to second nodule,\u000a1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro #9: Additional second nodule, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro #10; Medial posterior and anterior margins related to second nodule,\u000a1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro #11: Additional second nodules, 1 frag, RSS.\u000apal/\u000aReports to: CARTER, KATHARINE M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
