s a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: See prior core biopsy path. Atypical hyperplasia left breast.\u000aOperation: Left breast\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast mass\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Left breast mass - to mammo\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by SANTAGATA,SANDRO,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aRADIOLOGY REPORT:\u000aClip, calcification, wire in specimen.\u000aThe specimen, received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit\u000anumber, and "left breast mass", consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm breast\u000aexcision specimen with a localizing (by radiograph) a radiopaque nodule, clip\u000aand calcifications. On section the tip of the wire is localized in fibrous\u000adense tissue (1.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). Along the Path of the localizing wire is\u000aa lobulated, yellow/white, firm nodule (0.6 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm likely represent\u000afat necrosis. The entire specimen is sectioned and entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE - path of wire along nodule, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 3 - site of tip of wire and firm tissue, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 4 - non-wired localized tissue, 6 frags, ESS.\u000aReports to: REILLY, RAYMOND, JOHN, M.B.B.C.H.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
