e receptor POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) NEGATIVE (0)\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000acarcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but\u000aonly a portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity\u000ain >10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: DCIS - (L) breast. This is a re-excision for margins.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Wide re-excision\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by KINDELBERGER,DAVID W.,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, medical record\u000anumber, "Wide re-excision", and consists of a single fragment of\u000ayellow/tan/pink fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE cm from lateral to medial x\u000a6.5 cm from anterior to posterior x REMOVED_DATE cm from superior to inferior. A short\u000ablack suture was placed by the surgeon to indicate the superior aspect of the\u000aspecimen and a long black suture was placed by the surgeon to indicate the\u000alateral aspect of the specimen. On the anterior surface of the specimen is an\u000airregular fragment of pink skin (3.5 x REMOVED_DATE cm) with a well-healed, linear scar\u000a(1.8 cm in length). The specimen is inked by the pathologist per pathology\u000aprotocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue;\u000asuperior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. Serial\u000asectioning reveals a central area of white/tan to focally yellow fibrous tissue\u000a(1.1 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) which focally abuts the inked superior margin and\u000aapproaches to within REMOVED_DATE cm of the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the anterior\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the medial margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aof the lateral margin. Multiple small (less than REMOVED_DATE cm) punctate hemorrhages\u000aare present throughout the specimen. No additional lesions are grossly\u000aidentified. The specimen is composed of approximately 80% adipose tissue and\u000a20% fibrous tissue. The entire specimen is submitted for histologic\u000aevaluation.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Left breast tissue (from medial to lateral), multi frags, ESS.\u000adk\u000aReports to: IGLEHART, JAMES, DIRK M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
