VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Amend/Addenda\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: JULIE L JONES M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000a********** Addended Report ***********\u000aResident: Shakti Ramkissoon, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: William R Welch, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "LEFT BREAST WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION":\u000aBreast tissue with biopsy site changes, scarring, and\u000asclerosing adenosis.\u000aB. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "LEFT BREAST, ADDITIONAL MEDIAL TISSUE":\u000aBreast tissue with apocrine metaplasia, sclerosing\u000aadenosis, fibroadenoma (0.5 cm), and scarring.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 31 year old woman with breast enhancement on left breast MRI and\u000adiscordant core biopsy demonstrating sclerosing adenosis.\u000aOperation: Left breast MRI-guided wire-localized excisional biopsy.\u000aOperative Findings: Not provided.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal left breast MRI.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) left breast wire-localized excision with short stitch/superior, long\u000astitch/lateral - to mammo.\u000aB/2) left breast additional medial tissue, short stitch/superior, long in new\u000amedial margin - to mammo.\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000aSpecimen #1 - MRI loc: no mammo correlate. Clip not in specimen.\u000aC. Denison, M.D.\u000aSpecimen #2 - Enhancing area MRI with prior core bx tissue marker. Tissue\u000amarker present in specimen. C. Denison, M.D.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart A, "#1. Left breast wire localized excision, short stitch superior, long\u000astitch lateral", consists of a REMOVED_DATE (anterior to posterior) x REMOVED_DATE (medial to\u000alateral) x REMOVED_DATE (inferior to superior) cm breast excision with two localization\u000awires in placed and a short suture marking the superior margin and a long\u000asuture marking the lateral margin. An accompanying specimen radiograph\u000ademonstrates two areas of hyperlucency, which are associated with the\u000alocalization wires. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the\u000aevaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red;\u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. The anterior and posterior\u000aaspects of the specimen are removed and submitted as perpendicular sections.\u000aThe remaining specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a single tan/white firm\u000airregular area (1.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) located REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin,\u000aabuts the lateral margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000aposterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin, and abuts the inferior\u000amargin. The specimen is entirely submitted for histologic analysis.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Anterior aspect of the specimen, perpendicular sections, multi\u000afrags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Posterior aspect of the specimen, perpendicular sections, multi\u000afrags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Cross section of specimen, bisected, 1 frag per cassette, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Cross section of specimen, bisected, 1 frag per cassette, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Serial sections of specimen, 1 frag per cassette, ESS.\u000aPart B, "#2. Left breast additional medial tissue, short superior, long stitch\u000aon new medial margin", consists of a single breast excision specimen, measuring\u000a8.2 cm superior to inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm anterior to posterior, REMOVED_DATE cm lateral to\u000amedial, and containing a short stitch designating the superior margin and a\u000along stitch designating the medial margin. The superior and inferior aspects\u000aof the specimen are removed and submitted as perpendicular sections and the\u000aremaining specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a tan/yellow unremarkable\u000acut surface. The specimen is entirely submitted for histologic analysis.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Superior aspect of the specimen, perpendicular sections, multi\u000afrags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Inferior aspect of the specimen, perpendicular sections, multi\u000afrags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Serial sections of the specimen, multi frags, ESS.\u000aSRK/lp\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-08-REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by William R Welch M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000aAddendum\u000a(Documents margin evaluations)\u000aA. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "LEFT BREAST WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION":\u000a- There is no evidence of malignancy, including margins.\u000aB. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "LEFT BREAST, ADDITIONAL MEDIAL TISSUE":\u000a- There is no evidence of malignancy, including margins.\u000aAddendum #1 by William R Welch M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
