VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final Type: Surgical Pathology Pathology Report: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID OPERATION DATE: 27 REMOVED_MONTH 00 ACCESSIONED ON: 27 REMOVED_MONTH 00 at 12:07 CLINICAL DATA: Known left breast cancer. Need ER/PR and Her to be done on B. =============================================================================== *** FINAL DIAGNOSIS *** LYMPH NODE (LEFT AXILLARY SENTINEL), EXCISION: NO TUMOR SEEN IN REMOVED_DATE NODE SUBMITTED. CYTOKERATIN STAINS ARE NEGATIVE. BREAST (LEFT), EXCISIONAL BIOPSY: INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA. SEE TABLE #1. LOBULAR NEOPLASIA (LCIS). TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS #1 INVASIVE CARCINOMA Tumor size: REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. Grade: 3 Lymphatic vessel invasion: Not identified. Blood vessel invasion: Not identified. Margin of invasive carcinoma: The distance to all margins measure REMOVED_DATE cm. or greater. BREAST (LEFT), INFERIOR FINAL MARGIN: THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. FIBROCYSTIC CHANGE. BREAST (LEFT), POSTERIOR FINAL MARGIN: THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. FIBROCYSTIC CHANGE. Diagnosis by: Grace T. McKee,MD Signed On: 03 AUG 00 at 07:02 Consulting Pathologist(s): Frederick Carl Koerner, M.D. =============================================================================== *** BREAST CANCER IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum *** RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast (Left, block D): The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein. The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein. The tumor cells show moderate overexpression of HER-2/c-erbB-2. See note. Note: These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital. They have not been cleared or approved by the U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA). The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary; this laboratory has established and verified the test's accuracy and precision. Added by: Atul Kumar Bhan, M.D. Signed On: 04 AUG 00 at 16:20 Consulting Pathologist(s): Grace T. McKee,MD GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab, labeled with the patient's name and unit number, are four parts: Labeled "left axillary sentinel node" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm tan-red lymph node which is bivalved and submitted in toto in cassette A. Labeled "left breast" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm oriented breast excision containing two sutures designated long = lateral, short = superior. The specimen is externally unremarkable. It is inked as follows: black, superior; blue, inferior. The specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm firm, ill defined, white mass which comes to within REMOVED_DATE cm of the inferior margin centrally and REMOVED_DATE cm of the anterior margin centrally. Dr. Gadd examined the gross specimen. The remaining breast parenchyma (away from the mass) is unremarkable fibrofatty tissue. Representative sections of the specimen are submitted as follows: B: Mass in relation to closest (inferior) margin. C: Mass in relation to anterior margin. D: Representative section of the mass in the inferior and central portion of the specimen. E: Representative section of the mass in the posterior and central portion of the specimen. F: Representative section of the mass in the anterior and central portion of the specimen. G: Representative section of the mass in the inferior and medial portion of the tissue sample. H: Representative section of fibrofatty breast tissue away from the tumor mass in the medial portion of the specimen. Labeled "left breast final inferior margin" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm portion of breast tissue which is externally unremarkable. A stitch marks the edge furthest away from the tumor. The specimen is inked as follows: the surface which was furthest away from the tumor is inked in black; the opposite surface (which was closest to the tumor) is inked in blue. The specimen is sectioned to reveal gray-white to focally tan, firm tissue. The specimen is submitted entirely in cassettes I through L. Labeled "left breast final posterior margin" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm portion of breast tissue which is externally unremarkable. A stitch marks the edge which was furthest from the tumor. The surface which was furthest from the tumor is inked in black, and the opposite surface (which was closest to the tumor) is inked in blue. The specimen is sectioned to reveal unremarkable yellow, fibrofatty breast tissue. It is submitted entirely in cassettes M through Q. Resident: JOHN BRANDA, MD =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT - REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID REPORTS TO: Michele Annette Gadd, M.D. Christopher Lee Forthman, M.D. PART A: LYMPH NODE(LEFT AXILLARY SENTINEL),EXCISION PART B: BREAST (LEFT),EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART C: BREAST (LEFT),INFERIOR FINAL MARGIN PART D: BREAST (LEFT),POSTERIOR FINAL MARGIN\u000a[report_end]
