ved inked by the surgeon per pathology protocol for the\u000aevaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red;\u000ainferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. Sectioning reveals\u000amultiple nodules which are firm and associated with areas of white fibrotic\u000atissue as well as areas of focal hemorrhage. The specimen is entirely\u000asubmitted.\u000aMicro 1&2: superior margin, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  inferior, anterior and posterior margins, 5 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 7&8: inferior and posterior margins, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 9&10: lateral margins, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  remaining tissue including medial margins, 7 frags, ESS.\u000ajeb\u000aReports to: LESNIKOSKI, BETH-ANN M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
