D_DATE cm from the\u000aanterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin.\u000aThis area corresponds to the area of concern and the accompanying radiograph.\u000aThe specimen is sequentially submitted in its entirety.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin, radially, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross section, containing the cervical clip, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross section, from medial to lateral, 2 frags each,\u000aESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, radially, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000acp/ag\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jeffrey F Krane M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a2/2/2008\u000a[report_end]
