VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Sentinel Lymph Nodes(s)\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: MEHRA GOLSHAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Stefan Kraft, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: William R Welch, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aSPECIMEN DESIGNATED "RIGHT BREAST, EXCISION WIRE-LOCALIZATION FOR A MASS AND A\u000aCLIP (specimen B), AND SENTINEL NODE BIOPSY (specimen A):\u000aINVASIVE ADENOID CYSTIC CARCINOMA\u000aNEGATIVE LYMPH NODES\u000aSYNOPSIS:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA\u000aSize - REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aMultifocal - no\u000aHistologic Type - adenoid cystic\u000aHistologic Grade (SBR) - II (moderate)\u000aNuclear Grade - intermediate\u000aEIC - N/A\u000aLymphovascular invasion - absent\u000aDermal lymphatic invasion - N/A\u000aSkin invasion - N/A\u000aSkeletal muscle invasion - N/A\u000aFinal Margins (invasive)\u000aNegative (>0.3 cm) - anterior, lateral, superior, inferior\u000aClose (0.1-0.3 cm) - posterior (0.1 cm).\u000aVery close (<0.1cm from margin)- medial\u000aNOTE: Final posterior and medial margins in specimens C and D.\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU - absent\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - absent\u000aLYMPH NODES\u000aSentinel Lymph Nodes - negative (3 H&E levels examined)\u000aNumber of positive nodes - 0\u000aNumber of nodes examined - 3\u000aTOTAL POSITIVE NODES (all specimens)- 0:3\u000aOTHER FINDINGS\u000aCore biopsy site\u000aAprocine metaplasia\u000aAJCC CLASSIFICATION (6th edition) - REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDc pREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID MX\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER/PR/HER-2) - performed previously\u000aSPECIMEN DESIGNATED "RIGHT BREAST, FINAL MEDIAL MARGIN" (specimen C):\u000aADENOID CYSTIC CARCINOMA.\u000aFinal medial resection margin is negative for tumor (>0.3 cm).\u000aSPECIMEN DESIGNATED "RIGHT BREAST, FINAL POSTERIOR MARGIN" (specimen D):\u000aBreast tissue, negative for tumor.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 77-year-old female with right breast invasive adenoid cystic\u000acarcinoma, ER/PR/HER-2/neu negative, status post image-guided core biopsy.\u000aOperation:\u000a1. Right axilla sentinel node biopsy.\u000a2. Right breast wire localized lumpectomy.\u000aOperative Findings: Not given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast invasive adenoid cystic carcinoma.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Right axilla sentinel node biopsy.\u000aB/2. Right breast wire localized lumpectomy\u000ashort suture superior, long suture lateral (mammo).\u000aC/3. Right breast final medial margin suture on margin.\u000aD/4. Right breast final posterior margin suture on margin.\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000aMass & clip & intact wire in specimen. Discussed with Dr. Golshan. MN - REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in four parts, labeled with the patient's name,\u000aand medical record number.\u000aPart A, "#1. Right axilla sentinel node biopsy", consists of a single fragment\u000aof yellow/tan fibroadipose tissue (3.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). Three pink/tan,\u000arubbery, lymph nodes with focal bluish discoloration are identified (up to REMOVED_DATE \u000acm in greatest dimension).\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 lymph node candidate, bisected, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 2 lymph node candidates, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, "#2. Right breast wire localized lumpectomy short suture superior, long\u000asuture lateral", consists of a wire localized breast excision specimen (6.5 x\u000a2.0 cm). The specimen is accompanied by a radiograph, which shows a mass,\u000aclip, and intact wire in the specimen. There are two orienting sutures (long\u000aequals lateral; short equals superior). The specimen is inked per pathology\u000aprotocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue;\u000asuperior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. There is a REMOVED_DATE x\u000a1.6 x REMOVED_DATE cm, firm white mass with associated biopsy cavity, which is located\u000a0.2 cm from the deep, REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior, REMOVED_DATE \u000acm from the medial, REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior\u000amargin. Photographs of the specimen are taken. Representative sections of two\u000amass had been submitted for tissue banking.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Mass and posterior margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Mass and medial/superior margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Mass and inferior margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Mass in medial margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Remainder of mass, 2 frags each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Anterior and inferior margins, 3 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Superior and posterior margins, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aPart C, "#3. Right breast final medial margin suture on margin", consists of a\u000asingle fragment of yellow/tan fibroadipose tissue (1.9 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with an\u000aorienting suture on the final margin. No masses or lesions are identified\u000agrossly. The final margin is inked in blue and the opposite surface is inked\u000ain black.\u000aThe entire specimen is submitted for microscopic analysis.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Final medial margin, 7 frags, ESS.\u000aPart D, "#4. Right breast final posterior margin suture on margin", consists of\u000aa single fragment of tan/yellow fibroadipose tissue (1.9 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with\u000aan orienting suture designating the final posterior margin. Final posterior\u000amargin is inked in blue and the opposite surface is inked in black. The entire\u000aspecimen is submitted for microscopic analysis.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Final posterior margin, 6 frags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aSK/ajb\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by William R Welch M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
