VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Sentinel Lymph Nodes(s)\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: BETH ANN LESNIKOSKI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-05-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Jey-Hsin Chen, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Jason L Hornick, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. SENTINEL NODE #1, LEFT (including FSA):\u000aOne (1) lymph node with no tumor present (3 HE levels examined).\u000aB. LEFT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISIONAL BIOPSY (WIRE #3), ULTRASOUND\u000aIRREGULAR LESION AT 4:00:\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU.\u000aSclerosing adenosis.\u000aCalcifications in benign epithelium.\u000aC. LEFT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISIONAL BIOPSY (WIRE #2), CORE BIOPSY-PROVEN\u000aCANCER AT 3:00:\u000aINVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aSYNOPSIS:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA\u000aSize - REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aMultifocal - no\u000aHistologic Type - lobular\u000aHistologic Grade (SBR) - II (moderate)\u000aNuclear Grade - low\u000aEIC - negative\u000aLymphovascular invasion - absent\u000aDermal lymphatic invasion - N/A\u000aSkin invasion - N/A\u000aSkeletal muscle invasion - N/A\u000aFinal Margins (invasive)\u000aNegative (>0.3 cm) - posterior, lateral, superior, inferior\u000aClose (0.1-0.3 cm) - anterior (multifocal; REMOVED_DATE 2 cm)\u000aPositive (ink on carcinoma) - medial (focal)\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU - absent\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - present\u000aAJCC CLASSIFICATION (6th edition) - REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDc pREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID MX\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER/PR/HER-2) - performed previously\u000aD. LEFT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISIONAL BIOPSY (WIRE #1), MRI LOC FOR\u000aABNORMAL ENHANCEMENT:\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU.\u000aApocrine metaplasia, cysts, and papilloma.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Left breast cancer (specimen #2/was #3), abnormal ultrasound 3 mm\u000alesion (specimen #3/wire #2), abnormal MRI (specimen #4/wire #1).\u000aOperation: #1. Sentinel node biopsy.\u000a#2. Left wire localization biopsy - irregular ultrasound lesion 4 o'clock.\u000a#3. Left partial mastectomy with wire, #4. Left wire localization biopsy (MRI\u000alocalization).\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast cancer.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000a#1. Sentinel node #1 Left (FS).\u000a#2. Wire #3 (mammo) ultrasound irregular lesion 4:00.\u000a#3. Wire #2 (mammo) core biopsy proven cancer 3:00.\u000a#4. Wire #1 (mammo) - MRI localization for abn\u000aRADIOLOGY: Three specimens with wire within. Dr. (illegible)\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "SENTINEL NODE #1" (FSA):\u000aOne (1) lymph node negative for tumor.\u000aOR Consultation by: JASON L. HORNICK, M.D., PH.D.\u000aResident: JOANNA A GIBSON, PH.D., M.D.\u000aThe senior physician certifies that he/she personally conducted a gross and/or\u000amicroscopic examination of the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed\u000athe rapid diagnos(es) related thereto.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in four parts, each labeled with the patient?s\u000aname, unit number.\u000aPart A, labeled "#1. sentinel node #1 Left", is one fibroadipose tissue (2 x\u000a1.5 x REMOVED_DATE cm). The specimen is dissected revealing one lymph node (1.3 x REMOVED_DATE x\u000a0.3 cm) which is entirely submitted for frozen section analysis labeled "FSA".\u000aThe entire specimen including the non frozen soft tissue is submitted.\u000aMICRO REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: FSA remnant, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMICRO REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Non frozen section soft tissue, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, labeled "wire #2. specimen #3, irregular nodule at 4:00", is a\u000afibrofatty tissue (3.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) previously inked by the surgeon for the\u000ahistologic evaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red;\u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. In place is a wire which enters\u000athe inferior portion of the specimen at its lateral edge and exits the specimen\u000aat the medial edge. An accompanying mammogram bearing the patient's name and\u000aunit number and a green sticker labeled "#2" demonstrates a wire in place\u000awithin the specimen and an irregular nodule. The specimen is serially sectioned\u000afrom lateral to medial demonstrating a yellow/tan firm nodule (0.4 cm) in the\u000amedial-most section, which extends to within REMOVED_DATE cm of the closest inferior and\u000amedial margins. The remainder of the specimen is comprised of predominantly\u000ayellow/tan fatty tissue, grossly unremarkable (10% fibrous). No other\u000aabnormalities are grossly appreciated. The specimen is entirely submitted.\u000aMICRO REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral most sectioned, perpendicular, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMICRO REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Serial sections from lateral to medial, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMICRO REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial most sectioned, perpendicular, containing nodule, 2 frags ESS.\u000aPart C, labeled "#3. wire specimen #2, core biopsy proven cancer at 3", is a\u000afibrofatty tissue (4.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), previously inked by the surgeon for the\u000ahistologic evaluation of margins. The specimen is not accompanied by a wire. An\u000aaccompanying mammogram bearing the patient's name and unit number and a green\u000asticker labeled "#3", demonstrates tissue changes consistent with a core biopsy\u000asite. The specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral revealing a\u000afirm white/tan well circumscribed mass (1.3 cm) located in the medial portion\u000aof the specimen and extending to within less than REMOVED_DATE cm of the media margin,\u000aless than REMOVED_DATE cm of the anterior margin, less than REMOVED_DATE cm of the posterior\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the closest inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the closest superior\u000amargin, and greater than 2 cm from the lateral margin. The lesion occupies\u000aapproximately 30% of the specimen, with the remainder of the specimen comprised\u000aof yellow/tan fibrofatty tissue (approximately 20% fibrous). The tumor is\u000aentirely submitted.\u000aMICRO REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #1, medial most section, perpendicular, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMICRO REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #2, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMICRO REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #3, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMICRO REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #4, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMICRO REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #5, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMICRO REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #9, containing core biopsy site, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMICRO REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #10, containing core biopsy site, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMICRO REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #11, lateral most slice, perpendicular, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aPart D, labeled "#4. wire #1 MRI guided localization", is a fibrofatty tissue\u000a(4 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) received inked by the clinician for the histologic\u000aevaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red;\u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. In place is a wire that enters\u000athe specimen at the lateral surface, and directly medially to the exit at the\u000amedial surface. An accompanying mammogram bearing the patient's name and unit\u000anumber and a green sticking labeled "#4" reveals a focal area of\u000amicrocalcifications within the specimen. The specimen is serially sectioned\u000afrom medial to lateral to reveal a focal area of blue dye infiltrating the\u000ainferior surface. There is a focal fibrous area (1.1 cm) in the middle of the\u000aspecimen which contains a cyst (0.4 cm) and areas of focal yellow microscopic\u000adiscoloration. The fibrous area extends to the inferior surface and extends to\u000awithin REMOVED_DATE cm of the superior surface, REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior surface, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aof the superior surface, REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial surface, and greater than 1 cm\u000afrom the lateral surface. The fibrous area occupies approximately 30% of the\u000aspecimen. The remainder of the specimen is comprised of unremarkable yellow\u000afatty tissue (10% fibrous tissue). The specimen is entirely submitted.\u000aMICRO REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial most slice, perpendicular, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMICRO REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Serial sections from medial to lateral with fibrous area contained\u000ain blocks REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID through REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 7 frags, ESS.\u000aMICRO REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral most slice, perpendicular, 6 frags, ESS.\u000aJhc/ag\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Jey-Hsin Chen M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jason L Hornick M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a3/16/2005\u000a[report_end]
