VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aRICHARDSON, ANDREA, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by RICHARDSON,ANDREA,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, NEEDLE LOCALIZED BIOPSY:\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN-SITU, micropapillary type, low nuclear grade with\u000aassociated calcifications.\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN-SITU arises as scattered foci in a background of\u000aatypical ductal hyperplasia and columnar alteration of lobules with\u000aprominent snouts and secretions, involving an area measuring at least\u000a0.5 cm.\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN-SITU is present in REMOVED_DATE blocks (#2-5).\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN-SITU is within <0.1 cm of anterior margin (#3-4) and\u000ais REMOVED_DATE cm from lateral margin (#2). Other margins are >0.3 cm.\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN-SITU, extensive.\u000aCysts.\u000aCore biopsy site.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: None given.\u000aOperation: Right breast needle localization biopsy.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal mammogram, right breast microcalcifications.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Right breast needle localization biopsy, short suture\u000asuperior, long suture lateral.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by MILNER,DANNY A.,JR.,M.D.\u000aReceived is a single container, labeled with the patient's name, medical record\u000anumber and designating "right breast needle localization biopsy" which contains\u000aa single fragment of fibroadipose tissue which has been inked per the surgeon\u000ain the following manner: red - superior, green - inferior, yellow - lateral,\u000aorange - medial, black - anterior, blue - posterior (short suture superior,\u000along suture lateral). The specimen measures REMOVED_DATE cm from superior to inferior,\u000a5.5 cm from anterior to posterior, and REMOVED_DATE cm from medial to lateral. An\u000aaccompanying radiograph identifies microcalcifications which are located\u000aanteriorly and a clip which is located inferiorly. The specimen is serially\u000asectioned from anterior to posterior to reveal a biopsy site cavity which\u000ameasures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm and is hemorrhagic. A previous biopsy clip is\u000aidentified. The specimen is entirely submitted from anterior to posterior.\u000aMicro 1: most anterior aspect of specimen, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  serial sections of specimen, REMOVED_DATE frags each, ESS.\u000aMicro 9: section of specimen containing clip, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  remainder of serial sections from anterior to posterior, 1 or 2\u000afrags each, ESS.\u000adam\u000aReports to: WHANG, EDWARD, E. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
