VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: JULIE L JONES M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-06-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Eric L Snyder, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Gilbert Brodsky, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA/1 SPECIMEN LABELED "RIGHT BREAST, EXCISION":\u000aBreast tissue with focal atypical ductal hyperplasia, papillomas,\u000aepithelial hyperplasia, calcifications associated with benign\u000aepithelium, and biopsy site changes.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the\u000aspecimen, including margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Abnormal right mammogram with mass LUQ; core biopsy benign but no\u000afeatures of mass-forming lesion.\u000aOperation: Right breast wire localized excisional biopsy.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast mammographic mass.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Right breast wire localized excision, short stitch superior, long stitch\u000alateral.\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000aSpecimen contains clip, density tissue.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "#1 - rt breast wire localized excision", and consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm excision of fibroadipose tissue, oriented by sutures designating superior\u000a(short suture) and lateral (long suture) margins. The specimen is inked per\u000apathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black;\u000aanterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange\u000a(inked by prosector). Specimen is received along with a radiograph\u000ademonstrating a localizing wire in place within the specimen and an area of\u000adensity and associated metallic clip. Sectioning demonstrates an ill-defined\u000a11.9 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm firm fibrous lesion with central cavitation and surrounding\u000afat necrosis (compatible with prior core biopsy site), and containing a REMOVED_DATE cm\u000ametallic clip. Lesion appears grossly to abut the inferior margin and\u000aapproaches within REMOVED_DATE cm of the closest medial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the closest\u000alateral margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the closest superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the closest\u000aposterior margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm of the closest anterior margin. Specimen is\u000aentirely submitted, sequentially from anterior to posterior (area of interest\u000ain REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, clip in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Entire specimen, sequentially from anterior to posterior,\u000amultiple frags. ESS [Note: Micros: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - anterior, superior,\u000alateral; REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - superior, inferior, medial,\u000alateral; REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - superior, inferior, lateral, posterior; and, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - posterior].\u000adb/lp\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Gilbert Brodsky M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
