VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST MASTECTOMY - PARTIAL OR SIMPLE\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aKRANE, JEFFREY, FRED, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by KRANE,JEFFREY FRED,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, SIMPLE MASTECTOMY:\u000aPHYLLODES TUMOR, intermediate nuclear grade (3.1 cm).\u000aThe stroma is highly cellular with moderate nuclear pleomorphism.\u000aNo stromal overgrowth is seen.\u000aMitoses number up to 59 per 10 HPF's.\u000aFocal invasion into adjacent stroma is present.\u000aNo heterologous elements or necrosis are seen.\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia is present within the phyllodes tumor, but not\u000ain adjacent breast tissue.\u000aThe deep margin is free of tumor.\u000aThe phyllodes tumor is associated with biopsy site changes.\u000aNipple and skin with cicatrix.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Phyllodes tumor - malignant.\u000aOperation: Right simple mastectomy\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Cystosarcoma phyllodes, sarcoma right breast\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1. Right breast (long stitch superior; short stitch lateral)\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by REIMANN,JULIE DYLAN REGAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in one part, labeled with the patient's name,\u000aunit number and "#1. right breast (long stitch superior, short stitch lateral",\u000aand consists of a 522 gram (post fixation weight) simple mastectomy specimen\u000a(18.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with a short stitch indicating lateral and a long stitch\u000aindicating superior, with a tan skin ellipse (15.0 x REMOVED_DATE cm) with a brown\u000aareola (4.6 x REMOVED_DATE cm) and everted nipple (1.3 x REMOVED_DATE cm). The deep margin is\u000ainked black and the specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a tan/pink to gray\u000alobulated firm circumscribed mass (3.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) located REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000ainferior skin margin and REMOVED_DATE cm from the deep margin at the junction of upper\u000ainner and lower inner quadrants. A representative section of tumor and normal\u000atissue are submitted to the tissue bank. The remainder of the breast tissue is\u000acomposed of approximately 40% fibrous tissue, the rest is adipose tissue. No\u000aaxillary tail is present and careful dissection of the specimen does not reveal\u000aany lymph nodes. There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm mildly erythematous healing lesion\u000aon the skin ellipse just over to the tumor mass. Representative sections are\u000asubmitted for histologic examination.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  tumor with closest overlying skin, 1 frag each, RSS (#2 also\u000acontains healing scar on skin)\u000aMicro 3: additional section of tumor, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 4: closest deep margin to tumor, 1 frag, ESS\u000aMicro 5: fibrous tissue from UIQ, 2 frags, RSS\u000aMicro 6: fibrous tissue from LIQ, 2 frags, RSS\u000aMicro 7: fibrous tissue from UOQ, 2 frags, RSS\u000aMicro 8: fibrous tissue from LOQ, 2 frags, RSS\u000aMicro 9: representative section of nipple, 1 frag, RSS\u000ajdr\u000aReports to: BERTAGNOLLI, MONICA, MARIE M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY - PARTIAL OR SIMPLE\u000a[report_end]
