argins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green;\u000alateral/yellow; medial/orange (inked by surgeon). A localizing wire enters the\u000ainferior/anterior surface and exits medially. A blue bow-tie suture is present\u000aanteriorly, marking "divided ducts". This divided duct margin is removed and\u000asubmitted en face. The remaining specimen is sectioned from medial to lateral.\u000aAn accompanying radiograph demonstrates a localizing wire in placed adjacent to\u000aa metallic surgical clip in the medial aspect of the specimen. Sectioning in\u000athis area reveals a palpably firm ill-defined tan/white lobulated lesion (at\u000aleast REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), grossly abutting the medial margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000athe closest inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from closest anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000athe closest posterior margin, and remote (greater than REMOVED_DATE cm) from the\u000aremaining margins. Remaining specimen is comprised predominantly of lobulated,\u000acystic-appearing fibrous tissue (at least 85%), without additional palpable\u000alesions or visible masses grossly. The entire specimen is submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Duct margin, en face, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Remaining sequential cross sections from medial to lateral, with\u000aperpendicular medial margin in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, perpendicular lateral margin in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aand REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, and area of interest in micro cassette REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, multi frags,\u000aESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000adb/ag\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Hejin 