re identified in the lateral portion of the specimen, the largest\u000ameasuring REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest dimension.\u000aMicro 1&2: fibrous tissue with hemorrhage (area with clip), 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 3: fibrous tissue, right upper quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 4: fibrous tissue, right lower quadrant including deep margin, 1\u000afrag, RSS.\u000aMicro 5: fibrous tissue, left lower quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 6: fibrous tissue, left upper quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 7: nipple, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 8: largest lymph node, bisected, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 9: 2 lymph node candidates, 2 frags, ESS.\u000abgl\u000aReports to: CHRISTIAN, ROGER, L. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY W/REGIONAL LYMPH NODES\u000a[report_end]
