VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: JULIE L JONES M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-06-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Matthias D. Hofer, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Jason L Hornick, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia, columnar alteration of lobules with\u000aprominent snouts and secretions, focal epithelial hyperplasia, cysts,\u000aand apocrine metaplasia.\u000aCalcifications associated with benign epithelium.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the entire\u000aspecimen, including margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: ALH on core needle biopsy for ca++.\u000aOperation: Right breast wire-localized excisional biopsy.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: ALH on core biopsy right breast.\u000aORGANS/TISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Right breast wire-localized excision, short superior, long lateral\u000ato mammo.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Notified Dr. J. Jones @ 11:20 a.m. - clip, few round calcs, + wire\u000aincluded in specimen.\u000aDr. S. Raza and Dr. M. Noroozian\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "Right breast, long lateral, short superior", and measures S-I REMOVED_DATE cm, M-L\u000a1.7 cm, A-P REMOVED_DATE cm. Two sutures are attached, per surgeon: the long suture\u000adesignates the lateral margin, and the short suture designates the superior\u000amargin. There is a wire crossing the whole specimen from anterior to posterior.\u000aThe specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins:\u000aposterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow;\u000amedial/orange. The specimen is serially sectioned from anterior to posterior\u000ainto twelve sections. The clip was recovered in the sixth section. The\u000aspecimen is entirely submitted for histologic review.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 1 and 2, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 3 and 4, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 5, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 6 (clip), 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 7, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 8, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 9, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 10, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 11, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 12, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMDH/mmm\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jason L Hornick M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a8/25/2006\u000a[report_end]
