VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST MASTECTOMY - PARTIAL OR SIMPLE\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOGINO, SHUJI, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by OGINO,SHUJI,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, SIMPLE MASTECTOMY:\u000aRESIDUAL HIGH GRADE PHYLLODES TUMOR (2.5 cm), with prominent necrosis,\u000aadjacent to prior biopsy cavity.\u000aHeterologous liposarcomatous differentiation is present.\u000aMitoses number 22:10 HPF.\u000aThere is hypercellularity and marked nuclear atypia.\u000aDeep margin is free of tumor.\u000aNo skin or skeletal muscle invasion is present.\u000aApocrine cysts in non-neoplstic breast tissue.\u000aNOTE: This case has been reviewed by Dr. A. Richardson, Breast Pathology,\u000awho concurs.\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: by OGINO,SHUJI,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe residual tumor is grossly REMOVED_DATE cm away from the closest deep margin.\u000aThe diagnosis remains unchanged.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 48 year-old female status post (R) breast excision\u000aof a REMOVED_DATE cm mass (Bangor, ME) demonstrating a\u000ahigh grade phyllodes tumor with positive margins.\u000aPrevious surgery: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aOperation: Right simple mastectomy.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: (R) breast phyllodes tumor.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1. Tissue (R) breast (short stitch superior, long\u000astitch lateral, bowtie at palpable lymph node).\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by RUCKER-SCHMIDT,RACHEL L.,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "#1. Tissue (R) breast (short stitch superior, long stitch lateral, bowtie\u000aat palpable LN", and consists of a 1311 gm, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm right\u000amastectomy specimen, clinically right simple mastectomy. The attached REMOVED_DATE x\u000a11.5 cm tan/white skin ellipse demonstrates a REMOVED_DATE cm unremarkable nipple with\u000asurrounding REMOVED_DATE cm diameter areolar. There is a REMOVED_DATE cm curvilinear well-healed\u000ascar along the inferior border of the areolar (6 o'clock). The deep fascial\u000aplane is inked black, a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm fragment of fibromuscular tissue is\u000anoted, adherent to the deep margin in the lower inner/lower mid region.\u000aSectioning demonstrates a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm smooth walled cavity,\u000aapproximately REMOVED_DATE cm subjacent to the previously described scar and REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000athe closest deep margin. The intervening tissue between the skin and anterior\u000acavity wall demonstrates a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm tan/white firm ill-defined\u000alesion, possibly consistent with residual tumor. Remaining specimen is\u000acomprised of tan/white fibrinous tissue (60%), areas of which exude a thick,\u000atan/yellow fluid (particularly upper inner quadrant), REMOVED_DATE cm from previously\u000anoted lesion. Additionally, there is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm circumscribed nodule\u000awithin the lower outer quadrant, REMOVED_DATE cm from the closest deep margin. There\u000aare no additional lesions or other abnormalites noted grossly. Sutures are\u000apresent, designating superior, lateral and "palpable lymph node". Sutured\u000aaxillary tissue is dissected for lymph nodes.\u000aMicro 1: Nipple, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 2: Scar and subjacent tumor, cavity wall, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Cavity wall and associated tumor, 2 frags total, RSS.\u000aMicro 5: Closest deep margin, (1 frag with closest fibromuscular tissue),\u000a2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 6: Representative upper inner quadrant, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 7: Representative upper outer quadrant, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Representative lower outer quadrant, (micro 9 is previously\u000adescribed nodule and closest deep margin), 2 frags each, RSS.\u000aThere are no lymph nodes identified within the sutured axillary tissue.\u000adb\u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY - PARTIAL OR SIMPLE\u000a[report_end]
