VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Amend/Addenda\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: J. GREGORY KANE M.D.\u000aCASE: BG-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000a********** Addended Report ***********\u000aResident: Qinghong Yang, M.D., Ph.D.; Rachel L Rucker-Schmidt, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Andrea L Richardson, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. LEFT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A PRIOR BIOPSY SITE AND\u000aCALCIFICATIONS:\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, solid and papillary types, (intermediate nuclear\u000agrade), is present in three (3) of six (6) blocks, involving an area of REMOVED_DATE cm\u000a(as measured off a glass slide).\u000aDCIS is associated with calcifications and necrosis.\u000aDCIS is present at the anterior margin (focal, block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) and is present less\u000athan REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin (multifocal, blocks REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aDCIS is present REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin (focal, block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, see NOTE) and\u000a0.2 cm from the inferior margin (focal, block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aThe superior and posterior margins are negative (>0.3) for DCIS.\u000aColumnar cells changes.\u000aNOTE: Biopsy site changes are present and extensively involve the inferior and\u000amedial margins.\u000aImmunohistochemical analysis for estrogen receptor, progesterone receptor, and\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu will be performed and reported in an addendum.\u000aAJCC Classification (6th edition): Tis NX MX.\u000aB. LEFT BREAST, "ADDITIONAL TISSUE SUPERIOR TO SPECIMEN #1, SUTURE AT ASPECT\u000aCLOSEST TO SPECIMEN #1:"\u000aBiopsy site changes are present.\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy.\u000aC. LEFT BREAST, TISSUE "SUPERIOR AND LATERAL TO SPECIMEN #1 WITH SUTURE ON\u000aASPECT CLOSEST TO SPECIMEN #1:"\u000aBiopsy site changes are present.\u000aColumnar cell changes are present.\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy.\u000aD. LEFT BREAST, "TISSUE DEEP TO SPECIMEN #1:"\u000aSclerosing adenosis.\u000aApocrine cysts.\u000aColumnar cell changes.\u000aBiopsy site changes are present.\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy.\u000aE. LEFT BREAST, "TISSUE DEEP TO SPECIMEN #1:"\u000aColumnar cell changes.\u000aBiopsy site changes are present.\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 56 years old female with left breast calcifications. Previous core\u000abiopsy - atypical ductal hyperplasia and recommendation for surgical biopsy.\u000aOperation: Left wire localized breast resection.\u000aOperative Findings: Small hematoma from previous core biopsy.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast calcifications.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000a1. Left breast tissue (short stitch superior, long stitch lateral)\u000a2. Additional left breast tissue superior to specimen #1 aspect closest to\u000aspecimen #1\u000a3. Superior & lateral to specimen #1 with suture on aspect closest to specimen\u000a#1\u000a4. Tissue deep to specimen #1\u000a5. Tissue deep to specimen #1\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000aSpecimen with wire and CA# but not clip that was localized. The 2nd U-shaped\u000aclip is present.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in five parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and medical record number.\u000aPart A, "left breast tissue (short stitch superior, long stitch lateral)",\u000aconsists of a breast excision specimen (4.0 anterior to posterior x REMOVED_DATE \u000asuperior to inferior x REMOVED_DATE cm medial to lateral) with a short suture marking\u000athe superior margin and a long suture marking the lateral margin. There is a\u000alocalization wire enter the specimen from the anterior side and exits the\u000aspecimen from the lateral side. An accompanying radiograph showed a tight\u000acluster of calcifications at the anterior inferior side of the specimen and a\u000au-shaped metal clip at the inferior posterior portion of the specimen. The\u000aspecimen is inked per pathology protocol: red = superior, green = inferior,\u000ayellow = lateral, medial = orange, anterior = blue, posterior = black. There.\u000aThe specimen is serially sectioned from posterior to anterior into eleven\u000aslices (posterior margin slice #1 and anterior margin slice #11). The specimen\u000ais composed mostly of an ill-defined tan/pink fibrous tissue with punctate\u000ahemorrhage and a scant amount of tan/yellow adipose tissue (less than 5%). The\u000afibrous tissue appears to abut all margins. The specimen is serially sectioned\u000afrom posterior to anterior into 11 slices (posterior margin = slice #1 and\u000aanterior margin = slice #11).\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: slice #1, the posterior margin, perpendicularly sectioned,\u000amulti frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #2 to #4, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #5 to #6, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #7 to #8, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #9 to #10, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #11, the anterior margin, perpendicularly sectioned, multi\u000afrags, ESS.\u000aPart B, "additional left breast tissue superior to specimen #1, suture at\u000aaspect closest to specimen #1", consists of a tan/yellow adipose tissue (3.0 x\u000a1.5 x REMOVED_DATE cm) with a suture marking the aspect closest to specimen #1 (old\u000asuperior margin). The old superior margin is inked black and the opposite,\u000anew/true superior margin is inked blue. The specimen is composed of almost\u000a100% of tan/yellow adipose tissue. The specimen is serially sectioned and\u000asubmitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Additional left breast tissue superior to specimen #1, multi\u000afrags, ESS.\u000aPart C, "superior lateral to specimen #1 with suture on the aspect closet to\u000aspecimen #1", consists of a tan/pink/yellow fibroadipose tissue (2.0 x REMOVED_DATE x\u000a0.4 cm) with a suture marking the aspect closest to specimen #1 (old margin,\u000ainked black). The opposite, true margin is inked blue. 95% of the specimen is\u000acomposed of tan/pink fibrous tissue. It is serially sectioned and submitted\u000aentirely for microscopic examination.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Left breast tissue, lateral superior to specimen #1, 9 frags, 3\u000afrags in each block, ESS.\u000aPart D, "tissue deep to specimen #1", consists of three tan/yellow/pink\u000afibroadipose tissue (1.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm).\u000aThe outer surface of the three fragments is inked blue. The largest fragment\u000ais composed of about 85% of fibrous tissue and 15% adipose tissue. The two\u000asmaller fragments are composed almost entirely of tan/yellow adipose tissue.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: tissue deep to specimen #1, multiple frags, ESS.\u000aPart E, "tissue deep to specimen #1", consists of three tan/pink/yellow\u000afibroadipose tissue (1.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm). The outer surface of all three fragments is inked blue.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: tissue deep to specimen #1, multiple frags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: BG-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Andrea L Richardson M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a3/18/2008\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM:\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for DCIS (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) NEGATIVE (1+)\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000ainvasive carcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low > 0% - < 10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor cells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but only a\u000aportion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+):Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in >10% of\u000atumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+):Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in >30% of\u000atumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aExternal controls are evaluated and show appropriate Immunoreactivity.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aAddendum #1 by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
