VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID:REMOVED_CASE_ID Report Status: Signed\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aADDENDUM REPORT\u000aAddendum #1 Entered: REMOVED_DATE -1032\u005cE\u000aE\u005c\u000a*** ADDITIONAL DIAGNOSTIC INFORMATION ***\u000aThis report contains an addendum to the original for the purpose of providing\u000aadditional diagnostic information. The original diagnosis is unchanged.\u000aPer the surgeon, specimen B should be designated lateral margin rather than\u000amedial margin.\u000aAddeundum Signed Electronically Signed ROSS,MICHAEL J. M.D. REMOVED_DATE \u000aDIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. Left breast, upper inner quadrant, excision:\u000aDuctal carcinoma in situ, grade REMOVED_DATE \u000aFibrocystic changes.\u000aB. Left breast, medial margin, re-excision:\u000aIntraductal papilloma; ductal hyperplasia; fibroadenoma (1.2 cm.); duct\u000aectasia; fibrocystic changes.\u000aNo ductal carcinoma in situ seen.\u000aSYNOPTIC REPORT - DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aAJCC pTNM CLASSIFICATION (6TH Ed.)(Based on available surgical material:\u000apTis(DCIS) pNX pMX\u000aHISTOLOGIC TYPE: solid, comedocarcinoma, and\u000amicropapillary\u000aTUMOR SITE: left breast, upper inner quadrant\u000aHISTOLOGIC GRADE (Nuclear): intermediate (Grade 2) to high (Grade 3)\u000aTUMOR SIZE (greatest dimension): multifocal, spanning 4 cm. (largest focus\u000a1.9 cm.)\u000aNECROSIS: present, comedo\u000aMICROCALCIFICATIONS: present within DCIS\u000aRESECTION MARGINS: DCIS close to margin (0.1-0.2 cm.):\u000aInferior margin focally in specimen A\u000a(section REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aDCIS close to margin (<0.1 cm.):\u000aDCIS extends multifocally to within REMOVED_DATE \u000acm. of the junction of the anterior and\u000ainferior margin in specimen A (sections\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID)\u000aIMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING (for the DCIS):\u000aPrior specimen (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) reported as:\u000aEstrogen receptor: POSITIVE (>10% of nuclei stained)\u000aOTHER FINDINGS: fibrocystic changes\u000achanges consistent with prior biopsy site\u000aPRIOR RELATED SPECIMENS REVIEWED:\u000aSITE: Left breast, needle biopsy DATE: REMOVED_DATE  NUMBER: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aFinal Diagnosis by: Michael J. Ross, M.D.\u000aClinical diagnosis & history:\u000aLeft breast carcinoma\u000aTissue-Designation:\u000aA.Breast, excision with margins - left upper inner quadrant\u000aB.Breast, excision with margins - left breast, re-resection\u000aGross description:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in two parts.\u000aSpecimen A labeled "left breast lumpectomy, inner upper quadrant" consists of a\u000a62 gram, REMOVED_DATE x 8 x 4 cm. portion of partially yellow adipose, partly firm,\u000atan-pink tissue. The specimens have been previously marked by the surgeon as\u000afollows: anterior, green; inferior, blue; lateral, orange; medial, yellow;\u000aposterior, black; superior, red. A needle wire is present entering the\u000aanterior aspect of the specimen. Cut section reveals a REMOVED_DATE x 2 x REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000airregular portion area of hemorrhage and firm, white tissue located near the\u000ainferior and anterior margin. Cut section otherwise reveals predominantly\u000ayellow adipose tissue with small foci of firmer white tissue. The specimen is\u000aserially sectioned from medial to lateral, labeled REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. 32 agg.\u000aThe specimen clip is identified on the specimen mammogram near the entrance of\u000athe needle wire.\u000aTotal fixation time is 76 hours.\u000aSpecimen B labeled "re-resection left breast lumpectomy" consists of a 52 gram,\u000a6 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. portion of partly yellow adipose, partly firm, tan-pink\u000atissue. The specimen has been previously inked by the surgeon as follows:\u000aanterior, green; inferior, blue; lateral, orange; medial, yellow; posterior,\u000ablack; superior, red. Cut section reveals firm, tan-white, rubbery tissue\u000aadmixed with yellow adipose tissue. The firmer tissue is superior.\u000aThe specimen is serially sectioned from superior to inferior, labeled REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000a32 agg.\u000aTotal fixation time is 76 hours.\u000aDictated by: MJR____(signature on file)____DENNIS J. FEEN, M.D. REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a____(signature on file)____MICHAEL J. ROSS, M.D. REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a[report_end]
