the larger\u000atumor and negative (1+) on the smaller tumor\u000aEstrogen receptor (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, Ventana Medical Systems) and/or progesterone\u000areceptor (PgR 1REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, Ventana Medical Systems) is assessed visually by\u000aquantitation of the percent of tumor cells staining.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID (4REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, Ventana Medical Systems, FDA approved) is assessed by\u000aquantitation of the percent and intensity of tumor cells staining.\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU (DCIS):\u000a-histologic type: solid and cribriform patterns\u000a-histologic grade: intermediate\u000a-size (greatest dimension): microscopic foci within and around both the\u000ainvasive tumors\u000a-extent: multifocal\u000a-extensive intraductal component: absent\u000a-necrosis in DCIS: present, focal\u000a-microcalcifications in DCIS: present, focal\u000a-margins for DCIS: ductal carcinoma in situ is less than 1 mm.\u000afrom the deep margin along a broad front\u000anear the area of the larger tumor in the\u000aupper inner quadrant.\u000aLYMPH NODES:\u000aPositive lymph nodes out of total sampled: REMOVED_DATE \u000a(1/1 sentinel lymph nodes; REMOVED_DATE non-sentinel lymph nodes).\u000a-size of largest metastasis (greatest dimension): REMOVED_DATE cm. This is\u000asomewhat hard to determine as multiple isolated tumors cells and small\u000acluster of micrometastases (0.2 cm.) are scattered across a REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000aarea of the lymph nodes\u000a-extranodal extension: none\u000aCOMMENT: The sentinel lymph node, specimen A, is examined at multiple\u000alevels with H&E stains and immunohistochemical stains for keratin.\u000aAdditional keratin stains performed on specimen B highlight the metastasis\u000ain one of the non sentinel lymph nodes. Small foci of tumor were not\u000avisible on the section of sentinel lymph node (specimen A) sampled for\u000afrozen section.\u000aSKIN:\u000a-nipple: unremarkable\u000a-skin/dermis: unremarkable\u000aPRIOR RELATED SPECIMENS REVIEWED:\u000asite: right breast, upper outer quadrant and right breast upper inner\u000aquadrant, needle core biopsies, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_DATE  and REMOVED_DATE \u000aAJCC pTNM Classification (6th Ed.): pREMOVED_ACCESSION_IDc(m) pREMOVED_ACCESSION_IDa pMX\u000aThe pathologic TNM classification above is based only on the information\u000aavailable to the pathologist, and therefore may not be accurate.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by: Nicole A. Mihok, M.D.\u000aINTRA-OPERATIVE CONSULTATION:\u000aOPERATING ROOM CONSULTATION (FROZEN SECTION):\u000aRight sentinel node:\u000aBenign lymph node. Negative for metastasis.\u000aMJM\u000aClinical diagnosis & history:\u000aRight breast carcinoma\u000aTissue-Designation:\u000aA.Sentinel lymph node - right\u000aB.Lymph nodes, dissection - right axillary\u000aC.Adipose tissue - right axillary\u000aD.Breast, simple mastectomy - right\u000aGross description:\u000aSpecimen A is received in formalin, labeled "right sentinel lymph node" and\u000aconsists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. lymph node with a minimal amount of adjacent\u000aadipose tissue. Half of the node is sampled for frozen section and the remnant\u000aof the frozen is submitted in cassette AF. The remainder of the node is\u000aentirely submitted in cassette A. 2X all.\u000aSpecimen B is received in formalin, labeled "axillary lymph node, right" and\u000aconsists of a multipart specimen consisting of palpable lymph nodes and\u000aportions of adipose tissue. In aggregate, the specimen measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x\u000a0.8 cm. Four nodes are identified. The largest node is bisected and submitted\u000ain own cassette labeled REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. The second largest node is bisected and submitted\u000aalong with some small lobules of fat in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. The two smallest lymph nodes are\u000abisected and one node is inked blue and both nodes are submitted together in\u000acassette REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. 3 agg. all.\u000aSpecimen C is received in formalin, labeled "right axillary contents" and\u000aconsists of a rectangular portion of adipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm. It is sectioned and palpated. No lymph nodes are identified. The entire\u000aspecimen is submitted in two cassettes labeled REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. 2 agg. all.\u000aSpecimen D labeled "right breast" is received fresh from the Operating Room and\u000aconsists of a mastectomy specimen with a short stitch superior and a long\u000astitch lateral. The specimen is 668 grams and measures up to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm. There is a nipple with areola that is up to REMOVED_DATE cm. x REMOVED_DATE cm. in greatest\u000adiameter. The nipple is up to REMOVED_DATE cm. in height. Also received in the\u000aspecimen container jar is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. portion of skin. This portion of\u000askin is unremarkable. The nipple and areola are also unremarkable. Just\u000alateral to the nipple and areola is blue-tinged discoloration. The specimen is\u000ainked as follows: upper inner quadrant - green; upper outer quadrant - yellow;\u000alower inner quadrant - blue; lower outer quadrant - red; deep margin - black.\u000aThe specimen is serially sectioned and in the edge towards the axillary tail,\u000ano lymph nodes are identified. The cut surface shows an irregular firm mass in\u000athe upper inner quadrant of the breast. This mass grossly measures up to REMOVED_DATE x\u000a1.5 x REMOVED_DATE cm and is associated with a metallic clip. It is close to the deep\u000amargin. No additional mass lesions are identified grossly. The entire breast\u000ais x-rayed. A second metallic clip is identified in the breast. No visible\u000amass lesion is associated with this clip in the upper outer quadrant.\u000aRepresentative sections of the specimen are submitted as follows. 18 agg.\u000aSection code: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - random sections of the separate long strip of skin in the\u000aspecimen container jar as well as a section of nipple and\u000aareola\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - four sections of the upper inner quadrant tumor with the\u000aclosest (deep) margin in cassette REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - random sections of the upper inner quadrant, near the tumor\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - random sections of the lower inner quadrant\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - random sections of the upper outer quadrant\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - random sections of the lower outer quadrant\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - additional sections of upper outer quadrant\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - additional section of larger tumor in upper inner quadrant\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - sections, after specimen was x-rayed, of 2nd metallic clip\u000ain the upper outer quadrant\u000aTotal fixation time is 11 hours.\u000aDictated by: NAM____(signature on file)____MICHAEL J. ROSS, M.D. REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a____(signature on file)____NICOLE MIHOK, M.D. REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a[report_end]
