VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Amend/Addenda\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast core needle biopsy\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: EVA C. GOMBOS M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000a********** Addended Report ***********\u000aResident: Stephanie Schulte, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Deborah A Dillon, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. LEFT BREAST, UPPER INNER, 9G MRI-GUIDED CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR AN\u000aIRREGULAR MASS (0.7 CM):\u000aINVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA, well differentiated (modified Bloom-Richardson grade\u000aI/III), measuring at least REMOVED_DATE cm in this limited specimen (see note).\u000aNo lymphovascular invasion is seen in this limited specimen.\u000aATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA, with associated calcifications, is present.\u000aATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA is present.\u000aColumnar cell change with associated calcifications.\u000aNOTE: Immunohistochemistry for p63/REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID confirms the absence of\u000abasal/myoepithelial cells in the focus of invasive carcinoma.\u000aB. LEFT BREAST, LOWER OUTER, 9G MRI-GUIDED CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR A\u000aSEGMENTAL, HETEROGENEOUS AREA OF ENHANCEMENT:\u000aATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA arising in a background of columnar cell change\u000awith associated calcifications and extracellular mucin production.\u000aATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA is present.\u000aExtracellular mucin present within stroma (see note).\u000aNOTE: Multiple additional levels have been examined. This area would be\u000acharacterized best following excision.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHISTORY: Known left IDC (at 12:00) with a second focus of enhancement upper\u000ainner quadrant bx (site #1), and a third focus of enhancement lower outer\u000abreast (site #2).\u000aBREAST IMAGING FINDING:\u000a1. Left (site #1): 7 mm, non-palpable and irregular mass on MRI, mass\u000aforming with irregular border.\u000a2. Left (site #2): Non-palpable on breast imaging, non-mass forming,\u000asegmental and heterogeneous.\u000aLOCATION:\u000a1. Left (site #1): upper/inner.\u000a2. Left (site #2): lower/outer.\u000aTYPE OF CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY:\u000a1. Left (site #1): 9G MRI and vacuum-assisted.\u000a2. Left (site #2): 9G MRI and vacuum-assisted.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) Left breast core biopsy (site #1) in one green top/white bottom cassette.\u000aB/2) Left breast core biopsy (site #2) in one blue top/white bottom cassette.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, in two parts, each labeled with the\u000apatient's name, unit number.\u000aPart A, "green top, white bottom, site #1, left breast, REMOVED_DATE  9:40 a.m.",\u000aconsists of multiple yellow focally hemorrhagic fibrofatty tissues (aggregating\u000a5.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which are received in four white cassettes with green top.\u000aThe specimen is submitted in toto.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 white cassette with green top, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 white cassette with green top, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 white cassette with green top, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 white cassette with green top, multi frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, "blue top, white bottom, site #2, left breast, REMOVED_DATE  9:40 a.m.",\u000aconsists of multiple yellow focally hemorrhagic fibrofatty tissues (aggregating\u000a4.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which are received in three white cassettes with blue top.\u000aThe specimens are submitted in toto.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 white cassette with blue top, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 white cassette with blue top, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 white cassette with blue top, multi frags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000acp/lp\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Deborah A Dillon M.D., Electronically signed on Tuesday\u000aFebruary 03, 2009 at 12:48:38PM\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM (02/03/09):\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for invasive carcinoma (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE - LOW\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) NEGATIVE (0)\u000aMethod for Hormone receptor analysis:\u000aEstrogen receptor, progesterone receptor, and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu were evaluated by manual\u000amorphometric analysis using the following criteria:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low > 0% - < 10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor cells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but only a\u000aportion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+):Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in >10% of\u000atumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+):Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in >30% of\u000atumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aExternal controls are evaluated and show appropriate Immunoreactivity.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aAddendum #1 by Deborah A Dillon M.D., Electronically signed on Tuesday\u000aFebruary 03, 2009 at 01:07:52PM\u000a[report_end]
