ecimen\u000aThe specimen has been previously per surgeon as follows: posterior/black;\u000aanterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange.\u000aCut surfaces demonstrate focal fat necrosis medially (1.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) in\u000athe area of the localization wire head. Remaining tissue is hemorrhagic and\u000apredominantly fatty (60-70%) with occasional fibrodense bands. There is a REMOVED_DATE \u000acm circumscribed vaguely nodular area abutting the lateral inked margin,\u000ahowever, no discrete masses are noted grossly. Entire specimen is submitted\u000asequentially from medial to lateral.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  entire specimen (fat necrosis in micro REMOVED_DATE  possible nodule in\u000amicro 8), 12 frags total, ESS.\u000adb\u000aReports to: CARTER, KATHARINE M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
