 separate foci of invasion. However, it is unclear if the findings\u000arepresent separate tumor foci or portions of a single tumor mass.\u000aCorrelation with imaging findings may be helpful in determining the most\u000alikely size of the tumor.\u000aThis carcinoma would be classified as at least AJCC REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDb pREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID MX.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Breast cancer.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Consult slides.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by CARTER,MARK RYAN,M.D.\u000aReceived from Cape Cod Hospital, 27 Park Street, Hyannis, MA REMOVED_CASE_ID, are twenty\u000afour slides.\u000aTwo slides are labeled "01: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" and sublabeled "1", and "2", corresponding\u000ato a left core biopsy from a procedure performed on REMOVED_DATE  according to the\u000aaccompanying pathology report bearing the patient's name. This report refers\u000ato a consultation by Dr. David Page (Vanderbilt University).\u000aTwenty two slides are labeled "01:REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" and sublabeled "AI" to "AIII",\u000a"BII", "CI" to "CIII", "DI" to "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID", corresponding to A) sentinel lymph node\u000a#1, B) sentinel lymph node #2, C) sentinel lymph node #3, and D) left breast\u000abiopsy (6 x 5 x 3 cm) from a procedure performed on REMOVED_DATE  according to the\u000aaccompanying pathology report bearing the patient's name.\u000aReceived from Yale-New Haven Hospital, New Haven, CT is consultation report\u000anumbered "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" and corresponds to slides "01:REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID". The report is\u000asigned by Dr. Darryl Carter.\u000aReports to: IGLEHART, JAMES, DIRK M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: OUTSIDE SLIDE CONSULT - BREAST\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: OUTSIDE SLIDE CONSULT - BREAST\u000a[report_end]
