VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ROGER L CHRISTIAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-06-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Wai Chin Foo, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Alessandra F Nascimento, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, EXCISION FOR A MASS AND CLIP:\u000aFibroadenomatoid change and columnar cell change associated with prior biopsy\u000asite changes.\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy.\u000aRIGHT BREAST TISSUE, EXCISION FOR A MASS:\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia bordering on DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU (see NOTE).\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia; an E-cadherin stain highlights loss of membrane\u000astaining.\u000aApocrine cysts, focally ruptured.\u000aFibroadenomatoid changes.\u000aBiopsy site changes.\u000aNOTE: A focus of atypical ductal hyperplastic bordering on DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN\u000aSITU is seen <0.1 cm from the inferior margin.\u000aThis case was also reviewed by Drs. A. Richardson and D. Dillon, Breast\u000aPathology Service, who concur.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 2 non-palp. masses, Rt Brst.\u000aOperation: Loc/excis.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1.) Right breast issue, medial (mammo).\u000aB/2.) Right breast tissue, lateral (mammo).\u000aRADIOLOGY: Mass in specimen by ultrasound. - C. Denison, M.D.\u000aClip and mass in specimen. - C. Denison, MD.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in two parts each labeled with the patients\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart A, labeled Right Breast mass medial" consists of a breast excision\u000aspecimen (4 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with sutures designating superior (short suture)\u000aand lateral (long suture) margin and a needle localization wire. The specimen\u000ais received inked by the surgeon per pathology protocol for the evaluation of\u000amargins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green;\u000alateral/yellow; medial/orange. An accompanying specimen radiograph demonstrates\u000aa needle localization wire and clips within the specimen adjacent to a mass.\u000aThe localizing wire enters the medial aspect of the specimen and exits\u000alaterally. Sectioning demonstrates REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm cavity filled with\u000aclotted blood and with surrounding fibrosis and fat necrosis. The cavity\u000afocally abuts the posterior and inferior margins and is within REMOVED_DATE cm of the\u000aclosest superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the closest lateral margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the\u000aclosest medial margin and REMOVED_DATE cm from the closest anterior margin. There is no\u000adefinitive mass identified. The remaining specimen is predominantly adipose\u000atissue without additional discrete abnormalities. The entire specimen is\u000asubmitted, sequentially from lateral to medial.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Multiple frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, labeled "#2. Right breast tissue, lateral" consists of a breast\u000aexcision specimen (4.4 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with sutures designating superior (short\u000asuture) and lateral (long suture) margins and a needle localization wire in\u000aplace. The specimen is inked by surgeon per pathology protocol for the\u000aevaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red;\u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. Specimen is received with a\u000aradiograph demonstrating the localizing wire in place adjacent to a mass in the\u000aspecimen. The localizing wire enters the inferior surface of the specimen and\u000aexits superomedially. Sectioning demonstrates dense, lobulated fibrous tissue\u000a(48%), particularly within the area marked by the localizing wire. The tissue\u000ais palpably firm and vaguely nodular, but without discrete masses, lesions or\u000aother abnormalities grossly. There is a REMOVED_DATE cm cyst, REMOVED_DATE cm from the closest\u000a(inferior) margin. The entire specimen is submitted, sequentially from medial\u000ato lateral, with area marked by localizing wire in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID through REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, cyst in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aand REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Entire specimen, multiple frags, ESS.\u000aDB/mmm\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Alessandra F Nascimento M.D., Electronically signed on\u000a7/12/2006\u000a[report_end]
