VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Amend/Addenda\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ROGER L CHRISTIAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-06-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000a********** Addended Report ***********\u000aResident: Wai Chin Foo, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Susan Lester, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, RE-EXCISION:\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, solid and cribriform types (low nuclear grade), is\u000apresent in 6 of 12 blocks. No calcifications or necrosis are present.\u000aDCIS is focally present at the inferior margin with cautery on DCIS (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID),\u000a0.1 cm from the inferior margin (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), < REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin\u000a(block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), and > REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior, medial, lateral, and superior\u000amargins. Prior biopsy site changes are present at the lateral and superior\u000amargins.\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia is present.\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia is present.\u000aNote: Immunoperoxidase studies will be performed and reported in an addendum\u000a(block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aThis carcinoma would be classified as AJCC (6th edition) Tis NX MX.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Wire directed excision of 2 masses, right breast, done on REMOVED_DATE \u000alateral -> ADH bordering on DCIS, close to inferior margin.\u000aOperation: Re-excision.\u000aOperative Findings: None.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast mass.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) Tissue from right breast, sutures -long/lateral, short/superior, blue/new\u000ainferior margin.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "#1 - tissue from right breast", and consists of an irregular tan/pink to\u000atan/yellow portion of breast tissue (4.3 x 2 x REMOVED_DATE cm). There is a short\u000asuture marking superior, a long suture marking lateral, and an aspect of the\u000aspecimen is previously inked blue by the surgeon and designated "a new inferior\u000amargin." The remainder of the specimen is inked as follows: red equals\u000asuperior, blue equals inferior, black equals posterior, green equals anterior,\u000ayellow equals lateral, and orange equals medial (please note that this inking\u000adeviates from the established pathology inking protocol). The specimen is\u000aserially sectioned from lateral to medial, showing a parenchyma predominantly\u000aconsisting of dense, tan/white to tan/pink fibrous tissue, with focal cystic\u000aspaces (the largest of which is REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest dimension. The remainder of\u000athe specimen consists of tan/yellow lobulated fat (35%).\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Specimen sequentially sectioned, multiple frags, ESS.\u000aDRD/lp\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a7/25/2006\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM:\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for DCIS (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE - LOW\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) NEGATIVE (1+)\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000acarcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but only\u000aa portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in >10%\u000aof tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in\u000a>10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aAddendum #1 by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
