VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Amend/Addenda\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ROGER L CHRISTIAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-06-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000a********** Addended Report ***********\u000aResident: Elizabeth A. Steensma, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Michelle S Hirsch, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA) SPECIMEN LABELED "RIGHT BREAST, RE-EXCISION":\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, solid and cribriform types (intermediate nuclear\u000agrade), is present in nine of twenty-eight blocks (9/28).\u000aNo necrosis or calcifications are seen in association with DCIS.\u000aExtensive LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU, with pagetoid spread, is present.\u000aDCIS is present <0.1 cm from the posterior margin (black; block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) and REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom the posterior margin (black; block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID). DCIS is present <0.1 cm from the\u000ainferior margin (blue; block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) and REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin (blue;\u000ablock REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aDCIS is also present at the superior aspect (green; block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), <0.1 cm from\u000athe lateral aspect (yellow; blocks REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), and >0.3 cm from anterior\u000a(skin) and medial aspects of the specimen.\u000aBiopsy site changes.\u000aOne lymph node with no carcinoma seen.\u000aSkin with scar.\u000aNOTE: Immunohistochemistry for E-cadherin confirms retention of membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity in DCIS and absence of membrane immunoreactivity in LCIS.\u000aB) SPECIMEN LABELED "NEW INFERIOR SHAVE MARGIN":\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, solid and cribriform types (low to intermediate\u000anuclear grade), is present in at least seven of ten blocks (7/10).\u000aNo necrosis or calcifications are seen in association with DCIS.\u000aExtensive LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU, with pagetoid spread, is present.\u000aDCIS is present REMOVED_DATE cm from the new inferior margin (green; slides REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aDCIS is also present at the lateral aspect (slide REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), <0.1 cm from the medial\u000aaspect (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior aspect (slide REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), <0.1 cm from\u000athe superior aspect (adjacent to specimen A) and >0.3 cm from the anterior\u000aaspects of the specimen.\u000aBiopsy site changes are present.\u000aNOTE: Immunohistochemistry for E-cadherin confirms retention of membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity in DCIS and absence of membrane immunoreactivity in LCIS.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: DCIS, UOQ, right breast.\u000aOperation: Re-excision.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: See above.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Right breast re-excision (primary resection site) - long/lateral,\u000ashort/superior (inferior stained blue).\u000aB/2. New inferior shave margin.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname, unit number.\u000aPart A, "#1. Primary resection site, long/lateral, short/superior", consists of\u000aan irregular tan/yellow to tan/pink, fibrofatty portion of soft tissue (6.0 x\u000a5.5 x REMOVED_DATE cm) which is partially surfaced by a tan/white, wrinkled skin ellipse\u000a(2.3 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). There is a short suture marking superior and a long\u000asuture marking lateral. The inferior margin is inked blue and the posterior\u000amargin is inked black by the surgeon. The superior margin is inked green, the\u000alateral margin is inked yellow, and the medial margin is inked orange. The\u000aanterior margin is skin and is not inked. The specimen is sectioned from\u000aposterior to anterior to show a tan to tan/red irregular area (? previous\u000abiopsy site) (2.1 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) that is REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE \u000acm from the anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000alateral margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin and focally involves the\u000ainferior margin. The parenchyma surrounding the lesion is tan to tan/yellow\u000awith focal fat necrosis, calcification. The remaining parenchyma is tan/yellow\u000aand lobulated.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Specimen serially sectioned with the anterior\u000amargin perpendicularly sectioned from REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID to REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, multi\u000afrags total, ESS.\u000aPart B, "#2. New inferior shave margin, long lateral, short superior", consists\u000aof an irregular tan/pink to tan/yellow, fibrofatty, lobulated portion of breast\u000atissue (6.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), with a long suture designating lateral and a short\u000asuture designating superior aspects. The inferior aspect was previously inked\u000agreen by the surgeon. The superior aspect is focally cauterized with firm\u000atan/white fibrous tissue. Anterior equals blue, posterior equals black,\u000alateral equals yellow, medial equals orange, superior equals red. The specimen\u000ais serially sectioned from lateral to medial to show a tan to tan/pink\u000afibrofatty parenchyma with focally unilocular cystic structures. No other\u000agross lesions are identified.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Specimen serially sectioned with 12 frags total, ESS.\u000adrd/lp\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Deborah A Dillon M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM (9/15/06):\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for DCIS (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) NEGATIVE (1+)\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000acarcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but only\u000aa portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in >10%\u000aof tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in\u000a>10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aAddendum #1 by Deborah A Dillon M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
