u000aspecimen is sectioned from medial to lateral to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm\u000acavity. This cavity is located REMOVED_DATE cm from the deep margin and REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000anipple and is located in the center of the specimen. Adjacent to the cavity is\u000aa REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm firm multinodular white/pink fibrous mass that extends through\u000aapproximately seven sections (i.e., REMOVED_DATE cm). This area is REMOVED_DATE cm distant from\u000athe deep margin and REMOVED_DATE cm from the skin. The borders appear to be\u000aill-defined. In addition, there is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm firm area in the lower\u000aouter quadrant located REMOVED_DATE cm from the deep margin and REMOVED_DATE cm from the skin.\u000aThe remainder of the breast parenchyma predominantly consists of soft fatty\u000atissue without gross pathologic abnormalities. The axillary tail is separated\u000afrom the specimen, a clip is placed to designate the site of the axillary tail.\u000aAbout ten lymph nodes are found within the axillary tail, the largest measuring\u000a1.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. Lymph nodes placed in the same cassettes are differently\u000ainked.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Cavity and surrounding area, REMOVED_DATE frags each, RSS.\u000aNOTE: A surgical clip is recovered in section REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Multinodular area, REMOVED_DATE frags each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Firm area in the lower outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Upper outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Upper inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lower inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial area, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lymph nodes individually inked, REMOVED_DATE frags each, RSS.\u000aNOTE: Two large nodes were bisected and are located in micro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Section of the nipple, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Perpendicular sections of the nipple, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMDH/AJB\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Andrea L Richardson M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a11/13/2006\u000a[report_end]
