on of margins: Posterior/black;\u000aanterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange.\u000aThe localizing wire enters the superior aspect and exits inferomedially.\u000aSectioning in the area of interest demonstrates a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aill-defined firm tan/white lesion REMOVED_DATE cm from the closest posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE \u000acm from the closest medial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the closest superior margin, REMOVED_DATE \u000acm from the closest anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the closest inferior margin\u000aand greater than 2 cm from the closest lateral margin. The remaining specimen\u000ais comprised of predominantly tan/yellow lobulated fatty tissue (at least 90%)\u000awith occasional thin tan/white fibromembranous septa. The entire specimen is\u000asubmitted sequentially from inferior to superior (lesion and surrounding tissue\u000ain REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID through REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, clip in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), multiple frags, ESS.\u000aDB/mmm\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Michelle S Hirsch M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Michelle S Hirsch M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a2/2/2006\u000a[report_end]
