VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: JULIE L JONES M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-05-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Kevin B Long, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Deborah A Dillon, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR CALCIFICATIONS AND A CLIP:\u000aResidual ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA with associated calcifications is present\u000aadjacent to biopsy site changes (slide REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aCalcifications present in association with columnar cell change.\u000aNOTE: A separate REMOVED_DATE cm focus shows nuclear atypia present in association with\u000asecretory changes (slide REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID). Immunohistochemical study for keratin/p63 shows\u000aintact myoepithelium around the atypical glands. Multiple levels have been\u000aexamined. Findings are not sufficient for a diagnosis of DCIS. Slide REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID also\u000aseen by Dr. Susan Lester, who concurs.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: ADH on left breast core bx for Ca+.\u000aOperation: Left breast wire-localized excisional bx.\u000aOperative Findings: Dense breast tissue in the area of concern.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast ADH on core needle bx.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000a#1. Left breast wire-localized excisional biopsy - short stitch superior, long\u000alateral (mammo).\u000aRADIOLOGY REPORT: Residual calcifications; clip and wire are within the\u000aspecimen. - Dr. (ILLEGIBLE)\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient?s name, unit number,\u000aand "1. Left breast wire-localized excisional biopsy" and consists of a REMOVED_DATE \u000a(lateral to medial) x REMOVED_DATE (inferior to superior) x REMOVED_DATE (anterior to posterior)\u000acm breast biopsy with a localization wire in place and a short suture marking\u000athe superior margin and a long suture marking the lateral margin. An\u000aaccompanying specimen radiograph demonstrates residual calcifications, the clip\u000aand the wire in place within the specimen. The specimen is inked per pathology\u000aprotocol for the evaluation of margins: Posterior/black; anterior/blue;\u000asuperior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange.\u000aThe specimen is re-radiographed and the clip identified. The clip is adjacent\u000ato the possible prior needle-core biopsy site, measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm,\u000a0.7 cm from the posterior, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior, REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior,\u000a2.0 cm from the inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral and REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial\u000amargins. The tissue consists of approximately 80% adipose tissue and 20%\u000afibrous tissue. The location of the tissue blocks is reported on the specimen\u000adiagram. The entire specimen is submitted for histologic evaluation.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Core biopsy site, clip, and anterior, posterior and superior\u000amargins, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Closest anterior and inferior margins, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Remaining breast parenchyma, sequentially sectioned from\u000aLateral to medial, 11 frags, ESS.\u000aKEL/mmm\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Kevin B Long M.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aResident Review by Kevin B Long M.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aPrelim Dx Release by Kevin B Long M.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aNo Action - Prelim Sent by Deborah A Dillon M.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Deborah A Dillon M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
