ies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for invasive carcinoma (block 18):\u000aEstrogen receptor positive\u000aProgesterone receptor positive (low)\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) negative (1+)\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000ainvasive carcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but\u000aonly a portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity\u000ain >10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: History of left breast ca, treated with induction chemotherapy.\u000aOperation: Left modified radical mastectomy.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast ca.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Left breast, short stitch/superior, long stitch/lateral\u000a2. Redundant tissue left breast.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by YOU,MINGJIAN JAMES,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart one, labeled "#1, left breast", consists of a modified radical\u000amastectomy specimen (1221 grams, 23 x 19 x 53 cm overall). The left breast has\u000aa skin ellipse (22 x 12 cm) with no visible scar. The nipple (1.5 cm in\u000adiameter) and areola (2.5 cm in diameter) are unremarkable. The breast tissue\u000ahas one (1) short stitch placed by surgeon to designate superior and a long\u000astitch to designate lateral. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for\u000athe evaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red;\u000ainferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. The specimen is serially\u000asectioned at 3 mm intervals from medial to superior revealing 90% adipose\u000atissue and approximately 10% white/tan fibrous tissue, with several firm areas\u000asuspicious for tumor scattered throughout the breast ranging up to REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000aThere are no hemorrhagic areas. A possible biopsy site is identified close to\u000athe inferior margin. Twenty-one (21) white/tan firm lymph nodes (ranging from\u000a0.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) are identified and entirely\u000asubmitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  1 lymph node, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 3: 3 lymph nodes with one bisected lymph node (inked black), 4 frags,\u000aESS.\u000aMicro 4: 2 bisected lymph nodes (one lymph node inked black), 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 5: 1 bisected lymph node, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 6: 6 lymph nodes, 6 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 7: 2 lymph nodes and one (1) bisected lymph node (inked black), 4\u000afrags, ESS.\u000aMicro 8: 7 lymph nodes, 7 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  breast tissue with firm areas, 1 frag per cass., RSS.\u000aMicro 20: possible biopsy site, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 21: outer upper quadrant breast tissue, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 22: outer lower quadrant breast tissue, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 23: inner upper quadrant breast tissue, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 24: inner lower quadrant breast tissue, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 25: skin with nipple and areola, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aPart two, labeled "#2, redundant tissue of left breast", consists of an\u000aunoriented irregular fragment of skin (3.0 x REMOVED_DATE cm) and underlying\u000afibroadipose tissue (5.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The apparent deep margin is inked\u000ablack. The skin is normal appearing without scars or other lesions. The tissue\u000ais sectioned at 3 mm intervals revealing normal-appearing adipose tissue.\u000aRepresentative sections are submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  skin and fibroadipose tissue, 2 frags, RSS.\u000amjy\u000aReports to: MATORY, YVEDT M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY W/REGIONAL LYMPH NODES\u000a[report_end]
