terior-blue,\u000aposterior-green, medial-orange, lateral-yellow. The specimen is photographed\u000ato confirm the inking discrepancy, and is sequentially sectioned from lateral\u000ato medial, revealing patchy multifocal areas of hemorrhage, involving the\u000acentral and medial aspect of the specimen (30% of tissue), and abutting all\u000amargins, with exception of the lateral margin, which is within REMOVED_DATE cm. There\u000aare areas of fibrosis and fat necrosis in association with this hemorrhage, but\u000ano obvious masses, lesions or other abnormalities grossly. Remaining specimen\u000ashows occasional tan/white fibrous tissue without abnormality. Representative\u000asections are submitted, sequentially from lateral to medial, with\u000arepresentative perpendicular lateral margin in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and representative\u000aperpendicular medial margin in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Multi frags, RSS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aDB/ajb\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Alessandra F Nascimento M.D., Electronically signed on\u000a5/4/2007\u000a[report_end]
