VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aBRODSKY, GILBERT, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by BRODSKY,GILBERT,M.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST, RE-EXCISION:\u000aHealing prior excision site (1.7 cm); no residual phyllodes tumor present\u000a(cf. REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aFibroadenoma (2.0 cm), separate lesion.\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy or atypia, including evolution of\u000amargins.\u000aThis case was reviewed at the staff Surgical Pathology conference.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 30 year old female s/p L breast excision for a mass. Phyllodes tumor\u000aintermediate grade. Repeat u/s showed 2 other masses - to be excised\u000aat the time of re-excision.\u000aOperation: L breast re-excision and wire localized biopsy x 2\u000aClinical Diagnosis: L breast phyllodes tumor; abnormal (L) breast ultrasound\u000ax 2\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1. Left breast tissue - given to mammo\u000aRADIOLOGY: Masses in specimen. {illegible}\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by CHANG,MARTIN C,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name and unit number\u000aand only, and consists of a single torus-shaped fragment of breast tissue\u000ameasuring REMOVED_DATE (M-L) x REMOVED_DATE (S-I) x REMOVED_DATE cm, oriented with two surgical sutures\u000amarking the superior (short) and lateral (long) aspects. The specimen is\u000areceived inked by the surgeon per pathology protocol for the evaluation of\u000amargins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green;\u000alateral/yellow; medial/orange. There is a central cavity within the specimen\u000a(4.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) extending full-thickness through the anteroposterior\u000aaxis, resulting in a full thickness defect at anterior and posterior surfaces\u000a(4.2 x REMOVED_DATE cm). The breast parenchyma lining the central cavity is\u000ahemorrhagic. Contained within the specimen are two localization wires,\u000acorresponding to one well-defined, and one poorly-defined mass on the\u000aaccompanying specimen radiograph.\u000aContained within the specimen are two discrete masses. The first (designated\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) is a poorly defined tan/pink fibrous area measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm,\u000aextending to within REMOVED_DATE cm of the inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm of the posterior, REMOVED_DATE cm of\u000athe lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm of the superior, REMOVED_DATE cm of the medial margin, and grossly\u000aabutting the anterior margin. The second mass (designated REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) is located 2 cm\u000afrom the first and is a well-defined white/tan whorled nodule measuring REMOVED_DATE x\u000a1.5 x REMOVED_DATE cm, and extending to within REMOVED_DATE cm of the medial, REMOVED_DATE cm of the\u000ainferior, REMOVED_DATE cm of the posterior, REMOVED_DATE cm of the anterior, REMOVED_DATE cm of the\u000asuperior, and REMOVED_DATE cm of the lateral resection margin. The remainder of the\u000abreast parenchyma is composed of 50% of adipose tissue and 50% of tan/pink\u000afibrous tissue.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID in relation to inferior, posterior, and anterior margins, mult\u000afrags, RSS\u000aMicro 4: central cavity in relation to superior margin, 2 frags, RSS\u000aMicro 5: inferior edge, between REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 6: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID in relation to inferior, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 7: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID in relation to medial and posterior, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 8: additional medial edge, mult frags, RSS\u000aMicro 9: additional superior edge, 2 frags, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  additional central cavity, 3 frags, RSS\u000amcc\u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
