aCore biopsy site\u000aComplex sclerosing lesion\u000aMicrocalcifications associated with benign epithelium\u000aAJCC CLASSIFICATION (6th edition) - REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID pREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID (sn) MX\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER/PR/HER-2) - performed previously\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Right breast IDC on core biopsy.\u000aOperation: Right wire localized partial mastectomy and sentinel node biopsy.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast cancer.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) R wire localized partial mastectomy - short/superior, long/lateral,\u000askin/anterior (to mammo).\u000aB/2) R breast final inferior margin - short stitch/new inferior margin, long\u000astitch/lateral.\u000aC/3) Right axillary sentinel node (fs).\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000aMass, 2 clips, and wire in specimen. Dr. Jones was phoned in OR by Dr.\u000aDenison.\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000aArrival time: 1:54 PM\u000aReport time: 2:20 PM\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "2. RIGHT AXILLARY SENTINEL NODES" (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aTwo lymph nodes negative for carcinoma.\u000aOR Consultation by: JONATHAN NEIL GLICKMAN, M.D., PH.D.\u000aResident: ERIC SNYDER, M.D., PH.D.\u000aThe senior physician certifies that he/she personally conducted a gross and/or\u000amicroscopic examination of the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed\u000athe rapid diagnos(es) related thereto.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in three parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname, and medical record number.\u000aPart A, "right wire localized partial mastectomy - short/superior,\u000along/lateral", consists of a REMOVED_DATE (inferior to superior) x REMOVED_DATE (anterior to\u000aposterior) x REMOVED_DATE (medial to lateral) breast excision and a skin ellipse (3.5 x\u000a1.0 cm) with two orienting sutures - the long designated "lateral" and the\u000ashort designated "superior". The localization wire is not in the specimen.\u000aThe specimen is inked for evaluation of the margins. The specimen is inked per\u000apathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black;\u000aanterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange.\u000aThere is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm firm, white stellate mass that is grossly within\u000a1.0 cm to the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to the deep margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to the\u000aanterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to the medial margin,\u000aand REMOVED_DATE cm to the lateral margin. The remainder of the breast tissue consists\u000aof predominantly adipose tissue. Representative sections of the tumor are\u000ataken for breast bank. The entire mass is submitted for histologic\u000aexamination. A specimen radiograph is received. An accompanying report states\u000athat the mass, two clips and a wire are present in the specimen.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Mass and adjacent fibrous tissue (including the closest lateral,\u000aposterior, and inferior margins), multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Superior margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Anterior margin including skin, 3 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aPart B, "right breast final inferior margin, short stitch - new inferior\u000amargin, long stitch - lateral", consists of a fragment of breast tissue,\u000ameasuring REMOVED_DATE cm from anterior to posterior, REMOVED_DATE cm from medial to lateral, and\u000a0.5 cm from superior to inferior with two orienting suture: short designating\u000athe new inferior margin and long designating the lateral margin. The specimen\u000ais inked for evaluation of the margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue;\u000asuperior/red; inferior/green (new margin); lateral/yellow; medial/orange. The\u000asuperior margin appears ragged and is composed of mostly fibrous tissue,\u000aconsistent with old margins. The remainder of the breast specimen consists of\u000a60% adipose tissue and 40% fibrous tissue. No masses are identified. The\u000aspecimen is serially sectioned and entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Multi frags, ESS.\u000aPart C, "right axillary sentinel node", consists of a fragment of adipose\u000atissue (12.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) including two lymph nodes (#1, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm;\u000a#2, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). Each lymph node is bisected and submitted for frozen\u000asection analysis with lymph node #1 as REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and lymph node #2 as REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID remnant, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID remnant, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID remnant, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Non-frozen tissue, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aELC/lp\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-07-REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Michael W Bennett M.B., B.C.H., Electronically signed on\u000a5/29/2007\u000a[report_end]
