VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aGLICKMAN, JONATHAN, NEIL, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by GLICKMAN,JONATHAN NEIL,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST, EXCISION FOR CALCIFICATIONS AND A CLIP:\u000aBenign breast tissue with cysts, columnar alteration of lobules with\u000aprominent snouts and secretions, apocrine metaplasia, core biopsy site\u000achanges, and calcifications in benign epithelium.\u000aOne (1) intramammary lymph node with no significant pathologic change.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the\u000aspecimen, including margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 45-year-old female with left breast abnormal mammogram.\u000aOperation: Left needle localized breast biopsy.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Left breast tissue, stitch marking short/superior,\u000along/lateral, whip stitch on deep on deep margin, and\u000ainking per path protocol.\u000aCa++ and clip in specimen. Dr. Smith.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by DAVID,FRANK SAMUEL,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "#1, left breast tissue". It is a single fragment of soft tissue measuring\u000a4.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm, and contains a single localization wire. The specimen is\u000aoriented with a short superior, long lateral, and deep whip stitch, and has\u000abeen inked by the surgeon according to the pathology protocol for the\u000aevaluation of margins. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the\u000aevaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red;\u000ainferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. Sectioning reveals a\u000amixture of tan fibrous and yellow adipose tissue with no grossly identifiable\u000alesions. The specimen is entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  serial sections of specimen, 13 total frags, ESS.\u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
