VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: BRENT T SHOJI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Agoston Tony Agoston, M.D., Ph.D.; Eleanor Y. Chen, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Susan Lester, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A CLIP AND CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia (best seen in slides REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aFocal atypical ductal hyperplasia (best seen in slide REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aBiopsy site changes, transected at the deep margin in breast tissue.\u000aSkeletal muscle is present at the deep margin.\u000aCalcifications are associated with benign epithelium and cysts.\u000aSkin is present and is free of carcinoma.\u000aNOTE: By report, the patient has a diagnosis of DCIS on a prior core\u000aneedle biopsy (not reviewed). The core biopsy site was identified. All\u000afibrous tissue has been examined (including margins) and no residual DCIS is\u000aseen.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: DCIS R breast.\u000aOperation: None specified.\u000aOperative Findings: None specified.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: None specified.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) Right breast tissue (to mammo).\u000aRADIOLOGY: Specimen - targeted clip and calcifications. Called to Dr. Shoji.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name and medical\u000arecord number, and consists of one part.\u000aPart A, labeled "#1. Right breast tissue", consists of an 85-g breast specimen\u000a(3.0 cm SI, REMOVED_DATE cm ML, REMOVED_DATE cm AP) that is inked by the surgeon per pathology\u000aprotocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue;\u000asuperior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. There is also an\u000aattached skin ellipse laterally (4.3 x REMOVED_DATE cm). A wire enters the specimen\u000alaterally through the skin ellipse and exits posteriorly. The accompanying\u000aradiograph demonstrates the wire with a cluster of calcifications (annotated as\u000a"site of biopsied calcifications - DCIS") and second area more medially with\u000aradiographic density and a clip (annotated "biopsy clip/hematoma"). The\u000aspecimen is bisected along the wire into a superior and inferior half and there\u000ais a small firm white fibrous area associated with the clip (1.4 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm) that abuts the posterior margin, and is REMOVED_DATE cm to anterior, REMOVED_DATE cm to\u000ainferior, REMOVED_DATE cm to superior, REMOVED_DATE cm to medial, and REMOVED_DATE cm to lateral margins.\u000aThere is an adjacent larger firm tan/white area more medially (4.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm) that abuts the medial, posterior, superior, inferior, anterior margins, and\u000ais REMOVED_DATE cm to the lateral margin. Each half is serially sectioned from medial\u000ato lateral. All fibrous tissue has been submitted for histologic examination.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin, REMOVED_DATE frags per block, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Entirely submitted fibrous tissue from the superior half,\u000asubmitted medial to lateral, REMOVED_DATE frags per block, RSS. Note, the tissue\u000aassociated with the clip is in cassettes REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Entirely submitted fibrous tissue from the inferior half,\u000aincluding part of the biopsy site in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, submitted medial to lateral, 1 frag\u000aper block, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Representative fatty breast tissue near the inferior and lateral\u000amargins, REMOVED_DATE frags per block, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin with skin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aTA/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_