.\u000a3. Left - Site #3: upper/outer.\u000aTYPE OF CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY:\u000a1. Site #1 - 14G Ultrasound.\u000a2. Site #2 - 14G Ultrasound.\u000a3. Site #3 - 14G Ultrasound.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) Left breast - Site #1 in one orange cassette.\u000aB/2) Left breast - Site #2 in one yellow cassette.\u000aC/3) Left breast - Site #3 in one brown cassette.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, in three parts, each labeled with the\u000apatient's name, unit number.\u000aPart A, "left breast site #1, 4 o'clock", consists of multiple tan/yellow to\u000atan/white lobulated fibroadipose breast tissue cores (0.7 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The\u000abreast tissue cores are received in an orange cassette marked "left site #1"\u000aand are submitted in toto.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Multi frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, "left breast site #2", consists of multiple tan/white to tan/yellow\u000alobulated fibroadipose breast tissue cores (1.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate).\u000aThe breast tissue cores are received in a yellow cassette marked "left site #2"\u000aand are submitted in toto.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Multi frags, ESS.\u000aPart C, "left breast site #3", consists of multiple tan/yellow to tan/white\u000afibroadipose breast tissue cores (1.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate). The breast\u000atissue cores are received in a tan cassette "left site #3" and are submitted in\u000atoto.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Multi frags, ESS.\u000asek/lp\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jane E. Brock M.B., B.S., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a7/3/2008\u000a[report_end]
