VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID:REMOVED_CASE_ID Report Status: Signed\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aDIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. Sentinel lymph node, left axilla, excision:\u000aMetastatic adenocarcinoma in one of one submitted lymph node (1/1).\u000aB. Lymph nodes, left axilla, dissection:\u000aMetastatic adenocarcinoma in three of twelve (3/12) submitted lymph\u000anodes.\u000aC. Left breast, excision:\u000aInvasive ductal carcinoma, grade REMOVED_DATE  REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000aDuctal carcinoma in situ, grade REMOVED_DATE  solid type with central necrosis.\u000aSYNOPTIC REPORT - INVASIVE BREAST CANCER\u000aAJCC pTNM CLASSIFICATION (6TH Ed.)(Based on available surgical material:\u000apREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID pREMOVED_ACCESSION_IDa pMX\u000aHISTOLOGIC TYPE: invasive ductal carcinoma\u000aHISTOLOGIC GRADE (Nottingham System): II\u000aTUMOR LOCATION: upper outer quadrant of left breast\u000aTUMOR SIZE (greatest dimension): REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000aLYMPHATIC/VASCULAR INVASION: present\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU (DCIS): present\u000aType: solid\u000aGrade: 2\u000aExtent: focal\u000aSize (greatest dimension): microscopic foci within and around the\u000ainvasive tumor\u000aExtensive intraductal component:\u000aNecrosis: present, type: comedo\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU: none identified\u000aMICROCALCIFICATIONS: none identified\u000aRESECTION MARGINS:\u000aInvasive Carcinoma: invasive carcinoma close to margin (0.1 to\u000a0.2 cm.): REMOVED_DATE cm. from posterior margin\u000aDCIS: clear (greater than or equal to REMOVED_DATE cm.)\u000aIMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING (invasive carcinoma):\u000aPrior specimen REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID reported as:\u000aEstrogen receptor: POSITIVE (>10% of nuclei stained)\u000aProgesterone receptor: POSITIVE (>10% of nuclei stained)\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID): INDETERMINATE (2+) (at least 10% with at least weak,\u000acomplete membrane staining)\u000aFISH results: pending\u000aTotal Fixation Time: 10 hours\u000aLYMPH NODES:\u000aPositive nodes out of total sampled: REMOVED_DATE (1/1 sentinel node; REMOVED_DATE \u000anon-sentinel nodes)\u000a-largest metastasis (greatest dimension): REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000a-extranodal extension: focal\u000a-number with micrometastases (less than or equal to REMOVED_DATE cm.): 2\u000a-number with isolated tumor cells (less than or equal to REMOVED_DATE cm.): 0\u000aSKIN: unremarkable\u000aADDITIONAL PATHOLOGIC FINDINGS:\u000aPerineural involvement by tumor is seen.\u000aFibroadenoma.\u000aChanges consistent with prior biopsy site.\u000aPRIOR RELATED SPECIMENS REVIEWED:\u000aLeft breast, upper outer quadrant; REMOVED_DATE  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aFinal Diagnosis by: Kenan J. Sauder, M.D.\u000aINTRA-OPERATIVE CONSULTATION:\u000aOPERATING ROOM CONSULTATION (TOUCH PREPARATION):\u000aSentinel lymph node, left axilla:\u000aPositive for metastatic adenocarcinoma.\u000aKJS\u000aClinical diagnosis & history:\u000aLeft breast cancer\u000aTissue-Designation:\u000aA.Sentinel lymph node - left axillary\u000aB.Lymph nodes, dissection - left axillary\u000aC.Breast, excision with margins - left\u000aGross description:\u000aThe specimen is received in three containers.\u000aSpecimen A is received fresh for intraoperative diagnosis, labeled "left\u000aaxillary sentinel lymph node" and consists of a 2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. fragment of\u000apale yellow adipose tissue containing a REMOVED_DATE cm. lymph node. The lymph node is\u000aserially sectioned and reveals a firm, gritty, white cut surface. A frozen\u000asection is performed.\u000aSection code: AF - frozen section control, 1 agg. all.\u000aA - remainder of tissue, 1 agg. all.\u000aSpecimen B is received fresh, labeled "left axillary content" consists of a 12\u000ax 7 x 2 cm. yellowish-red fibroadipose tissue. Further disection and\u000aexamination reveals the presence of twelve yellowish-pink, glistening nodules\u000aranging in size from REMOVED_DATE cm. in greatest dimension to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000aSection code: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - individual nodule, 8X all.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - serially sectioned single nodule revealing gross\u000aevidence of fat infiltration\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - serially sectioned single nodule revealing tan-pink\u000alymph node tissue admixed with yellow fat\u000ainfiltration, 5X all.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - serially sectioned single lymph node revealing tan-pink\u000atissue admixed with bright yellow fat infiltration, 5X\u000aall.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - serially sectioned single lymph node revealing\u000agrayish-white tumor replacing the hilum of the lymph\u000anode, 5X all.\u000aSpecimen C is received fresh, labeled "left breast lumpectomy: consists of a 39\u000agram, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. excisional breast biopsy with overlying REMOVED_DATE x 1 x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm. skin ellipse. The biopsy is oriented with a long stitch lateral, a short\u000astitch superior, and has a pale yellow, lobulated outer surface with areas of\u000ablue dye staining. There is a firm, palpable nodule within the mid portion of\u000athe specimen. The specimen is inked: green, anterior; blue, inferior; orange,\u000alateral; yellow, medial; black, posterior; red, superior. The specimen is\u000aserially sectioned and reveals a pale yellow, soft cut surface with a stellate\u000ashaped nodule measuring REMOVED_DATE cm. in greatest dimension. This nodule is firm,\u000awhite and gritty with central hemorrhage and areas suggestive of fat necrosis.\u000aThe clip is identified. The nodule appears to abut the posterior margin\u000agrossly. The specimen is submitted from lateral to medial and includes the\u000aentire described tumor nodule and the margins. 17 agg.\u000aSection code: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - lateral margin\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - entire tumor (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, section with clip)\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - medial margin\u000aTotal fixation time is 28 hours.\u000aDictated by: KJS____(signature on file)____DENNIS J. FEEN, M.D. REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a____(signature on file)____ REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a[report_end]
