VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ROGER L CHRISTIAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Cheryl Adackapara, M.D.\u000aPathologist: William R Welch, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aSPECIMEN DESIGNATED "RIGHT BREAST TISSUE, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR\u000aMICROCALCIFICATIONS":\u000aBreast tissue with calcifications associated with epithelial hyperplasia\u000aand benign epithelium.\u000aCysts, apocrine metaplasia, and duct ectasia with inspissation and\u000ahemorrhage.\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy including evaluation of margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Microcalcs, Rt breast.\u000aOperation: Wire-directed excision.\u000aOperative Findings: See op note.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Microcalcs, Rt breast.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) Rt breast tissue; short - superior; long - lateral.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Microcalcifications, hook and wire seen in specimen.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "Rt breast", and consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm excision of fibroadipose\u000atissue, oriented by sutures designating superior (short suture) and lateral\u000a(long suture) margins. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the\u000aevaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red;\u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange (inked by prosector). A\u000alocalizing wire enters the medial aspect of the specimen and traverses\u000alaterally. The specimen is received with a radiograph demonstrating localizing\u000awire in place within the specimen, adjacent to an encircled cluster of\u000acalcification in the lateral aspect of the specimen. Sectioning demonstrates\u000atan firm lobulated fibrous tissue (at least 50% of the specimen), without\u000apalpable or visible masses, lesions or other abnormalities grossly. The entire\u000aspecimen is submitted, from lateral to medial, with perpendicular lateral\u000amargin in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, perpendicular medial margin in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, and area of interest (per\u000awire, radiograph) likely in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Multi frags, ESS\u000aDB/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by William R Welch M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
