VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST MASTECTOMY W/REGIONAL LYMPH NODES\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aRICHARDSON, ANDREA, L., M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by RICHARDSON,ANDREA L.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000a#1. RIGHT BREAST, MASTECTOMY:\u000aMETAPLASTIC CARCINOMA, WITH MALIGNANT EPITHELIAL AND NEUROGLIAL\u000aDIFFERENTIATION, REMOVED_DATE CM (SEE NOTE).\u000aLymphovascular invasion is present (block 14).\u000aTumor focally extends to within REMOVED_DATE cm of the deep margin (block 2).\u000aNormal surrounding breast tissue wtih fibrosis and epithelial changes\u000aconsistent with treatment effect.\u000aNo in-situ carcinoma seen.\u000aMETASTATIC TUMOR present as scattered isolated malignant\u000aepithelial-appearing cells in the subcapsular sinuses of 3 of 5 axillary\u000alymph nodes.\u000a#2. FINAL DEEP MARGIN:\u000aSkeletal muscle and fibroadipose tissue negative for tumor.\u000a#3. ADDITIONAL AXILLARY CONTENTS":\u000aMETASTATIC TUMOR in 2 of 3 lymph node (see note)\u000aLargest deposit = REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000aNo extranodal extension seen.\u000aNOTE: The tumor is composed of a malignant epithelial component, a\u000amesenchymal component with variably cellular small round to slightly spindled\u000ablue cells, and a more well-differentiated neuroglial component with larger\u000aganglion-like cells in a neuropil matrix.\u000aThe epithelial cells are arranged in sheets and clusters with occasional lumen\u000aformation. They are variably malignant in appearance, ranging from cells with\u000alow to intermediate nuclear/cytoplasmic ratios and abundant cytoplasm to\u000acells with high nuclear/cytoplasmic ratio, large nuclei, irregular nuclear\u000acontours, prominent nucleoli, and abundant necrosis. The epithelial component\u000alines cystic areas containing necrotic and hemorrhagic material. In other\u000aareas, nests of epithelial cells are intermingled with the mesenchymal\u000acomponent. The malignant epithelial-appearing cells stain strongly with\u000akeratins confirming epithelial differentiation, and occasional cells stain for\u000aGCDFP and PR supporting a breast origin. The epithelial cells are also focally\u000apositive for p63, and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. Stains for CEA(m), ER and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu were negative.\u000aThe epithelial-appearing component comprises REMOVED_DATE % of the tumor volume and was\u000anot appreciated on the limited prior biopsy specimen. There is no epithelial\u000ain situ component seen.\u000aThe spindle cells in the mesenchymal and neuropil matrix are variable in size,\u000aranging from small ovoid cells to larger cells with prominent nucleoli. Many of\u000athese cells stain positively for neurofilament, GFAP, synatophysin, and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aThese cells are negative for epithelial markers. Stains for AFP, bHCG, Hep Par\u000awere negative.\u000aSubjacent to the nipple are 2 foci of lymphovascular invasion. Both the\u000amalignant epithelial and the glial components are present in the\u000alymphatics. Three (3) lymph nodes are positive for scattered subcapsular\u000amalignant epithelial cells, and 2 lymph nodes have confluent areas of low\u000agrade spindle cells set in a glial matrix diffusely occupying the subcapsular\u000asinuses.\u000aThis excision is compared to the pre-treatment biopsy. The epithelial-appearing\u000aareas that support a breast origin were not well-represented or appreciated\u000aon the prior biopsy. The spindled mesenchymal areas and the well-differentiated\u000aneural-glial areas comprise the majority of the tumor volume, appear viable,\u000abut have decreased cellularity compared to the pre-treatment biopsy.\u000aThe findings in this case of a keratin positive malignant epithelial\u000acomponent, which also stains positively for breast epithelial markers, supports\u000aa diagnosis of a metaplastic carcinoma of breast origin with heterologous\u000aelements composed mainly of mature neural elements. The differential diagnosis\u000awould include a malignant mixed germ cell tumor with both embryonal and\u000ateratomatous elements, or a malignant neuroblastic tumor with epithelial\u000adifferentiation, though these are not likely.\u000aCytogenetics was performed on the tumor which showed a karyotype of 46, XX,\u000at(6;18)(p21-22;q11) seen in all metaphases counted (See separate cytogenetics\u000areport, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID). The XX karyotype rules out origin from the patients male\u000achild. The t(6;18) translocation is not characteristic of any particular type\u000aof tumor. Because the translocation was seen in all cells analyzed, it may\u000arepresent a constitutional rearrangement in the patient rather than a somatic\u000atumor-specific change. The possibility of a constitutional rearrangement could\u000abe evaluated by performing cytogenetics on patient blood cells, if clinically\u000awarranted.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Pre-op therapies breast service: This is 34 year old female with a\u000aright breast tumor that has never been report before in the world. #1 -\u000ateratoma. Brigham review neuroblastoma, Wash U and Children's teratoma.\u000aTreated with platinum and VP-16; pre-op four cycles.\u000aOperation: Right modified radical mastectomy.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Neuroblastoma vs teratoma of the breast.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1 - right breast modified radical mastectomy, short/superior\u000along/axillary tail.\u000a#2 - final deep margins, suture on new margin.\u000a#3 - additional axillary contents.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by WILLIAM,JACQUELINE M.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen was received fresh in three parts, labeled with the patient's name\u000aand unit number.\u000aPart one, "right breast modified radical mastectomy, short/superior,\u000along/axillary tail", consists of an 813 gram mastectomy, measuring 21 x REMOVED_DATE x\u000a6 cm with an axillary tail, measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. There is a REMOVED_DATE x\u000a7.2 cm tan skin ellipse with a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm brown areola and a REMOVED_DATE cm in\u000adiameter everted nipple. There is a short stitch designating the superior\u000aaspect of the specimen. There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm portion of muscle on the deep\u000amargin. The deep margin was inked black. There is a mass measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000ax REMOVED_DATE cm that abuts the deep margin over a 5 cm area. It is partially\u000aencapsulated tan/yellow, with soft, cystic and hemorrhagic areas. The cysts\u000aare filled with friable yellow and orange material. The tumor is close, less\u000athan REMOVED_DATE cm from the dermis, but does not invade skin. The uninvolved breast\u000atissue is composed of a 90% adiposed, 10% fibrous tissue with no other lesions\u000anoted. Five lymph nodes were identified within the axillary tail. Photographs\u000awere taken and a portion of the tumor was sent for EM and Cytogenetics.\u000aMicro #1+2: Possible viable tumor, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro #3-5: Cystic and hemorrhagic areas of tumor, 3 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro #6+7: Tumor showing capsule and deep margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro #8: Tumor in relation to skin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro #9: Tumor and adjacent normal breast tissue, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro #10: Breast tissue from upper/outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro #11: Breast tissue from upper/inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro #12: Breast from lower/outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro #13: Breast tissue from lower/inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro #14: Nipple, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro #15: Largest lymph node in axillary tail (1.2 cm), bisected, 2 frags,\u000aESS.\u000aMicro #16+17: Four lymph nodes, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro #18: Quick fix fleshy area, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro #19: Quick fix solid area, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro #20: Quick fix cystic area, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aPart two, "final deep margin with suture on new margin", consists of one\u000afragment of fibroadipose tissue, measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. There is a\u000asuture designating the new margin, which has been inked blue and the old\u000aopposite margin is inked black. Perpendicular sections were taken of the\u000aentire specimen.\u000aMicro #21-23: New margin 8 frags, ESS.\u000aPart three, "additional axillary contents", consists of multiple fragments of\u000afibroadipose tissue, measuring in aggregate 3 x REMOVED_DATE x 1 cm. Three potential\u000alymph nodes were identified.\u000aMicro #24: Two lymph nodes, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro #25: One lymph node sectioned, 2 frags, ESS.\u000ajaw/\u000aReports to: GOLSHAN, MEHRA M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY W/REGIONAL LYMPH NODES\u000a[report_end]
