VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: DAVID I SOYBEL M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Agoston Tony Agoston, M.D., Ph.D.; Wai Chin Foo, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Jeffrey F Krane, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aSPECIMEN DESIGNATED "LEFT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A CLIP":\u000aBreast parenchyma with atypical lobular hyperplasia, radial scar, columnar cell\u000achange, and core biopsy site.\u000aCalcifications are present in association with ALH and with benign\u000aepithelium.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: None given.\u000aOperation: None given.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: None given.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) Lt breast lump, stitch - long = lat; short = sup. To mammo.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, medical record\u000anumber, and "#1. Left breast lump; stitch, long lateral, short superior", and\u000aconsists of an oriented wire-localized lumpectomy specimen (47.3 g; S - I REMOVED_DATE x\u000aM - L REMOVED_DATE x A - P REMOVED_DATE cm) with a small pink/tan skin ellipse (1.8 x REMOVED_DATE cm),\u000atwo orienting sutures (short superior, long lateral) and a localization wire.\u000aThe wire enters at the skin ellipse and exits at the posterior/medial junction.\u000aDuring processing, the wire was dislodged from the specimen. The specimen is\u000ainked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black;\u000aanterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. An\u000aaccompanying radiograph demonstrates a densely fibrotic breast parenchyma with\u000aa localization wire, a surgical clip, and scattered microcalcifications\u000aadjacent to the clip. No masses are appreciated on the radiograph. The\u000aspecimen is serially sectioned. The cut surface of the breast demonstrates a\u000awhite/tan well-circumscribed area (1.1 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which is identified by\u000athe surgical clip. This area measures approximately REMOVED_DATE cm to the medial\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm to the lateral margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to\u000athe anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to the skin ellipse, REMOVED_DATE cm to the superior margin,\u000aand approximately REMOVED_DATE cm to the inferior margin. The remaining breast\u000aparenchyma is densely fibrotic (85%) with an area of hemorrhage at the\u000amedial/inferior junction. Representative sections of the margins are\u000asubmitted. The area in question marked by the surgical clip is entirely\u000asubmitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Superior margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Inferior margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Area in question (clip in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, area in question in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), 1\u000afrag per block, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Representative parenchyma (to include hemorrhage), 1 frag per\u000ablock, RSS.\u000aWCF/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jeffrey F Krane M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a7/20/2007\u000a[report_end]
