VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Cheryl Adackapara, M.D.; Jacqueline M William, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Jane E. Brock, M.B., B.S., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aLEFT BREAST WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A CLIP AND CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aRESIDUAL ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA, REMOVED_DATE cm focus associated with\u000acalcifications and biopsy site (best seen on REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aA focus suspicious for atypical lobular hyperplasia present in block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID is no\u000alonger present deeper sections used for E-Cadherin stain.\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia.\u000aApocrine cysts.\u000aThe margins were inked and evaluated for the final diagnosis.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 57 year old woman, S/P L breast core bx (7/15/08) revealing ADH -\u000aexcision recommended - history of R breast Ca. Prior surgery: REMOVED_DATE  -\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID; REMOVED_DATE  - REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID; REMOVED_DATE  - REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID; REMOVED_DATE  - REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aOperation: L breast WL exc bx.\u000aOperative Findings: Not provided.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: None given.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) left breast tissue - short suture/superior, long suture/lateral, whip\u000astitch @ chest wall margin --> mammo.\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000aSpecimen contained clip, hook and wire. Called Dr. Rhei at 1:30 pm by Aperta.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "left breast tissue, short suture superior, long suture lateral, whipstitch\u000adeep margin", and consists of a REMOVED_DATE cm (superior to inferior), REMOVED_DATE cm (anterior\u000ato posterior), REMOVED_DATE cm (medial to lateral) breast biopsy with a localization\u000awire in placed and a short suture marking the superior margin and the long\u000asuture marking the lateral margin. An accompanying specimen radiograph\u000ademonstrates clip, and hook wire. The specimen was inked per pathology\u000aprotocol (Superior red, inferior green, anterior blue, posterior black, medial\u000aorange, lateral yellow). There is a focal area of disruption, consisting of a\u000afriable multi-inked fragment of tissue (1.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which was loosely\u000aadherent to the wire. Examination of this fragment reveals the clip embedded\u000awithin it. The wire enters the remainder of the specimen in the anterior\u000alateral aspect and exits in the posteromedial aspect of the specimen.\u000aSectioning of the specimen from superior to inferior reveals the biopsy cavity\u000a(1.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with no evidence of hemorrhage and surrounded by dense\u000afibrous tissue (0.4 cm in greatest dimension), and located REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000aanterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior\u000amargin, and less than REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin. The remainder of the\u000aspecimen consists of tan/white fibroadipose tissue. The specimen is submitted\u000ain its entirety for histological examination.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Superior margin, perpendicular, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sections with anterior, posterior, medial, and lateral margins,\u000amulti frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Inferior margin, perpendicular, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Nonadherent fragment containing clip, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-08-REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aCAD/lp\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jane E. Brock M.B., B.S., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a8/15/2008\u000a[report_end]
