VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aBROWN, FELIX, MARCEL, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by BROWN,FELIX MARCEL,M.D.\u000aRIGHT BREAST EXCISION FOR CALCIFICATIONS AND A MASS:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA, ONE (1) FOCUS AND DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU.\u000aSYNOPSIS:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA\u000aSize - REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aMultifocal? - No\u000aHistologic Type - Ductal\u000aHistologic Grade (SBR) - III (Poor)\u000aNuclear Grade - High\u000aEIC - Negative\u000aLymphovascular invasion - Absent\u000aDermal lymphatic invasion - N/A\u000aSkin invasion - N/A\u000aSkeletal muscle invasion - N/A\u000aFinal Margins (invasive) -\u000aNegative (no ink on tumor) - Superior, inferior, anterior, lateral,\u000amedial\u000aClose (<0.1 cm from margin) - posterior (broadfront)\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aTypes - Comedo, solid\u000aNuclear grade - High\u000aCalcifications in DCIS - Present\u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - Present\u000aExtent of DCIS\u000aNumber of blocks/total - REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Margins (DCIS)\u000aNegative (>0.3 cm) - Lateral, anterior, superior, inferior\u000aClose (0.1 - REMOVED_DATE cm) - Medial (focal)\u000aClose (<0.1 cm) - Medial (multifocal), posterior (focal)\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - Absent\u000aOTHER FINDINGS\u000aFlorid epithelial hyperplasia.\u000aCore biopsy site.\u000aAJCC CLASSIFICATION - REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID pNx MX\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER/PR/HER-2) - Pending\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: by RICHARDSON,ANDREA L.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for invasive carcinoma:\u000aEstrogen receptor negative\u000aProgesterone receptor negative\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) negative (0)\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000ainvasive carcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but\u000aonly a portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity\u000ain >10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 51 year-old female with clinical diagnosis of breast cancer\u000aon physical exam and mammogram. Indeterminate core.\u000aOperation: Right breast biopsy.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast mass.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1) Right breast mass, short - superior, long - lateral.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by HASKELL,HENRY D.,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "right breast mass short superior, long lateral", and consists of a mass of\u000afibrofatty tissue (6.9 cm lateral to medial, REMOVED_DATE cm superior to inferior, REMOVED_DATE \u000acm anterior to posterior). The specimen is inked as follows: anterior = red,\u000aposterior = black, medial = orange, lateral = yellow, superior = blue, inferior\u000a= green. Within the breast is a woody, well-circumscribed white/tan nodule (2.1\u000acm superior to inferior, approximately REMOVED_DATE cm medial to lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aanterior to posterior). The mass is REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin,\u000aa