VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID SENTINEL LYMPH NODE\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aBRODSKY, GILBERT, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by BRODSKY,GILBERT,M.D.\u000a1) SENTINEL LYMPH NODE, BIOPSY (including REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aThree (3) lymph nodes negative for tumor.\u000a2) RIGHT BREAST MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY (540g):\u000aBiopsy cavity (4 cm) with prominant giant cell reaction.\u000aSkin with scar.\u000aFour (4) lymph nodes negative for tumor.\u000aThere is no evidence of residual invasive ductal carcinoma or DCIS.\u000a3) LEFT BREAST, TISSUE, REDUCTION:\u000aBreast tissue with cysts and epithelial hyperplasia (up to REMOVED_DATE cm).\u000aSkin with no significant pathologic change.\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 51-year-old female with right breast cancer\u000aOperation: Right MRM with tram flap; left breast reduction\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast cancer\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1) Sentinel nodes\u000a2) Right breast (short/superior; long/lateral)\u000a3) Left breast, reduction tissue\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "SENTINEL NODE" (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aThree (3) lymph nodes with no tumor seen.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by LOMBARD,DAVID B.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in the frozen section room, in three parts -\u000aeach labeled with the patient's name and unit number.\u000aPart one, "1) sentinel node", consists of a single fragment of yellow/tan\u000afibroadipose tissue (6 x 2 x 1 cm). Three (3) lymph nodes are found within the\u000aspecimen. The first (1 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) is bisected and entirely submitted as\u000aFSA. The second (1.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) is bisected, inked black, and entirely\u000asubmitted as REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. The third (1.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) is bisected, inked blue,\u000aand entirely submitted as REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. The frozen remnants are entirely\u000asubmitted for microscopic analysis in permanent sections.\u000aMicro 1: FSA-R, 1 frag, ESS\u000aMicro 2: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 1 frag, ESS\u000aMicro 3: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 1 frag, ESS\u000aMicro 4: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 1 frag, ESS\u000aPart two, "2) right breast", consists of a modified radical mastectomy specimen\u000a(540g; 19 cm medial to lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm superior to inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000asuperficial to deep) with a skin ellipse (5.5 x REMOVED_DATE cm) with areola (3.0 cm), a\u000acurvilinear healing incision is present lateral to the nipple (4.0 cm). A\u000ascant axillary tail (10.0 cm length, REMOVED_DATE cm width) is present on the specimen.\u000aA biopsy cavity (4 x 3 x 3 cm) is located in the extreme lateral breast\u000aadjacent to the axillary tail. This biopsy cavity abuts the deep margin and\u000afocally no deep margin is present deep to the biopsy site. Although there is\u000afibrosis of the biopsy cavity, no gross evidence of residual invasive carcinoma\u000ais present. The axillary tail is removed, incubated in Bouin's, and\u000aextensively examined for lymph nodes. Lymph nodes are located and entirely\u000asubmitted for analysis. Representative sections of the remainder of the breast\u000aare submitted for analysis. No other gross lesions are found within the\u000abreast.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  lymph nodes from axillary tail, 1 lymph node/cass, multi frag,\u000aESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  biopsy cavity and subjacent deep margin, multi frag, RSS\u000aMicro 13: nipple, 2 frag, ESS\u000aMicro 14: scar, 3 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 15: UOQ, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 16: LOQ (adjacent to biopsy cavity), 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 17: UIQ, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 18: LIQ, 1 frag, RSS\u000aPart three, "3) left breast, reduction tissue", consists of multiple fragments\u000aof yellow adipose tissue and skin (15 x 12 x 4 cm in aggregate). No lesions\u000aare present in this specimen. The breast tissue consists of 50% fibrous\u000atissue and 50% fat. Representative sections are submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  4 frag, RSS\u000adl\u000aReports to: MATORY, YVEDT, L. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: SENTINEL LYMPH NODE\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY W/REGIONAL LYMPH NODES\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST REDUCTION MAMMOPLASTY\u000a[report_end]
