VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aRICHARDSON, ANDREA, L., M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by RICHARDSON,ANDREA L.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A CLIP:\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia, multiple foci, present within an intraductal\u000apapilloma and in tissue away from papilloma, (multiple levels examined,\u000aentire specimen submitted).\u000aFlorid ductal hyperplasia, apocrine change and rare calcifications\u000aassociated with hyalinized intraductal papilloma.\u000aCore biopsy site.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: None given.\u000aOperation: Left wire directed breast excision.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Area of atypicality in mass left breast.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Tissue from left breast.\u000aRADIOLOGY: The radiographic specimen contians macromark clip and wire.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by YOU,MINGJIAN JAMES,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in one part, labeled with the patient's name,\u000aunit number, and "tissue from left breast", consists of a fragment of\u000ayellow/tan adipose tissue (4.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with an attached white/tan skin\u000aellipse (2.1 x REMOVED_DATE cm). The specimen is unoriented and its surface is inked in\u000ablue. There is a localization wire which was detached from the specimen prior\u000ato arriving to the department of Pathology. The skin surface has a pink/tan\u000aarea (less than REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest dimension). The specimen is sectioned,\u000arevealing a white/tan lesion (1.1 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) that is less than REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000athe inked surface and REMOVED_DATE cm from the skin surface. No other lesions\u000asuspicious for tumor are identified. The radiographed is examined, which\u000areveals a clip and a poorly circumscribed dense area. The specimen is entirely\u000asubmitted.\u000aMICRO #1: Skin including the red/tan area, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMICRO #2-8: Tissue from the dense area of the radiograph, 12 frags, ESS.\u000aMICRO #9-13: Grossly uninvolved breast tissue, 10 frags, ESS.\u000aMICRO #14: Remaining skin, 2 frags, ESS\u000amjy\u000aReports to: CHRISTIAN, ROGER, L. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
