VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ROGER L CHRISTIAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Sebastien de Feraudy, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Jane E. Brock, M.B., B.S., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A CLIP AND CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aINVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA, well differentiated (modified Bloom-Richardson grade\u000aI/III; tubules score 2, nuclei score 1, mitoses score 1), measuring REMOVED_DATE cm on\u000athe glass slide (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), see Note.\u000aNo lymphovascular invasion is present\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, micropapillary, solid and cribriform types (low\u000anuclear grade) with calcifications and without necrosis is present in 6 of 7\u000aslides.\u000aInvasive carcinoma is REMOVED_DATE cm from the unoriented inked margin (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aDCIS is < REMOVED_DATE cm from the unoriented inked margin (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aOther findings:\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, focal)\u000aBiopsy site.\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for INVASIVE CARCINOMA and DCIS (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) NEGATIVE (0)\u000aNOTE: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID double stain highlights the invasive carcinoma (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aAJCC Classification (6th edition): REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDa\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Micro calcs, Rt breast.\u000aOperation: Wire-directed excision.\u000aOperative Findings: See op note.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Micro calcs, Rt breast.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) Right breast tissue.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Clip and calcs in specimen. OR called 11;15 - LBS.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number\u000aand "tissue, right breast", consists of an irregular tan/yellow lobulated\u000aportion of fibroadipose breast tissue (3.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with a\u000aneedle-localization wire in place. The needle-localization wire enters through\u000aone long axis of the specimen and exits through the opposite long axis of the\u000aspecimen. The specimen is received unoriented and is inked black. The\u000aspecimen is serially sectioned and there is a well-circumscribed red/brown\u000agranular previous biopsy cavity (1.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) which comes within less\u000athan REMOVED_DATE cm from the overlying margin. Within the biopsy cavity is a silver\u000ametallic biopsy clip. The remainder of the cut surface is tan/white and\u000ahomogeneous with focal areas of dense white fibrous tissue constituting less\u000athan 5% of the breast parenchyma. The specimen is serially sectioned and\u000asubmitted in its entirety.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross sections block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID to include previous biopsy\u000acavity adjacent to needle-localization wire block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID to include biopsy clip.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 3 frags, ESS.\u000aImmunohistochemical studies for estrogen receptor, progesterone\u000areceptor, and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu were evaluated by manual morphometric analysis\u000ausing the following criteria:\u000aHormone receptor analysis:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low > 0% - < 10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not\u000ayet been determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10%\u000aof tumor cells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor\u000acells but only a portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aEquivocal (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity in >30% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aExternal controls are evaluated and show appropriate Immunoreactivity.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for\u000ainvestigational use only.\u000aSEK/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jane E. Brock M.B., B.S., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000aTuesday REMOVED_MONTH 06, 2009 at 09:13:49AM\u000a[report_end]
