VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aFOLKERTH, REBECCA, DUNN, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by FOLKERTH,REBECCA DUNN,M.D.\u000aRIGHT BREAST NEEDLE-DIRECTED BIOPSY FOLLOWING PREVIOUS NEEDLE CORE:\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia.\u000aFibrocystic changes, including mycrocysts and apocrine metaplasia.\u000aBiopsy site.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: None given.\u000aOperation: RIght needle directed breast biopsy.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal right mammogram.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Right breast tissue.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Clip in specimen. JL\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by HENDERSON,JOEL M.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number\u000aand "#1 right breast tissue". The specimen is accompanied by a radiograph of\u000athe whole specimen which shows a clip centrally located in the specimen\u000aassociated with an area of minute calcifications and increased density. The\u000aspecimen consists of a single fragment of tan/yellow fibroadipose tissue (5.0 x\u000a4.2 x REMOVED_DATE cm). A localization wire is in place and the specimen has been\u000apreviously inked by the surgeon according to pathology protocol for the\u000aevaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red;\u000ainferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. The specimen is sliced\u000afrom anterior to inferior to reveal an area of firm, diffuse fibrosity (3.0 x\u000a1.5 x REMOVED_DATE cm) located closest to the lateral and inferior aspects of the\u000aspecimen. The remaining 75% of the specimen consists of yellow adipose tissue.\u000aNo other lesions are identified. A specimen radiograph reveals a clip to be\u000alocated in slice 7. Representative sections are submitted. Approximately 70%\u000aof the specimen is submitted for histologic examination.\u000aMicro 1: slice 1, superior margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 2: slice 4, posterior aspect, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 3: slice 5, posterior aspect, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 4&5: slice 6, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 6&7: slice 7, clip and cassette 7, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 8&9: slice 8, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 10&11: slice 9, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 12&13: slice 10, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 14: slice 11, inferior margin, 3 frags, RSS.\u000ajmh\u000aReports to: SHOJI, BRENT, T. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
