VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Amend/Addenda\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: BRENT T SHOJI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-06-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000a********** Addended Report ***********\u000aResident: Rachel E Factor, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Andrea L Richardson, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aLEFT BREAST WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION WITH A CLIP\u000aSeverely atypical ductal hyperplasia in 8 of 20 blocks with rare duct spaces\u000afilling criteria for DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, cribriform type (low nuclear\u000agrade).\u000aThe severe atypical ductal hyperplasia is focally REMOVED_DATE cm from medial margin.\u000aThere are associated calcifications, but no necrosis is seen.\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU is present.\u000aThe prior core biopsy site is present.\u000aSkeletal muscle with no significant pathologic change.\u000aThis could be classified as an AJCC (sixth edition): Tis pNx Mx\u000aNOTE: Slides also reviewed by Dr. Susan Lester, who concurs that some foci are\u000aDCIS.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aClinical History: Abnormal left mammogram with atypia on core bx.\u000aOperation: Needle-directed left breast biopsy.\u000aOperative Findings: None provided.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: None provided.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Left breast tissue, short superior, long lateral - mammo.\u000aRADIOLOGY REPORT:\u000aClip, wire, + calcs. Called to T. Hanscom.\u000a---B. Townsend\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in one part, labeled with the patient's name,\u000aunit number, and "#1. Left breast tissue", and was accompanied by a radiograph\u000awith inking by the radiologist to show calcifications and the clip adjacent to\u000athe wire. The specimen was received with the wire separated from the lesion.\u000aExcisional biopsy consists of one fragment of yellow/beige fibroadipose tissue\u000a(5.2 cm superior to inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm medial to lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm anterior to\u000aposterior), oriented by the surgeon with a short suture for superior, and a\u000along suture for lateral. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the\u000aevaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red;\u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. The specimen does not contain\u000aany skin nor does it contain the nipple. Within the specimen is a hemorrhagic\u000ared/tan/black lesion with irregular borders (0.7 M-L x REMOVED_DATE A-P x REMOVED_DATE F-I cm),\u000alocated REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin, greater than REMOVED_DATE cm\u000ato the inferior margin, and greater than REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin. The\u000aspecimen is greater than 90% adipose tissue, and less than 10% fibrous tissue.\u000aIt is extending to 12 slices including superior and inferior end, and the\u000aaforementioned lesion is located in slice #5 and #6, and while the clip was not\u000agrossly visually identified. An x-ray revealed the clip in slide #6 from the\u000asuperior edge.\u000aNOTE: The red lesion containing the clip may be consistent with Gelfoam in the\u000abiopsy cavity. The clip and the small amount of surrounding tissue that came\u000aoff with it is retained in the specimen jar.\u000aMicro cassette REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #1A (S, A, M), 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro cassette REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #1B (S, A, M), 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro cassette REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #2 (P, L, A), 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro cassette REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #2 (P, M, A), 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro cassette REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #3 (P, L, A), 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro cassette REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #3 (P, M, A), 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro cassette REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #4 (P, L, A), 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro cassette REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #4 (P, M, A), 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro cassette REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #5 (P, L, A), 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro cassette REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #5 (P, M, A), 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro cassette REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #6 (A, P, M, L), 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro cassette REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #6B location of clip (A, P, M, L), 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro cassette REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #7 (A, P, M, L), 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro cassette REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #7 (A, P, M, L), 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro cassette REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #8 (A, P, M, L), 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro cassette REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #8 (P, L), 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro cassette REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #9 (A, P, M, L), 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro cassette REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #10 (P, M, L), 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro cassette REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #11A and 11B (P, M, L), 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro cassette REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #12A (I, M, L, ?P), 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro cassette REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #12B (I), 3 frags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-06-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aSAS/jp\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Andrea L Richardson M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a10/27/2006\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM:\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for DCIS (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) NEGATIVE (1+)\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000acarcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but only\u000aa portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in >10%\u000aof tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in\u000a>10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aAddendum #1 by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
