VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aWEINSTEIN, MICHAEL, H., M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by WEINSTEIN,MICHAEL H.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED BIOPSY FOR A MAMMOGRAPHIC ABNORMALITY:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA.\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU.\u000aSYNOPSIS:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA\u000aSize - REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000aHistologic Type - Ductal, mucinous (colloid).\u000aHistologic Grade (SBR) - II (Moderate).\u000aNuclear Grade - Intermediate.\u000aEIC - Negative.\u000aLymphovascular invasion - Absent.\u000aDermal lymphatic invasion - N/A.\u000aSkin invasion - N/A.\u000aSkeletal muscle invasion - N/A.\u000aFinal Margins (invasive)\u000aNegative (no ink on tumor) - Superior, lateral, deep, anterior.\u000aClose (<0.1 cm from margin) - Inferomedial (focal; block #2).\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aTypes - Cribriform.\u000aNuclear grade - Intermediate.\u000aCalcifications in DCIS - Absent.\u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - Absent.\u000aExtent of DCIS\u000aNumber of blocks/total: - REMOVED_DATE blocks.\u000aEstimated overall size: - REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000aFinal Margins (DCIS)\u000aNegative (>0.3 cm) - superior, anterior, deep, medial,\u000alateral\u000aClose (<0.1 cm) - inferior (focal; block #5).\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - Absent\u000aOTHER FINDINGS: Prior core biopsy site changes.\u000aAJCC CLASSIFICATION - REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDb pN MX\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER/PR/HER-2) - Pending.\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: by RICHARDSON,ANDREA L.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for invasive carcinoma (block 3 ):\u000aEstrogen receptor - POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor - POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) - NEGATIVE (0)\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000ainvasive carcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but\u000aonly a portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity\u000ain >10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: REMOVED_DATE  - core showed fibroadipose tissue.\u000aMammo subtle hypoechioic area (5 x 6 x 9 mm) in left upper inner\u000aquadrant.\u000aOperation: Left needle localized breast biopsy.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal mammogram.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Left breast tissue (mammo).\u000aMass in specimen. JL\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by BUNDOCK,ELIZABETH A.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit\u000anumber, and "#1, left breast tissue", and consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aportion of fibrofatty breast tissue with a needle localization wire in place.\u000aThe specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation\u000aof margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior =\u000agreen; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. The specimen is serially sectioned\u000a(superior to inferior) revealing a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm tan-white, focally\u000agritty, rubbery mass, which grossly appears to be at the inferior margin, comes\u000ato within REMOVED_DATE cm of the anterior margin and approximately REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000amedial margin (the remaining margins are at least REMOVED_DATE cm from the mass). This\u000alesion corresponds to the subtle hypoechoic area on the accompanying\u000aradiograph. Two (2) red-brown hemorrhagic foci are present adjacent to and\u000awithin the mass, which may correspond to previous FNA tracts. The remaining\u000abreast tissue consists of predominantly yellow-tan lobulated fat (approximately\u000a80%). No other lesions are grossly identified.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  mass (sequentially from superior most to inferior most aspect),\u000ain relationship to inferior, anterior, and medial margin, 5 frags\u000atotal, ESS.\u000aMicro 4 and 5 show mass at the inferior margin.\u000aMicro 6: posterior margin nearest lesion, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 7: superior margin nearest lesion, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 8: lateral margin nearest lesion, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aReports to: OSTEEN, ROBERT, T. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
