TED SPECIMENS REVIEWED:\u000aLeft breast, upper inner quadrant, needle biopsy; REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID; REMOVED_DATE \u000aCOMMENT: Smooth muscle myosin stain is positive for myoepithelial cells\u000aaround the ductal carcinoma in situ consistent with the diagnosis.\u000aAJCC pTNM Classification (6th Ed.): pTis pREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID(sn)(i-) pREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aThe pathologic TNM classification above is based only on the information\u000aavailable to the pathologist, and therefore may not be accurate.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by: Michael J. Ross, M.D.\u000aClinical diagnosis & history:\u000aDuctal carcinoma in situ of left breast\u000aTissue-Designation:\u000aA.Sentinel lymph node - left breast, upper and inner\u000aB.Breast, excision with margins - left\u000aGross description:\u000aThe specimen is received in two parts.\u000aSpecimen A labeled "sentinel lymph node, left breast" is received fresh and\u000aconsists of a 4 x 4 x 2 cm. aggregate of fat containing five soft, pink lymph\u000anodes ranging in diameter from REMOVED_DATE to REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000aSection code: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - two bisected lymph nodes, one inked, 4X\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - two bisected lymph nodes, one inked, 4X\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - smallest lymph node, 1X\u000aSpecimen B labeled "left upper and inner breast tissue" consists of a 61 gram,\u000a6 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. spherical portion of partly yellow adipose, partly firm,\u000atan-pink tissue containing a needle wire. No orienting sutures are present.\u000aThe margins are inked black prior to sectioning. Cut section reveals a central\u000a1.3 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. poorly circumscribed area of firmer pink tissue surrounded\u000aby yellow adipose tissue mixed with streaks of firmer white tissue. The\u000aspecimen is serially sectioned, labeled REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. All but a few trimmed\u000afragments are submitted. 29 agg.\u000aDictated by: MJR____(signature on file)____DENNIS J. FEEN, M.D. REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a____(signature on file)____MICHAEL J. ROSS, M.D. REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a[report_end]
