en sequentially from superior to inferior, multiple\u000afrags, ESS\u000aPart B, "tissue - left breast - non-palp mass," consists of an unoriented\u000aexcision of fibroadipose tissue (2.3 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with a localization wire\u000aembedded at one pole. The accompanying radiograph demonstrates the localization\u000awire in place within a vaguely dense area of the specimen. Cut surfaces\u000ademonstrate dense white-tan tissue with no obvious masses. The specimen (inked\u000ablue) is entirely submitted sequentially from localizing wire.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: entire specimen, 3 frags each, ESS\u000aDB/jp\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by William R Welch M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
