inel node mapping.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast ca.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Hot sentinel nodes x 4.\u000a2. Right breast, short superior, long lateral, bowtie axilla.\u000a3. Right axillary contents.\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "#1, HOT SENTINEL LYMPH NODES X 4" (FSA, TPA):\u000aConsistent with metastatic carcinoma in one (1) of (1) lymph node frozen.\u000aRest of lymph nodes sent for permanent sections.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by BARRY,MARC,M.B.,B.CH.,B.A.O.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in three parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart one, labeled "#1, hot sentinel nodes x 4", consists of fragments of\u000ared-yellow soft tissue (4.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with five firm lymph nodes (largest\u000ais REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). A representative section of the firmest lymph node\u000ais submitted for FSA. Touch preparation is prepared (TPA). Lymph nodes are\u000asampled in toto for microscopic examination.\u000aMicro 1: FSA remnant, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro 2: formalin fixed portion of frozen lymph node, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 3: 1 lymph node, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 4: 1 lymph node, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 5: 1 lymph node, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 6: 1 lymph node, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aPart two, labeled "#2, right breast tissue, short superior, long lateral,\u000abowtie axilla", consists of a right mastectomy specimen with skin (14 x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm), areola (2.5 cm) and nipple (1.5 cm). The breast tissue (16 x 13 x 3 cm)\u000aand axillary tail (1.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) are present. There is a tumor mass (3.5\u000ax REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) present centrally in the specimen lying REMOVED_DATE cm from the deep\u000amargin. Representative tumor and normal are taken for tumor bank by Dr.\u000aAndrea Richardson of the breast service. Remaining breast shows multiple areas\u000aof fibrosis, which extends to area to within REMOVED_DATE cm of deep margin. Underlying\u000athe nipple is an area of fibrosis (2.5 cm in diameter and REMOVED_DATE cm from deep\u000amargin) with cream colored areas present within ductal structures. No nodes\u000aare identified at the axillary end of the specimen. The specimen is sampled\u000afor microscopic examination.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  tumor with deep margin inked black, 3 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  tissue under nipple, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 12: nipple, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 13: upper inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 14: inner lower quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 15: outer lower quadrant, REMOVED_DATE cm from tumor, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 16: upper outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 17: central fibrosis, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aPart three, labeled "#3, right axillary contents", consists of an axillary\u000acontents (6.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate measurement). Lymph nodes are\u000aidentified. The specimen is sampled as follows for microscopic examination.\u000aMicro 18: 2 lymph nodes, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 19: ? lymph nodes, 5 frags, ESS.\u000amab\u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: SENTINEL LYMPH NODE\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY W/REGIONAL LYMPH NODES\u000a[report_end]
