VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST MASTECTOMY W/REGIONAL LYMPH NODES\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aWELCH, WILLIAM, ROBERT, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by WELCH,WILLIAM ROBERT,M.D.\u000a1) LEFT BREAST:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA, PREDOMINANTLY LOBULAR, BUT WITH SOME FEATURES OF\u000aDUCTAL DIFFERENTIATION (2.5 cm), moderately differentiated,\u000awith Pagetoid ductal spread.\u000aTumor invades at least into the reticular dermis.\u000aNo lymphatic/vascular invasion is identified.\u000aPerineural invasion is present.\u000aThe margins are free of invasive carcinoma.\u000aDCIS, solid and cribrifrom types (intermediate nuclear grade), is present\u000aoutside the area involved by the invasive tumor.\u000aThe margins are free of in situ and invasive tumor.\u000aLobular Carcinoma In Situ, focal.\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia.\u000aFibrocystic change including cysts and apocrine metaplasia.\u000aADENOCARCINOMA, metastatic in two of four (2:4) lymph nodes with prominent\u000aextranodal invasion; largest deposit REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000aAJCC Stage REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Mx.\u000a2) LEFT AXILLARY NODE:\u000aADENOCARCINOMA, metastatic in one (1) lymph node.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: None given.\u000aOperation: Left simple mastectomy\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast CA\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1) Left breast\u000a#2) Left axillary node\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by HORNICK,JASON L.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart one, labeled "left breast", consists of a 914g simple mastectomy specimen\u000a(25 x 19 x REMOVED_DATE cm) with a white/tan skin ellipse (24 x REMOVED_DATE cm) with an\u000aunremarkable nipple (1.4 x REMOVED_DATE cm). There is no grossly identifiable scar.\u000aThe deep margin is inked black. There is a hard, tan/white, irregular mass\u000a(2.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) in the lower inner quadrant located REMOVED_DATE cm from the inked\u000adeep margin and REMOVED_DATE cm from the skin. Representative mass is given to the\u000atumor bank. The remainder of the breast parenchyma is predominantly yellow\u000aadipose tissue, with scattered white firm areas, and several blue cysts\u000ameasuring up to REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest dimension. Four lymph nodes are identified\u000ain the lateral aspect of the specimen, the largest measuring REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest\u000adimension.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  mass, 3 frags, RSS\u000aMicro 4: inked deep margin closest to mass, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 5: skin closest to mass, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 6: upper inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 7: lower inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 8: upper outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 9: lower outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 10: nipple, 2 frags, RSS\u000aMicro 11: largest lymph node (bisected), 2 frags, ESS\u000aMicro 12: 3 lymph nodes, 3 frags, ESS\u000aPart two, labeled "left axillary node", consists of one fragment of yellow/tan\u000afibroadipose tissue (3.4 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), containing a firm, tan, irregular\u000alymph node measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The lymph node is sectioned and\u000aentirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  lymph node, 4 frags, ESS\u000ajlh\u000aReports to: CHRISTIAN, ROGER, L. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY W/REGIONAL LYMPH NODES\u000a[report_end]
