VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aCRUM, CHRISTOPHER, PAUL, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by CRUM,CHRISTOPHER PAUL,M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "LEFT BREAST, PARTIAL MASTECTOMY":\u000aResidual intraductal papilloma, present, within REMOVED_DATE mm of an inked margin.\u000aMild atypia is present, similar to the prior biopsy (See REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aFocal chronic inflammation, fibrosis, and hemosiderin deposition,\u000aconsistent with prior core biopsy site.\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy.\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "ANTERIOR ABDOMINAL WALL":\u000aFibroconnective tissue and degenerative muscle with no tumor present.\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "LEFT PARACOLIC GUTTER":\u000aPlease see separate cytopathology report.\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "RIGHT PARACOLIC GUTTER":\u000aPlease see separate cytopathology report.\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "ADHESION TO LIVER" (INCLUDING FSA):\u000aFragments of fibrous tissue.\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "ANTERIOR ABDOMINAL WALL ADHESION" (including FSB):\u000afragments of fibrous tissue.\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "SUPERCOLIC OMENTUM":\u000aFibroadipose tissue.\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "SMALL BOWEL ADHESIONS":\u000aFragments of fibroconnective and granulation tissue.\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "MASS FROM LEFT SIDE OF PELVIC SIDEWALL":\u000aFragment of fibroconnective tissue with multiple organizing intravascular\u000athrombi.\u000aComment: There is no evidence of malignancy (Clinical: second look\u000aprocedure following therapy for ovarian cancer;see REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: History of ovarian cancer. 2nd look laparotomy.\u000aOperation: Left breast partial mastectomy, open laparoscopy, exploratory\u000alaparotomy, multiple peritoneal biopsies\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast mass/ovarian cancer for 2nd look\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Left breast tissue with wire & palpable mass\u000a2. Anterior abdominal wall\u000a3. Left paracolic gutter\u000a4. Right paracolic gutter\u000a5. Biopsy of adhesion to liver (FS)\u000a6. Anterior abdominal wall adhesion (FS)\u000a7. Supercolic omentum\u000a8. Small bowel adhesions\u000a9. Mass from left side of pelvic sidewall\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "#5 ADHESION TO LIVER" (FSA):\u000aNo tumor present.\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "#6 ANTERIOR ABDOMINAL WALL ADHESIONS" (FSB):\u000aNo tumor present.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by SHEN,JIAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in 9 parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart 1, "left breast tissue with wire and palpable mass", consists of a\u000afragment of breast tissue (6 x 4 x REMOVED_DATE cm) with attached wire and mammogram.\u000aThe specimen was received inked by the surgeon per pathology protocol for the\u000aevaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red;\u000ainferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. The specimen was\u000asectioned perpendicular to medial and lateral axis to reveal a red/tan\u000ahemorrhagic adhesion (0.5 cm in diameter) which is located at the tip of the\u000awire, and extends REMOVED_DATE cm from anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from lateral margin, REMOVED_DATE \u000acm from superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from medial\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm from posterior margin. A chip is present within this area, and\u000aremoved before the histologic examination. The remainder of the breast\u000atissue is predominantly yellow/tan. The entire lesion is submitted.\u000aMicro 1 - center of lesion with posterior margin, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro 2 - center of lesion with closest anterior & lateral margin, 1 frag,\u000aESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE - clostest inferior & superior margin, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 5 - inferior, lateral, anterior margin, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro 6 - inferior & superior margin, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE - inferior & lateral margin, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 9 - superior medial margin, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 10 - inferior posterior & lateral margins, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 11 - inferior & superior margin, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE - area of fibrosis, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aPart 2, "anterior abdominal wall", consists of a fragment of white/tan soft\u000atissue (2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with cauterized edge. The entire specimen is\u000asubmitted.\u000aMicro 14 - anterior abdominal wall, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aPart 3 and part 4, "left and right pericolic gutter", are entirely submitted\u000ato cytology.\u000aPart 5, "adhesion to liver", consists of a single fragment of white/tan soft\u000atissue (1.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) which is entirely frozen and submitted as "FSA".\u000aMicro 15 - FSA remnant, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aPart 6, "anterior abdominal wall adhesion", consists of multiple fragments of\u000apink/tan soft tissue (0.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm, and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x\u000a0.1 cm) which are entirely submitted frozen and submitted as "FSB".\u000aMicro 16 - FSB remnant, multiple frags, ESS.\u000aPart 7, "supercolic omentum", consists of two fragments of white/tan omentum\u000a(8.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm and REMOVED_DATE x 2 x REMOVED_DATE cm). No gross lesion is identified\u000awithin the specimen. Representative sections are submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE - supercolic omentum, 6 frags, RSS.\u000aPart 8, "small bowel adhesions", consists of two irregular fragments of red/tan\u000asoft tissue (0.6 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) which are entirely submitted.\u000aMicro 19 - small bowel adhesions, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aPart 9, "mass from left side of pelvic sidewall", consists of a single fragment\u000aof white/tan irregular soft tissue (3 x 4 x REMOVED_DATE cm) which is entirely\u000asubmitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE - mass from left side of pelvic sidewall, 11 frags, ESS.\u000aReports to: MUTO, MICHAEL, GEORGE M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SOFT TISSUE BIOPSY\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SOFT TISSUE BIOPSY\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SOFT TISSUE BIOPSY\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: OMENTUM BIOPSY\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SOFT TISSUE BIOPSY\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SOFT TISSUE MASS OR SIMPLE EXCISION\u000a[report_end]
