VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aHIRSCH, MICHELLE, S., M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by HIRSCH,MICHELLE S.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR MICROCALCIFICATIONS:\u000aBenign breast tissue with atypical ductal hyperplasia, intraductal\u000apapilloma, epithelial hyperplasia, apocrine metaplasia, and\u000acalcifications in benign epithelium.\u000aFat necrosis, hemosiderin and a giant cell reaction consistent with prior\u000abiopsy site.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000a(The specimen is entirely submitted for histologic examination, and\u000alevels are examined on select tissue sections.)\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "NEW INFERIOR DEEP MARGIN":\u000aBenign breast tissue with atypical ductal hyperplasia, intraductal\u000apapilloma, epithelial hyperplasia, apocrine metaplasia, and\u000acalcifications in benign epithelium.\u000aFat necrosis, hemosiderin, and a giant cell reaction consistent with prior\u000abiopsy site.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000a(The specimen is entirely submitted for histologic examination, and levels\u000aare examined on select tissue sections.)\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 61 year old female s/p right stereo core REMOVED_DATE  biopsy for\u000aindeterminate microcalcifications with patch consistent with\u000aintraductal papilloma and florid epithelial hyperplasia.\u000aOperation: Right needle localization breast biopsy\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right abnormal mammogram\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1) Right breast tissue - needle loc.\u000a#2) New inferior deep margin - right breast\u000aRADIOLOGY: 1) Wire and calcifications in specimen. LBT.\u000a2) Clip in specimen. LBT.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by DAVID,FRANK SAMUEL,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart one, labeled "#1. right needle localized breast tissue", consists of a\u000asingle mass of yellow/tan fibroadipose tissue (4.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). There is a\u000alocalized wire protruding from the specimen. The specimen has been inked by\u000athe operating room per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins:\u000aposterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral\u000a= yellow; medial = orange. Near the medial aspect of the specimen is an area\u000aof scarring consistent with prior core biopsy site. The remainder of the\u000aspecimen is uniformly fibrofatty and grossly unremarkable. An accompanying\u000amammogram is reveiwed and demonstrates the presence of a localizing wire and a\u000aclip. The clip is not grossly identified. The specimen is serially sectioned\u000aand entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  medial (firmest area in #3), ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  lateral, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  remainder of specimen, medial to lateral, ESS (firmest area in\u000a#7-11)\u000aPart two, labeled "#2. new inferior deep margin right breast", consists of a\u000asingle fragment of yellow/tan fibroadipose tissue (6.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The\u000aspecimen has been inked by the operating room per pathology protocol for the\u000aevaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red;\u000ainferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. The interior of the\u000aspecimen is uniformly fibrofatty without discrete masses or suspicious lesions.\u000aThe specimen is entirely submitted.\u000aMicro 15: lateral, ESS\u000aMicro 16: medial, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  remainder of specimen, ESS\u000afsd\u000aReports to: LOCKHART, DIANE, CATHERINE M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN\u000a[report_end]
