 to REMOVED_DATE cm) inferior (0.1 cm)(REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID)\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU: Present\u000aLYMPH NODES\u000aSentinel lymph nodes (3 HE levels examined): Negative\u000aNumber of positive nodes 0\u000aNumber of nodes examined 2\u000aTOTAL POSITIVE NODES (all specimens) REMOVED_DATE \u000aOTHER FINDINGS:\u000aADH, ALH with pagetoid spread, core biopsy site, sclerosing adenosis\u000aAJCC CLASSIFICATION (6th edition) REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID pREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID MX [With multiple foci of invasion]\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER/PR/HER-2) Pending\u000aNOTE: The case has been reviewed by Dr. Andrea Richardson of Breast Pathology,\u000awho concurs.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 78-year-old woman with right breast cancer diagnosed REMOVED_DATE \u000awith right core biopsy showing ICD, DCIS (for mass).\u000aOperation: Right breast wire localized lumpectomy, SNM, SLNB, possible ALND.\u000aOperative Findings:\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Preop: Right breast cancer. Postop: Right breast\u000acancer.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Right sentinel node hot and blue x2 (FS).\u000aB/2. Right breast tissue, short superior, long lateral, whipstitch chest wall\u000amargin.\u000aRADIOLOGY REPORT:\u000aMass wire in specimen. Phoned to Dr. Rhei in the OR.\u000a---Golvez/Budinell\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "RIGHT SENTINEL NODE HOT BLUE REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aTwo lymph nodes negative for tumor.\u000aOR Consultation by: JONATHAN NEIL GLICKMAN, M.D., PH.D.\u000aResident: MICHAEL ROH, M.D., PH.D., Stefan Kraft, MD\u000aThe senior physician certifies that he/she personally conducted a gross and/or\u000amicroscopic examination of the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed\u000athe rapid diagnos(es) related thereto.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in parts, each labeled with the patient's name,\u000aunit number.\u000aPart A, "#1 right sentinel node hot and blue x2", and contains two lymph nodes,\u000athe smallest measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm and is entirely submitted as REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID,\u000athe second is measuring 2 x 1 x REMOVED_DATE cm and is entirely submitted as REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID remnant, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID remnant, ESS.\u000aPart B, "#2 right breast tissue short suture superior, long lateral whipstitch\u000achest wall margin, and contains one lumpectomy specimen measuring REMOVED_DATE cm medial\u000ato lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm superior to inferior and REMOVED_DATE cm anterior to posterior.\u000aThere are three sutures placed by the surgeon long indicating the lateral,\u000ashort indicating superior and a whipstitch indicating the chest wall margin.\u000aThere is also a localizing wire. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol\u000afor the evaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red;\u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. Included with the specimen is\u000athe mammogram showing a mass. Within the specimen, there is a stellate mass\u000ameasuring REMOVED_DATE cm medial to lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm superior to inferior and REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aanterior to posterior. It is REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000alateral margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior margin and REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID through REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Tumor with respect to lateral, inferior and posterior\u000amargin, 1 to 2 frags each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID through REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Tumor with respect to anterior and posterior margin, 1\u000afrag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID through REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Additional sections of tumor, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID through REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Closest medial margin, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID through REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Additional sections of fibrous tissue, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aNote: A 100% of the tumor and fibrous tissue and 80% of the overall specimen\u000aare submitted.\u000aOOB/ajb\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Lucian R Chirieac M.D., Electronically signed on\u000a7/12/2006\u000aSurgical Addendum: (7/12/06)\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for INVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) NEGATIVE (0)\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000acarcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but only\u000aa portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in >10%\u000aof tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in\u000a>10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aAddendum #1 by Andrea L Richardson M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a7/13/2006\u000a[report_end]
