ocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue;\u000asuperior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. Please note the\u000asutures that inked do not correspond to a right breast excision. Pathology\u000aspoke directly to Dr. Rhei on REMOVED_DATE  and she confirms that orientation is not\u000acorrect with the exception of anterior (blue ink) and posterior (black ink).\u000aThe specimen is accompanied by a radiograph, exhibiting an intact hookwire and\u000alucency, consistent with calcification (please see radiology report). The\u000aspecimen is serially sectioned from the red-inked margin to the green-inked\u000amargin. The breast tissue is composed of approximately 95% tan/white, dense,\u000afocally cystic (cyst measuring up to REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest dimension) fibrous\u000astroma and 5% yellow lobulated adipose tissue. No gross mass identified.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Breast tissue sequentially from red-inked margin to green-inked\u000amargin, multi frags, ESS.\u000aNote: Probable calcifications in micros REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aDL/ag\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jeffrey F Krane M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a10/8/2008\u000a[report_end]
