0aEstrogen receptor - POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor - POSITIVE - LOW\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) - NEGATIVE (0)\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000ainvasive carcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but\u000aonly a portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity\u000ain >10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 46 year old female with abnl mammo, core bx, REMOVED_DATE  showed\u000ainvasive R breast CA with features of ductal and lobular\u000adifferentiation. In RUIQ (clip placed after core biopsy),\u000ah/o Hodkin's disease 10 years ago treated by radiation.\u000aOperation: Right modified radical mastectomy.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast carcinoma.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Right breast modifed radical mastectomy.\u000a2. Right axillary contents.\u000a3. Core biopsy site.\u000a4. Left breast reduction specimen.\u000a5. Right breast tissue.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by ABBOTT,DEREK W,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received in five parts.\u000aPart one, "right breast modified radical mastectomy", received is a breast\u000a(23.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). This is a skin-sparing mastectomy and contains an\u000aareola (4 cm in diameter) with nipple (1.0 cm). An axillary tail is present on\u000athe specimen (9.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The deep surface is lined by smooth fascial\u000aplane without obvious skeletal muscle. The deep surface is inked in black\u000aand the specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a stellate mass (1.5 x REMOVED_DATE x\u000a1.0 cm) lying REMOVED_DATE cm from the deep margin. Representative tissue has been sent\u000afor special studies. The mass and underlying deep margin are submitted for\u000ahistologic evaluation. Representative quadrants of the breast are submitted\u000afor histologic evaluation. The axillary tail is dissected from lymph nodes and\u000athese are submitted for histologic evaluation.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  representative sections of mass including deep margin, 1 frag\u000aeach cassette, RSS.\u000aMicro 4: deep margin underlying mass, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 5: representative tissue from upper outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 6: representative tissue from lower outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 7: representative tissue from upper inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 8: representative section from lower inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 9: nipple, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  4 potential lymph nodes, each cassette, 4 frags, RSS.\u000aPart two, "right axillary contents", received are multiple fragments of fatty\u000asoft tissue (4.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The lymph nodes are dissected from the\u000aspecimen and they are submitted for histologic evaluation.\u000aMicro 13: 3 potential lymph nodes, 3 frags, RSS.\u000aPart three, "core biopsy site", received is a single fragment of white/tan soft\u000atissue (0.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The specimen is submitted in its entirety for\u000ahistologic evaluation.\u000aMicro 14: core biopsy site, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aPart four, "left breast reduction specimen", received are multiple fragments of\u000afatty soft tissue with attached skin (21.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The specimen is\u000aserially sectioned revealing no gross abnormalities. Representative sections\u000aare submitted for histologic evaluation.\u000aMicro 15&16: left breast tissue, 1 frag each cassette, RSS.\u000aPart five, "right breast tissue", received is a single skin fragment of with\u000aunderlying soft tissue (22.1 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). No gross abnormalities are\u000apresent. Representative sections are submitted for histologic evaluation.\u000aMicro 17: skin from right breast tissue, 2 frags, RSS.\u000adwa\u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY W/REGIONAL LYMPH NODES\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SKIN- OTHER THAN CYST, TAG OR DEBRIDEMENT\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST REDUCTION MAMMOPLASTY\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST BIOPSY W/O MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
