long stitch lateral", consists of\u000aa 450-g left simple mastectomy specimen (21.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with an\u000aoverlying tan/white wrinkled skin ellipse (5.0 x REMOVED_DATE cm), with nipple-areolar\u000acomplex (4.0 x REMOVED_DATE cm) and everted nipple (1.1 cm in diameter), and a short\u000asuture designating the superior margin, and a long suture designating the\u000alateral margin. The deep margin is inked black and the specimen is serially\u000asectioned to reveal focal areas of dense white fibrous tissue constituting\u000aapproximately 60% of the breast parenchyma and multiple tan/brown serous\u000afluid-filled unilocular cysts (ranging from REMOVED_DATE to REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest\u000adimension). No discrete lesions are grossly identified. A lateral aspect of\u000athe specimen is sectioned with no lymph nodes grossly identified.\u000aRepresentative sections are submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Nipple, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Upper outer quadrant with deep margin, 2 frags each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lower outer quadrant with deep margin, 2 frags each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lower inner quadrant with deep margin, 2 frags each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Upper inner quadrant with deep margin, 2 frags each, RSS.\u000aPart B, "right breast", consists of a 362-g right simple mastectomy specimen\u000a(18.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with an overlying tan/white ovoid skin excision (5.0 cm\u000ax REMOVED_DATE cm), with a nipple-areolar complex (4.2 x REMOVED_DATE cm) with everted nipple\u000a(0.9 cm in diameter), and a short suture designating the superior margin, and a\u000along suture designating the lateral margin. The deep margin is inked black and\u000athere is an irregular ragged posterior defect (3.0 x REMOVED_DATE cm - orange) located\u000awithin the right upper outer quadrant consistent with previous biopsy cavity.\u000aThe specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a variegated irregular tan/white\u000ato red/brown previous biopsy cavity (6.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) which is located\u000awithin the right upper outer quadrant underlying the previously described\u000aposterior/deep margin defect, and is located REMOVED_DATE cm from the overlying\u000atan/white skin excision. The remainder of the breast parenchyma is tan/yellow\u000aand lobulated with focal areas of dense white fibrous tissue constituting\u000aapproximately 10% of the breast parenchyma. No additional lesions are grossly\u000aidentified. The lateral aspect of the specimen is serially sectioned with no\u000alymph nodes grossly identified. Representative sections are submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Nipple-areolar complex, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lesion to nipple, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Posterior/deep margin defect, 2 frags each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lesion, biopsy cavity deep margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Representative sections, biopsy cavity, lateral to medial, 2 frags\u000aeach, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Representative sections, right upper outer quadrant, 2 frags\u000aeach, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Representative sections, right lower outer quadrant, 2 frags\u000aeach, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Representative sections, right upper inner quadrant, 2 frags\u000aeach, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Representative sections, right lower inner quadrant, 2 frags\u000aeach, RSS.\u000aPart C, "skin, right breast", consists of an irregular tan/white unoriented\u000askin excision (22.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). No discrete lesions or scars are grossly\u000aidentified. Representative sections are submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 4 frags, RSS.\u000aPart D, "skin, left breast", consists of an unoriented tan/white wrinkled\u000airregular skin excision (1.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). No discrete lesions or scars are\u000agrossly identified. Representative sections are submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 4 frags, RSS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000asek/lp\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Xiaohua Qian M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a10/1/2008\u000a[report_end]
