f fibrous tissue are submitted\u000aMicro 1: Breast tissue, skin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Fibrous areas of breast tissue, multiple frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 7: Possible region of dermis vs. prior surgical scar, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Further fibrous tissue, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aPart 2, "left breast tissue 260 gm", consists of multiple pieces of\u000afibroadipose tissue, some with attached skin, measuring in aggregate REMOVED_DATE x 14\u000ax 2 cm. The specimen weighs 260 gm. There is no scar on the pieces of skin\u000asubmitted. These pieces range in size from 12 x 7 x REMOVED_DATE to 6 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000aThere is no ink or orienting sutures included. Upon sectioning there is a REMOVED_DATE \u000ax REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm area of dense fibrous tissue. Representative sections from\u000athis area are submitted. In one region there is REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm firm,\u000asclerotic nodule. This nodule is entirely submitted. The specimen is 20%\u000afibrous tissue and 80% yellow adipose tissue.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Fibrous areas, 4 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 14: Tiny nodule, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Fibrous areas, 3 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 17: Breast tissue with skin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aksc\u000aReports to: PRIBAZ, JULIAN, JOSEPH M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST REDUCTION MAMMOPLASTY\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST REDUCTION MAMMOPLASTY\u000a[report_end]
