VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: DIANE C LOCKHART M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Oname O. Burlingame, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Michelle S Hirsch, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aSPECIMEN DESIGNATED "RIGHT BREAST TISSUE":\u000aBenign breast tissue with rare residual mucinous cysts, and\u000amicrocalcifications associated with benign epithelium.\u000aBiopsy site changes are present.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the\u000aspecimen, including margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 53 y o woman S/P stereotactic core for micro calcs REMOVED_DATE  which\u000ashowed mucinous cysts. Surgical excision recommended.\u000aOperation: R needle-loc breast bx.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: R abnl mammo.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) R breast tissue (to mammo); long = lateral; short = superior.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Specimen - clip in spec; wire intact. Called to OR at 11 A.M. -\u000aDr. Lockhart. - J. Ritner.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "#1. Right breast tissue long equals lateral, short equals superior", and\u000aconsists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm ragged, focally disrupted-appearing excision\u000aof fibroadipose tissue, oriented by sutures designating superior (short suture)\u000aand lateral (long suture) margins. The specimen is inked per pathology\u000aprotocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue;\u000asuperior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange (inked by surgeon).\u000aLocalizing wire enters the inferior aspect of the specimen. Specimen is\u000areceived with a radiograph demonstrating localizing wire in place with an\u000aill-defined mass marked by a metallic surgical clip (area consistent with prior\u000abiopsy site). In addition, the radiograph demonstrates a large central\u000aencircled area of interest, just superior to the biopsy site. Due to the\u000apresence of this additional ill-defined area of interest (not marked by clip),\u000athe entire specimen is submitted. The specimen is roughly sectioned from\u000asuperior to inferior, revealing predominantly soft, lobulated tan/yellow\u000aadipose tissue (at least 95%), admixed with occasional thin fibrous septae.\u000aThe inferior portion of the specimen exhibits a REMOVED_DATE cm ill-defined firm biopsy\u000asite containing the gray metallic clip. The biopsy site abuts the inferior and\u000aposterior margins, and is within REMOVED_DATE cm of the closest medial margin.\u000aRemaining margins are all greater than REMOVED_DATE cm from the biopsy site. There are\u000ano additional masses, lesions or other abnormalities grossly. Entire specimen\u000ais submitted, sequentially from roughly superior to inferior, with\u000aperpendicular superior margin in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, biopsy cavity in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, and\u000aperpendicular inferior/posterior/medial margin in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Multi frags, ESS.\u000aPlease Note: Section containing clip in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aDB/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Michelle S Hirsch M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a10/4/2007\u000a[report_end]
