VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Sentinel Lymph Nodes(s)\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ROGER L CHRISTIAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Adam Rosendorff, M.D.; Eric C Huang, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Susan Lester, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aLEFT BREAST, MASTECTOMY, AND SENTINEL LYMPH NODE BIOPSY (TWO\u000aSPECIMENS)(INCLUDING FROZEN SECTION):\u000aEXTENSIVE RESIDUAL DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, cribriform, papillary, and\u000amicropapillary types (intermediate nuclear grade), with apocrine features, is\u000apresent in the central and superior breast (and involving lactiferous sinuses\u000aof the nipple), in 23 of 38 blocks (over an area measuring 6 to 10 cm).\u000aCalcifications and focal necrosis are associated with DCIS.\u000aThe DCIS is present adjacent to the prior excisional site.\u000aNo lymphovascular invasion is seen.\u000aThe deep margin is free of carcinoma.\u000aThe skin and nipple are free of carcinoma.\u000aTwo (2) lymph nodes are free of carcinoma, including the one (1) sentinel lymph\u000anode and one lymph node found in the lateral tissue of the mastectomy specimen.\u000aThe sentinel node is examined with 3 H&E levels.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 68 yo F with left breast inv papillary cystic Ca + DCIS.\u000aOperation: L mastectomy/SLNB.\u000aOperative Findings: Not provided.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: L breast CA.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. L axillary SLN - FS.\u000aB/2. L breast, short stitch superior, long lateral.\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000aArrival time: 8:51 AM\u000aReport time: 9:05 AM\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "1. L AXILLARY SENTINEL LYMPH NODE" (FSA):\u000aLymph node, negative for tumor.\u000aOR Consultation by: VANIA NOSE, M.D., PH.D.\u000aResident: ELIZABETH A. STEENSMA, MD\u000aThe senior physician certifies that he/she personally conducted a gross and/or\u000amicroscopic examination of the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed\u000athe rapid diagnos(es) related thereto.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received in two parts, each labeled with the patient's name and\u000amedical record number.\u000aPart A, "#1. Left axillary sentinel lymph node to frozen section", consists of\u000aa REMOVED_DATE cm blue inked lymph node which is bisected and submitted entirely for\u000afrozen analysis as FSA.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sentinel lymph node (FSA remnant), 2 frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, "#2. Left breast, short stitch superior, long stitch lateral", consists\u000aof a 932-g left mastectomy specimen. The specimen has been oriented per\u000asurgeon; short stitch superior, long stitch lateral. There is a skin ellipse\u000a(16.0 cm medial to lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm superior to inferior) with a curvilinear\u000ascar present from 11 o'clock to 3 o'clock. The unremarkable nipple is REMOVED_DATE cm\u000ain diameter. There is a cystic, firm (1.9 cm x REMOVED_DATE cm) area containing blue\u000afluid, located REMOVED_DATE cm from the deep margin at 11:00 in the mid breast. There\u000ais a second, rubbery firm area which is REMOVED_DATE cm x REMOVED_DATE cm approximately REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom the posterior margin at 9:00 in the mid breast. The lateral aspect of the\u000aspecimen is examined and one lymph node is found and submitted for histologic\u000aexamination. All other fibrous areas in the lateral breast are submitted.\u000aAfter the examination of the initial sections, the specimen is re-examined by\u000aDr. Susan Lester. There is a 3 to 4 cm area of gritty cystic tissue in the\u000asuperior central portion of the breast at the site of the prior excision. No\u000adiscrete masses are present. There are focal gritty areas of breast tissue\u000aextending towards the nipple and into the central area of the breast. The\u000aremainder of the breast consists of grossly normal tissue. All of the grossly\u000aabnormal gritty tissue has been submitted for microscopic examination.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID through REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Cystic area at 11:00, 2 frags each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Closest deep margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID through REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Rubbery area at 9:00, mid breast, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Closest posterior margin.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Upper inner, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lower inner, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Upper outer, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lower outer, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Nipple, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID through REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lymph node candidates, multi frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: central 3 to 4 cm gritty area, mult frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: gritty tissue towards nipple, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Adjacent dilated ducts, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Upper outer quadrant, near mass, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Nodular tissue at 3:00, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Gritty central tissue, mult frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Nodular area superior to mass, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aARO/ajb\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a10/25/2007\u000a[report_end]
