VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID SENTINEL LYMPH NODE\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aRICHARDSON, ANDREA, L., M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by RICHARDSON,ANDREA L.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR CALCIFICATIONS, A MASS, AND A CLIP,\u000aAND SENTINEL NODE BIOPSY:\u000aINVASIVE PAPILLARY CARCINOMA.\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU and negative lymph nodes.\u000aSYNOPSIS:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA\u000aSize REMOVED_DATE (see note)\u000aMultifocal No\u000aHistologic Type Papillary\u000aHistologic Grade (SBR) II(Moderate)\u000aNuclear Grade Intermediate\u000aEIC Negative\u000aLymphovascular invasion No definitive\u000aDermal lymphatic invasion N/A\u000aSkin invasion N/A\u000aSkeletal muscle invasion N/A\u000aFinal Margins (invasive)\u000aNegative(>0.3 cm) - Anterior, posterior, lateral, superior\u000ainferior\u000aClose (0.1 to REMOVED_DATE cm) - Medial (0.25 cm, block #5) focal\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU Present\u000aTypes Cribriform and micropapillary\u000aNuclear grade Low\u000aCalcifications in DCIS Absent\u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS Absent\u000aExtent of DCIS\u000aNumber of blocks/total - REMOVED_DATE blocks, (blocks 7, 8, and 10)\u000aFinal Margins (DCIS)\u000aNegative (>0.3 cm) - medial, lateral, anterior, superior,\u000ainferior\u000aClose (0.1-0.3cm) - posterior (focally REMOVED_DATE cm, block #10)\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU Absent\u000aLYMPH NODES\u000aSentinel lymph nodes (3 H&E levels examined) - Negative\u000aNumber of positive nodes 0\u000aNumber of nodes examined 1\u000aTOTAL POSITIVE NODES (all specimens) REMOVED_DATE \u000aOTHER FINDINGS\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia.\u000aCore biopsy site.\u000aFibroadenoma with calcifications.\u000aCalcifications in benign epithelium.\u000aThere is extensive dystrophic calcifications associated with\u000apapillary carcinoma.\u000aImmunohistochemistry results for invasive carcinoma:\u000aESTROGEN RECEPTOR - STRONGLY POSITIVE\u000aPROGESTERONE RECEPTOR - POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/NEU - NEGATIVE (1+)\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - NEGATIVE (confirming invasion)\u000aWT-1 - NEGATIVE\u000aGCDFP - NEGATIVE\u000aNOTE: The carcinoma has a very unusual histologic pattern for breast\u000acancer with large infiltrating tubulo-papillary glands similar to a\u000amullerian endometrioid-type carcinoma. The invasive carcinoma does not\u000aappear to be arising from or associated with an intracystic papillary\u000alesion. Small foci of cribriform DCIS, somewhat dissimilar to the\u000ainvasive carcinoma, are present in surrounding tissue. Although the\u000apresence of an in situ component supports a breast origin, the possibility\u000aof a metastasis from a mullerian site (ovary, endometrium) should be\u000aconsidered. Clinical correlation is needed.\u000aRepresentative slides were reviewed by Drs. Stuart Schnitt and Marisa\u000aNucci.\u000aAJCC CLASSIFICATION (6th Edition) - REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID pREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID MX\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 60 year old female, S/P REMOVED_DATE  ultrasound-guided core biopsy of a REMOVED_DATE \u000acm mass revealing a papillary carcinoma. Also has separate area of\u000acalcifications on mammogram.\u000aOperation: R breast lumpectomy, R breast wire localized biopsies,\u000asentinel node mapping, sentinel node biopsy.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: R breast cancer.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1 - R sentinel lymph node - hot and blue (fs).\u000a#2 - R breast tissue - short suture/superior, long suture/lateral, whipstitch\u000aon anterior margin - to mammo.\u000aRadiology report: Mass with calcifications and separate Ca++ clusters in\u000aspecimen. Dr. D Smith.\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "#1 - SENTINEL LYMPH NODE - HOT AND BLUE" (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aOne (1) lymph node negative for tumor.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by GIBSON,JOANNA A,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aReceived in two parts.\u000aPart one, received fresh in the frozen section lab, labeled with the patient's\u000aname, unit number, and "#1 - sentinel lymph node - hot and blue", consists of a\u000aportion of yellow/tan lobulated fat (4.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) within which a single\u000alymph node candidate (3.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) is identified. The specimen is\u000atrisected and entirely frozen as REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aMicro #1: "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" residue, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro #2: "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" residue, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro #3: "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" residue, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aPart two, labeled "right breast mass", consists of a 158 gram, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm portion of fibrofatty breast tissue, with an accompanying radiograph, three\u000aorienting sutures (short suture/superior, long suture/lateral, and whipstitch\u000aon anterior margin [per phone conversation with Dr. Rhei, she confirms the\u000awhipstitch is "anterior margin"]). The specimen is inked by the surgeon as\u000afollows: anterior = black, posterior = blue, lateral = yellow, medial =\u000aorange, superior = red, and inferior = green (please note that the anterior and\u000aposterior inks are opposite of the normal inking protocol, per Dr. Rhei). The\u000aspecimen is serially sectioned, revealing a red/tan, gelatinous, partially\u000aencapsulated, soft, blue-dyed mass, which comes to within REMOVED_DATE cm of the\u000asuperior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the inferior margin,\u000a1.7 cm of the medial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the posterior (chest wall) margin, and\u000a3.0 cm of the lateral margin. The clip is identified adjacent to the mass.\u000aA second cluster of calcifications are identified upon radiographing of the\u000aserially sectioned specimen, and are noted to be present adjacent to the\u000alateral aspect of the specimen (please see included radiograph).\u000aMicro #4+5: Mass in relationship to superior margin, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000aMicro #6+7: Mass in relationship to inferior margin, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000aMicro #8+9: Mass in relationship to anterior margin, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000aMicro #10+11: Posterior margin nearest mass, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro #12+13: Medial margin nearest mass, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000aMicro #14: Breast tissue to include area of clip and adjacent mass, 1 frag,\u000aRSS.\u000aMicro #14-18: Second focus of calcifications adjacent to lateral margin, 4\u000afrags total, ESS.\u000adfi/\u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: SENTINEL LYMPH NODE\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
