R IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum *** RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast (Right, block C): The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein. The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein. The tumor cells show moderate(2+) overexpression of HER-2/c-erbB-2. See note. Note: These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital. They have not been cleared or approved by the U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA). The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary; this laboratory has established and verified the test's accuracy and precision. Added by: Grace T. McKee,MD Signed On: 13 REMOVED_MONTH 00 at 13:15 GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab, labeled with the patient's name and unit number, and "right axillary sentinel lymph node" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm lymph node and attached nodular fatty tissue. The lymph node is bisected and entirely frozen as FX#1, now in cassette A. The remaining nodular tissue is submitted in cassette B. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name and unit number, and "right breast" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm tan yellow lobular breast parenchyma, oriented with a long suture designating lateral margin, short suture superior inked as follows: Superior-red; inferior-green; medial-yellow; lateral-orange; anterior-black; and posterior-blue. The specimen is serially sectioned from lateral to medial to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm vaguely circumscribed tan white fibrotic mass with a tan red hemorrhagic core measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The tumor mass comes with in REMOVED_DATE cm of the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the inferior margin (the closest margin), REMOVED_DATE cm of the medial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the lateral margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the anterior margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm of the posterior margin. Section code: C: tumor mass to closest superior (red) soft tissue margin D: tumor to closest inferior (green) soft tissue margin E: tumor to closest posterior (blue) soft tissue margin F: anterior (black) margin G: medial (yellow) soft tissue margin, en face H: lateral (orange) soft tissue margin, en face I: additional sections of breast parenchyma away approximately 1 cm from the tumor mass. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name and unit number, and "right breast final shaved margin" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm tan yellow, lobular, fatty tissue fragment, serially sectioned and entirely submitted in cassettes J-T. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name and unit number, and "right breast final shaved inferior margin, stitch furthest from tumor" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm tan-yellow breast parenchyma oriented with a black suture designating the edge furthest from the tumor (inked in black). The surface directly opposite from the surface designated by the suture is and irregular with focal areas of hemorrhage (inked in blue). The specimen is serially sectioned and entirely submitted in cassettes U-Y. Resident: TAI-YUAN LIN, MD *** INTRA-OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS *** FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS #1, LYMPH NODE (RIGHT AXILLARY SENTINEL): THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. O.R. Resident: ARASH RADFAR, MD, PhD O.R. Diagnosis by: William C. Faquin,MD,PhD =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT - REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID REPORTS TO: Michele Annette Gadd, M.D. PART A: LYMPH NODE(RIGHT AXILLARY SENTINAL),EXCISION PART B: BREAST (RIGHT), EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART C: BREAST (RIGHT, FINAL MARGIN), EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART D: BREAST (RIGHT, FINAL INFERIOR MARGIN), EXCISIONAL\u000a[report_end]
