VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID:REMOVED_CASE_ID Report Status: Signed\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000a*** ADDENDUM MESSAGE ***\u000a*** ADDITIONAL DIAGNOSTIC INFORMATION ***\u000aThis report contains an addendum to the original for the purpose of providing\u000aadditional diagnostic information. Please refer to the ADDENDUM REPORT section\u000abelow for this information. The original diagnosis is unchanged.\u000aADDENDUM REPORT\u000aAddendum #1 Entered: REMOVED_DATE -1355\u000aImmunohistochemical studies performed reveal the following results for the\u000ainfiltrating carcinoma:\u000aEstrogen receptor: POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor: POSITIVE\u000aHer2/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID): NEGATIVE for overexpression.\u000aAddeundum Signed Electronically Signed MIHOK,NICOLE M.D. REMOVED_DATE \u000aDIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. Right axillary sentinel lymph node, excision:\u000aNo tumor seen (0/1).\u000aB. Right axillary lymph node, dissection:\u000aNo tumor seen (0/4).\u000aC. Right breast, excisional biopsy:\u000aInfiltrating ductal carcinoma moderately differentiated, two separate\u000afoci, REMOVED_DATE cm. and REMOVED_DATE cm. (See note).\u000aDuctal carcinoma in situ, intermediate grade, solid and cribriform type\u000awith focal necrosis, approximately REMOVED_DATE cm. (See note).\u000aFibrocystic changes.\u000aHealing biopsy site changes.\u000aNOTE: The ductal carcinoma in situ is patchy and extends in small foci\u000aover 75% of the lateral and mid portions of the specimen corresponding\u000ato an approximate REMOVED_DATE cm. area. An extensive intraductal component is\u000aseen in the area around the invasive tumor. The DCIS is less than REMOVED_DATE \u000amm. from the superior deep margin; REMOVED_DATE mm. from the anterior margin;\u000aand 4 mm. from the inferior margin in the mid portion of the specimen.\u000aThe REMOVED_DATE cm. focus of invasive tumor is in the mid portion of the\u000aspecimen and is greater than REMOVED_DATE mm. from all margins. However, the REMOVED_DATE \u000acm. focus of invasive tumor is in the lateral most portion of the\u000aspecimen and is less than REMOVED_DATE mm. from the deep-lateral margin. No\u000alymphovascular invasion seen. Estrogen receptors, progesterone\u000areceptors and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu studies have been requested and the results will\u000abe reported in an addendum. Level sections and Keratin\u000aimmunohistochemical stains do not show metastatic carcinoma in the\u000asentinel lymph node (part A).\u000aFinal Diagnosis by: Nicole A. Mihok, M.D.\u000aINTRA-OPERATIVE CONSULTATION:\u000aOPERATING ROOM CONSULTATION (TISSUE EXAMINATION WITH TOUCH PREPARATION):\u000aRight axillary sentinel lymph node: No tumor seen.\u000aNAM\u000aClinical diagnosis & history:\u000aRight breast carcinoma\u000aTissue-Designation:\u000aA.Sentinel lymph node - right\u000aB.Lymph nodes, dissection - right axillary\u000aC.Breast, excision with margins - right\u000aGross description:\u000aThe specimen is received in three containers.\u000aSpecimen A labeled "right sentinel lymph node" consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm. lymph node. The lymph node is bisected and shows partial fatty replacement\u000aof the lymph node with a rim of tan lymph node parenchyma. The lymph node is\u000aentirely submitted. 2X all.\u000aSpecimen B labeled "axillary nodes" consists of two portions of tissue. The\u000asmaller portion of tissue is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. portion of yellow adipose\u000atissue with a possible very small tan lymph node. This portion of tissue is\u000aentirely submitted in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. The larger portion of tissue consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000ax REMOVED_DATE cm. firm, tan lymph node with adjacent adipose tissue. The lymph node is\u000abisected. This node and adjacent adipose tissue is entirely submitted in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000a3X all.\u000aSpecimen C labeled "right lumpectomy" consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000aspherical shaped portion of breast tissue with a needle localization wire in\u000aplace and two sutures. The long suture is designated the lateral margin and\u000athe short suture, the superior margin. The deep margin is inked black; the\u000aanterior superior is inked blue; the anterior inferior is inked green. The\u000aspecimen is sectioned from the lateral to the medial margin and shows a REMOVED_DATE x\u000a0.5 x REMOVED_DATE cm. firm, stellate lesion in the center of the specimen near the tip\u000aof the localization wire. The entire specimen is submitted from the lateral\u000atowards the medial margins in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID with some having subdesignations\u000acorresponding each to complete serial section of tissue that is bisected or\u000atrisected. 14 agg. all.\u000aDictated by: NAM____(signature on file)____MICHAEL J. ROSS, M.D. REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a____(signature on file)____NICOLE MIHOK, M.D. REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a[report_end]
