VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: FinalType: Surgical Pathology Pathology Report: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID OPERATION DATE: 05 REMOVED_MONTH 02 ACCESSIONED ON: 05 REMOVED_MONTH 02 at 14:51 CLINICAL DATA: Right breast cancer. =============================================================================== *** FINAL DIAGNOSIS *** LYMPH NODES (RIGHT AXILLARY, SENTINEL), EXCISION: METASTATIC DUCTAL CARCINOMA, MINUTE FOCI (LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM), WITHIN EACH OF TWO LYMPH NODES (0.6 AND REMOVED_DATE CM IN GREATEST DIMENSION, RESPECTIVELY), WITHOUT EXTRANODAL EXTENSION; THE FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS IS CONFIRMED. SEE NOTE. NOTE: Tumor is present in the non-frozen half of the second node sampled for frozen section but not in the frozen portion of that node (frozen section diagnosis #2). BREAST (RIGHT), EXCISIONAL BIOPSY: INVASIVE CARCINOMA, WITH BOTH LOBULAR AND DUCTAL FEATURES. SEE TABLE. FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES. TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS INVASIVE CARCINOMA Tumor size: REMOVED_DATE X REMOVED_DATE X REMOVED_DATE CM (GROSS MEASUREMENT) Grade: 1 Lymphatic vessel invasion: Not identified. Blood vessel invasion: Not identified. Margin of invasive carcinoma: Invasive carcinoma extends to less than REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior inferior margin of the specimen in one focus. The distances to all other examined margins measure REMOVED_DATE cm or greater. Ductal carcinoma in situ: Not identified. Stains for receptors: Requested. BREAST (SUBAREOLAR, ADDITIONAL), EXCISION: INVASIVE CARCINOMA, EXTENDING FOCALLY TO A CAUTERIZED MARGIN. BREAST (SUBDERMAL NODULES), EXCISION: INVASIVE CARCINOMA; INVOLVING BOTH FRAGMENTS AND EXTENDING TO CAUTERIZED MARGINS. BREAST (RIGHT, SUPERIOR HALF OF CAVITY, FINAL SHAVED MARGIN), BIOPSY: THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. BREAST (RIGHT, INFERIOR HALF OF CAVITY, FINAL SHAVE MARGIN), BIOPSY: FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES. THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. LYMPH NODES (RIGHT AXILLARY, NON-SENTINEL), REGIONAL DISSECTION: THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 17 OF 17 LYMPH NODES. Diagnosis by: John H. Eichhorn, M.D. Signed On: 08 REMOVED_MONTH 02 at 21:19 =============================================================================== *** IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum *** RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast (Right, block J): The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein. The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein. The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER-2/c-erbB-2. See note. Note: These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital. They have not been cleared or approved by the U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA). The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary; this laboratory has established and verified the test's accuracy and precision. Added by: Grace T. McKee,MD Signed On: 14 REMOVED_MONTH 02 at 10:31 GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "right axillary sentinel node, hot and blue, 1985 and 1990", are 2 tan lymph nodes with attached adipose tissuE, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The specimens are bisected to reveal a blue dyed cut surface, with a tan-white nodule within the first node and a tan cut surface for the second node. One half of the first node is frozen as FX #1, now as A and the remainder is entirely submitted in cassette B. Half of the other node is frozen as FX #2, now as C, and the remainder is entirely submitted in cassette D. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "right breast mass", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm fibrofatty breast tissue fragment with a short suture designating superior and a long suture designating lateral. The specimen is inked (anterior blue, posterior black, superior overinked green) and serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm fairly well-circumscribed stellate gray-white mass, which comes to within REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior and anterior margins and abuts the anteroinferior margin. There are no other masses or lesions grossly identified. The remaining parenchyma is approximately 10% dense white fibrous tissue and the remaining tan-yellow lobulated adipose tissue. Representative sections are submitted as follows: E: Tumor to anterior margin. F: Tumor to posterior margin. G: Tumor to anteroinferior margin. H: Tumor to superior margin. I: Tumor. J: Fibrous tissue lateral to tumor. K: Fibrous tissue medial to tumor. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "additional subareolar tissue" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm aggregate of fibrofatty breast tissue fragments which are submitted in toto in cassette L. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "subdermal nodules" are two REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm tan-yellow tissue fragment which are submitted in toto as M. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "final shaved margin, superior half of cavity" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm aggregate of fibrofatty partially cauterized breast tissue fragments. The specimen is serially sectioned to display a cut surface consisting of approximately 10% dense white fibrous tissue and the remaining a tan-yellow adipose tissue. There are no masses grossly identified. The specimen is entirely submitted in cassettes N-V. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "final shaved margin, inferior half of cavity" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm aggregate of fibrofatty breast tissue fragments which are serially sectioned to reveal a cut surface consisting of approximately 10% dense white fibrous tissue and the remaining a tan-yellow lobulated adipose tissue. There are no distinct masses or lesions grossly identified. The specimen is serially sectioned and entirely submitted in cassettes W-DD. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "non-sentinel nodes, axillary contents" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm aggregate of tan-yellow lymph node bearing adipose tissue fragments. There are multiple lymph nodes dissected out ranging from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The lymph nodes are entirely submitted as follows: EE: 5 whole lymph nodes. FF: 4 whole lymph nodes. GG: 2 whole lymph nodes. HH-LL: 1 bisected lymph node each. MM-NN: Largest lymph node serially sectioned and entirely submitted. Gross Description by: JAMES BARRY Resident: TAI-YUAN LIN, MD *** INTRA-OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS *** FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS #1: SENTINEL NODE (RIGHT AXILLARY): POSITIVE FOR CARCINOMA. FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS #2: SENTINEL NODE #2 (RIGHT AXILLARY): THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN ONE HALF. O.R. Resident: JULIE ANN NAGLE, MD O.R. Diagnosis by: SELIM NASSER, MD =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: MGH-INPATIENT (FLR.UNKNOWN) REPORTS TO: Barbara Lynn Smith, M.D. PART A: RIGHT AXILLARY SENTINEL LYMPH NODE PART B: RIGHT BREAST, EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART C: ADDITIONAL SUBAREOLAR TISSUE,EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART D: SUBDERMAL NODULES, EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART E: BREAST (RIGHT, SUPERIOR HALF OF CAVITY, FINAL SHAV PART F: BREAST (RIGHT, INFERIOR HALF OF CAVITY, FINAL SHAV PART G: RIGHT AXILLARY NON-SENTINEL LYMPH NODES
