VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: FinalType: Surgical Pathology Pathology Report: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID OPERATION DATE: 25 REMOVED_MONTH 02 ACCESSIONED ON: 25 REMOVED_MONTH 02 at 11:28 CLINICAL DATA: Positive margin on nipple/areola skin on prior lumpectomy for cancer. =============================================================================== *** FINAL DIAGNOSIS *** BREAST (RIGHT), RE-EXCISION: INVASIVE CARCINOMA, SEVERAL NODULES RANGING FROM REMOVED_DATE CM TO AT LEAST REMOVED_DATE CM AND AGGREGATING TO AT LEAST REMOVED_DATE CM, EXTENDING TO LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE LATERAL MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN. SEE NOTE. Note: Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen. Diagnosis by: Frederick Carl Koerner, M.D. Signed On: 27 REMOVED_MONTH 02 at 10:43 =============================================================================== GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "re-excision, right breast" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm fibrofatty breast tissue which displays a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm elliptical skin in which a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm grossly unremarkable nipple areola complex occupies 90% of that space. The specimen is oriented with a short stitch designating superior and a long stitch designating lateral. The lateral aspect of the specimen contains a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm tan-yellow to brown focally hemorrhagic cavity consistent with a previous lumpectomy site. The specimen is inked (superior rim green, inferior rim blue and the remainder black) serially sectioned displaying a 90% tan-yellow adipose tissue and the remaining 10% is a dense white fibrous tissue. There are focal areas of fat necrosis surrounding the cavity. The specimen is serial sectioned into 18 slices and representative sections are submitted as follows: A: Slice 4. B: Slice 6. C: Slice 8 biopsy cavity to overlying nipple. D: Slice 9 cavity to superior. E-