VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOGINO, SHUJI, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by OGINO,SHUJI,M.D.,PH.D.\u000a1) LEFT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZATION FOR A MASS:\u000aBreast tissue with atypical ductal hyperplasia, sclerosing adenosis,\u000acysts, calcifications in benign epithelium, papillomas, dense\u000ainterlobular fibrous tissue, fibroadenomatoid change, and possible core\u000abiopsy site.\u000aNo carcinoma is seen in the specimen including the margin.\u000aNOTE:\u000aLevels examined on block #3. Selected slides (#3) were reviewed by Dr. J.\u000aConnolly.\u000a2) RIGHT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZATION FOR CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aSYNOPSIS:\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aTypes - cribriform, micropapillary\u000aNuclear grade - intermediate\u000aCalcifications in DCIS - present\u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - present\u000aExtent of DCIS\u000aNumber of blocks:total - 10:18 (#14, 16, 17, 18, 19, 20, 21,\u000a22, 23, and 24)\u000aFinal Margins (DCIS)\u000aNegative (>0.3 cm) - medial, superior\u000aClose (<0.1 cm) - lateral (block 23), inferior (block 16,\u000a18, 3 foci), posterior (block 21, 22),\u000aanterior (block 23)\u000aPositive (ink on DCIS) - lateral (block 24)\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - absent\u000aOTHER FINDINGS\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia\u000aCysts\u000aApocrine metaplasia\u000aCore biopsy site\u000aAJCC CLASSIFICATION - REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDs pNx MX\u000aNOTE:\u000aAssessment of the margins is focally compromised by extensive cautery\u000aartifact.\u000aSelected slides (#23) were reviewed by Dr. J. Connolly.\u000a3) SPECIMEN LABELED "LEFT BREAST, ANTERIOR MARGIN":\u000aBreast tissue with atypical ductal hyperplasia and cysts.\u000aNo residual carcinoma is present.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 55 y/o postmenopausal female, recently d/c HRT, whose REMOVED_DATE \u000amammograms demonstrate R breast calcifications, 2 clusters, and L breast 9:00\u000aaxis, REMOVED_DATE cm mass. Outside facility core biopsy of the R breast\u000acalcifications revealed DCIS. Core of the mass revealed ADH.\u000aOperation: R breast wire localization x2, L breast wire localization.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: R breast cancer. L breast atypical ductal hyperplasia.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. L breast wire loc - inking per path protocol.\u000a2. R breast doublewire loc, partial mastectomy.\u000a3. L breast anterior margin.\u000aRADIOLOGY: #1: No clip in specimen.\u000a#2: Ca++ in specimen - x2.\u000a#3: No clip in spec. J Meyer, MD\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by BUNDOCK,ELIZABETH A.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in three parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart one, labeled "#1 L breast wire loc", consists of one fragment of\u000afibrofatty tissue (4.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) which is received in Pathology already\u000ainked by the surgeon. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the\u000aevaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red;\u000ainferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. Also attached is a\u000alocalization wire. The specimen is received with a specimen radiograph which\u000ais reported as "no clip in specimen #1" by the radiologist but demonstrates a\u000acentrally located radiopaque mass in the area of the wire. The specimen is\u000aserially sectioned from superior to inferior revealing 60% fibrous tissue which\u000ais evenly distributed throughout the specimen. There is one area of increased\u000afirmness (0.8 cm greatest dimension) centrally located in the specimen,\u000acorresponding to the mass in the specimen radiograph. This area abuts the\u000ainferior margin and is REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom the superior, and more than 1 cm from the superior and inferior margins.\u000aThe specimen is submitted in series from superior to inferior with the mass in\u000ablocks 7&8.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  breast tissue, superior/inferior, 13 frags, ESS.\u000aPart two, labeled "R breast doublewire loc, partial mastectomy", consists of a\u000afragment of fibrofatty soft tissue (5.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) which is received in\u000aPathology inked by the surgeon. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol\u000afor the evaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior =\u000ared; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. Two localization\u000awires are present. The specimen is received with a specimen radiograph which\u000ais recorded as "calcifications in specimen x2". The specimen is serially\u000asectioned from medial to lateral revealing approximately 60% fibrous tissue\u000awhich is soft, rubbery and contains numerous cysts. The fibrous tissue extends\u000ato the medial, lateral, inferior and posterior margins. There are no hard foci\u000asuggestive of invasive carcinoma. There is a cystic cavity filled with blood\u000a(0.7 cm in greatest dimension), located in the area of one of the wires, which\u000ais centrally located in the specimen, REMOVED_DATE cm from the deep margin, greater\u000athan 1 cm from the superior, medial, lateral and inferior margins, and 1 cm\u000afrom the anterior margin. This area may represent a prior core biopsy site.\u000aFibrous portions of the specimen are submitted in series from medial to lateral\u000awith the area of the biopsy cavity entirely submitted in blocks 15 through 19.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  breast tissue in series medial to lateral, 16 frags, RSS.\u000aPart three, labeled "#3 L breast anterior margin", consists of one oriented\u000afragment of fibrofatty tissue (3.5 x 2 x REMOVED_DATE cm) with a stitch on one surface\u000aassumed to represent the new margin (inked black). The specimen is received\u000awith a specimen radiograph which is reported as "no clip in specimen" by the\u000aradiologist. The specimen is serially sectioned perpendicular to the new\u000amargin revealing predominantly fatty tissue with one focus of firm, tan/white\u000afibrous tissue which grossly extends to the new margin and is entirely\u000asubmitted in cassette #25.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  fibrofatty soft tissue, 8 frags, ESS.\u000aeab\u000aReports to: KAELIN, CAROLYN, MARY M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY - PARTIAL OR SIMPLE\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN\u000a[report_end]
