VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST MASTECTOMY - PARTIAL OR SIMPLE\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aNUCCI, MARISA, ROSE, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by NUCCI,MARISA ROSE,M.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST, SIMPLE MASTECTOMY (826 GRAMS):\u000aFocal atypical ductal hyperplasia associated with healing biopsy cavity.\u000aNo residual ductal carcinoma in situ is identified.\u000aNo invasive carcinoma is identified.\u000aFibrocystic changes including cyst formation and sclerosing adenosis.\u000aSkin with cicatrix.\u000aSkeletal muscle.\u000aThree (3) lymph nodes with no tumor present.\u000aSCAR, LEFT BREAST:\u000aSkin and subcutaneous tissue with no significant pathologic change.\u000aSCAR REVISION, RIGHT BREAST:\u000aSkin with cicatrix and a foreign body giant cell reaction to suture\u000amaterial.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: None given.\u000aOperation: Left simple mastectomy.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: CA, breast.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Left breast, short superior, long lateral.\u000a2. Scar, left breast.\u000a3. Revision, scar, right breast.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by HIRSCH,MICHELLE S.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in three parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname.\u000aThe first part, "#1 left breast", consists of an 826-gram, simple mastectomy\u000aspecimen (23 x 20 x 6 cm) including an overlying skin ellipse (19 x REMOVED_DATE cm)\u000awith a centrally located areola (5.0 x REMOVED_DATE cm) and nipple (1.5 x REMOVED_DATE cm). On\u000athe superior outer aspect of the areola is a well-healed, arched surgical scar\u000a(4.5 cm in length). The specimen is received with short and long sutures\u000awhich represent the superior and lateral margins, respectively. On the deep\u000asurface of the specimen, there is a smooth, glistening fascia with a small\u000afragment of skeletal muscle (2.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) identified. There is a\u000aprevious biopsy cavity (7.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) located in the central/superior\u000aportion of the specimen, deep to the surgical scar. The biopsy cavity is\u000aopened at the deep surface and this opening measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The\u000aremaining biopsy cavity is grossly identified within REMOVED_DATE cm of the deep\u000asurface, REMOVED_DATE cm of the overlying skin ellipse, REMOVED_DATE cm of the medial portion of\u000athe specimen and REMOVED_DATE cm of the lateral portion of the specimen.\u000aRepresentative sections are submitted for histological analysis and evaluation\u000aof deep margins. Potential lymph nodes are identified (ranging from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000ax REMOVED_DATE cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) in the lateral portion of the specimen. The\u000alymph nodes are entirely submitted.\u000aMicros REMOVED_DATE  biopsy cavity with deep margin, 6 frags, RSS.\u000aMicros REMOVED_DATE  biopsy cavity, random sections, 6 frags, RSS.\u000aMicros 10&11: biopsy cavity with overlying skin and scar, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicros 12&13: nipple, 8 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 14: upper outer quadrant, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 15: lower outer quadrant, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 16: lower inner quadrant, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 17: upper inner quadrant, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 18: 1 lymph node, bisected, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 19: 2 lymph nodes, bisected, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 20: 4 potential lymph nodes, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aThe second part, "breast #2", consists of a single, unoriented, curved,\u000apink/tan skin (14.0 x REMOVED_DATE cm, excised to a depth of REMOVED_DATE cm). No scars are\u000agrossly identified on the skin ellipse. No masses or lesions are grossly\u000aidentified within the specimen. The excised margin is inked black and\u000arepresentative sections are submitted.\u000aMicros 21&22: left breast scar, 5 frags, RSS.\u000aThe third part, "scar, right breast", consists of a single, unoriented,\u000apink/tan skin ellipse (6.5 x REMOVED_DATE cm, excised to a depth of REMOVED_DATE cm). There is a\u000awell-healed surgical scar (0.5 cm in length) identified, extending into one\u000atip. No masses or lesions are grossly identified. The excised margin is\u000ainked black and representative sections are submitted.\u000aMicros 23&24: right breast scar, 4 frags, RSS.\u000amsh\u000aReports to: MATORY, YVEDT M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY - PARTIAL OR SIMPLE\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SKIN- OTHER THAN CYST, TAG OR DEBRIDEMENT\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SKIN- OTHER THAN CYST, TAG OR DEBRIDEMENT\u000a[report_end]
