VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Leona A. Doyle, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Alessandra F Nascimento, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. LEFT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia.\u000aColumnar cell change, calcifications in benign epithelium and apocrine\u000ametaplasia.\u000aBiopsy site changes.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the\u000aspecimen, including margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 42 year old premenopausal woman, S/P REMOVED_DATE  L breast core bxs for\u000aCa++ revealing ALH not associated with Ca++.\u000aOperation: L breast WL bx.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left abnormal mammogram.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) left breast tissue, short/superior, long/lateral, whipstitch/chest wall\u000aand red = inferior, green = superior.\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000aClip, calcifications, hook and wire in specimen - called Dr. Rhei at 1:52 pm by\u000aAS.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name and medical\u000arecord number, and "#1. Left breast tissue short/superior, long/lateral,\u000awhip/chest wall", and consists of a 64-gram breast excision specimen with\u000asutures designating superior, lateral, and deep aspects. The specimen is\u000areceived previously inked per surgeon for the evaluation of the margins,\u000asuperior/red, inferior/green, medial/orange, lateral/yellow, anterior/blue,\u000aposterior/black. The specimen measures REMOVED_DATE cm superior to inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000amedial to lateral, and REMOVED_DATE cm anterior to posterior. An accompanying specimen\u000aradiograph demonstrates a localization wire entering the specimen associated\u000awith a metallic clip and scattered punctate calcifications. Grossly the wire\u000aenters anteriorly and exits the specimen inferiorly. The specimen is markedly\u000adisrupted at the inferomedial surfaces. On sectioning, the entire breast\u000aparenchyma consists of firm rubbery white fibrous breast tissue with minimal\u000a(less than 2%) adipose tissue. A metallic clip is situated REMOVED_DATE cm to the\u000aanterior surface and REMOVED_DATE cm to the medial surface and has no gross biopsy site\u000achanges surrounding it. No discrete lesions are identified. An area of REMOVED_DATE x\u000a3.0 cm surrounding the metal clip to include anterior, medial, and inferior\u000asurfaces are entirely submitted. In addition, representative sections of each\u000amargin to include fibrous breast parenchyma are also submitted for histologic\u000aevaluation.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Breast parenchyma surrounding clip (in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), REMOVED_DATE frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Additional superior margin, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Deep margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000aLDO/lp\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Alessandra F Nascimento M.D., Electronically signed on\u000aWednesday February 11, 2009 at 09:28:23AM\u000a[report_end]
