VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID OUTSIDE SLIDE CONSULT - BREAST\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aLESTER, SUSAN, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aCONSULT SLIDES FROM DAHL-CHASE PATHOLOGY, BANGOR, ME:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, EXCISIONAL BIOPSY FOR A MASS (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID; REMOVED_DATE ):\u000aEpithelial/stromal lesion (2.4 cm) (see note).\u000aThe stroma is mildly cellular with no significant nuclear pleomorphism.\u000aMinimal stromal overgrowth is present.\u000aMitoses range from 0 to 1 per 10 HPF's (average REMOVED_DATE per 10 HPF's; 50 HPF's\u000acounted).\u000aNo stromal invasion is seen.\u000aThe lesion is present at the margin.\u000aNote: The differential diagnosis includes a cellular fibroadenoma or a\u000alow grade phyllodes tumor. Given the features above, the former diagnosis is\u000afavored.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, 11:00, CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY FOR A MASS (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID; REMOVED_DATE ):\u000aStromal/epithelial lesion with low stromal cellularity, minimal\u000anuclear pleomorphism, and no mitoses seen (see note).\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia.\u000aNote: The findings would be consistent with a fibroadenoma. Diagnostic\u000afeatures suggestive of a phyllodes tumor are not present. However, if\u000athese lesion represents a possible recurrence of the lesion present in\u000a1996, excision may be helpful to exclude the possibility of a phyllodes\u000atumor.\u000aIf this is a new unrelated lesion, then it most likely represents a\u000afibroadenoma.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: None given.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Consult slides.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by CAI,YUN-CAI,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aReceived from Dahl-Chase Pathology, Dept. Pathology, 358 Broadway, Suite 306,\u000aBangor, ME, REMOVED_CASE_ID, are eight glass slides.\u000aSix slides are labeled "96-REMOVED_CASE_ID" and sublabeled "A" through "F", corresponding\u000ato right breast mass collected on REMOVED_DATE  according to the accompanying\u000apathology report bearing the patient's name.\u000aTwo slides are labeled "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" and sublabeled "L 1,2" and "L 3,4",\u000acorresponding to a biopsy of the right breast performed on REMOVED_DATE  according\u000ato the accompanying pathology report bearing the patient's name.\u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: OUTSIDE SLIDE CONSULT - BREAST\u000a[report_end]
