VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aWEINSTEIN, MICHAEL, H., M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by WEINSTEIN,MICHAEL H.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISIONAL BIOPSY FOR A CLIP:\u000aNo residual atypical ductal hyperplasia is identified.\u000aMicrocalcifications noted in association with benign epithelium.\u000aPrior biopsy site changes are identified.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 46 year old premenopausal female s/p REMOVED_DATE  core biopsy for\u000acalcifications noted on outside hospital REMOVED_DATE mammograms, with\u000apathology demonstrating atypical ductal hyperplasia.\u000aOperation: R breast wire localization excision.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: R breast abnormal mammogram, atypical ductal hyperplasia.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. R breast mass, long lateral, short superior, whip stitch\u000adeep.\u000aRADIOLOGY; Clip in specimen. OR called.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by ABBOTT,DEREK W,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aReceived fresh, labeled with the patient's name, medical record number and\u000a"right breast mass", is a fragment of fatty breast tissue (4.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm).\u000aThere is a wire within the specimen. An x-ray accompanies the specimen. The\u000ax-ray shows a clip within the center specimen near the wire. The specimen\u000acontains a long stitch marking the lateral margin, a short stitch marking the\u000amedial margin. The specimen has been inked according to inks protocol prior to\u000aits arrival in surgical pathology for the evaluation of margins: posterior =\u000ablack; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow;\u000amedial = orange. The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal areas of myxoid,\u000awhite whorled material. No other gross lesions are apparent and x-rays taken\u000aof the specimen to localize the clip. The x-ray shows the clip to be in block\u000a5.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  entire breast tissue, REMOVED_DATE frags each cassette, ESS.\u000aNOTE: Clip is in block 5.\u000adwa\u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
