VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aLESTER, SUSAN, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000a1) RIGHT BREAST, EXCISION FOR A MASS:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA AND DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aSYNOPSIS:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA\u000aSize - REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aMultifocal? - no\u000aHistologic Type - ductal\u000aHistologic Grade (SBR) - II (moderate)\u000aNuclear Grade - intermediate\u000aEIC - positive\u000aLymphovascular invasion - absent\u000aDermal lymphatic invasion - N/A\u000aSkin invasion - N/A\u000aSkeletal muscle invasion - N/A\u000aFinal Margins (invasive)\u000aNegative (no ink on tumor) - anterior, superior, lateral\u000aPositive (ink on tumor) - posterior, medial, inferior\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aTypes - solid\u000aNuclear grade - intermediate to high\u000aCalcifications in DCIS - absent\u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - absent\u000aExtent of DCIS\u000aNumber of blocks:total - 9:10 blocks\u000aFinal Margins (DCIS)\u000aNegative (>0.3 cm) - superior, anterior\u000aClose (<0.1 cm) - posterior\u000aPositive (ink on DCIS) - medial, lateral, inferior\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - absent\u000aAJCC CLASSIFICATION - REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDc NX MX\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER/PR/HER-2) - pending\u000a2) RIGHT BREAST, INFERIOR:\u000aBenign breast tissue.\u000aNote: No invasive or in situ carcinoma identified.\u000a3) RIGHT BREAST, SUPERIOR:\u000aBenign breast tissue.\u000aNote: No invasive or in situ carcinoma identified.\u000a4) RIGHT BREAST, LATERAL:\u000aDCIS is present in one of four (1:4) slides at the green-inked\u000amargin.\u000aThe yellow margin is free of carcinoma.\u000aNote: The clinical significance of DCIS at the green inked margin in this\u000alateral specimen requires clinical correlation.\u000a5) RIGHT BREAST TISSUE, MEDIAL:\u000aNo definite carcinoma is seen; however, cautery artifact precludes\u000aoptimal evaluation.\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aFIRST SURGICAL ADDENDUM REMOVED_DATE  DR. SUSAN LESTER\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for invasive carcinoma (block 5):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) NEGATIVE (0)\u000aNote: The DCIS shows strong immunoreactivity for REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu. Although the\u000amajority of the invasive carcinoma is completely negative, there is a minor\u000acompenent (< 10% of total) that shows weak to moderate complete membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity.\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000ainvasive carcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but\u000aonly a portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity\u000ain >10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aSECOND SURGICAL ADDENDUM REMOVED_DATE  DR. SUSAN LESTER\u000aThe immunoperoxidase study for REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu was repeated with the same results.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: None given.\u000aOperation: Right breast biopsy\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast 12:00 atypia\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1) Right breast tissue\u000a#2) Right breast tissue, inferior\u000a#3) Right breast tissue, superior\u000a#4) Right breast tissue, lateral\u000a#5) Right breast tissue, medial\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "#1. RIGHT BREAST TISSUE", (FSA):\u000aInvasive carcinoma, poorly-differentiated with lobular features.\u000aHigh grade DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by SMOUSE,JASON H.,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in five parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart one, labeled "#1. right breast tissue", consists of a solid mass of\u000afibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm previously inked per\u000apathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior\u000a= blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange.\u000aThere is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm ill-defined mass which is REMOVED_DATE cm from the black margin,\u000aabuts the green margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the orange, REMOVED_DATE cm from red, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom blue, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the yellow margin. Representative sections of the\u000anodule are submitted as FSA. The remainder of the specimen is entirely\u000asubmitted for histologic evaluation.\u000aMicro 1: FSA remnant, ESS\u000aMicro 2: posterior margin, ESS\u000aMicro 3: anterior margin, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  remainder of specimen posterior to anterior, ESS\u000aPart two, labeled "#2. right breast tissue inferior", consists of a single mass\u000aof breast tissue measuring 3 x REMOVED_DATE x 1 cm which has been inked by the surgeon\u000aper pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior = black;\u000aanterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial =\u000aorange. The interior of the specimen is yellow/white fibrofatty with no\u000adiscrete masses or lesions. Representative sections are submitted for\u000ahistologic analysis.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  lateral to medial, RSS\u000aPart three, labeled "#3. right breast tissue superior", consists of a solid\u000amass of breast tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x 2 x 1 cm which has been entirely inked in\u000ablue and green. The interior of the specimen consists of fibrofatty tissue\u000aconsistent with breast tissue and is hemorrhagic in nature. There are no\u000adiscrete masses of lesions noted. Representative sections are submitted for\u000ahistologic analysis.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  3 frags, RSS\u000aPart four, labeled "#4. right breast tissue lateral", consists of one solid\u000amass of fibroadipose tissue measuring 3 x REMOVED_DATE x 1 cm which has been inked by\u000athe surgeon per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior =\u000ablack; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow;\u000amedial = orange. The interior of the specimen consists of fibrofatty tissue\u000awith a non firm area of poorly-demarcated white discoloration measuring 1 x 1 x\u000a1.5 cm which abuts both the lateral and medial margins. Representative\u000asections are submitted for histologic analysis.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  fragments of breast tissue, posterior to anterior, RSS\u000aPart five, labeled "#5. right breast tissue medial", consists of a single mass\u000aof non firm fibroadipose tissue measuring 2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The specimen has\u000abeen inked by the surgeon per pathology protocol for the evaluation of\u000amargins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green;\u000alateral = yellow; medial = orange. There are multiple areas of the specimen\u000awhich have no ink making the orientation difficult to interpret. The interior\u000aof the specimen consists of fibrofatty tissue and a 1 x 1 cm area of\u000ahemorrhage. Representative sections are submitted for histologic analysis.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  breast tissue posterior to anterior, RSS\u000ajs\u000aReports to: LESNIKOSKI, BETH-ANN M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN\u000a[report_end]
