 specimen is received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit\u000anumber, and "right breast #2 POST", and consists of two (2) tan cassettes. One\u000acassette is labeled "A ca++" and contains multiple, soft, fragmented, yellow to\u000awhite tissue cores (1.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate). The other cassette is\u000alabeled "B" and contains similar tissue fragments (2.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in\u000aaggregate).\u000aMicro 3: "A", multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 4: "B", multi frags, ESS.\u000adfi\u000aReports to: KAELIN, CAROLYN, MARY M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY(IES)\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY(IES)\u000a[report_end]
