VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Amend/Addenda\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast core needle biopsy\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: LORRAINE B TWOHIG MB,BCH,BAO\u000aCASE: BS-06-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000a********** Addended Report ***********\u000aResident: Jian Shen, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Susan Lester, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, LOWER ANTERIOR, 14 G ULTRASOUND GUIDED CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR A\u000a0.9 CM CIRCUMSCRIBED PALPABLE MASS:\u000aINVASIVE SPINDLE CELL CARCINOMA, measuring at least REMOVED_DATE cm in size.\u000aNo lymphovascular invasion is seen in this limited specimen.\u000aNo carcinoma in situ is seen in this limited specimen.\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies are performed with the following results for invasive\u000acarcinoma:\u000aCytokeratin PANK POSITIVE - STRONG\u000aCytokeratin 14 POSITIVE - STRONG\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID POSITIVE - STRONG\u000aDesmin NEGATIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID NEGATIVE\u000aNote: This is an unusual histologic appearance for a breast carcinoma. The\u000apresence of cytokeratin 14 and p63 suggest that this the carcinoma has features\u000aof myoepithelial and/or squamous differentiation. The spindle cells show\u000alittle pleomorphism. Occasional mitotic figures are present.\u000aImmunohistochemical analysis for estrogen receptor, progesterone receptor, and\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu will be performed and reported in an addendum.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Right lower anterior quadrant, 9 mm solid circumscribed mass. History\u000aof REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID colon carcinoma in 2000.\u000aOperation: 14 G Ultrasound.\u000aOperative Findings: 4 x 14 G ultrasound guided cores.\u000aBreast Imaging Findings: Circumscribed.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: ? Carcinoma; ? benign.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aRight breast tissue in orange cassette.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit\u000anumber, and "Right breast", in an orange cassette, and consists of multiple,\u000asoft, fragmented, yellow to white tissue cores (1.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in\u000aaggregate).\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Multi frags, ESS.\u000aWP/elw\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a2/2/2006\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM:\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for invasive carcinoma (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor NEGATIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor NEGATIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) NEGATIVE (0)\u000aNote: Normal epithelial cells are appropriately immunoreactive for estrogen\u000aand progesterone receptors.\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000acarcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but only\u000aa portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in >10%\u000aof tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in\u000a>10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aAddendum #1 by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
