VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Sentinel Lymph Nodes(s)\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: RICHARD S SWANSON M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-06-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Travis J Hollmann, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Alessandra F Nascimento, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT AXILLARY SENTINEL LYMPH NODE, BIOPSY:\u000aOne lymph node with no tumor present.\u000aLevels examined.\u000aRIGHT LATERAL BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZATION FOR A MASS:\u000aSPINDLE CELL (METAPLASTIC) CARCINOMA.\u000aSYNOPSIS:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA\u000aSize - REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aMultifocal - no\u000aHistologic Type - spindle cell\u000aEIC - absent\u000aLymphovascular invasion - absent\u000aDermal lymphatic invasion - N/A\u000aSkin invasion - N/A\u000aSkeletal muscle invasion - N/A\u000aFinal Margins (invasive)\u000aNegative (>0.3 cm) - posterior, medial, lateral,\u000asuperior, anterior\u000aVery close (<0.1cm) - inferior (focal)\u000aMitoses number up to REMOVED_DATE HPF\u000aNo necrosis seen.\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU - absent\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - absent\u000aOTHER FINDINGS\u000aCore biopsy site\u000aPapilloma\u000aAJCC CLASSIFICATION (6th edition) - REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDc pREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID MX\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER/PR/HER-2) - performed previously\u000aNOTE:\u000aImmunohistochemistry performed at BWH demonstrates the following staining\u000aprofile in tumor cells:\u000aPositive - Pan-Keratin, SMA, desmin (scattered)\u000aNegative - B catenin\u000aThe immunohistochemical profile confirms the above diagnosis.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, NEW INFERIOR MARGIN,:\u000aCalcifications associated with benign breast epithelium.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000aFINAL ANTERIOR MARGIN:\u000aSkin with no significant pathologic change.\u000aBenign breast tissue.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Palpable REMOVED_DATE cm mass right breast at 7 o'clock; Bx = spindle cell\u000acarcinoma.\u000aOperation: R sentinel node + R wide breast excision.\u000aOperative Findings: REMOVED_DATE cm mss right breast at 7 o'clock.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Spindle cell CA R breast.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) R axillary sentinel lymph node --> painted margins.\u000aB/2) Wide excision R lateral breast.\u000aC/3) New inferior margin (painted margins).\u000aD/4) Final anterior margin - long suture - lateral, short - superior.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in four parts, each labeled with the patients\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart A, "1. Right axillary sentinel lymph node", consists of a single fragment\u000aof tan/white soft tissue (1.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), grossly consistent with lymph\u000anode. The specimen was bisected and entirely submitted for histological\u000areview.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Right axillary sentinel lymph node, bisected, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, "2. Wide excision right lateral breast", consists of a single pre-inked\u000alumpectomy specimen (6.2 [M-L], REMOVED_DATE [A-P] and REMOVED_DATE [S-I]) with a single,\u000aundesignated stitch on the red-inked surface. The specimen was presumably\u000ainked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: Posterior/black;\u000aanterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange.\u000aThe specimen was serially sectioned from lateral to medial to reveal a single,\u000afirm, white mass (1.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which focally abuts the green, inferior\u000amargin and comes to within REMOVED_DATE cm of the orange, medial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to the\u000ared, superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin. The mass predominantly\u000aoccupies the inferior medial aspect of the specimen and appears to be directly\u000aopposite the posterior margin, however, blue ink is scant and not grossly\u000aidentified after sectioning the specimen. The specimen was sectioned into 15\u000aslices with Slice #1 correlating with medial margin. Slices 1 through 6 were\u000aentirely submitted for histological review as was slice 15.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin, slice 1, 1 frag, ESS slice 1.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 2, 1 frag each, ESS Slice 2.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 3, 1 frag each, ESS Slice 3.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 4, 1 frag each, ESS Slice 4.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 5, 2 frags each, ESS Slice 5.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 6, 2 frags each, ESS Slice 6.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 15, lateral margin, 2 frags, ESS Slice 15.\u000aPart C, "New inferior margin, right breast", consists of a single, pre-inked\u000alumpectomy specimen (6.7 cm [medial to lateral], REMOVED_DATE cm [A-P] and REMOVED_DATE cm [S-I]\u000awith a single undesignated stitch, which exists at the inferior/lateral margin.\u000aThe specimen is received inked presumably per the pathology protocol for the\u000aevaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red;\u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. The specimen is serially\u000asectioned from medial to lateral into 17 slices, and no residual tumor mass is\u000aidentifiable. The specimen is comprised of 85% to 95% fatty tissue and 5%-15%\u000afibrous tissue. Alternate slices, starting at Slice 1 (medial margin) were\u000asubmitted for histological review.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin, Slice 1, 1 frag, ESS Slice 1.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 3, 2 frags, ESS, Slice 2.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 5, 2 frags, ESS, Slice 5.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 7, 1 frag each, ESS, Slice 7.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 9, 1 frag each, ESS, Slice 9.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 11, 1 frag each, ESS, Slice 11.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 13, 1 frag each, ESS, Slice 13.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 15, 1 frag each, ESS, Slice 15.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 17, lateral margin, 1 frag, ESS, Slice 17.\u000aPart D, "4. Final anterior margin - long suture lateral, short - superior",\u000aconsists of a single soft-tissue excision specimen (4.2 [M-L], REMOVED_DATE [M-I] and\u000a0.7 [A-P]) with a white/tan skin ellipse (3.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in depth) and two\u000a(2) orienting sutures, short = superior, long = lateral. The specimen was\u000ainked (Note changes): Superior = skin. Inferior = black. Anterior = blue.\u000aPosterior = green. Medial = orange. Lateral = yellow. The specimen was\u000aserially sectioned from medial to lateral to reveal no tumor, nodules or gross\u000aabnormalities. The specimen was entirely submitted for histological review\u000afrom medial to lateral.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Final anterior margin, ESS from medial to lateral,\u000a2-2-2-1-1 frags respectively, ESS.\u000aTH/mmm\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Travis J Hollmann M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Alessandra F Nascimento M.D., Electronically signed on\u000a2/24/2006\u000a[report_end]
