VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: JAMES D IGLEHART M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-05-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Eric C Huang, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Michelle S Hirsch, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "RIGHT BREAST", EXCISION:\u000aBenign breast tissue with epithelial hyperplasia (see NOTE).\u000aFat necrosis and a foreign body giant cell reaction consistent with\u000aprior core biopsy site are present.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the\u000aspecimen, including margins.\u000aNOTE: The area of the palpable mass designated by the surgeon consists\u000aof biopsy site and fibroadenomatoid changes. This case has been\u000areviewed by Dr. S. Lester (Breast Pathology Service), who concurs.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: right breast mass, recent L breast CA; probably REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - in region of a\u000arecent REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID core biopsy.\u000aOperation: Excision, right breast mass.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: None given.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/#1) Right breast mass (short stitch = superior, long stitch = lateral),\u000awhite stitch in region of mass.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen, Part A, is received fresh, labeled with the patient?s name, unit\u000anumber, and "1. Right breast", and consists of a discoid fragment of yellow/tan\u000ato pink/tan breast tissue (3.9 [M-L] x REMOVED_DATE [S-I] x REMOVED_DATE [A-P] cm), which is\u000aoriented per surgeon with three (3) sutures (short = superior, long = lateral,\u000awhite stitch in region of mass). The specimen is inked per pathology protocol\u000afor the evaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red;\u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. The specimen is serially\u000asectioned from lateral to medial into a total of nine (9) slices (Slice 1 =\u000alateral, Slice 9 = medial). In Slice 8 (adjacent to the surgeon's white\u000astitch, designated "region of mass", there is a small, ill-defined, area of\u000adense, white, fibrous tissue (0.4 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which is REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000aanterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin and\u000a1.9 cm from the lateral margin. The remainder of the specimen is composed of\u000aapproximately 70% dense, white/tan, fibrous stroma and approximately 30%\u000ayellow/tan, lobulated, adipose tissue. The specimen is entirely, sequentially\u000asubmitted from lateral to medial.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Specimen entirely submitted from lateral to medial (surgeon\u000awith white stitch and possible mass in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), multiple frags, ESS.\u000aLMB/mmm\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Michelle S Hirsch M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Michelle S Hirsch M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a11/29/2005\u000a[report_end]
