VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Wai Chin Foo, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Michael W Bennett, M.B., B.C.H.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aLEFT BREAST, UPPER OUTER, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aDuctal epithelial hyperplasia.\u000aSclerosing adenosis with associated calcifications.\u000aColumnar cell change.\u000aIntraductal papilloma with ductal epithelial hyperplasia.\u000aCalcifications associated with benign epithelium.\u000aFibroadenoma (0.5 cm).\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the\u000aspecimen, including margins.\u000aLEFT BREAST, LOWER OUTER, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aDuctal epithelial hyperplasia.\u000aColumnar cell change.\u000aIntraductal papilloma with ductal epithelial hyperplasia.\u000aCalcifications associated with benign epithelium.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the\u000aspecimen, including margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 67-year-old female S/P L breast core bx on REMOVED_DATE  for calcs -\u000ademonstrating ADH - excision recommended.\u000aOperation: L breast WL bx x 2.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: None given.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) L upper/outer breast tissue; suture - short --> superior, long -->\u000alateral, whip stitch on deep margin. To FS Rm for re-mammo.\u000aB/2) L lower/outer quadrant; suture - short --> superior, long --> lateral,\u000awhite --> deep margin. To FS Rm for re-mammo.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Ca++ present, no clip, intact wire. OR called/DGS\u000aClip in specimen/intact wire/DGS.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and medical record number.\u000aPart A, "#1. Left upper, outer breast tissue, suture short equals superior,\u000along equals lateral width equals deep margin," consists of an oriented, wire\u000alocalized breast specimen (S-I REMOVED_DATE x M-L REMOVED_DATE x A-P REMOVED_DATE cm) with three orienting\u000asutures (short superior, long lateral, width deep) and a localization wire\u000aentering at the inferior medial margin. An accompanying radiograph\u000ademonstrates a wire and a diffusely fibrotic breast with incidental\u000acalcifications.\u000aThe specimen is sectioned to reveal a diffusely firm, fibrotic breast without\u000adefinitive lesions or calcifications. Prior core biopsy site is not\u000aidentified.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: REMOVED_DATE frags per block, ESS.\u000aPart B, "#2. Left lower outer quadrant, suture short superior, long lateral,\u000awidth deep margin", consists of an oriented, wire localized excisional breast\u000aspecimen (S-I REMOVED_DATE x M-L REMOVED_DATE x A-P REMOVED_DATE cm) with three orienting sutures (short\u000asuperior, long lateral, width deep) and a localization wire entering at the\u000asuperior lateral margin. The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a\u000afibrotic tan/white mass (1.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) at the area designated by the\u000alocalization wire. The area appears to abut the medial and superior margin.\u000aAn accompanying radiograph demonstrates a wire and clip. The specimen is\u000aentirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Superior margin, REMOVED_DATE frags per block, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential sections from superior to inferior, 1 frag per block,\u000aESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Inferior margin, 4 frags per block, ESS.\u000aWCF/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Michael W Bennett M.B., B.C.H., Electronically signed on\u000a7/11/2007\u000a[report_end]
