VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Consult material\u000aProcedure Date:\u000aOrdering Provider: HAROLD J BURSTEIN M.D.,PH.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Jane E Brock, M.B., B.S., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Andrea L Richardson, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aCONSULT SLIDES FROM BAYSTATE HEALTH, SPRINGFIELD, MA:\u000aLEFT BREAST, ULTRASOUND GUIDED CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR AN OVAL CIRCUMSCRIBED\u000a2.6 CM MASS (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID; REMOVED_DATE ):\u000aFibroepithelial lesion, (see note).\u000aNOTE: The epithelium shows a predominantly pericanalicular growth pattern with\u000afocal intracanalicular (leaf-like) growth. Mild gynecomastia-like tufting\u000aepithelial hyperplasia is present. The stroma is mildly cellular with mitoses\u000anumbering up to REMOVED_DATE HPF. No heterologous stromal differentiation is present.\u000aThe findings are most consistent with a juvenile fibroadenoma. However, a\u000aphyllodes tumor is included in the differential given the focal\u000aintracanalicular growth pattern seen and presence of stromal mitoses. Excision\u000aof the mass is recommended for definitive diagnosis.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Left breast mass\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Cellular fibroepithelial lesion\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aConsult slides.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aReceived from Baystate Health, Pathology Department, 759 Chestnut Street,\u000aSpringfield, MA REMOVED_CASE_ID, are four (4) glass slides.\u000aThe slides are labeled "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" and sublabeled "1 1 LEV(#6)", "1 2", "1 3\u000aLEV"(#6) and "1 4 LEV"(#4), corresponding to a left breast ultrasound guided\u000acore needle biopsy (0.1 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm, and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) performed on\u000a7/13/07, according to the accompanying pathology report bearing the patient's\u000aname.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Andrea L Richardson M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a7/30/2007\u000a[report_end]
