VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: JULIE L JONES M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Elizabeth Amy Morgan, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Michael W Bennett, M.B., B.C.H.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aLEFT BREAST MASS EXCISION FOR A MASS:\u000aFIBROEPITHELIAL LESION, REMOVED_DATE cm (see note).\u000aThe stroma is multifocally moderately cellular.\u000aMinimal nuclear pleomorphism is present.\u000aMitoses are present (up to 3 per 10 HPF's).\u000aNo stromal invasion is seen.\u000aNo stromal overgrowth is present.\u000aNo heterologous elements are present.\u000aMild gynecomastia-like tufting epithelial hyperplasia is present.\u000aNote: The differential diagnosis includes a cellular (juvenile) fibroadenoma\u000aand a low grade phyllodes tumor. Definitive criteria for a phyllodes tumor, and\u000ain particular significant stromal overgrowth, are absent. The lesion appears\u000acircumscribed, but is present at the inked margin with cautery on the lesion.\u000aClose clinical follow-up is advisable.\u000aThis case was reviewed by Dr. Susan Lester and Dr. Jim Connolly who concur with\u000athe above diagnosis.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Left breast mass, s/p core bx demonstrating a fibroepithelial lesion,\u000aunable to exclude phyllodes tumor\u000aOperation: Left breast excisional biopsy\u000aOperative Findings: Not provided\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast mass\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Left breast mass\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "#1. Lt breast mass", and consists of an unoriented breast resection\u000aspecimen, measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm, inked black. There is a tan/pink,\u000alobulated, focally mucoid mass (3.6 cm in greatest dimension) comprising the\u000amajority of the specimen. The entire specimen is submitted for histologic\u000aevaluation.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Breast excision specimen, multi frags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aem\u005cpab\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Michael W Bennett M.B., B.C.H., Electronically signed on\u000a8/29/2007\u000a[report_end]
