nce or approval is not necessary; this laboratory has established and verified the test's accuracy and precision. Added by: Atul Kumar Bhan, M.D. Signed On: 23 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 14:35 GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name and unit number, and "right breast lump, needle localization", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm portion of fibroadipose tissue with needle localization wire. A short stitch is designated by the surgeon as superior and a long stitch as lateral. The specimen is inked as follows: anterior - blue; posterior - black; medial - green; lateral - yellow. The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm ill-defined, tan-brown, firm lesion located REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin. There are focal hemorrhages in the adjacent area of the lesion. The lesion is entirely submitted in A-D; REMOVED_DATE cm inferior to the lesion is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm area of calcification that grossly abuts the antero-lateral margin. This area is submitted entirely in E, following decalcification. The remainder of the breast parenchyma is grossly unremarkable. Representative sections are submitted in F-G. Received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "left sentinel node hot and blue, REMOVED_DATE " is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm, tan-pink fatty tissue fragment, bisected and entirely submitted in cassette H. Received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "final shaved margin, superior REMOVED_DATE cavity" is a yellow-tan unoriented fibrofatty tissue, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm, serially sectioned and entirely submitted in cassettes I-J. Received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "final shaved margin, inferior REMOVED_DATE cavity" are 2 unoriented light tan fibrofatty tissue fragment, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm, and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The larger piece is serially sectioned and entirely submitted in cassettes K-L. The smaller piece is submitted entirely in cassette M. Gross Description by: TAI-YUAN LIN, MD Resident: SARAH ROLLINS, MD =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT - REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID REPORTS TO: Barbara Lynn Smith, M.D. PART A: BREAST(LEFT),EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B: LYMPH NODE(LEFT SENTINEL #1375,4254,751),EXCISION PART C: BREAST(LEFT,FINAL SUPERIOR MARGIN,1/2 CAVITY),EXCI PART D: BREAST(LEFT,FINAL INFERIOR MARGIN,1/2 CAVITY),EXCI
