VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aGLICKMAN, JONATHAN, NEIL, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by GLICKMAN,JONATHAN NEIL,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, EXCISION:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA, ONE (1) FOCUS\u000aSYNOPSIS:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA\u000aSize - REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aMultifocal? - no\u000aHistologic Type - medullary (with extensive (>50%)\u000anecrosis)\u000aHistologic Grade (SBR) - III (poor)\u000aNuclear Grade - high\u000aEIC - negative\u000aLymphovascular invasion - absent\u000aDermal lymphatic invasion - N/A\u000aSkin invasion - N/A\u000aSkeletal muscle invasion - N/A\u000aFinal Margins (invasive) -\u000aClose (tumor <0.1 cm from margin - broad front, multifocal (unoriented\u000aspecimen)\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU - is not identified\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - absent\u000aAJCC CLASSIFICATION - REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID pNx MX\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER/PR/HER-2) - pending, to be reported in an addendum\u000aNOTE:\u000aMedullary carcinomas of size greater than 3 cm have been associated with a more\u000aaggressive clinical course than "typical" medullary carcinomas. Case reviewed\u000aby Dr. A. Richardson, BWH Breast Pathology Service.\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: by RICHARDSON,ANDREA,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for invasive carcinoma:\u000aEstrogen receptor negative\u000aProgesterone receptor negative\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) negative (0)\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000ainvasive carcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but\u000aonly a portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity\u000ain >10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 64 year old female with mass of right breast core biopsy - necrosis.\u000aOperation: Excision\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Mass - right breast\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Right breast tissue\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by JEDLICKA,PAVEL J.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit\u000anumber and "right breast tissue", and consists of a single unoriented fragment\u000aof yellow/tan fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The specimen\u000ais inked. Sectioning reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm tan mass with a largely\u000anecrotic (>50%) and partialy cavitated central core, grossly extending to\u000amargins. The specimen is entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  serial sections of specimen, 24 frags, ESS\u000apj\u000aReports to: CHRISTIAN, ROGER, L. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
