VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID LYMPH NODE BIOPSY\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aMUELLER, JAMES, D., M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by MUELLER,JAMES,D.,M.D.\u000a1. SPECIMEN LABELED "AXILLARY CONTENTS, RIGHT":\u000aMETASTATIC MEDULLARY BREAST CARCINOMA present as a REMOVED_DATE cm deposit in one\u000a(1) of twenty (20) lymph nodes.\u000aNo extracapsular spread is present.\u000a2. SPECIMEN LABELED "RIGHT BREAST, RE-EXCISION":\u000aBenign breast parenchyma with prior biopsy site (see note).\u000aSkin with cicatrix.\u000aThere is no residual invasive carcinoma.\u000aNote: Due to the preoperative clinical concern regarding the possibility of\u000atumor, the margins of this specimen were inked, sampled and examined\u000amicroscopically.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 64 year old female with cancer of right breast.\u000aOperation: Re-excision, cancer site right breast, axillary dissection\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast cancer\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1) Axillary contents, right\u000a#2) Right breast re-excision (long stitch/lateral;\u000ashort stitch/superior)\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by CORBO,JOSEPH,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart one, labeled "#1. axillary contents", consists of a portion of yellow/tan\u000afibrous adipose tissue (8 x 8 x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate). Multiple lymph nodes are\u000aidentified and submitted.\u000aMicro 1: 1 axillary lymph node, 2 frags, ESS\u000aMicro 2: 5 axillary lymph nodes, 5 frags, ESS\u000aMicro 3: 2 axillary lymph nodes, 2 frags, ESS\u000aMicro 4: 4 axillary lymph nodes, 4 frags, ESS\u000aMicro 5: 1 axillary lymph node (bisected), 2 frags, ESS\u000aMicro 6: 1 axilary lymph node (bisected), 2 frags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  1 large axillary lymph node (2 x 2 x REMOVED_DATE cm), mult frags, ESS\u000aMicro 11: 3 axillary lymph nodes, 3 frags, ESS\u000aMicro 12: 1 axillary lymph node, 2 frags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  1 large involved axillary lymph node, mult frags, ESS\u000aMicro 15: 1 possible lymph node, 1 frag, ESS\u000aPart two, labeled "#2. right breast re-excision", consists of a portion of\u000ayellow/tan fibroadipose (10.5 x 9 x REMOVED_DATE cm) with attached tan skin ellipse (10\u000ax REMOVED_DATE cm) in the center of which is a well-healed surgical scar (7.2 x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm). There are long and short orienting sutures attached to the skin ellipse\u000aand the specimen is received already inked per pathology protocol for the\u000aevaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red;\u000ainferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. Deep to the scar in the\u000acenter of the skin ellipse there is an irregular area of fibrosis and fat\u000anecrosis which is in continuity with and surrounds a single unilocular cystic\u000abiopsy cavity (2.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The biopsy cavity approaches grossly to\u000awithin REMOVED_DATE cm of the medial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of\u000athe anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the superior margin, 1 cm of the posterior\u000amargin and greater than 3 cm from the lateral margin. There is no evidence of\u000aresidual invasive carcinoma. Representative sections of the biopsy cavity, all\u000asurrounding margins, and skin ellipse are submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  biopsy cavity and nearest inferior and medial margins, 2 frags\u000aeach, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  biopsy cavity (representative sections), 1 frag each, RSS\u000aMicro 20: skin with scar and anterior margin adjacent to biopsy cavity, 1\u000afrag, RSS\u000aMicro 21: skin with scar and biopsy site with nearest superior margin, 1\u000afrag, RSS\u000aMicro 22: posterior margin nearest biopsy cavity, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 23: lateral margin (representative section), 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 24: representative section of scar with skin ellipse, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  representative portions of breast tissue away from biopsy\u000acavity, 1 frag each, RSS\u000ajc\u000aReports to: CHRISTIAN, ROGER, L. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: LYMPH NODE BIOPSY\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
