rt - superior; long - lateral.\u000aC/3) Right mastectomy skin.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in three parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and medical record number.\u000aPart A, labeled "#1. Left breast", consists of a simple mastectomy specimen (66\u000agrams, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with orienting sutures designating the superior\u000aand lateral aspects. There is an overlying skin ellipse (5.2 x REMOVED_DATE cm)\u000aincluding nipple areolar complex (1.0 x REMOVED_DATE cm). The nipple is everted, and\u000athere are no gross lesions involving the skin surface. The deep fascial plane\u000ais intact (11.0 x REMOVED_DATE cm) and inked black. The breast parenchyma comprises\u000aapproximately 80% firm fibrous tissue and 20% adipose tissue. Within the\u000afibrous breast parenchyma, there is focal cystic change, predominantly in a\u000acentral location. No discrete lesions are identified. No lymph nodes are\u000aidentified within the lateral breast tissue. Representative sections are\u000asubmitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Nipple, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Central breast parenchyma, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Upper outer quadrant, REMOVED_DATE frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lower outer quadrant, 2 frags each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Upper inner quadrant, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lower inner quadrant, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000aPart B, labeled "#2. Right breast", consists of a simple mastectomy (104 grams,\u000a14.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with orienting sutures designating the superior and\u000alateral aspects. There is an overlying skin ellipse (6.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm)\u000aincluding nipple-areolar complex (2.0 x REMOVED_DATE cm) with an everted nipple and no\u000agross lesions. The deep fascial plane is intact (13.0 x REMOVED_DATE cm, inked black).\u000aThere is no attached skeletal muscle. There is a smooth-walled cavity (1.6 x\u000a1.5 x REMOVED_DATE cm) situated in the central upper breast parenchyma consistent with\u000aprevious resection site, abutting the deep margin where it is associated with\u000aan area of puckered fascia. In addition, there is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm cyst in\u000athe upper outer quadrant, REMOVED_DATE cm from the deep margin. The remaining breast\u000aparenchyma comprises approximately 70% firm fibrous tissue and 30% adipose\u000atissue. No additional discrete lesions are identified. The entire excision\u000acavity and additional tissue superior to the cavity is submitted in addition to\u000arepresentative sections of remaining breast parenchyma.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Excision cavity, serially sectioned from medial to lateral, 1 frag\u000aeach, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Additional tissue superior to cavity site, 3 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Random central breast tissue, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Cyst, upper outer quadrant, REMOVED_DATE frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Random sections, lower outer quadrant, 2 frags each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Random sections, upper inner quadrant, REMOVED_DATE frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Random sections, lower inner quadrant, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Nipple, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aPart C, labeled "#3. Right mastectomy skin", consists of a circular ring of\u000askin REMOVED_DATE cm in diameter, REMOVED_DATE cm thick with no gross lesions, representative\u000asections are submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Skin, 4 frags, RSS.\u000aLDO/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jane E. Brock M.B., B.S., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000aSaturday REMOVED_MONTH 09, 2010 at 03:45:34PM\u000a[report_end]
