VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-06-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Jacqueline M William, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Xiaohua Qian, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aLEFT BREAST TISSUE, EXCISIONAL BIOPSY FOR A MASS:\u000aBenign breast tissue with focal dense fibrosis (1.1 cm).\u000aBiopsy site changes.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 53-year-old female with Hx R breast Ca and now with L breast mass.\u000a1/24/01 - R breast core neck Bx - IDL - ER/PR (+) HER 2/neu (-).\u000a2/12/01 R breast MRM and AND -"IDC, (multifocal), DCIS, mets to lymph nodes.\u000a2/28/02 - R mastectom - skin - "no pathologic change" -\u000aL breast tissue - "Benign breast tissue".\u000a3/15/06 - L breast core needle bx "minute fragment of nl breast tissue w/i\u000aadipose tissue - U/S REMOVED_DATE  - L breast - "4-mm hypoechoic solid mass at primary\u000asite of palpable mass.\u000aPREVIOUS SURGERY:\u000a1/24/01 - REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000a2/12/01 - REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000a2/28/02 - REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000a3/13/06 - BS-06-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aHx Radiation Rx, R breast.\u000aHx Chemotherapy (R) breast Ca.\u000aOn Tamoxifen.\u000aOperation: None given.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: None given.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) Left breast tissue - whip stitch, deep margin; short stitch, superior;\u000along stitch, lateral.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Soft-tissue density, clip + wire in specimen. Phone to Dr. Rhei in\u000athe OR. - R. Birdwell.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen, Part A, is received fresh, labeled with the patients name, unit\u000anumber, and "1. Left breast tissue, long - lateral, whip stitch - deep, short",\u000aand consists of an ovoid fragment of yellow/tan to tan/pink fibroadipose tissue\u000a(4.7 [M-L] x REMOVED_DATE [S-I] x REMOVED_DATE [A-P] cm), which is oriented per surgeon as\u000aindicated. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of\u000amargins: Posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green;\u000alateral/yellow; medial/orange. There is one (1) needle-localization wire in\u000aplace, which enters the posterolateral aspect of the specimen with no clear\u000aexit point. The specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral to\u000aexhibit a central focus of very dense white/tan fibrous stroma (occupying\u000aapproximately 40% of the specimen) with punctate areas of hemorrhage (0.1 to\u000a0.2 cm in greatest dimension) and approximately 60% yellow-tan adipose tissue.\u000aNo discrete masses or lesions are grossly identified. The tip of the\u000aneedle-localization wire is loosely imbedded within adipose tissue at the\u000alateral aspect of the specimen, near which the metal clip is identified. The\u000aspecimen is entirely sequentially submitted from medial to lateral.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Specimen from medial to lateral with dense fibrous stroma\u000a(corresponding to circled area of interest on radiograph in\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID through REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) (Clip identified, Slice in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), multiple\u000afrags total, ESS.\u000aLMB/mmm\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Xiaohua Qian M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a4/8/2006\u000a[report_end]
