VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID LYMPH NODES REGIONAL RESECTION\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aLESTER, SUSAN, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, EXCISION INCLUDING NIPPLE, AND AXILLARY NODE DISSECTION:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA WITH MIXED FEATURES\u000aSYNOPSIS:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA\u000aSize - REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aMultifocal - no\u000aHistologic Type - mixed ductal and lobular\u000aHistologic Grade (SBR) - III (poor)\u000aNuclear Grade - high\u000aEIC - negative\u000aLymphovascular invasion - present\u000aDermal lymphatic invasion - absent\u000aSkin invasion - present without ulceration\u000aSkeletal muscle invasion - N.A.\u000aFinal Margins (invasive)\u000aNegative (>0.3 cm) - all margins\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU - absent\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - absent\u000aLYMPH NODES\u000aAxillary Lymph Nodes - negative\u000aNumber of positive nodes - 0\u000aNumber of nodes examined - 14\u000aOTHER FINDINGS\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia\u000aCore biopsy site\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER/PR/HER-2) - pending\u000aNOTE: The carcinoma is predominantly in the dermis of the nipple and as\u000amultiple foci associated with fibrosis and hemosiderin deposition below the\u000anipple. These findings are suggestive of residual tumor with treatment\u000aeffect. However, the remaining carcinoma appears viable and numerous mitoses\u000aare present.\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for invasive carcinoma (block 7):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor NEGATIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) POSITIVE (3+)\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000acarcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but\u000aonly a portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity\u000ain >10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: History of locally advanced right breast cancer involving nipple s/p\u000aHerceptin/Navelbine x 12.\u000aOperation: Right partial mastectomy with nipple excision, axillary node\u000adissection\u000aOperative findings: Scarred nipple, no gross tumor\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast cancer\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1) Right axillary contents\u000a#2) Right breast tissue with nipple areolar contents suture, re-approximates\u000alateral margin\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by REIMANN,JULIE DYLAN REGAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart one, labeled "#1. right axillary contents", consists of multiple fragments\u000aof fibroadipose tissue measuring in aggregate 7 x 5 cm x 1 cm deep.\u000aMicro 1: soft tissue with candidate lymph nodes, 6 frags, ESS\u000aMicro 2: soft tissue with candidate lymph nodes, 4 frags, ESS\u000aMicro 3: soft tissue with candidate lymph nodes, 3 frags, ESS\u000aMicro 4: piece of soft tissue with 1 candidate lymph node serially sectioned,\u000a3 frags, ESS\u000aMicro 5: 1 lymph node inked blue and bisected, another piece of soft tissue\u000awith candidate lymph node, ESS\u000aMicro 6: piece of soft tissue, 1 frag, ESS\u000aPart two, labeled "#2. right breast tissue with nipple areolar contents -\u000asuture re-approximates lateral margin", consists of a skin ellipse (4.5 x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm); nipple (1.1 cm) and breast tissue (1.7 cm). The specimen has been inked\u000aby the surgeon per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior\u000a= black; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow;\u000amedial = orange. There are two hard white/tan nodules; the first measures 4 cm\u000afrom lateral, 3 cm from deep, REMOVED_DATE cm from superior, REMOVED_DATE cm from inferior, and\u000a1.5 cm from the medial margin. This area is consistent with residual tumor and\u000ameasures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm and is deep to the nipple. There is a second\u000anodule (approximately 1 cm) from the first nodule and measures REMOVED_DATE cm and\u000acontains nine cysts, and is not grossly definitively invasive. The area\u000aaround the first nodule has an area of white fibrous tissue (3 x 3 x 2 cm).\u000aMicro 7: anterior margin with 1st nodule, 1 frag, ESS\u000aMicro 8: posterior margin with 1st nodule, 1 frag, ESS\u000aMicro 9: superior margin with 1st nodule, 1 frag, ESS\u000aMicro 10: representative sections from inferior, superior and posterior\u000amargins, 3 frags, ESS\u000aMicro 11: representative sections from medial and lateral margins, 2 frags,\u000aESS\u000aMicro 12: representative piece of fibroadipose tissue from superior margin,\u000a1 frag, ESS\u000aMicro 13: representative sections from 1st nodule, 2 frags, ESS\u000aMicro 14: representative sections from superior and inferior skin margins, 2\u000afrags, ESS\u000aMicro 15: fibroadipose tisse contain in 2nd nodule, 1 frag, ESS\u000aMicro 16: soft tissue adjacent to 2nd nodule area, 1 frag, ESS\u000aMicro 17: area of soft tissue near 2nd nodule with ? intramammary lymph\u000anode, 2 frags, RSS\u000aMicro 18: soft tissue deep to the nipple containing 1st nodule, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 19: piece of fibroadipose tissue, bisected, 2 frags, ESS\u000aMicro 20: fibroadipose tissue near 2nd nodule, bisected, 2 frags, ESS\u000aMicro 21: additional fibroadipose tissue in region of 2nd nodule, 1 frag,\u000aESS\u000aMicro 22: piece of fibroadipose tissue near 2nd nodule, bisected, 2 frags,\u000aESS\u000ajdr\u000aReports to: LESNIKOSKI, BETH-ANN M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: LYMPH NODES REGIONAL RESECTION\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
