 a tan/yellow\u000aoriented fragment of fibradipose tissue (5.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), with a short\u000asuture marking superior, and a long suture marking lateral. A needle\u000alocalization wire is in place. The specimen is inked for the evaluation of\u000amargins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior =\u000agreen; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. Representative sections of margins\u000aare submitted for microscopic examination. The area contain the clip is grossly\u000aidentifiable, but the clip is not seen.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  area with clip, multiple frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  remainder of specimen, multiple frags,ESS.\u000aReports to: KAELIN, CAROLYN, MARY M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
