VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: JAMES D IGLEHART M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-05-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Peter M Sadow, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Jonathan N Glickman, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, EXCISION:\u000aIntraductal papillomas with florid epithelial hyperplasia (levels\u000aexamined) (see NOTE).\u000aColumnar cell hyperplasia.\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia.\u000aComplex sclerosing lesion with epithelial hyperplasia.\u000aBiopsy site changes.\u000aCalcifications in benign epithelium.\u000aSkeletal muscle.\u000aThere is no carcinoma present, including margins.\u000aNOTE: Immunohistochemistry for p63/REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID performed on one focus confirms the\u000apresence of myoepithelial cells, supporting the above diagnosis.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Right breast mass.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) right breast mass - short stitch/superior, long stitch/lateral -- mammo.\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000aNo clip in specimen. Wire-hook in specimen. Dr. Iglehart was phoned.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patients name, unit number,\u000aand "R breast mass, short/superior, long/lateral", and consists of a portion of\u000ayellow/tan/brown fibroadipose tissue (3.3 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with attached\u000afragments of fibromuscular tissue. There are two orienting sutures\u000a("short/superior; long/lateral") and a needle localization wire in place\u000a(entering laterally). The specimen is inked by the pro-sector according to the\u000apathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black;\u000aanterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange, and\u000aserially sectioned from medial to lateral, revealing a tan/white, focally\u000ahemorrhagic, ill-defined fibrous lesion (2.7 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which is\u000atraversed by the needle localization wire, and grossly extends to all surgical\u000amargins. The accompanying radiograph confirms the presence of a wire-hook\u000awithin the specimen (confirmed by Dr. Iglehart via phone). No clip is present\u000awithin the specimen. NOTE: a fragment of tan irregular, synthetic elastic\u000amaterial (0.3 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) is present loosely embedded within the breast\u000atissue. The remaining tissue consists of scant yellow/tan fibroadipose tissue.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: breast tissue sequentially from medial to lateral, multiple\u000afrags, ESS.\u000adfi/lp\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Peter M Sadow M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aPrelim Dx Release by Peter M Sadow M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jonathan N Glickman M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a12/29/2005\u000a[report_end]
