VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID LYMPH NODE BIOPSY\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aCORSON, JOSEPH, M., M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by CORSON,JOSEPH M.,M.D.\u000a1. SENTINEL NODE:\u000aOne (1) lymph node with no tumor seen.\u000aLevels examined.\u000a2. LEFT BREAST BIOPSY, WITH NEEDLE LOCALIZATION WIRE, FOR MASS:\u000aINVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA, (1.5 cm), poorly differentiated\u000a(modified Bloom-Richardson grade III/III).\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN-SITU, high nuclear grade, comedo,\u000acribriform, and solid types with focal necrosis in solid type.\u000aDCIS is present at the medial margin (block 3), REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000alateral margin (block 6), and REMOVED_DATE mm from the superior margin\u000a(block 8).\u000aNo lymphovascular invasion seen.\u000aMicrocalcifications are associated with DCIS and benign ducts.\u000aFibrocystic change, including microcysts, adenosis.\u000aMultifocal fibroadenomatoid change.\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: by RICHARDSON,ANDREA,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for invasive carcinoma:\u000aEstrogen receptor positive\u000aProgesterone receptor positive\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) positive (3+)\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000ainvasive carcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but\u000aonly a portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity\u000ain >10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast cancer.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Sentinel node.\u000a2. Left breast mass.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by LEE,BENJAMIN H.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fixed in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart one, sublabeled "#1, sentinel node", consists of a yellow/tan fragment of\u000asoft tissue (2.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The specimen is bisected and entirely\u000asubmitted.\u000aMicro 1: sentinel node, bisected, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aPart two, sublabeled "#2, left breast mass", consists of a yellow/tan fragment\u000aof fibroadipose tissue (5.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with a needle localization wire.\u000aThe specimen has been pre-inked in six colors by the surgeon. The specimen is\u000ainked for the evaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue;\u000asuperior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. There is\u000aa dense fibrous area (1.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with gritty calcifications in the\u000aproximity of the needle localization wire approximately REMOVED_DATE cm from the blue\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the orange margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the yellow margin, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom the black margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the red margin and REMOVED_DATE cm from the green\u000amargin. Representative sections are submitted for analysis.\u000aMicro 2: perpendicular green margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 3: tumor mass with respect to medial margin.\u000aMicro 4: tumor with respect to black margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 5: tumor with respect to blue margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 6: tumor with respect to yellow margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  tumor and areas of gritty calcifications, 1 frag each RSS.\u000aMicro 9: perpendicular superior (red) margins, ,4 frags, RSS.\u000aReports to: OSTEEN, ROBERT, T. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: LYMPH NODE BIOPSY\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
