en\u000aand progesterone receptors.\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000ainvasive carcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but\u000aonly a portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity\u000ain >10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: none given\u000aOperation: Right sentinel node Bx\u000aRight breast lumpectomy\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right Breast Cancer\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1) Right sentinel lymph node (stitch is of no consequence)\u000a2) Right breast cancer stich is longitudinal, short superior, skin anterior\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by SPRINGER,KIMBERLEY M.,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received in two parts, each labeled with the patient's name and\u000aunit number.\u000aPart one, "#1 right sentinel lymph node" consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afragment of fibroadipose tissue, containing one (1) candidate lymph node. The\u000alymph node is bisected and entirely submitted.\u000aMicro 1: Sentinel lymph node, 2 frags, ESS\u000aPart two, "#2 right breast cancer stitch long lateral short superior skin\u000aanterior", consists of one fragment of breast tissue (3.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cms),\u000ainked by the pathologist per pathology protocol for evaluation of margins\u000a(skin anterior). There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm white/tan skin ellipse. A REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000ax REMOVED_DATE cm mass is present and is located REMOVED_DATE cm to superior, REMOVED_DATE cm to deep,\u000a0.5 cm to inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm to medial, REMOVED_DATE cm lateral, and REMOVED_DATE cm to anterior\u000amargins. A representative section is submitted to tumor bank. The entire\u000aspecimen is submitted from lateral to medial.\u000aMicros: 2&3: Lateral margin, 2 frags each, ESS\u000aMicros: 4&5 & 8&9: Deep, inferior, anterior, superior margins (tumor taken for\u000atumor bank), 1 frag each, ESS\u000aMicros: 6&7: Tumor with deep, inferior, superior, skin margins, 1 frag each,\u000aESS\u000aMicro 10: Medial margin, 1 frag, ESS\u000aMicro 11: Medial margin, 2 frags, ESS\u000aReports to: IGLEHART, JAMES, DIRK M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: SENTINEL LYMPH NODE\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
