VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Scott Lovitch, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Hejin P Hahn, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR CALCIFICATION:\u000aColumnar cell change with associated microcalcifications.\u000aCore biopsy site changes.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 50-year-old premenopausal woman with mammo REMOVED_DATE  demonstrating\u000afocal group of punctate and indistinct calcs in UOQ; S/P R core bx, REMOVED_DATE \u000arevealing "flat atypia" - excision recommended.\u000aOperation: R breast WL bx.\u000aOperative Findings: None specified.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: None specified.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) Right breast tissue; stitch - short/superior, long-lateral; ship stitch\u000aat chest wall margin.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Tissue marker, Ca++s and hookwire in specimen. C. Denison MD.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number\u000aand "#1. Right breast tissue, short stitch superior, long lateral, whipstitch\u000aon chest wall margin", and consists of an irregular portion of fibrofatty\u000atissue (5.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), with a long suture designating lateral, a short\u000asuture designating superior, and a whipstitch designating chest wall margin\u000a(posterior). There is an inserted needle-localization wire, which enters along\u000athe inferior margin, and does not exit the specimen. The specimen is received\u000ainked per pathology protocol as anterior blue, posterior black, superior red,\u000ainferior green, lateral yellow, and medial orange. The specimen is serially\u000asectioned to reveal a cavity, consistent with a biopsy cavity (0.7 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm), REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000alateral margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin. A surgical clip is\u000aidentified within the biopsy cavity. The remaining cut surface displays 80%\u000ayellow lobulated adipose tissue, and 20% dense white fibrous tissue, with no\u000aadditional discrete masses or lesions identified. The specimen is sequentially\u000asubmitted in its entirety.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, radially, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 1 frag, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross section, bisected, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross section, bisected, with the cavity in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 1 frag\u000aeach, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross section, bisected, with the cavity in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 1 frag\u000aeach, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross sections, with the cavity in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 1 frag each,\u000aESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross section, bisected, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross sections, bisected, containing the area of\u000aconcern (? calcifications) on the accompanying radiograph, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross section, bisected, containing the possible area\u000aof calcifications on the accompanying radiograph, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin, radially, 3 frags each, ESS.\u000aCP/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Hejin P Hahn M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a3/31/2008\u000a[report_end]
