VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aODZE, ROBERT, DANIEL, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by ODZE,ROBERT DANIEL,M.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A CLIP:\u000aColumnar hyperplasia with atypia and associated with calcifications,\u000aadjacent to biopsy site (block #5).\u000aBiopsy site present.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Abnormal left mammogram, left core biopsy with CAPSS.\u000aOperation: left needle localized biopsy.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal left mammogram.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Left breast tissue.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Ca++ and marker in specimen (two wires). Dr. Smith.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by BROCK,JANE E.,M.B.,B.S.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "#1, left breast tissue", and consists of a breast excision (7 cm medial to\u000alateral, REMOVED_DATE cm posterior to anterior, REMOVED_DATE cm inferior to superior). The\u000aspecimen is received with a radiograph demonstrating two (2) wires and a clip\u000ain the specimen with a small area of microcalcification associated with one (1)\u000awire. The clipped area on the radiograph is close to the medial margin.\u000aThe specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation\u000aof margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior =\u000agreen; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. Sectioning the area containing the\u000aclip reveals the clip in a biopsy cavity (0.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The tissue is\u000aapproximately 90% fatty tissue and 10% fibrous tissue.No other lesions are\u000agrossly seen. The entire biopsy cavity and all fibrous tissue are submitted.\u000aMicro 1: left breast tissue, posterior margin, perpendicular margin, 2 frags,\u000aRSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  biospy cavity with clip site, medial, inferior, superior margin,\u000a4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 6: medial margin, perpendicular, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  fibrous tissue associated with second wire, with inferior,\u000alateral, posterior and superior margins, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  fibrous tissue with inferior, superior margins, 3 frags, ESS.\u000ajeb\u000aReports to: SHOJI, BRENT, T. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
