VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aBRODSKY, GILBERT, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by BRODSKY,GILBERT,M.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST, EXCISION WIRE-LOCLALIZATION FOR A CLIP:\u000aIN SITU CARCINOMA WITH MIXED FEATURES\u000aSYNOPSIS:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA - not present\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU - present (see NOTE)\u000aTypes - solid\u000aNuclear grade - intermediate\u000aCalcifications in DCIS - absent\u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - absent\u000aMicroinvasion (<0.1cm) - absent\u000aExtent of DCIS\u000aSize (max area in one block) - REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aNumber of blocks:total - 1:23 blocks\u000aFinal Margins (DCIS)\u000aNegative (>0.3 cm) - medial, lateral, superior, inferior,\u000aanterior, posterior\u000aOTHER FINDINGS\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia\u000aApocrine metaplasia\u000aCore biopsy site\u000aAJCC CLASSIFICATION (6th edition) - Tis pNx MX\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER/PR/HER-2) - pending\u000aLEFT BREAST, LATERAL SUPERIOR MARGIN:\u000aIN SITU CARCINOMA WITH MIXED FEATURES\u000aSYNOPSIS:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA - not present\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU - present (see NOTE)\u000aTypes - solid\u000aNuclear grade - intermediate\u000aCalcifications in DCIS - present\u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - present\u000aMicroinvasion (<0.1cm) - absent\u000aExtent of DCIS\u000aSize (max area in one block) - REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aNumber of blocks:total - 2:15 blocks\u000aFinal Margins (DCIS)\u000aNegative (>0.3 cm) - new lateral superior margin\u000aVery close (0.1-0.3 cm) - previous margin (blocks #25, #26)\u000aOTHER FINDINGS\u000aCore biopsy site\u000aApocrine metaplasia\u000aAJCC CLASSIFICATION (6th edition) - Tis pNx MX\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER/PR/HER-2) - pending\u000aNOTE:\u000aThe in situ tumor shows both ductal and lobular differentiation, but is best\u000aclassified as a ductal neoplasm.\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for DCIS (block 25):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) NEGATIVE (1+)\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000acarcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but\u000aonly a portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity\u000ain >10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: None given.\u000aOperation: Needle localized (L) breast biopsy.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: (L) breast cancer.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1. Left breast biopsy.\u000a#2. Lateral superior margin, stitch on most lateral and superior margin.\u000aRADIOLOGY REPORT:\u000aClip in specimen.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by CHEN,JEY-HSIN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received in two parts, each labeled with the patient's name and\u000aunit number.\u000aPart one, received in formalin, labeled "#1. Left breast biopsy", consists of a\u000abreast excision specimen (5.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with a pink/tan skin ellipse\u000a(2.5 x REMOVED_DATE cm). The specimen is received inked by the surgeon; however,\u000adistinct colors with the exception of green, could not be grossly discerned.\u000aThe specimen is re-oriented by the surgeon with a skin ellipse located at the\u000a3 o'clock surface (lateral), with tips directed superiorly and inferiorly. The\u000awire enters the specimen in the middle of the skin ellipse and is directed\u000asuperiomedially, with an accompanying mammogram demonstrating a clip at the\u000aedge of the specimen. Correlation with the mammogram reveals a scalloped area\u000anear the clip with a small focus of hemorrhage (0.5 cm). The specimen is\u000aserially sectioned along the axis of the wire from distal (medial) to proximal\u000a(skin, lateral) revealing breast tissue that is comprised of about 50% fatty\u000aand 50% yellow/tan firm lobulated tissue, which extends to an edge containing\u000aan area of hemorrhage in slices #4 and #5. The specimen is re-x-rayed and a\u000aclip cannot be identified. The gross specimen was reviewed with Dr. Susan\u000aLester. The specimen is entirely submitted.\u000aMicro 1: Slice #1, distal most (medial) section, perpendicular, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 2: Slice #2, portion corresponding to top half of specimen with wire\u000aper mammogram, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 3: Slice #2, portion corresponding to bottom half of specimen per\u000amammogram, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Slice #3, portion of specimen corresponding to top half of specimen\u000awith wire per mammogram, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Slice #3, portion of specimen corresponding to bottom half of\u000aspecimen per mammogram, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Slice #4, portion of specimen corresponding to top half of specimen\u000awith wire per mammogram, containing area of hemorrhage, 2 frags,\u000aESS.\u000aMicro 10: Slice #4, portion of specimen corresponding to bottom half of\u000aspecimen per mammogram, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Slice #5, portion of specimen corresponding to top half of\u000aspecimen with wire per mammogram, containing area of hemorrhage, 2\u000afrags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Slice #5, portion of specimen corresponding to bottom half of\u000aspecimen per mammogram, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Slice #6, portion of specimen corresponding to top half of\u000aspecimen with wire per mammogram, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 17: Slice #6,Portion of specimen corresponding to bottom half of\u000aspecimen per mammogram, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Slice #7, portion of specimen corresponding to top half of\u000aspecimen with wire per mammogram, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Slice #7, portion of specimen corresponding to bottom half of the\u000aspecimen per mammogram, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Slice #8, proximal most section including skin, perpendicular, 8\u000afrags, ESS.\u000aPart two, received fresh, labeled "#2. Lateral superior margin", is a\u000ayellow/tan fibroadipose tissue (3.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) oriented with a suture\u000amarking the new margin (lateral superior), inked yellow. The opposite surface\u000ais pink/brown, ragged, and firm and contains a focal area of hemorrhage (0.5\u000acm), which are inked orange. The specimen is serially sectioned revealing a\u000abreast tissue that is REMOVED_DATE % adipose tissue and REMOVED_DATE % yellow/tan firm\u000alobulated tissue, which extends to both the new and previous margins, and\u000acontains a focal area of brown/red hemorrhage. The specimen is received with\u000aan accompanying mammogram, without report, showing focal coarse calcifications.\u000aThe specimen is entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Serial sections with area of hemorrhage in blocks #24, 11 frags,\u000aESS.\u000ajhc\u000aReports to: SOYBEL, DAVID, IRA M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN\u000a[report_end]
