VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST MASTECTOMY - PARTIAL OR SIMPLE\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aCORSON, JOSEPH, M., M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by CORSON,JOSEPH M.,M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "RIGHT BREAST," MASTECTOMY (SKIN SPARING SIMPLE MASTECTOMY\u000aSPECIMEN):\u000aNo residual invasive carcinoma or carcinoma in situ is seen.\u000aOld biopsy site with fibrosis, chronic inflammation, fat necrosis and\u000aforeign body giant cell reaction.\u000aFibrocystic change.\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "CHEST NODULE":\u000aFibroadipose tissue with necrosis, peripheral nerve and skeletal muscle.\u000aNo tumor present.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 38 year old premenopausal female status post REMOVED_DATE  right partial\u000amastectomy and axillary dissectin showing REMOVED_DATE cm tumor, margin\u000apositive, REMOVED_DATE node positive for breast cancer.\u000aOperation: Right skin sparing mastectomy,\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Right mastectomy, skin is REMOVED_DATE o'clock to inframammary\u000afold.\u000aShort suture superior, long suture lateral.\u000a2. Right chest wall nodule.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by ZEMBOWICZ,ARTUR , M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in two parts, both labeled with the patient's\u000aname and number.\u000aThe first part, "right breast", consists of 350 gm skin sparing mastectomy\u000aspecimen (15 x 15 x 3 cm), oriented by short suture indicating superior margin\u000aand long suture indicating lateral margin, with a wedge shaped skin measuring 5\u000ax REMOVED_DATE cm, with areola measuring 3 cm and a nipple measuring 1 cm. The wedge\u000askin extends to inframammary fold in the area between REMOVED_DATE o'clock. Within\u000acenter of the skin wedge there is a REMOVED_DATE cm per secundeam healed surgical scar\u000asurrounded by a rim of bright red granulation tissue. REMOVED_DATE cm from the surgical\u000ascar there is a biopsy cavity (3 x 2 x 2 cm) with red\u005ctan nodular wall, which\u000acommunicates, with the deep surface of the specimen through REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm hole\u000ain the deep fascia Superiorly and anteriorly to the biopsy cavity there is a\u000anodule of firm tan breast tissue, bulging into the biopsy cavity and measuring\u000a2.5 x REMOVED_DATE x 3 cm, approaching to within REMOVED_DATE cm of the inked deep margin. The\u000aremainder of the breast tissue is grossly unremarkable and consists of\u000aapproximately 80% of adipose tissue.\u000aMicro 1, Nearest approach of wall biopsy cavity to deep resection margin,\u000aperpendicular, RSS, 1 f.\u000aMicro 2, Breast nodule, in relation to biopsy cavity, RSS, 1 F.\u000aMicro 3, Deep biopsy cavity wall, in the area of fascial discontinuity,\u000aRSS, 3 f.\u000aMicro 4, Biopsy cavity in relation to scar, RSS, 1 f.\u000aMicro 5, Nipple and areola, RSS, 1 f.\u000aMicro 6, Upper outer quadrant, RSS, 1 f.\u000aMicro 7, Lower outer quadrant, RSS, 1 f.\u000aMicro 8, Upper inner quadrant, RSS, 1 f.\u000aMicro 9, Lower inner quadrant, RSS, 1 f.\u000aMicro 10, Additional section of firm breast nodule associated with biopsy\u000acavity, RSS, 1 f.\u000aThe second part, "chest wall nodule", consists of a single fragment of\u000ayellow\u005ctan\u005cred soft tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000aMicro 11, Chest wall nodule, ESS, 1 f.\u000aMicros #12-21: Additional sections of biopsy cavity and surrounding breast\u000anodule in relation to deep margin, peripendicular, RSS, 10 frags.\u000aMicros #22-23: Biopsy cavity in relation to superficial breast tissue, RSS, 2\u000afrags.\u000aaz\u000aReports to: KAELIN, CAROLYN, MARY M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY - PARTIAL OR SIMPLE\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SOFT TISSUE BIOPSY\u000a[report_end]
