VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aWELCH, WILLIAM, ROBERT, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by WELCH,WILLIAM ROBERT,M.D.\u000a1) RIGHT BREAST, EXCISION WIRE-LOCALIZATION FOR CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aSYNOPSIS:\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU - present\u000aTypes - solid, cribriform, micropapillary\u000aNuclear grade - intermediate\u000aCalcifications in DCIS - present\u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - absent\u000aMicroinvasion (<0.1cm) - absent\u000aExtent of DCIS\u000aNumber of blocks:total - 6:11 blocks\u000aFinal Margins (DCIS)\u000aNegative (>0.3 cm) - lateral, anterior\u000aVery close (<0.1 cm) - superior #1 (focal), anterior #3 (focal)\u000amedial #5, 6 (multifocal), inferior #9,\u000alateral #1, 3 (multifocal), posterior\u000a#3 (focal)\u000aOTHER FINDINGS\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia\u000aCore biopsy site\u000aAJCC CLASSIFICATION (6th edition) Tis pREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID MX\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER/PR/HER-2) - pending\u000a2) RIGHT BREAST, MEDIAL SHAVE MARGIN:\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia.\u000aCysts and apocrine metaplasia.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: by RICHARDSON,ANDREA L.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for DCIS (block 1):\u000aEstrogen receptor - POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor - POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) - POSITIVE (2+)\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000ainvasive carcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but\u000aonly a portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity\u000ain >10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 44-year-old female status post REMOVED_DATE  right breast core biopsy for\u000aevaluation of calcifications demonstrating atypical ductal\u000ahyperplasia.\u000aOperation: Right breast wire localization excision.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal right mammogram.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Right breast tissue, suture marks long lateral, short\u000asuperior, whipstitch on deep margin.\u000a2. Right medial shave margin, whipstitch on new margin.\u000aSpecimen #1: Ca++ in specimen. E.P. Frost.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by BENNETT,MICHAEL W.,M.B.,B.C.H\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart one, labeled "#1, right breast tissue, suture marks long lateral, short\u000asuperior, whipstitch on deep margin", is a portion of fibrofatty tissue which\u000ameasures REMOVED_DATE cm from inferior to superior x REMOVED_DATE cm from medial to lateral x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm from anterior to posterior. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol\u000afor the evaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior =\u000ared; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. A wire localizing\u000aneedle enters the specimen from the anterior surface and exits the specimen\u000aposteriorly. Approximately 90% of the specimen consists of white fibrous\u000atissue, which extends to all margins. The center of the specimen has a cyst,\u000awhich measures REMOVED_DATE cm in maximum dimension and extends to within REMOVED_DATE cm of the\u000aanterior margin.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  entire specimen from superior to inferior, 15 frags, ESS.\u000aPart two, labeled "#2, right medial shave margin", consists of a portion of\u000afibrofatty tissue, which measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The specimen has been\u000amarked by a suture as indicated on the form 86. This surface is inked black,\u000athe opposite surface is inked orange. The specimen consists of 90% of white\u000afibrotic tissue, which extends to both margins. The specimen is serially\u000asectioned and entirely submitted for histological examination.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  entire specimen, 7 frags, ESS.\u000amwb\u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN\u000a[report_end]
