VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST MASTECTOMY W/REGIONAL LYMPH NODES\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aNOSE, VANIA, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by NOSE,VANIA,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST, MASTECTOMY AND AXILLARY NODE DISSECTION:\u000aEXTENSIVE RESIDUAL INVASIVE CARCINOMA, present predominantly as\u000alymphovascular invasion, involving (at least) an 8 cm central area\u000aof the breast (multiple foci in eleven (11) slides).\u000aThe largest area of stromal invasion is REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000aNo definite DCIS is seen.\u000aNo dermal lymphatic invasion is seen.\u000aThe deep margin is free of carcinoma.\u000aMETASTATIC CARCINOMA to ten of eleven (10:11) lymph nodes, the\u000alargest metastatic focus measures REMOVED_DATE cm; no extranodal extension\u000ais seen.\u000aNOTE:\u000aThe residual carcinoma in the breast and lymph nodes appears viable. Mitoses\u000aare present. Immunoperoxidase studies will be performed and reported in an\u000aaddendum.\u000aDr. Susan Lester concurs.\u000a(Clinical History: A 48-year-old woman presently with inflammatory carcinoma,\u000as/p chemotherapy with resolution of skin changes but with a palpable mass.)\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for invasive carcinoma and intralymphatic carcinoma\u000a(block 9):\u000aEstrogen receptor NEGATIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor NEGATIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) NEGATIVE (0)\u000aNote: Normal epithelial cells are appropriately immunoreactive for estrogen\u000aand progesterone receptors.\u000aThe patient's pre-treatment carcinoma was also reported to be negative for ER,\u000aPR, and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu.\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000acarcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but\u000aonly a portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity\u000ain >10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Status post neoadjuvant chemo, left inflammatory breast cancer.\u000aOperation: Left modified radical mastectomy.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast cancer.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Left breast, axillary contents -\u000aShort silk stitch = skin margin at 12:00,\u000aLong silk stitch = lateral axilla tail\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by FIRESTEIN,RON,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart 1, "Left breast and axillary contents - short stitch = skin margin at\u000a12:00, long stitch = lateral axillary tail", consists of a 598 gm left modified\u000aradical mastectomy specimen, consisting of: left breast (18.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm),\u000askin ellipse (14.5 x REMOVED_DATE cm), areola (3.5 x REMOVED_DATE cm), crusted, everted nipple\u000a(1.3 cm in diameter), axillary tail (10.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), and two sutures\u000a(short - 12:00 and long - axillary tail). There is no evidence of hyperemic\u000achange or previous biopsy site on the skin. Deep fascial margin is inked black\u000aand the specimen is serially sectioned medial to lateral, revealing a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000ax REMOVED_DATE cm, tan/white, firm, ill-defined lesion within the central portion of the\u000abreast, REMOVED_DATE cm from the deep margin and REMOVED_DATE cm deep to the nipple. Contiguous\u000awith the lesion is an area of dense, tan/white, fibrous tissue (8.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm - overall dimension) with areas of cystic change and yellow/tan, pasty\u000asubstance exuding from the probably duct (? necrosis). The remaining breast\u000astroma consists of predominantly yellow/tan, lobulated fat and strands of\u000atan/white fibrostroma. Multiple tan, rubbery lymph nodes (ranging from REMOVED_DATE to\u000a2.0 cm in greatest dimension) are identified within the axillary tail. The\u000afocally crusted nipple is taken en face and sectioned perpendicular to the\u000aduct.\u000aMicro 1: Nipple (perpendicular to duct), 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 2: Nipple (proximal en face cross-section), 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Firm, central breast mass in relationship to adjacent skin and\u000anipple, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Deep margin nearest mass, 2 frags total, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Dense, focally cystic and necrotic breast tissue adjacent to mass\u000a(sequentially from medial to lateral), 3 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 10: Most lateral/superior fibrous area, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 11: Most medial/superior aspect of fibrous area, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 12: Most medial/inferior aspect of fibrous area, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 13: Lateral/inferiormost aspect of fibrous area, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Single bisected lymph node, 2 frags total, ESS.\u000aMicro 16: Six single whole lymph node candidates, six frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 17: Two bisected lymph nodes (one lymph node inked blue), 4 frags\u000atotal, ESS.\u000aMicro 18: Single bisected lymph node, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 19: Single bisected lymph node, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aPart 2, "Additional axillary contents", consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aaggregate of yellow/tan, lobulated fat, within which two tan lymph nodes are\u000aidentified (0.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm).\u000aMicro 20: Single bisected lymph node, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 21: Single bisected lymph node, 2 frags, ESS\u000adfi\u000aReports to: LESNIKOSKI, BETH-ANN M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY W/REGIONAL LYMPH NODES\u000a[report_end]
