TE M-L and REMOVED_DATE S-I) with adjacent\u000aclip. The distance of mass to margins is as follows: Lateral-0.1 cm,\u000aposterior-0.4 cm, inferior-0.2 cm, medial-0.4 cm, anterior-0.5 cm and\u000asuperior-4.0 cm. The specimen is entirely submitted for histological review.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Entire specimen submitted inferior to superior, slices correspond\u000ato cassette number, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000ath/ag\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jeffrey F Krane M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a9/20/2006\u000a[report_end]
