VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final Type: Surgical Pathology Pathology Report: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID OPERATION DATE: 06 REMOVED_MONTH 99 ACCESSIONED ON: 06 REMOVED_MONTH 99 at 12:01 CLINICAL DATA: 35 year old with core biopsy showing right breast cancer. =============================================================================== *** FINAL DIAGNOSIS *** BREAST (RIGHT), EXCISIONAL BIOPSY: INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA. SEE TABLE BELOW. DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, INTERMEDIATE GRADE, HARBORING MICROCALCIFICATIONS. BREAST (RIGHT, ADDITIONAL DEEP MARGIN), BIOPSY: ADIPOSE TISSUE; THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. BREAST (RIGHT, ADDITIONAL MEDIAL MARGIN), BIOPSY: THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. BREAST (RIGHT, FINAL SHAVED MARGIN), BIOPSY: SCLEROSIS; THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. LYMPH NODE (SENTINEL, LEVEL 1), BIOPSY FOR FROZEN SECTION: THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY; THE FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS IS CONFIRMED. LYMPH NODE (SENTINEL, LEVEL 2), BIOPSY FOR FROZEN SECTION: METASTATIC DUCTAL CARCINOMA; REMOVED_DATE CM FOCUS WITHIN A REMOVED_DATE CM NODE, WIHTOUT EXTRACAPSULAR SPREAD; THE FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS IS CONFIRMED. LYMPH NODES (RIGHT AXILLARY CONTENTS), REGIONAL DISSECTION: THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 2 OF 2 NODES. LYMPH NODE (ADDITIONAL AXILLARY TISSUE), BIOPSY: THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY (ONE NODE). TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS INVASIVE CARCINOMA Tumor size: REMOVED_DATE X REMOVED_DATE X REMOVED_DATE cm. Grade: 2 Lymphatic vessel invasion: Not identified. Blood vessel invasion: Not identified. Margin of invasive carcinoma: The distances to all margins measure REMOVED_DATE cm or greater. Location of ductal carcinoma in-situ: Within the region of the mass. Margin of ductal carcinoma in-situ: The distances to all margins measure REMOVED_DATE cm or greater. Stains for receptors: Requested. Diagnosis by: John H. Eichhorn, M.D. Signed On: 09 REMOVED_MONTH 99 at 19:20 =============================================================================== *** BREAST CANCER IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY ADDENDUM Addendum *** RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast (Right): The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein. The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein. The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER-2/c-erbB-2. See note. Note: These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital. They have not been cleared or approved by the U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA). The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary; this laboratory has established and verified the test's accuracy and precision. Added by: Frederick Carl Koerner, M.D. Signed On: 19 REMOVED_MONTH 99 at 08:23 GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "excision right breast cancer" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 cm fatty tissue, with skin of 2 x .5 cm. The specimen is oriented with short stitch designating superior margin, long stitch designating lateral margin. The specimen is inked black and medial margin overinked with green, posterior margin overinked with yellow. The specimen is sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x 2 x REMOVED_DATE cm yellow-tan, firm, rubbery and hemorrhagic area with irregular border. The mass presented within .1 cm to the closest inferior and medial margins. Representative sections are submitted in cassettes A through E. Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "additional deep margin" are two pieces of fibroadipose tissue fragment of 2 x 1 x .5 cm and .5 x .5 cm, inked and dissected, submitted entirely in cassette F. Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, "additional medial margin #3" is a REMOVED_DATE x 2 x .5 cm fibrous breast tissue fragment, inked and entirely submitted in cassettes G and H. Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "final shaved margin" is a tissue aggregate of 4 x 2 x 1 cm breast fragment, inked and entirely submitted in cassettes I through K. Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "right axillary contents" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm fibrofatty tissue fragments. The specimen is dissected and reveals three lymph nodes ranging from .2 to REMOVED_DATE cm, bisected and submitted in cassette L. Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "additional axillary tissue #1" is a .5 x .5 x .5 cm fatty fibrotic tissue, entirely submitted in cassette M. Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "sentinel nodes #1" is a 2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm piece of fibroadipose tissue containing a .9 x .5 x .3 cm lymph node. Entirely frozen as FX #1, now entirely submitted in cassette N. Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "sentinel node #2" is a REMOVED_DATE x .8 x .5 cm piece of fibroadipose tissue containing a .8 cm lymph node. All frozen as FX #2, now in entirely submitted in cassette O. Resident: MANCONG ZHANG, MD *** INTRA-OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS *** FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS #1: SENTINEL NODE, LEVEL 1: NEGATIVE FOR CARCINOMA. FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS #2: SENTINEL NODE, LEVEL 2: POSITIVE FOR METASTATIC CARCINOMA. O.R. Resident: MONICA da SILVA NUNES, MD O.R. Diagnosis by: Suzanne B. Keel, M.D. =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT - REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID REPORTS TO: Barbara Lynn Smith, M.D. Simon Powell, M.D. W B Jerry Younger, M.D. PART A: LYMPH NODE (SENTINEL, LEVEL 1), BIOPSY PART B: LYMPH NODE (SENTINEL, LEVEL 2), BIOPSY PART C: BREAST (RIGHT, ADDITIONAL DEEP MARGIN), BIOPSY PART D: LYMPH NODE (ADDITIONAL AXILLARY TISSUE), EXCISION PART E: LYMPH NODES (RIGHT AXILLA), REGIONAL DISSECTION PART F: BREAST (RIGHT, ADDITIONAL MEDIAL MARGIN), BIOPSY PART G: BREAST (RIGHT, FINAL SHAVED MARGIN), BIOPSY\u000a[report_end]
