VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Amend/Addenda\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000a********** Addended Report ***********\u000aResident: Kremena V. Star, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Jason L Hornick, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. LEFT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED BIOPSY:\u000aCellular fibroepithelial neoplasm, most consistent with low grade\u000aphyllodes tumor (0.7 cm).\u000aMitoses number <1 per 10 HPF.\u000aFocal stromal overgrowth is present.\u000aFocal infiltration of adipose tissue is present.\u000aTumor involves the medial margin.\u000aThe remaining margins are negative for tumor.\u000aImmunohistochemistry performed at BWH demonstrates the following\u000astaining profile in lesional cells:\u000aPositive - REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, desmin (focal)\u000aThe immunohistochemical profile supports the above diagnosis.\u000aThe immunoperoxidase, immunofluorescence and in-situ hybridization tests\u000aperformed at Brigham and Women's Hospital were developed and their performance\u000acharacteristics determined by the Immunohistochemistry Laboratories in the\u000aDepartment of Pathology at BWH. They have not been cleared or approved by the\u000aU.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA). The FDA has determined that such\u000aclearance or approval is not necessary.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 43 year old premenopausal female whose REMOVED_DATE bilateral mammogram\u000asupplemented with L breast U/S, demonstrates a 12:30 L breast axis REMOVED_DATE cm mass.\u000a5/20/09 core biopsy revealed a fibroepithelial lesion. Excision is\u000arecommended.\u000aOperation: L breast wire localized biopsy.\u000aOperative Findings: Not provided.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal L mammogram.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) left breast tissue - short/superior, long stitch/lateral, whipstitch/deep\u000amargin.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in one part, labeled with the patient's name,\u000aunit number, and "left breast", and consists of an irregular fragment of\u000afibroadipose tissue (4.5 cm A-P x REMOVED_DATE S-I x REMOVED_DATE cm M-L) with a short suture\u000adesignating superior, a long suture designating lateral, and a whip-stitch\u000adesignating deep per surgeon. The specimen is received with a needle\u000alocalization wire, which is loosely adherent to the inferolateral aspect of the\u000aspecimen. The specimen exhibits a defect (4.0 x REMOVED_DATE cm) on the anterior aspect\u000aof the specimen. The specimen is serially sectioned to exhibit a 30% white\u000afibrous tissue to 70% yellow lobulated adipose tissue. No masses or lesions\u000acan be grossly appreciated. The specimen is submitted in its entirety.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Perpendicular superior margin, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Body, sequentially submitted from superior to inferior, multi\u000afrags total, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Perpendicular inferior margin, multi frags total, ESS.\u000ajc/lp\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jason L Hornick M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000aFriday REMOVED_MONTH 16, 2009 at 12:40:09PM\u000aADDENDUM:\u000aThe tumor is >5 mm from the remaining margins.\u000aAddendum #1 by Jason L Hornick M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on Friday\u000aREMOVED_MONTH 16, 2009 at 03:23:26PM\u000aADDENDUM:\u000aThe tumor is >1 cm from the remaining margins.\u000aAddendum #2 by Jason L Hornick M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000aWednesday REMOVED_MONTH 28, 2009 at 10:32:58AM\u000a[report_end]
