green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange (new margin). The\u000aspecimen is serially sectioned from superior to inferior perpendicular to the\u000anew margin to reveal approximately 50% dense fibrous scar tissue and 50% yellow\u000alobulated adipose tissue. The specimen is entirely submitted from superior to\u000ainferior.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Perpendicular superior margin, multi frags each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Body of specimen, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Perpendicular inferior margin, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: 1071.\u000aAWE/ajb\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Xiaohua Qian M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000aWednesday REMOVED_MONTH 13, 2010 at 02:36:22PM\u000a[report_end]
