VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast core needle biopsy\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: DIANNE GEORGIAN-SMITH M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: George Lin, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Susan Lester, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aLEFT BREAST, UPPER OUTER, 2:30, 14 G ULTRASOUND GUIDED CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES AN\u000aIRREGULAR REMOVED_DATE CM MASS WITH CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aPAPILLARY CARCINOMA is present associated with extensive mucin, with\u000aextravasation, measuring at least REMOVED_DATE cm in size in this limited specimen\u000a(additional levels examined) (see note). An immunoperoxidase study for p63\u000aconfirms the absence of myoepithelial cells in the carcinoma.\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with\u000athe following results for the papillary carcinoma (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor NEGATIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) EQUIVOCAL (2+)\u000aNormal epithelial cells are appropriately immunoreactive for estrogen\u000aand progesterone receptors.\u000aNote: Small fragments of this papillary carcinoma are present. It is not\u000apossible to evaluate this lesion for stromal invasion in this limited specimen.\u000aThe carcinoma would be classified best after excision (i.e. as in situ\u000acarcinoma, invasive carcinoma, or encapsulated papillary carcinoma).\u000aCalcifications are not seen in this limited specimen.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHISTORY: 56 year old woman with 1 cm irregular mass in the LUOQ associated\u000awith calcs. Differential diagnosis: highly suspicious for carcinoma.\u000aBREAST IMAGING FINDING:\u000a1. Left: 1 cm, calcifications and irregular mass.\u000aLOCATION:\u000a1. Left: 2:30, REMOVED_DATE cm from nipple.\u000aTYPE OF CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY:\u000a1. 14 G Ultrasound\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000a1. 14 G Ultrasound in formalin - Pink cassette.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aOne part received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name and medical\u000arecord number only, and consists of a pink cassette containing multiple\u000acylindrical fibrofatty soft tissues (0.7 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which is submitted in\u000atoto.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Contents of pink cassette, multi frags, ESS.\u000aJenC/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aImmunohistochemical studies for estrogen receptor, progesterone receptor, and\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu were evaluated by manual morphometric analysis using the following\u000acriteria:\u000aHormone receptor analysis:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low > 0% - < 10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not\u000ayet been determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10%\u000aof tumor cells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor\u000acells but only a portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aEquivocal (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity in >30% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aExternal controls are evaluated and show appropriate immunoreactivity.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for\u000ainvestigational use only.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000aWednesday REMOVED_MONTH 02, 2009 at 03:38:20PM\u000a[report_end]
