VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, mastectomy with regional lymph nodes\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: CHANDRAJIT P. RAUT M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-05-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Kevin B Long, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Alessandra F Nascimento, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "LEFT BREAST" (735 g):\u000aHIGH GRADE ANGIOSARCOMA, likely radiation-associated, present as single nodule\u000a(1 cm) (see NOTE).\u000aFocal necrosis is identified.\u000aMitoses number up to 16 per 10 HPF.\u000aResection margins are negative for tumor.\u000aTumor is at least REMOVED_DATE cm from the closest margins of resection (lateral and\u000adeep).\u000aSkin with scarring, dermal fibrosis and vascular ectasia.\u000aSkeletal muscle (deep/posterior margin) with no tumor present.\u000aCalcifications associated with benign breast epithelium.\u000aNo residual carcinoma present.\u000aNOTE: There is one well-defined nodule of high-grade angiosarcoma and several\u000asmall foci (measuring REMOVED_DATE  cm) of low-grade angiosarcoma present within breast\u000aparenchyma. These foci are associated with areas of ill-defined dense fibrosis\u000aand hemosiderin deposition, consistent with treatment effect. Skin and skeletal\u000amuscle involvement are not present.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Left breast angiosarcoma.\u000aOperation: Radical left mastectomy, left latissimus dorsi flap reconstruction.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast angiosarcoma.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000a#1 - left breast (short/superior, long/lateral) --> FS.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient?s name, unit number,\u000aand "#1 - left breast", and consists of a 735 gram simple mastectomy specimen\u000a(19.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), oriented by two sutures placed by the surgeon\u000a(short=superior aspect, long=lateral aspect). There is an overlying skin\u000aellipse (15.0 x REMOVED_DATE cm) with an unremarkable nipple (0.7 cm). Two well healed\u000asurgical scars are present: one curvilinear scar REMOVED_DATE cm lateral to nipple (5.0\u000acm in length) and one REMOVED_DATE cm linear scar in the upper/outer quadrant.\u000aOtherwise, the skin is unremarkable; no cutaneous lesions are identified. The\u000adeep margin is composed of a smooth fascial plane and underlying skeletal\u000amuscle (14.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which is inked black. The anterior, superior,\u000amedial, lateral and inferior margins are composed of unremarkable fibroadipose\u000atissue and inked by the pathologist according to the pathology protocol for the\u000aevaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red;\u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. The breast parenchyma is\u000acomposed of yellow adipose tissue associated with several ill-defined areas of\u000afibrosis and fibrous stranding (measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). Within the\u000afibrous tissue there is a well-defined, hemorrhagic nodule measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000ax REMOVED_DATE cm. This nodule is REMOVED_DATE cm from the closest resection margins (lateral and\u000adeep/posterior). The remaining ill defined fibrous breast parenchyma is REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom the posterior, REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom the anterior, REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior\u000amargins. A representative section of the mass was submitted for cytogenetics.\u000aA gross photograph was taken of the specimen.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: tumor to skin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID+REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: tumor to posterior margin, multiple frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: lateral margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: medial margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: superior margin and anterior margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: inferior margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: additional tumor, multiple frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: additional skin and subcutis, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: additional skeletal muscle, mult frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: additional skin, mult frags, RSS.\u000aKEL/lp\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Paula C Abreu-e-Lima M.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aPrelim Dx Release by Paula C Abreu-e-Lima M.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aNo Action - Prelim Sent by Alessandra F Nascimento M.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Alessandra F Nascimento M.D., Electronically signed on\u000a8/19/2005\u000a[report_end]
