VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aCORSON, JOSEPH, M., M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by CORSON,JOSEPH M.,M.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST, RE-EXCISION:\u000aRESIDUAL DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN-SITU\u000aSYNOPSIS:\u000aRESIDUAL DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aTypes - cribriform, papillary\u000aNuclear grade - low to intermediate (involving two (2)\u000asmall ducts within area of previous\u000abiopsy site\u000aCalcifications in DCIS - absent\u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - absent\u000aMicroinvasion (<0.1cm) - absent\u000aExtent of DCIS\u000anumber of blocks/total - REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Margins (DCIS)\u000aclose (0.1-0.3 cm) - focally at the (true) superior margin\u000a(block 11)\u000aOTHER FINDINGS\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia\u000aSclerosing adenosis\u000aCysts\u000aCalcifications in benign epithelium\u000aBiopsy site\u000aSkin with scar\u000aNOTE:\u000aThis case was reviewed by Dr. Andrea Richardson, who concurs.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: DCIS with close margins.\u000aOperation: Left breast re-excision tumor site.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Ductal carcinoma in situ.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Left breast, re-excision tissue, short stitch = superior,\u000along = lateral.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by HIRSCH,MICHELLE S.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "#1, left breast re-excision tissue", consists of a single oriented\u000afragment of yellow-tan fibroadipose tissue (7.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with an\u000aoverlying skin ellipse (5.3 x REMOVED_DATE cm). The specimen is received with short and\u000along sutures which represent the superior and lateral margins, respectively.\u000aThe specimen is inked, by the surgeon, per pathology protocol for the\u000aevaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red;\u000ainferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange.\u000aNote: It was indicated by the surgeon that red ink was applied to the "entire\u000aouter arc of tissue" and green inke was applied "along the inner arc". It is\u000ainterpreted by the pathologist that red and green ink were applied to lateral\u000aportions of the specimen, in addition to superior and inferior portions,\u000arespectively. The specimen is submitted as received inked by the surgeon.\u000aA portion of a surgical scar (2.3 cm in length) is identified at the radial\u000amargin of the skin ellipse on the inferior surface. Upon excising the\u000aspecimen, there is a stellate area of fibrous tissue (2.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm)\u000aidentified in the lateral portion of the specimen. Multiple small foci (up to\u000a0.2 cm in greatest dimension) are grossly suspicious for residual carcinoma.\u000aThe fibrous tissue is grossly present at the lateral margin and extends to\u000awithin REMOVED_DATE cm of the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of\u000athe superior/lateral margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the true superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the\u000atrue inferior margin and greater than REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin. The\u000aremainder of the breast parenchyma is composed of yellow-tan fibroadipose\u000atissue and is grossly unremarkable. Fibrous tissue in areas grossly suspicious\u000afor carcinoma are entirely submitted. Additional representative sections of\u000athe remaining breast parenchyma are also submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  left breast with true lateral margins, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  left breast with superior/lateral, inferior/lateral, and deep\u000amargins, 7 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  left breast with true superior, true inferior and deep margins,\u000a5 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  left breast with medial margin, multi frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  left breast with true superior and deep margins, 6 frags, RSS.\u000amsh\u000aReports to: CHRISTIAN, ROGER, L. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
