VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast core needle biopsy\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: DIANNE GEORGIAN-SMITH M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: George Lin, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Susan Lester, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, 14 G ULTRASOUND GUIDED CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR A PALPABLE REMOVED_DATE CM\u000aMICROLOBULATED SUBAREOLAR NODULE:\u000aMultiple cores with large ducts and dense breast tissue (additional\u000alevels examined).\u000aNote: Specific histologic features of a mass forming lesion are not\u000aseen. Radiologic correlation is suggested to ensure the biopsy is\u000arepresentative of the targeted lesion.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHISTORY: 77 year old with history of melanoma in 2008 (s/p sentinel node\u000abiopsies of right axilla and inguinal region) now with new right subareolar\u000anodule. Differential diagnosis: gynecomastia, metastatic melanoma, breast\u000acancer. Also has enlarged right axillary lymph nodes.\u000aBREAST IMAGING FINDING:\u000a1. Right: REMOVED_DATE cm, palpable circumscribed/lobulated mass.\u000aLOCATION:\u000a1. Right: subareolar.\u000aTYPE OF CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY:\u000a1. 14 G Ultrasound\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000a1. 14 G Ultrasound - Green cassette. In formalin at 10:20 am.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, in one part, labeled with the patient's\u000aname, unit number, and "right breast", consists of a green cassette labeled\u000a"right", which contains multiple irregular tan-pink to yellow fibrofatty\u000atissues (1.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate), which are submitted in toto.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Tissues in green cassette labeled right, multi frags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000almc/ag\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000aThursday REMOVED_MONTH 17, 2009 at 03:24:13PM\u000a[report_end]
