VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aNUCCI, MARISA, ROSE, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by NUCCI,MARISA ROSE,M.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISIONAL BIOPSY:\u000aFlorid epithelial hyperplasia, apocrine metaplasia and cyst formation.\u000aApocrine adenosis.\u000aMicrocalcifications associated with benign epithelium.\u000aMargins examined microscopically.\u000a(Levels examined).\u000aCase reviewed with Dr. J. Connelly, who concurs.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Hx of ADH on core bx REMOVED_DATE  at BWH in complex sclerosing lesion, left\u000abreast.\u000aOperation: Left wire loc.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal left mammogram.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Left breast tissue, short superior, long lateral.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Clip is in specimen. D. Smith, MD\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by PADERA,ROBERT F.,JR.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in one part, labeled with the patient's name and\u000amedical record number and the description "#1 left wire loc breast biopsy".\u000aThe specimen consists of a 41-gram, breast wire localization specimen measuring\u000a5.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The specimen is received with a wire in place. The\u000aspecimen is received with two orienting sutures. The double short suture\u000aindicates superior and the double long suture indicates lateral. The specimen\u000ais inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior =\u000ablack; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow;\u000amedial = orange. The breast is serially sectioned to reveal a clip within an\u000aarea of fibrous tissue measuring approximately REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm that is\u000alocated REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE \u000acm from the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000amedial margin and REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin. The clip is removed. In\u000aaddition, a second area of yellow, firm tissue suspicious for fat necrosis is\u000apresent measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The area of the clip and this yellow\u000aarea are submitted in their entirety. Representative sections of other margins\u000aare submitted for histologic evaluation. Approximately 50% of the breast\u000atissue is submitted for histologic evaluation.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  area of clip, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  area of fat necrosis, ESS.\u000aMicro 10: posterior margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 11: medial margin, 3 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 12: lateral margin, 4 frags, RSS.\u000aReports to: CARTER, KATHARINE M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
