VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aCORSON, JOSEPH, M., M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by CORSON,JOSEPH M.,M.D.\u000aRIGHT BREAST BIOPSY, WIRE LOCALIZATION FRO CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA WITH FEATURES OF BOTH DUCTAL AND LOBULAR CARCINOMA,\u000a1.1 cm. (SEE NOTE).\u000aThe carcinoma is moderate-poorly differentiated (modified Bloom Richardson\u000aGrade II-III/III).\u000aNo definite lymphatic or vascular invasion seen.\u000aThe margins are free of invasive carcinoma, closest margin is medial\u000a(within REMOVED_DATE cm).\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, solid, intermediate grade, is present in\u000afour (4) of six (6) blocks (slides 3,4,5,6), with pagetoid spread\u000aalong ducts and cancerization of lobules. (EIC negative).\u000aMicrocalcifications and necrosis are associated with DCIS.\u000aDCIS is at and within REMOVED_DATE cm, of the inked resection margins, (inferior,\u000aposterior).\u000aBiopsy site with repair reaction.\u000aMicrocalcifications are associated with benign epithelium and stroma.\u000aNOTE: Note: Immunohistochemical analysis for estrogen receptors, progesterone\u000areceptors, and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu will be performed and reported in an addendum.\u000aThis carcinoma would be classified as at least AJCC REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDc pNx MX.\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: by CONNOLLY,JAMES L.,M.D.\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for invasive carcinoma (block 5):\u000aEstrogen receptor positive\u000aProgesterone receptor positive - low\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) negative (0)\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000ainvasive carcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but\u000aonly a portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity\u000ain >10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 52 year old female with history of exogenous hormones. Right breast\u000acore biopsy REMOVED_DATE  showed focal atypical ductal hyperplasia.\u000aOperation: Right breast wire localization biopsy.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1, right breast tissue (short suture superior, long suture\u000alateral, whipstitch on deep margin).\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by HORNICK,JASON L.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000aCalcifications are seen in specimen.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in one part, labeled with the patient's name,\u000aunit number and "right breast tissue", and consists of a wire localized breast\u000aexcisional biopsy specimen (4 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), with a localization wire in\u000aplace, and three orienting sutures (short suture superior, long suture lateral\u000aand whipstitch on deep margin). The specimen is inked in six colors:\u000ablack=posterior, blue=anterior, yellow=lateral, orange=medial, red=superior,\u000aand green=inferior. There are no areas grossly suspicious for invasive\u000acarcinoma. The specimen is entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  breast, 12 frag., ESS.\u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
