VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST MASTECTOMY W/REGIONAL LYMPH NODES\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aWEINSTEIN, MICHAEL, H., M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by WEINSTEIN,MICHAEL H.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000a1. RIGHT BREAST, MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY AND AXILLARY LYMPH NODE\u000aDISSECTION:\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, micropapillary type, low nuclear grade, is\u000apresent in a single focus near the recent biopsy site (block 2).\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia.\u000aNo residual invasive tumor is identified.\u000aFibrocystic changes with microcysts, apocrine metaplasia, and epithelial\u000ahyperplasia.\u000aBiopsy site with repair reaction.\u000aSkin with cicatrix.\u000aNipple with no significant pathologic change.\u000aTen (10) lymph nodes negative for tumor.\u000a2. AXILLARY CONTENTS, LYMPH NODE BIOPSY:\u000aOne (1) lymph node negative for tumor.\u000a3. BREAST IMPLANT:\u000aGross diagnosis only.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 52-year-old female with history of exogenous hormones. Right core\u000abiopsy REMOVED_DATE showed atypical hyperplasia. REMOVED_DATE  right wire\u000alocalized biopsy showed invasive with ductal and lobular features.\u000aPoorly differentiated BR II-III/III carcinoma. No definite\u000aLVI, DCIS with pagetoid spread along ducts and cancerization of\u000alobules.\u000aOperation: Right modified radical mastectomy.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Right breast tissue, short suture superior, long suture\u000alateral. Bowtie on level I nodes.\u000a2. Axillary contents.\u000a3. Implant gross only.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by QIAN,XIAOHUA,M.D,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in three parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart one, labeled "Right breast", consists of a 482 gram, right modified\u000aradical mastectomy specimen (18.5 x 20 x REMOVED_DATE cm) with a white/tan skin ellipse\u000a(10.2 x REMOVED_DATE cm) and attached axillary tail (10 x 8 x 4 cm). There is a REMOVED_DATE cm\u000awell-healed surgical scar, REMOVED_DATE cm superior from the unremarkable REMOVED_DATE cm nipple.\u000aIn the upper outer quadrant, REMOVED_DATE cm from the surgical skin scar, there is a\u000abiopsy cavity (1.2 cm in diameter), which is REMOVED_DATE cm from the deep margin.\u000aInferior and laterally associated with the biopsy cavity is a white firm area\u000a(4.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which is REMOVED_DATE cm from the closest deep margin. The\u000aremainder of the breast parenchyma is predominantly yellow/tan adipose tissue.\u000aThere are nine (9) axillary lymph nodes found, with the largest measuring REMOVED_DATE \u000acm in greatest dimension. There is no lymph nodes found at or close to the\u000aarea with a bowtie suture.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  biopsy cavity, lateral aspect with closest deep margin, 2 frags,\u000aRSS.\u000aMicro 3: biopsy cavity, inferior aspect with associated fibrous tissue,\u000a1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 4: biopsy cavity anterior and superior aspect, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 5: biopsy cavity with medial aspect, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 6: fibrotic tissue, inferiorly associated with biopsy cavity,\u000awith closest deep margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 7: upper outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 8: lower outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 9: upper inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 10: lower inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 11: skin scar with deep biopsy cavity, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 12: nipple, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  two largest lymph nodes, bisected, 1 per cassettes, ESS.\u000aMicro 15: two bisected lymph nodes, inked in different colors, 4 frags,\u000aESS.\u000aMicro 16: 6 lymph nodes, ESS.\u000aPart two, labeled "Right axillary contents", consists of a single lymph node,\u000ameasuring REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest dimension, which is bisected and entirely\u000abisected.\u000aMicro 17: 1 axillary lymph node, ESS.\u000aPart three is an ovoid implant with a smooth dry surface and viscous\u000atranslucent contents (15 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). No gross ruptures, adherent tissue\u000aor identifying markers are present. Photographs are taken.\u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY W/REGIONAL LYMPH NODES\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST IMPLANT\u000a[report_end]
