VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID:REMOVED_CASE_ID Report Status: Signed\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aADDENDUM REPORT\u000aAddendum #2 Entered: REMOVED_DATE -0932\u000a*** ADDITIONAL DIAGNOSTIC INFORMATION ***\u000aThis report contains an addendum to the original for the purpose of providing\u000aadditional diagnostic information. The original diagnosis is unchanged.\u000aFluorescence in situ hybridization (FISH) with probes for REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu performed at\u000aMayo Medical Laboratories on block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID reveals the following results for the\u000ainfiltrating carcinoma:\u000aThe specimen showed evidence of REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu gene amplification.\u000aAddeundum Signed Electronically Signed SAMPSON,RICHARD J. M.D. REMOVED_DATE \u000aAddendum #1 Entered: REMOVED_DATE -1420\u000a*** ADDITIONAL DIAGNOSTIC INFORMATION ***\u000aThis report contains an addendum to the original for the purpose of providing\u000aadditional diagnostic information. The original diagnosis is unchanged.\u000aImmunohistochemical studies performed on formalin-fixed, paraffin-embedded\u000ablock REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID reveal the following results for the infiltrating carcinoma:\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID): 2+ staining. Further evaluation by fluorescence in\u000asitu hybridization (FISH) method will be performed\u000aand results reported in an addendum to follow.\u000a(Antibody: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. Detection system: avidin-biotin complex)\u000aAddeundum Signed Electronically Signed SAMPSON,RICHARD J. M.D. REMOVED_DATE \u000aDIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. Left axillary sentinel lymph nodes (3):\u000aThree lymph nodes, no tumor seen.\u000aB. Left axillary lymph node, biopsies (2):\u000aNo tumor seen in two lymph nodes.\u000aC. Left breast, excision:\u000aModerately differentiated infiltrating duct carcinoma (1.2 cm.) with\u000asmaller separate foci.\u000aDuctal carcinoma in situ, solid with necrosis, grade REMOVED_DATE \u000aD. Superior lateral margin of left breast, excision:\u000aModerately differentiated infiltrating duct carcinoma (0.2 cm.) focally\u000aat a definitive (outer) margin.\u000aSYNOPTIC REPORT BREAST:\u000aINVASIVE TUMOR:\u000a-histologic type: ductal\u000a-histologic grade: moderately differentiated\u000a-size (greatest dimension): REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000a-lymphatic/vascular invasion: present\u000a-perineural invasion: none identified\u000a-microcalcification: present\u000a-margins for invasive tumor: Positive at a superficial-inferior and\u000asuperficial-superior margin over a broad\u000afront near the lateral end of the specimen.\u000aA focus of tumor is present at a definitive\u000aouter margin in the separate lateral superior\u000amargin, specimen (D).\u000a-immunohistochemical staining on prior specimen (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) was reported as:\u000aEstrogen receptor: POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor: POSITIVE\u000a-immunohistochemical staining for REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu will be performed on block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and\u000areported in an addendum to follow.\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU (DCIS):\u000a-histologic type: solid with necrosis\u000a-histologic grade: REMOVED_DATE \u000a-size (greatest dimension): microscopic foci within and around the\u000ainvasive tumor\u000a-extent: multifocal\u000a-extensive intraductal component: present\u000a-necrosis in DCIS: present, extensive\u000a-microcalcifications in DCIS: present\u000a-margins for DCIS: Positive at a superficial-inferior margin\u000alaterally.\u000aLYMPH NODES:\u000aAll 5 lymph nodes sampled are negative for malignancy (0/5)\u000a(0/3 sentinel lymph nodes; REMOVED_DATE non-sentinel lymph nodes).\u000aCOMMENT: The sentinel lymph node, specimen A, is examined at multiple\u000alevels with H&E stains and immunohistochemical stains for keratin.\u000aADDITIONAL PATHOLOGIC FINDINGS:\u000aFibrocystic changes.\u000aChanges consistent with prior biopsy site.\u000aPRIOR RELATED SPECIMENS REVIEWED:\u000asite: Left breast (right upper quadrant) specimen #:REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aAJCC pTNM Classification (6th Ed.): pREMOVED_ACCESSION_IDc pREMOVED_ACCESSION_IDi- pMX\u000aThe pathologic TNM classification above is based only on the information\u000aavailable to the pathologist, and therefore may not be accurate.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by: Richard J. Sampson, M.D.\u000aINTRA-OPERATIVE CONSULTATION:\u000aOPERATING ROOM CONSULTATION (TOUCH PREPARATION):\u000aSmallest firm node: No tumor seen.\u000aJLF\u000aClinical diagnosis & history:\u000aCarcinoma of left breast\u000aTissue-Designation:\u000aA.Sentinel lymph node - left axilla\u000aB.Lymph node, biopsy - left axilla\u000aC.Breast, excision with margins - left\u000aD.Breast, excision with margins - left, superior lateral margin\u000aGross description:\u000aThe specimen is received in four containers.\u000aSpecimen A labeled "sentinel lymph node, left axilla" consists of three\u000alymph nodes, each bisected and submitted as REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. A fat pad is present\u000awithout a lymph node, 2 x 2 x 1 cm. is also submitted. This is not sectioned.\u000aSpecimen B labeled "two nodes from left axilla" consists of a fat pad\u000acontaining some small lymph nodes. Each of the two pieces are bisected and\u000ameasure together 2 x 1 x 1 cm. 4X all.\u000aSpecimen C labeled "left breast mass" consists of a piece of breast tissue 4 x\u000a4 x 2 cm. Two orienting sutures are present. A long suture is designated\u000alateral and a short suture is designated superior. Using this orientation, the\u000adeep margin which is concave is inked blue. The superficial margins are all\u000ainked with black with the superior superficial margin also inked in yellow.\u000aCut section through this piece reveals firm breast tissue seen with a few small\u000acysts. Sections are taken from lateral to medial. 15X all, labeled REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aSpecimen D labeled "superior lateral margin of left breast" consists of a\u000asimilar piece of breast tissue 3 x REMOVED_DATE x 1 cm. with a concave and convex side.\u000aThe concave side is assumed to be the inner portion, non margin of the\u000aspecimen. The outer margin is the convex portion and is deemed to be the true\u000anew margin. This margin is inked with black ink. 8X all, labeled REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aDictated by: RJS____(signature on file)____ REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a____(signature on file)____RICHARD SAMPSON, M.D. REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a[report_end]
