VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aBRODSKY, GILBERT, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by BRODSKY,GILBERT,M.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED BIOPSY FOR A MASS:\u000aBenign breast tissue with cysts, apocrine metaplasia, and\u000amicrocalcifications associated with benign epithelium.\u000aFat necrosis and dense fibrotic tissue consistent with prior biopsy site.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: None given.\u000aOperation: Left needle localized breast biopsy.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal mammogram.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1. Left breast tissue, long - lateral, short - superior.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Density in specimen. OR called.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by HONG,XUEFEI,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in one part, labeled with the patient's name,\u000aunit number, and "#1. left breast, long = lateral, short = superior", and\u000aconsists of a fragment of yellow/tan fibrofatty breast tissue (14.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm), which contains a short suture to designate superior, a long suture to\u000adesignate lateral margins; a needle localization wire is also present in the\u000aspecimen. A whip stitch is present along one portion (anteromedial aspect) of\u000athe specimen which is undesignated. An accompanying radiograph shows the\u000aspecimen with a needle localization wire at the site of an irregular,\u000aradio-opaque mass. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the\u000aevaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red;\u000ainferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. The whip stitch is along\u000athe anterior surface, approximately REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin. The\u000aspecimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral, revealing a firm,\u000awhite, irregularly shaped mass (1.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which abuts the anterior\u000amargin, and is present REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior, REMOVED_DATE cm from superior, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom the inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial, and greater than 4 cm from the\u000alateral margins. No other lesions or masses suspicious for malignancy are\u000aidentified. The remainder of the breast parenchyma is comprised predominantly\u000aof unremarkable, yellow adipose tissue (95%), and white fibrous tissue (5%).\u000aThe entire mass, and representative sections of medial and lateral\u000aperpendicular margins are submitted.\u000aMICRO #1-6: Mass with respect to anterior, posterior, superior and anterior\u000amargins, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMICRO #7: Medial perpendicular margins, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMICRO #8: Lateral perpendicular margins, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMICRO #9-10: Breast parenchyma away from mass, 2 frags, RSS.\u000alcl\u000aReports to: SHOJI, BRENT, T. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
