fications. Specimen is sectioned to reveal tan/red\u000abiopsy cavity with a clip in place (0.6 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which is located REMOVED_DATE \u000acm to the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to the lateral margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to the medial\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm to the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to the superior margin, and REMOVED_DATE \u000acm to the anterior margin. The specimen is entirely submitted for histological\u000aexamination from anterior to posterior.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Anterior margin perpendicular, 6 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Serial sections of specimen from anterior to posterior, multi\u000afrags, ESS. Micro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID contain sections with biopsy cavity.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Posterior margin perpendicular, multi frags, ESS.\u000aCAD/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Xiaohua Qian M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000aWednesday REMOVED_MONTH 28, 2009 at 09:18:34AM\u000a[report_end]
