tive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity\u000ain >10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 38 year old female with a solid nodule in left 10:00 breast (patient\u000ahas saline implants).\u000aBreast Imaging Findings: Irregular.\u000aOperation: 11g U/S guided\u000aOperative findings: Solid nodule\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Cancer\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Left breast tissue (1 blue cassette)\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by QIAN,XIAOHUA,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit\u000anumber, and "left breast", in a light blue cassette, and consists of multiple,\u000asoft, fragmented, yellow to white tissue cores (1.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in\u000aaggregate).\u000aMicro 1: Multi frags, ESS.\u000akks\u000aReports to: SMITH, DARRELL, NOLAN M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY(IES)\u000a[report_end]
