VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID SENTINEL LYMPH NODE\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aLESTER, SUSAN, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST, EXCISION, AND SENTINEL NODE BIOPSY (TWO SPECIMENS):\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA, DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, AND NEGATIVE LYMPH NODES\u000aSYNOPSIS:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA\u000aSize - REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aMultifocal? - no\u000aHistologic Type - mixed ductal and lobular\u000aHistologic Grade (SBR) - III (poor)\u000aNuclear Grade - high\u000aEIC - negative\u000aLymphovascular invasion - present\u000aDermal lymphatic invasion - N/A\u000aSkin invasion - N/A\u000aSkeletal muscle invasion - N/A\u000aFinal Margins (invasive)\u000aNegative (no ink on tumor) - all other margins\u000aClose (tumor REMOVED_DATE cm from margin) - posterior (focal)\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aTypes - cribriform\u000aNuclear grade - intermediate\u000aCalcifications in DCIS - absent\u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - present\u000aExtent of DCIS - DCIS is present as a minor component of\u000athe invasive carcinoma\u000aFinal Margins (DCIS)\u000aNegative (>0.3 cm) - all margins\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - absent\u000aLYMPH NODES\u000aSentinel Lymph Nodes - negative (3 H&E levels examined)\u000aNumber of positive nodes - 0\u000aNumber of nodes examined - 6\u000aOTHER FINDINGS\u000aCore biopsy site associated with the invasive carcinoma\u000aAJCC CLASSIFICATION - REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDc pREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID MX\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER/PR/HER-2) - performed previously\u000aLEFT BREAST, SUPERIOR SHAVE MARGIN (specimen #3 of 3 specimens):\u000aBreast tissue with no tumor seen.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 38 year old female premenopausal, not on hormones with family\u000ahistory of breast cancer (mother, 43) who noted a left breast mass (s/p\u000abilateral implants) with subsequent mammogram supplemented by U/S demonstrating\u000aa REMOVED_DATE cm mass with core biopsy revealing invasive carcinoma with ductal and\u000alobular features.\u000aOperation: Left breast excisional biopsy and sentinel node biopsy\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast cancer\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1) Sentinel node left axilla x 3 (hot and blue)\u000a#2) Left breast tissue (short/superior; long/lateral; whip/chest wall margin)\u000a#3) Left breast tissue (short/superior shave margin; whip stitch/new margin)\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "#1. SENTINEL NODE", (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aThree lymph nodes negative for carcinoma.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by JEDLICKA,PAVEL J.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in three parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart one, labeled "#1. sentinel node", consists of three fragments of yellow\u000aadipose tissue (3.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate), containing three candidate\u000alymph nodes. Two lymph nodes (0.7 cm and REMOVED_DATE cm) are differentially inked,\u000abisected and entirely submitted as REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. One lymph node (1.6 cm) is bisected\u000aand entirely submitted as REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. Three additional candidate lymph nodes (each\u000aless than REMOVED_DATE cm) are also identified.\u000aMicro 1: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID remnant, mult frags, ESS\u000aMicro 2: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID remnant, 2 frags, ESS\u000aMicro 3: 3 additional candidate lymph nodes, 3 frags, ESS\u000aPart two, labeled "#2. left breast tissue", consists of a fragment of soft\u000atissue (7.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) that has been inked by the surgeon per pathology\u000aprotocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue;\u000asuperior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange.\u000aSectioning reveals a tumor mass (1.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), located the following\u000adistances from the nearest margin: REMOVED_DATE cm from superior, less than REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000aposterior, REMOVED_DATE cm from anterior, REMOVED_DATE cm from medial, REMOVED_DATE cm from lateral, and\u000a2.0 cm from inferior. Representative tumor tissue is submitted to tumor bank\u000afor special studies. The remainder of the specimen consists of approximately\u000aequal proportions of rubbery fibrous and lobulated adipose tissue with no\u000aadditional gross lesions.\u000aMicro 4: tumor mass and nearest anterior and posterior margins, 2 frags, RSS\u000aMicro 5: nearest superior and medial margins, 2 frags, RSS\u000aMicro 6: nearest lateral and inferior margins, 2 frags, RSS\u000aMicro 7: remainder of tumor mass, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  additional representative sections of fibrous tissue away from\u000atumor mass, 4 frags, RSS\u000aPart three, labeled "#3. left breast tissue, superior shave margin, whip stitch\u000anew margin", consists of a fragment of yellow/tan soft tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x\u000a2.5 x REMOVED_DATE cm. One surface of the specimen contains a whip stitch and is inked\u000ablue; the opposite surface is inked black. The specimen is sectioned and\u000aentirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  serial sections of specimen, mult frags, ESS\u000apj\u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: SENTINEL LYMPH NODE\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN\u000a[report_end]
