VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY(IES)\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aLESTER, SUSAN, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST, 3:00, ULTRASOUND GUIDED CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES OF A 7 CM\u000aCIRCUMSCRIBED MASS:\u000aFibroepithelial lesion most consistent with a PHYLLODES TUMOR.\u000aThe stroma is moderately cellular and fasciculates with mild nuclear\u000apleomorphism.\u000aFocal stromal overgrowth is present.\u000aMitoses are present (up to 5 per 10 HPF's).\u000aThe margins cannot be evaluated.\u000aNote: The findings on this core needle biopsy are consistent with a low\u000agrade phyllodes tumor. Excision is recommended for final classification.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 50 year old female with left breast lump at 3 o'clock. Was solid\u000amass on U/S. Core biopsy of this lesion was performed. The patient had a\u000afibroadenoma at the same site in 1964.\u000aBreast Imaging Findings: Circumscribed.\u000aOperative findings: Solid mass at 3 o'clock left breast on U/S\u000aClinical Diagnosis: R/O carcinoma\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Left breast core biopsy at 3 o'clock (1 white cassette)\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by CARTER,MARK RYAN,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit\u000anumber, and "left breast", in a white cassette, and consists of multiple, soft,\u000afragmented, yellow to white tissue cores (2.1 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate).\u000aMicro 1: Multi frags, ESS.\u000adfi\u000aReports to: RAZA, SUGHRA M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY(IES)\u000a[report_end]
