VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aWEINSTEIN, MICHAEL, H., M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by WEINSTEIN,MICHAEL H.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST MASS, EXCISION:\u000aLOW-GRADE PHYLLODES TUMOR (5.5 cm).\u000aTumor approaches to within REMOVED_DATE cm (multifocal) of the inked surgical\u000amargin of resection.\u000aThe inked surgical margins of resection are free of tumor.\u000aSee note.\u000aNOTE: The tumor shows stromal overgrowth and areas of hypercellularity,\u000abut is well-circumscribed and without nuclear atypia. The mitotic\u000arate is low (focally up to 3 per 10 HPF), and there are no areas of\u000aheterologous differentiation, necrosis, or hemorrhage. Overall, the\u000afeatures are consistent with a low-grade phyllodes tumor. The tumor\u000aappears completely excised, but the margins are very close. Close\u000aclinical follow-up is recommended.\u000aDr. Andrea Richardson of the Breast Pathology Service has reviewed\u000athis case and concurs with the diagnosis.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: None given.\u000aOperation: Wide excision of left breast mass\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Phyllodes tumor of the left breast\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1. Phyllodes tumor left breast (long stitch/lateral; short\u000astitch/superior)\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by IAFRATE,ANTHONY JOHN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in one part, labeled with the patient's name,\u000aunit number and "#1. phyllodes tumor left breast", and consists of a single\u000afragment of tan/yellow fibroadipose tissue (7 x REMOVED_DATE x 5 cm) with an attached\u000atan skin ellipse (2.1 x REMOVED_DATE cm). It received with two orienting sutures, a\u000ashort suture designating superior and a long suture designating lateral. The\u000acut surface reveals a large firm white whorled tumor mass (5.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm)\u000athat approaches to within REMOVED_DATE cm of multiple inked margins. The capsule\u000aappears intact however. Representative sections are submitted. Representative\u000atissue is snap frozen and submitted for cytogenetics.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  superior margin, 2 frags, RSS\u000aMicro 3: inferior margin, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 4: anterior margin, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 5: posterior margin, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 6: lateral margin, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 7: medial margin, 1 frag, RSS\u000aaji\u000aReports to: IGLEHART, JAMES, DIRK M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
