VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST MASTECTOMY - PARTIAL OR SIMPLE\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aGLICKMAN, JONATHAN, NEIL, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by GLICKMAN,JONATHAN NEIL,M.D.,PH.D.\u000a1) RIGHT BREAST, SIMPLE MASTECTOMY:\u000aBenign breasat tissue with cysts, epithelial hyperplasia, and biopsy site\u000achanges.\u000aSkin with cicatrix.\u000aMicrocalcifications are seen in association with benign epithelium.\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy.\u000a2) LEFT BREAST, SIMPLE MASTECTOMY:\u000aBenign breast tissue with epithelial hyperplasia and cysts.\u000aMicrocalcifications are seen in association with benign epithelium.\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: None given.\u000aOperation: Bilateral mastectomies with lat. flaps\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast cancer\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1) Right breast tissue - stitch: short superior, long lateral\u000a2) Left breast tissue - stitch: short superior, long lateral.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by HONG,XUEFEI,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart 1, "right breast", consists of a single mastectomy specimen (17 x 16 x 2\u000acm) with skin ellipse (3.5 x REMOVED_DATE cm), nipple (1.4 cm diameter), and a\u000awell-healed surgical scar (1.3 cm length). Sectioning reveals a fibrous scar\u000a(1.0 cm diameter) underneath the skin scar. There is a yellow/tan rubbery\u000aarea (4.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) which is located superior to the fibrous scar.\u000aThere are no masses suspicious for carcinoma grossly identified. This specimen\u000acontains 40% fibrous tissue and 60% adipose tissue. Representative sections are\u000asubmitted.\u000aMicro 1: Nipple and skin scar, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 2: Biopsy site with deep margin, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 3: Rubbery area, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 4: Upper outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 5: Lower outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 6: Upper inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 7: Lower inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 13: Additional biopsy site, 2 frags, RSS\u000aPart 2, "left breast", consists of a mastectomy specimen (18 x 16 x REMOVED_DATE cm)\u000awith skin (4.5 x REMOVED_DATE ) and nipple (1.3 cm diameter). Sectioning reveals 50%\u000afibrous tissue and 50% adipose tissue. There are no masses or other lesions\u000agrossly suspicious for carcinoma. Representative sections are submitted.\u000aMicro 8: Nipple, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 9, 14: Upper inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 10, 15: Inner lower quadrant, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 11, 16: Upper outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 12, 17: Lower outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS\u000aReports to: LESNIKOSKI, BETH-ANN M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY - PARTIAL OR SIMPLE\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY - PARTIAL OR SIMPLE\u000a[report_end]
