VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST BIOPSY W/O MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aODZE, ROBERT, DANIEL, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by ODZE,ROBERT DANIEL,M.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST, EXCISION FOR NIPPLE DISCHARGE:\u000aIntraductal papillomas (up to REMOVED_DATE cm) within fibrotic breast tissue.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000aThe entire specimen is submitted for microscopic analysis.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 24 year old premenopausal female on oral contraceptives with left\u000abreast nipple discharge. REMOVED_DATE ductogram unsuccessful, unable to cannulate the\u000aduct. U/S demonstrates 2 intraductal soft masses. REMOVED_DATE  core biopsy revealed\u000adense fibrous tissue and large ducts, no mass forming lesion.\u000aOperation: Left breast wire localization, retroareolar duct excision\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left nipple discharge\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1. Left breast tissue\u000aRADIOLOGY: Clip in specimen. E.P. Frost\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by LOMBARD,DAVID B.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in one part, labeled with the patient's name,\u000aunit number and "left breast tissue". It consists of a mass of fibroadipose\u000atissue (3.2 cm lateral to medial x REMOVED_DATE cm anterior to posterior x REMOVED_DATE cm\u000asuperior to inferior). The specimen has been oriented by the surgeon via two\u000asutures placed in the specimen. In addition a needle is present in the\u000aspecimen. The specimen has been inked by the surgeon per pathology protocol\u000afor the evaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior =\u000ared; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. No lesion is present\u000agrossly in the specimen, which appears to consists predominantly of fibrous\u000atissue. A specimen radiograph is taken, and the clip located and removed.\u000aThe specimen is entirely submitted from medial to lateral.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  left breast tissue, mult frags, ESS (the fragment containing the\u000aclip is the larger fragment in micro 2)\u000adl\u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST BIOPSY W/O MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
