VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID:REMOVED_CASE_ID Report Status: Signed\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aADDENDUM REPORT\u000aAddendum #2 Entered: REMOVED_DATE -1418\u000a*** ADDITIONAL DIAGNOSTIC INFORMATION ***\u000aThis report contains an addendum to the original for the purpose of providing\u000aadditional diagnostic information. The original diagnosis is unchanged.\u000aFluorescence in situ hybridization (FISH) with probes for REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu performed at\u000aMayo Medical Laboratories on the block reveals the following results for the\u000ainfiltrating carcinoma:\u000aThe specimen showed evidence of REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu gene amplification.\u000aBased on the gene amplification assay for REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), the\u000aimmunohistochemistry should be considered as (3+).\u000aAddeundum Signed Electronically Signed FEEN,DENNIS J. M.D. REMOVED_DATE \u000aAddendum #1 Entered: REMOVED_DATE -1341\u000a*** ADDITIONAL DIAGNOSTIC INFORMATION ***\u000aThis report contains an addendum to the original for the purpose of providing\u000aadditional diagnostic information. The original diagnosis is unchanged.\u000aImmunohistochemical studies performed on the block reveal the following results\u000afor the infiltrating carcinoma:\u000aEstrogen receptor: POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor: POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID): 2+ staining. Further evaluation by fluorescence\u000ain situ hybridization (FISH) method will be\u000aperformed and results reported in an addendum to\u000afollow.\u000aAddeundum Signed Electronically Signed FEEN,DENNIS J. M.D. REMOVED_DATE \u000aDIAGNOSIS:\u000aLeft breast (2 o'clock), needle core biopsies:\u000aPoorly differentiated infiltrating ductal carcinoma.\u000aDuctal carcinoma in situ, grade REMOVED_DATE  cribriform.\u000aNOTE: No lymphovascular invasion present. Estrogen, progesterone receptors\u000aand REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu will be done at Newton-Wellesley Hospital and reported in\u000aan addendum.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by: Dennis J. Feen, M.D.\u000aClinical diagnosis & history:\u000aLeft breast mass at 2 o'clock; probable breast cancer\u000aTissue-Designation:\u000aBreast, needle biopsy - left, 2 o'clock\u000aGross description:\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin in one container, labeled "guided breast\u000abiopsies, left breast, 2 o'clock" and consists of four firm, yellowish-white,\u000aglistening needle biopsies measuring REMOVED_DATE cm. in length x REMOVED_DATE cm. in diameter to\u000a1.8 cm. in length x REMOVED_DATE cm. in diameter. 4X all.\u000aDictated by: LV____(signature on file)____MICHAEL J. ROSS, M.D. REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a____(signature on file)____DENNIS J. FEEN, M.D. REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a[report_end]
