VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID:REMOVED_CASE_ID Report Status: Signed\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aDIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. Left breast, excision:\u000aInvasive ductal carcinoma, poorly differentiated.\u000aFocal ductal carcinoma in situ, low grade, micropapillary and cribriform\u000atypes.\u000aMultiple radial scars with focal atypical ductal hyperplasia.\u000aFibrocystic changes with cysts, fibrosis and ductal hyperplasia.\u000aSkin with dermal scar and small seborrheic keratosis.\u000aChanges consistent with prior needle biopsy site.\u000aB. Final superior margin of left breast, excision:\u000aInvasive ductal carcinoma, poorly differentiated.\u000aDuctal carcinoma in situ, low grade, cribriform type with focal\u000amicrocalcifications.\u000aMultiple radial scars.\u000aFibrocystic changes with ductal hyperplasia and small fibroadenoma.\u000aC. Final nipple margin of left breast, excision:\u000aInvasive ductal carcinoma, poorly differentiated.\u000aRadial scar and small fibroadenoma.\u000aD. Left axillary lymph nodes, dissection:\u000aMetastatic adenocarcinoma consistent with mammary duct primary in 2 out\u000aof 24 lymph nodes (2/24), with extranodal extension present.\u000aSYNOPTIC REPORT\u000aINVASIVE TUMOR:\u000a-histologic type: Invasive ductal carcinoma\u000a-histologic grade: Poorly differentiated\u000a-size (greatest dimension): Estimated at least REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000a-lymphatic/vascular invasion: Present\u000a-perineural invasion: None identified\u000a-microcalcification in invasive tumor: None identified\u000a-margins for invasive tumor:\u000aIn specimen A, the invasive carcinoma is at the inked superior\u000aaspect of the lateral margin over a broad front from nearly the\u000asuperficial to nearly the deep aspect; it is at the medial margin in\u000amicroscopic foci at the superficial aspect; and it is at the mid superior\u000amargin in one microscopic focus. Invasive carcinoma is present in the\u000aseparate "final superior margin" (specimen B) where it is present at the\u000ainked margin. Invasive carcinoma is also present in the separate "final\u000anipple margin" (specimen C).\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU (DCIS):\u000a-histologic type: Micropapillary and cribriform\u000a-histologic grade: Low grade\u000a-size (greatest dimension): REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000a-extent: Focal\u000a-extensive intraductal component: Absent\u000a-necrosis in DCIS: None identified\u000a-microcalcifications in DCIS: None identified\u000a-margins for DCIS:\u000aIn specimen A, ductal carcinoma in situ is focally REMOVED_DATE to REMOVED_DATE cm. from the\u000ainked mid lateral margin. In the "final superior margin" specimen B,\u000aductal carcinoma in situ is present at the inked margin, focally.\u000aLYMPH NODES:\u000aPositive lymph nodes out of total lymph nodes sampled: REMOVED_DATE \u000a-size of largest metastatic focus (greatest dimension): REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000a-extranodal extension: Present, focal\u000aSKIN:\u000a-skin/dermis: Small seborrheic keratosis and adjacent dermal fibroplasia\u000aand chronic inflammation.\u000aADDITIONAL PATHOLOGIC FINDINGS:\u000aMultiple radial scars with foci of atypical ductal hyperplasia; fibrocystic\u000achanges with ductal hyperplasia; fibroadenomas.\u000aPRIOR RELATED SPECIMENS REVIEWED:\u000aLeft breast needle core biopsy; REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID; REMOVED_DATE \u000aLeft axillary tail fine needle aspiration; REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID; REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by: Daniel D. Koelliker, M.D.\u000aClinical diagnosis & history:\u000aLocally advanced left breast carcinoma; positive fine needle aspirate; left\u000aaxillary nodule; S/P chemotherapy\u000aTissue-Designation:\u000aA.Breast, excision with margins - left\u000aB.Breast, excision with margins - left, final superior margin\u000aC.Specimen designated as - left nipple margin\u000aD.Lymph nodes, dissection - left axillary\u000aGross description:\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin in four containers.\u000aSpecimen A labeled "left breast, long medial, short superior" consists of a 26\u000agram excision of fibroadipose tissue which has a REMOVED_DATE cm. long, REMOVED_DATE cm. wide\u000astrip of skin on the superficial surface which overlies a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000aportion of fibroadipose tissue which has a short suture oriented as the\u000asuperior edge and a long suture oriented as the medial surface of the left\u000abreast excision. The outer surfaces are grossly unremarkable and are inked\u000ablack throughout. The deep surface is double inked red; the medial surface is\u000adouble inked blue. The portion is sectioned. Cross sectioning demonstrates\u000acentrally firm and focally yellowish and reddish discolored fibrous tissue with\u000aa small amount of surrounding yellow adipose tissue. The entire specimen is\u000asubmitted as follows: 22 agg. all.\u000aSection code: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - superior half from superficial towards deep\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - skin\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - inferior half from superficial to deep\u000aSpecimen B labeled "left breast, final margin; stitch on side away from tumor"\u000aconsists of a 7 gram, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. portion of fibroadipose tissue which\u000ahas a suture on one convex surface which is clinically oriented as the side\u000aaway from the tumor and is inked black. Opposite from this surface is a\u000aconcave, granular appearing surface. On sectioning, there is firm, granular\u000atissue in the center of the specimen adjacent to the cavity. The entire\u000aspecimen is submitted sequentially in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. 7 agg. all.\u000aSpecimen C labeled "left nipple" consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. aggregate of\u000atwo separate portions of fibroadipose tissue. The larger is sectioned. The\u000aentire specimen is submitted in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. 5X all.\u000aSpecimen D labeled "left axillary contents" consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000aportion of adipose tissue. The adipose tissue is dissected revealing multiple\u000ared-tan lymph nodes, some of which have fatty replacement of the hilum and some\u000awhich appear somewhat firm on cut section. Sections of the entirety of each of\u000athe lymph nodes dissected from the adipose tissue are submitted as follows:\u000a13 agg.\u000aSection code: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - multiple lymph nodes, not sectioned\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - one lymph node, sectioned\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - one lymph node, sectioned\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - one lymph node, sectioned\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - multiple lymph nodes, not sectioned\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - one lymph node, sectioned\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - one lymph node, sectioned\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - multiple lymph nodes and fibrous tissue, not sectioned\u000aDictated by: DDK____(signature on file)____NICOLE MIHOK, M.D. REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a____(signature on file)____DANIEL D. KOELLIKER, M.D. REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a[report_end]
