ior/blue; superior/red;\u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. The specimen is received with a\u000aneedle localization wire entering the anterior aspect of the specimen and\u000aexiting through the posterior inferior aspect of the specimen. The specimen is\u000aserially sectioned from superior to inferior to exhibit an ill-defined firm\u000atan-yellow mass (0.9 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), abutting the posterior margin and located\u000aless than REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin, REMOVED_DATE \u000acm from the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior margin and REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000athe superior margin. A metallic clip is identified within this area.\u000aRemaining breast parenchyma consists of approximately 90% dense white fibrous\u000atissue to 10% yellow lobulated adipose tissue. The specimen is submitted in\u000aits entirety.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Perpendicular superior margin, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Body, sequentially submitted from superior to inferior to include\u000amass (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) and area of clip (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), 1 frag in each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Perpendicular inferior margin, 2 frags in each, ESS.\u000ajc/lp\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Lucian R Chirieac M.D., on Monday REMOVED_MONTH 05, 2009 at\u000a05:32:44PM\u000aAmendment #1 by Lucian R Chirieac M.D., Electronically signed on Wednesday\u000aREMOVED_MONTH 14, 2009 at 03:54:37PM\u000a[report_end]
