VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Consult material\u000aProcedure Date:\u000aOrdering Provider: JAY HARRIS M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Qinghong Yang, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Jane E. Brock, M.B., B.S., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aCONSULT SLIDES FROM MASSACHUSETTS GENERAL HOSPITAL, BOSTON, MA:\u000aLEFT BREAST WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISIONS X 2, ADDITIONAL LEFT BREAST 6 MARGINS,\u000aLEFT AXILLARY SENTINEL NODE BIOPSY AND LEFT AXILLARY DISSECTION & RIGHT BREAST\u000aWIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION (MS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_DATE ):\u000aLEFT BREAST WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A CLIP #1 (PART C), LEFT SUPERIOR FINAL\u000aMARGIN, LEFT MEDIAL FINAL MARGIN, LEFT DEEP FINAL MARGIN, LEFT ANTERIOR FINAL\u000aMARGON, LEFT LATERAL FINAL MARGIN, AND LEFT INFERIOR FINAL MARGIN (PARTS F, G,\u000aH, I, J, K), LEFT SENTINEL LYMPH NODES BIOPSY AND LEFT AXILLARY LYMPH NODE\u000a(PART D & E):\u000aTumor bed measuring up to REMOVED_DATE cm, with no residual invasive or in situ\u000acarcinoma present. Tumor bed is associated with biopsy site changes including\u000acollagen plug.\u000aTumor bed and biopsy site extend to the inferior and posterior inked margins of\u000aresection in the excision.\u000aNo lymphovascular invasion present.\u000aATYPICAL DUCTAL PROLIFERATION, single focus (0.05 cm), with high nuclear grade\u000aand mitoses partially involving a breast lobule, best classified as ATYPICAL\u000aDUCTAL HYPERPLASIA. This focus is present adjacent to the biopsy site (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) and\u000alocated REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin and REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior margin.\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia associated with microcalcifications and cysts.\u000aSeparately submitted additional final shave margins (including superior,\u000ainferior, medial, lateral, anterior, posterior) are negative for invasive\u000acarcinoma and in situ carcinoma. Inferior and posterior margins are negative\u000afor definite residual tumor bed. Biopsy site changes are present in the\u000aanterior margin (part I) in 1 of 3 slides.\u000aSix (6) lymph nodes, including five (5) sentinel lymph nodes, are negative for\u000acarcinoma (by report including keratin stains performed on 3 tissue levels of\u000asentinel and non-sentinel nodes). No definite evidence of treatment effect is\u000aseen.\u000aNOTE: The patient presented with a REMOVED_DATE cm irregular mass in the upper-inner\u000aquadrant of her left breast in REMOVED_DATE confirmed on core biopsy as poorly\u000adifferentiated IDC that was ER negative, PR negative, and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu negative (0)\u000a(see BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID). Axillary lymphadenopathy was present.\u000aAfter neoadjuvant chemotherapy, bilateral mammogram showed a left breast clip\u000alocated in the upper inner quadrant consistent with the known tumor bed site,\u000aand additional suspicious calcifications in the upper outer quadrant (see\u000aexcision #2). In addition, there were suspicious calcifications in the right\u000abreast (see right breast excision). Post chemotherapy ultrasound imaging\u000ashowed a biopsy clip in a hypoechoic structure that measured REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm with\u000aan additional hypoechoic focus (0.5 cm in greatest dimension) located ~ REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom the clip).\u000aGross examination of the left breast excision #1 reported two specimens; one\u000alarger oriented one and one smaller unoriented specimen. A cavity was present\u000ain the larger specimen (by report up to 4 cm in dimension) with approached to\u000athe medial and lateral margins, REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin and >0.3 cm\u000afrom the remaining margins. Both fragments were entirely submitted for\u000amicroscopic examination. The slides of the small fragment show benign breast\u000atissue with no definite tumor bed present and no biopsy site changes present.\u000aThe slides of the larger fragment show biopsy site changes and probable tumor\u000abed measuring up to REMOVED_DATE cm in diameter in the main excision, with no residual\u000ainvasive or in situ carcinoma present.\u000aThese findings are consistent with a complete pathologic response to\u000aneoadjuvant chemotherapy (Miller-Payne score of 5). Residual cancer burden is\u000a0 (RCB-0).\u000aLEFT BREAST WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION #2 FOR CALCIFICATIONS (PART B):\u000aCysts with microcalcifications and mucin production with adjacent stromal\u000acalcifications and extravasated stromal mucin suggestive of cyst rupture (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID)\u000aMicrocalcifications are also present associated with normal breast epithelium.\u000aRIGHT BREAST WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR CALCIFICATIONS (PART A):\u000aMicrocalcifications associated with normal breast epithelium and epithelial\u000ahyperplasia with patchy nuclear ATYPIA, see NOTE.\u000aCysts.\u000aNOTE: The cytological atypia present is difficult to classify being patchily\u000apresent in otherwise benign appearing hyperplastic breast ducts and lobules in\u000aall 5 blocks reviewed (slides from REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID were not received for review). It is\u000aassociated with and without calcifications and may be related to the patient's\u000arecent chemotherapy.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Left breast cancer, s/p neoadjuvant therapy for excision w/sentinel\u000anode\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Fibrocystic changes w/usual hyperplasia and calcifications\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aConsult slides.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aReceived from Massachusetts General Hospital, Pathology Department, 55 Fruit\u000aStreet, Boston, MA REMOVED_CASE_ID, are fifty-seven (57) glass slides.\u000aThe slides are labeled ?REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" and sublabeled "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID", "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" through\u000a"REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID", "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" through "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID", "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID", "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID", "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID", "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID", "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" through\u000a"REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" through "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID", "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID", "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID", "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" through "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID", "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID"\u000athrough "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID", "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID", "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" through "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID", "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID", "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID"," REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID", "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID",\u000a"REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" through "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID", "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID", "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID", "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" and "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID", corresponding to A)\u000aright breast excision (2.8 x REMOVED_DATE x 1 cm) B) left breast wire needle localized\u000aexcision (2.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) C) left breast wire needle localized excision\u000a(2.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm, and REMOVED_DATE x 2 x REMOVED_DATE cm) D) left axillary sentinel lymph\u000anode, count 7386, excision (2.5 x 2 x REMOVED_DATE cm) E) left non-sentinel axillary\u000alymph node excision (2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) F) left breast, final superior margin,\u000aexcision (1.6 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) G) left breast, final medial margin, excision\u000a(1.3 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm, and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) H) left breast, final deep margin,\u000aexcision (2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) I) left breast, final anterior margin, excision\u000a(2.3 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm, and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) J) left breast, final inferior\u000amargin, excision (1.3 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) K) left breast, final lateral margin,\u000aexcision (1.5 x 1 x REMOVED_DATE cm) performed on REMOVED_DATE  according to the accompanying\u000apathology report bearing the patient's name.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic 