VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast core needle biopsy\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: CHRISTINE M DENISON M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Mariana A. Stoleru, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Susan Lester, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, 12:00, 14 G ULTRASOUND GUIDED CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR A PALPABLE\u000a0.9 CM IRREGULAR MASS:\u000aINVASIVE ADENOCARCINOMA, measuring at least REMOVED_DATE cm (see note). An\u000aimmunoperoxidase for cytokeratin REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and p63 confirms the absence of\u000amyoepithelial cells in the area of invasive carcinoma.\u000aNo definitive lymphovascular invasion is seen in this limited specimen.\u000aNo carcinoma in situ is seen in this limited specimen.\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia is present.\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies are performed with the following results for\u000ainvasive carcinoma:\u000aEstrogen receptor NEGATIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor NEGATIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu NEGATIVE (0)\u000aCytokeratin - PANK POSITIVE\u000aCytokeratin REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID NEGATIVE\u000aTTF-1 NEGATIVE\u000aNormal epithelial cells are appropriately immunoreactive for estrogen\u000aand progesterone receptors.\u000aNote: The carcinoma has an unusual prominent exuberant stromal\u000adesmoplastic response.\u000aThe findings are most consistent with a breast primary carcinoma.\u000aOrigin from the patient's prior lung and skin carcinomas would be highly\u000aunlikely.\u000aRepeat studies for ER, PR, and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu on the excisional biopsy may be\u000aof value due to the small amount of carcinoma on the deeper levels used for\u000athese studies.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHISTORY: Left lung adenocarcinoma in 1992 (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), invasive squamous cell\u000acarcinoma of upper chest and left lateral leg (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID). New\u000a0.9 cm irregular solid mass, right breast at 12:00 o'clock, 4 cm from nipple.\u000aBREAST IMAGING FINDING:\u000a1. Right: REMOVED_DATE cm, palpable irregular mass.\u000aLOCATION:\u000a1. Right: 12:00.\u000aTYPE OF CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY:\u000a1. 14 G Ultrasound\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000a1. 14 G Ultrasound; 11:00 AM in formalin - Green cassette.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit\u000anumber, and "Right breast green", and consists of cores of fibroadipose tissue,\u000areceived in a green cassette with a green lid and aggregating REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Right breast green cassette cores, multi frags, ESS.\u000aDB/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000aTuesday February 17, 2009 at 05:07:09PM\u000a[report_end]
