VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Amend/Addenda\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Sentinel Lymph Nodes(s)\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ROGER L CHRISTIAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000a********** Addended Report ***********\u000aResident: Cheryl Adackapara, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Jeffrey F Krane, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. RIGHT AXILLARY SENTINEL LYMPH NODES (including REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aPlease see Part B.\u000aB. RIGHT BREAST, EXCISION FOR A MASS, AND SENTINEL LYMPH NODES BIOPSY,\u000aAND AXILLARY NODE DISSECTION (including Parts A, B, and C):\u000aINVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aMETASTATIC CARCINOMA TO LYMPH NODE\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA\u000aSize - REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aMultifocal - No\u000aHistologic type - Ductal\u000aHistologic grade (SBR) - II (Moderate) (6 to 7 points)\u000aTubules - < 10% (3 points)\u000aNuclear grade - High (3 points)\u000aMitotic counts - 1 point\u000aEIC - Negative\u000aLVI - Focus suspicious for LVI present\u000aDermal LVI - Not applicable\u000aSkin invasion - Not applicable\u000aSkeletal muscle invasion - Not applicable\u000aFinal Margins (invasive)\u000aNegative (> REMOVED_DATE cm) - Lateral, posterior, anterior, superior,\u000amedial, inferior\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aTypes - Comedo\u000aNuclear grade - High\u000aCalcifications in DCIS - Present\u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - Present\u000aDCIS is present as a minor component of the invasive carcinoma\u000aMargins (DCIS)\u000aNegative (> REMOVED_DATE cm) - Superior, anterior, posterior, medial\u000aVery close(<0.1 cm from margin)- Inferolateral, focal\u000aPositive (ink on carcinoma) - Inferior, focal\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - Present\u000aLYMPH NODES\u000aSentinel lymph nodes - Positive (3 H&E levels examined)\u000aNumber of positive nodes - 1\u000aNumber of nodes examined - 3\u000aAxillary lymph nodes - Negative\u000aNumber of positive nodes - 0\u000aNumber of nodes examined - 6\u000aTOTAL POSITIVE NODES (all specimens)- 1:9\u000aSize of largest metastatic focus - REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aNumber of nodes w/macrometastases- 1\u000aExtranodal extension - Absent\u000aOTHER FINDINGS\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia with pagetoid spread\u000aCore biopsy site\u000aCalcifications in benign epithelium\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER, PR, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) - Pending\u000aC. RIGHT AXILLARY CONTENTS:\u000aPlease see Part B.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: None given.\u000aOperation: SNB, wide excision.\u000aOperative Findings: See op-note.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Ca, right breast.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Right ax node(s), sentinel - FS.\u000aB/2. Tumor site, right breast, color markings.\u000aC/3. Right axillary contents.\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "RIGHT AXILLARY NODE(S), SENTINEL" (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID AND REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aMicrometastases (0.1 cm) in one (frozen section) lymph node.\u000aOR Consultation by: VANIA NOSE, M.D., PH.D.\u000aResident: Kremena V. Star, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aThe senior physician certifies that he/she personally conducted a gross and/or\u000amicroscopic examination of the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed\u000athe rapid diagnos(es) related thereto.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in three parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart A, "right axillary node, sentinel", consists of two soft tissue fragments\u000aconsistent with lymph node (2.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The\u000asmaller fragments are entirely submitted for frozen section analysis as REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aand the larger fragment is bisected and is entirely submitted for frozen\u000asection analysis as REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Frozen section remnant REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Frozen section remnant REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Frozen section remnant REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aPart B, "tumor site, right breast, color markings", consists of one excision\u000aspecimen (4.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) received previously inked. There is one suture\u000alocated at the junction of the yellow, black and green inks, though the\u000aoperative report states that three sutures were placed on the specimen. The\u000asurgeon confirmed that inking was done per pathology protocol. The specimen is\u000asectioned to reveal a tan/white firm fibrous nodular area (3.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm)\u000awhich grossly abuts the inferior and posterior margins, REMOVED_DATE cm to the medial\u000aand lateral margins, REMOVED_DATE cm to the superior margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm to the anterior\u000amargin. No other masses or lesions are grossly identified and the biopsy\u000acavity site is not identified. The specimen is entirely submitted for\u000ahistologic examination.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Excision specimen, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID contains the nodular area.\u000aPart C, "right axillary contents", consists of one tan/red fragment of\u000afibroadipose soft tissue (11.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with three lymph node\u000acandidates up to REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest dimension. The specimen is entirely\u000asubmitted for histological examination.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Fibroadipose soft tissue, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: REMOVED_DATE cm lymph node, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 2 lymph node candidates, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aCAD/ag\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jeffrey F Krane M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000aTuesday REMOVED_MONTH 24, 2009 at 05:00:02PM\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM:\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for invasive carcinoma (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor NEGATIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor NEGATIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) NEGATIVE (1+)\u000aNote: Normal epithelial cells are appropriately immunoreactive for estrogen\u000aand progesterone receptors.\u000aThese results confirm the findings on the prior core needle biopsy (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID)\u000aImmunohistochemical studies for estrogen receptor, progesterone receptor, and\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu were evaluated by manual morphometric analysis using the following\u000acriteria:\u000aHormone receptor analysis:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low > 0% - < 10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not\u000ayet been determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but\u000aonly a portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aEquivocal (2+):Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in\u000a>10% of tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+):Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in\u000a>30% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aExternal controls are evaluated and show appropriate Immunoreactivity.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aAddendum #1 by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on Thursday\u000aREMOVED_MONTH 26, 2009 at 04:13:11PM\u000a[report_end]
