VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ROGER L CHRISTIAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Kremena V. Star, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: William R Welch, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, RE-EXCISION:\u000aATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA, with pagetoid spread, is present in 2 of 11\u000aslides, adjacent to biopsy site changes (blocks REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) (see note).\u000aThe ADH is REMOVED_DATE to REMOVED_DATE cm from the closest anterior margin. The foci near\u000athe margin are < REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia with pagetoid spread is present (block\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aBiopsy site changes are extensively present at the posterior margin.\u000aNo carcinoma is seen close to the medial, lateral, inferior, superior,\u000aand posterior margins.\u000aNote: The patient has a history of a poorly differentiated invasive\u000aductal carcinoma, DCIS, and LCIS in a prior excision (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID). DCIS was\u000apresent at the inferior margin and close to the inferolateral margin. In\u000athis specimen there are small foci that may be areas of minimal residual\u000aDCIS adjacent to the biopsy site.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Not provided.\u000aOperation: Re-excision, right breast.\u000aOperative Findings: Not provided.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast cancer.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Right breast tissue light suture posterior to nipple.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "#1. Right breast tissue with suture posterior to the nipple", consists of\u000aa fragment of yellow lobulated fibrofatty tissue (4.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), with a\u000alight-colored suture designating "posterior to nipple", and a long suture\u000adesignating lateral, and a short suture designating superior (confirmed by Dr.\u000aChristian). The specimen is received partially previously inked blue at the\u000alight-colored suture (anterior), black at the opposite margin (posterior),\u000ayellow at the long suture designating lateral margin and green at the "presumed\u000anew" margin. The remaining margins are inked by the prosector as follows:\u000aOrange opposite the yellow lateral margin (medial) red at the short suture\u000adesignating superior (consistent with the biopsy cavity area). The specimen is\u000aserially sectioned to reveal 90% focally hemorrhagic dense white fibrous\u000atissue, and 10% yellow adipose tissue with no discrete masses or lesions\u000aidentified. The specimen is sequentially submitted in its entirety.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, radially, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross sections from lateral to medial, 1 frag each,\u000aESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin, radially, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aPlease note that the light-colored suture area is REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aCP/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by William R Welch M.D., Electronically signed on Wednesday\u000aREMOVED_MONTH 15, 2009 at 02:10:31PM\u000a[report_end]
