Progesterone receptor POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) NEGATIVE (1+)\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000ainvasive carcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but\u000aonly a portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity\u000ain >10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 66 yo female.\u000aOperation: Right total mastectomy, insertion of tissue expander.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast carcinoma.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Right total mastectomy (right breast), short/superior,\u000along/lateral.\u000a2. Right axillary lymph nodes.\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "2) RIGHT AXILLARY LYMPH NODE" (FSA):\u000aLymph node with fatty change.\u000aNo malignancy.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by SPRINGER,KIMBERLEY M.,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart one, "#1 right breast", consists of a 163-gram breast, including a REMOVED_DATE x\u000a3.6 cm, white/tan skin ellipse (including a REMOVED_DATE cm, unremarkable nipple). The\u000aspecimen measures 15 x 11 x REMOVED_DATE cm in overall dimensions. Supralateral to the\u000askin ellipse is a REMOVED_DATE cm incision leading to a biopsy cavity (4.5 x 4 x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm). The cavity is surrounded by fibrosis, fat necrosis and is located REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom the deep margin. The remaining breast tissue is yellow/tan and soft to\u000arubbery, with no other masses. Representative sections are submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  biopsy cavity, multi frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 9: lower inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 10: lower outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 11: nipple, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 13: upper outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 14: upper inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aPart two, "#2 right axillary lymph node", consists of one fragment of\u000afibroadipose tissue containing one lymph node (1.6 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). Lymph node\u000ais bisected and entirely submitted as FSA,\u000aMicro 12: FSA remnant, 2 frags, ESS.\u000akms\u000aReports to: LESNIKOSKI, BETHANN M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY W/REGIONAL LYMPH NODES\u000a[report_end]
