VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aWEINSTEIN, MICHAEL, H., M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by WEINSTEIN,MICHAEL H.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000a1. LEFT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION OF MASS:\u000aColumnar alteration of lobules with prominent snouts and secretions with\u000aatypia.\u000aRadial sclerosing lesion (approximately REMOVED_DATE cm; block #5).\u000aFibrocystic changes including cysts (largest measuring REMOVED_DATE cm),\u000aapocrine metaplasia, and associated microcalcifications.\u000aCore biopsy site with repair reaction.\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy , and margins are examined\u000amicroscopically.\u000a2. RIGHT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION OF MASS:\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia.\u000aComplex sclerosing lesion (block #11).\u000aExtensive epithelial hyperplasia is present.\u000aExtensive fibrocystic changes including cysts, apocrine metaplasia,\u000aand associated microcalcifications.\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy, and margins are examined\u000amicroscopically.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 46 year old female (premenopausal) with abnormal mammo on REMOVED_DATE \u000aCore biopsy on REMOVED_DATE  of a left breast 1 o'clock circumscribed mass, showed\u000afragments of cyst wall. Right breast spiculated mass, atypical lobular\u000ahyperplasia, complex lesion with fibroadeno- matoid stromal fibrosis,\u000asclerosing adenosis, cysts and apocrine metaplasia.\u000aOperation: Bilateral needle localized breast biopsy\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal bilateral mammogram\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1) Left breast tissue (short suture/superior at cyst\u000acavity; long suture/lateral; whipstitch/deep margin, cyst ruptured during\u000adissection)\u000a#2) Right breast tissue (short suture/superior; long suture/lateral;\u000awhipstitch)\u000aRADIOLOGY: Small cyst (4 mm) in specimen but REMOVED_DATE size of localized cyst\u000a(OR says it ruptured at biopsy).\u000aO. R. CONSULTATION REPORT:\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "#1. LEFT BREAST TISSUE", (GROSS ONLY):\u000a0.8 cm cyst present.\u000aNo areas grossly suspicious for invasive carcinoma.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by DRAPKIN,RONNY I.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart one, labeled "left breast tissue", consists of a single fragment of\u000afibrofatty tissue (4.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with a needle localization wire in\u000aplace. The specimen is oriented with three sutures (short=superior,\u000along=lateral, whip=deep). The short suture is located by the cyst cavity.\u000aAccording to the surgeon the cyst was ruptured during dissection. The specimen\u000ais inked by the surgeon. The specimen is inked for the evaluation of margins:\u000aposterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral =\u000ayellow; medial = orange. The specimen is serially sectioned and entirely\u000asubmitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  left breast tissue, REMOVED_DATE frags each, ESS\u000aPart two, labeled "right breast", consist of a single fragment of pink/tan\u000afibroadipose tissue (4.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) that is oriented with three sutures\u000a(short=superior, long=lateral, whipstitch=deep). A needle localization wire is\u000ain place. The specimen is inked by the surgeon for the evaluation of margins:\u000aposterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral\u000a= yellow; medial = orange. Cut sections reveal firm fibrous tissue with fluid\u000afilled cyst (ranging from REMOVED_DATE 2 cm) and focal fat necrosis. The specimen is\u000aentirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  right breast tissue, REMOVED_DATE frags each, ESS\u000ardr\u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: 