VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Amend/Addenda\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast core needle biopsy\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: DIANNE GEORGIAN-SMITH M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000a********** Addended Report ***********\u000aResident: Dominique P. Coco, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Susan Lester, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aLEFT BREAST, UPPER OUTER, 14 G ULTRASOUND GUIDED CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR A REMOVED_DATE \u000aCM OVAL MASS:\u000aFRAGMENTS OF A MUCINOUS PAPILLARY CARCINOMA (see note).\u000aNote: There are multiple fragments of a papillary neoplasm associated\u000awith abundant mucin. It is possible that this is a form of intracystic\u000aductal carcinoma in situ. Final classification should be made after excision.\u000aImmunohistochemical analysis for estrogen receptor, progesterone\u000areceptor, and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu will be performed and reported in an addendum.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHISTORY: 74 year old female with mammographic oval mass and hypoechoic oval\u000alesion in L breast. Diff Dx: Suspicious for cancer.\u000aBREAST IMAGING FINDING:\u000a1. Left: 15 mm, Nonpalpable circumscribed/lobulated mass.\u000aLOCATION:\u000a1. Left: upper outer\u000aTYPE OF CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY:\u000a1. 14G Ultrasound\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000a1. 14G Ultrasound - Pink cassette.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit\u000anumber and "Left breast", and consists of multiple tan/yellow tan/white\u000alobulated fibroadipose breast tissue cores (1.4 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate).\u000aThe breast tissue cores were received in a pink cassette and are submitted in\u000atoto.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Multi frags, ESS.\u000aSEK/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a11/8/2007\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM:\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed with the following results for the\u000apapillary carcinoma (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu NEGATIVE (1+)\u000aAn immunoperoxidase study for p63 does not show the presence of myoepithelial\u000acells within the carcinoma. This finding does not change the original\u000adiagnosis. Final classification should be made after excision.\u000aAddendum #1 by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
