VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Amend/Addenda\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Sentinel Lymph Nodes(s)\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ROGER L CHRISTIAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000a********** Addended Report ***********\u000aResident: Elizabeth Amy Morgan, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Gilbert Brodsky, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aSPECIMEN DESIGNATED "LEFT BREAST EXCISION FOR A MASS (Part C) AND SENTINEL NODE\u000aBIOPSIES (including FSA) (Part A):\u000aINVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aNEGATIVE LYMPH NODES\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA\u000aSize - REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aMultifocal - Yes (see note)\u000aHistologic type - Ductal, mucinous\u000aHistologic grade (SBR) - III (Poor) (8 or 9 points)\u000aTubules - < 10% (3 points)\u000aNuclear grade - Intermediate (2 points)\u000aMitotic rate - High (3 points)\u000aEIC - Positive\u000aLVI - Absent\u000aDermal LVI - Absent\u000aSkin invasion - Absent\u000aSkeletal muscle invasion - Not applicable\u000aFinal Margins (invasive)\u000aNegative (> REMOVED_DATE cm) - Inferior, anterior, posterior, medial\u000aClose (0.1 to REMOVED_DATE cm) - Superior (0.3 cm, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID)\u000aPositive (ink on carcinoma) - Lateral (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID; see also part D below)\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aTypes - Solid\u000aNuclear grade - Intermediate\u000aCalcifications in DCIS - Absent\u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - Absent\u000aExtent of DCIS\u000aNumber of blocks/total - REMOVED_DATE blocks\u000aMargins (DCIS)\u000aNegative (> REMOVED_DATE cm) - Posterior, medial, lateral\u000aClose (0.1 to REMOVED_DATE cm) - Anterior (0.3 cm, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID)\u000aVery close(<0.1 cm from margin)- Superior (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), inferior (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID)\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - Absent\u000aLYMPH NODES (including FSA)\u000aSentinel lymph nodes ? Negative (3 H&E levels examined)\u000aNumber of positive nodes - 0\u000aNumber of nodes examined - 2\u000aTOTAL POSITIVE NODES (all specimens)- REMOVED_DATE \u000aOTHER FINDINGS\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia\u000aCore biopsy site\u000aPapilloma\u000aAJCC Classification (6th edition) - REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDc REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID MX.\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER, PR, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) - Performed previously\u000aNOTE: There are two (2) foci of invasive carcinoma, measuring REMOVED_DATE cm and REMOVED_DATE \u000acm. Double stain for keratinous p63 confirms invasive carcinoma in both foci.\u000aSPECIMEN DESIGNATED "LEFT BREAST, TISSUE" (Part B):\u000aIntraductal papilloma with hyalinization.\u000aDuctal hyperplasia.\u000aSclerosing adenosis.\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy.\u000aSPECIMEN DESIGNATED "LATERAL SUPERIOR SHAVED MARGIN" (Part D):\u000aBenign breast tissue.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: CA of L breast.\u000aOperation: Wide excision L breast mass, lt sentinel node bx.\u000aOperative Findings: We took out "lt breast tissue" thinking tumor in it. Then\u000afound tumor lateral & took it out as "primary tumor site". Shave taken from\u000athere.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: L breast CA.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) left sentinel lymph nodes (fs).\u000aB/2) left breast tissue, short stitch/superior, long stitch/lateral.\u000aC/3) primary tumor site, short stitch/superior, long stitch/lateral.\u000aD/4) lateral superior shaved margin, short stitch/superior, long\u000astitch/lateral.\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000aArrival time: 3:40 PM\u000aReport time: 3:55 PM\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "#1 - LEFT SENTINEL LYMPH NODES" (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aTwo (2) lymph nodes negative for carcinoma.\u000aOR Consultation by: Lucian Chirieac, M.D.\u000aResident: STEFAN KRAFT, MD\u000aThe senior physician certifies that he/she personally conducted a gross and/or\u000amicroscopic examination of the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed\u000athe rapid diagnos(es) related thereto.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in four parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart A labeled, "#1. Left sentinel lymph node", consists of one fragment of\u000ayellow/tan fibroadipose tissue (3.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with two yellow/tan lymph\u000anodes. One lymph node (1.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) is bisected and submitted for\u000aintraoperative consultation as REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. The second lymph node (0.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm), inked blue and submitted for intraoperative consultation as REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. The\u000aremainder of the specimen is submitted for histologic evaluation.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID remnant, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID remnant, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Remainder of specimen, multi frags, ESS.\u000aPart B labeled, "#2. Left breast tissue", consists of a breast lumpectomy\u000aspecimen (medial to lateral REMOVED_DATE cm; anterior to posterior, REMOVED_DATE cm; inferior to\u000asuperior REMOVED_DATE cm) with attached skin ellipse at anterior surface (4.6 x REMOVED_DATE cm)\u000acomposed of tan, unremarkable skin. The specimen is marked by sutures: short\u000aequals superior, long equals lateral. The specimen is inked by the surgeon as\u000afollows; superior/red, inferior/green, lateral/yellow, medial/orange,\u000aanterior/blue, posterior/black. There is a central cavity (1.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm)\u000athat is surrounded by red/yellow adipose tissue and greater than 1 cm to all\u000amargins. The remainder of the specimen is composed entirely of adipose tissue.\u000aNo gross lesions are identified. The specimen is sectioned medial to lateral\u000aand representative sections are submitted for histologic evaluation.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Section containing cavity in relation to anterior, posterior,\u000ainferior and superior margins, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Section containing cavity in relation to anterior, posterior,\u000ainferior, and superior margins, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, radially sectioned, 7 frags, ESS.\u000aPart C labeled, "#3. Primary tumor site, left breast", consists of a breast\u000alumpectomy specimen (medial to lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm; anterior to posterior, REMOVED_DATE cm;\u000ainferior to superior, REMOVED_DATE cm) with attached skin ellipse (3.9 x REMOVED_DATE cm)\u000acomposed of tan, unremarkable skin. The specimen is marked by sutures: short\u000aequals superior, long equals lateral. The specimen is inked by the surgeon as\u000afollows; superior/red, inferior/green, lateral/yellow, medial/orange,\u000aanterior/blue, posterior/black. There is a firm, white nodule (2.1 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm) with associated hemorrhage that abuts the superior margin, is REMOVED_DATE cm to the\u000alateral margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to the anterior margin\u000aand REMOVED_DATE cm to the posterior margin, and is greater than REMOVED_DATE cm to the medial\u000amargin. The remainder of the specimen consists entirely of adipose tissue with\u000ano additional lesions identified grossly. The specimen is sectioned medial to\u000alateral and representative sections are submitted for histologic evaluation.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin, radially sectioned, 6 frags each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sections containing nodule and associated hemorrhage in relation\u000ato margins, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, radially sectioned, 6 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Additional superior, posterior margins, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Additional inferior, anterior margins, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aPart D labeled, "#4. Lateral superior shaved margin, short stitch/superior,\u000along/lateral", consists of a shave margin (medial to lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm; anterior\u000ato posterior, REMOVED_DATE cm; superior to inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm) that is marked by the\u000asurgeon, short stitch equals superior, long stitch equals lateral. The\u000aspecimen is inked on two surfaces by the surgeon: red to indicate the margin at\u000athe superior aspect of the specimen in Part C, and yellow to indicate the\u000amargin at the lateral aspect of the specimen in Part C. The remaining four\u000asurfaces are inked by the prosector as follows: superior (opposing red) equals\u000agreen, posterior equals black, anterior equals blue, medial (opposing yellow)\u000aequals orange. There is a hemorrhagic area (0.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) that is REMOVED_DATE cm\u000ato the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to the posterior\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm to the anterior margin, and greater than REMOVED_DATE cm to the medial\u000aand lateral margins. The remainder of the specimen is composed entirely of\u000aadipose tissue. No additional gross lesions are identified. The entire\u000aspecimen is submitted for histologic evaluation.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Entire specimen, multi frags, ESS.\u000aEM/lp\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-07-REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Gilbert Brodsky M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000aNOTE: On part B, "LEFT BREAST, TISSUE" , there is no malignancy seen upon\u000amicroscopic examination of the specimen, including margins.\u000aThe diagnosis is otherwise unchanged.\u000aAddendum #1 by Gilbert Brodsky M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
