ect. The opposite aspect\u000adisplays a suture, designating superior. This aspect is inked red. The\u000aspecimen is serially sectioned to reveal a focally chalky yellow cut surface,\u000awith no discrete masses or lesions are identified. The specimen is\u000asequentially submitted in its entirety.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross sections (micro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 2 frags each and\u000amicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 frag), ESS.\u000aPart B, "#2. Lt breast tissue inferior shaved margin, suture superior",\u000aconsists of an irregular portion of fibrofatty tissue (2.4 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm),\u000awhich is received previously inked green along one aspect. The opposite aspect\u000adisplays a suture, designating superior, and is inked red. The specimen is\u000atrisected, to reveal a yellow homogenous cut surface, with no discrete masses\u000aor lesions identified, and is submitted in its entirety.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 3 frags, ESS.\u000acp/lp\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Xiaohua Qian M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a1/8/2008\u000a[report_end]
