n H. Eichhorn, M.D. Signed On: 20 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 19:52 =============================================================================== *** IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum *** RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast (Left, block E): The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein. The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein. The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER-2/c-erbB-2. See note. Note: These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital. They have not been cleared or approved by the U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA). The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary; this laboratory has established and verified the test's accuracy and precision. Added by: Atul Kumar Bhan, M.D. Signed On: 22 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 11:08 *** FLUORESCENCE IN SITU HYBRIDIZATION Addendum *** RESULTS OF FLUORESCENCE IN SITU HYBRIDIZATION (FISH) FOR HER-2/NEU GENE AMPLIFICATION Breast (Left, block E): HER-2/neu gene in tumor cells: REMOVED_DATE (Not Amplified). See note. Note: Results are expressed as the average ratio of HER-2 to chromosome 17 signals in 60 tumor cell nuclei. A ratio of greater than REMOVED_DATE or equal to REMOVED_DATE indicates REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu gene amplification adjusted for chromosome 17 polysomy using PathVysion by Vysis. Added by: Grace T. McKee,MD Signed On: 24 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 14:43 GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "left breast", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm fibrofatty breast tissue with a short suture designating superior and a long suture designating lateral. The specimen is inked (anterior blue, posterior black, medial green, and lateral yellow), serially sectioned displaying a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm tan-yellow moderately defined dense fibrous area centrally located REMOVED_DATE cm from anterior, REMOVED_DATE cm from posterior, REMOVED_DATE cm from lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm from medial, REMOVED_DATE cm from superior, and REMOVED_DATE cm from inferior margins. The specimen is entirely submitted sequentially from superior to inferior in cassettes A-I. Received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "left breast additional deep margin" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm aggregate of tan-yellow lobulated fibroadipose tissue which is serially sectioned and entirely submitted in cassettes J-L. Received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "left final deep margin" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm aggregate of tan-yellow lobulated fibrofatty breast tissue which is serially sectioned and entirely submitted in cassettes M-N. Received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "final shaved anterior margin" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm aggregate of tan-yellow lobulated fibroadipose tissue which is serially sectioned and entirely submitted in cassettes O-P. Received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "final shaved superior REMOVED_DATE " is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm tan-yellow lobulated fibroadipose tissue which is serially sectioned and entirely submitted in cassettes Q-R. Received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "left breast inferior REMOVED_DATE " is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm aggregate of tan-yellow lobulated fibroadipose tissue which is serially sectioned and entirely submitted in cassette S. Gross Description by: JAMES BARRY Resident: RESIDENT-FREE SERVICE (JHE) =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: MGH-INPATIENT (FLR.UNKNOWN) REPORTS TO: Michele Annette Gadd, M.D. PART A: BREAST(LEFT),EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B: BREAST (LEFT FINAL DEEP MARGIN), EXCISION PART C: BREAS