VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY(IES)\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aLESTER, SUSAN, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST, CENTRAL OUTER, 11 G STEREOTACTIC CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR\u000aCALCIFICATIONS:\u000aATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA, best seen in the deeper levels of\u000ablock 2 (see note).\u000aApocrine cysts with calcium oxalate crystals (block 1).\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia.\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia.\u000aNote: The area of ADH closely approaches a diagnosis of ductal carcinoma\u000ain situ and would be evaluated best by excision. The ADH does not appear\u000ato be associated with calcifications.\u000aThis biopsy was also reviewed by Dr. James Connolly who concurred with the\u000adiagnosis.\u000aLEFT BREAST, UPPER OUTER, 11 G STEREOTACTIC CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR\u000aCALCIFICATIONS:\u000aATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA, associated with columnar alteration of\u000alobules with prominent snouts and secretions and calcifications (block 3;\u000alevels examined).\u000aApocrine cysts with calcifications.\u000aNote: ADH would be best evaluated by excision.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 61 year old female with two groups of heterogeneous calcifications\u000ain LUOQ (#2) and left central outer (#1) breast.\u000aOperation: 11g stereotactic breast core biopsy\u000aOperative findings: Calcifications in specimen\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Heterogeneous calcifications\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1) 12 biopsy specimens (2 sage cassettes - "A "with\u000acalcifications and "B")\u000a#2) 7 biopsy specimens (2 orange cassettes - "A" with\u000acalcifications and "B")\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by CARTER,MARK RYAN,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin in two parts, each labeled with the\u000apatient's name and unit number.\u000aPart one, labeled "left breast #1 anterior", and consists of two (2) light\u000agreen cassettes. One cassette is labeled "A" with calcifications and contains\u000amultiple, soft, fragmented, yellow to white tissue cores (1.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm\u000ain aggregate). The other cassette is labeled "B" and contains similar tissue\u000afragments (2.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate).\u000aMicro 1: "A", multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 2: "B", multi frags, ESS.\u000aPart two, labeled "left breast #2" posterior, and consists of two (2) orange\u000acassettes. One cassette is labeled "A" with calcifications and contains\u000amultiple, soft, fragmented, yellow to white tissue cores (1.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm\u000ain aggregate). The other cassette is labeled "B" and contains similar tissue\u000afragments (2.1 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate).\u000aMicro 3: "A", multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 4: "B", multi frags, ESS.\u000akks\u000aReports to: SEDGWICK, EMILY M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY(IES)\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY(IES)\u000a[report_end]
