VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST BIOPSY W/O MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aODZE, ROBERT, DANIEL, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by ODZE,ROBERT DANIEL,M.D.\u000a1. SPECIMEN LABELED "LEFT BREAST, EXCISION FOR CHRONIC INFLAMMATION:\u000aBreast tissue with inflammatory mass composed of acute abscess,\u000aabundant chronic inflammation, giant cell reaction, and\u000anecrotizing granulomas.\u000aSpecial stains will be reported in an addendum.\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: by ODZE,ROBERT DANIEL,M.D.\u000aGram-positive cocci are present in abscess cavities.\u000aNo micro-organisms present on MSS or AFB stains.\u000aNOTE: The case has been reviewed by Dr. Franz von Lichtenberg, who agrees.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: None given.\u000aOperation: Excision left breast chronic inflammation and chronic sinus\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast chronic infection\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1. Left breast chronic infection (short/superior;\u000along/lateral)\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by PADERA,ROBERT F.,JR.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in one part, labeled with the patient's name,\u000aunit number and "#1. left breast chronic infection", and consists of one piece\u000aof fibroadipose tissue with a short and a long suture measuring REMOVED_DATE cm medial\u000ato lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm anterior to posterior, and REMOVED_DATE cm superior to inferior. A\u000askin ellipse is attached to the anterior portion of the specimen measuring REMOVED_DATE \u000ax REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the\u000aevaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red;\u000ainferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. Upon sectioning there is\u000aa circumscribed cystic mass filled with tan mucopurulent debris. The cyst\u000ameasures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. It appears to be completely contained within the\u000aexcision specimen. It is located on the medial half of the specimen. Grossly\u000anormal-appearing breast tissue separates the circumscribed from the second\u000asmall region with similar mucopurulent material that measures REMOVED_DATE cm across.\u000aThis is located at the lateral half of the specimen.\u000aMicro 1: smaller cystic area, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 2: larger cystic area with perpendicular medial margin, 2 frags, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  grossly normal breast between the two cystic areas, 2 frags, RSS\u000aksc\u000aReports to: MATORY, YVEDT M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST BIOPSY W/O MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
