VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: KATHARINE CARTER M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Eleanor Y. Chen, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Jeffrey F Krane, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "RIGHT BREAST TISSUE AT REMOVED_DATE O'CLOCK", EXCISION FOR AN\u000aMRI IDENTIFIED MASS:\u000aBenign breast tissue with stromal and epithelial changes\u000aconsistent with treatment effect.\u000aBiopsy site identified.\u000aNo discrete mass forming lesion is identified.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: History of DCIS right breast; patient had abnormal right breast MRI\u000aand MRI core biopsy (clip left) showing atypia felt by the pathologist to be\u000aconsistent with radiation change; however, Dr. Frost (Radiology) has\u000arecommended excisional biopsy to exclude malignancy.\u000aOperation: Right mammographically directed breast biopsy.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal right breast MRI.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Right breast tissue at REMOVED_DATE o'clock short equals superior, long equals\u000alateral to mammo.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Specimen contains wire and clip; called to Dr. Carter in OR 11:10\u000aa.m. REMOVED_DATE  - GH/SR.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "#1. Right breast tissue short superior, long lateral", consists of a REMOVED_DATE x\u000a4.0 x REMOVED_DATE cm excision of fibroadipose tissue, oriented by sutures designating\u000asuperior (short suture) and lateral (long suture) margins. The specimen is\u000ainked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black;\u000aanterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange\u000a(inked by prosector). The localizing wire enters the inferior aspect of the\u000aspecimen and traverses superiorly. Specimen is received with a radiograph\u000ademonstrating a localizing wire in place within the specimen, adjacent to an\u000aencircled area of interest bearing a metallic clip. Sectioning in this area\u000ademonstrates an ill-defined firm tan/white fibrous lesion (maximally REMOVED_DATE cm),\u000a0.5 cm from the closest posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the closest anterior\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the closest superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the closest\u000ainferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the closest lateral margin, and remote (greater\u000athan REMOVED_DATE cm) from the medial margin. Previous biopsy site as marked by a REMOVED_DATE \u000acm metallic surgical clip is immediately adjacent to this lesion. Remaining\u000atissues shows scant tan/white fibrous tissue (less than 20% of specimen),\u000aadmixed with unremarkable tan/yellow, lobulated adipose tissue. Entire\u000aspecimen is submitted, sequentially from lateral to medial, with perpendicular\u000alateral margin in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and perpendicular medial margin in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. Majority of\u000alesion present in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Multi frags, ESS.\u000aDB/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: 4831.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jeffrey F Krane M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a2/3/2007\u000a[report_end]
