e. The cavity grossly comes to within REMOVED_DATE cm of the medial\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of\u000athe lateral margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the posterior margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm of the superior\u000amargin. The clip is identified within the spongy material within the cavity.\u000aThere are multiple clear fluid filled cysts (ranging from REMOVED_DATE up to REMOVED_DATE cm in\u000agreatest dimension). The remaining breast tissue is composed of approximately\u000a85% tan/white, dense fibrous stroma and 15% yellow lobulated adipose tissue.\u000aThe specimen is accompanied by a radiograph, exhibiting an intact hook wire,\u000aclip and probable associated calcification (see radiology report).\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Breast tissue sequentially from superior to inferior, multi\u000afrags, ESS.\u000aNote: Cavity in micro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. Areas of calcifications are\u000aprobably micro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000adfi/lp\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jason L Hornick M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a11/14/2008\u000a[report_end]
