VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST MASTECTOMY - PARTIAL OR SIMPLE\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aRENSHAW, ANDREW, ALEXANDER, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by RENSHAW,ANDREW ALEXANDER,M.D.\u000a#1. RIGHT BREAST, EXCISION FOR MASS (INCLUDING FSA):\u000aINVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA, REMOVED_DATE cm. moderately differentiated, modified\u000aBloom-Richardson grade 2 of 3.\u000aTumor extends to within REMOVED_DATE cm of the superior margin.\u000aAll other margins are negative.\u000aNo in-situ carcinoma seen.\u000aBiopsy site with repair reaction.\u000aFibrocystic change with epithelial hyperplasia.\u000a#2. SPECIMEN LABELED "AXILLARY CONTENTS":\u000aSeven lymph nodes with NO carcinoma seen.\u000a#3. SPECIMEN LABELED "SUPERIOR FACE" (INCLUDING FSB):\u000aFibrocystic change, proliferative, with epithelial hyperplasia.\u000aNo carcinoma seen.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: None given.\u000aOperation: Right breast lumpectomy and axillary node dissection.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast CA.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1 Right breast mass (frozen section), double suture =\u000asuperior margin, single suture = medial margin.\u000a#2 Right axillary contents.\u000a#3 Right breast, superior face; double suture marks\u000asite closest to tumor, single = superior, triple = medial.\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000a1. SPECIMEN LABELED "RIGHT BREAST MASS" (FSA):\u000aInvasive lobular carcinoma, extending to within REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aof the inked superior margin.\u000a3. SPECIMEN LABELED "SUPERIOR FACE" (FSB):\u000aBreast tissue.\u000aNo cancer seen.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by CHANG,SANDY,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen was received fixed in three parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart one is further designated "right breast mass" and consists of a tan skin\u000aellipse measuring 7 x REMOVED_DATE cm, excised to a depth of REMOVED_DATE cm. The skin ellipse\u000ahas a 2 cm well-healed scar. Two sutures are present, the long one designates\u000athe medial margin and the short double suture designates the superior margin.\u000aThere is a REMOVED_DATE cm stellate mass with a surrounding area of hemorrhage, which is\u000afirm to palpation, extends to within REMOVED_DATE cm of the superior margin. The mass\u000awas submitted as FSA. The breast mass was inked black in the frozen section\u000aroom to designate the superior margin and inked blue to designate the inferior\u000amargin. A hemorrhagic biopsy cavity, measuring REMOVED_DATE cm in diameter, is located\u000a0.6 cm from the medial margin.\u000aMicro 1: FSA remnant, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro 2: Superior perpendicular margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 3: Inferior perpendicular margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 4: Anteior perpendicular margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 5: Posterior perpendicular margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 6: Medial perpendicular margin and biopsy cavity, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 7: Lateral perpendicular margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 8: Additional breast tissue (medial margin), 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 9: Additional breast tissue (posterior margin), 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 10: Additional breast tissue, anterior, superior, and inferior margins,\u000a1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 11: Additional breast tissue, inferior margin, multiple frags, RSS.\u000aThe second part of the specimen is further designated "axillary contents" and\u000aconsists of yellow/tan, fibroadipose tissue soaked in Bouin's, measuring 10 x 5\u000ax REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate. Eight lymph nodes are isolated.\u000aMicro 12: One lymph node, multiple frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 13: Three lymph nodes, multiple frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Two lymph nodes per cassette, multiple frags, ESS.\u000aThe third part of the specimen is further designated "superior face" (double\u000asuture marks site closest to tumor, single superior, triple medial) and\u000aconsists of a fragment of yellow, fibroadipose tissue, measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1\u000acm. There is a double suture designating the site closest to the tumor which\u000ais inked red. A single suture designates the superior margin and a triple\u000asuture designates the medial margin. The site opposite to the tumor or near\u000athe margin is inked black in the frozen section room. No masses were detected\u000ain this specimen. A portion of the superior margin opposite the site of the\u000atumor was submitted as REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. The margin closest to the tumor is entirely\u000asubmitted.\u000aMicro 16: FSB remnant, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Perpendicular section through specimen, multiple frags, RSS.\u000aReports to: HECHTMAN, HERBERT, B. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY - PARTIAL OR SIMPLE\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: LYMPH NODES REGIONAL RESECTION\u000a[report_end]
