VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Amend/Addenda\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: KATHARINE CARTER M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-05-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000a********** Addended Report ***********\u000aResident: David Wu, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Jonathan N Glickman, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST EXCISION WIRE LOCALZATION FOR A CLIP (1 SPECIMEN):\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU.\u000aSYNOPSIS:\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU - Present\u000aTypes - Solid, cribriform, papillary\u000aNuclear grade - Intermediate\u000aCalcifications in DCIS - Absent\u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - Present\u000aMicroinvasion (<0.1cm) - Absent (see NOTE)\u000aExtent of DCIS\u000aSize (max area in one block): - REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aNumber of blocks/total: - REMOVED_DATE blocks\u000aFinal Margins (DCIS)\u000aNegative (>0.3 cm) Inferior\u000aClose (0.1-0.3 cm) (specify distance) Posterior (0.1 cm, blocks REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID)\u000aVery close (<0.1 cm) Medial (blocks REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), anterior (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID),\u000aSuperior, lateral (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID)\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - Absent\u000aOTHER FINDINGS - Core biopsy site\u000aSkeletal muscle\u000aSclerosing adenosis\u000aCalcifications\u000aAJCC CLASSIFICATION (6th edition) - Tis pNx MX\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER/PR/HER-2) - Pending\u000aNOTE: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID keratin/p63 immunostain examined, supporting the absence of\u000amicroinvasion. Case reviewed by Dr. A Richardson, Breast Pathology Service, who\u000aconcurs.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: S/P core bx @ BWH (ILLEGIBLE) nodule (0.8 cm) - showed ADH\u000aOperation: Right mammographically-directed breast biopsy.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast nodule.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000a#1 Right breast tissue; short=superior; long=lateral --> to mammo + then path\u000aRADIOLOGY REPORT:\u000aClip in specimen - Babaghian\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient?s name, unit number,\u000aand "1. Right breast tissue; short-superior, long-lateral, mammo + path", and\u000aconsists of a 45-gm oriented breast lumpectomy specimen (6 cm medial/lateral x\u000a5.5 cm superior/inferior x 3 cm anterior/posterior). The specimen is\u000aaccompanied by a radiograph labeled with the patient's name and unit number.\u000aand a report that reads "Clip in specimen". The specimen comes oriented by the\u000aby the surgeon, with a short suture designating superior, long designating\u000alateral, and a metallic wire that enters the lateral aspect of the specimen and\u000aexits towards the medial/posterior aspect. The specimen is inked by the\u000apathologist per protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black;\u000aanterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange.\u000aCorrelation with the radiograph suggests that the clip is located within the\u000amedial aspect of the specimen within 1 cm of the inked edge. Serially\u000asectioning reveals a metallic, S-shaped clip within a well-circumscribed area\u000aof white nodularity (0.6 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). Scattered discontinuously away from\u000athis foci of white tissue is, towards the anterior/superior margin, a\u000apoorly-circumscribed, heterogeneous, red/white/grey, partially hemorrhagic\u000adiscoloration (1.1 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). This area extends within less than REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aof the anterior/posterior/superior margin and is greater than 2 cm from the\u000ainferior/lateral margin. A portion of it extends to within less than REMOVED_DATE cm of\u000athe medial orange margin. The specimen is otherwise composed of yellow,\u000alobulated, adipose tissue composing 80% of the specimen. The fibrous areas are\u000aentirely submitted, sequentially from medial to lateral, including the area of\u000athe clip site.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial perpendicular margin, 3 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #1, multiple frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 2, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Clip site, Slice 3, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 4, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 5, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 6, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 7, multi frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 8, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 12, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral perpendicular margin, 3 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Additional Slice 7, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Additional Slice 9, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Additional Slice 10, 1 frag, RSS.\u000adwu/MMM\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by David Wu M.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jonathan N Glickman M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a5/19/2005\u000aSurgical Addendum: (5/19/05)\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor - positive\u000aProgesterone receptor - positive\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) - negative (1+)\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000acarcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but only\u000aa portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in >10%\u000aof tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in\u000a>10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aAddendum by Jonathan N Glickman M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aAddendum #1 by Andrea L Richardson M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a5/19/2005\u000a[report_end]
