VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast core needle biopsy\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: SUGHRA RAZA M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Mariana A. Stoleru, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Susan Lester, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, UPPER CENTRAL, 9 G MRI GUIDED CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR A 4 CM\u000aAREA OF REGIONAL HETEROGENEOUS ENHANCEMENT:\u000aCARCINOMA IN SITU, solid type (low to intermediate grade), extensively\u000ainvolving sclerosing adenosis (see note). An immunoperoxidase study for\u000acytokeratin REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and p63 confirms the presence of myoepithelial cells.\u000aNo necrosis is seen.\u000aCalcifications are associated with sclerosing adenosis, including some\u000aareas involved by CIS.\u000aFibroadenomatoid changes are present.\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies are performed with the following results for\u000aCIS (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu NEGATIVE (0)\u000aE-cadherin PREDOMINANTLY NEGATIVE\u000aNote: The histologic appearance of the CIS and the absence of e-cadherin\u000aare compatible with a diagnosis of lobular carcinoma in situ. However, the\u000alesion is difficult to classify due to the involvement of sclerosing adenosis.\u000aThe lesion would be evaluated best with excision.\u000aLEFT BREAST, UPPER OUTER, 14 G ULTRASOUND GUIDED CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR A\u000aGREATER THAN REMOVED_DATE CM AREA OF ARCHITECTURAL DISTORTION:\u000aCARCINOMA IN SITU, solid type (low to intermediate grade), extensively\u000ainvolving sclerosing adenosis (see note). An immunoperoxidase study for\u000acytokeratin REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and p63 confirms the presence of myoepithelial cells.\u000aNo necrosis is seen.\u000aFibroadenomatoid changes are present.\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies are performed with the following results for\u000aCIS (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu NEGATIVE (1+)\u000aE-cadherin WEAK\u000aNote: The histologic appearance of the CIS and the absence of e-cadherin\u000aare compatible with a diagnosis of lobular carcinoma in situ. However, the\u000alesion is difficult to classify due to the involvement of sclerosing adenosis.\u000aThe lesion would be evaluated best with excision.\u000aThe findings are very similar to the ones in the contralateral breast.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHISTORY: 50 year old woman with screening mammogram showing bilateral\u000aarchitectural distortion.\u000aBREAST IMAGING FINDING:\u000a1. Right: ~4 cm, nonpalpable, regional, heterogeneous and non-mass forming\u000aenhancement on MRI. Architectural distortion on mammogram.\u000a2. Left: > REMOVED_DATE cm architectural distortion on US.\u000aLOCATION:\u000a1. Right: Upper central\u000a2. Left: Upper outer\u000aTYPE OF CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY:\u000a1. 9 G MRI\u000a2. 14 G Ultrasound\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Right: White bottom, green top - 2 cassettes. Formalin at 9:00 am.\u000aB/2. Left: In formalin 12:05 p.m. - White cassette.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit\u000anumber, and "Green top, white bottom right breast", and consists of gross\u000afibroadipose tissue, received in two white cassettes, each with a green lid,\u000aand designated one from another. The first (arbitrary) contains cores\u000aaggregating REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm, entirely submitted in micro cassette REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aSecond cassette (arbitrary) contains cores aggregating REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm,\u000aentirely submitted micro cassette REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: White cassette green lid cores, multi frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, is received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "Left breast white cassette", and consists of multiple yellow-white\u000afibrofatty tissues (aggregating REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which are received in a\u000awhite cassette. The specimen is submitted in toto.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Multi frags, ESS.\u000aCP/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on Monday\u000aREMOVED_MONTH 09, 2009 at 04:20:16PM\u000a[report_end]
