nge cassette is\u000alabeled "B", and contains multiple cylindrical focally hemorrhagic fibrofatty\u000asoft tissues (1.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate). Specimen is submitted in toto.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Contents of orange cassette labeled "ACA++", multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Contents of orange cassette labeled "B", multi frags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000ajc/ag.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Deborah A Dillon M.D., Electronically signed on Monday\u000aREMOVED_MONTH 20, 2009 at 01:02:43PM\u000a[report_end]
