VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ROGER L CHRISTIAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Paul A. VanderLaan, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Jane E. Brock, M.B., B.S., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. LEFT BREAST, MEDIAL WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aCalcifications associated with columnar cell change (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aThe margins were inked and evaluated for the final diagnosis.\u000aB. LEFT BREAST, LATERAL WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A CLIP AND CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aATYPICAL HYPERPLASIA, see NOTE.\u000aCalcifications in normal epithelium.\u000aBiopsy site changes.\u000aThe margins were inked and evaluated for the final diagnosis.\u000aNOTE: A residual single lobule (0.1 cm) is partially involved by an atypical\u000alobular proliferation (adjacent to the biopsy site). The nuclear grade of the\u000aatypical cells is higher than usually seen in classic ALH. Margins of the\u000aspecimen are uninvolved (> REMOVED_DATE cm).\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Lt brst, area of calcs, area of ADH.\u000aOperation: Wire-directed excis.\u000aOperative Findings: See op note.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Lt brst, area of calcs, area of ADH.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) Medial area microcalcification, L breast (F.S.).\u000aB/2) Lateral area ADH L breast (F.S.).\u000aRADIOLOGY: Specimen image shows wire and cluster of Ca++; called to Dr.\u000aChristian's OR by E. Lizer.\u000aClip, calcifications and wire. Phoned to O.R. by E. Lizer at 12;10 p.m.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThis is a specimen received fresh, in two parts, both labeled with the\u000apatient's name and medical record number.\u000aPart A, "#1. Medial area microcalcification, left breast". The specimen\u000aconsists of a REMOVED_DATE gram lumpectomy that was oriented per the surgeon such that a\u000ashort stitch designates superior and a long stitch designates lateral. The\u000aspecimen measures REMOVED_DATE cm anterior to posterior, REMOVED_DATE cm superior to inferior,\u000aand REMOVED_DATE cm medial to lateral. The specimen is inked by the surgeon in the OR\u000asuch that red designates superior, green designates inferior, orange designates\u000amedial, yellow designates lateral, black designates posterior and blue\u000adesignates anterior. Accompanying the specimen is a mammogram showing a wire\u000aentering the anterior aspect of the specimen localizing an area of\u000acalcifications. No clip is present on the radiograph. The specimen is\u000aserially sectioned from inferior to superior and entirely submitted for\u000ahistology. The specimen is predominantly yellow lobulated fatty tissue with a\u000alittle white fibrous tissue.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Inferior end, perpendicular sections, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID through REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Serial slices, inferior to superior, 7 frags total, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Superior end, perpendicular sections, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, "#2. Lateral area ADH, left breast". The specimen consists of a\u000a9.6-gram portion of breast tissue that was oriented per the surgeon such that a\u000ashort stitch designates superior and a long stitch designates lateral. The\u000aspecimen measures REMOVED_DATE cm anterior to posterior, REMOVED_DATE cm superior to inferior,\u000aand REMOVED_DATE cm medial to lateral. The specimen is inked by the surgeon in the OR\u000asuch that red designates superior, green designates inferior, orange designates\u000amedial, yellow designates lateral, black designates posterior and blue\u000adesignates anterior. Also received with the specimen in the container is a\u000awire but the wire is not attached to the specimen. A radiograph accompanying\u000athe specimen demonstrates a surgical clip and the detached wire. Most of the\u000aspecimen has a firm tan/yellow consistency. The specimen is serially sectioned\u000afrom inferior to superior to reveal a previous biopsy site with the clip\u000a(located in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) abutting the anterior surface and measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000aThe remainder of the breast tissue is predominantly yellow lobulated fatty\u000atissue with focal firmer white fibrous areas. The entire specimen is submitted\u000afor histology.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Inferior end, perpendicular sections, 5 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID through REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Serial section, inferior to superior, 1 frag per\u000acassette, clip in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Superior end, perpendicular sections, 5 frags, ESS.\u000aPVA/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jane E. Brock M.B., B.S., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000aSunday REMOVED_MONTH 28, 2009 at 09:37:15AM\u000a[report_end]
