rt #1, "upper outer quadrant calcifications," consists of multiple fragments\u000aof fibrofatty tissue measuring in aggregate REMOVED_DATE x 5 x REMOVED_DATE cm. The largest\u000afragment of tissue measures 4 x 4 x REMOVED_DATE cm and has two metal wires to identify\u000aareas of microcalcifications corresponding to the mammogram.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  larger fragment of tissue, multiple frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  smaller fragments of tissue, ESS.\u000aPart #2, "retro-areolar calcifications," consists of a segment of breast tissue\u000ameasuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. A needle wire is present in the specimen. The\u000aspecimen is inked and entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  breast tissue, multiple frags, ESS.\u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
