VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST MASTECTOMY W/REGIONAL LYMPH NODES\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aDIAGNOSIS: by WELCH,WILLIAM ROBERT,M.D.\u000a1) RIGHT BREAST, SIMPLE MASTECTOMY:\u000aNo residual tumor present.\u000aBenign breast tissue with fibrosis, radiation changes,\u000amicrocalcifications, and focal secretory changes.\u000aForeign body reaction consistent with prior biopsy site.\u000aFibrosclerotic nodule (1.5 cm) with giant cell reaction (axilla, at the\u000abowtie); no tumor present in this nodule.\u000aOne (1) lymph node; no tumor present.\u000a2) SKIN, RIGHT BREAST:\u000aSkin with cicatrix.\u000a3) LEFT BREAST, TISSUE:\u000aSkin and benign breast tissue wtih fibrosis and cysts.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 37-year-old female with right breast cancer.\u000aOperation: Right simple mastectomy, free flap reconstruction.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast cancer.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Right breast with nipple marked at short superior, long\u000alateral, bowtie in axilla, positive palpable node to mammo at 11:00.\u000a2. Right breast skin.\u000a3. Left breast tissue.\u000aMammography report: Few small foci of calcification marked. Meyer.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by MAGI GALLUZZI,CRISTINA,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in three parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart one, labeled "right breast with nipple (marked at short suture, long\u000alateral, bowtie in axilla)", consists of a simple mastectomy specimen weighing\u000a425 grams and measuring 18 x 13 x 5 cm with an axillary tail measuring 14 x 4\u000ax REMOVED_DATE cm. The nipple and areolar skin are present in the specimen measuring\u000a1.3 and REMOVED_DATE cm in diameter, respectively. A short suture marks superior, a\u000along suture marks lateral and a bowtie defines the axillary tail. A REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000ax REMOVED_DATE cm cavity is present underneath the nipple. A 4 x 3 x REMOVED_DATE cm cavity is\u000apresent in the inferior outer quadrant (IOQ), REMOVED_DATE cm from the deep resection\u000amargin. The parenchyma surrounding both cavities consists of fibroadipose\u000atissue with no palpable masses identified. A REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm hemorrhagic\u000aarea is present underneath the larger cavity. The parenchyma in proximity to\u000athe hemorrhagic area is firm for about REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm and is REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000athe deep resection margin. The remaining parenchyma consists of fibrofatty\u000atissue. A REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm white-gray, firm, spiculated area is present in\u000athe "axilla", REMOVED_DATE cm from the deep resection margin. A few lymph nodes are\u000aidentified in the axillary tail.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  cavity underneath the nipple, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  cavity in the IOQ, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 5: hemorrhagic area underneath the larger cavity, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 6: firm area in proximity to the hemorrhagic area, 2 frags, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  larger cavity and deep resection margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  firm nodule in the axillary tail, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 11: upper outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 12: lower outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 13: lower inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 14: upper inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 15: nipple, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE possible lymph nodes of the axillary tail, multi frags, RSS.\u000aPart two, labeled "Right breast skin", consists of an irregular segment of\u000aunpigmented skin, measuring 18 x REMOVED_DATE cm and excised to a depth of REMOVED_DATE cm. A\u000a1.2 cm well-healed scar is present in the specimen.\u000aMicro 18: skin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aPart three, labeled "Left breast tissue", consists of multiple fragments of\u000afibrofatty tissue partially covered by unpigmented skin weighing in total 200\u000agrams, and measuring 15 x 13 x 4 cm in aggregate. The cut surface of the\u000aspecimen shows multiple areas of fibrosis ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. No distinct masses are identified in the specimen.\u000aMicro 19: skin, multi frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  fibrous areas, 4 frags, RSS.\u000aReports to: PRIBAZ, JULIAN, JOSEPH M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY W/REGIONAL LYMPH NODES\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SKIN, PLASTIC REPAIR\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST BIOPSY W/O MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
