e surgeon in\u000aaccordance with the pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins:\u000aposterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow;\u000amedial/orange. Ink is reapplied to the surfaces. An accompanying specimen\u000aradiograph demonstrates the shaft of the wire and a clip localized to an\u000airregularly-shaped, radio-dense mass. Sectioning reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm,\u000arelatively well-delineated, firm, white mass with a central biopsy site and\u000aclip located within REMOVED_DATE cm of the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE \u000acm from the lateral margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial and lateral margin, perpendicular, 2 frags each,\u000aRSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 6, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 7, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 8, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 9, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 10, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aVKV/lp\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by William R Welch M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
