; medial/orange.\u000aThere is a REMOVED_DATE cm ill-defined white/tan firm fibrous area including the biopsy\u000asite, which corresponds to the clip and fibrous area on the radiograph. The\u000afibrous area focally abuts the posterior margin and comes to within REMOVED_DATE cm to\u000athe inferior margin, at least REMOVED_DATE cm to the superior margin, at least REMOVED_DATE cm to\u000athe medial margin and REMOVED_DATE cm to the anterior margin. The remainder breast\u000aparenchyma is composed of predominantly adipose tissue. The specimen is\u000aserially sectioned from inferior to superior and entirely submitted for\u000ahistologic examination.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Serial sections from inferior to superior, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID including the\u000afibrous lesion, biopsy site, and surrounding breast parenchyma, multi frags,\u000aESS.\u000aELC/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-07-REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Hejin P Hahn M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a6/26/2007\u000a[report_end]
