ote. Note: These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital. They have not been cleared or approved by the U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA). The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary; this laboratory has established and verified the test's accuracy and precision. Added by: Grace T. McKee,MD Signed On: 14 REMOVED_MONTH 02 at 10:17 GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name and unit number, and "sentinel node hot and blue level I (1080)" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm previously blue dyed, tan, rubbery, fatty lymph node which is bisected and entirely submitted as A-B. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name and unit number, and "right breast lumpectomy" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm fibrofatty breast tissue which has short suture designating superior and a long suture designating lateral. The specimen is black inked along the anterior, blue inked along the posterior, and red inked along the lateral aspect. The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a 80% dens,e white fibrous to 10% yellow lobulated fatty tissue surface which contains a poorly delineated REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm poorly delineated grey-white firm area (? mass) which comes to within REMOVED_DATE cm of the posterior, REMOVED_DATE cm of the lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm of the anterior and medial, REMOVED_DATE cm of the inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm of the superior margins. The remaining fibrous tissue abuts all margins. Representative sections are submitted sequentially from superior to inferior as follows: C: superior margin D: fibrous tissue to anterior margin E: fibrous tissue to medial posterior margin F: fibrous tissue to medial anterior margin G: fibrous tissue to posterior margin H: fibrous tissue to posterior margin I: fibrous tissue to medial anterior margin J: ? mass to lateral posterior margin K: ? mass to lateral posterior margin L-M: full thickness sections remainder of mass with the posterior lateral margin in L and the medial margin in N. N: medial margin Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name and unit number, and "final shaved margins lateral half of cavity" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm aggregate of fibrofatty tissue which is serially sectioned and entirely submitted as O-Q. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name and unit number, and "final shaved margins, medial half of cavity" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm aggregate of fibrofatty tissue fragments which are serially sectioned and entirely submitted as R-U. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name and unit number, and "additional lateral tissue" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm fibrofatty tissue which is bisected and entirely submitted as V. Gross Description by: LORI MARINI Resident: TAI-YUAN LIN, MD =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT - REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID REPORTS TO: Barbara Lynn Smith, M.D. PART A: LYMPH NODE (SENTINEL LEVEL 1 #1080), EXCISION PART B: BREAST (RIGHT), LUMPECTOMY PART C: BREAST (LATERAL HALF OF CAVITY), FINAL SHAVED MARG PART D: BREAST (MEDIAL HALF OF CAVITY), FINAL SHAVED MARGI PART E: BREAST (LATERAL "ADDITIONAL TISSUE"), EXCISION
