VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast core needle biopsy\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: EREN D YEH M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Joanna A Gibson, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Susan Lester, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, 4:00, 14 G ULTRASOUND GUIDED CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR A 1 CM,\u000aIRREGULAR MASS:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA, moderately differentiated (modified Bloom-Richardson\u000agrade II/III) with ductal and lobular features, measuring at least REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000aLymphovascular invasion is present (focal - also present on the\u000aimmunohistochemical study for ER).\u000aNo carcinoma in situ is seen in this limited specimen.\u000aImmunohistochemical studies are performed with the following results for\u000ainvasive carcinoma (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu NEGATIVE (1+)\u000aRIGHT BREAST, 3:00, 14 G ULTRASOUND GUIDED CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR A REMOVED_DATE CM\u000aIRREGULAR MASS:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA, moderately differentiated (modified Bloom-Richardson\u000agrade II/III) with ductal and lobular features, measuring at least REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000aNo lymphovascular invasion is seen in this limited specimen.\u000aCARCINOMA IN SITU, solid type (intermediate nuclear grade), without\u000anecrosis or calcifications, is present. Patchy immunoreactivity is seen for\u000ae-cadherin. The CIS is positive for ER and PR and shows weak to moderate\u000apositivity for REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu. Final classification as lobular carcinoma in situ\u000aor ductal carcinoma in situ would be made best after excision.\u000aImmunohistochemical studies are performed with the following results for\u000ainvasive carcinoma (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu NEGATIVE (1+)\u000aE-cadherin NEGATIVE\u000aNote: The two carcinomas are similar in histologic appearances.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHISTORY: 64 year old female with right breast solid masses at 4:00 and 3:00,\u000a? cancer.\u000aBREAST IMAGING FINDING:\u000a1. Right: 1 cm, Nonpalpable irregular mass.\u000a2. Right: 6 mm, Nonpalpable irregular mass; 2 cm between lesions.\u000aLOCATION:\u000a1. Right: 4:00\u000a2. Right: 3:00\u000aTYPE OF CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY:\u000a1. 14 G Ultrasound\u000a2. 14 G Ultrasound\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. 5 cores - Orange cassette\u000aB/2. 3 cores - Yellow cassette.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, in two parts, each labeled with the\u000apatient's name and unit number.\u000aPart A, "4 o'clock, site #1, right breast", consists of multiple white-yellow\u000afocally hemorrhagic fibrofatty tissues (aggregating REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which\u000aare received in an orange cassette "right." The specimens are submitted in\u000atoto.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Multi frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, "Site #2, 3 o'clock, right breast", consists of multiple yellow-white\u000afocally hemorrhagic fibrofatty tissues (aggregating REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which\u000aare received in a yellow cassette "Right site #2." The specimens are submitted\u000ain toto.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Multi frags, ESS.\u000aCP/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a3/18/2008\u000a[report_end]
