VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Consult material\u000aProcedure Date:\u000aOrdering Provider: JULIE L JONES M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Rachel L Rucker-Schmidt, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Jane E. Brock, M.B., B.S., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aCONSULT SLIDES FROM FAULKNER HOSPITAL, BOSTON, MA:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, MASTECTOMY, AND SENTINEL LYMPH NODE BIOPSIES (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID;\u000a4/7/2008):\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA with ductal and lobular features, moderately differentiated\u000a(modified Bloom-Richardson grade II/III), measuring REMOVED_DATE cm (by gross report and\u000amicroscopic correlation, see NOTE).\u000aInvasive carcinoma is associated with prior biopsy site changes x 2 and with\u000afocal calcifications.\u000aOne focus of lymphovascular invasion is present in the slides submitted for\u000areview (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aCARCINOMA IN SITU with mixed ductal and lobular features, solid type (low and\u000aintermediate nuclear grade) is present in four (4) of four (4) slides submitted\u000afor review (in 11 of 20 blocks, by report), present away from the invasive\u000atumor (EIC positive).\u000aCIS is associated with rare calcifications, by report, but not necrosis.\u000aBy report, immunoperoxidase stains for E-cadherin performed at the outside\u000ahospital are negative in the invasive and in situ carcinomas.\u000aBy report, the deep margin is negative for invasive carcinoma (> REMOVED_DATE cm).\u000aCIS, low nuclear grade, is present as a single duct profile REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000adeep margin (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aISOLATED TUMOR CELLS are present in one (1) lymph node, by report of total four\u000a(4) lymph nodes, including one (1) of two (2) sentinel lymph nodes and zero (0)\u000aof two (2) intra-parenchymal lymph nodes. On review of the pankeratin stained\u000asentinel lymph node, approximately REMOVED_DATE keratin positive cells are present as\u000ascattered single cells within the lymph node sinus. These cells are not seen on\u000athe corresponding H&E stained slide.\u000aNOTE: By report, two tumor masses were identified grossly, measuring REMOVED_DATE cm and\u000a1.2 cm, located REMOVED_DATE cm from each other, each associated with a prior biopsy\u000aclip. By report, sections of breast tissue between the masses reveal foci of\u000ainvasive carcinoma, suggesting that the two masses are part of a larger,\u000acontinuous invasive carcinoma, estimated to be REMOVED_DATE cm in size.\u000aThis tumor could be classified as: AJCC Classification (6th edition): REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID(i+).\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Right breast cancer\u000aClinical Diagnosis: IDLC and LVI\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aConsult slides.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aReceived from Faulkner Hospital, Pathology Department, 1153 Centre Street,\u000aBoston, MA REMOVED_CASE_ID, are eight (8) glass slides.\u000aThe slides are labeled "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" and sublabeled "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID (3)", "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID PANCK(2)", "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPANCK(6)", "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID (1)", "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID (1)", "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID (1)" and "REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID (1)", corresponding to A)\u000aright axillary sentinel lymph node #1 excision (0.9 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) C) right\u000abreast total mastectomy (31 x 20 x 6 cm) performed on REMOVED_DATE  according to the\u000aaccompanying pathology report bearing the patient's name.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jane E. Brock M.B., B.S., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a4/18/2008\u000a[report_end]
