VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, mastectomy with regional lymph nodes\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: KATHARINE CARTER M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Marianna B Ruzinova, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Jane E. Brock, M.B., B.S., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. LEFT BREAST, MASTECTOMY (336 gm):\u000aCARCINOMA IN SITU with predominantly lobular features, solid type, (low nuclear\u000agrade), with focal microcalcifications and without necrosis is present in 6 of\u000a10 blocks.\u000aCIS is adjacent to excision site changes in the upper outer quadrant, focally\u000ain the nipple ducts, and as scattered foci in grossly unremarkable sections\u000afrom the lower inner and lower outer quadrants.\u000aSpecial studies were performed at BWH with the following results for CIS,\u000a(block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aESTROGEN RECEPTOR POSITIVE\u000aPROGESTERONE RECEPTOR POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/NEU NEGATIVE (0)\u000aNo lymphovascular invasion is present.\u000aNo residual invasive carcinoma is seen.\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia\u000aNipple with focal involvement of nipple ducts with LCIS.\u000aThe deep margin is negative for tumor.\u000aOther findings:\u000aFlorid epithelial hyperplasia\u000aIntraductal papilloma.\u000aColumnar cell change, cysts and calcifications.\u000aIn combination with Faulkner Pathology (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID; REMOVED_DATE ), AJCC\u000aClassification (6th edition): REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDb REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID (sn)(i+)\u000aB. RIGHT BREAST, MASTECTOMY (368 gm):\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU, in the lower outer quadrant.\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia\u000aOther findings:\u000aNipple adenoma (0.5 cm) with focal ADH\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia\u000aSclerosing adenosis\u000aColumnar cell change with cysts and calcifications.\u000aFibroadenomatoid change\u000aApocrine cysts\u000aThe deep margin is negative for tumor.\u000aAJCC Classification (6th edition): Tis\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: S/P Right breast bx 2006, showing LCIS; S/P Left wire-loc REMOVED_DATE \u000ashowing LCIS with DCIS with REMOVED_DATE mm focus invasive lobular cancer, insufficient\u000atissue for receptors. OR REMOVED_DATE  - sentinel node mapping with 2 clusters\u000aisolated tumor cells in 1 out of 2 SN. See MR path reports.\u000aOperation: bilateral total mastectomies.\u000aOperative Findings: None specified.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast cancer.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) Left breast; short = superior; long = lateral.\u000aB/2) Right breast; short = superior; long = lateral.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart A, "Left breast tissue", consists of a 336-g mastectomy specimen (23.0 x\u000a15.5 x REMOVED_DATE cm) with a long stitch designating lateral and a short stitch\u000adesignating superior per the surgeon. The specimen is partially surfaced by a\u000atan-white skin ellipse (5.8 x REMOVED_DATE cm) which exhibits an everted tan/brown\u000anipple (1.3 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), is tan-pink, smooth and intact with no skeletal\u000amuscles. The specimen is serially sectioned to exhibit a tan-white, stellate\u000aslightly indurated centrally hemorrhagic mass (1.6 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) located in\u000athe upper outer quadrant, REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior aspect. Extending from the\u000amass is tan-white nodular fibrocystic tissue with foci of blue-domed cyst (0.3\u000acm in greatest dimension). The remainder of the specimen consists of\u000aapproximately 60% dense white fibrous tissue to 40% yellow lobulated adipose\u000atissue. The most lateral tissue is examined for intramammary lymph node\u000acandidate, none of which are identified.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Upper outer quadrant to include stellate mass, in relationship to\u000adeep margin, 3 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lower outer quadrant, 2 frags in each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Upper inner quadrant, 2 frags in each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lower inner quadrant, multi frags total, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Nipple, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aPart B, "Right breast", consists of a 368-g mastectomy specimen (21.5 x REMOVED_DATE x\u000a1.5 cm) with a long stitch designating lateral and a short stitch designating\u000asuperior per the surgeon. The specimen is partially surfaced by a tan-white\u000aunremarkable skin ellipse (5.5 x REMOVED_DATE cm) which exhibits a tan/brown everted\u000anipple (1.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), with a posterior aspect of the specimen (inked\u000ablack) is tan-pink, smooth, intact and exhibits no skeletal muscles. The\u000aspecimen is serially sectioned to exhibit approximately 60% dense, nodular\u000afibrocystic tissue to 40% yellow unremarkable lobulated adipose tissue. Upon\u000afurther sectioning, pinpoint foci of yellow soft material exude from the\u000afibrous tissue from the more cystic areas a tan-yellow and mucinous fluid is\u000areleased. In the lower outer quadrant is a hemorrhagic cystic cavity (0.7 x\u000a0.7 x REMOVED_DATE cm) possibly consistent with a ? previous biopsy site. No definitive\u000amasses or lesions are identified. The most lateral tissues are examined for\u000apossible intramammary lymph node candidate, none of which are identified.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Upper outer quadrant, multi frags total, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lower outer quadrant to include hemorrhagic cystic cavity in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aand REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, multi frags total, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Upper inner quadrant, 2 frags in each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lower inner quadrant, 2 frags in each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Nipple, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aJenC/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-08-REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jane E. Brock M.B., B.S., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a10/8/2008\u000a[report_end]
