VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: JULIE L JONES M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-06-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Ann K Folkins, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Jonathan N Glickman, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A CLIP MARKING AN AREA OF\u000aCALCIFICATIONS:\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, clinging type (high nuclear grade) with apocrine\u000afeatures, is present involving a complex sclerosing lesion in 5 of 7 blocks\u000a(see note).\u000aCalcifications are present associated with the complex sclerosing lesion. The\u000acalcifications do not appear to be specifically associated with DCIS. No\u000anecrosis is seen.\u000aThe prior core needle biopsy site is present within the complex sclerosing\u000alesion.\u000aDCIS is < REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior, medial, posterior, anterior, and lateral\u000amargins. The superior margin is not well seen in the sections.\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies reveal that the majority of the DCIS is negative for\u000aestrogen and progesterone receptors. Focal positivity cannot be excluded due\u000ato the involvement of the sclerosing lesion. Some areas of the DCIS are\u000anegative for REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu and other areas show patchy moderate membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity.\u000aNote: This is an unusual form of DCIS. The degree of nuclear atypia (with\u000aanaplastic appearing nuclei in some areas) and the presence of occasional\u000aatypical mitotic figures, warrants a diagnosis of DCIS.\u000aThis case was reviewed by Dr. Susan Lester and Dr. Deborah Dillon, who concur\u000awith this interpretation.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Left breast calcifications with severe atypia on core needle biopsy.\u000aOperation: Left breast wire-localized excisional biopsy.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast atypia on core biopsy.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) Left breast wire-localized excision; short suture - superior, long\u000alateral to mammo via Frozen Section Room.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Ca++, clip wire in specimen. OR called. Dr. Sughra Raza\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patients name, unit number,\u000aand "1. Left breast wire-localized excision; short suture - superior, long -\u000alateral, to mammo", and consists of one (1) breast excision specimen (2.0 cm\u000asuperior to inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm medial to lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm anterior to posterior)\u000awith a wire extending into the anterior portion of the specimen. The specimen\u000ais inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: Posterior/\u000ablack; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow;\u000amedial/orange. The specimen is sectioned into seven (7) slices from medial to\u000alateral, and there is a central area of firm white tissue (0.9 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm)\u000asurrounding the wire. The firm tissue is grossly abutting the inferior margin\u000aand is REMOVED_DATE cm to the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to the medial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to\u000athe lateral margin, less than REMOVED_DATE cm to the posterior margin and REMOVED_DATE cm to the\u000aanterior margin. An accompanying specimen radiograph demonstrates the wire\u000awith a clip and several calcifications within the specimen. The specimen is\u000aentirely submitted from medial to lateral\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 1, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 2, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 3, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 4, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 5, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 6, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 7, 5 frags, ESS.\u000aAF/mmm\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jonathan N Glickman M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a6/29/2006\u000a[report_end]
