VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Sentinel Lymph Nodes(s)\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: JULIE L JONES M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-06-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Elizabeth A. Steensma, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Jeffrey F Krane, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "RIGHT AXILLARY SENTINEL NODES" (including REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aTwo lymph nodes, negative for tumor (0:2).\u000aB. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "RIGHT BREAST, SIMPLE MASTECTOMY":\u000aBenign breast tissue with ductal ectasia, apocrine metaplasia,\u000alactational change, cysts, and fibroadenomatous changes.\u000aSkin with no significant pathologic change.\u000aC. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "LEFT SENTINEL NODES" (including FSB):\u000aThree lymph nodes, negative for tumor (0:3).\u000aD. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "LEFT BREAST, SIMPLE MASTECTOMY":\u000aBenign breast tissue with florid epithelial hyperplasia,\u000abiopsy site changes, apocrine cysts, lactational changes,\u000aruptured cysts, sclerosing adenosis, and microcalcifications.\u000aSkeletal muscle with no significant pathologic change.\u000aNOTE:\u000aThis case was reviewed by Dr. Deborah Dillon, Breast Pathology Service, who\u000aconcurs.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Left breast DCIS, status post lumpectomy with positive margins.\u000aOperation: Bilateral total mastectomy and SNB.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast DCIS.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Right axillary sentinel node (FS).\u000aB/2. Right breast, suture on superior skin.\u000aC/3. Left sentinel nodes (FS).\u000aD/4. Left breast (stitch on superior skin).\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "#1. RIGHT AXILLARY SENTINEL NODE" (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aTwo (2) lymph nodes negative for tumor.\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED #3. LEFT SENTINEL NODE FOR FS" (FSB):\u000a3 lymph nodes with no tumor seen.\u000aOR Consultation by: WILLIAM WELCH, M.D.; SCOTT R. GRANTER, M.D.\u000aResident: WAI CHIN FOO, MD; ANN FOLKINS, M.D.\u000aThe senior physician certifies that he/she personally conducted a gross and/or\u000amicroscopic examination of the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed\u000athe rapid diagnos(es) related thereto.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in four parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart A, "#1. Right axillary sentinel node FS", consists of two lymph nodes, REMOVED_DATE \u000ax REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm (previously bisected and entirely submitted as REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), and REMOVED_DATE x\u000a0.9 x REMOVED_DATE cm (previously bisected and entirely submitted as REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID remnant, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID remnant, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, "#2. Right breast, stitch on superior skin", consists of a 545-gram,\u000a17.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm right simple mastectomy specimen. The attached REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm brown/tan skin ellipse demonstrates a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm brown areola with a\u000acentral REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm everted, unremarkable nipple. There are no scars or other\u000aabnormalities on the skin surface. A suture designates the superior border.\u000aThe deep surface of the specimen is comprised of a smooth, intact fascial plane\u000a(inked black). Sectioning demonstrates irregular-appearing granular fibrodense\u000atissue comprising at least 60% of the specimen, which diffusely shows dilated\u000aductal spaces filled with a thick, white, creamy material (maximum dimension of\u000airregular tissue is 13 cm). There are no definitive palpable masses. There is\u000ascant identifiable uninvolved fibrous tissue. There are no palpable lymph\u000anodes in the lateral soft tissue.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Nipple, central deep, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Central breast tissue, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Upper inner quadrant, 4 frags total, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lower inner quadrant, 4 frags total, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lower outer quadrant, 4 frags total, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Upper outer quadrant, 5 frags total, RSS.\u000aPart C, "#3. Left sentinel node for FS", consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afragment of fibroadipose tissue containing three lymph nodes ranging in size\u000afrom REMOVED_DATE to REMOVED_DATE cm. The largest node has been previously bisected and entirely\u000asubmitted as REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. The two remaining nodes are differentially inked and\u000abisected, previously entirely submitted as REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID remnant, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID remnant, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Non-frozen tissue, multi frags, ESS.\u000aPart D, "#4. Left breast, stitch on superior skin", consists of a 527-gram,\u000a20.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm left simple mastectomy specimen. The attached REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm brown/tan skin ellipse demonstrates a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm brown areola with a\u000acentral REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm everted, unremarkable nipple. There are no apparent scars\u000aon the skin ellipse. A suture designates the superior border. The deep\u000asurface is comprised of a smooth, intact fascial plane (inked black).\u000aSectioning demonstrates a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm cavity in the lower outer\u000aquadrant, REMOVED_DATE cm from the closest deep margin, and exposed at the anterior\u000asurface (1.7 x REMOVED_DATE cm inferior/anterior defect, inked blue). The cavity is\u000alined by smooth to nodular, hemorrhagic walls and surrounded by fibrosis and\u000afat necrosis. The remaining breast parenchyma is comprised of\u000airregular-appearing tan/brown, granular fibrous tissue (at least 60% of\u000aspecimen) with diffuse dilated ducts exuding a thick, tan/white to tan/yellow\u000amaterial. There are no obvious masses noted, grossly. The irregular fibrous\u000atissue is maximally REMOVED_DATE cm. There are no additional abnormalities. There are\u000ano palpable lymph nodes in the lateral soft tissue.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Nipple, central deep, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Additional central breast tissue, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Entire cavity and representative deep margin, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lower outer quadrant, adjacent to cavity, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lower outer quadrant, remote from cavity, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Upper inner quadrant, 3 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lower inner quadrant, 3 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Upper outer quadrant, 3 frags, RSS.\u000adb\u005cpab\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jeffrey F Krane M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a9/21/2006\u000a[report_end]
