VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast core needle biopsy\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: CHRISTINE M DENISON M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Kevin B Long, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Jane E. Brock, M.B., B.S., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aLEFT BREAST UPPER OUTER 11 G STEREOTACTIC CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR\u000aCALCIFICATIONS (1.0 CM):\u000aATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA is present associated with calcifications (see\u000aNOTE).\u000aNOTE: The atypical hyperplasia has apocrine features and single cell necrosis.\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia is evaluated best after excision.\u000aLEFT BREAST UPPER MID/INNER 11 G STEREOTACTIC CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR\u000aCALCIFICATIONS (0.3 CM):\u000aATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA is present (see NOTE).\u000aATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA is present (see NOTE).\u000aCalcifications are associated with a benign ectatic duct.\u000aNOTE: Both the ADH and ALH appear to be incidental findings not associated with\u000acalcifications. Atypical ductal hyperplasia is evaluated best after excision.\u000aDR S. Lester has also reviewed the case and agrees with the diagnosis.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHISTORY: 62 y. o. with 10-mm group of pleomorphic Ca++s LUOQ posteriorly.\u000aBiopsy of these pleomorphic Ca++s. Pt has 2nd group of more coarse Ca++s mid to\u000aslightly inner upper breast.\u000aBREAST IMAGING FINDING:\u000a1. Left: 10 mm calcifications.\u000a2. Left: 3 mm calcifications.\u000aLOCATION:\u000a1. Left: upper outer\u000a2. Left: upper mid/inner\u000aTYPE OF CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY:\u000a1. 11G Stereotactic\u000a2. 11G Stereotactic\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. A - tissue with Ca++ - 2 Orange Cassettes\u000aB/2. B - remainder of tissue.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, in two parts, each labeled with the\u000apatient's name and unit number.\u000aPart A, "Site #1. LUOQ posterior left breast", consists of two orange\u000acassettes:\u000aThe first orange cassette "A. Ca++" contains multiple cylindrical yellow/tan\u000atissues (1.1 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate).\u000aThe second orange cassette "B" contains multiple cylindrical yellow/tan tissues\u000a(2.4 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate).\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Orange cassette A. "Ca++", multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Orange cassette B, multi frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, "Site #2. L upper slightly inner breast more anterior, left breast",\u000aconsists of two white cassettes. The first white cassette "A CA++" contains\u000amultiple cylindrical white/yellow tissues (1.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate).\u000aThe second white cassette "B" contains multiple cylindrical tan/yellow tissues\u000a(2.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate).\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: White cassette A contents "Ca++", multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: White cassette B contents, multi frags, ESS.\u000aLM/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-08-REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jane E. Brock M.B., B.S., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a1/7/2008\u000a[report_end]
