in, REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000asuperior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin,\u000a2.0 cm from the posterior margin and REMOVED_DATE cm from the skin margin. The firm\u000anodule grossly corresponds to the area of calcifications, identified on the\u000aspecimen radiograph. Approximately 30% of the entire specimen and 50% of\u000afibrous tissue is submitted, including the entire region containing\u000amammographic calcifications.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Entire fibrous nodule and region corresponding to\u000acalcifications in\u000aspecimen radiograph, 18 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Fibrous tissue adjacent to entirely submitted area, 2 frags,\u000aESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Skin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Additional sections around biopsy site.\u000ajoc/MMM\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aPrelim Dx Release by Joseph Woodward Carlson M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aNo Action - Prelim Sent by Deborah A Dillon M.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Deborah A Dillon M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
