VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Amend/Addenda\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: JAMES D IGLEHART M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-06-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000a********** Addended Report ***********\u000aResident: Oname O. Burlingame, M.D., Ph.D.; Peter M Sadow, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Deborah A Dillon, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, EXCISION, SENTINEL AND NON-SENTINEL LYMPH NODE EXCISIONS AND NEW\u000aMEDIAL MARGIN (PARTS A-D):\u000aINVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA, poorly differentiated (modified Bloom-Richardson\u000agrade III/III), present as three foci (see note).\u000aLymphovascular invasion is present (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, solid type (high nuclear grade), is present in four\u000aof twenty slides (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) as a minor component (EIC negative).\u000aIn the main specimen, invasive carcinoma and biopsy site changes are present\u000a<0.1 cm from the medial margin (invasive carcinoma seen on frozen section for\u000aspecial studies). Invasive carcinoma is present >0.3 cm from all other margins.\u000aSeparate "new medial margin" with no carcinoma seen (part D).\u000aDCIS is present >0.3 cm from superior, inferior, posterior, anterior and medial\u000amargins. DCIS is present in slide REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, representing the most lateral section\u000a(see note).\u000aMETASTATIC CARCINOMA is present in at least one of three lymph nodes in\u000aspecimen labeled "tissue in anterior axilla under skin" (part A; see note). The\u000alargest metastatic focus measures REMOVED_DATE cm. No extracapsular extension is seen.\u000aNo carcinoma is seen in the sentinel lymph node (part B).\u000aNOTE: The invasive carcinoma is present as three foci. The two larger foci\u000agrossly measured REMOVED_DATE cm and REMOVED_DATE cm (see frozen section slides of tissue taken\u000afor special studies). A third focus, measuring REMOVED_DATE cm, is seen microscopically\u000ain association with DCIS distant from the two grossly identified masses.\u000aRadiologic correlation is suggested for best determination of tumor size.\u000aSlide REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID is not an en face margin; however, the presence of DCIS in this block\u000asuggests that DCIS may be present <0.2 cm from the lateral margin.\u000aSlides from block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID (labeled "tissue in anterior axilla under skin") show\u000aserial sections through three lymph nodes (grossly seen as three nodules).\u000aAdditional levels of block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID reveal two lymph node profiles with metastatic\u000acarcinoma, the largest focus measuring REMOVED_DATE cm. It cannot be determined with\u000acertainty if these two lymph node profiles represent sections of a single lymph\u000anode or two lymph nodes involved by metastatic carcinoma.\u000aImmunohistochemistry for E-cadherin demonstrates membrane immunoreactivity in\u000athe invasive carcinoma, confirming ductal phenotype.\u000aImmunohistochemistry for p63/REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID demonstrates myoepithelial cells around\u000afoci of DCIS and absence of myoepithelial cells in the REMOVED_DATE cm focus of invasive\u000acarcinoma.\u000aIn conjunction with the radiologic and gross measurements, this carcinoma could\u000abe classified as AJCC (6th edition) REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDc REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDa MX, with three foci of invasion.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aClinical History: Right breast cancer.\u000aOperation: Sentinel lymph node mapping and lumpectomy right wide excision\u000abreast.\u000aOperative Findings: Not given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Not given.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Tissue in anterior axilla under skin.\u000aB/2. Sentinel lymph node.\u000aC/3. Right breast lumpectomy - wide excision short superior; long lateral.\u000aD/4. New medial margin - stitch on new margin.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in four parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname, unit number.\u000aPart A, "#1. Tissue in anterior axilla under skin", and contains one fragment\u000aof yellow/tan soft tissue (1.9 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with three white/tan, firm\u000anodules (0.6, REMOVED_DATE  and REMOVED_DATE cm in largest dimension). The outer surface of the\u000aspecimen is inked black. The entire specimen is serially sectioned and\u000asubmitted for histologic examination.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 4 frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, "32. Sentinel lymph node". It contains one tan/white, firm, smooth,\u000ahomogeneous lymph node with attached fibroadipose tissue (1.3 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm)\u000aand a surgical suture. The entire specimen is submitted for histologic\u000aexamination.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 5 frags, ESS.\u000aPart C, "#3. Right breast lumpectomy wide excision marked" and contains one\u000abreast excision (5.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with a skin ellipse (3.5 x REMOVED_DATE cm). A\u000afirm, tan/brown mass (1.1 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) is REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin,\u000a2.0 cm from the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000athe anterior margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin. A satellite nodule\u000a(0.4 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) is REMOVED_DATE cm medial to the main mass and REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000amedial margin. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation\u000aof margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green;\u000alateral/yellow; medial/orange. Representative sections of the specimen are\u000ataken by Dr. A. Richardson for the Breast Tumor Bank. The remaining specimen\u000ais entirely submitted sequentially (medial-to-lateral) for histologic\u000aexamination.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 1 (most medial), 1 frag in each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 2 with mass in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 1 frag in each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 3 with adjacent sample site (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), 1 frag in each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 4, 1 frag in each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 5 with sampled site (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), 1 frag in each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 6, REMOVED_DATE frags in each, ESS.\u000aPart D, "#4. New medial margin stitch on new margin". It contains one fragment\u000aof yellow/tan fibroadipose tissue (2.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with a surgical stitch\u000aplaced by the surgeon to indicate the new shave margin. No lesions or palpable\u000amasses are identified. The new margin is inked black, and the old margin is\u000ainked blue. The specimen is entirely submitted for histologic examination.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: REMOVED_DATE frags in each, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aoob/ag\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Deborah A Dillon M.D., Electronically signed on\u000a10/22/2006\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM (11/20/06):\u000aFive additional levels of block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID were examined at the request of Dr. Dirk\u000aIglehart. The focus of DCIS is present in the first two levels, but is no\u000alonger seen on three sequential deeper levels approaching the true margin.\u000aAddendum #1 by Deborah A Dillon M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
