TE x 2 cm. Two orienting sutures are present. A long suture is\u000adesignated lateral and a short suture is designated superior. A wire marker\u000agoing to the superior superficial portion of the breast is also present. Using\u000athese orientations the deep margin is inked in blue. The superficial superior\u000amargin is inked in yellow and the superficial inferior margin is inked in\u000ablack. The specimen is cut into several slices showing that firm tissue is\u000apresent mostly in the medial portion of the specimen. Sections are taken from\u000alateral to medial. 11X all.\u000aDictated by: RJS____(signature on file)____MICHAEL J. ROSS, M.D. REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a____(signature on file)____RICHARD SAMPSON, M.D. REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a[report_end]
