aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in >10%\u000aof tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in\u000a>10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHISTORY: High risk for breast CA - spiculated mass in the lower outer breast.\u000aBREAST IMAGING FINDING:\u000a1. Left: REMOVED_DATE cm, Nonpalpable and irregular-border, mass.\u000aLOCATION:\u000a1. Left: lower outer\u000aTYPE OF CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY:\u000a1. 9G MRI Vacuum-assisted\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000a1. 9G MRI Vacuum-assisted - White bottom/green top cassette\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit\u000anumber and "First MRI biopsy green/white", and consists of multiple\u000ayellow-white focally hemorrhagic fibrofatty tissue cores (aggregating REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000ax REMOVED_DATE cm). The cores are received in a white cassette with a green top. The\u000aspecimen is submitted in toto.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Multi frags, ESS.\u000aCP/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jane E. Brock M.B., B.S., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a6/24/2008\u000a[report_end]
