h benign epithelium.\u000aD. LEFT AXILLARY LYMPH NODE, EXCISION:\u000aOne (1) lymph node with no carcinoma seen.\u000aNOTE: This carcinoma would be classified as AJCC (6th edition) REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDa REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Cancer left breast - Core biopsy proven infiltrating cancer in lower\u000aouter quadrant left breast.\u000aOperation: Left breast quadrantectomy and sentinel node\u000aOperative Findings: None given\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Cancer left breast\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000a1. Left breast tissue lesion and wire (short suture superior, long suture\u000alateral)\u000a2. Sentinel node left axilla (FS)\u000a3. Left breast tissue medial to specimen #1, suture on aspect closest to\u000aspecimen #1\u000a4. Axillary node - left\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "#2 SENTINEL NODE LEFT AXILLA" (FSA):\u000aNegative for carcinoma.\u000aOR Consultation by: VANIA NOSE, M.D., PH.D.\u000aResident: LI CHEN, M.D., PH.D.\u000aThe senior physician certifies that he/she personally conducted a gross and/or\u000amicroscopic examination of the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed\u000athe rapid diagnos(es) related thereto.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in 4 parts, all labeled with the patient's name\u000aand unit number.\u000aPart A, labeled "#1. Left breast tissue lesion and wire, FS", consists of a 48g\u000aleft breast wide local excision including a needle localization wire and\u000aorientating sutures with short stitch superior and long stitch lateral. The\u000askin ellipse measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm, overall dimensions of specimen REMOVED_DATE cm\u000amedial to lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm superior to inferior and REMOVED_DATE cm anterior to deep.\u000aThe specimen margin is inked as follows: Posterior black, medial orange,\u000alateral yellow, superior red, and inferior green. An accompanying specimen\u000aradiograph shows three clips and a single needle localization wire at one of\u000athe clips at the superior end. The specimen is serially sectioned from\u000asuperior to inferior margin into eight slices. The tip of the wire is located\u000ain an ill-defined mass REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in slice 4, distance from margins as\u000afollows: Medial margin REMOVED_DATE cm, lateral margin REMOVED_DATE cm, skin surface REMOVED_DATE cm,\u000aposterior margin REMOVED_DATE cm, superior margin REMOVED_DATE cm, and inferior margin REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000aThere is a second small firm nodule REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm with an embedded clip\u000apresent at the lateral and inferior margins in slice 8, REMOVED_DATE cm from medial\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm from posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from skin margin, and more than\u000a3.0 cm from superior margin. The remainder of the specimen is 50% fibrous and\u000a50% adipose tissue. There are biopsy site changes towards the superior aspect\u000a(slices REMOVED_DATE ). The entire specimen is submitted from superior to inferior\u000aaspect in cassettes REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID to REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Superior margin, slice 1, perpendicular sections, REMOVED_DATE frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 2, full face, 1 frag each ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 3, full face, 1 frag each, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 4, site of needle tip and beginning of the first nodule\u000a(REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), I frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 5, full face, first nodule in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 1 frag each, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 6, full face, 1 frag each, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 7, full face, 1 frag each, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Inferior margin, slice 8, perpendicular sections, with second\u000anodule in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_DATE frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, labeled "#2. Sentinel node left axilla FS", consists of a single\u000agray/tan lymph node REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm bisected and submitted for frozen\u000asection A, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: FSA remnant, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aPart C, labeled "#3. Breast tissue medial to aspect #1 suture aspect closest to\u000aspecimen #1", consists of a single piece of fibrofatty tissue REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm with a suture on the edge of the convex surface. At the opposite concave\u000asurface, there is fibrous tissue and a partial defect. The surface marked with\u000athe suture is inked black and opposite side inked blue. The specimen is\u000aserially sectioned.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Margin, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aPart D, labeled "#4. Left axillary node permanent", and consists of a single\u000alymph node (0.6 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) and fatty tissue REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. Submitted\u000ain toto.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 lymph node, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_DATE \u000aLAD/am\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Deborah A Dillon M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
