VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Amend/Addenda\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Sentinel Lymph Nodes(s)\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: DIANE C LOCKHART M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-06-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000a********** Addended Report ***********\u000aResident: Travis J Hollmann, M.D., Ph.D.; Rachel E Factor, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Jeffrey F Krane, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, SIMPLE MASTECTOMY AND SENTINEL NODE BIOPSIES (3\u000aSPECIMENS)(INCLUDING FSA AND FSB):\u000aINVASIVE MUCINOUS CARCINOMA (2 FOCI) AND NEGATIVE LYMPH NODES.\u000aSYNOPSIS:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA\u000aSize - REMOVED_DATE cm and REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aMultifocal - Yes\u000aHistologic Type - Mucinous\u000aHistologic Grade (SBR) - II-III (Moderate to Poor)\u000aNuclear Grade - High\u000aEIC - Positive\u000aLymphovascular invasion - Absent\u000aDermal lymphatic invasion - Absent\u000aSkin invasion - Absent\u000aSkeletal muscle invasion - N/A\u000aFinal Margins (invasive)\u000aNegative (> REMOVED_DATE cm) - deep\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU - Present\u000aTypes - Comedo, cribriform, micropapillary,\u000aclinging\u000aNuclear grade - High\u000aCalcifications in DCIS - Absent\u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - Present\u000aExtent of DCIS\u000aNumber of blocks/total: REMOVED_DATE blocks\u000aFinal Margins (DCIS)\u000aClose (0.1 cm) - Deep\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - Absent\u000aSENTINEL LYMPH NODES - Negative\u000aNumber of positive nodes - 0\u000aNumber of nodes examined - 3\u000aTOTAL POSITIVE NODES (all specimens) - REMOVED_DATE \u000aOTHER FINDINGS: Biopsy site\u000aAJCC CLASSIFICATION (6th edition) - REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID(sn) MX with multiple foci of\u000ainvasion (see NOTE).\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER/PR/HER-2) - Pending\u000aNOTE: Two (2) separate foci of invasive mucinous carcinoma are present, one\u000ameasuring REMOVED_DATE cm and the other REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest dimension. Tissue between the\u000atwo foci shows DCIS. The high nuclear grade is unusual in a mucinous\u000acarcinoma.\u000aSlides also reviewed by Dr. D. Dillon, Breast Pathology, who concurs.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 48-year-old woman diagnosed by ultrasound core biopsy, right breast\u000amucinous ductal ER/PR-positive, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu-negative, and DCIS.\u000aOperation: Right SLN BX, right simple mastectomy.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right invasive breast CA.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. SLN.\u000aB/2. SLN - FS.\u000aC/3. R breast, short stitch on tail of axilla, long stitch between 2 known\u000acancers.\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "#1. SLN":\u000aTwo lymph nodes; negative for tumor.\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "#2. SLN":\u000aOne lymph node; negative for tumor.\u000aOR Consultation by: WILLIAM WELCH, M.D.\u000aResident: WAI CHIN FOO, MD\u000aThe senior physician certifies that he/she personally conducted a gross and/or\u000amicroscopic examination of the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed\u000athe rapid diagnos(es) related thereto.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in three parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart A, "#1. Sentinel lymph node", consists of a single candidate lymph node\u000a(1.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which is entirely submitted as FSA.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: FSA remnant, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aPart B, "#2. Sentinel lymph node", consists of a single candidate lymph node\u000a(1.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which is entirely submitted as FSB.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: FSB remnant, 1 frag, ESS\u000aPart C, "#3. Right breast short stitch on axillary tail, long stitch between\u000atwo known cancers", consists of a 928 gram right mastectomy specimen (17 cm\u000aS-I, 21 cm M-L, REMOVED_DATE cm A-P) with an axillary tail designated with a stitch and\u000ameasuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The specimen contains a tan/white skin ellipse (23.5\u000acm M-L, REMOVED_DATE cm S-I and excised to a depth of REMOVED_DATE cm) with areola (4.5 cm in\u000amaximum diameter) and nipple (1.0 cm in maximum diameter). There is no\u000askeletal muscle located on the posterior aspect, which is inked black. The\u000aspecimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral revealing a firm, white\u000amass (designated mass A, REMOVED_DATE cm) located in the upper outer quadrant, within\u000a0.5 cm from the deep margin and REMOVED_DATE cm from the skin. A separate mass\u000a(designated B) located at approximately 9 o?clock, is firm and white and\u000ameasures REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest dimension and comes to within REMOVED_DATE cm of the deep\u000amargin and REMOVED_DATE cm from the skin. While the well-delineated, mass A has a\u000astreaming focus of connected fibrotic tissue extending superiorly 5 cm\u000a(bringing the entire mass plus fibrous streaming to a total size of REMOVED_DATE cm in\u000aGD). Mass A and mass B appear grossly separated by REMOVED_DATE cm of adipose tissue.\u000aAn additional area of firm, fibrous tissue is located in the medial aspect of\u000athe specimen in the lower inner quadrant (measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) and\u000acomes to within 2 cm of the deep margin and 5 cm of the skin. The remainder of\u000athe specimen is comprised of approximately 70% adipose tissue and 30% fibrous\u000atissue with no additional tumors, nodules, or gross abnormalities.\u000aApproximately five candidate lymph nodes are dissected from the axillary tail\u000aand therefore the entire axillary tail is submitted for histological review.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Mass A, contiguous, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Deep margin closest to mass A, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Mass A with fibrous streaming, contiguous sections, 1 frag each,\u000aRSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Mass B, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Closest posterior margin to mass B, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Fibrous area, C, 1 frag each, contiguous, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Nipple, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Closest skin to mass, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Upper outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lower outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Inner outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lower inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 5 candidate nodes, 5 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Remainder of axillary tail, multiple frags each, ESS axillary\u000atail.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Intervening tissue between the two masses A and B, 2 frags each, ESS.\u000ath\u005cpab\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jeffrey F Krane M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a9/22/2006\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM:\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed with the following results for the\u000a2.7 cm invasive carcinoma (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu WEAKLY POSITIVE (2+)\u000aNote: The DCIS shows stronger immunoreactivity for REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu.\u000aFISH was performed by USLABS using the PathVysion HER-2 DNA Probe Kit with the\u000afollowing results (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aResult: NOT AMPLIFIED\u000aThe Her-2/cen 17 ratio = REMOVED_DATE \u000aThe average of Her-2/neu copies per cell: REMOVED_DATE \u000aThe average of cen 17 copies per cell: REMOVED_DATE \u000aThe cutoff point for assessing HER-2/neu gene amplification is a ratio of 