VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID:REMOVED_CASE_ID Report Status: Signed\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aADDENDUM REPORT\u000aAddendum #1 Entered: REMOVED_DATE -1515\u000a*** ADDITIONAL DIAGNOSTIC INFORMATION ***\u000aThis report contains an addendum to the original for the purpose of providing\u000aadditional diagnostic information. The original diagnosis is unchanged.\u000aImmunohistochemical staining on the formalin-fixed, paraffin-embedded block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000areveals these results for the infiltrating carcinoma:\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID): POSITIVE (>30% with intense, complete membrane staining)\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, indirect biotin-free detection) is assessed visually by\u000aquantitation of the percent of tumor cells staining.\u000aAddeundum Signed Electronically Signed FRASER,JEAN L. M.D. REMOVED_DATE \u000aDIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. Right sentinel lymph node, biopsy:\u000aOne lymph node with isolated tumor cells.\u000aOne lymph node with no tumor seen.\u000aB. Right breast, upper outer quadrant, excision:\u000aInfiltrating ductal carcinoma.\u000aDuctal carcinoma in situ.\u000aFocal atypical lobular hyperplasia.\u000aChanges consistent with prior biopsy site.\u000aCalcifications associated with sclerosing adenosis, cysts, benign breast\u000alobules and blood vessels.\u000aApocrine metaplasia, fibroadenomatous changes and usual intraductal\u000ahyperplasia.\u000aSee synoptic report.\u000aSYNOPTIC REPORT:\u000aINVASIVE TUMOR:\u000a-histologic type: infiltrating ductal carcinoma\u000a-histologic grade: moderately differentiated\u000a-size (greatest dimension): REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000a-lymphatic/vascular invasion: none identified\u000a-perineural invasion: none identified\u000a-microcalcification: none identified\u000a-margins for invasive tumor: Tumor is present less than 1 mm. from the\u000aposterior margin, focally, toward the lateral\u000aaspect of the specimen. Tumor is present\u000aless than 1 mm. from the lateral margin,\u000afocally, toward the superior aspect of the\u000aspecimen.\u000a-immunohistochemical staining on prior specimen (S-07-REMOVED_CASE_ID) was reported as:\u000aEstrogen receptor: POSITIVE (>10% of nuclei stained)\u000aProgesterone receptor: POSITIVE (>10% of nuclei stained)\u000a-immunohistochemical staining for REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu will be performed on block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and\u000areported in an addendum to follow.\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU (DCIS):\u000a-histologic type: solid pattern\u000a-histologic grade: intermediate nuclear grade\u000a-size (greatest dimension): ductal carcinoma in situ is present on 6 of\u000a17 slides, spanning approximately REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000a-extent: focal\u000a-extensive intraductal component: absent\u000a-necrosis in DCIS: present, focal\u000a-microcalcifications in DCIS: present\u000a-margins for DCIS: Ductal carcinoma in situ is present at the\u000alateral margin, over a broad front,\u000atoward the superior aspect of the\u000aspecimen. Ductal carcinoma in situ is\u000apresent less than 1 mm. from the\u000aanterior-lateral margin, over a broad\u000afront. Ductal carcinoma in situ is\u000apresent less than 1 mm. from the\u000aposterior-lateral margin, two foci.\u000aLYMPH NODES:\u000aAll two lymph nodes sampled are negative for malignancy (0/2)\u000a(0/2 sentinel lymph nodes).\u000aLymph nodes with isolated tumor cells out of total sampled: REMOVED_DATE \u000a(1/2 sentinel lymph nodes).\u000aCOMMENT: The sentinel lymph nodes, specimen A, are examined at multiple levels\u000awith H&E stains and immunohistochemical stains for keratin.\u000aADDITIONAL PATHOLOGIC FINDINGS:\u000aFocal atypical lobular hyperplasia, fibrocystic changes, microcalcifications,\u000achanges consistent with prior biopsy site.\u000aPRIOR RELATED SPECIMENS REVIEWED:\u000aRight breast at 11 o'clock, needle biopsy; S-07-REMOVED_CASE_ID; REMOVED_DATE \u000aAJCC pTNM Classification (6th Ed.): pREMOVED_ACCESSION_IDc pREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID(i+)(sn) pMX\u000aThe pathologic TNM classification above is based only on the information\u000aavailable to the pathologist, and therefore may not be accurate.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by: Jean L. Fraser, M.D.\u000aClinical diagnosis & history:\u000aRight breast carcinoma\u000aTissue-Designation:\u000aA.Sentinel lymph node - right breast\u000aB.Breast, excision with margins - right, upper outer corner\u000aGross description:\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin in two parts.\u000aSpecimen A labeled "sentinel node, right" consists of a fragment of adipose\u000atissue containing a blue lymph node that measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. It is\u000abisected to reveal no gross abnormalities. The bisected lymph node is\u000asubmitted in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. A second smaller potential lymph node is submitted in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aThe remainder of the adipose tissue is submitted in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. 3 agg. all.\u000aSpecimen B labeled "right breast, upper outer corner" consists of a fragment of\u000afibroadipose tissue that weighs REMOVED_DATE grams and measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 cm. It\u000ais oriented with a short suture indicating superior and a long suture\u000aindicating lateral at 9 o'clock. A localization wire emerges from the superior\u000aaspect of the specimen. The specimen is inked as follows: medial = orange;\u000alateral = yellow; superior = blue; inferior = green; anterior = black;\u000aposterior = red. The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal firm, white\u000afibroglandular tissue with foci of hemorrhage. The specimen is submitted\u000aentirely in seventeen cassettes. 17X all.\u000aDictated by: JLF____(signature on file)____RICHARD SAMPSON, M.D. REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a____(signature on file)____ REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a[report_end]
