rates the localization wire in\u000aplace in the center of the specimen and a clip medial to the localization wire\u000ain the posterior half of the specimen. There is an ill-defined white/tan\u000anodular region (0.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) present REMOVED_DATE to inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm to\u000aposterior, REMOVED_DATE cm to lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm to superior, REMOVED_DATE cm to anterior, and REMOVED_DATE \u000acm to medial. The remainder of the breast tissue is composed of 20% dense\u000awhite fibrous tissue and 80% yellow adipose tissue. The specimen is submitted\u000ain its entirety for histological examination.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin, perpendicular sections, 4 frags each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, perpendicular sections, REMOVED_DATE frags each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Anterior margin from lateral to medial, perpendicular sections, 2\u000afrags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Posterior margin from lateral to medial (mass in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), REMOVED_DATE \u000afrags each, ESS.\u000aCEL/mgd/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Lucian R Chirieac M.D., Electronically signed on\u000aWednesday REMOVED_MONTH 14, 2009 at 03:55:32PM\u000a[report_end]
