VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aRICHARDSON, ANDREA, L., M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by RICHARDSON,ANDREA L.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED LOCALIZATION FOR A MASS AND A CLIP:\u000aPHYLLODES TUMOR\u000aPhyllodes tumor, low grade, (2.2 cm).\u000aThe stroma is moderately cellular with minimal stromal overgrowth or\u000anucler pleomorphism. No mitoses are seen (50 HPF examined). The margins\u000aof the lesion are predominantly circumscribed ("pushing") but are focally\u000ainfiltrative into fat with a few satellite stromal nodules. There is no\u000anecrosis, hemorrhage or heterologous differentiation.\u000aMargins: Negative: lateral, medial, anterior.\u000aClose: posterior (0.2 cm #3)\u000asuperior (0.2 cm #1)\u000aAdjacent breast tissue with florid ductal hyperplasia with focal\u000acentral necrosis (block 6, slide 1).The area of hyperplasia is no longer\u000apresent on deeper levels.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Phyllodes tumor, left breast.\u000aOperation: Left breast wire excisional biopsy.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Phyllodes tumor - left breast.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1. Tissue - left breast, short superior, long lateral -\u000amammo - red and green reversed by mistake -\u000ared inferior - green superior.\u000aRADIOLOGY REPORT:\u000aMass and clip in specimen.\u000aSigned: E.P. Frost, MD.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by HARRIS,MARIAN HESTER,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "Tissue left breast, short supterior, long lateral", and consists of one\u000awire localized breast excision specimen measuring REMOVED_DATE (anterior to posterior) x\u000a5.5 (medial to lateral) x REMOVED_DATE (inferior to superior) cm. The specimen has been\u000ainked by the surgeon differently from the usual protocol. The inks represent\u000athe following margins: red/inferior, green/superior, orange/medial,\u000ayellow/lateral, black/posterior, blue/anterior. There are orienting sutures\u000acores corresponding to short-superior, long-lateral. There is a white/pink\u000amass in the posterior/green (superior) aspect of the specimen measuring REMOVED_DATE x\u000a1.6 x REMOVED_DATE cm. The mass is REMOVED_DATE cm from the black margin, abuts the green\u000amargin, is REMOVED_DATE cm from the yellow margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from orange margin, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom the blue margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the red margin. There is a tan/gray\u000askin ellipse on the specimen measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. There is an accompanying\u000aspecimen radiograph demonstrating a mass and clip in the specimen. The\u000aspecimen is serially sectioned along the plane of the wire, which is between\u000aslice 3 and 4. The clip is located in either slice 2 or 3. Representative\u000asections are submitted including 100% of the mass and 100% of the fibrous\u000atissue, which is in slices REMOVED_DATE \u000aMicro 1: Slice 1, bisected, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Slice 2, bisected, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Slice 3, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Slice 4, portion containing tumor, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 8: Mid portion of slice 5, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 9: Anterior portion of slice 6, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 10: Medial portion of slice 6, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 11: Medial portion of slice 8, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 12: Slice 9, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro 13: Slice 4, remainder of slice, 1 frag, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE Slice 5, all remaining fibrous tissue, 3 frags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE Slice 6, all remaining fibrous tissue, 2 frags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE Slice 7, all remaining fibrous tissue, 2 frags, ESS\u000amah\u000aReports to: CHRISTIAN, ROGER, L. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
