ineated, pink/tan, granular\u000amacule (0.5 x REMOVED_DATE cm) that is less than REMOVED_DATE cm from the closest radial margin\u000aand REMOVED_DATE cm from the closest tip. The specimen is inked blue and serially\u000asectioned.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Tips, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Body to include lesion, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aPart C, "Presternal", is a REMOVED_DATE cm in diameter x REMOVED_DATE cm in length, tan/white,\u000asmooth, circular skin punch with a central poorly-delineated brown/tan speckled\u000amacule (0.4 x REMOVED_DATE cm) that is REMOVED_DATE cm from the closest radial margin. The\u000aspecimen is inked blue and bisected.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 2 frags, ESS.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Marian H Harris M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by George F Murphy MD, Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
