VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID:REMOVED_CASE_ID Report Status: Signed\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aADDENDUM REPORT\u000aAddendum #2 Entered: REMOVED_DATE -1611\u005cE\u000aE\u005c\u000a*** ADDITIONAL DIAGNOSTIC INFORMATION ***\u000aThis report contains an addendum to the original for the purpose of providing\u000aadditional diagnostic information. The original diagnosis is unchanged.\u000aNOTE: This case was discussed at Breast Cancer Conference on REMOVED_DATE  In\u000aaddition to the multifocal infiltrating carcinomas, extensive intraductal\u000acomponent is present.\u000aAddeundum Signed Electronically Signed MATTIA,ANTHONY R. M.D. REMOVED_DATE \u000aAddendum #1 Entered: REMOVED_DATE -1405\u005cE\u000aE\u005c\u000a*** ADDITIONAL DIAGNOSTIC INFORMATION ***\u000aThis report contains an addendum to the original for the purpose of providing\u000aadditional diagnostic information. The original diagnosis is unchanged.\u000aDue to a typographical error on specimen REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, the estrogen receptor,\u000aprogesterone receptor and Her 2/neu results were incorrectly reported. They\u000ashould read as follows as was stated on REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID:\u000aEstrogen receptor: POSITIVE (>10% of nuclei stained)\u000aProgesterone receptor: POSITIVE (>10% of nuclei stained)\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID): NEGATIVE (1+) (faint or <10% complete membrane\u000astaining)\u000aEstrogen receptor (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) and/or progesterone receptor (PgR REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) is assessed\u000avisually by quantitation of the percent of tumor cells staining.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID (4REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, Ventana Medical Systems, FDA approved) is assessed by quantitation\u000aof the percent and intensity of tumor cells staining.\u000aAddeundum Signed Electronically Signed FEEN,DENNIS J. M.D. REMOVED_DATE \u000aDIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. Left axillary sentinel lymph node #1, excision:\u000aNo diagnostic abnormalities recognized.\u000aNo metastatic tumor identified.\u000aB. Left axillary sentinel lymph node #2, excision:\u000aNo diagnostic abnormalities recognized.\u000aNo metastatic tumor identified.\u000aC. Left axillary sentinel lymph node #3, excision:\u000aNo diagnostic abnormalities recognized.\u000aNo metastatic tumor identified.\u000aD. Left axillary sentinel lymph node #4, excision:\u000aNo diagnostic abnormalities recognized.\u000aNo metastatic tumor identified.\u000aE. Left breast, excision:\u000aInvasive ductal carcinoma, grade 1, REMOVED_DATE cm., mid tumor.\u000aInvasive ductal carcinoma, grade 1, REMOVED_DATE cm. inferior tumor.\u000aDuctal carcinoma in situ, multifocal, high grade, micropapillary and\u000asolid, with necrosis.\u000aF. Left breast, extramedial margin, excision:\u000aInvasive lobular carcinoma, grade REMOVED_DATE  REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000aDuctal carcinoma in situ, multifocal, high grade, micropapillary and\u000asolid, with necrosis.\u000aSYNOPTIC REPORT - INVASIVE BREAST CANCER\u000aAJCC pTNM CLASSIFICATION (6TH Ed.)(Based on available surgical material:\u000apREMOVED_ACCESSION_IDb pREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID pMX - three separate primary carcinomas each with same\u000apTNM\u000aHISTOLOGIC TYPE: invasive ductal carcinoma, invasive\u000alobular carcinoma\u000aHISTOLOGIC GRADE (Nottingham System): I and II (see location line)\u000aTUMOR LOCATION: mid - grade 1\u000ainferior - grade REMOVED_DATE \u000amedial - grade 1\u000aTUMOR SIZE (greatest dimension): mid (0.7 cm.), inferior (0.5 cm.) and\u000amedial (1.0 cm.)\u000aLYMPHATIC/VASCULAR INVASION: none identified\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU (DCIS): present\u000aType: cribriform with necrosis\u000aGrade: REMOVED_DATE \u000aExtent: multifocal\u000aSize (greatest dimension): spans REMOVED_DATE cm. in and around invasive,\u000amid, inferior and medial tumors;\u000amultifocal, spanning REMOVED_DATE cm. and away\u000afrom the tumors\u000aExtensive intraductal component: absent\u000aNecrosis: present, comedo\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU: present, focal, within ductal carcinoma\u000ain situ\u000aMICROCALCIFICATIONS: none identified\u000aRESECTION MARGINS:\u000aInvasive Carcinoma: clear, mid, inferior and medial\u000aDCIS: ductal carcinoma in situ close to\u000amargin (0.1-0.2 cm.: section REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000a(posterior), REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID (lateral), REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000a(superior), REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID (superior) - separate\u000aindividual foci within REMOVED_DATE 2 cm. of\u000ainked margins\u000aIMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING (invasive carcinoma):\u000aPrior specimen REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID reported as:\u000aEstrogen receptor: NEGATIVE (0% of nuclei stained)\u000aProgesterone receptor: NEGATIVE (0% of nuclei stained)\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID): NEGATIVE (0) (no membrane staining)\u000aImmunohistochemical staining on the medial invasive carcinoma with calponin\u000aand E-cadherin stains are negative and supportive of the lobular nature of\u000athe carcinoma.\u000aRepeat immunohistochemical staining with Her2 on the mid invasive carcinoma\u000ais negative (1+), faint.\u000aTotal Fixation Time: 11 hours\u000aLYMPH NODES:\u000aAll 4 nodes sampled are negative for tumor (0/4) (0/4 sentinel nodes)\u000aCOMMENT: The sentinel lymph nodes, specimens A-D, are examined at multiple\u000alevels with H&E stains and immunohistochemical stains for cytokeratin REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/3.\u000aADDITIONAL PATHOLOGIC FINDINGS:\u000aNon-neoplastic breast: Fibrocystic changes, focal atypical lobular\u000ahyperplasia and atypical ductal hyperplasia\u000aChanges consistent with prior biopsy site.\u000aPRIOR RELATED SPECIMENS REVIEWED:\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aFinal Diagnosis by: Dennis J. Feen, M.D.\u000aINTRA-OPERATIVE CONSULTATION:\u000aOPERATING ROOM CONSULTATION (TISSUE EXAMINATION):\u000aSentinel lymph node #1:\u000aNo gross tumor seen.\u000aFinal diagnosis deferred to permanent sections.\u000aSentinel lymph node #2:\u000aNo gross tumor seen.\u000aFinal diagnosis deferred to permanent sections.\u000aSentinel lymph node #3:\u000aNo gross tumor seen.\u000aFinal diagnosis deferred to permanent sections.\u000aSentinel lymph node #4:\u000aNo gross tumor seen.\u000aFinal diagnosis deferred to permanent sections.\u000aDJF\u000aClinical diagnosis & history:\u000aLeft breast cancer\u000aTissue-Designation:\u000aA.Sentinel lymph node - #1\u000aB.Sentinel lymph node - #2\u000aC.Sentinel lymph node - #3\u000aD.Sentinel lymph node - #4\u000aE.Breast, excision with margins - left\u000aF.Breast, excision with margins - left, medial\u000aGross description:\u000aThe specimen is received in six containers.\u000aSpecimen A is received fresh from the Operating Room, labeled "sentinel node\u000a#1" and consists of a REMOVED_DATE cm. diameter grossly unremarkable lymph node. The\u000anode is bisected and submitted entirely in one cassette. 3X all.\u000aSpecimen B is received fresh from the Operating Room, labeled "sentinel node\u000a#2" and consists of a REMOVED_DATE cm. diameter lymph node. The node is trisected and\u000asubmitted entirely in one cassette. 3X all.\u000aSpecimen C is received fresh from the Operating Room, labeled "sentinel node\u000a#3" and consists of a REMOVED_DATE cm. diameter lymph node. The node is trisected and\u000asubmitted entirely in one cassette. 3X all.\u000aSpecimen D is received fresh from the Operating Room, labeled "sentinel node\u000a#4" and consists of a REMOVED_DATE cm. diameter lymph node. The node is bisected and\u000asubmitted entirely in one cassette. 2X all.\u000aSpecimen E is received in formalin, labeled "left breast masses" and consists\u000aof a 50 gram, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. fragment of fibroadipose tissue containing\u000atwo localizing needles. Two sutures are present which are not designated,\u000aalthough the long suture will be considered lateral and the short suture,\u000asuperior. The margins are inked as follows: posterior, black; superior,\u000ayellow; anterior, blue; inferior, orange; lateral, green; medial, red. On cut\u000asection, the mid and inferior aspects of the specimen contain two small masses\u000awith associated biopsy site changes and clips. The mid portion lesion is REMOVED_DATE x\u000a0.4 x REMOVED_DATE cm. and is located REMOVED_DATE cm. from the mid anterior margin. The second\u000alesion is REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. and is located inferior to the previously\u000adescribed mass. The second mass is REMOVED_DATE cm. from the posterior margin and REMOVED_DATE \u000acm. from the anterior margin. The remaining parenchyma is unremarkable.\u000aSections are submitted as follows. 30 agg. all.\u000aSection code: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - superior margin\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - superior/medial tissue\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - superior/lateral tissue\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - central portion with first described mass\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - central/medial tissue\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - central/lateral tissue\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - inferior lateral tissue with second described mass\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - additional inferior lateral tissue\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - inferior medial tissue\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - inferior tissue\u000aSpecimen F is received in formalin, labeled "extra medial tissue; short\u000asuperior and long lateral adjacent to previous biopsy" and consists of a 10\u000agram, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. fragment of fibroadipose tissue with the previously\u000anoted sutures. The specimen is inked as follows: posterior, black; superior,\u000ayellow; anterior, blue; lateral, orange; inferior, green; medial, red. On cut\u000asection, the central portion of the specimen contains a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000airregular, firm, tan-white mass with central biopsy site changes. This mass is\u000a0.3 cm. from the posterior margin centrally. The specimen is submitted\u000aentirely in eight cassettes, medial to lateral. 8X all.\u000aTotal fixation time is 52 hours.\u000aDictated by: ARM____(signature on file)____ REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a____(signature on file)____DENNIS J. FEEN, M.D. REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a[report_end]
