tive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but\u000aonly a portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity\u000ain >10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Core biopsy = atypical ductal hyperplasia.\u000aOperation: (R) needle directed breast excision.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: (R) breast mass.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1. Right breast tissue - to mammo short anterior,\u000along superior.\u000aRADIOLOGY REPORT:\u000a#1. RIGHT BREAST TISSUE TO MAMMO SHORT ANTERIOR, LONG LATERAL:\u000aCa++ and clip in specimen.\u000aSigned: E.P. Frost, MD.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by SANTAGATA,SANDRO,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in one part, labeled with the patient's name\u000aand medical record number, "#1. Right breast tissue", and consists of a REMOVED_DATE x\u000a3.7 x REMOVED_DATE cm breast excision specimen that is oriented by the surgeon with a\u000ashort suture indicating the anterior margin and a long suture indicating the\u000asuperior margin. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the\u000aevaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red;\u000ainferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. There is a localizing\u000awire entering the specimen at the medial margin. On section, the wire crosses\u000afrom the medial margin to the lateral margin and localizes an area of fibrous\u000atissue measuring REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest dimension. On the radiograph, this area\u000acorresponds with the area of calcification. Non wire localized areas contain\u000abluish cysts (largest measuring REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest dimension). The entire\u000aspecimen is submitted for histologic analysis.\u000aMicro 1: Most suspicious area per radiograph, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 2: Path wire, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Areas immediately flanking most suspicious area, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Areas flanking path wire, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Non wire localized area, towards superior margin, 6 frags, ESS.\u000assa\u000aReports to: REILLY, RAYMOND, JOHN, M.B.B.C.H.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
