otruding from the\u000asuperior/anterior surface. The specimen is accompanied by a radiograph showing\u000aa clip and localization wire within the specimen. The specimen is inked per\u000apathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black;\u000aanterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. The\u000aspecimen is serially sectioned from superior to inferior into twelve slices,\u000awith slice 7 containing an S-shaped surgical clip. Sectioning reveals nearly\u000a100% pink/tan, firm fibrous cut surface. The specimen is entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slices REMOVED_DATE  6 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slices 7, with surgical clip, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Remainder of specimen, serially sectioned, multiple frags, ESS.\u000aJGI/elw\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Joanna A Gibson M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Lucian Chirieac M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
