rm, tan fibrous tissue. The entire specimen\u000ais submitted. The specimen arrived previously inked by the surgeon per\u000apathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior\u000a= blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange.\u000aMicro 1: medial margin, perpendicularly sectioned, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  sections from medial to lateral (localization wire in slice 3), 7\u000afrags, ESS.\u000aMicro 6: lateral margin perpendicularly sectioned, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aPart two, labeled "left inferior shave margin, stitch in new margin", consists\u000aof a single fragment of tan/yellow fibroadipose tissue (2.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm).\u000aThere is whip stitch on one flat surface designating the new margin. The new\u000amargin is inked black. The old margin is inked blue. The specimen arrives\u000aaccompanied by a whole specimen radiograph which is unremarkable. Sectioning\u000areveals a specimen that consists of approximately 50% firm, tan/gray, dense\u000afibrous tissue and 50% dense yellow adipose tissue. The specimen is entirely\u000asubmitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  left inferior shave margin, 7 frags, ESS.\u000ajmh\u000aReports to: KAELIN, CAROLYN, MARY M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN\u000a[report_end]
