irst\u000aorange cassette, labeled "A Ca++", contains multiple cylindrical fibrofatty\u000asoft tissues (1.3 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate). The second orange cassette,\u000alabeled "B", contains multiple cylindrical focally hemorrhagic fibrofatty soft\u000atissues (2.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate). The specimen is submitted in toto.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Contents of orange cassette, labeled "ACA++", multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Contents of orange cassette, labeled "B", multi frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, labeled "left breast REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID", consists of two brown cassettes. The first\u000abrown cassette, labeled "A Ca++", contains multiple cylindrical fibrofatty soft\u000atissues (1.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate). The second brown cassette, labeled\u000a"B", contains multiple cylindrical focally hemorrhagic fibrofatty soft tissues\u000a(2.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The specimen is submitted in its entirety.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Contents of brown cassette, labeled "A CA++", multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Contents of brown cassette, labeled "B", multi frags, ESS.\u000ajc/lp\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Deborah A Dillon M.D., Electronically signed on Monday\u000aREMOVED_MONTH 20, 2009 at 03:57:36PM\u000a[report_end]
