VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID:REMOVED_CASE_ID Report Status: Signed\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aADDENDUM REPORT\u000aAddendum #3 Entered: REMOVED_DATE -1032\u000a*** ADDITIONAL DIAGNOSTIC INFORMATION ***\u000aThis report contains an addendum to the original for the purpose of providing\u000aadditional diagnostic information. The original diagnosis is unchanged.\u000aFluorescence in situ hybridization (FISH) with probes for REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu performed at\u000aMayo Medical Laboratories on block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID reveals the following results for the\u000ainfiltrating carcinoma:\u000aThe specimen showed NO evidence of REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu gene amplification.\u000aAddeundum Signed Electronically Signed SAMPSON,RICHARD J. M.D. REMOVED_DATE \u000aAddendum #2 Entered: REMOVED_DATE -1135\u000a*** ADDITIONAL DIAGNOSTIC INFORMATION ***\u000aThis report contains an addendum to the original for the purpose of providing\u000aadditional diagnostic information. The original diagnosis is unchanged.\u000aFocal extranodal extension is present in the separately submitted lymph node\u000a"A".\u000aAddeundum Signed Electronically Signed SAMPSON,RICHARD J. M.D. REMOVED_DATE \u000aAddendum #1 Entered: REMOVED_DATE -0955\u000a*** ADDITIONAL DIAGNOSTIC INFORMATION ***\u000aThis report contains an addendum to the original for the purpose of providing\u000aadditional diagnostic information. The original diagnosis is unchanged.\u000aImmunohistochemical studies performed on block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID reveal the following results\u000afor the infiltrating carcinoma:\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID): 2+ staining. Further evaluation by\u000afluorescence in situ hybridization (FISH)\u000amethod will be performed and results\u000areported in an addendum to follow.\u000aAddeundum Signed Electronically Signed SAMPSON,RICHARD J. M.D. REMOVED_DATE \u000aDIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. Left axillary lymph node, biopsy:\u000aMetastatic ductal carcinoma (1/1).\u000aB. Left breast, excision:\u000aPoorly differentiated infiltrating duct carcinoma (3 cm.) with apocrine\u000afeatures.\u000aDuctal carcinoma in situ, comedocarcinoma, grade REMOVED_DATE \u000aC. Left breast (inferior margin), excision:\u000aInfiltrating duct carcinoma in two foci on the superficial-superior\u000aaspect of the specimen at the margin.\u000aD. Left axillary lymph nodes, dissection:\u000aMetastatic adenocarcinoma in one of eleven lymph nodes (1/11).\u000aSYNOPTIC REPORT:\u000aINVASIVE TUMOR:\u000a-histologic type: ductal with apocrine features\u000a-histologic grade: poorly differentiated\u000a-size (greatest dimension): 3 cm.\u000a-lymphatic/vascular invasion: present\u000a-perineural invasion: none identified\u000a-microcalcification: present\u000a-margins for invasive tumor: focally positive at a mid anterior margin near\u000athe medial portion of the specimen. The\u000arelation between this positive margin and the\u000atumor foci in the "inferior margin" of\u000aspecimen C is not clear.\u000a-immunohistochemical staining on prior specimen (S-06-1101) was reported as:\u000aEstrogen receptor: POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor: NEGATIVE\u000a-immunohistochemical staining for REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu will be performed on block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and\u000areported in an addendum to follow.\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU (DCIS):\u000a-histologic type: comedocarcinoma with apocrine features\u000a-histologic grade: REMOVED_DATE \u000a-size (greatest dimension): microscopic foci within and around the\u000ainvasive tumor\u000a-extent: focal\u000a-extensive intraductal component: absent\u000a-necrosis in DCIS: present, extensive\u000a-microcalcifications in DCIS: present\u000a-margins for DCIS: clear\u000aLYMPH NODES:\u000aPositive lymph nodes out of total sampled: REMOVED_DATE \u000a(2/12 non-sentinel lymph nodes).\u000a-size of largest metastasis (greatest dimension): REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000aADDITIONAL PATHOLOGIC FINDINGS:\u000aFibrocystic changes; microcalcifications; changes consistent with biopsy\u000asite.\u000aPRIOR RELATED SPECIMENS REVIEWED:\u000asite: left breast, 11 o'clock specimen #: S-06-1101 date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aCOMMENT: The tumor has granular cytoplasm in large cells with little cohesion.\u000aThe tumor cells are negative for mucin in mucicarmine and PAS-D stains.\u000apTNM - PATHOLOGIC STAGE\u000aAJCC Pathologic Classification (6th Ed.): pREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID pREMOVED_ACCESSION_IDa pMX\u000aThe pathologic TNM classification above is based only on the information\u000aavailable to the pathologist, and therefore may not be accurate.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by: Richard J. Sampson, M.D.\u000aINTRA-OPERATIVE CONSULTATION:\u000aOPERATING ROOM CONSULTATION (FROZEN SECTION):\u000aMetastatic tumor, ? breast, ? other.\u000aRJS\u000aClinical diagnosis & history:\u000aLeft breast carcinoma\u000aTissue-Designation:\u000aA.Lymph node, biopsy - axillary\u000aB.Breast, excision with margins - left\u000aC.Breast, excision with margins - left inferior margin\u000aD.Lymph nodes, dissection - left axillary\u000aGross description:\u000aThe specimen is received in four containers.\u000aSpecimen A labeled "axillary lymph node, right" consists of a lymph node which\u000ameasures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. which appears to be nearly entirely replaced by\u000ayellow-tan tumor tissue. 5X all, labeled REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and AF.\u000aSpecimen B labeled "left breast carcinoma" consists of a mass of breast tissue\u000awhich weighs 111 grams. It measures 9 x 7 x 4 cm. Two wire markers come into\u000aeither end of the specimen and two orienting sutures are present with a long\u000asuture designated lateral and a short suture designated superior. The entire\u000aspecimen is inked with black ink. The deep margin is inked with blue ink. The\u000alateral superficial margin is inked with yellow ink. Sections are taken from\u000asuperior to inferior showing a 3 x REMOVED_DATE x 3 cm. firm, rounded nodule with\u000agrossly negative resection margins except near the medial end where the\u000asuperficial margin appears very close. Sections are taken from lateral to\u000amedial in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. 8X.\u000aSpecimen C labeled "left breast carcinoma inferior margin" consists of a piece\u000aof breast tissue 4 x 3 x 2 cm. Two orienting sutures are present; a long\u000asuture lateral and a short suture superior. The deep margin is so oriented and\u000ais inked with blue. The superficial superior margin is inked with yellow. The\u000aentire specimen is also inked with black. Sections are taken from lateral to\u000amedial. 9X all, labeled REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aSpecimen D labeled "left axillary lymph node dissection" consists of a fat pad\u000ameasuring 8 x 6 x 2 cm. Dissection of this yields eleven small lymph nodes\u000ameasuring from REMOVED_DATE to REMOVED_DATE cm. 11X.\u000aDictated by: RJS____(signature on file)____ REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a____(signature on file)____RICHARD SAMPSON, M.D. REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a[report_end]
