VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: FinalType: Surgical Pathology Pathology Report: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID OPERATION DATE: 14 REMOVED_MONTH 04 ACCESSIONED ON: 14 REMOVED_MONTH 04 at 13:15 CLINICAL DATA: Right breast cancer by core biopsy. =============================================================================== *** FINAL DIAGNOSIS *** LYMPH NODE (RIGHT AXILLARY, SENTINEL), EXCISION: FOLLICULAR HYPERPLASIA; THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. NOTE: Keratin-positive tumor cells are not identified on three REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.3/Cam5.2 immunostained levels. BREAST (RIGHT), EXCISIONAL BIOPSY: INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA, MEDULLARY TYPE. SEE TABLE #1. FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES, HARBORING CALCIFICATIONS. TABLE OF PATHOLOGICAL FINDINGS #1 INVASIVE CARCINOMA Tumor size: REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm (gross measurement) Grade: 3 Lymphatic vessel invasion: Not identified Blood vessel invasion: Not identified Margin of invasive carcinoma: Invasive carcinoma extends to less than REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin of the specimen along a broad front. Location of ductal carcinoma in-situ: Not identified Stains for receptors: Requested BREAST (RIGHT, SUPERIOR HALF OF CAVITY, SHAVED MARGIN), UNORIENTED BIOPSY: FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES, WITH SCLEROSING ADENOSIS. THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. BREAST (RIGHT, INFERIOR HALF OF CAVITY, SHAVED MARGIN), UNORIENTED BIOPSY: NO DIAGNOSTIC ABNORMALITY RECOGNIZED. THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. Diagnosis by: John H. Eichhorn, M.D. Signed On: 16 REMOVED_MONTH 04 at 20:12 =============================================================================== *** IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum *** RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast (Right, block B): The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein. Some tumor cells stain faintly for progesterone receptor protein. The tumor cells show moderate (2+) overexpression of HER-2/c-erbB-2. See note. Note: These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital. They have not been cleared or approved by the U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA). The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary; this laboratory has established and verified the test's accuracy and precision. Added by: Atul Kumar Bhan, M.D. Signed On: 21 REMOVED_MONTH 04 at 18:22 *** HER-2 Addendum *** RESULTS OF FLUORESCENCE IN SITU HYBRIDIZATION (FISH) FOR HER-2/NEU GENE AMPLIFICATION Breast (Right, block B): HER-2/neu gene in tumor cells: REMOVED_DATE (Not Amplified). See note. Note: Results are expressed as the average ratio of HER-2 to chromosome 17 signals in 60 tumor cell nuclei. A ratio of greater than REMOVED_DATE or equal to REMOVED_DATE indicates REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu gene amplification adjusted for chromosome 17 polysomy using PathVysion by Vysis. Added by: Atul Kumar Bhan, M.D. Signed On: 23 REMOVED_MONTH 04 at 16:20 GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number and "right breast lumpectomy", is an oriented lumpectomy specimen that measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The specimen is inked as follows: posterior, black; anterior, blue; medial, green and lateral, yellow. The section reveals a firm tan-grey well-circumscribed nodule that measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The nodule is REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin. The mass is REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral and REMOVED_DATE cm to the medial margin. Representative sections of the mass and nearby breast are submitted in cassette A-D from superior to inferior. Representative sections of grossly normal breast tissue away from the mass are submitted in cassette E-F. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number and "sentinel node, hot and blue" is an aggregate of probable lymph nodes and attached unremarkable fibroadipose tissue, which measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. Two probable lymph nodes are dissected out the largest of which measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. Each is submitted entirely in cassette G. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number and "final shaved margin, superior half of cavity" is a non-oriented aggregate of unremarkable yellow-white fibroadipose tissue, which measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The specimen is sectioned and submitted entirely in cassette H-J. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number and "final shaved margin, inferior cavity" is a non-oriented aggregate of unremarkable white-yellow fibroadipose tissue, which measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The specimen is sectioned and submitted entirely in cassettes K&L. Resident: JOSHUA B. KISH, MD =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT - REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID REPORTS TO: Barbara Lynn Smith, M.D. PART A: LYMPH NODE (RIGHT AXILLARY, SENTINEL) PART B: BREAST (RIGHT), EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART C: BREAST (RIGHT, SUPERIOR HALF OF CAVITY, SHAVED REMOVED_MONTH PART D: BREAST (RIGHT, INFERIOR HALF OF CAVITY, SHAVED REMOVED_MONTH
