VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ROGER L CHRISTIAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Elizabeth A. Steensma, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Alessandra F Nascimento, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, EXCISION FOR A MASS:\u000aPHYLLODES TUMOR, low-grade (2.4 cm) (see NOTE).\u000aMitoses number less than REMOVED_DATE HPF.\u000aNo necrosis is present.\u000aTumor is REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior resection margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral\u000aresection margin and REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior resection margin.\u000aTumor is > 1cm from medial, superior and inferior resection margins.\u000aDuctal epithelial hyperplasia and adenosis.\u000aArterial calcifications are present.\u000aNOTE: The stroma is cellular with mild nuclear pleomorphism and focal mild\u000astromal overgrowth. The tumor borders are predominantly pushing but with focal\u000ainfiltration into adipose tissue. No heterologous elements are present.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, INFRA-LATERAL SHAVE MARGIN:\u000aBreast with fibroadenomatoid changes.\u000aDuctal epithelial hyperplasia and columnar cell changes.\u000aNo definite residual phyllodes tumor is seen.\u000aThis case was also reviewed by Dr. Susan Lester, Breast Pathology Service, who\u000aconcurs.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Mass, tail, right breast core Bx phyllodes.\u000aOperation: Excision.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Right breast mass.\u000aB/2. Infra-lateral shave margin.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart A, "Right breast mass", consists of a 19-gram tan/yellow lobulated portion\u000aof fibroadipose breast tissue (6.3 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The specimen has been\u000apreviously inked per pathology protocol by the surgeon (superior red, inferior\u000agreen, medial orange, lateral yellow, anterior blue, and posterior black) and\u000ais serially sectioned from inferior to superior. There is a pink/tan\u000awell-circumscribed nodule (2.4 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which is located less than REMOVED_DATE \u000acm from the posterior and lateral margins, REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE \u000acm from the medial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000aanterior margin. The remainder of the cut surface is tan/yellow, homogenous\u000awith no additional lesions or areas of disruption identified. Representative\u000asections are submitted to the tissue bank. The remainder of the specimen is\u000asubmitted in its entirety for histology.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Superior margin, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross sections, block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID to REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID to include lesion, 1\u000afrag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Inferior margin, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, "Infra-lateral shave margin", consists of an irregular tan/yellow\u000alobulated portion of fibroadipose breast tissue (3.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). One-half\u000aof the specimen has been previously inked blue per the surgeon and the opposite\u000asurface is inked green. The cut surface is tan/yellow and homogenous with\u000afocal area of dense fibrous tissue constituting approximately 60% of the breast\u000aparenchyma. The specimen is submitted in its entirety.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross section, 2 frags each, ESS.\u000aSEK/mmm\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Alessandra F Nascimento M.D., Electronically signed on\u000a4/27/2007\u000a[report_end]
