VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: BRENT T SHOJI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-05-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Vijay K Vanguri, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Jason L Hornick, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED BIOPSY FOR CALCIFICATIONS AND A CLIP:\u000aBenign breast tissue with epithelial hyperplasia.\u000aBiopsy site with mucin extravasation.\u000aOne (1) lymph node with no significant pathologic change.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000aNOTE: No epithelial atypia is identified. This case was also reviewed by Dr.\u000aSusan Lester (Breast Pathology Service), who concurs.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Abnl L mammogram, core bx with atypia\u000aOperation: L needle-loc breast bx\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal left mammo, abnormal core bx\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Left needle-localized breast bx - mammo\u000aRADIOLOGY REPORT:\u000aClip and calcifications in specimen.\u000aDr. E.P. Frost\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "1. left needle-localized breast biopsy", and consists of a portion of\u000afibrofatty breast tissue (9.4 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with a needle-localization wire\u000ain place (entering medially, exiting laterally) and an accompanying radiograph.\u000aThe specimen is inked by the surgeon per pathology protocol for the evaluation\u000aof margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green;\u000alateral/yellow; medial/orange. The specimen is serially sectioned from medial\u000ato lateral, revealing an ill-defined, tan/white, firm lesion (2.4 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm) which abuts the superior margin, comes to within REMOVED_DATE cm of the anterior\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the medial and posterior\u000amargins, and REMOVED_DATE cm of the nearest lateral margin. Within this lesion, there\u000aare multiple tan/white, firm, synthetic, radiolucent beads. The wire traverses\u000athe lesion. At REMOVED_DATE cm lateral and inferior to the lesion, there is a tan,\u000aencapsulated nodule (0.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) which is REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin, and 4 cm from the\u000anearest medial margin. The remaining breast tissue consists of hemorrhagic,\u000afibrous stroma (predominantly an area adjacent to the wire) and yellow,\u000alobulated fat.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: lesion, sequentially submitted from medial to lateral,\u000a(clip in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), multi frag, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: well-circumscribed nodule, 2 frag, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: lateral margin nearest lesion, 2 frag, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: medial margin nearest lesion, 2 frag, RSS\u000adfipab\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Jason L Hornick M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jason L Hornick M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a6/27/2005\u000a[report_end]
