VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID:REMOVED_CASE_ID Report Status: Signed\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aDIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. Right breast, excision:\u000aDuctal carcinoma in situ, grade REMOVED_DATE  cribriform type, with\u000amicrocalcifications, extensive and admixed with atypical ductal\u000ahyperplasia (see note).\u000aFibrocystic changes with ductal hyperplasia and intraductal papillomas.\u000aB. Posterior margin of right breast, excision:\u000aFocal ductal carcinoma in situ, grade REMOVED_DATE  cribriform type.\u000aFibrocystic changes with ductal hyperplasia.\u000aNOTE: In the right breast excision (specimen A), ductal carcinoma in situ and\u000aatypical ductal hyperplasia are present in multiple microscopic foci\u000athroughout the specimen, as well as in two nodular areas near the\u000alocalizing wires and each associated with areas of fibroplasia and\u000achronic inflammation consistent with two prior needle biopsy sites (the\u000areport of the Massachusetts General Hospital slide review, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID is\u000anoted). Ductal carcinoma in situ and atypical ductal hyperplasia are\u000apresent less than 1 mm. from inked margins in multiple foci including\u000asuperior, lateral, medial and superficial margins.\u000aDuctal carcinoma in situ present in the posterior margin excision\u000a(specimen B) is greater than 4 mm. from the inked margin.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by: Daniel D. Koelliker, M.D.\u000aClinical diagnosis & history:\u000aRight breast ductal carcinoma in situ and atypical ductal hyperplasia\u000aTissue-Designation:\u000aA.Breast, excision with margins - right, long lateral, short inferior\u000aB.Breast, excision with margins - right, posterior margin, suture furthest from margin\u000aGross description:\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin in two containers.\u000aSpecimen A labeled "right breast, long lateral, short inferior" consists of a\u000a6.3 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. portion of fibroadipose tissue containing two localizing\u000awires and marked with two separate sutures, and accompanied by a specimen\u000aX-ray. The margins throughout are inked black. The sutures are designated as\u000along-lateral, short-inferior on the requisition; based on these orientations\u000athe deep surface is identified and is inked red. The lateral half is\u000adouble-inked blue. The specimen is cross sectioned from superior towards\u000ainferior. Located in the superior portion a bent wire transverses the specimen\u000afrom superficial to deep. In this area, there is a ill-defined REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm. hard, pink-tan mass. Within this, there is a small metallic clip present.\u000aAdjacent to this, there is extensive fat necrosis and hemorrhage in the\u000aotherwise yellow, lobulated adipose tissue. More inferiorly, there is a second\u000awire which extends from superficial to deep. Within this area near the wire,\u000athere is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. similar, hard, pink-tan mass with surrounding\u000afat necrosis. The entire specimen is submitted serially in fourteen equal\u000across sections from superior to inferior with most having subdesignations A for\u000asuperficial and B for deep in a total of twenty-five cassettes. The superior\u000amass is entirely submitted in cross sections #5, where the wire was and #6,\u000awhere the clip was. The inferior nodule is submitted in cross section #10-12.\u000a25 agg. all.\u000aSpecimen B labeled "right breast posterior margin, suture furthest from margin"\u000aconsists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. portion of fibroadipose tissue with a suture\u000aon one surface which is inked black. The specimen is cross sectioned and\u000aserially submitted in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. 6 agg. all.\u000aDictated by: DDK____(signature on file)____MICHAEL J. ROSS, M.D. REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a____(signature on file)____DANIEL D. KOELLIKER, M.D. REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a[report_end]
