VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID:REMOVED_CASE_ID Report Status: Signed\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aDIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. Right breast, excision:\u000aDuctal carcinoma in situ, grade REMOVED_DATE  cribriform type, small scattered\u000afoci concentrated near prior biopsy site.\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia, multiple foci.\u000aFibrocystic changes with intraductal hyperplasia and calcifications.\u000aB. Right breast, superior margin, excision:\u000aDuctal carcinoma in situ, grade REMOVED_DATE  cribriform type with\u000amicrocalcification at the surgical margin (section REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aC. Right breast, lateral margin, excision:\u000aFibrocystic changes with intraductal hyperplasia.\u000aD. Right breast, medial margin, excision:\u000aFibrocystic changes with intraductal hyperplasia.\u000aE. Right breast, inferior margin, excision:\u000aFibrocystic changes with intraductal hyperplasia.\u000aF. Right breast, posterior margin, excision:\u000aFibrocystic changes with intraductal hyperplasia.\u000aNOTE: In specimen A, there is residual ductal carcinoma in situ present\u000aconsisting of small scattered foci (multifocal) and concentrated near\u000athe previous biopsy site. The estimated aggregate size is less than REMOVED_DATE \u000acm. The inked margins appear free of ductal carcinoma in situ; however,\u000aone focus is present within REMOVED_DATE mm. of the superior-medial margin\u000a(section REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID). The prior biopsy is reviewed (S-01-9808).\u000aFinal Diagnosis by: Dennis J. Feen, M.D.\u000aClinical diagnosis & history:\u000aRight breast ductal carcinoma in situ\u000aTissue-Designation:\u000aA.Breast, excision with margins - right\u000aB.Breast, excision with margins - right, superior margin\u000aC.Breast, excision with margins - right, lateral\u000aD.Breast, excision with margins - right, medial margin\u000aE.Breast, excision with margins - right, inferior margin\u000aF.Breast, excision with margins - right, posterior margin\u000aGross description:\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin in six containers.\u000aSpecimen A labeled "right breast re-excision" consists of an oval mass of\u000ayellow adipose tissue with overall dimensions REMOVED_DATE x 4 x REMOVED_DATE cm. On the\u000asuperior surface is a short suture; on the lateral surface, a long suture. The\u000asuperior surface is inked with blue ink and the remainder of the specimen,\u000ablack ink. The superior margin is submitted designated REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. The remaining\u000atissue is sectioned from medial to lateral designated REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. Its cut surface\u000ashows a biopsy site cavity REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x .10 cm. with surrounding induration and\u000afat necrosis.\u000aSpecimen B labeled "superior margin" consists of two fragments of yellow\u000aadipose tissue. The smaller is REMOVED_DATE x 1 x REMOVED_DATE cm. and the larger, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x\u000a0.5 cm. The margins of each are inked. There are no orienting sutures on\u000athese specimens. 6X.\u000aSpecimen C labeled "lateral" consists of two small irregular fragments of\u000ayellow adipose tissue, each approximately REMOVED_DATE x 1 x REMOVED_DATE cm. The margins of\u000aeach are inked. 4X all.\u000aSpecimen D labeled "medial right breast margin" consists of two irregular\u000afragments of yellow adipose tissue. The smaller is 1 x 1 x REMOVED_DATE cm. and the\u000alarger, 5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. Each is inked. There are no orienting sutures on\u000athe specimen. 4X.\u000aSpecimen E labeled "right breast margin, inferior" consists of four small\u000alobular fragments of adipose tissue, each approximately 1 x 1 x REMOVED_DATE cm. The\u000amargins are inked. 4X all.\u000aSpecimen F labeled "right breast, posterior margin" consists of two fragments\u000aof tissue. The smaller is 2 x 1 x REMOVED_DATE cm. and the larger, 3 x 2 x 1 cm. Each\u000aspecimen is inked. 4X all.\u000aDictated by: DJF____(signature on file)____DANIEL D. KOELLIKER, M.D. REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a____(signature on file)____DENNIS J. FEEN, M.D. REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a[report_end]
