aining tissue with black ink. Serially sectioned from medial to\u000alateral. The deep side is granular, red-brown and consistent with the prior\u000abiopsy site. 18X all.\u000aSECTION CODE: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - superior margin\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - remaining breast\u000aSpecimen B labeled "right breast mass, final superior/anterior #2" consists of\u000aan irregular fragment of yellow adipose tissue REMOVED_DATE x 4 x REMOVED_DATE cm. There are\u000atwo sutures on this specimen. The short one designates the superior surface\u000aand a long one, the lateral surface. The margins are inked. The superior\u000asurface is inked with blue ink. The specimen is sectioned proceeding from\u000amedial to lateral with the superior surface separately designated with blue\u000aink. The cut surface consists of homogeneous adipose tissue. 17X all.\u000aSpecimen C labeled "right breast mass, final superior/posterior #3" consists of\u000aa rectangular fragment of what appears to be homogeneous adipose tissue with\u000aoverall dimensions REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. There is a suture in the mid portion of\u000athe specimen designating the surface furthest from the cavity. This surface is\u000amarked with blue ink. The opposite surface is inked with black ink. The\u000aentire specimen is embedded proceeding from one end to the other, sequentially\u000adesignated REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. The cut surface consists of homogeneous adipose tissue. 8X\u000aall.\u000aDictated by: DJF____(signature on file)____RICHARD SAMPSON, M.D. REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a____(signature on file)____DENNIS J. FEEN, M.D. REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a[report_end]
