VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID:REMOVED_CASE_ID Report Status: Signed\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aDIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. Sentinel lymph nodes, right:\u000aIsolated tumor cell clusters in 2 of 2 lymph nodes.\u000aB. Skin of right chest wall, excision:\u000aNo diagnostic abnormalities recognized.\u000aC. Right breast, simple mastectomy:\u000aInfiltrating ductal carcinoma, high nuclear grade. (see synoptic report)\u000aDuctal carcinoma in situ, high grade, solid and micropapillary types,\u000awith necrosis, microcalcifications, and lobular extension.\u000aFocal atypical ductal hyperplasia, columnar cell type.\u000aFibrocystic changes with usual type ductal hyperplasia.\u000aSYNOPTIC REPORT: BREAST\u000aINVASIVE TUMOR:\u000a-histologic type: infiltrating ductal carcinoma\u000a-histologic grade: high nuclear grade\u000a-size (greatest dimension): less than REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000a-lymphatic/vascular invasion: none identified\u000a-perineural invasion: none identified\u000a-microcalcification: none identified\u000a-margins for invasive tumor: clear (greater than or equal to REMOVED_DATE cm.)\u000a-immunohistochemical staining on the formalin-fixed, paraffin-embedded\u000ablock(s) REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID reveals these results:\u000aEstrogen receptor: Infiltrating carcinoma no longer in block\u000aProgesterone receptor: Infiltrating carcinoma no longer in block\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID): Infiltrating carcinoma no longer in block\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU (DCIS):\u000a-histologic type: solid and micropapillary\u000a-histologic grade: high\u000a-size (greatest dimension): REMOVED_DATE cm (gross measurement)\u000a-extent: focal\u000a-extensive intraductal component: present\u000a-necrosis in DCIS: present\u000a-microcalcifications in DCIS: present\u000a-margins for DCIS: focally REMOVED_DATE 2 cm. to anterior\u000afocally less than REMOVED_DATE cm. to posterior\u000amultifocally REMOVED_DATE 2 cm. to posterior\u000a-immunohistochemical staining on prior specimen (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) was reported as:\u000aEstrogen receptor: NEGATIVE (0% of nuclei stained)\u000aProgesterone receptor: NEGATIVE (0% of nuclei stained)\u000a-immunohistochemical staining on the formalin-fixed, paraffin-embedded\u000ablocks REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID reveals these results for the DCIS:\u000aEstrogen receptor: NEGATIVE (0% of nuclei stained)\u000aProgesterone receptor: NEGATIVE (0% of nuclei stained)\u000aEstrogen receptor (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, Ventana Medical Systems) is assessed visually by\u000aquantitation of the percent of tumor cells staining.\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU (LCIS):\u000aNone identified.\u000aLYMPH NODES:\u000aLymph nodes with isolated tumor cells out of total sampled: REMOVED_DATE \u000a(2/2 sentinel lymph nodes; REMOVED_DATE non-sentinel lymph nodes).\u000aThe sentinel lymph node, specimen A, is examined at multiple\u000alevels with H&E stains and immunohistochemical stains for keratin.\u000aThe isolated tumor cell clusters are found in multiple blocks including the\u000afrozen section control, however tumor cells cannot be identified on any of\u000athe H&E stained sections, including the frozen sections.\u000aSKIN:\u000a-nipple: unremarkable\u000aPRIOR RELATED SPECIMEN REPORTS REVIEWED:\u000aright breast, lower outer spec#: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aCOMMENT: After the discovery of isolated tumor cells, 6 additional blocks of\u000aDCIS were embedded and examined microscopically. Furthermore, three blocks\u000aeach containing a large section of tissue with extensive DCIS were each stained\u000awith three immunohistochemical stains (actin, calponin, smooth muscle myosin).\u000aThese stains demonstrate an intact myoepithelial layer in the vast majority of\u000aductal and lobular units involved by DCIS. There is, however, one minute focus\u000a(less than REMOVED_DATE cm.) that lacks evidence of a myoepithelial layer with all three\u000astains. This finding is supportive of the diagnosis of infiltrating ductal\u000acarcinoma. The infiltrating tumor cells have a high nuclear grade. The minute\u000aquantity of infiltrating carcinoma precludes full histologic grading.\u000aAJCC pTNM Classification (6th Ed.): pTmic pREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID (sn)(i+) pMX\u000aThe pathologic TNM classification above is based only on the information\u000aavailable to the pathologist, and therefore may not be accurate.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by: Todd E. Abbott, M.D.\u000aINTRA-OPERATIVE CONSULTATION:\u000aOPERATING ROOM CONSULTATION (FROZEN SECTION):\u000aRight sentinel lymph nodes (two):\u000aNo tumor seen in two lymph nodes.\u000aTEA\u000aClinical diagnosis & history:\u000aRight breast carcinoma\u000aTissue-Designation:\u000aA.Sentinel lymph node - right\u000aB.Skin, excision - right chest wall\u000aC.Breast, simple mastectomy - right\u000aGross description:\u000aThe specimen is received in three containers.\u000aSpecimen A is received fresh from the Operating Room for intraoperative\u000aevaluation, labeled "right sentinel node" and consists of a fragment of tissue\u000ameasuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. Cut section reveals the presence of two separate\u000alymph nodes. A representative section is submitted for frozen section. The\u000afrozen section remnant is resubmitted in cassette AF. 3 agg. all.\u000aSpecimen B is received in formalin, labeled "right chest wall skin" and\u000aconsists of a circular fragment of tissue with the following orienting sutures:\u000astitch = lateral. The outside diameter is REMOVED_DATE cm. The inside diameter is REMOVED_DATE \u000acm. 4 agg.\u000aSection code: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - 12 o'clock\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - 3 o'clock\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - 6 o'clock\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - 9 o'clock\u000aSpecimen C is received fresh, labeled "right simple mastectomy" and consists of\u000aa 430 gram, 19 x 17 x up to REMOVED_DATE cm. mastectomy specimen with the following\u000aorienting sutures: stitch on tail. The nipple measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. There\u000ais a palpable abnormality in the lower outer quadrant measuring approximately\u000a6.5 x 4 x 4 cm. The anterior surface is inked black. The posterior surface is\u000ainked orange. The specimen is serially sectioned in the superior-inferior\u000aaxis, revealing white, light tan, firm, gritty parenchyma that correlates to\u000athe palpable mass. This region is in the lower outer quadrant and measures REMOVED_DATE \u000ax REMOVED_DATE x approximately 4 cm. This mass grossly approaches the anterior and\u000aposterior margins.\u000aSection code: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - lateral margin\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - sequential cassettes showing greatest linear extent of\u000atumor in superior-inferior axis\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - tumor in relation to posterior margin\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - nipple sections\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - tumor in relation to anterior inked margin\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - upper inner quadrant\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - lower inner quadrant\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - upper outer quadrant\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - additional tumor blocks, 26 agg.\u000aTotal fixation time for blocks REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID is 28 hours.\u000aTotal fixation time for blocks REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID is 76 hours.\u000aDictated by: TEA____(signature on file)____ REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a____(signature on file)____ REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a[report_end]
