VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aBROWN, FELIX, MARCEL, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by BROWN,FELIX MARCEL,M.D.\u000aRIGHT BREAST EXCISION, WIRE LOCALIZATION FOR A CLIP:\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aSEVERE ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA (see NOTE)\u000aSYNOPSIS:\u000aNO INVASIVE CARCINOMA IDENTIFIED -\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aTypes - solid, cribriform\u000aNuclear grade - intermediate\u000aCalcifications in DCIS - absent\u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - absent\u000aMicroinvasion (<0.1cm) - absent\u000aExtent of DCIS\u000aNumber of blocks:total - 1:14 blocks\u000aFinal Margins (DCIS)\u000aNegative (>0.3 cm) - superior, medial, lateral, posterior,\u000ainferior\u000aClose (<0.1 cm) - anterior (broad front)\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - absent\u000aOTHER FINDINGS\u000aSevere atypical ductal hyperplasia (see NOTE)\u000aCysts\u000aApocrine metaplasia\u000aCalcifications in benign epithelium\u000aArterial calcifications\u000aCore biopsy site\u000aSkeletal muscle\u000aColumnar alteration of lobules with prominent snouts and secretions\u000aAJCC CLASSIFICATION - Tis pNx MX\u000aNOTE: The biopsy shows a spectrum of changes from severe ADH to frank DCIS with\u000aseveral foci difficult to precisely classify. This process is present in a\u000atotal of three of fourteen (3:14) blocks and involves (ink on lesion) the\u000aanterior and inferior margins.\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: by BROWN,FELIX MARCEL,M.D.\u000aThis case was subsequently reviewed by Dr. J. Connolly who felt the entire\u000aspectrum of proliferative changes is best characterized as atypical ductal\u000ahyperplasia with focal necrosis. No ductal carcinoma in-situ is present.\u000aTherefore, the above diagnosis should read:\u000aRIGHT BREAST EXCISION, WIRE LOCALIZATION FOR A CLIP:\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia with focal necrosis, present at the\u000aanterior and inferior resection margins.\u000aCalcifications in association with benign epithelium.\u000aArterial calcifications.\u000aColumnar alteration of lobules with prominent snouts and secretions.\u000aCore biopsy site.\u000aCysts and apocrine metaplasia.\u000aNo invasive or in-situ carcinoma identified.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: History of invasive ductal carcinoma of left breast with lymph node\u000amets, also history of colon cancer (per Pathology resident)\u000aOperation: Right needle directed breast\u000abiopsy Clinical Diagnosis: Atypical hyperplasia right breast\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1. Right breast tissue (long/lateral; short/superior)\u000aRADIOLOGY: Clip and calcifications in specimen. JL.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by PADERA,ROBERT F.,JR.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in one part, labeled with the patient's name,\u000aunit number and "#1. right breast tissue", and consists of a single needle\u000adirected breast biopsy specimen. The specimen is received with a wire in\u000aplace. The specimen is received with two orienting sutures. A double short\u000asuture indicates superior and a double long suture indicates lateral. The\u000aspecimen measures REMOVED_DATE cm from superior to inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm from medial to\u000alateral, and REMOVED_DATE cm from anterior to posterior. The specimen is inked by the\u000apathologist per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior =\u000ablack; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow;\u000amedial = orange. The breast is serially sectioned to reveal a nodular area in\u000athe region of the clip. This area is located adjacent to the anterior and\u000ainferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin.\u000aThis area measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. In addition to this mass a dense area\u000aof fibrous tissue is present adjacent to the anterior, superior, inferior\u000amargins, coming to within REMOVED_DATE cm of the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000alateral margin and REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin. The breast is thinly\u000asectioned and entirely submitted for histologic evaluation.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  right breast tissue, submitted from lateral to medial, mult\u000afrags, ESS (the area of the clip is in micro 4 and the firm\u000afibrous area is in micros REMOVED_DATE )\u000arp\u000aReports to: IGLEHART, JAMES, DIRK M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
