The cavity is filled with yellow tan tissue consistent with fat\u000anecrosis. There is serous fluid and fine multi-lobulated septae within the\u000acavity. The cavity is REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior and posterior margins, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom the lateral margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000ainferior margin and REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior margin. The biopsy cavity\u000acomposes 75% of the specimen and the remaining specimen is fibrofatty.\u000aRepresentative sections are submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  representative sections of breast tissue, 1 to 2 frags each, RSS.\u000amrk\u000aReports to: IGLEHART, JAMES, DIRK M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
