VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Kremena V. Star, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Alessandra F Nascimento, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. LEFT BREAST MASS, EXCISION:\u000aCellular fibroadenoma (2.0 cm), see NOTE.\u000aThe lesion extends to the anterior margin.\u000aNOTE: The lesion shows increased stromal cellularity and focal stromal\u000aovergrowth. Mitotic figures are very rare (<1:50 HPF). The borders are fairly\u000awell circumscribed. Therefore, the lesion would be best classified as a\u000acellular fibroadenoma.\u000aThis case was also reviewed by Dr. S. Lester, Breast Pathology Service, who\u000aconcurs.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 21 y/o female who noted a mass on BSE S/P REMOVED_DATE  core biopsy of a\u000a2.2-cm L 12:00 axis mass revealed a fibroepithelial lesion. Excision is\u000arecommended to determine if this is a cellular fibroadenoma vs phyllodes tumor.\u000a(Family history of breast cancer in her mother's cousin in her 20's).\u000aOperation: Excision of a left breast mass.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: L breast mass.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) Left breast mass - short stitch - superior, long stitch - lateral, whip\u000astitch @ chest wall.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "Left breast mass short stitch superior long stitch lateral whip stitch\u000achest wall", and consists of an irregular tan-yellow lobulated portion of\u000afibroadipose breast tissue (2.6 medial to lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm superior to inferior,\u000aand REMOVED_DATE cm anterior to posterior) with a short suture designating superior\u000amargin, long suture designating lateral margin, and a whip stitch designating\u000achest wall margins. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol (superior\u000ared, inferior green, medial orange, lateral yellow, anterior blue, and\u000aposterior black) and is serially sectioned from medial to lateral. The cut\u000asurface is composed of primarily dense white fibrous tissue (greater than 95%),\u000awhich extends through the resection margins. There is only a scant amount of\u000atan-yellow homogenous fibroadipose tissue present. No discrete lesions are\u000agrossly identified. The specimen is submitted in its entirety.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross sections medial to lateral, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aPlease note: The specimen is not received with a specimen radiograph or needle\u000alocalization wire.\u000aSEK/mmm\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Alessandra F Nascimento M.D., Electronically signed on\u000aThursday May 14, 2009 at 11:52:43AM\u000a[report_end]
