VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: MEHRA GOLSHAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Matthew D. Stachler, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Jacqueline M William, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. RIGHT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISIONAL BIOPSY FOR A CLIP:\u000aBreast tissue with columnar cell hyperplasia and focal\u000apseodoangiomatoid stromal hyperplasia.\u000aCore biopsy site changes are present.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the\u000aspecimen, including margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 45 year old female with history of right breast atypical ductal\u000ahyperplasia. Recent MRI core revealed focal atypia.\u000aOperation: Right breast wire localized excisional biopsy.\u000aOperative Findings: Not provided.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast abnormal mammogram.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) right breast wire localized excisional bx - short/superior, long/lateral\u000a--> mammo.\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000aClip in specimen. OR called. LBS.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in one part, labeled with the patient's name and\u000aunit number, labeled "#1. Right breast wire localized excision biopsy short\u000astitch superior long stitch lateral", and consists of irregular tan/yellow\u000alobulated fragment of breast tissue (3.1 cm medial to lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm superior\u000ato inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm anterior to posterior). The specimen is marked by sutures\u000aas follows: Short equals superior, long equals lateral. The specimen is inked\u000aper pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black;\u000aanterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange.\u000aThere is a needle localization wire, which enters the superior/medial border\u000aand exits the inferior/lateral margin and marks a clip as demonstrated on the\u000aaccompanying radiograph. The specimen is serially sectioned from lateral to\u000amedial to reveal approximately 80% fibrous tissue and 20% fatty tissue. There\u000ais a hemorrhagic core biopsy site encompassing a clip, which measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000ax REMOVED_DATE cm. No discrete masses are noted. The entire specimen is submitted for\u000ahistologic evaluation.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, radially sectioned, 5 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Body of specimen sectioned from lateral to medial including\u000ahemorrhagic core biopsy site and all sections (clip in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), in relation to\u000aanterior, posterior, superior, inferior margins, 2 frags each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin, radially sectioned, 5 frags, ESS.\u000aeam/lp\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jacqueline M William M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed\u000aon Monday August 24, 2009 at 10:16:43PM\u000a[report_end]
