VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID:REMOVED_CASE_ID Report Status: Signed\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aDIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. Right axilla sentinel lymph node, excision:\u000aNo tumor seen in one sentinel lymph node (0/1), (see note).\u000aB. Right axilla, lymph node, excision:\u000aAdipose tissue only; no lymph node seen.\u000aThe entire specimen has been submitted.\u000aC. Right breast, excision:\u000aInvasive poorly differentiated ductal carcinoma, REMOVED_DATE cm. (see note).\u000aDuctal carcinoma in situ, high grade, solid and comedo type, with\u000anecrosis.\u000aSkin with no tumor seen.\u000aHealing biopsy site changes.\u000aSkeletal muscle with no tumor seen.\u000aFocal fibrocystic changes.\u000aSYNOPTIC REPORT:\u000aINVASIVE TUMOR:\u000a-histologic type: ductal\u000a-histologic grade: poorly differentiated\u000a-size (greatest dimension): REMOVED_DATE cm. and located in the center of\u000aspecimen\u000a-lymphatic/vascular invasion: present, focal\u000a-perineural invasion: none identified\u000a-microcalcification in invasive tumor: none identified\u000a-margins for invasive tumor: clear (greater than or equal to REMOVED_DATE \u000acm.)\u000a-immunohistochemical staining for estrogen and progesterone receptors has\u000abeen performed and reported on the prior specimen S-05-294.\u000a-immunohistochemical staining performed on block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID reveal the following\u000aresults for the infiltrating carcinoma:\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID): POSITIVE (3+)\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU (DCIS):\u000a-histologic type: solid and comedo\u000a-histologic grade: high\u000a-size (greatest dimension): within and adjacent to invasive tumor\u000aand seen in sections from the\u000alateral end of the specimen and in\u000arandom sections from the area\u000abetween the tumor and medial and\u000alateral ends of the specimen\u000a-extent: multifocal\u000a-extensive intraductal component: absent\u000a-necrosis in DCIS: present, extensive\u000a-microcalcifications in DCIS: present\u000a-margins for DCIS: clear (greater than or equal to REMOVED_DATE \u000acm.)\u000aLYMPH NODES:\u000aA total of one lymph node sampled is negative for malignancy (0/1 sentinel\u000alymph nodes).\u000aCOMMENT: The sentinel lymph node, specimen A, is examined at multiple\u000alevels with H&E stains and with immunohistochemical stains for keratin.\u000aPRIOR RELATED SPECIMENS REVIEWED:\u000aRight breast needle core biopsies; S-05-294; REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by: Nicole A. Mihok, M.D.\u000aINTRA-OPERATIVE CONSULTATION:\u000aOPERATING ROOM CONSULTATION (FROZEN SECTION):\u000aSentinel lymph node: No evidence of malignancy in frozen section; final\u000adiagnosis deferred to permanent sections.\u000aDDK\u000aClinical diagnosis & history:\u000aRight breast carcinoma\u000aTissue-Designation:\u000aA.Sentinel lymph node - right\u000aB.Lymph node, biopsy - right axillary\u000aC.Breast, excision with margins - right\u000aGross description:\u000aThe specimen is received in three parts.\u000aSpecimen A labeled "right sentinel lymph node" is received fresh from the\u000aOperating Room and consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. tan lymph node with\u000aadjacent adipose tissue. The specimen is serially sectioned and sampled for\u000afrozen section. The remnant of the frozen is submitted entirely in AF. 1 agg.\u000aall.\u000aSpecimen B labeled "right axillary node" is received in formalin and consists\u000aof a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. portion of adipose tissue. The specimen is serially\u000asectioned and palpated. No visible lymph node is identified. The entire\u000aspecimen is submitted in cassettes REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID through REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. 2 agg. all.\u000aSpecimen C labeled "right breast" consists of a portion of breast tissue with a\u000askin ellipse received in formalin. The specimen measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000aOn the anterior surface is an ellipse of skin with a small scar. The skin\u000aellipse measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. There is a short stitch designating the\u000asuperior margin, and a long stitch designating the lateral edge. The superior\u000ahalf of the specimen is inked blue, the inferior is inked green, and the deep\u000amargin is inked black. The specimen is sectioned from lateral towards medial\u000aand the cut section shows a firm, palpable mass that measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm. It is located under the skin in the center of the specimen. It is grossly\u000aclear of the margins. Representative sections are submitted. 21 agg.\u000aSECTION CODE: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - entire lateral margin\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - entire medial margin\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - entire contiguous section containing the tumor and all\u000aof the margins adjacent to the tumor\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - there is no cassette REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID or block\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - two random sections from the slice next to the\u000alateral margin\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - two random sections from the slice just medial to the\u000aslice containing tumor\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - two sections from the slice that is the second most\u000amedial from the slice containing the tumor\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - two sections from the second most lateral slice of\u000atissue\u000aDictated by: LV____(signature on file)____DANIEL D. KOELLIKER, M.D. REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a____(signature on file)____NICOLE MIHOK, M.D. REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a[report_end]
