VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, partial mastectomy\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: MEHRA GOLSHAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Kyle L. Viani, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Jacqueline M William, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. LEFT BREAST, SIMPLE MASTECTOMY:\u000aBenign breast tissue with fibroadenomatoid changes,\u000asclerosis, biopsy site changes, epithelial hyperplasia,\u000aapocrine metaplasia and duct ectasia.\u000aSkin with no significant pathologic change.\u000aB. RIGHT MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY AND AXILLARY NODE DISSECTION\u000a(including Parts B and C):\u000aINVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA\u000aSize - REMOVED_DATE cm, located in retroareolar region\u000aMultifocal - There is a minute focus of microinvasion\u000a(< REMOVED_DATE cm) associated with a focus of\u000alymphovascular invasion (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aHistologic type - Ductal (confirmed by a positive\u000aE-Cadherin stain)\u000aHistologic grade (SBR) - II (Moderate) (6 to 7 points)\u000aTubules - < 10% (3 points)\u000aNuclear grade - High (3 points)\u000aMitotic counts - 1 point\u000aEIC - Negative\u000aLVI - Present in multiple foci (> 20) in\u000amultiple slides (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID,REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID,REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID,REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) close\u000ato mass.\u000aDermal LVI - Absent\u000aSkin invasion - Absent\u000aSkeletal muscle invasion - Not applicable\u000aFinal Margins (invasive)\u000aNegative (> REMOVED_DATE cm) - Deep\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aTypes - Cribriform\u000aNuclear grade - Intermediate\u000aCalcifications in DCIS - Absent\u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - Absent\u000aExtent of DCIS\u000aNumber of blocks/total - 2:11 blocks\u000aMargins (DCIS)\u000aNegative (> REMOVED_DATE cm) - Deep\u000aLYMPH NODES\u000aAxillary lymph nodes - Positive\u000aNumber of positive nodes - 3\u000aNumber of nodes examined - 15\u000aTOTAL POSITIVE NODES (all specimens)- 3:15\u000aSize of largest metastatic focus - REMOVED_DATE cm (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID)\u000aExtranodal extension - Present\u000aSize of extranodal extension REMOVED_DATE cm (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID)\u000aTumor is also identified within multiple extracapsular\u000alymphatics\u000aOTHER FINDINGS\u000aMarked background sclerosis and fibrosis\u000aCore biopsy site\u000aAJCC Classification (6th edition) - REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDc REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDa\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER, PR, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID:\u000aA REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID stain performed at BWH is negative (1+)\u000a(See report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID for prior receptor studies)\u000aC. RIGHT AXILLARY CONTENTS:\u000aPlease see Part B.\u000aThe immunoperoxidase, immunofluorescence and in-situ hybridization tests\u000aperformed at Brigham and Women's Hospital were developed and their performance\u000acharacteristics determined by the Immunohistochemistry Laboratories in the\u000aDepartment of Pathology at BWH. They have not been cleared or approved by the\u000aU.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA). The FDA has determined that such\u000aclearance or approval is not necessary.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 45 year old female with right breast cancer, node positive. Left\u000abreast - high risk of cancer.\u000aOperation: Left breast simple mastectomy, right breast modified radical\u000amastectomy.\u000aOperative Findings: Not provided.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast - high risk of cancer, right breast - cancer.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) left breast simple mastectomy - short suture/superior, long suture/lateral\u000a(to FS for Bst Bank).\u000aB/2) rt breast modified radical mastectomy - short suture/superior, long\u000asuture/axillary tail (to FS for Bst Bank).\u000aC/3) right axillary contents.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in three parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname, unit number.\u000aPart A, labeled "left breast simple mastectomy", consists of a 236-gram\u000a(postfixation) simple mastectomy specimen (15.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with overlying\u000atan/white wrinkled skin ellipse (9.0 x REMOVED_DATE cm) with a nipple-areolar complex\u000a(2.5 cm in diameter), and an everted nipple (1.0 cm in diameter). There is a\u000ashort suture designating the superior margin, and a long suture designating the\u000alateral margin. The deep margin is inked black and the specimen is serially\u000asectioned. There is an ill-defined stellate red/brown hemorrhagic area (1.0 x\u000a0.8 x REMOVED_DATE cm) consistent with a previous biopsy site. The previous biopsy site\u000acomes within REMOVED_DATE cm of the deep margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the nipple-areolar complex,\u000aand is located within the central left lower outer quadrant of the breast.\u000aAdjacent to the previous biopsy site is a well-circumscribed tan/white smooth\u000anodule (1.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which comes within REMOVED_DATE cm from the deep margin,\u000aand REMOVED_DATE cm from the nipple-areolar complex. Remainder of the breast parenchyma\u000ais tan/yellow and homogeneous and consists predominantly of dense white fibrous\u000atissue constituting approximately 90% of breast parenchyma. The lateral aspect\u000aof the specimen is serially sectioned with no lymph nodes grossly identified.\u000aNo additional lesions are grossly identified. Representative sections are\u000asubmitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Nipple areola section, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross sections medial to lateral biopsy cavity, 1 frag\u000aeach, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Firm nodule adjacent to biopsy cavity, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Left upper outer quadrant, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Left lower outer quadrant, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Left upper inner quadrant, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Left lower inner quadrant, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aPart B, labeled "right modified radical mastectomy, short superior, long\u000alateral/axillary tail", consists of a 280-gram (postfixation) simple mastectomy\u000aspecimen (15.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with an overlying tan/white wrinkled skin\u000aellipse (7.8 x REMOVED_DATE cm) with a nipple-areolar complex (3.0 cm in diameter) with\u000aan everted nipple (1.5 cm in diameter), and a small portion of attached\u000aaxillary tail (6.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). There is a short suture designating the\u000asuperior margin, and a long suture designating the lateral/axillary tail. The\u000adeep margin is inked black and the specimen is serially sectioned. There is a\u000astellate firm white lesion (1.3 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which is located REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000athe deep margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the nipple-areolar complex consistent with the\u000aprevious biopsy cavity. The biopsy cavity is located in the central aspect of\u000athe breast between the right upper outer and right upper inner quadrants.\u000aWithin the biopsy cavity is a silver metallic biopsy clip. Remainder of the\u000abreast parenchyma is tan/yellow and homogeneous with predominantly admixed\u000adense white fibrous tissue constituting approximately 80% of the breast\u000aparenchyma. No additional lesions are grossly identified. The scant amount of\u000aattached axillary tail is sectioned and there are seven well-circumscribed\u000apink/tan smooth rubbery nodules consistent with lymph nodes identified (ranging\u000afrom REMOVED_DATE cm to REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest dimension). Please note that representative\u000asections of the tumor and normal breast tissue are submitted from the right\u000abreast and normal tissue from the left breast for breast tissue banking special\u000astudies per Dr. Richardson.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Nipple-areolar complex to include biopsy cavity with clip, 1 frag,\u000aESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Remainder of biopsy cavity, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID to include longitudinal section\u000aof biopsy cavity to deep margin, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Breast parenchyma adjacent to biopsy cavity and area of tumor\u000atissue bank, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Representative sections right upper outer quadrant, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Representative sections right lower outer quadrant, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Representative sections right upper inner quadrant, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Representative sections right lower inner quadrant, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 4 possible lymph nodes, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 3 possible lymph nodes, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aPart C, labeled "Rt axillary contents", consists of multiple irregular\u000atan/yellow lobulated portions of fibroadipose tissue (3.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The\u000aspecimen is serially sectioned and there are several well-circumscribed\u000apink/tan to tan/white firm nodules consistent with lymph nodes (ranging from\u000a0.4 cm to REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest dimension). The larger lymph node is serially\u000asectioned, and the specimen is submitted in its entirety.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 5 possible lymph nodes, 5 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 possible grossly positive lymph node bisected, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 grossly positive lymph node serially sectioned, 5 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Remainder of fibroadipose tissue, multi frags, ESS.\u000asek/lp\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jacqueline M William M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed\u000aon Friday REMOVED_MONTH 20, 2009 at 05:38:30AM\u000a[report_end]
