VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Sentinel Lymph Nodes(s)\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ROGER L CHRISTIAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-05-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Jey-Hsin Chen, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Alessandra F Nascimento, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aLEFT BREAST EXCISION FOR A MASS (specimen #3 of 4), SENTINEL NODE BIOPSY\u000a(specimen #1 of 4) (INCLUDING FSA) AND AXILLARY NODE DISSECTION (specimen #2 of\u000a4):\u000aINVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA AND METASTATIC CARCINOMA TO LYMPH NODES.\u000aSYNOPSIS:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA\u000aSize - REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aMultifocal - No\u000aHistologic Type - Lobular\u000aHistologic Grade (SBR) - II (Moderate)\u000aNuclear Grade - Intermediate\u000aEIC - Negative\u000aLymphovascular invasion - Present\u000aDermal lymphatic invasion - Absent\u000aSkin invasion - Absent\u000aSkeletal muscle invasion - N/A\u000aFinal Margins (invasive)\u000aNegative (>0.3 cm) - Lateral, Superior\u000aClose (0.1 to REMOVED_DATE cm) - Inferior (focal, REMOVED_DATE cm, block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID)\u000aPositive (ink on carcinoma) - Anterior (broad front, blocks REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), posterior (broad front, block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), medial (broad front, block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID)\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU - Absent\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - Positive\u000aLYMPH NODES\u000aSentinel lymph node (3 HE levels examined): Positive\u000aNumber of positive nodes - 1\u000aNumber of nodes examined - 3\u000aAxillary lymph nodes: Negative\u000aNumber of positive nodes - 1\u000aNumber of nodes examined - 14\u000aTOTAL POSITIVE NODES (all specimens) - REMOVED_DATE \u000aSize of largest metastatic focus REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aExtranodal extension Present, focal, microscopic\u000aOTHER FINDINGS\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia\u000aCore biopsy site\u000aAJCC CLASSIFICATION (6th edition) - REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID pREMOVED_ACCESSION_IDa (including SN) MX\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER/PR/HER-2) - Pending\u000aLEFT BREAST, EXCISION, INFERIOR SHAVE MARGIN (specimen #4 of 4):\u000aINVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA, (at least REMOVED_DATE cm), moderately differentiated\u000a(modified Bloom Richardson grade II/III).\u000aTumor extends to the cauterized green and black inked resection margins as a\u000abroad front.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: None given.\u000aOperation: Left wide excisional breast biopsy, sentinel lymph node biopsy.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast cancer.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000a1. Sentinel nodes - FS\u000a2. Axillary tissue.\u000a3. Tumor site, left breast, suture long-lateral, short-superior - to tissue\u000abank via FS (Ruth Gomes).\u000a4. Inferior shaved margin.\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "LEFT SENTINEL NODES" (FSA):\u000aMetastatic carcinoma in one (1) of two 2) lymph nodes.\u000aOR Consultation by: JASON L. HORNICK, M.D., PH.D.\u000aResident: PATRICIA A. R. BRUNKER, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aThe senior physician certifies that he/she personally conducted a gross and/or\u000amicroscopic examination of the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed\u000athe rapid diagnos(es) related thereto.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in four parts, each labeled with the patient?s\u000aname, unit number.\u000aPart A. "#1 Left sentinel nodes", consists of one fragment of yellow\u000afibroadipose tissue (2.7 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The specimen is dissected, revealing\u000atwo lymph node candidates (0.9 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm, inked blue, and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm, not inked). The lymph node candidates are each bisected and entirely\u000asubmitted for frozen section analysis, labeled as FSA. A third lymph node\u000acandidate (0.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) is identified and not frozen. The specimen is\u000aentirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: FSA remnant, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Third lymph node candidate, bisected, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, "#2 Axillary tissue", consists of a yellow/tan fibroadipose tissue (8 x\u000a3.5 x REMOVED_DATE cm). The specimen is dissected and potential lymph nodes, ranging\u000afrom REMOVED_DATE to REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest dimension, are submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: One potential node, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: One potential node, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: One potential node, bisected, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Six potential nodes, 1 frag each, 6 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: One potential node, bisected, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Seven potential nodes, 1 frag each, 7 frags, ESS.\u000aPart C, "#3 Tumor site left breast", consists of a tan/yellow, lobulated\u000afibrofatty tissue (7.6 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) attached to a tan/white blue-tinged skin\u000aellipse (5.6 x REMOVED_DATE cm). The specimen is oriented with a short suture marking\u000athe superior surface and a long suture marking the lateral surface, and is\u000areceived inked by the surgeon for histologic evaluation of margins:\u000aposterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow;\u000amedial/orange. The skin ellipse is located on the anterior surface, and the\u000atissue is focally infiltrated by a blue dye at the anterior surface. The\u000aspecimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral to reveal a tan/gray,\u000alobulated, firm, ill-defined mass (2.1 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) that extends to within\u000a0.1 cm of the deep, puckered margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of\u000athe medial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the superior\u000amargin, and REMOVED_DATE cm of the lateral margin. Just superior and medial to the tumor\u000ais an ill-defined, focally bright yellow hemorrhagic area (2.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm).\u000aThe remainder of the breast parenchyma is comprised of approximately 50%\u000afibrous tissue, grossly unremarkable. A representative section of the tumor and\u000auninvolved breast is submitted to the breast bank and to Dr. Weinberg's lab for\u000aspecial studies. Representative sections are submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Tumor in relation to closest posterior and inferior margins, 2\u000afrags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Tumor in relation to inferior and anterior margins, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Tumor in relation to closest anterior and superior margins and\u000askin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Closest medial margin, perpendicular, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Closest lateral margin, perpendicular, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Area of hemorrhage in relation to inferior surface, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Skin tips, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Additional superior margin, 3 frags, RSS.\u000aPart D, "#4 Inferior shaved margin", is an unoriented yellow/tan rubbery\u000afibrofatty tissue (2.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), previously inked green on one surface\u000aof the specimen. The remaining surface is inked black. The specimen is serially\u000asectioned, revealing a yellow/tan color on cut surface. No masses are grossly\u000aappreciated. The specimen is entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Inferior shaved margin, 5 frags, ESS.\u000ajhc/elw\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Jey-Hsin Chen M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Alessandra F Nascimento M.D., Electronically signed on\u000a3/13/2005\u000a[report_end]
