ior surface of\u000athe specimen is a smooth, fascial plane except for an area of\u000apuckering/firmness subjacent to the nipple. The posterior surface is inked\u000ablack. The previous biopsy cavity is identified, subjacent to the nipple and\u000ameasures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The cavity and surrounding firmness abuts the\u000adeep margin. The remainder of the specimen consists of grossly unremarkable,\u000afibroadipose tissue. No lymph node candidates are identified within the\u000alateral portion of the specimen. Representative sections are submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Biopsy cavity to deep margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Additional biopsy cavity, 3 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Firm area adjacent to biopsy cavity, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Nipple with scar and biopsy cavity, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Upper/outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lower/outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Upper/inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lower/inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Additional firm area adjacent (lateral) to biopsy site,\u000a1 frag, RSS.\u000amah/MMM\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Marian H Harris M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by William R Welch M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
