VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aGLICKMAN, JONATHAN, NEIL, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by GLICKMAN,JONATHAN NEIL,M.D.,PH.D.\u000a1) SPECIMEN LABELED "PERIAREOLAR RIGHT BREAST TISSUE":\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia.\u000aFocal atypical ductal hyperplasia, sclerosing adenosis, cysts, apocrine\u000ametaplasia and intraductal papilloma.\u000aCalcifications in benign epithelium.\u000aCore biopsy site is identified.\u000a2) SPECIMEN LABELED "RIGHT PARASTERNAL BREAST TISSUE":\u000aSeverely atypical ductal hyperplasia, focal, involving intraductal\u000apapilloma.\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia, multiple foci.\u000aCalcifications are present in benign epithelium.\u000aBiopsy site is identified.\u000aThis case was reviewed by Drs. S. Lester and A. Richardson, Breast\u000aPathology, who concur.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 48 year old surgically postmenopausal female, currently on ERT,\u000awhole REMOVED_DATE  right breast U/S guided core biopsy of a 3 o'clock axis\u000amass has revealed highly atypical ductal proliferation, and\u000astereotactic core biopsy of RLIQ, 1 cm mass revealed complex sclerosing\u000alesion with ADH.\u000aOperation: Right breast wire localization excision x 2\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast atypical hyperplasia associated with 2 masses\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1) Periareolar right breast tissue, cyst ruptured during\u000adissection (short stitch/superior; long stitch/lateral; whip)\u000a#2) Right parasternal breast tissue\u000aRADIOLOGY: #1) Clip in specimen. J. Leung.\u000a#2) Clip in specimen. J. Leung.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by BUNDOCK,ELIZABETH A.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received in two parts, each labeled with the patient's name and\u000aunit number.\u000aPart one, labeled "#1. periareolar right breast tissue", consists of a portion\u000aof fibroadipose tissue (5.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with one short and one long suture\u000apresent, placed by the surgeon to designate superior and lateral respectively.\u000aA localization wire is in place. The specimen is received with an accompanying\u000aspecimen radiograph which is reported as clip in specimen. The specimen is\u000areceived already inked in pathology per pathology protocol for the evaluation\u000aof margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior =\u000agreen; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. The specimen is serially sectioned\u000aat 3 mm intervals from medial to lateral, revealing approximately 85% normally\u000alobulated adipose tissue and 15% scattered areas of white fibrous tissue which\u000acontain cysts and is slightly more firm in lateral inferior aspect of the\u000aspecimen. An additional specimen radiograph is taken in pathology to localize\u000athe clip, which is identified in the area of a small amount of white fibrous\u000atissue with focal old blood. All fibrous areas of the specimen and\u000arepresentatives of all margins are submitted with the area of the clip present\u000ain block #4, as indicated on the specimen radiograph.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  breast tissue, 14 frags, RSS\u000aPart two, labeled "#2. right parasternal breast tissue", consists of a single\u000aportion of fibroadipose tissue (8 x 5 x REMOVED_DATE cm) which is unoriented and has one\u000alocalization wire in place. An accompanying radiograph is received and is\u000areported as clip in specimen. The specimen is inked entirely in black and\u000asectioned at 3 mm intervals to reveal 90% normally lobulated adipose tissue\u000awith scattered small amounts of fibrous tissue and three rubbery foci of\u000ayellow/white tissue, two of which appear to contain areas of fat necrosis. A\u000aspecimen radiograph is taken in pathology to localize the clip, which is found\u000ain one of these firm areas including fat necrosis and hemorrhage. The more\u000adiscrete area of fibrous tissue, which does not have fat necrosis, measures REMOVED_DATE \u000ax REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. This area is submitted in cassettes ten and eleven. The area\u000aof the clip is submitted in cassette number twelve, and additional\u000arepresentative sections (including all fibrous tissue) submitted as indicated\u000aon the specimen radiograph.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  breast tissue, 8 frags, RSS\u000aeab\u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST BIOPSY W/O MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
