te membrane immunoreactivity\u000ain >10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Right breast mass\u000aOperation: 11G Ultrasound\u000aOperative findings: Solid mass\u000aBreast Imaging Findings: Spiculated\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Solid mass\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1) Right breast tissue in an orange cassette\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by LOMO,LESLEY C.,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit\u000anumber, and "Right breast", in an unlabeled orange cassette, and consists of\u000amultiple, soft, fragmented, yellow to white tissue cores (1.6 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in\u000aaggregate).\u000aMicro 1: Multi frags, ESS.\u000alm\u000aReports to: SMITH, DARRELL, NOLAN M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY(IES)\u000a[report_end]
