JCC CLASSIFICATION (6th edition) - REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDb pREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID MX\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER/PR/HER-2) - performed previously\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 57 year old female whose REMOVED_DATE  mammogram demonstrates an 8 mm\u000adensity in the right breast. REMOVED_DATE  core biopsy revealed invasive ductal and\u000alobular carcinoma.\u000aOperation: Right breast wire localized lumpectomy, sentinel node biopsy with\u000apossible level I and II dissection\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast cancer\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000a#1) Right sentinel lymph node, hot and blue\u000a#2) Right breast tissue (short stitch superior, long stitch lateral, whip\u000astitch chest wall margin)\u000aRADIOLOGY: Clip is seen in specimen. J.Meyer,MD\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "#1. RIGHT SENTINEL LYMPH NODE HOT AND BLUE", (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aTwo (2) lymph nodes; no carcinoma present.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by CHEN,JEY-HSIN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart one, labeled "#1. right sentinel lymph node hot and blue", consists of one\u000afragment of yellow lobulated soft tissue (2.4 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) which contains a\u000ablue tinted lymph node (0.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) which is bisected and entirely\u000asubmitted as REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and one tan/blue lymph node (0.4 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) which is\u000abisected and entirely submitted as REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, both of which are entirely submitted.\u000aMicro 1: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID remnant, 2 frags, ESS\u000aMicro 2: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID remnant, 2 frags, ESS\u000aPart two, labeled "#2. right breast tissue, short stitch superior, long stitch\u000alateral, whip stitch chest wall margin", consists of a tan/yellow breast\u000alumpectomy specimen (6.3 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) oriented by a short stitch marking the\u000asuperior surface and a long stitch marking the lateral surface. No whip stitch\u000ais grossly identified. The specimen is received inked by the surgeon per\u000apathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior\u000a= blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange.\u000aThe specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral revealing a tan/white\u000astellate gritty mass (1.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) located REMOVED_DATE cm from the closest\u000ainferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the closest deep\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior margin, and\u000a2.8 cm from the lateral margin. Abutting the mass laterally is a clotted\u000ablood-filled cavity (1.4 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) which contains a white plastic bead\u000a(0.3 cm) located REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the deep margin,\u000a1.2 cm from the anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000athe lateral margin, and opens to the medial margin. A representative section\u000aof the tumor and uninvolved breast parenchyma are submitted to the tissue\u000abank. The specimen is entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  serial sections from medial to lateral with biopsy cavity\u000aadjacent to tumor present block #12, 43 frags, ESS\u000ajhc\u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: SENTINEL LYMPH NODE\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
