VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aRICHARDSON, ANDREA, L., M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by RICHARDSON,ANDREA L.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZATION FOR CALCIFICATIONS AND A MASS:\u000aINVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aSYNOPSIS:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA\u000aSize - REMOVED_DATE cm, associated with stromal\u000acalcifications\u000aMultifocal - no\u000aHistologic Type - ductal\u000aHistologic Grade (SBR) - II (moderate)\u000aNuclear Grade - intermediate\u000aEIC - negative\u000aLymphovascular invasion - absent\u000aDermal lymphatic invasion - N/A\u000aSkin invasion - N/A\u000aSkeletal muscle invasion - N/A\u000aFinal Margins (invasive) -\u000aNegative (>0.3 cm) - anterior, superior, lateral, medial\u000aClose (0.1-0.3 cm) - posteroinferior (focal; block #3)\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aTypes - cribriform\u000aNuclear grade - intermediate\u000aCalcifications in DCIS - present\u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - absent\u000aMicroinvasion (<0.1cm) - absent\u000aExtent of DCIS\u000aNumber of blocks:total - 3:6 blocks\u000aDCIS is present as a minor component of the invasive carcinoma\u000aFinal Margins (DCIS)\u000aNegative (>0.3 cm) - all\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - absent\u000aOTHER FINDINGS\u000aExtensive atypical ductal hyperplasia in sclerosing adenosis, associated\u000awith extensive calcifications\u000aCore biopsy site\u000aAJCC CLASSIFICATION (6th edition) - REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDb pNx MX\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER/PR/HER-2) - see addendum\u000aOther special studies were performed with the following results:\u000ap63 NEGATIVE around malignant cells, confirming invasive\u000acarcinoma.\u000aE-cadherin POSITIVE MEMBRANE STAINING in invasive and in situ\u000acarcinoma, and in atypical hyperplasia confirming ductal\u000afeatures.\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: by RICHARDSON,ANDREA L.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for invasive carcinoma (block 3):\u000aEstrogen receptor - POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor - POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) - NEGATIVE (1+)\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000acarcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but\u000aonly a portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity\u000ain >10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: History of atypical ductal hyperplasia. Microcalcification.\u000aSee prior pathology.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast mass.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000a1. Right breast mass with stitch short/anterior, long/superior\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by REIMANN,JULIE DYLAN REGAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number\u000aand "right breast mass with stitch short anterior long superior", is a fragment\u000aof yellow/pink/tan soft tissue (4.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), accompanied by a second\u000afragment of yellow/pink/tan soft tissue (2.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), with a wire\u000aprotruding from it. Accompanying the specimen is a pink form\u000astating that the clip is in the specimen. The specimen is inked per the\u000apathology ink protocol for the evaluation of margins; blue=anterior, black=\u000aposterior, red= superior, green= inferior, orange=medial, and yellow=lateral.\u000aThe small fragment containing the wire is inked\u000aentirely in black. Serial sectioning of the larger fragment of soft tissue\u000areveals predominately firm white fibrous tissue. The smaller fragment\u000acontains predominantly adipose tissue. The entire specimen is submitted.\u000aMicro sections:\u000aMicro 1: section containing posterior, medial, lateral and inferior margins, 1\u000afrag, RSS.\u000aMicro 2: sections containing superior, lateral, posterior, and inferior\u000amargin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 3: section containing superior, posterior, medial\u000alateral, and anterior, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 4: section containing anterior, posterior, lateral, and\u000amedial margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 5: section containing superior, medial, anterior margin,\u000a1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 6: small fragment of predominately adipose tissue containing wire, 2\u000afrags, ESS.\u000aReports to: NEWMANN, SARA, JEANETTE, MD\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
