VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID SENTINEL LYMPH NODE\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aKRANE, JEFFREY, FRED, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by KRANE,JEFFREY FRED,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A PRIOR BIOPSY SITE AND\u000aCALCIFICATIONS:\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, cribriform type (low nuclear grade) is present\u000aas a REMOVED_DATE cm focus in one of 45 blocks (block 19). The DCIS is associated\u000awith calcifications, but no necrosis is seen. The DCIS is not immediately\u000aadjacent to the prior biopsy site and is > REMOVED_DATE cm from the margins.\u000aEXTENSIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU is present (45 of 45 blocks) and\u000ainvolves numerous areas of sclerosing adenosis. No invasion is seen.\u000aAn immunoperoxidase study for p63 is performed on the most suspicious area\u000a(block 14) and demonstrates myoepithelial cells in the areas involved by\u000aLCIS confirming that no invasion is present.\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia is present.\u000aNote: The DCIS does not appear to be close to the biopsy site and may be\u000aa second area of DCIS in this woman with very extensive atypical\u000ahyperplasia.\u000aThe majority of the calcifications appear to be associated with sclerosing\u000aadenosis and not with DCIS, ADH, or LCIS.\u000aSENTINEL NODE #1 (1369) (including REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aFour lymph nodes with no tumor seen (3 H&E levels examined).\u000aSENTINEL NODE #2 (1580) (including REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aTwo lymph nodes with no tumor seen (3 H&E levels examined).\u000aNON-SENTINEL NODE:\u000aTwo lymph nodes with no tumor seen.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: H/o R breast cancer, s/p excision (+) margins, middle wire marks\u000asite of known cancer. Two deep anterior wires mark two additional sites of\u000amicrocalcifications, anterior and deep to known cancer.\u000aOperation: R partial mastectomy. R sentinel node biopsy.\u000aOperative findings: Frozen section 5 negative nodes.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: R breast invasive carcinoma.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Sentinel node #1 1369.\u000a2. Sentinel node #2 1580.\u000a3. Non sentinel node REMOVED_DATE \u000a4. R breast tissue with 3 wires.\u000aRADIOLOGY REPORT: Many ca++ in specimen. Dr. E. Frost\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "#1 SENTINEL NODE #1 (1369)" (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aFour lymph nodes with no tumor seen.\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "SENTINEL NODE #2 (1580)" (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aNo tumor seen in one frozen section of one lymph node (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID). REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID does\u000anot reveal nodal tissue.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by HONG,XUEFEI,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received in four parts, each labeled with the patient's name\u000aand unit number.\u000aPart one, "#1 sentinel node #1", consists of four lymph nodes (1.1. REMOVED_DATE  REMOVED_DATE \u000aand REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest dimension). The lymph nodes are entirely submitted in\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID through REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aMicro 1: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID remnant, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro 2: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID remnant, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro 3: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID remnant, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro 4: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID remnant, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aPart two, "#2 sentinel node #2", consists of two fragments of tan soft tissue\u000a(1 cm and REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest dimension). The larger lymph node is bisected and\u000aentirely submitted as REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. The smaller one is entirely submitted as REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aMicro 5: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID remnant, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 6: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID remnant, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aPart three, "#3 non sentinel node", consists of one fragment of tan/yellow\u000aadipose soft tisuse (3 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). Two lymph node candidates are\u000aidentified. The specimen is entirely submitted.\u000aMicro 7: non sentinel node, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aPart four, "#4 right breast tissue with three wires", consists of wire\u000alocalized breast excision (10 cm lateral to medial, REMOVED_DATE cm superior to\u000ainferior, 5 cm anterior to posterior). The specimen is inked by the surgeon\u000aper pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior = black;\u000aanterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial =\u000aorange. An accompanying mammogram shows three wires, an ill-defined mass and\u000amultiple areas of calcifications that have been circled by the radiologist.\u000aMedial to lateral sectioning reveals a biopsy site (2 x REMOVED_DATE x 1 cm) which\u000ais 1 cm from inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm from superior, REMOVED_DATE cm from posterior, REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000aanterior, 2 cm from medial and REMOVED_DATE cm from lateral margins. The biopsy site is\u000aentirely submitted. Approximately 90% of the specimen and the majority of the\u000atissue with calcifications is submitted.\u000aMicro 8&9: biopsy site, superior, medial margins, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 10&11: biopsy site with anterior, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  biopsy site with posterior margin, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  biopsy site with superior and anterior margin, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  microcalcifications, multi frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 23&24: lateral margins, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  additional fibrous tissue, mult, frags, RSS.\u000axh\u000aReports to: LESNIKOSKI, BETH-ANN M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: SENTINEL LYMPH NODE\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SENTINEL LYMPH NODE\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: LYMPH NODE BIOPSY\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
