VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: MEHRA GOLSHAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Qinghong Yang, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Xiaohua Qian, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISIONAL BIOPSY FOR A MASS AND A CLIP:\u000aFibroadenoma (1.2 CM).\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 27 y/o female with left breast mass s/p image guided core biopsy\u000arevealing fibroadenoma.\u000aOperation: 1. Left breast wire localized excisional biopsy.\u000aOperative Findings: Not provided.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast fibroadenoma.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Left breast wire localized excisional biopsy - short suture superior;\u000along suture lateral.\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000aWire, clip and mass in specimen. RB phone MG in OR.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "#1. Left breast wire-localized excision biopsy - short suture superior,\u000along suture lateral", is an ovoid fragment of yellow/tan to pink/tan\u000afibroadipose tissue (4.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which is oriented per surgeon with\u000atwo sutures as previously indicated. The specimen is inked per pathology\u000aprotocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue;\u000asuperior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. There is one\u000aneedle-localization wire in place which enters the posterolateral aspect of the\u000aspecimen and exits the anteromedial aspect of the specimen. The specimen was\u000apreviously radiographed (per radiologist "wire, clip, and mass in specimen").\u000aThe specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral. In the medial\u000aaspect of the specimen, there is a well-delineated circumscribed tan/pink\u000ahomogeneous mass (1.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which is less than REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000asuperior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin, and REMOVED_DATE \u000acm from the lateral margin. A small metal clip is identified within the mass,\u000aand the aforementioned needle-localization wire traverses the parenchyma\u000aadjacent to the mass.\u000aThe remainder of the cut surface is composed of approximately 65% dense\u000awhite/tan fibrous stroma and 35% yellow/tan lobulated adipose tissue with no\u000aadditional discrete lesions identified.\u000aApproximately 75% of the specimen to include the mass in entirety is submitted\u000aas follows:\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin with mass, perpendicularly sectioned, 5 frags total,\u000aESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Remainder of mass with anterior, posterior, superior, and inferior\u000amargins, 1 frag in each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, perpendicularly sectioned, multi frags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-07-REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aLMB/ajb\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Xiaohua Qian M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a5/27/2007\u000a[report_end]
