 area abuts the posterior margin, and is located approximately REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom the anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000asuperior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin, and >1 cm from the lateral\u000amargin. The specimen is entirely submitted from medial to lateral.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: medial margin, perpendicular, 4 frags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: serial sections from medial to lateral (including the majority of\u000alesion in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), 7 frags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: lateral margin, perpendicular, 4 frags, ESS\u000aPSC/jp\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Priscilla S Chang M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Mark S Redston M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
