VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ROGER L CHRISTIAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Shakti Ramkissoon, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Jason L Hornick, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "LEFT BREAST TISSUE, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISIONAL BIOPSY":\u000aBreast parenchyma with focally dilated ducts, otherwise no significant\u000apathologic change.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the\u000aspecimen, including margins.\u000aB. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "LEFT BREAST, RE-EXCISION":\u000aBreast parenchyma with apocrine cysts and metaplasia and biopsy site\u000achanges.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the\u000aspecimen, including margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Non palp mass, left breast. Attempt core biopsy - discordant.\u000aOperation: Wire directed excision of mass left.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Non-palp mass, left breast.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Left breast tissue long lateral short superior.\u000aB/2. Left breast global re-excision.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Density and clip in specimen. Radiographing with density to edge of\u000aspecimen. Relayed to Dr. Christian via. RN K P Burns.\u000aRADIOGRAPH AND ULTRASOUND: No density on clip in radiograph. Relayed to Dr.\u000aChristian.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname, unit number.\u000aPart A, "#1. Left breast tissue, long lateral, short superior", consists of a\u000ayellow/tan breast excision (3.4 M-L x REMOVED_DATE S-I x REMOVED_DATE A-P cm) oriented per\u000asurgeon with two sutures: Short equals superior, long equals lateral. The\u000aspecimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins:\u000aposterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow;\u000amedial/orange. There is a needle-localization wire which enters the\u000aanteroinferior aspect of the specimen and exits the anteromedial aspect of the\u000aspecimen. The specimen was previously radiographed, confirming that neither a\u000adensity or a clip was radiographically identified. The specimen is serially\u000asectioned from medial to lateral, perpendicular to the wire, exhibiting\u000aapproximately 15% unremarkable white/tan fibrous stroma and 85% yellow/tan\u000alobulated adipose tissue. No discrete masses or lesions are identified. Also\u000areceived in the same container is a separate fragment of yellow/tan\u000afibroadipose tissue (2.4 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) which is not oriented.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin, perpendicularly sectioned, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Breast excision specimen sequentially submitted from medial to\u000alateral, multi frags total, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, perpendicularly sectioned, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Separately received unoriented tissue fragments serially sectioned,\u000amulti frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, "#2. L breast re-excision" received oriented on a radiographic grid\u000adevice is a yellow/tan breast excision specimen (5.3 M-L x REMOVED_DATE A-P x REMOVED_DATE S-I\u000acm) oriented per surgeon with two sutures: Short equals superior, long equals\u000alateral. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of\u000amargins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green;\u000alateral/yellow; medial/orange. The needle-localization wire is not present.\u000aIn the central/anteroinferior aspect of the specimen, there is an ill-defined\u000ahemorrhagic/cystic/focally friable area (0.9 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000aanterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the deep/posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin,\u000aand REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin. Within this area, a small metal clip is\u000aidentified, correlating with the accompanying radiograph of the specimen. The\u000aremainder of the cut surface is composed of greater than 95% yellow/tan adipose\u000atissue and less than 5% unremarkable pink/tan fibrous tissue. Please note that\u000athe central specimen partially fragmented during sectioning.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin, perpendicularly sectioned, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID though REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Central specimen from medial to lateral (ill-defined\u000alesion in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, with clip in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), multi frags total, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, perpendicularly sectioned, multi frags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-08-REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aLM/ag\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jason L Hornick M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a6/13/2008\u000a[report_end]
