VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aWELCH, WILLIAM, ROBERT, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by WELCH,WILLIAM ROBERT,M.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST, EXCISION OF A MASS:\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU, involving adenosis.\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia involving adenosis.\u000aCalcifications, epithelial hyperplasia, cysts, adenosis, and core biopsy\u000asite changes.\u000aThe case has been reviewed by Dr. S. Schnitt, Breast Pathology, who\u000aconcurs.\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "SUPERIOR LATERAL MARGIN, LEFT BREAST":\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU, involving adenosis.\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia involving adenosis; epithelial hyperplasia,\u000aand focal fat necrosis.\u000aThe case has been reviewed by Dr. S. Schnitt, Breast Pathology, who\u000aconcurs.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 56-year-old postmenopausal female, not on hormones. Status post\u000a4/18/03 left breast core biopsy for an are of ill-defined asymmetry\u000aon mammogram with pathology demonstrating columnar hyperplasia with\u000aatypia.\u000aPASH with surgical excision recommended.\u000aOperation: Left breast wire localization excision.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Biopsy with atypia.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Left breast tissue, short stitch superior, long stitch\u000alateral, whip stitch on deep margin.\u000a2. Superior lateral shave margin left breast.\u000aClip in specimen, OR called.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by DAVID,FRANK SAMUEL,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart one, labeled "#1, left breast tissue, short stitch/superior, long\u000astitch/lateral, whip stitch deep margin", consists of a single fragment of\u000ayellow-tan fibroadipose tissue, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The specimen is marked with\u000aa short stitch, long stitch and a whip stitch designating the superior,\u000alateral and deep margins, respectively. The specimen is inked per pathology\u000aprotocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue;\u000asuperior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. The\u000ainterior of this specimen is uniformly fibrofatty without discreet masses or\u000asuspicious lesions. Core biopsy site is grossly identified. A clip is not\u000agrossly identified. A mammogram accompanies the specimen demonstrating the\u000apresence of a surgical clip. The specimen is entirely submitted.\u000aMicro 1: anterior, ESS.\u000aMicro 2: posterior, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  remainder of specimen, anterior and posterior, (core biopsy site\u000achanges in 7 through 10), ESS.\u000aPart two, labeled "#2, superior lateral shave margin", consists of multiple\u000aunoriented fragments of yellow-tan fibroadipose tissue, measuring in aggregate\u000a4.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The specimen is uniformly fibrofatty, without discreet\u000amasses or suspicious lesions. A mammogram accompanying the specimen is grossly\u000aunremarkable. The specimen is serially sectioned and entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  multi frags, ESS.\u000afsd\u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN\u000a[report_end]
