PTION: by LEE,BENJAMIN H.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "right breast tissue", and consists of a right modified radical mastectomy\u000aspecimen (250g; REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with an attached axillary tail (8.0 x REMOVED_DATE \u000ax REMOVED_DATE cm). There is a short suture denoting the superior margin, and a long\u000asuture denoting the lateral margin. There is a brown skin ellipse (12.5 x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm) with an unremarkable nipple (1.2 cm). No visible scars are identified.\u000aThe deep fascial margin is inked in black. On cut section, there is a dense,\u000awell circumscribed, tan/gray tumor mass (2.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) that resides REMOVED_DATE \u000acm from the deep margin. The remainder of the breast parenchyma is comprised\u000aprimarily of white, firm, dense tissue admixed with unremarkable fatty adipose\u000atissue. Representative sections are submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  sections of tumor, 1 frag/cass, RSS\u000aMicro 5: deep margin to tumor, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 6: section of nipple, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 7: upper inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 8: lower inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 9: upper outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 10: lower outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 11: 3 lymph nodes, 3 frag, ESS\u000aMicro 12: 3 lymph nodes, 3 frag, ESS\u000aMicro 13: 3 lymph nodes, 3 frag, ESS\u000aMicro 14: 2 lymph nodes, 2 frag, ESS\u000aMicro 15: 2 lymph nodes, 2 frag, ESS\u000abhl\u000aReports to: OSTEEN, ROBERT, T. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY W/REGIONAL LYMPH NODES\u000a[report_end]
