VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aWEINSTEIN, MICHAEL, H., M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by WEINSTEIN,MICHAEL H.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST, NEEDLE-LOCALIZED BIOPSY FOR A CLIP (21g):\u000aFocal atypical ductal hyperplasia.\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia, apocrine metaplasia, and cysts.\u000aPrior core biopsy site changes.\u000aCalcifications are noted in association with benign epithelium.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the\u000aspecimen, including margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: None given.\u000aOperation: Left needle localized breast biopsy\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal mammo/atypical ductal hyperplasia\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1) Left needle localized breast biopsy\u000aRADIOLOGY: Calcium and clip are in specimen. (JM).\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by PADERA,ROBERT F.,JR.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in one part, labeled with the patient's name,\u000aunit number and "#1. left needle loc breast biopsy", and consists of a single\u000afragment of yellow/tan fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm and\u000aweighing 21g. The specimen is received with two wires in place. The specimen\u000ais received inked by the surgeon per pathology protocol for the evaluation of\u000amargins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green;\u000alateral = yellow; medial = orange. A single firm white nodule is present\u000ameasuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm that is located adjacent to the medial margin,\u000a1.2 cm from the lateral margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000athe posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000ainferior margin. An area of hemorrhage and focal fibrous tissue is present\u000acentrally within the mass and is adajcent to the area of the clip. The breast\u000atissue as a whole is comprised of approximately 90% adipose tissue and 10%\u000afibrous tissue. The specimen is serially sectioned and entirely submitted\u000afrom superior to inferior.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  left needle localized breast biopsy specimen, 4 frags, ESS\u000a(nodule adjacent to the medial margin is present primarily in\u000a#5 and 6 and the area of the clip is present in #8)\u000arp\u000aReports to: OSTEEN, ROBERT, T. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
