VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aMUELLER, JAMES, D., M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by MUELLER,JAMES,D.,M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "LEFT BREAST MASS" (3 GM):\u000aFocal ductal hyperplasia with apocrine change (see note).\u000aSclerosing adenosis.\u000aThere is no evidence of atypical hyperplasia or malignancy.\u000aNOTE: Due to the clinical suspicion regarding the possibility of tumor, the\u000amargins of this specimen were inked, submitted and histologically\u000aexamined.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 53 year old postmenopausal female on HRT whose REMOVED_DATE \u000amammograms demonstrate a L breast UOQ 8 mm cluster of\u000acalcifications. REMOVED_DATE  core biopsy revealed atypical\u000aductal hyperplasia.\u000aOperation: L breast wire localization biopsy.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: L breast atypical ductal hyperplasia.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: L breast mass. Short superior, long lateral, whipstich\u000ais deep margin.\u000aRadiology: Clip in specimen. C.Denison, MD\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by PADERA,ROBERT F.,JR.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in one part, labeled with the patient's name and\u000amedical record number and the description "#1 left breast mass". The specimen\u000aconsists of a 3-gram breast wire localization specimen. The specimen is\u000areceived with a wire in place. The specimen is received with two orienting\u000asutures. The double short suture indicates superior and the double long suture\u000aindicates lateral. The specimen has been inked by the surgeon per pathology\u000aprotocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue;\u000asuperior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. The\u000aspecimen is serially sectioned to reveal a clip in the superior aspect of the\u000aspecimen. Adjacent to this clip there is firm, fibrous tissue. The remainder\u000aof the breast is comprised largely of adipose tissue. The specimen is serially\u000asectioned. The clip is removed. The breast is submitted in its entirety for\u000ahistologic evaluation from superior to inferior. The specimen is received with\u000aa specimen radiograph.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  left breast mass, multi frags, ESS.\u000aPlease note that the area of the clip is primarily in micros 1&2.\u000arp\u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
