VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID SENTINEL LYMPH NODE\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aWELCH, WILLIAM, ROBERT, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by WELCH,WILLIAM ROBERT,M.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST, EXCISION, AND SENTINEL NODE BIOPSIES, AND AXILLARY NODE\u000aDISSECTION (specimens REMOVED_DATE of 6 specimens):\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA, ONE (1) FOCUS\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aSYNOPSIS:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA\u000aSize - REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aMultifocal? - no\u000aHistologic Type - mixed ductal and lobular\u000aHistologic Grade (SBR) - II (moderate)\u000aNuclear Grade - high\u000aEIC - negative\u000aLymphovascular invasion - absent\u000aDermal lymphatic invasion - N/A\u000aSkin invasion - N/A\u000aSkeletal muscle invasion - N/A\u000aFinal Margins (invasive) -\u000aNegative (no ink on tumor) - all\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aTypes - solid\u000aNuclear grade - intermediate\u000aCalcifications in DCIS - present\u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - absent\u000aExtent of DCIS\u000aDCIS is present as a minor component of the invasive carcinoma\u000aFinal Margins (DCIS)\u000aNegative (>0.3 cm) - all\u000aLYMPH NODES\u000aSentinel Lymph Nodes - positive (3 H&E levels examined)\u000aNumber of positive nodes - 1\u000aNumber of nodes examined - 4\u000aAxillary Lymph Nodes - positive\u000aNumber of positive nodes - 1\u000aNumber of nodes examined - 9\u000aTOTAL POSITIVE NODES (sentinel + axillary)- 2:13\u000aSize of largest metastatic focus - REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aExtranodal extension - present\u000aOTHER FINDINGS\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER/PR/HER-2) - performed previously\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "MEDIAL SHAVE MARGIN" (specimen #5 of 6 specimens):\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, comedo type, present in two of twelve (2:12)\u000ablocks.\u000aThe DCIS lies >0.3 cm from the nearest whipstitch margin.\u000aCalcifications are noted in association with benign epithelium.\u000aThere is no evidence of invasive carcinoma in this specimen.\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "RETROAREOLAR SHAVE MARGIN":\u000aFocal mild ductal hyperplasia.\u000aApocrine metaplasia.\u000aCalcifications are noted in association with benign breast tissue.\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for invasive carcinoma (block 15):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) NEGATIVE (0)\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000ainvasive carcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but\u000aonly a portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity\u000ain >10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 46 year old mulliparous premenopausal female, not on hormones, whose\u000a5/2/02 mammograms supplemented by U/S demonstrates a left breast UIQ spiculated\u000amass. REMOVED_DATE  core biopsy revealed infiltrating carcinoma with ductal and\u000alobular features.\u000aOperation: Left breast excisional biopsy and sentinel node biopsy\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast cancer\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1) Sentinel node - hot and blue (left axilla)\u000a#2) Sentinel node - warm and blue\u000a#3) Left axillary contents\u000a#4) Left breast tissue (short/superior; long/lateral; whip stitch is chest\u000awall)\u000a#5) Medial shave margin (whip stitch = new margin)\u000a#6) Retroareolar shave margin (whip new margin)\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "#1. SENTINEL LYMPH NODE, BOT AND BLUE", (FSA):\u000aMetastatic carcinoma.\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "#2. SENTINEL LYMPH NODE, WARM AND BLUE", (FSB):\u000aOne lymph node with no tumor seen.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by ABBOTT,DEREK W,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in six parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart one, labeled "#1. sentinel node - hot and blue", and consists of a single\u000afragment of yellow/tan/pink soft tissue (5.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with three\u000acandidate lymph nodes (largest measuring REMOVED_DATE cm in diameter). The largest is\u000abisected and grossly appears to be positive. A frozen section was done on this\u000agrossly positive lymph node. The remainder of the lymph nodes are submitted\u000afor histologic analysis.\u000aMicro 1: FSA remnant, 1 frag, ESS\u000aMicro 2: second bisected half of frozen lymph node, 1 frag, ESS\u000aMicro 3: 2 candidate lymph nodes, 2 frags, ESS\u000aMicro 4: remainder of fatty tissue from specimen, 1 frag, ESS\u000aPart two, labeled '#2. lymph node warm and blue", consists of a single fragment\u000aof yellow/pink/tan fatty soft tissue with a single lymph node (0.9 cm in\u000adiameter; total specimen = REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The entire lymph node is\u000asubmitted for frozen section evaluation. The remainder of the tissue is\u000asubmitted for histologic analysis.\u000aMicro 5: FSB remnant, 1 frag, ESS\u000aMicro 6: remainder from fat from specimen, 4 frags, ESS\u000aPart three, labeled "#3. left axillary contents", consists of two fragments of\u000afatty yellow/tan soft tissue (7.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). Lymph nodes are dissected\u000afrom the specimen and submitted for histologic analysis.\u000aMicro 7: single bisected lymph node, 2 frags, RSS\u000aMicro 8: single bisected lymph node, 2 frags, RSS\u000aMicro 9: 5 potential lymph nodes, 5 frags, ESS\u000aMicro 10: single bisected lymph nodes, 2 frags, ESS\u000aMicro 11: single bisected lymph nodes, 2 frags, ESS\u000aPart four, labeled "#4. left breast tissue", consists of a single fragment of\u000afatty breast tissue (8.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The specimen has been inked prior to\u000aits arrival in surgical pathology per pathology protocol for the evaluation of\u000amargins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green;\u000alateral = yellow; medial = orange. There is a short stitch marking the\u000asuperior margin and a long stitch marking the lateral margin, and a whip stitch\u000amarking the new chest wall margin. The specimen is serially sectioned to\u000areveal a white whorled mass (1.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). This mass lies REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000athe medial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superficial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the deep\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin, approximately 2 cm from the inferior\u000amargin and approximately 1 cm from the superior margin. No other gross lesions\u000aare appreciated. However, there are areas of suspected DCIS near the mass.\u000aRepresentative sections of the mass with all margins are submitted for\u000ahistologic evaluation.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  mass with nearest margin, 1 frag each, RSS\u000aMicro 18: nearest lateral margin, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 19: nearest inferior margin, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 20: nearest superior margin, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 21: additional superficial margin, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  areas near the mass with suspected DCIS, 1 frag each, RSS\u000aMicro 24: area of suspeted DCIS away from mass near the medial and\u000ainferior margin, 1 frag, RSS\u000aPart five, labeled "#5. medial shave margin, whip new margin left breast",\u000aconsists of a single fragment of fatty breast tissue (5.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm).\u000aThere is a whip stitch marking the new margin. The area surrounding the whip\u000astitch is inked in blue, the remainder of the breast is inked in black. The\u000aspecimen is serially sectioned revealing no gross lesion. The specimen is\u000aentirely submitted for histologic analysis.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  medial shave margin, REMOVED_DATE frags each, ESS\u000aPart six, labeled "#6. retroareolar shave margin, whip = new margin", consists\u000aof a fragment of fibrous breast tissue (6.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). There is a stitch\u000amarking the new margin. The area of the stitch is inked in blue. The\u000aremainder of the breast is inked in black. The specimen is serially sectioned\u000ato reveal dense fibrous breast tissue with no gross abnormalities. The entire\u000aarea of the whip stitch is submitted for histologic evaluation.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  retroareolar shave margin, REMOVED_DATE frags each, RSS\u000adwa\u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: SENTINEL LYMPH NODE\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SENTINEL LYMPH NODE\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: LYMPH NODE BIOPSY\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST BIOPSY W/O MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN\u000a[report_end]
