VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: Esther Rhei M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-05-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Patricia A. R. Brunker, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Lucian Chirieac, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, EXCISION FOR A MASS:\u000aPHYLLODES TUMOR, low grade (2.7 cm). See NOTE.\u000aRare scattered mitoses are present.\u000aNo necrosis is present.\u000aTumor is extensively present at the medial margin (blocks REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), anterior\u000amargin (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), and is extensively very close (<0.1 cm) from the inferior\u000a(blocks REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) and anterior margin (blocks REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aThe entire specimen was submitted for histologic evaluation.\u000aNOTE: This case was reviewed by Drs. D. Dillon and S. Lester, breast pathology\u000aservice, who concur.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 28 year old female palpable right breast mass. History of fibroadenoma\u000ain same breast 1997 and 2003. Ultrasound showed a REMOVED_DATE cm solid mass, core\u000abiopsy fibroepithelial lesion. ? cellular fibroadenoma vs. phyllodes tumor.\u000aExcision recommended for definitive diagnosis.\u000aOperation: Right breast excisional biopsy. Previous surgery - unavailable.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast mass.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/#1. right breast mass short stitch superior, long stitch lateral, whip stitch\u000achest wall.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in one part, labeled with the patient?s name,\u000aunit number, and "#1. right breast mass short stitch superior, long stitch\u000alateral, whip stitch chest wall", and consists of a fibrofatty portion of\u000abreast tissue (3.9 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which is oriented by two sutures placed by\u000athe surgeon, with a short suture designating "superior" and the long "lateral".\u000aThere is also a whip stitch placed orthogonal to the sutures, designating the\u000achest wall margin. The specimen is received inked by the surgeon, per\u000apathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black;\u000aanterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange.\u000aPlease note that the internal relationships of the inking are largely correct;\u000ahowever, the anterior (blue) margin is displaced far to the lateral side, as is\u000athe inferior (green) ink. The specimen is sectioned from medial to lateral,\u000arevealing a well-circumscribed, multi-loculated, nodular, white/yellow mass\u000a(2.7 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which grossly abuts the inferior and anterior margins,\u000aand is located REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior, REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000athe medial and REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margins. The specimen is entirely,\u000aserially submitted for histologic evaluation, after being photographed.\u000aMICRO REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Right breast mass, serially submitted from medial to lateral, mass\u000ain REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 9 frags, ESS.\u000aPab/ag\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Lucian Chirieac M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
