VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: JULIE L JONES M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-06-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Stacey A. Simons, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Jonathan N Glickman, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "LEFT BREAST, SCAR":\u000aSkin with scar and acute and chronic inflammation.\u000aB. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "LEFT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION":\u000aNodular sclerosing lesion with biopsy site changes (0.7 cm\u000ain greatest dimension); see NOTE.\u000aNOTE:\u000aThis lesion corresponds with the lesion seen on the core biopsy. There are\u000aarchitectural abnormalities, though there is positive staining for p63\u000a(myoepithelium) diffusely, and the overall appearance is of a benign entity.\u000aSelect slides were reviewed by Dr. A. Richardson and Dr. S. Lester, both of the\u000aBreast Pathology Service, who concur.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: History of stage 1 left breast cancer in 1998, now with two small\u000afoci of enhancement on MRI, two small solid nodules on correlative US, and FA\u000aat both sites on core; 1 o'clock lesion with atypia as well.\u000aOperation: Left breast wire-localized excisional biopsy of mass at 1 o'clock.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast atypia on core biopsy of mass at 1 o'clock.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Left breast scar.\u000aB/2. Left breast wire-localized excision - mammo.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Clip in center of tissue specimen, hook wire included,\u000aphoned to OR.\u000aElman/Birdwell\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two parts, each is labeled with the\u000apatient's name and unit number.\u000aPart A, "Left breast scar", consists of a fragment of tan/white skin and\u000asubcutis with focal hemorrhage. The entire specimen is submitted for\u000ahistologic analysis.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 frag, ESS.\u000aPart B, "Left breast wire-localized excision - mammo", consists of REMOVED_DATE (medial\u000ato lateral) x REMOVED_DATE (inferior to superior) x REMOVED_DATE (anterior to posterior) cm\u000abreast biopsy. Please note that localization wire fell out of the specimen in\u000athe specimen jar prior to processing. An accompanying specimen radiograph\u000ademonstrates an ill-defined mass and the localization wire. The specimen is\u000ainked for the evaluation of margins: Posterior/black, anterior/blue,\u000asuperior/red, inferior/green, lateral/yellow, and medial/orange. There is a\u000acavity (1.2 cm in greatest dimension, consistent with prior biopsy site), which\u000ahas a firm/fibrotic lining with scattered hemorrhage and fat necrosis, located\u000a0.1 cm from the closest posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the closest anterior\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the closest medial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the closest lateral\u000amargin and abutting the inferior margin. No other masses or lesions are\u000aidentified. The remainder of the breast parenchyma consists of 90% fibrous\u000atissue. The entire specimen is serially sectioned along the superior and\u000ainferior axes and entirely submitted for histologic analysis.\u000aMicor REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Specimen serially sectioned from superior to inferior, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID to\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID including the biopsy cavity, multi frags, ESS.\u000aELC/mmm\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jonathan N Glickman M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a11/1/2006\u000a[report_end]
