VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aNUCCI, MARISA, ROSE, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by NUCCI,MARISA ROSE,M.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR CALCIFICATIONS AND A CLIP:\u000aSUMMARY DIAGNOSIS:\u000aINVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aSYNOPSIS:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA\u000aSize - REMOVED_DATE cm (as measured on slide #13)\u000aMultifocal - no\u000aHistologic Type - ductal\u000aHistologic Grade (SBR) - I (well)\u000aNuclear Grade - low\u000aEIC - positive\u000aLymphovascular invasion - absent\u000aDermal lymphatic invasion - N/A\u000aSkin invasion - N/A\u000aSkeletal muscle invasion - N/A\u000aFinal Margins (invasive) -\u000aNegative (>0.3 cm) - anterior, superior, posterior, medial,\u000alateral\u000aClose (0.1-0.3 cm) - inferior (focal, REMOVED_DATE cm, block #13)\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aTypes - solid, cribriform, micropapillary,\u000aclinging\u000aNuclear grade - low to intermediate\u000aCalcifications in DCIS - present\u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - present\u000aExtent of DCIS\u000aNumber of blocks:total - 13:40\u000aFinal Margins (DCIS)\u000aNegative (>0.3 cm) - posterior, medial, lateral, superior,\u000aanterior\u000aVery close (<0.1 cm) - inferior, multifocal\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - present\u000aOTHER FINDINGS\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia\u000aCore biopsy site\u000aColumnar alteration of lobules with atypia\u000aReactive multinucleated stromal cells\u000aCysts (up to REMOVED_DATE cm)\u000aComplex sclerosing lesion\u000aPapilloma\u000aSclerosing adenosis\u000aCalcifications in benign epithelium\u000aAJCC CLASSIFICATION (6th Edition) - REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDb pNx MX\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER/PR/HER-2) - pending\u000aNOTE: This case was reviewed by Dr. S. Lester, breast pathology, who concurs.\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe correct AJCC T classification is REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDc.\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for invasive carcinoma (block 13):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) NEGATIVE (1+)\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000acarcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but\u000aonly a portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity\u000ain >10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: History of left breast core biopsy at BWH, shows atypical sclerosis\u000awith question of REMOVED_DATE cm focus worrisome for invasive cancer (around clip) and\u000aassociated three areas of calcs on mammogram.\u000aOperation: Left mammographically-directed breast biopsy.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal left mammogram.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1 - left breast tissue, left mid/lower quadrant (6 o'clock)\u000ashort/superior, long/lateral.\u000aRadiograph report: Clip, calcification and wire within specimen. SUB\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by CHEN,JEY-HSIN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aReceived fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "#1 - left\u000abreast tissue, left mid/lower quadrant (6 o'clock), short/superior,\u000along/lateral), is a 200 gram yellow/tan fibrofatty tissue (10 x 8 x 6 cm) with\u000aa wire in place. The specimen is oriented by a short stitch marking the\u000asuperior surface, and a long stitch marking the lateral surface. The specimen\u000ais inked per the pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins:\u000aposterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow;\u000amedial/orange. The specimen is serially sectioned from lateral to medial,\u000arevealing a white/pink lobulated area (7 x 3 x 2 cm) with ill-defined borders\u000aextending to within REMOVED_DATE cm of the inferior surface, REMOVED_DATE cm of the medial\u000asurface, REMOVED_DATE cm of the lateral surface, REMOVED_DATE cm of the anterior surface, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aof the superior surface, and within REMOVED_DATE cm of the posterior surface. Contained\u000awithin the lobulated areas are multiple cysts (up to REMOVED_DATE cm in diameter). No\u000aother lesions are grossly identified. The lobulated area comprises\u000aapproximately 40% of the specimen, and the remainder of the specimen is\u000acomprised of 70% to 80% adipose tissue. The specimen is X-rayed, revealing a\u000aclip and calcifications in the medial slices within the lobulated area.\u000aRepresentative sections, including the entire lobulated area, are submitted.\u000aMicro #1-3: Lobulated area in relation to inferior margin around area of\u000aclip, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro #4+5: Lobulated area around clip in relation to posterior margin, 2\u000afrags, ESS.\u000aMicro #6+7: Remaining lobulated area around clip, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro #8-39: Lobulated area in relation to inferior, posterior, superior,\u000amedial margins, multiple frags, ESS.\u000aMicro #40: Closest anterior and lateral resection margins, 2 frags, RSS.\u000ajhc/\u000aReports to: CARTER, KATHARINE M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
