 cell reaction consistent with previous\u000asurgical site\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia\u000aPapilloma\u000aCalcifications in benign epithelium\u000aAJCC CLASSIFICATION (6th edition) - pREMOVED_ACCESSION_IDmi MX (T stage is unknown, but\u000aprobably REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, based on the REMOVED_DATE cm tumor in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and the residual REMOVED_DATE cm\u000atumor in this specimen.)\u000aNOTE:\u000aThe two foci of metastasis to sentinel nodes (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) are not present on the\u000afrozen section slides that have been reviewed.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Hx of prior left breast biopsy at BWH REMOVED_DATE  - REMOVED_DATE cm invasive\u000acancer ER-positive, PR-positive, Her 2-Neum with close inferior margin + DCIS @\u000ainferior margin. Pt had significant post-op wound infection + has some\u000aresidual calcification in bx site (may be dystrophic). Wires, bracket,\u000acalcifications.\u000aOperation: Left partial mastectomy (re-excision).\u000aLeft breast biopsy site + left sentinel node mapping.\u000aOperative Findings: None given\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast cancer.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000a1. Sentinel node #1.\u000a2. Sentinel node #2.\u000a3. Left breast tissue @ 6 o'clock. Short - superior; long - lateral.\u000aInked per pathology protocol. Some on green ink; yellow anterior margin.\u000aRADIOLOGY REPORT:\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED: Multiple Ca++ clusters, which were bracketed for excision\u000aare contained L/W the wires.\u000a(unsigned)\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED: "1) SENTINEL NODE #1" (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aNo metastases\u000a"2) SENTINEL NODE #2" (FSB):\u000aNo metastases\u000aOR Consultation by: ODZE, ROBERT DANIEL,M.D.\u000aResident:\u000aThe senior physician certifies that he/she personally conducted a gross and/or\u000amicroscopic examination of the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed\u000athe rapid diagnos(es) related thereto.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen was received in three parts, each received fresh, labeled with the\u000apatient's name and medical record number:\u000aPart A, labeled "Left sentinel node #1", consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afragment of fatty tissue, containing a single, REMOVED_DATE cm lymph node which has been\u000apreviously bisected and entirely frozen as REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID remnant, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID remnant, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Non-frozen tissue, multiple frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, labeled "Left sentinel node #2", consist of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm fatty\u000atissue fragment containing a single, REMOVED_DATE cm lymph node, which has been\u000apreviously entirely frozen as FSB.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: FSB remnant, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Non-frozen tissue, multiple frags, ESS.\u000aPart C, labeled "1. Left breast tissue @ 6 o'clock; short-superior,\u000along-lateral", consists of a 57-gm, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm fibrofatty tissue\u000afragment, received with a radiograph and two, localizing wires in place.\u000aThe specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins:\u000aposterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow;\u000amedial/orange.\u000aThe specimen is oriented by sutures designating superior (short suture) and\u000alateral (long suture) margins. The anterior surface demonstrates at REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm tan/white skin ellipse with a REMOVED_DATE cm linear scar along its length. Specimen\u000aradiograph shows localizing wires in place with multiple clusters of\u000acalcifications in the intervening tissue. Sectioning through this area\u000ademonstrates a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm ill-defined, firm, fibrous scarred lesion\u000awith associated multifocal fat necrosis (25% of lesion). This area is\u000acompatible with prior biopsy site and exhibits streaming fibrous bands which\u000aextend to involve the anterior, posterior, lateral, medial margins and approach\u000awithin REMOVED_DATE cm of the closest inferior and REMOVED_DATE cm of the closest superior\u000amargin. Representative tissue is submitted:\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Intervening tissue; adjacent to superior wire (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID are one\u000aentire\u000across-section; REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID are one entire cross section.);\u000amultiple frags total, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Tissue adjacent to inferior wire (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID are one entire cross-\u000asection; REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID are one entire cross-section), multiple frags\u000atotal,\u000aESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Additional representative, intervening tissue and closest\u000amargins,\u000a4 frags, ESS. (REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDlateral, anterior; REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDposterior, medial;\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_IDanterior, superior; C-23 lateral.).\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Representative superior margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Representative inferior margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000adb/MMM\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aMicroscopic/Diagnostic Dictation by Rachel E Factor M.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aPrelim Dx Release by Rachel E Factor M.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aMicroscopic/Diagnostic Dictation by Rachel E Factor M.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Shuji Ogino M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a12/29/2004\u000a[report_end]
