VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ROGER L CHRISTIAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-06-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Wai Chin Foo, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Christopher D. M. Fletcher, M.D. FRCPath\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "RIGHT BREAST TISSUE, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION\u000aFOR CLIP AND MASS":\u000aBenign breast tissue with florid biopsy site changes, including\u000aextensive fat necrosis and hemorrhage.\u000aCalcifications in benign epithelium and focal columnar change noted.\u000aThere is no evidence of a neoplasm.\u000aB. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "RIGHT SUPERIOR SHAVE MARGIN":\u000aBenign breast tissue with scarring and fat necrosis.\u000aThere is no evidence of a neoplasm.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Area of architectural distortion, right breast, previous core biopsy\u000awas inconclusive.\u000aOperation: Wire-directed excision.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: None given.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Right breast tissue (mammo).\u000aB/2. Superior shaved margin, right breast.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Area of shadowing, clip + wire in specimen. E. P. Frost.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aTwo specimen is received fresh, in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart A, labeled "#1. Tissue right breast", consists of a breast excision (8.1\u000acm from medial to lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm from superior to inferior, and REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000aanterior to posterior). The specimen does not contain a localization wire. An\u000aaccompanying specimen radiograph demonstrates an ill-defined hypoechoic area on\u000athe medial side of the specimen and a localization wire. The tip of the\u000alocalization wire is located at the edge of the hypoechoic area. A clip is\u000alocated in the center of the hypoechoic area. The specimen is inked, by the\u000asurgeon, per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black;\u000aanterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange.\u000aThe specimen is sectioned from the medial towards the lateral margin into\u000aseventeen slices. Slices four through nine contain the biopsy site with an\u000aarea of coagulated blood (1.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which is located REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000asuperior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin, and\u000a3.0 from the lateral margin. The breast tissue around the area of coagulated\u000ablood contains white/yellow fat necrosis extending to the superior and anterior\u000amargins. The remaining breast tissue contains ill-defined, white, fibrous\u000aareas with cysts (up to REMOVED_DATE cm). A specimen radiograph is taken, showing the\u000aclip within a radiodense area in slice six.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin (slice #1), perpendicular, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin (slice #17), perpendicular, multi frags each,\u000aESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #2, 1 frag, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #3, 1 frag each, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #4, 1 frag each, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #5, 1 frag each, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #6 with clip, 1 frag each, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #7, 1 frag each, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #8, 1 frag each, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #9, 1 frag each, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #10, 1 frag each, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #11, 1 frag, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #12, 1 frag each, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slices #13-16, 1 frag each, ESS\u000aPart B, labeled "#2. Superior shaved margin, right breast", consists of one\u000afragment of breast tissue (2.3 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which was previously inked red\u000aon one side by the surgeon. The opposite side is inked green. The specimen\u000acontains ill-defined areas of hemorrhage and fat necrosis extending from the\u000ared-inked to the green-inked margin.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: superior shave margin, 2 frags each, ESS.\u000aSTS/mmm\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Christopher D. M. Fletcher M.D. FRCPath, Electronically\u000asigned on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
