VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aWEINSTEIN, MICHAEL, H., M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by WEINSTEIN,MICHAEL H.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000a1) LEFT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A MASS:\u000aPhylloides tumor, low-grade (1.5 cm).\u000aThe stroma is mildy hypercellular with minimal nuclear pleomorphism.\u000aNo stromal overgrowth is seen.\u000aThe mitotic rate averages 4 per 10 hpf (30 fields counted), and focally\u000aranges from 0 to 9 per 10 hpf.\u000aThe tumor shows very focal invasion into surrounding adipose tissue.\u000aThe closest margins are:\u000aposterior <0.1 (initial margin, see part #2)\u000asuperior REMOVED_DATE \u000aanterior REMOVED_DATE \u000aThe inked surgical margins of resection are negative for tumor.\u000aPrior core biosy site changes are identified.\u000aFibrocystic changes, including microcysts and apocrine metaplasia,\u000aare noted in the surrounding breat tissue.\u000a2) LEFT BREAST, NEW POSTERIOR MARGIN:\u000aBenign breast tissue.\u000aNOTE: Drs. Susan Lester and Andrea Richardson of the Breast Pathology\u000aservice have reviewed this case and concur with the diagnosis.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: None given.\u000aOperation: L needle directed breast biopsy.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal L breast mammogram.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Excision, left breast nodule, to mammo.\u000a2. New posterior margin.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Mass in specimen. OR called. (illegible signature)\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by HENDERSON,JOEL M.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart one, labeled "excision, left breast nodule, suture long lateral, short\u000asuperior", consists of a single fragment of tan/yellow, fibroadipose tissue (7\u000ax 6 x REMOVED_DATE cm). The specimen is accompanied by a whole specimen radiograph\u000awhich shows a localization wire in place, marking a circumscribed density\u000alocated closest to the medial and superior margins. The specimen arrives with\u000athe localization wire in place and oriented with sutures including a long\u000asuture to indicate lateral and a short suture to indicate superior. The\u000aspecimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins:\u000aposterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral\u000a= yellow; medial = orange. The localization wire marks a firm, tan/white,\u000alobulated, well circumscribed mass (1.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), that is abutting the\u000aposterior margin and comes to within REMOVED_DATE cm of the anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of\u000athe superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the medial margin\u000aand is well away from the lateral margin. The remainder of the specimen\u000aconsists of approximately 50% yellow, lobulated adipose tissue and 50% diffuse,\u000atan/white, firm fibrous tissue. No other discrete masses or lesions are\u000aidentified. Representative sections, including the entire mass are\u000asubmitted.\u000aMicro 1&2: mass in relation to anterior/posterior/superior and inferior\u000amargins, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 3: mass in relation to medial margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 4: additional medial margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 5&6: representative fibrous tissue, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 7: lateral margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  remainder of mass, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aNOTE: approximately 50% of the specimen was submitted.\u000aPart two, labeled "new posterior margin, suture on new margin", consists of a\u000asingle fragment of tan/yellow fibroadipose tissue (5 x 4 x REMOVED_DATE cm). The\u000aspecimen is marked by a single suture on one of flat surfaces, designating the\u000anew margin which is inked black. The opposite surface is inked blue. The\u000aspecimen consists of approximately 75% yellow, lobulated adipose tissue and 25%\u000afibrous tissue with a single area of firm dense tissue central in the specimen\u000aand abutting the new margin. Representative sections are submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  new posterior margin, 7 frags, RSS.\u000aNOTE: approximately 50% of the specimen was submitted.\u000ajmh\u000aReports to: IGLEHART, JAMES, DIRK M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN\u000a[report_end]
