VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Amend/Addenda\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ROGER L CHRISTIAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000a********** Addended Report ***********\u000aResident: George Lin, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: William R Welch, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aSPECIMEN DESIGNATED "RIGHT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZATION FOR A MASS":\u000aINVASIVE MUCINOUS CARCINOMA\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA\u000aSize - REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aMultifocal - No\u000aHistologic type - Mucinous\u000aHistologic grade (SBR) - I (Well)\u000aNuclear grade - Low\u000aEIC - Absent\u000aLVI - Absent\u000aFinal Margins (invasive) -\u000aNegative (> REMOVED_DATE cm) - medial, lateral, superior\u000aanterior, inferior\u000aClose (0.1 to REMOVED_DATE cm) - posterior (0.15 cm, block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID)\u000aExtruded mucin with associated fibrosis is present within o.1 cm\u000aof the posterior margin (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID)\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aTypes - Cribriform, papillary\u000aNuclear grade - Low\u000aCalcifications in DCIS - Absent\u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - Absent\u000aExtent of DCIS\u000aNumber of blocks/total - REMOVED_DATE blocks\u000aMargins (DCIS)\u000aNegative (> REMOVED_DATE cm) - superior, lateral\u000aClose (0.1 to REMOVED_DATE cm) - medial (0.25 cm), anterior (0.25 cm)\u000aVery close(<0.1 cm from margin)- inferior, posterior\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - Absent\u000aOTHER FINDINGS\u000aPapilloma\u000aAJCC Classification (6th edition) - Tic Nx MX.\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER, PR, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) - Pending\u000aNOTE:\u000aAn immunoperoxidase study for p63 and cytokeratin REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID confirms the absence\u000aof myoepithelial cells in invasive carcinoma (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID). Some of the tumor\u000acells are positive for p63.\u000aThis case was reviewed by Dr. Susan Lester, Breast Pathology Service, who\u000aconcurs.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: None given.\u000aOperation: Excision\u000aOperative Findings: See op note.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Non-palpable mass, Rt breast.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) Breast mass; long - lateral; short - superior.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "RT breast tissue", and consists of an irregular tan/yellow lobulated piece\u000aof fibroadipose tissue (3.5 cm medial and lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm superior to inferior,\u000aand REMOVED_DATE cm anterior to posterior). An accompanying specimen radiograph shows a\u000acentral circumscribed mass and the localization wire.\u000aThere is a needle-localization wire in place which enters through the lateral\u000aaspect of the specimen and exits through the medial aspect of the specimen.\u000aThere is a short suture designating the superior margin and a long suture\u000adesignating the lateral margin. The specimen radiograph shows a central\u000acircumscribed mass and the localization wire. The specimen is inked per\u000apathology protocol (superior red, inferior green, medial orange, lateral\u000ayellow, anterior blue, posterior black) and serially sectioned from medial to\u000alateral. The cut surface is tan/yellow and homogenous with a focal\u000awell-circumscribed hemorrhagic area (1.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) which comes to within\u000a0.2 cm at the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm at the anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000asuperior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial\u000amargin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin. The specimen is submitted in its\u000aentirety.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross sections, block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID to include hemorrhagic\u000aarea, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aSEK/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by William R Welch M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM:\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for invasive carcinoma (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) NEGATIVE (0)\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000ainvasive carcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low > 0% - < 10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor cells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but only a\u000aportion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+):Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in >10% of\u000atumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+):Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in >30% of\u000atumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aExternal controls are evaluated and show appropriate Immunoreactivity.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aAddendum #1 by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
