VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID:REMOVED_CASE_ID Report Status: Signed\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aDIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. Left breast, excision:\u000aDuctal carcinoma in situ, solid/cribriform, grade REMOVED_DATE  focal (0.3 cm.),\u000a0.1 cm. from a mid-superior superficial margin.\u000aHealing biopsy site.\u000aB. Left breast, left posterior margin, excision:\u000aBreast tissue, no diagnostic abnormalities recognized.\u000aC. Left breast, left superior margin, excision:\u000aBiopsy site.\u000aBreast tissue, no diagnostic abnormalities recognized.\u000aD. Left breast, left anterior margin, excision:\u000aBreast tissue, no tumor seen.\u000aSYNOPTIC REPORT: BREAST\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU (DCIS):\u000a-histologic type: solid/cribriform with apocrine features\u000a-histologic grade: REMOVED_DATE \u000a-size (greatest dimension): REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000a-extent: focal\u000a-extensive intraductal component: not applicable\u000a-necrosis in DCIS: none identified\u000a-microcalcifications in DCIS: present\u000a-margins for DCIS: REMOVED_DATE cm. from a mid-superior-superficial\u000amargin in the initial excision, but none\u000apresent in the superior margin (C)\u000asubsequently resected\u000a-immunohistochemical staining on prior specimen (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) was reported as:\u000aEstrogen receptor: POSITIVE (>10% of nuclei stained)\u000aPRIOR RELATED SPECIMENS REVIEWED:\u000asite: left breast, central spec#: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aAJCC pTNM Classification (6th Ed.): pTis pNX pMX\u000aThe pathologic TNM classification above is based only on the information\u000aavailable to the pathologist, and therefore may not be accurate.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by: Richard J. Sampson, M.D.\u000aClinical diagnosis & history:\u000aLeft breast ductal carcinoma in situ\u000aTissue-Designation:\u000aA.Breast, excision with margins - left\u000aB.Breast, excision (without margins) - left, posterior margin\u000aC.Breast, excision with margins - left, superior margin\u000aD.Breast, excision with margins - left, anterior margin\u000aGross description:\u000aThe specimen is received in four containers.\u000aSpecimen A labeled "left breast biopsy" consists of a piece of breast tissue\u000awhich measures 5 x 2 x 2 cm. and weighs 11 grams. Two sutures are present. A\u000along suture is designated lateral and a short suture, superior. A wire is\u000apresent which enters from the lateral side of the specimen. The specimen is\u000aoriented. The deep margin is inked with blue. The superior superficial margin\u000ais inked with green. The inferior superficial margin is inked with black.\u000aSections are taken from lateral to medial. 10X all.\u000aSpecimen B labeled "posterior margin, left breast" consists of a piece of fatty\u000abreast tissue 2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. No marks are present on the specimen. It is\u000atrisected and entirely embedded. 3X all.\u000aSpecimen C labeled "superior margin of left breast" consists of a piece of\u000atissue 2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. A long suture is present on one of the margins of the\u000aspecimen. This entire area is designated the new margin. This entire area is\u000ainked in black. The opposite margin is not inked. Sections are taken from one\u000aend to the other. 4X all.\u000aSpecimen D labeled "anterior margin of left breast, stitch marks new margin"\u000aconsists of a flat piece of firm breast tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x 1 x REMOVED_DATE cm. A\u000astitch is present on a flat margin. This edge, the new margin, is inked with\u000ablack. The opposite side is not inked. Sections are taken from one end to the\u000aother. 4X.\u000aDictated by: RJS____(signature on file)____ REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a____(signature on file)____RICHARD SAMPSON, M.D. REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a[report_end]
