VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID SENTINEL LYMPH NODE\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aWEINSTEIN, MICHAEL, H., M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by WEINSTEIN,MICHAEL H.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000a1, 2) LEFT BREAST AND SENTINEL LYMPH NODES, EXCISION AND SENTINEL LYMPH NODE\u000aBIOPSY:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA.\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU.\u000aLYMPH NODE METASTASES.\u000aSYNOPSIS:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA (part #2)\u000aSize - REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aMultifocal? - No\u000aHistologic Type - Mixed ductal and lobular\u000aHistologic Grade (SBR) - II (Moderate)\u000aNuclear Grade - Intermediate\u000aEIC - Negative\u000aDermal lymphatic invasion - Absent\u000aSkin invasion - Absent\u000aSkeletal muscle invasion - N/A\u000aFinal Margins (invasive) -\u000aNegative (no ink on tumor) - Superior, medial, lateral, anterior,\u000aposterior\u000aClose (<0.1 cm from margin) - Inferior (focal)\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU (part #2)\u000aTypes - Cribriform\u000aNuclear grade - Intermediate\u000aCalcifications in DCIS - Absent\u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - Absent\u000aMicroinvasion (<0.1cm) - Absent\u000aExtent of DCIS\u000aDCIS is present as a minor component of the invasive carcinoma\u000a(1/12 blocks).\u000aFinal Margins (DCIS)\u000aNegative (>0.3 cm) - Anterior, superior, inferior, medial,\u000alateral, posterior\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - Absent\u000aLYMPH NODES (part #1)\u000aSentinel lymph nodes (3 H&E levels examined) - Positive\u000aNumber of positive nodes 2 (one lymph node with\u000amultiple small foci\u000ameasuring in aggregate\u000a0.2-0.3 cm\u000a[macrometastasis];\u000asecond lymph node with\u000amicrometastasis <0.1 cm)\u000aNumber of nodes examined - 5\u000aTOTAL POSITIVE NODES (sentinel + axillary) - REMOVED_DATE \u000aExtranodal extension - Absent\u000aOTHER FINDINGS\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia.\u000aFlorid epithelial hyperplasia.\u000aCysts.\u000aApocrine metaplasia.\u000aCalcifications in benign epithelium.\u000aAJCC CLASSIFICATION - REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDc pNX MX\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER/PR/HER-2) - Pending\u000a3) LEFT BREAST SHAVE MARGIN (CAUDAD):\u000aCysts and apocrine metaplasia.\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy.\u000aNOTE: The focally close margin in part #2 does not represent a final margin.\u000aThe shave margin in part #3 represents the true inferior margin of\u000aresection and is negative for tumor.\u000aThough no prior biopsy site changes are identified, conversation\u000awith the surgeon, Dr. Christian, highlights the clinical certainty\u000aof correspondence between the preciously biopsied lesion and the\u000apresently resected tumor.\u000aSelected slides were reviewed by Dr. Sandy Borowski, who concurs with\u000athe diagnosis.\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: by BOROWSKY,ALEXANDER D.,M.D.\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for invasive carcinoma (block 5):\u000aEstrogen receptor - POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor - POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) - NEGATIVE (1+)\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000ainvasive carcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but\u000aonly a portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity\u000ain >10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 53 year old female with biopsy proven cancer of left breast.\u000aOperation: Wide excision, SNB, L AX\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast cancer\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1) Left sentinel node biopsy\u000a#2) Tumor site left breast\u000a#3) Shaved margin left breast, caudad\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by LOMO,LESLEY C.,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in three parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart one, labeled "#1. left sentinel node biopsy", consists of three fragments\u000aof yellow/tan, lobulated soft tissue fragments measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm,\u000a2.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm, and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. Five lymph nodes are identified,\u000aranging in size from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm, all of which are\u000aentirely submitted.\u000aMicro 1: largest lymph node bisected, 2 frags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  2 intact lymph nodes each, 2 frags, ESS\u000aPart two, labeled "#2. tumor site left breast", consists of a left breast wide\u000aexcisional biopsy specimen (8.7 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which contains white/tan skin\u000a(7.4 x REMOVED_DATE cm), and a short stitch to denote the superior, and long stitch to\u000adenote lateral margin. The specimen has been previously inked by the surgeon\u000aper pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior = black;\u000aanterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial =\u000aorange. The specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral, revealing a\u000awhite, irregularly shaped hard mass (1.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) which is REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000athe inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior, REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior (skin), REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom the posterior, REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin.\u000aThe remainder of the breast parenchyma is comprised predominantly of\u000aunremarkable yellow adipose tissue (75%), and white fibrous tissue (25%).\u000aRepresentative sections of the mass with respect to anterior and inferior\u000amargins, representative sections of the remaining margins and breast tissue\u000aaway from the mass are submitted.\u000aMicro 4: mass and inferior and anterior (skin) margins, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  representative sections of mass, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  superior margin, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  posterior margin, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 11: lateral perpendicular margin, 2 frags, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  medial perpendicular margins, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 14: fibrous tissue just lateral to mass, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 15: fibrous tissue away from mass, 1 frag, RSS\u000aPart three, labeled "#3. shaved margin left breast", consists of a single\u000ayellow fragment of fibrofatty breast tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm, which\u000abears a short stitch to denote seperior and long stitch to denote lateral\u000amargins. The specimen has been previously inked by the surgeon as follows:\u000ainferior margin inked green, and posterior margin inked black. The specimen is\u000ainked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior = black;\u000aanterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial =\u000aorange. The specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral, revealing\u000apredominantly yellow adipose tissue which is unremarkable (95%), and a small\u000aamount of white fibrous tissue (5%). No discrete nodules or lesions are\u000aidentified. Representative sections are submitted.\u000aMicro 16: medial perpendicular margins, 3 frags, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  shave margin left breast, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 22: lateral perpendicular margin, 3 frags, RSS\u000alcl\u000aReports to: CHRISTIAN, ROGER, L. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: SENTINEL LYMPH NODE\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN\u000a[report_end]
