VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Surgical margin\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: BETH ANN LESNIKOSKI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Stefan Kraft, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: William R Welch, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. RIGHT BREAST, WIRE-GUIDED EXCISION FOR DENSITIES AND A CLIP:\u000aSclerosing adenosis.\u000aIntraductal papilloma (0.2 cm).\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia.\u000aColumnar cell changes.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the\u000aspecimen, including margins.\u000aB. RIGHT BREAST, NEW MEDIAL MARGIN:\u000aSclerosing adenosis.\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia.\u000aColumnar cell changes.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the\u000aspecimen, including margins.\u000aThis case has also been reviewed by Dr. T. Ince (Breast Pathology Service), who\u000aconcurs.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: H/O atypical hyperplasia left breast, abnormal right breast MRI.\u000aOperation: Right breast wire localized biopsies x 2.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast radial sclerosing lesion.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Right breast tissue with 2 wires (mammo) standard ink.\u000aB/2. Right breast tissue additional medial margin orange = new margin.\u000aRADIOLOGY: (Medial) tissue is seen. MRI guided localization, Dr. Gombos Please\u000asubmit entire tissue.\u000aTwo wires and clip are seen within the specimen. MRI guided wire localization.\u000aPlease submit entire specimen for histological examination. Dr. Gombos.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart A, labeled "#1. R breast tissue with two wires", consists of a disrupted\u000airregularly shaped yellow/tan breast excision specimen (6.0 M-L x REMOVED_DATE S-I x REMOVED_DATE \u000aA-P cm). The specimen is inked by the surgeon per pathology protocol for the\u000aevaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red;\u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. There are two needle\u000alocalization wires, arbitrarily designated as wire 1 and 2 per prosector. Wire\u000a1 is more lateral, entering the superolateral aspect and exiting the\u000ainferoposterior aspect. Wire 2 is just medial to wire 1, loosely adherent to\u000athe superoanterior aspect of the specimen with the majority of the wire outside\u000aof the specimen. The specimen was previously radiographed, confirming the\u000apresence of two wires and a clip within the specimen. The specimen is serially\u000asectioned from lateral to medial to exhibit approximately 40%\u000adense/nodular/focally cystic fibrous stroma extending to all six inked margins\u000aand approximately 60% yellow/tan lobulated adipose tissue. The needle\u000alocalization wire traverse the dense fibrous stroma in the more lateral aspect\u000aof the specimen, with a small amount of clip identified just medial to wire 1.\u000aNo discrete masses are identified. The specimen is entirely sequentially\u000asubmitted from lateral to medial.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin perpendicularly sectioned, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Tissue traversed by wire 1, 1 frag in each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Tissue associated with tip of wire 2, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Clip site, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Central specimen from lateral to medial, multi frags total, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin perpendicularly sectioned, multi frags in each,\u000aESS.\u000aPart B, labeled "#2. R breast tissue additional medial margin", consists of an\u000aovoid yellow/tan soft tissue (5.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). Per surgeon, the more\u000aintact smooth surface of the specimen was previously inked orange, designating\u000athe new true medial margin. The opposite ragged/irregular surface is inked\u000ablue per prosector (please note, blue ink does not designate true margin). The\u000aspecimen is serially sectioned to exhibit approximately 45% dense/nodular\u000awhite/tan fibrous stroma extending to the new true orange-inked medial margin\u000asurface and approximately 55% yellow/tan lobulated adipose tissue. No discrete\u000amasses or lesions are grossly identified. Please note that the specimen was\u000apreviously radiographed and with no specific radiographic findings indicated\u000aper radiologist.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Multi frags total, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-08-REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aLM/ag\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by William R Welch M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
