VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: MEHRA GOLSHAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Michael A. Seidman, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Jason L Hornick, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. RIGHT BREAST WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISIONAL BIOPSY:\u000aBreast tissue with calcification associated with a hyalinized nodule\u000aand benign epithelium.\u000aCore biopsy site changes.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the\u000aentire specimen, including margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 84 year old female with right breast abnormal mammogram. Core biopsy\u000adiscordant with pathology.\u000aOperation: Right breast wire localized excisional biopsy.\u000aOperative Findings: Not provided.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast abnormal mammogram.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) Right breast wire localized excisional biopsy - short suture/superior,\u000along suture/lateral (to mammo).\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000aTarget, clip and mass in specimen. Called to Golshan by JAR @ 3:45 pm.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "#1. Right breast wire localized excisional biopsy, short suture/superior,\u000along suture/lateral", and consists of an irregular fragment of yellow lobulated\u000afibrofatty tissue (4.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), with a long suture designating lateral,\u000aand a short suture designating superior. There is an inserted needle\u000alocalization wire, as displayed on the accompanying radiograph, which enters\u000aalong the inferior-posterior margin, and traverses towards the superior medial\u000amargin, but does not exit the specimen. The specimen is inked by the\u000aprosector, per pathology protocol as anterior/blue, posterior/black,\u000asuperior/red, inferior/green, lateral/yellow and medial/orange. The specimen\u000ais serially sectioned to reveal a well-healed biopsy cavity (0.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm), containing a surgical clip as displayed on the accompanying radiograph.\u000aThe cavity is located less than REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000athe posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin and REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin. The\u000aremaining cut surface displays 50% focally dense white fibrous tissue, and 50%\u000ayellow lobulated adipose tissue, with no additional discrete masses or lesions\u000aidentified. The specimen is sequentially submitted in its entirety.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, radially, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross sections from lateral to medial, with the clip\u000aidentified in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, and the biopsy cavity in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID (please note REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID is one\u000across section, bisected), multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin, radially, 4 frags, ESS.\u000acp/lp\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jason L Hornick M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000aThursday REMOVED_MONTH 16, 2009 at 06:16:20PM\u000a[report_end]
