 Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity\u000ain >10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Left breast mass with nipple retraction; history of right breast\u000acancer in 1987.\u000aOperation: 11 G Ultrasound guided\u000aOperative findings: Solid mass\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Cancer\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Left breast tissue in pink cassette\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by WITKIEWICZ,AGNIESKA K.,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit\u000anumber, and "left breast", in a pink cassette, and consists of a single, soft,\u000afragmented, yellow to white tissue core (2.4 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate).\u000aMicro 1: Left breast, multi frags, ESS.\u000adf\u000aReports to: SMITH, DARRELL, NOLAN M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY(IES)\u000a[report_end]
