to within REMOVED_DATE cm of the black inked deep margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm subjacent to\u000athe scar. Adjacent to the gritty area is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm well-\u000adilineated, focally hemorrhagic, granular, dense white fibrous tissue with\u000adiffuse fibrocystic change, coming to within REMOVED_DATE cm of the deep margin. The\u000atotal tumor size is REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. (initial tumor bank measurement) The\u000aremaining parenchyma is predominatly yellow lobulated fatty tissue admixed with\u000ascant fibrous tissue. Within the in the attached axilla are multiple tan/red,\u000arubbery to tan/white firm lymph nodes, ranging from REMOVED_DATE to REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest\u000adimension. Representative sections are submitted as follows:\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Gritty mass to deep and lower inner quadrant, 1 frag in each, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Representative of gritty mass to include previous biopsy site, lower\u000ainner quadrant, 1 frag in each, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Gritty mass, lower outer quandrant, 1 frag in each, RSS\u000aMicro 7: Fibrous tissue, (? involvement), upper outer quadrant, 2\u000afrags, RSS\u000aMicro 8: Fibrous tissue, (? involvement), inner upper quandrant, 2 frags, RSS\u000aMicro 8: Nipple and scar, 2 frags, RSS\u000aMicro 10: Nine whole lymph nodes, 9 frags, RSS\u000aMicro 11: Five whole lymph nodes, 5 frags, ESS\u000aMicro 12: Five whole lymph nodes, 5 frags, ESS\u000aMicro 13: Four whole lymph nodes, 4 frags, ESS\u000aMicro 14: Three whole lymph nodes, 3 frags, ESS\u000aMicro 15: Two whole lymph nodes, 2 frags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  One bisected lymph node in each, 2 frags in each, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  One representative section of a grossly positive node in each, 1\u000afrag in each, RSS\u000aPart two, labeled "#2, highest axillary lymph node", consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x\u000a0.3 cm tan, focally white, firm, fatty lymph node, which is bisected and\u000aentirely submitted.\u000aMicro 27: Highest axillary lymph node, 2 frags, ESS\u000aPart three, laled "#3, left axillary lymph node", consists of a REMOVED_DATE cm in\u000agreatest dimension tan/white, firm, fatty lymph node, which is entirely\u000asubmitted.\u000aMicro 28: Left axillary lymph node, 1 frag, ESS\u000alm\u000aReports to: OSTEEN, ROBERT, T. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY W/REGIONAL LYMPH NODES\u000a[report_end]
