ass present. The needle tract is\u000anot grossly apparent. The specimen is entirely submitted from superior to\u000ainferior. A separate fragment of fibroadipose tissue is present in the\u000aspecimen (1.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) that is inked in black, bisected, and entirely\u000asubmitted for analysis.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 14: separate fragment, 2 frags, ESS.\u000adl\u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
