VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-06-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Stacey A. Simons, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Jason L Hornick, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, EXCISIONAL BIOPSY FOR CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU adjacent to biopsy site.\u000aCalcifications associated with benign epithelium.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 54-year-old postmenopausal female with abnormal right mammogram on\u000a07/12/2006 showing clusters of amorphous calc measuring 6 mm upper outer\u000aquadrant - status post right breast core biopsy REMOVED_DATE  revealing LCIS -\u000a(wire L exc recommended).\u000aOperation: Right breast WL BX.\u000aOperative Findings: None provided.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right abnormal mammogram.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Right breast tissue - FS mammo, short equals superior, long equals\u000alateral, whip equals chest wall margin.\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000aClip, intact hook-wire and 3 clusters of calcifications within the specimen.\u000aDr. Gombos.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen was received fresh, in one part, labeled with the patient's name\u000aand unit number, and "#1. Right breast tissue, short equals superior, long\u000aequals lateral, whipstitch equals chest wall margin", and consists of one wire\u000alocalized excisional biopsy specimen with accompanying radiograph and markings\u000aby the radiologist indicating three clusters of calcifications. The specimen\u000acontains three orienting sutures (short/superior, long/lateral,\u000awhipstitch/chest wall margin). The specimen is inked by the surgeon per\u000apathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black;\u000aanterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange.\u000aThe specimen is incompletely inked and will be touched up by the prosector\u000aaccording to the orientation designated by the surgeon. The wire enters the\u000aspecimen at the inferolateral aspect, and there is no exit point. The specimen\u000ais somewhat distorted, measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm overall (5.1 medial to\u000alateral, REMOVED_DATE superior to inferior, REMOVED_DATE anterior to posterior). The specimen is\u000aserially sectioned from medial to lateral into 14 slices, and the tip of the\u000awire is found between slices #8 and #9 at the inferoposterior aspect. The clip\u000ais not grossly identified.\u000aThere is a firm white mass (? fibrosis versus tumor) (5.2 cm x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm).\u000aThis white region extends to margins. Approximately, 40% of the total specimen\u000ais yellow lobulated adipose tissue. The entirety of the white firm tissue will\u000abe submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: White tissue from slice #1 (margins include M), 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: White tissue from slice #2 (margins include M), 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: White tissue from slice #3 (S, M), 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: White tissue from slice #4 (S, M, P), 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: White tissue from slice #5 (S, M, P), 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: White tissue from slice #6 (S, M, A, P), 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #7 white tissue (S, P, A, I), 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: White tissue from slice #8 (S, A, P, ?I), 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #9 white tissue including region of wire tip (S, A, I, ?P), 2\u000afrags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #9 fatty portion inferior to wire tip, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: White tissue from slice #10 bisected (S, L, I, P, A), 3 frags,\u000aESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #11 white tissue bisected (S, L, I), 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #12 (S, L, I), 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #13 (L, I), 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #14 (L, I, S), 2 frags, ESS.\u000aSAS/ajb\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jason L Hornick M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a11/1/2006\u000a[report_end]
