VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID:REMOVED_CASE_ID Report Status: Signed\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aDIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. Left breast, needle localized excision:\u000aPrior biopsy site changes.\u000aFew small foci of ductal carcinoma in situ with marked degenerative\u000achanges (status post chemotherapy), see note.\u000aB. Left breast, lateral margin, excision:\u000aFew small foci of ductal carcinoma in situ with marked degenerative\u000achanges (status post chemotherapy), see note.\u000aC. Left breast, medial margin, excision:\u000aPrior biopsy site changes.\u000aFew small foci of ductal carcinoma in situ with marked degenerative\u000achanges (status post chemotherapy), see note.\u000aD. Left breast, inferior margin, excision:\u000aBreast tissue with no diagnostic abnormalities recognized.\u000aNo tumor seen.\u000aE. Left breast, deep margin, excision:\u000aBreast tissue with no diagnostic abnormalities recognized.\u000aNo tumor seen.\u000aF. Left breast, superior margin, excision:\u000aFew small foci of ductal carcinoma in situ with marked degenerative\u000achanges (status post chemotherapy), see note.\u000aG. Left breast, anterior margin, excision:\u000aOne duct with ductal carcinoma in situ with marked degenerative changes\u000a(status post chemotherapy), see note.\u000aNOTE: The prior needle core biopsy report (MGH REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) has been noted and\u000athe sentinel lymph node report (NWH S-03-7623) has been noted.\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU (DCIS):\u000a-histologic type: Not evaluable due to marked therapy\u000aeffect\u000a-histologic grade: Intermediate grade\u000a-size (greatest dimension): In the main specimen A, a few scattered\u000aducts of ductal carcinoma in situ are\u000aseen over a REMOVED_DATE cm. area. Each focus\u000ais less than REMOVED_DATE cm. In specimen B,\u000atwo foci of ductal carcinoma in situ\u000aare seen and each is less than REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000aIn specimen C, two foci are seen, each\u000ais less than REMOVED_DATE cm. In specimen F,\u000atwo foci are seen and each foci is REMOVED_DATE \u000acm. In specimen G, only one focus of\u000aductal carcinoma in situ is seen and\u000ait is REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000a-extent: Focal\u000a-extensive intraductal component: Not evaluable\u000a-necrosis in DCIS: Present, very focal\u000a-microcalcifications in DCIS: None identified\u000a-margins for DCIS:\u000aIn the main specimen, a few duct of ductal carcinoma in situ are\u000afocally at the deep margin, less than REMOVED_DATE cm. from the superior margin\u000aand less than REMOVED_DATE cm. from the inferior-lateral margin (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) and REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000afrom the anterior margin. In specimen B, one of the ducts with ductal\u000acarcinoma in situ is REMOVED_DATE cm. from the true inked margin. In specimen C,\u000aboth foci of ductal carcinoma in situ are REMOVED_DATE cm. from the true inked\u000amargin. In specimen F, one of the foci of ductal carcinoma in situ, is\u000afocally less than REMOVED_DATE cm. from the inked true margin. In specimen G, the\u000aone focus of ductal carcinoma in situ is in the middle of the unoriented\u000aspecimen.\u000aNOTE: The degenerative changes seen in the ductal carcinoma in situ foci is\u000amost likely due to recent chemotherapy protocol effect. Viability of\u000athe ductal carcinoma in situ cannot be evaluated.\u000aNo residual invasive tumor identified.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by: Nicole A. Mihok, M.D.\u000aClinical diagnosis & history:\u000aLeft breast mass; sentinel node mapping at Newton-Wellesley Hospital; status\u000apost chemo; resolution of left breast mass by exam and mammo; clip localized\u000atoday; left breast mass\u000aTissue-Designation:\u000aA.Breast, excision with margins - left\u000aB.Breast, excision with margins - left, lateral margin\u000aC.Breast, excision with margins - left, medial margin\u000aD.Breast, excision with margins - left, inferior margin\u000aE.Breast, excision with margins - left, deep margin\u000aF.Breast, excision with margins - left, superior margin\u000aG.Breast, excision with margins - left, anterior margin\u000aGross description:\u000aThe specimen is received in seven containers.\u000aSpecimen A labeled "left breast mass" is received in formalin and consists of a\u000aneedle localized specimen with a short stitch on the superior margin and a long\u000astitch at the lateral margin. The specimen measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. It is\u000asectioned from the lateral towards the medial end and shows a needle biopsy\u000atract and a small firm, white area that is up to REMOVED_DATE cm. The entire specimen\u000ais submitted from the lateral towards the medial end in cassettes REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID is\u000amost lateral; REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID is most medial). 4 agg. all.\u000aSpecimen B labeled "left breast margin, left lateral" is received in formalin\u000aand consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. portion of breast tissue with a stitch\u000adesignated on the requisition form as the side away from the tumor. This is\u000athe true margin. This surface is inked black. The other surfaces are not\u000ainked. The specimen is sectioned and submitted in one cassette. 1 agg. all.\u000aSpecimen C is labeled "left breast margin, medial" consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x\u000a0.5 cm. portion of breast tissue with a stitch designating the surface furthest\u000afrom the tumor. This is the true margin. The surface is inked black. The\u000aother surfaces are not inked. The specimen is serially sectioned and entirely\u000asubmitted in one cassette. 1 agg. all.\u000aSpecimen D labeled "left breast margin, inferior" consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm. portion of breast tissue with a stitch designating the surface furthest\u000afrom the tumor. This is the true margin. The surface is inked black. The\u000aother surfaces are not inked. The specimen is serially sectioned and entirely\u000asubmitted in one cassette. 1 agg. all.\u000aSpecimen E labeled "left breast shaved margin, deep" is received in formalin\u000aand consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. portion of breast tissue with a stitch\u000adesignating the surface furthest from the tumor which is the true margin. This\u000asurface is inked black. The other surfaces are not inked. The specimen is\u000aserially sectioned and entirely submitted in one cassette. 1 agg. all.\u000aSpecimen F labeled "left breast margin, superior" is received in formalin and\u000aconsists of a portion of breast tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. There is\u000aa stitch designating the surface furthest from the tumor. This surface is\u000ainked black. It is the true margin. The other surfaces are not inked. The\u000aspecimen is serially sectioned and entirely submitted in one cassette. 1 agg.\u000aall.\u000aSpecimen G labeled "left breast margin, anterior" consists of two unoriented\u000aportions of fibrofatty tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm. They are both submitted in one cassette. 2X all.\u000aDictated by: NAM____(signature on file)____DENNIS J. FEEN, M.D. REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a____(signature on file)____NICOLE MIHOK, M.D. REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a[report_end]
