VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID:REMOVED_CASE_ID Report Status: Signed\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aDIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. Left breast, excision:\u000aDuctal carcinoma in situ, multiple foci, with marked degenerative changes\u000a(S/P chemotherapy), see synoptic report.\u000aPrior biopsy site changes.\u000aB. Left breast (superior margin), excision:\u000aDuctal carcinoma in situ, multiple foci, with marked degenerative changes\u000a(present within REMOVED_DATE cm. of resected surgical margin.\u000aC. Left breast (medial margin), excision:\u000aDuctal carcinoma in situ, single focus with marked degenerative changes\u000a(present within REMOVED_DATE cm. of inked surgical margin).\u000aD. Left breast (lateral margin), excision:\u000aPrior biopsy site changes.\u000aSYNOPTIC REPORT:\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU (DCIS):\u000a-histologic type: Not evaluable due to marked chemotherapy\u000aeffect\u000a-histologic grade: Intermediate\u000a-size (greatest dimension): See note.\u000a-extent: Focal\u000a-extensive intraductal component: Not evaluable\u000a-necrosis in DCIS: Present, focal\u000a-microcalcifications in DCIS: None identified\u000a-margins for DCIS: See note.\u000aNOTE: In specimen A, there are several foci of ductal carcinoma in situ seen\u000aover approximately a 3 x 3 cm. area. Each focus is less than REMOVED_DATE cm. in\u000asize and several are present at the inked surgical margin as well as\u000awithin REMOVED_DATE cm. of the margin. In specimen B, there are also several\u000afoci of ductal carcinoma in situ, two of which are within REMOVED_DATE cm. of the\u000asurgical margin. In specimen C, one focus of ductal carcinoma in situ\u000ais present within REMOVED_DATE cm. of the margin.\u000aSKIN:\u000aUnremarkable, small segment in specimen A.\u000aPRIOR RELATED SPECIMENS REVIEWED:\u000aThe degenerative change in the ductal carcinoma in situ most likely reflects\u000arecent chemotherapy effect. Viability of the neoplastic cells cannot be\u000aassessed. No residual invasive carcinoma is seen. The previous surgical\u000aspecimen (S-03-REMOVED_CASE_ID) is reviewed.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by: Dennis J. Feen, M.D.\u000aClinical diagnosis & history:\u000aLeft breast carcinoma\u000aTissue-Designation:\u000aA.Breast, excision with margins - left\u000aB.Breast, excision (without margins) - left, superior margin\u000aC.Breast, excision with margins - left, medial margin\u000aD.Breast, excision with margins - left, lateral margin\u000aGross description:\u000aSpecimen A labeled "left breast excision" is received in formalin and consists\u000aof three fragments of tissue. The largest tissue fragment is 3 x REMOVED_DATE x 1 cm.\u000aThere is a short green suture designating the superior margin and a long green\u000asuture, the medial margin. The superior margin is inked with blue ink. The\u000aother two fragments are 2 x 1 x REMOVED_DATE cm. and REMOVED_DATE x 1 x REMOVED_DATE cm. Each is bisected\u000aalong the long axis and submitted designated REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. The larger fragment is\u000asectioned with the superior margin separately removed and submitted REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. The\u000arest is sectioned from lateral to medial designated REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aSpecimen B labeled "left breast, superior margin" is received in formalin and\u000aconsists of two irregular fragments of yellowish-red fibroadipose tissue. One\u000ais 2 x 2 x REMOVED_DATE cm. and the other is 3 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. 2X all.\u000aSpecimen C labeled "left breast, medial margin" consists of a small fragment of\u000ayellowish-red fibroadipose tissue 2 x 1 x REMOVED_DATE cm. The margins are inked. 1X\u000aall.\u000aSpecimen D labeled "left breast, lateral margin" consists of a small\u000ayellowish-red fragment of fibroadipose tissue 1 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The margins\u000aare inked. 1X all.\u000aDictated by: DJF____(signature on file)____DANIEL D. KOELLIKER, M.D. REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a____(signature on file)____DENNIS J. FEEN, M.D. REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a[report_end]
