VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID:REMOVED_CASE_ID Report Status: Signed\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aDIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. Left breast, simple mastectomy:\u000aFocal ductal carcinoma in situ, with marked degenerative changes (status\u000apost chemotherapy).\u000aChanges consistent with prior excision site.\u000aSkin with dermal scar and nipple with no diagnostic abnormalities\u000arecognized.\u000aFibrocystic changes with focal ductal hyperplasia.\u000aB. Skin of medial left chest wall, excision:\u000aMild chronic inflammation.\u000aNOTE: Adjacent to the prior excision site there are multiple ducts with\u000aductal carcinoma in situ (present in five consecutive slide and REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000ain greatest span measured on a slide). The margins are free of ductal\u000acarcinoma in situ. The ductal carcinoma in situ shows degenerative\u000achanges similar to those seen in the prior excisions (S-03-REMOVED_CASE_ID and\u000aS-03-REMOVED_CASE_ID). No necrosis or microcalcifications are seen in the ductal\u000acarcinoma in situ.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by: Daniel D. Koelliker, M.D.\u000aClinical diagnosis & history:\u000aLeft breast carcinoma\u000aTissue-Designation:\u000aA.Breast, simple mastectomy - left\u000aB.Skin, excision - left chest wall\u000aGross description:\u000aThe specimen is received in two containers.\u000aSpecimen A labeled "#1 left breast" consists of a 278 gram, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 cm.\u000asimple mastectomy specimen which is marked at one aspect with a suture\u000aclinically oriented as 12 o'clock of the left breast. On the superficial\u000asurface, there is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. skin ellipse which has a 3 cm. in diameter\u000aareola with an unremarkable REMOVED_DATE cm. in diameter nipple located eccentrically on\u000athe ellipse, and located REMOVED_DATE cm. in the REMOVED_DATE o'clock aspect of the skin ellipse,\u000athere is a REMOVED_DATE cm. well healed linear scar. Otherwise, the superficial\u000asurfaces are unremarkable. The deep surface shows smooth adipose tissue with a\u000afocal area of REMOVED_DATE cm. thick skeletal muscle located in the 5 o'clock aspect of\u000athe deep surface. No gross evidence of tumor is seen. The margins throughout\u000aare inked black. Cross sectioning the specimen demonstrates primarily yellow\u000alobulated adipose tissue with thin strands of white-tan fibrous tissue and\u000afocal rubbery, white-tan fibrous areas. Located deep to the skin scar, there\u000ais a REMOVED_DATE x 1 cm. area of fat necrosis. No gross evidence of tumor is seen in\u000athe surrounding tissue which shows yellow streaks of fat necrosis.\u000aSection code: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - entire area surrounding prior excision site\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - representative sections from medial portion of specimen\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - nipple\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - skin with scar\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - representative sections of mid portion of specimen\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - lateral aspect of specimen, representative sections\u000aSpecimen B labeled "#2, medial left chest wall skin" is received fresh and\u000aconsists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. ellipse of skin. No gross suspicious areas\u000aare seen. The specimen is sectioned and entirely submitted in one cassette.\u000a3X all.\u000aDictated by: DDK____(signature on file)____DANIEL D. KOELLIKER, M.D. REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a[report_end]
