VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Amend/Addenda\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast biopsy\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ROGER L CHRISTIAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000a********** Addended Report ***********\u000aResident: Adam Rosendorff, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Susan Lester, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, EXCISION FOR A REMOVED_DATE CM PALPABLE MASS:\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, cribriform type (low nuclear grade),\u000aassociated with rare calcifications, is present in two of two blocks.\u000aThe DCIS involves an area of cysts and fibroadenomatoid changes,\u000aconsistent with an area of juvenile papillomatosis.\u000aDCIS is < REMOVED_DATE cm from the unoriented margins.\u000aA definite prior core needle biopsy site is not seen.\u000aNote: The patient underwent a prior core needle biopsy that showed\u000afocal cribriforming and nuclear atypia (reviewed as REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID). The DCIS\u000aappears to be an incidental finding.\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies for ER, PR, and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu will be reported in an\u000aaddendum.\u000aThis carcinoma would be classified as AJCC (6th edition) Tis NX.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: None given.\u000aOperation: Excision.\u000aOperative Findings: See op-note.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast mass.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Right breast tissue.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit\u000anumber and "right breast tissue", and consists of an unoriented portion of\u000adense pink/tan fibrous tissue (1.6 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The specimen is inked\u000ablack and serially sectioned, exhibiting a tan/white dense, fibrotic to focally\u000acystic cut surface. No other gross lesions identified.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 4 frags total, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000adl/ag\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a10/12/2007\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM:\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for DCIS (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) NEGATIVE (1+)\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000ainvasive carcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low > 0% - < 10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor cells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but only a\u000aportion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+):Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in >10% of\u000atumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+):Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in >30% of\u000atumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aExternal controls are evaluated and show appropriate Immunoreactivity.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aAddendum #1 by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
