VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ROGER L CHRISTIAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Kevin B Long, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Alessandra F Nascimento, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, RE-EXCISION:\u000aNo residual carcinoma in situ identified.\u000aBiopsy cavity changes.\u000aSkin with scarring.\u000aCalcifications associated with benign epithelium.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Incidentally found DCIS @ previous excision of mass, rt breast.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: DCIS rt breast.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) DCIS site right breast, long suture/lateral, short suture/superior.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "DCIS right breast tissue, long/lateral, short/superior", and consists of\u000aan irregular tan/yellow lobulated portion of fibroadipose tissue (3.6 cm medial\u000ato lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm anterior to posterior, and REMOVED_DATE cm superior to inferior) with\u000aan overlying tan/white wrinkled skin ellipse at the anterior margin (2.1 x REMOVED_DATE \u000ax REMOVED_DATE cm). There is a short suture designating the superior margin and a long\u000asuture designating the lateral margin. The skin ellipse displays a dense white\u000afibrous linear scar (1.2 x REMOVED_DATE cm), which comes within REMOVED_DATE cm of the nearest\u000aradial margin. The specimen has been previously inked per the surgeon per\u000apathology protocol (superior/red, inferior/green, medial/orange,\u000alateral/yellow, anterior/blue, and posterior/black) and the specimen is\u000aserially sectioned from medial to lateral. The cut surface is tan/yellow and\u000ahomogeneous with a focal area of dense white fibrous tissue underlying the\u000apreviously described scar, which constitutes approximately 30% of the breast\u000aparenchyma. No discrete lesion or biopsy sites are grossly identified. The\u000aspecimen is submitted in its entirety.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross sections medial to lateral, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, 3 frags, ESS.\u000asek/lp\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Alessandra F Nascimento M.D., Electronically signed on\u000a12/13/2007\u000a[report_end]
