VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST BIOPSY W/O MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aKRANE, JEFFREY, FRED, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by KRANE,JEFFREY FRED,M.D.,PH.D.\u000a1) RIGHT BREAST AT 10 O'CLOCK, EXCISIONAL BIOPSY FOR A MASS:\u000aFibroadenoma (1 cm).\u000aAdjacent breast tissue with no significant pathologic change.\u000aPrior biopsy site.\u000a2) RIGHT BREAST, PERIAREOLAR AT 9 O'CLOCK, EXCISIONAL BIOPSY FOR A MASS:\u000aFibroadenoma (2 cm).\u000aAdjacent breast tissue with no significant pathologic change.\u000aPrior biopsy site.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Right breast masses.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Right breast biopsy.\u000a2. Right breast biopsy.\u000aMasses in specimens.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by BARRY,MARC,MB,BCH,BAO\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number. Both specimens are received with specimen mammogram\u000ashowing masses in specimen.\u000aPart one, labeled "#1, right wire localized breast biopsy, short stitch\u000asuperior, long stitch lateral", and consists of a fragment of fibrofatty tissue\u000aand REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm with a wire localization needle in situ and long and\u000ashort sutures designating lateral and superior margins respectively. This\u000acontains a focal hemorrhagic white nodule (1.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) present near the\u000amedial aspect of the specimen. This is focally hemorrhagic. The remainder of\u000athe specimen shows adipose tissue. The specimen is inked per pathology\u000aprotocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue;\u000asuperior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. This\u000aspecimen is representatively sampled for microscopic examination as follows.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  white firm nodule, 5 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 4: section from remainder of tissue, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aPart two, labeled "#2, right wire localized breast biopsy and two short suture\u000asuperior, one long lateral 9 o'clock peri-areolar", consists of a fragment of\u000afibrofatty tissue at 8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm with a wire localization needle in situ\u000aand one (1) suture designating the lateral peri-areolar and two (2) short\u000adesignating superior. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the\u000aevaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red;\u000ainferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. The specimen is serially\u000asectioned at 3 mm intervals from medial to lateral and shows a fibrous cut\u000asurface with nodular areas. The specimen is representatively sampled for\u000amicroscopic examination as follows.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  right breast mass, 8 frags, RSS.\u000aincluding peri-areolar area in cassette #9.\u000amab\u000aReports to: MATORY, YVEDT M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST BIOPSY W/O MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST BIOPSY W/O MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
