VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY(IES)\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aRICHARDSON, ANDREA, L., M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by RICHARDSON,ANDREA L.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST, 11 G ULTRASOUND GUIDED CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR A MASS:\u000aINVASIVE METAPLASTIC CARCINOMA, at least REMOVED_DATE cm (See NOTE.)\u000aThe carcinoma is poorly differentiated (modified Bloom-Richardson grade\u000aIII/III).\u000aNo lymphovascular invasion or in situ carcinoma seen.\u000aNOTE: The carcinoma in this biopsy shows a biphasic appearance with\u000apredominance of high grade sarcomatoid spindle and giant cell\u000adifferentiation and focal areas of high grade squamous cell\u000adifferentiation.\u000aCytokeratin REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 34REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, Cam5.2, and PAN-K each show strong diffuse\u000apositivity in the squamous cell component and focal positivity in\u000arare spindle cells in the sarcomatoid component, supporting the diagnosis\u000aof a metaplastic carcinoma.\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for invasive carcinoma:\u000aEstrogen receptor NEGATIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor NEGATIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) NEGATIVE (0)\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000ainvasive carcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but\u000aonly a portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity\u000ain >10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Positive FNA of left breast mass at BIDMC.\u000aOperation: 11g U/S\u000aOperative findings:\u000a3.5 cm mass indeterminate\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 7 passes (gray cassette)\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by PREISINGER,ELIZABETH ANN,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit\u000anumber, and "left breast", in a gray cassette, and consists of multiple, soft,\u000afragmented, yellow to white tissue cores (2.3 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate).\u000aMicro 1: Multi frags, ESS.\u000adfi\u000aReports to: RAZA, SUGHRA M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY(IES)\u000a[report_end]
