VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aODZE, ROBERT, DANIEL, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by ODZE,ROBERT DANIEL,M.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST EXCISION AND AXILLARY NODE DISSECTION:\u000aINVASIVE METAPLASTIC CARCINOMA AND NEGATIVE LYMPH NDOES.\u000aSYNOPSIS:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA\u000aSize - REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aMultifocal - No\u000aHistologic Type - Metaplastic\u000aHistologic Grade (SBR) - III(Poor)\u000aNuclear Grade - High\u000aEIC - N/A\u000aLymphovascular invasion - Absent\u000aDermal lymphatic invasion - N/A\u000aSkin invasion - N/A\u000aSkeletal muscle invasion - N/A\u000aFinal Margins (invasive) -\u000aNegative (>0.3 cm) anterior, posterior, medial, lateral,\u000asuperior, inferior\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU - Absent\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - Absent\u000aLYMPH NODES\u000aAxillary lymph nodes: Negative\u000aNumber of positive nodes: 0\u000aNumber of nodes examined: 16\u000aTOTAL POSITIVE NODES (sentinel + axillary) - REMOVED_DATE \u000aAJCC CLASSIFICATION (6th edition): REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID pREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID MX\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER/PR/HER-2) - Performed previously\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Invasive metaplastic cancer of left breast.\u000aOperation: Lumpectomy and axillary node dissection\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Invasive metaplastic cancer left breast\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1) Left needle directed breast biopsy (no mammo per Dr.\u000aIglehart)\u000a#2) New lateral and inferior margin, left breast - stitch on\u000anew margin\u000a#3) Axillary nodes, left - stitch apex\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by HAHN,HEJIN P.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in three parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart one, labeled "#1. left needle directed breast biopsy", consists of a piece\u000aof left breast tissue (8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with two orienting sutures. The\u000aspecimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins:\u000aposterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral\u000a= yellow; medial = orange. There is a firm tan/white tumor mass (4.5 x 3 x 3\u000acm) that is well-circumscribed and contains a small area of hemorrhage that\u000alikely represents core biopsy site. The mass contains a few pale yellow areas\u000asuggestive of necrosis. The mass is less than REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin,\u000aless than REMOVED_DATE cm from the deep margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom the anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin and REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000amedial margin. Representative sections of the tumor mass are submitted to the\u000atumor bank. The remainder of the breast parenchyma is 20% white fibrous\u000atissue. Approximately 30% of the entire specimen is submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  tumor with lateral margin, 2 frags, RSS\u000aMicro 3: tumor with posterior margin, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 4: tumor with inferior margin, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 5: tumor with inferior and posterior margins, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  tumor with superior margin, 2 frags, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  anterior margin, 2 frags, RSS\u000aMicro 10: medial margin, 2 frags, RSS\u000aPart two, labeled "#2. new lateral and inferior margin left breast", consists\u000aof a piece of breast tissue (6 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with a stitch on one surface\u000aindicating the new margin. The new margin is inked blue and the old margin is\u000ainked black. Serial sectioning reveals that the specimen is 90% yellow adipose\u000atissue. No lesions are grossly identified. Approximately 50% of the\u000aspecimen is submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  new shave margin, 6 frags, RSS\u000aPart three, labeled "#3. axillary nodes, left, stitch apex", consists of a\u000apiece of yellow/tan fibroadipose tissue (12.2 x 9 x REMOVED_DATE cm) that contains\u000aseventeen pink/tan lymph nodes (ranging from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x\u000a1.0 cm). The lymph nodes are entirely submitted.\u000aMicro 17: 4 lymph nodes, 4 frags, ESS\u000aMicro 18: 4 lymph nodes, 4 frags, ESS\u000aMicro 19: 2 lymph nodes, 1 inked blue and bisected, 3 frags, ESS\u000aMicro 20: 3 lymph nodes, 3 frags, ESS\u000aMicro 21: 1 lymph node, bisected, 2 frags, ESS\u000aMicro 22: 2 lymph nodes, 1 inked blue and bisected, 3 frags, ESS\u000aMicro 23: 1 lymph node, bisected, 2 frags, ESS\u000ahph\u000aReports to: IGLEHART, JAMES, DIRK M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: LYMPH NODE BIOPSY\u000a[report_end]
