VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Surgical margin\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ROGER L CHRISTIAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Marianna B Ruzinova, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Jane E. Brock, M.B., B.S., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. RIGHT BREAST EXCISION (SUPERIOR):\u000aNormal breast tissue with biopsy site changes.\u000aThe margins were inked and evaluated for the final diagnosis.\u000aB. RIGHT BREAST WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A CLIP AND CALCIFICATIONS\u000a(INFERIOR):\u000aResidual columnar cell change with flat epithelial atypia associated with\u000abiopsy site changes (< REMOVED_DATE cm focus, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID)\u000aNormal breast tissue with biopsy site changes.\u000aThe margins were inked and evaluated for the final diagnosis.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Unusual atypia, rt breast.\u000aOperation: Loc/excis.\u000aOperative Findings: See Op Note.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Unusual atypia, rt breast.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) tissue, right breast - superior.\u000aB/2) tissue, right breast - inferior.\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000aSpecimen #2: Called to OR 11:19 am - hookwire/clip/few Ca++. H. Peters #REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname, unit number.\u000aPart A, labeled "tissue right breast - superior", consists of an unoriented\u000aportion of fibrofatty soft tissue (5.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which was received with\u000aan accompanying radiograph showing two densities but no clip in the specimen.\u000aThe specimen is inked black and serially sectioned to exhibit a white\u000aill-defined nodular area (1.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), abutting the black-inked margin.\u000aThe remaining cut surface exhibits unremarkable lobulated adipose tissue with\u000ano fibrous tissue. The specimen is submitted in its entirety.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Entire specimen to include ill-defined nodular area (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID),\u000amulti frags total, ESS.\u000aPart B, labeled "tissue right breast - inferior", consists of an irregular\u000afragment of unoriented fibroadipose tissue (3.4 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) received with a\u000aneedle localization wire in placed, which is also demonstrated on the\u000aaccompanying radiograph along with a clip. The specimen is inked and serially\u000asectioned to exhibit a metallic clip within an ill-defined focally firm\u000atan-yellow area (0.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which abuts the margin. The remaining\u000acut surface exhibits a fibrohemorrhagic area, consistent with previous biopsy\u000asite, which runs the length of the specimen (2.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which also\u000acontains packing material. The fibrous area abuts the margin while the\u000ahemorrhagic biopsy cavity is located REMOVED_DATE cm from the margin and REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000aarea designated by the clip. The specimen is submitted in its entirety.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Perpendicular sections through slice containing clip, 3 frags in\u000aeach, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Remainder of the specimen to include hemorrhagic biopsy cavity, 1\u000afrag in each, ESS.\u000ajc/lp\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jane E. Brock M.B., B.S., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a11/10/2008\u000a[report_end]
