VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aLESTER, SUSAN, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR CALCIFICATIONS AND A CLIP:\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, solid and cribriform types (high nuclear\u000agrade) is present in 3 of 14 blocks (blocks 12 to 14). No calcifications\u000aor necrosis are associated with DCIS. The DCIS is associated with an\u000aunusual eosinophilic amorphous secretory material.\u000aDCIS is present at the medial margin and is < REMOVED_DATE cm from inferior and\u000aposterior margins. DCIS is not seen close to other margins.\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia is present.\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia with pagetoid spread, is present (e.g. block\u000a11).\u000aCalcifications are present associated with benign epithelium\u000a(predominantly small cysts and epithelial hyperplasia in lobules).\u000aBiopsy site changes are present.\u000aNote: The DCIS is not located adjacent to the prior core needle biopsy\u000asite and appears to be an incidental finding.\u000aThis carcinoma would be classified as AJCC Tis NX MX.\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for DCIS (block 12):\u000aEstrogen receptor NEGATIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor NEGATIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) NEGATIVE (0)\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID POSITIVE for myoepithelial cells surrounding\u000aareas of DCIS\u000aNote: Rare ER and PR positive cells are intermingled in the areas of DCIS.\u000aThese cells appear to be residual normal luminal cells rather than DCIS.\u000aNormal epithelial cells are appropriately immunoreactive for estrogen and\u000aprogesterone receptors.\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000acarcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but\u000aonly a portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity\u000ain >10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 67 yo woman with abnormal right mammogram, on screening.\u000aStereotactic bx found marked pleomorphism assocociated with ca++.\u000aOperation: Right needle breast bx.\u000aOperative findings: Radiology confirms microcalc/clip in specimen.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right abnl mammogram.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Right breast tissue - colors per path - mammo.\u000aRADIOLOGY REPORT: Clip and calcifications in specimen. Dr. Frost\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by RUCKER-SCHMIDT,RACHEL L.,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in one part, labeled with the patient's name,\u000aunit number and "right breast tissue - colors per path", and consists of a REMOVED_DATE \u000ax REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm lumpectomy specimen which includes a needle localizaiton wire.\u000aA radiograph accompanies the specimen which shows the needle localization wire\u000aadjacent to a clip and near several clusters of microcalcifications. The\u000aspecimen is received previously inked by the surgeon as follows: anterior -\u000ablue, posterior - black, medial - orange, lateral - yellow, superior - red, and\u000ainferior - green. The specimen is serially sectioned from lateral to medial to\u000areveal no gross lesions. The specimen is approximately 85% fibroadipose tissue\u000aand 15% fibrous tissue. The clip is removed and the entire specimen is\u000asubmitted serially from lateral to medial for microscopic examination.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  lateral margin, perpendicular, 7 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  serial sections from lateral to medial including superior,\u000ainferior, anterior, and posterior margins, 10 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  medial margin, perpendicular, 7 frags, ESS.\u000arlr\u000aReports to: LOCKHART, DIANE, CATHERINE M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
