VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aKRANE, JEFFREY, FRED, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by KRANE,JEFFREY FRED,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, EXCISION WIRE LOCALIZATION FOR CALCIFICATIONS AND A CLIP:\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aSYNOPSIS:\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aTypes - solid, cribriform, micropapillary,\u000aclinging\u000aNuclear grade - intermediate to high\u000aCalcifications in DCIS - present\u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - present\u000aMicroinvasion (<0.1cm) - absent\u000aExtent of DCIS\u000aNumber of blocks:total - 11:14 blocks\u000aFinal Margins (DCIS)\u000aNegative (>0.3 cm) - posterior\u000aClose (0.1-0.3 cm) - superior (focal)\u000aVery close (<0.1 cm) - medial (multifocal), lateral\u000a(multifocal), anterior (multifocal),\u000ainferior (multifocal)\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - absent\u000aOTHER FINDINGS\u000aCalcifications in benign epithelium\u000aAJCC CLASSIFICATION (6th edition) - REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDs pNx MX\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER/PR/HER-2) - performed previously\u000aNOTE:\u000aThe eosinophilic secretory material associated with DCIS in a prior specimen\u000a(REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) is also associated with DCIS in the current specimen.\u000aAn atypical focus in block 5 is p63 reactive in myoepithelial cells and is\u000apositive for E-cadherin, consistent with a focus of atypical ductal\u000ahyperplasia.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 67 year old female with right breast DCIS by needle localization\u000abiopsy; post biopsy review of mammo showed additional area of\u000amicrocalcifications a distance away- stereotactic biopsy evaluation done but\u000aunable to do biopsy; scheduled for right needle loc. of new area.\u000aOperation: Right needle loc. breast biopsy\u000aOperative findings: Microcalcifications in spec.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast DCIS\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1. Right breast tissue - needle loc\u000aRADIOLOGY: Calcifications in specimen. E.P. Frost,MD\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by CHANG,PRISCILLA S.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "#1. right breast tissue needle loc.", and consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm portion of breast tissue with a wire. An accompanying radiograph\u000ademonstrates a cluster of microcalcifications. The specimen is inked by the\u000asurgeon per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior =\u000ablack; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow;\u000amedial = orange. Serial sectioning reveals that the tissue consists of\u000aapproximately 25% firm white fibrous area, mostly near the area demarcated by\u000athe wire. The fibrous area is located REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000amedial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior\u000amargin. The specimen is entirely submitted from medial to lateral.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  medial margin, perpendicular, 6 frags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  serial sections, mult frags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  lateral margin, perpendicular including fibrous area, 7 frags,\u000aESS\u000apsc\u000aReports to: LOCKHART, DIANE, CATHERINE M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
