VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Qinghong Yang, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Kirstine Yung-Ting Oh, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA/1). LEFT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A CLIP:\u000aBenign breast tissue with flat atypia, columnar cell change, intraductal\u000apapilloma and biopsy site changes. (Levels examined).\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 44 year old premenopausal female whose REMOVED_DATE  mammogram demonstrate\u000aLUOQ calcifications. REMOVED_DATE  core biopsy revealed columnar cell hyperplasia\u000awith atypia for which excision is recommended.\u000aOperation: Left breast wire localized excision.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal mammogram.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Left breast tissue short - superior, long - lateral, whip stitch - deep\u000amargin.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Clip in specimen. E.P. Frost\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "#1. Left breast tissue, short superior, long lateral, whip suture deep\u000amargin", and consists of REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm excision of fibroadipose tissue,\u000aoriented by sutures designating superior (short suture), lateral (long suture),\u000aand deep (whip stitch) margins. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol\u000afor the evaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red;\u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange (inked by surgeon). A localizing\u000awire enters the posterior/superior aspect of the specimen and exits the\u000aposterior/inferior aspect. The specimen is received with a radiograph\u000ademonstrating localizing wire in place within the posterior aspect of the\u000aspecimen, adjacent to a metallic surgical clip. Sectioning demonstrates dense\u000agranular tan/white fibrous tissue (at least 85% of the specimen), without\u000adiscrete masses, lesions, or other abnormalities grossly. The area bearing the\u000asurgical clip is within REMOVED_DATE cm of the nearest posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of\u000anearest medial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the closest lateral margins, REMOVED_DATE cm of closest\u000asuperior margin, and is remote from the anterior margin. The entire specimen\u000ais submitted, sequentially from anterior to posterior, with area of interest in\u000amicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID (tissue with clip in micro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Entire specimen, sequentially (perpendicular anterior margin in\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, perpendicular posterior margin (area of interest) in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), multi frags\u000atotal, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000adb/ag\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Kirstine Yung-Ting Oh M.D., Electronically signed on\u000a12/7/2007\u000a[report_end]
