VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Amend/Addenda\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, re-excisional tissue for DCIS\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000a********** Addended Report ***********\u000aResident: Anna Laury, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Alessandra F Nascimento, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. LEFT BREAST TISSUE, RE-EXCISION:\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU - Present\u000aTypes - Solid, cribriform\u000aNuclear grade - Intermediate\u000aCalcifications in DCIS - Absent\u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - Absent\u000aMicroinvasion (<0.1cm) - Absent\u000aExtent of DCIS:\u000aNumber of blocks/total - 4:21 blocks\u000aMargins (DCIS)\u000aNegative (> REMOVED_DATE cm) - Anterior, posterior, medial, lateral,\u000asuperior, inferior\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - Present\u000aOTHER FINDINGS\u000aBiopsy cavity\u000aCalcifications in benign epithelium\u000aAJCC Classification (6th edition) - Tis NX MX.\u000aSelected slides of this case have also been reviewed by Dr. Jane Brock and Dr.\u000aSusan Lester, Breast Pathology Service, who concur.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 55-year-old premenopausal woman S/P REMOVED_DATE  L breast excision\u000arevealing intermediate nuclear grade DCIS with (+) margins; ADH.\u000aOperation: L breast re-excision.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: L breast DCIS.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) Left breast tissue\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number\u000aand "#1. Left breast tissue", and consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm excision of\u000afibroadipose tissue, oriented by sutures designating superior (short suture),\u000alateral (long suture), and designated with a skin ellipse at the anterior\u000asurface (1.8 x REMOVED_DATE cm), bearing an ill-defined linear scar. The specimen has\u000abeen previously partially inked by the surgeon as follows: Anterior - blue,\u000asuperior - red, inferior - green, lateral - yellow, medial - orange. The entire\u000aposterior surface exhibits an exposed REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm biopsy cavity. The edge of\u000athis cavity posteriorly is inked in black by the prosector (black ink may not\u000arepresent true surgical margin and is for purposes of specimen orientation\u000aonly). Cut surfaces demonstrate focal fibrosis and fat necrosis along the\u000apreviously mentioned biopsy cavity wall. There is only scant dense tan/white\u000afibrous tissue laterally (25% of the specimen), no obvious residual lesional\u000atissue grossly. The entire specimen is sequentially submitted from lateral to\u000amedial following further fixation.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Entire specimen, sequentially, multi frags, ESS.\u000aDB/mmm\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Alessandra F Nascimento M.D., Electronically signed on\u000a11/18/2008\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: (11/26/08)\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for DCIS (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) NEGATIVE (1+)\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000ainvasive carcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low > 0% - < 10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor cells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but only a\u000aportion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+):Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in >10% of\u000atumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+):Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in >30% of\u000atumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aExternal controls are evaluated and show appropriate Immunoreactivity.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aAddendum #1 by Andrea L Richardson M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000aWednesday REMOVED_MONTH 26, 2008 at 03:54:26PM\u000a[report_end]
