VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: JAMES D IGLEHART M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-06-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Briana Gleason, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Marisa R Nucci, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A MASS:\u000aHyalinized fibroadenoma (1.0 cm).\u000aApocrine cysts.\u000aCore biopsy site.\u000aMargins examined microscopically.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: History of phyllodes tumor of the left breast --> left simple\u000amastectomy. Core needle of R --> "fragment of fibroadenoma".\u000aOperation: Right needle localized breast bx.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: R breast mass.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) right needle loc breast mass, stitches: short/superior, long/lateral -->\u000amammo.\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000aRad: Clip in specimen. SR/JMS.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patients name, unit number,\u000aand "right breast mass", and consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm oval fragment of\u000afibrofatty tissue with two orienting sutures: a short stitch=superior, and a\u000along stitch=lateral. The margins are inked as follows: superior/red,\u000ainferior/blue, medial/orange, lateral/yellow, anterior/green, and\u000aposterior/black. There is a needle localization wire, which enters at the\u000aposterior/lateral aspect and runs obliquely and appears to terminate in the\u000amid-portion of the parenchyma. The specimen is accompanied by two identical\u000aradiographs with a circled area of interest showing an ill-defined density and\u000aa small metal clip. There is also a pink slip from radiology, stating: "clip\u000ain specimen. SR/JMS". The specimen is serially sectioned from anterior to\u000aposterior, respectively, showing the tip of the wire embedded in the anterior\u000aaspect of the specimen. The metal clip is identified and is directly adjacent\u000ato a somewhat circumscribed REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm glistening white nodule, grossly\u000aconsistent with a fibroadenoma, which is located REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin.\u000aThere is also a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm cystic cluster in the same plane, located\u000a0.4 cm from the lateral superior margin. The mid-portion of the specimen also\u000ashows a cystic area adjacent to the nodular lesion, which has some injected\u000aradio-opaque material. The rest of the parenchyma is predominantly fatty.\u000aRepresentative sections are submitted from anterior to posterior, respectively,\u000ain cassettes REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, with all of the suspicious lesions submitted in their\u000aentirety.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: perpendicular anterior margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: tissue at tip of wire with anterior and superior margins, 1\u000aand 2 frags, respectively, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: continuous section of fibroadenoma and cystic cluster (clip\u000aremoved) and demonstrating all surrounding margins, 1 frag\u000aeach, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: continuous section of fibroadenoma and cystic cluster with\u000asurrounding margins, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: continuous section of fibroadenoma and cystic cluster with\u000asurrounding margins, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: area of radiographic injected material with surrounding\u000amargins, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: perpendicular posterior margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aNOTE: Cassettes REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID correspond to the circled area of interest\u000aon the radiograph, and approximately 30% of the entire specimen\u000ais submitted.\u000awp/lp\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Marisa R Nucci M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
