VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY(IES)\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aDILLON, DEBORAH, A, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by DILLON,DEBORAH A,M.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST, 14G ULTRASOUND-GUIDED CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR AN IRREGULAR MASS:\u000aHIGH GRADE DUCTAL CARCINOMA (see note).\u000aNOTE: This may represent invasive carcinoma, but is difficult to interpret in\u000athis small, fragmented biopsy. This lesion would be best characterized\u000afollowing excision.\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: by DILLON,DEBORAH A,M.D.\u000aImmunoperoxidase stain for p63 demonstrates absence of myoepithelium\u000asurrounding nests of tumor cells, consistent with invasive carcinoma.\u000aAppropriate immunoreactivity for p63 is seen in myoepithelium surrounding\u000aadjacent benign glands, serving as a positive internal control.\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for invasive carcinoma (block 1):\u000aEstrogen receptor NEGATIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor NEGATIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) NEGATIVE (1+)\u000aNote: Normal epithelial cells are appropriately immunoreactive for estrogen\u000aand progesterone receptors.\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000acarcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but\u000aonly a portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity\u000ain >10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Left breast - painful solid mass.\u000aOperation: 14g ultrasound\u000aOperative findings: Breast Imaging Findings: irregular\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1) 4 core samples, left breast mass.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by KUTEN,ADAM,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit\u000anumber, and "Left breast", in a peach cassette, labeled "Left", and consists\u000aof multiple, soft, fragmented, yellow to white tissue cores (0.6x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm\u000ain aggregate).\u000aMicro 1: Multi frags, ESS.\u000akks\u000aReports to: GOMBOS, EVA, C. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY(IES)\u000a[report_end]
