issue with scant additional fibrous\u000atissue and no mass lesions. The entire specimen is sequentially submitted from\u000asuperior to inferior in eight total cassettes.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Entire specimen from superior to inferior (area of interest in\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), multi frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, "#2. Retroareolar tissue, right breast", consists of three fragments of\u000afirm fibroadipose tissue, REMOVED_DATE cm, REMOVED_DATE cm, and REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest dimension.\u000aThe largest fragment is inked and sectioned and the entire specimen is\u000asubmitted. Please note: Ink may not represent true surgical margins due to\u000athe possible fragmentation of the specimen. Cut surfaces are diffusely firm,\u000atan, and hemorrhagic.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Smaller fragments, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Largest fragment, inked and sectioned, multi frags, ESS.\u000adb\u005cpab\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Lucian R Chirieac M.D., Electronically signed on\u000a2/28/2008\u000a[report_end]
