phatic/vascular invasion: none identified\u000a-perineural invasion: none identified\u000a-microcalcifications: present\u000a-margins for invasive tumor: Focally present within REMOVED_DATE cm. of anterior/\u000ainferior margin (slides 29&30) and\u000aposterior margin (slide 27)\u000a-immunohistochemical staining on prior specimen (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) was reported as:\u000aEstrogen receptor: NEGATIVE (0% of nuclei stained)\u000aProgesterone receptor: NEGATIVE (0% of nuclei stained)\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID): NEGATIVE (0) (no membrane staining)\u000aEstrogen receptor (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, Ventana Medical Systems) and/or progesterone receptor\u000a(PgR 1REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, Ventana Medical Systems) is assessed visually by quantitation of\u000athe percent of tumor cells staining.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID (4REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, Ventana Medical Systems, FDA approved) is assessed by\u000aquantitation of the percent and intensity of tumor cells staining.\u000a-immunohistochemical staining for estrogen and progesterone receptors and\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu will be performed on block 27 and reported in an addendum to\u000afollow.\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU (DCIS):\u000a-histologic type: solid and partly cribriform\u000a-histologic grade: REMOVED_DATE \u000a-size (greatest dimension): spans an area around the invasive tumor\u000a3.0 x REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000a-extent: multifocal\u000a-extensive intraductal component: not applicable\u000a-necrosis in DCIS: present, focal\u000a-microcalcifications in DCIS: present\u000a-margins for DCIS: focally present at and along a broad front\u000aprimarily involving anterior/inferior\u000amargin\u000aLYMPH NODES:\u000aAll 2 lymph nodes sampled are negative for malignancy (0/2)\u000a(0/2 sentinel lymph nodes; REMOVED_DATE non-sentinel lymph nodes).\u000aCOMMENT: The sentinel lymph node, specimen REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID&REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, is examined at multiple\u000alevels with H&E stains and immunohistochemical stains for keratin.\u000aADDITIONAL PATHOLOGIC FINDINGS:\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia, columnar cell type with calcifications.\u000aApocrine metaplasia with ductal hyperplasia and calcification, fibroadenoma,\u000aintraductal papilloma.\u000a-microcalcifications, changes consistent with prior biopsy site.\u000aPRIOR RELATED SPECIMENS REVIEWED:\u000aLeft breast, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_DATE \u000aAJCC pTNM Classification (6th Ed.): pREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID pREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID pMX\u000aThe pathologic TNM classification above is based only on the information\u000aavailable to the pathologist, and therefore may not be accurate.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by: Dennis J. Feen, M.D.\u000aClinical diagnosis & history:\u000aLeft breast carcinoma\u000aTissue-Designation:\u000aA.Sentinel lymph node - left breast\u000aB.Breast, excision with margins - left\u000aGross description:\u000aThe specimen is received in two containers.\u000aSpecimen A labeled "sentinel lymph node, left breast" is received in formalin\u000aand consists of a fat pad which contains two lymph nodes. The largest is\u000aapproximately 2 x 2 x REMOVED_DATE cm. There are two additional lymph nodes in the fat\u000apad, both approximately REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The cut surface of the small lymph\u000anodes contains brownish-tan tissue. The cut surface of the larger lymph node\u000aalso bears brownish-tan lymphoid tissue. 7X all, labeled REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aSpecimen B labeled "lumpectomy, left breast" is received in formalin and\u000aconsists of an oval mass of breast tissue, 8 x 6 x REMOVED_DATE cm. A long suture\u000adesignates the lateral margin; a short suture, the superior margin; a wire\u000aexits both from the superior and the medial margins. The superior margin is\u000ainked with blue ink. The anterior inferior margin is inked with green ink.\u000aThe cut surface of the breast in the mid to lateral portion shows a hemorrhagic\u000afirm area over 3 x 2 cm. The superior half of the specimen is sectioned from\u000alateral to medial designated REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. The inferior half of the specimen is also\u000asectioned lateral to medial designated REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. In the mid specimen, there is\u000aa REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. x REMOVED_DATE cm. span of induration, recent hemorrhage which surrounds\u000athe prior biopsy site. This induration extends grossly close to the\u000aanterior/inferior edges as well as the posterior edges.\u000aSection code: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - superior half of specimen sectioned lateral to medial\u000a15-31 - inferior half of specimen sectioned lateral to medial\u000aTotal fixation time is 28 hours.\u000aDictated by: DJF____(signature on file)____ REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a____(signature on file)____DENNIS J. FEEN, M.D. REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a[report_end]
