VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast core needle biopsy\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ALISA SUZUKI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Mariana A. Stoleru, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Jane E. Brock, M.B., B.S., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST UPPER OUTER 14 G ULTRASOUND GUIDED CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR A REMOVED_DATE \u000aCM CIRCUMSCRIBED LOBULATED MASS:\u000aFibroepithelial lesion (see Note).\u000aNOTE: The lesion shows increased cellularity and stromal overgrowth with an\u000airregular margin. No nuclear atypia or heterologous elements are present. Rare\u000astromal mitoses are seen (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID). The differential diagnosis includes a cellular\u000afibroadenoma and a low grade Phyllodes tumor. Excision is recommended for\u000adefinitive classification.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHISTORY: Right breast, probable fibroadenoma.\u000aBREAST IMAGING FINDING:\u000a1. Right: REMOVED_DATE cm, palpable and circumscribed/lobulated mass.\u000aLOCATION:\u000a1. Right: upper outer\u000aTYPE OF CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY:\u000a1. 14G Ultrasound\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000a1. 14G Ultrasound 4 core samples - Green cassette.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit\u000anumber, and "Right breast green 10 o'clock", and consists of cores of\u000afibroadipose tissue, received in a green cassette with a green lid and\u000aaggregating REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Right breast green cassette cores, multi frags, ESS.\u000aDB/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jane E. Brock M.B., B.S., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000aThursday REMOVED_MONTH 22, 2009 at 01:23:05PM\u000a[report_end]
