VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Kristin S. Ricci, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Jason L Hornick, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aSPECIMEN DESIGNATED "RIGHT BREAST MASS, EXCISION":\u000aPHYLLODES TUMOR (4.5 cm), LOW GRADE, with stromal overgrowth; see NOTE.\u000aMitoses number up to 5 per 10 HPF.\u000aNo necrosis present.\u000aTumor is present at the medial and anterior margins, is <0.1 cm from the\u000aanterior and inferior margins, and is REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin.\u000aThe superior margin is uninvolved.\u000aNOTE: The tumor shows markedly infiltrative margins into surrounding adipose\u000atissue and between parenchymal elements beyond the boundary of the main mass.\u000aThis case was also reviewed by Dr. Andrea Richardson, Breast Pathology Service,\u000awho concurs.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 22 year old woman with R breast mass, S/P R breast core bx (1/21/09)\u000arevealing fibroepithelial lesion.\u000aOperation: Exc of R breast mass.\u000aOperative Findings: Not provided.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast mass.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) right breast mass with long stitch/lateral, short stitch/superior,\u000awhipstitch/deep margin.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "#1. Right breast tissue with long stitch/lateral, short stitch/superior,\u000awhipstitch/deep margin", and consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm excision of\u000afibroadipose tissue, oriented by sutures designating superior (short stitch),\u000alateral (long stitch), and deep (whipstitch) margins. The specimen is inked\u000aper pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black;\u000aanterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange\u000a(inked by prosector). Sectioning demonstrates hemorrhagic tan lobulated cut\u000asurfaces (maximally REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest dimension), occupying greater than 90%\u000aof the total specimen, with only scant peripheral relatively uninvolved breast\u000aparenchyma (particularly superiorly). This ill-defined tan hemorrhagic lesion\u000aabuts all margins grossly. The specimen is submitted entirely.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Superior margin and lesional tissue, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Inferior margin and lesional tissue, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Anterior margin and lesional tissue, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Posterior/deep margin and lesional tissue, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin and lesional tissue, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin and lesional tissue, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Relatively uninvolved peripheral breast parenchyma (superior), multi\u000afrags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Remainder of specimen, multi frags each, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000adb/lp\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jason L Hornick M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000aTuesday REMOVED_MONTH 17, 2009 at 04:04:56PM\u000a[report_end]
