VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Amend/Addenda\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional of discrete lesion\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: MEHRA GOLSHAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000a********** Addended Report ***********\u000aResident: Agoston Tony Agoston, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Xiaohua Qian, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. RIGHT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A MASS WITH A CLIP:\u000aFibroadenoma (1.3 cm).\u000aCore biopsy site changes.\u000aB. RIGHT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A MASS:\u000aINVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA\u000aSize - REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aMultifocal - No\u000aHistologic type - Ductal\u000aHistologic grade (SBR) - III (Poor) (8 or 9 points)\u000aTubules - < 10% (3 points)\u000aNuclear grade - High (3 points)\u000aMitotic counts - 2 points\u000aEIC - Negative\u000aLVI - Present\u000aDermal LVI - Not applicable\u000aSkin invasion - Not applicable\u000aSkeletal muscle invasion - Not applicable\u000aFinal Margins (invasive)\u000aNegative (> REMOVED_DATE cm) - Superior, medial, anterior\u000aClose (0.1 to REMOVED_DATE cm) - Lateral (0.2 cm)\u000aPositive (ink on carcinoma) - Inferior (broad front)\u000aPosterior (broad front)\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aTypes - Comedo, cribriform\u000aNuclear grade - High\u000aCalcifications in DCIS - Absent\u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - Present\u000aExtent of DCIS\u000aNumber of blocks/total - REMOVED_DATE blocks\u000aDCIS is present as a minor component of the invasive carcinoma\u000aMargins (DCIS)\u000aNegative (> REMOVED_DATE cm) - Superior, anterior, medial, lateral\u000aClose (0.1 to REMOVED_DATE cm) - Inferior (0.1 cm)\u000aPositive (ink on carcinoma) - Posterior\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - Absent\u000aAJCC Classification (6th edition) - REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDc Nx MX\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER, PR, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) - Pending\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 49 y/o female with h/o left breast phyllodes tumor, malignant. Right\u000abreast abnormal mammogram x 2.\u000aOperation: Right breast wire-localized excisional biopsy x 2.\u000aOperative Findings: None specified.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast abnormal mammogram x 2.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) Right breast wire-localized incision; short - superior, long - lateral\u000afor a clip. --> mammo.\u000aB/2) Right breast wire-localized biopsy. Superior wire; long stitch - lateral\u000a--> mammo; short stitch - superior.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Mass, clip, intact wire/Call OR.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, and labeled with the patient's name and medical\u000arecord number, and consists of two parts.\u000aPart A, "#1. Right breast wire localized excision", consists of a wire\u000alocalized excision (2.5 cm SI, REMOVED_DATE cm ML, REMOVED_DATE cm AP) that is oriented with a\u000ashort suture designating superior and a long suture designating lateral. The\u000aspecimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins:\u000aposterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow;\u000amedial/orange. A wire enters the specimen from the superior/medial/anterior\u000aaspect and exits laterally. A radiograph demonstrates the specimen of mass,\u000athe wire, and associated clip. The specimen is sectioned along the wire\u000aperpendicular to the AP axis into three slices with slice #1 most anterior.\u000aSlices #2 and #3 surround the wire and clip. There is a firm white\u000awell-circumscribed mass (1.4 cm SI, REMOVED_DATE cm ML, REMOVED_DATE cm AP) that is in\u000aassociation with the wire and clip and is located in slices #2 and #3. It\u000aabuts the superior, lateral, and posterior margins, and is REMOVED_DATE cm to inferior,\u000a0.4 cm to anterior, and REMOVED_DATE cm to medial margins.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #1, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #2, 1 frag per block, ESS. Note, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID contains the mass.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #3, multi frags, ESS. Note, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID contains the mass and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aperpendicular sections to represent posterior margin.\u000aPart B, "#2. Right breast wire localized biopsy", consists of a wire localized\u000aexcision (3.4 cm SI, REMOVED_DATE cm ML, REMOVED_DATE cm AP) that is oriented with a short suture\u000adesignating superior and a long suture designating lateral. The specimen is\u000ainked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black;\u000aanterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. A\u000awire enters the specimen from the superior/medial/posterior aspect, runs along\u000athe posterior margin and exits inferiorly. A radiograph demonstrates the\u000aspecimen with mass and wire. The specimen is sectioned perpendicular to the\u000asuperior inferior axis into four slices with slice #1 designated the superior\u000amargin. There is firm white ill-defined fibrous area (1.1 cm SI, REMOVED_DATE cm ML,\u000a1.2 cm AP) in slices #2 through #4 that abuts the inferior, medial, lateral,\u000aanterior and posterior margins, and is REMOVED_DATE cm to the superior margin.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Superior margin, perpendicular section, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #2, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #3, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #4/inferior margin, multi frags, ESS.\u000aTA/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Xiaohua Qian M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a5/20/2008\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM:\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for invasive carcinoma (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) NEGATIVE (0)\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000ainvasive carcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low > 0% - < 10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor cells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but only a\u000aportion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+):Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in >10% of\u000atumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+):Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in >30% of\u000atumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aExternal controls are evaluated and show appropriate Immunoreactivity.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aAddendum #1 by Jane E. Brock M.B., B.S., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a5/22/2008\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM:\u000aA paraffin block of invasive carcinoma was sent for the genomic health oncotype\u000aDX Breast Cancer Assay with the following results (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aRecurrence Score = 15\u000aPatients with a Recurrence Score of 15 in the clinical validation study had an\u000aAverage Rate of Recurrence at 10 years of 9% (95% CI: 7% - 12%).\u000aQUANTITATIVE HORMONE RECEPTOR ANALYSIS:\u000aER Score = REMOVED_DATE Positive\u000aPR Score = REMOVED_DATE Positive\u000aAddendum #2 by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
