ight breast\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Rt breast ca\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Rt axilla sentinal node biopsy #1\u000aB/2. Rt axilla sentinel node biopsy #2\u000aC/3. Rt superior mastectomy flap\u000aD/4. Rt breast simple mastectomy (short suture/superior, long suture/lateral)\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "#1. RIGHT AXILLARY SENTINEL NODE BIOPSY" (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aLymph node, negative for tumor.\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "#2. RIGHT AXILLARY SENTINEL NODE BIOPSY" (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aLymph node, negative for tumor.\u000aOR Consultation by: NOSE,VANIA,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aResident: Agoston T. Agoston, M.D., PH.D.\u000aThe senior physician certifies that he/she personally conducted a gross and/or\u000amicroscopic examination of the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed\u000athe rapid diagnos(es) related thereto.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in four parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart A, "#1. RT axilla, sentinel node biopsy #1", consists of one tan/yellow\u000asoft tissue fragment (2.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) previously inked black and bisected,\u000aand entirely frozen as REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID through REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID remnant respectively, 1 frag in each, ESS.\u000aPart B, "#2. RT axilla, sentinel node biopsy #2, FS", consists of one\u000atan/yellow soft tissue fragment (3.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) previously inked black and\u000abisected, and entirely frozen as REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID through REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID remnant respectively, 1 frag in each, ESS.\u000aPart C, "#3. RT superior mastectomy flap", consists of an irregular fragment of\u000ayellow/tan fibroadipose tissue (3.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with an unremarkable cut\u000asurface. No skin is identified.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID through REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Multi frags each, ESS.\u000aPart D, "#4. RT breast simple mastectomy, short suture superior, long suture\u000alateral", consists of 1085-g right simple mastectomy specimen (22.5 x REMOVED_DATE x\u000a5.5 cm) with attached tan skin ellipse (19.5 x REMOVED_DATE cm) with a central focally\u000adepressed/retracted nipple (1.3 x REMOVED_DATE cm) and tan/brown areola (4.8 x REMOVED_DATE cm)\u000asurrounded by blue/green dye discoloration as consistent with prior sentinel\u000anode mapping procedure. Per surgeon, the specimen is oriented with two\u000asutures: Short equals superior, long equals lateral). There is an REMOVED_DATE cm in\u000alength curvilinear scar surrounding the inferior half of the areola. A REMOVED_DATE cm\u000amedial to the nipple is a well-healed linear scar (3.4 cm in length). An\u000aaxillary tail is not present.\u000aThe deep margin (inked black) has a smooth fascial plane. The specimen is\u000aserially sectioned from medial to lateral to exhibit two separate biopsy\u000acavities. Biopsy cavity A (3.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) is in the upper inner quadrant\u000a(approximately 1 o'clock), REMOVED_DATE cm from the nipple, with a granular pink/tan\u000afibrous wall surrounded by areas of gritty yellow/tan probable fat necrosis and\u000ahemorrhage. Biopsy cavity A comes to within REMOVED_DATE cm of the deep margin in the\u000aupper inner quadrant.\u000aA REMOVED_DATE cm inferomedial to cavity A is biopsy cavity B (2.7 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) in\u000athe central breast (approximately 3 to 4 o'clock), REMOVED_DATE cm from the deep margin\u000aand REMOVED_DATE cm from the nipple. Cavity B exhibits a granular pink/tan fibrous\u000asurface also with associated gritty yellow/tan fat necrosis and hemorrhage.\u000aBetween cavity A and cavity B, there is an area of very dense/nodular pink/tan\u000afibrous tissue (4.3 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), REMOVED_DATE cm from the deep margin and REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom the nipple. Discrete residual mass/tumor is not grossly identified.\u000aThe remainder of the specimen is composed of approximately 30 to 35%\u000adense/nodular fibrous stroma and 65% to 70% yellow/tan lobulated adipose\u000atissue.\u000aThe most lateral tissue is examined for intramammary lymph node candidates and\u000aone focally blue/green dye lymph node candidate (1.4 cm in greatest dimension)\u000ais identified.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Nipple and areola/skin with scar, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Deep margin closest to cavity A, upper inner quadrant, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID through REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Cavity A, upper inner quadrant (1 o'clock) with adjacent\u000afat necrosis/fibrous tissue, multi frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID through REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Cavity B with adjacent very dense/nodular fibrous area\u000abetween cavity A and cavity B, 1 frag in each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Deep margin, central breast, closest to cavity B, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID through REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Additional dense/nodular fibrous area between cavity A\u000aand cavity B, multi frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Dense/nodular fibrous stroma, upper outer quadrant, 3 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Dense/nodular fibrous stroma, upper inner quadrant, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Dense/nodular fibrous stroma, lower outer quadrant, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Dense/nodular fibrous stroma, lower inner quadrant, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 intramammary lymph node candidate, serially sectioned, multi\u000afrags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID through REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Remainder of cavity A, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID through REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Remainder of cavity B, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000alm\u005cpab\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Alessandra F Nascimento M.D., Electronically signed on\u000a6/18/2008\u000a[report_end]
