VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, partial mastectomy\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: MEHRA GOLSHAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-05-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Justine A Barletta, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Alessandra F Nascimento, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, SKIN-SPARING SIMPLE MASTECTOMY:\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aSYNOPSIS:\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU - Present\u000aTypes - papillary, micropapillary\u000aNuclear grade - low\u000aCalcifications in DCIS - absent\u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - absent\u000aMicroinvasion (<0.1cm) - absent\u000aExtent of DCIS\u000aNumber of blocks/total - REMOVED_DATE blocks\u000aFinal Margins (DCIS)\u000aNegative (>0.3 cm) - deep\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - absent\u000aOTHER FINDINGS\u000aBiopsy cavity\u000aPapilloma\u000aSkin with scar\u000aSkeletal muscle\u000aAJCC CLASSIFICATION (6th edition) - Tis (DCIS) pNX MX\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER/PR/HER-2) - Pending\u000aNOTE: This case was reviewed by Dr. Susan Lester, Breast Pathology Service, who\u000aconcurs.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Right breast DCIS, micropapillary type incompletely excised involving\u000aall margins.\u000aOperation: Right breast skin-sparing simple mastectomy.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast DCIS.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000a1. Right breast skin-sparing mastectomy (630 gms); short suture - superior,\u000along suture - axillary tail)\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient?s name, unit number,\u000aand "1. Right breast skin-sparing mastectomy, 630 gm, short suture - superior,\u000along suture - axillary tail", and consists of a 567-gm (pathology cutting room\u000ascale), right breast (20 [S-I] x REMOVED_DATE [M-L] x REMOVED_DATE [A-C] cm) which is oriented,\u000aper surgeon, with two (2) sutures (short = superior, long = axillary tail).\u000aThere is an adherent, small, tan, wrinkled skin ellipse (4.0 x REMOVED_DATE cm) with an\u000aeverted, tan/pink nipple (1.3 cm in diameter) and an unremarkable, tan,\u000awrinkled areola (2.7 cm in greatest dimension). REMOVED_DATE cm lateral to the nipple\u000ais a well-healed, retracted, curvilinear scar (1.8 cm in greatest dimension).\u000aThe deep margin (inked black) is predominantly a smooth, fascial plane, but\u000aexhibits scant, adherent fragments of red/brown, striated, skeletal muscle (1.2\u000ato REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest dimension). The specimen is serially sectioned from\u000amedial to lateral. Adjacent and abutting the deep surface of the\u000ainferior/medial aspect of the skin ellipse, there is a well-delineated,\u000atan/pink, predominantly smooth, fibrous biopsy cavity (4.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) in\u000athe lower/inner quadrant, which is completely open to the anterior/inferior\u000aaspect of the specimen (adjacent soft tissue - inked blue). The cavity is REMOVED_DATE \u000acm from the deep margin and exhibits multiple, focal areas of gritty,\u000ayellow/tan fat necrosis and associated, red/brown hemorrhage (0.4 to REMOVED_DATE cm in\u000agreatest dimension).\u000aThe remainder of the specimen is composed of approximately 40%, diffusely\u000adense/lumpy to nodular, white/tan, fibrous stroma and approximately 60%\u000ayellow/tan, lobulated, adipose tissue. Within the fibrous stroma are multiple,\u000afocal cyst-like spaces (ranging from REMOVED_DATE to REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest dimension),\u000awhich express friable, yellow/tan to orange/tan substance. No additional\u000amasses or lesions are identified.\u000aA definitive axillary tail is not grossly identified. The most lateral breast\u000aparenchyma is thinly sectioned and examined for intraparenchymal lymph node\u000acandidates, but none are identified.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Nipple/areola with adjacent scar, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Deep margin closest to biopsy cavity, sequentially submitted\u000afrom medial to lateral, 2 frags in each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Skin with adjacent, open, biopsy cavity, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Biopsy cavity with adjacent, dense, nodular, fibrous stroma,\u000a1 frag in each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Biopsy cavity open to adjacent, blue-inked,\u000aanterior/inferior soft tissue, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Additional biopsy cavity, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Dense, cystic, fibrous stroma, upper/outer quadrant,\u000a4 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Dense cystic fibrous stroma, upper/inner quadrant, 4 frags,\u000aRSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Dense, fibrous stroma, lower/outer quadrant, 4 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Dense, lumpy, fibrous stroma, lower/inner quadrant, 4\u000afrags,\u000aRSS.\u000aLMB/mmm\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Alessandra F Nascimento M.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Alessandra F Nascimento M.D., Electronically signed on\u000a8/16/2005\u000a[report_end]
