VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Amend/Addenda\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: BRENT T SHOJI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-05-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000a********** Addended Report ***********\u000aResident: Eric L Snyder, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Robert D Odze, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aLEFT BREAST, EXCISION WIRE-LOCALIZATION FOR CALCIFICATIONS AND A CLIP:\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aSYNOPSIS:\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aTypes - solid, cribriform\u000aNuclear grade - low to intermediate\u000aCalcifications in DCIS - present\u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - absent\u000aExtent of DCIS\u000aNumber of blocks:total - 7:18 blocks\u000aFinal Margins (DCIS)\u000aNegative (>0.3 cm) - medial, posterior, superior\u000aClose (0.1-0.3 cm) - lateral (0.2 cm, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID)\u000aVery close (<0.1 cm) - anterior and inferior (focal)\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - absent\u000aOTHER FINDINGS\u000aCore biopsy site\u000aPapilloma\u000aAJCC CLASSIFICATION (6th edition) - Tis pNx MX\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER/PR/HER-2) - pending\u000aNOTE:\u000aThe DCIS has a variety of appearances including solid and cribriform with low\u000agrade nuclei (resembling LCIS but confirmed as DCIS due to immunoreactivity\u000awith e-cadherin), solid, with intermediate grade nuclei, and cribriform with\u000aintermediate nuclei associated with mucin production and calcifications.\u000aThis case has been reviewed by Dr. S. Lester of the Breast Pathology Service.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Abnl L mammogram, CRC bx with ALH.\u000aOperation: L needle loc br bx.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnl L mammogram.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1 - left breast mass --> mammo.\u000aRADIOGRAPHY REPORT: Clip and few Ca++ in specimen. E.P. Frost, M.D.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patients name and unit number\u000aonly, and consists of a breast excision specimen measuring 5 cm medial to\u000alateral, REMOVED_DATE cm superior to inferior, and REMOVED_DATE cm anterior to posterior. The\u000aspecimen has been inked by the surgeon according to the pathology protocol for\u000athe evaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red;\u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. A wire is placed in the\u000aspecimen to localize calcifications and the previous biopsy site. The specimen\u000ais sectioned from medial to lateral. The cut surface of the specimen is a mix\u000aof yellow adipose tissue and white fibrous tissue. The biopsy site corresponds\u000aapproximately to Micros REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. No masses are seen. The specimen is entirely\u000asubmitted as follows:\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: medial-most portion of the specimen, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: remainder of specimen, 1 frag in each cassette, ESS.\u000aESN/lp\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Eric L Snyder M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Robert D Odze M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM:\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for DCIS (blocks REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) NEGATIVE (1+)\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000acarcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but only\u000aa portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in >10%\u000aof tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in\u000a>10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aAddendum #1 by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
