0avisible in the specimen entering in the anterior aspect of the superior margin\u000aand exiting from the anterior-inferior aspect of the medial margin. Two cysts\u000a(0.4 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) are filled with a thin, brown\u000afluid. The larger cyst is REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000aposterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin. The\u000asmaller cyst is REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE \u000acm from the lateral margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin. The breast\u000aparenchyma is otherwise unremarkable. The specimen is inked per pathology\u000aprotocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue;\u000asuperior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. The specimen is\u000aserially submitted. The specimen is accompanied by a radiograph showing a thin\u000ascattered calcification and two needle-localization wires within the specimen.\u000aHowever, no second needle localization wire is found inside the specimen.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Smaller cyst in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID; larger cyst in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID through REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID; micro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID,\u000asection bisected inferiorly to superiorly; 1 frag in each, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: BG-06-REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aOOB:jjk\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by William R Welch M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
