VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID SKIN- OTHER THAN CYST, TAG OR DEBRIDEMENT\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aMCKEE, PHILLIP, H., M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by MCKEE,PHILLIP H.,M.D.\u000a1) SKIN, UPPER MEDIAL LEFT BREAST:\u000aThe sections show skin with minimal subcutaneous fat. A large particle of\u000acalcified material is present in the lower reticular dermis. This does not\u000arepresent calciphylaxis. There is no evidence of vasculitis or thrombosis.\u000aMultiple levels examined.\u000a2) SKIN, MEDIAL/LATERAL LEFT BREAST:\u000aThe sections show skin and subcutaneous fat. Necrotic epidermis with\u000aunderlying regenerating epithelium is noted. There is no evidence of\u000avasculitis, thrombosis or calciphylaxis.\u000a3) CORE BIOPSY, LEFT BREAST:\u000aThe sections show multiple fragments of breast parenchyma plus fibrofatty\u000atissue. The latter shows focal necrosis, widespread infarction and\u000athrombosed vessels. A fibrin stain is positive. No evidence of\u000acalciphylaxis is seen and a von Kossa stain is negative. The features are\u000acertainly consistent with a hypercoagulable state. They could be related to\u000athe prior episode of Coumadin therapy. There is no evidence of a\u000avasculitis. Multiple levels examined.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Calciphylaxis, parathryoidectomy, failed renal transplant 1988 and\u000a2000.\u000aOperation: Excisions.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: ESRD.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Skin: 1) Upper medial left breast.\u000a2) Medial/lateral left breast.\u000a3) Core biopsy, left breast, multiple.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by KWAAN,MARY R.,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in three parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart 1, "Upper medial lt breast skin", consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm tan,\u000aunoriented elliptical skin. There is a central REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm red/tan,\u000aill-defined, hyperemic lesion which extends to multiple radial margins. The\u000aspecimen is inked, sectioned and entirely submitted.\u000aMicro 1: Skin (end), 2 frags, ESS\u000aMicro 2: Skin (lesion), 2 frags, ESS\u000aPart 2, "Medial/lateral lt breast skin", consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm tan/red,\u000airregular skin, excised to a maximum depth of REMOVED_DATE cm. The specimen is inked and\u000abisected.\u000aMicro 3: Skin, 2 frags, ESS\u000aPart 3, "Core biopsy, lt breast multiple", consits of multiple tan/red to\u000ayellow fibrofatty soft tissue cores (2.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate).\u000aMicro 4: Core biopsy, left breast, multiple frags, ESS\u000adfi\u000aReports to: MATORY, YVEDT, L. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: SKIN- OTHER THAN CYST, TAG OR DEBRIDEMENT\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SKIN- OTHER THAN CYST, TAG OR DEBRIDEMENT\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY(IES)\u000a[report_end]
