VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aWEINSTEIN, MICHAEL, H., M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by WEINSTEIN,MICHAEL H.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aRIGHT BREAST MASS AT 10:00, EXCISIONAL BIOPSY:\u000aFibrocystic changes including dense stroma, adenosis, apocrine\u000ametaplasia, microcysts, epithelial hyperplasia, and papillomatosis.\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy.\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: by WEINSTEIN,MICHAEL H.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aRe-review of selected slides from this case reveals a somewhat\u000acircumscribed area of benign pseudoangiomatous stromal hyperplasia\u000a(PASH) measuring approximately REMOVED_DATE cm on the glass slide.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Right breast mass at 10 o'clock. Ultrasound showed REMOVED_DATE cm solid\u000amass. Status post core biopsy which showed normal tissue, specific\u000amass lesion not seen. For excision.\u000aOperation: Right breast mass excision.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Right breast tissue (short suture designated superior,\u000along suture designated lateral, whipstitch on deep margin).\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by HORNICK,JASON L.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in one part, labeled with the patient's name,\u000aunit number, and "Right breast mass", and consists of an excisional biopsy of\u000abreast tissue (3.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). There are three orienting sutures\u000adesignated as above. The specimen is inked for the evaluation of margins:\u000aposterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral\u000a= yellow; medial = orange. Sections of margins are submitted for microscopic\u000aexamination. Upon sectioning, there are no areas grossly suspicious for\u000ainvasive carcinoma.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  breast, excisional biopsy, multi frags, ESS.\u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
