VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Amend/Addenda\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast core needle biopsy\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: SARA M DURFEE M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000a********** Revised Report **********\u000aResident: George Lin, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Susan Lester, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, UPPER INNER, 11 G STEREOTACTIC CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR\u000aCALCIFICATIONS:\u000aATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA, cribriform pattern, associated with\u000acalcifications (see note).\u000aNote: The differential diagnosis includes a small focus of ductal\u000acarcinoma in situ (0.1 cm) or ADH. Due to the small size, a diagnosis of\u000aADH is favored. Final classification would be made best after excision.\u000aThe report was briefly signed out and then unsigned (for less than 5\u000aminutes), to make a minor correction to the final diagnosis.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHISTORY: 46 year old woman with clustered amorphous Ca++ in the medial right\u000abreast at the level of the nipple for which stereotactic biopsy was\u000arecommended. R/O DCIS. Time in formalin - 10:10 am. History of phyllodes\u000atumor of left breast in 2005.\u000aBREAST IMAGING FINDING:\u000a1. Right: Non-palpable calcifications on mammo.\u000aLOCATION:\u000a1. Right: upper/inner.\u000aTYPE OF CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY:\u000a1. 11 G Stereotactic and vacuum-assisted.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) Right breast core tissue in two pink cassettes - A/with calcifications and\u000aB/without calcifications.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit\u000anumber, and "right breast", and consists of two pink cassettes. The first pink\u000acassette, labeled "A Ca++", contains multiple cylindrical focally hemorrhagic\u000afibrofatty soft tissues (1.3 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate). The second pink\u000acassette is labeled "B", contains multiple cylindrical focally hemorrhagic\u000afibrofatty soft tissues (1.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate). The specimen is\u000asubmitted in toto.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Contents of pink cassette labeled "A Ca++", multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Contents of pink cassette labeled "B", multi frags, ESS.\u000ajc/lp\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., on Wednesday August 19, 2009 at\u000a02:06:24PM\u000aAddendum #1 by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., on Wednesday August 19, 2009 at\u000a02:08:48PM\u000aAmendment #1 by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on Wednesday\u000aAugust 19, 2009 at 02:11:57PM\u000a[report_end]
