VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: BRENT T SHOJI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-06-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Ann K Folkins, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Xiaohua Qian, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, NEEDLE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A CLIP AND CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA (best seen in block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID; levels examined).\u000aATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA.\u000aBiopsy site changes.\u000aMicrocalcifications associated with benign epithelium (normal breast epithelium\u000aand columnar cell changes).\u000aAn immunostain for REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID showed no keratin positive cells in an area with\u000acellular stroma.\u000aThere is no carcinoma seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: History of core biopsy of atypia (calcifications).\u000aOperation: Right needle localized breast biopsy.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) right breast tissue (to mammo 4:00 pm).\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000aClip, calcs, and wire in specimen. OR called. LBT.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in a container, labeled with the patients name,\u000aunit number, and "#1 - right breast tissue - mammo", and consists of one breast\u000aexcision specimen (3.5 cm medial to lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm anterior to posterior, REMOVED_DATE \u000acm superior to inferior) with a disrupted piece of wire in the specimen\u000acontainer. The specimen is received inked by the surgeon, presumably according\u000ato the protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue;\u000asuperior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. An accompanying\u000aspecimen radiograph demonstrates the needle localization wire adjacent to a\u000aclip with surrounding calcifications in the specimen. The specimen is\u000asectioned into eight slices, from inferior to superior, and it consists of\u000aapproximately 90% fibrous tissue and 10% adipose tissue. There is a collection\u000aof gel-foam beads (1.1 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) in slices five and six, which grossly\u000aabuts the anterior margin, and is REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000athe lateral margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior\u000amargin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin. The specimen is entirely\u000asubmitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: slice one, 7 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: slice two, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: slice three, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: slice four, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: slice five with gel-beads, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: slice six with gel-beads, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: slice seven, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: slice eight, 8 frags, ESS.\u000aAF/lp\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Xiaohua Qian M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a6/13/2006\u000a[report_end]
