VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID SENTINEL LYMPH NODE\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aLESTER, SUSAN, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, EXCISION, DOUBLE WIRE-LOCALIZATION FOR TWO (2) MASSES (ONE\u000aWITH A CLIP), SENTINEL NODE BIOPSY, AND AXILLARY DISSECTION (THREE SPECIMENS):\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA, MULTIPLE FOCI, DCIS, AND NEGATIVE LYMPH NODES\u000aSYNOPSIS:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA\u000aSize - multiple foci, at least six\u000a(0.9 cm, REMOVED_DATE cm, REMOVED_DATE cm, REMOVED_DATE cm,\u000a0.4 cm, REMOVED_DATE cm)\u000aMultifocal? - yes (see note)\u000aHistologic Type - ductal\u000aHistologic Grade (SBR) - III (poor)\u000aNuclear Grade - intermediate\u000aEIC - negative\u000aLymphovascular invasion - absent\u000aDermal lymphatic invasion - absent\u000aSkin invasion - absent\u000aSkeletal muscle invasion - N/A\u000aFinal Margins (invasive)\u000aNegative (no ink on tumor) - lateral, inferior, superior, anterior,\u000aposterior\u000aPositive (ink on tumor) - medial (cautery on carcinoma; see\u000aadditional specimen)\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aTypes - solid\u000aNuclear grade - high\u000aExtent of DCIS - DCIS is present as a minor component of\u000athe invasive carcinoma\u000aFinal Margins (DCIS)\u000aNegative (>0.3 cm) - all margins\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - absent\u000aLYMPH NODES\u000aSentinel Lymph Nodes - negative (3 H&E levels examined)\u000aNumber of positive nodes - 0\u000aNumber of nodes examined - 1\u000aAxillary Lymph Nodes - negative\u000aNumber of positive nodes - 0\u000aNumber of nodes examined - 13\u000aTOTAL NODES (sentinel + axillary)- 0:14\u000aOTHER FINDINGS\u000aSkin with scar\u000aAJCC CLASSIFICATION - REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDb pREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID MX with multiple foci of\u000ainvasion\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER/PR/HER-2) - pending on more medial breast\u000acarcinoma (previously biopsied at\u000aCarney Hospital)\u000aNOTE: There are multiple separate foci of invasion each with a similar\u000ahistologic appearance. The two largest foci correspond to the radiologic\u000adensities and both were previously biopsied.\u000aThe focus in the lateral breast (previously biopsied at BWH, blocks 2 & 3) is\u000apresent in breast tissue with no evidence of a lymph node.\u000aThe second largest focus is located 3 cm away from the first (previously\u000abiopsied at Carney Hospital; blocks 7 & 8). REMOVED_DATE cm medial to this focus, and\u000aassociated with DCIS, are additional smaller foci of invasive carcinoma.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, MEDIAL AND CAUDAL SHAVE MARGIN:\u000aBreast tissue with no malignancy seen.\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for the invasive carcinoma originally biopsied at Carney\u000aHospital (block 7):\u000aEstrogen receptor NEGATIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor NEGATIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) NEGATIVE (0)\u000aNote: Normal epithelial cells are appropriately immunoreactive for estrogen\u000aand progesterone receptors.\u000aThe other focus of invasion that was biopsied at BWH (see prior core needle\u000abiopsy) was also negative for these three markers.\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000ainvasive carcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but\u000aonly a portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity\u000ain >10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: REMOVED_DATE  breast core biopsy (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), right breast shows invasive\u000aductal carcinoma, poorly differentiated. On REMOVED_DATE  left breast mastectomy\u000awith axillary contents for infiltrating ductal CA.\u000aOperative findings: Right breast wire directed excisional biopsies.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: CA of right breast.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Sentinel node.\u000a2. Right breast tissue.\u000a3. Axillary contents.\u000a4. Right breast shave margin (medial and caudal).\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "SENTINEL LYMPH NODE(S)" (FSA):\u000aLymph node negative for carcinoma.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by OH,KIRSTINE YUNG-TING,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received in four parts.\u000aPart one, received fresh in the frozen section room, labeled with the patient's\u000aname, unit number and "sentinel node", and consists of a single fragment of\u000atan/pink soft tissue within which a single lymph node (2.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) is\u000aidentified, bisected and entirely frozen as FSA.\u000aMicro 1: FSAR, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aPart two, received fresh in the frozen section room, labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number only, and consists of a portion of fibrofatty breast\u000atissue (12.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with an overlying brown skin ellipse (11.0 x\u000a2.7 cm), containing two sutures (short superior, long lateral per the surgeon)\u000aand two needle localization wires and an accompanying radiograph. Per the\u000asurgeon, the specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of\u000amargins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green;\u000alateral = yellow; medial = orange. The specimen is serially sectioned\u000arevealing two separate, irregular tan/white, granular masses. The first\u000amore lateral mass (0.9 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) is approximately REMOVED_DATE cm from the deep\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin, and 4\u000acm from the lateral margin. The second more medial mass (0.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm)\u000ais approximately 3 cm medial/anterior to the aforementioned mass, REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000athe anterior and medial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000athe superior margin and 3 cm from the deep margin. Additional tan/white,\u000arubbery, circumscribed nodules (0.3 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm, and REMOVED_DATE \u000ax REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) are present at least REMOVED_DATE cm medial to the second circumscribed\u000amass with the nearest nodule coming to within REMOVED_DATE cm of the medial margin and\u000a0.5 cm from the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin and all other\u000amargins at least REMOVED_DATE cm. Representative tumor is submitted to tumor bank for\u000aspecial studies. The sectioned specimen is re-radiographed and a clip is not\u000aidentified.\u000aThe specimen radiograph reveals two irregular densities marked by two\u000alocalization wires. There is a clip in one of the masses.\u000aMicro 2: first mass (more lateral) in relationship to deep, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro 3: additional deep margin from first mass, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 4: superior margin nearest first mass, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 5: inferior margin nearest first mass, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 6: lateral margin nearest first mass, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 7: second more medial/anterior mass to anterior/inferior margin, 1\u000afrag, RSS.\u000aMicro 8: superior/medial margin to second mass and adjacent circumscribed\u000anodules, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 9: anterior/inferior margin nearest second mass, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 10: deep margin nearest second margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 11: area of granularity adjacent to second mass, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 12: superior/medial margin nearest second mass, to include adjacent\u000acircumscribed nodule, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 13: representative skin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aPart three, received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number and\u000a"#3 axillary contents", consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm aggregate of\u000afibrofatty soft tissue, within which multiple lymph nodes (ranging from REMOVED_DATE to\u000a1.9 cm in greatest dimension).\u000aMicro 14: single whole lymph nodes, 7 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 15: single bisected lymph node, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 16: single bisected lymph node, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 17: single bisected lymph node, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 18: single bisected lymph node, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 19: single bisected lymph node, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aPart four, received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number and "#4\u000aright breast shave margin (medial and caudal)", consists of a portion of\u000afibrofatty breast tissue with two undesignated sutures (short and long). The\u000abreast is received inked orange and blue/green. The remaining uninked breast\u000atissue is arbitrarily inked red by the crossector. The specimen is serially\u000asectioned revealing approximately 85% yellow/tan lobulated fat and only 15%\u000ascant tan/white fibrous stroma. No lesions are grossly identified.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  breast tissue to include medial and caudal margins, 6 frags\u000atotal, RSS.\u000adfi\u000aReports to: CHRISTIAN, ROGER, L. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: SENTINEL LYMPH NODE\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SENTINEL LYMPH NODE\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: LYMPH NODES REGIONAL RESECTION\u000a[report_end]
