VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID SKIN- OTHER THAN CYST, TAG OR DEBRIDEMENT\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aGRANTER, SCOTT, R., M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by GRANTER,SCOTT R.,M.D.\u000a#1. SPECIMEN LABELED "LEFT TRAM FLAP":\u000aSkin with keloid formation.\u000a#2. SPECIMEN LABELED "RIGHT BREAST, SIMPLE MASTECTOMY":\u000aBenign breast tissue and skeletal muscle with no tumor seen.\u000aSkin and breast with scar.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Cancer of left breast many years ago. Mastectomy with tram and\u000asevere keloid formation. Cancer of right.\u000aOperation: Right simple mastectomy, left tram flap removal.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast cancer/keloid formation, left tram flap.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Left tram flap.\u000a2. Right breast (short/superior, long/lateral).\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by KINDELBERGER,DAVID W.,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart one, labeled "#1, left tram flap", consists of two (2) oriented skin\u000aellipse. The first measures REMOVED_DATE cm from tip to tip x REMOVED_DATE cm, excised to a\u000adepth of REMOVED_DATE cm with brown skin and marked keloid formation along the superior\u000aedge (the largest focus REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The second fragment measures 24 cm from\u000atip to tip x REMOVED_DATE cm, excised to a depth of REMOVED_DATE cm with extensive keloid\u000aformation (largest focus REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). There is a well-healed scar REMOVED_DATE cm\u000along approaching to within REMOVED_DATE cm of the nearest keloid formation. No areas\u000aof hemorrhage or grossly suspicious lesions are identified within the\u000aparenchyma. Representative sections are submitted for histological evaluation.\u000aMicro 1: area of worse keloid formation, skin ellipse, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro 2: area of greatest keloid formation on larger skin ellipse, 1 frag,\u000aRSS.\u000aMicro 3: representative section of scar on largest skin ellipse, 1 frag,\u000aRSS.\u000aPart two, labeled "#2, right breast", consists of a simple mastectomy specimen\u000ameasuring 27 cm from lateral to medial, x 20 cm superior to inferior x REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aanterior to posterior. There is a brown skin ellipse measuring REMOVED_DATE cm lateral\u000ato medial x 10 cm superior to inferior with an old healed scar, 9 cm long\u000aextending from the lateral skin tip. There is marked keloid formation along\u000athe scar. No biopsy cavity is definitively identified and no discrete masses\u000aor suspicious lesions are seen. The breast is approximately 90% adipose and\u000a30% fibrous tissue, with the fibrous tissue concentrated more at the tips.\u000aRepresentative sections are submitted for histological evaluation.\u000aMicro 4: nipple, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  scar with deep margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  upper outer quadrant, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  lower outer quadrant, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  upper inner quadrant, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  lower inner quadrant, 2 frags, RSS.\u000adk\u000aReports to: CHRISTIAN, ROGER, L. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: SKIN- OTHER THAN CYST, TAG OR DEBRIDEMENT\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY - PARTIAL OR SIMPLE\u000a[report_end]
