VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ROGER L CHRISTIAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Wai Chin Foo, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Jason L Hornick, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia, columnar cell change, apocrine cysts,\u000acalcifications associated with atypical ductal hyperplasia, and\u000acore biopsy site changes.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the\u000aentire specimen, including margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: ADH, lt breast.\u000aOperation: Wire-directed excision.\u000aOperative Findings: See Op Note.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: ADH, lt breast.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) tissue, left breast - short/superior, long/lateral --> mammo.\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000aImage of the specimen shows clip within specimen.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number\u000aand "#1. Tissue, left breast, short - superior, long - lateral", consists of a\u000a4.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm excision of fibroadipose tissue, oriented by sutures\u000adesignating superior (short suture) and lateral (long suture) margins. The\u000aspecimen is inked by the surgeon per pathology protocol for the evaluation of\u000amargins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green;\u000alateral/yellow; medial/ orange (inked by surgeon). A localizing wire enters\u000alaterally and traverses medially. The specimen is received with a radiograph\u000ademonstrating localizing wire in place within an ill-defined mass bearing a\u000agray metallic surgical clip, centrally within the specimen. Sectioning\u000ademonstrates focally hemorrhagic fibrous tissue in this area, without a\u000adefinitive palpably firm or grossly discrete mass lesion. The specimen itself\u000ais comprised of at least 75% tan/white fibrous tissue admixed with soft,\u000alobulated tan/yellow adipose tissue. There are no definitive mass, lesions or\u000aother abnormalities. The specimen is entirely sequentially submitted from\u000amedial to lateral, with perpendicular medial margin in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, perpendicular\u000alateral margin in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, and section bearing metallic surgical clip in micro\u000acassette REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Multi frags, ESS.\u000adb/lp\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jason L Hornick M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a4/3/2008\u000a[report_end]
