D_DATE \u000aincluding a REMOVED_DATE cm nipple). Located REMOVED_DATE cm from the nipple areola complex in\u000athe 10:00 direction is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm tan skin ellipse with a REMOVED_DATE cm healed\u000ascar. Deep to this ellipse is a 2 x 2 x REMOVED_DATE cm smooth-walled biopsy cavity,\u000awhich is open anteriorly and has focal yellow discoloration within the wall.\u000aThe cavity extends to REMOVED_DATE cm from the deep margin. No masses are associtaed\u000awith the cavity.\u000aLocated REMOVED_DATE cm from the nipple areola complex in the 2:00 direction is a REMOVED_DATE x\u000a0.4 cm tan skin ellipse with a REMOVED_DATE cm healed surgical scar. Deep to the\u000aellipse is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm thin-walled cavity with focal yellow\u000adiscoloration of the smooth wall. The cavity extends to within REMOVED_DATE cm of the\u000adeep margin. No masses are associated with the cavity.\u000aOne cm deep to the nipple is a ill-defined, approximately 2 cm area of\u000aapparently dilated ducts containing caseous material. The remainder of the\u000abreast parenchyma is fatty, with additional areas of dense breast parenchyma,\u000asome of which abut the biopsy cavities.\u000aThe deep margin is inked in black, and a small blue dot is placed near the\u000aupper inner quadrant biopsy cavity for identification purposes only, and a\u000asmall green dot is placed near the upper outer quadrant biopsy cavity for\u000aidentification only. The green and blue dots do not indicate margins. All\u000amargins are taken perpendicular.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Upper inner quadrant, biopsy cavity with skin and deep\u000amargin, ESS of biopsy cavity and skin ellipse.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Upper outer quadrant, biopsy cavity, skin and deep margin,\u000aESS of biopsy cavity and skin.\u000aMicro 12: Possible ducts with caseous material, deep to nipple, RSS.\u000aMicro 13: Nipple, and separate fragment of breast parenchyma located\u000abetween biopsy cavities, RSS.\u000aBecause of extensive sampling performed, with entire submission the biopsy\u000acavities and adjacent dense parenchyma, no further quadrant survey is\u000aundertaken.\u000aReports to: KAELIN, CAROLYN, MARY M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY - PARTIAL OR SIMPLE\u000a[report_end]
