 cm from the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000athe inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin and approximately 3 cm from the medial\u000amargin. The remainder of the specimen is approximately REMOVED_DATE % fibrous tissue,\u000apredominantly located in the posterior region. The parenchyma contains areas\u000aof blue cysts, consistent with fibrocystic change. The area around the clip\u000aand the area of calcifications are submitted, and approximately 50% of the\u000afibrous tissue is submitted.\u000aMicros REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Area around clip, including closest superior and\u000ainferior margins, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicros REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Area of calcifications, including lateral and posterior\u000amargins, multiple frags, ESS.\u000aMicros REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Area surrounding clip, including biopsy site and closest\u000asuperior, inferior and posterior margins, 4 frags, RSS.\u000aMicros REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Closest approach of fibrous tissue to anterior margin,\u000a2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Closest approach of fibrous tissue to medial margin,\u000a3 frags, RSS.\u000apsc/MMM\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Priscilla S Chang M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Gilbert Brodsky M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
