VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aHORNICK, JASON, L., M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by HORNICK,JASON L.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED BREAST BIOPSY FOR A CLIP:\u000aAtypical (columnar) ductal hyperplasia, adjacent to prior biopsy site.\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia.\u000aNo carcinoma is seen upon microscopic examination of the entire specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000aNOTE: This case was also reviewed by Dr. Susan Lester (Breast Pathology\u000aService), who concurs.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 72 yo postmenopausal female whose REMOVED_DATE mammograms (Norwood)\u000ademonstrate increasing R subareolar calcifications. REMOVED_DATE  core\u000abiopsy revealed columnar hyperplasia with atypia.\u000aOperation: R breast WL excision.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal R mammogram.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. R needle directed breast bx, short superior, long\u000alateral, whip stitch deep margin.\u000aRADIOLOGY: 1 clip and 1 intact wire seen.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by HAHN,HEJIN P.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number\u000aand "#1 right needle directed breast biopsy", and consists of a piece of breast\u000atissue (3.4 cm from superior to inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm from medial to lateral, and\u000a1.5 cm from anterior to posterior), that contain three sutures and a wire. The\u000aspecimen has been inked by the surgeon per pathology protocol for the\u000aevaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red;\u000ainferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. The specimen is\u000aaccompanied by a radiograph which demonstrates a clip and a wire. Serial\u000asectioning reveals that the specimen is 90% firm white fibrous tissue with\u000aareas of hemorrhage and yellow fat necrosis. The specimen is radiographed and\u000aa clip is identified. The entire specimen is submitted serially from lateral\u000ato medial.\u000aMicro 1&2: lateral margin perpendicular, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 3: slice lateral to clip, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro 4: slice with clip, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  serial slices medial to clip, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 10: medial margin, perpendicular, 4 frags, ESS.\u000ahph\u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
