_ACCESSION_IDa pREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID MX (with multiple foci of\u000ainvasion)\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER/PR/HER-2) - pending\u000aNOTE: There are approximately seven (7) scattered foci of invasive lobular\u000acarcinoma, ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE 5 cm, present in five (5) different\u000ablocks (#3,5,6,7,9). Some of the foci are up to 1 cm apart from each other.\u000aThis case was reviewed by Dr. A. Richardson (Breast Pathology Service), who\u000aconcurs.\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: by RICHARDSON,ANDREA L.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for invasive carcinoma (block 3):\u000aEstrogen receptor - POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor - POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) - NEGATIVE (0)\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000ainvasive carcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but\u000aonly a portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity\u000ain >10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: LCIS & DCIS with microinvasion for wide excision and sentinel node\u000abiopsy.\u000aOperation: L needle directed breast excision. L sentinel node bx.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: L breast CA.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000a1. Left upper outer breast tissue, short sup, long lateral, mammo.\u000a2. Left axillary sentinel lymph node #1.\u000a3. Left axillary sentinel #2.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Wires and calcs in specimen. OR called/SR.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by HAHN,HEJIN P.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in three parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart one, labeled "#1 left upper outer breast tissue, short = superior, long =\u000alateral", consists of a piece of left breast tissue (8.5 cm from medial to\u000alateral, REMOVED_DATE cm from superior to inferior, 4 cm from anterior to posterior)\u000awith two sutures and two wires. The specimen has been inked by the surgeon\u000aper pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior = black;\u000aanterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial =\u000aorange. The specimen is accompanied by a radiograph which demonstrates two\u000awires and multiple calcifications. Serial sectioning revealed an irregular\u000aarea of white, firm, fibrous tissue (6 x 4 x REMOVED_DATE cm) that abuts the medial\u000amargin, is 3 cm from the lateral margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin, abuts\u000athe inferior margin, is REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior margin and is REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000aposterior margin. No discrete lesions are grossly identified. Dense fibrous\u000atissue comprises approximately 70% of the entire specimen. The specimen is\u000asubmitted serially from medial to lateral. Approximately 40% of the entire\u000aspecimen is submitted. All fibrous tissue is submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  fibrous tissue with medial margin, multi frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  fibrous tissue, with superior margin, 3 frags RSS.\u000aMicro 6: fibrous tissue and superior and anterior margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 7: fibrous tissue with inferior margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 8: fibrous tissue with posterior margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 9: fibrous tissue with anterior margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 10: fibrous tissue with posterior margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  fibrous tissue with inferior margin, 3 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  fibrous tissue with lateral margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aPart two, labeled "#2 left axillary sentinel lymph node #1", consists of one\u000ayellow/tan fragment of fibroadipose tissue (2.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) that contains\u000aone lymph node (2 x REMOVED_DATE x 1 cm).\u000aMicro 16: 1 lymph node, bisected, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aPart three, labeled "#3 left axillary sentinel lymph node #2", consists of one\u000ayellow/tan piece of fibroadipose tissue (2.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) that contains\u000athree potential lymph nodes (largest REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest dimension).\u000aMicro 17: 1 lymph node, bisected, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 18: 2 potential lymph nodes, 1 inked blue and bisected, 3 frags, ESS.\u000ahph\u000aReports to: SWANSON, RICHARD, S. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SENTINEL LYMPH NODE\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SENTINEL LYMPH NODE\u000a[report_end]
