VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST MASTECTOMY - PARTIAL OR SIMPLE\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aWELCH, WILLIAM, ROBERT, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by WELCH,WILLIAM ROBERT,M.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST, MASTECTOMY AND AXILLARY NODE DISSECTION:\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aNEGATIVE LYMPH NODE(S)\u000aSYNOPSIS:\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - present\u000aLYMPH NODES\u000aAxillary Lymph Nodes - negative (3 H&E levels examined)\u000aNumber of positive nodes - 0\u000aNumber of nodes examined - 17\u000aTOTAL POSITIVE NODES (all specimens)- 0:17\u000aOTHER FINDINGS\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia with pagetoid spread\u000aBiopsy cavity\u000aSkin with scar\u000aSkeletal muscle\u000aPapilloma\u000aCalcifications in benign epithelium\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: History of left breast cancer with positive margins, now for left\u000amastectomy.\u000aAlso history of carcinoid SB and liver.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Left total mastectomy, short/superior, long/lateral.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by REIMANN,JULIE DYLAN REGAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "left total mastectomy, short/superior, long/lateral", and consists of a\u000a515 gram (formalin fixed weight) left total mastectomy (24 x 19 x REMOVED_DATE cm), to\u000ainclude: breast (19.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), axillary tail (8.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm),\u000atan-pink, irregular skin (10 x 4 cm), eccentric areola (2.4 x REMOVED_DATE cm), and\u000aeverted nipple (1.1 cm in diameter x REMOVED_DATE cm in length). Two sutures are present\u000a(short-superior, long-lateral). There is a well-healed linear scar (6.2 cm in\u000alength) which extends from the areola to the lateral aspect coming to within\u000a0.5 cm of the radial skin margin. The deep fascia/skeletal muscle is inked\u000ablack, and the specimen is serially sectioned. Adjacent to the skin scar,\u000awithin the right upper quadrant, is a yellow-tan, firm, fibrotic lesion (4.5 x\u000a2.8 x REMOVED_DATE cm) with fat necrosis (? biopsy cavity/previous biopsy site), which\u000acomes to within REMOVED_DATE cm of the deep margin. The remaining breast tissue\u000aconsists of approximately equal portions of yellow-tan, lobulated fat and\u000atan-white, dense, diffusely nodular, fibrous stroma with focal necrosis.\u000aMultiple tan-pink, rubbery lymph nodes are identified within the axillary tail\u000a(ranging from REMOVED_DATE to REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest dimension).\u000aRepresentative sections of tumor/normal are submitted to tumor bank for special\u000astudies.\u000aMicro 1: nipple, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 2: probable biopsy cavity in relation to skin scar, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  biopsy cavity to deep, 4 frags total, RSS.\u000aMicro 6: additional biopsy cavity, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 7: upper outer quadrant, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 8: upper inner quadrant, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 9: lower inner quadrant, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 10: lower outer quadrant, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 11: 6 single whole lymph nodes, 6 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 12: 2 single whole lymph nodes, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 13: single bisected lymph node, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 14: 3 single whole lymph nodes, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  large fatty section of lymph node, 5 frags total, ESS.\u000aMicro 17: single bisected lymph node candidate, 2 frags, ESS.\u000adfi\u000aReports to: SWANSON, RICHARD, S. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY - PARTIAL OR SIMPLE\u000a[report_end]
