e superior surface, long suture designating the lateral surface,\u000aand a whipstitch designating the deep surface. A single localization wire\u000aenters along the anterior margin and terminates within the specimen. An\u000aaccompanying specimen radiograph demonstrates a clip, which is associated with\u000athe localization wire; however, no definitive mass lesions are identified. The\u000aposterior and anterior aspects of the specimen removed and submitted as\u000aperpendicular sections. The remaining tissue is serially sectioned from\u000aposterior to anterior to reveal an area of tan/white nodularity, likely\u000arepresenting the biopsy site, which measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The core\u000abiopsy site is present REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000asuperior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin,\u000a0.8 cm from the posterior margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin. A clip\u000ais identified within the specimen and is associated with a section of tissue in\u000amicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. The specimen is entirely submitted for histologic analysis.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Posterior margin, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Anterior margin, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross sections of specimen from posterior to anterior,\u000a1 frag per cassette, ESS.\u000aNote: Micro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID contains tissue associated with clip.\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-08-REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aSRK/lp\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jane E. Brock M.B., B.S., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a10/9/2008\u000a[report_end]
