dle\u000alocalization wire, which enters along the anterior-inferior margin, and exits\u000aat the medial margin (as displayed on the accompanying radiograph). Specimen\u000ais serially sectioned to reveal a well-healed biopsy cavity (1.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm), containing a surgical clip, as displayed on the accompanying radiograph.\u000aThe cavity is REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin,\u000a0.5 cm from the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000athe anterior margin and REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin. The remaining cut\u000asurface displays 90% yellow lobulated adipose tissue and 10% white fibrous\u000atissue, with no additional discrete masses or lesions identified. The specimen\u000ais sequentially submitted in its entirety.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Anterior margin, radially, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross sections from anterior towards posterior, with\u000athe cavity in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and the surgical clip identified in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross section, bisected, with the cavity in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 1 frag\u000aeach, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross section, bisected, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross section, bisected, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross section, bisected, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross section, bisected, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross section, bisected, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross sections, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Posterior margin, radially, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000acp/ag\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jacqueline M William M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed\u000aon Monday REMOVED_MONTH 27, 2009 at 08:40:34PM\u000a[report_end]
