VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Amend/Addenda\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: BETH ANN LESNIKOSKI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-06-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000a********** Addended Report ***********\u000aResident: Travis J Hollmann, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Xiaohua Qian, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. RIGHT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZATION FOR CALCIFICATIONS AND A MASS:\u000aINVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA\u000aSYNOPSIS:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA\u000aSize - REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aMultifocal - no\u000aHistologic Type - ductal\u000aHistologic Grade (SBR) - III (poor)\u000aNuclear Grade - high\u000aEIC - negative\u000aLymphovascular invasion - present\u000aDermal lymphatic invasion - N/A\u000aSkin invasion - N/A\u000aSkeletal muscle invasion - N/A\u000aFinal Margins (invasive) -\u000aNegative (>0.3 cm) - posterior, medial, superior, lateral.\u000aClose (0.1-0.3 cm) - Inferior; see NOTE.\u000aVery close (<0.1cm from margin)- anterior (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID)\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU - absent\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - absent\u000aOTHER FINDINGS\u000aFocal adjacent foreign body giant cell reaction, dense fibrous tissue and\u000acalcifications in both benign epithelium and in invasive carcinoma.\u000aAJCC CLASSIFICATION (6th edition) - REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDc pNx MX\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER/PR/HER-2) - pending\u000aNOTE: There are tumor cells present on one of the green-colored edges on block\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, most likely due to green ink overflow to a non-margin tissue edge. The\u000acloset distance from IDC to the inferior margin is REMOVED_DATE cm (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) in this\u000aspecimen. See specimen C for additional/final inferior margin.\u000aB. LEFT ABDOMINAL SKIN TAGS:\u000aAcrochordon.\u000aC. NEW INFERIOR MARGIN:\u000aCalcifications in benign breast epithelium.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins (multiple levels examined).\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: H/O benign R breast biopsy, 2003; now with suspicious mass, R breast -\u000amass at 4:00 midway between areolar margin and periphery of breast, adjacent to\u000achest wall\u000aOperation: R breast wire loc biopsy, excision L abdominal skin tags\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right abnormal mammogram\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Right breast tissue with wire and mass (FS for mammo)\u000aB/2. Left abdominal skin tags\u000aC/3. New inferior margins\u000a(Black marks prior resection margin; green marks new true inferior margin)\u000aRADIOLOGY COMMENT:\u000aMass with ca++ and loc wire in specimen H.P.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in three parts, each labeled with the patients\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart A, "1. right breast tissue with wire in mass", consists of a single\u000awire-directed lumpectomy specimen (4.2 cm medial to lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm superior to\u000ainferior, and REMOVED_DATE cm anterior to posterior). The specimen contains a single\u000alocalization wire, in place. The specimen is inked, presumably per pathology\u000aprotocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue;\u000asuperior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. The specimen was\u000athinly sectioned from superior to inferior to reveal dense, fibrous tissue (85%\u000aof specimen) which is traversed by the localization wire. No discrete tumors,\u000anodules, or gross abnormalities are appreciated. The specimen is entirely\u000asubmitted from superior to inferior.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: superior-most fragment, slice 1, 1 frag, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: slice 2, 1 frag, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: slice 3, 1 frag, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: slice 4, 1 frag/cass, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: slice 5, 1 frag/cass, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: slice 6, 1 frag/cass, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: slice 7, 1 frag/cass, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: slice 8, 1 frag/cass, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: slice 9, inferior-most, 1 frag, ESS\u000aPart B, "2. left abdominal skin tags", consists of two fragments of\u000awhite/yellow soft tissue (0.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm each). The specimen is entirely\u000asubmitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 2 frag, ESS\u000aPart C, "3. new inferior margin, black=prior resection margin, green=new true\u000ainferior margin", consists of a single shave excision margin (pre-inked: REMOVED_DATE x\u000a1.7 x REMOVED_DATE cm). The old margin was inked black by the surgeon, and the new\u000amargin was inked green by the surgeon. The specimen is serially sectioned to\u000areveal no tumors, nodules, or gross abnormalities. The specimen is entirely\u000asubmitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: new inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE -3 frag, respectively, ESS\u000athpab\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Travis J Hollmann M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Xiaohua Qian M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a2/14/2006\u000aSurgical Addendum: (2/22/06)\u000aSPECIMEN DESIGNATED RIGHT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZATION FOR CALCIFICATIONS AND A\u000aMASS:\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for carcinoma (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) POSITIVE (2+)\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000acarcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but only\u000aa portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in >10%\u000aof tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in\u000a>10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aAddendum by Andrea L Richardson M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aAddendum #1 by Andrea L Richardson M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a2/22/2006\u000aSurgical Addendum: (2/28/06)\u000aFISH was performed by USLABS using the PathVysion HER-2 DNA Probe Kit with the\u000afollowing results (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aResult: NOT AMPLIFIED\u000aThe Her-2/cen 17 ratio = REMOVED_DATE \u000aThe average of Her-2/neu copies per cell: REMOVED_DATE \u000aThe average of cen 17 copies per cell: REMOVED_DATE \u000aThe cutoff point for assessing HER-2/neu gene amplification is a ratio of REMOVED_DATE \u000aAddendum by Deborah A Dillon M.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aAddendum #2 by Deborah A Dillon M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
