ainder of the breast tissue is predominately\u000apink/white and fibrous. Representative sections are submitted from superior to\u000ainferior.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: perpendicular superior margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: continuous section of lesion, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: lesion, 3 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: inferior breast tissue adjacent to lesion, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: perpendicular inferior margin, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aWP/ajb\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Edilberto G Bauza M.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Xiaohua Qian M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a2/21/2006\u000a[report_end]
