VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, partial mastectomy\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: KATHERINA ZABICKI CALVILLO M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Shakti Ramkissoon, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Hejin P Hahn, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. LEFT BREAST, SIMPLE MASTECTOMY:\u000aBreast tissue with papilloma, fibroadenoma (0.4 cm), and\u000amicrocalcifications in association with benign epithelium.\u000aCore biopsy site is present.\u000aSkin with no significant pathologic change.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000aB. LEFT AXILLARY SENTINEL LYMPH NODE #1, BIOPSY (including FSA):\u000aOne lymph node, negative for tumor (0:1).\u000a(3 H&E Levels examined.)\u000aC. LEFT AXILLARY SENTINEL LYMPH NODE #2, BIOPSY (including FSB):\u000aOne lymph node, negative for tumor (0:1).\u000a(3 H&E Levels examined.)\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: None specified.\u000aOperation: Lt simple mastectomy with sentinel lymph node.\u000aOperative Findings: None specified.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: None specified.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) Lt breast; short stitch - superior; long stitch - lateral.\u000aB/2) Lt axillary sentinel lymph node #1 (2245) - FS.\u000aC/3) Lt axillary sentinal lymph node #2 (725) - FS.\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "#2. LEFT AXILLARY LYMPH NODE (2245) (FSA):\u000aOne lymph node, negative for tumor.\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "#3. LT AXILLARY LYMPH NODE" (#2) (725) (FSB):\u000aLymph node, negative for carcinoma.\u000aOR Consultation by: ALESSANDRA F. NASCIMENTO, M.D.\u000aThe senior physician certifies that he/she personally conducted a gross and/or\u000amicroscopic examination of the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed\u000athe rapid diagnos(es) related thereto.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in three parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart A, "#1. Left breast, short stitch superior, long stitch lateral", consists\u000aof a 300-gram left simple mastectomy specimen (14.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with a\u000awhite/tan skin ellipse (3.5 x REMOVED_DATE cm) including an unremarkable nipple (1.0\u000acm). The specimen is oriented with a short suture designating superior and a\u000along suture designating lateral. The deep surface of the specimen is inked\u000ablack and it is serially sectioned to reveal a biopsy cavity with associated\u000ametal clip (0.7 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), present in the upper outer quadrant (micro\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID). The remainder of the breast parenchyma is composed of approximately\u000a50% unremarkable tan/white fibrous tissue and 50% yellow lobulated unremarkable\u000afibroadipose tissue. No other lesions are grossly identified in the specimen.\u000aNo lymph nodes are identified in the specimen.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Biopsy cavity, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Upper outer quadrant, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lower outer quadrant, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Upper inner quadrant, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lower inner quadrant, 2 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Representative section of nipple, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aPart B, "#2. Left axillary sentinel node #1", consists of a tan/yellow portion\u000aof lobulated fibroadipose tissue (2.4 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with a single lymph node\u000a(1.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) which is entirely submitted for intraoperative\u000aconsultation as FSA.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: FSA remnant, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Remaining fibroadipose tissue, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aPart C, "#3. Left sentinel lymph node #2", consists of a single portion of\u000atan/yellow lobulated fibroadipose tissue (1.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) which contains a\u000asingle tan/pink lymph node (0.6 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) which is entirely submitted for\u000aintraoperative consultation as FSB.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: FSB remnant, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Remaining fibroadipose tissue, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aSRK/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-08-REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Hejin P Hahn M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a1/25/2008\u000a[report_end]
