VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aKRANE, JEFFREY, FRED, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by KRANE,JEFFREY FRED,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST MASS, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISIONAL BIOPSY FOR CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia (block 3, levels examined).\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia (blocks 3 and 5; present on deeper levels).\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia.\u000aColumnar alteration of lobules with prominent snouts and secretions.\u000aCalcifications in benign epithelium.\u000aCore biopsy site.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000aNOTE:\u000aPortions of this case have been reviewed by Dr. S. Lester, Breast Pathology.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: None given.\u000aOperation: L needle-directed bresas biopsy for calcifications; core needle\u000a[illegible]\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal mammogram, L.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. L breast mass (FS), mammo (calcification), stitch marking\u000ashort/superior, long lateral.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Calcs in spec. SU/jms\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by KWAAN,MARY R.,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number\u000aand "#1 left breast mass". The specimen is accompanied by a mammogram\u000ademonstrating a wire within a portion of breast containing small\u000acalcifications. There is a pink sheet accompanying the mammogram that states\u000a"rad/calcs in specimen". The specimen consists of a yellow/tan fibrous soft\u000atissue fragment (5.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with a wire from the specimen and two\u000astitches - short superior, long lateral. The specimen is inked per pathology\u000aprotocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue;\u000asuperior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. It is 90%\u000afibrous tissue.\u000aMicro 1: anterior margin, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 2: inferior and anterior margin, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro 3: medial margin, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro 4: inferior margin, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro 5&6: specimen around needle tip, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro 7: medial margin, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro 8: lateral and inferior margin, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro 9&10: deep and superior margin, 2 frags each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  additional breast tissue, mult frags, ESS\u000amrk\u000aReports to: IGLEHART, JAMES, DIRK M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
