VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast core needle biopsy\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: SUGHRA RAZA M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Mariana A. Stoleru, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Jane E. Brock, M.B., B.S., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. RIGHT BREAST 1:00 #1 11G ULTRASOUND GUIDED CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR AN\u000aIRREGULAR REMOVED_DATE CM MASS WITH CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aColumnar cell change and normal breast epithelium with cysts and\u000amicrocalcifications (see NOTE).\u000aFocal epithelial hyperplasia.\u000aFocal dense fibrous breast tissue.\u000aFragment of cyst wall.\u000aNOTE: The histological correlate of an irregular mass is not seen. Radiologic\u000acorrelation is advised to ensure the biopsy is representative of the radiologic\u000alesion.\u000aB. RIGHT BREAST 6:30 #2 14G ULTRASOUND GUIDED CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR\u000aCALCIFICATIONS:\u000aApocrine cysts with calcifications.\u000aColumnar cell change with cysts and calcifications.\u000aSclerosing adenosis with calcifications.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHISTORY: 2 cm irregular mass R breast 1:00 positive with calcs. D. Dx: IDC\u000a(Site #1); and, R breast segmental calcifications - with focal irregularity on\u000aUS - R 6:30. D Dx - DCIS, IDC (Site #2).\u000aBREAST IMAGING FINDING:\u000a1. Right/Site #1: 2 cm, non-palpable and irregular mass on ultrasound/mammo.\u000a2. Right/Site #2: Non-palpable and calcifications on ultrasound/mammo.\u000aLOCATION:\u000a1. Right/Site #1: 1:00\u000a2. Right/Site #2: 6:30.\u000aTYPE OF CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY:\u000a1. Site #1: 11G Ultrasound and vacuum-assisted.\u000a2. Site #2: 14G Ultrasound.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) Right breast (Site #1) in white cassette - AS.\u000aB/2) Right breast (Site #2) in yellow cassette.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, in two parts, each labeled with the\u000apatient's name, unit number.\u000aPart A, "#1. Right breast white cassette", consists of multiple white/yellow\u000afibrofatty tissue cores (aggregating REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which are received in\u000atwo white cassettes. The specimens are submitted in toto.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Multi frags each, ESS.\u000aPart B, "#2. Right breast yellow", consists of multiple yellow/white focally\u000ahemorrhagic fibrofatty tissue cores (aggregating REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which are\u000areceived in a yellow cassette. The specimens are submitted in toto.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Multi frags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000acp/lp\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jane E. Brock M.B., B.S., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a10/15/2008\u000a[report_end]
