VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Amend/Addenda\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast core needle biopsy\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: LORRAINE B TWOHIG MB,BCH,BAO\u000aCASE: BS-06-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000a********** Addended Report ***********\u000aResident: Rachel E Factor, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Deborah A Dillon, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, 11:00, 14 G ULTRASOUND GUIDED CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR AN\u000aILL-DEFINED MASS:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA, poorly differentiated (modified Bloom-Richardson grade\u000aIII/III), measuring at least REMOVED_DATE cm in this limited specimen.\u000aNo lymphovascular invasion is seen in this limited specimen.\u000aNo in situ carcinoma is present in this limited specimen.\u000aNOTE: Immunohistochemical analysis for estrogen receptor, progesterone\u000areceptor, and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu will be performed and reported in an addendum.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Clinically inflammatory carcinoma right breast, focal hypoechoic mass\u000aat 11 o'clock biopsied (ill-defined).\u000aOperation: 14G ultrasound.\u000aOperative Findings: 4 x 14G cores.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Neoplastic.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Right breast tissue in white cassette.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit\u000anumber, and "right breast", and consists of multiple irregular tan/yellow to\u000awhite fibroadipose breast tissue cores (1.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate). The\u000aspecimen is received in a white cassette marked "right" and is submitted in\u000atoto.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Multi frags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000asek\u005cpab\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Deborah A Dillon M.D., Electronically signed on\u000a12/11/2006\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM:\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for invasive carcinoma (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor NEGATIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor NEGATIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) POSITIVE (2+) (HETEROGENEOUS)\u000aCytokeratin REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID POSITIVE\u000aTTF-1 NEGATIVE\u000aNote: The tumor cells are positive for the cytokeratin marker REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and are\u000anegative for TTF-1. This pattern is consistent with, but not specific for,\u000abreast carcinoma.\u000aNormal epithelial cells are not present to serve as an internal control for ER\u000aand PR. Repeat studies on the excision should be considered. The carcinoma\u000ademonstrates cytoplasmic immunoreactivity for ER, which is considered a\u000anegative result.\u000aThe block has been sent for FISH studies for REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu amplification.\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000acarcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but only\u000aa portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in >10%\u000aof tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in\u000a>10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aAddendum #1 by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM:\u000aFISH was performed by USLABS using the PathVysion HER-2 DNA Probe Kit with the\u000afollowing results (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aResult: NOT AMPLIFIED\u000aThe Her-2/cen 17 ratio = REMOVED_DATE \u000aThe average of Her-2/neu copies per cell: REMOVED_DATE \u000aThe average of cen 17 copies per cell: REMOVED_DATE \u000aThe cutoff point for assessing HER-2/neu gene amplification is a ratio of REMOVED_DATE \u000aAddendum #2 by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
