VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, mastectomy with regional lymph nodes\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Rachel L Rucker-Schmidt, M.D.\u000aPathologist: James L Connolly, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, MASTECTOMY AFTER NEO-ADJUVANT CHEMOTHERAPY AND AXILLARY\u000aDISSECTION (LEVELS 1 AND 2):\u000aSCATTERED HIGHLY ATYPICAL SINGLE CELLS, consistent with RESIDUAL TREATED\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA, poorly differentiated, present in the central and\u000aupper/outer portions of the breast as at least three foci (each measuring up to\u000a0.3 cm (blocks REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID). The cells are present over an area of\u000aapproximately REMOVED_DATE cm, in an area consistent with treated tumor bed.\u000aLymphovascular invasion is present (two foci, blocks REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, clinging type (high nuclear grade) is present in\u000athree (3) of sixteen (16) blocks (blocks REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID). No necrosis or\u000acalcifications are associated with the DCIS.\u000aDeep margin is free (>0.3 cm) of invasive and in situ carcinoma.\u000aSkin and nipple are free of tumor.\u000aScant skeletal muscle is present.\u000aNo lymph nodes are present in the additionally submitted axillary dissection\u000a(levels 1 and 2). The specimen consists of fibroadipose tissue with focal\u000achronic inflammation (entire specimen submitted).\u000aAJCC Classification (6th edition): ypREMOVED_ACCESSION_IDa NX\u000aNOTE: The pre-treatment size of the tumor was at least REMOVED_DATE cm, based on the\u000aprior core biopsy; by ultrasound, four focal irregular hypoechoic masses were\u000aseen in the distal axillary tail/axilla, deep to a region of axillary skin\u000aretraction. The largest of the masses measured REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The other masses\u000aadjacent to the largest mass measured REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm, and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm. It is not clear if these represent primary tumor masses or lymph nodes\u000ainvolved by tumor. No discrete tumor mass was visualized post-treatment by\u000aMRI. Grossly, a REMOVED_DATE cm area of fibrosis was seen in the mid to upper outer\u000aquadrant. Histologically, this corresponds to small (up to REMOVED_DATE cm) foci of\u000ascattered single tumor cells in three blocks, spanning up to REMOVED_DATE cm. This\u000acorresponds to a Miller-Payne score of 4 and a Residual Cancer Burden of REMOVED_DATE \u000a(RCB Class I).\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 57-year-old postmenopausal female status post right breast core\u000abiopsy REMOVED_DATE  revealing poorly differentiated grade II/III IC with no LVI, no\u000aCIS.\u000aOperation: R MRM.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: None given.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Right breast - short suture superior - long suture lateral and core\u000abiopsy site - bowtie at axilla.\u000aB/2. Right level 1 and 2 axillary contents.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart A, labeled "#1. Right breast short stitch superior long stitch lateral at\u000acore biopsy bowtie at axilla", consists of 1060-gram, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aright mastectomy specimen, with a suture designating superior (short suture),\u000aaxilla (bowtie), and prior biopsy site (long suture). The attached REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm tan/white skin ellipse demonstrates a central REMOVED_DATE cm areola and REMOVED_DATE cm\u000ainverted nipple, without obvious induration or other abnormality. There are no\u000askin lesions in the area of prior biopsy. The posterior surface is comprised\u000aof a smooth fascial plane, and is entirely inked black. Sectioning\u000ademonstrates tissue hemorrhage in the area of the prior biopsy site, in the\u000amid-upper/outer quadrant (maximally REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest dimension). The\u000asurrounding fibrous tissue (maximally REMOVED_DATE cm) is dense and tan/white, but is\u000awithout obvious residual tumor or other gross abnormality. Remaining specimen\u000ais comprised predominantly of soft, lobulated tan/yellow adipose tissue (at\u000aleast 80%), admixed with occasional tan/white fiber-dense tissue. There are no\u000aadditional masses, lesions or other abnormalities grossly. The axillary soft\u000atissue is palpated for lymph nodes. No obvious lymph nodes are identified,\u000ahowever, a separate axillary tail is submitted as specimen B. Sections are\u000asubmitted as follows:\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Nipple, underlying fibrous tissue, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Majority of soft tissue hemorrhage in area of prior biopsy site,\u000ato include closest deep and anterior margins, multi frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Surrounding fibrous tissue in area of prior biopsy site,\u000asequentially from lateral to medial, multi frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Upper outer quadrant (remote from site), 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lower outer quadrant (remote from site), 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Central breast, 3 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lower inner quadrant, 3 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Upper inner quadrant, 3 frags, RSS.\u000aPart B, labeled "#2. Right level 1 and 2 axillary contents", consists of a REMOVED_DATE \u000ax REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm aggregate of multiple fragments of soft, focally firm adipose\u000atissue. Tissue is dissected for lymph nodes. There are no palpably firm\u000adiscrete lymph nodes noted grossly. The entire specimen is submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Multi frags each, ESS.\u000aDB/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by James L Connolly M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
