VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aGLICKMAN, JONATHAN, NEIL, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by GLICKMAN,JONATHAN NEIL,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST, EXCISION OF A MASS:\u000aBenign breast tissue with a complex sclerosing lesion, mucinous\u000aspherulosis, and florid epithlelial hyperplasia.\u000aIntraductal papilloma with epithelial hyperplasia.\u000aFibroadenoma (0.3 cm).\u000aColumnar alteration of lobules with prominent snouts and secretions.\u000aCysts, apocrine metaplasia, and interlobular fibrosis.\u000aCore biopsy site.\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy, including margins.\u000aThe specimen is entirely submitted for histologic examination.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: None given.\u000aOperation: Left breast biopsy\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast mass\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1. Left breast mass (short stitch/posterior margin; long\u000astitch/lateral margin)\u000aRADIOLOGY: Mass is in the specimen. (ES)\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by DAVID,FRANK SAMUEL,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in one part, labeled with the patient's name,\u000aunit number and "#1. left breast mass, short stitch posterior margin, long\u000astitch lateral", and consists of a single mass of yellow/tan fibroadipose\u000atissue (5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which bears a localizing wire. The specimen is\u000aoriented with a short stitch and a long stitch designating the posterior and\u000alateral aspects, respectively. The specimen is inked by the pathologist per\u000apathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior\u000a= blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange.\u000aWithin the specimen is a firm, irregular red/tan mass (3 cm in greatest\u000adimension), which grossly approaches the posterior margin. The remainder of\u000athe specimen is grossly unremarkable. A mammogram accompanying the specimen\u000ademonstrates a localizing wire, a clip and a mass. The specimen is entirely\u000asubmitted.\u000aMicro 1: anterior, ESS\u000aMicro 2: posterior, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  remainder of specimen, anterior to posterior, ESS\u000afsd\u000aReports to: JACOBSEN, DAVID M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
