VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY(IES)\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aLESTER, SUSAN, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, UPPER INNER, 11 G STEREOTACTIC CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR A MASS\u000aWITH CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA, moderately differentiated (modified Bloom-Richardson\u000agrade II/III), measuring at least REMOVED_DATE cm in size.\u000aCARCINOMA IN SITU, solid type (intermediate nuclear grade) with central\u000anecrosis and calcifications.\u000aNote: Both the invasive and in situ carcinoma consist of discohesive\u000acells and appear "lobular" in type. However, the presence of necrosis in\u000athe CIS would be more typical of ductal carcinoma in situ.\u000aImmunohistochemical analysis for estrogen receptor, progesterone\u000areceptor, and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu will be performed and reported in an addendum.\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for invasive carcinoma (blocks 1 and 2):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) SEE NOTE\u000aNote: The carcinoma appears to have prominent but grainy membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity for REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu. Given the "lobular" type morphology of the\u000atumor, this may represent edge artifact rather than true overexpression.\u000aAdditional studies by FISH are suggested if clinically warrented.\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000ainvasive carcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but\u000aonly a portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity\u000ain >10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 68 year old female with RUI 6 mm pleomorphic calcifications\u000aassociated with a density.\u000aOperation: 11g stereotactic breast core biopsy\u000aClinical Diagnosis: R/O invasive cancer\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Right stereotactic core biopsy (2 green cassettes - "A" with\u000acalcifications and "B" no calcification)\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by SHAH,RAJSHRI N.,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit\u000anumber, and "right breast", and consists of two (2) light green cassettes. One\u000acassette is labeled "A" with calcifications and contains multiple, soft,\u000afragmented, yellow to pink tissue cores (1.3 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate).\u000aThe other cassette is labeled "B" and contains similar tissue fragments (2.5 x\u000a1.5 x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate).\u000aMicro 1: "A", multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 2: "B", multi frags, ESS.\u000ajks\u000aReports to: LEUNG, JESSICA, WAI M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY(IES)\u000a[report_end]
