VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST MASTECTOMY W/REGIONAL LYMPH NODES\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aWELCH, WILLIAM, ROBERT, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by WELCH,WILLIAM ROBERT,M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN DESIGNATED "RIGHT BREAST, MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECOTMY, FOR INVASIVE\u000aCARCINOMA":\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA WITH DUCTAL AND LOBULAR FEATURES (two adjacent masses,\u000aupper outer quadrant, REMOVED_DATE and REMOVED_DATE cm), moderately differentiated\u000a(modified B-R grade II/III).\u000aNo lymphatic/vascular invasion is identified.\u000aThe resection margin is free of invasive carcinoma.\u000aHormone receptor status will be reported in an addendum.\u000aCARCINOMA IN-SITU WITH DUCTAL AND LOBULAR FEATURES, solid and cribriform\u000atypes, intermediate nuclear grade, present in the six (6) of six (6)\u000ablocks with the invasive component, comprising 30% of the area involved\u000aby invasive carcinoma. Small foci of CARCINOMA IN-SITU and ADH are\u000apresent in the other three quadrants (blocks #8, 9, 10) and in the\u000anipple block (#11).\u000aThe resection margin is free of carcinoma in-situ.\u000aOne (1) intramammary and twelve (12) axillary lymph nodes; no tumor\u000apresent.\u000aNOTE: This tumor would be classified as AJCC REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDpREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aSPECIMEN DESIGNATED "RIGHT AXILLA, EXTRA CONTENTS, DISSECTION":\u000aFive (5) lymph nodes with no tumor identified.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: None given.\u000aOperation: Right modified radical mastectomy and TRAM-flap reconstruction\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast cancer\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1) Right breast and axillary contents\u000a2) Extra axillary contents\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by WENG,ANDREW PHILIP,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two (2) parts, each labeled with the\u000apatient's name and unit number.\u000aPart one, "right breast and axillary contents", consists of a 440g modified\u000aradical mastectomy specimen (25 x 12 x 3 cm) with a white/tan nipple-areolar\u000acomplex (3 x 3 cm) including an unremarkable REMOVED_DATE cm nipple and an attached\u000aaxillary tail (7 x 6 x 3 cm). The deep margin is a smooth fascial plane\u000awithout skeletal muscle present and is inked in black. There are two (2)\u000atan/white, firm masses (2.3 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) in the upper\u000aouter quadrant which are REMOVED_DATE cm distant from one another. Both have an\u000airregular infiltrative border. No previous biopsy cavities identified. The\u000alarger mass is located REMOVED_DATE cm from the deep margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superficial\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin, 15 cm from the medial margin, and 4 cm\u000afrom the superior margin. The smaller mass is located REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000asuperifical margin; REMOVED_DATE cm from the deep margin, 4 cm from the lateral margin,\u000a13 cm from the medial margin, 3 cm from the superior margin, and 6 cm from the\u000ainferior margin. The remainder of the breast parenchyma is approximately 60%\u000adense, white, fibrous parenchyma and 40% tan/yellow adipose tissue with\u000amultiple blue-domed cysts identified. After sectioning, the superficial margin\u000ais inked in green. After sectioning, an area of organized hemorrhage (0.7 x\u000a0.6 x REMOVED_DATE cm) consistent with previous biopsy site is identified in the larger\u000amass.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Larger (more inferior) mass, 3 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 4: Parenchyma between larger and smaller masses, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Smaller (more superior) mass, 2 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 7: Upper outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 8: Upper inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 9: Lower outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 10: Lower inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 11: Nipple, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 12: Single lymph node, 2 frag, ESS\u000aMicro 13: 2 bisected lymph nodes, 2 frag, ESS\u000aMicro 14: 2 bisected lymph nodes, 2 frag, ESS\u000aMicro 15: 2 bisected lymph nodes, 2 frag, ESS\u000aMicro 16: 3 bisected lymph nodes, 3 frag, ESS\u000aMicro 17: 2 bisected lymph nodes, 2 frag, ESS\u000aPart two, "extra axillary contents, right", consists of a single fragment of\u000atan/yellow fibroadipose tissue (4 x 4 x 2 cm).\u000aMicro 18: Single bisected lymph node, 1 frag, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  4 bisected lymph nodes, 4 frag, ESS\u000aapw\u000aReports to: HERGRUETER, CHARLES, A. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY W/REGIONAL LYMPH NODES\u000a[report_end]
