VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID:REMOVED_CASE_ID Report Status: Signed\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aDIAGNOSIS:\u000aLeft breast, localization excision:\u000aFocal invasive ductal carcinoma, moderately differentiated, two foci, REMOVED_DATE \u000acm. and REMOVED_DATE cm. in size, and multifocal microinvasive foci, present within\u000aextensive intraductal component.\u000aDuctal carcinoma in situ, intermediate grade, cribriform type with necrosis,\u000aextensive.\u000aSYNOPTIC REPORT:\u000aINVASIVE TUMOR:\u000a-histologic type: invasive ductal carcinoma\u000a-histologic grade: moderately differentiated\u000a-size (greatest dimension): REMOVED_DATE cm., REMOVED_DATE cm. and microinvasive foci within\u000aextensive ductal carcinoma in situ, confirmed with negative staining in\u000athese foci with calponin immunohistochemical stains\u000a-lymphatic/vascular invasion: none identified\u000a-perineural invasion: none identified\u000a-microcalcification in invasive tumor: none identified\u000a-margins for invasive tumor: clear (greater than REMOVED_DATE cm.).\u000a-immunohistochemical staining performed on blocks 8B and 11B reveal the\u000afollowing results for the infiltrating carcinoma:\u000aEstrogen receptor: NEGATIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor: NEGATIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID): POSITIVE (3+) for overexpression\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU (DCIS):\u000a-histologic type: cribriform type\u000a-histologic grade: intermediate\u000a-size (greatest dimension): multifocal, spanning 7 cm. (largest\u000afocus 2 cm.)\u000a-extent: focal\u000a-extensive intraductal component: present\u000a-necrosis in DCIS: present, focal\u000a-microcalcifications in DCIS: none identified\u000a-margins for DCIS: present at the cauterized superficial margin near the\u000amedial end of the specimen (slide 16A) over a broad front and\u000a0.1 to REMOVED_DATE cm. from the superficial margin in multiple foci in the mid\u000aspecimen.\u000a-immunohistochemical staining for estrogen receptor is mostly negative in\u000athe DCIS with only focal staining seen; staining for progesterone receptor\u000ais negative.\u000aADDITIONAL PATHOLOGIC FINDINGS:\u000aFibrocystic changes with sclerosing adenosis and microcalcifications; small\u000afibroadenoma.\u000aPRIOR RELATED SPECIMENS REVIEWED:\u000aLeft breast, 5 o'clock, needle core biopsies; S-04-REMOVED_CASE_ID; REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by: Daniel D. Koelliker, M.D.\u000aClinical diagnosis & history:\u000aLeft breast ductal carcinoma in situ\u000aTissue-Designation:\u000aBreast, excision with margins - left\u000aGross description:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled "left breast mass" and consists of a 66\u000agram, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. portion of fibroadipose tissue containing a\u000alocalizing wire and marked with two sutures. At one end is a long suture\u000aoriented as lateral and 90 degrees from this, in the mid portion of one side,\u000ais a short suture oriented as superior of the left breast. Based on these\u000aorientations, the wire enters the superficial surface near the mid lateral\u000aaspect. The margins throughout are grossly free of tumor and there is a small\u000aamount of apparent skeletal muscle on the deep surface. The margins throughout\u000aare inked black. The deep margin is double inked red and the superior half is\u000adouble inked blue. Cut section demonstrates a central area of rubbery,\u000awhite-tan fibrous tissue containing multiple cysts, focal yellowish, granular\u000amaterial and focal areas of linear hemorrhage. The entire specimen is\u000asubmitted as 19 equal cross sections from lateral towards medial with some\u000ahaving subdesignations A, B and/or C. 44 agg. all.\u000aDictated by: DDK____(signature on file)____DENNIS J. FEEN, M.D. REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a____(signature on file)____DANIEL D. KOELLIKER, M.D. REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a[report_end]
