reast, excision; REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_DATE \u000aNo residual invasive tumor identified.\u000aCOMMENT: Foci of sclerosing adenosis are positive for myoepithelial cells by\u000acalponin stain consistent with the diagnosis in specimen G.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by: Michael J. Ross, M.D.\u000aINTRA-OPERATIVE CONSULTATION:\u000aOPERATING ROOM CONSULTATION (TISSUE EXAMINATION):\u000a#1 Sentinel lymph node, biopsy: No gross tumor seen. Blue.\u000a#2 Sentinel lymph node, biopsy: No gross tumor seen.\u000a#3 Sentinel lymph node, biopsy: No gross tumor seen. Blue.\u000a#4 Sentinel lymph node, biopsy: No gross tumor seen. Blue.\u000a#5 Sentinel lymph node, biopsy: No gross tumor seen. Blue.\u000aMJR\u000aClinical diagnosis & history:\u000aLeft breast ductal carcinoma in situ and invasive ductal carcinoma, path; left\u000abreast carcinoma\u000aTissue-Designation:\u000aA.Sentinel lymph node - #1 left\u000aB.Sentinel lymph node - #2 left\u000aC.Sentinel lymph node - #3 left\u000aD.Sentinel lymph node - #4 left\u000aE.Sentinel lymph node - #5 left\u000aF.Lymph node, biopsy - left axillary\u000aG.Breast, excision with margins - left\u000aGross description:\u000aThe specimen is received in seven parts.\u000aSpecimen A labeled "sentinel lymph node #1 (#30)" consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm. firm blue stained lymph node. 2X.\u000aSpecimen B labeled "left sentinel node" consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. soft,\u000apink lymph node. 2X all.\u000aSpecimen C labeled "left sentinel node #3" consists of a 1 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000ablue stained firm lymph node. 2X all.\u000aSpecimen D labeled "left sentinel node #4" consists of a REMOVED_DATE x 1 x 1 cm. firm\u000ablue stained lymph node with attached tags of fat. 4X all.\u000aSpecimen E labeled "left sentinel node #5" consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000anodule of firm, blue stained tissue. 2X all.\u000aSpecimen F labeled "left axillary non-sentinel node" consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x\u000a0.4 cm. firm, pink lymph node with attached fat. 2X.\u000aSpecimen G labeled "left breast" consists of a 34 gram, REMOVED_DATE x 5 cm. up to 3 cm.\u000adeep cup-shaped portion of partly yellow adipose, partly firm, tan-pink tissue\u000awith an overlying skin ellipse measuring 5 x REMOVED_DATE cm. surmounted by a 4 cm. long\u000alinear scar. A long suture marks the lateral margin. A short suture marks the\u000asuperior margin. The posterior aspect of the specimen is a concave excision\u000acavity which is opened posteriorly for an area of 5 x 4 cm. The inner lining\u000aof the cavity is irregular. No gross tumor is identified. The\u000aanterior-superior margin is painted with blue ink. The anterior-inferior\u000amargin is painted with green ink. The deep margin, which is only seen at the\u000aperiphery of the open cavity, is painted with black ink. The specimen is\u000aserially sectioned from medial to lateral labeled REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. 35 agg. all.\u000aDictated by: MJR____(signature on file)____DANIEL D. KOELLIKER, M.D. REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a____(signature on file)____MICHAEL J. ROSS, M.D. REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a[report_end]
