 a\u000amass contained within the specimen. Serial sections reveal a rubbery tan/pink\u000anodular mass (2.2 cm) contained within the specimen and extending to within\u000aless than REMOVED_DATE cm of the resection margin. Contained within the mass is a\u000awhite/tan cystic area (0.4 cm) which extends to within REMOVED_DATE cm of the resection\u000amargin. The remainder of the tissue is yellow/orange, fatty and grossly\u000aunremarkable (approximately 40% of the specimen). The specimen is entirely\u000asubmitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: left breast, lateral, serial sections from tip of needle to\u000aproximal\u000aportion of needle, with mass contains in blocks REMOVED_DATE  14 frags,\u000aESS\u000aPart B, labeled "#2. left breast mass medial", consists of a tan/orange/yellow\u000arubbery soft tissue (2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The specimen is unoriented and the\u000aexternal surface is inked black. A needle traverses through the specimen along\u000aits short axis. An accompanying radiograph demonstrates a localization wire\u000aand mass contained within the specimen. The specimen is serially sectioned\u000afrom tip of the wire extending proximally revealing a firm white/tan mass (2.0\u000acm) which extends to within less than REMOVED_DATE cm of the resection margin. The\u000aspecimen is entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: serial sections, 5 frags, ESS\u000aPart C, labeled "#3. re-excision left breast", consists of an unoriented\u000ayellow/tan rubbery soft tissue (3 x 2 x REMOVED_DATE cm). An accompanying radiograph\u000ademonstrates a clip contained within the specimen. The external surface is\u000ainked blue and the specimen is serially sectioned along its long axis revealing\u000aa white/tan calcified cyst (0.3 cm) in an otherwise unremarkable breast. The\u000aparenchyma is comprised of approximately 40% pink/tan fibrous tissue, the\u000aremaining 60% comprised of unremarkable yellow/orange adipose tissue. A clip\u000ais not grossly identified. The specimen is fixed and decalcified and entirely\u000asubmitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: serial sections, 9 frags, ESS\u000aJhc/jl\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aMicroscopic/Diagnostic Dictation by Jey-Hsin Chen M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Alessandra F Nascimento M.D., Electronically signed on\u000a12/17/2004\u000a[report_end]
