VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Dick Guang-Iong Hwang, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: William R Welch, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aSPECIMEN DESIGNATED "LEFT BREAST TISSUE, WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISION":\u000aBenign breast tissue.\u000aCalcifications associated with benign epithelium.\u000aDuct ectasia.\u000aApocrine cysts.\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia.\u000aDense intralobular fibrosis.\u000aNecrosis and associated chronic inflammation and hemosiderin\u000adeposition, consistent with biopsy site.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 33 y/o female S/P REMOVED_DATE  L stereotactic core biopsy for\u000aarchitectural distortion revealing normal breast tissue with no calcifications\u000aseen. Excision is recommended.\u000aOperation: L breast wire localized excision.\u000aOperative Findings: None specified.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: L breast mammographic calcifications and architectural\u000adistortion.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) Left breast tissue; short suture - superior, long - lateral; whip stitch\u000aat chest wall margin; to mammo.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Ca++ and distortion at wire. RB phone OR.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number\u000aand "#1. Left breast tissue, short suture superior, long lateral, whipstitch at\u000achest wall margins", and consists of an ovoid fragment of yellow/tan\u000afibroadipose tissue (4.5 M - L x REMOVED_DATE F - I x REMOVED_DATE A - P cm) which is oriented\u000aper surgeon as follows: Short equals superior, long equals lateral, and\u000awhipstitch equals chest wall margins. The specimen is inked by the surgeon per\u000apathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black;\u000aanterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange.\u000aThe specimen is received with one needle-localization wire in place, with no\u000aclear entry point, but exiting from the inferomedial aspect of the specimen. A\u000asecond needle-localization wire is received free-floating within the specimen\u000acontainer. The specimen was previously radiographed, indicating the presence\u000aof calcification and distortion at the wires within the specimen. The specimen\u000ais serially sectioned to exhibit approximately 90% diffusely dense/lumpy\u000awhite/pink fibrous stroma and 10% yellow/tan lobulated adipose tissue with no\u000adiscrete masses or lesions grossly identified. The dense fibrous stroma\u000aextends to all six-inked margins. There are punctate areas of hemorrhage\u000ascattered throughout the specimen, particularly in the medial aspect. The\u000aspecimen is entirely sequentially submitted from medial to lateral.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin perpendicularly sectioned, multi frags in each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Central specimen sequentially submitted from medial to lateral to\u000ainclude circled areas of distortion/calcifications (predominantly corresponding\u000ato tissue in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), multi frags total, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin perpendicularly sectioned, multi frags in each,\u000aESS.\u000aLM/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-08-REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by William R Welch M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
