VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Amend/Addenda\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Sentinel Lymph Nodes(s)\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: MEHRA GOLSHAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-06-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000a********** Addended Report ***********\u000aResident: Eleanor Y. Chen, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Alessandra F Nascimento, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aLEFT BREAST, EXCISION FOR A MASS (specimen 5 of 6)(including FSA) AND SENTINEL\u000aNODE BIOPSIES (specimens 1, 2 and 3 of 6):\u000aINVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA WITH MIXED FEATURES\u000aMETASTATIC CARCINOMA TO LYMPH NODES\u000aSYNOPSIS:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA\u000aSize - REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aMultifocal - no\u000aHistologic Type - mixed ductal and lobular\u000aHistologic Grade (SBR) - III (poor)\u000aNuclear Grade - high\u000aEIC - negative\u000aLymphovascular invasion - absent\u000aDermal lymphatic invasion - N/A\u000aSkin invasion - N/A\u000aSkeletal muscle invasion - N/A\u000aFinal Margins (invasive) -\u000aNegative (>0.3 cm) - posterior, anterior, superior, medial\u000aClose (0.1-0.3 cm) - lateral (0.25cm, focal, block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID)\u000aVery close (<0.1 cm) - inferior (broad front, blocks REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID,\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID)\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU - absent\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - absent\u000aLYMPH NODES\u000aSentinel Lymph Nodes - positive (3 H&E levels examined)\u000aNumber of positive nodes - 1\u000aNumber of nodes examined - 3\u000aTOTAL POSITIVE NODES (all specimens)- 1:3\u000aSize of largest metastatic focus - REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aExtranodal extension - absent\u000aAJCC CLASSIFICATION (6th edition) - REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDc pREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID (sn) MX\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER/PR/HER-2) - pending\u000aNOTE: Immunohistochemistry performed at BWH demonstrates the following staining\u000aprofile in tumor cells:\u000aPositive - Pan-K, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID protein (focal)\u000aNegative - REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aThe immunohistochemical profile supports the above diagnosis.\u000aLEFT BREAST, FINAL ANTERIOR MARGIN (specimen 4 of 6):\u000aSkin with no tumor present.\u000aLEFT BREAST, FINAL INFERIOR MARGIN (specimen 6 of 6):\u000aBreast tissue with no tumor present.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 36-year-old female, left breast cancer on FNA. Palpable mass since\u000a6/06. Status post FNA and core biopsy.\u000aOperation:\u000a1. Left axilla sentinel node biopsy.\u000a2. Left breast lumpectomy.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast cancer.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Left axilla sentinel lymph node #1-perm.\u000aB/2. Left axilla sentinel lymph node #2-perm.\u000aC/3. Left axilla sentinel lymph node #3-perm.\u000aD/4. Left breast final anterior margin, suture on margin, perm.\u000aE/5. Left breast lumpectomy, short suture=superior, long suture=lateral, FS.\u000aF/6. Left breast final inferior margin, suture on margin-perm.\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "#5 LEFT BREAST LUMPECTOMY (FSA):\u000aPoorly differentiated carcinoma.\u000aClosest gross margin is <0.1 cm to inferior.\u000aCase discussed with Dr. Golshan.\u000aOR Consultation by: MICHELLE S. HIRSCH, M.D., PH.D.\u000aResident: QINGHONG YANG, MD, PHD, JUSTINE BARLETTA, M.D., and [illegible\u000asignature]\u000aThe senior physician certifies that he/she personally conducted a gross and/or\u000amicroscopic examination of the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed\u000athe rapid diagnos(es) related thereto.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in six parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart A, "left axilla sentinel lymph node #1", consists of a fragment of\u000afibroadipose tissue (2.7 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), including a lymph node candidate (0.4\u000ax REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The entire specimen is submitted for histological analysis.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sentinel lymph node, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Remaining fibroadipose tissue, multi frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, "left axilla sentinel lymph node #2", consists of a fragment of\u000afibroadipose tissue (1.4 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), including a lymph node candidate (1.3\u000ax REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The entire specimen is submitted for histological analysis.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 lymph node, bisected, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aPart C, "left axilla sentinel lymph node #3", consists of a fragment of\u000afibroadipose tissue (1.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), including a lymph node (1.3 x REMOVED_DATE x\u000a0.3 cm). The entire lymph node is submitted for histological analysis.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 lymph node, bisected, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aPart D, "left breast final anterior margin-suture on margin", consists of a\u000afragment of skin and underlying fibroadipose tissue (1.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm).\u000aThere is a black suture designating the margin, inked black. The entire\u000aspecimen is submitted for histological analysis.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: specimen bisected, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aPart E, "left breast lumpectomy, short suture = superior, long suture =\u000alateral", consists of a lumpectomy specimen (superior to inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm;\u000amedial to lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm; anterior to posterior, REMOVED_DATE cm) with orienting\u000asutures, short = superior, long = lateral. The specimen is inked per pathology\u000aprotocol (posterior-black, anterior-blue, superior-red, inferior-green,\u000alateral-yellow, medial-orange). There is a firm, yellow/white\u000awell-circumscribed mass (1.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) less than REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior\u000amargin. The mass is REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin, and\u000a1.5 cm from the medial margin. The remaining breast parenchyma is composed of\u000a90% adipose tissue. A representative section of the mass is submitted as FSA.\u000aThe specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral and entirely\u000asubmitted for histological analysis.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: FSA remnant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Serial sections of the specimen, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID including closest inferior\u000amargin, multi frags, ESS.\u000aPart F, "left breast final inferior margin, suture on margin-perm", consists of\u000aa fragment of fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. There is a\u000asuture designating the margin, inked blue. The entire specimen is submitted\u000afor histological analysis.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Fibroadipose tissue, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aELC/jp\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Alessandra F Nascimento M.D., Electronically signed on\u000a10/5/2006\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM:\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for invasive carcinoma (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor NEGATIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor NEGATIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) NEGATIVE (1+)\u000aNote: Normal epithelial cells are appropriately immunoreactive for estrogen\u000aand progesterone receptors.\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000acarcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but only\u000aa portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in >10%\u000aof tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in\u000a>10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aAddendum #1 by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
