VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aWELCH, WILLIAM, ROBERT, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by WELCH,WILLIAM ROBERT,M.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZATION FOR CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aTypes - cribriform, micropapillary\u000aNuclear grade - low\u000aCalcifications in DCIS - absent\u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - absent\u000aMicroinvasion (<0.1cm) - absent\u000aExtent of DCIS\u000aNumber of blocks:total - 4:11 blocks (#1-3L, #2-2L, #3-3L, #9-1L)\u000aFinal Margins (DCIS)\u000aNegative (>0.3 cm) - all\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - absent\u000aOTHER FINDINGS\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia with associated calcifications\u000aCore biopsy site\u000aAJCC CLASSIFICATION (6th edition) - Tis pNx MX\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER/PR/HER-2) - pending\u000aNOTE:\u000aThere are approximately four (4) foci of DCIS involving only a few duct spaces\u000aeach arising in a larger area of ADH and columnar alteration with atypia. The\u000acalcifications are associated with the atypical columnar alteration.\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: by RICHARDSON,ANDREA L.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for atypical columnar hyperplasia (block 2):\u000aEstrogen receptor - POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor - POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) - NEGATIVE (0)\u000aNOTE: The foci of DCIS were very focal and only present on 1 of 4 levels of\u000aof the involved original blocks. No DCIS is seen on the deeper sections used\u000afor immunostudies. However, atypical columnar hyperplasia is present on these\u000asections and the results are reported. The significance of these results is\u000auncertain.\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000acarcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but\u000aonly a portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity\u000ain >10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: ADH on core biopsy.\u000aOperation: Left needle localized biopsy.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast ca.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Left breast calcifications, long stitch/lateral,\u000ashort stitch/superior.\u000aCa++ present in specimen. C. Denison, MD.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by SPRINGER,KIMBERLEY M.,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "#1, left breast calcifications, long stitch/lateral, short\u000astitch/superior", and consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm fragment of breast\u000atissue oriented with two (2) stitches and received with a wire. Accompanying\u000athe specimen is a radiograph demonstrating a cluster of calcifications in close\u000aproximity to the wire. The cluster corresponds to a REMOVED_DATE cm stellate area of\u000afibrotic tissue that is REMOVED_DATE cm from superior, REMOVED_DATE cm from posterior, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom anterior, REMOVED_DATE cm from inferior, greater than 1 cm from lateral and medial\u000amargins. The remainder of the breast tissue is approximately 80% adipose and\u000ahas no other masses. The entire specimen is submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  fibrotic area, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  remainder of breast, REMOVED_DATE frags each, ESS.\u000akms\u000aReports to: IGLEHART, JAMES, DIRK M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
