le cylindrical\u000afibrofatty soft tissues (1.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), which are submitted in toto.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Contents of blue cassette, labeled "A. Ca++", multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Contents of blue cassette, labeled "B", multi frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, labeled "right breast site 2 anterior", and consists of two pink\u000acassettes, one labeled "A. Ca++", containing multiple cylindrical fibrofatty\u000asoft tissues (1.3 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate). The second pink cassette is\u000alabeled "B", and contains multiple cylindrical fibrofatty soft tissues (1.5 x\u000a1.0 x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate). The specimen is submitted in toto.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Contents of pink cassette, labeled "A. Ca++", multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Contents of pink cassette, labeled "B", multi frags, ESS.\u000aJenC/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000aWednesday REMOVED_MONTH 08, 2009 at 08:39:58PM\u000a[report_end]
