east cyst wall", consists of an irregular, ragged pink-white\u000asoft tissue (1.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) which is bisected to exhibit a tan-pink\u000amucinous cut surface.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 2 frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, "Left breast mass", consists of an irregular, hemorrhagic fibrofatty\u000asoft tissue (1.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) which is inked and serially sectioned to\u000aexhibit an unremarkable fibrous cut surface.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 5 frags, ESS.\u000aPart C, "Additional left breast cyst wall", consists of an irregular\u000ahemorrhagic fibromembranous soft tissue (1.6 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) which exhibits a\u000apreviously disrupted ? cyst which is tan-pink and semi-translucent. The\u000aspecimen is serially sectioned to exhibit a pink-red cut surface.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Multi frags total, ESS.\u000aPart D, "Left breast mass, posterior cyst wall", consists of an irregular\u000atan-pink fibrofatty soft tissue (0.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) which is inked and\u000abisected to exhibit a tan-pink surface.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 2 frags, ESS.\u000aJenC/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-08-REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Robert D Odze M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
