0% of tumor cells but\u000aonly a portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity\u000ain >10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: New left upper inner 7 mm mass with adjacent calcifications\u000ain 75 year-old - Ca++ not difinitively in mass.\u000aOperation: 11 G Stereotactic.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Left breast core sample in blue cassttes, "A" = Ca++.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by YANG,TAO,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit\u000anumber, and "Left breast", and consists of two (2) blue cassettes. One\u000acassette is labeled "A Ca++" and contains multiple, soft, fragmented, yellow\u000ato white tissue cores (1.6 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate). The other blue\u000acassette is labeled "B" and contains similar tissue fragments (2.3 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm in aggregate).\u000aMicro 1: "A Ca++", multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 2: "B", multi frags, ESS.\u000adf\u000aReports to: MEYER, JACK, E. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY(IES)\u000a[report_end]
