ration: L breast needle loc partial mastectomy, (L) SLN bx.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: L breast invasive ductal CA.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. SLN - left.\u000a2. L breast tissue.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Mammography - clip is seen in specimen. lf\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "1) SENTINEL LYMPH NODE (LT)" (FSA):\u000aLymph node; no tumor present.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by CHEN,JEY-HSIN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in the Frozen Section Room, in two parts, each\u000alabeled with the patient's name and unit number.\u000aPart one, labeled "#1 sentinel lymph node (left)", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm\u000atan/brown lymph node which is entirely submitted for frozen section analysis\u000alabeled as FSA and is entirely submitted.\u000aMicro 1: FSA remnant, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aPart two, labeled "#2 left breast tissue", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm tan/yellow\u000afatty tissue with a wire in place and an accompanying radiograph that confirms\u000athe wire in the specimen. The specimen is previously inked by the surgeon per\u000apathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior\u000a= blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange.\u000aThe specimen is sectioned in the Frozen Section Room to reveal a tan/white\u000afirm nodule (0.7 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), located within REMOVED_DATE cm of the inferior\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE \u000acm from the anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin and REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000athe medial margin. An FNA of the nodule is submitted to the Breast Bank and\u000atouch preps of the nodule is submitted to the Breast Bank. The specimen is\u000aserially sectioned from lateral to medial and is entirely submitted.\u000aMicro 2: tumor in relation to superior and posterior margins, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  lateral-most slice, perpendicular, 11 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  slice #2, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  slice #3, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 12&13: slice #4, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 14&15: slice #5, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 16&17: slice #6, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 18&19: slice #7, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 20&21: slice #8, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 22&23: slice #9, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  medial-most slice, perpendicular, 9 frags, ESS.\u000ajhc\u000aReports to: LOCKHART, DIANE, CATHERINE M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: SENTINEL LYMPH NODE\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
