VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aNUCCI, MARISA, ROSE, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by NUCCI,MARISA ROSE,M.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR CALCIFICATIONS AND TWO CLIPS:\u000aSUMMARY DIAGNOSIS:\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU.\u000aSYNOPSIS:\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aTypes - Solid, cribriform, micropapillary,\u000aapocrine\u000aNuclear grade - Intermediate\u000aCalcifications in DCIS - Present\u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - Present\u000aMicroinvasion (<0.1cm) - Absent\u000aExtent of DCIS\u000aNumber of blocks/total: REMOVED_DATE blocks\u000aFinal Margins (DCIS)\u000aClose (0.3 cm) posterior (focal; block 5)\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - Absent\u000aOTHER FINDINGS\u000aSclerosing adenosis.\u000aCysts.\u000aCalcifications in benign epithelium.\u000aCore biopsy site.\u000aAJCC CLASSIFICATION - Tis pNX MX\u000aNOTE: DCIS is present adjacent to both clips and involving tissue between the\u000aclips. DCIS is also present associated with the "additional area of\u000acalcification at 3 o'clock".\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: History of core biopsy of nodule showing ADH in (marker) and calcs\u000awith DCIS (clip); (both LUOQ) also additional area of calcs not\u000apreviously biopsied at 3 o'clock left lateral breast.\u000aNone given.\u000aOperation: Left wire localized excision.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal mammogram.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1. Left breast tissue, long lateral short superior\u000aNOTE: Specimen should contain 2 wires, 2 clips and additional\u000aareas of calcifications spearate from clip.\u000ashort = superior, long = lateral, inked per path protocol.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Both clips, the calcification and both wires are in the\u000aspecimen. OR called at 1:00 LBT\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by SHEN,JIAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in one part, la