ed; inferior/green; lateral/yellow;\u000amedial/orange. The specimen is received with a needle localization wire\u000aentering the medial/posterior aspect of the specimen and exiting through the\u000alateral/anterior aspect of the specimen. The specimen radiograph demonstrates\u000athe localization wire, a biopsy clip (marked by radiology), and two areas of\u000acalcifications (marked by radiology). The anterior/inferior aspect of the\u000aspecimen exhibits an area of disruption (2.5 x REMOVED_DATE cm) and is focally loosely\u000aadherent to the body of the specimen. The specimen is serially sectioned from\u000amedial to lateral to exhibit a hemorrhagic area (1.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm),\u000aconsistent with a previous biopsy site; this area contains a metallic clip,\u000aabuts the superior margin, and is located REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE \u000acm from the medial and posterior margins, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior and\u000alateral margins. The breast parenchyma surrounding the needle localization\u000awire is focally cystic. The remaining breast parenchyma consists of 98% dense\u000awhite fibrous tissue to 2% yellow lobulated adipose tissue. The specimen is\u000asubmitted in its entirety.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Perpendicular medial margin, 2 frags in each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Body, sequentially submitted from medial to lateral to include\u000abiopsy cavity (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), area of clip (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) and cystic parenchyma surrounding the\u000aneedle localization wire (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), multi frags total, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Perpendicular lateral margin, 2 frags in each, ESS.\u000ajc/lp\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Christopher D. M. Fletcher M.D. FRCPath, Electronically\u000asigned on Friday REMOVED_MONTH 04, 2009 at 07:28:32PM\u000a[report_end]
