VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aGLICKMAN, JONATHAN, NEIL, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by GLICKMAN,JONATHAN NEIL,M.D.,PH.D.\u000a1) RIGHT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED EZCISION FOR A MASS:\u000aMultiple scattered foci of atypical ductal hyperplasia,\u000awith associated calcifications.\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia, apocrine metaplasia, columnar alteration of\u000alobules with prominent snouts and secretions, and cysts,\u000aMedial arterial calcifications.\u000aCore biopsy site.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000a(Levels examined.)\u000a2) RIGHT BREAST, DEEP MARGIN:\u000aBenign breast tissue with medial arterial calcifications.\u000aOne (1) lymph node with no tumor present.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000aNOTE:\u000aCase reviewed by Dr. A. Richardson, Breast Pathology, who concurs.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Screening mammo - vague density right breast. Core bx - ADH.\u000aOperation: Right breast needle localiztion bx.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal mammo.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Right breast tissue, short/superior, long lateral.\u000a2. Right breast tissue, deep, short/superior, long/lateral.\u000aRadiology:\u000aClip and wire in specimen. (JM)\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by HAHN,HEJIN P.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart one, labeled "#1, right breast tissue, short superior, long lateral",\u000aconsists of a piece of breast tissue (8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) that has two (2)\u000aorienting sutures. The specimen was inked by the surgeon per pathology\u000aprotocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue;\u000asuperior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. Attached\u000ato the breast tissue is a tan-white skin ellipse (4.6 x REMOVED_DATE cm) on the\u000aanterior margin. The specimen contains a hookwire. The specimen is\u000aaccompanyied by a radiograph, which demonstrates a hookwire, a clip and an\u000aill-defined opacity. The specimen is serially sectioned and radiograph. The\u000aclip is identified within an area of firm white fibrous tissue that contains\u000athe prior core biopsy site. This fibrous tissue comprises approximately 30% of\u000athe specimen. Representative sections are submitted. All fibrous tissue is\u000aentirely submitted. Approximately 50% of the entire specimen is submitted.\u000aMicro 1,2: section anterior to clip area, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 3,4: section with clip, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  sections posterior to clip, 6 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  lateral and posterior margins, perpendicular, 5 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  anterior margin including skin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aPart two, labeled "#2, right breast tissue, deep, short/superior,\u000along/lateral", consists of a piece of breast tissue (5.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with\u000atwo (2) orienting sutures. The specimen has been inked by the surgeon. The\u000asuperior surface is red, the inferior green, the lateral yellow, and no inked\u000a(orange) is seen for medial. There is an uninked surface anteriorly, which\u000alikely represents the old margin. Serial sectioning reveals that the specimen\u000ais greater than 99% yellow-tan grossly unremarkable adipose tissue.\u000aApproximately 50% of the specimen is submitted. This specimen is submitted\u000aserially from superior to inferior.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  superior margin, perpendicular, 3 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  lateral margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  posterior margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  inferior margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000ahph\u000aReports to: CHRISTIAN, ROGER, L. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
