VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast core needle biopsy\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: MITRA NOROOZIAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-06-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Priscilla S Chang, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Susan Lester, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aLEFT BREAST, UPPER CENTRAL, 11 G STEREOTACTIC CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR\u000aCALCIFICATIONS:\u000aDetached fragments of mucin with calcifications associated with rare epithelial\u000acells (best seen in additional deeper levels examined) (see note).\u000aFragments of normal breast tissue.\u000aNote: The calcifications are present in fragments of mucin detached from the\u000acores of breast tissue. The type of lesion associated with the mucin\u000aproduction cannot be determined in this specimen, but could include both benign\u000aand malignant entities. Radiologic correlation is suggested.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 41-year-old female with clustered three punctate calcs in left\u000aupper central breast.\u000aOperation: An 11-G stereotactic.\u000aOperative Findings: Positive calcs, without difficulties.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Benign - rule out DCIS.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) Calcs seen in specimen - "A" cassette, others in "B" orange cassette.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aReceived in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "Left\u000abreast", are two (2) orange cassettes. First orange cassette is labeled "A CA\u000a++" and contains multiple, yellow/white fibrofatty soft tissue cores (1.3 x REMOVED_DATE \u000ax REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate). Second orange cassette is labeled "B" and contains\u000asimilar tissue fragments (2.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate).\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Cassette A contents "CA ++", multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Cassette B contents, multi frags, ESS.\u000aLMB/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a8/28/2006\u000a[report_end]
