VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ROGER L CHRISTIAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-06-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Michael H Roh, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Lucian R Chirieac, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aLEFT BREAST EXCISION, WIRE LOCALIZATION FOR A FOCAL DENSITY AND A CLIP:\u000aBenign breast tissue with fibroadenomatoid change, calcifications in benign\u000aepithelium, and columnar cell change.\u000aThe area marked by the clip is a core biopsy site.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Area of micro calcs, left breast core biopsy - inconclusive.\u000aOperation: Wire-directed excision.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Micro calcs - left breast.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Left breast tissue, short stitch superior, long stitch lateral.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Clip and focal density (likely hematoma) in specimen.\u000a---C. Denison.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "#1. Left breast tissue, short superior, long lateral", and consists of REMOVED_DATE \u000ax REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm excision of fibroadipose tissue, oriented by sutures designating\u000asuperior (short suture) and lateral (long suture) margins. The specimen is\u000ainked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black;\u000aanterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange\u000a(inked by surgeon). A localizing wire enters the superior aspect of the\u000aspecimen and enters inferior/posteriorly. Specimen is received along with\u000alocalizing wire demonstrating a localizing clip and focal density adjacent to\u000athe wire. Sectioning of this area demonstrates circumscribed firm tan/white\u000anodule (1.3 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), abutting the lateral and posterior margins and\u000aapproaching within REMOVED_DATE cm of the closest inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the closest\u000aanterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the closest medial margin, and remote (greater than\u000a1.5 cm) from the nearest superior margin. Remaining specimen is comprised of\u000atan/white fibrinous tissue (25% to 30%), without definitive additional lesions\u000aor other abnormalities. There is focal hemorrhage along the localizing wire\u000atract, but the tan/yellow adipose tissue is otherwise unremarkable.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Inferior margin, perpendicular sections, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Mass on closest lateral, and posterior margins,\u000a3 frags total, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Closest medial, anterior margins, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Additional fibrous tissue, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Superior margin, sectioned, multi frags, ESS.\u000aNote: Approximately 50% of the tissue has been submitted, to include entire\u000amass and closest margins. The specimen will be submitted following further\u000afixation.\u000aDB/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(se)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Lucian R Chirieac M.D., Electronically signed on\u000a11/30/2006\u000a[report_end]
