VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Elgida Radoncipi, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Alessandra F Nascimento, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. RIGHT BREAST TISSUE, EXCISION:\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU and columnar cell change.\u000aBiopsy site changes.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 41-year-old premenopausal female with a family history of breast\u000acancer in her mother (62). Patient noted a right breast mass. REMOVED_DATE \u000amammogram demonstrated an area of focal asymmetry, REMOVED_DATE cm by ultrasound.\u000a7/8/09 core biopsy revealed fibrous breast tissue without features of a mass\u000aforming lesion. The patient prefers excision.\u000aOperation: excision of a right breast mass.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast mass.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Right breast tissue. Short suture superior, long suture lateral,\u000awhipstitch on deep margin.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "right breast tissue short suture superior long lateral whip stitch deep\u000amargin", and consists of a tan/yellow lobulated portion of fibroadipose breast\u000atissue (4.0 cm medial to lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm superior to inferior, and REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aanterior to posterior) with a short suture designating the superior margin,\u000along suture designating the lateral margin, and whip stitch designating the\u000aposterior/deep margin. There is no needle localization wire in place and the\u000aspecimen is not received with a radiograph. The specimen is inked per\u000apathology protocol (superior red, inferior green, medial orange, lateral\u000ayellow, anterior blue, and posterior black) and serially sectioned from medial\u000ato lateral. The cut surface consists primarily of dense white fibrous tissue\u000aconstituting greater than 95% of the breast parenchyma. No discrete lesions,\u000aprevious biopsy, or areas of disruption are grossly identified. The specimen\u000ais submitted in its entirety.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Medial margin, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross sections medial to lateral, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral margin, 3 frags, ESS.\u000asek/elw\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Alessandra F Nascimento M.D., Electronically signed on\u000aWednesday August 26, 2009 at 10:24:43AM\u000a[report_end]
