PTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart A, "#1. Sentinel node #1", consists of an irregular fragment of\u000ayellow/tan, lobulated adipose tissue (2.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) which is dissected to\u000aexhibit one pink/tan lymph node candidate (0.5 cm in greatest dimension).\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: One lymph node candidate, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aPart B, "#2. Left breast tissue with wire", and consists of an ovoid fragment\u000aof yellow/tan to tan/pink breast tissue (4.3 S-I x REMOVED_DATE M-L x REMOVED_DATE A-P cm). The\u000aspecimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins:\u000aposterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow;\u000amedial/orange. There is one needle localization wire in place, which enters\u000athe superior aspect of the specimen and exits the posteromedial aspect of the\u000aspecimen. The specimen was previously radiographed and shows a clip and a\u000airregular density within the specimen. The specimen is serially sectioned from\u000asuperior to inferior (slice #1 equals superior, slice #9 equals inferior). In\u000aslices #3-#5, there is an irregular, poorly-delineated, indurated, pink/white\u000amass (1.6 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The mass grossly extends to the posterior margin,\u000a0.1 cm from the anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000alateral margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior\u000amargin. The needle localization wire traverses the mass, and the clip is\u000aidentified within the mass (slice #3). The remainder of the specimen is\u000acomposed of approximately 85% yellow/tan, lobulated adipose tissue and 15%\u000adense white/tan, fibrous stroma with no additional discrete lesions identified.\u000aRepresentative sections to include the mass are submitted for histologic\u000aexamination. Approximately 80% of the specimen is submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slices 1 and 2, respectively, to include superior margin\u000aclosest to mass, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slices REMOVED_DATE  respectively, (slice 5 bisected) to include mass\u000ain entirety (in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) with closest anterior, posterior,\u000amedial, and lateral margins, 1 frag in each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slices REMOVED_DATE  dense fibrous stroma away from mass with\u000ainferior margin closest to mass, 2 frags in each, RSS.\u000aLMB/mmm\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Alessandra F Nascimento M.D., Electronically signed on\u000a8/18/2006\u000a[report_end]
