VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ELOF ERIKSSON M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Scott Lovitch, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Robert D Odze, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. LEFT BREAST EXCISION FOR A MASS:\u000aLOW GRADE PHYLLODES TUMOR, (2.9 cm)(see NOTE).\u000aFocal stromal overgrowth is present.\u000aMitoses number up to REMOVED_DATE HPF\u000aNo heterologous elements are present.\u000aThe inked margins of excision are negative, however tumor is present < REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom inked margins (including medial margin).\u000aNOTE: The tumor shows focal stromal overgrowth and although it is predominantly\u000awell circumscribed, has rare foci suggestive of infiltrative growth at the\u000amargin. In combination with the mitotic rate (5/10 HPF), the tumor is best\u000aconsidered a low grade phyllodes tumor. DR S. Lester and DR J Brock (Breast\u000aPathology) have reviewed selected slides and concur with the diagnosis.\u000aB. LEFT BREAST TISSUE (54G):\u000aBenign breast tissue with apocrine metaplasia.\u000aSkin with no significant pathologic change.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: History of slowly growing lump in upper, outer quadrant left breast.\u000aNeedle biopsy at N-W Hospital - fibroadenoma. Removal today with small\u000areduction.\u000aOperation: Fibroadenoma.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: None given.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Left breast tissue, fibroadenoma - stitch medial.\u000aB/2. left breast tissue.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart A, "#1. Left breast fibroadenoma", consists of an ovoid fragment of\u000ayellow/tan to pink/tan fibroadipose tissue (5.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) which is\u000apartially oriented per surgeon with one stitch designating "medial" No further\u000aorientation is provided. The sutured/medial half of the specimen is inked\u000aorange per prosector, and the opposite non-sutured half of the specimen is\u000ainked blue. The specimen is serially sectioned to exhibit a\u000awell-circumscribed, bulging, homogeneous, finely cystic rubbery mass (2.9 x REMOVED_DATE \u000ax REMOVED_DATE cm) which grossly extends to the orange-inked medial margin and is REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom the blue-inked opposite margin. The mass occupies approximately 60% of\u000athe cut surface. The remaining cut surface is composed of approximately 80%\u000adense focally cystic white/tan fibrous stroma and 20% yellow/tan lobulated\u000aadipose tissue. No additional lesions are grossly identified.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID through REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Representative sections of mass to margins, 1 frag in\u000aeach, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Uninvolved parenchyma away from mass with margins, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aPlease note: Approximately 50% of the specimen (to include approximately 60%\u000aof the mass) is submitted.\u000aPart B, "#2. Left breast tissue", consists of a 54-gram specimen consisting of\u000amultiple fragments of yellow/tan fibroadipose tissue admixed with tan wrinkled\u000askin (10.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate). The fragments are sectioned to\u000aexhibit approximately 20% focally dense white/tan fibrous stroma and 80%\u000ayellow/tan lobulated adipose tissue with no discrete masses or lesions grossly\u000aidentified.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID & REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Skin and focally dense fibrous stroma, multi frags in each, RSS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-08-REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000alm/ag\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Robert D Odze M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
