VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ELOF ERIKSSON M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Kevin Golden, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Hejin P Hahn, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aLEFT BREAST, RE-EXCISION:\u000aBenign breast tissue with biopsy cavity changes and\u000acalcifications in association with benign epithelium.\u000aNo residual phyllodes tumor is identified.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: S/p left breast lumpectomy/mastopexy.\u000aOperation: Left breast lumpectomy.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast mass.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. left breast mass phyllodes sac.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in one part, labeled with the patient's name,\u000aunit number, and "phyllodes sac", and consists of an unoriented irregular\u000aportion of fibrofatty tissue (5.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). Along one aspect of the\u000aspecimen is a loosely attached piece of fibroadipose tissue (2.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm), which is held in place to the main part of the specimen with an\u000aundesignated black suture. The specimen displays a defect (3.0 x REMOVED_DATE cm),\u000aexposing a cavity (4.3 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The specimen is inked black and blue\u000aink is applied within the previously described area of the loosely adherent\u000aportion of fibrofatty tissue, and the specimen is serially sectioned to reveal\u000athe previously described biopsy cavities, surrounded by 95% yellow lobulated\u000aadipose tissue, and 5% focally dense white fibrous tissue, with no discrete\u000amasses or lesions identified. As previously described, the cavity is exposed\u000aon an undesignated margin. The specimen is sequentially submitted in its\u000aentirety.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Loosely adherent portion of adipose tissue (previously described\u000aas being attached by an undesignated suture), with the blue ink towards the\u000aspecimen, and the black ink the "true margin", 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross sections, of area underlying the loosely adherent\u000afibrofatty tissue with the blue ink towards the loosely adherent fibrofatty\u000atissue (not true margin), REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID 3 frags each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential trisected cross section, with the exposed cavity in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID,\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential trisected cross section, with the exposed cavity in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID,\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross section, serially sectioned, with the exposed\u000abiopsy cavity in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 2 frags each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross section, serially sectioned, with the exposed\u000acavity in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential trisected cross section, with the exposed cavity in\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential trisected cross section, with the exposed biopsy\u000acavity in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential trisected cross section, with the exposed biopsy\u000acavity in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Opposite unoriented end, radially, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000acp/ag\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Hejin P Hahn M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a1/29/2008\u000a[report_end]
