VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-09-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Tanya Rege, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Jane E. Brock, M.B., B.S., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A REMOVED_DATE CM MASS AND CLIP:\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, papillary and cribriform types, (low and intermediate\u000anuclear grade) with calcifications and without necrosis is present in 4 of 12\u000ablocks (see NOTE).\u000aDCIS is present at the inferior margin (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), medial margin (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), < REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000athe lateral margin (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), and REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID). Anterior and\u000aposterior margins are negative for DCIS (> REMOVED_DATE cm).\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for DCIS (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) NEGATIVE (0)\u000aOther findings:\u000aBiopsy site.\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia.\u000aColumnar cell hyperplasia with atypia.\u000aApocrine cysts.\u000aNOTE: Papillary DCIS forms a solid mass (0.8 cm; REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID). A p63/REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID double\u000aimmunohistochemical stain highlights retained myoepithelial cells around the\u000apapillary cores and around the perimeter of the lesion confirming the diagnosis\u000aof in situ carcinoma. Additional scattered small foci of DCIS are present\u000aadjacent to and away from the mass lesion.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 55 year old woman with history of L breast ca with abnormal mammo\u000a2/5/09 and s/p right breast core biopsy REMOVED_DATE  revealing highly atypical\u000apapillary lesion.\u000aOperation: Right breast wire loc biopsy.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: None given.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Right breast tissue, short stitch superior, long stitch lateral, whip\u000astitch at deep margin.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Called to OR at 10:24 am by H. Retus. Mass/wire in specimen. HP\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in one part, labeled with the patient's name,\u000amedical record number, and "#1. Right breast tissue", consists of a REMOVED_DATE gram\u000abreast excision (1.6 cm anterior to posterior, REMOVED_DATE cm superior to inferior, and\u000a5.5 cm medial to lateral), oriented with a short stitch designated superior,\u000along stitch designated lateral, and a whipstitch designated deep margin by the\u000asurgeon. The specimen was received inked by the surgeon, per BWH pathology\u000aprotocol, for the evaluation of margins; superior/red, inferior/green,\u000alateral/yellow, medial/orange, anterior/blue and posterior/black. A\u000alocalization wire enters the lateral aspect of the specimen. An accompanying\u000aradiograph demonstrates a mass, a clip, and a hookwire. A firm white/tan\u000anodule (0.6 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) is designated by clip and is present REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000athe superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin,\u000aand REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Breast excision, medial to lateral, REMOVED_DATE frags each, ESS.\u000aThe clipped lesion is present in micro cassette REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aImmunohistochemical studies for estrogen receptor, progesterone\u000areceptor, and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu were evaluated by manual morphometric analysis\u000ausing the following criteria:\u000aHormone receptor analysis:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low > 0% - < 10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not\u000ayet been determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10%\u000aof tumor cells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor\u000acells but only a portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aEquivocal (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity in >30% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aExternal controls are evaluated and show appropriate Immunoreactivity.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for\u000ainvestigational use only.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aTR/ag\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jane E. Brock M.B., B.S., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000aTuesday REMOVED_MONTH 07, 2009 at 05:08:22PM\u000a[report_end]
