ormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000ainvasive carcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but\u000aonly a portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity\u000ain >10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 55 year old nulliparous postmenopausal female with a REMOVED_DATE cm right\u000asuperior density with 2 non diagnostic core needle biopsies.\u000aOperation: Right breast wire localization excisional biopsy\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast cancer\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1. Right breast wire localized partial mastectomy\u000aRADIOLOGY: Mass is in the specimen. Dr. Smith.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by BUNDOCK,ELIZABETH A.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in one part, labeled with the patient's name,\u000aunit number and "#1. right breast wire localized partial mastectomy", and\u000aconsists of a portion of fibroadipose tissue (4.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with a\u000alocalization wire in place. Also received is a specimen radiograph which is\u000areported as mass is in the specimen. The specimen is received in pathology\u000aalready inked by the surgeon per pathology protocol for the evaluation of\u000amargins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green;\u000alateral = yellow; medial = orange. The specimen is serially sectioned at 3 mm\u000aintervals from medial to lateral revealing 90% firm white fibrous tissue\u000agrossly suspicious for invasive carcinoma (2.9 x 2 x REMOVED_DATE cm) extending to the\u000amedial, inferior, anterior, and lateral margins, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior,\u000aand REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margins. Adjacent to the edge of the mass, in\u000athe posterolateral portion of the specimen, is a hemorrhagic cavity (0.5 x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm) lined with a small amount of fibrous tissue and fat necrosis, grossly\u000aconsistent with a prior site. No other areas suspicious for biopsy site are\u000aidentified. The mass corresponds to the mass seen in the specimen radiograph.\u000a75% of the tumor, including the biopsy cavity, and numerous samples of all\u000amargins are submitted for permanent histology.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  breast tissue, 11 frags, RSS\u000aeab\u000aReports to: KAELIN, CAROLYN, MARY M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY - PARTIAL OR SIMPLE\u000a[report_end]
