VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST MASTECTOMY W/REGIONAL LYMPH NODES\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aLESTER, SUSAN, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by WELCH,WILLIAM ROBERT,M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "LEFT BREAST" (LEFT MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY) (INCLUDING\u000aFROZEN SECTION AND SMEAR):\u000aINVASIVE APOCRINE CARCINOMA (at least 8 cm), poorly differentiated\u000a(modified Bloom-Richardson Grade III/III) with extensive necrosis (greater\u000athan 1 HPF) and calcifications.\u000aInvasive carcinoma extends to within REMOVED_DATE cm of the deep margin, but is not\u000apresent at the deep margin.\u000aInvasive carcinoma extensively invades subcutaneous adipose tissue and\u000afocally invades deep dermal collagen of the reticular dermis. The\u000apapillary dermis and epidermis are free of carcinoma.\u000aLymphatic/vascular invasion is present within the breast.\u000aDeep dermal lymphatic invasion is present (blocks 20 and 21).\u000aAPOCRINE DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, cribriform type, with intermediate\u000agrade nuclei is present associated with, and away from, the areas of\u000ainvasive carcinoma.\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU extends to within REMOVED_DATE cm of the deep margin.\u000aLactational changes.\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "LEFT, LEVEL I AND II AXILLARY NODE DISSECTION";\u000aMETASTATIC CARCINOMA, in twelve (12) of fifteen (15) separate lymph nodes\u000a(some metastases are seen on the deeper levels of blocks 11, 14, and 15).\u000aThe largest metastatic deposit is REMOVED_DATE cm in size. Extranodal invasion is\u000apresent and carcinoma is present in extranodal lymphatics.\u000aNote: The larger metastatic deposits may represent multiple matted\u000alymph nodes or massively enlarged single nodes.\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies on formalin fixed tissue reveal that invasive\u000acarcinoma is not immunoreactive for estrogen receptors. Estrogen receptor\u000aimmunohistochemistry on frozen tissue was also reported to be negative.\u000aRare cells (<1%) are immunoreactive for progesterone and this finding is\u000ainterpreted as negative. Adjacent epithelium is appropriately immunoreactive\u000afor both estrogen and progesterone receptors.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 41-year-old post-partum, nursing female with clinical REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID (15 cm)\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID left breast upper outer quadrant cancer.\u000aOperation: Left MRM\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1) Left breast (short=superior; long=lateral; tumor=UOQ)\u000a2) Left level I and II axillary node dissection.\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "LEFT BREAST" (FSA, SMA):\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA.\u000aTissue for ER/PR\u000aTissue for flow.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by LIGON,KEITH LLOYD,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen was received fresh, in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit numnber.\u000aPart one, "left breast (short=superior;long=lateral; tumor=uoq)", is a single\u000amastectomy specimen (18.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm overall) oriented with a long stitch\u000alateral, and short stitch superior, weighing 650g with a tan skin ellispe\u000ameasuring REMOVED_DATE x 10 cm with a REMOVED_DATE cm nipple, 6 cm from the inferior margin, 11\u000acm from the superior, 7 cm from the medial, and 13 cm from the lateral\u000aaxillary margin. The deep surface is inked black and the parenchyma contains\u000aa 8 x 6 x 6 cm multilobulated mass which is white/tan and firm in the upper\u000aouter quadrant. The cut surface of the mass reveals areas of white/tan soft\u000amaterial suspicious for necrosis. The mass is less than REMOVED_DATE cm from the deep\u000amargin, 5 cm from the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral axillary margin,\u000aand 6 cm from the medial margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the overlying the skin\u000asurface. The carcinoma is directly below the skin in subcutanous adipose\u000atissue over an area measuring 8 cm. The skin is freely mobile over the\u000amass. The skin has no scars, retractions, or other lesions. Representative\u000asections are submitted as FSA and the FSA is entirely sent for ER/PR.\u000aMicro 1: Breast mass and deep margin, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 2: Breast mass and deep margin, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 3: Breast mass and overlying skin, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Breast mass, RSS\u000aMicro 6: Upper outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 7: Lower outer quadrant, 1 frag, RES\u000aMicro 8: Upper inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 9: Lower inner quadrant, 2 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 10: Nipple, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Additional sections of mass and skin, 10 frag, RSS.\u000aPart two, "level I & II", is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name,\u000aunit number, and "left level I and II axillary node dissection", and consists\u000aof a single fibrofatty tissue fragment (8.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) containing fifteen\u000apossible lymph nodes, the largest measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm, the smallest\u000abeing REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm, with four nodes greater than 2 cm in size and grossly\u000areplaced by firm white tumor. The larger nodes consist of multilobulated\u000amasses of firm white tumor.\u000aMicro 11: 3 possible lymph nodes, ESS\u000aMicro 12: 3 possible lymph nodes, RSS\u000aMicro 13: 2 possible lymph nodes, 2 ESS, 2RSS\u000aMicro 14: 3 possible lymph nodes, ESS\u000aMicro 15: 3 possible lymph nodes, ESS.\u000aMicro 16: 1 lymph node, 1 frag, ESS.\u000akll\u000aReports to: KAELIN, CAROLYN, MARY M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY W/REGIONAL LYMPH NODES\u000a[report_end]
