VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID:REMOVED_CASE_ID Report Status: Signed\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000a*** ADDENDUM MESSAGE ***\u000a*** ADDITIONAL DIAGNOSTIC INFORMATION ***\u000aThis report contains an addendum to the original diagnosis for the purpose\u000aof adding additional diagnostic information. Please refer to the ADDENDUM\u000aREPORT data section for this information. The original diagnosis is unchanged.\u000aADDENDUM REPORT\u000aAddendum #1 Entered: REMOVED_DATE -1203\u000aFluorescence in situ hybridization (FISH) with probes for REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu performed at\u000aMayo Medical Laboratories on block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID reveals the following results for the\u000ainfiltrating carcinoma:\u000aThe specimen showed NO evidence of REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu gene amplification.\u000aAddeundum Signed Electronically Signed KOELLIKER,DANIEL D. M.D. REMOVED_DATE \u000aDIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. Right breast, excision:\u000aPoorly differentiated infiltrating ductal carcinoma, REMOVED_DATE cm. in size.\u000aDuctal carcinoma in situ, grade REMOVED_DATE  solid type with lobular involvement.\u000aFocal fibroplasia and chronic inflammation (prior needle biopsy site).\u000aB. Final deep margin of right breast, excision:\u000aFocal ductal carcinoma in situ (single microscopic focus in lobule,\u000a1-2 mm. from inked margin).\u000aC. Final medial inferior margin of right breast, excision:\u000aFocus of infiltrating ductal carcinoma (see note).\u000aDuctal carcinoma in situ (in multiple lobules, less than 1 mm. from inked\u000amargin).\u000aD. Final lateral margin of right breast, excision:\u000aFocal ductal carcinoma in situ (single microscopic focus in lobule, less\u000athan 1 mm. from inked margin).\u000aE. Sentinel lymph nodes (right):\u000aTwo lymph nodes with no evidence of malignancy.\u000aImmunohistochemical stains for keratin are negative.\u000aF. Lymph node (right axillary):\u000aOne lymph node with no evidence of malignancy.\u000aNOTE: In the right breast excision specimen (A) the infiltrating carcinoma is\u000aless than 1 mm. from the margin opposite short suture. There is a focus\u000aof infiltrating carcinoma present in the final medial inferior margin\u000aspecimen (C) and this is less than 1 mm. from the inked margin (surface\u000afurthest from tumor). No vascular or lymphatic invasion is seen.\u000aImmunohistochemical stains performed on block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID reveal the following\u000aresults for the infiltrating carcinoma: Estrogen receptor NEGATIVE;\u000aProgesterone receptor NEGATIVE; and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) nondiagnostic\u000aresult (cytoplasmic staining; further evaluation by fluorescence in situ\u000ahybridization (FISH) method will be performed and results reported in an\u000aaddendum to follow). Ductal carcinoma in situ is present in multiple\u000afoci over an area approximately REMOVED_DATE to REMOVED_DATE cm. in size adjacent to the\u000ainfiltrating tumor. Ductal carcinoma in situ is less than 1 mm. from\u000athe margins opposite both sutures over a broad front, 1 to 2 mm. from\u000athe margin with the long suture focally, and 1 to 2 mm. from the\u000apresumed deep margin in multiple foci. The report of the prior right\u000abreast needle biopsy, Massachusetts General Hospital consultation review\u000a(MGH, S-01-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) is noted.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by: Daniel D. Koelliker, M.D.\u000aINTRA-OPERATIVE CONSULTATION:\u000aOPERATING ROOM CONSULTATION (TISSUE EXAMINATION WITH TOUCH PREPARATION):\u000aLarger of two sentinel lymph nodes: Touch prep - no tumor seen.\u000aTwo blue lymph nodes: Final diagnosis deferred to permanent sections.\u000aDJF\u000aClinical diagnosis & history:\u000aRight breast carcinoma\u000aTissue-Designation:\u000aA.Breast, excision with margins - right breast\u000aB.Breast, excision with margins - right final deep margin\u000aC.Breast, excision with margins - right final medial inferior\u000aD.Breast, excision with margins - right final lateral\u000aE.Sentinel lymph node - right axillary x 2\u000aF.Lymph node, biopsy - right axillary\u000aGross description:\u000aThe specimen is received in six containers.\u000aSpecimen A labeled "right breast lumpectomy" consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000aportion of fibroadipose tissue marked by two sutures. No specific designation\u000ais made on the requisition or container to the orientation of the sutures. It\u000awill be presumed short is superior and long is lateral. Assuming this\u000aorientation, the deep surface is double inked red and the lateral surface (long\u000asuture) is double inked blue. The specimen is serially sectioned from the end\u000amarked with the short suture (superior) and towards the opposite end revealing\u000abluish discoloration within the yellow lobulated adipose tissue. There is a\u000afirm area in the mid portion close to the surface. Somewhat more inferior to\u000athis is a central REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. hard, white-tan tumor with a central\u000ayellowish and reddish, punctate discoloration. The entire specimen is serially\u000asubmitted from the end marked with the short suture towards the opposite end in\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. 12 agg. all.\u000aSpecimen B is received in formalin, labeled "final deep margin, suture furthest\u000afrom tumor" and consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. portion of fibroadipose\u000atissue, one surface of which is marked with a suture and this surface is inked\u000ablack. The specimen is cross sectioned and entirely submitted in B. 1 agg.\u000aall.\u000aSpecimen C is received in formalin, labeled "right medial inferior" and\u000aconsists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. portion of fibroadipose tissue, one surface\u000aof which has a suture oriented as furthest from tumor, and this surface is\u000ainked. the specimen is cross sectioned and serially submitted in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. 3\u000aagg. all.\u000aSpecimen D is received in formalin, labeled "right lateral" and consists of a\u000a2.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. portion of fibroadipose tissue marked on one surface with a\u000asuture, and this surface is inked. The specimen is cross sectioned and\u000aserially submitted in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. 2 agg. all.\u000aSpecimen E is received fresh, labeled "right axillary sentinel nodes x 2" and\u000aconsists of a portion of adipose tissue within which a larger REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm. lymph node and a smaller REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. lymph node is identified.\u000aBoth are cross sectioned revealing bluish discoloration of the tissue. No\u000agross evidence of tumor is seen. A touch prep from the surfaces is submitted.\u000aThe entirety of each lymph node is submitted in its respective cassette REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. The entire remainder of the adipose tissue is submitted in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. 3 agg.\u000aall.\u000aSpecimen F is received in formalin, labeled "right axillary lymph node,\u000anon-sentinel" and consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. lymph node which shows\u000afatty replacement of the hilum. No gross evidence of tumor is seen on the cut\u000asurface. It is entirely submitted in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. 2 agg. all.\u000aDictated by: DDK____(signature on file)____DENNIS J. FEEN, M.D. REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a____(signature on file)____DANIEL D. KOELLIKER, M.D. REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a[report_end]
