VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID:REMOVED_CASE_ID Report Status: Signed\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aDIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. Right breast, "re-excision #1":\u000aSingle focus (less than 1 mm.) of lobular involvement by\u000aductal carcinoma in situ, intermediate grade in the inferior-anterior\u000aportion of the specimen, REMOVED_DATE mm. from the anterior margin.\u000aNo residual invasive carcinoma seen.\u000aHealing biopsy site changes.\u000aScattered microcalcifications in benign breast tissue.\u000aFocal atypical lobular hyperplasia.\u000aB. Right breast, "additional cavity":\u000aFocal atypical lobular hyperplasia.\u000aHealing biopsy site changes.\u000aScattered microcalcifications in benign breast tissue.\u000aNo residual invasive carcinoma seen.\u000aNOTE: The prior report (S-01-9818) is noted.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by: Nicole A. Mihok, M.D.\u000aClinical diagnosis & history:\u000aRight breast carcinoma\u000aTissue-Designation:\u000aA.Breast, excision with margins - right, re-excision #1\u000aB.Breast, excision with margins - right, additional cavity\u000aGross description:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in two containers from the Operating Room.\u000aSpecimen A labeled "right breast tissue", designated "#1 re-excision" consists\u000aof a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. portion of tissue with three sutures oriented as long\u000alateral, short superior and medium inferior. One surface of the specimen\u000aconsists of indurated adipose tissue. The other surface of the specimen shows\u000aa cystic cavity with focal congestion and clotted blood consistent with a\u000ahealing biopsy site. The noncystic surface is inked: the medial half in black\u000aand the lateral half in blue. The specimen is sectioned from the superior\u000atowards the inferior edges to show healing biopsy cavities streaked with areas\u000aof congestion admixed with punctate, yellow areas of necrosis and firm, white\u000athickening at the periphery. The entire specimen is submitted from the\u000asuperior towards the inferior margin in eleven cassettes with REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID being the most\u000asuperior and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID being the most inferior. 11 agg. all.\u000aSpecimen B labeled "right breast tissue", designated "additional cavity"\u000aconsists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. oval shaped portion of tissue oriented with a\u000along suture at the medial margin and a short suture at the inferior margin.\u000aOne surface of the specimen consists of a cystic and healing biopsy cavity with\u000afocal congestion. The other surface consists of yellow adipose tissue with\u000afocal congestion. The margin opposite the biopsy cavity is inked as follows:\u000athe medial half in black and the lateral half in blue. The specimen is\u000aserially sectioned from the superior towards the inferior margin to show a\u000afirm, white cut surface streaked with areas of congestion consistent with\u000ahealing biopsy site. No other lesions are identified. The entire specimen is\u000asubmitted in seven cassettes, from the superior towards the inferior edge with\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID being the most superior and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, the most inferior. 7 agg. all.\u000aDictated by: NAM____(signature on file)____DANIEL D. KOELLIKER, M.D. REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a____(signature on file)____NICOLE MIHOK, M.D. REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a[report_end]
