graph that reveals the specimen\u000acontaining a wire adjacent to a clip but no calcifications. The specimen is\u000acomposed of approximately 50% yellow adipose tissue and 50% tan fibrous tissue\u000athat grossly extends to all margins. A REMOVED_DATE cm diameter, hemorrhagic cavity is\u000aconsistent with a prior biopsy site. The specimen is entirely submitted for\u000ahistologic examination.\u000aMicro 1: superior pole, 5 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  specimen superior to inferior, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 11&12: inferior pole, multi frags, ESS.\u000aNOTE: Micro 5 contains the clip.\u000agmw\u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
