VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: FinalType: Surgical Pathology Pathology Report: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID OPERATION DATE: 26 REMOVED_MONTH 02 ACCESSIONED ON: 26 REMOVED_MONTH 02 at 11:19 CLINICAL DATA: Extensive DCIS, left breast. =============================================================================== *** FINAL DIAGNOSIS *** BREAST (LEFT), SIMPLE MASTECTOMY: DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN-SITU, GRADE 2 INVOLVING MUCH OF THE BREAST AND EXTENDING TO LESS THAN REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE DEEP MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN IN THE REGION OF THE UPPER INNER QUADRANT. SEE NOTE. NOTE: Invasion of the stroma, blood vessels, and lymphatic vessels is not seen. LYMPH NODE (LEFT AXILLA "SENTINEL"), EXCISION: THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN ONE OF ONE LYMPH NODE. SEE NOTE. NOTE: The lymph node does not contain keratin positive carcinoma cells. Diagnosis by: Frederick Carl Koerner, M.D. Signed On: 08 REMOVED_MONTH 02 at 11:52 =============================================================================== GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab, labeled with the patient's name and unit number, and "left axillary node frozen" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm gray tan gritty lymph node which is bisected and entirely submitted for frozen section as FX#1, now as A. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "left simple mastectomy" is a 1,079 g, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm left mastectomy specimen, with an undesignated black stitch, arbitrarily upper-outer quadrant. There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm gray-tan skin ellipse with a central REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm unremarkable nipple. A REMOVED_DATE cm well-healed linear scar comes to REMOVED_DATE cm of the inferior margin. The specimen is inked green and serially sectioned to reveal an 80% yellow-orange adipose, and a 20% gray-white fibrous cut-surface with no discrete lesions. The fibrous tissue is focally nodular to gritty and rubbery, with no suspicious induration. There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm hemorrhagic cavity in the upper-inner quadrant, which possibly represents previous biopsy site and is greater than REMOVED_DATE cm of the deep margin. Sectioning of the possible axillary region reveals 3 possible tan-pink lymph nodes, ranging from REMOVED_DATE cm to REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest dimension. Representative sections are submitted as follows: SECTION CODE: B-D: Lower-inner quadrant, with the inferior superficial margin as D. E-G: Upper-inner quadrant, with E representing cavity and deep margin closest to cavity. H-J: Lower-outer quadrant, with inferior margin as H-I. K-M: Upper-outer quadrant. N : Possible lymph nodes. Gross Description by: STEPHANIE KUEHN Resident: AQING ('AHCHEAN') CHEN, MD *** INTRA-OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS *** FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS #1: LEFT AXILLARY SENTINEL NODE: THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. O.R. Resident: HEIKE VARNHOLT, MD O.R. Diagnosis by: ESTHER OLIVA, MD =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT - REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID REPORTS TO: Michele Annette Gadd, M.D. Jonathan Michael Winograd, M.D. PART A: LYMPH NODE (LEFT AXILLARY SENTINEL), EXCISION PART B: BREAST(LEFT),SIMPLE MASTECTOMY
