VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: MEHRA GOLSHAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Eleanor Y. Chen, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Hejin P Hahn, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. LEFT BREAST WIRE-LOCALIZED EXCISIONAL BIOPSY:\u000aBenign breast tissue with calcifications associated with benign\u000aepithelium and columnar cell change.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the\u000aspecimen, including margins.\u000aB. FINAL POSTERIOR MARGIN, LEFT BREAST:\u000aBenign breast tissue with columnar cell change, calcifications\u000aassociated with columnar cell change and epithelial hyperplasia.\u000aCore biopsy site.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the\u000aspecimen, including margins.\u000a(Levels examined.)\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 48 y/o female with personal h/o right cancer; S/P MRM. Left breast\u000acalcifications S/P image-guided core biopsy revealing atypical ductal\u000ahyperplasia.\u000aOperation: Left breast wire-localized excisional biopsy.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast atypical ductal hyperplasia.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) Left breast wire-localized excisional biopsy; short suture - superior;\u000along suture - lateral (to mammo)\u000aB/2) Final posterior margin suture on margin, left breast to mammo.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Clip NOT in specimen #1. Dr. Golshan called.\u000aClip IN specimen #2.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in two parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and medical record number.\u000aPart A, labeled "Left breast wire localized excisional biopsy, short superior,\u000along suture lateral", consists of a REMOVED_DATE (medial to lateral) x REMOVED_DATE (inferior to\u000asuperior) x REMOVED_DATE (anterior to posterior) cm breast biopsy with a localization\u000awire in place and a short suture marking the superior margin, and a long suture\u000amarking the lateral margin. An accompanying specimen radiograph demonstrates a\u000alocalization wire in place. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for\u000athe evaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red;\u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. The tissue consists of an area\u000aof white/ill-defined, firm fibrous lesion (2.3 cm in greatest dimension),\u000acorresponding to the dense fibrous area on the radiograph, which abuts the\u000alateral, posterior and inferior margins, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE \u000acm from the anterior margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin. The breast\u000atissue is composed approximately 30% fibrous and 70% adipose tissue. The\u000aspecimen is serially sectioned from superior to inferior and entirely submitted\u000afor histologic examination.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Serial sections from superior to inferior, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID including the\u000afibrous areas, multi frags, ESS.\u000aPart B, labeled "Final posterior margin, suture on margin from left breast",\u000aconsists of a fragment of irregular breast tissue (2.6 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with the\u000asuture marking the final margin. The accompanying radiograph shows a clip and\u000aadjacent calcification. There is a REMOVED_DATE cm hemorrhagic area (biopsy site) that\u000acorresponds to the clip site on the radiograph and comes to within REMOVED_DATE cm of\u000athe new inferior margin. The specimen is composed of approximately 40% fibrous\u000atissue. The tissue at the final margin is composed of predominantly adipose\u000atissue. The final margin is inked green and the opposite surface is inked red.\u000aThe entire specimen is serially sectioned and submitted for histologic\u000aexamination.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Serial sections, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID including the biopsy site, multi\u000afrags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-07-REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Hejin P Hahn M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a6/27/2007\u000a[report_end]
