VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID:REMOVED_CASE_ID Report Status: Signed\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aDIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. Left breast, needle localized excision:\u000aFocal residual poorly differentiated infiltrating ductal carcinoma, REMOVED_DATE \u000acm., see note.\u000aHealing biopsy site changes.\u000aB. Left breast, superior margin, excision:\u000aNo tumor seen.\u000aHealing biopsy site changes.\u000aC. Left breast, deep margin, excision:\u000aNo tumor seen.\u000aD. Left breast, lateral margin, excision:\u000aNo tumor seen.\u000aE. Left breast, inferior margin, excision:\u000aNo tumor seen.\u000aF. Left breast, medial margin, excision:\u000aNo tumor seen.\u000aSYNOPTIC REPORT:\u000aINVASIVE TUMOR:\u000a-histologic type: Ductal\u000a-histologic grade: Poorly differentiated\u000a-size (greatest dimension): REMOVED_DATE cm. (present in slides REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID). The tumor is surrounded by\u000aan extensive xanthomatous\u000ainflammatory reaction.\u000a-lymphatic/vascular invasion: None identified\u000a-perineural invasion: None identified\u000a-microcalcification in invasive tumor: None identified\u000a-margins for invasive tumor:\u000aFocally, the invasive tumor is REMOVED_DATE cm. from the anterior margin in slide\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. All separate margins (B-F) are free of tumor.\u000a-immunohistochemical stains were performed on the prior needle core biopsy\u000a(S-03-9407) and revealed the following results for the infiltrating\u000acarcinoma:\u000aEstrogen receptor: NEGATIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor: NEGATIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID): NEGATIVE for overexpression\u000aPRIOR RELATED SPECIMENS REVIEWED:\u000aLeft breast, S-03-9407, REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by: Nicole A. Mihok, M.D.\u000aClinical diagnosis & history:\u000aLeft breast carcinoma\u000aTissue-Designation:\u000aA.Breast, excision with margins - left\u000aB.Breast, excision with margins - left, superior margin\u000aC.Breast, excision with margins - left, deep margin\u000aD.Breast, excision with margins - left, lateral margin\u000aE.Breast, excision with margins - left, inferior margin\u000aF.Breast, excision with margins - left, medial margin\u000aGross description:\u000aThe specimen is received in six containers.\u000aSpecimen A labeled "left breast" is received in formalin. It has a long stitch\u000adesignating the medial margin and a short stitch designating the superior\u000amargin. There is a needle localization wire protruding from the specimen. The\u000asuperior half is inked blue; the inferior half, green; the deep margin, black.\u000aThe specimen is sectioned from medial towards lateral. In the center of the\u000aspecimen, there is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. fairly well circumscribed lesion with\u000ayellow areas. The lesion extends focally towards the deep and superior margin.\u000aThe entire specimen is submitted from medial towards lateral in cassettes\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID is the most medial; REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID is the most lateral). 11X all.\u000aSpecimen B labeled "left breast, superior margin", is received in formalin and\u000ais designated to have stitch on the surfaces furthest from the tumor, consists\u000aof two portions of tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000aThe surfaces designated furthest from the tumor are inked blue. The other\u000asurfaces are not inked. Each specimen is serially sectioned and submitted in\u000aits representative cassette labeled REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. 2 agg. all.\u000aSpecimen C labeled "left breast, deep margin" is received in formalin and\u000aconsists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. portion of tissue with a stitch furthest\u000afrom the tumor. This surface is inked blue. The other surfaces are not inked.\u000aThe specimen is serially sectioned, bisected and submitted in one cassette. 2X\u000aall.\u000aSpecimen D labeled "left breast margin, lateral" is received in formalin and\u000aconsists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. portion of breast tissue with a stitch\u000adesignating the surface furthest from the tumor. This surface is inked blue.\u000aThe other surfaces are not inked. The specimen is serially sectioned and\u000aentirely submitted in one cassette. 1 agg. all.\u000aSpecimen E labeled "left breast margin, inferior" is received in formalin and\u000aconsists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. portion of breast tissue with a stitch\u000adesignating the surface furthest from the tumor. This surface is inked blue.\u000aThe other surfaces are not. The specimen is trisected and submitted in one\u000acassette. 3X all.\u000aSpecimen F labeled "left breast, medial margin" is received in formalin and\u000aconsists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. portion of breast tissue with a stitch\u000adesignating the surface furthest from the tumor. This surface is inked blue;\u000athe other surfaces are not inked. The specimen is serially sectioned and\u000aentirely submitted in one cassette. 1 agg. all.\u000aDictated by: NAM____(signature on file)____DANIEL D. KOELLIKER, M.D. REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a____(signature on file)____NICOLE MIHOK, M.D. REMOVED_DATE  (Final)\u000a[report_end]
