VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID SENTINEL LYMPH NODE\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aWELCH, WILLIAM, ROBERT, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by WELCH,WILLIAM ROBERT,M.D.\u000aRIGHT BREAST EXCISION (#3) AND SENTINEL NODE (#1), AND AXILLARY NODE DISSECTION\u000a(#2):\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA, DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU and METASTATIC CARCINOMA\u000aTO LYMPH NODE.\u000aSYNOPSIS:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA\u000aSize - REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aMultifocal? - No\u000aHistologic Type - Mixed Ductal and Lobular\u000aHistologic Grade (SBR) - II (Moderate)\u000aNuclear Grade - Intermediate\u000aEIC - Negative\u000aLymphovascular invasion - Present (extensive, multiple foci in\u000amultiple blocks)\u000aDermal lymphatic invasion - Absent\u000aSkin invasion - Absent\u000aSkeletal muscle invasion - N/A\u000aFinal Margins (invasive)\u000aNegative (no ink on tumor) - Anterior, posterior, medial, lateral,\u000ainferior, superior\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aTypes - Solid, cribriform\u000aNuclear grade - High\u000aCalcifications in DCIS - Absent\u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - Absent\u000aExtent of DCIS\u000aNumber of blocks/total: - REMOVED_DATE blocks\u000aDCIS is present as a minor component of the invasive carcinoma\u000aFinal Margins (DCIS)\u000aNegative (>0.3 cm) - All margins\u000aLYMPH NODES\u000aSentinel lymph nodes (3 H&E levels examined): Positive (microscopic,\u000aconfirmed with keratin\u000aimmunoperoxidase)\u000aNumber of positive nodes: - 1\u000aNumber of nodes examined : - 2\u000aAxillary lymph node: - Negative\u000aNumber of positive nodes: - 0\u000aNumber of nodes examined: - 4\u000aTOTAL POSITIVE NODES (including all specimens): REMOVED_DATE \u000aSize of largest metatatic focus <0.1\u000aExtranodal extension - Absent\u000aOTHER FINDINGS\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia\u000aCysts\u000aApocrine metaplasia\u000aCalcifications in benign epithelium\u000aSkin with no significant pathologic change.\u000aAJCC CLASSIFICATION - REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDc pREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID MX (see note)\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER/PR/HER-2) - Pending\u000a#2) SPECIMEN LABELED "CAUDAD SHAVE MARGIN":\u000aBreast parenchyma with atypical ductal hyperplasia, cysts and apocrine\u000ametaplasia.\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy.\u000aNOTE: A cluster of approximately 15 keratin-positive cells representing\u000ametastatic disease is present in a sentinel lymph node. In the most recent\u000aclassification scheme, this does not warrant a stage above pREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. This case has\u000abeen reviewed by Dr. Susan Lester of the Breast Pathology service, who agrees.\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: by SCHNITT,STUART J.,M.D.\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for invasive carcinoma (block 10):\u000aEstrogen receptor - POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor - POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) - NEGATIVE (1+)\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000ainvasive carcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but\u000aonly a portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity\u000ain >10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 54 year old female with core biopsy proven cancer of right breast.\u000aOperation: Right breast wide excision, right axillary sentinel node biopsy\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast cancer\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1) Right breast sentinel node\u000a#2) Right axillary contents\u000a#3) Right breast mass - short superior\u000a#4) Caudad shave margin - medial short superior\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "#1. SENTINEL NODE", (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID (ESS): No tumor seen.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID (RSS): No tumor seen.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by PADERA,ROBERT F.,JR.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in four parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart one, labeled "#1. right breast sentinel node", consists of a single\u000afragment of yellow/tan soft tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. There are two\u000alymph nodes present, each measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. One of these lymph\u000anodes is entirely submitted as REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. The other node is bisected and one-half\u000aof the node is frozen as REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. The lymph nodes are submitted in their entirety\u000afor histologic evaluation.\u000aMicro 1: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID remnant, 1 frag, ESS\u000aMicro 2: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID remnant, 1 frag, ESS\u000aMicro 3: remainder of unfrozen REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID node bisected, 2 frags, ESS\u000aPart two, labeled "#2. right axillary contents", consists of a single fragment\u000aof yellow adipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. Within this tissue are\u000afour potential lymph nodes, the largest of which measures REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest\u000adimension. These lymph nodes are entirely submitted for histologic evaluation.\u000aMicro 4: 1 lymph node, 2 frags, ESS\u000aMicro 5: 1 lymph node, 4 frags, ESS\u000aMicro 6: 1 lymph node, 2 frags, ESS\u000aMicro 7: 1 lymph node, 3 frags, ESS\u000aPart three, labeled "#3. right breast mass", consists of a 37g lumpectomy\u000aspecimen with skin. The specimen measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm and contains a\u000awhite/tan skin ellipse measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The specimen is received with\u000atwo sutures. A single short suture on the skin ellipse indicates superior and\u000aa single long suture at one tip indicates lateral. The specimen has been inked\u000aby the surgeon per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior\u000a= black; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow;\u000amedial = orange. Within the tissue there is a firm white/tan stellate tumor\u000amass measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm that is REMOVED_DATE cm from the deep margin, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000aanterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral\u000amargin. The remainder of the breast parenchyma is comprised of approximately\u000a60% adipose tissue and 40% fibrous tissue. The fibrous tissue is nodular with\u000asome microcysts. No other discrete masses are present. Representative\u000asections of the tumor and uninvolved breast parenchyma are submitted for\u000aspecial studies to the tumor bank. Representative sections are submitted for\u000ahistologic analysis.\u000aMicro 8: inferior and anterior margins, 2 frags, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  superior margin with anterior and posterior margins, mult frags,\u000aRSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  posterior margin, 2 frags, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  posterior and inferior margins, 3 frags, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  medial margin with skin, 3 frags, RSS\u000aMicro 18: skin and anterior margin, 2 frags, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  lateral margin, 5 frags, RSS\u000aPart four, labeled "#4. caudad shave margin", consists of a single fragment of\u000ayellow adipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. One surface of this\u000aspecimen is inked green by the surgeon. The specimen is received with two\u000aorienting sutures. A double short suture is present on the surface opposite\u000athe green inked surface and designates superior. A double long suture is\u000apresent and not designated. The side opposite the green ink is inked black\u000arepresenting the old margin. The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal\u000aunremarkable adipose tissue and is entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  caudad shave margin, 6 frags, ESS\u000arp\u000aReports to: CHRISTIAN, ROGER, L. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: SENTINEL LYMPH NODE\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: LYMPH NODE BIOPSY\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST BIOPSY W/O MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN\u000a[report_end]
