VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: SARA RUSSELL M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-05-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Ann K Folkins, M.D.; Joseph Woodward Carlson, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Susan Lester, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY:\u000aRESIDUAL INVASIVE CARCINOMA with ductal and lobular features, poorly\u000adifferentiated (modified Bloom-Richardson grade III/III), REMOVED_DATE cm, adjacent to\u000abiopsy site changes and a clip.\u000aNo lymphovascular invasion is present.\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, cribriform type (intermediate nuclear grade), without\u000aassociated calcifications and necrosis is present in 2 of 10 slides (EIC\u000anegative).\u000aSkin and nipple with no involvement by carcinoma.\u000aInvasive carcinoma and DCIS are present > REMOVED_DATE cm from the deep margin.\u000aSkeletal muscle is present with no involvement by invasive carcinoma.\u000aNOTE: This patient had a REMOVED_DATE cm mass with possible muscle invasion by MRI and a\u000anegative sentinel lymph node and is now s/p neoadjuvant chemotherapy. A\u000agrossly evident REMOVED_DATE cm lesion was present consisting of the tumor bed which\u000ashows involvement by tumor throughout. The tumor bed was REMOVED_DATE cm from the deep\u000amargin and the skeletal muscle is not involved. Overall, the cellularity\u000aappears reduced, but comparison with the patient's pre-treatment carcinoma\u000awould be necessary for accurate assessment (reviewed as REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID but slides no\u000alonger available for review). The overall response to chemotherapy would be\u000aconsistent with a Miller-Payne Grade 2 response.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 58 year old female S/P core bx + sentinel node bx (neg) right breast.\u000aPt underwent chemo - neoadjuvant. Now for simple mastectomy, poorly\u000adifferentiated adenocarcinoma with pectoralis involvement.\u000aOperation: None given.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: R breast CA.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000a1. Right breast, short stitch - superior; long stitch - lateral.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in a container labeled with the patient?s name,\u000aunit number, and "1. Right breast", and consists of a 1,340 gm right, modified\u000aradical mastectomy specimen (33.5 x 22 x REMOVED_DATE cm) with an attached skin ellipse\u000aanteriorly (20 cm long x REMOVED_DATE cm wide) and fragment of muscle posteriorly (17 x\u000a8.9 x REMOVED_DATE cm). There is no attached axillary tail. The breast is composed of\u000aapproximately 90% adipose tissue and 10% fibrous tissue, and it also contains a\u000astellate, white, fibrous mass (1.6 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) in the lower/outer quadrant,\u000awhich is REMOVED_DATE cm from the deep margin, 5 cm from the lateral aspect of the\u000abreast and greater than 5 cm from the skin. A clip is visualized just to the\u000aside of the stellate mass, and the deep margin appears grossly uninvolved by\u000athe tumor. The skin is pink-tan with no scars, and the nipple measures REMOVED_DATE x\u000a0.9 x REMOVED_DATE cm. No lymph nodes are found within the breast tissue. The area\u000awith the clip in it is in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Deep margin over mass, 3 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Deep margin over mass and perpendicular section of nipple,\u000a3 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sections of the mass, 7 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Upper/inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Upper/outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lower/inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lower/outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Additional skin adjacent to nipple, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aAF/mmm\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aResident Review by Ann K Folkins M.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aResident Review by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., on REMOVED_DATE \u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a8/3/2005\u000a[report_end]
