red as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 40 year old female with large right UOQ lump, clinically highly\u000asuspicious for carcinoma, right axillary adenopathy.\u000aOperation: 14g U/S core biopsy\u000aOperative findings: 5 cores - white tissue\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Carcinoma\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Five 14g cores (1 aqua casette)\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name and unit\u000anumber only, in an aqua cassette, and consists of multiple, soft, fragmented,\u000ayellow to white tissue cores (1.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate).\u000aMicro 1: Multi frags, ESS.\u000artv\u000aReports to: FROST, ELISABETH, PEPPERELL M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY(IES)\u000a[report_end]
