VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: CAPRICE CHRISTIAN GREENBERG M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Scott Lovitch, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: William R Welch, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "LEFT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A MASS\u000aAND A CLIP":\u000aGranular Cell Tumor (1.4 cm), associated with extensive core biopsy site\u000achanges.\u000aTumor extends to within REMOVED_DATE cm of the anterior resection margin\u000aand REMOVED_DATE cm of the posterior resection margin.\u000aAll other margins (superior, inferior, medial, lateral) are distant\u000afrom the tumor.\u000aSkeletal muscle; no significant pathologic change.\u000aB. SPECIMEN DESIGNATED "LEFT POSTERIOR MARGIN WITH FASCIA":\u000aAdipose tissue, skeletal muscle, and fascia; negative for tumor.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: None given.\u000aOperation: Left wire localized excision, breast mass\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Benign granular cell tumor.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Left breast mass short - superior, long lateral to mammo.\u000aB/2. Left posterior margin with fascia.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Called to OR: Mass, clip and intact wire on specimen radiographs and\u000aUS. A Odulate\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number\u000aand "#1. Left breast mass, short - superior, long - lateral", consists of a REMOVED_DATE \u000ax REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm excision of fibroadipose tissue, oriented by sutures designating\u000asuperior (short suture) and lateral (long suture) margins. The specimen is\u000ainked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior/black;\u000aanterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange\u000a(inked by prosector). A localizing wire enters laterally and exits medially.\u000aThe specimen is received with an accompanying radiograph demonstrating\u000alocalizing wire in place within an ill-defined mass within the specimen, marked\u000aby a metallic surgical clip. Cut surfaces in this area demonstrate a probably\u000afirm ill-defined lesion (1.4 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm, with associated surrounding fat\u000anecrosis. The borders of the lesion are obscured by the REMOVED_DATE cm biopsy cavity\u000acontaining the metallic clip. The lesion appears to abut the posterior margin,\u000aand approaches within REMOVED_DATE cm of the closest anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the\u000aclosest inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the closest medial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the\u000aclosest superior margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm of the closest lateral margin. The entire\u000aspecimen is submitted, sequentially from lateral to medial, with perpendicular\u000alateral margin in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and perpendicular medial margin in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. Majority of lesion\u000ain REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Entire specimen, sequentially from lateral to medial, multi frags,\u000aESS.\u000aPart B, "#2. Left posterior margin with fascia", consists of an unoriented,\u000acauterized fragment of fibroadipose tissue (1.4 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). Tissue is\u000aentirely inked black, sectioned and submitted for routine processing.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Multi frags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000adb/ag\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by William R Welch M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
