VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aGLICKMAN, JONATHAN, NEIL, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by GLICKMAN,JONATHAN NEIL,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZATION FOR A MASS AND SENTINEL NODE BIOPSIES:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aNEGATIVE SENTINEL LYMPH NODES\u000aSYNOPSIS:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA\u000aSize - REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aMultifocal? - No\u000aHistologic Type - Ductal\u000aHistologic Grade (SBR) - I (Well)\u000aNuclear Grade - Intermediate\u000aEIC - Positive\u000aLymphovascular invasion - Absent\u000aDermal lymphatic invasion - N/A\u000aSkin invasion - N/A\u000aSkeletal muscle invasion - N/A\u000aFinal Margins (invasive) -\u000aNegative (no ink on tumor) - All\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aTypes - Solid, cribriform, and micropapillary.\u000aNuclear grade - Intermediate\u000aCalcifications in DCIS - Present\u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - Present\u000aExtent of DCIS\u000aNumber of blocks/total: - REMOVED_DATE blocks.\u000aFinal Margins (DCIS)\u000aNegative (>0.3 cm): - All\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - Absent\u000aSentinel lymph nodes (3 H&E levels examined): - Negative.\u000aNumber of nodes examined: - 2\u000aTOTAL POSITIVE NODES (sentinel + axillary) - REMOVED_DATE \u000aOTHER FINDINGS: Columnar alteration of lobules with prominent snouts and\u000asecretions, ADH, papilloma, sclerosing adenosis, cysts, apocrine metaplasia,\u000acalcifications in benign epithelium and core biopsy site.\u000aAJCC CLASSIFICATION - REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDc pREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID MX\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES - pending\u000aNOTE: Microcalcifications are present in the invasive carcinoma.\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for invasive carcinoma (block 8):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE - LOW\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) NEGATIVE (0)\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000ainvasive carcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but\u000aonly a portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity\u000ain >10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Core biopsy - suspicious for well-differentiated tubular\u000aadenocarcinoma.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1) Left breast needle localization excision (single long\u000asuture - inferior and anterior, short suture/superior; long suture/lateral)\u000a#2) Left axilla sentinel node #1\u000a#3) Left axilla sentinel node #2\u000aRADIOLOGY: Mass in specimen. OR called 3 pm - CG.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by BUNDOCK,ELIZABETH A.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in three parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart one, labeled "#1. left breast needle loc, excis", consists of an oriented\u000aportion of fibroadipose tissue (6.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with a localization wire in\u000aplace and one short, one double long, and one single long suture present,\u000aplaced by the surgeon to designate superior, lateral and inferoanterior\u000arespectively. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation\u000aof margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior =\u000agreen; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. The specimen is serially sectioned\u000aat 3 mm intervals from superior to inferior, revealing 60% adipose tissue and\u000a40% firm fibrous white tissue, essentially in one mass with irregular borders\u000a(4.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The fibrous area has cysts and many areas of granular\u000atissue. There is a centrally located particularly firm granular area\u000a(approximately REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) suspicious for invasive carcinoma, which is\u000alocated 1 cm from the lateral, REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000amedial, REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior, and more than 2 cm from the superior\u000amargins. In the inferior portion of the fibrous area, is an area of\u000ahemorrhage (0.2 x REMOVED_DATE cm) which may correspond to a prior core biopsy site.\u000aAll fibrous tissue including the potential biopsy site and probable invasive\u000acomponent are submitted in series from inferior to superior.\u000aMicro 1: breast tissue including potential core biopsy site, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  breast tissue, 7 frags, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  probable invasive component, 2 frags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  remainder of fibrous tissue, 13 frags, ESS\u000aPart two, labeled "#2. left axilla sentinel node #1", consists of one fragment\u000aof yellow/tan soft tissue (4.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) containing one lymph node (1.3\u000acm greatest dimension) which is sectioned and entirely submitted.\u000aMicro 20: 1 lymph node, 4 frags, ESS\u000aPart three, labeled "#3. left axilla sentinel node #2", consists of one\u000afragment of yellow/tan soft tissue (2.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) containing one lymph\u000anode (1.6 cm greatest dimension), which is sectioned and entirely submitted.\u000aMicro 21: 1 lymph node, 4 frags, ESS\u000aeab\u000aReports to: SWANSON, RICHARD, S. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SENTINEL LYMPH NODE\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SENTINEL LYMPH NODE\u000a[report_end]
