VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final Type: Surgical Pathology Pathology Report: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID OPERATION DATE: 11 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON: 11 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 13:15 CLINICAL DATA: {None Provided} =============================================================================== *** FINAL DIAGNOSIS *** BREAST (RIGHT, SPECIMEN #1), EXCISION: INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA, APOCRINE TYPE, REMOVED_DATE CM, GRADE 2, EXTENDING TO REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN. DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, CONFINED TO REGION OF THE MASS. SEE NOTE. NOTE: Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen. The frozen section diagnosis is confirmed. BREAST (RIGHT, SPECIMEN #2), BIOPSY: NO DIAGNOSTIC ABNORMALITY RECOGNIZED. THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY. LYMPH NODES (RIGHT AXILLA): THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 18 OF 18 LYMPH NODES. Diagnosis by: Frederick Carl Koerner, M.D. Signed On: 14 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 16:31 =============================================================================== *** RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum *** RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST (RIGHT, SPECIMEN #1): The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein. The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein. See note. Note: In this laboratory, we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way (paraffin sections) and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay. 91% of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay. 96% of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay. When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections, the predictive value of a positive result was 97% and the predictive value of a negative result was 95%. In this laboratory, we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay. Sixty-five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay, and 98% of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors. THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY. THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES. Added by: Frederick Carl Koerner, M.D. Signed On: 18 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 14:27 GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name and unit number in three separate containers. Received fresh, in the Frozen Section Lab, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "right breast" is REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm yellow-red lumpectomy specimen with two short suture superiorly and and the two long suture laterally. The specimen is inked black and the lateral half is inked yellow over black. Sectioning reveals a ill-defined REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm area suspicious for infiltrating ductal carcinoma, that extends to within REMOVED_DATE cm of inked resection margin. Representative sections in cassette A through J. Received labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "breast tissue" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm fragment of breast tissue. Inked and sectioned to reveal unremarkable breast parenchyma. Submitted entirely in cassettes K through M. Labeled "right axillary nodes" is an aggregate of soft to grey firm lymph nodes, the largest measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm; representative lymph nodes submitted in cassette N through P. Resident: EDI BROGI, MD, PhD *** INTRA-OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS *** GROSS DIAGNOSIS: BREAST (RIGHT): SUSPICIOUS FOR INFILTRATING CARCINOMA CLOSEST MARGINS MEDIAL AND POSTEROMEDIAL. O.R. Resident: Ajit J. Alles, MD, PhD O.R. Diagnosis by: Michael Pins, M.D. =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT - REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID REPORTS TO: Barbara Lynn Smith, M.D. Edi Brogi, M.D. PART A: RIGHT BREAST, SPECIMEN #1 PART B: RIGHT BREAST, SPECIMEN #2 PART C: RIGHT AXILLARY LYMPH NODES\u000a[report_end]
