VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Amend/Addenda\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, partial mastectomy\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: MEHRA GOLSHAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000a********** Addended Report ***********\u000aResident: Leona A. Doyle, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Jane E. Brock, M.B., B.S., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. RIGHT BREAST SKIN SPARING SIMPLE MASTECTOMY:\u000aBenign breast tissue with fibroadenomatoid change, and calcifications in normal\u000aepithelium.\u000aNipple and skin with no significant pathologic change.\u000aB. LEFT SENTINEL LYMPH NODE BIOPSY (INCLUDING FSA):\u000aOne lymph node negative for carcinoma (6 H&E levels examined).\u000aC. LEFT BREAST SKIN SPARING SIMPLE MASTECTOMY:\u000aNo residual invasive carcinoma (3 biopsy sites identified, see NOTE).\u000aRESIDUAL DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, solid type (intermediate to high nuclear\u000agrade), without necrosis or calcifications is present associated with the most\u000asuperior biopsy site and the most inferior biopsy site (5 of 27 blocks; largest\u000afocus REMOVED_DATE cm; see NOTE).\u000aNo lymphovascular invasion is present.\u000aThe deep margin is negative for tumor.\u000aOther findings:\u000aApocrine metaplasia\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia and cysts\u000aCalcifications in normal epithelium.\u000aNOTE: The patient had 3 left breast MRI guided biopsies with clips placed\u000awithin the last 6 months. Two biopsies labeled "superior to nipple for an\u000airregular mass" and "central for an area of enhancement" (July 2008) showed\u000anormal breast tissue. A third MRI guided biopsy ((REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID; REMOVED_MONTH 2008)\u000awas for a "smooth bordered enhancing REMOVED_DATE cm mass" and was found to be grade 3\u000aER negative PR negative and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu negative invasive ductal carcinoma (0.4 cm\u000ain the biopsy) with DCIS and an extensive lymphocytic infiltrate.\u000aOn examination of the gross specimen the three clip sites were located and\u000atissue from up to 3 cm around each site was entirely submitted for histological\u000aevaluation.\u000aThe most superior biopsy site (#1) shows scattered small foci of DCIS within a\u000adense lymphocytic infiltrate adjacent to the biopsy gel plug (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), and is\u000aconsistent with the biopsy site of the invasive carcinoma. No residual invasive\u000acarcinoma is identified within a REMOVED_DATE cm vicinity of this biopsy site.\u000aThe second clip site (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) immediately inferior to the first (#2, correlating\u000awith the biopsy superior to the nipple for an irregular mass (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID)\u000ashows benign breast tissue.\u000aThe most inferior biopsy site (#3, correlating with the central biopsy for an\u000aarea of enhancement (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) has 3 areas of DCIS present (largest focus\u000a0.7 cm) in 3 slides located around the well healed prior biopsy site (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID,\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID). Hormone receptor profile for the additional foci of DCIS will be reported\u000ain an addendum.\u000aIn combination with the prior specimen (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) this tumor could be\u000aclassified as AJCC Classification (6th edition): REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDa REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID (sn)\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 45 year old female with inherited pre-disposition to breast and\u000aovarian cancer. New left breast cancer.\u000aOperation: Right breast simple mastectomy, left axilla sentinel node biopsy,\u000aleft breast.\u000aOperative Findings: Not provided.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast - high risk of cancer, and left breast cancer.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) right breast - skin sparing simple mastectomy, short/superior,\u000along/lateral.\u000aB/2) left sentinel lymph node bx #1 (fs).\u000aC/3) left breast simple mastectomy - skin sparing, short/superior,\u000along/lateral.\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "#2 - LEFT SENTINEL LYMPH NODE BX" (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aLymph node, negative for tumor.\u000aOR Consultation by: WILLIAM ROBERT WELCH, M.D.\u000aThe senior physician certifies that he/she personally conducted a gross and/or\u000amicroscopic examination of the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed\u000athe rapid diagnos(es) related thereto.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in three parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname, and medical record number.\u000aPart A, labeled "#1. Right breast skin sparing simple mastectomy, short\u000asuperior, long lateral", consists of a right mastectomy (380 g, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x\u000a3.0 cm) including skin ellipse (8.5 x REMOVED_DATE cm), everted nipple (1.6 x REMOVED_DATE cm)\u000aand an intact deep fascial plane (14.0 x REMOVED_DATE cm) inked black. No skeletal\u000amuscle is included. The skin surface and nipple are grossly unremarkable. The\u000aspecimen is oriented with sutures designating superior and lateral positions. A\u000aspecimen radiograph does not demonstrate an area corresponding to the MRI\u000adescribed enhancement in the lower outer quadrant is detected either grossly or\u000aradiographically. The radiograph shows a circumscribed area (0.3 x REMOVED_DATE cm in\u000athe upper inner quadrant) which corresponds to a nodule of firm breast\u000aparenchyma (this area is entirely submitted). The remaining breast parenchyma\u000aconsists of approximately 60% fibrous breast tissue, 40% adipose tissue. No\u000alymph nodes are identified. Representative sections of each quadrant are\u000asubmitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Upper inner quadrant to include REMOVED_DATE cm nodule, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Upper inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lower inner quadrant, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lower outer quadrant, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Upper outer quadrant, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Two lymph node candidates from upper outer quadrant, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Central breast parenchyma, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Nipple, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aPart B, labeled "#2. Left sentinel lymph node biopsy", consists of a tan-yellow\u000afragment of adipose tissue (2.4 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with a single lymph node (2.4 x\u000a1.4 x REMOVED_DATE cm) containing blue dye. The lymph node is bisected and entirely\u000asubmitted as REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and 2. Remaining adipose tissue is submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID remnant, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID remnant, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Remaining adipose tissue, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aPart C, labeled "#3. Left breast simple mastectomy, skin sparing, short\u000asuperior, long lateral", consists of a left mastectomy (353 g, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x\u000a2.2 cm), including skin (9.6 x REMOVED_DATE cm) and everted nipple (1.0 x REMOVED_DATE cm).\u000aThere is an intact deep fascial plane (15.0 x REMOVED_DATE cm), inked black. No\u000askeletal muscle is included. The overlying skin and nipple are grossly\u000aunremarkable. A specimen radiograph demonstrates three metal clips in the\u000acentral breast extending sequentially from the upper to mid central aspects.\u000aThe most superior clip has a circular appearance and is situated in a firm\u000afibrous lesion (1.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), REMOVED_DATE cm to the deep margin. This area is\u000aentirely submitted. The metal clip immediately below (rod-like appearance on\u000aspecimen radiograph) is situated in adipose tissue adjacent to grossly\u000aunremarkable breast parenchyma, present REMOVED_DATE cm to the deep margin.\u000aRepresentative sections of surrounding breast parenchyma at this area are\u000asubmitted. The third clip (rod-like appearance on specimen radiograph) is the\u000amost inferior clip and is slightly more medial to the two clips above, and is\u000aembedded in firm grossly unremarkable breast parenchyma, REMOVED_DATE cm to the deep\u000amargin. No lymph nodes are identified. Representative sections to include\u000abreast parenchyma around each clip and random quadrant sections are submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Firm area at most superior clip (clip located in cassette REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), REMOVED_DATE \u000afrags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Deep margin at most superior clip, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Breast parenchyma surrounding second (middle) clip (clip located\u000ain cassette REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), multi frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Deep margin adjacent to second clip.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Breast parenchyma surrounding third clip (clip located in cassette\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), REMOVED_DATE frags, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Deep margin adjacent to third clip, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Upper outer quadrant, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lower outer quadrant, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Upper inner quadrant, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lower inner quadrant, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Central breast parenchyma (lower), 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Nipple, 2 frags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Additional breast parenchyma surrounding site of upper 2 clips,\u000a1-2 frags, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Additional breast parenchyma surrounding site of most inferior\u000aclip, 1 frag each, RSS\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aLDO/lp\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000