rior margin, long suture designating the lateral margin, and whip\u000astitch designating the posterior margin. There is a needle localization wire\u000aloosely placed, entering through the medial inferior aspect of the specimen and\u000aexiting through the lateral posterior aspect of the specimen. The specimen has\u000abeen previously inked per the surgeon according to the pathology protocol\u000a(superior/red, inferior/green, medial/orange, lateral/yellow, anterior/blue,\u000aand posterior/black). The specimen is serially sectioned from superior to\u000ainferior. There is an irregular red/brown granular area (1.4 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm)\u000aadjacent to the needle localization wire with a metallic clip within the\u000acavity. The biopsy cavity is located REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom the lateral margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000aposterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior\u000amargin. No additional lesions or areas of disruption are grossly identified.\u000aThe remainder of the breast parenchyma is tan/yellow and homogenous with focal\u000aareas of dense white fibrous tissue. The specimen is submitted in its\u000aentirety.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Superior margin, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Sequential cross sections superior to inferior (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID to\u000ainclude metallic clip, blocks REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID to contain biopsy cavity), 1 frag\u000aeach, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Inferior margin, 4 frags, ESS.\u000asek/lp\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Lucian R 