VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aLESTER, SUSAN, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST BIOPSY, WIRE LOCALIZATION FOR A MASS:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA AND DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU.\u000aSYNOPSIS:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA:\u000aSize: - REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aMultifocal? - No\u000aHistologic Type: - Tubular\u000aHistologic Grade (SBR): - I(Well)\u000aNuclear Grade: - Intermediate\u000aEIC: - Negative\u000aLymphovascular invasion: - Absent\u000aDermal lymphatic invasion: - N/A\u000aSkin invasion: - N/A\u000aSkeletal muscle invasion: - N/A\u000aFinal Margins (invasive): - Positive (ink on tumor) (not\u000aoriented), over a broad front\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aTypes: - Solid, cribriform\u000aNuclear grade: - Intermediate\u000aCalcifications in DCIS: - Absent\u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS: - Absent\u000aDCIS is present as a minor component of the invasive carcinoma and is not\u000aseen away from the invasive carcinoma.\u000aDCIS is close to the margin in the region of the positive margin for\u000ainvasive carcinoma.\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - Absent\u000aOTHER FINDINGS:\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia.\u000aThe core biopsy site is present less than REMOVED_DATE cm from the carcinoma.\u000aHyalinized fibroadenoma with calcifications.\u000aAJCC CLASSIFICATION: REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDb pNX MX\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER/PR/HER-2): - Pending\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for invasive carcinoma (block 1):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) NEGATIVE (0)\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000ainvasive carcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but\u000aonly a portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity\u000ain >10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Infiltrating ductal ca, right breast 1988. Left breast REMOVED_DATE core\u000abiopsy with benign findings, does not correlate with spiculated mass.\u000aOperation: Left needle-directed biopsy\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Left needle-directed biopsy\u000aRADIOLOGY REPORT: Mass is seen in specimen. C. Denison, MD\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by WOLGAMOT,GREGORY M.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "left needle-directed biopsy", and consists of a single fragment of\u000atan/yellow fibroadipose tissue (5 x 5 x 1 cm). There is no orientation to the\u000aspecimen. The specimen is received without the wire. Together with the\u000aspecimen, there is a mammogram which is reviewed and shows a mass within the\u000aspecimen. The specimen is entirely inked in black. On sectioning, a\u000atan/white, firm, ill-defined mass (0.6 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) is identified. The mass\u000ais grossly at the resection margin. The mass is entirely submitted for\u000ahistologic analysis, as well as representative sections of the remainder of the\u000abreast tissue.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  nodule, 3 frag, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  representative sections of breast tissue, multi frag, RSS\u000aafn\u000aReports to: HECHTMAN, HERBERT, B. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
