k) and inferior (green) resection margin. The remainder of the specimen\u000aconsists of 90% yellow adipose and 10% tan/pink fibrous tissue. The specimen\u000awas previously inked by the surgeon according to standard pathology protocol:\u000aposterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral\u000a= yellow; medial = orange. No further lesions are noted. The biopsy site and\u000athe adjacent margins are extensively sampled.\u000aMicros REMOVED_DATE  biopsy site in relation to inferior margin, 4 frags, RSS.\u000aMicros REMOVED_DATE  biopsy site in relation to posterior margin, 4 frags, RSS.\u000aMicros 9&10: biopsy site in relation to superior margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicros 11&13: biopsy site in relation to lateral margin, 3 frags, RSS.\u000aMicros 14&15: biopsy site in relation to medial margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicros 16&17: anterior resection margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicros 18&19: representative section of biopsy site, 2 frags, RSS.\u000atb\u000aReports to: OSTEEN, ROBERT, T. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: LYMPH NODE BIOPSY\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
