VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Amend/Addenda\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: ESTHER RHEI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000a********** Revised Report **********\u000aResident: Li Chen, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Christopher D. M. Fletcher, M.D. FRCPath\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZATION FOR CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA, see NOTE.\u000aMargins :\u000aNegative (> REMOVED_DATE cm) - Anterior, lateral, superior, inferior\u000aClose (0.1 to REMOVED_DATE cm) - Posterior REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aVery close(<0.1 cm from margin)- Medial\u000aOTHER FINDINGS\u000aCore biopsy site\u000aCalcifications in benign epithelium\u000aNOTE : Although the degree of atypia (focally) borders on DCIS, given the very\u000asmall size of the lesion (approx. 1mm at most) and the fact that the subsequent\u000are-excision (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) shows no evidence of adjacent, more obvious DCIS,\u000athen, after review with the Breast Service (Drs. Susan Lester, Deborah Dillon\u000aand Andrea Richardson), it is the concensus view that the abnormality in this\u000aspecimen is best classified as severe ADH and not as DCIS (as originally\u000adiagnosed).\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 59 year old female, S/P L breast UOQ core bx REMOVED_DATE  revealing\u000aepithelial hyperplasia in cribriform pattern with atypia (seen only in deeper\u000alevels of Block One). ? ADH - best evaluated with excision.\u000aOperation: L breast WL bx.\u000aOperative Findings: Not provided.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Abnormal mammogram.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1) left breast tissue, short stitch/superior, long/lateral, whip stitch on\u000adeep margin (to mammo).\u000aRADIOLOGY:\u000aClip and wire intact. DL.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in one part, labeled with the patient's name,\u000aunit number, and "#1. Left breast tissue", and consists of a REMOVED_DATE (medial to\u000alateral) x REMOVED_DATE (superior to inferior) x REMOVED_DATE (anterior to posterior) cm breast\u000aexcision specimen with localization wire in place and a short suture marking\u000athe superior margin and long suture marking the lateral margin, whipstitch on\u000adeep margin. An accompanying specimen radiograph demonstrates a clip in the\u000acenter of the specimen, adjacent to the localization wire. The specimen is\u000ainked for the evaluation of margins posterior equals black, anterior equals\u000ablue, superior equals red, inferior equals green, lateral equals yellow, medial\u000aequals orange. The specimen is bisected along the localization wire and the\u000aclip is identified in the center of the specimen. A gross lesion at the site\u000aof the clip is not seen. The specimen consists of 50% white dense fibrous\u000atissue and 50% of yellow adipose tissue. The specimen is serially sectioned\u000afrom superior to inferior and entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Serial section from superior to inferior with clip site in\u000acassette REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, multi frags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Christopher D. M. Fletcher M.D. FRCPath, on REMOVED_DATE \u000aAmendment #1 by Christopher D. M. Fletcher M.D. FRCPath, Electronically\u000asigned on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
