VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST BIOPSY W/O MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aWELCH, WILLIAM, ROBERT, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by WELCH,WILLIAM ROBERT,M.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZED BIOPSY FOR A MASS AND CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aFibroadenoma (0.6 cm), associated with small scattered calcifications,\u000aand epithelial hyperplasia.\u000aCysts and sclerosing adenosis.\u000aPrior core biopsy site is identified.\u000aNOTE: Reviewed by Dr. T. Jacobs (Breast Pathology).\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 37 year old s/p core bx REMOVED_DATE  for (L) breast periareolar\u000amass - fibroepithelial lesion with atypia.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Left breast tissue.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Mass and calcs are in specimen. L. Frost, MD\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by LOMO,LESLEY C.,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in one part, labeled with the patient's name,\u000aunit number and "#1 left breast tissue, long lateral, deep stitch deep margin,\u000ashort medial" and consists of a single, wire localized breast biopsy specimen\u000a(3.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with a short suture to designate medial, a long suture to\u000adesignate lateral, and another suture to designate deep margin and contains a\u000aneedle localization wire. The specimen has been previously inked by the\u000asurgeon per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior =\u000ablack; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow;\u000amedial = orange. An accompanying radiograph shows the specimen with a needle\u000alocalization wire. The specimen is serially sectioned from anterior to\u000aposterior, revealing predominantly white, rubbery fibrous tissue with focal\u000aareas of hemorrhage. No masses or lesions suspicious for malignancy are\u000aidentified. The entire specimen is submitted.\u000aMicro 1: anterior perpendicular margin, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro RE