VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Amend/Addenda\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast core needle biopsy\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: MITRA NOROOZIAN M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000a********** Addended Report ***********\u000aResident: Martin C Chang, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Susan Lester, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, UPPER OUTER, 11 G ULTRASOUND GUIDED CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR AN\u000aILL-DEFINED MASS AND CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA, well differentiated (modified Bloom-Richardson grade\u000aI/III), measuring at least REMOVED_DATE cm in size (see note). Calcifications are\u000apresent within the invasive carcinoma.\u000aNo lymphovascular invasion is seen in this limited specimen.\u000aNo definite carcinoma in situ is seen in this limited specimen.\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia is present.\u000aAdenosis with calcifications is present in the adjacent tissue.\u000aNote: The carcinoma would be classified as a tubular carcinoma. Final\u000aclassification should be made after excision.\u000aImmunohistochemical analysis for estrogen receptor, progesterone receptor, and\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu will be performed and reported in an addendum.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: History of DCIS on left. Calcifications on right ? FA, rule out CA,\u000ashadowing mass seen in RUOQ.\u000aBreast Imaging Findings: ill-defined.\u000aOperation: 11-gauge ultrasound.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: FA with calcifications, rule out cancer.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Right breast shadowing mass at 9:30-10 o'clock, 11-gauge vacuum-assisted\u000aUS x4. Specimens in yellow cassette.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit\u000anumber, and "right breast yellow", consists of cores of fibroadipose tissue,\u000asequestered in a yellow cassette and aggregating REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Right breast cores, multi frags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000adb/ag\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a1/11/2007\u000aSurgical Addendum: (1/16/07)\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for invasive carcinoma (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) NEGATIVE (0)\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000acarcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but only\u000aa portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in >10%\u000aof tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in\u000a>10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aAddendum #1 by Andrea L Richardson M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a1/16/2007\u000a[report_end]
