VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Amend/Addenda\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, partial mastectomy\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: JULIE L JONES M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000a********** Addended Report ***********\u000aResident: Eleanor Y. Chen, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Vania Nose, MD, PhD\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. LEFT BREAST, WIRE-LOCALIZATION FOR CALCIFICATIONS (1 SPECIMEN):\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU AND LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aSYNOPSIS:\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU - Present, solid, cribriform, papillary,\u000aMicropapillary.\u000aNuclear grade: Intermediate.\u000aCalcifications in DCIS: - Present\u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS: - Present\u000aMicroinvasion (<0.1 cm): - Present-single focus (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID)\u000aExtent of DCIS:\u000aNumber of blocks/total: REMOVED_DATE blocks\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aMargins (DCIS):\u000aNegative (>0.3 cm) Superior, medial, anterior.\u000aClose (0.1-0.3 cm) (0.2 cm) lateral (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID)\u000aVery close (<0.1 cm) inferior (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), posterior (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID)\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU: Present\u000aOTHER FINDINGS: ADH, Biopsy cavity prominent, core biopsy site, Columnar\u000aalteration of lobules with prominent snouts and secretions, Complex sclerosing\u000alesion, Papilloma, Sclerosing adenosis, Calcifications in benign epithelium.\u000aAJCC Classification (6th Edition): REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Nx Mx.\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER, PR, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID): Pending (REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID)\u000aNOTE: Dr. S Lester, Breast Pathology Service, reviewed selected slide of the\u000acase, and concurs.\u000aB., C. RIGHT BREAST, EXCISION WIRE LOCALIZATION FOR A MASS AND SENTINEL NODE\u000aBIOPSIES (2 SPECIMENS); PARTS B (INCLUDING FSA) AND C.\u000aINVASIVE TUBULAR CARCINOMA\u000aSYNOPSIS:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA\u000aSize - REMOVED_DATE CM\u000aMultifocal - No\u000aHistologic Type - Tubular\u000aHistologic Grade (SBR) - II (Moderate)\u000aNuclear Grade - Low\u000aEIC - N/A\u000aLymphovascular invasion - Absent\u000aDermal lymphatic invasion - N/A\u000aSkin invasion - N/A\u000aSkeletal muscle invasion - N/A\u000aFinal Margins (invasive)\u000aNegative (>0.3 cm) - All\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU - Absent\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - Absent\u000aLYMPH NODES\u000aSentinel lymph nodes\u000a(3 H&E levels examined): - Negative\u000aNumber of positive nodes - 0\u000aNumber of nodes examined - 2\u000aTOTAL POSITIVE NODES (all specimens)- REMOVED_DATE \u000aOTHER FINDINGS: ADH, Core biopsy site, Columnar alteration of lobules with\u000aprominent snouts and secretions, Complex sclerosing lesion,\u000aSclerosing adenosis, Calcifications in benign epithelium,\u000aAJCC CLASSIFICATION (6th edition) - pREMOVED_ACCESSION_IDc pREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID(sn) MX\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER/PR/HER-2) - Performed previously\u000aNOTE: Dr. S Lester, Breast Pathology Service, reviewed selected slide of the\u000acase, and concurs.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Left breast, DCIS. Right breast, IDC.\u000aOperation: Bilateral wire localized partial mastectomy, right sentinel node\u000abiopsy.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Bilateral breast cancer.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Left wire localized partial mastectomy, short superior, long lateral to\u000amiddle.\u000aB/2. Right axillary node x2, FS.\u000aC/3. Right wire localized partial mastectomy, short stitch equals superior,\u000along stitch equals lateral to middle.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Biopsy clip, lumpectomy site, + Ca++ all included in specimen.\u000aCore biopsy clip and cluster of calcification in specimen. (Hendler Bidwell).\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "#2 RT AXILLARY SENTINEL NODES X 2" (FSA 1, 2, 3, 4):\u000aTwo (2) lymph nodes, negative for tumor.\u000aOR Consultation by: MICHAEL W. BENNETT, M.B.B.C.H.\u000aThe senior physician certifies that he/she personally conducted a gross and/or\u000amicroscopic examination of the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed\u000athe rapid diagnos(es) related thereto.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in three parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart A, "#1. Left partial mastectomy, short superior, long lateral", consists\u000aof an ovoid fragment of yellow/tan to pink/tan fibroadipose tissue (7.0 M-L x\u000a5.3 S-I per surgeon with two sutures as indicated).\u000aThe specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins:\u000aposterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow;\u000amedial/orange.\u000aThere are two needle localization wires in place. Wire one enters the\u000asuperoanterior aspect of the specimen with no clear exit point. Wire two\u000aenters the anterolateral aspect of the specimen and exit the inferoposterior\u000aaspect of the specimen. The specimen was previously radiographed (per\u000aradiologist "by sequence, lumpectomy site, and calcifications all included in\u000aspecimen"). The specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral and to a\u000atotal of 11 sites (slice one equals medial, slice 11 equals lateral). In\u000aslices four through eight, there is an ill defined, stellate, indurated\u000apink/tan fibrous lesion (? retracted cavity, REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) within which a\u000ametal clip is identified (slice eight) through which needle localization wire\u000aone traverses. The lesion comes within REMOVED_DATE cm at the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aat the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm at the anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm at the posterior\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm at the medial margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm at the lateral margin. In\u000aslice 9, REMOVED_DATE cm superolateral to the aforementioned fibrous, there is a second\u000aill-defined dense nodular white/tan fibrous lesion (1.3 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) which\u000aabuts the superior margin and comes within REMOVED_DATE cm of the posterior margin.\u000aThe remainder of the breast parenchyma is composed of approximately 75%\u000ayellow/tan lobulated adipose tissue. Needle localization wire #2 traverses the\u000auninvolved breast parenchyma inferior to the aforementioned larger fibrous\u000alesion/cavity. The specimen is entirely sequentially submitted from medial to\u000alateral as follows:\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 1/medial margin perpendicularly sectioned, multi frags\u000atotal, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 2 section, 3 frags total, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 3 section, 3 frags total, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 4 to include larger fibrous lesion/cavity, sectioned, 3\u000afrags total, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 5 to include larger fibrous lesion/cavity, section, 4\u000afrags total, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 6 to include larger fibrous lesion/cavity, section, 1 frag\u000ain each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 7 to include large fibrous lesion/cavity, section, 1 frag\u000ain each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 8 to include remainder of large fibrous lesion/cavity and\u000aportion of smaller ill-defined fibrous lesion (in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID), 4 frags total, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 9 to include remainder of smaller ill-defined fibrous\u000alesion, section, 1 frag in each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 10, section, 1 frag in each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 11/lateral margin perpendicularly sectioned, multi frags\u000atotal, ESS.\u000aPart B, "#2. Right axillary sentinel node x2", received fresh in frozen section\u000aroom consists of two tan/yellow lobulated adipose tissue (3.1 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in\u000aaggregate) including two lymph node candidate (2.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000ax REMOVED_DATE cm). Each of the lymph node candidate was previously inked and bisected.\u000aThe first lymph node candidate was previously entirely frozen as FSA-1 and\u000aFSA-2. The second lymph node candidate was previously entirely frozen as FSA-3\u000aand FSA-4.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: FSA-1 and FSA-2 remnants respectively, 1 frag in each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: FSA-3 and FSA-4 remnants respectively, 1 frag in each, ESS.\u000aPart C, "#3. Right wire localized partial mastectomy, short - superior, long -\u000alateral", consists of an ovoid fragment of yellow/tan to pink/tan fibroadipose\u000atissue (5.8 M-L x REMOVED_DATE A-P x REMOVED_DATE F-I cm), which is oriented per surgeon with two\u000asutures as indicated.\u000aThe specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins:\u000aposterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow;\u000amedial/orange.\u000aThere are two needle localization wires in place. Needle localization wire #1\u000aenters the lateral aspect of the specimen and exits the superomedial aspect of\u000athe specimen. Needle localization wire #2 enters the inferoposterior aspect of\u000athe specimen and exits the medial aspect of the specimen. The specimen was\u000apreviously radiographed (per radiologist "core biopsy clip and cluster of\u000acalcification in specimen"). The specimen is serially sectioned from lateral\u000ato medial including total of 9 slices (slice 1 equals lateral, slice 9 equals\u000amedial). In slices 3 through 5, there is an ill-defined, indurated, dense\u000awhite/pink lesion (1.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with multiple areas of hemorrhage (0.3\u000ato REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest dimension). A small metal clip is identified within the\u000alesion in slice 4. The lesion comes within REMOVED_DATE cm of the anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE \u000acm of the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm of the\u000alateral margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm of the medial margin. Wire one and wire two\u000atraverse the uninvolved breast parenchyma along the superior and inferior\u000alesion. The remainder of the cut surface is composed of approximately 30%\u000adense/nodular white/tan fibrous tissue and 70% yellow/tan lobulated adipose\u000atissue with no additional discrete lesions identified.\u000aRepresentative sections are submitted as follows:\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 1/lateral margin perpendicularly sectioned, multi frags\u000atotal, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 3 to include ill-defined mass, sectioned, 1 frag in each,\u000aESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 4 to include mass, bisected, 1 frag in each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 5 to include remainder of mass, bisected, 1 frag in each,\u000aESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 7, separate area of dense fibrous tissue with superior,\u000aposterior, and inferior margins, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice 9/medial margin, perpendicularly sectioned, multi frags\u000atotal, ESS.\u000aPlease note that approximately 75% of the specimen to include the mass in\u000aentirety is submitted.\u000aLMB/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_DATE \u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Vania Nose MD, PhD, on REMOVED_DATE \u000aAmendment #1 by Vania Nose MD, PhD, Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM:\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for DCIS of the left breast (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor POSITIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor POSITIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) NEGATIVE (1+)\u000aNote: The patient's right breast tubular breast carcinoma is also positive for\u000aER and PR and negative for REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (see REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000acarcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but only\u000aa portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane immunoreactivity in >10%\u000aof tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity in\u000a>10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aAddendum #1 by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
