VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID OUTSIDE SLIDE CONSULT - BREAST\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aLESTER, SUSAN, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aCONSULT SLIDES FROM CAPE COD HOSPITAL, HYANNIS, MA:\u000aLEFT BREAST ULTRASOUND GUIDED CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY FOR AN IRREGULAR/SOLID MASS\u000a(03:REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID; REMOVED_DATE ):\u000aPOORLY DIFFERENTIATED CARCINOMA, at least REMOVED_DATE cm in size in this limited\u000aspecimen with tumor necrosis.\u000aNo lymphovascular invasion is seen.\u000aNo carcinoma is present in this limited specimen.\u000aSpecial studies were performed at an outside institution with the\u000afollowing results (reviewed):\u000aESTROGEN RECEPTOR - NEGATIVE\u000aPROGESTERONE RECEPTOR - NEGATIVE\u000aNormal epithelial cells are appropriately immunoreactive for\u000aestrogen and progesterone receptors.\u000aThe carcinoma is poorly differentiated and there is no in situ component.\u000aAlthough the findings could be consistent with breast carcinoma, the\u000apossibility of metastasis from another site should be considered.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Breast cancer.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Consult slides.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by WITKIEWICZ,AGNIESKA K.,M.D.\u000aReceived from Cape Cod Hospital, Department of Pathology, 27 Park Street,\u000aHyannis, MA REMOVED_CASE_ID, are six (6) slides.\u000aThe slides are labeled "03:REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID" and sublabeled "I", "II", "ER(+)", "ER(-)",\u000a"PR(+)" and "PR(-)", corresponding to a left breast ultrasound guided core\u000abiopsy (0.1 x REMOVED_DATE cm) performed on REMOVED_DATE  according to the accompanying\u000apathology report bearing the patient's name.\u000aReports to: IGLEHART, JAMES, DIRK M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: OUTSIDE SLIDE CONSULT - BREAST\u000a[report_end]
