VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID SENTINEL LYMPH NODE\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aFLETCHER, CHRISTOPHER, D.M., M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by FLETCHER,CHRISTOPHER,D.M.,M.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST, LUMPECTOMY FOR A MASS (specimen #3 of 3 specimens) AND SENTINEL\u000aNODE BIOPSIES (specimen #1 of 3 specimens):\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA, POORLY DIFFERENTIATED, ONE (1) FOCUS\u000aNEGATIVE LYMPH NODE(S)\u000aSYNOPSIS:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA\u000aSize - REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aMultifocal - no\u000aHistologic Type - poorly differentiated (no ducts)\u000aHistologic Grade (SBR) - III (poor)\u000aNuclear Grade - high\u000aEIC - negative\u000aLymphovascular invasion - absent\u000aDermal lymphatic invasion - absent\u000aSkin invasion - absent\u000aSkeletal muscle invasion - N/A\u000aFinal Margins (invasive) -\u000aNegative (>0.3 cm) - all margins\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU - absent\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - absent\u000aLYMPH NODES\u000aSentinel Lymph Nodes - negative (3 H&E levels examined)\u000aNumber of positive nodes - 0\u000aNumber of nodes examined - 2\u000aTOTAL POSITIVE NODES (all specimens)- 0:2\u000aOTHER FINDINGS\u000aApocrine metaplasia\u000aCalcifications in benign epithelium\u000aAJCC CLASSIFICATION (6th edition) - REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID pREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID MX\u000aNOTE:\u000aImmunohistochemistry performed at BWH demonstrates the following staining\u000aprofile in tumor cells:\u000aPositive - ER (focal, weak), keratin REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID (focal), EMA (focal)\u000aNegative - synaptophysin, chromogranin, NFP, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, S-100, TTF-1\u000aHER-2/neu, PR\u000aThe poorly differentiated morphology in this case raises the possibility\u000aof BRCA-1 predisposition. Immunostains have helped to exclude the\u000apossibility of a metastasis from the most likely morphologic mimics of\u000athis lesion. The case was also reviewed by Dr. Susan Lester and Dr.\u000aJames Connolly who concur.\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "LEFT BREAST, BIOPSY" (specimen #2 of 3 specimens):\u000aBenign breast tissue with atypical ductal hyperplasia (block #6),\u000aapocrine metaplasia, sclerosing adenosis, calcifications in benign\u000aepithelium, and duct ectasia.\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Left breast cancer core biopsy, positive calcification under left\u000anipple.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast cancer.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1 - left sentinal lymph nodes (perm).\u000a#2 - left breast biopsy with needle stitch, long/lateral,\u000ashort/superior.\u000a#3 - left breast lumpectomy, stitch, long/lateral, short/superior.\u000aRadiology #2: Calcification in specimen\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by YOU,MINGJIAN JAMES,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received in three parts, each labeled with the patient's name\u000aand medical record number.\u000aPart one, "#1 - left sentinal lymph nodes", consists of a fragment of\u000ayellow/pink soft tissue (2.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). Two lymph nodes (1.8 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE \u000acm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) are identified. The lymph nodes and attached\u000ayellow/tan soft tissue are bisected and entirely submitted.\u000aMicro #1: Larger lymph node and attached tissue, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro #2: Smaller lymph node and attached tissue, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aPart two, "#2 - left breast biopsy", consists of a fragment of yellow/pink/tan\u000asoft tissue (5.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The surgeon placed a short and a long\u000astitches to indicate the superior and lateral margins, respectively. The\u000aspecimen was radiographed, which showed the localization wire and two possible\u000acalcification areas. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the\u000aevaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red;\u000ainferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. The specimen is\u000asectioned from medial to lateral margins, revealing approximately 90% of\u000ayellow/tan adipose tissue and approximately 10% white/tan fibrous tissue.\u000aRadiographs are taken in the department of pathology, which reveals the\u000acalcification areas. The calcification areas and fibrous tissue are entirely\u000asubmitted.\u000aMicro #3: Lateral and inferior margins, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro #4: Inferior, anterior and lateral margins, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro #5: Posterior, lateral and inferior margins, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro #6: Superior, anterior and inferior margins, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro #7: Superior, lateral, inferior and posterior margins, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro #8: Superior, medial and inferior margins, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro #9: Posterior and superior margins, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro #10: Superior, lateral and inferior margins, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro #11: Superior, lateral and inferior margins, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro #12: Posterior and inferior margins, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro #13: Superior and medial margins, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro #14: Superior, inferior and medial margins, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro #15: Superior and medial margins, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro #16: Superior and medial margins, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aPart three, "#3 - left breast lumpectomy", consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aspecimen with a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm brown/tan skin ellipse. The surgeon placed short\u000aand long stitches to indicate the superior and lateral margins, respectively.\u000aThe specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins:\u000aposterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral =\u000ayellow; medial = orange. The specimen is sectioned, revealing approximately\u000a70% of yellow/tan adipose tissue and approximately 30% of white/tan fibrous\u000atissue. There is a white/pink/tan mass (2.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) that is REMOVED_DATE cm to\u000athe posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to the inferior\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm to the lateral margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to the medial margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm\u000ato the anterior margin. Representative mass was submitted to Tumor Bank. No\u000adefinitive biopsy cavity is identified.\u000aMicro #17: Mass, medial and posterior margins, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro #18: Mass, medial and posterior margins, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro #19: Mass, posterior and inferior margins, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro #20: Mass, anterior margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro #21: Mass, superior and anterior margins, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro #22: Mass, inferior and posterior margins, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro #23: Medial margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro #24: Lateral and superior margins, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro #25: Lateral margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro #26: Skin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aReports to: IGLEHART, JAMES, DIRK M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: SENTINEL LYMPH NODE\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
