pecimen is composed 75% of yellow lobulated adipose tissue and 30% of\u000afibrous tissue; located REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior, REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial, and\u000aabutting both superior and inferior margins, is a white fibrous area grossly\u000aconsistent with prior biopsy cavity measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. No other\u000agross mass lesions are identified.\u000aMicro 1: skin ellipse, lateral half, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 2: skin ellipse, medial half, 5 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  left breast tissue from anterior to posterior in serial sections,\u000amulti frags, ESS.\u000aMicro 15&16: posterior edge, multi frags, ESS.\u000amcc\u000aReports to: IGLEHART, JAMES, DIRK M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
