s: posterior = black; anterior\u000a= blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange.\u000aContained in the breast parenchyma is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm tan-gray, partially\u000aencapsulated lobulated mass extending to within REMOVED_DATE cm of the superior, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom the inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial, REMOVED_DATE cm from the deep, REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000athe anterior, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral resection margins. A representative\u000asection of the tumor and of normal breast are submitted to the tumor bank.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  specimen and serial sections from medial to lateral, multi frags,\u000aESS.\u000amcc\u000aReports to: CHRISTIAN, ROGER, L. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
