ire in the specimen. The specimen shows a short\u000asuture, which per surgeon designates the superior margin and a long suture,\u000awhich per surgeon designate the lateral margin. A whip suture is not present.\u000aThe specimen is previously inked per protocol: posterior/black; anterior/blue;\u000asuperior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. A wire is\u000aentering the anterior/superior/medial part of the specimen. The specimen is\u000abisected along the wire. There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm firm, white/tan mass\u000awith focal hemorrhage associated with the clip, which is located REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000athe medial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin, and\u000a1.8 cm from inferior margin. The remainder of the specimen consists of 80%\u000ayellow multilobulated adipose tissue and 20% firm white fibrous tissue. No\u000aother masses are identified.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Mass and medial, anterior, posterior margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Mass and anterior, posterior, superior, medial margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Mass and superior margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Remainder mass, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Additional posterior margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lateral and inferior margin, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000aSK/mmm\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Alessandra F Nascimento M.D., Electronically signed on\u000a3/19/2007\u000a[report_end]
