VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: GREGORY J KANE M.D.\u000aCASE: BG-06-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Lynette M Sholl, M.D.\u000aPathologist: William R Welch, M.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA) SPECIMEN LABELED "RIGHT BREAST TISSUE, WIRE LOCALIZATION FOR A MASS AND\u000aCLIP":\u000aEpithelial hyperplasia and pseudoangiomatous stromal hyperplasia.\u000aCore biopsy site with fat necrosis and foreign body giant cell\u000areaction encapsulated by dense fibrosis.\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy (entire lesion submitted for\u000ahistologic evaluation).\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Dilated duct and 2 suspicious areas on ultrasound and mammogram. Core\u000abiopsy -> PASH.\u000aOperation: Left resection and wire localization\u000aOperative Findings: No palpable lesion\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Suspicious area right breast\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aRight breast tissue - short marks lateral and long is inferior -> mammo\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patients name, unit number,\u000aand "right breast tissue", and consists of one wire localized breast excision\u000aspecimen (5.1 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), with a long stitch designated inferior and a\u000ashort stitch designated lateral. The specimen is received with a localizing\u000awire in place. An accompanying radiogram demonstrates that a mass and wire are\u000apresent within the specimen. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for\u000athe evaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red;\u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. The specimen is serially\u000asectioned to reveal a firm, white, homogeneous nodule (0.7 cm in greatest\u000adimension) abutting the posterior margin and approximately 2 mm from the\u000ainferior and anterior margins and 1 cm from the medial margin and distant from\u000athe lateral and superior margins. Adjacent to the nodule is an area of\u000asoftening, hemorrhage and granular material, consistent with prior biopsy site.\u000aA clip cannot be grossly identified. The remainder of the breast tissue\u000aconsists of approximately 70% unremarkable yellow adipose tissue and 30%\u000aunremarkable white fibrous tissue. The specimen is entirely submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - mass adjacent prior biopsy site, ?clip, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - remainder of white nodule, multiple frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - sections including superior, posterior, anterior, inferior\u000amargins, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - lateral margin, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID - medial and inferior margins, multiple frags, ESS.\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by William R Welch M.D., Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE \u000a[report_end]
