he medial margin, 1 cm from the lateral margin, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom the superior margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin. The remainder of\u000athe specimen consists of yellow/white adipose tissue. No areas grossly\u000asuspicious for invasive carcinoma are seen. The entire biopsy site and\u000arepresentative sections of the margins are submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  entire biopsy site, 1 frag each, ESS.\u000aMicro 6 : inferior margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 7 : superior margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 8 : deep margin, 2 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 9 : medial margin, 3 frags, RSS.\u000aMicro 10 : lateral margin, 4 frags,RSS.\u000aMicro 11 : lesion and skin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aReports to: MATORY, YVEDT M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
