VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aWELCH, WILLIAM, ROBERT, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by WELCH,WILLIAM ROBERT,M.D.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A MASS AND A CLIP:\u000aATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA involving a ductal adenoma (best seen in\u000aslides 13 and 14; levels examined) (see note).\u000aThe ductal adenoma measures REMOVED_DATE cm in size and is associated with the\u000aprior core needle biopsy site.\u000aADH is also focally present in adjacent breast tissue (blocks 11 and 12;\u000alevels examined).\u000aNote: Immunoperoxidase studies for p63 and smooth muscle alpha actin\u000areveal myoepithelial cells within the ductal adenoma and in areas of ADH.\u000aThe adenoma, and the areas of ADH, are < REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior-lateral\u000amargin. Due to the proximity to the margin, involvement by an adjacent\u000aarea of DCIS cannot be excluded.\u000aThis case was reviewed by Dr. Stuart Schnitt and Dr. Susan Lester, who\u000aconcur with this interpretation.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 48 year old female s/p REMOVED_DATE left mastectomy for diffuse DCIS, REMOVED_DATE \u000aright reduction, s/p REMOVED_DATE  right core biopsy of a 9 mm mass revealing\u000aatypical ductal hyperplasia, approaching DCIS.\u000aOperation: Right breast wire localization excision\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast mass/ADH\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1. Right breast tissue\u000aRADIOLOGY REPORT: Mass and clip in specimen. C. Denison,MD\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by KINDELBERGER,DAVID W.,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number\u000aand "#1. right breast wire localized excision", and consists of a single\u000afragment of yellow/tan fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE cm from lateral to\u000amedial x REMOVED_DATE cm from anterior to posterior x REMOVED_DATE cm superior to inferior. The\u000aspecimen was inked by the surgeon per pathology protocol for the evaluation of\u000amargins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green;\u000alateral = yellow; medial = orange. A metal localizing wire is present within\u000athe specimen.\u000aAn accompanying specimen radiograph demonstrates the presence of a localizing\u000awire, a metal clip, and an associated mass within the specimen.\u000aIn the area surrounding the clip is a firm, well-circumscribed white nodule\u000ameasuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The mass appears to abut the lateral and\u000aanterior margins. There is a focal area of hemorrhage adjacent to the nodule,\u000aconsistent with prior biopsy site. The specimen is composed of approximately\u000a85% adipose and 15% fibrous tissue. The specimen is entirely submitted for\u000ahistologic examination.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  right breast excision from posterior to anterior, mult frags,\u000aESS (region of nodule and clip in blocks REMOVED_DATE ).\u000adk\u000aReports to: KAELIN, CAROLYN, MARY, M.PH. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
