VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aMUELLER, JAMES, D, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by MUELLER,JAMES D,M.D.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, EXCISION, CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU WITH MICROINVASION\u000aSYNOPSIS:\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aTypes - comedo, cribriform\u000aNuclear grade - high\u000aCalcifications in DCIS - absent\u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - present\u000aMicroinvasion (<0.1cm) - present, single focus (block #14)\u000aExtent of DCIS\u000aNumber of blocks:total - 3:15 (#13, #14, #15)\u000aFinal Margins (DCIS)\u000aPositive (ink on DCIS)\u000aOTHER FINDINGS\u000aCysts\u000aCalcifications in benign epithelium\u000aCore biopsy site\u000aAJCC CLASSIFICATION - REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDmic pNx MX\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER/PR/HER-2) - not reported\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe area of microinvasion is in block 15 (not block 14). The area of\u000amicroinvasion is not present on the deeper levels used for immunohistochemical\u000aanalysis. Therefore, the results are for DCIS.\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies were performed on formalin fixed tissue with the\u000afollowing results for DCIS (block 15):\u000aEstrogen receptor NEGATIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor NEGATIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (c-erb-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID) POSITIVE (3+)\u000aNote: Normal epithelial cells are appropriately immunoreactive for estrogen\u000aand progesterone receptors.\u000aInterpretation:\u000aHormone receptor analysis: The percent of immunoreactive nuclei in the\u000ainvasive carcinoma is assessed visually and reported as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but\u000aonly a portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity\u000ain >10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Calcifications in right breast.\u000aOperation: Right needle localized breast biopsy.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Calcifications right breast.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Tissue from right breast.\u000aRadiology: Ca++ in specimen.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by OH,KIRSTINE YUNG-TING,M.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "#1, tissue from right breast", and also a screening mammogram. The\u000ascreening mammogram shows a single fragment of tissue with a localizing wire\u000aand thick calcification a linear array. The fragment of tissue is yellow-pink\u000aand tan, fibroadipose (4.7 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm), with a single wire embedded in it.\u000aThe wire is removed and the unoriented specimen is inked blue. Serial\u000asectioning reveals the specimen is comprised of approximately 40% firm dense\u000awhie fibrous tissue with intermixed yellow fatty tissue. A central area of\u000ahemorrhage with orange discoloration consistent with fat necrosis is identified\u000a(0.2 cm in diameter).\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  breast tissue, REMOVED_DATE frags each, ESS.\u000ako\u000aReports to: CHRISTIAN, ROGER, L. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
