VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID SENTINEL LYMPH NODE\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aWELCH, WILLIAM, ROBERT, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by WELCH,WILLIAM ROBERT,M.D.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, RE-EXCISION, SENTINEL NODE BIOPSY, AXILLARY NODE DISSECTION:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aNEGATIVE LYMPH NODES\u000aSYNOPSIS:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA\u000aSize - REMOVED_DATE cm (multiple additional foci with\u000amicroinvasion (blocks 8, 13, 25, 26)\u000aMultifocal? - yes\u000aHistologic Type - ductal\u000aHistologic Grade (SBR) - III (poor)\u000aNuclear Grade - high\u000aEIC - positive\u000aLymphovascular invasion - absent\u000aDermal lymphatic invasion - absent\u000aSkin invasion - absent\u000aSkeletal muscle invasion - N/A\u000aFinal Margins (invasive) -\u000aNegative (no ink on tumor) - all\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aTypes - comedo\u000aNuclear grade - high\u000aCalcifications in DCIS - absent\u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - present\u000aMicroinvasion (<0.1cm) - present, multiple foci\u000aExtent of DCIS\u000aNumber of blocks/total - REMOVED_DATE blocks\u000aFinal Margins (DCIS)\u000aNegative (>0.3 cm) - superior, posterior, anterior, medial\u000aClose (0.3 cm) - lateral\u000aClose (0.1 cm) - inferior\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - absent\u000aLYMPH NODES\u000aSentinel Lymph Nodes - negative (3 H&E levels examined)\u000aNumber of positive nodes - 0\u000aNumber of nodes examined - 3\u000aAxillary Lymph Nodes - negative\u000aNumber of positive nodes - 0\u000aNumber of nodes examined - 1\u000aTOTAL POSITIVE NODES (sentinel + axillary)- 0:4\u000aOTHER FINDINGS\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia with pagetoid spread\u000aFibroadenoma\u000aCore biopsy site\u000aBiopsy cavity\u000aSkin with scar\u000aAJCC CLASSIFICATION - REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDa pREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID MX\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER/PR/HER-2) -\u000aEstrogen Receptor - negative\u000aProgesterone Receptor - negative\u000aHER/2-neu - positive (3+)\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Ductal carcinoma in situ of right breast with microinvasion; for\u000areexcision and sentinel node biopsy\u000aOperation: Right reexcision, right breast, sentinel node biopsy\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Ductal carcinoma in situ of right breast\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1) Sentinel nodes, right axilla\u000a2) Right axillary contents\u000a3) Ductal carcinoma in situ, right breast; short stitch superior, long stitch\u000alateral\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED: "SENTINEL LYMPH NODES" REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID:\u000aThree lymph nodes negative for carcinoma\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by SMOUSE,JASON H.,M.D.\u000ayThe specimen is received fresh in three parts each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart 1, "sentinel nodes, right axilla", consists of three lymph nodes (1.4 cm,\u000a0.6 cm, REMOVED_DATE cm). The REMOVED_DATE cm lymph node is inked in green and sent entirely as\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. The REMOVED_DATE cm lymph node is inked in black and sent entirely as REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID. The\u000a1.7 cm lymph node is entirely sent as REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aMicro 1: FSAR, ESS\u000aMicro 2: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 2 frags, ESS\u000aMicro 3: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, 2 frags, ESS\u000aPart 2, "right axillary content", consists of a single fragment of fibroadipose\u000atissue measuring REMOVED_DATE cm x 2 cm x 1 cm. There is one potential lymph node\u000ameasuring 2 cm in greatest dimension which is bisected and entirely submitted.\u000aMicro 4: 1 node, 2 frags, ESS\u000aPart 3, "DCIS site, right breast, short stitch superior, long stitch lateral",\u000aconsists of a single fragment of breast tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE cm x REMOVED_DATE cm x 3 cm\u000awith an attached skin ellipse measuring 5 cm in length, REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest\u000awidth, excised to a depth of 6 cm. The specimen is inked by the surgeon for\u000aevaluation of margins per pathology protocol: posterior = black; anterior =\u000ablue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange.\u000aThere is a long stitch and a short stitch designating the lateral and superior\u000asides respectively, placed on the skin. There is a scar measuing REMOVED_DATE cm in\u000alength on the surface of the skin. The remainder of the skin is hyperpigmented\u000awithout any discrete masses or lesions. The specimen is serially sectioned\u000afrom posterior to anterior revealing a biopsy cavity measuring REMOVED_DATE cm x 1 cm x\u000a1 cm in the posterior aspect of the specimen and is grossly 1 cm from the\u000aposterior margin, 1 cm from the inferior margin and greater than 1 cm from all\u000aother margins. Within and around the biopsy cavity are areas of hemorrhage.\u000aThe cavity is surrounded by dense, firm fibrous tissue. A clip is found in the\u000amedial aspect of the specimen with a cylindrical area of scar tissue measuring\u000a1 cm in length from the posterior side and REMOVED_DATE cm in width, tracking to the\u000aarea where the clip is found. The remainder of the breast parenchyma consists\u000aof fibrofatty tissue, 60% adipose tissue and 40% fibrous tissue. Representive\u000aof the entire biopsy cavity, and representive sections of the remainder of the\u000atissue are submitted for histological evaluation. Approximately 60% of the\u000aspecimen is submitted for histological evaluation.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Biopsy cavity with inferior and posterior margins, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Biopsy cavity with lateral and inferior margins\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Core needle biopsy site with superior, inferior and medial\u000amargins, ESS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Fibrous areas, REMOVED_DATE cm anterior to biopsy cavity, and REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aanterior to core biopsy site, with medial and lateral margins\u000aMicro 19: Skin with underlying area of fat necrosis with medial and inferior\u000amargins\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  fibrous areas and core biopsy site, 7 frags, RSS\u000aReports to: CHRISTIAN, ROGER, L. M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: SENTINEL LYMPH NODE\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: LYMPH NODE BIOPSY\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
