000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity\u000ain >10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 50 year old female with right 12:00 breast mass.\u000aBreast Imaging Findings: Ill-defined.\u000aOperation: 11g U/S breast core biopsy\u000aOperative findings: Cores obtained\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Suspected carcinoma\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: Cores (1 brown cassette)\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by BROWNE,TARA-JANE,MB,BCH,BAO\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in one part, labeled with the patient's name,\u000aunit number and "right breast", and consists of a brown cassette containing\u000acores. These are entirely submitted histologic analysis.\u000aMicro 1: cores from brown cassette, 1 frag, ESS\u000ajhl\u000aReports to: FROST, ELISABETH, PEPPERELL M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY(IES)\u000a[report_end]
