VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aKRANE, JEFFREY, FRED, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by KRANE,JEFFREY FRED,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZATION FOR A MASS AND A CLIP (SPECIMEN #1) AND\u000aAXILLARY NODE DISSECTION (SPECIMEN #4):\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA, 1 FOCUS, DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU, LOBULAR CARCINOMA\u000aIN SITU, AND NEGATIVE LYMPH NODES.\u000aSYNOPSIS:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA\u000aSize - REMOVED_DATE cm\u000aMultifocal? - No\u000aHistologic Type - Mixed ductal and lobular\u000aHistologic Grade (SBR) - II (Moderate)\u000aNuclear Grade - Intermediate\u000aEIC - Negative\u000aLymphovascular invasion - Absent\u000aDermal lymphatic invasion - N/A\u000aSkin invasion - N/A\u000aSkeletal muscle invasion - N/A\u000aFinal Margins (invasive)\u000aNegative (no ink on tumor) - All margins.\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU\u000aTypes - Solid and cribriform\u000aNuclear grade - Intermediate\u000aCalcifications in DCIS - Present\u000aCentral necrosis in DCIS - Absent\u000aMicroinvasion (<0.1cm) - Absent\u000aExtent of DCIS\u000aNumber of blocks/total - REMOVED_DATE blocks.\u000aDCIS is present as a minor component of the invasive tumor.\u000aFinal Margins (DCIS)\u000aNegative (>0.3 cm) - Medial, superior, lateral, deep,\u000asuperficial.\u000aClose (0.1-0.3 cm) - Inferior (focal; see specimen #2 for\u000aadditional inferior margin).\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU - Present\u000aLYMPH NODES\u000aAxillary lymph nodes: - Negative.\u000aNumber of positive nodes: - 0\u000aNumber of nodes examined: - 15\u000aTOTAL POSITIVE NODES (axillary) - REMOVED_DATE \u000aOTHER FINDINGS: Atypical lobular hyperplasia with pagetoid spread, florid\u000aepithelial hyperplasia, sclerosing adenosis, cysts, apocrine metaplasia,\u000acalcifications in benign epithelium, core biopsy site.\u000aAJCC CLASSIFICATION - REMOVED_ACCESSION_IDc pREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID MX\u000aSPECIAL STUDIES (ER/PR/HER-2) - Performed previously.\u000a2. SPECIMEN LABELED "INFERIOR SHAVE MARGIN":\u000aLOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU.\u000aAtypical lobular hyperplasia with pagetoid spread.\u000aCysts and sclerosing adenosis.\u000aNo residual DCIS or invasive carcinoma identified.\u000a3. SPECIMEN LABELED "MEDIAL SHAVE MARGIN":\u000aFibrocystic changes.\u000aThere is no evidence of malignancy.\u000aNOTE: Specimens #1 and 2 were reviewed with Dr. A. Richardson, Breast\u000apathology, who concurs.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 50 year old postmenopausal female with recent HRT, whose REMOVED_DATE \u000amammograms demonstrate a 2 cm R breast spiculated mass. REMOVED_DATE \u000acore biopsy revealed invasive carcioma with ductal and lobular features.\u000aOperation: R wire localization excision and axillary dissection.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: R breast cancer.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1. Right breast tissue - short stitch superior, long\u000astitch on chest wall margin.\u000a2. Inferior shave margin & whip stitch new margin.\u000a3. Medial shave margin, whip stitch new margin.\u000a4. Axillary contents.\u000aRADIOLOGY: Clip and mass in specimen. OR called at 12:50 p.m. CG\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by ABBOTT,DEREK W,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name and medical\u000arecord number in four parts.\u000aPart one, "right breast tissue", consists of a fragment of fatty breast tissue\u000a(4.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The specimen has been inked prior to its arrival in\u000asurgical pathology according to the inks protocol. The specimen is inked per\u000apathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior = black; anterior\u000a= blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow; medial = orange.\u000aThe specimen has a long stitch margin marking the lateral margin and short\u000astitch marking the superior margin. The specimen is serially sectioned to\u000areveal a hard white stellate tumor mass (1.7 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with an adjacent\u000alarger but somewhat softer area of possibly representing DCIS and which\u000ameasures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The tumor grossly lies REMOVED_DATE cm from the deep\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE \u000acm from the medial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin and the tumor grossly\u000aextends to the inferior margin. Representative tissue has been submitted for\u000aspecial studies. The specimen is x-rayed and the clip is found to be cassette\u000a1. The clip is removed from the specimen.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  mass at grossly involved inferior margin, 1 frag each cassette,\u000aESS. Cassette 1 with clip + positive inferior margin, 1 frag,\u000aESS.\u000aMicro 5: mass at nearest superior margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 6: mass with nearest medial margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  area of suspected DCIS, 1 frag each cassette, RSS.\u000aMicro 10: nearest superficial margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 11: nearest superior and superficial margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 12: nearest lateral margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 13: nearest deep margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aPart two, "inferior shave margin, whip stitch - new margin", received is a\u000asingle fragment of fatty breast tissue (5.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). There is a stitch\u000aon the specimen marking the new margin. This area around the stitch is inked\u000ain black. The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal areas of suspected DCIS\u000a(1.2 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). These areas lie grossly REMOVED_DATE to REMOVED_DATE cm from the new\u000amargin. The specimen is submitted in its entirety for histologic evaluation.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  inferior shave margin, 2 frags each cassette, ESS.\u000aPart three, "medial shave margin, whip stitch near new margin", received is a\u000asingle fragment of fatty breast tissue (4.6 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). There is a stitch\u000amarking the new margin. This area near the stitch is inked in black. The\u000aspecimen is serially sectioned to reveal fatty breast tissue without gross\u000aabnormality.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  medial shave margin, 2 frags each cassette, ESS.\u000aPart four, "axillary contents", received are multiple fragments of fatty soft\u000atissue (7.4 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm). The lymph nodes are dissected from the specimen\u000aand submitted in their entirety for histologic evaluation.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  4 potential lymph nodes each cassette, 4 frags each cassette,\u000aESS.\u000adwa\u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: LYMPH NODES REGIONAL RESECTION\u000a[report_end]
