VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: FinalType: Surgical Pathology Pathology Report: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID OPERATION DATE: 23 REMOVED_MONTH 04 ACCESSIONED ON: 23 REMOVED_MONTH 04 at 12:24 CLINICAL DATA: Severely atypical ADH on prior biopsy. =============================================================================== *** FINAL DIAGNOSIS *** BREAST (RIGHT), EXCISIONAL BIOPSY: ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA, FOCALLY BORDERING ON DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN-SITU, WITH ASSOCIATED CALCIFICATIONS. SEE NOTE. LOBULAR NEOPLASIA (ATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA). FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH CALCIFICATIONS. HEALING BIOPSY SITE. NOTE: The most atypical focus of atypical ductal hyperplasia extends to REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior margin of the specimen in one focus. Multiple levels examined. BREAST (RIGHT INFERIOR LATERAL), EXCISION: FOCAL ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA. FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH CALCIFICATIONS. HEALING BIOPSY SITE. BREAST (RIGHT POSTERIOR), EXCISION: FOCAL ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA WITH CALCIFICATIONS. FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH CALCIFICATIONS. HEALING BIOPSY SITE. Diagnosis by: MELINDA J. LERWILL, M.D. Signed On: 25 REMOVED_MONTH 04 at 18:45 =============================================================================== GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "right breast" is an oriented fragment of yellow fibrofatty breast parenchyma measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. A short suture denotes the superior margin and a long suture denotes the lateral margin. A silver needle localization wire is in place. The specimen is inked as follows: anterior-blue, posterior-black, superior-green, and inferior-yellow. The specimen is serially sectioned medially towards laterally to reveal a REMOVED_DATE cm silver clip in the medial portion of the specimen with surrounding hemorrhage and golden yellow fat necrosis. This region appears to communicate with the medial, superior, and inferior margins. The specimen is entirely submitted laterally towards medially into cassettes A-J with the hemorrhagic region surrounding the surgical clip into cassettes G-J. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "additional tissue right breast inferior lateral" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm fragment of yellow and firm fibroadipose tissue which is serially sectioned to reveal scattered tan-white fibrous tissue and scattered small yellow foci. The specimen is entirely submitted into cassettes K-L. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "additional tissue right breast deep" is an oriented fragment of yellow fibrofatty tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The black stitch present denotes the deep margin. This surface is inked black and the specimen is serially sectioned and does not reveal any grossly identified nodules. The specimen is entirely submitted into cassettes M-R. Resident: PAUL MICHAELS, MD =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT - REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID REPORTS TO: Michele Annette Gadd, M.D. PART A: BREAST(RIGHT),EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B: BREAST(RIGHT INFERIOR LATERAL),EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART C: BREAST(RIGHT POSTERIOR),EXCISIONAL BIOPSY
