VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast core needle biopsy\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: EVA C. GOMBOS M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Patricia A. R. Brunker, M.D., D. Phil.\u000aPathologist: Susan Lester, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, UPPER INNER, 14 G ULTRASOUND GUIDED CORE NEEDLE BIOPSIES FOR A\u000a2.3 CM PALPABLE IRREGULAR MASS:\u000aPOORLY DIFFERENTIATED EPITHELIOID NEOPLASM, measuring at least REMOVED_DATE cm in\u000asize, with extensive tumor necrosis (> 1 HPF)(see note).\u000aFocal osteoid production is present. Scattered osteoclast-like giant\u000acells are present.\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies are performed with the following results for\u000atumor cells (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID):\u000aEstrogen receptor NEGATIVE\u000aProgesterone receptor NEGATIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu NEGATIVE\u000aCytokeratin REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID NEGATIVE\u000aPANK NEGATIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.2 NEGATIVE\u000aCytokeratin REMOVED_DATE NEGATIVE\u000aCytokeratin 14 NEGATIVE (see note)\u000aCytokeratin 34REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID NEGATIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID POSITIVE - focal, weak\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID NEGATIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID NEGATIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID NEGATIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID NEGATIVE\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID NEGATIVE\u000aNote: Normal breast tissue is not present to act as an internal control\u000afor ER and PR. External controls are appropriately positive.\u000aThere is nucleolar positivity for cytokeratin 14 which is considered a\u000anon-specific result.\u000aThe immunoperoxidase studies do not show evidence of epithelial origin\u000a(i.e. all the keratins are negative) or a vascular origin (i.e. REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aare negative). The melanoma markers are also negative. The presence of\u000afocal osteoid and osteoclast-like giant cells raise the possibility of\u000aosteosarcoma.\u000aThis case was also reviewed by Dr. Jason Hornick.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHISTORY: History of left breast cancer in 1974, s/p chest wall radiation. Now\u000awith right breast mass.\u000aBREAST IMAGING FINDING:\u000a1. Right: REMOVED_DATE cm, palpable irregular mass.\u000aLOCATION:\u000a1. Right: upper inner\u000aTYPE OF CORE NEEDLE BIOPSY:\u000a1. 14 G Ultrasound.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000a1. 14 G Ultrasound - White cassette.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received in formalin, labeled with the patient's name, unit\u000anumber, and "Right breast white cassette", and consists of one white cassette\u000acontaining multiple pink/tan cores (2.3 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm in aggregate).\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: White cassette contents, multi frags, ESS.\u000aLM/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-08-REMOVED_CASE_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Susan Lester M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a6/18/2008\u000a[report_end]
