VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, partial mastectomy\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: JAMES D IGLEHART M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-08-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Stefan Kraft, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPathologist: Jason L Hornick, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY:\u000aPOORLY DIFFERENTIATED EPITHELIOID MALIGNANT NEOPLASM (2.5 cm); see NOTE.\u000aMitoses number up to 68:10 HPF.\u000aNecrosis is present.\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU (2:14 blocks), high nuclear grade, cribriform\u000aand solid types, with necrosis and no calcifications.\u000aDeep surgical margin is negative for tumor (including DCIS; >0.3 cm).\u000aNo lymphovascular invasion.\u000aFifteen lymph nodes, negative for tumor (0:15).\u000aAJCC Classification (6th edition): REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID MX.\u000aImmunohistochemistry performed at BWH demonstrates the following\u000astaining profile in lesional cells:\u000aPositive - EMA (multifocal)\u000aNegative - Pan-K, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.2, p63, S-100, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/6, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID,\u000aER, PR, HER-2/neu, desmin\u000aNOTE: Although all cytokeratin immunostains are negative, given the presence of\u000aadjacent high grade DCIS and EMA expression, the tumor is most consistent with\u000aUNDIFFERENTIATED CARCINOMA.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Not provided\u000aOperation: Right modified radical mastectomy, R axillary node dissection\u000aOperative Findings: Not provided\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Right breast ca\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Right breast and axilla, stitch on apex of axilla\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "right breast and axilla, stitch on apex of axilla", and consists of a 239\u000ag (post-fixation) mastectomy specimen (14.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with overlying\u000atan/white wrinkled skin ellipse (12.5 x REMOVED_DATE cm) with a nipple-areolar complex\u000a(2.5 cm in diameter) with an everted nipple (1.0 cm in diameter). The\u000aepidermal surface is tan/white slightly mottled with no discrete lesions\u000agrossly identified. The deep margin is inked black, and the specimen is\u000aserially sectioned to reveal a well-circumscribed variegated red/brown to\u000atan/white focally necrotic and hemorrhagic mass lesion (2.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm)\u000awhich is located REMOVED_DATE cm from the deep margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from the overlying\u000atan/white wrinkled skin ellipse and is located within the right upper inner\u000aquadrant of the breast. The remainder of the cut surface is tan/yellow and\u000ahomogenous with focal areas of dense white fibrous tissue consistent with\u000aapproximately 15% of the breast parenchyma. There is a scant amount of\u000aattached axillary content which is designated by a black suture. The axillar\u000acontent is sectioned to reveal well-circumscribed pink/tan smooth rubbery\u000anodules consistent with lymph nodes (ranging from REMOVED_DATE cm to REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest\u000adimension). Representative sections are submitted for tissue banking and\u000aspecial studies.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Nipple-areolar complex, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lesion to overlying skin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lesion to deep margin, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Lesion to adjacent breast parenchyma, 1 frag each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Fibrous tissue right upper inner quadrant, 2 frags each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Fibrous tissue right lower inner quadrant, 2 frags each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Fibrous tissue right upper outer quadrant, 2 frags each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Fibrous tissue right lower outer quadrant, 2 frags each, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 7 possible lymph nodes, 7 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 7 possible lymph nodes, 7 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 3 possible lymph nodes, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: 1 possible lymph node, bisected, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000asek\u005cpab\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Jason L Hornick M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a7/3/2008\u000a[report_end]
