ctioning\u000ademonstrates an ill-defined REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm tan/white focally hemorrhagic\u000afirm mass abutting the posterior and medial margins, REMOVED_DATE cm from the closest\u000ainferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the closest anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000aclosest lateral margin, and at least REMOVED_DATE cm from the closest superior margin.\u000aThere are no additional masses grossly. Remaining specimen is comprised\u000apredominantly soft, lobulated tan/yellow adipose tissue (at least 95%), with\u000aoccasional thin fibrous septae. Representative sections are submitted, to\u000ainclude entire mass and surrounding tissue.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Entire mass and surrounding tissue, sequentially from superior to\u000ainferior, multi frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Closest perpendicular inferior margin, multi frags, RSS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Closest superior, anterior margins, 2 frags each, RSS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000adb/elw\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Michelle S Hirsch M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a10/3/2007\u000a[report_end]
