E x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The entire specimen is submitted.\u000aMicro 1: candidate lymph node in adipose tissue, 2 frags, ESS.\u000aPart two, labeled "#2", consists of an oriented left lumpectomy specimen\u000ameasuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. There is a short and long stitch, assuming to\u000aindicate superior and lateral, respectively. There is no skin ellipse on this\u000aspecimen. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation\u000aof margins: posterior = black; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior =\u000agreen; lateral = yellow; medial = orange. Cross sectioning reveals a\u000abrown-black region REMOVED_DATE cm from the deep margin measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm,\u000aconsistent with prior biopsy site. The remaining parenchyma is unremarkable\u000aand consists more than 70% yellow and lobulated adipose tissue. The inked\u000amargins of the previous biopsy site are as follows: REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral\u000amargin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom the inferior margin and REMOVED_DATE cm from the anterior margin. The entire\u000aspecimen is submitted.\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  breast specimen, 10 frags, ESS.\u000aqqd\u000aReports to: IGLEHART, JAMES, DIRK M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: SENTINEL LYMPH NODE\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
