 with a radiograph demonstrating the localizing wire\u000ain place in the area of a metallic surgical clip and a cluster of\u000acalcifications at one edge of the central portion of the specimen (? inferior).\u000aSectioning demonstrates 40% tan/white granular fibrous tissue without palpable\u000aor visible masses, lesions, or other abnormalities. The entire specimen is\u000asequentially submitted from medial to lateral, with perpendicular medial margin\u000ain REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, perpendicular lateral margin in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, and area of interest per radiograph,\u000awire, clip in REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID, REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: The entire specimen, sequentially, multi frags, ESS.\u000aCASE NUMBER: REMOVED_CASE_ID.\u000aDB/ag\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Christopher D. M. Fletcher M.D. FRCPath, Electronically\u000asigned on Friday REMOVED_MONTH 30, 2009 at 01:08:51PM\u000a[report_end]
