aining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  04 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 14 48 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab  labeled with the patient s name and unit number only  is a 20 x 12 x 4 cm  370 gram mastectomy specimen with an overlying 19 x 10 cm skin ellipse with a central REMOVED_DATE cm unremarkable nipple  A 12 x REMOVED_DATE cm area of red yellow to blue discolored skin is centrally located on the ellipse  A REMOVED_DATE cm well healed scar is located REMOVED_DATE cm from the nipple  A biopsy cavity is located REMOVED_DATE cm deep to the scar and REMOVED_DATE cm from the closest surgical margin which is the deep margin  The biopsy cavity measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm  The biopsy cavity is almost completely filled with hemorrhagic  granulation tissue  Surrounding the biopsy cavity is white  fibrotic tissue without evidence of carcinoma  The remainder of the breast parenchyma is composed to breast tissue and adipose tissue without evidence of carcinoma  SECTION CODE  A  biopsy cavity  lateral  B  biopsy cavity  middle  C  biopsy cavity and skin  D  biopsy cavity  E  biopsy cavity  F  deep margin  G  lateral margin  H  lateral margin  I  nipple and skin  J  representative breast tissue  K  FX 1  Resident  Eugene F  Ruffolo  MD 