 performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital. They have not been cleared or approved by the U.S. Food and Drug Administration (FDA). The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary; this laboratory has established and verified the test's accuracy and precision. Added by: Atul Kumar Bhan, M.D. Signed On: 24 REMOVED_MONTH 04 at 15:59 GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "left breast lumpectomy", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm lumpectomy specimen with a short stitch indicating the superior aspect and a long stitch indicating the lateral aspect. The specimen is inked as follows: posterior black, anterior blue, medial green and lateral yellow. The specimen is serially sectioned from superior to inferior to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm tan stellate mass, REMOVED_DATE cm to the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to the anterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to the lateral margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to the medial margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to the superior margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm to the inferior margin. There is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm hemorrhagic area within the mass, consistent with a prior biopsy site. The remainder of the breast parenchyma is tan and fibrofatty with no other masses or lesions identified. Representative sections of the tissue are submitted as follows: A-D: Tumor to margins. E-F: Unremarkable breast parenchyma away from mass. R: Tumor to anterior margin. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "sentinel node, hot and blue, left axilla, REMOVED_DATE ", are two tan firm possible lymph nodes measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. Both lymph nodes are entirely submitted in cassette G. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "additional inferior margin", is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm fibrofatty tissue fragment, which is serially sectioned and entirely submitted in cassettes H-J. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "final shaved margin', superior one half of cavity", are multiple fragments of fibrofatty tissue, aggregating to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The entire specimen is submitted in cassettes K-M. Received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "final shaved margin, inferior half of cavity", are multiple fragments of fibrofatty tissue, aggregating to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The entire specimen is submitted in cassettes N-Q. Resident: NORMA RODRIGUEZ, MD =============================================================================== SOURCE CARE UNIT: SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT - REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID REPORTS TO: Barbara Lynn Smith, M.D. PART A: BREAST(LEFT),EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B: LYMPH NODE(LEFT AXILLA,SENTINEL REMOVED_DATE ),EXCISION PART C: BREAST(LEFT,ADDITIONAL INFERIOR MARGIN),EXCISION PART D: BREAST(LEFT,SHAVED MARGIN SUPERIOR REMOVED_DATE OF CAVITY),EXCISION PART E: BREAST(LEFT,SHAVED MARGIN INFERIOR REMOVED_DATE OF CAVITY),EXCISION
