dial to lateral to\u000areveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm well-circumscribed tan/pink focally hemorrhagic\u000alobulated mass located REMOVED_DATE cm from the deep, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior, REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom the inferior, REMOVED_DATE cm from the medial, REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral, and REMOVED_DATE cm\u000afrom the anterior margins. Representative sections of the tumor and normal\u000atissue are submitted to the tissue bank. No other lesions were identified.\u000aAbutting the mass is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm hemorrhagic area with focal firm\u000ayellow areas which may represent calcifications.\u000aMicro 1: Lesion to posterior margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 2: Hemorrhagic area and lesion to superior margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 3: Lesion to superior and posterior margins, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 4: Lesion to medial and superior margins, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 5: Lesion to inferior margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 6: Lesion to anterior margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 7: Lateral margin, 1 frag, RSS.\u000aMicro 8, 9, 10: Fibrous areas of breast parenchyma, 4 frags, RSS.\u000assa\u000aReports to: RHEI, ESTHER M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000a[report_end]
