VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aFOLKERTH, REBECCA, DUNN, M.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by FOLKERTH,REBECCA DUNN,M.D.\u000a#1. LEFT PARTIAL MASTECTOMY:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA WITH DUCTAL AND LOBULAR FEATURES, multiple foci up to\u000a1.4 cm, well-differentiated, present in 41 of 45 blocks.\u000aThe carcinoma is extensively present at the inferior, medial, lateral and\u000adeep inked margins, and focally at superior margin.\u000aCARCINOMA IN SITU WITH MIXED DUCTAL AND LOBULAR FEATURES present in 41 of\u000a45 blocks.\u000a#4. LEVEL I AND II AXILLARY DISSECTION:\u000aMETASTATIC CARCINOMA in three (3) of eight (8) lymph nodes.\u000a#2. SUPERIOR SHAVE MARGIN:\u000aBreast tissue with no tumor seen.\u000a#3. INFERIOR SHAVE MARGIN:\u000aINVASIVE CARCINOMA present at the new inked resection margin.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: 75-year-old post-menopausal female, not on hormones who underwent\u000aa core biopsy on REMOVED_DATE  at another hospital, for evaluation of a left breast\u000aspiculated density with associated microcalcifications. Pathology revealed\u000ainvasive carcinoma with ductal and lobular features, carcinoma in situ with\u000aductal and lobular features. Clinically the patient has left axillary\u000aadenopathy.\u000aOperation: Left breast partial mastectomy and Level I & II axillary dissection.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast cancer.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1 Left breast partial mastectomy.\u000a#2 Breast tissue, superior shave margin.\u000a#3 Breast tissue, inferior shave margin.\u000a#4 Level I & II axillary dissection.\u000aO.R. CONSULTATION:\u000aSPECIMEN LABELED "LEFT BREAST PARTIAL MASTECTOMY TISSUE" (gross only):\u000aSpiculated ill-defined mass, approximately REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest dimension,\u000agrossly suspicious for invasive carcinoma. The tumor is located below\u000athe skin ellipse and comes to within less than REMOVED_DATE cm of the inferior\u000amargin and REMOVED_DATE cm of the superior margin (closest margin).\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by DRAPKIN,RONNY I.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in four (4) parts, each labeled with the\u000apatient's name and unit number.\u000aPart 1, labeled "Left breast lumpectomy tissue", consists of a single fragment\u000aof pink/yellow fibroadipose tissue (11.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) with an overlying tan\u000askin ellipse (3.6 x REMOVED_DATE cm) that is oriented with three sutures (long=lateral,\u000ashort=superior, whip=deep). The specimen is inked as follows: deep=black;\u000alateral=red; medial=green; superior=blue; inferior=orange; anterior=skin. Upon\u000asectioning, an ill-defined spiculated mass (1.4 cm in greatest dimension) is\u000aidentified that is less than REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000athe superior margin, grossly. The entire specimen is submitted.\u000aCassette REMOVED_DATE  Left breast lumpectomy tissue, REMOVED_DATE fragments each, ESS.\u000aPart 2, labeled "Breast tissue superior shave margin", consists of a single\u000afragment of fibroadipose tissue (5.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) that is oriented with a\u000awhip stitch designating the new margin. The specimen is sectioned at 2 mm\u000aintervals and entirely submitted.\u000aCassette REMOVED_DATE  Breast tissue superior shave margin, REMOVED_DATE fragments each, ESS.\u000aPart 3, labeled "Breast tissue inferior shave margin", consists of a single\u000afragment of fibroadipose tissue (3.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) that is oriented with a\u000awhip stitch designating the new margin. The new margin is inked black. The\u000aspecimen is serially sectioned and entirely submitted.\u000aCassette REMOVED_DATE  Breast tissue, inferior shave margin, multiple fragments each,\u000aESS.\u000aPart 4, labeled "Left axillary contents level I & II", consists of a single\u000afragment of fibroadipose tissue (8.0 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm) that contains ten (10)\u000alymph nodes, the largest measuring REMOVED_DATE cm in greatest dimension.\u000aCassette REMOVED_DATE  Axillary nodes, 1 node, multiple fragments, ESS.\u000aCassette 58: 2 lymph nodes, 4 fragments, ESS.\u000aCassette 59: 2 lymph nodes, 2 fragments, ESS.\u000aCassette 60: 1 lymph node, 2 fragments, ESS.\u000aCassette 61: 1 lymph node, 3 fragments, ESS.\u000aCassette 62: 1 lymph node, 2 fragments, ESS.\u000aCassette REMOVED_DATE  Fibroadipose tissue, multiple fragments, RSS.\u000ardr\u000aReports to: KAELIN, CAROLYN, MARY M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST - EXCISIONAL TISSUE W/MARGINS\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: SURGICAL MARGIN\u000aADDITIONAL SPECIMEN TYPE: LYMPH NODE BIOPSY\u000a[report_end]
