VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aPathology Report REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID BREAST MASTECTOMY - PARTIAL OR SIMPLE\u000aAccessioned On: REMOVED_DATE \u000aKRANE, JEFFREY, FRED, M.D.~PH.D.\u000aDIAGNOSIS: by KRANE,JEFFREY FRED,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aLEFT BREAST, SIMPLE MASTECTOMY (710g):\u000aRESIDUAL INVASIVE CARCINOMA, well differentiated (Bloom-Richardson grade\u000aI/III), present multifocally adjacent to old biopsy site.\u000aThere is an additional focus of invasive carcinoma (0.2 cm) in the same\u000aquadrant (lower outer), not associated with the previous biopsy site.\u000aCARCINOMA IN SITU with ductal and lobular features is present in\u000aassociation with invasive carcinoma.\u000aThe deep resection margin is free of invasive and in situ carcinoma.\u000aOne (1) lymph node negative for metastasis.\u000aBiopsy site with repair reaction.\u000aSkin with recent surgical incision.\u000aMicrocalcifications are present associated with benign epithelium.\u000aNOTE:\u000aIn the current specimen, the invasive tumor has features predominantly of\u000alobular carcinoma. HER-2/neu analysis will be performed and reported as an\u000aaddendum.\u000aSURGICAL ADDENDUM: by LESTER,SUSAN,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aImmunoperoxidase studies on formalin fixed tissue (blocks 10 and 14) do not\u000areveal membrane immunoreactivity for REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu (0) in invasive carcinoma.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 75-year-old postmenopausal woman (not on hormones), s/p a core\u000abiopsy (1/99) revealing invasive ductal carcinoma; a partial mastectomy\u000a(3/16/99) revealing invasive carcinoma (1.4 cm) with ductal and lobular\u000afeatures present at multiple margins, with metastatic carcinoma in three\u000aof eight (3:8) lymph nodes\u000aOperation: Left simple mastectomy\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Left breast cancer\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: 1) Left breast (short/superior; long/lateral)\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by CHAN,JENNIFER A.,M.D.,C.M.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient's name, unit number,\u000aand "left breast (short/superior; long/lateral)", and consists of a left simple\u000amastectomy specimen (710g) including breast (23 x 15 x 5 cm) and attached\u000atan/white skin ellipse (22 x 13 cm). A nipple (1 x 1 x REMOVED_DATE cm) is present.\u000aWithin the skin ellipse, lateral to the nipple in the lower outer quadrant,\u000athere is a recent surgical scar (5 cm). Immediately deep to the scar, there is\u000aa biopsy cavity (6 x 5 x 3 cm). The specimen is received with the biopsy\u000acavity open at the deep margin. The open area, with an irregular border,\u000ameasures 5 cm in greatest dimension. The deep margin is inked black. An\u000aaxillary tail is not attached. Representative sections are submitted.\u000aMicro 1: Nipple, 3 frag, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Skin, 2 frag/cass, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Deep margin and biopsy cavity, multi frag, RSS\u000aMicro REMOVED_DATE  Biopsy cavity, multi frag, RSS\u000aMicro 11: Possible lymph nodes, multi frag, RSS\u000aMicro 12: Upper outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 13: Upper inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 14: Lower outer quadrant, 1 frag, RSS\u000aMicro 15: Lower inner quadrant, 1 frag, RSS\u000ajch\u000aReports to: KAELIN, CAROLYN, MARY M.D.\u000aSPECIMEN TYPE: BREAST MASTECTOMY - PARTIAL OR SIMPLE\u000a[report_end]
