 has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary; this laboratory has established and verified the test's accuracy and precision. Added by: Grace T. McKee,MD Signed On: 09 REMOVED_MONTH 00 at 15:16 GROSS DESCRIPTION: Received fresh in the frozen section are the, labeled with the patient's name, unit number and "left axillary sentinel node" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm tan-red fatty lymph node which is bisected and entirely frozen as FX 1 now as A. Received fresh labeled with the patient's name, unit number, "left breast lumpectomy" is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x to REMOVED_DATE cm portion of breast tissue with a short sutures designating superior and a long suture designating lateral. There is a localizing wire in place without an accompanying radiograph. The specimen is black inked along the posterior aspect, blue inked along the anterior aspect, red inked along the superior aspect, and orange inked along the inferior aspect. Sectioning the specimen reveals a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm hemorrhagic fibrous area surrounded by fat necrosis which is within REMOVED_DATE cm of the posterior margin and a REMOVED_DATE cm of the inferior margin. The remaining parenchyma is predominantly yellow lobulated fatty tissue. Representative sections are submitted and B-K, with the designated area are entirely submitted as B-F. Received fresh labeled with the patient's name, unit number, and "left breast, final shaved margins" are two portions of breast tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm and REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm. The smaller portion is designated as the superior aspect and the larger portion is designated as the deep aspect. The superior aspect is blue inked, the deep margin is blackened. Specimen is serially sectioned and entirely submitted as follows: L-N: Superior margin. O-T: Deep margin. Gross Description by: LORI MARINI Resident: HONGMEI LI, MD *** INTRA-OPERATIVE D