VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: JULIE L JONES M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Matthias D. Hofer, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Hejin P Hahn, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aA. RIGHT BREAST, UPPER OUTER QUADRANT, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR A MASS:\u000aBenign breast tissue with cysts, apocrine metaplasia, fibroadenomatous change,\u000aand calcifications in association with benign epithelium.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000aB. RIGHT BREAST, UPPER INNER QUADRANT, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR\u000aCALCIFICATIONS:\u000aBenign breast tissue with columnar cell change and flat epithelial atypia that\u000ahas associated calcifications.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000aC. RIGHT BREAST, LOWER INNER QUADRANT, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR\u000aCALCIFICATIONS AND A CLIP:\u000aBenign breast tissue with columnar cell change and flat epithelial atypia that\u000ahas associated microcalcifications.\u000aCore biopsy site.\u000aThere is no malignancy seen upon microscopic examination of the specimen,\u000aincluding margins.\u000aNOTE: Parts B & C were also reviewed by Dr. M.W. Bennett, breast pathology who\u000aconcurs.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: Right breast calcifications in the upper inner quadrant and lower\u000ainner quadrant with ADH on core biopsy of lower inner quadrant calcifications\u000aand solid mass in upper outer quadrant.\u000aOperation: Right breast wire-localized excisional biopsy x3.\u000aOperative Findings: None given.\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Preop: Right breast mass and calcifications. Postop:\u000aRight breast mass and calcifications.\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000aA/1. Right breast wire-localized excision of upper outer quadrant mass - short\u000astitch superior, long stitch lateral - mammo.\u000aB/2. Right breast wire-localized excision of upper inner quadrant calcs -\u000ashort stitch superior, long stitch lateral.\u000aC/3. Right breast wire-localized excision of lower inner quadrant calcs -\u000ashort stitch superior, long stitch lateral.\u000aRADIOLOGY: NOTE - Localized cyst was ruptured during needle placement.\u000a#1. RUOQ complicated cyst - specimen radiograph non-specific. U/S - equivocal\u000ahypoechoic lesion that may be small cyst.\u000a#2. Ca++s in specimen.\u000a#3. RLIQ Ca++s: Core bx clip and at least two groups of pleomorphic Ca++s\u000apresent.\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, in three parts, each labeled with the patient's\u000aname and unit number.\u000aPart A, "#1. Right wire-localized excision of upper outer quadrant mass", and\u000aconsists of a REMOVED_DATE (S-I) x REMOVED_DATE (A-P) x REMOVED_DATE (M-L) cm wire-localized breast\u000aexcision specimen accompanied by a radiograph which shows a wire in place in\u000abreast tissue. On the radiograph is a, by the radiologist, "a localization of\u000acomplicated cyst which was drained with wire placement". The accompanying pink\u000asheet reads specimen radiograph nonspecific ultrasound equivocal hypoechoic\u000alesion that may be a small cyst. Two sutures are attached to the specimen\u000adesignating the superior and the lateral margin. The specimen is inked per\u000apath protocol. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation\u000aof margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green;\u000alateral/yellow; medial/orange. A wire enters the specimen at the lateral\u000amargin. The specimen is sectioned into six slices, from lateral to medial with\u000athe most lateral slice designated as slice #1 and the medial margin designated\u000aas slice #6. The wire transfers to all six slices. A 90% of the cut surface\u000aof each slice consists of dense whitish tissue. In slice #6 is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE cm\u000acystic structure which abuts the anterior margin. It is located REMOVED_DATE cm from\u000athe posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm from the superior, REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior, about\u000a0.2 cm to the medial, and roughly REMOVED_DATE cm to the lateral margin. The specimen\u000ais entirely submitted for histologic review. On note; the cyst is in cassette\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID (en face) and REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID (perpendicular).\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #1, lateral margin, perpendicular, 4 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #2, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #3, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #4, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #5, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #6, medial margin, perpendicular, ESS.\u000aPart B, "#2. Right breast wire-localized excision of upper inner quadrant\u000acalcs", and consists of a REMOVED_DATE (S-I) x REMOVED_DATE (A-P) x REMOVED_DATE (M-L) cm breast excision\u000aspecimen. The sutures designate the superior and lateral margins. A\u000aradiograph accompanies the specimen that shows minute calcifications. The\u000aspecimen is six inked. The specimen is inked per pathology protocol for the\u000aevaluation of margins: posterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red;\u000ainferior/green; lateral/yellow; medial/orange. A wire enters the specimen in\u000athe medial aspect and exits in the lateral aspect. The specimen is sectioned\u000ainto four slices from lateral to medial, the lateral aspect designates slice\u000a#1, the medial aspect designates slice #4. A wire cavity can be appreciated in\u000aotherwise normal fatty breast tissue. No firmness, lesions, or other\u000apathologic abnormalities can be appreciated. The specimen is entirely\u000asubmitted for histologic review.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #1, lateral margin, perpendicular, 5 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #2, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #3, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #4, medial margin, perpendicular, 6 frags, ESS.\u000aPart C, "#3. Right breast wire-localized excision of lower inner quadrant\u000acalcs", and consists of a REMOVED_DATE (S-I) x REMOVED_DATE (A-P) x REMOVED_DATE (M-L) cm wire-localized\u000abreast excision specimen. The specimen is received oriented with two stitches\u000adesignating superior and lateral aspects. The specimen is _____ inked. The\u000aspecimen is inked per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins:\u000aposterior/black; anterior/blue; superior/red; inferior/green; lateral/yellow;\u000amedial/orange. A wire enters the specimen in the medial aspect. The specimen\u000ais accompanied by radiograph that shows calcifications in two areas and a clip.\u000aThe accompanying radiology report reads, "right upper quadrant calcs; core\u000abiopsy clip, and at least two groups of pleomorphic calcifications present".\u000aThe specimen is sectioned from lateral to medial into five slices, the lateral\u000aaspect designates slice #1 and the medial aspect designates slice #5. The wire\u000aextended from slice #5 to slice #2. Most prominent in slice #3 and #4 is a REMOVED_DATE \u000acm densely calcified and firm area, which extends from slice #3 to slice #4.\u000aThis area is located about REMOVED_DATE cm from the lateral margin and REMOVED_DATE cm from the\u000amedial margin as well as REMOVED_DATE cm from the inferior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to the\u000asuperior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to the anterior margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm to the posterior\u000amargin. There is one additional area of firmness located in slice #2 measuring\u000a0.2 cm in diameter and located REMOVED_DATE cm from the posterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to the\u000aanterior margin, REMOVED_DATE cm to the superior margin, and REMOVED_DATE cm to the inferior\u000amargin as well as being located approximately REMOVED_DATE cm to the lateral and REMOVED_DATE cm\u000ato the medial margin. The remainder of the specimen consists of 10% fibrous\u000atissue and 90% fatty tissue.\u000aThe specimen is submitted in entirety for histologic review.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #1, lateral margin, perpendicular sections, 5 frags, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #2, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #3, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #4, 1 frag, ESS.\u000aMicro REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID: Slice #5, medial margin, perpendicular, 3 frags, ESS.\u000aMDH/mmm\u000aCASE NUMBER: BS-07-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aBy his/her signature below, the senior physician certifies that he/she\u000apersonally conducted a microscopic examination ("gross only" exam if so stated)\u000aof the described specimen(s) and rendered or confirmed the diagnosis(es)\u000arelated thereto.\u000aFinal Diagnosis by Hejin P Hahn M.D., Ph.D., Electronically signed on\u000a2/16/2007\u000a[report_end]
