VAccession Number: REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID Report Status: Final\u000aType: Surgical Pathology\u000aSpecimen Type: Breast, excisional tissue\u000aProcedure Date: REMOVED_DATE \u000aOrdering Provider: BETH ANN LESNIKOSKI M.D.\u000aCASE: BS-05-REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID\u000aPATIENT: REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME\u000aResident: Lynette M Sholl, M.D.\u000aPathologist: Susan Lester, M.D., Ph.D.\u000aPATHOLOGIC DIAGNOSIS:\u000aRIGHT BREAST, WIRE LOCALIZED EXCISION FOR CLIPS AND CALCIFICATIONS:\u000aTumor bed consisting of fibrous tissue, chronic inflammation, giant cell\u000areaction, and hemosiderin deposition (2 cm) (see note).\u000aOne focus of atypical cells in a duct in the tumor bed consistent with residual\u000aDUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID). This area is REMOVED_DATE cm from the closest\u000amargin.\u000aAtypical ductal hyperplasia, single focus (block REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID).\u000aCalcifications are present in stroma.\u000aNote: The patient presented with a 5 cm poorly differentiated invasive ductal\u000acarcinoma. She is now s/p chemotherapy with a decrease in size of the mass by\u000aMRI to REMOVED_DATE cm.\u000aNo residual invasive carcinoma is present. This would be a Miller-Payne Grade\u000a5 response (complete pathologic response).\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: R breast ca with neoadjuvant chemotherapy.\u000aOperation: R partial mastectomy with mammograph-guided wire localization\u000aOperative Findings: None given\u000aClinical Diagnosis: R breast cancer\u000aRADIOLOGY REPORT: Both clips, calcifications, and both wires are in the\u000aspecimen. Dr. Peter Dean\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED:\u000a1. Right breast tissue with three wires, short stitch at site of residual\u000aultrasound lesion + anterior clip, long stitch posterior clip with residual\u000acalcification\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION:\u000aThe specimen is received fresh, labeled with the patient?s name, unit number,\u000aand "#1 right breast tissue with three wires", and consists of a tan-yellow\u000afi