ed as follows:\u000apositive >10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000apositive - low >0% to <10% of nuclei immunoreactive\u000anegative 0% nuclei immunoreactive\u000aThe lower threshold for clinically significant immunoreactivity has not yet\u000abeen determined.\u000aREMOVED_ACCESSION_ID/neu analysis:\u000aNegative (0): No immunoreactivity or immunoreactivity in <10% of tumor\u000acells.\u000aNegative (1+): Faint weak immunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells but\u000aonly a portion of the membrane is positive.\u000aPositive (2+): Weak to moderate complete membrane\u000aimmunoreactivity in >10% of tumor cells.\u000aPositive (3+): Moderate to strong complete membrane immunoreactivity\u000ain >10% of tumor cells.\u000aCytoplasmic immunoreactivity alone is scored as a negative result.\u000aSome of the reagents used in these assays may be approved for investigational\u000ause only.\u000aCLINICAL DATA:\u000aHistory: A 43 year old female with right breast mass.\u000aOperation: Right breast mass biopsy\u000aClinical Diagnosis: Pending path result\u000aTISSUE SUBMITTED: #1. Right breast mass - stitch marking short superior,\u000along lateral\u000aGROSS DESCRIPTION: by LOMBARD,DAVID B.,M.D.,PH.D.\u000aThe specimen is received fresh in one part, labeled with the patient's name,\u000aunit number and "#1. right breast mass, stitch marking short superior, long\u000alateral", and consists of a mass of fibroadipose tissue (5.2 cm superior to\u000ainferior x REMOVED_DATE cm lateral to medial x REMOVED_DATE cm superficial to deep). Sutures\u000ahave been placed in the specimen by the surgeon marking the superior and\u000alateral aspects of the specimen. The specimen is inked by the pathology\u000aresident per pathology protocol for the evaluation of margins: posterior =\u000ablack; anterior = blue; superior = red; inferior = green; lateral = yellow;\u000amedial = orange. There is an area of hemorrhage adjacent to the posterior\u000aaspect of the specimen (1.5 x REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE 